COLLDATA("hakim","en",[[1,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The most complete of the believers in faith are those with the best character.”"],[2,"The most complete of the believers in faith is the best of them in character."],[3,"Whoever it pleases to find the sweetness of faith, let him love a person, not loving him except for the sake of Allah."],[4,"Umar went out to the mosque one day and found Mu'adh b. Jabal at the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping. He said, \"What makes you weep, O Mu'adh?\" He said, \"A hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ makes me weep. He said, 'The least bit of showing off is shirk, and whoever shows enmity to the friends of Allah has challenged Allah to war. Indeed, Allah loves the righteous, the God-fearing, the hidden ones—those who, when they are absent, are not missed, and when they are present, are not recognized. Their hearts are lamps of guidance; they emerge from every dusty, dark place.'\""],[5,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Īmān (faith) wears out (deteriorates) within [the depths] of each one of you just as worn out clothing has been worn out. Therefore, ask Allah to renew Īmān in your hearts.\"[1]"],[6,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When the servant [of Allah] commits a sin, a black spot appears upon his heart. If he repents, it is polished away. But if he repeats, [the black spot] increases until it grows large in his heart. That is the \"rān\" that Allah mentions in His Book: “Nay! But on their hearts is the rān...” [Muṭaffifīn 83:14][1]"],[7,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued to be asked about the Hour until it was revealed: {In what [position] are you that you should mention it? To your Lord is its finality} [al-Nazi'at 44]."],[8,"When the servant says, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great,' his Lord confirms him, saying, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and I am alone.' And when he says, 'There is no god but Allah, alone, without partner,' his Lord confirms him, saying, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me, and I have no partner.' And when he says, 'There is no god but Allah; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise,' He says, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no god but Me; to Me belongs dominion and to Me belongs praise.' And when he says, 'There is no god but Allah, and there is no might and no power except with Allah,' He says, 'My servant has spoken truth: there is no might and no power except with Me.'"],[9,"Indeed, Allah will single out a man from my ummah before all creation on the Day of Resurrection, and will spread out for him ninety-nine registers, each register as vast as this. Then He will say, 'Do you deny anything of this? Have My recording scribes wronged you?' He will say, 'No, my Lord.' He will say, 'Do you have any excuse?' He will say, 'No, my Lord.' He will say, 'Rather, you have with Us a good deed, and indeed there is no injustice for you today.' Then a card will be brought out, on it: 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.' He will say, 'My Lord, what is this card compared to these registers?' He will say, 'Indeed, you will not be wronged.' Then the registers will be placed in one pan of the scale, and the card in the other pan; the registers will be light, and the card will be heavy. Nothing outweighs the name of Allah."],[10,"The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and the Christians likewise, and my ummah will split into seventy-three sects."],[11,"The covenant that is between us and them is prayer, so whoever abandons it has disbelieved."],[12,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not consider the abandonment of any deed as disbelief except prayer. He did not comment on it, and its isnad is acceptable."],[13,"Whoever commits an offense for which a prescribed punishment is due, and Allah hastens his punishment in this world, then Allah is more just than to double the punishment for His servant in the Hereafter. And whoever commits an offense, and Allah conceals it for him and pardons him, then Allah is more generous than to return to something He has already pardoned."],[14,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him with a horse of his, leading it, a nursing mare, and with her a foal following her. He said, 'Who are you?' He replied, 'I am a prophet.' He said, 'What is a prophet?' He replied, 'A messenger of Allah.' He said, 'When will the Hour arise?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'It is of the unseen, and no one knows the unseen except Allah.' He said, 'Show me your sword.' The Prophet ﷺ gave him his sword, and the man shook it, then returned it to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed, you would not have been able to do what you intended.' He said—and he had said, 'Go to him and ask him about these traits.'"],[15,"Whoever goes to a soothsayer or a fortune-teller and believes him in what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[16,"There is no soul on the earth that dies without associating anything with Allah, bearing witness that I am the Messenger of Allah, with that returning to a certain heart, except that Allah forgives it."],[17,"Shyness and hesitation in speech are two branches of Iman, [while] crudeness and [bluntness] are two branches of hypocrisy.\""],[18,"Wearing simple, modest clothing is part of faith; wearing simple, modest clothing is part of faith."],[19,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the Day of the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Worship your Lord, pray your five prayers, fast your month, pay the zakat of your wealth, and obey those in authority among you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.'"],[20,"A Jew said to his companion, 'Let us go to this prophet ﷺ and ask him about this verse: {And We certainly gave Moses nine clear signs} [Al-Isra 17:101].' He said, 'Do not call him a prophet, for if he hears you, he will become four-eyed.' He said, 'So they asked him, and he said: \"Do not associate anything with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, do not practice sorcery, do not consume usury, do not bring an innocent person to a ruler to have him killed, and do not falsely accuse a chaste woman—and you, O Jews, are specifically obligated not to transgress on the Sabbath.\"' Then they kissed his hand and his foot and said, 'We bear witness that you are a prophet.' He said, 'What prevents you two from embracing Islam?' They said, 'David ﷺ prayed that a prophet would never cease from his descendants, and we fear that the Jews will kill us.'"],[21,"By Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe.' They said, 'And what is that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'A neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his harms.' They said, 'And what are his harms?' He said, 'His evil.'"],[22,"The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the believer is the one whom people trust with their blood and their wealth."],[23,"The most complete of the believers in faith is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[24,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: 'Shall I not inform you about the believer? He is the one whom people trust with their lives and their wealth. The Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The mujahid is the one who strives against his own soul in obedience to Allah. The emigrant is the one who abandons sins and transgressions.' And another addition that meets the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[25,"The believer is the one whom people trust, and the Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is the one who abandons evil. By the One in whose hand is my soul, a servant will not enter Paradise if his neighbor is not safe from his harms."],[26,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'Beware of injustice, for injustice will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of obscenity and deliberate obscenity. Beware of miserliness, for those before you were only destroyed due to miserliness: it commanded them to sever ties, so they severed them; to be stingy, so they were stingy; and to commit immorality, so they committed immorality.' Then a man stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which Islam is best?' He said, 'That the Muslims are safe from your tongue and your hand.' Then that man or another said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which emigration is best?' He said, 'That you abandon what your Lord dislikes.' He said, 'Emigration is of two types: emigration of the settled and emigration of the Bedouin. The emigration of the Bedouin is to respond when called and obey when commanded, while the emigration of the settled is greater in trial and greater in reward.' They both included the hadith of al-Sha'bi from Abdullah b. Amr in abbreviated form, but they did not include this hadith. They agreed on Amr b. Murrah and Abdullah b. al-Harith al-Najrani. As for Abu Kathir Zuhayr b. al-Aqmar al-Zubaydi, he heard from Ali and Abdullah, and from those after them among the Companions. This very hadith is with al-A'mash from Amr b. Murrah."],[27,"Beware of injustice.' Then he mentioned the hadith in full, 'And these additions that we mentioned from Abdullah b. Amr have a sound witness that meets the condition of Muslim from the narration of Abu Hurayrah. They both agreed on Amr from Abdullah b. al-Harith al-Najrani. As for Abu Kathir Zuhayr b. al-Aqmar al-Zubaydi, he heard from Ali and Abdullah, and al-A'mash narrated it from al-A'mash from Amr.'"],[28,"Beware of obscenity and deliberate obscenity, for Allah does not love the obscene or the deliberately obscene. Beware of injustice, for it will be darkness on the Day of Resurrection. Beware of miserliness, for it called those before you and they shed their blood, it called those before you and they severed their ties of kinship, and it called those before you and they violated their sacred things."],[29,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The believer is not one who defames, curses, or is obscene or foul-mouthed.\""],[30,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The believer is not one who defames, curses, or is obscene or foul-mouthed.\" [The hadith has a second witness from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, which must be mentioned even if its chain does not meet the criteria of the two Shaykhs.] [Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis.]"],[31,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The believer is not one who defames, nor is obscene or foul-mouthed.\" [Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla, even if he is accused of poor memory, is one of the jurists of Islam and its virtuous figures, and among the great children of the Companions and Followers from the Ansar, may Allah's mercy be upon them.] [Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis.]"],[32,"\"Whoever does an evil deed and dislikes it while doing it, and does a good deed and is pleased by it, is a believer.\""],[33,"A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?\" He said: \"When your good deed pleases you and your evil deed grieves you, then you are a believer.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is sin?\" He said: \"When something pricks in your chest, leave it.\" This is how 'Ali b. al-Mubarak and Ma'mar b. Rashid narrated it from Yahya b. Abi Kathir. Ma'mar and 'Ali b. al-Mubarak followed him, and it meets their criteria."],[34,"I heard Abu Umamah say: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"What is faith?\" He said: \"When your good deed pleases you and your evil deed grieves you, then you are a believer.\""],[35,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"What is faith?\" He said: \"Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer.\" [These hadiths are all authentic and connected according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs.]"],[36,"I heard 'Awf b. Malik al-Ashja'i say: We camped with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a place. I woke up during the night and saw nothing in the army taller than the back of my saddle; every person and his camel had stuck to the ground. I got up and walked among the people until I reached the resting place of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he was not there. I placed my hand on the bed and found it cold. I went out among the people saying: {Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return} [Al-Baqarah 156], \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been taken away!\" until I left the entire army. Then I saw a black shape and threw a stone at it. I went toward the black shape, and there were Mu'adh b. Jabal and Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, and before us was a sound like the rumble of a mill or like the sound of pebbles when the wind hits them. Some of us said to others: \"O people, stay put until morning or until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ comes to you.\" He said: We waited as long as Allah willed, then he called out: \"Are Mu'adh b. Jabal, Abu 'Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, and 'Awf b. Malik there?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He came toward us, and we went out walking with him, not asking him about anything nor telling him anything. He sat on his bed and said: \"Do you know what my Lord has offered me tonight?\" We said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"He offered me a choice between admitting half of my community to Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.\" We said: \"O Messenger of Allah, ask Allah to make us among its people.\" He said: \"It is for every Muslim.\""],[37,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not fight a people until he had called them [to Islam].\""],[38,"He heard Rabi'ah b. 'Ibad al-Du'ali say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina in their dwellings before he migrated to Madinah, saying: \"O people, Allah commands you to worship Him and not associate anything with Him.\" He said: Behind him a man was saying: \"O people, this one commands you to abandon the religion of your forefathers.\" I asked: \"Who is this man?\" It was said: \"Abu Lahab.\""],[39,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period at the market of Dhu al-Majaz, saying: \"O people, say: There is no god but Allah, and you will prosper.\" He repeated it many times while people gathered around him and followed him. Behind him was a cross-eyed man with two braids and a bright face, saying: \"He is a Sabian, a liar.\" I asked: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"His uncle Abu Lahab.\" [And I only cited 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Zinad as evidence, following their example, for they both cited him as evidence.]"],[40,"An old woman came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was with me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: \"Who are you?\" She said: \"I am Jaththamah al-Muzaniyyah.\" He said: \"Rather, you are Hassana al-Muzaniyyah. How are you? How is your condition? How have you been since we last saw you?\" She said: \"Fine, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah.\" When she left, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do you give such attention to this old woman?\" He said: \"She used to visit us during the time of Khadijah, and keeping good relations is part of faith.\""],[41,"“Indeed, Allah has ninety-nine Names, one hundred less one, whoever counts them shall enter Paradise. He is Allah, the one whom there is none worthy of worship except for Him (Allāhu Lā Ilāha Illā Huwa), the Most Merciful (to the creation) (Ar-Raḥmān), the Most Beneficent (to the believers) (Ar-Raḥīm), the King (Al-Malik), the Free of Deficiencies (Al-Quddūs), the Granter of Safety (As-Salām), the Granter of Security (Al-Mu’min), the Watcher (Al-Muhaimin), the Mighty (Al-ʿAzīz), the Compeller (Al-Jabbār), the Supreme (Al-Mutakabbir), the Creator (Al-Khāliq), the Originator (Al-Bāri’), the Fashioner (Al-Muṣawwir), the Pardoner (Al-Ghaffār), the Overwhelming (Al-Qahhār), the Giving (Al-Wahhāb), the Provider (Ar-Razzāq), the Opener (Al-Fattāḥ), the Knowing (Al-ʿAlīm), the Taker (Al-Qābiḍ), the Giver (Al-Bāsiṭ), the Abaser (Al-Khāfiḍ), the Exalter (Ar-Rāfiʿ), the One who grants honor (Al-Muʿizz), the One who humiliates (Al-Mudhil), the Hearing (As-Samīʿ), the Seeing (Al-Baṣīr), the Judge (Al-Ḥakam), the Just (Al-ʿAdl), the Kind (Al-Laṭīf), the Aware (Al-Khabīr), the Forbearing (Al-Ḥalīm), the Magnificent (Al-ʿAẓīm), the Oft-Forgiving (Al-Ghafūr), the Grateful (Ash-Shakūr), the Most High (Al-ʿAliyy), the Great (Al-Kabīr), the Guardian (Al-Ḥafīẓ), the Powerful (Al-Muqīt), the Reckoner (Al-Ḥasīb), the Glorious (Al-Jalīl), the Generous (Al-Karīm), the Watcher (Ar-Raqīb), the Responder (Al-Mujīb), the Liberal Giver (Al-Wāsiʿ), the Wise (Al-Ḥakīm), the Loving (Al-Wadūd), the Majestic (Al-Majīd), the Reviver (Al-Bāʿith), the Witness (Ash-Shahīd), the Truth (Al-Ḥaqq), the Guarantor (Al-Wakīl), the Strong (Al-Qawiyy), the Firm (Al-Matīn), the One Who Aids (Al-Waliyy), the Praiseworthy (Al-Ḥamīd), the Encompasser (Al-Muḥṣi), the One Who Begins things (Al-Mubdi’), the One Who brings things back (Al-Muʿīd), the One Who gives life (Al-Muḥyi), the One Who causes death (Al-Mumīt), the Living (Al-Ḥayyu), the Self-Sufficient (Al-Qayyūm), the One Who brings into existence (Al-Wājid), the Illustrious (Al-Mājid), the One (Al-Wāḥid), the Master (Aṣ-Ṣamad), the Able (Al-Qādir), the Powerful (Al-Muqtadir), the One who hastens (Al-Muqaddim), the One who delays (Al-Mu’akhkhir), the First (Al-Awwal), the Last (Al-Ākhir), the Apparent (Aẓ-Ẓāhir), the Inner (Al-Bāṭin), the Owner (Al-Wāli), the Exalted (Al-Mutaʿāli), the Doer of Good (Al-Barr), the Acceptor of repentance (At-Tawwāb), the Avenger (Al-Muntaqim), the Pardoning (Al-ʿAfuww), the Kind (Ar-Ra’ūf), the Owner of Dominion (Mālikul-Mulk), the Possessor of Glory and Generosity (Dhul Jalāli wal Ikrām), the One who does justice (Al-Muqsiṭ), the Gatherer (Al-Jāmiʿ), the Rich (Al-Ghaniyy), the Enricher (Al-Mughni), the Preventer (Al-Māniʿ), the Harmer (Aḍ-Ḍār), the One who benefits (An-Nāfiʿ), the Light (An-Nūr), the Guide (Al-Hādi), the Originator (Al-Badīʿ), the Lasting (Al-Bāqi), the Inheritor (Al-Wārith), the Guide (Ar-Rashīd), the Tolerant (Aṣ-Ṣabūr).” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3507)"],[42,"the Messenger of Allah (saas) said: \"Allah has ninety-nine names, one hundred less one, for He is One and loves the odd (numbered). Whoever learns them will enter Paradise. They are: Allah, Al-Wahid (the One), As-Samad (the Self-Sufficient Master who all creatures need, He neither eats nor drinks), Al-Awwal (the First), Al-Akhir (the Last), Az-Zahir (the Most High), Al-Batin (the Most Near), Al-Khaliq (the Creator), Al-Bari (the Inventor of all things), Al-Musawwir (the Bestower of forms), Al-Malik (the King), Al-Haqq (the Truth), As-Salam (the One free from all defects), Al-Mu'min (the Giver of security), Al-Muhaymin (the Watcher over His creatures), Al-'Aziz (the All-Mighty), Al-Jabbar (the Compeller), Al-Mutakabbir (the Supreme), Ar-Rahman (the Most Gracious), Ar-Rahim (the Most Merciful), Al-Latif (the Most Subtle and Courteous), Al-Khabir (the Aware), As-Sami' (the Hearing), Al-Basir (the Seeing), Al-'Alim (the All-Knowing), Al-'Azim (the Most Great), Al-Barr (the Source of goodness), Al-Muta'al (the Most Exalted), Al-Jalil (the Sublime One), Al-Jamil (the Beautiful), Al-Hayy (the Ever-Living), Al-Qayyum (the One Who sustains and protects all that exists), Al-Qadir (the Able), Al-Qahir (the Irrestible), Al-'Ali (the Exalted), Al-Hakim (the Most Wise), Al-Qarib (the Ever-Near), Al-Mujib (the Responsive), Al-Ghani (the Self-Sufficient), Al-Wahhab (the Bestower), Al-Wadud (the Loving), Ash-Shakur (the Appreciative), Al-Majid (the Most Gentle), Al-Wajid (the Patron), Al-Wali (the Governor), Al-Rashid (the Guide), Al-'Afuw (the Pardoner), Al-Ghafur (the Forgiver), Al-Halim (the Forbearing One), Al-Karim (the Most Generous), At-Tawwab (the Acceptor of Repentance), Ar-Rabb (the Lord and Cherisher), Al-Majid (the Most Glorious), Al-Wali (the Helper), Ash-Shahid (the Witness), Al-Mubin (the Manifest), Al-Burhan (the Proof), Ar-Ra'uf (the Compassionate), Ar-Rahim (the Most Merciful), Al-Mubdi' (the Originator), Al-Mu'id (the Restorer), Al-Ba'ith (the Resurrector), Al-Warith (the Supreme Inheritor), Al-Qawi (the All-Strong), Ash-Shadid (the Severe), Ad-Darr (the One Who harms), An-Nafi' (the One Who benefits), Al-Baqi' (the Everlasting), Al-Waqi (the Protector), Al-Khafid (the Humble), Ar-Rafi' (the Exalter), Al-Qabid (the Retainer), Al-Basit (the Expander), Al-Mu'izz (the Honorer), Al-Mudhill (the Humiliator), Al-Muqsit (the Equitable), Ar-Razzaq (the Providor), Dhul-Quwwah (the Powerful), Al-Matin (the Most Strong), Al-Qa'im (the Firm), Ad-Da'im (the Eternal), Al-Hafiz (the Guardian), Al-Wakil (the Trustee), Al-Fatir (the Originator of creation), As-Sami' (the Hearer), Al-Mu'ti (the Giver), Al-Muhyi (the Giver of life), Al-Mumit (the Giver of death), Al-Mani' (the Withholder), Al-Jami' (the Gatherer), Al-Hadi (the Guide), Al-Kafi (the Sufficient), Al-Abad (the Eternal), Al-'Alim (the Knower), As-Sadiq (the Truthful), An-Nur (the Light), Al-Munir (the Giver of light), At-Tamm (the Perfect), Al-Qadim (the Earlier), Al-Witr (the One), Al-Ahad (the Lone), As-Samad [(the Self-sufficient Master, Who all creatures need, (He neither eats no drinks)]. He begets not, nor was He begotten. And there is none co-equal or comparable unto him.\"(One of the narrators) Zuhair said: We heard from more than one of the scholars that the first of these (names) should begin after saying: La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu, bi yadihil-khair wa Huwa 'ala kulli shay-in Qadir, la ilaha illallahu lahul-asma'ul-husna [None has the right to be worshipped but Allah, with no partner or associate. His is the dominion and all praise is His. In His Hand is (all) goodness, and He is Able to do all things, none has the right to be worshipped but Allah, and His are the (Most) Beautiful Names]. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3861)"],[43,"I heard ʿĪsā, a man from Banū Asad, relate from Zirr, from ʿAbd Allāh, from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Belief in omens is polytheism, but God ﷻ removes it through reliance on Him.\" This ʿĪsā is Ibn ʿĀṣim al-Asadī, a Kufan, trustworthy; ʿĪsā ibn Abī ʿĀṣim is trustworthy."],[44,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Belief in omens is part of polytheism, and a refuge, but God removes it through reliance on Him.\""],[45,"\"Whoever swears by other than God has disbelieved.\""],[46,"\"Every oath sworn by other than God is polytheism.\""],[47,"Abū al-ʿĀliyah came to me, I and a companion of mine, and said: \"Come, for you two are younger and more retentive of hadith than I.\" He took us until we came to Naṣr ibn ʿĀṣim al-Laythī and said: \"Relate to these two your hadith.\" Naṣr said: ʿUqbah ibn Mālik, who was of his clan, related to us: The Messenger of God ﷺ sent out a raiding party, and they raided a people. A man from the people fled, and a man from the raiding party followed him with his sword drawn. The fugitive from the people said: \"I am a Muslim,\" but he paid no heed to it and struck him and killed him. The report reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he spoke harshly. It reached the killer, and while the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering a sermon, the killer said: \"O Messenger of God, by God, he only said what he said to seek protection from being killed.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned away from him and from those in front of him among the people and resumed his sermon. Then he said a second time: \"O Messenger of God, by God, he only said what he said to seek protection from being killed.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned away from him and from those in front of him among the people and resumed his sermon. Then he could not refrain from saying a third time: \"By God, O Messenger of God, he only said what he said to seek protection from being killed.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ turned to him, displeasure evident on his face, then said: \"God ﷻ has refused to accept my intercession for one who kills a believer.\" He said it three times."],[48,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said: \"Now then, what is the matter with a man who kills a man while he says, 'I am a Muslim'?\" The killer said: \"O Messenger of God, he only said it seeking protection.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Thus,\" and he disliked his statement and turned his face away from him, then said: \"God has refused to accept my intercession for one who kills a Muslim. God has refused to accept my intercession for one who kills a Muslim.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[49,"Three things I swear by: God will not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share. The shares of Islam are fasting, prayer, and charity. God will not entrust a servant to other than Himself on the Day of Resurrection. And a man does not love a people except that God will place him with them. The fourth, if I swear by it, I hope not to sin: God does not conceal a servant's faults in this world except that He will conceal them in the Hereafter."],[50,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"I wish to embrace Islam, so teach me some of the laws of Islam.\" He mentioned prayer, the month of Ramadan, and the times of prayer. I said: \"O Messenger of God, you mention hours in which I am busy, but teach me a comprehensive word.\" He said: \"If you are busy, do not be distracted from the two ʿaṣrs.\" I said: \"What are the two ʿaṣrs?\" It was not the language of my people. He said: \"Fajr and ʿAṣr.\""],[51,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me, and among what he taught me he said: \"Guard the five prayers.\" I said: \"These are hours in which I have occupations, so tell me a comprehensive matter that, if I do it, will suffice me.\" He said: \"Guard the two ʿaṣrs.\" He said: It was not from our language, so I said: \"What are the two ʿaṣrs?\" He said: \"A prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.\" Abū Ḥarb ibn Abī al-Aswad al-Dīlī is a major successor, having met senior Companions; his hearing is not diminished from Faḍālah ibn ʿUbayd al-Laythī, for Hushaym ibn Bashīr is a well-known memorizer, and Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh al-Wāsiṭī is the author of a book. This is in sum as Muslim included in the Book of Faith the hadith of Shuʿbah from ʿUthmān ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Mawhab, and after it from Muḥammad ibn ʿUthmān from his father. Hushaym was contradicted; Khālid ibn ʿAbd Allāh related it from Abū Ḥarb, from ʿAbd Allāh ibn Faḍālah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of God ﷺ taught me."],[52,"\"Islam has a light and a beacon like the beacon of a road.\""],[53,"\"Islam is that you worship God without associating anything with Him, establish prayer, give zakah, fast Ramadan, perform pilgrimage to the House, enjoin good, forbid evil, and greet your family. Whoever omits any of these has left a share of Islam, and whoever abandons all of them has turned his back on Islam.\""],[54,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not teach you, or shall I not guide you to a word from beneath the Throne, from the treasures of Paradise?' You say: 'There is no power or might except with Allah.' So Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, says: 'My slave has submitted and surrendered.'\""],[55,"\"If two men enter Islam and then shun each other, one of them is outside Islam until the wrongdoer returns.\""],[56,"When a servant commits fornication, faith departs from him and is like a canopy; then when he desists from it, faith returns to him."],[57,"Whoever commits fornication and drinks wine, Allah strips faith from him just as a man strips a shirt from his head."],[58,"Modesty and faith are paired together; when one is lifted, the other is lifted."],[59,"The translation of the given Arabic phrase is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Verily, the believer is kind and there is no goodness in one who is not kind and is not shown kindness.'\""],[60,"There is no servant who worships Allah, associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, and avoids the major sins, but that he enters Paradise.\" He said: They asked him, \"What are the major sins?\" He said, \"Associating partners with Allah, fleeing from the battlefield, and killing a soul."],[61,"When he came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what thing makes Paradise obligatory?\" He said: \"You must speak well and give food.\""],[62,"He came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ heard him being addressed by the kunya Abu al-Hakam, so he said: \"Allah is al-Hakam (the Judge); why are you given the kunya Abu al-Hakam?\" He said: \"When my people disagree, I judge between them and both parties are satisfied.\" He said: \"Do you have children?\" He said: \"Shurayh, 'Abd Allah, and Muslim, the sons of Hani'.\" He said: \"Which of them is the eldest?\" He said: \"Shurayh.\" He said: \"Then you are Abu Shurayh.\" And he supplicated for him and his children. [I have mentioned in the Book of Knowledge, in the mention of the mukhadramun, Shurayh b. Hani', for he lived through the pre-Islamic era and Islam, and he never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he is counted among the Followers.] Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[63,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {Indeed Allah is ever Hearing and Seeing} [al-Nisa' 58], then he placed his index finger on his eyes and his thumbs on his ears."],[64,"There has been no trial, nor will there be until the Hour arises, greater than the trial of the Dajjal; and there is no prophet but he warned his people about him. I will tell you something about him that no prophet before me told: he placed his hand on his eye, then said, 'I bear witness that Allah, exalted is He, is not one-eyed.'"],[65,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was of shabby appearance. He said: 'Do you have any wealth?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What kind of wealth?' I said: 'Of every kind, camels, horses, slaves, and sheep.' He said: 'If Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen on you.' He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do the camels of your people give birth to young with healthy ears, then you take a razor and cut their ears and say they are buhr, and slit them or slit their hides and say they are haram, thereby forbidding them to yourself and your family?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Everything that Allah has given you is lawful for you. Allah's forearm is stronger than your forearm, and Allah's razor is sharper than your razor.'"],[66,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding this verse: {And when his Lord appeared to the mountain, He made it} [al-A'raf 143]: 'There appeared from Him the amount of this.' [On the condition of Muslim]"],[67,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {He said: My Lord, show me that I may look at You} [al-A'raf 143]. He said: 'He brought forth from the light the like of this' and he pointed with his hand to half of the little finger's fingertip, and he struck the chest of Hammad with it. He said: 'And the mountain sank.'"],[68,"There are three whom Allah loves and at whom He laughs: the one who, when a company is exposed, fights behind it with his own soul for Allah, exalted is He."],[69,"“No one enters Paradise who has in his heart a grain’s weight of pride.” A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I like my garment to be new, my head to be oiled, and the strap of my sandal to be new” — and he mentioned other things until he mentioned the thong of his whip. He said: “That is beauty, and Allah is beautiful and loves beauty. But pride is rejecting the truth and looking down on people.”"],[70,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, is it part of pride that I wear a fine suit?” He said: “Allah is beautiful and loves beauty.”"],[71,"Allah summoned Jibril and sent him to Paradise and said: “Look at it and what I have prepared in it for its people.” He said: “By Your might, no one hears of it except that he enters it.” So it was surrounded with hardships. He said: “Return to it and look at it.” So he returned and said: “By Your might, I fear that no one will enter it.”"],[72,"When Allah created Paradise, He said: “O Jibril, go and look at it.” He said: so he went and looked at it, and said: “No one hears of it except that he enters it.” Then He surrounded it with hardships. Then He said: “Go and look at it.” He said: so he went and looked at it, and said: “By Your might, I fear that no one will enter it.” Then He created the Fire and said: “O Jibril, go and look at it.” He said: so he went and looked at it, and said: “No one hears of it and enters it.” He said: so He surrounded it with desires. Then He said: “Go and look at it.” He said: so he went and looked at it, and said: “O Lord, by Your might, I fear that no one will remain except that he enters it.”"],[73,"He said to it and to the earth: “Come willingly or unwillingly.” He said to the sky: “Bring out your sun, your moon, and your stars,” and He said to the earth: “Split open your rivers and bring out your fruits.” They said: “We come willingly.”"],[74,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us in what was read to Malik, from Zayd b. Abi Unaysa, from ‘Abd al-Hamid b. ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Zayd b. al-Khattab, from Muslim b. Yasar al-Juhani, that ‘Umar b. al-Khattab was asked about this verse: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their backs, their offspring} [Al-A‘raf: 172]. ‘Umar b. al-Khattab said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about it, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah created Adam, then wiped his back with His right hand and extracted from him a progeny and said: ‘I created these for Paradise, and they will act with the deeds of the people of Paradise.’ Then He wiped his back and extracted from him a progeny and said: ‘I created these for the Fire, and they will act with the deeds of the people of the Fire.’””"],[75,"Allah took the covenant from the back of Adam and extracted from his loins a progeny that He scattered like tiny particles before Him, then He spoke to them and said: “Am I not your Lord?” They said: “Yes, we bear witness” — lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection: “We were unaware of this,” or lest you should say: “Our fathers associated partners before, and we were descendants after them. Will You destroy us for what the falsifiers did?”"],[76,"“On the day Allah spoke to Musa, he was wearing a woolen cloak, woolen trousers, a woolen cap, a woolen wrap, and two sandals made from the hide of a donkey that was not properly slaughtered.”"],[77,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You must wear wool; you will find the sweetness of faith in your hearts.” He transmitted it through a weak chain."],[78,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys, his companions drew near in their travel, so he raised his voice with these two verses: {O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing. On the day you see it, every nursing mother will be distracted from what she nurses, and every pregnant woman will deliver her burden, and you will see people drunk, though they are not drunk, but the punishment of Allah is severe} [Al-Hajj: 1–2]. When his companions heard that, they urged their mounts on and knew that he was about to say something. When they gathered around him, he said: “Do you know which day that is?” They said: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “That is the day when Adam will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: ‘O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire.’ He will say: ‘What is the delegation of the Fire?’ He will say: ‘From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.’” He said: so they were struck with despair until they did not even show a smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he said: “Know and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations that never accompany anything except that they make it numerous: Ya’juj and Ma’juj, and those who have perished from among the children of Adam and the children of Iblis.” He said: so that relieved the people. He said: “Know and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among mankind only like a mark on the foreleg of a beast, or like a mole on the side of a camel.”"],[79,"When this verse was revealed: {O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the quaking of the Hour is a tremendous thing} [Al-Hajj: 1] up to His saying: {but the punishment of Allah is severe} [Al-Hajj: 2], to the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a journey, he mentioned the hadith similarly. They both agreed on transmitting the hadith of al-A‘mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa‘id, part of this text. They transmitted the hadith of al-A‘mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa‘id."],[80,"“O Adam,” and he will say: “At Your service, at Your service, and all good is in Your hands.” He said: He will say: “Send forth the delegation of the Fire.”"],[81,"«Guard yourselves against the supplications of the wronged, for they ascend to the sky as if they were sparks.»"],[82,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I am the master of the people on the Day of Resurrection, and I say this without pride. There is no one except he will be under my banner on the Day of Resurrection, awaiting deliverance. With me is the banner of praise. I shall walk and the people shall walk with me until I come to the gate of Paradise and seek to open it. It will be said, 'Who is this?' I will say, 'Muhammad.' It will be said, 'Welcome to Muhammad.' When I see my Lord, I will fall down prostrate before Him, gazing at Him."],[83,"Al-Awza'i praised and the wording of this hadith is from Abu al-Abbas who said: Rabia bin Yazid and Yahya bin Abi 'Amr al-Saybani narrated to me, they said: 'Abdullah bin Firoz al-Daylami narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Abdullah bin 'Amr bin al-'As while he was in a wall in Taif called al-Wahat and he was lecturing a young man from the Quraysh. And this young man would indulge in drinking wine. So I said to Abdullah bin 'Amr bin al-'As, \"Tell me something about you that I can narrate from you about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"Whoever drinks wine, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings.\" The young man clenched his hand with the hand of Abdullah, then he turned away. Abdullah said: \"Indeed, a miserable person is the one who is miserable in his mother's womb. And whoever leaves his house intending only to pray in al-Masjid al-Haram, he will come out of his sin like the day his mother gave birth to him.\" Abdullah bin 'Amr bin al-'As said: \"O Allah! I will not permit anyone to attribute to me what I did not say. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever drinks wine, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings. But if he repents, Allah will accept his repentance. But if he returns to it, his repentance will not be accepted for forty mornings.' I do not remember if it was on the third or fourth time that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then it is a right upon Allah to make him drink from the mud of the Kohl on the Day of Resurrection.'\" He said: \"I also heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Indeed, Allah created His creation in darkness and then He cast upon them some of His light. So whoever receives some of that light on that day, then he has been guided. And whoever is misguided, then it is because of that.' So I say: The pen has dried upon the knowledge of Allah.\" And I also heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Indeed, Sulaiman bin Dawud asked his Lord three times, so He gave him two and we hope that He gave him the third. He asked Him for a judgment that aligns with his judgment, so He gave it to him. And he asked Him for a kingdom that none after him should have, so He gave it to him. And he asked Him that whenever a man leaves his house and intends only to pray in this mosque, he should come out of his sin like the day his mother gave birth to him. We hope that Allah has given him that.' Al-Awza'i said: Rabia bin Yazid narrated this hadith to me between al-Miqsilat and al-Jasa'ir."],[84,"Allah created Adam, then created the creatures from his loins, then said: 'These are for Paradise, and I care not; and these are for the Fire, and I care not.' The narrator said: It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then on what basis should we act?' He said, 'On the conformity with divine decree.'"],[85,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Indeed, Allah is the Creator of every maker and his making.» According to the condition of Muslim."],[86,"«Indeed, Allah is the Creator of every maker and his making.»"],[87,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, incantations which we used to recite and medicines which we used to treat with—do they repel anything from the decree of Allah, Exalted?' He said: «It is from the decree of Allah.»"],[88,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, incantations which we used to recite and medicines which we used to treat with—do they repel anything from the decree of Allah?' He said: «It is from the decree of Allah.»"],[89,"«Birds fly according to decree.» And he liked a good omen."],[90,"«A servant does not believe until he believes in four things: until he testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah who sent me with the truth; and he believes in resurrection after death; and he believes in divine decree.»"],[91,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it. «Abu Hudhayfah Musa b. Mas'ud al-Nahdi—though al-Bukhari relies on him as evidence—he makes many errors; he is not to be preferred over Abu 'Asim al-Nabil and Muhammad b. Kathir and their peers; rather, he is to be deemed mistaken when he contradicts them. The evidence for what I have mentioned is the corroboration of Jarir b. 'Abd al-Hamid al-Thawri in his narration from Mansur, from Rib'i, from 'Ali. Jarir is among the most knowledgeable of people in the hadith of Mansur.» According to the conditions of both (al-Bukhari and Muslim)."],[92,"ʿNo one (truly) believes until he believes in four things; until he believes that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah Who sent me with the truth, and until he believes in the resurrection after death, and until he believes in the divine will and decree.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 758)"],[93,"«The affair of this community will continue to be in harmony—or he said: near to one another—as long as they do not speak about the children and divine decree.»"],[94,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Indeed, Allah has divided your characters among you just as He has divided your provisions among you. And Allah gives the world to whom He loves and whom He does not love, but He gives faith only to whom He loves.»[1]"],[95,"\"Indeed Allah has apportioned among you your characters just as He has apportioned among you your provisions; and indeed Allah gives wealth to whom He loves and whom He does not love, but He does not grant faith except to whom He loves.\""],[96,"I heard Kurz b. 'Alqamah say: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: O Messenger of Allah, is there a limit to Islam? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes, whichever household of the Arabs and non-Arabs Allah intends good for, He brings Islam upon them, then trials fall upon them as if they were clouds.\" Muhammad b. Rashid and Yunus b. Yazid concurred with this from al-Zuhri. They did not include it in their two Sahihs due to 'Urwah's being alone in narrating from Kurz, and he is a companion."],[97,"A bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, is there a limit to Islam? He said: \"Yes, whichever household of the Arabs and non-Arabs Allah intends good for, He brings Islam upon them, then trials fall upon them as if they were clouds.\""],[98,"Abu Ali Al-Janbi informed him that he heard Fadalah bin Ubaid telling that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying: \"Blessed is the one who is guided to Islam and his livelihood is sufficient and content.\""],[99,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the punishment of the grave.\""],[100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O people, I am only a mercy that has been gifted.\""],[101,"He narrated to us: Faith used to be given before the Qur'an, and a surah would descend upon Muhammad ﷺ, and he would learn its lawful and unlawful and what it was proper to pause at within it, just as you learn the Qur'an.\" Then he said: \"I have indeed seen men to whom one of them would be given the Qur'an, and he would read from its opening to its end without knowing its command or its prohibition, or what it was proper to pause at within it, scattering it as one scatters worthless dates.\""],[102,"Six are those whom I curse and Allah curses, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: the one who denies Allah's decree, the one who adds to Allah's Book, the one who dominates with tyranny, abasing whom Allah has honored and honoring whom Allah has abased, the one who regards as lawful what Allah has forbidden from His sacred things, the one who regards as lawful from my offspring what Allah has forbidden, and the one who abandons my sunnah."],[103,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Muhammad, do you see a paradise whose width is the heavens and the earth—where then is the Fire? He said: \"Do you see the night that has covered everything—where then has the day been placed?\" The man said: Allah knows best. He said: \"Thus Allah does whatever He wills.\""],[104,"\"I do not know whether Tubba' was a prophet or not, and I do not know whether Dhu al-Qarnayn was a prophet or not, and I do not know whether the prescribed punishments are expiations for those who undergo them or not.\""],[105,"\"When Allah created Adam, He formed him and left him in the Garden for as long as Allah willed to leave him. Iblis began to circle around him, and when he saw that he was hollow, he knew that he was a creature who would not have self-control.\""],[106,"\"You shall surely follow the ways of those before you, span by span, cubit by cubit, and handspan by handspan, until even if they entered a lizard's hole you would enter it with them.\" He said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, the Jews and the Christians? He said: \"Who else then?\""],[107,"\"O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the grave.\" Then he said: \"When the Muslim man is at the approach of the Hereafter and the severance from this world, the Angel of Death comes and sits at his head, and angels descend from heaven whose faces are like the sun, with them shrouds from the shrouds of Paradise and perfume from the perfume of Paradise, and they sit from him at the distance of the sight.\" He said: Then the Angel of Death says: O tranquil soul, come out to forgiveness from Allah and good pleasure. He said: Then it comes out, flowing as a drop flows from a waterskin, and they do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye, but they ascend with it to heaven, and they do not pass by any host of angels but they say: What is this good spirit? And they say: So-and-so son of so-and-so, with the best of his names. Then when it reaches the heaven, the gates of heaven are opened for it, and then the nearest angels of each heaven escort it to the heaven that follows, until it is brought to the seventh heaven. Then it is said: Write his record in 'Illiyyin. Then it is said: Return My servant to the earth, for I promised them that from it I created them, and into it I return them, and from it I shall bring them forth another time. Then his soul is returned to his body, and the angels come to him and say: Who is your Lord? He said: He says: Allah. They say: What is your religion? He says: Islam. They say: Who is this man who was sent among you? He said: He says: The Messenger of Allah. He said: They say: And what makes you know that? He said: He says: I read the Book of Allah and believed in it and affirmed it. He said: Then a caller calls from heaven: He has spoken the truth, so spread for him from Paradise and clothe him from Paradise and show him his place in Paradise. He said: And his grave is widened for him, and the breeze and fragrance of Paradise come to him. He said: That is done for them, and a man with a handsome face, handsome clothes, and a pleasant scent appears to him and says: Rejoice in what will delight you; this is your day which you were promised. He says: Who are you? Your face is a face that brings good tidings. He said: He says: I am your righteous deeds. He said: Then he says: Lord, establish the Hour, so that I may return to my family and my wealth. Then he recited: {Allah makes firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter} [Ibrahim 27]. As for the wicked man, when he is at the approach of the Hereafter and the severance from this world, the Angel of Death comes to him and sits at his head, and the angels descend with black faces, with them coarse haircloth, and they sit from him at the distance of the sight. Then the Angel of Death says: Come out, O wicked soul, to wrath from Allah and anger. He said: Then it disperses through his body, and the veins and nerves are torn with it, as wet wool is pulled out with a many-pronged skewer. He said: Then they rise to it and do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye, but they ascend with it to heaven, and they do not pass by any host of angels but they say: What is this wicked spirit? He said: They say: So-and-so, with the ugliest of his names. He said: Then when it is brought to the heaven, the gates of the heavens are shut before it. He said: And it is said: Write his record in Sijjin. He said: Then it is said: Return My servant to the earth, for I promised them that from it I created them, and into it I return them, and from it I shall bring them forth another time. He said: Then his soul is cast down until it falls into his body. He said: Then he recited: {And whoever associates others with Allah, it is as if he had fallen from the sky and the birds had snatched him, or the wind had blown him to a far-off place} [al-Hajj 31]. He said: Then the angels come to him and say: Who is your Lord? He said: He says: I do not know. Then a caller calls from heaven: He has lied, so spread for him from the Fire and clothe him from the Fire and show him his place in the Fire. He said: Then his grave becomes narrow upon him until his ribs interlace within it. He said: And its heat and burning come to him. He said: That is done to him, and a man with an ugly face, ugly clothes, and a foul smell appears to him and says: Rejoice in what will grieve you; this is your day which you were promised. He said: He says: Who are you? Your face is a face that brings evil tidings. He said: He says: I am your wicked deeds. He said: And he says: Lord, do not establish the Hour.\""],[108,"\"Sleep the sleep of the God-fearing for the first believer, and it is said to the wicked: Sleep, bitten, for there is no creature on the earth but has a share in his body.\""],[109,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a funeral, and we came to the grave before it was dug as a lahd. And he mentioned the hadith. As for the hadith of Shu'bah,"],[110,"from the Prophet ﷺ in the hadith of the grave, on their condition, for they both used al-Minhal as evidence. As for the hadith of Za'idah,"],[111,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over the funeral of a man from the Ansar. Then he mentioned the hadith of the grave in full."],[112,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the believer and the disbeliever, then he mentioned a portion of the hadith of the grave. It has thus become clear, through the original and the supporting narration, that this hadith is sound. And perhaps someone might imagine that the hadith which"],[113,"he said: 'We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the funeral of a man from the Ansar, and we came to the grave before it was dug as a lahd. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down, faced the qiblah, and we sat around him.' Then he mentioned the hadith. 'This hadith is deemed defective, but it is not so, for the mention of Abu al-Bakhtari in this hadith is an error by Shu'ayb b. Safwan, due to the consensus of the trustworthy imams' on its transmission from Yunus b. Khabbab, from al-Minhal b. 'Amr, from Zadhan, that he heard al-Bara'. Ja'far b. Muhammad b. Nasr al-Khuldi narrated to us in Baghdad, from dictation, confirming the soundness of what I have mentioned: 'Ali b. 'Abd al-'Aziz narrated to us: Ibrahim b. Ziyad Sabalan narrated to us: 'Abbad b. 'Abbad narrated to us, saying: I came to Yunus b. Khabbab at Mina, near the minaret, while he was relating stories, and I asked him about the hadith of the punishment of the grave, and he narrated it to me."],[114,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a funeral, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat on the grave and we sat around him. And he mentioned the hadith in full. 'This is the correct, preserved version from the hadith of Yunus b. Khabbab.' And thus it was narrated by Abu Khalid al-Dalani, 'Amr b. Qays al-Mula'i, and al-Hasan b. 'Abd Allah al-Nakha'i, from al-Minhal b. 'Amr. 'As for the hadith of Abu Khalid al-Dalani,'"],[115,"from al-Minhal b. 'Amr. 'And as for the hadith of 'Amr b. Qays al-Mula'i,'"],[116,"from al-Minhal b. 'Amr. 'And as for the hadith of al-Hasan b. 'Ubayd Allah,'"],[117,"from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it. These chains of transmission that I have mentioned are all sound according to the condition of the two Shaykhs."],[118,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Bilal were walking in al-Baqi', the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Bilal, do you hear what I hear?' He said: 'No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not hear it.' He said: 'Do you not hear the people of the graves being punished?'"],[119,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was feverish, with a velvet cloak over him. He placed his hand on it and found its heat above the cloak. Abu Sa'id said: 'How severe is the heat of your fever, O Messenger of Allah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, for us trial is intensified and reward is multiplied.' Then he said: 'O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried?' He said: 'The prophets.' He said: 'Then who?' He said: 'The scholars.' He said: 'Then who?' He said: 'Then the righteous. One of them would be tried with poverty until he found nothing but a cloak to wear, and would be tried with lice until it killed him. And one of them was more joyful at trial than one of you is at a gift.' Abu al-'Abbas narrated to us from Bahr in the Musnad and from al-Rabi' in al-Fawa'id, and I combined them."],[120,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked: 'Which people are most severely tried?' He said: 'The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tried according to his religion. If his religion is firm, his trial is severe; and if his religion is weak, his trial is light.' And"],[121,"“I said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tested?’ He said: ‘The Prophets, then the next best and the next best. A person is tested according to his religious commitment. If he is steadfast in his religious commitment, he will be tested more severely, and if he is frail in his religious commitment, his test will be according to his commitment. Trials will continue to afflict a person until they leave him walking on the earth with no sin on him.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4023)"],[122,"When the appointed time of one of you is in a land, Allah establishes for him a need to go there; then when he reaches the farthest trace of it, He takes him in death. Then the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'O Lord, this is what You entrusted to me.'"],[123,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"If anyone's buried body is in the ground, and the need of that person arises, he is allowed to be dug up. When the remains are taken out, the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'O Lord, this is what You entrusted me with.' And this hadith is narrated by Hisham from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid.\""],[124,"When the appointed time of one of you is in a land, a need is made for him to go there, and Allah fulfills it for him there. Then the earth will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'O Lord, this is what You entrusted to me.'"],[125,"When Allah decrees death for a man in a certain town, He makes for him a need therein."],[126,"Allah does not set the appointed time of a man in a land except that a need is made for him therein."],[127,"When Allah wills to take a servant in a certain land, He makes for him a need to go there."],[128,"The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked is deceitful and ignoble."],[129,"The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked is deceitful and ignoble."],[130,"The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked is deceitful and ignoble."],[131,"I was in Makkah, and Waki' b. al-Jarrah asked me to read to him and his son the book of testaments. I said: 'When I reach Mina, I will narrate.' So when I reached Mina, I carried my book and narrated to him. Then I went to Makkah for the visitation, and Abu Usamah met me and said: 'O Yamani, that Ru'asi lad tricked you.' I said: 'How did he trick me?' He said: 'You carried your book to him and narrated to him.' I said: 'It is no wonder that he tricked me.'"],[132,"The believer is guileless and noble, while the wicked is deceitful and ignoble."],[133,"Whoever kills a person under a covenant without its right will not find the fragrance of Paradise, and indeed its fragrance is found from a distance of five hundred years' journey."],[134,"Whoever kills a person under a covenant without its right, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him, that he should smell its fragrance; and its fragrance is found from a distance of five hundred years' journey."],[135,"Whoever kills a person under a covenant without just cause, Allah forbids him from Paradise."],[136,"A servant may utter a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah becomes pleased with him due to it until the Day of Resurrection. And a servant may utter a word displeasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah becomes displeased with him due to it until the day he meets Him."],[137,"A man may utter a word displeasing to Allah, not knowing that it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His displeasure for him until the Day of Resurrection. And a man may utter a word pleasing to Allah, not knowing that it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His pleasure for him until the day he meets Him. As for the hadith of Isma'il b. Ja'far."],[138,"One of you may utter a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His pleasure for him due to it until the day he meets Him. And one of you may utter a word displeasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His displeasure upon him due to it until the day he meets Him."],[139,"One of you may utter a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His pleasure for him due to it until the day he meets Him. And one of you may utter a word displeasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His displeasure upon him due to it until the day he meets Him."],[140,"A man with honor passed by him while he was in the city market and greeted him. Alqamah said to him, \"O so-and-so, you have a heart and a right. I have seen you enter upon these princes and speak to them as Allah wills you to speak. I have heard Bilal ibn Al-Harith Al-Muzani, the companion of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), say: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Verily, one of you speaks a word from Allah's pleasure, not realizing how far it reaches, but Allah writes His Pleasure therewith until the Day he shall meet Him. And verily, one of you speaks a word from Allah's displeasure, not realizing how far it reaches, but Allah writes His displeasure therewith until the Day he shall meet Him.'\" Alqamah said, \"Woe to you! Consider what you say and what you speak. Much of what I have heard from Bilal ibn Al-Harith has prevented me from what you are saying. Malik ibn Anas also shortened the narration of this Hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr, and did not mention Alqamah ibn Waqqas.\""],[141,"A man may utter a word pleasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His pleasure for him due to it until the day he meets Him. And a man may utter a word displeasing to Allah, not thinking it would reach what it reached, and Allah records His displeasure for him due to it until the day he meets Him."],[142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Woe to him who tells things, speaking falsely, to make people laugh thereby. Woe to him! Woe to him!. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4990)"],[143,"Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I heard so-and-so mention and praise good, claiming that you gave him two dinars.\" He said, \"But so-and-so does not say that, yet he received from me between a hundred and ten.\" Then he said, \"One of you leaves my presence carrying his request under his arm.\" Ahmad said, \"Or something similar, 'It is nothing but fire.'\" Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, why do you give them?\" He said, \"What can I do? They ask me, and Allah refuses for me to be stingy.\""],[144,"Two men entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about something, so he called for two dinars for them. They praised him well. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"But so-and-so does not say that, yet I gave him between ten and a hundred, and he does not say that. One of you leaves with charity from me carrying it under his arm, but it is only fire for him.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how can you give him when you know it is fire for him?\" He said, \"What can I do? They insist on asking me, and Allah refuses for me to be stingy.\" As for Mu'tamir b. Sulayman al-Raqqi, they did not include it, while Muslim narrated from 'Abdullah b. Bishr al-Raqqi, except that this hadith is not a defect for the hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Salih, for it corroborates it with another chain."],[145,"It is not fitting for a believer to be a curser."],[146,"It is not fitting for a Muslim to be a curser.\" Salim said, \"I never heard Ibn 'Umar curse anything at all."],[147,"You cannot be both cursers and truthful ones."],[148,"You cannot be both cursers and truthful ones."],[149,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Those who frequently curse will not be witnesses or intercessors.\" \"Muslim reported it with this wording.\" This is reported by Muslim."],[150,"“Do not invoke curses upon one another with the curse of Allah, nor with the wrath of Allah, nor with the Fire.”"],[151,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “Indeed, Allah is Generous and loves generosity, and He loves noble character and hates its lowly aspects.”"],[152,"“Indeed, Allah is Generous and loves generosity and noble character, and He detests its lowly aspects.”"],[153,"“Indeed, Allah is Generous and loves generosity and the noblest of matters, and He detests—or he said: He hates—its lowly aspects.”"],[154,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing a cloak of Tayalisa fabric trimmed with silk brocade and said: “This companion of yours wants to raise every shepherd and the son of a shepherd, and to lower every horseman and the son of a horseman.” The Prophet ﷺ stood up, then sat down, and said: “When death approached Noah, he called his two sons and said: ‘I am relating to you the testament: I command you with two things and forbid you from two things. I forbid you from associating partners with Allah and from arrogance, and I command you with “There is no god but Allah.” For if the heavens and the earth and all that is within them were placed on one scale of the balance and “There is no god but Allah” were placed on the other scale, it would outweigh them. And if the heavens and the earth and all that is within them were a ring, and “There is no god but Allah” were placed upon it, it would shatter them. And I command you with “Glory be to Allah and with His praise,” for it is the prayer of everything, and by it everything is provided sustenance.’”"],[155,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: “I have never seen a man give more to a shepherd of sheep than Muhammad.” Then he mentioned something similar. Sahih al-isnad."],[156,"I was sitting with Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad when the heads of the Kharijites were brought. Each time a head came, I said: “To the Fire.” Then Abdullah b. Yazid al-Ansari said: “Do you not know, O son of my brother, that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Indeed, the punishment of this Ummah was placed in its worldly life’?”"],[157,"“The punishment of my Ummah is in its worldly life.”"],[158,"The plague was mentioned in the presence of Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, and Abu Musa said: “We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, and he said: ‘It is your brothers—or he said: your enemies—from the jinn, and it is a martyrdom for you.’”"],[159,"This phrase, \"عَنِ النَّبِيِّ ﷺ نَحْوَهُعلى شرط مسلم\" translates to \"From the Prophet ﷺ like it upon the condition of a Muslim.\""],[160,"“Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.”"],[161,"“Whoever plays with dice—or he said: with the dice—has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.”"],[162,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ when dice were mentioned in his presence: “He has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, he has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger—whoever strikes with its dice, playing with it.”"],[163,"\"Indeed, the best of Allah's servants are those who observe the sun, the moon, the stars, and the shades for the remembrance of Allah.\""],[164,"Indeed, \"the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah are those who endear Allah to people, and those who observe the sun and the moon.\""],[165,"Abu al-Nadr al-Faqih and Abu al-Hasan al-Anbari informed us, they said: Uthman b. Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; and Ahmad b. Ya'qub al-Thaqafi narrated to me: Muhammad b. Ayyub narrated to us; they said: Muhammad b. al-Sabbah narrated to us: Sa'id b. Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah b. Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Instruct me.\" He said, \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prayer, give the zakat, fast the month of Ramadan, perform the Hajj to the House and the Umrah, and listen and obey.\""],[166,"A bedouin came to Umar and asked him about the religion. He said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, teach me the religion.\" He said, \"You bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, you establish the prayer, you give the zakat, you fast Ramadan, you perform the Hajj to the House, and you must adhere to openness and beware of secret matters, and beware of everything of which you would be ashamed.\" He said, \"Then when you meet Allah, you will say: 'Umar b. al-Khattab commanded me to do this.'\" He said, \"O servant of Allah, take hold of this, and when you meet Allah, the Exalted, say whatever seems appropriate to you.\""],[167,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not swear by your fathers. Whoever swears by something other than Allah has committed shirk.\""],[168,"Umar used to swear by his father, and the Prophet ﷺ forbade him, saying: \"Whoever swears by something other than Allah has committed shirk.\" And the other said: \"It is shirk.\""],[169,"\"Whoever swears by other than Allah has committed kufr.\""],[170,"the Messenger of Allah Prophet ﷺ said: Hesitation and shyness [in speech] are two branches of Iman, [while] crudeness and antipathy are two branches of hypocrisy."],[171,"\"Modesty is part of faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire.\""],[172,"\"Modesty is part of faith, and faith leads to Paradise. Obscenity is part of harshness, and harshness leads to the Fire.\""],[173,"\"Among the most complete of the believers in faith are those who have the best character and are kindest to their families.\""],[174,"Quraysh said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Call upon your Lord to make al-Safa gold for us, and we will believe in you.\" He said, \"Will you do so?\" They said, \"Yes.\" So he called upon Allah, and Jibril came to him and said, \"Allah sends you peace and says: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold by morning, and whoever disbelieves after that I will punish with a punishment with which I have not punished anyone in the worlds. And if you wish, I will open for them the gates of repentance and mercy.\" He said, \"Rather, the gate of repentance and mercy.\""],[175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Will you do it?\" They said: 'Yes.' Then Gabriel came and said: 'Secure it.' Then Gabriel came and said: 'O Muhammad, Allah has granted you what you asked. If you wish, the Safa will turn to gold for you, and whoever disbelieves after that I will punish with a punishment I have not inflicted on anyone in the worlds. If you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance and return.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The door of repentance and mercy is dearer to me.\" \"This confusion does not weaken al-Thawri's hadith, for I do not know 'Imran b. al-Ja'd among the Successors; rather Isma'il b. Abi Khalid narrated from 'Imran b. Abi al-Ja'd. As for 'Imran b. al-Ja'd, he is from the followers of the Successors.\""],[176,"\"Whoever does an evil deed and dislikes it while doing it, and does a good deed and is pleased with it, is a believer.\""],[177,"\"O Abu Dharr, fear Allah wherever you are, follow up an evil deed with a good deed and it will erase it, and treat people with good character.\""],[178,"Mu'adh b. Jabal wanted to travel and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, advise me.' He said: \"Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him.\" He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, give me more.' He said: \"If you do wrong, then do good.\" He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, give me more.' He said: \"Remain upright and improve your character.\""],[179,"It is that a man commits an indecency and then repents from it. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, if You forgive, You forgive much; and which servant of Yours has not occasionally erred?\""],[180,"The one who commits a sin occasionally and then gives it up. Have you not heard the poet's saying [rajaz meter]: 'If You forgive, O Allah, You forgive much; and which servant of Yours has not occasionally erred?' \" And this verification does not weaken the first chain of transmission, for Zakariyya b. Ishaq is a reliable memorizer; Rawh b. 'Ubadah narrated it from Zakariyya. I mentioned in the conditions of this book the inclusion of exegeses from the Companions."],[181,"\"All of my ummah will enter Paradise except those who refuse.\" They said: 'And who refuses, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: \"Whoever disobeys me has refused.\""],[182,"\"You will surely enter Paradise except he who refuses and strays from Allah as a camel strays.\""],[183,"From the softest word he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Every one of you will enter Paradise except he who strays from Allah as a camel strays from its owner.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[184,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Allah has one hundred mercies. He distributed one mercy among the people of this world, and it suffices them until their appointed times. He withheld ninety-nine for His friends. Allah ﷻ will take back that mercy which He distributed among the people of this world, adding it to the ninety-nine, thus completing one hundred mercies for His friends on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[185,"\"When Allah created the heavens and the earth, He created one hundred mercies, each mercy as vast as the heavens and the earth. He distributed one mercy among all creatures and withheld ninety-nine mercies for Himself. On the Day of Resurrection, He will return this mercy, making one hundred mercies with which He will have mercy on His servants.\""],[186,"A Bedouin came, made his riding camel kneel down, then hobbled it, and prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salutation, he went to his camel, untied its hobble, mounted it, then called out: 'O Allah, have mercy on me and Muhammad, and do not associate anyone with us in Your mercy.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do you say? Is he more astray or his camel? Did you not hear what he said?\" They said: 'Yes.' He said: \"He has restricted a vast mercy. Allah created one hundred mercies and sent down one mercy by which creatures show compassion to one another—its jinn, humans, and beasts—while with Him are ninety-nine. Do you say he is more astray or his camel?\""],[187,"Gabriel was stuffing clay into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing that he would say: There is no god but Allah."],[188,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he mentioned that Gabriel began stuffing clay into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing that he would say: There is no god but Allah, and Allah would have mercy on him—or he said: fearing that Allah would have mercy on him."],[189,"\"O Allah, call me to account with an easy reckoning.\" When he finished, I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the reckoning? He said: \"His record will be looked at, and he will be pardoned. Indeed, whoever is scrutinized in the reckoning on that day, O 'A'ishah, will perish. And whatever afflicts the believer, Allah expiates from him thereby, even the thorn that pricks him.\""],[190,"“The wise man is the one who takes account of himself and strives for that which is after death. And the helpless man is the one who follows his own whims then indulges in wishful thinking about Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4260)"],[191,"\"The believer is expiated.\" \"They have both agreed upon 'Abd al-Rahman b. Humayd and...\""],[192,"This community will be gathered in three categories: a category who will enter Paradise without reckoning; a category who will be given an easy reckoning and then enter Paradise; and a category who will come carrying on their backs sins like towering mountains. Allah will ask about them, though He knows them best, saying: Who are these? They will say: These are servants of Your servants. He will say: Throw them down from them and place them upon the Jews and the Christians, and admit them to Paradise by My mercy."],[193,"There was a child on the pathway, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by with some people. When the child's mother saw the group, she feared that her son would be trampled, so she hurried and carried him, saying: My son! My son! The people said: O Messenger of Allah, she would never throw her son into the Fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And Allah will not throw His beloved into the Fire.\""],[194,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, one of us commits a sin. He said: \"It is recorded against him.\" He said: Then he seeks forgiveness for it and repents. He said: \"He is forgiven and it is not recorded against him, and Allah does not tire until you tire.\""],[195,"The major sins are from the beginning of Surat al-Nisa' up to: {If you avoid the great sins which you are forbidden} [al-Nisa' 31]—from the beginning of the surah, thirty verses. \"\""],[196,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Indeed, the allies of Allah are the ones who pray: whoever establishes the five prayers that have been prescribed for him, fasts Ramadan and seeks reward for his fast, considering it a duty upon him, gives the zakat of his wealth seeking reward for it, and avoids the major sins which Allah has forbidden.\" Then a man asked him: O Messenger of Allah, what are the major sins? He said: \"They are nine: associating partners with Allah; killing a believer without right; fleeing on the day of battle; consuming the property of an orphan; consuming usury; slandering chaste women; disobedience to Muslim parents; and deeming the Sacred House, your qiblah, lawful to violate, for the living and the dead.\" Then he said: \"No man who does not commit these major sins, and establishes the prayer and gives the zakat, dies except that he will be with the Prophet ﷺ in a dwelling whose doors are panels of gold.\" \"They have used the narrators of this hadith as evidence except 'Abd al-Hamid b. Sinan. As for 'Umayr b. Qatadah, he is a companion, and his son 'Ubayd is agreed upon for his transmission and use as evidence.\" 'Umayr b. Qatadah is a companion, and they did not use 'Abd al-Hamid as evidence. He said: I said: because of his unknown status, but Ibn Hibban deemed him trustworthy."],[197,"Abdullah ibn Abbas and Ibn Amr met and Ibn Abbas asked him, \"Which verse in the Book of Allah do you find the most hopeful?\" Ibn Amr replied, \"O my servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah.\" (Surah Az-Zumar, 39:53) Ibn Abbas said, \"But what about the statement of Ibrahim, 'My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead.' He said, 'Have you not believed?' He said, 'Yes, but I ask only that my heart may be satisfied.'\" (Surah Al-Baqarah, 2:260) This is because of what is in the hearts and whispers of Satan, so Allah was pleased with the statement of Ibrahim by His saying, 'Did you not believe?' He said, 'Yes.'\" (Surah Al-Baqarah, 2:260)"],[198,"\"Indeed, a man may attain by his good character the degrees of one who stands in prayer at night and fasts during the day.\""],[199,"\"Indeed, Allah causes a servant to attain by his good character the degree of fasting and prayer.\""],[200,"He said to him: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, we are the Banu al-Mughirah, a people among whom there is pride. Have you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say anything about that? 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no man who is arrogant in himself and swaggers in his walk except that he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.\""],[201,"“Shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise? The weak and those who are considered insignificant; and the people of the Fire: every harsh, arrogant, and self-conceited person.”"],[202,"“Pride is My cloak, so whoever contests with Me over My cloak, I shall crush him.”"],[203,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ride the donkey, wear wool, and care for the sheep, and he would attend to the needs of the guest.” On their condition (both Bukhari and Muslim)."],[204,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to ride the donkey, wear wool, and care for the sheep, and he would attend to the needs of the guest.”"],[205,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: “Whoever abandons fine clothing out of humility before Allah despite being able to afford it, Allah will call him on the heads of all creatures and let him choose whichever garment of faith he wishes to wear.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[206,"Umar b. al-Khattab went out to Syria, and with us was Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah. They came to a ford, and Umar was on a she-camel of his. He dismounted from it, took off his two leather socks, placed them on his shoulder, took hold of his she-camel’s halter, and led it through the ford. Abu Ubaydah said, “O Commander of the Believers, are you doing this? You take off your two leather socks, put them on your shoulder, take your she-camel’s halter, and lead it through the ford? It would not please me for the people of the town to see you like this.” Umar said, “Oh! No one but you would say this, Abu Ubaydah. I made it a lesson for the community of Muhammad ﷺ. We were the most humiliated people, and Allah honored us with Islam. So whenever we seek honor through anything other than what Allah honored us with, Allah will humiliate us.”"],[207,"When Umar arrived in Syria, the troops met him while he was wearing a lower garment, two leather socks, and a turban, and he was holding the head of his camel, wading through the water. Someone said to him, “O Commander of the Believers, the troops and the commanders of Syria meet you while you are in this state?” Umar said, “We are a people whom Allah has honored through Islam, so we will never seek honor through anything else.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[208,"“He is not one of us who does not have mercy on our young and does not recognize the right of our elders.”"],[209,"“Blessing is with your elders.”"],[210,"“Indeed, I admonish you regarding the right of the two weak ones: the orphan and the woman.”"],[211,"He gathered a hadith and then met Abu Dharr while he was near the middle pillar, and the people were around him. He said, “I sat next to him until my knee touched his knees, and I forgot that hadith and everything I wanted to ask him slipped away from me. I raised my head to the sky and began to remember. I said, ‘O Abu Dharr, guide me to a deed which, if a servant does it, he will enter Paradise.’ He said, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You believe in Allah.”’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, is there any action along with faith?’ He said, ‘He gives from what Allah has provided him.’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, what if he is destitute and has nothing?’ He said, ‘He speaks good with his tongue.’ I said, ‘What if he is unable to speak and his tongue cannot convey?’ He said, ‘Then let him help one who is overcome.’ I said, ‘What if he is weak and has no strength?’ He said, ‘Then let him make something for an unskilled person.’ I said, ‘What if he is unskilled?’ He turned to me and said, ‘Do you want to leave any good in your companion?’ He said, ‘He refrains from harming people.’ I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, all of this is indeed easy.’ He said, ‘By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, there is no one of these traits which a servant practices seeking thereby the face of Allah except that it will take him by the hand on the Day of Resurrection and will not leave him until it makes him enter Paradise.’”"],[212,"“Deliberateness in everything is good except in works for the Hereafter.”"],[213,"When Allah created Adam and breathed into him the spirit, he sneezed and said, 'Praise be to Allah.' He praised Allah by Allah's permission. His Lord said to him, 'May your Lord have mercy on you, O Adam.' And He said to him, 'O Adam, go to those angels, to a group of them sitting, and say, \"Peace be upon you.\"' So he went, and they said, 'And upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.' Then he returned to his Lord, and He said, 'This is your greeting and the greeting of your descendants and their descendants.' Allah said to him, while His two hands were closed, 'Choose whichever of them you wish.' He said, 'I chose the right hand of my Lord, and both hands of my Lord are right and blessed.' Then He spread it open, and behold, in it were Adam and his offspring. He said, 'O Lord, who are these?' He said, 'Your offspring.' And behold, every human had his lifespan written between his eyes. And among them was a man, the brightest of them—or he said, one of the brightest of them—for whom only forty years were written. He said, 'O Lord, increase his lifespan.' He said, 'That is what was written for him.' He said, 'I have given him sixty years from my own lifespan.' He said, 'You and that.' Then Adam was made to dwell in Paradise for as long as Allah willed, then he was brought down from it. Adam was counting for himself, and the Angel of Death came to him. Adam said to him, 'You have come early. A thousand years were written for me.' He said, 'Yes, but you gave sixty of them to your son Dawud.' So he denied, and his descendants denied; and he forgot, and his descendants forgot. Thus on that day we were commanded with writing and witnesses."],[214,"From the Prophet ﷺ similar to it. Sahih"],[215,"\"To be solitude for Ibrahim, words for Musa, and visions for Muhammad ﷺ .\""],[216,"Mohammed ﷺ saw his Lord, and he had a third witness with a reliable chain of narrators."],[217,"Muhammad ﷺ saw his Lord."],[218,"He saw Him twice. A hadith of such and such. The two Shaykhs have relied in this chapter on the reports of 'A'ishah bt. al-Siddiq, Ubayy b. Ka'b, 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, and Abu Dharr that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Jibril ﷺ . \"And these reports that I have mentioned are all sahih, and Allah knows best.\""],[219,"The prophets will have pulpits of gold. He said: They will sit upon them, and my pulpit will remain—I will not sit upon it, or I will not sit upon it—standing before my Lord, fearing that He might send me to Paradise and leave my nation after me. So I will say, 'O Lord, my nation, my nation.' Allah, exalted is He, will say, 'O Muhammad, what do you want me to do with your nation?' I will say, 'O Lord, hasten their reckoning.' They will be summoned and judged. Among them are those who will enter Paradise by the mercy of Allah, and among them are those who will enter Paradise by my intercession. I will not cease interceding until I am given writs for men who have been sent to the Fire. I will come to Malik, the keeper of the Fire, and he will say, 'O Muhammad, you have left nothing for the Fire from the wrath of your Lord upon your nation.'"],[220,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys.\" Then he mentioned the hadith. \"As for the hadith of Hisham al-Dastuwa'i.\""],[221,"\"We were with the Prophet ﷺ.\" Then he mentioned the hadith in full. \"The hadith of Qatadah.\""],[222,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his campaigns, and we stopped one night but did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his place. The camels had laid down their necks, and I saw some ropes, and there was Mu'adh b. Jabal. He came toward me and I went toward him, and I said, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Behind me.' And he mentioned the hadith. \"And this is sahih from the hadith of Abu Qilabah according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs.\" This hadith has been narrated from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari from 'Awf b. Malik \"with a sahih chain according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it.\" Its matn has passed, and he said: This is according to the condition of Muslim."],[223,"From 'Awf b. Malik that they were with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his campaigns. 'Awf said: I heard behind me a humming like the humming of a mill, and there was the Prophet ﷺ. I said, 'When the Prophet ﷺ is in enemy territory, guards are posted over him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A messenger from my Lord came to me and gave me a choice between admitting half of my nation to Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.' Mu'adh b. Jabal said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you know my strength, so make me one of them.' He said, 'You are one of them.' 'Awf b. Malik said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you know that we left our people and our wealth desiring Allah and His Messenger, so make us among them.' He said, 'You are one of them.' Then we came to the people, and they had risen. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Sit down.' They sat down as if none of them had stood up. He said, 'A messenger from my Lord came to me and gave me a choice between admitting half of my nation to Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, make us among them.' He said, 'It is for whoever dies not associating anything with Allah.'"],[224,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the delegation of Thaqif. We took one of the roads of Madinah until we made our camels kneel at the gate. There was no man among the people more hateful to us than the man upon whom we were about to enter. We entered, greeted, and pledged allegiance. We did not leave his presence until there was no man among the people more beloved to us than the man from whose presence we left. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you not ask your Lord for a kingdom like the kingdom of Sulayman?' He laughed and said, 'Perhaps your companion has with Allah something better than the kingdom of Sulayman. Allah did not send any prophet except that He gave him a supplication. Among them are those who used it for worldly things and were given them, and among them are those who supplicated with it against their people and they were destroyed by it. Allah has given me a supplication, and I have stored it with my Lord as intercession for my nation on the Day of Resurrection.' \"Muslim has used 'Ali b. Hashim as proof, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi 'Aqil al-Thaqafi is a companion whom our imams cite in their musnads. As for 'Abd al-Jabbar b. al-'Abbas, he is one whose hadith is collected and whose musnads are counted among the Kufans.\" Not established."],[225,"I was shown what my nation will face after me, and the shedding of some of their blood by others, and that was preceded from Allah as it was preceded for the nations before them. I asked Him to grant me intercession for them on the Day of Resurrection, and He did."],[226,"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[227,"Intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[228,"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[229,"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[230,"My intercession is for the grave sinners of my community."],[231,"He heard him say, \"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , 'What did your Lord say to you regarding intercession?' He replied, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, I thought that you would be the first to ask me about this, due to your eagerness for knowledge. By the One in whose hand is my soul, what concerns me most is not the completion of my intercession, but rather my intercession for those who testify sincerely that there is no god but Allah, and their hearts and tongues are in accordance with that.'\""],[232,"Bring out from the Fire anyone who said, 'There is no god but Allah,' and has in his heart the weight of a particle of faith. Bring out from the Fire anyone who said, 'There is no god but Allah,' or remembered Me or feared Me in any station."],[233,"Bring out from the Fire anyone who remembered Me or feared Me in any station."],[234,"Indeed, more people than the tribe of Tamim will enter Paradise through the intercession of a single man from my community."],[235,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed, more people than the tribe of Tamim will enter Paradise through the intercession of a single man from my community.' He said: 'We said, \"Other than you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Other than me.\"' I said: 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: 'Yes.' When he stood up, I said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'This is Ibn Abi al-Jad'a'."],[236,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are no two Muslims who kill three people before they reach the age of accountability except that Allah will admit them both into Paradise by His mercy.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about the one who kills two people?\" He said, \"Even the one who kills two people.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, there are those among my Ummah who will enter Paradise by his intercession, more than the count of Mudar, and indeed there are those among my Ummah who will be doomed to the Fire until one of its corners is filled.\""],[237,"Indeed, a man from my community will enter Paradise and intercede for more people than the tribe of Mudar."],[238,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will be the leader of the prophets, their spokesman, and the bearer of their intercession, without boasting."],[239,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will be the leader of the prophets, their spokesman, and the bearer of their intercession, without boasting."],[240,"\"I indeed know a word that no servant says truthfully from his heart and then dies upon that except that Allah forbids him to the Fire: 'There is no god but Allah.'\""],[241,"\"Whoever knows that prayer upon him is a binding right enters Paradise.\""],[242,"Three will not enter Paradise: the one who is disobedient to his parents, the cuckold, and the masculine woman."],[243,"From Nuwas bin Sam'an, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ , who narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah sets forth an example of a straight path with walls on both sides. Between these walls, there are open doors, and on these doors, there are curtains. On this path, there is a caller who calls out, saying: 'Oh people, walk on this path altogether and do not deviate.' There is also a caller who calls out against this path, and if any one of you wants to open any of those doors, he will say: 'Woe to you! Do not open it, for if you do, you will enter it.' This path represents Islam, the walls are the limits of Allah, the open doors are the prohibitions of Allah, the caller on top of the path is the Qur'an, and the caller from above is Allah's admonition, reminding every Muslim in their hearts.\""],[244,"\"The likeness of the believing servant when thunder and fever strike him is only like an iron that enters the fire; its impurities go away and its pure substance remains.\""],[245,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon some of his family while he was in pain from fever. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Mother of fever.' A woman said, 'Yes, may Allah curse her.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not curse her, for she washes away or removes the sins of the children of Adam as the bellows removes the impurities of iron.'"],[246,"The friends are three. As for a friend, he says to you, 'What you gave and what you withheld is not for you; that is your wealth.' As for a friend, he says, 'I am with you until you reach the king's gate, then I return and leave you.' That is your family and your clan; they escort you until you reach your grave, then they return and leave you. As for a friend, he says, 'I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you leave.' That is your deeds. He says, 'By Allah, you were the least of the three to me.'"],[247,"The Prophet ﷺ said: After the death of a believer, three things follow him: his family, his wealth, and his deeds. Two of them return, and only one remains. His family and wealth return, while his deeds remain. Imran al-Qattan al-Hajjaj continued the narration with its length."],[248,"\"There is no servant except that he has three friends.\""],[249,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The likeness of the believer and the likeness of death is that of a man who has three close friends. One of them said to him: 'Your wealth is my wealth; take whatever you wish and leave whatever you wish.' The other said: 'I will carry you and put you on me, and if you die, I will not leave you.' And the third said: 'I will be with you wherever you go, whether you live or die.' So the man said: 'This is his family.' And he said about the third: 'This is his deed according to the condition of a Muslim.'\""],[250,"Zayd b. Thabit: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me, so I learned for him the writing of the Jews. He said, 'By Allah, I do not trust the Jews with my writing.' So I learned it, and half a month had not passed before I became skilled at it. He said, 'I used to write for him when he wrote, and read for him when it was written to him.' 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi al-Zinad and [another] both testified to it."],[251,"\"Indeed Allah does not love the obscene nor the vulgar. By the One in whose hand is Muhammad's soul, the Hour will not arise until obscenity, vulgarity, severing kinship ties, and bad neighborliness appear, and the trustworthy is betrayed and the treacherous is trusted. The likeness of the believer is like the bee: it eats what is good, produces what is good, and lands on what is good, so it neither corrupts nor breaks. The likeness of the believing servant is like a good piece of gold: it is blown upon, so it comes out pure, and it is weighed, so it does not decrease.\""],[252,"From Abu Sabrah al-Hudhali, and he mentioned the hadith in full."],[253,"\"My basin is from Aylah to Sana'a, its width like its length. In it are two spouts pouring from Paradise: one of them is silver and the other gold, sweeter than honey, colder than snow, whiter than milk, and softer than butter. In it are pitchers as many as the stars of the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never thirst until he enters Paradise.\""],[254,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You are not one part in a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to the basin.' They asked him, 'How many were you?' He said, 'Eight hundred or nine hundred.' Abu Hamzah al-Ansari is Talhah b. Yazid, and al-Bukhari cited him as evidence."],[255,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"You are not a part of a thousand parts of those who will come to me at the Pond on the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: We said to Zayd, \"How many were you on that day?\" He said, \"Between six hundred and nine hundred.\""],[256,"What are these hadiths that have reached me from you, which you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, claiming that he has a Pond in Paradise? He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that and promised it to us.\" He said, \"You have lied, but you are an old man who has become senile.\" He said, \"Indeed, my two ears heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" meaning, and I heard him say: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\" And I have not lied about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[257,"\"Whoever leaves the community by a handspan has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck until he returns to it.\" He said, \"And whoever dies without having upon him an imam of the community, his death is a death of ignorance.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"O people, I am your predecessor at the Pond, and its width is what is between Kufa and the Black Stone, and its vessels are as numerous as the stars. And I saw some people of my community, when they came near to me, a man went out against them and said, 'Take them away from me.' Then another group came, and he did the same to them, and none of them escaped except like the cattle.\" Abu Bakr said to 'Ali, \"Are they from them, O Prophet of Allah?\" He said, \"No, but they are a people who will come after you and walk backwards.\""],[258,"I entered upon 'Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad while they were discussing the mention of the Pond. He said, \"Anas has come to you.\" He said, \"O Anas, what do you say about the Pond?\" He said, \"I said: I did not think that I would live until I saw the like of you disputing about the Pond. I have left behind me old women, none of whom prays a prayer except that she asks her Lord to bring her to the Pond of Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[259,"I entered upon 'Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad while they were discussing the mention of the Pond."],[260,"He was sitting at the door of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: He came out while we were sitting, and he said, \"Listen.\" We said, \"We have heard, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"There will be rulers after me, so do not believe them in their lying and do not help them in their wrongdoing. For whoever believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing will never come to me at the Pond.\""],[261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day while we were in the mosque, five Arabs and four non-Arabs, and he said, \"Do you hear?\" We said, \"We have heard,\" twice. He said, \"Listen: There will be rulers after me. Whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Pond. And whoever does not enter upon them, and does not believe them in their lying, and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond.\" Mis'ar b. Kidam and Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Abu Husayn, from al-Sha'bi, from 'Asim al-'Adawi, from Ka'b b. 'Ujrah: \"As for the hadith of al-Thawri.\""],[263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us while we were nine, and among us there were cushions of red leather. He said, \"There will be rulers after me. Whoever believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Pond. And whoever does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me, and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Pond.\" And Jabir b. 'Abd Allah witnessed this statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Ka'b b. 'Ujrah."],[264,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ka'b b. 'Ujrah: \"May Allah protect you, O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, from the rule of the foolish.\" He said, \"And what is the rule of the foolish?\" He said, \"Rulers who will be after me, who do not follow my guidance and do not follow my Sunnah. Whoever believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing, those are not of me, and I am not of them, and they will not come to me at my Pond. And whoever does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing, those are of me, and I am of them, and they will come to me at my Pond. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is a means of drawing near—or he said, a proof.\""],[265,"I entered Paradise, and there I was at a river flowing with its banks of tents of pearls. I struck my hand into the flowing water, and it was fragrant musk. I said to Gabriel, \"What is this?\" He said, \"This is al-Kawthar which your Lord has given you, may He be exalted.\""],[266,"\"Paradise has one hundred degrees, between every two degrees is like what is between the heaven and the earth, and al-Firdaws is the highest of them in degree, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws.\""],[267,"From the Prophet ﷺ something similar, and likewise it is narrated with an authentic chain from 'Ubadah b. al-Samit, according to the conditions of the two shaykhs."],[268,"“Paradise has one hundred degrees, between every two degrees as between the heaven and the earth, and Firdaws is the highest of them in degree, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for Firdaws.”"],[269,"“In Paradise there are chambers whose outside is seen from their inside and whose inside is seen from their outside.” Abu Malik al-Ashʿari said, “For whom, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “For one who makes his speech good, feeds food, and spends the night standing while people are asleep.”"],[270,"From Anas, in his statement {by the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary}, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A tree was raised for me whose boundaries reach the seventh heaven. Its fruits are like the baskets of Hiraa, and its leaves are like the ears of elephants. Two visible rivers flow from its trunk, and two hidden rivers flow from it.\" I said: \"O Jibril, what are these?\" He said: \"As for the hidden rivers, they are in Paradise, and as for the visible rivers, they are the Nile and the Euphrates.\""],[271,"The Lote Tree was raised up for me, and behold there were four rivers: two apparent and two hidden. As for the two apparent, they are the Nile and the Euphrates; and as for the two hidden, they are two rivers in Paradise. And I was brought three cups: a cup with milk, a cup with honey, and a cup with wine. I took the one with milk and drank, and it was said to me, “You have hit the fitrah, you and your nation.”"],[272,"“The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; this nation comprises eighty rows of them.”"],[273,"“The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; eighty of them are from this nation.”"],[274,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us while we were around him, “How would you be as a quarter of the people of Paradise?” We said, “A lot.” He said, “How would you be as a third?” He said, we said, “That is more.” He said, “How would you be as a half?” We said, “That is more.” He said, “The people of Paradise are one hundred and twenty rows; you are eighty rows of them.” He said, we said, “That is two-thirds, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Yes.” ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud did not hear from his father in most reports. ʿAbd al-Rahman did not hear from his father."],[275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, He said, Allah ﷻ says, “Do you desire anything that I may increase you?” They say, “Our Lord, what is above what You have given us?” He said, He says, “My greatest pleasure.”"],[276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise, Allah ﷻ says, “Shall I not inform you of what is greater than this?” They say, “Yes, and what is greater than this?” He says, “The pleasure.”"],[277,"Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection in the form of a speckled ram, and it will be said, “O people of Paradise,” and they will look out fearful and trembling, afraid that they might be taken out of what they are in. Then it will be said, “Do you recognize this?” They will say, “Yes, this is death.” Then it will be said, “O people of the Fire,” and they will look out rejoicing and happy that they might be taken out of what they are in. Then it will be said, “Do you recognize this?” They will say, “Yes, this is death.” Then He will command it, and it will be slaughtered on the bridge, and it will be said to both groups, “Eternity in what you find, no death therein ever.”"],[278,"“Death will be brought on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[279,"On the authority of Abu Hurayrah: “The two Shaykhs agreed on including this hadith with a wording other than this one from the hadith of al-Aʿmash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Saʿid.” According to the condition of Muslim."],[280,"“O Banu Awd, I am the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Do you know the return to Allah, then to Paradise or to the Fire, and an abode with no departure therein, and eternity with no death, in bodies that do not die?”"],[281,"Abu Musa said about the saying of Allah Almighty: \"And for those who fear the position of their Lord, there will be two gardens\" [Ar-Rahman verse 46]. He said: \"Two gardens of gold for those who race ahead and two gardens of silver for those who follow.\" This is an authentic chain of narration according to the conditions of Imam Muslim. However, they did not mention it like this. Rather, they cited it from the narration of Al-Harith ibn 'Ubayd and 'Abdul 'Aziz ibn 'Abdus Samad from Abu Imran Al-Jawni from Abu Bakr ibn Abu Musa from his father who narrated it from the Prophet ﷺ. The hadith mentions \"two gardens of silver\" but does not mention the \"racing ahead\" and \"following\" parts. I heard Abu Hasan 'Ali ibn 'Umar Al-Hafiz saying that he heard Abu Fadl Al-Wazir saying that he heard Ma'mun Al-Misri saying: I asked Abu 'Abdul Rahman An-Nasai, \"Why did Muhammad ibn Ismail leave the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah?\" He said, \"By Allah, Hammad ibn Salamah is more reliable and truthful than Ismail ibn Abi Uways.\" And he mentioned a long story similar to the replacement of Al-Harith ibn 'Ubayd with Hammad."],[282,"The Day of Resurrection [will be] about the span between noon and mid-afternoon."],[283,"The Day of Resurrection upon the believers [will be] about the span between noon and mid-afternoon."],[284,"Ibn Umar had a friend from the people of Syria with whom he corresponded. Abdullah b. Umar wrote to him: It has reached me that you have spoken about something concerning divine decree. Beware of writing to me [about that], for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There will be among my community people who deny divine decree.'"],[285,"The Qadariyya are the Magians of this community. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend their funerals."],[286,"From Ibn Umar ؓ"],[287,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone acquires knowledge that should be sought seeking the Face of Allah, but he acquires it only to get some worldly advantage, he will not experience the arf, i.e. the fragrance, of Paradise. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3664)"],[288,"Whoever learns knowledge by which the face of Allah is sought, but does not learn it except to attain thereby some worldly gain, will not find the fragrance of Paradise."],[289,"Do not learn knowledge in order to vie with the scholars, or to dispute with the foolish, or to gain prominence in gatherings. Whoever does that, then the Fire, the Fire!"],[290,"From Ibn Jurayj, and he connected it. And Yahya is agreed upon for his transmission in the two Sahihs. Abdullah b. Wahb sent it as mursal. I adhere to the principle I established regarding accepting the addition from a trustworthy narrator in chains and texts. Ibn Wahb narrated it and sent it as mursal."],[291,"Do not learn knowledge in order to vie with the scholars, or to dispute with the foolish, or to narrate it in gatherings. Whoever does that, then the Fire, the Fire!"],[292,"Whoever seeks knowledge in order to vie with the scholars, or dispute with the foolish, or turn people's attention to him, then [he goes] to the Fire."],[293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at al-Khayf and said: 'May Allah brighten [the face of] a servant who hears my words, memorizes them, then conveys them to one who has not heard them. For many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him. Three things: a believer's heart does not harbor rancor regarding them: sincerity of action for Allah, obedience to those in authority, and adherence to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them.'"],[294,"And Abu Ali al-Hafiz narrated to us, Abu Ya'la informed us, Abu Khaythama narrated to us, they said: Ya'qub b. Ibrahim b. Sa'd narrated to us, my father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq. And Abu al-Hasan Muhammad b. Abdullah al-Jawhari informed me, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ya'la narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, Ya'la b. Ubayd al-Tanafisi and Ahmad b. Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us. And Muhammad b. al-Muzaffar al-Hafiz informed me, Muhammad b. Harun narrated to us, Sulayman b. Umar narrated to us, Yahya b. Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us from Muhammad b. Ishaq. And Abu Amr Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Ishaq al-Adl informed me, Muhammad b. Khuzaym al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham b. Ammar narrated to us, he said: Sa'id b. Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to me, Ibn Ishaq narrated to us. And Ali b. Isa narrated to me, and the wording is his: Musaddad b. Qatan narrated to us, Uthman b. Abi Shayba narrated to us, Ya'la b. Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ishaq narrated to us from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad b. Jubayr b. Mut'im, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at al-Khayf in Mina and said: 'May Allah brighten [the face of] a servant who hears my words, memorizes them, then conveys them to one who has not heard them. For many a bearer of understanding has no understanding, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him. Three things: a believer's heart does not harbor rancor regarding them: sincerity of action for Allah, good counsel to those in authority, and adherence to the community, for their supplication encompasses those behind them.' These trustworthy narrators agreed upon transmitting this hadith from Muhammad b. Ishaq from al-Zuhri. Abdullah b. Numayr alone contradicted them, saying: from Muhammad b. Ishaq from Abd al-Salam, who is Ibn Abi al-Janub, from al-Zuhri. Ibn Numayr is trustworthy, and Allah knows best. Then we examined it and found for al-Zuhri a corroborating narrator from Muhammad b. Jubayr."],[295,"May Allah have mercy on a servant who hears my words, comprehends them, and then conveys them to one who has not heard them. Many a bearer of understanding has no understanding of his own, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him. Three things the heart of a believer does not harbor treachery against: sincerity of action, giving good counsel to those in authority, and adhering to the community. For their supplication encompasses them from behind."],[296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: May Allah brighten the face of a person who hears my words and carries them. Many a bearer of understanding is not himself a jurist, and many a bearer of understanding conveys it to one who has more understanding than him. Three things a believer's heart does not harbor treachery against: sincerity of action for Allah Almighty, giving good counsel to those in authority, and adhering to the community of Muslims. \"\" Muslim has already adduced as evidence in the authentic musnad the hadith of Simak b. Harb from al-Nu'man b. Bashir that he said: I saw our Prophet ﷺ one day filling his belly with inferior dates. And from Simak from al-Nu'man: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to straighten our rows... the hadith. \"Hatim b. Abi Saghira and Abdullah b. Bakr al-Sahmi are agreed upon by both [al-Bukhari and Muslim] in including them.\" It has also been narrated from al-Sha'bi and Mujahid from al-Nu'man b. Bashir from the Prophet ﷺ according to the conditions of Muslim."],[297,"He said: \"Welcome to the testament of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to enjoin us concerning you.\""],[298,"\"No man takes a path seeking knowledge therein except that Allah makes easy for him thereby a path to Paradise. And whoever is slowed by his deeds will not be hastened by his lineage.\""],[299,"\"Whoever takes a path in which he seeks knowledge, Allah makes easy for him a path to Paradise.\""],[300,"\"Know your lineages so that you may maintain your kinship ties. For there is no closeness for a kinship tie when it is severed, even if it is near, and no distance for it when it is maintained, even if it is far.\""],[301,"\"Learn your lineages so that you may maintain your kinship ties.\""],[302,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, which land is worst? He said: \"I do not know.\" When Gabriel came to him, he said: \"O Gabriel, which land is worst?\" He said: I do not know until I ask my Lord. Gabriel departed and remained as long as Allah willed him to remain, then he came and said: O Muhammad, you asked me which land is worst, and I said I do not know, and I asked my Lord, saying: Which land is worst? He said: \"Its marketplaces.\" Both [al-Bukhari and Muslim] have adduced as evidence all the narrators of this hadith except Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Aqil, while al-Bukhari alone has adduced as evidence Abu Hudhayfa. This hadith is a foundational principle for the scholar's saying 'I do not know,' and it has a corroborating witness from Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Aqil. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[303,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which land is the worst?\" He ﷺ said, \"I do not know.\" When Gabriel came to Muhammad ﷺ , he said, \"O Gabriel, which land is the worst?\" Gabriel replied, \"I do not know until I ask my Lord.\" So Gabriel went and stayed as long as Allah willed, then he came back and said, \"O Muhammad, you asked me which land is the worst? Indeed, it is its markets. 'Amr ibn Thabit is the son of Abu al-Miqdam al-Kufi, and he is not one of the two sheikhs (al-Bukhari and Muslim). I mentioned him as a witness, and the narration is from Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, who urged me to mention him. But I have doubted the authenticity of this narration from multiple aspects.\""],[304,"From him, narrated by Abd al-Samad b. al-Nu'man, and he is weak."],[305,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, which places are best? He said: \"I do not know.\" He said: Which places are worst? He said: \"I do not know.\" He said: Ask your Lord. He said: When Gabriel descended, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I was asked which places are best and which places are worst, and I said I do not know. Gabriel said: And I do not know until I ask my Lord. He said: Gabriel shuddered with a shudder that almost made Muhammad ﷺ swoon from it. Then Allah said: O Gabriel, Muhammad asks you which places are best, and you said I do not know, and he asks you which places are worst, and you said I do not know. Verily, the best of places are the mosques, and the worst of places are the marketplaces."],[306,"\"People are on the verge of striking the livers of camels [in travel] and will not find a scholar more learned than the scholar of Madinah.\""],[307,"\"People are on the verge of striking the livers of camels.\""],[308,"Whoever comes to this mosque of ours to learn good or teach it is like a mujahid in the path of Allah, and whoever comes for other than this is like a man who sees something that pleases him but it is not his. Perhaps he said: he sees those who pray but is not one of them, and he sees those who remember Allah but is not one of them."],[309,"Whoever enters this mosque of ours to learn good or teach it is like a mujahid in the path of Allah, and whoever enters it for other than that is like one who looks at what is not his."],[310,"Whoever goes early to the mosque, intending only to learn good or teach it, will have the reward of a person who performs a complete 'Umrah. Whoever goes later to the mosque, intending only to learn good or teach it, will have the reward of a person who performs a complete Hajj."],[311,"There are two greedy types who are never satisfied: one greedy for knowledge who is never satisfied, and one greedy for worldly things who is never satisfied."],[312,"Abu Huraira came to Ka'b to ask about someone, and Ka'b was among the people. Ka'b asked, \"What do you want from him?\" Abu Huraira replied, \"I do not know anyone from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who preserves his hadiths better than me.\" Ka'b responded, \"Indeed, you have not found anyone who seeks something without being satisfied with it for a day in his entire life, except for a seeker of knowledge and a seeker of worldly gains.\" Then he said to Abu Huraira, \"You are Ka'b, so I have come for something like this.\""],[313,"The virtue of knowledge is more beloved to me than the virtue of worship, and the best of your religion is piety (wara')."],[314,"And Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ahmad b. Balawayh narrated to me: Ibrahim b. Ishaq al-Siraj narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us: Khalid b. Makhlad narrated to us from Hamza al-Zayyat from al-A'mash from Mus'ab b. Sa'd, and he mentioned it similarly but did not mention al-Hakam."],[315,"Abu Ali al-Husayn b. Ali al-Hafiz narrated it to us: Ibrahim b. Muhammad b. Yahya b. Mandah al-Asbahani informed us: Ibrahim b. Sa'dan and Ahmad b. Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, they said: Bakr b. Bakkar narrated to us: Hamza al-Zayyat narrated to us: al-A'mash narrated to us from a man from Mus'ab b. Sa'd from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something similar. Then we examined and found that Khalid b. Makhlad was more reliable, more retentive, and more trustworthy than Bakr b. Bakkar, so we judged in his favor for the addition. And Abdullah b. Abd al-Quddus narrated it from al-A'mash with another chain, according to their conditions."],[316,"The virtue of knowledge is better than the virtue of worship, and the best of your religion is piety (wara')."],[317,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people during the Farewell Pilgrimage and said: \"Satan has despaired of being worshiped in your land, but he is content to be obeyed in matters other than that: deeds of yours that you consider insignificant, so beware. O people, I have left among you that which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ. Every Muslim is a Muslim’s brother; the Muslims are brothers. None of his brother’s property is lawful for a person except what he gives willingly. Do not wrong one another, and do not revert after me to being unbelievers, striking one another’s necks.\"[1]"],[318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, I have left among you two things that you will never go astray as long as you hold fast to them: the Book of Allah and my Sunnah. And they will never separate from each other until they meet me at the Pond.\""],[319,"There were two brothers in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. One of them would come to the Prophet ﷺ, and the other would work for a living. The working brother complained about his brother to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Perhaps you are provided for because of him.\""],[320,"Mu'awiya came out of the bathhouse in Hims and said to his servant: \"Bring me my two garments.\" He put them on, then entered the mosque of Hims and prayed two rak'ahs. When he finished, he found people sitting. He said to them: \"What makes you sit?\" They said: \"We prayed the obligatory prayer, then the storyteller told his story, and when he finished we sat to discuss the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Mu'awiya said: \"There is no man who met the Prophet ﷺ with fewer hadiths from him than I. I will tell you two things that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. No man is in charge of people and men stand at his head, who loves that disputes become many in his presence, will enter Paradise. I was with the Prophet ﷺ one day when he entered the mosque and found a group of people sitting. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What makes you sit?' They said: 'We prayed the obligatory prayer, then we sat to discuss the Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When Allah mentions something, its mention becomes great.'\""],[321,"When the companions of the Prophet ﷺ sat together, their talk was about fiqh, unless a man recited a surah or asked another man to recite a surah."],[322,"Discuss hadith among yourselves, for discussing hadith enlivens hadith."],[323,"Study the hadith among yourselves, for if you do not, it will be obliterated."],[324,"Study the hadith among yourselves, for the remembrance of hadith is its life."],[325,"We heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as he would narrate to us while our companions were occupied with tending the camels."],[326,"You will hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you."],[327,"You will hear, and it will be heard from you, and it will be heard from those who hear from you."],[328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer, then he turned to face us and admonished us with an exhortation that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is as if it were the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so advise us.' He said, 'I enjoin upon you the fear of Allah, and hearing and obeying, even if a black slave is placed in authority over you. For whoever lives among you will see much disagreement. You must adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, guided caliphs. Bite upon it with the molar teeth. And beware of newly invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance.'"],[329,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day and stood and admonished the people, encouraged them, and warned them, and said what Allah willed him to say. Then he said, 'Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, and obey the one whom Allah has placed in authority over you, and do not dispute the matter with its people, even if he is a black slave. And you must adhere to what you know of the Sunnah of your Prophet and the rightly guided, guided caliphs. And bite upon the truth with your molar teeth.' This is a sound chain of transmission according to the conditions of both of them, and I do not know of any defect in it. Damrah b. Habib corroborated Khalid b. Ma'dan in narrating this hadith from 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Amr al-Sulami."],[330,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ admonished us with an exhortation that made the eyes shed tears and the hearts tremble. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, indeed this is the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so what do you entrust to us?' He said, 'I have left you upon a clear path whose night is like its day. No one deviates from it after me except one who is destroyed. And whoever lives among you will see much disagreement. You must adhere to what you know of my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs after me. And you must obey, even if he is an Abyssinian slave. Bite upon it with the molar teeth.' Asad b. Wada'ah would add in this hadith: 'For the believer is like a camel with a nose ring; wherever it is led, it follows.' And 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Amr was corroborated in his narration from al-'Irbad b. Sariyah by three trustworthy, reliable transmitters from the imams of the people of Sham. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[331,"We came to al-'Irbad b. Sariyah, who was among those about whom it was revealed: 'Nor upon those who, when they came to you so that you might provide them with mounts, you said, \"I find nothing upon which to mount you,\" they turned away with their eyes overflowing with tears out of grief that they could not find anything to spend' [al-Tawbah 92]. We greeted him and said, 'We have come to you as visitors and seekers of knowledge.' Al-'Irbad said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer one day, then he turned to face us and admonished us with an eloquent exhortation that made the eyes shed tears and the hearts tremble. Someone said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is as if it were the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so what do you entrust to us?\" He said, \"I enjoin upon you the fear of Allah, and hearing and obeying, even if he is an Abyssinian slave. For whoever lives among you will see much disagreement. You must adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided, guided caliphs. Hold fast to it and bite upon it with the molar teeth. And beware of newly invented matters, for every newly invented matter is an innovation, and every innovation is misguidance.\""],[332,"I heard al-'Irbad b. Sariyah al-Sulami say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us one morning and admonished us with an exhortation that made the hearts tremble and the eyes shed tears.' He said: 'We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have admonished us with the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so entrust to us.\" He said, \"You must have the fear of Allah—I think he said—and hearing and obeying. And after me you will see severe or much disagreement. You must adhere to my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly guided caliphs. Bite upon it with the molar teeth. And beware of newly invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance.\" And among them is Ma'bad b. 'Abd Allah b. Hisham al-Qurashi, but the route to him is not according to the condition of this book, so I left it. I have been exhaustive to some extent in authenticating this hadith as far as my effort allowed, and it has been written as Shu'bah, the imam of the imams of hadith, said about the hadith of 'Abd Allah b. 'Ata' from 'Uqbah b. 'Amir when he sought it in Basra, Kufa, Madinah, and Makkah, then the hadith returned to Shahr b. Hawshab, so he abandoned it. Then Shu'bah said: \"If such a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were authenticated for me, it would be dearer to me than my father, my son, and all the people.\" And this hadith is authentic, praise be to Allah, and may Allah bless Muhammad and his family all together."],[333,"When Mu'adh b. Jabal was on his deathbed, they said, 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, advise us.' He said, 'Sit me up.' Then he said, 'Indeed, knowledge and faith are in their place; whoever seeks them will find them.' He said that three times. 'And seek knowledge from four men: from 'Uwaymir Abu al-Darda', from Salman al-Farisi, from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, and from 'Abd Allah b. Salam. For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, he is the tenth of ten in Paradise.\""],[334,"Mu'adh b. Jabal fell ill one day while Yazid b. 'Umayrah al-Zubaydi was with him. Yazid wept over him. Mu'adh said to him, 'What makes you weep?' He said, 'What makes me weep is that what I used to ask you about every day will be cut off from me.' Mu'adh said, 'Indeed, knowledge and faith are cheerful. Arise and seek them.' Yazid said, 'From whom shall I seek them?' Mu'adh said, 'From four persons: from 'Uwaymir Abu al-Darda', from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, from Salman al-Farisi, and from 'Abd Allah b. Salam, for it used to be said that he is the tenth of ten in Paradise.' Yazid said, 'And from 'Umar b. al-Khattab?' He said, 'Do not ask him about anything, for he is too preoccupied for you.'"],[335,"\"Knowledge and faith are found by those who seek them.\""],[336,"He said: 'Awf b. Malik al-Ashja'i said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the sky one day and said, “This is the time when knowledge will be lifted.” A man from the Ansar called Ibn Labid said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, how will knowledge be lifted when it has been established in the Book and hearts have comprehended it?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I had thought you were one of the most knowledgeable of the people of Madinah.” Then he mentioned the misguidance of the Jews and Christians despite what they had in their hands of the Book of Allah. He (the narrator) said: I met Shaddad b. Aws and told him the hadith of 'Awf b. Malik. He said, “'Awf spoke the truth. Shall I inform you of the first of that to be lifted?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Khushu' (humility), until you will not see anyone humble.” This is sahih, and the two Shaykhs have used all its narrators as proof. The supporting witness for that in it is Shaddad b. Aws, for Jubayr b. Nufayr heard the hadith from both of them, and from a third Companion, who is Abu al-Darda'."],[337,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he raised his gaze to the sky, then said, “This is the time when knowledge will be snatched away from people until they are unable to obtain any of it.” Ziyad b. Labid al-Ansari said, “O Messenger of Allah, how will it be snatched away from us when we have read the Quran? By Allah, we will certainly read it and make our women and children read it.” He said, “May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ziyad! I used to count you among the jurists of the people of Madinah. This Torah and Gospel are with the Jews and Christians, so what does it avail them?” Jubayr said: I met 'Ubadah b. al-Samit and said to him, “Do you not hear what your brother Abu al-Darda' says?” and I informed him of what he said. He said, “Abu al-Darda' spoke the truth. If you wish, I will tell you of the first knowledge to be lifted from people: khushu' (humility). Soon you will enter a congregational mosque and not see a single humble man in it.”"],[338,"“This is the time of the departure of knowledge.” Shu'bah said: Or he said, “The time of the cutting off of knowledge.” They said, “How can that be when the Book of Allah is among us, and our children teach it to their children?” He said, “May your mother be bereaved of you, Ibn Labid! I did not think you to be anything but one of the most intelligent of the people of Madinah. Do not the Jews and Christians have the Book of Allah, the Torah and the Gospel, yet they benefit from it nothing?”"],[339,"He came asking him about something. He said, “What made you come to me except that?” He said, “I came to you only for that.” He said, “Rejoice, for no man goes out seeking knowledge but the angels spread their wings for him in pleasure at what he does, until he returns.”"],[340,"A man from Murad called Safwan b. 'Assal came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “What has brought you?” He said, “Seeking knowledge.” He said, “Indeed, the angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he does.” And he mentioned the hadith. 'Arim, who is Abu al-Nu'man Muhammad b. al-Fadl al-Basri, is a trustworthy hafiz. Al-Bukhari relied on him in a portion of this hadith, narrating it from him in the Sahih. Sinan b. Farrukh differed from him in this hadith, narrating it from al-Sa'q b. Hazn."],[341,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned the hadith. Abu Janab al-Kalbi stopped it at Talhah b. Musarrif, from Zirr b. Hubaysh, but Abu Janab is one whose narration is not used as proof in this book. Shu'ban differed from him."],[342,"\"Indeed, he does not do what you have done for him, except that the angels have placed their wings over him in satisfaction of what he does. And we have mentioned in this Hadith of what is not weakened, as this Hadith has been narrated by a group and another group has stopped at it, and the one who narrated it is more reliable, and the addition from them is accepted.\""],[343,"“Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it, he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection bridled with a bridle of fire.”"],[344,"“Whoever is asked about knowledge and conceals it, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[345,"“Whoever conceals knowledge, Allah will bridle him on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of fire.”"],[346,"“Do you know why I walked with you?” They said, “Yes, we are the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; you walked with us.” He said, “You are going to come to the people of a town who have a humming with the Quran like the humming of bees. Do not begin with them with hadiths, lest they occupy you. Strip down to the Quran and reduce narration from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Go on, and I am your partner.” When Qarazah arrived, they said, “Narrate to us.” He said, “Ibn al-Khattab forbade us.”"],[347,"I entered upon Qarazah b. Ka'b, Abu Mas'ud, and Zayd b. Thabit, and there were slave girls with them singing. I said to them, “Do you do this while you are Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” They said, “If you can hear, then stay; otherwise leave, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted us amusement at weddings and weeping over the dead.”"],[348,"“Whoever attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire. And whoever's brother consults him and he advises him without sound judgment has betrayed him. And whoever gives a fatwa without firm knowledge, its sin is upon the one who gave the fatwa.”"],[349,"Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his place in Hellfire. Whoever gives a fatwa without knowledge, its sin is upon the one who gave it. Whoever advises his brother in a matter knowing that the right course lies elsewhere has betrayed him."],[350,"There will be at the end of time people from my ummah who will narrate to you what neither you nor your forefathers have heard. Beware of them and keep away from them."],[351,"Moderation in the Sunnah is better than striving in innovation."],[352,"From 'Abdullah, the like of it."],[353,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from four: knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard."],[354,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from four: knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard."],[355,"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard. And at the end of that he says: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from these four."],[356,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he is only a human who becomes angry as humans become angry. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, Quraysh say: You write from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he is only a human who becomes angry as humans become angry. He said: He pointed to his lips and said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing comes out from between them except truth, so write."],[357,"He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should I write down what I hear from you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Should I write down both when you are angry and when you are pleased?\" He said, \"Yes, for it is not permissible for me to speak except the truth.\" So let the seeker of this knowledge know that no one ever narrated in the lifetime of Amr ibn Shu'aib except Muslim, who heard from Shu'aib through Abdullah ibn Amr. And when a hadith is narrated from Amr ibn Shu'aib from Mujahid from Abdullah ibn Amr, then it is an authentic hadith, although I have mentioned it as a witness to the hadith of Abdul Wahid ibn Qays, and this same hadith has been narrated verbatim from Yusuf ibn Mahak."],[358,"I used to write everything I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wanting to memorize it. Then Quraysh forbade me and said: You write everything you hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is a human who speaks in pleasure and anger? He said: So I stopped, and I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Write, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, nothing comes out from him except truth. And he pointed with his hand to his mouth. The narrators of this hadith have been relied upon by both al-Bukhari and Muslim, all of them except this al-Walid. I think he is al-Walid b. Abi al-Walid al-Shami, for he is al-Walid b. 'Abdullah, and his father is known to have been a scribe. If that is the case, then Muslim has relied upon him. It has been authentically reported from the Commander of the Believers, 'Umar b. al-Khattab, that he said: Restrain knowledge with writing. If al-Walid is Ibn Abi al-Walid al-Shami, then the hadith meets Muslim's criterion."],[359,"Restrain knowledge with writing. And likewise the report from Anas b. Malik is authentic as his statement, and it has been raised to the Prophet from an unreliable route. As for the report from his statement: And the like of it is authentic from Anas's statement."],[360,"\"He used to say to his sons, 'Record knowledge in writing.' It was narrated by some of the people of Basra from the Ansari, and it was also narrated by a respected elder from the people of Mecca who heard it from Ibn Jurayj.\""],[361,"Restrain knowledge. I said: And what is restraining it? He said: Writing it."],[362,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, I said to a man from the Ansar: Come, let us ask the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for today they are many. He said: How strange of you, O Ibn 'Abbas! Do you think people will need you when among the people are the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: So I left that and began to ask the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. If a hadith from a man reached me, I would go to his door while he was taking a midday nap, and I would use my cloak as a pillow at his door, with the wind blowing dust upon me. Then he would come out and see me, and say: O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what brought you? Why did you not send for me so that I could come to you? I would say: No, I am more deserving of coming to you. He said: So I would ask him about the hadith. That Ansari man lived until he saw me with people gathered around me asking me questions, and he would say: This young man was wiser than me."],[363,"The first of people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection will be three: a man who was martyred. He will be brought and Allah will make known to him His favors, and he will recognize them. He will say, 'What did you do therein?' He will say, 'I fought in Your cause until I was martyred.' He will say, 'You have lied. You only wanted it to be said, \"So-and-so is daring,\" and it was said.' Then he will be commanded and dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire. And a man who learned knowledge and recited the Qur'an. He will be brought and Allah will make known to him His favors, and he will recognize them. He will say, 'What did you do therein?' He will say, 'I learned knowledge and recited the Qur'an and acted upon it for Your sake.' He will say, 'You have lied. You only wanted it to be said, \"So-and-so is a scholar and so-and-so is a reciter,\" and it was said.' Then he will be commanded and dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire. And a man whom Allah gave abundant wealth. He will be brought and Allah will make known to him His favors, and he will recognize them. He will say, 'What did you do therein?' He will say, 'I did not leave any way You love for money to be spent except that I spent in it for Your sake.' He will say, 'You have lied. You only wanted it to be said, \"So-and-so is generous,\" and it was said.' Then he will be commanded and dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire."],[364,"Three will be destroyed at the Reckoning: a generous one, a brave one, and a scholar."],[365,"Were it not for the covenant Allah took from the People of the Book, I would not have narrated anything to you. Then he recited: {And when Allah took the covenant of those who were given the Scripture: 'You shall make it clear to the people and not conceal it.'}"],[366,"Abu Hurayrah used to stand on Friday beside the pulpit and place the heels of his sandals in his arms, then grasp the pommel of the pulpit and say: Abu al-Qasim ﷺ said, Muhammad ﷺ said, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, the Truthful and Trusted ﷺ said. Then he would say on some of those occasions: 'Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near.' When he heard the movement of the door of the enclosure with the imam's coming out, he would sit."],[367,"I will not find any of you reclining on his couch, and a command of mine comes to him from what I have commanded or forbidden, and he says, 'I do not know; whatever we find in the Book of Allah, we follow it.'"],[368,"Let me not know of a man reclining, and a command of mine comes to him from what I have commanded or forbidden, and he says, 'We do not know this; this is the Book of Allah, and this is not in it.'"],[369,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said while people were around him: Let me not know of any of you who receives a command of mine that I have commanded or forbidden while he is reclining on his couch, and he says, 'Whatever we find in the Book of Allah, we act upon it; otherwise, no.'"],[370,"That he heard Miqdam b. Ma'dikarib al-Kindi, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, say: The Prophet ﷺ forbade certain things on the day of Khaybar, among them the domestic donkey and others. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is near that a man among you will sit on his couch and be told of my hadith, and he will say, \"Between us and you is the Book of Allah; whatever we find in it lawful, we deem lawful, and whatever we find in it unlawful, we deem unlawful.\" Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade just as Allah forbade.' As for the second hadith: al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[371,"About the Sunnah of our Prophet ﷺ when a man said to him, 'O Abu Nujayd, narrate to us the Qur'an.' Imran said to him: 'You and your companions recite the Qur'an. Would you inform me about the prayer and what is in it and its limits? Would you inform me about zakat on gold, camels, cattle, and types of wealth? But I was present and you were absent.' Then he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ obligated upon us in zakat such and such.' The man said, 'You have revived me, may Allah revive you.' Al-Hasan said: That man did not die until he became one of the jurists of the Muslims. Uqbah b. Khalid al-Shanni is among the trustworthy and devoted worshippers of the Basrans, and he is rare in hadith; his hadith is collected and does not reach ten in number. And may Allah bless Muhammad and all his family. Uqbah is trustworthy, a worshipper."],[372,"Tawus used to pray two rak'ahs after 'Asr, and Ibn Abbas said to him, 'Leave them.' He said, 'It was only forbidden to take them as a ladder to reach sunset.' Ibn Abbas said, 'The Prophet ﷺ forbade prayer after 'Asr, and I do not know whether he will be punished or rewarded for it, because Allah Almighty says: {It is not for a believing man or woman, when Allah and His Messenger have decreed a matter, to have any choice in their affair.}'"],[373,"To Ibn Mas'ud, Abu al-Darda', and Abu Dharr: 'What is this hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I think he kept them in Madinah until he was afflicted.' Narrated by Affan and others from him, i.e., from Shu'bah."],[374,"From Shu'bah, and he mentioned the hadith with its chain similarly."],[375,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he trembled and his clothes trembled,” then he said, “or something like this.”"],[376,"Sharik narrated to us, and he mentioned it in a similar manner."],[377,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, until when it was one evening, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Then I looked at him, and there he was with the buttons of his shirt undone, his jugular veins bulging, and his eyes flooded with tears.” Then he said, “like this, or more than this, or close to this, or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.”"],[378,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, and 'Ali b. Hamshadh al-'Adl narrated to me, Abu al-Hasan Muhammad b. Ahmad al-'Awdi narrated to us, Abu al-Rabi' narrated to us, Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ishaq, from Ma'bad b. Ka'b b. Malik, who said: I heard Abu Qatadah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while he was on the pulpit: “Beware of narrating too much from me. Whoever says something about me, let him say nothing but the truth. Whoever attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.” In the hadith of Muhammad b. 'Ubayd: Ibn Ka'b and others narrated to me from Abu Qatadah."],[379,"Narrate to me something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I fear that my tongue may slip with something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not say. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Beware of narrating too much from me. Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.”"],[380,"“It is enough of a sin for a man to narrate everything he hears.”"],[381,"“It is enough of a sin for a man to narrate everything he hears.”"],[382,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, until you rode the difficult and the easy.” “This is a sound chain according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, and it has another witness similar to it” according to their conditions."],[383,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, if he did not lie about him. When the people rode the difficult and the easy, we abandoned narrating from him. May Allah bless Muhammad and his family and grant them peace.”"],[384,"The last thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enjoined upon us was that he said: “Hold fast to the Book of Allah. You will return to a people who love to hear hadith from me—or a similar word—so whoever has memorized something, let him narrate it, and whoever attributes to me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.” The narrators of this hadith, down to the last of them, are reliable and may be used as proof. As for Abu Musa Malik b. 'Ubadah al-Ghafiqi, he is a Companion who resided in Egypt. This hadith is among what we have transmitted from a Companion when the chain to him is sound, though Wada'ah al-Juhani also narrated from Malik b. 'Ubadah al-Ghafiqi. This hadith has combined two rare expressions: one is his saying, “You will return to a people who love to hear hadith from me,” and the other is, “Whoever has memorized something, let him narrate it.” A group of the imams of Islam held that a narrator may not narrate what he does not memorize. They did not include it. Its narrators are reliable and may be used as proof, and Abu Musa Malik b. 'Ubadah is a Companion."],[385,"He heard Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman say: The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil, fearing that it might overtake me. I said: O Messenger of Allah, we were in ignorance and evil, then Allah brought this good. Is there any evil after this good? He said: “Yes, and there will be some taint in it.” I said: What is its taint? He said: “People who guide by other than my guidance; some of them you will recognize and some you will disapprove.” I said: Will there be any evil after that good? He said: “Yes, callers at the gates of Hell. Whoever answers them, they will cast him into it.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us. He said: “They are of our own skin and speak with our tongues.” I said: What do you command me if I live to see that? He said: “Cling to the community of Muslims and their imam.” I said: What if they have no imam and no community? He said: “Then withdraw from all those factions, even if you have to bite onto the root of a tree until death overtakes you while you are in that state.”"],[386,"I stood among you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us, and he said: “I enjoin you to my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread, until a man swears and is not asked to swear, and gives testimony and is not asked to testify. Whoever among you desires the spaciousness of Paradise, let him cling to the community, for Satan is with the solitary individual and is farther from two. Indeed, no man should be alone with a woman except that Satan is the third of them.” He said it three times. “And upon you is the community, for Satan is with the solitary individual and is farther from two. Indeed, whoever is pleased by his good deeds and distressed by his evil deeds is a believer.”"],[387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us as I am standing among you, and said: \"Treat my Companions well.\" Then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner, \"…and as for the second witness…\""],[388,"Indeed I stood among you just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us. Then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. \"As for the disagreement in this hadith from 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Umayr, it has been compiled for me in a volume. What I hold is that the two imams narrate this hadith from that disagreement among the imams regarding 'Abd al-Malik in it, and those chains are not to be deemed defective by these chains that lie outside them.\" And we have narrated it with a sound chain from Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, from 'Umar, under the conditions of the two shaykhs."],[389,"He heard my speech and retained it. Indeed I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand among us as I am standing among you, then he said: \"Take care of me through my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them\"—three times—\"then there will be much killing and lying will spread, and a man will testify though he is not asked to testify, and he will swear though he is not asked to swear. Whoever among you loves the spaciousness of Paradise, let him adhere to the congregation, for Satan is with the one and he is farther from the two. Beware, let no man be alone with a woman, for Satan is the third of them. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer.\" The second hadith regarding what the scholars have used as evidence that consensus is authoritative is a hadith that is disputed from al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman in seven ways. The first way among them: And this is authentic."],[390,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah will never unite this ummah upon misguidance.\" And he also said: \"The hand of Allah is over a [united] group, so follow the majority, for whoever deviates will deviate into the Hellfire.\""],[391,"\"Allah will never gather my ummah upon misguidance ever.\""],[392,"\"Allah will never gather my ummah upon misguidance ever, and the hand of Allah is over the congregation like this\"—and he raised his hands—\"so indeed whoever deviates, deviates into the Fire.\""],[393,"\"Allah will never gather my ummah upon misguidance ever, and the hand of Allah is over the congregation like this, so follow the great majority, for indeed whoever deviates, deviates into the Fire.\""],[394,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah will never gather my ummah—or he said: the ummah of Muhammad ﷺ—upon misguidance ever, and the hand of Allah is over the congregation.\" And he said, gesturing with his hand, spreading it out: \"Indeed whoever deviates, deviates into the Fire.\""],[395,"\"Allah will never gather my ummah—or he said: this ummah—upon misguidance ever, and the hand of Allah is over the congregation.\""],[396,"\"Allah will never gather my ummah upon misguidance ever, and the hand of Allah is over the congregation.\"[1]"],[397,"\"He asked his Lord that they not die of hunger, and that was granted. He asked his Lord that they not unite upon misguidance, and that was granted. He asked his Lord that they not turn back to disbelief, and that was granted. He asked his Lord that no enemy of theirs overcome them and deem their might permissible, and that was granted. He asked his Lord that their might not be between them, and that was not granted.\""],[398,"Whoever separates from the community by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck."],[399,"Whoever opposes the community of Muslims by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck."],[400,"Whoever departs from the community by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his neck until he returns to it. And he said: Whoever dies without having an imam of the community, his death is a death of ignorance."],[401,"I command you with five words which Allah commanded me: the community, hearing and obedience, emigration, and jihad in the path of Allah. So whoever departs from the community by a span has cast off the yoke of Islam from his head unless he returns."],[402,"Indeed Allah commanded me with five things to act upon."],[403,"Indeed Allah commanded Yahya b. Zakariyya with five things to act upon, and He commanded the Children of Israel to act upon them. Then he mentioned the hadith and said in it: Indeed Allah commands me with five things."],[404,"Whoever separates from the community by a span enters the Fire."],[405,"Whoever separates from a nation or returns to being a Bedouin after his emigration has no argument for himself."],[406,"Whoever separates from the community and humiliates the authority will meet Allah and he has no argument for himself."],[407,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever separates from the community and humiliates the authority will meet Allah and he has no argument for himself with Allah."],[408,"Three [types of people] you should not ask about: a man who separated from the community and disobeyed his imam and died while disobedient; and a slave woman or slave who runs away from his master and dies; and a woman whose husband was absent and he had sufficed her with the provision of the world, then she displayed her adornment after him. Do not ask about them."],[409,"The prescribed prayer to the prescribed prayer that comes after it is an expiation for what is between them, and the Friday prayer to the Friday prayer, and the month to the month - meaning from the month of Ramadan to the month of Ramadan - is an expiation for what is between them. Then after that he said: Except from three things. So I knew that that was from a matter that had occurred. He said: Except from associating partners with Allah, breaking the covenant, and abandoning the sunnah. I said: O Messenger of Allah, as for associating partners with Allah, we have come to know it. But what is breaking the covenant and abandoning the sunnah? He said: As for breaking the covenant, it is that you pledge allegiance to a man with your right hand, then you differ with him and confront him with your sword. As for abandoning the sunnah, it is departing from the community."],[410,"\"It is near that you will know the people of Paradise from the people of the Fire,\" or he said, \"your best from your worst.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by what?\" He said, \"By good praise and bad praise. You are witnesses over one another.\""],[411,"\"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the funeral of a man from the Ansar, and we reached the grave before it was prepared. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and we sat around him as if birds were on our heads.\" And he mentioned the hadith. The authenticity of this hadith has been established in the Book of Faith, and they did not include it in the two Sahihs."],[412,"\"When we sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we did not raise our heads to him, out of respect for him.\""],[413,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his companions were with him as if birds were on their heads. I greeted and sat down. Then some Bedouins came asking him about things, until they said, \"Should we seek treatment?\" He said, \"Seek treatment, for Allah Almighty has not placed any disease except that He has placed for it a cure.\" Then they asked him about other things, and he said, \"O servants of Allah, hardship has been removed, except for a man who wrongs another man; that is hardship and destruction.\" Then they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing given to people?\" He said, \"Good character.\""],[414,"I entered the mosque and there was a circle as if their heads had been cut off. There was a man narrating to them, and it was Hudhayfah. He said: \"The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil.\" And he mentioned the hadith at length. The text of this hadith is included in the two Sahihs, but I have included it in this place for the attentive listening to the narrator and the manner of honoring him, for this wording was not included in the two Sahihs. Sahih."],[415,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, none of us would raise his head except Abu Bakr and Umar, for they would smile at him and he would smile at them.\""],[416,"Salman was among a group remembering Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by them and came to them deliberately until he drew near. They stopped talking out of respect for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"What were you saying? For I saw mercy descending upon you, and I wanted to share in it with you.\""],[417,"Today a man asked me about something I do not know what to say to him. He said, \"What do you think of a man who is well-mannered, energetic, eager for jihad, and our commanders impose upon us things we cannot count?\" I said, \"By Allah, I do not know what to say to you except that we used to be with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and perhaps he would not command something except that we did it. What remains of this world is like a pool whose clear water has been drunk and only its dregs remain. One of you will continue to be in good as long as he fears Allah Almighty, and when something troubles his soul, he goes to a man and asks him, and he heals him. By Allah, it is near that you will not find him.\""],[418,"\"He is not one of us who does not honor our elders, show mercy to our young, and recognize the right of our scholar.\""],[419,"From Jabir b. Abdullah regarding {Obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [al-Nisa' 59]: He said, \"Those possessing understanding and goodness.\""],[420,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of the Almighty {Obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [al-Nisa' 59]: It means \"the people of understanding and religion, the people of obedience to Allah who teach the people the noble aspects of their religion, enjoin them to do good, and forbid them from evil. Allah has obligated obedience to them.\" \"These are explicit hadiths about what scholars must do in humility toward those they teach.\""],[421,"Hafsah said to Umar, \"Will you not wear a garment softer than your garment and eat food better than your food, when Allah has opened the matter for you and expanded provision for you?\" He said, \"I will contend with you against yourself,\" and he mentioned the affair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the hardship of living he used to endure. He kept mentioning it until she wept. Then he said, \"I have resolved to share with them in their harsh living, so that perhaps I may attain with them their easy living.\""],[422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The nobility of a believer is his religion, his manliness is his intellect, and his lineage is his character.'"],[423,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'The nobility of a believer is his religion, his manliness is his intellect, and his lineage is his character.'"],[424,"You cannot encompass the people with your wealth, but let them be encompassed by your cheerful countenance and good character."],[425,"You cannot encompass the people with your wealth, but let them be encompassed by your cheerful countenance and good character."],[426,"Kindness to people protects its doer from evil deaths, calamities, and destructions. The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter."],[427,"Regarding His saying ﷻ {Take to forgiveness} [al-A'raf 199], he said: 'Allah commanded His Prophet ﷺ to adopt forgiveness in dealing with people's character.'"],[428,"Allah did not reveal this verse except concerning people's character: {Take to forgiveness} [al-A'raf 199] and enjoin what is good and turn away from the ignorant."],[429,"The Prophet ﷺ detained a man from his tribe on suspicion. A man from his tribe came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering a sermon and said: 'O Muhammad, why do you detain my neighbor?' The Prophet ﷺ remained silent. Then he said: 'Some people say that you forbid evil but you delight in it.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'What do you say?' So I began to interpose between them with speech, fearing that he would understand it and supplicate against my people with a supplication after which they would never prosper. The Prophet ﷺ continued until he understood it, then said: 'Have they said that? Or is the one saying it among them? By Allah, if I did that, it would be upon them as it was upon them. Release his neighbors.' And the discussion has already been mentioned in the scroll of Bahz b. Hakim, which suffices from repeating it, although the supporting evidences for this hadith are extracted in the two Sahihs. Among them is the hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Wa'il from 'Abdullah: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed a distribution, and a man from the Ansar said, 'This is a distribution by which the Face of Allah is not intended.' Among them is the hadith of Malik from Ishaq b. 'Abdullah b. Abi Talha from Anas: I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was wearing a Najrani cloak with a thick border. A bedouin pulled his cloak... the hadith. Among them is the hadith of Sharik b. 'Abdullah b. Abi Namir from Anas in the story of Hunayn: 'Why do you compel me to this tree?' and other than this, which would take long to mention."],[430,"Three qualities, whoever has them, Allah will shelter him in His protection, cover him with His mercy, and admit him into His love.' It was said: 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Whoever, when given, is thankful; when able, forgives; and when angry, restrains himself.'"],[431,"When 'Umar b. al-Khattab became caliph, he addressed the people from the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: 'O people, I know that you perceive severity and harshness from me. That is because I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was his servant and attendant. He was, as Allah said, {with the believers kind and merciful}. I was before him like a drawn sword, unless he sheathed me or forbade me from a matter, then I would refrain; otherwise I would advance upon the people because of his gentleness.'"],[432,"Whoever is gentle, soft, and approachable, Allah will forbid him to the Fire."],[433,"Whoever gives fatwa to people without knowledge, his sin is upon the one who gave him the fatwa."],[434,"Do not write down anything from me except the Quran. Whoever writes down anything from me other than the Quran, let him erase it."],[435,"He heard a hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'We had an estate and occupations, but people in those days did not lie, so the one who was present would narrate to the one who was absent.'"],[436,"Then if it is not in the Book of Allah, and there is something from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning it, he would act according to it. Then if there is nothing from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning it, he would act according to what Abu Bakr and Umar acted upon. Then if there is nothing from Abu Bakr and Umar concerning it, he would give his own opinion."],[437,"Lying is not appropriate, whether in seriousness or in jest, nor for a man to promise his son something and then not fulfill it. Indeed, truthfulness leads to righteousness, and righteousness leads to Paradise. And lying leads to wickedness, and wickedness leads to the Fire. It is said of the truthful one: he spoke the truth and was righteous. And it is said of the liar: he lied and was wicked. A man continues to be truthful until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful one, or he continues to lie until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."],[438,"The Jews split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, the Christians split into seventy-one or seventy-two sects, and my community will split into seventy-three sects."],[439,"“The Jews split into seventy-one sects and my nation will split into seventy-three sects.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3991)"],[440,"We performed Hajj with Mu'awiya ibn Abi Sufyan, and when we arrived in Mecca, he was informed of a storyteller who was narrating to the people of Mecca, a servant of the Banu Farrukh. Mu'awiya sent for him and asked, \"Were you ordered to give these narrations?\" He replied, \"No.\" Mu'awiya then asked, \"So what led you to narrate without permission?\" The man replied, \"We are imparting knowledge that Allah has taught us.\" Mu'awiya said, \"Had I warned you beforehand, I would have severed a part of you.\" Then, after the Dhuhr prayer in Mecca, Mu'awiya stood up and said: The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The People of the Book divided themselves into seventy-two sects in their religion, and this Ummah will divide into seventy-three, all of which will be in the fire except one, which is the congregation. From my Ummah, there will emerge people driven by desires just as rabies drives its host, leaving no vein or joint without being infected. By Allah, O Arabs, if you do not uphold that which Muhammad ﷺ brought, surely nothing else will you uphold.\"[1]"],[441,"There will certainly come upon my community the like of what came upon the Children of Israel, exactly, just as one sandal matches the other, so much so that if there were among them one who openly had intercourse with his mother, there would be in my community someone like him. The Children of Israel split into seventy-one religious communities, and my community will split into seventy-three religious communities, all of them in the Fire except one religious community.\" It was said to him: \"Which is the one?\" He said: \"That upon which I and my companions are today."],[442,"We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his mosque when he said: 'You will certainly follow the ways of those before you, just as one sandal matches the other, and you will take exactly as they took, if a span then a span, if a cubit then a cubit, if a fathom then a fathom, so much so that if they entered the hole of a lizard, you would enter it. Verily, the Children of Israel split concerning Moses into seventy-one sects, all of them astray except one sect: Islam and their community. And they split concerning Jesus son of Mary into seventy-one sects, all of them astray except one sect: Islam and their community. Then they will be upon seventy-two sects, all of them astray except one sect: Islam and their community.' End of the Book of Knowledge."],[443,"When the servant performs ablution and rinses his mouth, sins depart from his mouth. When he sniffs water into his nose and blows it out, sins depart from his nose. When he washes his face, sins depart from his face, even from the edges of his eyelids. When he washes his hands, sins depart from his hands, even from under his fingernails. When he wipes his head, sins depart from his head, even from his ears. When he washes his feet, sins depart from his feet, even from under his toenails. Then his walking to the mosque and his prayer are an additional reward."],[444,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Adhere to righteousness even though you will not be able to do all acts of virtue. Know that the best of your deeds is Salat (prayer) and that no one maintains his ablution except a believer.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 277)"],[445,"From Thawban."],[446,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Adhere to righteousness even though you will not be able to do all acts of virtue. Know that the best of your deeds is Salat (prayer) and that no one maintains his ablution except a believer.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 277)"],[447,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Adhere to righteousness even though you will not be able to do all acts of virtue. Know that the best of your deeds is Salat (prayer) and that no one maintains his ablution except a believer.'\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 277)"],[448,"Whoever performs ablution and perfects his ablution, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, his previous sins will be forgiven."],[449,"Abu Bakr b. Ishaq narrated to us: al-Abbas b. al-Fadl al-Asfati informed us: Abu Thabit narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Hisham b. Sa'd, and he mentioned it similarly."],[450,"From Uqba b. Amir."],[451,"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not once, nor twice, nor three times, saying: “When the believing servant performs ablution and rinses his mouth and sniffs water into his nostrils and expels it, sins depart from the sides of his mouth. Then when he washes his hands, sins scatter from his fingernails. Then when he wipes his head, sins scatter from the sides of his head. Then if he stands and prays two rak'ahs, turning his heart and his gaze in them toward Allah ﷻ, he departs from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him.”"],[452,"He was narrating to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? 'Amr b. 'Abasa said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not once, nor twice—until he counted five times—saying: “When the Muslim brings his ablution water and washes his palms, his sins depart from between his fingers and the tips of his fingertips. Then when he washes his face, his sins depart from the sides of his beard. Then when he wipes his head, his sins depart from the ends of his hair. Then when he washes his feet, his sins depart from the soles of his feet.”"],[453,"The Prophet said: \"Sins are expiated by well-performed ablution despite difficulties, increasing the number of steps one takes towards the mosque, (and waiting for the next prayer after prayer).\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 428)"],[454,"“The key to prayer is purification, its sanctification is the takbir, and its conclusion is the taslim.”"],[455,"Abu Bakr and 'Uthman, the two sons of Abu Shayba, narrated to us, they said: Abu Usama narrated to us. And Abu al-Walid al-Faqih informed me: 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. Shirawyh narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us: Abu Usama reported to us: al-Walid b. Kathir narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water that is in the wilderness and what visits it of predators and beasts. He said: “If the water is two qullahs, nothing makes it impure.”"],[456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water and what visits it of beasts and predators. He said: “If the water is two qullahs, it does not carry impurity.” “And thus al-Shafi'i narrated it in al-Mabsut from the trustworthy one, and he is Abu Usama, without doubt about it.”"],[457,"If the water is two qullahs, it does not carry impurity, or he said: filth."],[458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water and what visits it of beasts and predators. The Prophet ﷺ said: “If the water is two qullahs, it does not carry impurity.” “And with this narration the soundness of the hadith is established and confirmed, and it is clear that Abu Usama narrated the hadith from al-Walid b. Kathir from both of them together, for Shu'ayb b. Ayyub al-Sarifini is trustworthy and reliable, and likewise the path to him. And Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Yasar al-Qurashi has followed al-Walid b. Kathir in his narration from Muhammad b. Ja'far b. al-Zubayr.”"],[459,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ when he was asked about water that is in the wilderness and what visits it of beasts and predators. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If the water is the amount of two qullahs, it does not carry impurity.” And thus narrated it Sufyan al-Thawri, Za'ida b. Qudama, Hammad b. Salama, Ibrahim b. Sa'd, 'Abd Allah b. al-Mubarak, Yazid b. Zuray', Sa'id b. Zayd the brother of Hammad b. Zayd, Abu Mu'awiya, and 'Abda b. Sulayman. 'Abd Allah narrated it from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah, “and 'Abd Allah together, with the soundness of what I have mentioned.”"],[460,"I entered with 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar a garden in which there was a pool of water containing the skin of a dead camel. He performed ablution from it. I said: Do you perform ablution from it while it contains the skin of a dead camel? He narrated to me from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “If the water reaches two qullahs or three, nothing makes it impure.”"],[461,"I asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and said: One of us prays and does not know how many he has prayed. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: When one of you prays and does not know how many he has prayed, let him prostrate twice while he is sitting. And when Satan comes to one of you and says: You have broken your ablution, let him say: You have lied, unless he finds an odor with his nose or hears a sound with his ear."],[462,"That he asked Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and mentioned something similar. And as for the hadith of 'Ali b. al-Mubarak,”"],[463,"From 'Iyad, and he mentioned something similar. And as for the hadith of Ma'mar."],[464,"About 'Iyad, he mentioned something similar to this: \"Al-Bukhari and Muslim agreed on extracting scattered hadiths from the two Sahih collections, which are used as evidence that touching is not considered adultery. Among them is the hadith of Abu Hurairah: 'The hand is its own adultery' and the hadith of Ibn Abbas: 'Perhaps you touched' and the hadith of Ibn Mas'ood: 'Establish the prayer at the two ends of the day.' There are still authentic hadiths related to them in tafsir and other matters.\""],[465,"There was hardly a day, or seldom a day, except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would visit all of us, kissing and touching without intercourse. Then when he came to the one whose day it was, he stayed with her."],[466,"From 'Abdullaah regarding His ﷻ saying, {or you have touched women} [al-Nisa' 43], he said: \"It is that which is less than sexual intercourse, and for it is wudu'.\""],[467,"Kissing is from touching, so perform ablution from it."],[468,"That he was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a man who has had something with a woman not lawful for him, and he did not leave anything? \"Perform a good ablution, then stand and pray.\" He said: And Allah ﷻ revealed {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approach of the night} [Hud 114] the verse. He said: He said: Is it for me specifically or for the Muslims generally? He said: \"Rather for the believers generally.\" \"These hadiths and those which I have mentioned, the two shaykhs agreed upon them, except that they are reported in the two books in scattered places, and all of them are authentic, indicating that the touching which necessitates ablution is less than sexual intercourse.\""],[469,"About the touching of the private parts, if it is touched without any harm, then 'Urwah narrated that Busrah bint Safwan informed me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you touches his private parts, he should not pray until he performs ablution.\" Marwan sent someone to ask Busrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and said: \"Yes, he (Hisham) used to say, 'When one touches his private parts or his organs or his anus, he should not pray until he performs ablution.' It is like this,\" and Hammad bin Zaid reported this Hadith and mentioned the hearing of 'Urwah from Busrah and Khalaf bin Hisham as proof of its authenticity. Khalaf is trustworthy and one of the leading Qur'an reciters. Among the evidence confirming the authenticity of the narration from the majority of the companions of Hisham bin 'Urwah from Hisham, from his father, from Busrah, including Ayub bin Abu Tameemah As-Sakhtiyani, Qays bin Sa'd Al-Makki, Ibn Jurayj, Ibn 'Uyaynah, 'Abdul-'Aziz bin Abu Hazim, Yahya bin Sa'id, Hammad bin Salamah, Ma'mar bin Rashid, Hisham bin Hassan, 'Abdullah bin Muhammad Abu 'Alqamah, 'Asim bin Hilal Al-Bariqi, Yahya bin Tha'labah Al-Mazini, Sa'id bin 'Abd Ar-Rahman Al-Jumahi, 'Ali bin Al-Mubarak Al-Hunai'i, Aban bin Yazid Al-'Atari, Muhammad bin 'Abd Ar-Rahman At-Tufawi, 'Abdul-Hamid bin Ja'far Al-Ansari, 'Abdul-'Aziz bin Muhammad Ad-Darawardi, Yazid bin Sinan Al-Jazri, 'Abd Ar-Rahman bin Abi Az-Zinad, 'Abd Ar-Rahman bin 'Abdul-'Aziz, Harithah bin Harimah Al-Fuqaymi, Abu Ma'mar, 'Abbad bin Suhayb, and others. A group has differed from them, but they transmitted it from Hisham bin 'Urwah from his father from Marwan, including Sufyan bin Sa'id Ath-Thawri, and it has been narrated from Hisham bin Hassan, and Hammad bin Salamah, Malik bin Anas, Wahb bin Khalid, Salam bin Abi Muti', 'Umar bin 'Ali Al-Muqaddami, 'Abdullah bin Idris, 'Ali bin Musahir, Abu Usamah, and others. The difference in the narration has been mentioned regarding Hisham bin 'Urwah among his companions, so we looked into it and found that the group who confirmed hearing 'Urwah from Busrah were greater in number, and some of them were more trustworthy than those who transmitted it from Marwan, except that also some of the reliable Hafiz were mentioned among them who mentioned hearing Marwan from Busrah. So, we considered that those who did not mention this difference had not studied it, and that it is baseless to criticize the narrators of Hadith for narrating from Marwan. Therefore, we found a group of reliable Hafiz narrating this statement from Hisham bin 'Urwah from his father from Marwan from Busrah, and then they mentioned in their narrations that 'Urwah said, 'Then I met Busrah after that, and she narrated the Hadith to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as Marwan narrated it from her.' This indicated the authenticity and preservation of the Hadith according to the condition of the two sheikhs, and the difference and doubt were eliminated. The hearing of 'Urwah from Busrah has been confirmed, and among those mentioned who heard 'Urwah from Busrah is Shu'ayb bin Ishaq Ad-Dimashqi."],[470,"About Busra bint Safwan, who had accompanied the Prophet ﷺ , it is reported that the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever touches their private parts should perform ablution.\" Urwah narrated, \"I asked Busra about this and she confirmed what the Prophet ﷺ had said.\""],[471,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution.\"[1]"],[472,"\"Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution.\""],[473,"\"Whoever touches his private part, let him not pray until he performs ablution.\""],[474,"From Busrah bt. Safwan, and she had been a companion of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you touches his penis, let him not pray until he performs ablution.\" \"Urwah denied that, so he asked Busrah, and she confirmed it to him: Hazm al-Ansari, Muhammad b. Muslim al-Zuhri, Abu al-Zinad 'Abdullah b. Dhakwan al-Qurashi, Muhammad b. 'Abdullah b. 'Urwah, Abu al-Aswad Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Nawfal al-Qurashi, 'Abd al-Hamid b. Ja'far al-Ansari, al-Hasan b. Muslim b. Yannaq, and others among the tabi'in and their followers. As for Busrah bt. Safwan, she is from the noble women of Quraysh.\""],[475,"\"Do you know who Busrah bt. Safwan is? She is the grandmother of 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan, the mother of his mother, so know her.\""],[476,"Muhammad b. Yusuf al-Mu'adhdhin informed us, Muhammad b. 'Imran al-Nasawi narrated to us, Ahmad b. Zuhayr narrated to us, Mus'ab b. 'Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: And Busrah bt. Safwan b. Nawfal b. Asad was from the women who gave the pledge, and Waraqah b. Nawfal was her paternal uncle. Safwan b. Nawfal had no descendants except through Busrah, and she was the wife of Mu'awiyah b. Mughirah b. Abi al-'As. \"This hadith has been narrated from a group of the Sahabah and Tabi'in from Busrah, among them 'Abdullah b. 'Umar b. al-Khattab, 'Abdullah b. 'Amr b. al-'As, Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, 'Amrah bt. 'Abd al-Rahman al-Ansariyyah, 'Abdullah b. Abi Mulaykah, Marwan b. al-Hakam, and Sulayman b. Musa.\" And we have narrated from Busrah bt. Safwan from the Prophet ﷺ five hadiths other than this one. It has been established by what we have mentioned the fame of Busrah bt. Safwan, and the name of being unknown has been lifted from her by these narrations. And we have narrated the obligation of ablution from touching the penis from a group of male and female companions from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, among them 'Abdullah b. 'Umar, Abu Hurayrah, Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, Jabir b. 'Abdullah, Umm Habibah, Umm Salamah, and Arwa."],[477,"\"When a woman touches her private part with her hand, ablution is upon her.\""],[478,"\"When a woman touches her private part, she performs ablution.\""],[479,"Abu Bakr Muhammad b. 'Abdullah b. al-Jarrah al-'Adl al-Hafiz narrated to us in Marw, 'Abdullah b. Yahya al-Qadi al-Sarakhsi narrated to us, Raja' b. Murajja al-Hafiz narrated to us, he said: We gathered in the mosque of al-Khayf: I, Ahmad b. Hanbal, 'Ali b. al-Madini, and Yahya b. Ma'in. They debated about touching the penis. Yahya b. Ma'in said: One performs ablution from it. 'Ali b. al-Madini held the view of the Kufans and adhered to their opinion. Yahya b. Ma'in argued with the hadith of Busrah bt. Safwan, and 'Ali b. al-Madini argued with the hadith of Qays b. Talq from his father. He said to Yahya b. Ma'in: How can you adhere to the chain of Busrah, when Marwan was only sent as a policeman until he brought her answer back to him? Yahya said: Then that did not satisfy 'Urwah until he came to Busrah and asked her, and she directly told him the hadith. Then Yahya said: People have spoken much about Qays b. Talq, and that his hadith is not to be used as proof. Ahmad b. Hanbal said: Both matters are as you two have said. Yahya said: Malik from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that he performed ablution from touching the penis. 'Ali said: Ibn Mas'ud used to say: One does not perform ablution from it; it is only a part of your body. Yahya said: From whom? He said: From Sufyan from Abu Qays from Huzayl from 'Abdullah. And when Ibn Mas'ud and Ibn 'Umar meet and differ, Ibn Mas'ud is more worthy to be followed. Ahmad b. Hanbal said to him: Yes, but Abu Qays al-Awdi's hadith is not to be used as proof. 'Ali said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to me, Mis'ar narrated to us, from 'Umayr b. Sa'id from 'Ammar b. Yasir, he said: I do not care whether I touch it or take precaution (not to). Ahmad said: 'Ammar and Ibn 'Umar are equal, so whoever wishes takes this, and whoever wishes takes that. Yahya said: Between 'Umayr b. Sa'id and 'Ammar b. Yasir there is a desert."],[480,"We used to pray with the Prophet ﷺ and we would not perform ablution from [stepping on] a place trodden upon. Abu Mu'awiyah and 'Abdullah b. Idris concurred with him, narrating from al-A'mash. As for the hadith of Abu Mu'awiyah, it meets their criteria."],[481,"Abu Mu'awiya praised him and mentioned him with his chain of narration similar to him: \"As for the hadith of Abu Idris\""],[482,"From al-A'mash, and he mentioned something similar."],[483,"The Prophet ﷺ never removed his sandals in prayer except once. He removed them, so the people removed theirs. He said: 'What is the matter with you?' They said: 'You removed your sandals, so we removed ours.' He said: 'Jibril informed me that there was filth or harm in them.'"],[484,"The Prophet ﷺ removed his sandal and said: 'Jibril informed me that...'"],[485,"From al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah."],[486,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to relieve himself, he would go far away so that no one could see him."],[487,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the water of the sea, and he said, \"The water of the sea is purifying.\""],[488,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, all of them from Malik, from Safwan b. Sulaym, from Sa'id b. Salamah, a freed slave of the family of al-Azraq, that al-Mughirah b. Abi Burdah, a man from Banu 'Abd al-Dar, informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O Messenger of Allah, we travel by sea and carry with us a small amount of water. If we perform ablution with it, we will thirst. Can we perform ablution with seawater?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is the pure one; its water is purifying, and its dead are lawful.' 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq and Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Muzani concurred with Malik b. Anas in his narration from Safwan b. Sulaym. As for the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq, Abu Bakr b. Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abdullah b. Ayyub b. Zadhan informed us, Muhammad b. al-Minhal narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq narrated to us, from Safwan b. Sulaym. He said: And Abu Yusuf b. Ya'qub informed us, Muhammad b. Abi Bakr narrated to us, Yazid b. Zuray' narrated to us, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ishaq narrated to us, Safwan b. Sulaym narrated to us, from Sa'id b. Salamah, from al-Mughirah b. Abi Burdah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[489,"From Abu Hurayrah."],[490,"He informed him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day when a fisherman came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we go out to sea seeking fish. One of us carries a water skin with him, hoping to catch fish nearby. Sometimes he finds it so, and sometimes he does not find fish until he reaches a place in the sea he did not think he would reach. Perhaps he experiences a wet dream or needs to perform ablution. If he bathes or performs ablution with this [fresh] water, one of us may perish from thirst. Do you think it is permissible to bathe from seawater or perform ablution with it when we fear that?' It was claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Bathe from it and perform ablution with it, for it is the pure one; its water is purifying, and its dead are lawful.' Muslim used al-Julah, Abu Kathir, as evidence, and Yahya b. Sa'id al-Ansari and Yazid b. Muhammad al-Qurashi concurred with Sa'id b. Salamah al-Makhzumi in narrating this hadith, but there was disagreement about it."],[491,"From the Prophet ﷺ, something similar."],[492,"Abu al-Hasan Muhammad b. al-Hasan informed us, 'Ali b. 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us, Hajjaj b. Minhal narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Yahya b. Sa'id, from al-Mughirah b. 'Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. Sulayman b. Bilal said: from Yahya b. Sa'id, from 'Abdullah b. al-Mughirah, from his father. Muslim used al-Julah as evidence."],[493,"A group of people came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'We fish in the sea, and we have fresh water with us. Sometimes we fear thirst. Is it permissible for us to perform ablution with salty seawater?' He said: 'Yes, perform ablution with it.' Al-Bukhari mentioned Yazid b. Muhammad al-Qurashi in his Tarikh, and that al-Layth b. Abi Burdah narrated from him, among them Sa'id b. al-Musayyib."],[494,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about seawater: 'Should we perform ablution with it?' He said: \"Its water is purifying and its dead are lawful.\""],[495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about performing ablution with seawater, and he said: \"It is purifying — its water, lawful — its dead.\""],[496,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about seawater and he said: \"It is purifying — its water, lawful — its dead.\" \"As for the hadith of Ibn Abbas, we have already mentioned it.\""],[497,"He said about the sea: \"It is purifying — its water, lawful — its dead.\""],[498,"\"The dead of the sea are lawful and its water is purifying.\""],[499,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of the people of the Book (Christians and Jews), they drink alcohol and eat pork. So what do you think about their utensils and pots?\" He said, \"Leave them as long as you do not find any impurities on them. But if you do not find any impurities, then wash them with water or pour water over them.\" Then he said, \"Cook in them and eat.\" Hammad said, I think he said, \"And drink.\" This is how Shu'bah narrated it from Ayyub."],[500,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'We are in a land of many People of the Book, so how should we deal with their vessels?' He said: \"Set aside what you can do without, and if you cannot do without them, wash them with water and then cook in them.\" And thus Khalid al-Hadhdha' narrated it from Abu Qilabah."],[501,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the vessels of the polytheists, and he said: \"Wash them and then cook in them.\""],[502,"He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of the People of the Book, and we cook in their pots and drink from their vessels?' He said: \"If you find no others, then clean them.\""],[503,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I said, \"We raid and travel in the land of the disbelievers, and we need some utensils from their possessions in order to cook in them.\" He said, \"Wash them with water and then cook in them and benefit from them.\"[1]"],[504,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the skins of wild animals.\""],[505,"Abu Bakr b. Ishaq informed us; Abu al-Muthanna, Muhammad b. Ayyub, and Yusuf b. Ya'qub said: Muhammad b. al-Minhal narrated to us; Yazid b. Zurai' narrated to us; Sa'id narrated to us, and he mentioned it in a similar manner. A shaykh from Basra narrated it from Muhammad b. al-Minhal and said in it: from Shu'bah, and that is an error from him. \"This chain is sound, for Abu al-Malih's name is Amir b. Usamah, and his father Usamah b. Umayr is a companion from Banu Lihyan, whose hadith is recorded in the musnads, but they did not narrate it.\""],[506,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought two-thirds of a mudd of water, performed ablution, and began rubbing his forearms."],[507,"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said during his illness in which he passed away, \"Pour upon me from seven Qirab, which have not been mixed or touched, in order that I may make a bequest to the people.\" Aisha said, so we sat him in a basin made of copper for Hafsa and poured water on him, and he gestured to us that we had indeed done so, then he left."],[508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the illness in which he was taken: \"Pour over me from seven water-skins.\""],[509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the illness in which he died, \"Pour over me from seven water-skins.\" \"Both chains of transmission are authentic according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs.\""],[510,"\"Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr entered, and with him was a tooth-stick with which he was cleaning his teeth.\" I said to him, \"Give me this tooth-stick, O Abd al-Rahman.\" He gave it to me, I broke it, then chewed it, and gave it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he cleaned his teeth with it while leaning against my chest."],[511,"\"The Messenger of Allah used to pray in the night (Qiyamul-Lail) two Rak'ah by two, then when he finished he would use the tooth stick.\" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 288)"],[512,"The superiority of the prayer for which the tooth-stick is used over the prayer for which it is not used is seventy-fold."],[513,"Were it not that I would impose hardship on my community, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them together with ablution, and I would have delayed the night prayer until midnight."],[514,"Were it not that I would impose hardship on my community, I would have made the tooth-stick obligatory upon them at every prayer just as I made ablution obligatory upon them."],[515,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no prayer for one who does not have ablution, and there is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah upon it.' Muhammad bin Isma'il bin Abi Fudayk narrated it from Muhammad bin Musa al-Makhzumi.'\""],[516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The prayer of a person who does not perform ablution is not valid, and the ablution of a person who does not mention the name of Allah (in the beginning) is not valid. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 101)"],[517,"There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."],[518,"He called for a vessel containing water, scooped a handful, rinsed his mouth and sniffed water into his nose, then took another handful and brought his hands together with it and washed his face, then took another and washed his right hand, then took another scoop and washed his left hand, then took a handful of water and shook his hand and wiped his head and ears with it, then scooped another handful and sprinkled it on his right foot while the sandal was on it, and the left similarly, and he wiped the bottoms of the two sandals.\" Then he said, \"This is how the ablution of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was."],[519,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned some matters, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Perform ablution thoroughly, pass the fingers between the toes and fingers, and when you sniff water into the nose, do it thoroughly unless you are fasting.\""],[520,"That he and a companion of his came to Aisha seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but they did not find him. Aisha fed them dates and porridge. Before long, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came striding and swaying. He said, \"Has anyone fed you two?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" Then I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell us about prayer.\" He said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly, pass the fingers between the toes and fingers, and when you sniff water into the nose, do it thoroughly unless you are fasting.\""],[521,"\"When you sniff water into the nose, do it thoroughly unless you are fasting, and do not strike your wife as you strike your slave-girl.\""],[522,"I was the delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about ablution.\" He said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly, pass the fingers between the toes and fingers, and sniff water into the nose thoroughly unless you are fasting.\" This hadith has a corroborating narration from Ibn Abbas."],[523,"\"Blow out water from the nose twice thoroughly or three times.\""],[524,"I saw 'Uthman perform ablution: he washed his face, rinsed his nose, and rinsed his mouth three times; he wiped his head and his ears, their outer and inner parts; and he ran his fingers through his beard three times while washing his face before washing his feet. Then he said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do what you have seen me do.\" The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting channels for the hadith of 'Uthman regarding the completion of his ablution, but they did not mention in their narrations running the fingers through the beard three times. This is a sound chain; they have used all its narrators as proof except 'Amir b. Shaqiq, and I do not know of any criticism of 'Amir b. Shaqiq in any way. And for running the fingers through the beard, there is a sound witness from 'Ammar b. Yasir, Anas b. Malik, and 'A'ishah. Ibn Ma'in said: And it has a sound witness."],[525,"\"And what prevents me when I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ running his fingers through his beard?\" Sufyan said: And Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah narrated to us from Qatadah from Hassan b. Bilal from 'Ammar from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ something similar."],[526,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and run his fingers through his beard from beneath it, and he said, \"This is what my Lord commanded me.\""],[527,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and run his fingers through his beard, and he said, \"This is what my Lord commanded me.\""],[528,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, he would run his fingers through his beard. This is a sound witness for wiping the inner part of the ears."],[529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped the inner and outer parts of his ears. He said: And Ibn Mas'ud used to enjoin that. Za'idah b. Qudamah is trustworthy and reliable; he traced it back to al-Thawri, while others stopped it. Za'idah is trustworthy, and others stop it."],[530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution twice for each part."],[531,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution once each (for each part) and combined rinsing the mouth and nose."],[532,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Dawud b. Qays al-Farra' narrated to us from Zayd b. Aslam from 'Ata' b. Yasar from Ibn 'Abbas that the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution with a single handful (of water) for each limb."],[533,"\"I entered the markets with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he went to relieve himself.\" He said: \"He came back and I handed him water, and he performed ablution. Then he tried to bring his arms out of his collar but could not, so he brought them out from under the cloak, performed ablution, and wiped over his leather socks.\""],[534,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the markets and went to relieve himself, and Bilal was with him. Then they came out, and I asked Bilal, \"What did he do?\" He said, \"He performed ablution, washing his face and hands, wiping his head, and wiping over his leather socks.\""],[535,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ablution, and he took water for his ears other than the water with which he had wiped his head.\""],[536,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped his ears with water other than that with which he wiped his head. This clearly states the meaning of the first, and it is authentic like it."],[537,"The Prophet ﷺ wiped the inside and outside of his ears. They did not use Ibn ʿAqil as evidence, but he is upright in hadith and given precedence in nobility."],[538,"\"We entered upon Ali, me and two other men, one of whom was from our tribe and the other from the tribe of Banu Asad. Ali said to them, 'So they sent them for a need, and he said, \"Indeed, you two are sick, so treat yourselves according to your religion.\"' Then he entered the restroom and came out. He called for water and washed his hands, then he began to recite the Quran. It seemed as if we disapproved, so he said, 'It seems that you two disapproved. The Messenger of Allah used to fulfill his needs, recite the Qur'an, and eat meat without anything preventing him from recitation except impurity (janabah).'\""],[539,"When any of you has intercourse with his wife, then wishes to repeat, let him perform ablution, for it invigorates him for repetition."],[540,"I asked Aisha: How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ deal with janabah? Did he bathe before sleeping or sleep before bathing? She said: He would do all of that. Sometimes he bathed and then slept, and sometimes he performed ablution and then slept. I said: Praise be to Allah who has made the matter flexible. Muslim narrated it in the Sahih from Qutaybah, and he did not mention its supporting narrations with their wordings. Ghudayf b. al-Harith also followed him from Aisha."],[541,"About the Prophet's ﷺ bath from janabah, she said: Sometimes he would bathe before sleeping, and sometimes he would sleep before bathing. Kahmas b. al-Hasan followed him from Burd."],[542,"I said to Aisha: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of janabah, did he bathe at the beginning of it or at the end? She said: Sometimes he would bathe at the beginning, and sometimes at the end. I said: Allah is greatest. Praise be to Allah who has made the matter flexible. May Allah bless our master Muhammad, his family, and all his companions."],[543,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would pray the two rakʿahs before the dawn prayer, and I do not think he renewed his ablution after the bath."],[544,"He would not perform ablution after the bath."],[545,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about ablution after the bath, and he said: What ablution is better than the bath?"],[546,"He would warm himself with her after the bath."],[547,"He had a cloth with which he would dry himself after ablution."],[548,"I saw Ibn Umar make his camel kneel facing the qiblah, then he sat urinating towards it. I said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, was this not forbidden? He said: That was forbidden only in open ground. If there is something between you and the qiblah that screens you, there is no harm."],[549,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited us from turning our backs to the Qibla or facing it with our private parts exposed when we urinate. However, we saw him do this before his death while facing the Qibla."],[550,"The price of a dog is impure, and it is more impure than it."],[551,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding this verse: {In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves} [al-Tawbah 108]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O assembly of the Ansar, Allah has praised you well concerning purification. So what is this purification of yours?” They said: O Messenger of Allah, we perform ablution for prayer and wash from major impurity. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is there anything else besides that?” They said: No, except that when one of us comes out from defecation, he likes to cleanse himself with water. He said: “That is it.”"],[552,"The Prophet ﷺ said to the people of Quba’: “Allah has praised you well concerning purification,” and he said: {In it are men who love to purify themselves} [al-Tawbah 108] until the verse was completed. Then he said to them: “What is this purification?”"],[553,"From my father, from Ibn Ishaq: Muhammad b. Yahya b. Hibban al-Ansari, then al-Mazini of the Mazin of Banu al-Najjar, narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, who said: I said to him: Tell me about the ablution of 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar for every prayer, whether he was in a state of purity or not; from whom is it? He said: Asma' bt. Zayd b. al-Khattab narrated to him that 'Abd Allah b. Hanzalah b. Abi 'Amir al-Ghasil narrated to her."],[554,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Dhat al-Riqa' from Nakhl. A man among the Muslims captured a woman from the polytheists. When the Messenger ﷺ returned, her husband came, as he had been absent. When he was informed of the news, he swore that he would not stop until he shed blood among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So he set out following the trail of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at a place and said: “Which man will guard us this night of ours?” A man from the Muhajirun and a man from the Ansar volunteered, saying: We will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Then be at the mouth of the mountain pass.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions had stopped at the pass from the valley. When the two men went out to the mouth of the pass, the Ansari said to the Muhajir: Which part of the night would you like me to take over for you? He said: Take over the first part for me. So the Muhajir lay down and the Ansari stood praying. He said: The husband of the woman came. When he saw the figure of the man, he knew that he was a watchman of the people. He said: He shot an arrow at him and hit him. He said: He pulled it out and set it aside, and remained standing praying. Then he shot another arrow and hit him. He pulled it out and set it aside, and remained standing praying. Then he came back a third time and hit him. He pulled it out and set it aside, then he bowed, then he roused his companion and said: Sit up, I have been wounded. So he jumped up. When the man saw the two of them, he knew that he had been detected, so he fled. When the Muhajir saw the blood on the Ansari, he said: Glory be to Allah! Why did you not rouse me at the first shot? He said: I was in a surah that I was reciting, and I did not like to interrupt it until I completed it. When the shooting continued, I bowed and alerted you. By Allah, had I not feared neglecting a post that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had ordered me to guard, my breath would have been cut off before I cut it off or completed it.”"],[555,"From the Prophet ﷺ something similar. Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad b. 'Ali al-Warraq, whose nickname is Hamdan, narrated to us: Abu Yahya 'Abd al-Samad b. Hassan al-Marwadhi narrated to us: Sufyan b. Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah b. 'Ammar. And Abu Bakr b. Ishaq al-Faqih informed us, and the wording is his: 'Ali b. 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us: Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Ammar narrated to us: Qasim b. Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah b. 'Ammar, from Yahya b. Abi Kathir, from 'Iyad, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the two who are defecating from conversing with each other, for Allah abhors that.”"],[556,"He forbade the two who are defecating from conversing with each other, and he said: “For Allah abhors that.”"],[557,"“Two men should not go out to relieve themselves, exposing their private parts, for Allah abhors that.”"],[558,"\"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'When any one of you performs wudu, let him perform an odd number of units (of prayer) as Allah is odd and He loves that which is odd. Have you not seen that the heavens are seven and the earths are seven and tawaf is seven?' And he mentioned other things.\""],[559,"I entered upon 'A'ishah and heard her saying: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from defecation, he said: “Your forgiveness.”"],[560,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up from defecation, he said: “Your forgiveness.”"],[561,"“A woman among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ performed a major ritual ablution, and the Prophet ﷺ performed ablution or washed from her leftover water.” Shu'bah concurred with him from Simak."],[562,"The Prophet ﷺ wanted to perform ablution from a vessel. One of his wives said: O Messenger of Allah, I have already performed ablution from this. The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution and said: “Water is not made impure by anything.” Al-Bukhari used hadiths of 'Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim used hadiths of Simak b. Harb as evidence."],[563,"It was said to ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb: Relate to us about the affair of the hour of hardship. ʿUmar said: We set out to Tabūk in intense heat and stopped at a place where thirst afflicted us until we thought our necks would snap, until a man would slaughter his camel, squeeze its undigested stomach contents, drink it, and place what remained on his liver. Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has accustomed you to good in supplication, so supplicate to Him. He said, “Would you like that?” He said: Yes. He raised his hands and did not lower them until the sky spoke, then shaded us, then poured down, and they filled what they had with them. Then we went to look and did not find it; it had passed beyond the army."],[564,"Abū Qatādah entered upon her, and she poured water for his ablution. A cat came to drink from it, and Abū Qatādah tilted the vessel for it until it drank. Kabshah said: He saw me looking at him and said: Are you surprised, O daughter of my brother? I said: Yes. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is not impure; it is one of those that go around among you, male and female.”"],[565,"From ʿĀʾishah: “And the opposite of this is authentic according to the condition of the two shaykhs, yet they did not include it either.” Ṣaḥīḥ."],[566,"“The purification of the vessel of one of you when a dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first with earth, and the cat is the same.”"],[567,"“The purification of the vessel when a dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first with earth, and the cat once or twice.”"],[568,"“For the cat, once or twice.”"],[569,"“The purification of the vessel of one of you when a dog laps in it is to wash it seven times, the first of them with earth.”"],[570,"About the cat that laps in the vessel, he said, “It is washed once or twice.”"],[571,"The Prophet ﷺ wanted to perform ablution from a waterskin and it was said to him that it was from a dead animal. He said, “Its tanning removes its filth, or its impurity, or its defilement.”"],[572,"“A mudd suffices for ablution and a ṣāʿ for major ritual impurity.” A man said to him: That is not enough for us, O Jābir. He said, “It sufficed one better than you and with more hair.”"],[573,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought two-thirds of a mudd, performed ablution, and began rubbing his forearms."],[574,"\"We used to perform ablution, both men and women, and wash our hands in a single vessel during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[575,"“Indeed, there is a devil for ablution called al-Walahān, so beware of him and avoid the whispering about water.”"],[576,"Indeed there will be in this nation a people who transgress in purification and supplication."],[577,"Woe to the heels and the soles of the feet from the Fire."],[578,"He forbade a man from entering the water except with a waist-wrapper."],[579,"Bathing is required from four things: from janabah (major ritual impurity), on the day of Jumu'ah, from washing the dead, and from cupping."],[580,"Fatimah entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was crying. He said, \"O my dear daughter, what makes you cry?\" She said, \"O my father, why should I not cry when these chiefs of Quraysh are in the Hijr, swearing by al-Lat, al-'Uzza, and Manat, the third, the other? If they saw you, they would rise against you and kill you, and there is not a man among them but has known his share of your blood.\" He said, \"O my dear daughter, bring me water for ablution.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution, then went out to the mosque. When they saw him, they said, \"There he is,\" and they lowered their heads, and their chins fell between their hands, and they did not raise their eyes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of dust and threw it at them, saying, \"May the faces be ugly.\" No man among them was hit by a pebble from his pebbles except that he was killed on the day of Badr as a disbeliever."],[581,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of his mission while he was in Makkah, and he was then in hiding. I said, \"What are you?\" He said, \"I am a prophet.\" I said, \"And what is a prophet?\" He said, \"A messenger of Allah.\" I said, \"Did Allah send you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"With what did He send you?\" He said, \"To worship Allah, to break the idols and the religions, and to maintain ties of kinship.\" I said, \"Excellent is what He sent you with.\" I said, \"Then who follows you in this?\" He said, \"A slave and a free man,\" meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. 'Amr used to say: \"I saw myself as a quarter or the fourth of Islam.\" He said: \"So I accepted Islam. I said, 'Shall I follow you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'No, but join your people, and when you are informed that I have come forth, then follow me.'\" He said: \"So I joined my people and began to await his news and his coming forth, until a caravan from Yathrib came. I met them and asked them about the news. They said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come forth from Makkah to Madinah.' I said, 'And has he reached it?' They said, 'Yes.'\" He said: \"So I set out until I came to him. I said, 'Do you recognize me, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, you are the man who came to me in Makkah.' So I began to seek a private moment with him. When he was alone, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me of what Allah has taught you, and be concise.' He said, 'Ask about whatever you wish.' I said, 'Which part of the night is most heard?' He said, 'The last part of the night, so pray as much as you wish, for the prayer is witnessed and written until you pray the morning prayer. Then stop until the sun rises and is raised a spear's length or two spear's lengths, for it rises between the two horns of a devil, and the disbelievers pray to it. Then pray as much as you wish, for the prayer is witnessed and written until the spear's shadow equals its length. Then stop, for Hell is stoked and its gates are opened. Then when the sun declines, pray as much as you wish, for the prayer is witnessed and written, until you pray the 'Asr prayer. Then stop until the sun sets, for it sets between the two horns of a devil, and the disbelievers pray to it. And when you perform ablution, wash your hands, for when you wash your hands, your sins depart from your forearms. Then when you wipe your head, your sins depart from the ends of your hair. Then when you wash your feet, your sins depart from your feet. Then if you remain in your sitting, you will have a portion of your ablution, and if you stand and remember your Lord, praise Him, and pray two rak'ahs with your heart attentive to them, you will be free of your sins as on the day your mother gave birth to you.'\" He said: \"I said, 'O 'Amr, know what you are saying, for you are saying something great.' He said, 'By Allah, my age has advanced and my term has drawn near, and I have no need to lie. If I had heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ only once or twice, I would not have narrated it, but I have heard it more than that.' Thus Abu Sallam narrated to me from him, from Abu Umamah, except that I may make a mistake or add something, so I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him. Muslim has transmitted some of these words from the hadith of al-Nadr b. Muhammad al-Jurashi, from 'Ikrimah b. 'Ammar, from Shaddad b. 'Abdullah, from Abu Umamah. He said: 'Amr b. 'Abasah said: And this hadith of al-'Abbas b. Salim is more complete and perfect than the hadith of 'Ikrimah b. 'Ammar."],[582,"A man became junub (in a state of major ritual impurity) in winter, so he asked and was ordered to perform ghusl. He performed ghusl and died. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"What is wrong with them? They killed him; may Allah kill them,\" three times. \"Allah has made the earth, or tayammum, a purifier.\""],[583,"Regarding His saying, the Exalted: {And if you are ill or on a journey} [al-Nisa' 43], he said: \"If a man has a wound in the path of Allah, or sores, or smallpox, and becomes junub, and he fears that if he performs ghusl he will die, then he should perform tayammum.\""],[584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the urine of an infant: \"The urine of a boy is sprinkled, and the urine of a girl is washed.\""],[585,"Al-Husayn urinated in the lap of the Prophet ﷺ. I said, \"Give me your garment so that I may wash it.\" He said, \"Only the urine of a female is washed, and the urine of a male is sprinkled.\" And the second witness is sahih."],[586,"I was the servant of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Hasan or al-Husayn was brought, and he urinated on his chest. They wanted to wash it, but he said, \"Sprinkle it with a sprinkling, for the urine of a girl is washed, and the urine of a boy is sprinkled.\" The two shaykhs have transmitted hadiths of 'A'ishah and Umm Qays bt. Mihsan concerning the urine of a boy, that the Prophet ﷺ ordered water to be poured over the urine of the boy. As for the mention of the urine of a girl, they did not transmit it. Sahih."],[587,"If one of you steps with his sandals on something filthy, then the dust is a purifier for it."],[588,"When one of you steps with his sandals in filth, then dust is a purifier for them."],[589,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was urinating and greeted him, but he did not return the greeting until he had performed ablution. Then he apologized to him and said: I disliked mentioning Allah except in a state of purity, or he said: upon purification."],[590,"She said: The Prophet ﷺ had a wooden bowl under his bed in which he would urinate at night."],[591,"Beware of the three cursed places: relieving oneself in water sources, in the middle of the road, and in the shade used for defecation."],[592,"None of you should urinate in his bathing place and then bathe in it or perform ablution in it, for most whispering (of the devil) comes from that."],[593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade any of us from combing the hair every day or urinating in one's bathing place."],[594,"He went out for Hajj or Umrah, and the people were with him while he led them in prayer. One day, when the prayer was called for the morning prayer, he said: Let one of you go forward, and he went to relieve himself. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When one of you wants to go to relieve himself and the prayer is about to start, let him begin with relieving himself."],[595,"It is not lawful for a man who believes in Allah and the Last Day to pray while he is restraining the need to urinate or defecate until he relieves himself."],[596,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Prayer should not be offered in the presence of food, nor while one is resisting the two impure things (urine and stool)."],[597,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us, so we brought out water for him in a vessel of brass, and he performed ablution. This is a sound hadith according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not record it. It has a supporting narration from Aisha according to their conditions."],[598,"I, Aisha, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bathe together from a vessel made of brass."],[599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military expedition, and they were struck by cold. When they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he ordered them to wipe over their turbans and leather socks."],[600,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform ablution (wudu') while wearing a Qatari turban (imamah), then he would put his hand under the turban and wipe the front part of his head without uncovering the turban. Although this hadith may not meet the criteria set by scholars, it contains an unusual phrase stating that he wiped a part of his head without wiping his turban. If this is correct, it indicates that he wiped a part of his head."],[601,"That Jarir “urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over the leather socks,” and said: What prevents me from wiping when I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe? They said: That was only before the revelation of al-Ma’idah. He said: I did not become Muslim except after the revelation of al-Ma’idah."],[602,"About the ablution of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “He would go out to relieve himself, and I would bring him water, and he would perform ablution and wipe over his turban and his leather socks.”"],[603,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “wiped over the leather socks.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, you forgot. He said: “Rather, you forgot; this is what my Lord ﷻ commanded me.” “The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting the chains of the hadith of al-Mughirah b. Shu’bah regarding wiping, but they did not transmit his statement ﷺ” “this is what my Lord commanded me” “and its chain is authentic.” Sahih."],[604,"From Ubayy b. ‘Umarah—who had prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ facing both qiblahs—that he said: O Messenger of Allah, should I wipe over the leather socks? He said: “Yes.” He said: One day? He said: “And two days.” He said: And three? He said: “Yes, as long as you wish.” “Ubayy b. ‘Umarah is a well-known Companion, and this is an Egyptian chain in which not one of them has been accused of any defect. Malik b. Anas held this view, but they did not transmit it.”"],[605,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated, he performed ablution and sprinkled water.”"],[606,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ “urinate, then sprinkle his private part.”"],[607,"“We would not perform ablution because of stepping on something, nor would we tuck up our hair or garment.”"],[608,"“The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image, or a dog, or a person in a state of major ritual impurity.”"],[609,"Regarding the one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating, he said: “He should give charity of a dinar or half a dinar.”"],[610,"“If he has intercourse with her during the bleeding, then a dinar; and if he has intercourse with her after the bleeding stops, then half a dinar.”"],[611,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “would command us at the onset of our menstruation to wear a waist-wrapper, then he would be intimate with us. And which of you can control his desire as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to control his desire?”"],[612,"I was suffering from a severe, prolonged, and heavy istihadah, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask his ruling and inform him. I found him in the house of my sister Zaynab bt. Jahsh. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman suffering from istihadah with a severe, prolonged, and heavy flow. What do you think about it, for it has prevented me from praying and fasting? He said: “I prescribe for you cotton, for it absorbs the blood.” She said: It is more than that; it gushes profusely. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I will command you two things; whichever you do will suffice you for the other, and if you are able to do both, you know best.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “This is only a kick from the kicks of Satan. Consider your menstruation to be six or seven days according to Allah’s knowledge ﷻ, then bathe until you see that you have become pure and cleansed. Then pray for twenty-three or twenty-four nights and their days, and fast, for that will suffice you. And do likewise every month, as women menstruate and become pure according to their menstrual and purity periods. And if you are able to delay the Zuhr prayer and hasten the ‘Asr prayer, then bathe and combine the two prayers, Zuhr and ‘Asr; and delay the Maghrib prayer and hasten the ‘Isha’ prayer, then bathe and combine the two prayers, then do so and fast if you are able to do that.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And this is the more preferable of the two matters to me.” “The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting the hadith of istihadah from the hadith of al-Zuhri and Hisham b. ‘Urwah from A’ishah that Fatimah bt. Abi Hujaysh asked the Prophet ﷺ, and it does not contain these words found in the hadith of Hamnah bt. Jahsh. And it is the transmission of ‘Abdullah b. Muhammad b. ‘Aqil b. Abi Talib, who is among the nobles of Quraysh and among the most prolific transmitters, except that they did not use him as proof.” Its supporting witnesses include the hadith of al-Sha’bi from Qamir, the wife of Masruq, from A’ishah, and the hadith of Abu ‘Aqil Yahya b. al-Mutawakkil from Buhayyah from A’ishah, and mentioning them here would be lengthy. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is not menstruation, but it is a vein, so perform the ritual bath.\""],[614,"Umm Habibah experienced prolonged non-menstrual bleeding for seven years while she was married to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. The Prophet ﷺ instructed her, saying: \"When the menstrual period arrives, leave the prayer; and when it departs, bathe and pray.\" [The hadith of 'Amr b. al-Harith and al-Awza'i is sound according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. Muslim only included the hadith of Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah and Ibrahim b. Sa'd from al-Zuhri.] Muhammad b. 'Amr b. 'Alqamah corroborated al-Awza'i in his narration from al-Zuhri with these exact words: \"It is sound according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it\" according to their conditions."],[615,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"When it is the blood of menstruation, it is dark blood that is recognizable. When that occurs, refrain from prayer; and when it is the other, perform ablution and pray, for it is only a vein.\" According to the condition of Muslim."],[616,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh has had prolonged non-menstrual bleeding for such and such a time and has not prayed.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Glory be to Allah! This is from Satan. Let her sit in a large tub, and when she sees yellowness above the water, let her bathe once for Zuhr and 'Asr, bathe once for Maghrib and 'Isha', bathe for Fajr, and perform ablution in between those times.\""],[617,"\"We used not to consider the dark discharge and the yellow discharge as anything.\""],[618,"\"We used not to consider the dark discharge and the yellow discharge after purification as anything.\""],[619,"\"They do not make up [the prayers]. A woman among the wives of the Prophet ﷺ would remain in her post-natal period for forty nights, and the Prophet ﷺ did not command her to make up the prayers of the post-natal period.\""],[621,"My maternal aunt Fatimah bt. Abi Hubaysh came to 'A'ishah and said: \"I fear that I will fall into the Fire, for I abandon the prayer for a year or two and do not pray.\" She said: \"Wait until the Prophet ﷺ comes.\" He came, and 'A'ishah said: \"This is Fatimah; she says such and such.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Tell her to leave the prayer each month during the days of her menstrual period, then to bathe once each day, then to purify herself at the time of every prayer, to clean herself, and to use a cloth, for it is only a disease that has appeared, or a kick from Satan, or a vein that has burst.\""],[622,"\"A period of forty days has been appointed for women in their post-natal bleeding.\""],[623,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Women wait for forty nights. If they see purity before that, then they are pure. But if they exceed the forty nights, then they are in the state of istihada (abnormal bleeding). They should wash and pray, and if bleeding overwhelms them, they should perform ablution for each prayer.\" \"Amr bin Al-Husayn and Muhammad bin Uthatha are not among the two Sheikhs (referring to Abu Bakr and Umar), and I only mentioned this Hadith as a witness marveling.\""],[624,"\"When seven days have passed for a woman in post-natal bleeding and then she sees purification, let her bathe and pray.\""],[625,"Some livestock were gathered with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"O Abu Dharr, go out to pasture with them.\" So I went out to al-Rabadhah, and I would be afflicted with major ritual impurity, and I would remain for five or six days. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Dharr said: I remained silent. He said: \"May your mother lose you, Abu Dharr! Woe to your mother!\" Then he called for a servant girl, and she brought a wooden bowl of water. She screened me with a cloth, and I screened myself with the mount. I bathed, and it was as if I had cast off a mountain from myself. He said: \"Clean earth is the ablution of the Muslim, even up to ten years. But when you find water, let it touch your skin, for that is better.\""],[626,"'Amr b. al-'As was in command of a military detachment, and they were struck by severe cold the like of which he had never seen. He went out for the dawn prayer and said: \"By Allah, I had a wet dream last night, but by Allah, I have never seen cold like this. Has anything like it ever come upon your faces?\" They said: \"No.\" So he washed his private parts, performed ablution as for prayer, and then led them in prayer. When he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: \"How did you find 'Amr and his companions as leaders for you?\" They praised him well and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, he led us in prayer while he was in a state of major ritual impurity.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for 'Amr and asked him, and he informed him of that and of the cold he had encountered. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah said: 'And do not kill yourselves' [Quran 4:29]. If I had bathed, I would have died.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed at 'Amr."],[627,"I had a wet dream on a cold night during the campaign of Dhat al-Salasil. I feared that if I performed the full bath, I would perish, so I performed tayammum and then led my companions in the dawn prayer. They mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “O ‘Amr, did you lead your companions in prayer while you were in a state of major ritual impurity?” I told him what had prevented me from bathing, and I said, “I heard that Allah says: ‘And do not kill yourselves, for Allah is ever Merciful to you’ [Qur’an 4:29].” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and did not say anything.This hadith of Jarir b. Hazim does not invalidate the hadith of ‘Amr b. al-Harith, which connected it by mentioning Abu Qays, for the people of Egypt know their hadith better than the people of Basra."],[628,"A man got injured during the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ . Then he experienced a wet dream, so he took a bath and died. This news reached the Prophet ﷺ , and he said, \"They killed him, may Allah kill them. Wasn't the treatment for a sick eye to ask for a cure?\" It has reached us that the Prophet ﷺ was asked about this incident, and he said, \"If he had washed his body and left his head where the injury was, it would have been sufficient.\" Al-Hakam ibn Ziyad narrated this, and he is considered reliable among the companions of Al-Awza'i. However, he did not mention hearing it from Ata."],[629,"A man was injured during the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ and it caused him to have a state of impurity (janabah). He sought advice and was instructed to perform a ritual washing (ghusl), which he did. However, he died afterwards. When the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was informed about this, he said, \"They killed him, may Allah kill them. Wasn't the washing of the affected area sufficient for him?\" Ata, a companion of the Prophet, reported that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ was asked about this incident later on and he replied, \"If he had washed his body and left the area affected by the injury, it would have been sufficient for him.\""],[630,"Two men went out on a journey. The time for prayer came and they had no water, so they performed tayammum with clean earth and prayed. Then they found water while the time had not yet expired. One of them repeated the prayer and the ablution, but the other did not. They then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said to the one who did not repeat: “You have followed the Sunnah and your prayer was sufficient for you.” To the one who performed ablution and repeated, he said: “You will have the reward twice.”"],[631,"Abu Bakr b. Ishaq narrated to us, Ahmad b. Ibrahim b. Milhan informed us, Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us from ‘Umayrah b. Abi Najiyah, from Bakr b. Sawadah, from ‘Ata’ b. Yasar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. And Allah knows best. It is upon the conditions of the two of them, and Ibn Nafi‘ is trustworthy; he alone connected it."],[632,"Tayammum consists of two strikes: one strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows."],[633,"We performed tayammum with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We struck our hands on clean earth, then shook off our hands and wiped our faces with them. Then we struck clean earth another time, shook off our hands, and wiped with our hands from the elbow to the palm, over the hair growth, both the outer and inner sides."],[634,"He said regarding tayammum: “Two strikes: one strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows.”"],[635,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “I have become ritually impure, and I rolled in the dust.” He said, “Strike like this,” and he struck the ground with his hands and wiped his face. Then he struck with his hands and wiped with them up to the elbows. Sahih."],[636,"Tayammum consists of two strikes: one strike for the face and one strike for the hands up to the elbows."],[637,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform tayammum at a place called Mirbad al-Na‘am, while he could see the houses of Madinah."],[638,"Ibn Umar performed Tayammum on a mound or two mounds of sand near Al-Madinah, then he prayed Asr, and he arrived while the sun was still high, and he did not repeat the prayer."],[639,"I left al-Sham for Madinah on Friday, and I entered Madinah on Friday. I went in to see ‘Umar b. al-Khattab, and he said to me, “When did you put your leather socks on your feet?” I said, “On Friday.” He said, “Did you take them off?” I said, “No.” He said, “You have followed the Sunnah.”"],[640,"He came as a delegate to ‘Umar b. al-Khattab one year. ‘Uqbah said: I was wearing leather socks of those thick ones. ‘Umar said to me, “When did you last put them on?” I said, “I put them on on Friday, and this is Friday.” He said to me, “You have followed the Sunnah.”"],[641,"When one of you performs ablution and puts on his leather socks, let him pray in them and wipe over them, and then let him not take them off—if he wishes—except for major ritual impurity."],[642,"“What is the matter with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, standing up since the Criterion was revealed to him?”"],[643,"The Prophet ﷺ “urinated standing because of a wound on his inner thigh.”"],[644,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ rinse his mouth and sniff water into his nostrils from one palm, doing that three times.”"],[645,"“When you perform ablution, pass your fingers between the toes.”"],[646,"“When you perform ablution, pass your fingers between the fingers of your hands and your toes.”"],[647,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to the house of a group of the Ansar, while beyond them were houses that he did not come to. That weighed heavily on them, so they said, “O Messenger of Allah, you come to the house of so-and-so but you do not come to our house.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “There is a dog in your house.” They said, “There is a cat in their house.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “The cat is a wild animal.”"],[648,"Abu Hatim said: He is not strong."],[649,"We were with Salman al-Farisi on a journey, and he relieved himself. We said to him, “Perform ablution so that we may ask you about a verse of the Quran.” He said, “Ask me, for I do not touch it.” Then he recited to us what we wanted, and there was no water between us and him."],[650,"From Salman, and he mentioned it in a similar manner."],[651,"“Most of the punishment of the grave is from urine.”"],[652,"“The general punishment of the grave is from urine.”"],[653,"“When one of you breaks wind during his prayer, let him hold his nose and then leave.”"],[654,"“When one of you breaks wind during his prayer, let him take hold of his nose and leave, then perform ablution.”"],[655,"I set out with ‘Amr b. al-‘Āṣ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us holding a leather shield or something resembling a shield. He screened himself with it and urinated while sitting. I said to my companion, “Do you not see how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinates as a woman does?” He said: Then he came to us and said, “Do you not know what befell the companion of the Children of Israel? When any of them was soiled by urine, he would cut it off with scissors. He forbade them that, so he was punished in his grave.” [The conditions of the two shaykhs are met.]"],[656,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ urinated while shielding himself with a small leather bucket. They said, “You urinate as a woman does?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed the Children of Israel, when urine touched any of them, he would cut it off with scissors. He forbade them that, so he is being punished in his grave.”"],[657,"She said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never urinated standing since the Furqān was sent down to him.” [The conditions of the two shaykhs are met.]"],[658,"I heard ‘Ā’ishah swearing by Allah that no one ever saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “urinate standing since the Furqān was sent down to him.”"],[659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while I was urinating standing, and he said, “O ‘Umar, do not urinate standing.” He said: So I never urinated standing after that. And it is related from Abū Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the prohibition of it."],[660,"“Let none of you urinate in his bathing place, for most whispering [of Satan] comes from that.”"],[661,"“He forbade, or he was restrained from, urinating in the washing place.”"],[662,"“Beware of the two who bring curses.” They said, “And what are the two who bring curses, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “The one who relieves himself in the roadway of the Muslims and in their shade.”"],[663,"A man said to Abū Hurayrah, “You have given us legal rulings about everything, until you are near to giving us rulings about excrement.” He said: Abū Hurayrah then said, “Everything I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever releases his ill-natured anger on a frequented road of the Muslims, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people.’” And Muḥammad b. ‘Amr al-Anṣārī is among those whose ḥadīth is compiled among the Baṣrans, and he is very rare in ḥadīth."],[664,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Let none of you urinate into a hole.” [The conditions of the two shaykhs are met.]"],[665,"I heard Abū Zakariyyā al-‘Anbarī, Yaḥyā b. Muḥammad, say: I heard Muḥammad b. Isḥāq b. Khuzaymah say: He forbade urinating into holes because of the report of ‘Abd Allāh b. Sarjis that the Prophet ﷺ said, “Let none of you urinate into a hole.” And Qatādah said, “They are dwelling places of the jinn.” “But I will not definitively assert that they are the dwelling places of the jinn, because this is from the statement of Qatādah.”"],[666,"Indeed these places of relieving oneself are attended. So when one of you enters the privy, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male filth, the impure, the accursed devil."],[667,"Indeed these places of relieving oneself are attended. So when one of you enters them, let him say: I seek refuge in You from the male and female devils."],[668,"He used to, when he entered the privy, put down his ring."],[669,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a ring whose inscription was 'Muhammad the Messenger of Allah,' and he used to, when he entered the privy, put it down."],[670,"When this verse was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Uwaym b. Sa'idah and said: 'What is this purification for which Allah has praised you?' They said: 'O Prophet of Allah, no man or woman among us comes out from the privy except that he washes his rear—or he said his seat.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'So it is in this.'"],[671,"They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, who are those about whom [it is said], \"In it are men who love to purify themselves, and Allah loves those who purify themselves\" [al-Tawbah 108]?' He said: 'They used to clean themselves with water, and they used not to sleep the whole night.' This is the last that has reached us from the Book of Purification according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, what they have not included."],[672,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which deed is most excellent?' He said: 'Prayer at its earliest time.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'Jihad in the path of Allah.' I said: 'Then which?' He said: 'Kindness to parents.'"],[673,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which deed is most excellent?' He said: 'Prayer at its earliest time.'"],[674,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Which deeds are most excellent?' He said: 'Prayer at its earliest time.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Jihad in the path of Allah.' I said: 'Then what?' He said: 'Kindness to parents. And if I had asked for more, he would have increased me.'"],[675,"From a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which deeds are most excellent?' He said: 'Prayer at its earliest time.' The man is Abdullah b. Mas'ud due to the agreement of the narrators in it upon Abu Amr al-Shaybani, and among them."],[676,"The best of deeds is prayer at its earliest time."],[677,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: 'Which deed is most excellent?' He said: 'Prayer at its earliest time.'"],[678,"from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, something similar. I heard Abu al-Abbas Muhammad b. Yaqub say, I heard al-Abbas b. Muhammad al-Duri say, I heard Yahya b. Main say, \"Abd Allah b. Umar narrated from al-Qasim b. Ghannam, but his brother Ubayd Allah b. Umar did not narrate from him.\""],[679,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not ever pray a prayer at its final time until Allah took him."],[680,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not ever pray a prayer at its final time twice until Allah took him. And it has another supporting witness from the hadith of al-Waqidi, but it is not according to the condition of this book."],[681,"I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delay a prayer to the final time until Allah took him."],[682,"Abu Ayyub came to us as a warrior, and Uqbah b. Amir was then governor of Egypt. He delayed the Maghrib prayer. Abu Ayyub stood up to us and said, \"What is this prayer, O Uqbah?\" He replied, \"We were busy.\" He said, \"By Allah, I do not grieve except that people will think you saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do this. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'My community will remain upon good—or upon the natural disposition—as long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars appear thickly.'\""],[683,"My community will remain upon the natural disposition as long as they do not delay Maghrib until the stars appear thickly."],[684,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There are two [types] of Fajr (dawn) [times]: a Fajr in which food is forbidden while prayer becomes permissible, and a Fajr in which prayer is forbidden while food becomes permissible."],[685,"The dawn is of two kinds. As for the dawn that is like the tail of the wolf, prayer is not permitted in it, nor is food forbidden. As for the one that extends lengthwise across the horizon, it permits prayer and forbids food."],[686,"\"Shall I not guide you to that by which Allah expiates sins and increases good deeds?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Performing ablution thoroughly in difficult circumstances, and waiting for the next prayer after the previous one. There is no man among you who leaves his house, prays with the imam, then sits waiting for the next prayer except that the angels say, 'O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him.'\""],[687,"We were sitting with Ali in the Great Mosque, and Kufa at that time had reed huts. The muezzin came to him and said, \"Prayer, O Commander of the Faithful, for Asr.\" He said, \"Sit.\" He sat. Then he came back and said the same. Ali said, \"This dog teaches us the Sunnah.\" Ali stood and led us in Asr. Then we left and returned to the place where we had been sitting. We knelt down and watched the sun declining toward setting."],[688,"\"We used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would slaughter a camel and divide it into ten portions, then cook it and eat well-cooked meat before the sun set.\" Bukhari and Muslim agreed on the hadith of al-Awzai from Abu al-Najashi from Rafi b. Khadij, who said, \"We used to pray Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then we would leave and one of us could see the places where his arrows fell.\" It has two authentic supporting witnesses for praying early, which they did not include. The first of them is:"],[689,"He used to pray Asr while the sun was white and high, then a man would travel from there to Dhu al-Hulayfah, which is six miles, before sunset."],[690,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned something similar."],[691,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked about the times of prayer, so he advanced and then delayed, and said, 'Between them is a time.'"],[692,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told them: 'Jibril came to him and prayed with him the prayer at two times, except Maghrib.' He said, 'He came to me and prayed with me at the moment the sun set. Then he came to me the next day and prayed with me at the moment the sun set; he did not change it.'"],[693,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'This is Jibril teaching you your religion.' Then he mentioned the times of prayer. Then he mentioned that he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set. Then when he came to him the next day, he prayed Maghrib when the sun had set, at one time. On the condition of Muslim."],[694,"'I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, the last Isha prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it at the setting of the moon for the third night.' Raqabah b. Masqalah concurred with Abu Bishr in this manner. Raqabah and Hushaym agreed on the narration of this hadith from Abu Bishr, from Habib b. Salim, and it is a sound chain. Shu'bah and Abu Awanah differed from them and said: from Abu Bishr, from Bishr b. Thabit, from Habib b. Salim, and its chain is sound."],[695,"'I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of the last Isha prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it at the setting of the moon for the third or fourth night.' Shu'bah was uncertain."],[696,"'I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer, the last Isha prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it at the setting of the moon for the third night.'"],[697,"'I used to pray Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I would take a handful of pebbles so they would cool in my palm. I would place them for my forehead to prostrate on them due to the intense heat.'"],[698,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Shall I inform you of the prayer of the hypocrite? He delays Asr until the sun is like the stomach of a cow, then he prays it.' Muslim extracted the hadith of al-Ala b. Abd al-Rahman from Anas from the Prophet ﷺ: 'That is the prayer of the hypocrite: one of them sits until the sun turns yellow...' the hadith."],[699,"'The two men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whose houses were farthest were Abu Lubabah b. Abd al-Mundhir and his family in Quba, and Abu Abs b. Jabr, whose dwelling was among the Banu Harithah. They used to pray Asr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then they would come to their people and they had not yet prayed, because of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastening it.'"],[701,"That Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ teaching him the prayer, and he narrated the text like the hadith of Wahb b. Kaysan exactly. 'As for the second witness'—authentic and well-known."],[702,"The Prophet ﷺ said, “Gabriel led me in prayer in Makkah twice.” Then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner. “This 'Abd al-Karim is, without a doubt, Ibn Abi al-Mukhariq. I only cited it as a corroborating witness.” 'Abd al-Karim is weak."],[703,"Abu Ahmad Bakr b. Muhammad al-Sayrafi narrated to us; Abu Isma'il Muhammad b. Isma'il al-Sulami narrated to us; Ayyub b. Sulayman b. Bilal narrated to us; Abu Bakr b. Abi Uways narrated to me; from Sulayman b. Bilal; from 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith and Muhammad b. 'Amr; from Hakim b. Hakim; from Nafi' b. Jubayr; from Ibn 'Abbas: “Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed the prayers with him at two times, except Maghrib.”"],[704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Command your children to pray at seven years old, and strike them for it at ten years old, and separate them in their beds.” I heard Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub say: I heard al-'Abbas b. Muhammad al-Duri say: I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: “'Amr b. Shu'ayb is trustworthy.”"],[705,"The words of adhan were pronounced from the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice in pairs (i.e. four times) each, and the words of iqamah were pronounced once in pairs (twice each), except that the phrase \"The time for prayer has come\" would be pronounced twice. When we heard iqamah, we would perform ablution, and go out for prayer. Shu'bah said: I did not hear AbuJa'far narrating any other tradition except this one. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 510)"],[706,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal to say the phrases of the Adhan twice and the phrases of the Iqamah once.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 627)"],[707,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Bilal to give the call to prayer and perform the qiyam (night prayer). The two shaykhs did not mention this context, but it is correct according to their condition."],[708,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Two supplications are not rejected, or rarely rejected: the supplication at the call to prayer and at the time of battle when they are locked in combat.”"],[709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Supplication is answered between the call to prayer and the iqamah.”"],[710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to say at the call to Maghrib prayer: “O Allah, this is the approach of Your night and the retreat of Your day, and the voices of Your callers; so forgive me.”"],[711,"Messenger of Allah, appoint me the leader of the tribe in prayer. He said: You are their leader, but you should follow on who is the weakest of them: and appoint a mu'adhdhin who does not charge for the calling of adhan. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 531)"],[712,"“The duration of the Prophet's prayer ﷺ was three steps, and in winter five steps to seven steps.”"],[713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, and among what he taught me was: “Guard the five prayers.” I said, “These are times in which I have occupations, so command me with a comprehensive matter which, if I do it, will suffice me.” He said, “Guard the two 'asrs.” It was not from our dialect, so I said, “What are the two 'asrs?” He said, “A prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.”"],[714,"\"I heard Sa'd and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'There were two brothers during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and one of them was better than the other. The one who was better passed away, and the other brother lived for forty more days before he also passed away. So they mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the virtue of the first over the second. He said, 'Was the second one not praying?' They replied, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, he was praying and there was no problem with his prayer.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What do you think the value of his prayers reached? The example of prayer is like a river flowing at the gate of a man's house, and he immerses himself in it five times a day. So what do you think remains of his dirt?' You do not know how far his prayers reached.\""],[715,"He heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri and Abu Hurayrah reporting from the Prophet ﷺ that he sat on the pulpit and said, “By the One in Whose hand is my soul,” three times, then fell silent. Every man among us hung his head, weeping in sorrow at the oath of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said, “There is no servant who performs the five prayers, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the seven major sins, except that the gates of Paradise will be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection, so much so that they will clatter.” Then he recited: {If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will expiate your evil deeds} [Quran 4:31]."],[716,"A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, how many prayers has Allah made obligatory upon His servants?” He said, “Five prayers.” He said, “Is there anything before or after them?” He said, “Allah has made five prayers obligatory upon His servants.” The man swore by Allah that he would not add to them nor subtract from them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If he is truthful, he will enter Paradise.”"],[717,"“When your children reach seven years old, separate their beds; and when they reach ten years old, strike them for prayer.”"],[718,"“O Messenger of Allah, make me the imam of my people.” He said, “You are their imam, so follow the weakest of them, and appoint a mu'adhdhin who does not take payment for his call to prayer.”"],[719,"“Bilal used to give the adhan and then wait, and when he saw that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had come out, he would give the iqamah for the prayer.”"],[720,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would be in the mosque when the prayer was called. If he saw that the people were few, he would sit and then pray; and if he saw them as a congregation, he would pray.”"],[721,"\"I saw Bilal calling the Adhan, and turning, and his (face) was following here and there, and his (index) fingers were in his ears, and Messenger of Allah was in a small red tent\" - \"I think,\" he (one of the narrators) said, \"it was made from a hide\" - so Bilal went out in front of him with an Anazah which he planted (in the ground) at Batha. Messenger of Allah prayed facing it, and a dog and a donkey passed in front of him; he was wearing a red Hullah, and it is as if I am now looking at the radiance of his shins.\" Sufyan said: \"We think that it was a Hibrah.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 197)"],[722,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ alight at al-Abtah—then he mentioned the hadith in similar fashion. “The two Shaykhs have agreed upon transmitting the hadith of Malik b. Mighwal and Umar b. Abi Za’idah from Awn b. Abi Juhayfah from his father concerning the mention of his ﷺ alighting at al-Abtah, except that they did not mention in it inserting the finger into the ears and turning around during the adhan. It is authentic according to the criterion of both of them, and these are two established sunnahs.”"],[723,"Abdullah b. al-Mubarak, when he saw a mu’adhdhin not inserting his two fingers into his ears, would shout at him: “Anfasta bi-kawsh? Anfasta bi-kawsh?”"],[724,"Whoever says upon hearing the mu’adhdhin—and I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger—: “I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Muhammad as Prophet, and with Islam as religion,” his sins will be forgiven."],[725,"“When one of you hears the call to prayer while the vessel is in his hand, he should not put it down until he has fulfilled his need from it.”"],[726,"He used to say: “Come with us to the martyr woman and let us visit her.” And he commanded that the adhan and iqamah be called for her, and that she lead the people of her house in the obligatory prayers."],[727,"She used to give the adhan and iqamah, lead the women in prayer, and stand in the middle of their row."],[728,"\"Messenger of Allah said to Bilal: \"O Bilal! When you call the Adhan then do so deliberately and slowly, and when you call the Iqamah then be quick. Allow enough time between your Adhan and Iqamah for the person eating to finish what he is eating, the person drinking to finish what he is drinking, and the one who needs time to relive himself, and do not stand until you see me.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 195)"],[729,"When he heard the mu’adhdhin, he would say the same as he says, until he fell silent."],[730,"When he heard the mu’adhdhin, he would say: “And I too, and I too.”"],[731,"He narrated to him that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Bilal stood up to call the adhan. When he fell silent, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever says the like of this with certainty will enter Paradise.”"],[732,"“Whoever gives the adhan for twelve years, Paradise becomes obligatory for him, and sixty good deeds are written for him for each adhan and thirty good deeds for each iqamah.”"],[733,"Whoever calls the adhan for twelve years, Paradise becomes guaranteed for him, and sixty good deeds are written for him for every adhan and thirty good deeds for every iqamah."],[734,"He would not call the adhan for any of the prayers while traveling, nor give the iqamah, except for Fajr, for which he would call the adhan and give the iqamah."],[735,"Ibn Umar would not call the adhan while traveling, nor give the iqamah for any of his prayers."],[736,"When one of you hears the call to prayer while a vessel is in his hand, let him not put it down until he has satisfied his need from it."],[737,"Messenger of Allah said: \"What is between the east and the west is Qiblah.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 344)"],[738,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘What is between the east and the west is the Qiblah (prayer direction).’”* *This refers to the Qiblah for the the inhabitants of Al-Madinah. (Makkah is to the exact south of Al-Madinah.) (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1011)"],[739,"We prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during a journey, and clouds overshadowed us, so we were confused and differed about the qiblah. Each one of us prayed in a different direction, and each one of us drew a line in front of him so that we would know our places. We mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not command us to repeat the prayer, and he said: \"Your prayer is sufficient.\""],[740,"When one of you performs ablution in his house and then comes to the mosque, he remains in prayer until he returns, so let him not do this—and he interlaced his fingers."],[741,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ka'b b. Ujrah: \"When you have performed ablution and then enter the mosque, do not interlace your fingers.\" It was narrated by Sharik b. Abdullah from Muhammad b. Ajlan, but he erred in its chain. Sharik narrated it from Ibn Ajlan from his father from Abu Hurayrah, so Sharik erred."],[742,"When you are in the mosque, do not place your fingers like this."],[743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you enters the mosque, let him send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and say: 'O Allah, protect me from the accursed Satan.'\""],[744,"A man came to the prayer while the Prophet ﷺ was leading us in prayer. When he reached the row, he said: \"O Allah, give me the best of what You give Your righteous servants.\" When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: \"Who spoke just now?\" The man said: \"I, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the path of Allah.\""],[745,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered into prayer, he would say: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the accursed Satan, from his prodding, his blowing, and his sputtering.\" He said: \"His prodding is madness, his sputtering is poetry, and his blowing is arrogance.\""],[746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite aloud: \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\" Al-Bukhari used Salim, who is Ibn Ajlan al-Aftas, as evidence, and Muslim used Sharik as evidence. This chain is authentic and has no defect, but they did not include it."],[747,"Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. 'Ali b. Duhaym al-Shaybani informed us"],[748,"\"The farther, then the farther from the mosque, the greater the reward.\""],[749,"\"Prayer in congregation equals twenty-five prayers, and if he prays it in an open land and completes its bowing and prostrations, it reaches fifty prayers.\""],[750,"'Abdullah b. Maslama al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Tahla', from Mihsan b. 'Ali, from 'Awf b. al-Harith, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then goes and finds that the people have already prayed, Allah ﷻ gives him the like of the reward of the one who prayed it and attended it, without diminishing anything from their rewards.\""],[751,"\"Do not prevent your women from the mosques, though their houses are better for them.\""],[752,"\"The best mosques for women are the innermost parts of their houses.\""],[753,"\"A woman's prayer in her house is better than her prayer in her courtyard, and her prayer in her private chamber is better than her prayer in her house.\""],[754,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone and said, \"Is there not a man who may give charity to this one and pray with him?\""],[755,"\"Whoever leads a people and hits the right time, then he has it and they have it; and whoever detracts from that anything, then it is upon him and not upon them.\""],[756,"Hudhayfa led the people at Mada'in on a bench, so Abu Mas'ud grabbed his shirt and pulled him. When he finished his prayer, he said, \"Did you not know that they used to forbid that?\" Or he said, \"Did you not know that it used to be forbidden?\" He said, \"Yes, I remembered when you pulled me.\""],[757,"Hudhayfa prayed with the people at Mada'in and stepped forward onto a bench. Abu Mas'ud took hold of the collar of his garment and pulled him, so he stepped back. When he finished the prayer, Abu Mas'ud said to him, \"Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the imam to stand elevated while the people remain behind him?\" He said, \"Why do you think I responded when you pulled me?\""],[758,"We prayed behind an amir from among the commanders, and the people were forced into rows, so we prayed between two pillars. When we prayed, Anas b. Malik said, \"We used to avoid this at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[759,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His ﷻ saying: {Indeed, the recitation of dawn is ever witnessed} [al-Isra' 78], he said: “The angels of the night and the angels of the day attend it, gathering together at that time.”"],[760,"“When we missed a man at the later evening prayer (al-ʿishāʾ al-ākhirah) and the dawn prayer, we would think ill of him.”"],[761,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There are no three persons in a village or desert among whom the prayer is not established, but Satan has gained mastery over them. So adhere to the congregation, for the wolf eats only the stray sheep.”"],[762,"“When a man purifies himself and then proceeds to the mosque to observe the prayer, his scribe or scribes record for him ten good deeds for every step he takes to the mosque. And the one who sits waiting for the prayer is like the one in devout obedience, and he is recorded among those who pray from the time he leaves his house until he returns.”"],[763,"He passed by Muʿādh b. Jabal while he was sitting at his door gesturing with his hand as if talking to himself. ʿAbd Allāh said to him: What is the matter with you, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, talking to yourself? He said: And what is wrong with me? The enemy of Allah wants to distract me from words I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Do not struggle with your human weakness. Will you not go out to the mosque and speak? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Whoever strives in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever sits in his house not backbiting anyone with evil is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever visits a sick person is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever goes out to the mosque in the morning or evening is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever enters upon a ruler to honor him is guaranteed by Allah.” So the enemy of Allah wants to drive me out of my house to the gathering."],[764,"“Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[765,"“Give glad tidings to those who walk in the dark of night to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When you see a man frequenting the mosque, then testify to his faith.” Allah ﷻ said: {Only those who believe in Allah and the Last Day maintain the mosques of Allah} [al-Tawbah 18]. This is a chapter heading for the Egyptians; they did not differ regarding its authenticity and the truthfulness of its narrators, except that the two Shaykhs of the Ṣaḥīḥ did not include it. I have presented the discussion of its authenticity earlier. Dirāj has many rejected reports."],[767,"“None of you sets foot toward the mosques for prayer but Allah receives him with joy from the moment he leaves his house, just as the family of an absent loved one rejoices when he returns to them.”"],[768,"“Whoever leads the people in prayer and hits the right time, then he and they have the reward. And whoever falls short of that in anything, then the shortcoming is upon him and not upon them.”"],[769,"“The muezzin of the Prophet ﷺ would give the call to prayer and then wait. When he saw that the Prophet ﷺ had come, he would begin the iqāmah.”"],[770,"“Whoever joins a row, Allah joins him; and whoever breaks a row, Allah cuts him off.”"],[771,"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who join the rows."],[772,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second row once."],[773,"When one of you enters the mosque while the people are in bowing, let him bow when he enters, then let him move along bowing until he enters the row, for that is the sunnah. 'Ata said: And I saw him doing that."],[774,"While I was in Madinah in the mosque in the front row standing praying, a man pulled me from behind with a tug, moved me aside, and stood in my place. He said: By Allah, I did not comprehend my prayer. When he finished, it was Ubayy b. Ka'b. He said: O young man, may Allah not grieve you. This is the covenant of the Prophet ﷺ to us: that we should be nearest to it. Then he faced the qiblah and said: The people of the knot have perished, three times, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. Then he said: By Allah, I do not grieve for them, but I grieve for what they have led astray. I said: Whom do you mean by this? He said: The rulers."],[775,"When the imam says Allahu Akbar, say Allahu Akbar. And when he says Sami'a Allahu liman hamidah, say Rabbana wa laka al-hamd."],[776,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two silent pauses: a pause when he said the takbir and a pause when he finished his recitation before bowing."],[777,"Abu Hurayrah came to us in the mosque of Banu Zurayq and said three things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do which the people have abandoned: he would raise his hands until they passed his ears, and he would remain silent after the recitation for a short while, asking Allah of His bounty."],[778,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he rose in the second rak'ah, would begin with 'Al-hamdu lillahi rabbil 'alamin' and would not pause."],[779,"When you come and we are prostrating, then prostrate and do not count it as anything. Whoever catches a rak'ah has caught the prayer."],[780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the lightest of people in prayer while still complete. He said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and at the moment he said the salam he would stand up. Then I prayed with Abu Bakr, and when he said the salam he sprang up in his place as if he were rising from hot stones."],[781,"I used to see him put forward young men from the youth of his people and they would lead him in prayer. I said: You are the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you have virtue and precedence, yet you put forward these boys and they lead you in prayer? Will you not come forward and lead your people? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The imam is a guarantor. If he completes it, it is for him and for them, and if he falls short, it is upon him and not upon them. So I do not want to bear that."],[782,"Press together in the row so that the children of al-hadhaf do not pass between you. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what are the children of al-hadhaf? He said: Hairless black sheep that are in the land of Yemen."],[783,"Part of the excellence of prayer is straightening the rows."],[784,"He used to seek forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second row once."],[785,"From the time one of you leaves his house to go to his mosque, one foot records a good deed and the other erases a bad deed."],[786,"When one of you performs ablution and does it well, then goes out to prayer, nothing takes him to the mosque except the prayer, his left foot does not cease erasing a bad deed from him, and his right foot records a good deed for him until he enters the mosque."],[787,"It is part of the Sunnah that when you enter the mosque, you begin with your right foot, and when you leave, you begin with your left foot."],[788,"The Prophet ﷺ urged them to pray and forbade them from leaving before he left from the prayer."],[789,"I offered the Friday prayer along with Anas ibn Malik. We were pushed to the pillars (due to the crowd of people). We, therefore, stopped forward and backward. Anas then said: We used to avoid it (setting a row between the pillars) during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 673)"],[790,"We were forbidden to pray between the pillars and were driven away from it forcefully."],[791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved that the Muhajirun and the Ansar be close to him so that they could learn from him."],[792,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let those of you who learn from me be close to me,\" meaning in prayer. The two Shaykhs agreed on the hadith of Abu Mas'ud: \"Let those of you who are mature and wise be close to me\" only. This addition has a sound chain according to their conditions, and it has a sound corroborating witness."],[793,"Do not precede me in saying Amin."],[794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited a prostration verse in the year of the conquest, and all the people prostrated, including the rider and the one prostrating on the ground, so much so that the rider prostrated on his hand."],[795,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw in my dream last night, as a sleeper sees, as if I was praying behind a tree. Then I saw as if I recited a prostration verse and prostrated, and I saw the tree as if it prostrated along with my prostration. I heard it while it was prostrating, saying: O Allah, record for me with You a reward for it, make it a treasure for me with You, remove from me a burden by it, and accept it from me as You accepted it from Your servant Dawud. Ibn Abbas said: Then I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite the prostration verse and then prostrate, and I heard him while prostrating saying the same as what the man said about the words of the tree. Sahih."],[796,"He used to say in the prostration of Quran recitation at night: 'My face has prostrated to the One who created it and split open its hearing and sight by His might and power.'"],[797,"He used to say in the prostration of Quran recitation: 'My face has prostrated to the One who created it and split open its hearing and sight.'"],[798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in the prostration of Quran recitation at night: 'My face has prostrated to the One who created it and split open its hearing and sight by His might and power. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.'"],[799,"The first surah in which a prostration was revealed was al-Hajj. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it and prostrated, and the people prostrated, except for a man who took some dust and prostrated upon it. I saw him later killed as a disbeliever. Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah followed him from Abu Ishaq in this manner, according to their conditions."],[800,"The first surah the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to the people was al-Hajj, until when he recited it he prostrated and the people prostrated, except for a man who took some dust and prostrated upon it. I saw him later killed as a disbeliever."],[801,"Surah al-Hajj was favored with two prostrations; whoever does not prostrate for them should not recite them."],[802,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed zuhr and we thought that he recited Tanzil al-Sajdah."],[803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent a night with me. She said: I missed him and thought he had gone to one of his wives. She said: I searched for him and found him prostrating. I placed my hand on him and heard him saying: 'Forgive me what I have concealed and what I have made public.'"],[804,"We used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ while he recited the Quran, and sometimes he would come to a prostration and prostrate, and we would prostrate with him."],[805,"On the day of Badr I fought for a while, then I came quickly to see what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was doing. I came and found him prostrating, saying: 'O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting,' not adding anything to that. I returned to the fighting, then came again and found him prostrating and saying that. Then I went back to the fighting, then came again and found him prostrating and saying that. He kept saying that until Allah granted him victory."],[806,"I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was leaving it. I followed him, walking behind him while he was unaware, until he entered a palm grove. He faced the qiblah and prostrated, prolonging the prostration while I was behind him, until I thought that Allah had taken his soul. I came walking until I reached him, lowered my head to look at his face. He raised his head and said: 'What is the matter, O Abd al-Rahman?' I said: When you prolonged the prostration, O Messenger of Allah, I feared that your soul had been taken, so I came to look. He said: 'When I entered the palm grove, Jibril met me and said: I bring you glad tidings that Allah says: Whoever greets you, I greet him, and whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him.'"],[807,"It was narrated from ‘Amr bin ‘As that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him fifteen prostrations in the Qur’an, including three in the Mufassal and two in Al-Hajj. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1057)"],[808,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished Umm al-Quran, he raised his voice and said: 'Amin.'"],[809,"Abu Hurayrah fell ill or was absent, so Abu Sa'id al-Khudri led us in prayer. He said the takbir aloud when he began the prayer, when he bowed, when he said 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' when he raised his head from prostration, when he prostrated, when he rose, and when he stood up from the two rak'ahs, until he completed his prayer in that manner. It was said to him, 'The people have differed about your prayer.' He went out, stood on the pulpit, and said, 'O people, by Allah, I do not care whether your prayer differs or not. This is how I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray.'"],[810,"When he bowed, he spread his fingers apart."],[811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us the prayer. He said, 'He said the takbir. When he wanted to bow, he placed his hands between his knees and bowed.' He said, 'That reached Sa'd, and he said, \"My brother has spoken the truth. We used to do this, then we were commanded with this,\" meaning holding the knees.'"],[812,"Narrate to us about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He stood before us in the mosque and said the takbir. When he bowed, he said the takbir, placed his palms on his knees, and positioned his fingers below that, then he kept his elbows away from his sides. Then he said, 'This is how we saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do it.'"],[813,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, 'Place it in your bowing.'"],[814,"When the verse 'So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great' [al-Waqi'ah 74] was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, 'Place it in your bowing.' When the verse 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' [al-A'la 1] was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, 'Place it in your prostration.'"],[815,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, among what was read to Malik; and Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Salamah informed me; Uthman b. Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us; Yahya b. Bukayr narrated to us; Malik narrated to us; and Ahmad b. Ja'far informed us; Abdullah b. Ahmad b. Hanbal narrated to us; my father narrated to me, saying: I read to Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi, from Malik, from Nu'aym b. Abdullah al-Mujmir, from Ali b. Yahya b. Khallad al-Zuraqi, from his father, from Rifa'ah b. Rafi' al-Zuraqi, that he said: One day we were praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he raised his head from the rak'ah, he said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him.' A man said, 'Our Lord, and to You is all praise, abundant, good, and blessed praise therein, plentiful.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said, 'Who spoke just now?' The man said, 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I saw thirty-some angels rushing to it, each of them striving to write it down first.'"],[816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed qunut for a continuous month in the Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr prayers, after every prayer when he said, 'Allah hears the one who praises Him' in the last rak'ah, supplicating against a tribe of Banu Sulaym, against Ri'l, Dhakwan, and Usayyah, and those behind him said ameen. He had sent to them calling them to Islam, and they killed them. Ikrimah said, 'This is the origin of qunut.'"],[817,"And he said: The Prophet ﷺ used to do that."],[818,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the takbir, and he aligned his thumbs with his ears. Then he bowed until every joint of his settled, and he descended with the takbir until his knees preceded his hands. This is a sound chain according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, and I do not know any defect in it, though they did not include it."],[819,"The two hands prostrate just as the face prostrates. When one of you places his face down, let him place his hands down, and when he raises it, let him raise them."],[820,"I heard al-Bara' b. 'Azib say: The Prophet ﷺ used to prostrate on the fleshy parts of the palms."],[821,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Dawud b. Qays narrated to us, from 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. Aqram, from his father, that he was with his father at al-Qa' of Namira, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying, and I was looking at the whiteness of the two armpits of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ every time he prostrated."],[822,"He used to, when he prostrated, join his fingers together."],[823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not spread out your forearms, but rest on your palms and keep your upper arms apart from your sides, for when you do that, every limb of yours prostrates with you.\" Al-Bukhari used Adam b. 'Ali al-Bakri as evidence, and Muslim used Muhammad b. Ishaq, and this is sahih, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed, would jakhkha. I heard Abu Zakariyya al-'Anbari say: \"Jakhkha a man in his prayer means he stretched his upper arms and spread them in bowing and prostration.\""],[825,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ from behind him, and I saw the whiteness of his armpits while he was mujakhkhin and had brought out his hands."],[826,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prostrated, the whiteness of his armpits would be seen."],[827,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prostrated, if an animal had wanted to pass between his hands, it would have passed."],[828,"'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, said: I missed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had been with me on my bed. I found him prostrating, pressing his heels together, facing the qiblah with the tips of his toes, and I heard him saying: \"I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and in You from You. I cannot praise You fully; You are as You have praised Yourself.\" When he finished, he said: \"O 'A'ishah, has your devil taken hold of you?\" I said: \"Do you not have a devil?\" He said: \"There is no human being but has a devil.\" I said: \"And you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"And me, but Allah helped me against him, so he became Muslim.\""],[829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade pecking like a crow, spreading the arms like a beast of prey, and a man fixing a place for himself as a camel fixes it."],[830,"From Abu Hurayrah."],[831,"The worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how does he steal from his prayer?\" He said: \"He does not complete its bowing or its prostration.\""],[832,"Indeed, the worst of people in theft is the one who steals from his prayer.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, and how does he steal from his prayer?\" He said: \"He does not complete its bowing and its prostration.\""],[833,"\"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited a man from relying on his left hand when sitting in prayer.\" In the hadith of Ishaq, it is mentioned: \"A man should rely on his hands in prayer.\""],[834,"It pertains to the sunnah to utter the tashahhud quietly. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 986)"],[835,"This verse was revealed concerning the tashahhud: {And do not recite [too] loudly in your prayer or [too] quietly}"],[836,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Fadalah b. 'Ubayd al-Ansari, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man who prayed without praising Allah, without glorifying Him, and without invoking blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and then left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This one has been hasty.' He called him and said to him and to others: 'When one of you prays, let him begin by praising his Lord and extolling Him, and let him invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then let him supplicate for whatever he wishes.'"],[837,"He used to give one salam in prayer, facing forward, leaning a little to the right."],[838,"Abbreviating the salam is a sunnah."],[839,"Abbreviating the salam is a sunnah."],[840,"When Jibril came to him and recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim, he knew that it was a surah."],[841,"The Prophet ﷺ would not know the end of a surah until Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim was revealed."],[842,"The Muslims would not know the completion of a surah until Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim was revealed. When Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim was revealed, they knew that the surah had ended."],[843,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite {Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim} [al-Fatihah 1] {Alhamdu lillahi rabbil 'alamin} [al-Fatihah 2], stopping at each word."],[844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited in prayer {Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim} [al-Fatihah 1] and counted it as one verse, {Alhamdu lillahi rabbil 'alamin} [al-Fatihah 2] as two verses, {Al-Rahman al-Rahim} [al-Fatihah 1] as three verses, {Maliki yawmi al-din} as four verses, and he said likewise {Iyyaka na'budu wa iyyaka nasta'in} [al-Fatihah 5] and joined his five fingers. 'Umar b. Harun is an authority in sunnah, but they did not include it, and I included it only as a supporting witness. They unanimously agreed on his weakness, meaning 'Umar b. Harun, and al-Nasa'i said he is abandoned."],[845,"I was behind Abu Hurayrah and he recited {Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim} [al-Fatihah 1], then recited Umm al-Qur'an until he reached {wa la al-dallin} [al-Fatihah 7], then he said 'Amin' and the people said 'Amin'. He would say 'Allahu akbar' whenever he prostrated, and when he said the salam he said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, I am the most similar among you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud. Muhammad is weak, meaning Muhammad b. Qays."],[847,"Mu'awiya prayed in Madinah a prayer in which he recited aloud, and in it he recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim for Umm al-Qur'an but did not recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim for the surah that followed it until he finished that recitation. When he said the salam, those who heard that from the Muhajirun and the Ansar called out to him from every direction: 'O Mu'awiya, did you omit part of the prayer or did you forget?' Then when he prayed after that, he recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim for the surah that followed Umm al-Qur'an and said the takbir when he went down for prostration."],[848,"Anas b. Malik was asked: How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: It was extended. Then he recited {Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim} [al-Fatiha 1], extending al-Rahman and extending al-Rahim."],[849,"From Anas b. Malik."],[850,"I prayed behind al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman more times than I can count, the dawn prayer and the sunset prayer, and he would recite Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud before Fatihat al-Kitab and after it. And I heard al-Mu'tamir say: I spare no effort to follow the prayer of my father. And my father said: I spare no effort to follow the prayer of Anas b. Malik. And Anas b. Malik said: I spare no effort to follow the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The narrators of this hadith, down to the last of them, are trustworthy, and among them: its narrators are trustworthy."],[851,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and behind Abu Bakr and behind Umar and behind Uthman and behind Ali, and all of them would recite the recitation of Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud. I mentioned this hadith only as a witness for what preceded it. In these reports that we have mentioned there is opposition to the hadith of Qatada which our imams narrate from him. There remain in the chapter reports from the Commander of the Faithful Uthman and Ali and Talha b. Ubayd Allah and Jabir b. Abd Allah and Abd Allah b. Umar and al-Hakam b. Umayr al-Thumali and al-Nu'man b. Bashir and Samura b. Jundub and Burayda al-Aslami and A'isha bt. al-Siddiq; all of them are documented by me in the chapter, but I have omitted them preferring brevity, and I have abridged from them what is appropriate to this chapter. Likewise I have mentioned in the chapter those who recited Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim aloud among the Companions, the Followers, and their followers. As for the author, is he not ashamed to cite this fabricated hadith? I bear witness by Allah, and for Allah, that it is a lie."],[852,"Abu Hurayra entered upon us at the mosque of Banu Zurayq and said: Three things the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that people have abandoned. When he stood for prayer he would do like this—and Abu Amir gestured with his hand, neither spreading his fingers apart nor closing them together."],[853,"He would spread his fingers in prayer, spreading them wide."],[854,"When he began the prayer he would say: 'Allahu akbar kabira, wa al-hamdu lillahi kathira, wa subhan Allahi bukratan wa asila' three times. 'Allahumma inni a'udhu bika min al-shaytan al-rajim min hamzihi wa nafthihi wa nafkhihi.'"],[855,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the prayer he would say: 'Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika wa tabaraka ismuka wa ta'ala jadduka wa la ilaha ghayruk.'"],[856,"When he began the prayer he would say: 'Subhanaka Allahumma wa bihamdika wa tabaraka ismuka wa ta'ala jadduka wa la ilaha ghayruk.'"],[857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Dhuhr prayer with us, and when he finished, he called out to a man who was at the back of the rows and said, \"O so-and-so, don't you fear Allah? Don't you pay attention to how you pray? Indeed, when any of you stands for prayer, he is conversing privately with his Lord, so let him pay attention to how he converses with Him. Surely, you all see me, but by Allah, I see what is behind my back just as I see what is in front of me.\""],[858,"Allah continues to face the servant as long as he does not turn away, but when he turns his face away, He turns away from him."],[859,"Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, commanded Yahya b. Zakariyya with five words to act upon them: When you set your faces, do not turn away, for Allah, Exalted, sets His face to the face of His servant until he prays to Him, and He does not turn His face away from him until the servant himself turns away."],[860,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would turn in his prayer to the right and left, but he would not twist his neck behind his back."],[861,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out to Hunayn, he said: \"Is there a man to guard us tonight?\" Anas b. Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi said: \"I, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Go.\" When the next day came, the Prophet ﷺ went out and said: \"Have you sensed your horseman?\" They said: \"No.\" The Prophet ﷺ began to pray and turn toward the mountain pass. When he said the salam, he said: \"Your horseman has arrived.\" When he came, he said: \"Perhaps you dismounted?\" He said: \"No, except to pray or to relieve myself.\" Then he said: \"I looked into the two mountain passes, and there were the Hawazin with their women, sheep, and camels heading to Hunayn.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Spoils for the Muslims tomorrow, if Allah wills.\" Sahih."],[862,"He would recite Surat al-A'raf in both rak'ahs of Maghrib."],[863,"Umm al-Qur'an is a substitute for other than it, and nothing other than it is a substitute for it."],[864,"Whoever prays an obligatory prayer with the imam, let him recite the Fatihah of the Book during his pauses. Whoever reaches Umm al-Kitab, it suffices him."],[865,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Subh and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished, he said: \"I see you reciting behind your imam.\" We said: \"Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, this.\" He said: \"Do not do so except with Umm al-Qur'an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.\" Mahmud b. al-Rabi' inserted Wahb b. Kaysan between him and Ubadah."],[866,"\"Do you recite with me in prayer?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Do not do so except with the Fatihah of the Book.\""],[867,"Ubadah b. al-Samit stood beside me and recited with the imam while he was reciting. When he finished, I said: \"O Abu al-Walid, you recite and I hear, while he recites aloud?\" He said: \"Yes, we recited with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ erred, then he said subhan Allah. When he finished, he said to us: 'Did anyone recite with me?' We said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I was amazed. I said: Who is this contending with me over the Qur'an? When the imam recites, do not recite except with Umm al-Qur'an, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it.'\""],[868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to go out and announce among the people: \"There is no prayer except with reciting the Fatihah of the Book and whatever is more.\""],[869,"He asked Umar about reciting behind the imam, and he said: \"Recite the Fatihah of the Book.\" I said: \"Even if it is you?\" He said: \"Even if it is me.\" I said: \"Even if you recite aloud?\" He said: \"Even if I recite aloud.\" Sahih."],[870,"He used to command that behind the imam in the first two rak'ahs, one recite the Fatihah of the Book and a surah, and in the last two, the Fatihah of the Book."],[871,"The Prophet ﷺ would pray approximately like your prayer, but he would make the prayer light. In the Fajr prayer, he would recite al-Waqi'ah and surahs like it."],[872,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the two protective surahs (al-Mu'awwidhatayn): 'Are they from the Qur'an?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited them for us in the Fajr prayer.'"],[873,"I was leading the Messenger of Allah ﷺ's riding camel on a journey, and he said: 'O Uqbah, shall I not teach you the best two surahs ever recited?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Say: \"I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak\" and \"Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind.\"' When he dismounted, he prayed the morning prayer with them, then said: 'How do you see it, O Uqbah?' As for the hadith of Zayd b. al-Hubab, from Mu'awiyah b. Salih, it is similar to this chain of transmission. 'And this chain of transmission does not invalidate the first one, for this is a chain of transmission for another text, and Allah knows best.'"],[874,"A man used to lead them in prayer at Quba. Whenever he wanted to start a surah to recite, he would recite 'Say: He is Allah, the One,' then recite the surah. He did that in all his prayers. His companions said to him: 'Will you not leave this surah, or recite \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" and then leave it?' He said to them: 'I will not leave it. If you like me to lead you in prayer with that, I will do so; otherwise, no.' He was one of the best of them, and they disliked that anyone other than him should lead them. They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: 'O so-and-so, what prevents you from doing what your companions ask of you? And what makes you cling to this surah?' He said: 'I love it, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your love of it will admit you to Paradise.'"],[875,"I heard Abu Dharr say: 'The Prophet ﷺ stood with a verse until morning, repeating it. The verse is: {If You punish them, they are Your servants; and if You forgive them, indeed You are the Exalted in Might, the Wise} [al-Ma'idah: 118].'"],[876,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will suffice me from the Qur'an, for I do not recite.' He said: 'Say: Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah.' The man clasped his hand over them and said: 'This is for my Lord, so what is for me?' He said: 'Say: Forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, provide for me, and grant me well-being.' The man clasped his other hand over them and stood up. Ja'far b. 'Awn added in his hadith: Mis'ar said: 'I was with Ibrahim while he was narrating this hadith, and I sought confirmation of it from someone other than him.'"],[877,"He was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came and entered the mosque and prayed. When he finished his prayer, he came and greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.' He mentioned that either two or three times. The man said: 'I do not know what fault you find with my prayer.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The prayer of any of you is not complete until he performs ablution thoroughly as Allah ﷻ commanded him: he washes his face and his hands up to the elbows, wipes his head and his feet up to the ankles, then says takbir, praises Allah, glorifies Him, and recites from the Qur'an what Allah has permitted him, then says takbir and bows, placing his palms on his knees until his joints are at ease and he is upright, then says \"Allah hears the one who praises Him\" and stands upright until every bone takes its proper place, then straightens his back, then says takbir and prostrates, placing his forehead firmly on the ground until his joints are at ease and he is level, then says takbir and raises his head and sits upright on his seat and straightens his back.' He described the prayer thus until he finished, then said: 'The prayer of any of you is not complete until he does that.'"],[878,"A man entered the mosque after the Prophet ﷺ had prayed and then prayed. 'Then he mentioned the hadith. This chain of transmission has been established by Dawud b. Qays al-Farra', Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Yasar, and Isma'il b. Ja'far b. Abi Kathir.' As for the hadith of Dawud b. Qays."],[879,"'I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque when a man entered and prayed two rak'ahs, then came and greeted.' And he mentioned the hadith in full. 'As for the hadith of Muhammad b. Ishaq b. Yasar.'"],[880,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, a man from the Ansar came after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished the prayer. He prayed, then came forward until he stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him. He said: 'And upon you. Go back and pray, for you have not prayed.' Then he mentioned the hadith. 'As for the hadith of Isma'il b. Ja'far.'"],[881,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in the mosque one day, Rifa'ah said: 'We were with him when a man who looked like a Bedouin came and prayed.' Then he mentioned the hadith in full, according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs."],[882,"'The people should be led in prayer by the one who has the most Qur'an among them. If they are equal in Qur'an, then the earliest of them in emigration. If they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of them in fiqh. If they are equal in fiqh, then the oldest of them in age.'"],[883,"'The people should be led in prayer by the earliest of them in emigration. If they are equal in emigration, then the most knowledgeable of them in religion. If they are equal in religion, then the one who recites the Qur'an most. And a man should not be led in his own domain of authority, nor should one sit on his place of honor except with his permission.'"],[884,"No prophet dies until a man from his people leads him in prayer."],[885,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for prayer, he would say this and this, to his right and to his left, then say: “Stand straight and be aligned.”"],[886,"He was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the call to prayer was given. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and prayed, then returned while Mihjan remained in his seat as he was. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “What prevented you from praying with the people? Are you not a Muslim man?” He said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, but I had already prayed at home.” He said: “When you come, pray with the people even if you have already prayed.”"],[887,"Abu al-Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us: al-Rabi' b. Sulayman informed us: al-Shafi'i informed us: Abd al-Aziz b. Muhammad informed us, from Zayd b. Aslam, and he mentioned it in a similar manner. This is an authentic hadith, and Malik b. Anas is the authority in the hadith of the Medinans, and it has been used as evidence in the Muwatta'. It is of the type I mentioned earlier: that if a companion does not have two narrators, they would not have included it. Mihjan — only his son narrated from him."],[888,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Mina. When he said the salam, he noticed two men at the back of the people, so he called them and said: “What prevented you two from praying with the people?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, we prayed at our mounts.” He said: “Do not do that. If one of you prays at his mount and then catches the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him, for it is a supererogatory prayer for him.”"],[889,"Whoever hears the call and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him."],[890,"Whoever hears the call and does not come to it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse."],[891,"Whoever hears the call and does not come to it, there is no prayer for him except with an excuse."],[892,"Whoever hears the caller and no excuse prevents him from following him, there is no prayer for him.” They said: “What is the excuse?” He said: “Fear or illness.”"],[893,"Whoever hears the prayer being called while healthy and without excuse, and does not come to it, Allah will not accept any prayer from him besides it.” It was said: “What is the excuse?” He said: “Illness or fear.”"],[894,"There is no prayer for the neighbor of the mosque except in the mosque."],[895,"Whoever hears the call while free and healthy and does not answer it, there is no prayer for him."],[896,"There are not three people in a town or in the desert among whom the prayer is not established except that Satan has gained mastery over them, so adhere to the congregation."],[897,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Madinah has many vermin and beasts of prey.' He said, 'Do you hear \"Come to prayer, come to success\"?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then hasten to it.'"],[898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the people during the Isha prayer and said, 'I was about to go to those who stay behind from this prayer and burn their houses down upon them.' Ibn Umm Maktum stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you know my condition, and I have no guide.' He said, 'Do you hear the call to prayer (iqamah)?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then attend it.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, between me and it there are palm trees and trees, and I have no guide.' He said, 'Do you hear the iqamah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then attend it,' and he did not grant him a concession. 'It has another witness from the hadith of Asim b. Bahdalah.'"],[899,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am a man with weak eyesight, far from the mosque, and I have no guide who suits me. Is there a concession for me to pray in my house?' He said, 'Do you hear the call?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I find no concession for you.'"],[900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Fajr prayer and then said, 'Is so-and-so present?' referring to a group of hypocrites who had not attended the prayer. Then he said, 'These two prayers are among the heaviest prayers for the hypocrites. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even crawling,' meaning the Isha and Fajr prayers."],[901,"From Ubayy b. Ka'b. 'As for the hadith of al-Thawri.'"],[902,"Ubayy b. Ka'b: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer one day. When he said the salam, he said, 'Is so-and-so present?' Then he mentioned the hadith. 'And as for the hadith of Abu al-Ahwas.'"],[903,"Ubayy b. Ka'b: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the Fajr prayer, then he mentioned the hadith. 'They have disagreed about the hadith on the authority of Abu Ishaq in four ways, and the narration from Abi Basir and his son Abdullah is all authentic, and the evidence for it is the narration of Khalid b. al-Harith.' Shu'bah narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, and Mu'adh b. Mu'adh al-Anbari and Yahya b. Sa'id from Shu'bah. 'As for the hadith of Khalid b. al-Harith.'"],[904,"Abu Ishaq: I heard it from him and from his father, from Ubayy b. Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the Fajr prayer, then he mentioned the hadith. 'And as for the hadith of Yahya b. Sa'id.'"],[905,"\"Abu Ishaq, I heard from him and from his father, from Ubayy who said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer.' And he mentioned the narration, 'The scholars of hadith, Yahya ibn Ma'in, Ali ibn Al-Madini, Muhammad ibn Yahya Al-Zuhri, and others have ruled the authenticity of this hadith.' I heard Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub saying, 'I heard Abbas ibn Muhammad Al-Dawri saying, 'I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in saying, 'The hadith of Abu Ishaq from Abu Basir from Ubayy ibn Ka'b is mentioned by Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiya and Shu'bah narrated it from Abu Ishaq from Abdullah ibn Abu Basir and from his father from Ubayy ibn Ka'b. The statement is Shu'bah's and it is more reliable than Zuhayr's.'\""],[906,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the Fajr prayer and then said, 'Is so-and-so present?' It was narrated by Abu Ishaq from a shaykh from whom he heard only this, and he is Abdullah b. Abi Basir. Shu'bah said from Abu Ishaq that he heard from his father and from him. Al-Ahwas said from Abu Ishaq from al-Ayzar b. Hurayth. 'I do not consider the hadith anything but authentic.' I heard Abu Bakr b. Ishaq al-Faqih say: I heard Ibrahim b. Ishaq al-Harbi say: I heard Ali b. al-Madini say: Abu Ishaq heard from Abdullah b. Abi Basir and from his father Abi Basir. Abu Bakr b. Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard Abdullah b. Muhammad al-Madini say: I heard Muhammad b. Yahya say: The narration of Yahya b. Sa'id and Khalid b. al-Harith from Shu'bah, and the statement of Abu al-Ahwas from Abu Ishaq from al-Ayzar b. Hurayth, 'All of them are preserved, so the authenticity of the hadith has become clear from the statements of the imams of hadith. As for the two shaykhs, they did not include it because of this disagreement.'"],[907,"I heard Salamah bin Al-Akwa' saying, \"I asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'If I am engaged in hunting and I have nothing except one shirt or one cloak, should I tighten or tuck it up?' He said, 'Yes, even if it is done with a thorn.'\""],[908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade praying in a wrapper that is not worn over the shoulder, and he forbade a man praying in trousers while not wearing a cloak."],[909,"She asked the Prophet ﷺ: May a woman pray in a shift and a headcover without a waist wrapper? He said: \"If the shift is ample and covers the tops of her feet.\""],[910,"I saw Ibn Umar praying with his waist wrapper unfastened. I asked him about that, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing it."],[911,"The prayer of a menstruating woman is not accepted except with a headcover."],[912,"The prayer of a menstruating woman is not accepted except with a headcover."],[913,"The whole earth is a place of prostration except the bathhouse and the graveyard."],[914,"The whole earth is a place of prostration except the bathhouse and the graveyard."],[915,"Do not pray except toward a sutrah, and do not let anyone pass in front of you. If he refuses, then fight him, for with him is a companion (qarin)."],[916,"When one of you prays, let him pray toward a sutrah and draw close to it, so that Satan does not interrupt his prayer."],[917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray in our haircloth and our blankets. Ubaydullah said: My father was uncertain."],[918,"A sutrah equivalent to the back of a saddle suffices, even if it is as thin as a hair."],[919,"Let one of you screen his prayer, even with an arrow."],[920,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Cover yourselves with your prayers, even with an arrow if necessary, as long as a Muslim fulfills his conditions.\""],[921,"He used to say after the prayer: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief, poverty, and the punishment of the grave.”"],[922,"We were commanded to glorify Allah thirty-three times after every prayer, to praise Him thirty-three times, and to magnify Him thirty-four times. [The narrator] said: Then a man from the Ansar was told in his sleep: “Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command you to glorify Allah after every prayer such-and-such?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “Then make them twenty-five and include the tahlil in them.” When morning came, he went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then do so.”"],[923,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Recite the Mu‘awwidhat after every prayer.” “Sahih according to Muslim’s criterion, but they did not include it.” according to Muslim's condition"],[924,"“When one of you prays in a single garment, let him tie it around his waist, and do not wrap yourselves as the Jews wrap themselves.”"],[925,"“He forbade sadl (letting the garment hang loosely) and that a man cover his mouth.”"],[926,"I traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition. He stood to pray, and I had a burdah (garment). I went to cross its ends, then I fastened it so it would not fall. Then I came to the left side of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he took my hand and turned me around until he stood me on his right. Then Ibn Sakhr came and stood on his left, and he took both of us by his hands until he stood us behind him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept glancing at me while I was unaware, then I noticed it, and he gestured to me to wrap it as a waistcloth. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, he said: “O Jabir.” I said: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “If it is wide, cross its ends; and if it is narrow, tie it around your waist.” “This is sahih according to Muslim’s criterion, but they did not include it.” according to Muslim's condition"],[927,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ “come out after finishing his tawaf to the edge of the mataf and pray two rak‘ahs, with no one between him and the two tawafs.”"],[928,"He was praying when a sheep passed in front of him, so he raced it toward the qiblah until he pressed his belly against the qiblah (wall)."],[929,"“A cat does not interrupt the prayer because it is among the household goods.”"],[930,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in one of his prayers: “O Allah, bring me to account with an easy reckoning.” When he finished, I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the easy reckoning?” He said: “One looks into his record and is pardoned. Indeed, whoever is questioned closely about the account on that day, O ‘A’ishah, will be destroyed. And whatever befalls a believer, Allah expiates for him, even a thorn that pricks him.”"],[931,"Umm Sulaym came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I can supplicate with in my prayer.” He said: “Glorify Allah ten times, praise Allah ten times, magnify Allah ten times, then ask Allah whatever you wish.”"],[932,"He saw Abu Barzah al-Aslami praying while holding the reins of his mount in his hand. When he bowed, the reins slipped from his hand, and the mount went off. Abu Barzah stepped backward on his heels without turning around until he caught up with the mount and took it. Then he walked as he was, returned to the place where he had been praying, completed his prayer, then said the salam. Then he said: “I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on many expeditions—until he counted expeditions—and I saw his rukhsah (concession) and his facilitation, so I adopted that. If I had left my mount to reach the desert, then had gone as an old man stumbling in the darkness, that would have been harder for me.”"],[933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded killing the two black ones during prayer: the snake and the scorpion."],[934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would turn in his prayer to the right and to the left, but he would not twist his neck behind his back."],[935,"When you are in prayer, do not spit in front of you nor to your right, but spit to your left if it is empty, or under your feet. And he gestured with his foot as if he was scraping it with his foot."],[936,"He prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he spat mucus, then rubbed it with his left sandal."],[937,"He used to like the palm stalks to hold them in his hand. One day he entered the mosque and in his hand was one of them. He saw sputum in the direction of the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped them until he cleaned them. Then he turned to the people angrily and said: 'Would any of you like a man to face him and spit in his face? When one of you stands for prayer, he is facing his Lord, and the angel is on his right. So let him not spit in front of him nor to his right, but let him spit under his left foot or to his left. And if something forces him, let him spit like this into the edge of his garment.' And he folded part of it over another part."],[938,"He used to lead his people in prayer. He came when the prayer had been established, and he said: 'Let one of you pray, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: When the prayer is present and the call of nature is present, then begin with the call of nature.'"],[939,"From Ibn al-Daylami, who used to live in Jerusalem, that he rode in search of Abd Allah b. Amr b. al-As in Madinah. He asked about him and they said he had gone to Makkah, so he followed him and found that he had gone to al-Ta'if, so he followed him and found him in the farm called al-Waht. Ibn al-Daylami said: I entered upon him and found him walking, conversing with a man from Quraysh, and the Qurayshi was weighing wine. I met him, greeted him, and he greeted me. He said: What brought you today, and from where have you come? I informed him, then I asked him: Have you heard, O Abd Allah b. Amr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'No man of my community drinks wine but his prayer is not accepted for forty mornings'?"],[940,"Abd Allah said: 'O son of my brother, Allah sent Muhammad ﷺ to us and we did not know anything. We only do as we saw Muhammad do.'"],[941,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying cross-legged."],[942,"Teach the child to pray at seven years old, and beat him for it at ten."],[943,"Ali b. Abi Talib passed by a madwoman of Banu So-and-so who had committed adultery, and Umar b. al-Khattab had ordered her stoning. Ali sent her back and said to Umar: 'O Commander of the Faithful, will you stone this woman?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Do you not remember that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The pen is lifted from three: from the insane person overcome by his mind, from the sleeping person until he wakes, and from the child until he has a wet dream?' He said: 'You have spoken the truth.' So he released her."],[944,"He used to pray on the mat and the tanned fur."],[945,"Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated to us, Zam'ah b. Salih narrated to us, from Salamah b. Wahram, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas that he prayed on a rug, then said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on a rug.\""],[946,"When one of you prays, let him wear his sandals or take them off and place them between his feet, and not harm others with them."],[947,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of the conquest, and he prayed the morning prayer, then took off his sandals and placed them on his left."],[948,"When one of you prays, let him not place his sandals on his right or on his left, unless there is no one on his left, and let him place them between his feet."],[949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed and took off his sandals, so the people took off their sandals. When he finished, he said: 'Why did you take off your sandals?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you take them off, so we took ours off.' He said: 'Jibril came to me and informed me that there was some filth on them. So when one of you comes to the mosque, let him turn over his sandals and look for filth in them. If he finds filth in them, let him wipe them on the ground, then pray in them.'"],[950,"Differ from the Jews, for they do not pray in their leather socks or sandals."],[951,"When one of you prays, let him take off his sandals and place them between his feet, or pray in them."],[952,"When one of you breaks wind while in prayer, let him place his hand over his nose and then leave."],[953,"When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed three or four [rak'ahs], let him perform one rak'ah, perfecting its bowing and prostration, and then prostrate twice."],[954,"I prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs, then left. A man said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, you forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs.' So he ordered Bilal, who called the iqamah, then he completed that rak'ah. I asked the people about the man who said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you forgot,' and it was said to me: 'Do you know him?' I said: 'No, unless I see him.' Then a man passed by me, and I said: 'It is this one.' They said: 'This is Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah.' Al-Layth b. Sa'd abridged it from Abu Habib. Al-Layth reported it from Yazid in abridged form, and it meets the conditions of both of them."],[955,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then said the salam and left, while one rak'ah of the prayer remained."],[956,"The Prophet ﷺ called the two prostrations of forgetfulness 'the two humiliators' (al-murghimatayn)."],[957,"He saw Abu Rafi', the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ, pass by al-Hasan b. 'Ali while he was praying standing, having tied his braid at the back of his neck. Abu Rafi' untied it, and al-Hasan turned to him angrily. Abu Rafi' said: 'Attend to your prayer and do not be angry, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"That is the devil's share,\" meaning the devil's seat, meaning the place where his braid was tied.'"],[958,"He used to say between the two prostrations: 'O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, grant me well-being, and provide for me.'"],[959,"He feared Ziyad, so he came to Madinah and met Abu Hurayrah. He said: He asked me my lineage, and I told him. He said: 'O young man, shall I not narrate to you a hadith?' I said: 'Yes, may Allah have mercy on you.' Yunus said: I think he mentioned it from the Prophet ﷺ: 'The first thing for which people will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection from their deeds is the prayer.' He said: 'Our Lord ﷻ will say to the angels, though He knows best: \"Look at the prayer of My servant—did he complete it or fall short?\" If it is complete, it will be recorded for him as complete. If he fell short in something, He will say: \"Look, does My servant have any voluntary prayers?\" If he has voluntary prayers, He will say: \"Complete My servant's obligatory prayer from his voluntary prayer.\" Then the other deeds will be taken according to that.'"],[960,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection is the prayer. If he completed it, it will be recorded for him as complete. If he did not complete it, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say to His angels: 'Do you find any voluntary prayer for My servant with which you can complete what he neglected of his obligatory prayer?' Then the zakat is the same, then the rest of deeds according to that."],[961,"From a man among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and from Dawud b. Abi Hind, from Zurarah b. Awfa, from Tamim al-Dari, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection is his prayer.' And he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[962,"Abu al-Hasan Muhammad b. al-Hasan narrated to us: 'Ali b. 'Abd al-'Aziz informed us: Hajjaj b. al-Minhal narrated to us: Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd, from al-Hasan, from a man of Banu Sulayt, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. This disagreement regarding it from Hammad b. Salamah has been mentioned so that the careful examiner may know that the one we deemed authentic is the hadith of Dawud b. Abi Hind, in which there is no disagreement from Hammad, and the rest of the narrations on it are chains from Hammad other than Dawud. May Allah bless Muhammad and all his family."],[963,"He used to say in his prostration: 'O Allah, forgive me all my sin, its major and minor, its first and last, its open and secret.'"],[964,"When he recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' he said: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.'"],[965,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying and a sound came from his breast like the rumbling of a mill owing to weeping. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 904)"],[966,"'There is no deficiency in prayer or in the greeting of salam.'"],[967,"'There is no deficiency in the greeting of salam or in prayer.'"],[968,"'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade placing the hand on the waist during prayer.' Abu 'Abd Allah al-'Abdi said: That is when a man puts his hand on his flank."],[969,"One of my companions said to me: 'Would you like to meet a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?' I said: 'Yes, a prize.' He brought us to Wabisah b. Ma'bad. I said to my companion: 'Let us begin by looking at his appearance.' He was wearing a close-fitting cap with two earflaps and a worn-out woolen burnoose, and he was leaning on a staff in his prayer. After we greeted him, he said: 'Umm Qays bt. Mihsan narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he grew old and gained weight, took a staff to lean on during prayer.'"],[970,"I asked A'ishah whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite a surah in each rak'ah. She said, \"From the mufassal.\" I said, \"Did he pray sitting?\" She said, \"When old age had weakened him.\""],[971,"We did not know what to say when we sat in prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been given comprehensive speech and its conclusions. He mentioned the tashahhud and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us words just as he taught us the tashahhud: \"O Allah, bring our hearts together, reconcile our differences, guide us to the paths of peace, deliver us from darkness into light, keep us away from indecencies, both open and hidden, bless us in our hearing, our sight, our hearts, our spouses, and our offspring, and turn to us in mercy. Indeed, You are the Ever-Relenting, the Most Merciful. Make us grateful for Your blessings, praising You for them, accepting them, and complete them upon us.\""],[972,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us... then he mentioned the same as above.On the condition of Muslim."],[973,"The Messenger of Allah( may peace be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he would teach us the Qur’an, and would say: The blessed adoration of the tongue, acts of worship (and) all good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah’s mercy and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah’s upright servants. I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is Allah’s apostle (peace be upon him). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 974)"],[974,"Abdullah b. Salamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Abdul Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us from Hisham b. Urwah from his father that Umar b. al-Khattab used to teach the people the tashahhud in prayer while he was delivering a sermon from the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He would say: When one of you recites the tashahhud, let him say: \"In the name of Allah, the best of names. Greetings, pure words, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.\" Umar said, \"Begin with yourselves after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and send peace upon the righteous servants of Allah.\""],[975,"Abdullah b. Abbas took me by the hand and counted the tashahhud on my fingers, saying: I am taking your hand just as Umar b. al-Khattab took mine. And Umar said: I am taking your hand just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took mine. Then he counted the tashahhud: \"Greetings, prayers, good things, and pure words are due to Allah.\""],[976,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Quran: \"In the name of Allah and by Allah. Greetings are due to Allah.\" Abu al-Abbas said: Then he mentioned the hadith, and at its end: \"O Allah, I ask You for Paradise and I seek refuge in You from the Fire.\""],[977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach us the tashahhud just as he taught us a surah from the Quran: \"In the name of Allah and by Allah. Greetings, prayers, and good things are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. We ask Allah for Paradise and seek refuge in Him from the Fire.\""],[978,"From the Prophet ﷺ similar to it. \"I heard Abu Ali al-Hafiz authenticate Ibn Qahtabah, except that he erred in it, for in the version of al-Mu'tamir from Ayman b. Nabil it is as we mentioned previously. And may Allah bless Muhammad and all his family.\" Ayman is relied upon by al-Bukhari, and a group narrated from him."],[979,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque and found a man who had finished his prayer and was reciting the tashahhud, saying: \"O Allah, I ask You by Allah, the One, the Eternal Refuge, who neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent, to forgive me my sins. Indeed, You are the Forgiving, the Merciful.\" He said, \"He has been forgiven. He has been forgiven. He has been forgiven.\""],[980,"\"It is from the Sunnah to make the tashahhud silent.\""],[981,"\"He narrated to me regarding sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ , 'When a Muslim person prays upon him in their prayer.'\""],[982,"A man approached and sat in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while we were with him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we know how to greet you with peace, but how do we send blessings upon you when we have already sent blessings upon you in our prayers and Allah has already sent blessings upon you?\" He remained silent until we wished that the man had not asked him. Then he said, \"When you say the prayer upon me, say: 'O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, the Prophet who is unlettered, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. And bless Muhammad, the Prophet who is unlettered, and the family of Muhammad, as You blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Verily, You are full of praise and majesty.'\""],[983,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying without praising or glorifying Allah, nor sending blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ , and then he left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Bring him quickly.\" He called him and said to him and others, \"When one of you prays, let him start with praising his Lord and glorifying Him, then let him send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ , and then he may supplicate with whatever he wishes.\""],[984,"Abdullah said: \"A man recites the tashahhud, then sends blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then supplicates for himself.\" \"This hadith has been attributed to Abdullah b. Mas'ud with a sound chain.\""],[985,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"When any one of you performs the Tashahhud (bearing witness) in prayer, let him say: O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, and have mercy upon Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have sent prayers, blessed, and had mercy upon Ibrahim. Verily, You are Worthy of Praise and Glorious. And the majority of the narrations for this principle are for the obligations of prayer.\""],[986,"He used to say: \"There is no prayer for one who has no ablution, and no ablution for one who does not mention Allah's name over it, and no prayer for one who does not send blessings upon the Prophet of Allah in his prayer.\""],[987,"In the first two rakʿahs, he was as if on scorching stones. He said: We said, 'Until he stands?' He said: 'Until he stands.'"],[988,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded us to respond to the imam, to love one another, and that some of us should greet others."],[989,"An imam of ours, whose kunyah was Abu Rimthah, led us in prayer. He said: I performed this prayer—or one like it—with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Abu Bakr and Umar would stand in the front row to his right. A man had caught the opening takbir of the prayer. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ prayed, then gave salam to his right and his left until we could see the whiteness of his cheek. He then turned around as Abu Rimthah turned—meaning himself. The man who had caught the opening takbir of the prayer with him then stood to add another prayer. Umar sprang toward him, took him by the shoulder, shook him, and said: Sit down, for the People of the Book were only ruined because there was no separation between their prayers. The Prophet ﷺ raised his gaze and said: \"Allah has guided you to what is right, O son of al-Khattab.\"[1]"],[990,"There is no prayer for one whose nose does not touch the ground."],[991,"There is no prayer for one whose nose does not touch the ground."],[992,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded placing the hands and standing the feet upright in prayer."],[993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded placing the palms and standing the feet upright in prayer."],[994,"I was with Umm Salamah when a young relative of hers with long hair entered. He stood to pray and blew. She said: 'O my son, do not blow, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to a black slave of ours: \"O Rabāḥ, may your face be dusty.\""],[995,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man from squatting on his heels in his prayer."],[996,"He used to say when he raised his head from prostration: 'My Lord, forgive me.'"],[997,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say between the two prostrations: 'O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, mend me, raise me, guide me, and provide for me.'"],[998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sitting on the heels in prayer."],[999,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbās about sitting on the heels. He said: 'It is a sunnah.' I said: 'We consider it rude.' Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'It is the sunnah.' And it is authentic in permitting that according to the condition of Muslim."],[1000,"He forbade a man who was sitting resting on his left hand in prayer, saying, \"It is the prayer of the Jews.\""],[1001,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Two steps, one of them is more beloved to Allah and the other is the most hateful of steps to Allah. As for the step that Allah ﷻ loves, it is a man who sees a gap in the row and fills it. As for the one that Allah hates, it is when a man wants to stand up, he extends his right leg, places his hand on it, and fixes his left, then stands up.\""],[1002,"When he said the salam, he said, \"Glory be to the King, the Holy,\" three times, raising his voice."],[1003,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand one day and said, \"O Mu'adh, by Allah, I love you.\" Mu'adh said, \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by Allah, I love you.\" He said, \"I enjoin you, O Mu'adh, do not fail to say after every prayer: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.\" He said: And Mu'adh enjoined that upon al-Sunabihi, and al-Sunabihi enjoined it upon Abu 'Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman enjoined it upon 'Uqbah b. Muslim."],[1004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say after every prayer: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave, from the punishment of the Fire, from the trials of life and death, and from the trial of the false messiah, the Dajjal.\""],[1005,"\"When you come to prayer while we are prostrating, prostrate and do not count it as anything. Whoever catches the rak'ah has caught the prayer.\""],[1006,"\"Whoever prays one rak'ah of the morning prayer and then the sun rises, let him pray the morning prayer.\""],[1007,"\"Whoever prays one rak'ah of the morning prayer and then the sun rises, let him complete his prayer.\""],[1008,"\"Whoever does not pray the two rak'ahs of Fajr until the sun rises, let him pray them.\""],[1009,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey of his, and they slept through the dawn prayer. They woke up with the heat of the sun, so they moved a little until it was high, then \"he commanded the muezzin, who called the adhan, then he prayed the two rak'ahs before Fajr, then the muezzin gave the iqamah and he prayed Fajr.\""],[1010,"He came while the Prophet ﷺ was praying the Fajr prayer, so he prayed with him. When he said the salam, he stood up and prayed the two rak'ahs of Fajr. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"What are these two rak'ahs?\" He said, \"I had not prayed them before Fajr.\" So he remained silent and did not say anything. \"Qays b. Fahd al-Ansari is a Companion, and the route to him is authentic according to their conditions.\" Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Taymi narrated it from Qays b. Fahd. Qays b. Fahd is a Companion and has a supporting witness."],[1011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man praying two rak'ahs after the morning prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The morning prayer twice?\" The man said, \"I had not prayed the two rak'ahs before it, so I prayed them now.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent about him."],[1012,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about praying on a ship. He said, \"How do I pray on a ship?\" He replied, \"Pray in it standing, unless you fear drowning.\""],[1013,"\"Whoever combines two prayers without an excuse has approached a door from the doors of major sins.\""],[1014,"She said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying while seated.\""],[1015,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray long nights standing and long nights sitting. When he prayed standing, he bowed standing; and when he prayed sitting, he bowed sitting.\""],[1016,"\"We used to prompt the imams during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Yahya b. Ghaylan and Abdullah b. Baziʿ al-Tustariyyan are both trustworthy."],[1017,"\"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to prompt one another during prayer.\" The narrator is abandoned (matruk)."],[1018,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received a matter that pleased him or by which he was made happy, he would fall down in prostration out of gratitude to Allah ﷻ."],[1019,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The master of days is Friday; on it, Adam was created, on it he entered Paradise, and on it he was expelled from it. And there is no Hour except that it will be established on Friday.\""],[1020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah will resurrect the days on the Day of Judgment in their own nature, and He will raise Friday as a radiant and shining day. Its people will be protected by it like brides being presented to their husbands, and it will illuminate for them as they walk in its light. Their colors will be as white as snow, and their fragrance will shine like musk. They will enter the mount of camphor and the two weighty things (heavens and earth) will look at them in amazement. They will not be touched by anything until they enter Paradise. No one will be in their company except the Mu'adhins (callers to prayer) who keep account.\""],[1021,"\"O Salman, what is the day of Jumuʿah?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"O Salman, the day of Jumuʿah is the day on which your father—or your forefather—was gathered. And I will tell you about the day of Jumuʿah: no man purifies himself on the day of Jumuʿah as he has been commanded, then leaves his house until he comes to the Jumuʿah prayer, then sits and listens attentively until he finishes his prayer, except that it is an expiation for what came before it from the previous Jumuʿah.\""],[1022,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Indeed among the best of your days is the day of Jumuʿah. On it Adam was created, on it he was taken in death, on it is the trumpet blast, and on it is the thunderous cry. So increase in sending blessings upon me on that day, for your blessings are presented to me.\" They said, \"How can our blessings be presented to you when you have turned to dust?\" He said, \"Indeed Allah ﷻ has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets.\""],[1023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday; on it Adam was created, on it he was expelled (from Paradise), on it his contrition was accepted, on it he died, and on it the Last Hour will take place. On Friday every beast is on the lookout from dawn to sunrise in fear of the Last Hour, but not jinn and men, and it contains a time at which no Muslim prays and asks anything from Allah but He will give it to him. Ka'b said: That is one day every year. So I said: It is on every Friday. Ka'b read the Torah and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has spoken the truth. AbuHurayrah said: I met Abdullah ibn Salam and told him of my meeting with Ka'b. Abdullah ibn Salam said: I know what time it is. AbuHurayrah said: I asked him to tell me about it. Abdullah ibn Salam said: It is at the very end of Friday. I asked: How can it be when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has said: \"No Muslim finds it while he is praying....\" and this is the moment when no prayer is offered. Abdullah ibn Salam said: Has the Messenger of Allah ﷺ not said: \"If anyone is seated waiting for the prayer, he is engaged in the prayer until he observes it.\" I said: Yes, it is so. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1046)"],[1024,"I came to al-Tur and met Kaʿb al-Ahbar there. I narrated to him from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he narrated from the Torah, and they did not differ until I came to the day of Jumuʿah. He said: I said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'In every Friday there is an hour in which no believer coincides with it while praying, asking Allah for something, except that He gives it to him.'\" Kaʿb said, \"Is that in every year?\" I said, \"That is not what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.\" He returned and recited, then said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth: it is in every Friday.\" Abu Hurayrah said: Then I met Abdullah b. Salam and told him about my sitting with Kaʿb, \"and he mentioned the hadith in a manner similar to the hadith of Malik.\""],[1025,"\"The day of Jumuʿah has twelve hours. There is no Muslim servant who asks Allah for something at any of them except that Allah gives it to him. So seek it in the last hour after ʿAsr.\""],[1026,"I said, \"By Allah, if I went to Abu Saʿid al-Khudri and asked him about this hour, perhaps he would have some knowledge of it.\" So I came to him and said, \"O Abu Saʿid, indeed Abu Hurayrah...\""],[1027,"\"Whoever abandons three Jumuʿahs out of negligence toward them, Allah will set a seal upon his heart.\""],[1028,"Whoever omits the Friday prayer without an excuse, let him give a dinar in charity; if he cannot find it, then half a dinar."],[1029,"Whoever misses the Friday prayer without an excuse, let him give a dirham or half a dirham, or a saa of wheat, or half a saa, in charity."],[1030,"Hammam, in our view, has a stronger memory than Ayyub b. al-ʿAlaʾ."],[1031,"Two men from Iraq came to him and asked about performing the Friday bath, is it obligatory? Ibn Abbas said to them, \"Whoever performs the bath, it is better and purer.\" Then he informed them that at the beginning of performing the bath, during the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , people used to be in need, wearing wool, and water from palm trees would be poured on their backs. The mosque was narrow, reaching close to the ceiling. On a hot summer day, the Prophet ﷺ came out on Friday and his pulpit was short, consisting of only three steps. He addressed the people, and the people sweated profusely in their wool garments. The smell of sweat and wool filled the air to the point where some people were harming each other. Finally, the smell reached the Prophet while he was on the pulpit, and he said, \"O people, if it is this day, then perform the bath and let each one of you apply the best fragrance or perfume that he can find.\""],[1032,"I was the leader of my father when his eyesight deteriorated, so I went with him to the Friday prayer. When he heard the call to prayer, he prayed for Abu Umamah As'ad bin Zurarah and sought forgiveness for him. So I stayed for a long time without hearing the call to Friday prayer until he did that. So I said, \"Oh father, do you see your seeking forgiveness for Abu Umamah every time you hear the call to Friday prayer?\" He said, \"O my son, he was the first one to gather with us in Madinah during the Battle of Khandaq from the tribe of Banu Bayadah, which is called Naqiyah Al-Khadamat.\" I said, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Forty men.\""],[1033,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, mentioning Friday: 'Whoever washes and performs the major ablution, goes early and comes early, draws near, remains silent and listens, will be forgiven for what is between that Friday and the next, with an addition of three days. And whoever touches the pebbles has engaged in idle talk.' Narrated by Yahya b. al-Harith al-Dhimari and Hassan b. ʿAtiyya from Abu al-Ashʿath. It was narrated exclusively by Ibrahim b. Abi al-Layth from al-Ashjaʿi, and he is weak, and its wording is objectionable, but others corroborated him."],[1034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever washes and purifies himself, then goes early and sits close to the Imam, listening and being attentive, will have the reward of fasting and praying the whole year for every step he takes.\""],[1035,"Whoever washes and performs the major ablution on Friday, then goes early and comes early, draws near and listens and does not engage in idle talk, for every step he takes he gets the reward of a year's deeds: the reward of its standing in prayer and its fasting."],[1036,"Whoever washes on Friday and performs the major ablution, draws near to the imam and comes close, listens and remains silent, for every step he takes he gets the reward of fasting and praying at night for a year."],[1037,"My father came in upon me while I was performing the major ablution on Friday and said, 'Is this a major ablution due to janabah or for Friday?' I said, 'Due to janabah.' He said, 'Perform another ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever performs the major ablution on Friday remains in a state of purification until the next Friday.\"'"],[1038,"Whoever washes on Friday, uses the tooth-stick, wears his best clothes, applies perfume if he can find it, then comes and does not step over people, and prays as much as Allah wills, then remains silent when the imam comes out, that atones for his sins until the next Friday."],[1039,"Whoever performs the major ablution on Friday, uses the tooth-stick, applies some perfume if he has it, wears his best clothes, then comes to the mosque without stepping over people's necks, then prays as much as Allah wills, then remains silent when his imam comes out until he prays, this will be an atonement for him for what is between that Friday and the previous Friday.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"And three extra days, for Allah has made a good deed equal to ten times its like."],[1040,"When the Prophet ﷺ came out on Friday and sat on the pulpit, Bilal gave the call to prayer."],[1041,"The Prophet ﷺ ascended the pulpit on Friday and said to the people, \"Sit down.\" Ibn Mas'ood heard it while he was at the door of the mosque, so he sat down. The Prophet ﷺ then said to him, \"Come, O Ibn Mas'ood.\""],[1042,"Ibn ʿAbbas said to his mu'adhdhin on a rainy day, 'When you say \"I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah\", do not say \"Come to prayer\", but say \"Pray in your homes\".' The people seemed to disapprove of that, so he said, 'One who is better than me did that. The Friday prayer is obligatory, but I disliked bringing you out so that you would walk in mud and water.'"],[1043,"I did not memorize [Surah] Qaf except from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who used to recite it every Friday.\" She said: \"Our oven and the oven of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were one."],[1044,"\"I recited Qaf. By the Glorious Quran from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he used to recite it every Friday when he addressed the people.\" Yahya b. Abdullah is Ibn Abd al-Rahman b. Asʿad b. Zurara."],[1045,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us one day and recited Sad. When he came to the prostration, he descended and prostrated, and we prostrated. He recited it another time, and when he came to the prostration, we prepared ourselves for prostration. When he saw us, he said, \"It is only the repentance of a prophet, but I see that you have prepared yourselves for prostration.\" So he descended and prostrated, and we prostrated. And"],[1046,"When I approached the city of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I made my mount kneel, untied my bag, put on my fine garment, and entered while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ greeted me, and the people stared at me. I said to my companion, \"O Abdullah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention anything about me?\" He said, \"Yes, he mentioned you with the best mention. He said: 'Indeed, there will enter upon you from this door, or from this mountain pass, one of the best of those blessed, and on his face is the touch of an angel.'\" So I praised Allah for what He had bestowed upon me."],[1047,"Abu Saʿid al-Khudri entered on Friday while Marwan b. al-Hakam was delivering the sermon. He stood up to pray, and the guards came to make him sit, but he refused until he had prayed. When Marwan finished, we came to him and said, \"May Allah have mercy on you, they almost did something to you.\" He said, \"I would not leave it after something I saw from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Then he mentioned a man who came on Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and then came on the following Friday while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the people to give charity, so the man threw one of his two garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed, then rebuked him and said, \"Take your garment.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This man entered in a shabby appearance, so I ordered the people to give charity, and this one threw one of his two garments.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to pray two rakʿahs."],[1048,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was delivering the sermon and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a stranger has come asking about his religion, not knowing what his religion is.\" He turned to me, left his sermon, and a chair with iron legs was brought. He began teaching me from what Allah had taught him, then he returned to his sermon and completed its end. On the condition of Muslim."],[1049,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ settled on the pulpit, he said, \"Sit down.\" Ibn Masʿud heard him and sat at the door of the mosque. The Prophet ﷺ saw him and said, \"Come here, O Abdullah b. Masʿud.\""],[1050,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to deliver the sermon sitting on the pulpit. He denied it, saying, \"I witnessed him: he used to deliver the sermon standing, then sit, then stand and deliver another sermon.\" He said: I said, \"How was his sermon?\" He said, \"Words with which he exhorted the people and recited verses from the Book of Allah, then descended. It was moderate, meaning his sermon, and his prayer was moderate, about the length of al-Shams, Duha, al-Samaʾ, and al-Tariq, except the morning prayer and the noon prayer. Bilal would give the call to prayer when the sun declined; if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, he would give the iqamah, otherwise he would remain silent until he came out. The afternoon prayer was about the time you pray it, the sunset prayer was about the time you pray it, and the late evening prayer he would delay a little from your prayer.\""],[1051,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering the sermon saying, \"Have I warned you of the Fire? Have I warned you of the Fire?\" until even a man in the market would have heard it from this place of mine, until his cloak fell from his shoulder to his feet."],[1052,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon when al-Hasan and al-Husayn came forward wearing two red shirts, stumbling and getting up. He descended, took them, and placed them in front of him. Then he said, \"Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth: {Indeed, your wealth and your children are only a trial} [al-Taghabun 15]. I saw these two sons of mine and could not bear it until I descended and took them.\" Then he resumed his sermon. This is a sound hadith on the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it. It is a basis for interrupting the sermon and descending from the pulpit when necessary. On the condition of Muslim."],[1053,"I entered the mosque while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and I sat near Ubayy b. Kaʿb. The Prophet ﷺ recited Surah Baraʾah. I said to Ubayy, \"When was this surah revealed?\" The hadith."],[1054,"He was narrating to us until the imam came out. Then a man came stepping over people's necks while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering the sermon. He said to him, \"Sit down, for you have caused harm and come late.\""],[1055,"The Friday prayer is a right and obligatory upon every Muslim in congregation, except four: an owned slave, a woman, a child, or a sick person."],[1056,"Ilyas ibn AbuRamlah ash-Shami said: I witnessed Mu'awiyah ibn AbuSufyan asking Zayd ibn Arqam: Did you offer along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the Friday and 'Id prayers synchronised on the same day? He said: Yes. He asked: How did he do? He replied: He offered the 'Id prayer, then granted concession to offer the Friday prayer, and said: If anyone wants to offer it, he may offer. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1070)"],[1057,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Two festivals ('Id and Friday) have synchronised on this day. If anyone does not want to offer the Friday prayer, the 'Id prayer is sufficient for him. But we shall offer the Friday prayer. This tradition has been narrated by 'Umar from Shu'bah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1073)"],[1058,"A speaker gave sermon before the prophet (May peace be upon him). He said : he who obeys Allah and his Prophet will follow the right course, and he who disobeys them. He (The prophet) said: get up; he said: go away, a bad speaker you are. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4981)"],[1059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to shorten the sermons."],[1060,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not prolong the exhortation on Friday; they were only brief words."],[1061,"Attend the remembrance and draw near to the imam, for a man will keep distancing himself until he is delayed in Paradise, even if he enters it."],[1062,"He forbade sitting with the knees drawn up on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon."],[1063,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come down from the pulpit, and a man would approach him for a need, and he would stand with him until he fulfilled his need."],[1064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in his chamber while the people followed him from behind the chamber."],[1065,"When he was in Makkah and prayed the Friday prayer, he would step forward and pray two rakʿahs, then step forward and pray four. When he was in Madinah, he would pray the Friday prayer, then return to his house and pray two rakʿahs, and he would not pray in the mosque. It was said to him, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that.\""],[1066,"That he saw Ibn ʿUmar praying on Friday, and he would step forward from the place where he had prayed the Friday prayer a little, not much, and pray two rakʿahs. He said: \"Then he would walk a bit further than that and pray four rakʿahs.\" I said to ʿAtaʾ: \"How many times did you see Ibn ʿUmar do that?\" He said: \"Many times.\""],[1067,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, does it well, purifies himself, does the purification well, wears the best of his clothes, and applies some of what Allah has decreed for him of perfume or the oil of his family, and does not separate between two people, Allah will forgive him until the next Friday."],[1068,"When one of you becomes drowsy on Friday in his sitting place, let him move from that sitting place."],[1069,"We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we would hasten to the shade, and it would only be about a foot or two."],[1070,"Whoever catches one rakʿah of the Friday prayer has caught the prayer."],[1071,"From Abū Hurayrah."],[1072,"\"Whoever catches one rakʿah of Friday prayer, let him add another to it.\""],[1073,"\"I was determined to order a man to lead the people in prayer, then burn the houses of a people who stay away from Friday prayer.\""],[1074,"\"Whoever neglects Friday prayer three times without necessity, Allah will set a seal upon his heart.\""],[1075,"From Abu al-Jaʿd al-Ḍamrī — and I declared it authentic according to Muslim's criterion, and this is the high witness that I found afterward, and it has another witness from the hadith of Muḥammad b. ʿAjlān, authentic according to Muslim's criterion, and they did not include it — ṣaḥīḥ."],[1076,"\"Indeed, would one of you take a small flock of sheep at the distance of a mile or two, and then the pasture become difficult for him at a mile or two, so he goes up until Friday comes and he does not attend it, until a seal is placed upon his heart.\""],[1077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When there is heavy rain, then pray in your dwellings.\" Nāṣiḥ b. al-ʿAlāʾ is a Basran, trustworthy. The one who is criticized is Nāṣiḥ Abū ʿAbd Allāh al-Muḥallimī al-Kūfī, for Simāk b. Ḥarb narrated rejected reports from him. Al-Nasāʾī deemed him weak, meaning Nāṣiḥ b. al-ʿAlāʾ, and al-Bukhārī said: munkar al-ḥadīth."],[1078,"He witnessed the Prophet ﷺ at the time of al-Ḥudaybiyyah, and rain fell upon them on a Friday but did not wet the bottoms of their sandals. \"So the Prophet ﷺ commanded them to pray in their dwellings.\" This is a hadith with an authentic chain, and the two shaykhs have used its narrators as proof. It is of the type in which they sought a follow-up for the tābiʿī from the Companion, and they did not include it. ṣaḥīḥ."],[1079,"Nāfiʿ b. Jubayr sent him to al-Sāʾib b. Yazīd to ask him about something Muʿāwiyah had seen him do. He said: I prayed with him in the maqṣūrah, then I stood to pray in my place, and he said: \"Do not pray until you move forward from that spot or speak, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to do that.\""],[1080,"\"None of you should make his brother get up from his seat and then take his place in it.\" I said to him: We are on Friday. He said: \"On Friday and other days.\""],[1081,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not go out on the day of fiṭr until he had eaten, and he would not eat on the day of naḥr until he returned.\""],[1082,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would break his fast on the day of fiṭr with some dates before going out.\""],[1083,"I heard Anas say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not go out on the day of Fitr until he had eaten three dates, or five, or seven, or fewer than that, or more than that, an odd number.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[1084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while they had two days on which they played. He said: “What are these two days?” They said: “Two days on which we used to play in the Jahiliyyah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed Allah has replaced them for you with two better than them: the day of Adha and the day of Fitr.”"],[1085,"Abdullah b. Busr, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, went out with the people on the day of Eid al-Fitr or Adha and objected to the imam's lateness, saying: “We were with the Prophet ﷺ and had finished by this hour of ours, and that was at the time of glorification.”"],[1086,"I attended the Eid prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he finished the prayer he said: “We shall deliver the sermon, so whoever wishes to sit for the sermon, let him sit, and whoever wishes to leave, let him leave.” This is a sahih hadith according to the conditions of the two shaykhs but they did not include it. It is the meaning of the hadith that is asked about regarding the Eids, except that it is from Ibn Abbas according to the conditions of the two shaykhs."],[1087,"He heard Abu Yahya Ubayd Allah al-Taymi narrate from Abu Hurayrah that rain fell on them on a day of Eid, “so the Prophet ﷺ led them in the Eid prayer in the mosque.” This hadith has a sahih chain but they did not include it. Abu Yahya al-Taymi is truthful; only his son Yahya b. Ubayd Allah is criticized, according to their conditions."],[1088,"He went out on a day of Eid to the prayer place and did not pray before it or after it, and he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ did that."],[1089,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed before the sermon on a day of Eid. This is the wording of the hadith of Ahmad b. Abdah, and in the hadith of Sulayman there is some omission."],[1090,"I witnessed Ibn al-Zubayr in Mecca while he was the emir, and it happened to be either the day of Fitr or Adha coinciding with a Friday. He delayed going out until the day had risen high, then he went out and ascended the pulpit, delivered a lengthy sermon, and then performed two rak'ahs (units of prayer) and did not perform the Friday prayer. Some people from Banu Umayya ibn Abd Shams reproached him for this. When Ibn Abbas heard about it, he said, \"Ibn al-Zubayr has followed the Sunnah.\" When Ibn al-Zubayr heard about Ibn Abbas's comment, he said, \"I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab do the same thing when both Eids coincided.\""],[1091,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took one route on a day of Eid and then returned by another route."],[1092,"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ went out to the two Eid prayers, he would return by a route different from the one he took going out."],[1093,"I used to go early with the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the prayer place on the day of Fitr, and we would travel through the middle of Buthan until we came to the prayer place, then we would pray with the Prophet ﷺ, then we would return to our homes."],[1094,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would go out on the day of Fitr and pray those two rak’ahs, then say the taslim, then stand and face the people while they were seated, and say: “Give charity, give charity.” The majority of those who gave charity were women, with earrings and rings."],[1095,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the prayer place, he would pray two rak’ahs. This is a rare sunnah with a sahih chain, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[1096,"The people began the day fasting to complete thirty, then two men came and testified that they had seen the crescent the previous day, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the people, and they broke their fast."],[1097,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I saw the crescent tonight.' He said, 'Do you testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Arise, O Bilal, and announce to the people that they should fast.' Al-Bukhari used ʿIkrimah as evidence, and Muslim used Simāk."],[1098,"He used to say takbīr on the day of Fiṭr from the time he left his house until he reached the prayer place."],[1099,"He used to go out on the two ʿĪds from the mosque saying takbīr until he reached the prayer place."],[1100,"They were more emphatic in takbīr on Fiṭr than on Aḍḥā."],[1101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say twelve takbīrs in the two ʿĪds besides the opening takbīr, and he would recite 'Qāf. By the glorious Qurʾān' and 'The Hour has drawn near'."],[1102,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say seven takbīrs in the first rakʿah and five takbīrs in the second before the recitation in the two ʿĪds."],[1103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abū Bakr, and ʿUmar used to pray the two ʿĪds before the sermon."],[1104,"He used to recite aloud 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful' in the obligatory prayers, and he used to perform qunūt in the dawn prayer, and he used to say takbīr from the day of ʿArafah at the dawn prayer and stop it at the ʿAṣr prayer on the last of the days of Tashrīq."],[1105,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb used to say takbīr after the dawn prayer from the day of ʿArafah until the Ẓuhr prayer on the last of the days of Tashrīq."],[1106,"ʿAlī used to say takbīr after the dawn prayer on the morning of ʿArafah, then he would not stop until the imam prayed on the last of the days of Tashrīq, then he would say takbīr after ʿAṣr."],[1107,"He used to say takbīr from the morning of ʿArafah until the ʿAṣr prayer on the last of the days of Tashrīq."],[1108,"Ibn Masʿūd came to us, and he used to say the takbīr from the dawn prayer on the day of ʿArafah until the afternoon prayer on the last of the days of tashrīq."],[1109,"He was asked about the takbīr on the day of ʿArafah, and he said: 'The takbīr is said from the morning of ʿArafah until the last of the days of tashrīq, as ʿAlī and ʿAbdullāh said the takbīr.'"],[1110,"\"A good practice, performed by the Prophet ﷺ and Muslims after him, but it is not obligatory.\""],[1111,"‘Ali ؓ said: Verily, Witr is not a must like your prescribed prayers, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Witr, then he said: “Pray Witr, O people of the Qurʿan. Pray Witr, for Allah is One and loves that which is odd numbered.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1262)"],[1112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There are three obligations upon me, and optional acts for you: the sacrifice, Witr prayer, and the two units of prayer before Fajr prayer."],[1113,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abū Bakr: 'When do you perform witr?' He said: 'I perform witr before I sleep.' And he said to ʿUmar: 'When do you perform witr?' He said: 'I sleep, then I perform witr.' So he said to Abū Bakr: 'You have taken hold of the firmest option' or 'of the surest option,' and he said to ʿUmar: 'You have taken hold of strength.'"],[1114,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abū Bakr: 'When do you perform witr?' He said: 'I perform witr, then I sleep.' He said: 'You have taken hold of the firmest option.' And he asked ʿUmar: 'When do you perform witr?' He said: 'I sleep, then I get up during the night and perform witr.' He said: 'You have done the deed of the strong one.' Ṣaḥīḥ."],[1115,"\"That Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri informed them that they asked the Prophet ﷺ about Al-Witr (a prayer performed in odd numbers) and he said, 'Perform Witr before the Fajr (dawn) prayer.' Ma'mar ibn Rashid continued, narrating from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir.\""],[1116,"Observe Witr prayer before it is morning. Abu Sa'id reported that they (the Prophet's Companions) asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Witr (prayer). (In reply to their inquiry) he said: Observe Witr prayer before it is morning. (Using translation from Muslim 754a)"],[1117,"The messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Hasten to perform the Witr (odd) prayer before dawn.\" Sahih (authentic)."],[1118,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Whoever experiences dawn and does not perform the Witr prayer, there is no Witr prayer for them.\""],[1119,"Ibn Umar used to say: \"Whoever prays at night, let him make the Witr prayer his last prayer. For the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that. So, when it is dawn, the night prayer and the Witr are gone. For the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Perform the Witr prayer before dawn.'\" (Sahih)"],[1120,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone oversleeps and misses the witr, or forgets it, he should pray when he remembers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1431)"],[1121,"“Witr is Haqq.* Whoever wishes let him pray Witr with five (Rak’ah), and whoever wishes let him pray Witr with three (Rak’ah), and whoever wishes let him pray Witr with one (Rak’ah).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1190)"],[1122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Odd numbers for prayers of Witr are either five, three, or one.\""],[1123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Witr is a confirmed duty; whoever wishes may perform it with three (units), and whoever wishes may perform it with five, and whoever would like to perform witr with one (unit), let him perform it with one.”"],[1124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perform Witr prayer in odd numbers, and if you are unable, then perform it in three, and if you are still unable, then perform it in one.\""],[1125,"That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, \"Witr (odd number of units for prayer) is a right (obligation).\" So he mentioned it in this way and they left it."],[1126,"\"Al-Witr is a right\" so Abu Ayyub mentioned it repeatedly."],[1127,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Witr (the nightly odd numbered prayer) is a right (that it should be performed).\" Then the narrated something similar.[1]"],[1128,"Perhaps I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying witr (odd numbered night prayer) while the people were standing for Fajr prayer."],[1129,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you wakes up in the morning and has not performed the Witr prayer, let them perform it.\""],[1130,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not perform Witr (the odd numbered nightly prayer) to three rakahs making is seem like the Maghrib prayer. Rather extend it to five, or seven, nine, or eleven rakahs, or even more than that.\""],[1131,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not perform Witr (the odd numbered nightly prayer) to three rakahs making is seem like the Maghrib prayer. Rather extend it to five, or seven.\""],[1132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not offer the taslim (salam) after the first two rakahs of the Witr prayer."],[1133,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with three rakahs, and he would do the taslim only in the last rakah. And this is the Witr prayer of Amir al-Muminin, Umar b. al-Khattab\"[1]"],[1134,"It was said to Al-Hasan that Ibn Umar used to do the taslim after the two rakahs of Witr. He replied, \"Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was more knowledgeable than him; he would rise up for the third rakah with the takbir.\""],[1135,"He used to perform the Witr prayer with three rakahs without the tashahhud (sitting) in between them, and he would not do the tashahhud except in the last rakah.\""],[1136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the two Rak'ahs of Witr after them \"Subhanallahi Walhamdulillahi Wa La Ilaha Illallah Wallahu Akbar\" (Glorified is Allah, and praised is Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest), and recite in Witr \"Qul Huwallahu Ahad\" (Say, He is Allah, the One), and say \"A'udhu bi Rabbil Falaq\" (I seek refuge with the Lord of Daybreak), and say \"A'udhu bi Rabbin Nas\" (I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind). Sa'id bin Abi Maryam narrated it from Yahya bin Ayyub."],[1137,"The translation is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform the Witr prayer with three units. In the first unit, he would recite \"Subhanak Allahumma wa bihamdika, tabarakasmuka, wa ta'ala jadduka, wa la ilaha ghairuka\" (Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. Blessed is Your name and exalted is Your majesty. There is no deity worthy of worship except You). In the second unit, he would recite \"Qul ya ayyuhal kafirun\" (Say, O disbelievers). And in the third unit, he would recite \"Qul huwa Allahu ahad\" (Say, He is Allah, the One). Then he would seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak (Al-Falaq) and seek refuge in the Lord of mankind (An-Nas).\"[1]"],[1138,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Tahiyyatul-Wudu (a prayer after performing ablution) consisting of five units (rak'ahs). He would not sit down except in the fifth unit, and he would only give the salaam (conclude the prayer) in the fifth unit."],[1139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Witr (odd-numbered prayers) is a right, so whoever does not perform Witr is not among us.\""],[1140,"The passage translates to: \"He mentioned it similarly, 'This is an authentic hadith.' Abu Al-Munib Al-Ataki from Marw is trustworthy, and his hadith is compiled.\""],[1141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: Allah the Exalted has given you an extra prayer which is better for you then the red camels (i.e. high breed camels). This is the witr which Allah has appointed for you between the night prayer and the daybreak. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1418)"],[1142,"\"The Prophet would perform Witr with thirteen [Rak'ah]. When he was older and became weak he performed Witr with seven.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 457)"],[1143,"It was narrated from ʿAli ؓ that The Prophet ﷺ used to say at the end of his Witr ʿO Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot praise You enough, You are as You have praised Yourself.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 751)"],[1144,"'The two rakʿahs of Fajr are better than the entire world.'"],[1145,"The most that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the two rakʿahs of Fajr was {Say: We believe in Allah and what has been sent down to us and what was sent down to Ibrāhīm} [al-Baqarah:136] to the end of the verse, and in the second rakʿah {Say: O People of the Book, come to a word that is equitable between us and you} [Āl ʿImrān:64] up to His saying {and bear witness that we are Muslims} [Āl ʿImrān:52]."],[1146,"'Whoever forgets the two rakʿahs of Fajr, let him pray them when the sun has risen.'"],[1147,"The prayer was called, so I stood to pray the two rakʿahs, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pulled me and said: 'Will you pray the morning prayer as four?'"],[1148,"He was asked: Which prayer is best after the prescribed one, and which fasting is best after the month of Ramaḍān? He said: 'The best prayer after the prescribed one is prayer in the middle of the night, and the best fasting after the month of Ramaḍān is the month of Allah, al-Muḥarram.'"],[1149,"'You must observe night prayer, for it is the practice of the righteous before you, and it is a means of drawing near to your Lord, an expiation for misdeeds, and a deterrent from sin.'"],[1150,"One night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ found something, and when morning came it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the trace of the pain is evident upon you. He said: 'I am only, as you see, by the praise of Allah; I have recited the seven long sūrahs.'"],[1151,"ʿĀʾishah said to me: Do not abandon night prayer, 'for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never abandoned it, and when he was ill or felt sluggish, he would pray sitting.'"],[1152,"Shu'bah narrated to us, and he mentioned it with the same chain and text entirely."],[1153,"\"Whoever guards these prescribed prayers will not be written among the heedless, and whoever recites one hundred verses in a night will be written among the devout.\""],[1154,"\"Whoever prays one hundred verses in a night will not be written among the heedless, and whoever prays two hundred verses in a night will be written among the devout and sincere.\""],[1155,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was encamped at 'Ukaz and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there any supplication closer than another, or an hour that remains or should be remembered?\" He said, \"Yes, the closest the Lord is to the servant is in the last part of the night, so if you can be among those who remember Allah in that hour, then be so.\""],[1156,"Indeed, Allah guided His Prophet to a proof, so he said to them, \"Guide me to what my Prophet ﷺ guided to.\" So, they said, \"Indeed, Allah guided him to the Night Prayer.\""],[1157,"\"May Allah have mercy on a man who gets up at night, prays, and wakes his wife; if she refuses, he sprinkles water on her face. May Allah have mercy on a woman who gets up at night, prays, and wakes her husband; if he refuses, she sprinkles water on his face.\""],[1158,"He asked Umm Salamah about the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night. She said, \"What concern is it of yours with his prayer? He would pray, then sleep as long as he had prayed, then pray as long as he had slept, then sleep as long as he had prayed, until morning.\" She described his recitation to him, and it was a clear, letter-by-letter recitation."],[1159,"When he rose at night, he would raise his voice at times and lower it at times, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[1160,"He asked 'A'ishah, \"How was the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night? Did he recite aloud or quietly?\" She said, \"He did all of that: sometimes aloud and sometimes quietly.\" He said, \"Praise be to Allah who has made the matter broad.\""],[1161,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Abu Bakr while he was praying and lowering his voice, and he passed by 'Umar while he was praying and raising his voice. When they gathered with the Prophet ﷺ, he said to Abu Bakr, \"O Abu Bakr, I passed by you while you were praying and lowering your voice?\" He said, \"I made it audible to the One I was confiding in.\" Then he said, \"I passed by you, O 'Umar, while you were raising your voice?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I seek reward by it and wake the drowsy.\" He said to Abu Bakr, \"Raise your voice a little,\" and to 'Umar, \"Lower your voice.\""],[1162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ retired to the mosque. He heard them (the people) reciting the Qur'an in a loud voice. He removed the curtain and said: Lo! every one of you is calling his Lord quietly. One should not trouble the other and one should not raise the voice in recitation or in prayer over the voice of the other. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1332)"],[1163,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever goes to bed intending to stand (in prayer) during the night, but his eyes overpower him (i.e., he falls asleep) until morning, then his intention will be recorded for him, and his sleep will be a charity from his Lord.\""],[1164,"Abu Bakr b. Ishaq narrated to us, Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Nadr informed us, Mu'awiyah b. 'Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, and he mentioned it with its chain from the saying of Abu al-Darda'. This does not weaken it, for al-Husayn b. 'Ali al-Ju'fi is older, more retentive, and more knowledgeable of the hadith of Za'idah than others, and Allah knows best."],[1165,"\"Do not single out Friday for fasting among the days, and do not single out Friday night for night prayer among the nights.\""],[1166,"\"Whoever prays twelve rak'ahs in a day, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise: four before Zuhr, two after it, two before 'Asr, two after Maghrib, and two before Subh.\""],[1167,"Whoever prays twelve prostrations voluntarily, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."],[1168,"Whoever consistently performs four rak'ahs before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid him to the Fire."],[1169,"Buraydah said: I went out one day walking for a need, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walking. I thought he wanted something, so I kept away from him, and I continued doing that until he saw me and gestured to me. I came to him, and he took my hand, and we went off walking together. Then I saw a man in front of us praying, performing many bowings and prostrations. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you think this man is showing off?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, then he let go of his hand and clasped his hands three times, raising and lowering them, saying, \"Upon you is a moderate way; upon you is a moderate way, for whoever contends with this religion will be overcome by it.\""],[1170,"He prayed Maghrib with the Prophet ﷺ, then he prayed until he prayed 'Isha'."],[1171,"Honor your homes with some of your prayers."],[1172,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up and called Bilal, saying, \"O Bilal, how have you preceded me to Paradise? Last night I entered Paradise and heard the rustling of your footsteps ahead of me.\" Bilal said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have never called the adhan but that I prayed two rak'ahs, and I have never had a ritual impurity but that I performed wudu' at that time.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is because of this.\""],[1173,"A blind man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Supplicate Allah to heal me.\" He said, \"If you wish, you may postpone that, and it is better; and if you wish, I will supplicate.\" He said, \"Supplicate.\" He said, and he ordered him to perform wudu' and perfect his wudu', then pray two rak'ahs and supplicate with this supplication, saying: \"O Allah, I ask You and turn to You through Your Prophet Muhammad, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I have turned through you to my Lord concerning this need of mine, that it may be fulfilled. O Allah, accept his intercession for me and accept my intercession for him.\""],[1174,"Keep the proposal secret, then perform wudu' and perfect your wudu', then pray what Allah has decreed for you, then praise your Lord and extol Him, then say: 'O Allah, You are able and I am not able, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see that [name of woman]—naming her—is good for me in my religion, my worldly life, and my Hereafter, then decree her for me; and if someone other than her is better for me than her in my religion, my worldly life, and my Hereafter, then decree her for me,' or say: 'then decree her for me.' This is the Sunnah of the prayer of Istikharah, rare, unique to the people of Egypt, and its narrators to the last are trustworthy, but they did not include it in the two Sahihs."],[1175,"No one consistently performs the Duha prayer except the oft-returning to Allah.\" He said, \"And it is the prayer of the oft-returning."],[1176,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during a journey praying the Duha voluntary prayer, eight rak'ahs. When he finished, he said, \"I prayed a prayer of desire and fear, and I asked my Lord for three things. He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my nation by famine, and He did so; I asked Him not to give their enemy dominance over them, and He did so; and I asked Him not to make them into factions, and He refused me.\""],[1177,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not die until most of his prayer was performed sitting."],[1178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray standing and sitting. When he began the prayer standing, he bowed standing; and when he began the prayer sitting, he bowed sitting."],[1179,"I had a fistula, so I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Pray standing; if you cannot, then sitting; and if you cannot, then on your side.”"],[1180,"He said, “I traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on eighteen journeys, and I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ abandon the two rak'ahs when the sun declines.”"],[1181,"The Prophet ﷺ would not alight at any place except that he bid it farewell with two rak'ahs."],[1182,"Whoever wakes up at night and wakes his family, and they pray two rak'ahs together, they are recorded among the men who remember Allah much and the women who remember."],[1183,"While he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ʿAli b. Abi Talib came to him and said, “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah! This Qur'an has slipped from my chest, and I find that I cannot hold onto it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O Abu al-Hasan, shall I not teach you words by which Allah will benefit you and benefit those you teach, and which will fix what you have learned in your chest?” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, teach me.” He said, “When it is Friday night, if you are able to stand in the last third of the night, for it is a witnessed hour and supplication in it is answered—and it is the saying of my brother Yaʿqub to his sons: ‘I will ask forgiveness for you from my Lord’—until Friday night comes. If you cannot, then stand in its middle; if you cannot, then stand in its beginning. Then pray four rak'ahs. In the first, recite the Opening of the Book and Surah Yasin; in the second rak'ah, the Opening of the Book and Alif Lam Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah; in the third rak'ah, the Opening of the Book and Ha Mim al-Dukhan; and in the fourth rak'ah, the Opening of the Book and Tabarak al-Mufassal. When you finish the tashahhud, praise Allah, extol Allah with the best praise, send blessings upon me and upon all the prophets, praise well, seek forgiveness for your brothers who preceded you in faith, and seek forgiveness for the believing men and the believing women. Then say at the end of that: ‘O Allah, have mercy on me by enabling me to abandon sins forever as long as You keep me alive; have mercy on me from burdening myself with what does not concern me; and grant me good insight into what pleases You from me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honor and might that cannot be rivaled, I ask You, O Allah, O Most Merciful, by Your majesty and the light of Your face, to make my heart cling to memorizing Your Book as You taught me, and to enable me to recite it in the manner that pleases You from me. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honor and might that cannot be rivaled, I ask You, O Allah, O Most Merciful, by Your majesty and the light of Your face, to illuminate my sight with Your Book, release my tongue through it, dispel distress from my heart through it, expand my chest through it, and occupy my body with it. For none helps me upon the truth except You, and none grants it except You, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah, the Most High, the Most Great.’ Do this, Abu al-Hasan, for three Fridays, or five, or seven, and you will be answered by Allah's permission. By the One who sent me with the truth, it never fails a believer.” ʿAbdullah b. ʿAbbas said, “By Allah, ʿAli did not tarry except five or seven nights before he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a similar gathering and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, previously I would not learn four verses or so without them slipping away when I recited them to myself. But today I learn forty verses or so, and when I recite them to myself, it is as if the Book of Allah is before my eyes. I used to hear a hadith and it would slip away when I wanted it, but today I hear hadiths and when I narrate them, I do not omit a single letter.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him then, ‘A believer, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah, O Abu al-Hasan.’”"],[1184,"Umm Sulaym went to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Teach me words to say in my prayer.” He said, “Say Allahu akbar ten times, glorify Allah ten times—or praise Him ten times—then ask whatever you wish. He says, ‘Yes, yes.’”"],[1185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to al-ʿAbbas b. ʿAbd al-Muttalib, “O ʿAbbas, O my uncle, shall I not give you? Shall I not bestow upon you? Shall I not do for you ten qualities—if you do that, Allah will forgive your sin, the first of it and the last of it, the old of it and the new of it, its error and its deliberate commission, its small and its great, its secret and its open? You pray four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah the Opening of the Book and a surah. When you finish the recitation in the first rak'ah, while standing you say: ‘Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great’ fifteen times. Then you bow and say it ten times while bowing. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. That is seventy-five in each rak'ah. Do this in four rak'ahs. If you can pray it every day, do so; if not, then once every Friday; if not, then once every month; if not, then once every year; if not, then once in your lifetime.”"],[1186,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his uncle al-ʿAbbas—and he mentioned the hadith. “This mursal transmission does not weaken the connected hadith, for the addition of a trustworthy narrator is preferable to mursal transmission. Moreover, the imam of his age in hadith, Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Hanzali, established this isnad from Ibrahim b. al-Hakam b. Aban and connected it.”"],[1187,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Musa b. ʿAbd al-ʿAziz from al-Hakam. “The narration from ʿAbdullah b. ʿUmar b. al-Khattab is authentic that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught this prayer to his cousin Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib, just as he taught it to his uncle al-ʿAbbas ؓ.”"],[1188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Jaʿfar b. Abi Talib to the land of Abyssinia. When he arrived, he embraced him and kissed him between his eyes, then said, “Shall I not grant you something? Shall I not give you glad tidings? Shall I not bestow upon you? Shall I not gift you?” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Pray four rak'ahs, reciting in each rak'ah the Opening of the Book and a surah. Then after the recitation, while standing before bowing, say: ‘Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is most great, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah’ fifteen times. Then bow and say them ten times, completing this rak'ah before beginning the second. Do this in the three rak'ahs as I described to you until you complete four rak'ahs.” “This is a sound isnad, free from defect. Among the evidence for the authenticity of this hadith is the practice of the imams from the followers of the Followers up to our own time, their persistence in it, and their teaching it to people—among them ʿAbdullah b. al-Mubarak, may Allah have mercy on him.”"],[1189,"I asked ʿAbdullah b. al-Mubarak about the prayer in which glorification is performed. He said, “You say takbir, then say: ‘Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; blessed is Your name, exalted is Your majesty, and there is no god other than You.’ Then you say fifteen times: ‘Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great.’ Then you seek refuge and recite ‘In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate,’ the Opening of the Book, and a surah. Then you say ten times: ‘Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is most great.’ Then you bow and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. Then you prostrate and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. Then you make the second prostration and say it ten times. Then you raise your head and say it ten times. You pray four rak'ahs in this manner. That is seventy-five glorifications in each rak'ah, making a total of three hundred. If he prays it at night, I prefer that he say the salam after two rak'ahs. If he prays it during the day, he may say the salam or not, as he wishes.”"],[1190,"The two rak'ahs before the dawn prayer are at the setting of the stars, and the two rak'ahs after sunset are at the passing of the pre-dawn meal."],[1191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day and sat down, then said: 'Whoever has a need from Allah or from any of the children of Adam, let him perform ablution and perfect his ablution, then pray two rak'ahs, then praise Allah, and invoke blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, and say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. I ask You for the determinations of Your forgiveness, protection from every sin, and safety from every wrongdoing.' Fā'id b. 'Abd al-Raḥmān Abū al-Warqā' is a Kufan, counted among the successors. I have seen a group of his descendants, and he is upright in hadith, except that the two shaykhs did not transmit from him. I have made this hadith of his only as a corroborating witness for what preceded."],[1192,"'In Paradise there are chambers whose outside is seen from their inside and whose inside is seen from their outside.' Abū Mālik al-Ash'arī said: 'For whom are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'For one who speaks good words, feeds food, and spends the night standing in prayer while people are asleep.'"],[1193,"I prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night in Ramadan in a room made of palm branches. He stood and said the takbir, then said: 'Allah is the Greatest, Possessor of might and dominion, and Possessor of pride and greatness.' Then he began al-Baqarah and recited. I said: 'He will reach one hundred verses.' Then I said: 'He will reach two hundred.' Then he began Āl 'Imrān and recited it, then he began al-Nisā' and recited it, not passing by a verse of warning except that he stopped and sought refuge. Then he bowed for the same length as he had stood, saying: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent,' repeating it. Then he raised his head and said: 'Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise,' for the same length as his bowing. Then he prostrated for the same length as his standing, saying: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,' and saying between the two prostrations: 'Lord, forgive me.' He did not pray except four rak'ahs from the night prayer from the beginning of the night until its end, until Bilal came and announced to him the dawn prayer."],[1194,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If one of you doubts in his prayer, let him cast aside the doubt and build on what he is certain of. If he becomes certain that he has completed it, he should perform two prostrations. If his prayer was complete, then the (extra) rak‘ah and the two prostrations will be voluntary; and if it was incomplete, then the rak‘ah will complete his prayer, and the two prostrations will rub Satan’s nose in the dust.”"],[1195,"When one of you prays and does not know whether he prayed three or four, let him pray one rak'ah, perfecting its prostration and bowing, then prostrate twice."],[1196,"He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in one of the prayers and stood up after two rak'ahs, so they glorified Allah to alert him, but he continued until he finished his prayer and only the salam remained. Then he prostrated twice while sitting before he said the salam.'"],[1197,"He got up after two rak'ahs, so they glorified Allah to alert him, but he continued and completed it, then prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness when he finished. He said: 'Do you think I would sit? I only did as I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.'"],[1198,"I prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs, then left. A man said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, you forgot and said the salam after two rak'ahs.' He ordered Bilal, who called the iqamah for the prayer, then he completed that rak'ah. I asked the people about the man who said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you forgot,' and it was said to me: 'Do you know him?' I said: 'No, unless I see him.' Then a man passed by me and I said: 'It is this one.' They said: 'This is Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah.'"],[1199,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the tashahhud in the two prostrations of forgetfulness, then said the salam."],[1200,"The Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer and forgot in his prayer, so he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam and after speaking."],[1201,"The Prophet ﷺ called the two prostrations of forgetfulness 'the two humiliators' (al-murghimatayn)."],[1202,"I asked Abū Sa'īd al-Khudrī: 'One of us prays and does not know how many rak'ahs he prayed.' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When one of you prays and does not know how many he prayed, let him prostrate twice. And if Satan comes to one of you and says: You have broken your ablution, let him say: You have lied, unless he finds a smell with his nose or hears a sound with his ear.'"],[1203,"Whoever forgets in his prayer regarding three or four [rakʿahs], let him complete [it], for the addition is better than the deficiency."],[1204,"There is no [prostration for] forgetfulness in the leap of prayer except for standing after sitting or sitting after standing."],[1205,"Have you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or from any of his Companions anything that mentions what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded when a person forgets in his prayer? I said: No. Or have you not heard, O Commander of the Believers? He said: No. Then ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf came in to us and said: What are you two discussing? ʿUmar said: I asked him whether he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or any of his Companions mention what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded when a person forgets in his prayer. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I have knowledge of that. ʿUmar said: Come, for you are the just and acceptable one. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When one of you doubts regarding the two [rakʿahs], let him make them one; and when he doubts regarding the two and the three, let him make them two; and when he doubts regarding the three and the four, let him make them three; then let him complete the remainder of his prayer so that the uncertainty is in the addition; then let him prostrate twice while sitting before he gives the salutation.'"],[1206,"ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī prayed with us and stood up while he had to sit. The people said: Subḥān Allāh, Subḥān Allāh. But he did not sit and continued standing. When he was at the end of his prayer, he prostrated twice while sitting. When he gave the salutation, he said: I heard you just now saying Subḥān Allāh so that I would sit, but the Sunnah is what I did."],[1207,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"A prophet came out from among the prophets seeking rain. Suddenly, he saw an ant lifting one of its legs towards the sky. He said, 'Go back, for you have been answered due to the status of this ant.'\""],[1208,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain and turned his cloak inside out so that the drought might turn away."],[1209,"The Sunnah of praying for rain is the Sunnah of prayer on the two Eids, except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned his cloak inside out, placing its right side on his left and its left side on his right. He prayed two rakʿahs, saying seven takbīrs in the first, and he recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,' and in the second he recited 'Has there come to you the account of the Overwhelming?' and he said five takbīrs in it."],[1210,"O son of my brother, how did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ perform the rain prayer on the day he prayed for rain with the people? He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out humbly, humble, and humble, and he performed in it as he would in the Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha.\""],[1211,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out humble, shabby, fearful, supplicating, unhurried, and prayed two rakʿahs as he prayed on the Eid, and he did not deliver a sermon like your sermons."],[1212,"The Prophet ﷺ did not raise his hands in any of his supplications except in the prayer for rain. Shuʿbah said: I said to Thābit: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Subḥān Allāh. I said: Did you hear it from Anas? He said: Subḥān Allāh."],[1213,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for rain wearing a black cloak. He wanted to take hold of its lower part and make it its upper part, but when it became heavy on him, he turned it over his shoulder. The two [Bukhārī and Muslim] agreed on the ḥadīth of ʿAbbād b. Tamīm, but they did not transmit it with this wording. It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim."],[1214,"Some weepers came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'O Allah, give us abundant, wholesome, productive, immediate, not delayed, beneficial, not harmful rain.' Then the sky closed over them."],[1215,"From ʿUmayr, the freed slave of Abū al-Laḥm, that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the stones of al-Zayt praying for rain, veiled with his hands, supplicating like this."],[1216,"I witnessed Khaybar with my masters. They spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about me and informed him that I was a slave. He ordered [something] for me, and I was given a sword to wear, so I was dragging it. Then he ordered for me some odds and ends of goods. I presented to him a ruqyah I used to recite over the insane, and he ordered me to discard some of it and keep some of it."],[1217,"The people complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the withholding of rain. He ordered a pulpit to be placed for him in the prayer area and promised the people a day on which they would come out. 'A'ishah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out when the edge of the sun appeared, sat on the pulpit, said 'Allah is greater,' praised Allah, and then said: 'You have complained of the drought in your lands and the delay of rain beyond its usual time. Allah has commanded you to call upon Him and promised to answer you.' Then he said: 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment. There is no god but Allah; He does what He wills. O Allah, You are Allah, there is no god but You, the Self-Sufficient, and we are the needy. Send down rain upon us and make what You send down a strength and a provision for us until a time.' Then he raised his hands and kept raising them until the whiteness of his armpits appeared. Then he turned his back to the people and turned or reversed his cloak while raising his hands. Then he faced the people, descended, and prayed two rak'ahs. Allah brought forth clouds, which thundered and flashed with lightning, then rained by Allah's permission. He did not reach his mosque until the torrents were flowing. When he saw how quickly they rushed to shelter, he laughed until his molars showed and said: 'I bear witness that Allah has power over all things and that I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.'"],[1218,"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicate against Mudar. I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has given you and answered you, but your people have perished, so supplicate to Allah for them. He said: 'O Allah, give us rain, a helpful, pleasant, swift, abundant, widespread, immediate rain, not delayed, beneficial, not harmful.' It was only about a Friday or so until they were given rain."],[1219,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated in the prayer for rain and said: 'O Allah, give us rain, a helpful, pleasant, swift, abundant, widespread, immediate rain, not delayed, beneficial, not harmful.' It was only about a Friday or so until they were given rain. End of the Book of Istisqāʾ."],[1220,"While I was shooting arrows, the sun eclipsed. I threw them away and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I reached him while he was standing, raising his hands, glorifying Allah, saying 'Allah is greater,' praising his Lord, and supplicating until the eclipse cleared. He recited two surahs in two rak'ahs."],[1221,"\"The sun set during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and prolonged his standing until it was said he would not prostrate. Then he prostrated and prolonged his prostration until it was said he would not raise his head. Then he raised his head and prolonged his standing until it was said he would not bow. Then he bowed and prolonged his bow until it was said he would not raise his head. Then he raised his head and prolonged his standing until it was said he would not prostrate.\" And the rest of the narration mentions the Hadith of Al-Thawri narrated by Ya'la bin 'Ata', which is a strange, authentic Hadith. \"So the two sheikhs have provided evidence with Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il, but they did not exclude it. As for 'Ata' bin Al-Sa'ib, they did not exclude it.\""],[1222,"Samurah said: One day while I and a boy from the Ansar were shooting at a target of ours during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when the sun was about two or three spear-lengths above the horizon in the eye of the beholder, it darkened until it became like a colocynth. One of us said to his companion: Let us go to the mosque, for by Allah, the affair of this sun will certainly bring about something new for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in his community. We rushed to the mosque and found him coming out. We met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ just as he came out to the people. He came forward and led us in prayer with the longest standing he ever did in any prayer, and we did not hear his voice. Then he bowed with the longest bowing he ever did in any prayer, and we did not hear his voice. Then he prostrated with the longest prostration he ever did in any prayer, and we did not hear his voice. Then he did the same in the second rak'ah. The clearing of the sun coincided with his sitting in the second rak'ah. Then he said the salam, praised Allah, extolled Him, bore witness that there is no god but Allah, and bore witness that he is His servant and Messenger. Then he said: 'O people, I am only a human being and the Messenger of Allah. I remind you of Allah: if you know that I have fallen short in conveying any of the messages of my Lord, then tell me so that I may convey the messages of my Lord as they ought to be conveyed. And if you know that I have conveyed the messages of my Lord, then tell me.' The people stood up and said: We bear witness that you have conveyed the messages of your Lord, advised your community, and fulfilled what was upon you. Then they fell silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'To proceed: Some men claim that the eclipse of this sun, the eclipse of this moon, and the disappearance of these stars from their rising places are due to the death of great men among the people of the earth. They have lied. Rather, they are signs among the signs of Allah by which He tests His servants, to see who among them will turn in repentance. By Allah, since I stood to pray, I have seen what you will encounter in your worldly life and your hereafter. By Allah, the Hour will not come until thirty liars appear, the last of whom is the one-eyed Dajjal, whose left eye is effaced, as if it were the eye of Abu Yahya, an old man from the Ansar. When he appears, he will claim that he is Allah. Whoever believes in him, accepts him, and follows him, no righteous deed he did before will benefit him. Whoever disbelieves in him and rejects him will not be punished for anything he did before. He will dominate the entire earth except the Haram and Jerusalem. He will besiege the believers in Jerusalem, and they will be shaken with a severe earthquake. Then Jesus, son of Mary, will appear among them, and Allah will defeat him and his armies, until the base of a wall and the root of a tree will call out to the believer: \"Here is a disbeliever hiding behind me, come and kill him.\"' He said: 'That will not happen until you see matters whose importance grows in your minds, and you ask among yourselves whether your Prophet ﷺ mentioned any of them to you, and until mountains move from their foundations. Then, in the wake of that, the taking of souls'—and he gestured with his hand. Then he witnessed another sermon and mentioned this hadith, neither advancing nor delaying it."],[1223,"The sun eclipsed on the day Ibrahīm, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died. People thought it eclipsed because of his death. The Prophet ﷺ stood and said: 'O people, the sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah. They do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. If you see that, then hasten to prayer, to the remembrance of Allah, supplicate, and give charity.'"],[1224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the freeing of slaves at the solar eclipse."],[1225,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the freeing of slaves when the sun eclipsed."],[1226,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He mentioned the hadith and said in it: 'If you see that, then supplicate to Allah, pray, give charity, and free slaves.'"],[1227,"The sun eclipsed, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs until it cleared. Then he said: 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse for anyone's death, but they are two creatures among His creation. Allah brings about in His creation whatever He wills. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, manifests Himself to anything of His creation, it submits to Him. Whichever of them eclipses, pray until it clears or Allah brings about a matter.'"],[1228,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for a very long time leading the people, then bowed, then stood, then bowed, then stood, then bowed. He performed two rak'ahs, in each rak'ah three bowings. He bowed the third, then prostrated. Men fainted that day from how long he stood with them, and buckets of water were poured on them. When he bowed he said 'Allah is greater,' and when he rose he said 'Allah hears the one who praises Him,' until the sun cleared. Then he said: 'The sun and the moon do not eclipse for anyone's death or life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah by which Allah frightens His servants. If they eclipse, then hasten to prayer.'"],[1229,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ led them in prayer, recited a long surah, bowed five times, and prostrated twice. Then he stood for the second rak'ah, recited a long surah, bowed five times, and prostrated twice. Then he sat facing the qiblah, supplicating until the eclipse cleared. The two Shaykhs abandoned Abu Ja'far al-Razi and did not narrate from him, but his standing with the other imams is excellent, and this hadith has sound wording and truthful narrators."],[1230,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he came out alarmed, dragging his garment, and I was with him that day in Madinah. He prayed two rak'ahs and prolonged the standing in them, then he finished and the eclipse cleared. He said: \"These signs are only meant for Allah to instill fear through them. So when you see them—meaning, pray as the most recent obligatory prayer you have prayed.\""],[1231,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and prayed with the people. He said: I estimated his recitation, and we thought he recited Surah al-Baqarah, then he prostrated twice. Then he said: He prolonged the recitation, and I estimated his recitation, and I thought he recited Surah Aal 'Imran."],[1232,"The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon on him) recited from teh Qur'an in a loud voice in the prayer at an eclipse. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1188)"],[1233,"I went to Anas b. Malik and said: O Abu Hamzah, did something like this ever strike you during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Allah forbid! \"When the wind would become severe, he would hasten to the mosque fearing the Hour.\""],[1234,"\"The Prophet led us in prayer during an eclipse; we did not hear his voice.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 562)"],[1235,"The sun eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"The sun and the moon are two signs among the signs of Allah; they do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone. So when you see them, give charity, pray, say takbeer, and supplicate to Allah.\""],[1236,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ performed two units of prayer, similar to your prayer now, at the time of the solar and lunar eclipses. He did not delay it and may Allah send blessings upon Muhammad and his family and all of his companions.\""],[1237,"\"We were with Sa'eed bin Al-'Asi in Tabaristan, and Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman was with us. He said: 'Which of you offered the fear prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' Hudhaifah said: 'I did.' So Hudhaifah stood and the people formed two rows behind him, one row behind him and one row facing the enemy. He led those who were behind him in praying one rak'ah, then they went and took the place of the others, and the others came and he led them in praying one rak'ah, and they did not make it up.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1530)"],[1238,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear at Dhu Qarad, one rak'ah each, and they did not make up [the other rak'ahs].\" This is a corroborating witness for the hadith before it, \"and its chain is authentic.\""],[1239,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear at Dhu Qarad. A row formed behind him and another row faced the enemy. He prayed one rak'ah with them, then they went to the positions of those others, and those others came to the positions of these, and they prayed one rak'ah with the Prophet ﷺ, then he said the salam to them.\""],[1240,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about praying in a bow, so he said, \"Pray in a bow and drop the horn.\""],[1241,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding the prayer of fear: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood with a group behind him and another group behind that group, seated, all of them facing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbeer, and both groups said the takbeer. He bowed, and the group behind him bowed with him while the others remained seated. Then he prostrated, and they prostrated as well while the others remained seated. Then he stood, and they stood and moved backward until they were in the place of their companions, seated. Then the other group came forward, and he led them in one rak'ah and two prostrations, then he said the salam while the others were seated. Then he said the salam, and both groups stood up and prayed for themselves one rak'ah and two prostrations, one rak'ah and two prostrations.\""],[1242,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear.\" She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided the people into two groups. One group formed a row behind him, and the other group stood facing the enemy. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbeer, and the group that formed the row behind him said the takbeer. Then he bowed and they bowed, then he prostrated and they prostrated. Then he raised his head and they raised theirs. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained seated, and they prostrated the second prostration by themselves. Then they stood and moved backward on their heels, walking in reverse until they stood behind them. Then the other group came forward and formed a row behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said the takbeer, then they bowed by themselves. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated his second prostration, and they prostrated with him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for his second rak'ah, and they prostrated the second prostration by themselves. Then both groups stood together and formed a row behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He led them in one rak'ah and they bowed together, then he prostrated and they prostrated together, then he raised his head and they raised theirs with him. All of this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was very quick, sparing no effort to lighten it as much as he could. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, and they said the salam. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, having shared with the people in his entire prayer.\""],[1243,"\"The Prophet ﷺ prayed Maghrib with the people in the prayer of fear, three rak'ahs, then he finished. Then the others came, and he led them in three rak'ahs.\" I heard Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz say this."],[1244,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at 'Usfan, with Khalid b. al-Walid in command of the polytheists. We prayed Dhuhr, and the polytheists said: We have caught them off guard, we have caught them unawares. If only we had attacked them while they were praying. Then the verse of shortening was revealed between Dhuhr and 'Asr. When 'Asr arrived, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood facing the qiblah while the polytheists were in front of him. A row formed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and behind that row another row. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed and they all bowed. Then he prostrated, and the row nearest to him prostrated while the others remained standing guarding them. When those had performed the two prostrations and stood up, the others who were behind them prostrated. Then the row nearest to him moved back to the position of the others, and they all bowed. Then the row nearest to him prostrated while the others stood guarding them. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the row nearest to him sat, the others prostrated, then they all sat together, and he said the salam to them. He prayed it at 'Usfan and also prayed it on the day of Banu Sulaym."],[1245,"He asked Abu Hurayrah: Did you pray the prayer of fear with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Abu Hurayrah said: Yes. Marwan said: When? Abu Hurayrah said: \"In the year of the Najd expedition. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood for the 'Asr prayer, and a group stood with him while another group faced the enemy with their backs to the qiblah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbeer, and all of them said the takbeer—those with him and those facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed one rak'ah and the group behind him bowed. Then he prostrated, and the group nearest to him prostrated while the others remained standing facing the enemy. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood, and the group with him stood and went to face the enemy, and the group that had been facing the enemy came forward and bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained standing as he was. Then they stood, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bowed another rak'ah and they bowed with him and prostrated with him. Then the group that had been facing the enemy came forward and bowed and prostrated while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was seated along with those with him. Then came the salam, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salam, and they all said the salam. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two rak'ahs, and each man of the two groups had one rak'ah each.\""],[1246,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon them while 'Abbas, the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was complaining of illness. 'Abbas wished for death, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"O my uncle, do not wish for death. If you are a doer of good, being delayed so you may increase in goodness upon your goodness is better for you. And if you are a wrongdoer, being delayed so you may seek pardon for your wrongdoing is better for you. So do not wish for death.\""],[1247,"\"Shall I not tell you about the best of you and the worst of you?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"The best of you are those who live longest and have the best deeds.\""],[1248,"A man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the people is best?\" He said, \"The one whose life is long and whose deeds are good.\" He said, \"Then which of the people is worst?\" He said, \"The one whose life is long and whose deeds are evil.\""],[1249,"\"When Allah intends good for a servant, He employs him.\" It was said, \"How does He employ him?\" He said, \"He grants him success in doing righteous deeds before death.\""],[1250,"\"When Allah loves a servant, He sweetens him.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what does 'sweetens him' mean?\" He said, \"He grants him success in doing righteous deeds before his appointed time, until his neighbors are pleased with him\" or he said, \"those around him.\""],[1251,"I heard Allah's Apostle ﷺ as saying. Every servant would be raised (in the same very state) in which he dies. (Using translation from Muslim 2878a)"],[1252,"\"Indeed, the deceased will be resurrected in the clothes in which he dies.\""],[1253,"Whoever dies upon one of these stations will be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection: ribat, or Hajj, or other than that."],[1254,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ, not once or twice, saying: \"When a servant is doing a righteous deed and is then hindered from it by illness or travel, it is recorded for him like the righteous deed he used to do while healthy and resident.\""],[1255,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to visit Abdullah b. Ubayy during the illness in which he died. When he entered upon him, he recognized death in him and said, \"I had forbidden you from loving the Jews.\" He said, \"Sa'd b. Zurarah detested them, so what?\" When he died, his son came to him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abdullah b. Ubayy has died, so give me your shirt to shroud him in it.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took off his shirt and gave it to him."],[1256,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to visit me, not riding a mule or a workhorse.\""],[1257,"\"No man visits a sick person in the evening except that seventy thousand angels go out with him, seeking forgiveness for him until morning, and he will have a garden in Paradise. And whoever comes to him in the morning, seventy thousand angels go out with him, seeking forgiveness for him until evening, and he will have a garden in Paradise.\""],[1258,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me due to a pain that was in my eyes.\""],[1259,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Zayd b. Arqam due to an eye inflammation he had.\""],[1260,"\"I fell ill in Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit me. He placed his hand on my forehead, then wiped my chest and belly.\" Then he said, \"O Allah, heal Sa'd and complete his emigration for him.\""],[1261,"On the authority of Ibn Abbas"],[1262,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever visits his Muslim brother and sits by his head, then says seven times, 'I ask Allah, the Great, the Lord of the Great Throne, to cure you of your illness, if it is not his appointed time (to die),' Allah will cure him of his illness if it is not his appointed time.\""],[1263,"There is no Muslim who visits his brother, enters upon him, and his appointed time has not yet come, then says, “I ask Allah, the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal so-and-so from his illness,” seven times, except that Allah heals him of it."],[1264,"Al-Qaʿnabi narrated to us from what was read to Malik from Yazid b. Khusayfah; and Abu al-Fadl Muhammad b. Ibrahim al-Muzakki narrated to us: Ahmad b. Salamah narrated to us: Qutaybah b. Saʿid narrated to us: Ismaʿil b. Jaʿfar narrated to us: Yazid b. Khusayfah narrated to us from ʿAmr b. ʿAbd Allah b. Kaʿb al-Sulami that Nafiʿ b. Jubayr informed him that Uthman b. Abi al-ʿAs came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while a pain had seized him that had nearly incapacitated him. He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Place your right hand on the spot that hurts you and wipe it seven times, and say with each wipe: I seek refuge in the might and power of Allah from the evil of what I find.”"],[1265,"Two men came seeking healing from urinary retention, so they were taken to Abu al-Darda and mentioned the pain in their testicles to him. He said, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever among you suffers something, or his brother suffers it, let him say: Our Lord is Allah who is in heaven, hallowed be Your name. Your command is in heaven and earth, and as Your mercy is in heaven, place Your mercy on earth. Forgive us our sins and our errors. You are the Lord of the good. So send down a mercy from Your mercy and a healing from Your healing upon this ailment, and he will be cured, if Allah, Exalted is He, wills.” [The two Shaykhs relied on all the narrators of this hadith except Ziyad b. Muhammad, and he is a shaykh from the people of Egypt with few hadiths.]"],[1266,"When one of you visits a sick person, let him say: O Allah, heal Your servant, that he may wound an enemy for You or walk for You to prayer."],[1267,"Indeed a man may have a station with Allah that he does not attain through deeds, so He continues to afflict him with what he dislikes until He brings him to that."],[1268,"When Adam ﷺ was near death, he said to his sons, “Go and gather fruits of Paradise for me.” His sons went out, and the angels met them and said, “Where are you heading, O sons of Adam?” They said, “Our father sent us to gather fruits of Paradise for him.” They said, “Return, for you have been spared.” They returned with them until they entered upon Adam. When Hawwa saw them, she was startled by them and began to draw close to Adam and cling to him. Adam said to her, “Away from me, away from me! It was because of you that I was brought to this. Leave me alone with the angels of my Lord.” Then they took his soul, washed him, embalmed him, shrouded him, prayed over him, dug for him, and buried him. Then they said, “O sons of Adam, this is your practice for your dead, so do likewise.”"],[1269,"“Adam was a tall man,” and he mentioned a long hadith at the end of which he said, “Leave me alone with the messengers of my Lord, for you brought this upon me.” Then they took his soul, washed him with water and lote leaves three times, shrouded him, prayed over him, and buried him. Then they said, “This is the practice of your descendants after you.”"],[1270,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a sick man suffering from a fever, and Abu Hurayrah was with him. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Rejoice, for Allah says: It is My fire which I set upon My believing servant in this world so that it may be his share of the Fire in the Hereafter.”"],[1271,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was struck by a pain and began tossing on his bed.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, if one of us did this, it would be feared that you would be upset with him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed the believer is severely tested, and there is no believer afflicted by a misfortune or pain except that Allah removes a sin from him and raises a degree for him.”"],[1272,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited a woman from the Ansar and said to her, “Is it Umm Mildam?” She said, “Yes, may Allah curse it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do not revile it, for it washes away the sins of the servant as the bellows removes the dross of iron.”"],[1273,"Fever came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked permission to enter. He said, “Who are you?” She said, “I am Umm Mildam.” He said, “Will you be sent to the people of Quba?” She said, “Yes.” He said, “Then go to them.” They fell feverish and met severe hardship from it, so they complained to him, saying, “O Messenger of Allah, what we have met from this fever!” He said, “If you wish, I will pray to Allah and He will remove it from you; and if you wish, it will be a purification for you.”"],[1274,"\"Affliction will keep befalling the believer in his self, his wealth, and his children until he meets Allah with no sin upon him.\""],[1275,"\"The believer's fever is an expiation for his sins.\""],[1276,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a bedouin, \"Has your mother ever experienced the pain of childbirth?\" He asked, \"What is the pain of childbirth?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is a burning sensation between the skin and the flesh.\" He said, \"I have never experienced this before.\" The Prophet ﷺ then asked, \"Have you ever experienced a headache?\" He asked, \"What is a headache?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"It is a vein that strikes a person in their head.\" He said, \"I have never experienced this before.\" When the bedouin turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of Hell, let them look at this person.\""],[1277,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No vein of a believer is struck but Allah thereby removes from him a sin, writes for him a good deed, and raises him a degree.\""],[1278,"\"Nothing afflicts the believer in his body and harms him but it expiates for him some of his evil deeds.\""],[1279,"\"Allah indeed afflicts His servant with illness until it expiates for him every sin.\""],[1280,"\"No Muslim is afflicted with a trial in his body but Allah commands the guardian angels who protect him: 'Write for My servant, every day and night, the good he used to do as long as he remains confined in My bonds.'\""],[1281,"\"The parable of the believing servant when fever or heat afflicts him is like an iron that enters the fire: its impurity goes away and its goodness remains.\""],[1282,"Allah said: \"O Jesus, I am sending after you a nation who, if what they love befalls them, praise Allah, and if what they hate befalls them, seek reward and remain patient, though they have neither forbearance nor knowledge.\" He said: \"O Lord, how can this be for them when they have neither forbearance nor knowledge?\" He said: \"I shall give them from My forbearance and My knowledge.\""],[1283,"\"When I afflict My believing servant and he does not complain of Me to his visitors, I release him from My bonds, then I replace for him flesh better than his flesh and blood better than his blood, and then he resumes his deeds anew.\""],[1284,"A woman had been a prostitute in the pre-Islamic era. A man passed by her, or she passed by him, and he stretched his hand toward her. She said: \"Stop! Allah has taken away shirk and brought Islam.\" So he left her and turned away, but kept looking back at her until his face hit a wall. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: \"You are a servant for whom Allah wills good. When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wills good for a servant, He hastens for him the punishment of his sin so that he meets Him on the Day of Resurrection with it already requited.\""],[1285,"A Muslim owes another Muslim four duties: to answer him when he calls, to visit him when he is sick, to respond to his sneeze with a supplication, and to follow his funeral when he dies."],[1286,"Abu Musa al-Ash'ari came to visit al-Hasan b. Ali. Ali said to him: \"Have you come as a visitor or as a gloater?\" He said: \"Rather, I have come as a visitor.\" Ali said: \"If you have come as a visitor, then I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever comes to his brother as a visitor is in the orchards of Paradise. When he sits, mercy envelops him. If he comes in the morning, seventy thousand angels pray for him until evening; and if he comes in the evening, seventy thousand angels pray for him until morning.'\""],[1287,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no Muslim who visits a sick person except that seventy thousand angels go out with him, escorting him. If it is in the morning, until evening, and he will have an orchard in Paradise; and if it is in the evening, seventy thousand angels escort him until morning, and he will have an orchard in Paradise.\" This is of the type I mentioned more than once, that this does not leave it defective, for Abu Mu'awiya is the most accurate memorizer of the companions of al-A'mash, and al-A'mash is more knowledgeable of the hadith of al-Hakam than others."],[1288,"\"Whoever visits a sick person continues to wade through mercy until he sits down, and when he sits, he immerses himself in it.\""],[1289,"\"Do not force your sick to eat, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink.\""],[1290,"“What is the matter with you, O Abu Muhammad? Perhaps you are upset about your cousin being appointed as caliph?” [referring to Abu Bakrؓ ]. He said: “No.” And he spoke highly of Abu Bakr ؓ , [then he said:] “But I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: ʿ[There is] a word which no one says when he is dying but Allah will relieve him of distress and his colour will brighten.” Nothing prevented me from asking him about it except the fear of not being able to comply with it and I did not ask him about it until he died.” ‘Umar said to him: “I know what it is.” Talhah said to him: “What is it?ʿ ‘Umar said: “Do you know any word that is greater than the word he enjoined his uncle to say when he was dying, ‘La ilaha illallah’?” Talhah said: “You are right. By Allah, that is what it is.” (Using translation from Aḥmad 1386)"],[1291,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed I know a word which, if a servant says it truthfully from his heart and then dies, will be forbidden to the Fire.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away and did not tell it to us. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: I will tell you it. It is the word of sincerity which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his uncle Abu Talib at death: the testimony that there is no god but Allah, and it is the word by which Allah honored Muhammad and his companions."],[1292,"\"Whoever's last words are 'There is no god but Allah' will enter Paradise.\""],[1293,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, in what was read to Malik, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. Jabir b. 'Atik that 'Atik b. al-Harith b. 'Atik, who is the grandfather of 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah, the father of his mother, informed him that Jabir b. 'Atik informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to visit 'Abd Allah b. Thabit and found him overcome. He called to him but he did not answer, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the istirja' and said: \"We have been overcome regarding you, O Abu al-Rabi'.\" The women cried out and wept, and Ibn 'Atik began to silence them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Leave them, and when it becomes obligatory, no crying woman should weep.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the obligation? He said: \"When he dies.\" His daughter said: By Allah, I was hoping that you would be a martyr, for you had completed your equipment. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has already granted his reward according to his intention. What do you consider martyrdom?\" They said: Being killed in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the path of Allah: the one who dies of plague is a martyr, the one who drowns is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one with a stomach disease is a martyr, the one who dies in a fire is a martyr, the one who dies under a collapsed building is a martyr, and the woman who dies in childbirth is a martyr.\""],[1294,"\"When you are present with the dying, close the eyes, for the sight follows the soul, and speak good, for the angels say 'Amin' to the supplication of the family.\""],[1295,"When the believer is dying, the angels of mercy come to him with white silk and say: \"Come out, content and pleasing, to the spirit of Allah, and sweet basil, and a Lord who is not angry.\" It comes out like the best scent of musk, so much so that they pass him to one another, smelling him, until they bring him to the gate of heaven. They say: \"How good is this scent that has come to you from the earth!\" Every time they come to a heaven, they say that until they bring him to the spirits of the believers. He said: \"They are happier with him than one of you with his absent one when he comes to him.\" He said: \"They ask him: 'What did so-and-so do?'\" He said: \"They say: 'Leave him until he rests, for he was in the distress of the world.' And if he says to them: 'Did he not come to you? He has died.'\" He said: \"They say: 'He was taken to his mother, the abyss.'\" He said: \"As for the disbeliever, the angels of punishment come to him and say: 'Come out, angry and subjected to anger, to the punishment of Allah and His wrath.' It comes out like the foulest smell of a carcass, and they go with him to the gate of the earth. They say: 'How foul is this smell!' Every time they come upon a land, they say that until they bring him to the spirits of the disbelievers.\""],[1296,"Abu Bakr b. 'Abd Allah informed me, al-Hasan b. Sufyan related to us, Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami related to us, Mu'adh b. Hisham related to us, my father narrated to me from Qatada, from Qasama b. Zuhayr, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly. And Hammam b. Yahya said from Qatada, from Abu al-Jawza', from Abu Hurayra."],[1297,"\"When death comes to the believer, the angels of mercy come to him.\""],[1298,"When the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, he asked about al-Bara' b. Ma'rur. They said: He has died and bequeathed a third of his wealth to you, O Messenger of Allah, and he instructed that he be turned toward the qibla when he was dying. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He has hit upon the natural disposition, and I have returned his third to his children.\" Then he went and prayed over him and said: \"O Allah, forgive him, have mercy on him, and admit him into Your Paradise, and You have already done so.\" This is an authentic hadith. Al-Bukhari used Nu'aym b. Hammad as evidence, and Muslim b. al-Hajjaj used al-Darawardi as evidence, but they did not include this hadith. I know of no other hadith about directing the dying person toward the qibla besides this one."],[1299,"\"When they began to wash the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, suddenly there was a caller from inside saying: 'Do not remove the shirt from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'\""],[1300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever washes a deceased person and conceals it, forty times will be forgiven for him. And whoever shrouds a deceased person, Allah will cover him with silk and spread the paradise for him. And whoever digs a grave for a deceased person and straightens it, he will be rewarded with the reward of a house in which he will be housed until the Day of Judgment.\""],[1301,"«The best of your garments are white, so clothe your living in them and shroud your dead in them.»"],[1302,"«Wear white garments and shroud your dead in them, for they are the purest and best.»"],[1303,"«When you perfume the deceased with incense, use an odd number.»"],[1304,"«We saw ourselves with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we almost had to jog with the funeral bier.»"],[1305,"I was sitting with 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far b. Abi Talib in al-Baqi' when a funeral procession came into view. Ibn Ja'far turned to us and marveled at their slow walking with it. He said, \"It is astonishing how people's condition has changed. By Allah, it was nothing but a quick pace. A man would reproach another, saying, 'O servant of Allah, fear Allah!' as if you yourself had been carried at a quick pace, amazed at their slow walking.\""],[1306,"«The one on foot walks in front of the funeral bier, the rider behind it, and funeral prayer is performed for a child.»"],[1307,"«The Prophet ﷺ accompanied a funeral procession and was brought a mount but refused to ride it. When he returned, he was brought a mount and rode it.» He was asked about this, and he said, \"The angels were walking, and I would not ride while they walked. When they departed—or he said, ascended—I rode.\""],[1308,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with a funeral procession and saw people riding.» He said, «Are you not ashamed? The angels of Allah are on their feet while you are on the backs of beasts.»"],[1309,"«When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with a funeral procession, he would not sit until it was lifted or placed down.»"],[1310,"The Prophet ﷺ said, «When you follow a funeral procession, do not sit until it is placed down.» The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting the hadith of Ibn 'Umar from 'Amir b. Rabi'ah: \"Whoever follows it should not sit until it is placed down.\""],[1311,"When a funeral procession passed by him, he would stand until it passed."],[1312,"He witnessed a funeral prayer led by Marwan b. al-Hakam. Abu Hurayrah went with Marwan until they sat in the cemetery. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri came and said to Marwan, \"Give me your hand.\" Marwan gave him his hand. Abu Sa'id said, \"Stand up.\" Marwan stood, then asked, \"Why did you make me stand?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he saw a funeral procession, would stand until it passed, and he would say, 'Indeed, death is a fright.'\" Marwan said, \"Did he speak the truth, O Abu Hurayrah?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" Marwan said, \"What prevented you from telling me?\" Abu Hurayrah said, \"You were the leader and sat, so I sat.\""],[1313,"He said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, a funeral of the disbelievers passes by us, should we stand for it?\" He said, \"Yes, stand for it, for you are not standing for it; rather you stand in veneration of the One who takes the souls.\""],[1314,"\"A Jewish funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he stood.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is a Jewish funeral.\" He said, \"I only stood for the angels.\""],[1315,"We were in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and when one of us was near death we would inform the Prophet ﷺ, and he would attend him and seek forgiveness for him until we arrived. Then the Prophet ﷺ and those with him would leave, and sometimes they would sit until the burial. Sometimes that detention became long for the Prophet of Allah ﷺ. When we feared the hardship of that, some of the people said to others, \"If only we did not inform the Prophet ﷺ about anyone until he had died; then when he died we would inform him, and there would be no hardship or detention in that.\" So we would inform him of the deceased after he had died, and he would come and pray over him."],[1316,"\"That it is a sunnah.\""],[1317,"I prayed behind Ibn Abbas at a funeral, and I heard him recite the Opening of the Book. When he finished, I took his hand and asked him, \"Do you recite?\" He said, \"Yes, it is a right and a sunnah.\""],[1318,"The translation of the given phrase from Arabic to English is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say the takbeer four times over our funeral processions and recite the opening chapter of the Quran in the first takbeer.\""],[1319,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a dead person, he said: O Allah, forgive those of us who are living and those of us who are dead, those of us who are present and those of us who are absent, our young and our old, our male and our female. O Allah, to whomsoever of us Thou givest life grant him life as a believer, and whomsoever of us Thou takest in death take him in death as a follower of Islam. O Allah, do not withhold from us the reward (of faith) and do not lead us astray after his death. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3201)"],[1320,"I asked Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, \"How was the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over the deceased?\" She said, \"He would say: O Allah, forgive our living and our dead, our male and our female, our present and our absent, our young and our old. O Allah, whoever of us You keep alive, keep him alive upon Islam, and whoever of us You take in death, take him in death upon faith.\""],[1321,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up for a funeral prayer, he would say, 'O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your female servant is in need of Your mercy, while You are not in need of His punishment. If he was righteous, then increase his good deeds, and if he was a wrongdoer, then overlook his sins.'\""],[1322,"I attended Abdullah b. Abbas when he prayed with us at a funeral at al-Abwa'. He said the takbir, then recited the Mother of the Quran, raising his voice with it, then invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then said: \"O Allah, Your servant and the son of Your servant and the son of Your maidservant, he bears witness that there is no god but You alone, without partner, and he bears witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. He has become poor in need of Your mercy, and You have become rich beyond needing his punishment. He is being released from this world and its people. If he was pure, then purify him; and if he was in error, then forgive him. O Allah, do not deprive us of his reward, and do not lead us astray after him.\" Then he said three more takbirs, then he left. He said, \"O people, I did not recite aloud except so that you know that it is the sunnah.\" The two Shaykhs did not use Shurahbil b. Sa'd as an authority, and he is among the Followers of the people of Madinah. I only brought out this hadith as a witness for the hadiths that we presented earlier, for they are abbreviated and general."],[1323,"A daughter of his died, and he followed her on a mule, walking behind the funeral, while women were lamenting her. He said, \"Are they lamenting or not lamenting? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade lamentations. Let each of you shed tears as much as she wishes.\" Then he prayed over her and said four takbirs, then after the fourth he stood for the length between two takbirs, seeking forgiveness for her and supplicating. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do this.\""],[1324,"the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed him about the funeral prayer. \"The Imam should start by saying the takbir, then send blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ , and complete the prayer with three additional takbirs before making the tasleem in a quiet manner when he leaves. And the Sunnah is for those behind him to do the same as what he has done.\"Zuhri said, \"Abu Umamah and Ibn al-Musayyib informed me about this, and Ibn Shihab mentioned what Abu Umamah had told me about the Sunnah in the funeral prayer for Muhammad bin Suyaid.\" He said, \"And I heard ad-Dahhak ibn Qays narrating from Habib ibn Muslimah in a prayer he performed for the deceased, similar to what Abu Umamah informed us.\""],[1325,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a funeral and said four takbirs, then gave one salutation. The single salutation is for the funeral.\" The narration has been authenticated from Ali b. Abi Talib, Abdullah b. Umar, Abdullah b. Abbas, Jabir b. Abdullah, Ibn Abi Awfa, and Abu Hurayrah that they used to give one salutation at the funeral."],[1326,"\"The believer dies with sweat on his forehead.\""],[1327,"\"The Prophet ﷺ kissed Uthman b. Maz'un while he was dead, and he was weeping.\" He said, \"And his eyes were shedding tears.\""],[1328,"\"The best perfume is musk.\" Al-Mustamirr b. al-Rayyan concurred with him, from Abu Nadrah."],[1329,"The Prophet was asked about musk and he said: \"It is the best of your perfumes.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 992)"],[1330,"Ali said, \"And it is the virtue of Hanoot, the messenger of Allah peace be upon him.\""],[1331,"When they began washing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a caller called out to them from inside: 'Do not remove the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ shirt.'"],[1332,"Ali ibn Abi Talib, I washed the Messenger of Allah, then I went to see what would happen to the deceased, but I did not see anything. He was a good person, both alive and dead. I had the duty to bury him and shroud him. Four people were with me: Ali, al-Abbas, al-Fadl, and Salih, who was a servant of the Messenger of Allah. We buried the Messenger of Allah according to Islamic customs, and poured milk over his grave."],[1333,"Whoever washes a dead person and conceals [what he sees], he will be forgiven forty times; and whoever shrouds a dead person, Allah will clothe him from the silk and brocade of Paradise; and whoever digs a grave for a dead person and buries him in it, he will be given a reward like the reward of a dwelling until the Day of Resurrection."],[1334,"When a funeral procession was brought to him to pray over it and its people were few, he would divide them into three rows and pray with them over it, and he would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'No three rows of Muslims line up over a funeral except that it becomes obligatory [for forgiveness].' This wording is the hadith of Ibn 'Ulayya; in the wording of al-Mahbubi: 'except that he is forgiven.'"],[1335,"There was a Jewish boy who served the Prophet ﷺ, and he fell ill. The Prophet ﷺ visited him and said: 'Say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah.' The boy looked at his father, who said: 'Say what Muhammad says to you.' When he died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Pray over your brother.'"],[1336,"The rider is behind the funeral procession, the walker is near it, and the child is prayed over."],[1337,"He raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'The rider proceeds behind the funeral procession, and the walker on its right and left, near it. The miscarried fetus is prayed over and supplication is made for its parents for well-being and mercy.' Ibrahim b. Abi Talib said at the end of this hadith: Yunus b. 'Ubayd said: Some of his family narrated to me that he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ as a narration of Yunus b. 'Ubayd from Sa'id b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Jubayr b. Hayya."],[1338,"If the infant cries out [at birth], it inherits and is prayed over."],[1339,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in Khaybar when a man from among us died, who was one of the bravest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Pray for him.\" So we went to look for something to use as a shroud, and we found only two dirhams worth of beads belonging to Jews. This hadith was narrated by people from Yahya ibn Sa'id. This is Abu 'Amrah, a man from Juhaynah known for his honesty, and he did not lie."],[1340,"A man died in the time of the Prophet ﷺ. A man came to him and said: 'So-and-so has died.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'He has not died.' Then he came to him a second time and said: 'So-and-so has died.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He has not died.' Then he came to him a third time and said: 'So-and-so has died.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'How did he die?' He said: 'He cut his own throat with a blade he had with him.' The Prophet ﷺ did not pray over him."],[1342,"When the Prophet ﷺ was invited to a funeral, he would ask about [the deceased]. If good was said of him, he would pray over him, and if other than that was said of him, he would say to his family: 'Take care of him yourselves,' and he would not pray over him."],[1343,"In the early days of the Prophet ﷺ, when one of us was on his deathbed, we would inform the Prophet ﷺ, and he would attend and seek forgiveness for him until he died. Then the Prophet ﷺ and those with him would leave until he was buried. Sometimes this waiting was prolonged for the Prophet ﷺ. When we feared that this was burdensome for him, some of the people said to others: 'If only we did not inform the Prophet ﷺ about anyone until he had died; then after he died we would inform him, and there would be no burden or waiting for him in that.' So we did that: we would inform him of the deceased after he had died, and he would come and pray over him. Sometimes he would leave, and sometimes he would stay until the deceased was buried. We continued on that for a while, then we said: 'If only the Prophet ﷺ did not have to go out, and we carried our funeral to him so that he could pray over it at his house, that would be more convenient for him.' So we did that, and that has been the practice until today."],[1344,"Abu Talha invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [to the funeral] of 'Umayr b. Abi Talha when he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to them and prayed over him in their home. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went forward, Abu Talha was behind him, and Umm Sulaym was behind Abu Talha; there was no one else with them."],[1345,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, who had been mutilated and disfigured. He said: 'Were it not that Safiyya would grieve, I would have left him so that Allah would gather him from the bellies of birds and beasts.' He shrouded him in a striped cloak: when his head was covered, his feet showed, and when his feet were covered, his head showed. He covered his head. He did not pray over any of the martyrs other than him, and he said: 'I am a witness over you today.' He would gather three and two [martyrs] in one grave and ask: 'Which of them knew more of the Quran?' and he would put him first in the niche. He shrouded two and three men in a single cloth."],[1346,"The martyrs of Uhud were not washed, and they were buried with their blood, and no funeral prayer was offered for them."],[1347,"When you place your dead in their graves, say: In the name of Allah and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah."],[1348,"When he placed the deceased in his grave, he would say: In the name of Allah and upon the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah. The hadith of al-Bayadi, who is well-known among the Companions, is a witness for the hadith of Hammam from Qatadah, traced back as a musnad."],[1349,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: When the deceased is placed in his grave, let those who place him say, at the moment he is placed in the niche, 'In the name of Allah and by Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[1350,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a funeral at a grave and said, 'Whose grave is this?' They said, 'So-and-so the Abyssinian, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no god but Allah, there is no god but Allah. He was driven from his land and his sky to the soil from which he was created.'"],[1351,"When Allah wills to take a servant in a land, He creates for him a need therein or thereby."],[1352,"The appointed term of a man was not made in a land except that a need for him was made therein."],[1353,"When Allah wills to take a servant in a land, He creates for him a need to go to it."],[1354,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed he is awwah (one who sighs).' He said, then he died, and a man saw fire in his grave, so he came to it, and behold, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in it, and he was saying, 'Come to your companion.' And behold, it was the man who used to raise his voice in remembrance."],[1355,"I saw fire in the graveyard, so I came to them, and behold, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the grave, and he was saying, 'Hand me your companion.'"],[1356,"I heard a man who was in Makkah, and he was a Byzantine—and in Shu'bah's hadith his name is Waqqas—narrating from Abu Dharr, who said: There was a man circumambulating the House, and he was saying in his supplication, 'Awwah, awwah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed he is awwah.' Abu Dharr said: Then I went out one night, and behold, the Prophet ﷺ was in the graveyard burying that man, and with him was a lamp."],[1357,"The Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon one day and mentioned a man from his companions who had died and was shrouded in a shroud of little worth and was buried at night. The Prophet ﷺ prohibited that a man be buried at night until prayer be said over him, except if a person is compelled to do that. And he said, \"When one of you shrouds his brother, let him make his shroud good.\""],[1358,"He informed me that the Prophet ﷺ gave a sermon one day and mentioned a man from his companions who had died and was shrouded in a shroud of little worth and buried at night. The Prophet ﷺ prohibited that a man be buried at night without prayer being said over him, except if a person is compelled to do that. And he said, \"When one of you takes charge of his brother, let him make his shroud good.\""],[1359,"To Abu Hayyaj: \"I am sending you on what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me: that you leave no image without effacing it and no raised grave without leveling it.\""],[1360,"I Ali, am unwilling to send you on what the Prophet ﷺ did not command me regarding, so he mentioned the narration in its form."],[1361,"I entered upon Aisha and said, \"O mother, uncover for me the grave of the Prophet ﷺ and his two companions.\" She uncovered for me three graves, neither raised nor flat, spread with the red pebbles of the courtyard. \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in front, Abu Bakr with his head between the shoulders of the Prophet ﷺ, and Umar with his head at the feet of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[1362,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade building over a grave, plastering it, sitting on it, and writing on it."],[1363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade plastering graves, writing on them, building over them, and sitting on them. These chains are authentic, but the practice is not upon them, for the imams of the Muslims from east to west have writing on their graves, and it is a practice the later generations took from the earlier ones."],[1364,"My community—or this community—will remain in a firm hold of its religion as long as they do not entrust funerals to their families."],[1365,"I heard Uthman b. Affan say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a funeral at a grave while its occupant was being buried. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Seek forgiveness for your brother and ask Allah for him to be made steadfast, for he is now being questioned.\""],[1366,"Uthman b. Affan, when he stood at a grave, would weep until his beard became wet. It was said to him, \"You remember Paradise and Hell and do not weep, yet you weep at this?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The grave is the first of the stages of the Hereafter. If one is saved from it, what comes after is easier. If one is not saved from it, what comes after is more severe.'\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have never seen a sight but the grave is more dreadful than it.\""],[1367,"I traveled with the Prophet ﷺ more than once, and I never saw him pass by the corpse of a human being except that he ordered its burial, without asking whether he was a Muslim or a disbeliever."],[1368,"Every person has three friends. One friend says, \"What you spend is yours, and what you withhold is not yours\"—that is his wealth. Another friend says, \"I am with you, but when you reach the king's door, I will leave you and return\"—that is his family and retainers. Another friend says, \"I am with you wherever you enter and wherever you go out\"—that is his deeds. Then he says, \"You were the least of the three in my eyes.\""],[1369,"The example of a man and death is like a man who has three friends. One of them says, \"This is my wealth, take from it what you wish.\" Another says, \"I am with you as long as you live, but when you die, I will leave you.\" The other says, \"I am with you; I enter and leave with you, whether you die or live.\" As for the one who said, \"Take from it what you wish and leave what you wish,\" that is his wealth. The other is his kinsfolk. The other is his deeds."],[1370,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Prepare food for the family of Ja'far, for there has come to them a matter that occupies them.\""],[1371,"If only you had seen me, Qutham, and 'Ubayd Allah b. al-'Abbas playing when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by on a mount. He said: \"Lift this one up to me,\" and he placed me in front of him. Then he said to Qutham: \"Lift this one up to me,\" and he placed him behind him. He was not ashamed before his uncle al-'Abbas to carry Qutham and leave 'Ubayd Allah. Then he wiped my head three times, and when he wiped it he said: \"O Allah, be a successor to Ja'far in his children.\" I said to 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far: \"What happened to Qutham?\" He said: \"He was martyred.\" I said to 'Abd Allah: \"Allah and His Messenger knew best of his fate.\" He said: \"Indeed.\""],[1372,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his hand over my head. He said: I think he said three times. When he wiped it he said: \"O Allah, be a successor to Ja'far in his children.\" Ja'far b. Khalid has brought two precious things: one is the wiping of the orphan's head, and the other is looking after the bereaved family with what sustains them for their night. \"May Allah grant us success in acting upon it on his behalf.\""],[1373,"Bashir, the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me. His name in the pre-Islamic era was Zahm b. Ma'bad, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"What is your name?\" He said: \"Zahm b. Ma'bad.\" He said: \"You are Bashir.\" So that became his name. He said: While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"O son of al-Khasasiyyah, what do you resent against Allah? You have come to walk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" I said: \"I do not resent anything against Allah. Every good, the Prophet of Allah did.\" Then he came upon graves of the polytheists and said: \"These have preceded with much good\" three times. Then he came upon graves of the Muslims and said: \"These have attained much good\" three times. While he was walking, he happened to glance, and behold, there was a man walking among the graves wearing two sandals. He said: \"O owner of the two sihtiyyah sandals, woe to you! Throw off your two sihtiyyah sandals.\" The man looked, and when he recognized the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he removed his sandals and threw them away."],[1374,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man walking in two sandals among the graves and said: \"O owner of the two sihtiyyah sandals, throw them off.\""],[1375,"We buried a man with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . When we returned and approached his door, we found him with a woman whom we did not think he knew. He said, \"O Fatimah, where did you come from?\" She replied, \"I came from the family of the deceased, I showed them sympathy for their dead and offered them condolences.\" He asked, \"Did you reach the graves with them?\" She said, \"May Allah forbid me from reaching the graves with them, but I heard you mentioning something about them.\" He said, \"If you had reached the graves with them, you would not have seen Paradise until your grandfather sees it.\" The graves are called \"al-Kuda.\" This narration was reported by Haywah bin Shurayh al-Hadrami from Rabee'ah bin Seef."],[1376,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a woman returning from a funeral procession and asked her: \"Where have you come from?\" She said: \"From offering condolences to the family of this deceased.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By Allah, if you had reached with them al-Kuda, you would not have seen Paradise until the grandfather of your father sees it.\""],[1377,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who visit graves, and those who take them as places of prostration and lamps.\""],[1378,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed women who frequently visit graves.\" These hadiths narrated about the prohibition of visiting graves are abrogated."],[1379,"\"I had forbidden you from visiting graves, but now visit them, for in them is a lesson. And I had forbidden you from nabidh, so now make nabidh, but I do not permit any intoxicant. And I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrificial animals, so eat and store it.\""],[1380,"\"I had forbidden you from visiting graves, from eating the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days, and from nabidh in certain vessels. Now, visit graves, for they make one abstemious in this world and remind of the Hereafter. Eat the meat of sacrificial animals and keep what you wish, for I only forbade you to do so when provisions were scarce, as a relief for the people. Indeed, no vessel makes anything forbidden; every intoxicant is forbidden.\""],[1381,"\"I had forbidden you from visiting graves, but now visit them, for they remind you of death.\""],[1382,"\"The Prophet ﷺ visited the grave of his mother with a thousand veiled men, and no one was seen weeping more than on that day.\""],[1383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited the grave of his mother and wept, and made those around him weep. Then he said: “I asked my Lord for permission to visit her grave and He granted me permission. And I asked Him for permission to seek forgiveness for her, but He did not grant me permission. So visit the graves, for they remind of death.” This hadith is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, though they did not record it."],[1384,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nearly a thousand riders. He dismounted with us and prayed two rak‘ahs with us. Then he turned to us with his face while his eyes were shedding tears. ‘Umar stood up to him, ransoming him with his mother and father, saying: What is the matter with you, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: “I asked my Lord for permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, but He did not permit me. So my eyes shed tears out of mercy for her. And I asked my Lord for permission to visit her grave, and He permitted me. I had previously forbidden you from visiting graves, so now visit them, and may your visiting them increase you in good.”"],[1385,"‘A’ishah came one day from the gravesites. I said to her: O Mother of the Believers, where have you come from? She said: From the grave of my brother ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr. I said to her: Did not the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid visiting graves? She said: Yes, “he had forbidden it, then he was commanded to visit them.”"],[1386,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I used to prohibit you from visiting graves, but now I encourage you to do so, for it softens the heart, brings tears to the eyes, and reminds you of the hereafter. However, do not say anything that will bring harm.\""],[1387,"“I had forbidden you from visiting graves. So whoever wishes to visit a grave, let him visit it, for it softens the heart, brings tears to the eye, and reminds of the Hereafter.”"],[1388,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Visit the graves, and thereby remember the Hereafter. Wash the dead, for tending to a body is an eloquent admonition. And pray over funeral processions, perhaps that will make you sorrowful, for the sorrowful one is in the shade of Allah, seeking every good.”"],[1389,"Fatimah, daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, used to visit the grave of her uncle Hamzah every Friday, and she would pray and weep beside it. The narrators of this hadith, to the last of them, are trustworthy. I have thoroughly examined the encouragement to visit graves, seeking to share in the urging, and so that the miserly, with his sin, may know that it is an established sunnah. May Allah bless Muhammad and all his family."],[1390,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a funeral procession passed by. He said: “What is this?” They said: The funeral of so-and-so the son of so-and-so. He used to love Allah and His Messenger, act in obedience to Allah, and strive in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is affirmed, it is affirmed, it is affirmed.” Then another funeral procession passed by. They said: The funeral of so-and-so the son of so-and-so. He used to hate Allah and His Messenger, act in disobedience to Allah, and strive in it. He said: “It is affirmed, it is affirmed, it is affirmed.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, your statement about the funeral and the praise of it: the first was praised with good and the other with evil, yet you said about them: it is affirmed, it is affirmed, it is affirmed. He said: “Yes, O Abu Bakr. Allah has angels who speak on the tongues of the children of Adam about what is in a person of good or evil.”"],[1391,"No Muslim dies and four of his closest neighbors testify that they know nothing of him but good, but Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: I have accepted your statement, or He said: your testimony, and I have forgiven him for what you do not know."],[1392,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, guide me to a deed which, if I do it, I will enter Paradise. He said: “Be a good-doer.” He said: How do I know that I am a good-doer? He said: Ask your neighbors. If they say that you are a good-doer, then you are a good-doer; and if they say that you are a wrongdoer, then you are a wrongdoer."],[1393,"It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the people of Paradise? He said: “He who does not die until his ears are filled with what he loves.” It was said: Who are the people of the Fire? He said: “He who does not die until his ears are filled with what he hates.”"],[1394,"Umm al-‘Ala’, a woman of the Ansar who had pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reported that they cast lots among the Muhajirun, and ‘Uthman b. Maz‘un fell to us, so we lodged him in our dwellings. He fell ill with the sickness in which he died. When he passed away, he was washed and shrouded in his garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and I said: O ‘Uthman b. Maz‘un, may Allah have mercy on you, Abu al-Sa’ib. My testimony for you is that Allah has honored you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What makes you know that Allah has honored him?” She said: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. Then whom does Allah honor? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for him, certainty has come to him. By Allah, I hope for good for him. By Allah, I do not know, and I am the Messenger of Allah, what will be done with me.” She said: By Allah, I will never vouch for anyone after him again."],[1395,"He used to say, after the tashahhud, words that he greatly emphasized. I said: In both of the two? He said: Rather in the second tashahhud, after the tashahhud. I said: What is it? He said: “I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of Hell, and I seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of the false messiah, the Dajjal, and I seek refuge in Allah from the trials of life and death.” He said: And he used to greatly emphasize them."],[1396,"From the Prophet ﷺ: He said, “Indeed the deceased hears the tapping of their sandals when they turn away. If he is a believer, prayer is at his head, fasting is at his right, zakah is at his left, and the good deeds of charity, prayer, maintaining ties, kindness, and beneficence to people are at his feet. He is approached from his head, and prayer says, ‘There is no entrance before me.’ He is approached from his right, and fasting says, ‘There is no entrance before me.’ He is approached from his left, and zakah says, ‘There is no entrance before me.’ He is approached from his feet, and good deeds say, ‘There is no entrance before me.’ It is said to him, ‘Sit up,’ so he sits up. The sun is made to appear to him as if it has drawn near to setting. It is said to him, ‘What do you say about this man who was among you, and what do you testify concerning him?’ He says, ‘Leave me to pray.’ They say, ‘You will do so, but tell us what we ask you about.’ He says, ‘What are you asking me about?’ They say, ‘Tell us what we ask you about.’ He says, ‘Leave me to pray.’ They say, ‘You will do so, but tell us what we ask you about.’ He says, ‘What are you asking me about?’ They say, ‘Tell us what you say about this man who was among you, and what do you testify concerning him?’ He says, ‘I testify that Muhammad is the servant of Allah and that he came with the truth from Allah.’ It is said to him, ‘Upon that you lived, upon that you died, and upon that you will be resurrected, if Allah wills.’ Then a door is opened for him facing the Fire, and it is said to him, ‘Look at your abode and what Allah prepared for you had you disobeyed.’ He increases in delight and joy. Then a door is opened for him facing Paradise, and it is said to him, ‘Look at your abode and what Allah prepared for you.’ He increases in delight and joy. That is the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Allah keeps firm those who believe, with the firm word, in worldly life and in the Hereafter. And Allah sends astray the wrongdoers. And Allah does what He wills} [Ibrahim 27].” He said: And Abu al-Hakam said, from Abu Hurayrah: It is said to him, “Give him the sleep of a bridegroom whom none awakens except the dearest of his family to him, or the most beloved of his family to him.” Then he returned to the hadith of Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah. He said: If he is a disbeliever, he is approached from his head and nothing is found; he is approached from his right and nothing is found; then he is approached from his left and nothing is found; then he is approached from his feet and nothing is found. It is said to him, ‘Sit up,’ so he sits up fearful and terrified. It is said to him, ‘What do you say about this man who was among you, and what do you testify concerning him?’ He says, ‘Which man?’ They say, ‘The man who was among you.’ He said: He cannot identify him. He said: They say, ‘Muhammad.’ He says, ‘I heard people say, so I said as they said.’ They say, ‘Upon that you lived, upon that you died, and upon that you will be resurrected, if Allah wills.’ Then a door is opened for him facing Paradise, and it is said to him, ‘Look at your abode and what Allah prepared for you had you obeyed Him.’ He increases in regret and ruin. He said: Then his grave is constricted for him until his ribs interlock. He said: That is the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Then indeed, for him is a life of narrowness, and We will raise him on the Day of Resurrection blind} [Ta-Ha 124]."],[1397,"“By the One in Whose hand is my soul, he certainly hears the tapping of their sandals when they turn away from him.”"],[1398,"From Abu Hurayrah concerning the saying of Allah, Exalted and Glorified: {a life of narrowness} [Ta-Ha 124], he said: “The punishment of the grave.”"],[1399,"The Prophet ﷺ went out for a funeral, and with him was Umar b. al-Khattab. He heard women weeping, and Umar rebuked them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Umar, leave them, for the eye sheds tears, the soul is afflicted, and the time is near.”"],[1400,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping. He said: “But Hamzah has no weepers.” That reached the women of the Ansar, so they wept for Hamzah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept, then woke while they were weeping. He said: “Woe to them! They have not stopped weeping since the day. Let them be silent, and let them not weep for any dead after today.”"],[1401,"Should you throw dust upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: And Fatimah said: “O father, he answered a Lord who called him. O father, how near he is to his Lord. O father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode. O father, to Jibril we announce his death.” Said b. Mansur added in his hadith from Abu Usamah: He said: I heard Hammad b. Zayd say: “I saw Thabit al-Bunani 149 when he narrated this hadith to us weep until I saw his ribs shaking.”"],[1402,"“When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not wailed over.”"],[1403,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, Osama bin Zaid shouted, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is not from me, nor is it the cry of someone truly grieving. The heart feels sorrow and the eye sheds tears, but Allah is not angered.\""],[1404,"\"Abu Huraira said: 'When I die, do not lament over me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not lamented over.' This statement attributed to Abu Huraira is very strange, except that Uthman Al-Ghaffani is not one of the conditions of our book here.\""],[1405,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid elegies.” Ibrahim b. Muslim al-Hajari is not abandoned, except that the two shaykhs did not use him as a proof. This hadith is a witness for what preceded it, and it is strange and sahih, for Muslim used Sharik b. Abd Allah as a proof."],[1406,"“Indeed among my Ummah there are four matters of the pre-Islamic era that they will not abandon: boasting about lineages, defaming genealogies, seeking rain by the stars, and wailing over the dead. Indeed the wailing woman, if she does not repent before she rises, she will rise on the Day of Resurrection wearing garments of tar, then over them will boil coats of flame from the Fire.”"],[1407,"When it was revealed: {When the believing women come to you pledging allegiance to you} [al-Mumtahanah 12] up to His saying {and they do not disobey you} [al-Mumtahanah 12], among it was wailing. I said: O Messenger of Allah, except the family of so-and-so, for they helped me in the pre-Islamic era, so I must help them. He said: “Except the family of so-and-so.”"],[1408,"“Three are from disbelief in Allah: tearing the front opening of the garment, wailing, and defaming lineage.”"],[1409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to care for the Ansar, visit them, and ask about them. It reached him about a woman of the Ansar whose son had died, and she had no other child, and that she grieved for him with severe grief. The Prophet ﷺ came to her and commanded her to fear Allah and be patient. She said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a barren woman who does not give birth, and I had no other child. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The barren one is she whose child remains alive.” Then he said: “There is no Muslim man or Muslim woman who has three children die, except that Allah admits them to Paradise because of them.” Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, and two? He said: “And two.” Sahih isnad, but they did not record it with the mention of the barren one."],[1410,"A man used to come to the Prophet ﷺ with a son of his, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Do you love him?” He said, “May Allah love you as you love him.” Then the Prophet ﷺ missed him and said, “What happened to so-and-so?” They said, “His son died.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Would it not please you that you will not come to any gate of the gates of Paradise except that you will find him waiting for you?” A man said, “Is that for him specifically or for all of us?” He said, “Rather, for all of you.”"],[1411,"“The children of the believers are in a mountain in Paradise, cared for by Ibrahim and Sarah until they return them to their fathers on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[1412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “forbade insulting the dead. So why do you insult ‘Ali when he has died?”"],[1413,"“Do not harm a Muslim by insulting a disbeliever.”"],[1414,"“Mention the good qualities of your dead and refrain from their faults.”"],[1415,"“Do not declare your dead impure, for a Muslim is not impure, alive or dead.”"],[1416,"“The angels said four takbirs over Adam, Abu Bakr said four takbirs over the Prophet, ‘Umar said four takbirs over Abu Bakr, Suhayb said four takbirs over ‘Umar, al-Hasan said four takbirs over ‘Ali, and al-Husayn said four takbirs over al-Hasan.”"],[1417,"“The last time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said takbir over funerals was four.” And ‘Umar said four takbirs over Abu Bakr, ‘Abdullah b. ‘Umar said four takbirs over ‘Umar, al-Hasan b. ‘Ali said four takbirs over ‘Ali, al-Husayn b. ‘Ali said four takbirs over al-Hasan, and the angels said four takbirs over Adam. “I am not one from whom it is hidden that al-Furat b. al-Sa’ib is not according to the condition of this book; I only included it as a witness.”"],[1418,"Ibn ‘Abbas prayed over a funeral and recited the Opening of the Book. I said to him, and he said, “It is from the Sunnah, or from the completion of the Sunnah.”"],[1419,"“You do not have to perform ghusl after washing your dead, for your dead is not impure; it is enough for you to wash your hands.”"],[1420,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Arabs apostatized. ‘Umar b. al-Khattab said, “O Abu Bakr, do you want to fight the Arabs?” He said, and Abu Bakr said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘I was commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and establish prayer and give zakah. By Allah, if they withhold from me a young goat that they used to give to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I will fight them over it.’” ‘Umar said, “When I saw that Abu Bakr’s view had been made clear to him, I knew that it was the truth.”"],[1421,"“I was commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah and establish prayer and give zakah; then their blood and their wealth are forbidden to me, and their reckoning is with Allah.”"],[1422,"The first three to enter Paradise and the first three to enter Hell were presented to me. As for the first three who will enter Paradise: the martyr, a slave who perfects the worship of his Lord and is sincere to his master, and a chaste, self-restrained man with dependents. And as for the first three who will enter Hell: an oppressive ruler, a wealthy man who does not give Allah's due from his wealth, and a poor person who is insolent."],[1423,"The consumer of ribā, its provider, its two witnesses when they know it, the woman who tattoos and the woman who has tattoos done, the one who withholds zakāh, and the one who reverts to being a Bedouin after the Hijrah — they are cursed on the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ on the Day of Resurrection."],[1424,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"In camels, their charity is in their offspring, in sheep, their charity is in their milk, in cows, their charity is their milk, and in horses, their charity is in their offspring. Whoever accumulates silver coins, gold coins, or land and does not count them as a debt nor spends them in the cause of Allah, it will be a treasure folded for him on the Day of Judgment.\" This was narrated by Ibn Jarir from Imran ibn Abi Anas."],[1425,"For camels there is their zakāh, for sheep there is their zakāh, and for wheat there is its zakāh."],[1426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen and said: \"Take grain from grain, a sheep from sheep, a camel from camels, and a cow from cattle.\" This is a sound chain according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs, if the hearing of ʿAṭāʾ b. Yasār from Muʿādh b. Jabal is authentic, for I am not certain of it."],[1427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever leaves behind a treasure, it will be transformed for him on the Day of Resurrection into a bald-headed snake with two fangs that will pursue him by his mouth. It will say, 'Woe to you! I am your treasure that you left behind.' It will keep pursuing him until it forces him to put his hand in its mouth, and it will bite it. Then it will pursue the rest of his body.\""],[1428,"\"The treasure of one of you on the Day of Resurrection will be a bald-headed snake with two fangs that will pursue its owner, while he seeks refuge from it. It will keep pursuing him while he flees from it, until it forces him to put his two fingers in its mouth.\""],[1429,"I heard Abū Umāmah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us during the Farewell Pilgrimage, mounted on his she-camel al-Jadʿāʾ, with his feet placed in the stirrups, stretching himself to make the people hear him. He said: \"Do you hear my voice?\" A man from among the groups of people said: \"What do you command us?\" He said: \"Worship your Lord, perform your five prayers, fast your month, pay the zakāh of your wealth, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Paradise of your Lord.\" He (the sub-narrator) said: I said: \"O Abū Umāmah, how old were you then?\" He said: \"I, O son of my brother, was then thirty years old. I was pushing the camel aside, drawing it close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[1430,"We entered upon ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in to me and saw on my hand a string of silver beads. He said: \"What is this, O ʿĀʾishah?\" I said: \"I made them to adorn myself for you, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Will you pay their zakāh?\" I said: \"No, or whatever Allah wills of that.\" He said: \"They will be enough for you from the Fire.\""],[1431,"She used to wear silver ornaments and asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, saying: \"Is it a treasure?\" He said: \"If you pay its zakāh, it is not a treasure.\""],[1432,"\"If you pay the zakāh of your wealth, you have removed its evil from yourself.\""],[1433,"\"If you pay the zakāh, you have fulfilled what is due from you. And whoever accumulates unlawful wealth then gives it in charity, he will have no reward in it, and its burden will remain upon him.\""],[1434,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Then he mentioned the hadith similar to the hadith of Mūsā b. Ismāʿīl from Ḥammād in its entirety, and for these words there is a supporting witness from the hadith of al-Zuhrī from Sālim from his father.\""],[1435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote the document of charity but did not send it out to his agents until he passed away. He tied it to his sword, and Abu Bakr acted upon it until he passed away, then Umar acted upon it until he passed away. In it was: \"For five camels, one sheep; for ten, two sheep; for fifteen, three sheep; for twenty, four sheep; for twenty-five, a bint makhāḍ (a one-year-old female camel) up to thirty-five. If one more is added, then a bint labūn (a two-year-old female camel) up to forty-five. If one more is added, then a ḥiqqah (a three-year-old female camel) up to sixty. If one more is added, then a jadhaʿah (a four-year-old female camel) up to seventy-five. If one more is added, then two bint labūn up to ninety. If one more is added, then two ḥiqqahs up to one hundred and twenty. If the camels are more than that, then for every fifty a ḥiqqah and for every forty a bint labūn. For sheep: for every forty sheep, one sheep up to one hundred and twenty. If one more is added, then two sheep up to two hundred. If one more is added above two hundred, then three sheep up to three hundred. If the sheep are more than that, then for every hundred sheep, one sheep. Nothing is due on them until they reach one hundred. Neither separated from a combined herd nor combined between separated ones out of fear of charity. Whatever is from two partners, they settle between them equally. Neither an old animal nor one with a defect is taken in charity.\" Al-Zuhrī said: \"When the collector comes, the sheep are divided into thirds: one third worst, one third best, and one third middle, and the collector takes from the middle.\" Al-Zuhrī did not mention cattle."],[1436,"This is a copy of the document of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which he wrote the charity, and it is with the family of Umar b. al-Khattab. Ibn Shihāb said: Sālim b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar read it to me, and I memorized it accurately. It is the one that ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz copied from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar and Sālim b. ʿAbd Allāh when he was appointed governor over Madinah. He ordered his agents to act upon it and wrote it to al-Walīd, and al-Walīd ordered his agents to act upon it. Then the caliphs continued to order that after him. Then Hishām ordered it and copied it to every agent of the Muslims and ordered them to act upon its contents and not to exceed it. This is a document that explains it: \"No charity is taken from any camels until they reach five dhawd (a small herd). When they reach five, then one sheep is due until they reach ten. When they reach ten, then two sheep are due until they reach fifteen. When they reach fifteen, then three sheep are due until they reach twenty. When they reach twenty, then four sheep are due until they reach twenty-five. When they reach twenty-five, a fariḍah (obligatory due) is imposed, and in it is a bint makhāḍ. If no bint makhāḍ is found, then a male ibn labūn up to thirty-five. When they reach thirty-six, then a bint labūn is due up to forty-five. When they are forty-six, then a ḥiqqah ṭarūqat al-jamal (a three-year-old female camel that has been mounted) is due up to sixty. When they are sixty-one, then a jadhaʿah is due up to seventy-five. When they reach seventy-six, then a bint labūn is due up to ninety. When they are ninety-one, then two ḥiqqahs ṭarūqatā al-jamal are due up to one hundred and twenty. When they are one hundred and twenty-one, then three bint labūn are due up to one hundred and twenty-nine. When they are one hundred and thirty, then two bint labūn and one ḥiqqah are due up to one hundred and thirty-nine. When they are one hundred and forty, then two ḥiqqahs and one bint labūn are due up to one hundred and forty-nine. When they are one hundred and fifty, then three ḥiqqahs are due up to one hundred and fifty-nine. When they are one hundred and sixty, then four bint labūn are due up to one hundred and sixty-nine. When they are one hundred and seventy, then three bint labūn and one ḥiqqah are due up to one hundred and seventy-nine. When they are one hundred and eighty, then two ḥiqqahs and two bint labūn are due up to one hundred and eighty-nine. When they are one hundred and ninety, then three ḥiqqahs and three bint labūn are due up to one hundred and ninety-nine. When they are two hundred, then four ḥiqqahs or five bint labūn, whichever age you find, you take according to what we have written in this document. Then everything of camels is based on that, taken according to what we have written in this document. No charity is taken from sheep until they reach forty sheep. When they reach forty sheep, then one sheep is due until they reach one hundred and twenty. When they are one hundred and twenty-one, then two sheep are due until they reach two hundred. When they are two hundred and one, then three sheep are due until they reach three hundred. If they exceed three hundred sheep, then only three sheep are due until they reach four hundred sheep. Then four sheep are due until they reach five hundred sheep. When they reach five hundred, then five sheep are due until they reach six hundred sheep. Then six sheep are due. When they reach seven hundred, then seven sheep are due until they reach eight hundred sheep. When they reach eight hundred sheep, then eight sheep are due until they reach nine hundred sheep. When they reach nine hundred sheep, then nine sheep are due until they reach one thousand sheep. When they reach one thousand sheep, then ten sheep are due. Then for every additional hundred sheep, one sheep is due.\" And part of what testifies to the authenticity of this hadith is..."],[1437,"When ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz was made caliph, he sent to Madinah seeking the covenant of the Prophet ﷺ and his practice regarding charities. He found with the family of ʿUmar b. al-Khattab the document of ʿUmar to his agents regarding charities, similar to the document of the Prophet ﷺ to ʿAmr b. Ḥazm. ʿUmar b. ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ordered his agents in charge of charities to act according to those two documents. In them was: \"The charity for camels: if they exceed ninety by one, then two ḥiqqahs are due up to one hundred and twenty. If they exceed one hundred and twenty by one, then three bint labūn are due until they reach one hundred and twenty-nine. If the camels are more than that, then nothing is due on what does not reach ten of them until they reach ten.\" As for the document of the Prophet ﷺ to ʿAmr b. Ḥazm, its chain meets the criteria of this book, and for that reason I mentioned the full context."],[1438,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the document that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to ʿAmr b. Ḥazm: \"When the value of gold reaches two hundred dirhams, then for every forty dirhams, one dirham is due.\""],[1439,"He wrote to the people of Yemen a document containing the obligatory shares, the sunnah, and the blood monies, and it was sent with ʿAmr b. Ḥazm, and it was read to the people of Yemen. This is its copy: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. From Muhammad the Prophet to Shuraḥbīl b. ʿAbd Kulāl, al-Ḥārith b. ʿAbd Kulāl, and Nuʿaym b. Kulāl, meaning Dhū Ruʿayn, Maʿāfir, and Hamdān. Now then: \"Your messenger has returned, and you have been given from the spoils one-fifth of Allah and what Allah has prescribed for the believers of the tithe on real estate: what the sky waters, or is flood-irrigated, or is watered by a spring, then a tithe is due on it when it reaches five awsuq. What is watered by a bucket or a waterwheel, then half a tithe is due on it when it reaches five awsuq. For every five grazing camels, one sheep is due until they reach twenty-four. If one more is added over twenty-four, then a bint makhāḍ is due; if not found, then a male ibn labūn, until they reach thirty-five. If one more is added over thirty-five, then a bint labūn is due until they reach forty-five. If one more is added over forty-five, then a ḥiqqah ṭarūqat al-faḥl is due until they reach sixty. If one more is added over sixty, then a jadhaʿah is due until they reach seventy-five. If one more is added over seventy-five, then a bint labūn is due until they reach ninety. If one more is added over ninety, then two ḥiqqahs ṭarūqatā al-jamal are due until they reach one hundred and twenty. What exceeds one hundred and twenty, then for every forty a bint labūn and for every fifty a ḥiqqah ṭarūqat al-jamal. For every thirty grazing cattle, a tabīʿ (a one-year-old male calf), and for every forty cattle, a cow. For every forty grazing sheep, one sheep is due until they reach one hundred and twenty. If one more is added over one hundred and twenty, then two sheep are due until they reach two hundred. If one more is added, then three sheep are due until they reach three hundred. If they increase, then for every additional hundred sheep, one sheep is due. Neither an old animal nor a lean one nor one with a defect is taken in charity, nor a male goat, unless the collector wishes. Neither combined between separated ones nor separated between a combined herd out of fear of charity. Whatever is taken from two partners, they settle between them equally. For every five ounces of silver, five dirhams are due, and what exceeds that, then for every forty dirhams, one dirham is due. Nothing is due on what is below five ounces. For every forty dinars, one dinar is due. Charity is not lawful for Muhammad nor for the family of Muhammad; it is only the zakah by which they purify themselves, and it is for the poor believers, in the cause of Allah, and for the wayfarer. Nothing is due on slaves, nor on a farm, nor on its workers if it pays its charity from the tithe. And there is nothing due on a Muslim slave nor on his horse.\""],[1440,"\"For every grazing camel, for every forty, an ibn labūn. Camels are not separated from their count. Whoever gives it seeking reward will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it and half of his camels as a firm command from the commands of our Lord. None of it is lawful for the family of Muhammad.\""],[1441,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to Yemen and ordered him to take from cattle: for every thirty cattle, a tabīʿ; for every forty cattle, a musinnah; and from every ḥālim (one who has reached puberty), one dinar or its equivalent in Maʿāfir cloth."],[1442,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him as a collector. His father said: \"Do not leave until you make a covenant with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" When he wanted to leave, he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"O Qays, do not come on the Day of Resurrection with a camel on your neck that has a grumble, or a cow that has a moo, or a sheep that has a bleat, and do not be like Abū Righāl.\" Saʿd said: \"Who is Abū Righāl?\" He said: \"A collector whom Ṣāliḥ sent. He found a man in al-Ṭāʾif with a small flock of about one hundred thin sheep except one sheep and a suckling boy with no mother, whose sustenance was the milk of that sheep. The owner of the sheep said: 'Who are you?' He said: 'I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He welcomed him and said: 'This is my flock, take whatever you like.' He looked at the milking sheep and said: 'This one.' The man said: 'This boy, as you see, has no food or drink other than it.' He said: 'If you love milk, I love it too.' He said: 'Take two sheep instead of it,' but he refused. He kept increasing and offering until he offered five thin sheep instead of it, but he refused. When he saw that, he took his bow and shot him, killing him. He said: 'It is not fitting for anyone to bring this news to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before me.' The owner of the sheep came to Ṣāliḥ the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. Ṣāliḥ said: 'O Allah, curse Abū Righāl. O Allah, curse Abū Righāl.' Saʿd b. ʿUbādah said: 'O Messenger of Allah, excuse Qays from the water-giving duty.'\""],[1443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Saʿd b. ʿUbādah as a collector and said: \"O Saʿd, beware of coming on the Day of Resurrection with a camel that you carry and it has a grumble.\" He said: \"I will not find it, and I will not come with it.\" So he excused him."],[1444,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me as a collector. I passed by a man, and he gathered his wealth for me, and I found nothing due on it except a bint makhāḍ. I said to him: \"Pay a bint makhāḍ, for it is your charity.\" He said: \"That is one that has no milk and no riding ability, but this is a great, fat she-camel, so take it.\" I said to him: \"I will not take what I have not been commanded to, and here is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ near you. If you like to come to him and present to him what you presented to me, then do so. If he accepts it from you, I will accept it, and if he rejects it to you, I will reject it.\" He said: \"I will do that.\" He went out with me and took the she-camel that he offered to me until we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"O Prophet of Allah, your messenger came to me to take from the charity of my wealth. By Allah, neither the Messenger of Allah ﷺ nor his messenger ever stood over my wealth before him. I gathered my wealth for him, and he claimed that nothing is due on it except a bint makhāḍ, and that is one that has no milk and no riding ability. I offered him a great she-camel to take, but he refused me. Here she is; I have brought her to you, O Messenger of Allah, take her.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"That is what is due from you. If you voluntarily give good, Allah will reward you for it, and we will accept it from you.\" He said: \"Here she is, O Messenger of Allah, I have brought her to you, take her.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to be taken and prayed for blessing in his wealth."],[1445,"\"No charity is due on silver until it reaches two hundred dirhams.\""],[1446,"\"Nothing is due on one hundred and ninety. When it reaches two hundred, then five dirhams are due.\""],[1447,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, that he sent to a man, and the man sent to him a young weaned camel with its nose pierced. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah’s collector and His Messenger’s collector came to him, and he sent a young weaned camel with its nose pierced. O Allah, do not bless him in it nor in his camels.” That reached the man, so he sent to him a she-camel of her finest and most beautiful. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said reached so-and-so, so he sent a she-camel of her finest. O Allah, bless him in it and in his camels.”"],[1448,"Some people from the people of Syria came to Umar and said, “We have acquired wealth, horses, and slaves, and we would like there to be zakāh and purification for us in them.” He said, “What my two companions before me did I will do.” Umar consulted Ali, along with a group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Ali said, “It is good, if it is not a fixed jizyah taken from them every year.”"],[1449,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, that he only took charity from wheat, barley, raisins, and dates."],[1450,"“On what the sky waters, and what is watered by underground springs, and by flood water, a tenth is due; and on what is watered by artificial means, half a tenth. And that applies only to dates, wheat, and grains. As for cucumbers, melons, pomegranates, and sugar cane, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has pardoned them.”"],[1451,"“Do not take charity except from these four: barley, wheat, raisins, and dates.”"],[1452,"“There is no zakāh due on a Muslim man for his vineyard or his crops if they are less than five wasqs.”"],[1453,"He forbade two varieties of dates: the juʿrūr and the color of the ḥubayq. He said, “People used to deliberately select the worst of their fruits and give them in charity, so they were forbidden from two varieties of dates, and then it was revealed: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that]}”"],[1454,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that charity be given. A man came with clusters from this sahl — Sufyan said, meaning the shīṣ (inferior dates) — and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who brought this?” No one would bring something but it was attributed to the one who brought it. Then it was revealed: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that]} [Al-Baqarah: 267]. He said, “And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the juʿrūr and the color of ḥubayq from being taken in charity.” Al-Zuhrī said, “Two varieties of charity dates.”"],[1455,"There were people who deliberately selected the worst of their fruits, so Allah ﷻ revealed: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that], while you would not take it [yourself] except with closed eyes} [Al-Baqarah: 267]. He said, “So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two varieties: the juʿrūr and the color of ḥubayq.”"],[1456,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When you estimate the produce, take and leave a third. If you do not take or leave a third — Shuʿbah doubted about the third — then leave a fourth.”"],[1457,"Umar b. al-Khaṭṭāb sent him to estimate the dates, and he said, “When you come to a land, estimate it and leave for them the amount that they eat.”"],[1458,"A man from Banū ʿĀmir passed by him, and it was said, “This is one of the wealthiest people.” Abū Hurayrah called him and asked him about that, and it was said, “Yes, I have a hundred red camels, and I have a hundred brown ones, and I have such and such sheep.” Abū Hurayrah said, “Beware of the pads of camels, beware of the hooves of sheep. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There is no man who has camels and does not pay their due in their strength, their ease, their hardship, and their prosperity, except that they will come forth to him on a vast, level plain, as numerous, as swift, as fat, and as large as they can be — Shuʿbah doubted — and they will trample him with their pads and gore him with their horns. Every time the last of them passes over him, the first of them will be returned to him on a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until judgment is passed among the people, and he sees his path. And there is no servant who has cattle and does not pay their due in their strength and their ease.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘And in their strength and their ease, their hardship and their prosperity, except that they will come forth to him on a vast, level plain, as numerous, as swift, as fat, and as large as they can be, and they will trample him with their hooves and gore him with their horns. Every time the first of them passes over him, the last of them will be returned to him on a day whose length is fifty thousand years, until Allah judges between the people, and he sees his path.’” Al-ʿAbbās said to him, “And what is the due of camels, O Abū Hurayrah?” He said, “You give the noble one, lend the abundant-milk one, give the riding camel to the one whose camel is exhausted, lend the stallion for breeding, and give the milk to drink.”"],[1459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the zakat from the qabaliyyah mines, and he granted Bilal b. al-Harith the whole of al-‘Aqiq. When ‘Umar came, he said to Bilal: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not grant it to you to hold it back from the people; he only granted it to you to be worked. So ‘Umar b. al-Khattab allotted al-‘Aqiq to the people. Al-Bukhari used Nu‘aym b. Hammad as evidence, and Muslim used al-Darawardi."],[1460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from Banu Makhzum to collect zakat, and he said to Abu Rafi‘: Accompany me so that we may get some of it. He said: No, not until I come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He went to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he said: Zakat is not lawful for us, and the mawali of a people are of themselves."],[1461,"A collector of unlawful taxes will not enter Paradise."],[1462,"While the Prophet ﷺ was in her house, and with him were some men of his Companions conversing, a man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, how much zakat is due on such-and-such amount of dates? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Such-and-such amount of dates. The man said: So-and-so has transgressed against me and taken from me such-and-such, and added a sa‘. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Then how will it be when there are appointed over you those who will transgress against you more severely than this transgression? The people engaged in discussion and the talk overwhelmed them, until one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, if a man is absent from you with his camels, livestock, and crops, and he pays the zakat of his wealth, but the right is transgressed against him, what should he do while he is absent? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Whoever pays the zakat of his wealth with a good heart, seeking thereby the face of Allah and the abode of the Hereafter, and does not hide anything of his wealth, and establishes the prayer and pays the zakat, then the right is transgressed against him, and he takes up his weapon and fights and is killed, then he is a martyr."],[1463,"In the year of al-Ramadiyy, when the land became barren, ‘Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to ‘Amr b. al-‘As: From ‘Abdullah ‘Umar, Commander of the Believers, to ‘Amr b. al-‘As. Al-‘Umari informed me: What do you care if you are fat and those with you are fat, while I and those with me are thin? O help! ‘Amr wrote back: Peace be upon you. To proceed: Labbayk, labbayk. A caravan has come to you whose first is with you and whose last is with me, and I hope to find a way to send by sea. When the first caravan arrived, he called al-Zubayr and said: Go out with the first of this caravan and meet it tomorrow, and carry to every household as much as you can carry to me. For those you cannot carry to, order for every household a camel with its load, and tell them to clothe the people as they have come, and to slaughter the camel, carry its hair, cut its meat into strips, use its skin for sandals, and then take a piece of dried meat, a piece of fat, and a bowl of flour, cook it and eat until Allah brings them provision. Al-Zubayr refused to go out, so he said: By Allah, you will not find the like of it until you leave this world. Then he called another, I think Talhah, and he came. Then he called Abu ‘Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, and he went out for that. When he returned, he sent him a thousand dinars. Abu ‘Ubaydah said: I did not work for you, O Ibn Khattab; I worked only for Allah, and I will not take anything for that. ‘Umar said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us for things he sent us for, and we disliked it, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ insisted upon us. So accept it, O man, and use it to help you in your worldly affairs. So Abu ‘Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah accepted it."],[1464,"Whomever we appoint to a task and give him provision, then whatever he takes after that is unlawful gain."],[1465,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: Whoever is a worker for us, let him acquire a wife; if he does not have a servant, let him acquire a servant; and if he does not have a dwelling, let him acquire a dwelling. He said: And I was informed that the Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever takes anything other than that, he is a defrauder or a thief."],[1466,"The collector of zakat with justice is like the warrior in the path of Allah until he returns to his house."],[1467,"The best charity is that given to a hostile relative."],[1468,"Charity to a poor person is charity, and to a relative it is two: charity and maintaining ties."],[1469,"Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and healthy."],[1470,"Charity is not lawful for a rich person, nor for one who is strong and capable."],[1471,"“Whoever begs while he has enough to make him self-sufficient will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches or gashes or lacerations on his face.” It was said, “O Messenger of God, what constitutes sufficiency?” He said, “Fifty dirhams or their equivalent in gold.”"],[1472,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Charity is not lawful for a rich person except for five: a fighter in the path of God, an administrator over it, a debtor, or a man who had a poor neighbor and charity was given to the poor man, then the poor man gave it as a gift to the rich man."],[1473,"Al-Qaʿnabī narrated to us, in what was read to Mālik, from Zayd b. Aslam, from ʿAṭāʾ b. Yasār, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Charity is not lawful except for five,” and he mentioned the hadith. This is according to my condition in the preface of the book that it is authentic, for Mālik may send it as mursal, but a trustworthy narrator connects it and gives it a chain, and the decisive statement is the statement of the trustworthy narrator who connects it and gives it a chain."],[1474,"“Whoever is struck by poverty and brings it to the people, his poverty will not be removed; but whoever brings it to God, God will soon bring him wealth—either by a near death or by quick riches.”"],[1475,"The hands are three: the hand of God is the highest, the hand of the giver is the one that follows it, and the hand of the beggar is the lowest. So give from your surplus and do not hold back from yourself."],[1476,"The hands are three: the hand of God is the highest, the hand of the giver is the one that follows it, and the hand of the beggar is the lowest until the Day of Resurrection. So refrain from begging as much as you are able."],[1477,"“So refrain from begging as much as you are able.”"],[1478,"When this verse was revealed: {And those who hoard} gold and silver [Qur’an 9:34], it weighed heavily on the Muslims. ʿUmar said, “I will relieve you of your distress.” He went and said, “O Prophet of God, this verse has weighed heavily on your companions.” He said, “God has only made zakāh obligatory in order to purify what remains of your wealth, and He has only made inheritance obligatory”—and he mentioned a word—“so that it may be for those after you.” He said, “Then ʿUmar exclaimed Allāhu akbar.”"],[1479,"“The Messenger of God ﷺ made zakāh al-fiṭr obligatory as a purification for the fast from idle talk and obscenity, and as food for the poor. Whoever pays it before the prayer, it is an accepted zakāh; and whoever pays it after the prayer, it is an ordinary charity.”"],[1480,"“The people used to give ṣadaqat al-fiṭr during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ as a ṣāʿ of dates, or a ṣāʿ of barley, or sulṭ, or raisins.”"],[1481,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say when he made ṣadaqat al-fiṭr obligatory: a ṣāʿ of dates or a ṣāʿ of barley. And nothing was given except dates."],[1482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to give the zakah of fitr before the zakah (on wealth) was revealed. When the zakah (on wealth) was revealed, he neither commanded us nor forbade us, and we continue to do it."],[1483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded a crier in the middle of Makkah to announce: 'The zakah of fitr is a true obligation upon every Muslim, young or old, male or female, free or slave, present or Bedouin: one sa' of barley or dates.'"],[1484,"The Prophet ﷺ urged the giving of the Ramadan charity upon every person: one sa' of dates, or one sa' of barley, or one sa' of wheat."],[1485,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made obligatory the zakah of fitr: one sa' of dates or one sa' of wheat upon every free person or slave, male or female, among the Muslims."],[1486,"Abu Sa'id (al-Khudri) — when zakah al-fitr was mentioned in his presence — said: 'I will not give anything except what I used to give at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: one sa' of dates, or one sa' of wheat, or one sa' of barley, or one sa' of dried curd (aqit).' A man from the group said to him: 'Or two mudds of wheat?' He said: 'No, that is the valuation of Mu'awiyah. I do not accept it and I will not act upon it.' These chains of transmission that I have mentioned earlier regarding the sa' of wheat are all sound, and the most famous of them is the hadith of Abu Ma'shar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, in which we have a high chain, but I have omitted it because it is not according to the criterion of this book. And it has been narrated from 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ."],[1487,"He said regarding zakah al-fitr: for every young or old, free or slave, one sa' of wheat or one sa' of dates."],[1488,"He heard 'Ali b. Abi Talib commanding the zakah al-fitr, saying: 'One sa' of dates, or one sa' of barley, or one sa' of wheat, or one sa' of sult (a kind of barley), or one sa' of raisins.'"],[1489,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'Whoever has food, let him give charity with one sa' of wheat, or one sa' of barley, or one sa' of dates, or one sa' of flour, or one sa' of raisins, or one sa' of sult.'"],[1490,"She narrated to him that they used to give the zakah al-fitr during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the mudd by which the people of the household measured their daily food, or the sa' by which they measured, and all the people of Madinah did that."],[1491,"Who will guarantee for me that he will not ask people for anything, and I will guarantee for him Paradise? Thawban said: 'I will.' And he never asked people for anything."],[1492,"‘Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked Is there anyone of you who provided food to a poor man today? Abu Bakr said I entered the mosque where a beggar was begging ; I found a piece of bread in the hand of ‘Abdal-Rahman which I took and gave it to him (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1670)"],[1493,"Whoever asks you by Allah, give him. Whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge. Whoever invites you, respond to him. Whoever gives you a gift, repay him. If you do not find anything with which to repay him, then supplicate for him until you think that you have repaid him."],[1494,"Abu 'Awanah narrated to us — and as for the hadith of Jarir —"],[1495,"Jarir narrated to us. As for the hadith of 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Muslim,"],[1496,"\"Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; and whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge; and whoever invites you, accept his invitation.\""],[1497,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him with something like an egg of gold and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I found this in a mine. Take it, for it is charity; I own nothing besides it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. Then he came to him from his right side and said the same, and he turned away from him. Then he came to him from his left side, and he turned away from him. Then he came to him from behind, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and threw it at him. Had it hit him, it would have hurt him and wounded him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, \"One of you brings what he owns and says, 'This is charity,' then sits and begs from people. The best charity is that which is given out of surplus wealth.\""],[1498,"He heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: A man entered the mosque, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered that they throw clothes to him, so they threw them to him. Then he ordered that he be given two garments from them. Then he urged charity, and the man came and threw one of the two garments (as charity). He shouted at him and said, \"Take your garment.\""],[1499,"He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which charity is best?\" He said, \"The effort of the one with little, and begin with those you support.\""],[1500,"I heard 'Umar b. al-Khattab say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us one day to give charity, and it coincided with wealth I had. I said, \"Today I will surpass Abu Bakr, if I ever surpass him.\" So I came with half of my wealth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What have you left for your family?\" I said, \"The like of it.\" Abu Bakr came with all that he had, and he said, \"O Abu Bakr, what have you left for your family?\" He said, \"I have left them Allah and His Messenger.\" I said, \"I will never race you to anything again.\""],[1501,"From Sa'd b. 'Ubadah: He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Which charity is most pleasing to you?\" He said, \"Providing water.\" Hammam agreed with him from Qatadah."],[1502,"Sa'd came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Which charity is most pleasing to you?\" He said, \"Water.\""],[1503,"From Maymunah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: I had a slave-girl, and I freed her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me and said, \"May Allah reward you. If you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.\""],[1504,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered charity, and a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a dinar.\" He said, \"Give it in charity on yourself.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Give it in charity on your child.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Give it in charity on your wife\" or he said, \"on your spouse.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"Give it in charity on your servant.\" He said, \"I have another.\" He said, \"You know best.\""],[1505,"\"It is enough sin for a man to waste those whom he is obligated to feed.\""],[1506,"Abu Amir al-Aqadi and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us. And Abu al-Abbas Muhammad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Bishr ibn Umar and Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, they said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Kathir, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and said: \"Beware of miserliness, for those before you were destroyed only by miserliness. It commanded them to be stingy and they were stingy, commanded them to sever ties and they severed them, and commanded them to sin and they sinned.\""],[1507,"\"Every person will be in the shade of his charity until judgment is passed between the people,\" or he said, \"until it is decided between the people.\""],[1508,"That deeds will boast, and charity will say: \"I am the best of you.\""],[1509,"\"A dirham has surpassed a hundred thousand.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how can a dirham surpass a hundred thousand?\" He said, \"A man had two dirhams and took one of them and gave it in charity, and another man had much wealth and took from its surplus a hundred thousand.\""],[1510,"Three whom Allah loves and three whom Allah hates. As for the three whom Allah loves: a man who came to a people and asked them by Allah, not by any kinship between them and him, and a man from among their descendants lagged behind and gave him secretly, none knowing of his gift except Allah and the one to whom he gave; and a people who traveled through their night until sleep became dearer to them than anything equal to it, so they dismounted and laid down their heads, and a man stood up flattering Me and reciting My verses; and a man who was in a detachment and met the enemy and they were defeated, so he advanced with his chest until he was killed or victory was granted to him. And the three whom Allah hates: the adulterous old man, the arrogant poor man, and the oppressive rich man."],[1511,"\"No man goes out with anything of charity until the jaws of seventy devils are loosened from it.\""],[1512,"That the Prophet ﷺ commanded from every walled garden a bunch of dates for the mosque."],[1513,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted the sale of unripe dates for ripe dates by estimation, one wasq, two wasqs, three, and four, and he said: \"For every ten wasqs, a bunch of dates is to be placed in the mosque for the poor.\""],[1514,"That his grandmother narrated to him, and she was Umm Bujayd, and she claimed that she was among those who gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, a poor person stands at my door and we find nothing to give him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"If you find nothing to give him except a burnt hoof, then give it to him in his hand.\" This hadith has a sound chain of narration, but they did not record it."],[1515,"\"There are two types of jealousy: one Allah loves and the other Allah hates. And two types of pride: one Allah loves and the other Allah hates. Jealousy in suspicion Allah loves, and jealousy without suspicion Allah hates. Pride when a man gives charity Allah loves, and pride from arrogance Allah hates.\""],[1516,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Allah ﷻ says: I asked My servant for a loan but he did not lend to Me, and My servant insulted Me while he did not know. He says: 'Woe to time! Woe to time!' And I am time.\""],[1517,"That he entered Madinah and saw a man surrounded by people. He asked, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"Abu Hurayrah.\" He said, \"So I approached him until I sat before him while he was narrating to the people. When he fell silent and was alone, I said, 'I adjure you by Allah, by right and right, to narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and knew.' Abu Hurayrah said, 'I will do so. I will narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me, which I understood and knew.' Then Abu Hurayrah sobbed, remained quiet for a while, then recovered and said, 'I will narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me while he and I were in this house, with no one else present except me and him.' Then Abu Hurayrah sobbed again, remained so for a while, then recovered, wiped his face, and said, 'I will do so. I will narrate to you a hadith the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me while he and I were in this house, with no one else present except me and him.' Then Abu Hurayrah sobbed again, then fell forward on his face, and I supported him for a long time. Then he recovered and said...\""],[1518,"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left at his death neither a dinar nor a dirham, nor a slave, nor a slave woman, except his mule, his weapons, and land which he left as charity."],[1519,"When Uthman b. Affan was dying, he looked down upon them from above his house and said, \"I remind you by Allah: do you know that the well of Rumah—no one drank from it except for a price—so I bought it with my own money and made it for the rich, the poor, and the wayfarer?\" They said, \"Yes.\""],[1520,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, from what he read to Malik, from Sa'id b. Amr b. Shurahbil b. Sa'id b. Abbad, from his father, from his grandfather, that he said: Sa'd b. Ubadah went out with the Prophet ﷺ on one of his expeditions, and the death of Sa'd's mother approached. It was said to her, \"Make a will.\" She said, \"Concerning what should I make a will? The wealth belongs to Sa'd.\" She died before Sa'd returned. When Sa'd returned, that was mentioned to him, and he said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Sa'd said, \"The garden of such-and-such is charity on her behalf\"—the garden, he named it."],[1521,"To the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"My mother has died. Will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"I have a garden, and I call upon you to witness that I have given it in charity on her behalf.\""],[1522,"\"When the first night of Ramadan comes, the devils and the rebellious jinn are chained, the gates of the Fire are closed and not one of them is opened, the gates of Paradise are opened and not one of them is closed, and a caller cries out: 'O seeker of good, come forward; O seeker of evil, desist! And Allah has those freed from the Fire.'\""],[1523,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, direct me to an action.\" He said, \"You must fast, for there is nothing equal to it.\""],[1524,"Allah revealed to Yahya b. Zakariyya (peace be upon them both) five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon, but it seemed he was slow in doing so. Isa ﷺ came to him and said, \"Allah has commanded you with five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon. Either you tell them, or I tell them.\" He said, \"O my brother, do not do that, for I fear that if you precede me with them, the earth will swallow me and I will be punished.\" He said, \"So he gathered the Children of Israel in Jerusalem until the mosque was full, and they sat on the balconies. Then he addressed them, saying, 'Allah has revealed to me five words: that I act upon them and command the Children of Israel to act upon them. The first of them: do not associate anything with Allah. The likeness of one who associates with Allah is like a man who bought a slave with his pure wealth, gold or silver, then lodged him in a house and said, \"Work and bring the earnings to me.\" But the slave worked and brought the earnings to other than his master. Which of you would be pleased to have his slave do that? Allah created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with Him. When you stand for prayer, do not turn away, for Allah faces His servant as long as he does not turn away. He commanded you to fast, and the likeness of that is like a man in a group with a pouch of musk: all of them love to find its fragrance. The fragrance of fasting is like the fragrance of musk. He commanded you to give charity, and the likeness of that is like a man captured by the enemy; they tied his hand to his neck and brought him forward to strike his neck. He kept saying, \"Will you let me ransom myself from you?\" And he gave little and much until he ransomed himself. He commanded you to remember Allah much, and the likeness of remembering Allah is like a man whom the enemy pursued swiftly in his tracks until he reached a fortified fortress and secured himself in it. Likewise, the servant does not escape from Satan except by the remembrance of Allah.'\""],[1525,"\"The fasting person has a supplication at the time of breaking the fast: 'O Allah, I ask You by Your mercy that encompasses all things to forgive my sins.'\""],[1526,"He said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ broke his fast, he said, \"Thirst is gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is established, if Allah wills.\""],[1527,"\"The thankful eater is like the patient faster.\""],[1528,"We were in Ramadan during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished broke the fast and ransomed with food for a poor person, until the verse was revealed: {So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it} [al-Baqarah 185]—the verse."],[1529,"\"Allah has made the crescent moons as markers of time. So when you see it, fast, and when you see it, break the fast. If it is obscured for you, then estimate for it. And know that the months do not exceed thirty.\""],[1530,"I heard A'ishah say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pay more attention to the crescent of Sha'ban than to any other, then he would fast upon seeing the crescent of Ramadan; if it was obscured from him, he would count thirty days and then fast.'"],[1531,"The people sighted the crescent, and I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I had seen it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted and commanded the people to fast. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it."],[1532,"We were with 'Ammar b. Yasir when he ordered a roasted sheep and said, 'Eat.' Some of the people held back, and one of them said, 'I am fasting.' 'Ammar said, 'Whoever fasts on the day of doubt has disobeyed Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.'"],[1533,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I have seen the crescent,' meaning the crescent of Ramadan. He said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Do you bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'O Bilal, announce to the people that they should fast tomorrow.' Sufyan al-Thawri and Hammad b. Salama followed him in narrating it from Simak b. Harb."],[1534,"A bedouin man came on the night of the crescent of Ramadan and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have seen the crescent.' He said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then announce to the people that they should fast.'"],[1535,"A bedouin came on the night of the crescent of Ramadan and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have seen the crescent.' He said, 'Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then he announced that they should fast.'"],[1536,"They were instructed not to stand (for prayer) and not to fast. Then a bedouin came from al-Harrah and testified that he had seen the crescent. The Prophet ﷺ ordered Bilal to announce that they should stand (for prayer) and fast. Al-Bukhari used the hadiths of 'Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim used the hadiths of Simak b. Harb and Hammad b. Salama as evidence. This hadith is authentic, but they did not include it."],[1537,"I entered upon 'Ikrimah on the day about which there is doubt regarding Ramadan, and he was eating. He said, 'Come near and eat.' I said, 'I am fasting.' He said, 'By Allah, you will come near.' I said, 'Then narrate to me.' He said:"],[1538,"'Observe the crescent of Sha'ban for Ramadan.'"],[1539,"Dawn is of two types. As for the first, it does not prohibit food nor permit the prayer. As for the second, it prohibits food and permits the prayer."],[1540,"'Let not the call of Bilal deceive you, nor this whiteness of the pillar of dawn, until it spreads.'"],[1541,"'Seek help in the pre-dawn meal for fasting during the day, and in the midday nap for standing in prayer at night.'"],[1542,"“When one of you hears the call while the vessel is in his hand, he should not put it down until he fulfills his need from it.”"],[1543,"“The Prophet ﷺ vomited and broke his fast.” Then I met Thawban in the mosque of Damascus and mentioned that to him, and he said, “He spoke the truth; I poured for him the water for his ablution.”"],[1544,"“The Prophet ﷺ vomited and broke his fast.”"],[1545,"The translation of the given Arabic sentence is: \"That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, fasted and then broke his fast.\""],[1546,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If the fasting person mistakenly eats or drinks, then he should continue fasting, and if he vomits involuntarily, then it does not break his fast.\" This was narrated by Isa ibn Yunus from Hisham."],[1547,"“Whoever is overcome by vomiting is not obliged to make up the fast, but whoever intentionally vomits must make it up.”"],[1548,"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when eighteen nights of Ramadan had passed. When he was at al-Baqi', the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at a man being cupped and said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.” Al-Awza'i established this chain and made it sound, clarifying each narrator's hearing from his source. “Shayban b. 'Abd al-Rahman al-Nahwi and Hisham b. Abi 'Abd Allah al-Dastuwa'i concurred with him on that, and all of them are trustworthy.” If so, the hadith is authentic according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[1549,"Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking in al-Baqi' during Ramadan, he saw a man being cupped and said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.” Ahmad b. Hanbal said, “And it is the most authentic report on this topic.”"],[1550,"He informed him; he said: While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was walking in al-Baqi' during Ramadan, he saw a man being cupped and said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.” These chains, in which the hearing of the narrators who transmitted them is clarified and who are trustworthy and precise, are not to be deemed defective because of a disagreement among those who are criticized concerning Abu Qilabah or others. And according to Yahya b. Abi Kathir, there is another chain that is authentic according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs."],[1551,"“The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast,” and in the hadith of Ishaq al-Dabari, “and the one who seeks cupping.” Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ishaq said in his hadith: I heard al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-'Azim say: I heard 'Ali b. al-Madini say: I do not know any hadith about the cupper and the one cupped more authentic than this. Mu'awiyah b. Sallam concurred with him from Yahya b. Abi Kathir."],[1552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon a man in al-Baqi' while he was being cupped, and he was holding my hand, when eighteen nights of Ramadan had passed, and said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.” I heard Muhammad b. Salih say: I heard Ahmad b. Salamah say: I heard Ishaq b. Ibrahim say: This is a sound chain that establishes proof. This hadith is authentic with multiple chains, and he held this view—may Allah be pleased with our Imam Abu Ya'qub—for he ruled a hadith whose authenticity is evident as authentic and acted upon it. Al-Thawri and Shu'bah agreed on reporting it from 'Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilabah in this manner."],[1553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Ma'qil b. Yasar on the morning of the eighteenth of Ramadan while he was being cupped and said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.”"],[1554,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man being cupped on the seventeenth of Ramadan and said, “The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.” Abu Muhammad al-Hasan b. Muhammad b. Ishaq al-Isfara'ini narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Bara' narrated to us: 'Ali b. al-Madini narrated to us; he said: The hadith of Shaddad b. Aws from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he saw a man being cupped in Ramadan, was reported by 'Asim al-Ahwal from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ash'ath, and reported by Yahya b. Abi Kathir from Abu Qilabah from Abu Asma' from Thawban. “I consider both hadiths authentic, for it is possible that he heard it from both of them.” As for the license for cupping for a fasting person, Muhammad b. Isma'il al-Bukhari included it in the Sahih."],[1555,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped while he was fasting. Now listen to the words of the Imam of the people of hadith in his era, without dispute, on this hadith, so that you may be guided by it to the most correct view."],[1556,"And Abu Ali al-Hafiz informed me; Abu Ya'la reported to us; they said: Abu Khaythama Zuhayr b. Harb narrated to us; Rawh b. Ubada narrated to us from Sa'id b. Abi Aruba from Matar al-Warraq from Bakr b. Abd Allah al-Muzani from Abu Rafi', who said: We entered upon Abu Musa while he was being cupped after Maghrib. I said, 'Why were you not cupped during the day?' He said, 'Do you command me to shed my blood while I am fasting? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast.\"'"],[1557,"While I was sleeping, two men came to me, took me by my upper arms, and brought me to a rugged mountain. They said to me, 'Climb.' I said, 'I cannot.' They said, 'We will make it easy for you.' So I climbed until I reached the top of the mountain, and there I heard loud voices. I said, 'What are these voices?' They said, 'This is the howling of the people of the Fire.' Then they took me on, and I saw people hanging by their hamstrings, their cheeks split, and blood flowing from their mouths. I said, 'Who are these?' They said, 'These are those who break their fast before it is lawful to do so.'"],[1558,"Whoever breaks his fast in Ramadan out of forgetfulness, there is no makeup for him and no expiation."],[1559,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Fasting is not from eating and drinking; rather, fasting is from vain talk and obscenity. If someone insults you or behaves ignorantly toward you, say, 'I am fasting.'"],[1560,"Many a fasting person gets nothing from his fast but hunger, and many a standing person gets nothing from his standing but sleeplessness."],[1561,"He said: One day I felt desire and kissed while I was fasting. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Today I did a grave thing: I kissed while fasting.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What do you think if you rinsed your mouth with water while fasting?' I said, 'There is no harm in that.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'So this.' This is a sound hadith according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[1562,"The religion will remain uppermost as long as people hasten to break the fast, because the Jews and Christians delay it."],[1563,"Whoever finds dates, let him break his fast with them; and whoever does not, let him break his fast on water, for it is purifying."],[1564,"When one of you is fasting, let him break his fast with dates; if he does not find dates, then with water, for water is purifying."],[1565,"He heard Anas b. Malik say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to break his fast with fresh dates before praying; if there were no fresh dates, then with dried dates; if there were no dried dates, he would take a few sips of water."],[1566,"He would not pray Maghrib until he broke his fast, even if with a sip of water."],[1567,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-'Arj pouring water on his head from the heat while he was fasting."],[1568,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated on what was recited from Malik, from Sumayy, the freed slave of Abu Bakr, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman, from some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ , who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding the people during his travel in the year of conquest, saying: \"Prepare yourselves for your enemy.\""],[1569,"Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness."],[1570,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who works with riding camels; I treat them, travel on them, and hire them out. Sometimes this month—meaning the month of Ramadan—comes upon me while I find strength and I am a young man, and I find that fasting, O Messenger of Allah, is easier for me than delaying it so that it becomes a debt. Should I fast, O Messenger of Allah, for greater reward, or should I break the fast? He said: \"Whichever you wish, O Hamzah.\""],[1571,"The Prophet ﷺ traveled during Ramadan, and fasting became severe for a man among his companions. His riding camel began to wander with him under the trees, and the Prophet ﷺ was informed of his condition. He ordered him to break the fast. Then the Prophet ﷺ called for a vessel, placed it in his hand, and drank while the people were watching."],[1572,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Marr al-Zahran, and food was brought. He said to Abu Bakr and 'Umar: \"Come near and eat.\" They said: \"We are fasting.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Work for your companion; prepare to depart for your companion; come near and eat.\""],[1573,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"My community will continue to follow my Sunnah as long as it does not wait for the stars to break its fast.\" When the Prophet ﷺ was fasting, he would order a man to climb a hill, and when he said that the sun had set, he would break the fast."],[1574,"He heard 'A'ishah say: \"The most beloved of months to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to fast was Sha'ban, then he would connect it to Ramadan.\""],[1575,"\"The Day of 'Arafah, the Day of Sacrifice, and the days of Tashriq are our festival, O people of Islam; they are days of eating and drinking.\""],[1576,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fasting on the Day of 'Arafah at 'Arafat."],[1577,"It is as if I am looking at 'Ali b. Abi Talib on the white mule of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mountain pass of the Ansar, saying: \"O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'These are not days of fasting; they are days of eating, drinking, and remembrance.'\""],[1578,"He entered upon 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr, whose father was 'Amr b. al-'As, and he brought them food. He said: \"Eat.\" He replied: \"I am fasting.\" 'Amr said: \"Eat, for these are the days in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to order us to break the fast and forbade us to fast.\" Malik said: \"They are the days of Tashriq.\""],[1579,"\"Whoever fasts perpetually has neither fasted nor broken his fast,\" or \"he has not fasted and has not broken his fast.\""],[1580,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"So-and-so does not break his fast during the entire daytime forever.\" He said, \"He has neither fasted nor broken his fast.\""],[1581,"Do not fast on Saturday except what is obligatory upon you, and if one of you finds nothing but the bark of a grapevine or a twig of a tree, let him chew it."],[1582,"He informed him that Ibn Abbas and some people from among the companions of the Messenger ﷺ sent me to Umm Salamah to ask her about which days the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted most with her. She said, \"Saturday and Sunday.\" So I returned to them and informed them, and it was as if they rejected that. They all arose and went to her and said, \"We sent this one to you about such-and-such, and he mentioned that you said such-and-such.\" She said, \"He has spoken the truth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasted most often on Saturday and Sunday, and he used to say, 'They are two festival days for the polytheists, and I want to differ from them.'\""],[1583,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ while we were with him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my husband Safwan b. al-Mu'attal beats me when I pray, breaks my fast when I fast, and does not pray the dawn prayer until the sun rises.\" He said, and Safwan was with him. He said, \"So he asked him about what she said.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, as for her saying that he beats me when I pray, she recites two surahs which I forbade her, and I said, 'If it were one surah, it would suffice the people.' As for her saying that he breaks my fast when I fast, she goes off and fasts, while I am a young man and cannot be patient.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on that day, \"A woman is not to fast except with her husband's permission.\" And as for her saying that he does not pray until the sun rises, we are a household known for that; we hardly wake up until the sun rises. He said, \"When you wake up, then pray.\""],[1584,"Friday is a festival, so do not make your festival day a day of fasting unless you fast before it or after it."],[1585,"I asked Abu Dharr, saying, \"Did you ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the Night of Decree?\" He said, \"I was the one who asked people about it.\" He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me about the Night of Decree. Is it in Ramadan or in other than it?' He said, 'Rather, it is in Ramadan.'\" He said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, will it be with the prophets as long as they exist, and when the prophets are taken, it is lifted, or is it until the Day of Resurrection?' He said, 'Rather, it is until the Day of Resurrection.'\" He said, \"Then I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, in which Ramadan is it?' He said, 'Seek it in the first ten and the last ten.'\" He said, \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued speaking and I seized a moment of his inattention and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, in which of the two tens?' He said, 'Seek it in the last ten; do not ask me about anything after that.'\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued speaking and I seized a moment of his inattention and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I adjure you to tell me, or will you not tell me, in which ten it is?\" He said, \"He became angry with me with an anger like which he had never become angry with me before or after, and he said, 'If Allah willed, He would have made it known to you. Seek it in the last seven.'\""],[1586,"Abu al-Hasan Ahmad b. Abi Uthman al-Zahid narrated to me, Abu Abdullah Muhammad b. Barawayh al-Mu'adhdhin narrated to us, Yahya b. Yahya narrated to us, Abdullah b. Idris informed us, Asim b. Kulayb al-Jarmi narrated to us from his father from Ibn Abbas, who said: Umar b. al-Khattab used to invite me with the companions of Muhammad ﷺ and say to me, \"Do not speak until they speak.\" He said, \"So he invited them and asked them about the Night of Decree. He said, 'What do you think of the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Seek it in the last ten\"—which night do you think it is?'\" He said, \"Some of them said, 'The twenty-first night,' some said, 'The twenty-third night,' and another said, 'The twenty-fifth night,' while I was silent. He said, 'What is the matter with you that you do not speak?' I said, 'If you permit me, O Commander of the Faithful, I will speak.' He said, 'I did not send for you except that you speak.' I said, 'I will tell you my opinion.' He said, 'About that we ask you.' I said, 'The seventh. I see that Allah mentioned seven heavens, and of the earths seven, and created man from seven, and the plants of the earth emerge from seven.' He said, 'This has told me what I know. What do you think of what I do not know—what is your saying that the plants of the earth are from seven?' I said, 'Allah says: {We split the earth in clefts} [Abasa 26] until His saying {and fruit and pasture} [Abasa 31], and pasture is the plants of the earth from what the animals eat and people do not eat.' He said, 'Umar said, \"Were you unable to say as this boy said, whose skull bones have not yet knit together? By Allah, I do not think the saying is other than what you said.\"' He said, \"And he said, 'I had commanded you not to speak until they speak, and I now command you to speak with them.'\" Ibn Idris said, \"Abd al-Malik narrated to us from Said b. Jubayr from Ibn Abbas the like of it.\""],[1587,"I mentioned the Night of Decree in the presence of Abu Bakrah, and he said, \"I do not seek it except in the last ten: in the ninth or seventh remaining, or the fifth remaining, or the third remaining, or the last night.\" He used not to pray in the twenty nights except as he prayed throughout the rest of the year, but when the ten entered, he exerted himself."],[1588,"The voluntary faster is the commander of himself: if he wishes, he fasts, and if he wishes, he breaks his fast."],[1589,"The one who fasts voluntarily has the choice: if he wishes, he fasts, and if he wishes, he breaks his fast."],[1590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to observe i'tikaf in the last ten of Ramadan, then he did not observe i'tikaf one year. When the next year came, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days."],[1591,"The Prophet ﷺ used to observe i'tikaf in the last days of Ramadan, then he traveled one year and did not observe i'tikaf, and he observed i'tikaf for twenty nights in the following year."],[1592,"\"There is no fasting required of the one performing i'tikaf unless he imposes it upon himself.\""],[1593,"that he should observe i'tikaf for a day. So he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Observe i'tikaf and fast one day.\" The second hadith."],[1594,"\"There is no i'tikaf except with fasting.\""],[1595,"that he had made a concession for the very old man who is not able to fast, and he ordered that he feed one who knows that he cannot bear it."],[1596,"\"The very old man has been given a concession to break the fast and to feed one poor person for each day, with no making up required of him.\""],[1597,"I heard al-Nu'man b. Bashir on the pulpit of Hims saying, \"We stood in prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the month of Ramadan on the night of the twenty-third until the first third of the night. Then we stood with him on the night of the twenty-fifth until half the night. Then we stood with him on the night of the twenty-seventh until half the night. Then we stood with him on the night of the twenty-seventh until we thought we would not attain al-falah. We used to call it al-falah, but you call it al-sahur.\""],[1598,"that al-Aqra' b. Habis asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, is Hajj every year or once only?\" He said, \"Once only, and whoever does more, it is voluntary.\" This is a sound chain of transmission, and this Abu Sinan is al-Du'ali. They did not include it, for they did not include Sufyan b. Husayn, but he is among the trustworthy whose hadith is collected."],[1599,"\"Benefit from this House, for it has been destroyed twice and will be raised the third time.\""],[1600,"The delegations of Allah are three: the warrior, the pilgrim, and the one performing 'umrah."],[1601,"\"O Allah, forgive the pilgrim and the one for whom the pilgrim seeks forgiveness.\""],[1602,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the saying of the Blessed and Exalted, {And due to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way} [Al 'Imran 97]. He said: It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the way?\" He said, \"Provisions and a mount.\""],[1603,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the saying of Allah, {whoever is able to find thereto a way} [Al 'Imran 97]. It was said, \"What is the way?\" He said, \"Provisions and a mount.\""],[1604,"A woman should not travel a night's journey except with a mahram."],[1605,"A woman should not travel a barid except with a mahram."],[1606,"Abdullah, wait so that I may bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bid us farewell: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the last of your deeds."],[1607,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions performed Hajj on foot from Madinah to Makkah. He said: 'Tie your izars around your waists,' and he walked at a pace between walking and jogging."],[1608,"Some people complained to the Prophet ﷺ about walking, so he called them and said: 'You should adopt the nasalan pace.' So we adopted it and found it lighter for us."],[1609,"The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."],[1610,"The best of companions are four, and the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will not be defeated due to small numbers."],[1611,"Ibrahim b. Abdullah narrated to us; Abu Asim al-Nabil informed us; Abdul Hamid b. Ja'far narrated to us from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Ata from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition of a few men and said: 'How much of the Quran is with you?' He asked them one by one until he came to a man among them who was the youngest of them. He said: 'How much of the Quran is with you, O so-and-so?' He said: 'I have such-and-such and Surah al-Baqarah.' He said: 'Go, for you are their commander.'"],[1612,"When there are three people, let them appoint one of them as their leader. That is the commander whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed."],[1613,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted us on weak camels from the zakah camels for Hajj. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we do not think these can carry us.' He said: 'There is no camel but that on its hump is a devil, so mention the name of Allah when you mount them as He commanded you, then use them for your needs, for it is Allah who carries.'"],[1614,"Ride these mounts while they are sound, and leave them sound, and do not take them as chairs."],[1615,"On the back of every camel there is a devil, and when you mount them, mention the name of Allah and do not fall short in your needs."],[1616,"“Indeed, on every camel’s peak there is a devil, so humble them by riding, for Allah ﷻ only carries.”"],[1617,"“He forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin, and [forbade] the jalālah (an animal that eats filth) and the mujaththamah (an animal tied up and shot).”"],[1618,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘The bell is the flute of Satan.’”"],[1619,"“Travel by night, for the earth is folded up for the traveler at night.”"],[1620,"“When he made a night stop, he would lie on his right side; and when he stopped just before dawn, he would set up his forearms upright and place his head on his palm.”"],[1621,"“Reduce your going out when the feet are still (i.e., in the stillness of night), for Allah spreads from His creation at night whatever He wills.”"],[1622,"“A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending to travel, and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, give me advice.’ He said, ‘I advise you to fear Allah and to say takbīr upon every elevated place.’ When he went on, he said, ‘O Allah, roll up the earth for him and make the journey easy for him.’”"],[1623,"“Ṣuhayb, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, related to him that the Prophet ﷺ did not see a town he intended to enter without saying when he saw it: ‘O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people and the evil of what is in it.’”"],[1624,"“The Prophet ﷺ did not stop at a place without bidding it farewell with two rak‘ahs.”"],[1625,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a journey and dawn appeared to him, he said, ‘A listener has heard, with the praise of Allah and His grace and His excellent trial upon us. Our Lord, accompany us and bestow favor upon us, seeking refuge in Allah from the Fire.’ He would say that three times and raise his voice with it.”"],[1626,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a military expedition or a journey and night overtook him, he said, ‘O earth, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of every lion, every black [creature], snake, and scorpion, and from the inhabitants of the land, and from the evil of a parent and what he begot.’”"],[1627,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ghusl, then put on his clothes. When he reached Dhū al-Ḥulayfah, he prayed two rak‘ahs, then sat on his camel. When he was upright on it on the open desert (al-Baydā’), he entered into ihrām for the Ḥajj.”"],[1628,"It is part of the sunnah to perform ghusl when one intends to enter ihram and when one intends to enter Makkah."],[1629,"Nasiyah al-Khuza'i, the keeper of the sacrificial camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me that he asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what to do with any of his sacrificial camels that became disabled. He said: \"He commanded me to slaughter every camel that became disabled, then to cast its halter in its blood, then to leave it between it and the people so they could eat it.\""],[1630,"Whoever offers a voluntary sacrifice and then it goes astray, if he wishes he may replace it, and if he wishes he may leave it. But if it was for a vow, then he must replace it."],[1631,"Ihram for Hajj is not assumed except in the months of Hajj. It is part of the sunnah of Hajj to assume ihram for Hajj in the months of Hajj."],[1632,"O Banu 'Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying at any hour he wishes, whether by night or day."],[1633,"There is no sarurah in Islam."],[1634,"Whoever intends to perform Hajj, let him hasten."],[1635,"I heard Ali say, \"Perform Hajj before you are unable to do so.\" It was as if I could see a deaf Abyssinian breaking down a building stone by stone with a pickaxe in his hand. I asked him, \"Is this something you are saying based on your own opinion, or did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He replied, \"No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, but I heard it from your Prophet ﷺ.\""],[1636,"I was a man who hired out camels for this journey, and some people told me that I had no Hajj. I met Ibn 'Umar and said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, I am a man who hires out camels for this journey, and some people tell me that I have no Hajj. He said: Do you not enter ihram, recite the talbiyah, circumambulate the Ka'bah, pour forth from 'Arafat, and stone the jamarat? I said: Yes. He said: Then you have a Hajj. A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about something similar to what you asked me, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not answer him until this verse was revealed: {There is no blame on you in seeking bounty from your Lord} [al-Baqarah: 198]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him and recited this verse to him, and said: \"You have a Hajj.\""],[1637,"In the early days of Hajj, people used to trade at Mina, 'Arafah, the market of Dhu al-Majaz, and the Hajj gatherings. They feared engaging in trade while in ihram, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {There is no blame on you in seeking bounty from your Lord} [al-Baqarah: 198] regarding the Hajj gatherings. He said: 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr narrated to me that he used to recite it from the mushaf."],[1638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[1639,"Among the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: Labbayk, O God of truth."],[1641,"The Prophet ﷺ used to raise his voice with the talbiyah."],[1642,"Jibril came to me and said, 'Command your companions to raise their voices in the talbiyah and the ihlal.'"],[1643,"Jibril came to me and said, 'O Muhammad, command your companions to raise their voices in the talbiyah, for it is the slogan of Hajj.'"],[1644,"Jibril commanded me to raise the voice with the ihlal, for it is among the rites of Hajj."],[1645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, 'Which deed is best?' He said, 'The ajj and the thajj.'"],[1646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'There is no believer who recites the talbiyah but that the trees and stones on his right and left recite it with him, until the earth is cut off from here and here, on his right and on his left.'"],[1647,"I said to 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas, 'O son of al-'Abbas, I am astonished at the difference among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the ihlal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he entered ihram.' He said, 'I am the most knowledgeable of the people about that. It was only one Hajj from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and from that they differed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out as a pilgrim. When he prayed in his mosque at Dhu al-Hulayfah his two rak'ahs, he entered ihram in his sitting place, and he made the ihlal for Hajj when he finished his two rak'ahs. Some people heard that from him and memorized it from him. Then he mounted. When his she-camel stood up with him, he made the ihlal, and some people caught that from him. That is because the people used to come in groups. They heard him making the ihlal when his she-camel stood up with him, so they said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the ihlal only when his she-camel stood up with him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on. When he ascended the height of al-Bayda', he made the ihlal, and some people caught that from him. They said, \"He made the ihlal only when he ascended the height of al-Bayda'.\" By Allah, he entered ihram in his prayer place, made the ihlal when his she-camel stood up with him, and made the ihlal when he ascended the height of al-Bayda'.' Sa'id b. Jubayr said, 'Whoever follows the statement of Ibn 'Abbas makes the ihlal in his prayer place when he finishes his two rak'ahs.'"],[1648,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the road of al-Fur', he made the ihlal when his mount stood up with him.'"],[1649,"The meat of land game is lawful for you while you are in ihram, as long as you did not hunt it or it was not hunted for you."],[1650,"Ostrich eggs were gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in ihram, and he returned them?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[1651,"I met Jabir b. 'Abdullah and asked him about the hyena: 'Do we eat it?' He said, 'Yes.'"],[1652,"“I asked Jabir bin ‘Abdullah about hyenas: ‘Are they game (that can be hunted)?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ I said: ‘Can I eat them?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ I said: ‘Is this something that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?’ He said: ‘Yes.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3236)"],[1653,"The hyena is game. If a pilgrim in ihram catches it, then he owes a penalty of a full-grown ram, and it is eaten."],[1654,"Ibn 'Abbas: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had cupping done on his head while he was in ihram.'"],[1655,"The Prophet ﷺ was cupped while in ihram on the back of his feet due to a pain he had."],[1656,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered someone in ihram to kill a snake in the Haram at Mina."],[1657,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as pilgrims, and the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the mount of Abu Bakr were one. We alighted at al-ʿArj, and our mount was with the servant of Abu Bakr. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat, and ʿAʾisha sat beside him, and Abu Bakr sat beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the other side, and I sat beside Abu Bakr, waiting for his servant and our mount, until when would he come to us? Then the servant appeared walking, without his camel. He said: Abu Bakr said to him: Where is your camel? He said: I lost it last night. She said: Abu Bakr stood up and beat him, saying: One camel, and you lost it, though you are a man? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did nothing but smile and say: \"Look at this man in ihram, what he is doing.\""],[1658,"We used to cover our faces from men, and we used to comb our hair before that while in ihram."],[1659,"Why the ramal now and the uncovering of the shoulders, when Allah has established Islam firmly and expelled disbelief and its people? And yet we do not abandon anything we used to do with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[1660,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced the Stone, touched it, then placed his lips upon it, weeping for a long time. Then he turned and saw ʿUmar weeping, and he said: \"O ʿUmar, here is where tears are shed.\""],[1661,"We entered Makkah at the time of mid-morning. The Prophet ﷺ came to the gate of the mosque, made his mount kneel, then entered the mosque and began with the Stone, touched it, and his eyes overflowed with tears. Then he did ramal three times and walked four times until he finished. When he finished, he kissed the Stone, placed his hands on it, and wiped his face with them."],[1662,"I saw Muḥammad b. ʿAbbād b. Jaʿfar kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, then he said: I saw your maternal uncle Ibn ʿAbbās kiss it and prostrate upon it, and Ibn ʿAbbās said: I saw ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb kiss it and prostrate upon it, then he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do like this, so I did it."],[1663,"He informed him that he heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"O our Lord, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and protect us from the punishment of the Fire.\""],[1664,"Ibn ʿAbbās used to say: Preserve this hadith, and he would trace it back to the Prophet ﷺ, and he would supplicate with it between the two corners: \"O Lord, make me content with what You have provided me, bless it for me, and replace every absent thing of mine with good.\""],[1665,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed the Yamani Corner and placed his cheek upon it."],[1666,"When he circumambulated the House, he wiped—or said: touched—the Stone and the Corner in every circuit."],[1667,"The Corner and the Maqam are two rubies of the rubies of Paradise. Allah has blotted out their light, and were it not for that, they would illuminate all between the east and the west."],[1668,"The Corner and the Station are two rubies of the rubies of Paradise."],[1669,"The Corner and the Station are two rubies of the rubies of Paradise. Allah effaced their light, and were it not for that they would illuminate all between the east and the west."],[1670,"Verily this Stone has a tongue and two lips, bearing witness on the Day of Resurrection with truth for whoever touches it."],[1671,"On the Day of Resurrection the Corner will come greater than Abu Qubays, with a tongue and two lips, speaking for the one who touches it with intention. It is Allah's right hand with which He shakes hands with His creation."],[1672,"Indeed I know that you are a stone, you do not harm or benefit, and were it not that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss you I would not kiss you. Then he kissed it. Ali b. Abi Talib said to him: Of course, O Commander of the Believers, it harms and benefits. He said: Then he said: By the Book of Allah, Blessed and Exalted. He said: And where is that in the Book of Allah? He said: Allah ﷻ said: {And when your Lord took from the children of Adam, from their loins, their progeny, and made them testify upon themselves: Am I not your Lord? They said: Yes} [Al-A'raf 172]. Allah created Adam and wiped his back, making them acknowledge that He is the Lord and they are the servants, and He took their covenants and pledges, wrote that on a parchment, and this Stone had two eyes and a tongue. He said to it: Open your mouth. He said: It opened its mouth, and He placed that parchment in it, and said: Bear witness on the Day of Resurrection for whoever comes to you with fulfillment. And I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"On the Day of Resurrection the Black Stone will be brought, and it will have an eloquent tongue, bearing witness with monotheism for whoever touches it.\" So, O Commander of the Believers, it harms and benefits. Umar said: I seek refuge with Allah from living among a people in which you are not, O Abu al-Hasan."],[1673,"My master Abdullah b. al-Sa'ib told me: I was among those who built the House, so I took a stone, shaped it, and placed it beside the House. He said: I used to worship it; if there was something in the House, I would send it to it, until one day there was good milk, and I sent it to it, and they poured it over it. Quraysh disagreed about the Stone when they wanted to place it, until there was nearly fighting among them with swords. He said: Make the first man who enters from the gate arbiter among you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and they said: This is the trustworthy one—they used to call him al-Amin in the pre-Islamic era. They said: O Muhammad, we are pleased with you. He called for a garment, spread it out, placed the Stone in it, then said: For this clan and this clan—except that he named clans—so that each clan of you takes a side of the garment. They did so, then raised it, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and placed it with his hand."],[1674,"When Uthman was killed, people were terrified that day with a severe terror, and the drawing of swords among us was great. I sat in my house, and a need appeared for me in the market, so I went out. There in the shade of the palace were a group of about forty men sitting, and a chain was displayed on the door. I wanted to enter, but the doorkeeper prevented me. The people said: Let the man in. I entered, and there were the nobles and notables of the people. A handsome man came in a robe, with no shirt or turban, and sat down; it was Ali b. Abi Talib. Then he said: When Ibrahim wanted to build the House, he was at a loss and did not know what to do. Allah sent the Sakina, a wind that curled up, and he built upon it each day one cubit. Makkah was very hot. When he reached the place of the Stone, he said to Ismail: Go and look for a stone and place it here. He went around the mountains, and Jibril brought him the Stone and placed it. Ismail came and said: Who brought this? Or where is this from? Or from where was this brought? He said: The one who did not rely on my building or yours brought it. He built it. Then it collapsed, and the Amalekites built it. Then it collapsed, and Jurhum built it. Then it collapsed, and Quraysh built it. When they wanted to place the Stone, they quarreled over its placement. He said: The first to come out of this gate will place it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out from the gate of Banu Shaybah, ordered a garment, it was spread, he placed the Stone in its middle, then ordered a man from each clan of Quraysh to take a side of the garment, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it with his hand and placed it. The two Shaykhs agreed on extracting the long hadith from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani and Kathir b. Kathir, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas: the story of the building of the Ka'ba, the first time Ibrahim al-Khalil ﷺ built it. This is different."],[1675,"The throwing of the pebbles, the circumambulation, and the walking between Safa and Marwa were only ordained for the establishment of the remembrance of Allah, not for anything else."],[1676,"Circumambulation of the House is prayer, except that Allah has made speech permissible for you in it. Whoever speaks, let him speak only good."],[1677,"Circumambulation of the House is like prayer, except that you may speak. Whoever speaks, let him speak only good."],[1678,"Because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated the House from behind it. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: {And let them circumambulate the Ancient House} [Al-Hajj 29]."],[1679,"The Prophet ﷺ drank water during circumambulation."],[1680,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by the Kaaba with a man leading another man by a nose ring in his nose, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut it with his hand. Then he ordered him to lead him by his hand. He said, \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by while he was performing tawaf with a man who had tied a strap to a hand or a leg, or with a thread or something else, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut it.\" And he said, \"Lead him by your hand.\" Ibn Jurayj said: Sulayman al-Ahwal informed me of all this, that Tawus informed him that Ibn Abbas said that from the Prophet ﷺ."],[1681,"\"Every mountain pass of Makkah is a road and a place of sacrifice.\""],[1682,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever performs Hajj from Makkah on foot until he returns to Makkah, Allah will record for him for every step seven hundred good deeds, each good deed like the good deeds of the Haram.\" It was said, \"And what are the good deeds of the Haram?\" He said, \"For every good deed, one hundred thousand good deeds.\""],[1683,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when it was one day before the Day of Tarwiyah, would address the people and inform them of their rites.\""],[1684,"\"The Prophet ﷺ prayed five prayers in Mina.\""],[1685,"\"It is part of the Sunnah of Hajj that the imam prays Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, the later Isha, and Subh in Mina, then goes in the morning to Arafah and proceeds wherever it is decreed for him, until when the sun has declined, he addresses the people, then prays Zuhr and Asr together, then stands at Arafat until the sun sets, then departs and prays at Muzdalifah or wherever Allah decrees, then stands at Jam' until it becomes light and departs before sunrise. When he has thrown the great Jamrah, everything that was forbidden to him becomes lawful except women and perfume, until he visits the House.\""],[1686,"I went in the morning with Abdullah b. Mas'ud from Mina to Arafah. Abdullah was a dark-skinned man with two braids, having the mark of the desert dwellers, and he was reciting the talbiyah. A group of people gathered around him and said, \"O Bedouin, this is not a day for talbiyah; it is a day for takbir.\" He said, \"At that, he turned to me and said, 'Have the people become ignorant or forgotten? By the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Mina to Arafah, and he did not stop the talbiyah until he threw the Jamrah, except that he would mix it with takbir or tahlil.'\""],[1687,"\"Keep away from the interior of Urana and keep away from the interior of Muhassir.\""],[1688,"\"Keep away from Muhassir and keep away from Uranat.\""],[1689,"I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you. He says to you, \"Remain at these sacred sites of yours, for you are upon an inheritance from the inheritance of Ibrahim.\""],[1690,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Jam' and said, \"Do I have a Hajj?\" He said, \"Whoever prays this prayer with us in this place, then stands with us at this standing place until the imam departs, and came before that from Arafat by night or by day, his Hajj is complete and he has fulfilled his ritual duties.\""],[1691,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing at Jam' and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have come to you from the mountain of Tayyi', and I have exhausted my mount and worn out myself. By Allah, I have not left any mountain without standing on it. Do I have a Hajj?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever catches this prayer with us and has come to Arafat before that, by night or by day, has fulfilled his ritual duties and completed his Hajj.\""],[1692,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at the standing place (Arafah), and I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I have come from the mountain of Tayy; I have worn out my riding mount and exhausted myself. By Allah, there was no mountain among those mountains except that I stood upon it.” He said: \"Whoever catches this prayer with us —that is, the morning prayer— and had come to Arafah before that, by night or day, has completed his Hajj and fulfilled his tafath.\"[1]"],[1693,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ at Arafah, and some people from Najd came to him while he was at Arafah and asked him. He ordered a caller, who proclaimed: “The Hajj is Arafah. Whoever comes on the night of Jam' (Muzdalifah) before the break of dawn has caught it. The days of Mina are three; whoever hastens in two days, there is no sin upon him, and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him.” And he mounted a man behind him, and he proclaimed."],[1694,"Quraysh used to depart from Muzdalifah and say, “We are the Hums, so we do not leave the sacred precinct,” and they had abandoned the standing at Arafah. He said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the pre-Islamic period standing with the people at Arafah on a camel of his, then he would spend the night with his people at Muzdalifah and stand with them, departing when they departed.”"],[1695,"There is no day on which Allah frees more servants from the Fire than the day of Arafah. Indeed, He draws near, then He boasts to the angels, saying: “What do these people want?”"],[1696,"We were with Ibn Abbas at Arafah, and he said to me: “O sayyid, why do I not hear the people reciting the Talbiyah?” I said: “They fear Mu'awiyah.” He said: Then Ibn Abbas came out of his tent and said: “Labbayk Allahumma labbayk, for they have abandoned the Sunnah out of hatred for Ali.”"],[1697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at Arafat. When he said “Labbayk Allahumma labbayk,” he said: “Indeed, the good is the good of the Hereafter.” Al-Bukhari used Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim used Dawud as evidence, and this hadith is sahih, though they did not include it."],[1698,"Allah boasts to the inhabitants of the heaven about the people of Arafat, saying to them: “Look at My servants, they have come to Me disheveled and dusty.”"],[1699,"The Prophet ﷺ mounted him behind him when he departed from Arafah, and he departed with tranquility. He said: “O people, you must be tranquil.” And he said: “Righteousness is not in making horses and camels run fast.” I did not see a camel lifting its leg until he reached Mina."],[1700,"The origin of the hastening was from the desert dwellers. They would stand at the edges of the people, having hung up wooden bowls and staffs, and when they departed, these clattered and startled the people. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while the two sides of his camel's hooves did not touch the ground, riding at a swift pace, and he was saying: “O people, you must be tranquil.”"],[1701,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me on the morning of Aqabah: “Bring me the pebbles, pick for me small pebbles like those for throwing.” When they were placed in his hand, he said: “With the like of these, with the like of these, and beware of extremism in religion, for those before you were destroyed only by extremism in religion.”"],[1702,"Abu Ali al-Hanafi and Abu Asim al-Nabil narrated to us; they said: Ayman b. Nabil narrated to us; he said: I heard Qudamah b. Abdullah b. Ammar al-Kilabi say: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ throwing the Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice from a reddish camel, with no striking, no driving away, and no saying ‘Get away, get away.’”"],[1703,"\"When Ibrahim, the beloved friend of Allah, performed the rituals, Satan appeared to him at the Jamrat al-Aqabah and threw stones at him seven times until he sank into the ground. Then he appeared to him at the second Jamrah and threw stones at him seven times until he sank into the ground. Then he appeared to him at the third Jamrah and threw stones at him seven times until he sank into the ground.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"You are stoning the Shaytan and boasting about the faith of your father.\""],[1704,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Shall we not build for you at Mina a structure to shade you?” He said: “No, Mina is the resting place of whoever arrives first.”"],[1705,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ offered among his sacrificial animals in the year of Hudaybiyah a camel of Abu Jahl, with a silver nose ring on its head, to enrage the polytheists thereby."],[1706,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed two rams on the day of Eid, then said when he turned them: \"I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. He has no partner. With that I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. In the name of Allah, and Allah is greatest. O Allah, from You and for You, on behalf of Muhammad and his ummah.\""],[1707,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed a cow on behalf of those of his wives who performed 'umrah in the Farewell Hajj, divided among them."],[1708,"From Shu'bah, and this wording is the hadith of Abu al-'Abbas. He said: I heard Sulayman b. 'Abd al-Rahman say: I heard 'Ubayd b. Fayruz say: I said to al-Bara': Tell me what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked or forbade among sacrificial animals. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, gesturing with his hand like this—and my hand is shorter than the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—: \"Four are not sufficient as sacrificial animals: the one-eyed whose blindness is evident, the sick whose sickness is evident, the lame whose lameness is evident, and the emaciated that has no marrow.\" I said: I dislike that there be any defect in the ear or horn. He said: \"Whatever you dislike, leave it, but do not forbid it to others.\""],[1709,"He forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or a slit ear."],[1710,"I heard 'Ali say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to inspect the eyes and ears.\""],[1711,"\"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded us to inspect the eyes and ears.\""],[1712,"We were sitting with 'Utbah b. 'Abd al-Sulami when Yazid Dhu Misr al-Maqra'i came. He said to 'Utbah: O Abu al-Walid, we went out just now looking for a sacrificial kid, and we could hardly find anything sound, except that I found a fat animal with broken teeth. 'Utbah said: Why did you not bring it to us? He said: O Allah, forgiveness! Is it valid for you but not valid for me? He said: Yes. He said: Why is that? He said: Because you doubt and I do not doubt. Then 'Utbah stretched out his hand and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade only five: the musilah, the musfarrah, the bakhqa', the mushayya'ah, and the kasra'. He said: The musilah is the one whose horn is completely gone; the musfarrah is the one whose ear is completely gone; the bakhqa' is the one whose blindness is evident; the mushayya'ah is the emaciated or sick one that does not follow the flock; and the kasra' is the one with a broken leg."],[1713,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Umm Salamah on the night of sacrifice, and she threw the pebbles before dawn, then went on and performed the ifadah. That was the second day on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with her. Sahih according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[1714,"When one of you departs, let his last act be at the House, except for menstruating women, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted them a concession."],[1715,"Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has exited ihram, and he must perform the hajj the following year."],[1716,"The Prophet ﷺ performed two hajjs before he emigrated—meaning, and he performed one hajj after he emigrated, combining it with an 'umrah."],[1717,"Al-Aqra' b. Habis asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Is hajj every year? He said: \"No, rather one hajj. If I said yes, it would become obligatory, and if it became obligatory, you would not listen and would not be able.\""],[1718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O people, Hajj has been prescribed for you.” Al-Aqraʿ b. Ḥābis said, “Every year, O Messenger of Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, then said, “No, rather once. Then whoever performs Hajj after that, it is voluntary. Had I said yes, it would have become obligatory upon you, and then you would neither hear nor be able.”"],[1719,"“Hajj and ʿUmrah are two obligations upon all people except the people of Makkah, for their ʿUmrah is their circumambulation. Let them go out to al-Tanʿīm and then enter it. By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not enter it except as a pilgrim for Hajj or as a performer of ʿUmrah.”"],[1720,"“Hajj and ʿUmrah are two obligations; it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin.”"],[1721,"He was asked about ʿUmrah before Hajj. He said, “They are two prayers; it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin.”"],[1722,"“There is no one among Allah’s creation except that Hajj and ʿUmrah are obligatory upon him, for whom a way is possible. Whoever adds anything after them, it is good and voluntary.”"],[1723,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her regarding her ʿUmrah, “You will have reward according to your effort and your expenditure.”"],[1724,"The Prophet ﷺ said to her regarding her ʿUmrah, “Your reward in your ʿUmrah is only according to your expenditure.”"],[1725,"ʿAlī and ʿUthmān performed Hajj. When they were on part of the road, ʿUthmān forbade tamattuʿ (combining ʿUmrah with Hajj). It was said to ʿAlī, “He has forbidden tamattuʿ.” He said, “When you see him depart, depart.” So ʿAlī and his companions pronounced the talbiyah for ʿUmrah, and ʿUthmān did not forbid them. Then ʿAlī said, “Was I not informed that you forbid tamattuʿ with ʿUmrah?” He said, “Yes.” ʿAlī said, “Did you not hear that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tamattuʿ?” He said, “Yes.”"],[1726,"“Labbayk, with Hajj and ʿUmrah together.”"],[1727,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined Hajj and ʿUmrah only because he knew that he would not perform Hajj after it.”"],[1728,"A man came to Ibn ʿAbbās and said, “Where have you come from?” He said, “I drank from Zamzam.” Ibn ʿAbbās said to him, “Did you drink from it as one ought?” He said, “And how is that, O Abū ʿAbbās?” He said, “When you drink from it, face the qiblah, mention Allah’s name, breathe three times, and drink your fill. When you finish, praise Allah, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘A sign between us and the hypocrites is that they do not drink their fill from Zamzam.’”"],[1729,"“Zamzam water is for whatever it is drunk for. If you drink it seeking healing, Allah will heal you. If you drink it seeking refuge, Allah will grant you refuge. If you drink it to quench your thirst, it will quench it.”"],[1730,"\"That the Prophet ﷺ prostrated on the stone.\""],[1731,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say while he was addressing the people upon his slit-eared camel during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “O people, obey your Lord, perform your five prayers, pay the zakah of your wealth, fast your month, and obey those in authority over you, and you will enter the Garden of your Lord.” I said to Abu Umamah: “Since when have you heard this hadith?” He said: “I heard it when I was thirty years old.”"],[1732,"People’s talk increased, so we set out for Hajj until there remained between us and our release only a few nights, when we were commanded to release the ihram. One of us would set out for Arafah while his private part was dripping with semen. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood to give a sermon and said: “O people, are you teaching me about Allah? By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of you about Allah and the most reverent of you toward Him. If I could have foreseen in my affair what I did not, I would not have brought a sacrificial animal, and I would have released ihram as they did. Whoever does not have a sacrificial animal with him should fast three days, and seven when he returns to his family. Whoever finds a sacrificial animal should slaughter it.” So we used to slaughter a camel on behalf of seven."],[1733,"He said: “When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw the pebble at the Jamrah and slaughtered his sacrificial animal, he handed the barber his right side, and he shaved it. Then he handed him the left side, and he shaved it. Then he handed it to Abu Talhah and ordered him to distribute it among the people.”"],[1734,"His father was present with the Prophet ﷺ at Al-Manhar during the Hajj pilgrimage. The Prophet ﷺ shaved his head and gave his father a portion of his hair. He also cut his nails and gave them to his companion. They said, \"Indeed, he is with us and has applied henna and kohl.\""],[1735,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the Ifāḍah on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed the noon prayer at Mina. Nafiʿ said: “Ibn ʿUmar used to perform the Ifāḍah on the Day of Sacrifice, then return and pray the noon prayer at Mina, and he mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ did that.”"],[1736,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not jog in the seven rounds in which he performed the Ifāḍah. ʿAtaʾ said: “There is no jogging in it.”"],[1737,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to the water station and asked for water. Al-ʿAbbas said: “O Fadl, go to your mother and bring the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a drink from what she has.” He said: “Give me water.” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, they put their hands in it.” He said: “Give me water.” So he drank from it. Then he came to Zamzam while they were drawing water and working with it. He said: “Work, for you are engaged in a righteous deed.” Then he said: “Were it not that you would be overcome, I would descend and place the rope on this,” meaning his shoulder, and he pointed to his shoulder."],[1738,"“The meat of land game is lawful for you while you are in ihram, as long as you did not hunt it or it was not hunted for you.”"],[1739,"From the Prophet ﷺ similar to it. As for the hadith of Sulayman b. Bilal."],[1740,"From the Prophet ﷺ similar to it."],[1741,"“People used to depart from Mina in various directions, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to make their last contact be at the House, and he gave dispensation to the menstruating woman.”"],[1742,"We said: “O Messenger of Allah, these pebbles that you throw with – they are carried away, and one would think they would be hurled away.” He said: “Indeed, whatever is accepted of them is lifted up; were it not for that, you would see them like mountains.”"],[1743,"“When one of you completes his Hajj, let him make his journey to his family, for it is greater for his reward.”"],[1744,"\"Gabriel came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took him to show him the rituals. A slit opened for him, and he entered Mina. He saw the Jamrat Al-Aqaba (stone pillars) and then saw Arafat. The devil intercepted the Prophet ﷺ at the Jamrat, so he pelted him with seven pebbles until he disappeared. Then he intercepted him at the second Jamrat and pelted him with seven pebbles until he disappeared. Then he intercepted him at the Jamrat Al-Aqaba and he pelted him with seven pebbles until he disappeared. And that's how it ended.\""],[1745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to throw the pebbles on the Day of Sacrifice before the sun declines from its zenith; but after that, at the time of its decline."],[1746,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed from Mina on the last day of his life after he had prayed Zuhr, then he returned and stayed in Mina during the nights of the days of Tashriq. He would throw the pebbles when the sun had declined, each jamrah with seven pebbles, saying ‘Allahu Akbar’ with each pebble. He would stand at the first and second jamrah and prolong the standing, supplicating humbly, then he would throw the third jamrah and not stand at it."],[1747,"When he threw the jamrah that is next to the mosque of Mina, he would throw it with seven pebbles, saying ‘Allahu Akbar’ with each pebble. Then he would go forward before it and stand facing the qiblah, raising his hands and supplicating, and he would prolong the standing. Then he would come to the second jamrah and throw it with seven pebbles, saying ‘Allahu Akbar’ with each pebble. Then he would descend to the left, toward the valley, and stand facing the qiblah, raising his hands. Then he would come to the jamrah at the Aqabah and throw it with seven pebbles, saying ‘Allahu Akbar’ with each pebble, then he would leave and not stand at it."],[1748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave permission to the shepherds to throw the pebbles one day and omit one day. Abu al-Baddah is the son of Asim b. Adi; he is well known among the Followers, and Asim b. Adi is a well-known Companion, the man involved in the li'an. Whoever says ‘from Abu al-Baddah b. Adi’ has attributed him to his grandfather, and what I have mentioned is correct."],[1749,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave permission to the camel herders to spend the nights away from Mina: they would throw the pebbles on the Day of Sacrifice, then throw on the morrow or the day after for two days, then throw on the Day of Departure."],[1750,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray the Asr prayer at al-Abtah as two rak'ahs."],[1751,"Aisha used to say: It is astonishing that a Muslim man, when he enters the Kaaba, raises his gaze toward the ceiling; he should abandon that out of reverence and magnification of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Kaaba and his gaze did not leave the place of his prostration until he came out of it."],[1752,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out from me with a glad eye and a happy soul, then he returned to me sad. I said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, you went out from me happy and joyful and you have returned sad.’ He said, ‘I entered the Kaaba, and I wish I had not done it. I fear that I have burdened my community after me.’"],[1753,"Did you hear Ibn Abbas say, ‘You have only been commanded to circumambulate, not to enter it’? He replied, ‘He did not forbid us from entering it, but I heard him say…’"],[1754,"O Aisha, were it not that your people are recent in Jahiliyyah, I would demolish the House and incorporate into it what they excluded from it in the Hijr, for they fell short of the expenses. I would make for it two doors, an eastern door and a western door, and I would join it to the ground and place it upon the foundation of Ibrahim."],[1755,"He informed him that the Prophet ﷺ shaved his head in the Farewell Pilgrimage. People used to shave in the Hajj then perform Umrah at the time of departure, saying, ‘Why does this one shave?’ He would say, ‘Pass the razor over your head.’"],[1756,"The Prophet ﷺ made Aisha perform Umrah from al-Tan'im in Dhu al-Hijjah on the night of al-Hasbah."],[1757,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: My father is an old man who embraced Islam but has not performed Hajj and cannot sit firmly on the mount; if I tie him with a rope on the mount, I fear I might kill him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\""],[1758,"O Messenger of Allah, my father is an old man who is unable to perform Hajj and Umrah or to travel. He said: \"Perform Hajj and Umrah on behalf of your father.\""],[1759,"\"When a child performs Hajj, it counts for him as a Hajj until he reaches the age of discernment; and when he reaches discernment, another Hajj is obligatory upon him. And when a Bedouin performs Hajj, it counts for him as a Hajj; and when he migrates, another Hajj is obligatory upon him.\""],[1760,"A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I hired myself out to some people and left for them part of my wages so that they would let me perform the rites. Does that suffice for me? Ibn Abbas said: This is among those concerning whom Allah ﷻ said: {They will have a share of what they have earned, and Allah is swift in reckoning} (Al Imran 3:199)."],[1761,"In the early days of Hajj, people used to trade at Mina, Arafah, the market of Dhu al-Majaz, and the seasons of Hajj. They feared doing business while in a state of consecration, so Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord} [al-Baqarah 2:198] during the seasons of Hajj."],[1762,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before revelation came to him, standing on a camel of his at Arafat with the people, departing with them, and that was only by a grant of success from Allah ﷻ to him."],[1763,"From his father the hadith concerning the Hums: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to stand at Arafah in Makkah."],[1764,"Marwan sent to Umm Maqil to ask her about this hadith, and she narrated that her husband dedicated a young camel in the path of Allah, and she wanted to perform Umrah, so she asked her husband for the young camel but he refused her. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to give it to her and said: \"Hajj and Umrah are among the path of Allah, and an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj\" or \"counts as a Hajj.\""],[1765,"\"Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has exited the state of consecration and owes another Hajj.\""],[1766,"\"Whoever breaks a bone or becomes lame has exited the state of consecration and owes the Hajj the following year.\""],[1767,"Quraysh were called al-Hums, and they used to enter through doors while in a state of consecration, while the Ansar and the rest of the Arabs would not enter through doors while in a state of consecration. While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a garden, he came out through its door, and Qutbah b. Amir al-Ansari came out with him. They said: O Messenger of Allah, Qutbah b. Amir is an immoral man; he came out with you through the door. He said: \"What made you do that?\" He said: I saw you do it, so I did as you did. He said: \"I am an Ahmasī.\" He said: \"My religion is your religion.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {It is not righteousness to enter houses from their backs, but righteousness is [in] one who fears Allah. And enter houses from their doors} [al-Baqarah 2:189]."],[1768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: What is the piety of Hajj? He said: \"Feeding food and good speech.\""],[1769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to perform the Hajj. A woman said to her husband, 'Take me for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'I do not have what I could use to take you for Hajj.' She said, 'Then take me for Hajj on your camel.' He said, 'That one we use alternately, myself and your child.' She said, 'Then take me for Hajj on your such-and-such camel.' He said, 'That one is devoted for the cause of Allah.' She said, 'Then sell your dates.' He said, 'That is my sustenance and yours.' He said, 'When the Prophet ﷺ returned from Makkah, she sent her husband to him and said, 'Convey my greetings to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him what equals a Hajj with you?' Her husband came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my wife conveys greetings to you and the mercy of Allah, and she said to take her for Hajj with you, and I told her I do not have [the means]. She said, 'Then take me for Hajj on my such-and-such camel,' and I told her that it is devoted for the cause of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Indeed, if you had taken her for Hajj, it would have been in the cause of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ then laughed in amazement at her eagerness for Hajj. He said, 'And she ordered me to ask you what equals a Hajj with you?' He said, 'Convey to her my greetings and the mercy of Allah, and inform her that an Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj with me.'"],[1770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded the people in the year of the Farewell Hajj, saying, 'Whoever would like to return with an Umrah before the Hajj, let him do so.'"],[1771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed three circuits at a fast pace and walked four when he arrived for the Hajj and Umrah, when he had performed Umrah."],[1772,"We set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in three groups. Among us were those who entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together, among us were those who entered ihram for Hajj alone, and among us were those who entered ihram for Umrah. Whoever entered ihram for Hajj and Umrah together did not exit ihram from anything forbidden to him until he completed the rites of Hajj. Whoever entered ihram for Hajj alone did not exit ihram from anything until he completed the rites of Hajj. Whoever entered ihram for Umrah, circumambulated the House and went between al-Safa and al-Marwa, exited ihram, then initiated the Hajj."],[1773,"Aisha used to carry Zamzam water and reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to do that."],[1774,"From Hisham ibn Urwah, and he mentioned it."],[1775,"\"From Amr ibn Maymun, explaining and summarizing.\""],[1776,"I set out for Umrah in the year when the people of Syria besieged Ibn al-Zubayr in Makkah, and some men of my people sent sacrificial animals with me. When we reached the people of Syria, they prevented us from entering the Haram, so I slaughtered the sacrificial animal where I was, exited ihram, and returned. The next year, I set out to make up my Umrah. I came to Ibn Abbas and asked him. He said, 'Replace the sacrificial animal, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded his companions to replace the sacrificial animals they slaughtered in the year of Hudaybiyyah during the Umrah of al-Qada.' Amr said: My father was concerned about what they had slaughtered in the year of Hudaybiyyah, saying, 'I do not know whether the companions of the Prophet ﷺ replaced the sacrificial animals they slaughtered at Hudaybiyyah during the Umrah of al-Qada or not,' until Abu Hadir narrated to him."],[1777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Makkah, 'How good you are as a land and how beloved you are to me! Were it not that your people expelled me, I would not have lived anywhere else.'"],[1778,"He forbade women in their ihram from wearing gloves and the face veil, and from clothes touched by wars or saffron. After that, she may wear whatever she likes of colored clothes, whether dyed with safflower, silk, jewelry, trousers, khuffs, or a shirt."],[1779,"He would go out from al-Madinah and find a woodcutter with a green branch he had cut from some tree of al-Madinah, and he would take his belongings and speak to him about it. Bishr said: He spoke about it. He would say, 'I will not abandon any spoil that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted me, even though I am among the wealthiest of people.'"],[1780,"Sa'd rode to his palace at al-Aqiq and found a slave cutting a tree. He confiscated his belongings. When he returned, the slave's people came to him asking him to return what he had taken from their slave. He said, 'I seek refuge with Allah from returning anything that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me as booty.' So he did not return anything to them."],[1781,"A man from Banu Amr ibn Awf and a man from Banu Khudrah disagreed and disputed about the mosque founded on piety. The Awfi said it is the mosque of Quba, and the Khudri said it is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him. He said, 'It is this mosque of mine, and in that there is much good.'"],[1782,"“A prayer in the mosque of Qubāʾ is like an ʿUmrah.”"],[1783,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go often to Qubāʾ, sometimes walking and sometimes riding.”"],[1784,"From ʿĀʾishah; I heard her say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up, put on his clothes, and went out.” So I ordered my slave girl Barīrah to follow him and see where he went. She followed him until “he came to al-Baqīʿ and stood at its nearest part as long as Allah willed him to stand, then he turned back.” Barīrah preceded him and informed me. ʿĀʾishah said: I did not mention anything of that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until morning, when I mentioned it to him. He said, “I was sent to the people of al-Baqīʿ to pray over them.”"],[1785,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a journey and saw his family, he would say, “A return, a return to our Lord, in repentance, leaving no sin upon us.”"],[1786,"“We came from Makkah after a Hajj or ʿUmrah, and Usayd b. Ḥuḍayr was riding ahead of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then some boys of the Anṣār met us, who used to go out to meet their families when they returned.”"],[1787,"I heard Abū Thaʿlabah al-Khushanī say: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a military expedition and entered the mosque, where he prayed two rakʿahs. He liked, when he returned from a journey, to enter the mosque and pray two rakʿahs in it before leaving.” Then he went to Fāṭimah and began with her. She received him and started kissing his face and his eyes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “What is with you?” She said, “O Messenger of Allah, I see that your complexion has become pale.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “O Fāṭimah, Allah (mighty and sublime be He) has sent your father with a command by which He has brought honor or humiliation to every house of mud or hair on the face of the earth, until it reaches wherever the night reaches.”"],[1788,"\"The Prophet ﷺ, when he went out for battles, his first concern was always Fatimah.\" Then he mentioned the rest of the narration with different wording."],[1789,"\"That Ibn Umar used to vie for the two corners (of the Kaaba). So I said, 'O Abu Abdullah, indeed you vie for the two corners with great competition; I have not seen anyone among the companions of the Messenger of Allah vie for them.' He said, 'If I do so, then indeed I have heard the Messenger of Allah say, 'Indeed, wiping over them (the two corners) is an expiation for sins.\"\""],[1790,"And from his mother Zaynab bt. Abī Salamah, both of them narrating it from Umm Salamah; they both narrated this from her. She said: It was my night when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to me. Wahb b. Zamʿah entered upon me, and with him was a man from the family of Abū Umayyah, both wearing shirts. The Prophet ﷺ said to Wahb, “Have you performed the ifāḍah, O Abū ʿAbd Allāh?” He said, “No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Take off your shirt.” So he took it off from his head, and his companion took off his shirt from his head. They said, “Why, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “This has been permitted for you: when you have thrown the pebbles at the jamrah, you may exit from all the restrictions of iḥrām except women. Then when you enter the evening before you have circumambulated this House, you return to the state of iḥrām, just as you were before throwing the pebbles at the jamrah, until you perform the circumambulation.” Abū ʿUbaydah said: And Umm Qays narrated to me."],[1791,"“Nothing is more honorable to Allah than supplication.”"],[1792,"“Supplication is worship.” Then he recited, {And your Lord said, ‘Call upon Me; I will respond to you.’}"],[1793,"From Dharr, similar to it. As for the ḥadīth of Jarīr—"],[1794,"From Dharr, who mentioned it with his chain of transmission, similar to it. This ḥadīth has a corroborating witness with a sound chain from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās."],[1795,"“The best form of worship is supplication.” And he recited, {And your Lord said, ‘Call upon Me; I will respond to you. Indeed, those who disdain My worship will enter Hell in humiliation.’}"],[1796,"Whoever does not supplicate to Allah, He becomes angry with him."],[1797,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever does not supplicate to Allah, He becomes angry with him. Indeed, Allah becomes angry with the one who does not supplicate to Him, and no one does that except himself.\""],[1798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no group of people who sit together in a gathering and disperse from it without mentioning Allah in it, except that it is as if they have dispersed from the carcass of a dead donkey, and they will have regret on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[1799,"Ismail b. Muhammad b. al-Fadl b. Muhammad al-Sha'rani narrated to us, saying: My grandfather narrated to us, saying: Ismail b. Abi Uways narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Suhayl b. Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a similar narration."],[1800,"No people sit in a gathering and then disperse before remembering Allah and invoking blessings upon His Prophet ﷺ except that it will be a regret for them on the Day of Resurrection."],[1801,"No people gather together and then disperse without having remembered the name of Allah except that they disperse as if from the carcass of a donkey."],[1802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Duʿāʾ (supplication) is the weapon of the believer, the pillar of religion, and the nūr (light) of the heavens and the earth.\""],[1803,"Caution does not avail against destiny, but supplication benefits from what has descended and what has not descended. Indeed, affliction descends, and supplication meets it, and they struggle until the Day of Resurrection."],[1804,"Nothing repels destiny except supplication, and nothing increases one's lifespan except righteousness. Indeed, a man is deprived of provision because of a sin he commits."],[1805,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Supplication benefits from what has come down and what has not yet come down, so upon you is to supplicate, O servants of Allah.\""],[1806,"There is no Muslim who supplicates to Allah with a supplication that contains no sin and no severing of kinship except that He grants him one of three things: either He answers his supplication promptly, or He averts from him an evil equivalent to it, or He stores up for him an equivalent reward. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then we should increase supplication.' He said, 'Allah is more abundant.'"],[1807,"Supplicate to Allah while you are certain of the answer, and know that Allah does not accept supplication from a heedless, distracted heart."],[1808,"Do not be incapable in supplication, for no one perishes with supplication."],[1809,"Allah will call the believer on the Day of Resurrection until He stops him before Him and says, 'My servant, I commanded you to supplicate to Me and promised you that I would answer you. Did you supplicate to Me?' He will say, 'Yes, O Lord.' Then He says, 'Indeed, you did not supplicate to Me with any supplication except that I answered it for you. Did you not supplicate to Me on such-and-such a day for a distress that had befallen you, that I relieve you of it, and I relieved you?' He will say, 'Yes, O Lord.' Then He says, 'I hastened it for you in this world. And you supplicated to Me on such-and-such a day for a distress that had befallen you, that I relieve you of it, but you did not see relief.' He will say, 'Yes, O Lord.' Then He says, 'I have stored up for you thereby in Paradise such-and-such.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Allah will not leave any supplication that His believing servant made except that He will show him whether it was hastened for him in this world or stored up for him in the hereafter.' He said, 'The believer will say in that station: Would that nothing had been hastened for him in any of his supplications.'"],[1810,"Jabir b. Abd Allah: The Prophet ﷺ came out to us and said, 'O people, Allah has troops of angels that descend and stand over gatherings of remembrance on earth, so graze in the meadows of Paradise.' They said, 'Where are the meadows of Paradise?' He said, 'Gatherings of remembrance. So go forth morning and evening in the remembrance of Allah and remind yourselves of Him. Whoever would like to know his standing with Allah, let him look at how Allah stands with him, for Allah places a servant with Him where the servant places Him with himself.'"],[1811,"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \"Verily, Allah has angels who roam the earth in search of gatherings of remembrance. When they find such a gathering, they surround it with their wings until it reaches the heavens. Then Allah asks them, although He already knows the answer: 'From where have you come?' They reply: 'We have come from Your servants on Earth who glorify You, praise You, and declare Your greatness. They seek Your forgiveness, ask for Your protection, and beseech You.' Allah then asks: 'What do they ask of Me?' And He already knows the answer. They reply: 'They ask for Paradise.' Allah asks: 'Have they seen it?' They reply: 'No, O Lord.' He then asks: 'How would it be if they were to see Paradise?' They respond: 'They would be even more eager in their worship and obedience to You.' He asks: 'From what do they seek protection?' And He already knows the answer. They reply: 'From the Fire.' Allah asks: 'Have they seen it?' They reply: 'No, O Lord.' He then asks: 'How would it be if they were to see it?' They respond: 'They would be even more fearful and committed to avoiding it.' Then Allah says: 'Bear witness, O angels, that I have forgiven them and granted them what they asked for, and I have accepted their seeking of my protection.' They say: 'Our Lord, among them is a servant who is a sinner. He happens to be sitting amongst them, although he is not truly one of them.' Allah says, 'He too is forgiven, for they are a people whose sitting companions will not be unfortunate.'\""],[1812,"A man said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'The laws of Islam have become numerous for me, so tell me of something I can cling to.' He said, 'Let your tongue remain moist with the remembrance of Allah.'"],[1813,"“The singled-out have gone ahead.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, who are the singled-out?” He said, “Those who are devoted to the remembrance of Allah.”"],[1814,"Indeed Allah says: “I am with My servant when he remembers Me and his lips move for Me.”"],[1815,"“Shall I not inform you of the best of your deeds, the purest of them with your Sovereign, the loftiest of them in your ranks, and better for you than giving gold and silver, and better for you than that you meet your enemy and strike their necks and they strike your necks?” They said, “And what is that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “The remembrance of Allah ﷻ.” And Muʿādh b. Jabal said, “No human being performs a deed that is more saving for him from the punishment of Allah than the remembrance of Allah ﷻ.”"],[1816,"Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ said: “Any people who sit and lengthen their sitting, then disperse before remembering Allah and invoking blessings upon His Prophet ﷺ, there will be upon them from Allah a loss; if Allah wills, He will punish them, and if He wills, He will forgive them.”"],[1817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never rose from a gathering except that he said: “Glory be to You, O Allah, my Lord, and with Your praise. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You.” I said to him, “O Messenger of Allah, how often you say these words when you rise!” He said, “No one says them when he rises from his gathering except that he is forgiven for what occurred from him in that gathering.”"],[1818,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, Mighty and Exalted, says, \"I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me. Mentioning Me is a way to bring me closer, and making supplication is a unique way to gain nearness to Me. Indeed, Muhammad ibn Al-Qasim is trustworthy and in this chain of narration Saleh narrates, 'Jazra said.'\""],[1819,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no servant who directs his face to Allah ﷻ in a request except that Allah gives it to him, either by hastening it or by storing it for him.”"],[1820,"“Indeed Allah is shy that a servant should stretch out his hands to Him with good in them, then He should return them empty and disappointed.”"],[1821,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah is Ḥayī (shy) and Karīm (generous). He is too shy to let His servant extend his hands in supplication and then return them empty.\"[1]"],[1822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Verily, Allah is Merciful, Modest, and Generous. He is too modest to let his servant raise his hands to Him and then not put anything good in them.\""],[1823,"“Whoever among you has the door of supplication opened for him, the doors of Paradise are opened for him. And no servant asks Allah for anything more beloved to Him than asking for well-being.”"],[1824,"“The best remembrance is: There is no god but Allah, and the best supplication is: Praise be to Allah.”"],[1825,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ begin a supplication only by beginning it with: “Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, the Most Exalted, the Bestower.”"],[1826,"“Persist in invoking: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[1827,"“Persist in invoking: O Possessor of Majesty and Honor.”"],[1828,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, \"O people, would you love to strive hard in supplication?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Say: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.\""],[1829,"“Increase in the remembrance of Allah until they say, ‘Madman.’”"],[1830,"When something pleasing came to the Prophet ﷺ, he would say, \"Praise be to Allah by whose blessing good things are completed,\" and when something he disliked came to him, he would say, \"Praise be to Allah in every situation.\""],[1831,"“Those who remember Allah through majestic glorification, declaring His glory, declaring His greatness, and declaring His oneness—they encircle the Throne, making a sound like the buzzing of bees, saying on behalf of their reciter: Would not one of you love to have something with the Most Merciful that reminds Him of him?”"],[1832,"“Whoever’s last words are ‘There is no god but Allah’ will enter Paradise.”"],[1833,"“Whoever says one hundred times in a day: ‘There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of all things,’ no one before him shall surpass him, and no one after him shall catch up with him except one who does deeds better than his.” I heard Ustadh Abu al-Walid al-Qurashi say: I heard Ibrahim b. Abi Talib say: I heard Ishaq b. Ibrahim say: If the narrator from Amr b. Shuayb is trustworthy, then he is like Ayyub from Nafi from Ibn Umar."],[1834,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said, \"Is there any stranger among you?\" meaning from the People of the Book. We said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah.\" He ordered the door to be locked and said, \"Raise your hands and say: There is no god but Allah.\" We raised our hands for a while, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lowered his hand and said, \"Praise be to Allah. O Allah, You sent me with this word, commanded me to it, and promised me Paradise for it; indeed You do not break Your promise.\" Then he said, \"Rejoice, for Allah has forgiven you.\""],[1835,"Whoever says, \"There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is capable of all things,\" ten times is like one who frees a slave."],[1836,"From Abu Abd Allah al-Jasri, a clan of Anaza, from Abd Allah b. al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, by my mother and father, which speech is most beloved to Allah?\" He said, \"That which Allah chose for His angels: ‘Glory be to my Lord and with His praise; glory be to my Lord and with His praise.’\""],[1837,"Whoever says \"Glory be to Allah the Almighty,\" a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."],[1838,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the meaning of \"Subhan Allah\" (Glory be to Allah). He said, \"It is declaring Allah free from every evil.\""],[1839,"The Prophet ﷺ used to frequently say, \"Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me.\" When the verse {When the victory of Allah and the conquest comes} [al-Nasr 1] was revealed, he said, \"Glory be to You, O Allah; O Allah, forgive me, for You are the Bestower.\" This is a sound chain if Abu Ubayda b. Abd Allah b. Masud heard from his father, though the two Shaykhs did not record it."],[1840,"Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah,' Allah says: 'My servant has submitted and surrendered.'"],[1841,"The first to be called to Paradise are those who praise Allah in prosperity and adversity."],[1842,"The best remembrance is 'there is no god but Allah,' and the best supplication is 'praise be to Allah.'"],[1843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no person on Earth who says, 'There is no deity except Allah, Allah is the Greatest, Glory be to Allah, Praise be to Allah, and there is no power or strength except with Allah,' except that his sins will be forgiven, even if they are as abundant as the foam of the sea.\" This was narrated by Shu'bah from Abi Balj Yahya ibn Abi Sulaim, and he narrated it standing."],[1844,"Whoever says: 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest, and praise be to Allah, and glory be to Allah, many times, and there is no power and no strength except with Allah,' his sins are expiated, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."],[1845,"Among the majesty of Allah, of what they remember, are glorification, praise, and declaring His oneness. They circle around the Throne, having a buzzing like the buzzing of bees, mentioning the one who says them. Would not any of you love to have someone with Allah who mentions him?"],[1846,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and a man was offering prayer. He then made supplication: O Allah, I ask Thee by virtue of the fact that praise is due to Thee, there is no deity but Thou, Who showest favour and beneficence, the Originator of the Heavens and the earth, O Lord of Majesty and Splendour, O Living One, O Eternal One. The Prophet ﷺ then said: He has supplicated Allah using His Greatest Name, when supplicated by this name, He answers, and when asked by this name He gives. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1495)"],[1847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying: 'O Allah, I ask You by the fact that praise is Yours, there is no god but You, You are the Bestower, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Possessor of majesty and honor. I ask You for Paradise and seek refuge in You from the Fire.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'He has called upon Allah by His name by which, when called upon, He answers, and when asked by it, He gives.'"],[1848,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying: O Allah, I ask Thee, I bear witness that there is no god but Thou, the One, He to Whom men repair, Who has not begotten, and has not been begotten, and to Whom no one is equal, and he said: You have supplicated Allah using His Greatest Name, when asked with this name He gives, and when supplicated by this name he answers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1493)"],[1849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man saying: O Allah, I ask Thee, I bear witness that there is no god but Thou, the One, He to Whom men repair, Who has not begotten, and has not been begotten, and to Whom no one is equal, and he said: You have supplicated Allah using His Greatest Name, when asked with this name He gives, and when supplicated by this name he answers. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1493)"],[1850,"The greatest name of Allah is 'Lord, Lord.'"],[1851,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Verily, the greatest name of Allah is mentioned in three Surahs of the Quran: Surah Al-Baqarah, Surah Al-Imran, and Surah Ta-Ha.\" Al-Qasim said, \"So I sought it, and it is 'Al-Hayy, Al-Qayyum.'\""],[1852,"The supplication of Dhul-Nun when he called out while in the belly of the whale: 'There is no god but You, glory be to You, indeed I was among the wrongdoers.' No Muslim ever supplicates with it for anything but Allah answers him."],[1853,"The supplication of Dhul-Nun when he called out while in the belly of the whale: 'There is no god but You, glory be to You, indeed I was among the wrongdoers.' No Muslim man ever supplicates with it for anything but Allah answers him."],[1854,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ and he said: 'Shall I not inform you of something that, if a distress or a trial from the trials of this world befalls a man among you and he supplicates with it, he is relieved?' It was said to him: 'Yes.' He said: 'The supplication of Dhul-Nun: There is no god but You, glory be to You, indeed I was among the wrongdoers.'"],[1855,"Shall I guide you to the greatest name of Allah, by which when He is called upon He answers, and when He is asked by it He gives? It is the supplication with which Yunus called when he cried out in the three darknesses: 'There is no god but You, glory be to You, indeed I was among the wrongdoers.' A man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, was it special to Yunus or general for the believers?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you not hear the saying of Allah ﷻ: {And We delivered him from distress, and thus do We deliver the believers} [al-Anbiya' 88].' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Any Muslim who supplicates with it in his illness forty times and then dies in that illness, he is given the reward of a martyr, and if he recovers, he recovers with all his sins forgiven.'"],[1856,"About the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"Indeed, the greatest name of Allah is in three Surahs of the Quran: Surah Al-Baqarah, Surah Al-Imran, and Surah Taha. So, I searched for it and found it in Surah Al-Baqarah, Ayat Al-Kursi (Allahu la ilaha illa huwa al-Hayyul-Qayyum) [Surah Al-Baqarah 2:255], and in Surah Al-Imran (Alif Lam Meem Allah la ilaha illa huwa al-Hayyul-Qayyum) [Surah Al-Imran 3:2], and in Surah Taha (And the faces will humble themselves before the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence) [Surah Taha 20:111].\""],[1857,"Narrated by the Prophet ﷺ: \"Indeed, the greatest name of Allah is found in three Surahs of the Quran.\" Isa ibn Musa said, while I was listening, \"O Aba Zabir, I heard Ghaylan ibn Anas say that he heard Al-Qasim Abu Abdur Rahman say that he heard Abu Umamah narrate from the Prophet ﷺ: 'Indeed, the greatest name of Allah is found in three Surahs.' Then he mentioned a similar narration from Amr ibn Abi Salamah: 'This does not invalidate the hadith of Al-Walid ibn Muslim, for Al-Walid is more knowledgeable, skillful, and well-acquainted with the hadith of his land, although the two sheikhs did not rely on Al-Qasim Abu Abdur Rahman.'\""],[1858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Stand straight so that I may praise my Lord.' They formed rows behind him, and he said: 'O Allah, to You belongs all praise. O Allah, there is no withholder of what You extend, and no extender of what You withhold, and no guide for the one You lead astray, and no misleader for the one You guide, and no giver of what You prevent, and no preventer of what You give, and no bringer near of what You distance, and no distancer of what You bring near. O Allah, spread upon us from Your blessings, Your mercy, Your bounty, and Your provision. O Allah, I ask You for bliss on the Day of Resurrection and security on the Day of fear. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You have given us and the evil of what You have withheld. O Allah, make faith beloved to us and beautify it in our hearts, and make disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience hateful to us, and make us among the rightly guided. O Allah, cause us to die as Muslims and live as Muslims and join us with the righteous, not disgraced nor tempted. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who deny Your messengers and hinder from Your path, and place upon them Your punishment and torment, O God of truth.'"],[1859,"There will come upon you a time in which none will be saved except the one who supplicates with the supplication of a drowning person."],[1860,"Whoever eats food and says: 'Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided it to me without any strength or power from me,' his previous sins will be forgiven. And whoever wears a garment and says: 'Praise be to Allah who clothed me this without any strength or power from me,' his previous sins will be forgiven."],[1861,"Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant and he says: 'Praise be to Allah,' except that he has fulfilled its gratitude. If he says it a second time, Allah renews its reward for him. If he says it a third time, Allah forgives his sins."],[1862,"While they were on a journey, the people dismounted to eat in the morning. Shaddad said: 'Bring this dining cloth near so we may eat.' Then he said: 'I seek Allah's forgiveness. I have not spoken a word since I embraced Islam except that I rein it in and bridle it before this word of mine. It is not like that. Muhammad ﷺ said: But he said: O Shaddad, when you see people hoarding gold and silver, then hoard these words: O Allah, I ask You for steadfastness in all affairs and determination in righteousness. I ask You for gratitude for Your blessings and excellence in worshipping You. I ask You for a sound heart, a truthful tongue, and upright character. I seek Your forgiveness for what You know. I ask You for the good of what You know, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of what You know. Indeed, You are the Knower of the unseen.'"],[1863,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, when distress befell me, to say: 'There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, and blessed is Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'"],[1864,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me these words to say when I am afflicted with hardship or distress: \"There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Honorable, Glorified and Exalted is He. Blessed is Allah, the Lord of the Great Throne, and all praise is due to Allah, the Lord of all worlds.\" Abdullah bin Ja'far used to teach this to a dead person and blow it on the afflicted area. Bukhari and Muslim have narrated this hadith in a summarized form from Qatadah, from Abu Al-'Aliyah, from Ibn Abbas."],[1865,"When anxiety or grief befell the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say: 'O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining, by Your mercy I seek help.'"],[1866,"No matter ever distressed me except that Gabriel ﷺ appeared to me and said: 'O Muhammad, say: I have put my trust in the Ever-Living who does not die, and praise be to Allah who has not taken a son, and has no partner in sovereignty, and has no protector out of weakness; and magnify Him with all magnificence.'"],[1867,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"No Muslim is afflicted with any hardship or grief, and they say: 'O Allah, I am Your servant, the son of Your servant, my forelock is in Your hand, Your command over me is forever executed, and Your decree over me is just. I ask You by every name belonging to You which You have named Yourself with, or revealed in Your Book, or You taught to any of Your creation, or You have preserved in the knowledge of the unseen with You, that You make the Quran the life of my heart and the light of my chest, and a departure for my sorrow and a release for my anxiety.' So Allah will remove his hardship and replace it with ease.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we not learn these words?\" He replied, \"Of course, whoever hears them should learn them.\""],[1868,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate, saying: 'O Allah, make me content with what You have provided me, bless me in it, and replace every absent thing for me with something better.'"],[1869,"O Allah, benefit me with what You have taught me, teach me what benefits me, and provide me with knowledge that benefits me."],[1870,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ before embracing Islam. When he wanted to leave, he said: 'What should I say?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul, and resolve for me the most guided of my affairs.' He said it and then left, and he had not embraced Islam. Then he embraced Islam and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what should I say now that I have embraced Islam?' He said: 'Say: O Allah, protect me from the evil of my soul, and resolve for me the most guided of my affairs. O Allah, forgive me what I have concealed and what I have made public, what I have done in error and what I have done deliberately, what I know and what I am ignorant of.'"],[1871,"I heard Abu al-Mughirah or al-Mughirah Abu al-Walid narrating from Hudhayfah that he said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I am a man with a sharp tongue, and most of that is directed at my family.' He said: 'Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah's forgiveness a hundred times in the day and night, or in the night or in the day.'"],[1872,"I was sharp-tongued towards my family. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I fear that my tongue will cause me to enter the Fire.' He said: 'Where are you with regard to seeking forgiveness? I seek Allah's forgiveness a hundred times a day.'"],[1873,"O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness for what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have done openly and what I have done secretly. You are the One who brings forward and You are the One who defers, and You are over all things competent."],[1874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever says, 'Astaghfirullah al-'Azeem, alladhee la ilaha illa huwal Hayyul Qayyum, wa atubu ilayhi,' three times, his sins will be forgiven, even if he had run away from the battle.\""],[1875,"Excellent! Excellent! Five things, how heavy they are on the Scale: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greatest, and a righteous child who dies for a Muslim and he seeks reward for it."],[1876,"Indeed Allah chose the speech from 'Glory be to Allah', 'Praise be to Allah', 'There is no god but Allah', and 'Allah is greatest'. So when the servant says 'Glory be to Allah', Allah writes for him twenty good deeds and erases from him twenty evil deeds. And when he says 'Allah is greatest', it is the same. And when he says 'There is no god but Allah', it is the same. And when the servant says 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds' from his own self, thirty good deeds are written for him and thirty evil deeds are erased from him."],[1877,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he was planting a plant, so he said, 'What are you doing, O Abu Hurayrah?' He said, 'I am planting a plant.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Shall I not direct you to a planting better for you than this?' I said, 'What is it?' He said, 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. A tree is planted for you for each one of them.'"],[1878,"Whoever says 'Glory be to Allah the Magnificent', a palm tree is planted for him in Paradise."],[1879,"‘Abound in the enduring righteous deeds.’ It was said, 'And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'The creed.' It was said, 'And what is it?' He said, 'Takbir (saying Allahu akbar), tahlil (saying la ilaha illa Allah), tasbih (saying subhan Allah), tahmid (saying al-hamdu lillah), and la hawla wa la quwwata illa billah.'"],[1880,"Whoever says takbir once, twenty good deeds are written for him and twenty evil deeds are erased from him. And whoever says tasbih once, twenty good deeds are written for him and twenty evil deeds are erased from him. And whoever says tahmid once, thirty good deeds are written for him and thirty evil deeds are erased from him."],[1881,"There is no servant who says: 'Praise be to Allah as much as the number of what Allah has created, praise be to Allah as much as what fills what Allah has created, praise be to Allah as much as the number of what is in the heavens and the earth, praise be to Allah as much as the number of what His Book has enumerated, praise be to Allah as much as the number of everything, and glory be to Allah the like of them.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarded that as great."],[1882,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'Command me with words that I say when I enter upon morning and when I enter upon evening.' He said: 'Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Lord of everything and its Sovereign, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self and the evil of Satan and his polytheism.' He said: 'Say it when you enter upon morning, and when you enter upon evening, and when you take to your bed.'"],[1883,"I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, I am a woman who has grown old and weak, so direct me to a deed.' He said, 'Say takbir of Allah one hundred times, praise Allah one hundred times, and glorify Allah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred accepted camels, and better than one hundred saddled and bridled horses in the path of Allah, and better than one hundred accepted slaves. And saying la ilaha illa Allah does not leave any sin, and no deed resembles it.'"],[1884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Never a blessing that Allah bestows upon a servant and he realizes that it is from Allah, except that Allah writes down his gratitude for it even before he praises Him for it.Never a servant commits a sin and he feels remorse for it, except that Allah writes down his forgiveness for it even before he seeks His forgiveness.And never a servant purchases a garment for a dirham or half a dirham, and he wears it and praises Allah for it, except that Allah forgives him before his knees to touch the ground [in prayer].\""],[1885,"There is no servant who says in the morning of every day and the evening of every night: 'In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing,' three times, and then anything harms him."],[1886,"Whoever says: 'O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You. You created me and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from all that I have done, and I admit my sin, so forgive my sins, for none forgives sins except You.' Then he dies during that day or that night, he enters Paradise."],[1887,"Let none of you refrain from doing a thousand good deeds until morning by saying 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' one hundred times, for that is a thousand good deeds, and he will not have done, if Allah wills, the like of that in his day of sins, and whatever good he does besides that will be abundant."],[1888,"Abū Bakr came to me and said, \"Have you heard a supplication from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he taught me?\" I asked, \"What is it?\" He said, \"Jesus, the son of Mary, used to teach it to his companions. If any of you had a debt as great as a mountain, and he invoked Allah with it, Allah would fulfill it for him. Say: allāhuma fārij al-hamm, kāshif al-ghamm, mujība daʿwat al-muḍṭarrīn, Raḥmān al-dunyā wa-al-ākhirah wa-raḥīmahumā, anta tarḥamunī, fa-irḥamnī bi-raḥmatin tughnīnī bihā ʿan raḥmati man siwāk (O Allah, reliever of distress, dispeller of sorrow, answerer of the supplication of the distressed, al-Raḥmān (Most Merciful) of the world and the Hereafter and the One Who who bestows mercy upon them, You are the One who [also] bestows mercy upon me, so bestow mercy upon me with a mercy that will suffice me from the mercy of anyone other than You.)\"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said, \"I had some remaining debt that I was a burden on me. I invoked Allah with this supplication, and Allah fulfilled it for me.\"ʿĀʾishah said, \"Asmāʾ b. ʿUmays had a debt of one dinar and three dirhams upon me, and she used to visit me. I was embarrassed to face her because I had nothing to pay her with. So, I invoked Allah with this supplication, and soon after, Allah provided me with some wealth, not as charity to be given, nor as a heritage received, but Allah settled it for me. I distributed a good share among my relatives and set free the slave girl of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān with three 'ūqiyyah and he had a good favor upon us.\"[1]"],[1889,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Every word that the son of Adam speaks is recorded against him. So if he commits a sin and wishes to repent to Allah, let him go to a high place and stretch out his hands to Allah ﷻ, then say: 'O Allah, I repent to You from it, never to return to it ever.' Then he will be forgiven as long as he does not return to that deed.\""],[1890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him and commanded him to look after his family every morning with: \"Here I am, O Allah, here I am. Here I am, and at Your service. All good is in Your hands, and from You and to You. O Allah, whatever I have said of a saying, or sworn of an oath, or vowed of a vow, Your will comes before all of that. What You will happens, and what You do not will does not happen. There is no might and no power except with You. Indeed, You have power over all things. O Allah, whatever prayer I have prayed, it is upon the one for whom You prayed, and whatever curse I have uttered, it is upon the one whom You cursed. You are my protector in this world and the Hereafter. Cause me to die a Muslim and join me with the righteous. O Allah, I ask You for contentment after the decree, the coolness of life after death, the delight of looking at Your face, and longing to meet You without harmful harm or misleading trial. I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged, from transgressing or being transgressed against, and from earning a sin or a fault that You do not forgive. O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, Possessor of majesty and honor, I covenant with You in this world and call You as witness, and sufficient is You as witness, that I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, with no partner. Yours is the dominion and Yours is the praise, and You have power over all things. I bear witness that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. I bear witness that Your promise is true, the meeting with You is true, the Hour is coming, there is no doubt about it, and that You will resurrect those in the graves. And that if You entrust me to myself, You entrust me to weakness, fault, sin, and error. I trust only in Your mercy, so forgive me all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Turn to me in mercy, for You are the Ever-Relenting, the Most Merciful.\""],[1891,"We were walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in some of the gardens of Madinah when he said: \"O Abu Hurayrah.\" I replied, \"Here I am, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Those who have much wealth are the ones with the least, except for one who does like this and like this with his wealth,\" and he gestured with his hand to his right and to his left, \"and few are they.\""],[1892,"I heard Ibn ʿUmar say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not abandon these words when he entered upon morning and when he entered upon evening: \"O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly affairs, my family, and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and calm my fears. O Allah, protect me from before me, from behind me, from my right, from my left, and from above me. I seek refuge in Your greatness from being swallowed up from beneath me,\" meaning being swallowed by the earth."],[1893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"One of the happinesses of the son of Adam is to seek Allah's guidance (Istikhara), and one of the miseries of the son of Adam is to abandon seeking Allah's guidance (Istikhara).\""],[1894,"Whoever says, 'I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger,' Paradise becomes obligatory for him."],[1895,"We were sitting in the mosque of Hims when a man passed by, and they said: 'This one served the Prophet ﷺ.' I got up and asked him: 'Tell me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, one that men have not passed around among yourselves.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There is no servant who says when evening comes and when morning comes, \"I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Prophet,\" except that it is binding upon Allah to make him pleased on the Day of Resurrection.'\""],[1896,"Whoever says when morning comes one hundred times and when evening comes one hundred times, 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him,' his sins are forgiven, even if they are more than the foam of the sea."],[1897,"When he left his house, he would say: \"In the name of Allah. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from slipping or going astray, from wronging or being wronged, from acting ignorantly or having ignorance done against me.\""],[1898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say when he left his house: \"In the name of Allah. There is no might and no power except with Allah. Reliance is upon Allah.\""],[1899,"A blind man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Supplicate Allah Almighty to heal me.' He said: 'If you wish, I will delay that, and if you wish, I will supplicate.' He said: 'Supplicate to Him.' He commanded him to perform ablution and perfect the ablution, and to pray two rakʿahs, and to supplicate with this supplication: 'O Allah, I ask You and turn to You by Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I turn by you to your Lord in this need of mine, that He may fulfill it for me. O Allah, accept his intercession for me and accept my intercession for him.'\""],[1900,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ was: \"My Lord, help me and do not help against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory over me, plan for me and do not plan against me, guide me and make guidance easy for me, and grant me victory over those who transgress against me. My Lord, make me greatly thankful to You, constantly remembering You, deeply fearful of You, obedient to You, humble before You, lamenting and turning to You. Accept my repentance, answer my supplication, guide my heart, make firm my proof, make my tongue upright, and remove the malice from my heart.\""],[1901,"About the Prophet ﷺ , this is what Muhammad asked his Lord: \"O Allah, I ask You for the best of requests, the best of supplications, the best of success, the best of actions, the best of rewards, the best of lives, the best of deaths, and to make me steadfast. And make my scales heavy, and fulfill my faith, and elevate my ranks, and accept my prayers, and forgive my sins. And I ask You for the highest levels of Paradise, O Allah, I ask You for the beginnings of goodness, the endings of goodness, and the entirety of goodness, the outward and the inward, and the highest levels of Paradise. Amen, O Allah, I ask You for the best of what I am given, and the best of what I do, and the best of what I work for, and the best of what is invisible to others, and the best of what is visible, and the highest levels of Paradise. Amen, O Allah, I ask You to elevate my remembrance, and to take away my sins, and to rectify my affairs, and to purify my heart, and to protect my modesty, and to enlighten my heart, and to forgive my sins, and I ask You for the highest levels of Paradise. Amen, O Allah, I ask You to bless me in my self, and in my hearing, and in my sight, and in my soul, and in my creation, and in my disposition, and in my family, and in my life, and in my death, and in my actions. So accept my good deeds, and I ask You for the highest levels of Paradise. Amen.\""],[1902,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, and he mentioned the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, saying: 'Say: O Allah, I ask You for good things, and the abandonment of evil deeds, and love of the poor, and that You accept my repentance, forgive me, and have mercy on me. And if You intend a trial for a people, then take me to You without being tried.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: 'Teach them, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, they are the truth.'"],[1903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delayed from the Fajr prayer until the sun almost caught us. Then he came out and prayed with us, making the prayer light. Then he finished and turned his face towards us, saying: 'Stay in your places. I will inform you what delayed me from you today in this prayer. I prayed in this night of mine as much as Allah willed, then sleep overcame my eyes and I slept. I saw my Lord, Blessed and Exalted, and He inspired me to say: O Allah, I ask You for good things, and the abandonment of evil deeds, and love of the poor, and that You accept my repentance, forgive me, and have mercy on me. And if You intend a trial among Your creation, then rescue me to You from it without being tried. O Allah, I ask You for Your love, and the love of those who love You, and the love of deeds that bring me closer to Your love.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to us and said: 'Learn them and study them, for they are the truth.'"],[1904,"Something similar from the Prophet ﷺ. Abu Nu'amah said this, and Shu'bah is more reliable than him, and when he contradicts him, the word is that of Shu'bah."],[1905,"He used to supplicate, saying: 'O Allah, forgive us our sins, our wrongs, our jesting, our seriousness, our deliberate acts—and all of that is with us.'"],[1906,"She said, \"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet (saw) and said, 'Verily, Allah commands you to invoke these words, for He will grant you one of them. O Allah, I ask for Your expedited recovery, patience in facing Your trials, or departure from this world to Your mercy.'\""],[1907,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: 'O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight, and make them my heirs, and grant me victory over the one who wrongs me, and show me my vengeance upon him.'"],[1908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ advised Salman al-Khayr, saying: 'O Salman, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wants to grant you words by which you ask the Most Merciful, desire Him, and supplicate with them night and day. Say: O Allah, I ask You for health in faith, faith in good character, success followed by prosperity, mercy from You, well-being, forgiveness from You, and good pleasure.'"],[1909,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says, 'O Allah, I testify that You are Allah, there is no god but You, alone, without partner, and I testify that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger,' Allah will free one-third of him from the Fire. Whoever says it twice, Allah will free two-thirds of him from the Fire. Whoever says it three times, Allah will free him completely from the Fire.\""],[1910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was praying and said: 'Ask and you will be given, O son of Umm 'Abd.' 'Umar said: Abu Bakr and I hurried to him, and Abu Bakr got to him before me. He said: Among my supplications that I hardly ever abandon is: 'O Allah, I ask You for delight that does not perish, coolness of eyes that does not run out, and the companionship of the Prophet ﷺ in the highest Garden of Eternity.'"],[1911,"He used to supplicate with these words: 'O Allah, You are the First, nothing is before You, and You are the Last, nothing is after You. I seek refuge with You from the evil of every creature whose forelock is in Your hand. I seek refuge with You from sin and laziness, from the punishment of the grave, from the trial of wealth, and from the trial of the grave. I seek refuge with You from wrongdoing and debt. O Allah, purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from filth. O Allah, distance between me and my sins as You distanced between the East and the West.'"],[1912,"He prayed with his companions, and there was no prayer in which he was more concise. It was said to him: 'O Abu al-Yaqzan, you have made it light.' He said: 'There is no blame on me for that. I supplicated in it with supplications I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: A man—who was Abu 'Ata'—stood up and followed him, asking about the supplication. So he returned and came and reported: 'O Allah, by Your knowledge of the unseen and Your power over creation, keep me alive as long as You know life is better for me, and cause me to die when death is better for me. O Allah, I ask You for fear of You in secret and in public, and I ask You for the word of wisdom in anger and pleasure, and I ask You for moderation in wealth and poverty. I ask You for delight that does not perish, and I ask You for coolness of eyes that does not run out or cease. I ask You for contentment after the decree, and I ask You for a pleasant life after death. I ask You for the delight of looking at Your Face, and I ask You for longing to meet You without harmful adversity or misleading trial. O Allah, adorn us with the adornment of faith and make us guides who are guided.'"],[1913,"He used to supplicate: 'O Allah, protect me with Islam while standing, protect me with Islam while sitting, and protect me with Islam while lying down. Do not let a gloating enemy rejoice at my misfortune. O Allah, I ask You for every good whose treasures are in Your hand, and I seek refuge with You from every evil whose treasures are in Your hand.'"],[1914,"It was among the duas of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: allāhumma innā nasʾaluka mūjibāti raḥmatik, wa-ʿazāʾima maghfiratik, wa-al-salāmata min kulli ithm, wa-al-ghanīmata min kulli birr, wa-al-fawza bi-al-jannah, wa-al-najāta bi-ʿawnika mina al-nār (O Allah, we ask You for the causes that make Your mercy incumbent, the firm means to Your forgiveness, safety from every sin, the gain of every righteousness, success in attaining Paradise, and salvation, by Your help, from the Fire.)[1]"],[1915,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no heart except that it is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful. If He wills, He keeps it straight, and if He wills, He causes it to deviate.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: 'O Allah, O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion. And the Balance is in the hand of the Most Merciful; He raises some peoples and lowers others until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[1916,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say often: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.”"],[1917,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Ask, and you shall be given.” He said: I said: “O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, bliss that does not run out, and the companionship of Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ in the highest degree of Paradise, the Garden of Eternity.”"],[1918,"A blind man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, teach me a supplication by which I may call upon Allah to restore my sight.” He said to him: “Say: O Allah, I ask You and turn to You by Your Prophet, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I have turned by you to my Lord. O Allah, make him intercede for me and make me intercede for myself.” He supplicated with this, and he stood up and could see. Shabib b. Saʿid al-Habati followed him from Rawh b. al-Qasim: “Additions in the text and the chain, and the statement about it is the statement of Shabib, for he is trustworthy and reliable.”"],[1919,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a blind man came to him and complained of the loss of his sight. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have no guide and it has become hard for me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Go to the place of ablution, perform ablution, then pray two rakʿahs, then say: O Allah, I ask You and turn to You by Your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, the Prophet of mercy. O Muhammad, I turn by you to your Lord that He may remove my blindness. O Allah, make him intercede for me and make me intercede for myself.” ʿUthman said: “By Allah, we had not separated and the conversation had not lengthened before the man entered as if he had never had any affliction at all.”"],[1920,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Say: O Allah, I am weak, so strengthen my weakness in Your pleasure; take the good by my forelock; and make Islam the utmost of my satisfaction. O Allah, I am weak, so strengthen me; I am lowly, so honor me; I am poor, so provide for me.”"],[1921,"It was said to me: “O Muhammad, say and you will be heard; ask and you will be given.” He said: I said: “O Allah, I ask You for the doing of good deeds, the abandoning of evil deeds, love of the poor, and that You forgive me and have mercy on me. And if You intend a trial for a people, take me to You without being tried. O Allah, I ask You for Your love, the love of those who love You, and a love that brings me to Your love.”"],[1922,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: “O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight until You make them my heirs, grant me well-being in my religion and my body, and help me against the one who wronged me until You show me my revenge upon him. O Allah, I have surrendered myself to You, entrusted my affair to You, leaned my back upon You, and turned my face to You. There is no refuge from You except to You. I believe in Your Messenger whom You sent and in Your Book which You revealed.”"],[1923,"\"He would never sit in a gathering without anyone else present, except that he would say, 'O Allah, forgive me for what I have done in the past and what I will do in the future, and what I have hidden and what I have made public, and what You know of me that I do not know. O Allah, grant me from Your obedience what will come between me and Your disobedience, and grant me from Your fear what will bring me closer to Your mercy, and grant me from certainty what will make worldly tribulations easier for me. Bless my hearing and my vision and make them my heirs. O Allah, seek revenge for me from those who wrong me, and help me against those who oppose me, and do not make the world my greatest concern, and do not allow knowledge to be beyond my reach. O Allah, do not let those who do not show mercy towards me have control over me.'\" Ibn 'Umar was asked about them, and he said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to conclude his gatherings with them.\""],[1924,"When the table was lifted, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: “Praise be to Allah, much, good, blessed therein, not sufficient, nor forsaken, nor dispensed with, our Lord.”"],[1925,"Moses ﷺ said: “O Lord, teach me something by which I remember You and call upon You.” He said: “O Moses, say: There is no god but Allah.” He said: “O Lord, all Your servants say this.” He said: “Say: There is no god but Allah.” He said: “There is no god but You, O Lord, but I want something You single me out with.” He said: “O Moses, if the seven heavens and their inhabitants besides Me, and the seven earths were on one scale, and ‘There is no god but Allah’ on the other, it would outweigh them: There is no god but Allah.”"],[1926,"A man from my community will be called out before all creatures on the Day of Resurrection, and ninety-nine scrolls will be spread out for him, each scroll as far as the eye can see. Then it will be said to him: “Do you deny anything of this?” He will say: “No, O Lord.” He will say: “Do you have an excuse or a good deed?” The man will be afraid and say: “No, O Lord.” He will say: “Yes, you have good deeds with Us, and no injustice will be done to you.” Then a card will be brought out for him, on which is: “I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.” He will say: “O Lord, what is this card compared to these scrolls?” He will say: “You will not be wronged.” He said: The scrolls will be placed on one scale and the card on the other, and the scrolls will be light and the card will outweigh."],[1927,"I heard Awsat al-Bajali on the pulpit of Hims saying: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say — then he was overcome with tears and wept, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on this pulpit say in the first year: “Ask Allah for pardon, well-being, and certainty in the first and the last, for after certainty the servant is not given anything better than well-being.”"],[1928,"The Prophet ﷺ said to his uncle: “Make much supplication for well-being.”"],[1929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to teach those who embraced Islam to say, “O Allah, guide me, provide for me, grant me well-being, and have mercy on me.”"],[1930,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “O Allah, grant me well-being in my body, grant me well-being in my sight, and make it the inheritor of me. None has the right to be worshipped but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the Worlds.”"],[1931,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think—if I were to coincide with the Night of Decree, what should I say during it?” He said, “Say: O Allah, You are Pardoning and You love pardon, so pardon me.”"],[1932,"He used to seek refuge from five things: cowardice, miserliness, the evils of old age, the punishment of the grave, and the trial of the heart."],[1933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in his supplication: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, senility, hard-heartedness, heedlessness, poverty, humiliation, and destitution. I seek refuge in You from poverty, disbelief, wickedness, dissension, hypocrisy, seeking reputation, and showing off. I seek refuge in You from deafness, muteness, madness, leprosy, vitiligo, and all bad diseases.”"],[1934,"He used to supplicate with these words: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from being overcome by debt, from being overcome by the enemy, and from the gloating of enemies.”"],[1935,"He used to supplicate, saying: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the cessation of Your blessings, from the removal of Your well-being, from the sudden onset of Your punishment, and from all that displeases You.”"],[1936,"“Seek refuge in Allah from poverty, scarcity, humiliation, and from wronging others or being wronged.”"],[1937,"He used to supplicate, saying: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from destruction by collapsing, from falling from a height, from senility, from grief, from drowning, and from burning. I seek refuge in You from Satan seizing me at the time of death. I seek refuge in You from dying while retreating in Your path, and I seek refuge in You from dying from a sting in Your path.”"],[1938,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, keep me away from reprehensible morals, desires, actions, and diseases.”"],[1939,"“I seek refuge in Allah from disbelief and debt.” A man said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you equate disbelief with debt?” He said, “Yes.”"],[1940,"He used to say in his supplication: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a bad neighbor in the permanent abode, for the neighbor of the desert moves away.”"],[1941,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"Seek refuge with Allah from the evil of the settled neighbor, for the traveler's neighbor, if he wishes, can depart.\""],[1942,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me a refuge-seeking supplication that I may seek refuge by it. He took hold of my palm and said: \"Say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my hearing, and from the evil of my sight, and from the evil of my soul, and from the evil of my semen,\" until I memorized it."],[1943,"My father heard me saying: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from anxiety, laziness, and the punishment of the grave.\" He said: O my son, from whom did you hear this? I said: I heard you saying them. He said: \"Hold fast to them, for I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying them.\""],[1944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: \"I seek refuge in You from the punishment of Hell, and the punishment of the grave, and the trial of life, and the trial of death, and the trial of the Dajjal.\""],[1945,"\"Seek refuge with Allah from greed that leads to stinginess, and from greed for something not desired when there is no desire.\""],[1946,"Among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was: \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble, a supplication that is not heard, a soul that is not satisfied, and from hunger, for it is an evil bedfellow; and from treachery, for it is an evil inner trait; and from laziness, miserliness, cowardice, senility, and from being brought back to the worst age; and from the trial of the Dajjal, the punishment of the grave, and the trial of life and death. O Allah, we ask You for hearts that are humble, submissive, and repentant in Your path. O Allah, we ask You for the determinations of Your forgiveness, the means of salvation in Your command, safety from every sin, booty from every act of piety, success in attaining Paradise, and deliverance from the Fire.\""],[1947,"He heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from four things: knowledge that does not benefit, a heart that does not humble, a soul that is not satisfied, and a supplication that is not heard."],[1948,"The translation of the above sentence is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought refuge from knowledge that does not benefit, supplication that is not answered, a heart that does not humbly fear Allah, and a soul that is never satisfied.\""],[1949,"Whoever asks Allah for Paradise three times, Paradise says: O Allah, admit him into Paradise. And whoever seeks refuge with Allah from the Fire three times, the Fire says: O Allah, protect him from the Fire."],[1950,"When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would hear near his face a sound like the buzzing of bees. One day revelation descended upon him, and we remained silent for a while. He then faced the qiblah, raised his hands, and said: \"O Allah, increase us and do not decrease us; honor us and do not humiliate us; give us and do not deprive us; prefer us and do not prefer others over us; be pleased with us and make us pleased.\" Then he said: \"Ten verses have been revealed to me; whoever upholds them will enter Paradise.\" Then he recited, 'The believers have certainly succeeded' [Quran 23:1] until he completed ten verses. Abd al-Razzaq and Yunus b. Sulaym said: This was his uncle who was a governor. He said: My uncle sent me to Yunus b. Yazid so that he dictated hadiths to me."],[1951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah is too merciful to be ashamed to turn away the hands of His servant empty-handed.\""],[1952,"He saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the stones of al-Zayt supplicating while he was covering his face with his palms."],[1953,"I never saw the Prophet ﷺ raising his hands wide open while supplicating on his pulpit or elsewhere. He would place his fingers at the level of his shoulders and supplicate."],[1954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"One, One.\" This sunnah has been narrated from Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas."],[1955,"From Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas: The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was supplicating with two fingers, and he said, \"One, one,\" and he pointed with the index finger."],[1956,"\"That the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to keep his hands extended in supplication, and would not retract them until he wiped his face with them.\" And it has been narrated from Abdullah bin Abbas."],[1957,"When you ask Allah, ask Him with the palms of your hands, and do not ask Him with their backs, and wipe your faces with them."],[1958,"No people sit in a gathering in which there is much idle talk, and then one of them says before he rises: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, our Lord, and with Your praise. There is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance,' except that he is forgiven for whatever was in that gathering."],[1959,"Whoever says: 'Glory be to Allah and with His praise. Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance,' and says it in a gathering of remembrance, it will be like a seal stamped upon it; and whoever says it in a gathering of idle talk, it will be an expiation for him."],[1960,"At the end of his life, when a gathering became long, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance.' Some of us said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have not heard this saying from you before.' He said: 'This is an expiation for what occurs in the gathering.'"],[1961,"When his companions gathered around him and he wanted to get up, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise. I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek Your forgiveness and I turn to You in repentance. I have done wrong and have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, are these words you have newly introduced?' He said: 'Yes. Jibril came to me and said: O Muhammad, these are an expiation for gatherings.'"],[1962,"Shall I not teach you words that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me? If you had a debt like Mount Sabir, Allah would pay it off for you. Say: 'O Allah, suffice me with what You have made lawful against what You have made unlawful, and make me content with Your bounty over anyone other than You.'"],[1963,"Whoever enters the market and says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death. In His hand is all good, and He has power over all things,' Allah will record for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million bad deeds, raise him a million degrees, and build for him a house in Paradise. He said: Then I came to Khurasan and went to Qutaybah b. Muslim. I said to him: I have brought you a gift. I narrated the hadith to him, and Qutaybah b. Muslim used to ride in his procession until he reached the gate of the market, say it, and then leave."],[1964,"Whoever says in the market: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. In His hand is all good, and He has power over all things,' Allah will record for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million bad deeds, and build for him a house in Paradise."],[1965,"Whoever enters the market, sells and buys in it, and says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He has power over all things,' Allah will record for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million bad deeds, and build for him a house in Paradise."],[1966,"Whoever says in the market: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise. In His hand is all good, and He has power over all things,' Allah will record for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million bad deeds, and build for him a house in Paradise."],[1967,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the market, he would say, 'In the name of Allah, O Allah, I ask You for the goodness of this market and the goodness within it. And I seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil within it. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from acquiring an unrighteous oath or a losing transaction within it.'\""],[1968,"He used to like comprehensive supplications and leave aside what was in between."],[1969,"He heard his son saying: 'O Allah, I ask You for the white palace on the right side of Paradise.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There will be in this nation people who go to extremes in supplication and purification.'"],[1970,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned over during the night, he said: “There is no god but Allah, the One, the Compeller, Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them, the Mighty, the Forgiving.”"],[1971,"When he woke up at night, he said: “There is no god but You; glory be to You. O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness for my sin, and I ask You by Your mercy. O Allah, increase me in knowledge, and do not let my heart deviate after You have guided me, and grant me mercy from Yourself. Truly, You are the Bestower.”"],[1972,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down on his side, he said: “O Allah, forgive me, drive away my devil, release my pledge, make my scales heavy, and place me in the highest assembly.”"],[1973,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say in his supplication: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty, from insufficiency, and from humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged.”"],[1974,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the trial of the Fire and the punishment of the Fire, and I seek refuge in You from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the grave, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the trial of wealth and from the evil of the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of the trial of the false Messiah. O Allah, wash away my sins with water of snow and hail, and purify me from my sins as a white garment is purified from filth, and put distance between me and my sins as You have put distance between the east and the west. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from laziness, senility, sin, and debt.”"],[1975,"“Take your shields.” We said: “O Messenger of Allah, from an enemy who has come?” He said: “No; your shields from the Fire. Say: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is greatest. For they will come on the Day of Resurrection as saviors and foremost, and they are the enduring good deeds.”"],[1976,"The Prophet Muhammad (pbuh) used to pray, \"O Allah, I ask You for a pure life, a just death, and a return that is not shameful or embarrassing.\""],[1977,"He used to supplicate: “O Allah, make the most expansive of Your provision upon me in my old age and when my life comes to an end.”"],[1978,"There were two assurances among you: one has passed and the other remains. {And Allah would not punish them while you are among them, and Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness.}"],[1979,"There were two assurances on earth: one was lifted and the other remains. {And Allah would not punish them while you are among them, and Allah would not punish them while they seek forgiveness.}"],[1980,"“Whoever says: There is no might and no power except with Allah, it is a remedy for ninety-nine ailments, the least of which is worry.”"],[1981,"Abu Talib fell ill and became gravely sick, so the Prophet ﷺ visited him. He said: “O son of my brother, call upon your Lord who sent you to heal me.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, heal my uncle.” Then it was as if he were released from a bond. Abu Talib said: “Your Lord sent you that people might obey you.” He said: “And you, O uncle, if you obey Allah, He will surely obey you.”"],[1982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: “Which supplication is most excellent?” He said: “A person’s supplication for himself.”"],[1983,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—I think he was Awf b. Malik—and said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, the sons of so-and-so raided me and took my son and my camels.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘The family of Muhammad has such-and-such households’—I think he said nine households—‘and they do not have a saa‘ of food or a mudd of food. Ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic.’ He said, ‘So he returned to his wife. She said, “What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reply to you?” So he informed her.’ He said, ‘It was not long before the man’s camels and his son were returned to him, more abundant than they had been. So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He stood on the minbar, praised and extolled Allah, commanded them to ask Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and to turn to Him with longing, and recited to them: “And whoever fears Allah, He will make for him a way out and will provide for him from where he does not expect” [al-Talaq 3].’"],[1984,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, ‘O my sins! O my sins!’—saying this two or three times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, ‘Say: O Allah, Your forgiveness is vaster than my sins, and Your mercy is more hoped for by me than my deeds.’ So he said it. Then he said, ‘Repeat.’ So he repeated. Then he said, ‘Repeat.’ So he repeated. Then he said, ‘Rise, for Allah has forgiven you.’ This is a hadith whose narrators, down to the last of them, are from Madinah, none of whom is known for any disparagement, and they did not record it."],[1985,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man while he was saying, ‘O Most Merciful of the merciful.’ The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, ‘Ask, for Allah has looked upon you.’ Al-Fadl b. Isa is al-Raqashi, and I fear that his uncle might be Yazid b. Aban, except that I found a supporting witness for it from the hadith of Abu Umamah al-Bahili."],[1986,"Allah has an angel entrusted with those who say, ‘O Most Merciful of the merciful.’ Whoever says it three times, the angel says, ‘The Most Merciful of the merciful has turned to you, so ask.’"],[1987,"Whoever would like his supplication to be answered at times of distress and hardship, let him supplicate abundantly in times of ease."],[1988,"Jibril ﷺ descended to the Prophet ﷺ in the most beautiful form in which he had ever descended, smiling and rejoicing. He said, ‘Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.’ He replied, ‘And upon you be peace, O Jibril.’ He said, ‘Allah has sent me to you with a gift from the treasures of the Throne, with which Allah has honored you.’ He asked, ‘And what is that gift, O Jibril?’ Jibril said, ‘Say: O You who makes beautiful things manifest and conceals ugly things, O You who does not take to task for the offense and does not tear the veil, O Great in pardon, O Beautiful in overlooking, O Vast in forgiveness, O You who spreads out Your hands in mercy, O Knower of every secret, O Ultimate end of every complaint, O Generous in forbearance, O Great in favor, O Initiator of blessings before they are deserved, O our Lord, O our Master, O our Protector, O goal of our desire, I ask You, O Allah, not to scorch my body with the Fire.’ Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘What is the reward of these words?’ Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith after the supplication in its full length."],[1989,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: What prevents one of you, when he recognizes that his supplication has been answered—so he is healed from an illness or returns from a journey—from saying: Praise be to Allah, by whose might and majesty righteous deeds are completed. Isa b. Maymun alone narrated it from al-Qasim b. Muhammad from Aishah, and Isa is not accused of fabrication."],[1990,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah: What prevents you from listening to what I advise you? Say when you wake in the morning and when you reach the evening: O Ever-Living, O Self-Subsisting, by Your mercy I seek help; set right all my affairs and do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye."],[1991,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever says, when he goes to his bed, 'Alhamdulillahil-ladhi kafaani wa aawani, Alhamdulillahil-ladhi at'amani wa saqaani, Alhamdulillahil-ladhi mann 'alayya fa afdala. Allahumma inni as-aluka bi'izzatika an tunajjiyani min an-naar, faqad hamidallaha bijami'i mahamidil-khalqi kullihim,' it will be a source of thanksgiving to Allah for all the praises of creation.\""],[1992,"When one of you comes to his bed, let him say: O Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the earth, our Lord and Lord of everything, You hold the forelock. You are the First, so there is nothing before You. You are the Last, so there is nothing after You. You are the Outward, so there is nothing above You. You are the Inward, so there is nothing below You. Enrich us from poverty and settle our debt."],[1993,"A man from the Ansar, from the people of Quba, invited the Prophet ﷺ, and we went with him. When he had eaten and washed his hands—or he said his hand—he said: ‘Praise be to Allah who feeds and is not fed. He bestowed favor upon us, guided us, fed us, gave us drink, and every good trial He has tried us with. Praise be to Allah, not bidding farewell, nor recompensed, nor denied, nor dispensed with. Praise be to Allah who fed from food, gave drink from drink, clothed from nakedness, guided from misguidance, gave sight from blindness, and favored over many of those He created with great favor. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.’"],[1994,"When the caller to prayer calls, the gates of heaven are opened and supplication is answered. Whoever is afflicted by distress or hardship, let him wait for the caller. When he says the takbir, say the takbir. When he bears witness, bear witness. When he says, ‘Come to prayer,’ say, ‘Come to prayer.’ When he says, ‘Come to success,’ say, ‘Come to success.’ Then say: O Allah, Lord of this truthful, answered call—the call whose answer is sought—the call of truth and the word of piety, make us live by it, die by it, and raise us by it, and make us among the best of its people, living and dead. Then ask Allah for his need."],[1995,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ counting glorification on his fingers. Al-A‘mash narrated it from Ata’ b. al-Sa’ib."],[1996,"“I saw the Prophet ﷺ counting the tasbīḥ with his fingers.”"],[1997,"“Hold fast to glorification (tasbīḥ), declaration of God’s oneness (tahlīl), and sanctification (taqdīs), and do not be heedless lest you forget monotheism. Count with the fingertips, for they will be questioned and made to speak.”"],[1998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while there were four thousand date pits in front of me, with which I was glorifying Allah. He said, “O daughter of Ḥuyayy, what is this?” I said, “I am glorifying Allah with them.” He said, “I have glorified Allah since I stood before you more than this.” I said, “Teach me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Say: ‘Glory be to Allah, as many times as the number of things He has created.’”"],[1999,"He entered with the Prophet ﷺ upon a woman who had date pits or pebbles in front of her. He said, “Shall I inform you of what is easier for you than this and more excellent? Say: ‘Glory be to Allah, as many times as the number of what He has created in the heaven; glory be to Allah, as many times as the number of what He has created in the earth’; and you glorify Allah.” Then he said: “Glory be to Allah, as many times as the number of what is between that; glory be to Allah, as many times as the number of what He is going to create; Allah is greater, the like of that; praise be to Allah, the like of that; there is no god but Allah, the like of that; there is no power except with Allah, the like of that.”"],[2000,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanding words to be said at times of terror: “I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from His wrath, from His punishment, from the evil of His servants, from the whisperings of the devils, and from their coming to me.” He said: ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUmar used to teach them to those of his children who had reached puberty, and they would say them when they were with their people. For those who had not reached puberty, he would write them down and hang them around their necks."],[2001,"When one of you retires to his bed, an angel and a devil rush to him. The devil says, “Begin with evil,” and the angel says, “Begin with good.” If he remembers Allah, the devil departs and the angel comes and guards him. When he wakes up, an angel and a devil rush to him. The devil says, “Begin with evil,” and the angel says, “Begin with good.” If he says: “Praise be to Allah who restored my soul to me after its death and did not cause it to die in its sleep. Praise be to Allah who holds the heaven lest it fall upon the earth except by His permission; indeed Allah is kind and merciful to mankind. Praise be to Allah who gives life to the dead, and He is capable of everything,” then if he falls from a riding animal, he dies as a martyr, and if he rises and prays, he prays in a state of excellence."],[2002,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lay down to sleep, he would say: “O Allah, forgive me my sin, drive away my devil, release my pledge, make my scale heavy, and place me in the highest assembly.”"],[2003,"When a man comes to visit a sick person, he should say: “O Allah, heal Your servant, that he may strike an enemy for You or walk to prayer for You.”"],[2004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited me while I was ill and said: “O Salmān, may Allah heal your sickness, forgive your sin, and grant you well-being in your body and your frame until the end of your appointed term.”"],[2005,"“Indeed the miser is the one in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me.”"],[2006,"“May the nose of a man be rubbed in dust in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not invoke blessings upon me.”"],[2007,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “No people sit remembering Allah and do not invoke blessings upon their Prophet ﷺ but that gathering will be a loss for them. And no people sit without remembering Allah but that will be a loss for them.”"],[2008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever sends one blessing upon me, Allah sends ten blessings upon him and removes from him ten sins.”"],[2009,"I met Gabriel ﷺ and he gave me glad tidings, saying, “Your Lord says: Whoever sends blessings upon you, I send blessings upon him; and whoever sends greetings of peace upon you, I send greetings of peace upon him.” So I prostrated to Allah in gratitude."],[2010,"He informed him that he [Ibn Abbas] said regarding {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated} [al-Hijr 87]: “It is the Mother of the Quran.” My father said: Sa'id b. Jubayr recited to me {In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [al-Fatihah 1] the seventh verse. Sa'id b. Jubayr said: Ibn al-Abbas recited it to me as I recited it to you, then he said: {In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [al-Fatihah 1] is the seventh verse. Ibn Abbas said, “Allah brought it out for you, and He did not bring it out for anyone before you.”"],[2011,"He said, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, is it a verse from the Book of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Then he said, \"Ibn Abbas recited it, 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' in both raka'ahs.\""],[2012,"\"And indeed We have granted you, [O Muhammad], seven of the often repeated [verses] and the great Qur'an.\" (Surah Al-Hijr 15:87) He (Said bin Jubair) recited it to me as, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful\" (Surah Al-Fatiha 1) when he completed it, and he said, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful\" (Surah Al-Fatiha 1) is the seventh verse. And Sa'id bin Jubair said to me, 'Indeed Allah has brought it out for you, and He did not bring it out for anyone before you.'\""],[2013,"{In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds} [al-Fatihah 2]. I said to my father: Did Sa'id inform you that Ibn Abbas said, “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful is a verse from the Book of Allah?” He said: Yes."],[2014,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He, {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated} [al-Hijr 87], he said: “The Opening of the Book.” It was said to Ibn Abbas: Then where is the seventh? He said: { “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful” } [al-Fatihah 1]."],[2015,"\"He counted it for me in my hand {In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, praise be to Allah, the Lord of all worlds, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, Master of the Day of Judgment. You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help. Guide us on the Straight Path, the path of those who have received Your grace; not the path of those who have brought down wrath upon themselves, nor of those who have gone astray.} Then he said, 'Allah brought it out for you, and not for anyone else.'\""],[2016,"{In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [al-Fatihah 1] is the seventh. Ibn Abbas said, “Allah has stored it up for you, and He has not brought it out for anyone before you.”"],[2017,"Uthman b. Affan asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.” He said, “It is one of the names of Allah, and between it and the Greatest Name of Allah is only as close as the black of the eye is to its white.”"],[2018,"“Whoever reads the Quran has drawn prophethood within his sides, except that it is not revealed to him. It is not proper for the companion of the Quran to be harsh with one who is harsh, nor to be ignorant with one who is ignorant; while in his heart is the speech of Allah, Exalted is He.”"],[2019,"The companion of the Quran will come on the Day of Resurrection, and the Quran will say, “O Lord, adorn him.” So he will be clothed with the crown of honor. Then it will say, “O Lord, increase him; O Lord, be pleased with him.” So He will be pleased with him, and it will be said to him, “Recite and ascend,” and he will increase in goodness with every verse.”"],[2020,"“It will be said to the companion of the Quran on the Day of Resurrection: Recite and ascend, and recite with measured recitation as you used to recite in the world, for your station will be at the last verse you recite.”"],[2021,"The first Book came down from one gate upon one letter, but the Quran came down from seven gates upon seven letters: as a restrainer, a commander, lawful, unlawful, clear, ambiguous, and parables. So make lawful its lawful, make unlawful its unlawful, do what you are commanded, refrain from what you are forbidden, take lesson from its parables, act upon its clear verses, believe in its ambiguous verses, and say: We believe in it; all is from our Lord."],[2022,"“Guard this Quran, for it is more elusive and quicker to slip from the hearts of men than camels from their hobbles. None of you should say, ‘I forgot such-and-such a verse,’ but rather he was made to forget.”"],[2023,"that he used to recite while on the roof of his house, and he had a beautiful voice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and he said: While I was reciting, something like a cloud overshadowed me, while the woman was in the house and the horse was in the courtyard. I feared lest the woman fall and the horse bolt, so I stopped. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Recite, O Usayd, for it was only an angel listening to the Qur'an.\""],[2024,"that Usayd b. Hudayr came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned the hadith similarly, and in it he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Recite, Usayd, recite, Usayd, for that was an angel listening to the Qur'an.\""],[2025,"While I was reciting Surat al-Baqarah tonight, when I reached its end I heard a thud behind me, and I thought that my horse was being set loose. He said: \"Recite, Abu 'Atik.\" And I turned, and behold, there were things like lamps suspended between the sky and the earth. He said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I could not continue. He said: \"Those were angels who descended for the recitation of the Qur'an. Indeed, had you continued, you would have seen wonders.\""],[2026,"Fasting and the Qur'an will intercede for the servant. Fasting says: My Lord, I deprived him of food and desires during the day, so let me intercede for him. And the Qur'an says: I deprived him of sleep at night. So they will both intercede."],[2027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Verily, the one who has nothing of the Quran in his heart is like a ruined house.\""],[2028,"\"The one who recites the Qur'an aloud is like the one who gives charity openly, and the one who recites the Qur'an silently is like the one who gives charity secretly.\""],[2029,"\"You will not return to Allah with anything more excellent than what came forth from Him.\""],[2030,"\"Indeed this Qur'an is the banquet of Allah, so accept from His banquet as much as you can. Indeed this Qur'an is the rope of Allah, the clear light, and the beneficial healing. It is a protection for the one who clings to it and a salvation for the one who follows it. It does not deviate lest it be corrected, and it does not bend lest it be straightened. Its wonders do not cease, and it does not wear out from much repetition. Recite it, for Allah will reward you for its recitation: for every letter, ten good deeds. Indeed I do not say that Alif Lam Mim is a letter, but Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter.\""],[2031,"\"Whoever recites ten verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless.\""],[2032,"\"Whoever recites ten verses in a night will not be recorded among the heedless, and whoever recites one hundred verses will be recorded among the devout.\""],[2033,"On the Day of Resurrection, the Qur'an will come like a young man and say to its companion: I am the one who kept you awake at night and made you thirsty during the day."],[2034,"that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, I bought the portion of Banu So-and-so in a container containing such-and-such. He said: \"Shall I not inform you of something that has more fragrance than it?\" The man said: Does such a thing exist? He said: \"A man who learns ten verses.\" So the man went and learned ten verses, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. \"If 'Amr b. Khalid preserved in his chain Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd, then it is authentic according to Muslim's criterion, but the Basrans among the companions of al-Mu'tamir disagreed with him about it.\""],[2035,"I heard my father narrate from Qatadah, from Abu al-Ja'd or Ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Umamah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similarly."],[2036,"\"Indeed, Allah has people among mankind.\" They said, \"Who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"The people of the Qur'an; they are the people of Allah and His elite.\""],[2037,"\"When we learned ten verses of the Qur'an from the Prophet ﷺ, we would not learn from the ten that were revealed after them until we learned what was in them.\" It was said to Sharik, \"From the practice?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[2038,"\"Shall I not teach you a surah the like of which was not sent down in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Qur'an?\" I said, \"Yes, indeed.\" He said, \"I hope that you will not leave through that door until you learn it.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and I stood with him. He began to speak to me while my hand was in his hand. I started to walk slowly, disliking that he would leave before telling me it. When I approached the door, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the surah you promised me?\" He said, \"How do you recite when you stand for prayer?\" So I recited the Opening of the Book. He said, \"It is it, it is it, and it is the seven oft-repeated verses that Allah ﷻ said: {And We have certainly given you seven of the oft-repeated verses and the great Qur'an} [al-Hijr 87], which I was given.\""],[2039,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy b. Ka'b while he was praying, and when he finished his prayer, he beckoned to him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand on my hand. He said: He intended to leave through the door of the mosque, so he said, \"I hope that you will not leave the mosque until you learn a surah the like of which was not sent down in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Qur'an.\" He said: I began to walk slowly, hoping for that. Then I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the surah you promised me?\" He said, \"How do you recite when you begin the prayer?\" He said: I recited, \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,\" until I came to its end. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is this surah, and it is the seven oft-repeated verses and the great Qur'an that I was given.\""],[2040,"He recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,\" until he completed it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, it is the seven oft-repeated verses and the great Qur'an that I was given.\" \"And I found a corroborating witness for the hadith of 'Abd al-Hamid b. Ja'far in Abu Hurayrah's hearing of this hadith from Ubayy b. Ka'b from the hadith of the Madinans.\""],[2041,"The Prophet ﷺ called out to Ubayy b. Ka'b while he was standing in prayer, but he did not answer him. He said, \"What prevented you from answering me, O Ubayy?\" He said, \"I was praying.\" He said, \"Did not Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, say: {Respond to Allah and to the Messenger when he calls you} [al-Anfal 24]? Do not leave the mosque until I teach you a surah the like of which Allah has not sent down in the Torah, the Gospel, or the Psalms. Indeed, it is the seven long ones that I was given, and indeed, it is the great Qur'an.\" \"Al-Bukhari included in the Sahih the hadith of Ibn Abi Dhi'b from Sa'id al-Maqburi from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ: 'Praise be to Allah is the Mother of the Qur'an, the seven oft-repeated verses, and the great Qur'an.' This wording only.\""],[2042,"While Jibril ﷺ was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he heard a creaking sound from the sky. He raised his head and then said, \"A gate of heaven has been opened that was never opened before.\" Then an angel said, \"Rejoice in two lights that you have been given, which no prophet before you was given: the Opening of the Book and the closing verses of Surat al-Baqarah. You will not recite a letter from them except that you will be given it.\""],[2043,"\"I was given the Opening of the Book from beneath the Throne, and the Mufassal as an extra.\""],[2044,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us on a military expedition or a raiding party. We passed by a household and sought their hospitality, but they did not host us. We camped near another group, and their chief was stung by a scorpion. They came to us and said, \"Is there anyone among you who can perform ruqyah?\" I said, \"I am a raqi.\" They said, \"Then perform ruqyah on our companion.\" I said, \"No, we sought your hospitality, but you did not host us.\" They said, \"We will give you a reward.\" So they set aside thirty sheep for us. He said: I went to him and began to wipe him and recite the Opening of the Book, repeating it until he recovered. We took the sheep and said, \"We took them, but we do not know how to perform ruqyah. We are not ones to eat them until we ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So we came to him and mentioned it to him. He began to say, \"What made you know that it is a ruqyah?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I did not know that it was a ruqyah, but it was something that Allah cast into my heart.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Eat, and assign a share for me with you.\""],[2045,"He passed by a people who had a madman bound in iron. Some of them said to him, \"Do you have anything with which to treat this one? For your companion has come with good.\" He said: I recited the Opening of the Book over him for three days, twice each day, and he recovered. They gave him one hundred sheep. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, \"Eat, for whoever eats by a false ruqyah, you have eaten by a true ruqyah.\""],[2046,"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey and he halted, and a man halted beside him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ turned to him and said, \"Shall I not inform you of the best of the Qur'an?\" He said: He recited to him, \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.\""],[2047,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when he said, \"Learn Surat al-Baqarah and Al 'Imran, for they are the two shining ones that will shade their companion on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks.\""],[2048,"\"Indeed, for everything there is a hump, and the hump of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah.\""],[2049,"\"Surah al-Baqarah contains a verse which is the master of the verses of the Quran. It is not recited in a house in which there is a devil except that he leaves it: Ayat al-Kursi.\""],[2050,"\"Indeed, for everything there is a hump, and the hump of the Quran is Surah al-Baqarah. Indeed, when the devil hears Surah al-Baqarah being recited, he leaves the house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited.\""],[2051,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I was given Surah Al-Baqarah from the first remembrance.\""],[2052,"\"Recite Surah al-Baqarah in your houses, for indeed the devil does not enter a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited.\""],[2053,"\"Recite Surah al-Baqarah in your houses, for indeed the devil does not enter a house in which Surah al-Baqarah is recited.\""],[2054,"He had a storehouse for dates and noticed it diminishing. He guarded it one night and saw a being like a young boy who had reached puberty. He greeted him and he returned the greeting. He said, \"Are you a jinni or a human?\" He said, \"Rather, a jinni.\" He said, \"Show me your hand.\" So he showed him, and it was the hand of a dog with the hair of a dog. He said, \"Thus is the creation of the jinn.\" He said, \"The jinn know that there is no man among them stronger than me.\" He said, \"What brought you?\" He said, \"We were informed that you love charity, so we came to take some of your food.\" He said, \"What protects us from you?\" He said, \"You recite Ayat al-Kursi from Surah al-Baqarah: 'Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence.'\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"If you recite it in the morning, you are protected from us until evening, and if you recite it in the evening, you are protected from us until morning.\" Ubayy said, \"So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning and informed him of that, and he said, 'The wicked one spoke the truth.'\""],[2055,"\"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, wrote a Book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and He sent down from it two verses with which He concluded Surah al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three nights but that the devil approaches it.\""],[2056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah concluded Surah al-Baqarah with two verses that He gave me from His treasure which is beneath the Throne. So learn them and teach them to your women, for they are a prayer, a Quran, and a supplication.\""],[2057,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, similar to it. Muslim has transmitted the hadith of Abu Malik al-Ashja'i from Rib'i b. Hirash from Hudhayfah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I was given the concluding verses of Surah al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne.\""],[2058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed me over the charity of the Muslims. I put the fruit in a room and found it diminishing, so I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"This is the devil taking it.\" He said, \"So I entered the room and locked the door upon myself. Then a great darkness came and covered the door. Then it took the form of an elephant, then it took another form, and it entered through a crack in the door. I tightened my lower garment around myself, and it began to eat from the dates. He said, 'I leaped upon it and seized it, and my hands locked around it. I said, \"O enemy of Allah!\" It said, \"Release me, for I am old with many dependents, and I am poor. I am from the jinn of Nasibin. This village belonged to us before your companion was sent, and when he was sent, we were expelled from it. So release me, and I will never return to you.' So I released him. Then Jibril ﷺ came and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what had happened. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer, and his caller called out, 'Where is Mu'adh b. Jabal?' So I stood up to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What did your captive do, O Mu'adh?' So I informed him, and he said, 'Indeed, he will return.' So he returned. He said, 'I entered the room and locked the door upon myself, and he entered through a crack in the door and began to eat from the dates. I did to him as I did the first time. He said, \"Release me, for I will never return to you.\" I said, \"O enemy of Allah, did you not say I will not return?\" He said, \"Indeed, I will not return. And the sign of that upon me is that none of you recites the conclusion of al-Baqarah but that one of us enters his house that night.'\""],[2059,"I said to Mu'adh b. Jabal, \"Tell me about the story of the devil.\" Then he mentioned the hadith."],[2060,"\"Whoever takes the first seven of the Quran is better.\""],[2061,"Learn the Quran, for it will intercede for its people on the Day of Resurrection. Recite the two bright ones.\" It was said: \"What are the two bright ones?\" He said: \"Al-Baqarah and Al 'Imran, for they will come on the Day of Resurrection as if they were two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of white birds in ranks, defending their companions with their wings. Learn Al-Baqarah, for learning it is a blessing, abandoning it is a regret, and the sorcerers cannot master it."],[2062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites Surah Al-Kahf as it was revealed, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection from his place to Mecca. And whoever recites the last ten verses of it and then the Antichrist appears, he will not be harmed by him. And whoever performs ablution and then says: 'Glory be to You, O Allah, and praise be to You. There is no god except You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You,' it will be written on a parchment, then sealed with a seal and it will not be broken until the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2063,"Whoever recites Surah al-Kahf"],[2064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Recite Surah Yasin at the time of your death.\" Yahya ibn Sa'id and others narrated this from Sulaiman al-Taymi. \"And the saying concerning it is the saying of Ibn al-Mubarak when he said, 'The additional narration from a trustworthy individual is accepted.'\""],[2065,"\"A surah of the Quran consisting of thirty verses interceded for a man until he was forgiven: it is Tabarak alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk.\""],[2066,"\"I wish that it were in the heart of every believer\" – meaning Tabarak alladhi bi yadihi al-mulk."],[2067,"\"From his father, the Prophet ﷺ gave his daughter Umm Salama to him and said, 'You are my son-in-law.' He then approached him and said, 'What did you do with Juwayriyah or the slave girl?' I said, 'She was with her mother.' He said, 'So, what you have come for?' I said, 'I came so that you can teach me something to say in my dreams.' He said, 'Recite: Say, O disbelievers, for it is a disassociation from polytheism.'\""],[2068,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Idha Zulzilat is equal to half of the Qur'an, Qul Huwa Allahu Ahad is equal to a third of the Qur'an, and Yul Ya Ayyuhal-Kafirun is equal to a fourth of the Qur'an.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2894)"],[2070,"He heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he heard a man reciting {Say: He is Allah, the One; Allah, the Eternal Refuge; He neither begets nor is born, nor is there to Him any equivalent} [al-Ikhlas 2]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It has become obligatory.\" I asked him: \"What, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Paradise.\" Abu Hurayrah said: I wanted to go to the man and give him glad tidings, but I feared that I would miss lunch with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I preferred lunch. Then I went to the man and found that he had gone."],[2071,"\"The most empty of houses is a house in which there is nothing of the Book of Allah. So recite the Quran, for you will be rewarded for it with ten good deeds for every letter. Indeed, I do not say that Alif Lam Mim is a letter, but I say Alif is a letter, Lam is a letter, and Mim is a letter.\""],[2072,"\"Can any of you not recite a thousand verses every day?\" They said: \"Who can do that?\" He said: \"Can any of you not recite Alhakum al-takathur?\""],[2073,"\"None of you should sleep until he has recited a third of the Quran.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, how can any of us recite a third of the Quran?\" He said: \"Can he not recite Say: He is Allah, the One, and Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak, and Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind?\""],[2074,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the two refuge surahs. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the dawn prayer with them.\""],[2075,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh and Abu Musa to Yemen and commanded them to teach the people the Quran."],[2076,"\"Whoever recites the Quran and acts upon what is in it, his parents will be clothed on the Day of Resurrection with a crown whose light is better than the light of the sun in the houses of this world, and it will be upon him. So what do you think of the one who acted upon it?\""],[2077,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites the Quran, learns it, and acts upon it will be clothed on the Day of Resurrection with a crown of light whose radiance is like the radiance of the sun, and his parents will be clothed with two garments that the world cannot equal. They will say: 'Why have we been clothed?' It will be said: 'Because your child took the Quran.'\""],[2078,"Act upon the Qur'an, deem lawful what it makes lawful and deem unlawful what it makes unlawful, follow it, and do not disbelieve in any part of it. Whatever of it is unclear to you, refer it to Allah and to those in authority after me, so that they may inform you. Believe in the Torah, the Gospel, the Psalms, and what the prophets were given from their Lord. Let the Qur'an and the clear explanation in it suffice you, for it is an intercessor whose intercession is accepted, and whatever it declares lawful is confirmed. Every verse has a light on the Day of Resurrection. I was given Surah al-Baqarah from the earlier Reminder, and I was given Ta-Ha, the Tawasin, and the Hawamim from the Tablets of Moses, and I was given the Opening of the Book from beneath the Throne."],[2079,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best?' He said, 'The one who alights and departs.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the one who alights and departs?' He said, 'He strikes from the beginning of the Qur'an to its end, and from its end to its beginning.'"],[2080,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are best?' He said, 'The one who alights and departs.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the one who alights and departs?' He said, 'The companion of the Qur'an strikes from its beginning until he reaches its end, and from its end until he reaches its beginning. Whenever he alights, he departs.'"],[2081,"A man stood up to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which deed is best? Or which deed is most beloved to Allah?' He said, 'The one who alights and departs: the one who opens the Qur'an and seals it. The companion of the Qur'an strikes from its beginning to its end, and from its end to its beginning. Whenever he alights, he departs.'"],[2082,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'He is not one of us who does not chant the Qur'an.' Sufyan said, 'Meaning he does not deem himself sufficient by it.' And according to Sufyan b. Uyaynah, there is another chain for it."],[2083,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'He is not one of us who does not chant the Qur'an.'"],[2084,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He who does not recite the Quran is not of us.\" \"The narration of Layth does not prevent the narration of Abdullah ibn Abi Nahik, for they are two followers and the evidence of the authenticity of both narrations is the narration of Amr ibn al-Harith, who is one of the reliable memorizers, narrating from Ibn Abi Muleika.\""],[2085,"People entered upon Saad b. Abu Waqqas and asked him about the Quran. Saad said, \"Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \"He is not one of us who does not recite the Quran melodiously.\"\"[1]"],[2086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He is not one of us who does not chant the Qur'an.' Al-Harith b. Murrah al-Thaqafi al-Basri narrated it from 'Isl b. Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, from the Prophet ﷺ. And al-Harith narrated with this chain from Ibn Abbas."],[2087,"'He is not one of us who does not chant the Qur'an.'"],[2088,"'Allah listens more intently to a man with a beautiful voice reciting the Qur'an than the owner of a singing slave-girl listens to his singing slave-girl.'"],[2089,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Qur'an with your voices.' Thus Mansur b. al-Mu'tamir narrated it."],[2090,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the front rows.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn your voices with the Qur'an.' Thus Za'idah b. Qudamah, 'Amr b. Abi Qays, Jarir b. 'Abd al-Hamid, 'Ammar b. Muhammad, and Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated it from Mansur b. al-Mu'tamir."],[2091,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a long hadith: 'Adorn the Qur'an with your voices.'"],[2092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Beautify the Quran with your voices.”"],[2093,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Beautify the Quran with your voices.”"],[2094,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Beautify the Qur'an with your voices. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1468)"],[2095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Beautify the Quran with your voices.”"],[2096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first rows, and beautify the Quran with your voices.”"],[2097,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Adorn the Quran with your voices.\" This was narrated by Jarir ibn Hazim from Zubeid ibn Al-Harith from Talhah ibn Musarrif. The narration was lengthy and did not mention \"Adorn the Quran with your voices.\""],[2098,"From Talhah b. Musarrif, and he mentioned it."],[2099,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Embélissez le Coran avec vos voix\", and in the Hadith of Ma'mar, \"Embélissez vos voix avec le Coran.\""],[2100,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Beautify the Quran with your voices.” Abd al-Rahman said, “I had forgotten this phrase until al-Dahhak b. Muzahim reminded me of it.”"],[2101,"From Shu'bah, and he mentioned the hadith in full."],[2102,"“Beautify the Quran with your voices.”"],[2103,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he would come to the edge of the row, to the far end, straightening the chests and shoulders of the people, and he would say, “Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first rows.”"],[2104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to us when the prayer was about to begin and wipe our shoulders and say, “Straighten your rows and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Let those of you who are possessed of reason and understanding stand closest to me, and beautify the Quran with your voices. Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the front row.”"],[2105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ “would wipe our shoulders during the prayer,” and he mentioned the hadith."],[2106,"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row, and beautify the Quran with your voices.”"],[2107,"Adorn the Quran with your voices."],[2108,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would come to us while we were in prayer and pass his hand over our chests and say, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.'"],[2109,"Adorn the Quran with your voices."],[2110,"Adorn the Quran with your voices."],[2111,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.'"],[2112,"Adorn the Quran with your voices."],[2113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.'"],[2114,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.'"],[2115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.' We have found for 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awsajah, from al-Bara', corroborating narrators in the transmission of this hadith from al-Bara': Zadhan Abu 'Umar, 'Adi b. Thabit, and Aws b. Dam'aj."],[2116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices, for a beautiful voice increases the Quran in beauty.'"],[2117,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.'"],[2118,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Adorn the Quran with your voices.' Then we looked and found for Talhah b. Musarrif two corroborating narrators in his transmission from 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awsajah: al-Hakam b. 'Utaybah and Zubayd b. al-Harith."],[2119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row.\""],[2120,"\"Beautify the Quran with your voices.\""],[2121,"I heard 'Amr b. al-'As say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for me, so I came to him and he ordered me to put on my clothes and take my weapons and then come to him. He said: So I did that, then I came to him while he was performing ablution. He looked up at me, then lowered his gaze, then said, \"O 'Amr, I intend to send you on a military expedition; may Allah grant you spoils and keep you safe, and I desire for you a sound desire for wealth.\" He said: So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I did not embrace Islam out of desire for wealth; rather I embraced Islam out of desire for Islam and to be with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Then he said, \"O 'Amr, how excellent is sound wealth for a righteous man.\""],[2122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them with the traces of a bath on him, and he was in good spirits. He said: So we thought he had been intimate with his wife, so we said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we see you have arisen in good spirits.\" He said, \"Yes, and praise be to Allah.\" Then he mentioned wealth, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no harm in wealth for one who fears Allah, and health for one who fears Allah is better than wealth, and cheerfulness of spirit is part of bliss.\""],[2123,"Hakim b. Hizam carried out a raid with two horses on the day of Khaybar, and they were both wounded. So he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"My two horses have been wounded, O Messenger of Allah.\" So he gave him something, then he asked for more and he gave him more, then he asked for more. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Hakim, this wealth is green and sweet. Whoever asks people, they give him, and the one who asks from it is like one who eats but never becomes full.\""],[2124,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Seek the beauty in pursuit of the world, for indeed every person is facilitated for what has been written for them from it.\""],[2125,"\"Do not think the provision is slow, for no servant will die until he receives the last of the provision that is his. So be moderate in seeking: take the lawful and leave the unlawful.\""],[2126,"\"Indeed, one of you will not die until he completes his provision, so do not think provision is slow. Fear Allah, O people, and be moderate in seeking. Take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden.\""],[2127,"\"There is no deed that draws nearer to Paradise except that I have commanded you to do it, and no deed that draws nearer to the Fire except that I have forbidden you from it. Let none of you think his provision is slow, for Jibril ﷺ cast into my heart that none of you will depart this world until he completes his provision. So fear Allah, O people, and be moderate in seeking. If any of you thinks his provision is slow, let him not seek it through disobedience to Allah, for Allah's bounty is not obtained through disobedience.\""],[2128,"Let not the one who amasses wealth without its right be envied—or he said, without its due—for if he gives charity, it will not be accepted from him, and whatever remains will be his provision for the Fire."],[2129,"We were a people who called ourselves brokers, and we used to sell in al-Baqi'. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and called us by a name better than our own name, saying, \"O company of merchants, this selling is attended by lying and oaths, so mix it with charity.\""],[2130,"We were in Madinah selling loads and buying them, and we used to call ourselves brokers and the people used to call us that. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and called us by a name that was better than the name we called ourselves and better than what the people called us. Then he said, \"O company of merchants, your selling is witnessed by vain talk and swearing, so mix it with charity.\""],[2131,"The Prophet ﷺ came to us at the market and said, \"O company of merchants, this market is mixed with swearing, so mix it with charity.\""],[2132,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were selling slaves in Madinah, and we used to call ourselves brokers, so he called us by a better name than we called ourselves. He said: \"O company of merchants, indeed this selling is attended by vain talk and oaths, so mix it with charity.\" This is the wording of the hadith of al-Thawri."],[2133,"The truthful, trustworthy Muslim merchant will be with the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection."],[2134,"The truthful, trustworthy merchant will be with the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs."],[2135,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to the prayer place in Madinah, and he found the people trading. He said: \"O company of merchants,\" and they responded to him, raising their eyes and necks toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Indeed, the merchants will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection as wicked, except those who feared Allah, acted righteously, and spoke the truth.\""],[2136,"Indeed, the merchants are the wicked.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah permitted selling?\" He said: \"Yes, but they swear and thus sin, and they speak and thus lie."],[2137,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The merchants are the wicked, the merchants are the wicked.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, has not Allah permitted selling?\" He said: \"Yes, but they say and thus lie, and they swear and thus sin.\""],[2138,"Indeed, among the signs of the Hour is that wealth will overflow, ignorance will increase, trials will appear, and trade will spread."],[2139,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the lands is worst?\" He said: \"I do not know.\" When Jibril ﷺ came to him, he said: \"O Jibril, which of the lands is worst?\" He said: \"I do not know, until I ask my Lord.\" So Jibril departed and remained as long as Allah willed him to remain, then he came and said: \"O Muhammad, you asked me which of the lands is worst, and I said I do not know, and I asked my Lord, saying: Which of the lands is worst? He said: Its marketplaces.\""],[2140,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the places is best?\" He said: \"I do not know.\" He said: \"Then which of the places is worst?\" He said: \"I do not know.\" Then Jibril came to him, and he said: \"Ask your Lord.\" Jibril said: \"We do not ask Him about anything,\" and he trembled a trembling by which Muhammad ﷺ almost fell unconscious from the two of them. When Jibril ascended, Allah, exalted is He, said: \"Muhammad asked you which of the places is best, and you said I do not know, and he asked you which of the places is worst, and you said I do not know.\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then tell him that the best of places are the mosques and the worst of places are the marketplaces.\""],[2141,"Let those of you who possess maturity and intellect be nearest to me, then those who come after them, then those who come after them. And do not differ, lest your hearts differ. And beware of the clamor of the marketplaces."],[2142,"On the authority of Abu Hurayrah: A man swore about his goods, the hadith—and this is other than that, with an addition of the revelation of the verse and other things. Sahih."],[2143,"The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim. It is not lawful for a Muslim, if he sells to his brother a sale that has a defect, not to make it clear to him."],[2144,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man selling food, and it impressed him. So, he put his hand in it, and it turned out to be wet food. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"He who deceives us is not one of us.\""],[2145,"The Prophet ﷺ came to the market and saw wheat piled up. He put his hand into it and found moisture, so he said: \"Indeed, whoever deceives us is not of us.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2146,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a pile of food and put his hand into it, and his fingers touched moisture. He said: \"What is this, O owner of the food?\" He replied: \"The sky (rain) fell on it, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Why did you not put it on top of the food so that people could see it?\" Then he said: \"Whoever deceives us is not of me.\" Muslim included the hadith of Suhayl from his father from Abu Hurayrah that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever deceives us is not of us.\" As for the detailed account in these hadiths, they did not include it, but all of them are authentic according to Muslim's criterion. Muslim narrated it in abridged form."],[2147,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to al-Baqi' and saw food being sold in sacks. He put his hand in and took out something he disliked, and said: \"Whoever deceives us is not of us.\""],[2148,"I bought a she-camel from the house of Wathilah ibn al-Asqa'. When I left with it, Wathilah caught up with me, dragging his lower garment, and said: \"O 'Abd Allah, did you buy?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Did he make clear to you what is in it?\" I said: \"And what is in it? It is fat and evidently healthy.\" He said: \"Do you intend to travel with it or do you intend it for meat?\" I said: \"I intend to go on Hajj with it.\" He said: \"Then return it.\" Its owner said: \"You only intended this—may Allah set you right—to spoil it for me.\" He said: \"Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'It is not lawful for anyone to sell something unless he makes clear what is in it, and it is not lawful for one who knows that to conceal it.'\""],[2149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"Which earning is purest or most excellent?\" He said: \"A man's work with his own hands and every righteous transaction.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2150,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: \"Which earning is most excellent?\" He said: \"A righteous earning.\""],[2151,"It was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which earning is purest?\" He said: \"A man's earning with his own hands and every righteous transaction.\""],[2152,"A man detained his debtor for ten dinars and said: \"By Allah, I will not leave you until you pay me or bring me a guarantor.\" So the Prophet ﷺ became guarantor for it. Then he brought him the amount he had promised, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"From where did you get this gold?\" He said: \"From a mine.\" He said: \"We have no need for it; there is no good in it.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid it on his behalf."],[2153,"\"A time will surely come upon people when no one will remain except that he consumes usury, and if he does not consume it, its dust will reach him.\""],[2154,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade hoarding food.\" Muslim included the hadith of Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Muhammad ibn 'Amr ibn 'Ata' from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab from Ma'mar ibn 'Abd Allah ibn Nadlah that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No one hoards except a sinner.\" This hadith is one of the things that refute the view that a Companion's hadith is not authentic unless two Followers narrate from him, for this Ma'mar has no narrator other than Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab. As for the hadith of al-Qasim from Abu Umamah, it is not with that wording. Reports have been narrated about the prohibition of hoarding food and refraining from helping Muslims in times of hardship, which must be mentioned in this place as Muslims are driven to it at the present time. Among them: Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2155,"\"The hoarder is cursed.\" And among them: 'Ali ibn Salim is weak."],[2156,"\"Whoever hoards food for forty nights has disowned Allah and Allah has disowned him. And any people of a dwelling in whose midst a person becomes hungry, the protection of Allah has been withdrawn from them.\""],[2157,"Whoever hoards, intending to raise prices thereby against the Muslims, is a sinner, and the protection of Allah is free from him."],[2159,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man in the market selling food at a price cheaper than the market price. He said, \"Do you sell in our market at a price cheaper than ours?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"With patience and seeking reward?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Rejoice, for the one who brings goods to our market is like the one who strives in the path of Allah, and the one who hoards in our market is like the heretic in the Book of Allah.\" And from it is a rejected report and a dark chain."],[2160,"Whoever interferes in any of the prices of the Muslims in order to raise them against them, it is incumbent upon Allah to cast him into the greatest part of Hellfire, head downward."],[2161,"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, for goodness is tranquility and evil is doubt."],[2162,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali, \"Like whom were you during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and what did you comprehend from him?\" He said, \"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, for evil is doubt and goodness is tranquility.'\" Its witness is the hadith of Abu Umamah al-Bahili. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in this place."],[2163,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"What is faith?\" He said, \"When your good deed pleases you and your evil deed displeases you, then you are a believer.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is sin?\" He said, \"When something troubles your heart, then leave it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in this place."],[2164,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about righteousness and sin. He said, \"Righteousness is good character, and sin is what troubles your heart and you would hate for people to see it.\""],[2165,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ tossed and turned one night, and it was said to him, \"What kept you awake?\" He said, \"I found a fallen date and ate it. Then I remembered dates we had from the dates of charity, and I do not know whether that date was from that or from my family's dates. That is what kept me awake.\""],[2166,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I do not know whether Tubba was a cursed or not. And, I do not know whether Dhu al-Qarnayn was a Prophet or not. And, I do not know whether hudud (capital punishments) [serve] as expiation for those are deserve them.\""],[2167,"Whoever buys a sale and the option becomes binding, it is his as long as his companion has not parted from him. If he wishes, he may take it. But if he parts from him, there is no option for him."],[2168,"A man bought a slave from another man during the time of the Prophet ﷺ. He kept him as long as Allah willed, then returned him due to a defect found in him. When he returned the slave, the man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, he has benefited from my slave since he was with him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The produce is with the liability.\" Sahih."],[2169,"A man bought a slave during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and there was a defect in him that he was not informed of. He benefited from him, then learned of the defect and returned him. He brought the dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, he has benefited from him for a long time.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The gain is with the liability.\""],[2170,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the produce is with the liability.\" And the hadith of 'Asim: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the produce is with the liability.\" It was narrated by al-Thawri, Ibn al-Mubarak, and Yahya b. Sa'id from Ibn Abi Dhi'b. \"As for the hadith of al-Thawri.\""],[2171,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"decreed that the produce belongs to the one who bears liability,\" and as for the hadith of Ibn al-Mubarak"],[2172,"\"The produce belongs to the one who bears liability,\" and as for the hadith of Yahya b. Sa'id"],[2173,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"decreed that the produce belongs to the one who bears liability\""],[2174,"\"The two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated, and each of them may take from the sale what he desires,\" he said it three times"],[2175,"that when Salman came to Madinah, he brought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a gift on a tray and placed it before him. He said, \"What is this, O Salman?\" He said, \"Charity for you and your companions.\" He said, \"I do not eat charity.\" So he removed it. Then the next day he came to him with something similar and placed it before him. He said, \"What is this?\" He said, \"A gift for you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions, \"Eat.\" He said, \"To whom do you belong?\" He said, \"To a people.\" He said, \"Ask them to enter into a contract of manumission with you.\" He said, \"They contracted with me for such and such palm trees that I would plant for them, and Salman would tend them until they bore fruit.\" He said, \"They did so.\" He said, \"The Prophet ﷺ came and planted all the palms except one palm that 'Umar planted. His palms bore fruit that year except that one palm. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Who planted it?' They said, ''Umar.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ planted it with his own hand, and it bore fruit that same year.\""],[2176,"that a man from the Jews bought him and brought him to Madinah. He said, \"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a gift and said, 'This is charity.' He said to his companions, 'Eat,' but he did not eat.\" Then he mentioned the hadith similarly. According to the condition of Muslim."],[2177,"\"A loan and a sale are not lawful, nor two conditions in a sale, nor profit from what is not yet guaranteed, nor selling what you do not have.\""],[2178,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I hear things from you that I fear I may forget. Will you permit me to write them down?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Among what he wrote from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was that when he sent 'Attab b. Usayd to the people of Makkah, he said: 'Tell them that two sales in one sale are not valid, nor selling what one does not own, nor a loan and a sale, nor two conditions in a sale.'\""],[2179,"and he was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ. And 'Ali b. Hamshadh al-'Adl narrated to us, Isma'il b. Ishaq al-Qadi and al-Hasan b. 'Ali b. Ziyad narrated to us, they said: Isma'il b. Abi Uways narrated to us, my brother Abu Bakr narrated to us, from Sulayman b. Bilal, from Muhammad b. Abi 'Atiq, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Umara b. Khuzayma, that his uncle informed him—and he was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a horse from a man among the Bedouins. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him to follow him so that he could pay him the price of his horse. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked quickly, and the Bedouin was slow. Some men began to intercept the Bedouin and bargain with him over the horse, not knowing that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had already bought it, until some of them raised the price for the Bedouin. When they raised it, the Bedouin called out, 'O Messenger of Allah, if you are buying this horse, then buy it; otherwise, I will sell it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up when he heard the Bedouin's call and came to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Did I not already buy it from you?' He said, 'No, by Allah, I did not sell it to you.' He said, 'Indeed, I bought it from you.' The people began to gather around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Bedouin as they argued back and forth. The Bedouin began to say, 'Bring a witness that I sold it to you.' Khuzayma said, 'I bear witness that you sold it to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to Khuzayma and said, 'On what basis do you testify?' He said, 'Because I believe you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made Khuzayma's testimony equal to the testimony of two men."],[2180,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bought a horse from Sawa' b. al-Harith al-Muharibi, but he denied it. Khuzayma b. Thabit testified for him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'What made you testify when you were not with him?' He said, 'You spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah, but I believed what you said, and I knew that you speak only the truth.' He said, 'Whoever Khuzayma testifies for or against, it is sufficient for him.'\""],[2181,"\"We used to sell the mothers of children during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr. When 'Umar came, he forbade us, so we stopped.\""],[2182,"We used to \"sell the mothers of children during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Sahih."],[2183,"Any woman who gives birth from her master, she is free after his death."],[2185,"He forbade selling grain until it hardens, selling grapes until they blacken, and selling dates until they redden and yellow."],[2186,"I heard Abu Sa'id al-Sa'idi and Ibn Abbas giving a fatwa that a dinar for two dinars is permissible. Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi said to him and was harsh with him. He said: Ibn Abbas said: I never thought that anyone who knows my kinship to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say such a thing to me, O Abu Usayd. Abu Usayd said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A dinar for a dinar, a dirham for a dirham, a sa' of wheat for a sa' of wheat, a sa' of barley for a sa' of barley, a sa' of salt for a sa' of salt, no excess between them in any of that.' Ibn Abbas said: This is only something I used to say and I had not heard anything about it."],[2187,"O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has a palm tree and I use it to support my wall. Order him to give it to me so that I may support my wall with it. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Give it to him for a palm tree in Paradise.' He refused. Abu al-Dahdah came to him and said: Sell me your palm tree for my wall. He did so. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have purchased the palm tree with my wall. He made it for him. The Prophet ﷺ said repeatedly: 'How many lush clusters does Abu al-Dahdah have in Paradise.' He came to his wife and said: O Umm al-Dahdah, leave the wall, for I have sold it for a palm tree in Paradise. She said: You have profited from the sale, or words to that effect."],[2188,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: So-and-so has a cluster in my wall and its location has harmed me and made things difficult for me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him and said: Sell me your cluster that is in so-and-so's wall. He said: No. He said: Give it as a gift. He said: No. He said: Then sell it to me for a cluster in Paradise. He said: No. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I have never seen anyone more miserly than you except one who withholds the greeting of salam."],[2189,"It is enough of a lie for a person to narrate everything he hears, and it is enough of miserliness for a person to say: I will take my right and not leave any of it."],[2190,"The Prophet ﷺ bought Safiyya from Dihya al-Kalbi for seven heads."],[2191,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The warranty period for slaves is three nights.' Sa'id said: I said to Qatada: How can this be? He said: If the buyer finds a defect in the goods, he may return it during those days without needing proof. If days pass, he cannot return it except with proof that he bought it and that defect was in it; otherwise, the seller's oath that he did not sell it with a disease. Thus said Sa'id and Hammam from Qatada, and likewise Yunus b. Ubayd narrated from al-Hasan. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2192,"There is no warranty period beyond four."],[2193,"The warranty period for slaves is four nights."],[2194,"Hibban b. Munqidh was a weak man and had suffered a head wound that reached the brain membrane. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him the option in what he bought for three days. His tongue had become heavy, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Sell and say, 'No cheating.' I used to hear him say: 'La khidhaba, la khidhaba' (mispronouncing). He would buy something and bring it to his family, and they would say: This is expensive. He would say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has given me the option in my sale. Sahih."],[2195,"She used to incur debt. It was said to her: What is with you and debt when you have no means to pay? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There is no servant who has the intention to repay his debt except that he has help from Allah, so I am seeking that help.'"],[2196,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “There is no servant who has the intention to repay his debt except that he has help from Allah, so I seek that help.” And its witness is the hadith of Maymunah."],[2197,"She used to incur debt and do so frequently. She was told about that, and she said: “I will not give up debt, because for it there is help from Allah, so I seek that help.”"],[2198,"“Indeed Allah is with the debtor until he pays off his debt, as long as it is not in something Allah dislikes.”"],[2199,"“Whoever incurs a debt while intending to repay it, then dies, Allah will pardon him and satisfy his creditor with whatever He wills. And whoever incurs a debt while not intending to repay it, then dies, Allah will exact retribution for his creditor from him on the Day of Resurrection.” Bishr is abandoned."],[2200,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had on two Qatari cloaks that were thick and coarse. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, your two garments are coarse and thick, and you sweat in them so they become heavy on you. So-and-so has received cloth from Syria; if you sent to him and took from him two garments on credit until a time of ease.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to him, and he said: “I know what Muhammad wants: he wants to take my two garments and delay payment for them.” The messenger came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “He has lied. They know that I am the most God-fearing of them and the most fulfilling of trust.”"],[2201,"I said: “O Messenger of Allah, your two garments are thick; if you took them off and sent to so-and-so the merchant, he would send you two garments on credit until a time of ease.” He said: “So he sent to him: Send me two garments on credit until a time of ease? But he refused.”"],[2202,"A caravan arrived and the Prophet ﷺ bought from it a sale and profited some uqiyahs of gold, then gave them as charity among the sons of Banu ‘Abd al-Muttalib and said: “I do not buy what I do not have the price for.” Al-Bukhari used ‘Ikrimah as evidence, and Muslim used Simak and Sharik. “The hadith is sahih but they did not include it.” Sahih."],[2203,"“Debt is the banner of Allah on earth. When He wants to humiliate a servant, He places it on his neck.”"],[2204,"He used to supplicate with these words: “O Allah, You are the First, so there is nothing before You, and You are the Last, so there is nothing after You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every creature whose forelock is in Your hand, and I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, from the punishment of the grave, from the punishment of the Fire, from the trial of wealth and the trial of poverty, and I seek refuge in You from sin and debt.”"],[2205,"Al-Qa‘nabi narrated to us: ‘Abd al-‘Aziz b. Muhammad narrated to us: al-‘Ala’ b. ‘Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Kathir, the freed slave of Muhammad b. Jahsh, from Muhammad b. Jahsh, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting where the funeral biers are placed. He raised his head toward the sky, then lowered his gaze and placed his hand on his forehead and said: “Glory be to Allah, glory be to Allah! What severity has Allah sent down?” He said: We understood and remained silent. The next day I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “O Messenger of Allah, what is the severity that came down?” He said: “Regarding debt. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if a man were killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, and had a debt, he would not enter Paradise until he paid it off.”"],[2206,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one day, and when he finished he said: “Is there anyone here from Banu So-and-so?” The people remained silent, for when he sought them for something they would stay silent. Then he said: “Is there anyone here from Banu So-and-so?” A man said: “Here is so-and-so.” He said: “Your companion has been detained at the gate of Paradise because of a debt he owed.” A man said: “I will pay his debt,” and he paid it. This is how Firas narrated it from al-Sha‘bi."],[2207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one day and said: “Is there anyone here from Banu So-and-so?” He called out three times, and no one answered him. Then he said: “The man who died among you has been withheld from Paradise because of the debt he owed. If you wish, ransom him; and if you wish, hand him over to Allah’s punishment.”"],[2208,"He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to his companions: “Do not burden yourselves.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah, and how do we burden ourselves? He said: “With debt.”"],[2209,"Whoever departs from the soul and the body while being free of three things will enter Paradise: misappropriation, debt, and arrogance."],[2210,"“Whoever dies while being free of three things — arrogance, misappropriation, and debt — will enter Paradise.”"],[2211,"“The soul of the believer is suspended by his debt until it is paid on his behalf.”"],[2212,"“The soul of the believer is suspended by his debt until it is paid on his behalf.”"],[2213,"Indeed Iblis despaired of idols being worshipped in the land of the Arabs, but he will be content with less than that from you through the minor sins of your deeds, which are the destructive ones. So beware of injustices as much as you can, for a servant will come on the Day of Resurrection with good deeds that he thinks will save him, and a servant will keep standing and saying: O Lord, so-and-so wronged me in some matter. It will be said: Remove from his good deeds until no good deed remains for him."],[2214,"“Whoever's intercession prevents a punishment from the punishments of Allah has opposed Allah in His command. Whoever dies with a debt, there is neither dinar nor dirham there, but rather it is good deeds and bad deeds. Whoever disputes in falsehood while knowing it, he remains in the displeasure of Allah until he desists. Whoever says about a believer what is not in him, he will be detained in the mire of corruption until he brings about an exit from what he said.”"],[2215,"A man had never done any good, and he used to lend to people and would say to his servant: Take what is easy and leave what is difficult, and overlook, perhaps Allah will overlook us. When he died, Allah said: Did you ever do any good? He said: No, except that I had a servant and I used to lend to people, and when I sent him to collect, I would say to him: Take what is easy and leave what is difficult, and overlook, perhaps Allah will overlook us. Allah said: Then I have overlooked you."],[2216,"I and my father went out seeking knowledge among this tribe of the Ansar before they perished. The first person we met was Abu al-Yasar, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was a servant of his. He was wearing a Ma'afiri cloak, and his servant also had a Ma'afiri cloak, and he had a bundle of scrolls. My father said to him: I see in your face a trace of anger. He said: Yes, I had money owed to me by so-and-so, the son of so-and-so, the Harami. I went to his family and said: Is he there? They said: No. Then his son came out, and I said to him: Where is your father? He said: He heard your voice and entered my mother's bedchamber. I said: Come out, for I know where you are. He came out to me and I said to him: What made you hide from me? He said: I, by Allah, will tell you and not lie to you. I feared, by Allah, that if I spoke to you I would lie to you, or if I promised you I would break my promise, and you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: By Allah, were you truly in hardship? I said: By Allah. He said: By Allah. I said: By Allah. He said: By Allah. Then he spread out the scroll and erased the debt, and said: If you find means to pay, then pay; otherwise you are released. I bear witness that these two eyes of mine saw — and he placed his two fingers on his eyes — and these two ears of mine heard — and he placed his two fingers in his ears — and my heart comprehended it — and he pointed to the artery of his heart — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: “Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty and waives for him, Allah will shade him in His shade.”"],[2217,"“Whoever grants respite to a debtor in difficulty, for each day before the debt becomes due there is a charity for him. Then when the debt becomes due and he grants him respite after that, for each day there is the like of it as charity.”"],[2218,"A man was called to account and no good was found for him. He had wealth and used to lend to people, and he would say to his servants: Whoever you find wealthy, take from him, and whoever you find in hardship, overlook him, perhaps Allah will overlook me. Allah said: “I am more entitled to overlook him.” This is a sound chain according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. It has also been narrated from Abdullah b. Numayr from al-A'mash."],[2219,"A man was called to account and no good was found for him."],[2220,"A man clung to a debtor of his for ten dinars and said to him, \"By Allah, I have no payment with which to pay you today.\" He said, \"By Allah, I will not part from you until you pay or bring a guarantor who will bear it on your behalf.\" He said, \"By Allah, I have no payment and I cannot find anyone to bear it on my behalf.\" He said, \"So he dragged him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is my debtor. I granted him a delay of one month, but he refused unless I pay him or bring him a guarantor.' I said, 'By Allah, I cannot find a guarantor, and I have no payment today.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Will you grant him a delay of only one month?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Then I will bear it on your behalf.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bore it on his behalf. The man went and brought the amount he had promised. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Where did you obtain this gold?' He said, 'From a mine.' He said, 'Then go, for we have no need of it; there is no good in it.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ paid it on his behalf."],[2221,"I sold to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a young camel. I came to demand payment and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, pay the price of my young camel.' He said, 'Yes, I will not pay you except at its proper time.' Then he paid me and was excellent in his payment. Then a bedouin came to him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, pay for my young camel.' He paid him without any stipulated delay. The bedouin said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is better than my young camel.' He said, 'It is yours. The best of people are those who are best in repayment.'"],[2222,"I and Makhramah al-Abdi brought cloth from Hajar or al-Bahrayn. When we were at Mina, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and bought from us trousers and a cloak. There was a weigher weighing for a fee, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him the price and said, 'Weigh and give more.' Shu'bah narrated it from Simak ibn Harb."],[2223,"I heard Abu Safwan say: I sold to the Prophet ﷺ trousers, and he weighed for me and gave more. Abu Safwan is the kunyah of Suwayd ibn Qays; they are one of my companions from the Ansar. The hadith is sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it."],[2224,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the people of measure and weight: 'You have been entrusted with a matter in which the previous nations perished.'"],[2225,"He forbade breaking the coinage of the Muslims that is current among them, except for a valid reason, or that a dirham is broken and made into silver, or a dinar is broken and made into gold."],[2226,"Gabriel came to me and said: 'O Muhammad, Allah has cursed wine, its presser, its squeezer, its drinker, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its pourer, and the one who gives it to drink.'"],[2227,"Allah has cursed wine, and He has cursed its pourer, its drinker, its presser, its squeezer, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, and the consumer of its price."],[2228,"The Prophet ﷺ bought from a bedouin a camel for dates, and he thought that the dates were with him, but some of them were with him and some were not. He said, 'Would you like to take some of your dates now and the rest at the time of date-picking?' He refused, so the Prophet ﷺ borrowed the dates for him and handed them over to him."],[2229,"Zayd ibn Sa'nah, one of the Jewish rabbis, came to the Prophet ﷺ to demand repayment. He grabbed his garment from his right shoulder and said, 'You, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, are people of delay, and I am well acquainted with you.' Umar rebuked him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'O Umar, I and he were in need of something other than this from you: that you command me to pay well and command him to demand well. Go, O Umar, and give him his due. Indeed, there remain three days of his term, so add thirty sa's for your harshness toward him.'"],[2230,"Whoever seeks a right, let him seek it with chastity, whether it is fulfilled or not."],[2231,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the one who has a right: Take your right with chastity, and I think he said, whether it is fulfilled or not."],[2232,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, they were among the most deficient of people in measure. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {Woe to those who give less than due} [Al-Mutaffifin: 1]. Thereafter, they were fair in measure."],[2233,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Khaybar, he appointed Siba' b. 'Urfutah al-Ghifari as his deputy. We arrived and attended the Fajr prayer with him. In the first rak'ah he recited {Kaf. Ha. Ya. 'Ain. Sad.} [Maryam: 1], and in the second {Woe to those who give less than due} [Al-Mutaffifin: 1]. I said to myself: Woe to Abu Fulan; he has two measures, he takes full with one and gives less with the other. Then we went to Siba' b. 'Urfutah and he equipped us. “We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day before the conquest or one day after it?”"],[2234,"“The dowry of an adulteress is not lawful, nor is the price of a dog.”"],[2235,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog, the dowry of a prostitute, the earnings of a soothsayer, and the earnings of a cupper.”"],[2236,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog and a cat.” 'Isa b. Yunus concurred from al-A'mash, according to the condition of Muslim."],[2237,"'Abdullah b. Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, 'Isa b. Yunus narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the price of a dog and a cat.” Abu al-Zubayr concurred from Jabir."],[2238,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited eating a cat and consuming its price.” The hadith of al-A'mash from Abu Sufyan is “authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it.” 'Umar b. Zayd is weak."],[2239,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the milk of a jallalah (animal that eats filth), eating a mujaththamah (animal that is tied and shot), and drinking from the mouth of a waterskin.”"],[2240,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited eating a jallalah and its milk.”"],[2241,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited riding a jallalah—meaning camels—or drinking its milk.”"],[2242,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a mujaththamah and a jallalah.”"],[2243,"“He prohibited selling a sheep for meat.”"],[2244,"He forbade selling meat for animals."],[2245,"Whoever buys a stolen item knowing it is stolen has shared in its disgrace and sin."],[2246,"Any man who makes a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them; and any woman married off by two guardians, she belongs to the first of them."],[2247,"Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan: When a man's property is stolen and he finds it, he is more entitled to it wherever he finds it. He said: Marwan wrote that to me while I was over al-Yamamah, so I wrote to Marwan that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ ruled that when the property is with an unsuspected man, the owner may either take it by paying its price or pursue the thief. Then Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman ruled accordingly after him. He said: Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan: You are not the one—nor is Usayd—to judge against me in what I have been given authority, but I judge over you both, so carry out what I have commanded you. Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter to him, and he said: By Allah, I will never judge by it."],[2248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: If you were to sell dried dates to your brother and they were smitten by blight, it will not be allowable for you to take your brother's property unjustly. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3470)"],[2249,"How can any of you deem his brother's wealth lawful if a calamity from the sky befalls it?"],[2250,"Do you think that if Allah withholds the dates, how can any of you deem his brother's wealth lawful?"],[2251,"Riba has seventy-three doors, the least of which is like a man marrying his own mother, and the worst form of riba is harming the honor of a Muslim man."],[2252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are four individuals who have no right to enter Paradise and will not taste its blessings: the habitual drinker, the one who consumes interest, the one who unjustly consumes the wealth of orphans, and the one who disobeys and mistreats their parents.\""],[2253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade buying fruit until it ripens, and he said: When adultery and riba appear in a village, they have made Allah's punishment lawful upon themselves."],[2254,"Riba, even if it increases, its outcome ultimately leads to decrease."],[2255,"He said: I heard Jabir b. Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling a heap of dates of unknown measure for a specified measure of dates."],[2256,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being asked about fresh dates for dry dates, and he asked those around him: Does it decrease when it dries? They said: Yes. He said: Then no. Abu al-Walid said: I heard Malik b. Anas another time say: He disliked it. This is the wording of Abu al-Walid's hadith. Ismail b. Umayyah narrated similarly from Abdullah b. Yazid, the freed slave of al-Aswad b. Sufyan. Malik narrated it once and disliked it."],[2257,"Two men made a transaction in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ involving unripe dates and fresh dates, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Does fresh dates decrease when they dry? They said: Yes. He said: Then no. This is how Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Ismail b. Umayyah."],[2258,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about fresh dates for dried dates, and he said: \"Does it decrease when it dries?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"So he forbade it.\" Yahya b. Abi Kathir has followed them in his narration from Abdullah b. Yazid."],[2259,"He informed him that he heard Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling fresh dates for dried dates on credit.\""],[2260,"A man's record will be raised on the Day of Resurrection until he thinks that he is saved. Then the injustices against people will keep pursuing him until he has no good deed left, and more of their sins will be added to him."],[2261,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the jallalah (animals that eat dung) from having its meat eaten, its milk drunk, leather goods carried on it, or people riding it until it has been fed clean fodder for forty nights."],[2262,"He forbade that goods be sold where they are bought until the buyer takes possession of them to his own camp. Indeed, he would send men who would beat us for that."],[2263,"I bought oil in the market, and when I had completed the purchase, a man met me and offered me a good profit for it. I wanted to shake his hand, but a man behind me took hold of my arm. I turned and it was Zayd b. Thabit, who said: Do not sell it where you bought it until you take it to your camp, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"forbade that goods be sold where they are bought until the merchants take them to their camps.\""],[2264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade every wild animal with fangs, the killing of children, and the purchase of spoils until they are distributed."],[2265,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling spoils until they are distributed. Sahih."],[2266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"set aside the loss due to natural calamities (jawa'ih).\" Ali b. al-Madini said: Sufyan had narrated to us from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir from the Prophet ﷺ that he \"set aside the loss due to natural calamities.\""],[2267,"A man in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suffered a loss in fruits he had bought, and his debt mounted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Give charity to him.\" So they gave charity to him, but it did not amount to enough to pay off his debt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take whatever you find, and you have nothing but that.\""],[2268,"He cultivated some land, and the Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was watering it. He asked him: \"For whom is the crop and for whom is the land?\" He said: My crop with my seed and my labor; I get half and the family of so-and-so get half. He said: \"You have dealt in usury. Return the land to its owners and take your expenses.\""],[2269,"I taught some people of the Suffa writing and the Quran, and a man among them gave me a bow as a gift. I said: It is not wealth, and I shoot with it in the way of Allah. I will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him. So I came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man gave me a bow as a gift from among those I teach writing and the Quran. It is not wealth, and I shoot with it in the way of Allah. He said: \"If you love to be collared with a collar of fire, then accept it.\""],[2270,"The earnings of the cupper are vile, the price of a dog is vile, and the bridal gift of an adulteress is vile."],[2271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us today—then he mentioned some things—and said: “He forbade us from the earnings of a slave woman except what she earns with her own hands,” and he said, gesturing with his finger toward spinning, baking, and carding."],[2272,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the earnings of a slave woman until it is known where they come from.” We cited it as a corroborating report."],[2273,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the stud fee of a stallion.”"],[2274,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while he was with his wife Umm Salamah, said: “I crave some ‘ajwah dates.” So she sent two ṣāʿs of dates to a man of the Anṣār, and he brought back, in place of the two ṣāʿs, one ṣāʿ of ‘ajwah dates. She got up and presented it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he saw it, he was pleased, and he took one date, then held back and said: “Where did you get this?” Umm Salamah said: “I sent two ṣāʿs of dates to a man of the Anṣār, and he brought us this one ṣāʿ in place of the two ṣāʿs. Here it is; eat.” He threw the date down in front of him and said: “Return it. I have no need of it. Dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, gold for gold, silver for silver, hand to hand, like for like. Whoever adds more, that is usury.” Then he said: “Likewise whatever is measured by volume or weight.” Ibn ʿAbbās said: “May Allah reward you, Abū Saʿīd, with Paradise, for you reminded me of something I had forgotten. I seek Allah’s forgiveness and turn to Him.” After that he would forbid it most severely."],[2275,"Saʿd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about buying fresh dates for dry dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Is there any superiority between them?” They said: “Yes, fresh dates lose weight.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then it is not valid.”"],[2276,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked about it. Authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[2277,"I used to sell camels at al-Naqīʿ, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars. Something about that fell into my heart, so I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the house of Ḥafṣah—or he said when he came out of the house of Ḥafṣah—and I said: “O Messenger of Allah, wait a moment so I may ask you. I sell camels at al-Baqīʿ, selling for dinars and taking dirhams, and selling for dirhams and taking dinars.” He said: “There is no harm in taking them at the exchange rate of that day, as long as you do not part while something remains between you.”"],[2278,"“He used to forbid the sale of water.”"],[2279,"\"Do not sell the gift of water to people, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited the selling of water.\" And Ibn Jurayj also has another report regarding this matter."],[2280,"“He forbade the sale of water, the stud service of a camel, and that a man sell his land and its water.”"],[2281,"“He forbade the sale of water.”"],[2282,"We raided with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ toward Syria. Nabataean farmers from Syria would come to us, and we would pay them in advance for wheat and oil at a known price and a known term. It was said to him: “From whom do they have that?” He said: “We would not ask them.”"],[2283,"Whoever cancels a sale for a Muslim, Allah will cancel his slip."],[2284,"Whoever makes two sales in one sale, he gets the lesser of the two or usury."],[2285,"If the two parties to a sale differ and there is no evidence between them, then the word is that of the owner of the goods, or they may revoke the transaction."],[2286,"A man's child is from his earnings, from the purest of his earnings, so eat of their wealth."],[2287,"She asked Aisha: I have an orphan in my care, may I eat from his wealth? She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Among the purest of what a man eats is from his earnings, and his child is from his earnings.' Sahih."],[2288,"Deliver the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."],[2289,"The Prophet ﷺ said: Pay the deposit to him who deposited it with you, and do not betray him who betrayed you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3535)"],[2290,"It is not lawful for a man to give a gift or bestow a grant and then take it back, except a father in what he gives his child. The example of one who gives a gift and then takes it back is like a dog that eats until it is full, vomits, then returns to its vomit."],[2291,"On his father's authority, said that his grandfather reported the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is not permissible for a woman to present a gift from the property which she has in her possession when her husband owns her chastity. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3546)"],[2292,"The Prophet ﷺ borrowed a shield from him on the day of Hunayn, so he said, \"Should I rob you, O Muhammad?\" He (the Prophet) said, \"No, but it is guaranteed (to be returned).\" This is witnessed by Ibn Abbas."],[2293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ borrowed from Safwan b. Umayya coats of mail and spearheads during the battle of Hunayn. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is it a loan to be returned? He said: 'A loan to be returned.'"],[2294,"On the hand is what it takes until it returns it."],[2295,"He had a vicious she-camel that entered a garden and damaged it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was spoken to about it, and he ruled that guarding gardens by day is the responsibility of their owners, and guarding livestock by night is the responsibility of their owners, and the owners of livestock are liable for what their livestock damages."],[2296,"I attended Abu Ubayda b. Abdullah b. Mas'ud when two men came to him who had traded goods. One of them said: I took it for such and such, and the other said: I sold it for such and such. Abu Ubayda said:"],[2297,"The Prophet ﷺ bought from a bedouin—I think he said from Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'a—a load of khubat. When the deal was concluded, the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'Choose.' The bedouin said: I have never seen a seller like you today. May Allah grant you long life, who are you from? He said: 'From Quraysh.' Ibn Wahb followed him from Ibn Jurayj, and it is on the condition of Muslim."],[2298,"The Prophet ﷺ bought a load of khubat from a bedouin, and when the sale was concluded, the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Choose.\" The bedouin said, \"May Allah grant you long life as a seller.\""],[2299,"\"The taker and the giver are equal in ribā.\""],[2300,"\"Dinar for dinar and dirham for dirham, with no excess between them. Whoever has a need for silver should exchange it for gold, and whoever has a need for gold should exchange it for silver, and the exchange is hand to hand.\""],[2301,"\"Muslims are bound by their conditions, and reconciliation is permissible among Muslims.\""],[2302,"\"Muslims are bound by their conditions as long as they conform to the truth.\""],[2303,"\"Every act of kindness is charity. What a man spends on himself and his family is recorded for him as charity, and what a person uses to protect his honor is recorded for him as charity. Whatever a believer spends, if he leaves it to Allah, Allah is its guarantor, except what is in building or disobedience.\""],[2304,"\"Whoever among you is able to protect his religion and honor with his wealth, let him do so.\""],[2305,"\"Reconciliation among Muslims is permissible.\""],[2306,"\"Any man who dies or becomes bankrupt, the owner of the goods is more entitled to his goods if he finds them in their exact form.\""],[2307,"\"The pledge is not foreclosed; its benefit belongs to its owner, and its liability is upon him.\""],[2308,"\"The pledge is not foreclosed; its owner has its benefit and bears its liability.\""],[2309,"A pledge is not to be foreclosed; the pledge belongs to the one who pledged it, and upon him is its liability."],[2310,"A pledge is not to be foreclosed until its benefit is yours and its liability is upon you."],[2311,"A pledge is not to be foreclosed; to him belongs its benefit, and upon him is its liability."],[2312,"A pledge is not to be foreclosed; to you belongs its benefit, and upon you is its liability."],[2313,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah says, \"I am the third of the two partners as long as one of them does not betray his companion. When he betrays, I withdraw from between them.\" And"],[2314,"Whoever gives a gift is more entitled to it as long as he has not received a reward for it."],[2315,"When a gift is given to a close relative with whom marriage is forbidden, he does not take it back."],[2316,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to expel the Banu al-Nadir, they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have ordered our expulsion, yet we have debts owed by people that are not yet due.\" He said, \"Reduce the debt and hasten payment.\""],[2317,"Makkah is a resting place: its properties are not to be sold and its houses are not to be rented."],[2318,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Makkah is sacred, the sale of its properties is sacred, and the rent of its houses is sacred.\" The narrations are authentic that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah peacefully. Among them is Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, who is weak."],[2319,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched toward Makkah to conquer it, he said to Abu Hurayrah, \"Call out to the Ansar.\" So he said, \"O Ansar, respond to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" They came as if they had an appointment. Then he said, \"Take this road, and let no one of yours be seen except that you grant him safety.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched, and Allah granted him its conquest. He circumambulated the House and prayed two rak'ahs, then went out through the gate facing al-Safa. He ascended al-Safa and addressed the people while the Ansar were below him. The Ansar said to one another, \"As for the man, compassion for his people and desire for his town have taken hold of him.\" Allah sent down revelation about what the Ansar said. He said, \"O Ansar, you say: 'As for the man, compassion for his people and desire for his town have taken hold of him.'\" He said, \"Then who am I? No, by Allah, I am truly the servant of Allah and His Messenger. My life is your life, and my death is your death.\" They said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we did not say that except out of fear that he might turn away from us.\" He said, \"You are truthful before Allah and His Messenger.\" He said, \"By Allah, there was not one of them but that his chest was wet with tears.\" And among them: authentic."],[2320,"On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted security to all except for four men and two women. He said, \"Kill them even if you find them clinging to the curtains of the Kaaba.\" The four men were Ikrimah ibn Abi Jahl, Abdallah ibn Khatal, Maqis ibn Subabah, and Abdallah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh."],[2321,"He was called Sarraq. I said to him, \"What is this name?\" He said, \"A name the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me, and I will never abandon it.\" I said, \"Why did he name you that?\" He said, \"I came to Madinah and informed them that my masters had sold me and I had consumed their wealth. They brought me to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'You are Sarraq.' He sold me for four camels and said to the creditors who bought me, 'What will you do with him?' They said, 'We will free him.' They said, 'We are not less desirous of the Hereafter than you.' So they freed me among themselves, and my name remained."],[2322,"Captives were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered me to sell two brothers. I sold them and separated them. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, and he said: \"Catch up with them, reclaim them, and sell them together, and do not separate them.\""],[2323,"He sold a slave woman and her child and separated them, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade him from doing that. This is another text with a sound chain of narrators. Sahih."],[2324,"\"Cursed is the one who separates.\" This has a sound chain of narrators, but they did not include it, and its explanation is in the hadith of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, which is Sahih."],[2325,"\"Whoever separates a mother from her child, Allah will separate him from his loved ones on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[2326,"He heard Ubadah b. al-Samit say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade separating a mother from her child. It was asked: O Messenger of Allah, until when? He said: \"Until the boy reaches puberty and the girl menstruates.\""],[2327,"He said: On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling spoils of war until they were distributed, and forbade having intercourse with pregnant captives until they gave birth to what was in their wombs. He also said: \"Do not water the crops of another,\" and forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and the meat of every fanged beast of prey."],[2328,"\"Whoever has a partner in a walled garden should not sell his share of it until he offers it to his partner.\""],[2329,"\"Allah loves leniency in selling, leniency in buying, and leniency in repayment.\""],[2330,"If you see someone selling or buying in the mosque, say: \"May Allah not make your trade profitable.\" And if you see someone announcing a lost item in it, say: \"May Allah not return it to you.\""],[2331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to equip an army, but the camels were insufficient. So he commanded him to keep back the young camels of sadaqah, and he was taking a camel to be replaced by two when the camels of sadaqah came. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3357)"],[2332,"\"He forbade advance payment for animals.\""],[2333,"\"He forbade selling deferred for deferred.\""],[2334,"\"He forbade selling deferred for deferred, meaning credit for credit.\""],[2335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade muhaqala, mukhadara, and munabadha. Ustadh Abu al-Walid said: Mukhadara is that none of it is sold until it turns red or yellow."],[2336,"There is no harm and no reciprocating harm. Whoever harms, Allah harms him, and whoever causes hardship, Allah causes hardship upon him."],[2337,"A man died, so we washed him, shrouded him, embalmed him, and placed him for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ where funeral biers are placed, near the Station of Jibril. Then we notified the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pray over him, and he came with us step by step. Then he said, \"Perhaps your companion has a debt?\" They said, \"Yes, two dinars.\" So he held back. A man among us called Abu Qatada said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, they are upon me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to say, \"They are upon you and from your wealth, and the deceased is free of them.\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he prayed over him. Then whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Abu Qatada, he would say, \"What have the two dinars done?\" until the last time he said, \"I have paid them off, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Now, when his skin has cooled.\""],[2338,"The pledge is milked and ridden. Al-A'mash said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he disliked benefiting from any of it. \"This is an authentic chain according to the condition of the two Shaykhs,\" but they did not record it due to the consensus of al-Thawri and Shu'ba on its being mawquf from al-A'mash. I, according to my principle, which I established regarding accepting additions from a trustworthy narrator, [accept it] according to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2339,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed a restriction on Mu'adh's wealth and sold it for a debt he owed."],[2340,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ deemed some people too young on the day of Uhud, among them Zayd b. Haritha—meaning himself—and al-Bara' b. 'Azib, Zayd b. Arqam, Sa'd, Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, and 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, and he mentioned Jabir b. 'Abd Allah."],[2341,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The pen is lifted from three: the child until he reaches puberty, the insane until he regains his senses, and the sleeping until he wakes up.\""],[2342,"A madwoman of Banu So-and-so who had committed adultery was brought past 'Ali, and 'Umar b. al-Khattab had ordered her stoning. 'Ali b. Abi Talib sent her back and said to 'Umar, \"O Commander of the Faithful, did you order the stoning of this woman?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Do you not remember that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The pen is lifted from three: the insane person whose mind is overcome, the sleeping until he wakes up, and the child until he reaches puberty?\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" So he released her."],[2343,"This verse was revealed, {And settlement is best} [al-Nisa' 128], concerning a man who had a wife whose companionship had lasted long and who had borne him children, and he wanted to replace her, so she appeased him on the condition that she remain with him and he would not have to divide his time for her."],[2344,"Sawda gave her day to 'A'isha, and I think that about this was revealed {And if a woman fears from her husband contempt or evasion} [al-Nisa' 128]."],[2345,"The truce between the Prophet ﷺ and the people of Makkah at al-Hudaybiya lasted four years."],[2346,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I am a guarantor, and the guarantor is the one who bears responsibility, for whoever believes in me, submits, and emigrates, for a house in the outskirts of Paradise.\""],[2347,"My mother lost her father and came to the city, and the people proposed to her. She said, \"I will not marry except to a man who takes care of this orphan for me.\" So a man from the Ansar married her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to present the young men of the Ansar every year, and he would marry off those who reached the age of marriage. So I was presented one year, and a young man married me, and then divorced me. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you have married me off, and he divorced me.\" He said, \"Marry him.\" So I married him, and I prevailed over him."],[2348,"He was a partner of the Prophet ﷺ at the beginning of Islam in trade. When the day of the conquest came, he said: \"Welcome to my brother and my partner; he does not deceive nor dispute.\" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[2349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ protected al-Baqi' and said: \"There is no protected reserve except for Allah and His Messenger.\" They agreed on the hadith of Yunus from al-Zuhri with its chain: \"There is no protected reserve except for Allah and His Messenger,\" but they did not transmit it in this manner, and its chain is authentic according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim, and they transmitted only its ending from it."],[2350,"He forbade the sale of water."],[2351,"He forbade the sale of surplus water."],[2352,"The surplus water of a well shall not be withheld."],[2353,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning the flood stream of Mahzur and Mudhnib that the upper landowner should release water to the lower landowner and retain only up to the ankles."],[2354,"Whoever receives a favor from his brother without asking or desiring it should accept it and not reject it, for it is a provision that Allah has brought to him."],[2355,"Do not persist in asking, for by Allah, if any of you asks me for something and his request extracts it from me while I am reluctant, it will not be blessed for him in what I give him."],[2356,"A man gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a milch-camel, and he rewarded him with six young she-camels for it. The man was displeased with them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Who will excuse me from so-and-so? He gifted me a milch-camel, and it is as if I can see it in the face of some of his family, so I rewarded him with six young she-camels for it, and he was displeased. I have resolved not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi, an Ansari, a Thaqafi, or a Dausi.\""],[2357,"My family sent me with a milch-camel to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a gift. He said to me: \"Milk it and leave what stimulates the milk.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2358,"My father narrated to us: Umm Khalid bint Khalid narrated to me, she said: The Prophet ﷺ was brought some garments, among them a small black khamisah (a square cloth with markings). He said: \"Who do you think I should clothe with this?\" The people remained silent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Bring me Umm Khalid.\" She said: So I was brought to him, and he dressed me in it with his own hand and said: \"Wear it out and wear it ragged,\" saying it twice. He began looking at a yellow and red marking on the khamisah and saying: \"O Umm Khalid, this is sana, sana.\" And sana in the language of Abyssinia means beautiful."],[2359,"The Ansar have taken all the reward. He said: \"No, as long as you supplicate Allah for them and praise them.\""],[2360,"“Whoever asks you by Allah, give him; and whoever seeks your protection by Allah, grant him protection; and whoever does you a favor, repay him; but if you find nothing, then supplicate for him until you know that you have repaid him; and whoever seeks refuge with you by Allah, grant him refuge.”"],[2361,"A man brought the Prophet ﷺ a donkey while he was walking and said, “Ride, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The owner of the mount is more entitled to the front of his mount, unless you assign it to me.” He said, “I have done so.”"],[2362,"“Whoever shelters a stray animal is himself astray as long as he does not announce it.”"],[2363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about a found item (luqaṭah). He said, “Announce it, do not conceal it, and do not hide it. If its owner comes, [give it to him]; otherwise, it is Allah’s property, which He gives to whomever He wills.”"],[2364,"“He forbade picking up found items of pilgrims.”"],[2365,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about a treasure a man found: “If you found it in an inhabited village or on a frequented road, then announce it. But if you found it in a ruin of the pre-Islamic era or in an uninhabited village or on an unfrequented road, then in it and in the buried treasure (rikāz) the fifth is due.” I have presented many arguments in this book for authenticating the narrations of ʿAmr b. Shuʿayb when the narrator from him is trustworthy; and none is reported from him better than these narrations. I had been seeking clear evidence for Shuʿayb b. Muḥammad’s hearing from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, but I have not obtained it until now. Sahih."],[2366,"A man came to Abdullah b. Amr, asking him about a muhrim who had intercourse with his wife. He pointed to Abdullah b. Umar and said, “Go to that one and ask him.” Shuayb said: The man did not recognize him, so I went with him, and he asked Ibn Umar. He said, “Your Hajj is invalid.” The man said, “So what should I do?” He said, “Enter ihram with the people, do what they do, and when you reach the coming year, perform Hajj and offer a sacrificial animal.” He then returned to Abdullah b. Amr while I was with him, and he said, “Go to Ibn Abbas and ask him.” Shuayb said: So I went with him to Ibn Abbas, and he asked him, and he said to him the same as Ibn Umar had said. He returned to Abdullah b. Amr while I was with him and informed him of what Ibn Abbas had said. Then he said, “What do you say?” He replied, “My view is like what the two of them said.” This is a hadith of trustworthy narrators; its transmitters are memorizers. It is as if it takes one by the hand in establishing the soundness of Shuayb b. Muhammad’s hearing from his grandfather Abdullah b. Amr. This is the end of what my independent effort has led me to add in the Book of Sale beyond what the two imams, Abu Abdullah al-Bukhari and Abu al-Husayn al-Qushayri, compiled. Within this book I have mentioned books for which al-Bukhari set chapter headings at the end of the Book of Sales, among them: the Book of Salam, the Book of Pre-emption, the Book of Leasing, the Book of Transfer of Debt, the Book of Cultivation, the Book of Sharecropping, the Book of Irrigation Partnerships, the Book of Grants, the Book of Gifts, the Book of Qirad, the Book of Lost Property, the Book of Wrongs, the Book of Refraining from Begging, the Book of Pledge, the Book of Partnership, the Book of Manumission, the Book of the Mukatab, the Book of Testimonies, the Book of Settlement, the Book of Conditions, the Book of Bequests, and the Book of Endowment. I have only explained them at the end of this book so that no one might suppose that I left the Book of Sales devoid of these books. Allah is the Helper in what I establish through tracing the reports of the two imams, and He is sufficient for me and the best disposer of affairs.[1]"],[2367,"When the people of Makkah expelled the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said, “Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return. They have expelled their Prophet—they will surely perish.” He said: Then was revealed: {Permission [to fight] is given to those who are fought, because they have been wronged, and indeed Allah is Able to give them victory} [al-Ḥajj: 39]. Ibn ʿAbbās used to recite it as “udhina.” Abu Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said, “Then I knew that it would be fighting.” Ibn ʿAbbās said, “It is the first verse revealed concerning fighting.”"],[2368,"ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf and some companions of his came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Prophet of Allah, we were in honor while we were polytheists, but when we believed we became humiliated.” He said, “I have been commanded to pardon, so do not fight the people.” When He transferred him to Madinah, He commanded him to fight, but they refrained. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {Have you not seen those who were told, “Restrain your hands and establish prayer and give zakāh”? Then when fighting was prescribed for them, at once a party of them feared people} [al-Nisāʾ: 77]."],[2369,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon on the day of Tabūk and said, “There is none among the people like a man who takes hold of the reins [of his horse] and strives in the path of Allah, avoiding the evils of people, and like a man in the desert with his sheep, who entertains his guest and fulfills his right.” He said: I said, “Did he say it?” He said, “He said it three times,” so I said takbīr, praised Allah, and gave thanks."],[2370,"“Shall I not inform you of the best of people in station?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “A man holding the rein of his horse in the path of Allah until he is killed or dies. Shall I not inform you of the one who follows him? A man secluded in a mountain pass, who establishes prayer, gives zakāh, and bears witness that there is no god but Allah.”"],[2371,"\"in the year of Tabuk, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people, while leaning against his mount. He said: 'Shall I not tell you of the best of the people and the worst of the people? Among the best of the people is a man who strives in the cause of Allah on the back of his horse, or on the back of his camel, or on his own two feet, until death comes to him. And among the worst of the people, is an immoral man (Fajir) who reads the Book of Allah but he does not refrain from doing anything bad because of it.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3106)"],[2372,"“A day in the path of Allah is better than a thousand days elsewhere. So let every person look to himself.”"],[2373,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ passed by a mountain pass in which there was a spring of sweet water. Its pleasantness and beauty impressed him, and he said, “If only I were to seclude myself from people and stay in this mountain pass.” Then he said, “I will not do so until I consult the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said, “Do not do it, for the station of one of you in the path of Allah is better than his prayer in his house for sixty years. Would you not love that Allah forgive you and admit you to Paradise? Raid in the path of Allah. Whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a camel, Paradise becomes due for him.”"],[2374,"A man's standing in the battle line in the path of Allah is better in the sight of Allah than a man's worship for sixty years."],[2375,"A group of us from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down and said, \"If only we knew which deeds are most beloved to Allah, we would do them.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth exalts Allah, and He is the Mighty, the Wise} until the end of the surah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to us. This is how al-Awza'i said it, and Yahya b. Abi Kathir recited it to us in Makkah. Muhammad b. Kathir said, and al-Awza'i recited it to us in this way. Abu al-Walid said, and Ibn Kathir recited it to us in this way. Abu al-Hasan b. 'Uqbah said, and Abu al-Walid recited it to us in this way."],[2376,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"If only we knew which deeds are most beloved to Allah.\" Then he mentioned the hadith. This is not to be called the hadith of al-Walid b. Muslim, for al-Hiql b. Ziyad, although his status is trustworthy and reliable, he doubted its chain. And from the evidence for the soundness of Abu Salamah's chain is that Abu Ishaq Ibrahim b. Muhammad al-Fazari, the most retentive of al-Awza'i's companions, narrated it with additional wording in it by the first chain, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2377,"We gathered and discussed among ourselves which of us should go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah. Then we dispersed, and we were in awe that any one of us should go to him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for us and gathered us, and some of us began gesturing to others. He recited to us: {Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth exalts Allah} until the end of the surah. Abu Salamah said: 'Abdullah b. Salam recited it to us to its end. Yahya b. Abi Kathir said: Abu Salamah recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Mahbub said: Abu Ishaq recited it to us from its beginning to its end, meaning Surah al-Saff."],[2378,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Paradise is beneath the shadows of swords.' A young man of shabby appearance said, 'Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'Yes.' Then he broke the scabbard of his sword with him, then said to his companions, 'Peace be upon you,' and entered the fight."],[2379,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Do you know the first group from my Ummah to enter Paradise?' He said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'The emigrants will come on the Day of Resurrection to the gate of Paradise and seek to open it. The keepers will say to them, \"Have you been brought to account?\" They will say, \"For what would we be brought to account? Our swords were upon our shoulders in the path of Allah until we died upon that.\"' He said, 'So it will be opened for them, and they will rest therein for forty years before the people enter it.'"],[2380,"He was asked, 'Which of the believers is most complete in faith?' He said, 'The one who strives in the path of Allah with his self and his wealth, and a man who worships Allah in one of the mountain passes and has spared the people his evil.'"],[2381,"From 'Amr b. Malik al-Janbi that he heard Abu Fadalah b. 'Ubayd say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'I am the guarantor, and the guarantor is the one who bears responsibility, for the one who believes and submits and strives in the path of Allah, of a house in the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the middle of Paradise. And I am the guarantor for the one who believes of a house in the middle of Paradise. And I am the guarantor for the one who believes and submits and emigrates of a house in the outskirts of Paradise and a house in the middle of Paradise and a house in the highest part of Paradise. Whoever does that and leaves no avenue of good untaken and no escape from evil unheeded, he may die wherever he wishes to die.'"],[2382,"The Prophet ﷺ said: A section of my community will continue to fight for the right and overcome their opponents till the last of them fights with the Antichrist. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2484)"],[2383,"The first group to enter Paradise are the poor emigrants, through whom misfortunes are warded off. When they are commanded, they hear and obey. If one of them had a need to the ruler, it would not be fulfilled for him until he dies with it still in his breast. And Allah, Exalted is He, will call Paradise on the Day of Resurrection, and it will come with its adornments and beauty. Then He will say, 'Where are My servants who fought in My path, were killed in My path, were harmed in My path, and strove in My path? Enter Paradise.' So they will enter it without reckoning or punishment. Then the angels will come and say, 'Our Lord, we glorify You night and day and sanctify You. Who are these whom You have preferred over us?' The Lord, Blessed and Exalted, will say, 'These are those who fought in My path and were harmed in My path.' Then the angels will enter upon them from every gate: 'Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. Excellent is the final home.'"],[2384,"They will not gather together in Hell in a gathering that harms one of them the other: a Muslim who killed a disbeliever, then the Muslim remained steadfast and did right. And they will not gather together in the belly of a servant: dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell. And they will not gather together in the heart of a servant: faith and miserliness."],[2385,"Dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never gather together in the belly of a servant. And miserliness and faith will never gather together in the heart of a servant."],[2386,"“The dust in the way of Allah and the smoke of Hell will never come together on the face of a Muslim man.”"],[2387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched a military detachment, and a woman came to him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, you sent out this detachment, and my husband went out with it. I used to keep the same fasts as him, perform the same prayers as him, and engage in worship as he did. So guide me to a deed by which I may attain the like of his deed.” He said: “You would have to pray continuously without sitting, fast continuously without breaking your fast, and remember Allah without flagging.” She said: “And can I bear that, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Even if you could bear that—by the One in whose hand is my soul—you would not attain a tenth of his deed.”"],[2388,"A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, grant me permission to travel about as a wandering ascetic.” He said: “The wandering asceticism of my community is striving in the way of Allah.”"],[2389,"“A return from a military expedition is like another expedition.”"],[2390,"“Three are each guaranteed by Allah: a man who goes out as a warrior in the way of Allah—he is guaranteed by Allah until He takes his soul and admits him to Paradise, or returns him with whatever reward or booty he has attained; a man who goes to the mosque—he is guaranteed by Allah until He takes his soul and admits him to Paradise, or returns him with whatever reward or booty he has attained; and a man who enters his house with peace—he is guaranteed by Allah.”"],[2391,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a military detachment to set out. They said: “O Messenger of Allah, shall we go out tonight or wait until morning?” He said: “Would you not love to spend the night in a garden of the gardens of Paradise?” The word “kharīf” means orchard."],[2392,"A man came to the prayer while the Prophet ﷺ was leading us in prayer. When he reached the row he said: “O Allah, grant me the best of what You grant Your righteous servants.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: “Who spoke just now?” The man said: “I did, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Then your horse will be hamstrung and you will be martyred in the way of Allah.”"],[2393,"“The martyrs are beside a shining river at the gate of Paradise, in a green dome. Their provision comes to them morning and evening.”"],[2394,"“You must strive in the way of Allah, for it is a gate of the gates of Paradise by which Allah removes anxiety and grief.” Another added to it: “And strive in the way of Allah against the near and the far, and establish the limits of Allah upon the near and the far, and let no blame of any blamer deter you in the cause of Allah.”"],[2395,"A man from the people of Paradise will be brought, and Allah will say to him: “O son of Adam, how have you found your dwelling?” He will say: “O Lord, the best dwelling.” Then Allah will say: “Ask and wish.” He will say: “What should I ask and wish for? I ask You to return me to the world so that I may be killed in Your way ten times”—because of the excellence of martyrdom he had seen. He said: And a man from the people of the Fire will be brought, and Allah will say: “O son of Adam, how have you found your dwelling?” He will say: “O Lord, the worst dwelling.” Then the Lord, glorified and exalted be He, will say: “Would you ransom yourself from it with the earth’s fill of gold?” He will say: “Yes.” Then Allah will say: “You have lied. I asked you for less than that, and you did not do it.”"],[2396,"While the Prophet ﷺ was at al-Rawḥāʾ, a bedouin from Sarif descended upon them and said: “Who are the people, and where are you heading?” They said: “To Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “Why do I see you with shabby appearance and little weaponry?” They said: “We await one of the two best outcomes: either we are killed and attain Paradise, or we prevail and Allah combines for us victory and Paradise.” He said: “Where is your Prophet?” They said: “Here he is.” So he said to him: “O Prophet of Allah, I have some business; I will take care of my business and then catch up.” He said: “Go to your family and take care of your business.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out heading for Badr, and the man went to his family until he finished his errand, then he caught up with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Badr while he was arranging the people for battle in their ranks. He entered the ranks with them, and the people fought, and he was among those whom Allah granted martyrdom. After Allah defeated the polytheists and gave victory to the believers, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked among the martyrs with ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb at his side and said: “Here, O ʿUmar, you love to narrate accounts. Indeed the martyrs have masters, nobles, and kings, and this one, O ʿUmar, is among them.”"],[2397,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “When the companions of Uḥud are mentioned—by Allah, I wish I had been left with my companions at the mountain fortress.”"],[2398,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of Tabuk. He said to me, 'If you wish, I will tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump.' He said: I said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'As for the head of the matter, it is Islam; as for its pillar, it is prayer; and as for the peak of its hump, it is jihad.'"],[2399,"On the day of Uhud he said, 'Will you not come so that we may supplicate Allah?' So they went off to a corner. Sa'd supplicated and said, 'O Lord, when we meet the enemy tomorrow, grant me a man of fierce might and fierce anger, so that I may fight him for Your sake and he fights me. Then grant me victory over him until I kill him and take his spoils.' Then Abdullah b. Jahsh stood up and said, 'O Allah, grant me tomorrow a man of fierce anger and fierce might; I fight him for Your sake and he fights me. Then he seizes me and cuts off my nose and ear. Then when I meet You tomorrow, You will say, \"O Abdullah, for what were your nose and ear cut off?\" and I will say, \"For You and Your Messenger,\" and You will say, \"You have spoken truth.\"' Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas said, 'O my son, the supplication of Abdullah b. Jahsh was better than my supplication. I saw him at the end of the day, and his ear and nose were hung on a thread.'"],[2400,"Whoever fights in the path of Allah, a Muslim man, for the time between two milkings of a she-camel, Paradise becomes incumbent for him. And whoever asks Allah for death from his own self, sincerely, then dies or is killed, he has the reward of a martyr."],[2401,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever asks Allah for death in the path of Allah sincerely, then dies, Allah gives him the reward of a martyr.' [On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim]"],[2402,"Whoever asks Allah for martyrdom with sincerity, Allah will cause him to reach the stations of the martyrs, even if he dies on his bed."],[2403,"O people, do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being. But when you meet them, be patient, and know that Paradise is under the shade of the swords."],[2404,"There is no raiding party that raids in the path of Allah and obtains spoils except that they hasten two-thirds of their reward from the Hereafter, and one-third remains for them. But if they do not obtain spoils, their reward is completed for them."],[2405,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Indeed prayer, fasting, and remembrance are multiplied over spending in the path of Allah by seven hundred times.'"],[2406,"Whoever sets out in the path of Allah and dies or is killed, he is a martyr; or his horse or camel throws him and breaks his neck, or a venomous creature bites him, or he dies on his bed by any death Allah wills, then he is a martyr, and indeed for him is Paradise."],[2407,"Every deceased person's deeds are sealed, except for the one stationed in the path of Allah (murabit). Indeed his deeds grow for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he is secured from the trial of the grave."],[2408,"Whoever dies and has not fought and has not spoken to himself about fighting, dies upon a branch of hypocrisy."],[2409,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever dies without taking part in Jihad and does not have the intention to participate, dies a death of hypocrisy.\""],[2410,"Whoever meets Allah without any trace of jihad meets Him with a defect in him."],[2411,"I heard Ibn al-Khaṣāṣiyah say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him upon Islam, and he stipulated upon me: “You testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and you perform the five prayers, fast Ramadan, give the zakah, perform the Hajj to the House, and wage jihad in the path of Allah.” He said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, as for two of them, I cannot endure them. As for the zakah, I have no property except ten camels; they are my family's mounts and their carriers. As for jihad, they claim that whoever turns back has incurred wrath from Allah, so I fear if fighting is present with me, I would hate death and my soul would lose courage.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ withdrew his hand, then moved it, then said: “No charity and no jihad, so with what will you enter Paradise?” He said: Then I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I pledge allegiance to you,” so he accepted my pledge upon all of them."],[2412,"“Whoever keeps guard for a day and a night in the path of Allah, he will have the reward of fasting a month and standing in prayer during it. Whoever dies as a guard, the like of that reward will continue for him, provision will be granted to him, and he will be safe from the trial (of the grave).”"],[2413,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, similar to it. Sahih."],[2414,"“Shall I tell you of a night better than the Night of Decree? A guard who keeps watch in a land of fear, perhaps he may not return to his family.”"],[2415,"Thawr bin Yazid was praised for narrating a hadith with a chain of narration that is connected but has a break, on the condition of Al-Bukhari."],[2416,"“Guarding for one night in the path of Allah is better than a thousand nights in which its night is spent in prayer and its day is spent in fasting.”"],[2417,"“Strive against the polytheists with your wealth, your lives, and your tongues.”"],[2418,"I was beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when tranquility descended upon him, and the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell upon my thigh. I have not found the weight of anything heavier than the thigh of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon my thigh. Then it was relieved from him and he said: “Write.” So I wrote on a shoulder blade: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home] – other than those who are disabled – and those who strive in the cause of Allah} [al-Nisa' 95] to the end of the verse. Then Ibn Umm Maktūm, who was a blind man, stood up when he heard the virtue of the strivers and said: “O Messenger of Allah, what about those believers who are unable to wage jihad?” When he finished his words, tranquility descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ again and his thigh fell upon my thigh, and I felt the same heaviness as the first time. Then it was relieved from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: “Recite, O Zayd.” So I recited: {Not equal are those believers who sit [at home]} [al-Nisa' 95]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: {other than those who are disabled} [al-Nisa' 95], the whole verse. Zayd said: Allah sent it down alone, and I appended it. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is as if I am looking at its attachment at a crack in the shoulder blade."],[2419,"“Let one man go out from every two men.” Then he said to the one remaining: “Whichever of you stays behind and looks after the family and property of the one who goes out with good, he will have the like of half the reward of the one who goes out.”"],[2420,"“Three eyes will not be touched by the Fire: an eye blinded in the path of Allah, an eye that kept watch in the path of Allah, and an eye that wept from fear of Allah.”"],[2421,"The Fire is forbidden to two eyes: an eye that wept from fear of Allah, and an eye that spent the night guarding Islam and its people from the people of disbelief."],[2422,"From Abu 'Ali al-Janbi, from Abu Rayhana, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition, and we reached a high place. Severe cold afflicted us, until one of us would dig a pit, then enter it and cover himself with his shield. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that from the people, he said: “Is there not a man who will guard us tonight? I will supplicate Allah for him with a supplication by which he will attain excellence.” A man from the Ansar stood up and said: “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” So he supplicated for him. Abu Rayhana said: Then I said: “I will,” and he supplicated for me with a supplication lesser than what he did for the Ansari. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Fire is forbidden to an eye that shed tears from fear of Allah. The Fire is forbidden to an eye that stayed awake in the path of Allah.” He said: And I forgot the third. Abu Shurayh said: I later heard that he said: “The Fire is forbidden to an eye that lowered its gaze from what Allah has forbidden, or an eye blinded in the path of Allah.”"],[2423,"He heard Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah mention that they traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn and prolonged the journey until it was evening. The prayer time came and a horseman came and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I went ahead of you until I ascended such-and-such a mountain, and there I saw Hawazin with their entire gathering, their women, their camels, and their sheep, gathered at Hunayn.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said: “That is the spoils of the Muslims tomorrow, if Allah wills.” Then he said: “Who will guard us tonight?” Anas b. Marthad al-Ghanawi said: “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Mount.” So he mounted a horse of his and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Face this mountain pass until you are at its top, and do not flee tonight from your position.” When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to his prayer place and prayed two rak'ahs, then said: “Have you sensed your horseman?” A man said: “We have not sensed him.” Then he called the prayer, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept looking toward the mountain pass until he finished his prayer, then said: “Rejoice, for your horseman has come.” He said: We began looking at the shadows of the trees in the mountain pass, and there he came until he stood before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greeted him. He said: “I went until I was at the top of this mountain pass where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me. When morning came, I looked down upon the two passes and saw no one.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Did you dismount tonight?” He said: “No, except to pray or to relieve myself.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You have made it obligatory, so there is no harm if you do not perform any deed after it.” This chain of transmission from its beginning to its end is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, except that they did not include the narrations of Sahl b. al-Hanzaliyyah because of the scarcity of narrations from the Successors from him, and he is among the senior Companions, as I mentioned earlier. On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim, but they did not transmit from Sahl, and he is a senior Companion."],[2424,"We set out on an expedition from Madinah, intending Constantinople, and over the army was ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Khālid b. al-Walīd. The Byzantines had backed themselves against the wall of the city. A man charged against the enemy. The people said, \"Stop, stop! There is no god but Allah! He is throwing himself into destruction with his own hands.\" Abū Ayyūb said, \"This verse was revealed concerning us, the Helpers. When Allah granted victory to His Prophet and made Islam prevail, we said, 'Let us remain with our wealth and put it in order.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: 'And spend in the way of Allah, and do not throw yourselves into destruction with your own hands' (al-Baqarah 195). Throwing ourselves into destruction means remaining with our wealth and putting it in order while abandoning jihad.\""],[2425,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Raiding is of two kinds. As for one who seeks the Face of Allah, obeys the leader, gives generously, is easygoing with his companion, and avoids corruption, then his sleep and his wakefulness are entirely reward. As for one who raids for pride, showing off, and reputation, disobeys the leader, and spreads corruption in the land, he will not return even with his expenses covered.\""],[2426,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"O Messenger of Allah, a man wants to wage jihad in the way of Allah, but he also seeks some worldly gain.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"He has no reward.\" The man asked him a second and third time, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"He has no reward.\""],[2427,"ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about jihad and raiding.\" The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, if you fight patiently, seeking reward, Allah will resurrect you patient, seeking reward. But if you fight for show and to boast, Allah will resurrect you showing off and boasting. O ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr, in whatever state you fight or are killed, Allah will resurrect you in that state.\""],[2428,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on the guard of the guard.\""],[2429,"Abū Hurayrah ؓ reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"No servant spends a pair of every kind of his wealth in the way of Allah except that the keepers of Paradise meet him, each calling him to what they have.\" I (the narrator) asked: \"How is that?\" He said: \"If it is men, then two men; if camels, then two camels; if cattle, then two cows.\""],[2430,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever spends anything in the way of Allah, it will be recorded for him as seven hundred times its value.\""],[2431,"From Abū Yaḥyā Khuraym b. Fātik ؓ."],[2432,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever recites a thousand verses in the way of Allah, Allah will record him among the prophets, the truthful, the martyrs, and the righteous.\""],[2433,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, when your brothers were struck down at Uḥud: \"Allah placed their souls inside green birds that come to the rivers of Paradise, eat from its fruits, and shelter in golden lamps hanging in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food, drink, and resting place, they said, 'Who will inform our brothers that we are alive in Paradise, being provided for, so that they will not lose interest in jihad or shrink from war?' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said, 'I will inform them on your behalf,' and Allah revealed: 'Do not consider those who were killed in the way of Allah as dead' (Āl ʿImrān 169).\""],[2434,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever leaves his house as a fighter in the way of Allah\" — then he closed his three fingers — \"and where are the fighters in the way of Allah? If he falls from his mount and dies, his reward is with Allah. If an animal bites him and he dies, his reward is with Allah. And whoever dies a natural death\" — he said, \"This is a word I have not heard from any Arab before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ\" — meaning by 'natural death' dying in one's bed, \"then his reward is with Allah. And whoever is killed outright, he has indeed deserved Paradise.\""],[2435,"I used to hear a hadith from Abu Dharr and I wished to meet him. So I met him and said, “O Abu Dharr, I used to hear a hadith from you and I wished to meet you.” He said, “May your father be devoted to Allah, for you have met me.” He said, “I said, ‘Tell me: I have heard that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told you…’” He said, “Indeed Allah loves three and hates three.” He said, “I do not think that I would lie about my close friend (the Prophet).” He said, “I said, ‘Who are those whom Allah loves?’ He said, ‘A man who goes on a military expedition in the path of Allah, patiently, seeking reward, striving, then meets the enemy and fights until he is killed. You find this in the Book of Allah, the revealed.’ Then he recited this verse: {Indeed, Allah loves those who fight in His cause in a row as though they are a solid structure} [al-Saff: 4]. I said, ‘And who else?’ He said, ‘A man who has a bad neighbor who harms him, and he bears his harm patiently until Allah suffices him, either by life or by death.’ I said, ‘And who else?’ He said, ‘A man who travels with a group, and they travel by night until, when it is the last part of the night, drowsiness and sleepiness overcome them, so they lay down their heads. Then he gets up, purifies himself, out of fear of Allah and desire for what is with Him.’ I said, ‘And who are the three whom Allah hates?’ He said, ‘The arrogant boaster. You find this in the Book of Allah, the revealed: {Indeed, Allah does not love everyone who is arrogant and boastful} [Luqman: 18]. I said, ‘And who else?’ He said, ‘The miser who reminds of his favors.’ He said, ‘And who else?’ He said, ‘The merchant or seller who swears much.’”"],[2436,"“Whoever shades the head of a warrior, Allah will shade him on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever equips a warrior until he is fully equipped, he will have a reward like his.”"],[2437,"“Whoever helps a mujahid in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a slave in his contract of emancipation, Allah will shade him in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade.”"],[2438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You will have for it on the Day of Resurrection seven hundred, all of them bridled.”"],[2439,"“Whoever strives in the path of Allah is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever enters upon a leader to honor him is guaranteed by Allah. Whoever sits in his house and does not backbite anyone with evil is guaranteed by Allah.”"],[2440,"He wanted to go on a military expedition, so he said, “O assembly of the Muhajirun and the Ansar, among your brothers are people who have neither wealth nor clan. Let each of you attach to himself two or three men. None of us has a mount to carry him except a turn like the turn of one of them.” He said, “So I attached to myself two or three, and I had only a turn like one of them.”"],[2441,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, “Which charity is best?” He said, “The service of a slave, or the shade of a tent, or a stallion camel in the path of Allah.”"],[2442,"On the day of Badr, we took turns three of us on one camel. Ali and Abu Lubabah were the two companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When it was the turn of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they said to him, “Ride, and let us walk.” He said, “I am not more in need of the reward than you two, nor are you two stronger in walking than me.”"],[2443,"“Goodness is tied to the forelocks of horses, and their owners are aided upon them, and the one who spends on them is like one who extends his hand in charity.”"],[2444,"My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda’ in Damascus. There was in Damascus a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah al-Ansari. He passed by us one day and greeted. Abu al-Darda’ said to him, “A word that benefits us and does not harm you.” He said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: ‘The one who spends on horses in the path of Allah is like one who extends his hands in charity and does not withdraw them.’” We have cited it as a witness."],[2445,"“Whoever withholds a horse in the path of Allah, out of faith in Allah and belief in Allah’s promise, its satiety, its drinking, its dung, and its urine will be good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2446,"There is no Arabian horse except that it is permitted every day to make two supplications. It says, “O Allah, as You have granted me to whomever You have granted me, make me among the most beloved of his wealth and his family to him.”"],[2447,"The best of horses is the black one with a white forehead, white stockings, and a white upper lip, with the right foreleg white. If it is not black, then a dark bay with these markings."],[2448,"When you intend to raid, buy a black horse with a white forehead, white stockings, and a white right foreleg, for you will gain booty and remain safe."],[2449,"Fitan (trials) will overshadow you like pieces of a dark night. The safest of people from them will be a man upon a mountain peak eating from the milk of his sheep, or a man behind the mountain passes holding the rein of his horse, eating from the spoils of his sword."],[2450,"From Abu Ali al-Janbi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as Messenger, Paradise becomes obligatory for him.\" Abu Sa'id said: \"I praised Allah, said takbir, and rejoiced at it.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And another thing by which Allah raises its people in Paradise one hundred degrees, the distance between each two degrees being like that between the heaven and the earth, or farther than between the heaven and the earth.\" He said: \"I asked, 'What is that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Jihad in the path of Allah, jihad in the path of Allah.'\""],[2451,"O Allah, make the destruction of my ummah by killing in Your path, by stabbing and by the plague."],[2452,"A black man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a black man with a foul odor and an ugly face, and I have no wealth. If I fight these people [in the path of Allah] until I am killed, where will I be?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"In Paradise.\" So he fought until he was killed.Then the Prophet ﷺ came to him and said, \"Allah has brightened your face, sweetened your fragrance, and increased your wealth.\" And he said to him or to someone else, \"I have seen his wife from the beautiful black-eyed maidens stripping off her garment of silk to cover him."],[2453,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a people shooting arrows and said: \"Shoot, O sons of Ishmael, for your father was an archer.\""],[2454,"The Prophet ﷺ went out while a group from Aslam were shooting arrows. He said: \"Shoot, O sons of Ishmael, for your father was an archer. Shoot, and I am with the son of al-Adra'.\" The people held back their bows and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, whoever you are with wins.\" He said: \"Shoot, and I am with all of you.\" [Reported] according to the condition of Muslim."],[2455,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by some people shooting arrows and said: \"This is good. O Allah,\" twice or thrice. \"Shoot, and I am with the son of al-Adra'.\" The people stopped their hands and said: \"By Allah, we will not shoot with him while you are with him, O Messenger of Allah; then he will outshoot us.\" He said: \"Shoot, and I am with all of you.\" They said: \"They shot for most of that day, then dispersed evenly; none of them outshot the others.\""],[2456,"I was an archer, shooting against 'Uqbah b. 'Amir. One day he passed by me and said: 'O Khalid, come out with us to shoot.' I was slow to respond, so he said: 'O Khalid, come, let me tell you what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told me, and I will say to you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed Allah admits three persons into Paradise by a single arrow: its maker, who sought good in making it; its shooter; and the one who hands it to the shooter. Shoot and ride, but shooting is dearer to me than riding. There is no legitimate amusement except three: a man training his horse, playing with his wife, and shooting with his bow among his people. And whoever learns archery then abandons it, it is a blessing he has disbelieved.\"'"],[2457,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Every amusement of the worldly life is false except three: your shooting with your bow, your training your horse, and your playing with your family, for they are from the truth.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Shoot and ride, but shooting is dearer to me. Indeed Allah admits three persons into Paradise by a single arrow: its maker, who seeks good in it; the one who hands it; and the archer who shoots it.\" [Reported] according to the condition of Muslim."],[2458,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, he will have the reward of freeing a slave.' He said: 'That day I reached sixteen arrows.'"],[2459,"Whoever shoots an arrow at the enemy, and his arrow reaches, whether it misses or hits, it is equivalent to freeing a slave."],[2460,"From his father they said: When we met the enemy on the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us, “When they close in on you, shoot arrows and conserve your arrows.”"],[2461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the Muslims on the day of Uhud, \"Fight bravely, Sa'd, throw, O Sa'd, for Allah has thrown for you. May my father and mother be sacrificed for you.\""],[2462,"“Lo! Has the Messenger of Allah come? Indeed I protected my companions with the shafts of these arrows of mine.” A hadith with a sound chain, though they did not include it. Sahih."],[2463,"Thana Abu al-Muwajjih, anba’a Abdan, anba’a Abdullah, anba’a al-Mas‘udi; and ‘Ali b. Hamshadh al-‘Adl narrated to me, anba’a al-Harith b. Abi Usama, thana Yazid b. Harun, anba’a al-Mas‘udi; and Abu Sa‘id ‘Amr b. Muhammad b. Mansur al-‘Adl narrated to us, thana ‘Umar b. Hafs al-Sadusi, thana ‘Asim b. ‘Ali, thana ‘Abd al-Rahman b. ‘Ubayd Allah al-Mas‘udi, from Abu Bakr b. Hafs, from ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Amir b. Rabi‘a, from his father, and he was a participant in Badr. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would send us out on expeditions when we had no provisions except leaves of dates. We would divide them up handful by handful until it came to a single date, single date. I said, “Father, what could a single date avail you?” He said, “Do not say that, my son, for we had only just lost them when we came to need them.”"],[2464,"‘Abd Allah: Wait until I bid you farewell as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to bid us farewell: “I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds.”"],[2465,"“I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds.”"],[2466,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “Messenger of Allah, I intend to travel, so provide for me.” He said, “May Allah provide you with piety.” He said, “Give me more.” He said, “And forgive your sin.” He said, “Give me more, may my father and mother be your ransom.” He said, “And ease for you good wherever you are.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2467,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bade farewell to an army, he would say: “I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the final outcomes of your deeds.”"],[2468,"“That I should escort a fighter in the path of Allah and help him onto his mount in the morning or evening is dearer to me than the world and all that is in it.”"],[2469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked with them to Baqi‘ al-Gharqad when he dispatched them, then said, “Depart in the name of Allah. O Allah, help them.” Al-Bukhari cited Thawr b. Yazid and ‘Ikrima as authorities, and Muslim cited Muhammad b. Ishaq. “And"],[2470,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ intending to travel and said, “Messenger of Allah, advise me.” He said, “I advise you to fear Allah and to say Allahu akbar upon every rise.” When he had gone, he said, “O Allah, fold up the earth for him and make the journey easy for him.”"],[2471,"He was riding behind ‘Ali. When he placed his foot in the stirrup, he said, “In the name of Allah.” When he was settled on the back of the mount, he said, “Praise be to Allah” three times and “Allahu akbar” three times, and {Glory be to the One Who subjected this to us, for we could never have subdued it} [al-Zukhruf 13] to the end of the verse. Then he said, “There is no god but You. Glory be to You. Indeed I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins but You.” Then he inclined to one side and laughed. I said, “Commander of the Faithful, what makes you laugh?” He said, “I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did exactly as I did, so I asked him as you asked me, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘Allah marvels at the servant when he says, “There is no god but You. Indeed I have wronged myself, so forgive me my sins, for none forgives sins but You.” He says, “My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives and punishes.”’”"],[2472,"I saw ‘Ali being brought a mount."],[2473,"I kept holding the camel's nose-rein, staying with it until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was settled upon it, then he said: \"O Allah, You are the Companion in the journey and the Deputy in the family. O Allah, accompany us with good companionship and return us with a safeguard. O Allah, grant me the closure of the earth, and make the journey easy for us. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the hardships of travel and the gloom of return.\" Abu Zur'ah said: Abu Hurayrah was an Arab man; if he wanted to say 'hardships of travel,' he would have said: O Allah, return us with a safeguard. O Allah, roll up the earth for us and make us traverse it."],[2474,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ once seated me behind him, and he confided to me a statement that I will not tell any of the people. He said: The most beloved thing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to screen himself with for his need was a target or a wall of palm trees. So he entered a garden belonging to a man of the Ansar, and there was a camel. When it saw the Prophet ﷺ, it yearned toward him and its eyes shed tears. The Prophet ﷺ came to it and wiped its cheek, and it became calm. He said: 'Who is the owner of this camel? To whom does this camel belong?' A young man from the Ansar came and said: 'It is mine, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast that Allah has put in your possession? It complained to me that you starve it and overwork it.'"],[2475,"Ride these mounts while they are sound, and leave them sound; and do not take them as chairs."],[2476,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on a military expedition or traveled and night overtook him, he said: 'O earth, my Lord and your Lord is Allah. I seek refuge in Allah from your evil and the evil of what is in you and the evil of what He created in you and from the evil of what crawls upon you. I seek refuge in Allah from the evil of every lion, black serpent, snake, scorpion, and from the evil of the dweller of the land, and from the evil of a parent and what he begot.'"],[2477,"Suhayb, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, related to him that the Prophet ﷺ never saw a town he intended to enter without saying when he saw it: 'O Allah, Lord of the seven heavens and what they shade, Lord of the seven earths and what they carry, Lord of the devils and what they mislead, Lord of the winds and what they scatter, we ask You for the good of this town and the good of its people, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of its people and the evil of what is in it.'"],[2478,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The best companions are four, and the best raiding parties are four hundred, and the best armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand will never be defeated due to small numbers.' This is a sound chain according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it because of a disagreement among the transmitters from al-Zuhri."],[2479,"The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the best of them to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of Allah is the best of them to his neighbor."],[2480,"Some people complained to the Prophet ﷺ about walking, so he called them and said: 'You should use the nasalan gait.' So we went at a quick pace, and we found it lighter for us."],[2481,"The Prophet ﷺ would not alight at a place without bidding it farewell with two rak'ahs."],[2482,"If people knew what I know about being alone, no rider would ever travel alone by night."],[2483,"A man set out from Khaybar, and two men followed him, and another man came after them saying: 'Return!' until he caught up with them and sent them back. Then he said: 'These two are devils. Convey peace to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and inform him that we are in the midst of collecting our alms; if they were suitable for him, we would have sent them to him.' When he arrived to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, he then forbade isolation."],[2484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Whom did you accompany?' He said: 'I accompanied no one.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A single rider is a devil, two riders are two devils, and three are a group.'"],[2485,"One is a devil, two are two devils, and three are a riding party."],[2486,"He forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin, and riding a jalāla (an animal that eats dung), and a mujaththama (an animal tied up and used as a target)."],[2487,"On the day of Khaybar he forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, and the jalāla (animal that eats dung), and riding it and eating its flesh."],[2488,"When Allah ﷻ sent down {And do not approach the property of the orphan except in the way that is best} [al-An'ām 152] and {Indeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly} [al-Nisā' 10] up to His saying {a blazing fire} [al-Nisā' 10], he said: Those who had an orphan with them went and separated his food from their food and his drink from their drink, setting aside a portion of his food so it was kept for him until he ate it or it spoiled and they threw it away. That became hard on them, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah ﷻ sent down {They ask you about orphans. Say: Setting things right for them is best. And if you mix with them, they are your brothers} [al-Baqarah 220] up to {Mighty, Wise} [al-Baqarah 220]. So they mixed their food with their food and their drink with their drink."],[2489,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, we eat but we are not satisfied. He said: \"Perhaps you eat separately from your food. Gather together over it and mention the name of Allah, and you will be blessed.\""],[2490,"A man emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Yemen and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have emigrated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"You have abandoned shirk (polytheism), but it is jihād (struggle). Do you have anyone in Yemen?\" He said: My parents. He said: \"Did they give you permission?\" He said: No. He said: \"Return and ask their permission. If they permit you, then fight; otherwise, be dutiful to them.\""],[2491,"Jāhimah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: I intended to go on a military expedition, so I came to seek your advice. He said: \"Do you have a mother?\" He said: Yes. He said: \"Go and keep her company, for Paradise is at her feet.\""],[2492,"Abū Ṭalḥah recited the Qur'an: {Go forth, light and heavy} [al-Tawbah 41], and said: I think that both old men and young men should be called out. They said: O our father, you have fought with the Prophet ﷺ until he died, and with Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, so we will fight on your behalf. He refused and rode the sea until he died. They did not find an island to bury him on until after seven days. He said: And he did not change."],[2493,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {If you do not go forth} [al-Tawbah 39], He will punish you with a painful punishment. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called upon a tribe of the Arab tribes to go forth, but they were reluctant, so rain was withheld from them, and that was their punishment.\""],[2494,"His banner on the day he entered Makkah was white."],[2495,"The banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was white and his standard was black. Yazīd is weak."],[2496,"He narrated to him: While I was sitting in the Ḥijr, a man came to me and asked me about {the charging steeds, panting} [al-ʿĀdiyāt 1]. I said to him: \"The horses when they raid in the path of Allah, then they return to the night, and they prepare their food and kindle their fire.\" He turned away from me and went to ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib, who was under the drinking place of Zamzam, and asked him about the charging steeds. He said: Did you ask anyone about it before me? He said: Yes, I asked Ibn ʿAbbās about it. He said: They are the horses when they raid in the path of Allah. He said: Go and call him for me. When he stood at his head, he said: You give fatwā to the people without knowledge. By Allah, the first military expedition in Islam was Badr, and we had only two horses with us: a horse belonging to al-Zubayr and a horse belonging to al-Miqdād b. al-Aswad. So how can it be the charging steeds, panting? {The charging steeds, panting} [al-ʿĀdiyāt 1] are only from ʿArafah to al-Muzdalifah and from al-Muzdalifah to Minā, {then they raise dust thereby} [al-ʿĀdiyāt 4] when they trample it with their feet and hooves. Ibn ʿAbbās said: So I withdrew from my statement and returned to what ʿAlī said."],[2497,"I was walking alongside ‘Ammār on the Day of the Camel, and with him was a horn attached to his saddle into which he urinated when he needed to urinate. When the fighting was about to begin, he said, “O Mukhāriq, go to the banner of your people.” I said, “I am not going to fight while I am today in this condition.” He said, “Rather, O Mukhāriq, go to the banner of your people, for I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prefer that a man fight under the banner of his people.”"],[2498,"“Seek me among the weak, for you are only provided for and given victory because of your weak.”"],[2499,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the battle cry of the Emigrants on the Day of Badr ‘Abd al-Raḥmān, the Aws “Banī ‘Abd Allāh,” and the Khazraj “Banī ‘Ubayd Allāh.”"],[2500,"I heard Ibn ‘Abbās say: Four hundred households—or four hundred men—from Azd Shanū’ah came as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “Welcome to the Azd—the most handsome of people in face, the sweetest in mouth, the bravest in meeting, and the most trustworthy in trust. Your battle cry is ‘O Mabrūr!’”"],[2501,"If you are attacked at night, let your battle cry be “Ḥā Mīm, they will not be helped.”"],[2502,"And he said while he feared that Abū Sufyān would attack him at night: “If you are attacked at night and I call you, then ‘Ḥā Mīm, they will not be helped.’”"],[2503,"You will meet your enemy tomorrow, so let your battle cry be “Ḥā Mīm, they will not be helped.”"],[2504,"From the Prophet ﷺ: “You will meet tomorrow, so let your battle cry be ‘Ḥā Mīm, they will not be helped.’”"],[2505,"I went on a military expedition with Abū Bakr during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and our battle cry—meaning that of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—was “Die! Die!” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. It has a sound witness according to the condition of Muslim. According to the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[2506,"The battle cry of the Prophet ﷺ was “Die! Die!” According to the condition of Muslim."],[2507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard a man calling out in his battle cry, “O Ḥarām! O Ḥarām!” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Ḥalāl! O Ḥalāl!” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs as a mursal report. The man whom Muḥammad b. Kathīr did not name, from al-Thawrī, is ‘Abd Allāh b. Mughaffal al-Muzanī. According to the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[2508,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab came out to a gathering while he was in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they were mentioning an expedition of the expeditions that had perished in the cause of Allah. One speaker among them said, 'They are the workers of Allah; they perished in His cause, and their reward has become incumbent upon Him.' Another speaker said, 'Allah knows best about them; theirs is what they reckoned.' When they saw 'Umar approaching, leaning on his staff, they fell silent. 'Umar approached until he greeted them, then said, 'What were you discussing?' They said, 'We were mentioning this expedition that perished in the cause of Allah. One of us says, \"They are the workers of Allah; they perished in His cause, and their reward has become incumbent upon Him.\" Another says, \"Allah knows best about them; theirs is what they reckoned.\"' 'Umar said, 'Allah knows best. Among people are those who fight while their only concern is fighting, so they cannot do anything but that. Among people are those who fight for show and reputation. Among people are those who fight seeking the face of Allah. Those are the martyrs. Every one of them will be resurrected upon that which he died upon. By Allah, no soul knows what will be done with it. This man is not the one who has made clear to us that he has been forgiven his past and future sins ﷺ.'"],[2509,"And another [saying] you say about one who is killed in your campaigns or dies: 'So-and-so was killed and he is a martyr,' or 'So-and-so died a martyr,' though perhaps he had loaded the hindquarters of his beast—or he said his mount—with gold or silver seeking trade. So do not say that, but say as the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Whoever is killed in the cause of Allah or dies, he is in Paradise.'"],[2510,"\"Whoever goes on an expedition intending in his expedition nothing but a rope fetter, his is what he intended.\""],[2511,"The Prophet ﷺ used to send me in his expeditions. One day he sent me, and there was a man who would ride. I said to him, 'Saddle up.' He said, 'I will not go out with you.' I said, 'Why?' He said, 'Until you give me three dinars.' I said, 'Now, after I have bid farewell to the Prophet ﷺ? I will not return to him. Saddle up, and you have three dinars.' When I returned from my expedition, I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Give them to him, for it is his share of his expedition.'"],[2512,"A brother of the people of Syria said to him, 'O shaykh, tell us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The first of people to be judged on the Day of Resurrection is a man who was martyred. He will be brought, and He will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them.\" He will say, \"What did you do therein?\" He will say, \"I fought for You until I was killed.\" He will say, \"You lie, but you fought so that it would be said, 'He is brave,' and it was said.\" Then he will be ordered, and he will be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire. And a man who learned knowledge and taught it, and recited the Qur'an. He will be brought, and He will make him recognize His blessings upon him, and he will recognize them. He will say, \"What did you do therein?\" He will say, \"I learned knowledge for You and taught it, and I recited the Qur'an for You.\" He will say, \"You lie, but you learned knowledge so that it would be said, 'He is a scholar,' and you recited the Qur'an so that it would be said, 'He is a reciter,' and it was said.\" Then he will be ordered, and he will be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire. And a man to whom Allah gave ample wealth and gave him of all kinds of property. He will be brought, and He will make him recognize His blessings, and he will recognize them. He will say, \"What did you do therein?\" He will say, \"I have not left any way in which You love that wealth be spent without spending in it.\" He will say, \"You lie, but you did it so that it would be said, 'He is generous,' and it was said.\" Then he will be ordered, and he will be dragged on his face until he is thrown into the Fire.'"],[2513,"\"Beware of these testimonies that you say, 'So-and-so was killed a martyr,' for a man fights out of tribal zeal, fights seeking worldly gain, and fights while being bold-hearted. But I will tell you something for which you may testify: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition one day, and it was only a little while before he stood, praised and extolled Allah, then said, 'Your brothers have met the polytheists and cut them off, so none of them remained. They said, \"Our Lord, convey to our people that we are pleased, and our Lord is pleased with us.\" I am their messenger to you: they are pleased, and He is pleased with them.'\""],[2514,"Some people went out and were killed, and they said, 'So-and-so was martyred.' 'Abdullah said, 'A man may fight for worldly gain and fight to be known, and a man may die on his bed while he is a martyr.' Then he recited: {And those who believe in Allah and His messengers—it is they who are the truthful and the martyrs in the sight of their Lord} [al-Hadid 19]."],[2515,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I stand in the station desiring the face of Allah and desiring that my position be seen.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not reply to him at all until there descended: {So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him work righteous deeds and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord} [al-Kahf 110]."],[2516,"The first of people to enter the Fire on the Day of Resurrection are three persons. A man—or he said one of them—will be brought, and he will say, 'Lord, You taught me the Book, and I recited it through the hours of night and day hoping for Your reward.' It will be said, 'You lie; you only prayed so that it would be said, \"A reciter, a devotee,\" and it was said. Take him to the Fire.' Then another will be brought, and he will say, 'Lord, You provided me wealth, and I maintained ties of kinship with it, gave charity from it to the poor, and helped the wayfarer, hoping for Your reward and Your Paradise.' It will be said, 'You lie; you only gave charity and maintained ties so that it would be said, \"You are generous and magnanimous,\" and it was said. Take him to the Fire.' Then the third will be brought, and he will say, 'Lord, I went out in Your cause and fought for You until I was killed, advancing, not retreating, hoping for Your reward and Your Paradise.' It will be said, 'You lie; you only fought so that it would be said, \"You are brave and courageous,\" and it was said. Take him to the Fire.'"],[2517,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me about jihad and military expeditions.' He said, \"O 'Abdullah b. 'Amr, if you fight patiently, seeking reward, Allah will resurrect you patient, seeking reward. If you fight for show and to boast, Allah will resurrect you for show and to boast. O 'Abdullah b. 'Amr, in whatever state you fight or are killed, Allah will resurrect you in that state.\""],[2518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave permission to go on an expedition, and I was an old man with no servant. I sought a hired man to suffice me, and I would give him his share. I found a man. When departure drew near, he came to me and said, 'I do not know what the shares are, nor how much my share will amount to. Specify something for me, whether the share comes or not.' I specified for him three dinars. When the spoils arrived, I wanted to give him his share, but I remembered the dinars. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned his matter to him. He said, 'I find for him in this expedition of his in this world nothing but his dinars that he specified.'"],[2519,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Our Lord ﷻ marvels at a man who went out on an expedition in the cause of Allah, and his companions fled, but he knew what was upon him and returned until his blood was shed. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says to His angels, 'Look at My servant; he returned out of desire for what is with Me and fear of what is with Me until his blood was shed.'"],[2520,"Three whom Allah loves and three whom Allah hates. As for those whom Allah loves: a man who came to a people and asked them by Allah, not by kinship between them and him, so a man lagged behind at their heels and gave him secretly, no one knowing of his gift except Allah and the one who gave it; and a group who marched through their night until, when sleep became dearer to them than anything of equal weight, they alighted and laid down their heads, and one arose, seeking to draw near to Me and reciting My verses; and a man who was in a raiding party and met the enemy and they were routed, so he advanced with his chest until he was killed or victory was granted to him. And the three whom Allah hates: the adulterous old man, the arrogant poor person, and the oppressive rich person."],[2521,"Amr ibn Uqaysh had given usurious loans in pre-Islamic period; so he disliked to embrace Islam until he took them. He came on the day of Uhud and asked: Where are my cousins? They (the people) replied: At Uhud. He asked: Where is so-and-so? They said: At Uhud. He asked: Where is so-and-so? They said: At Uhud. He then put on his coat of mail and rode his horse; he then proceeded towards them. When the Muslims saw him, they said: Keep away, Amir. He said: I have become a believer. He fought until he was wounded. He was then taken to his family wounded. Sa'd ibn Mu'adh came to his sister: Ask him (whether he fought) out of partisanship, out of anger for them, or out of anger for Allah. He said: Out of anger of Allah and His Apostle. He then died and entered Paradise. He did not offer any prayer for Allah. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2537)"],[2522,"Two are not rejected—or he said rarely are they rejected: the supplication at the call to prayer, or at the time of battle when they are locked in combat with one another."],[2523,"Keep to traveling by night, for the earth is folded up at night."],[2524,"Whoever enters a horse between two horses without being safe from being outrun, it is not gambling; and whoever enters a horse between two horses while being safe from being outrun, it is gambling."],[2525,"From the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[2526,"Ibn Jurayj said: {O you who have believed, obey Allah and obey the Messenger and those in authority among you} [an-Nisa 59]. Abdullah b. Qays b. Adi—the Prophet ﷺ sent him on a raiding party. Ya'la b. Muslim informed me of it, from Sa'id b. Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas."],[2527,"The Prophet ﷺ sent a detachment. I gave a sword to a man from among them. When he came back, he said: Would that you saw us how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rebuked us, saying: When I sent out a man who does not fulfil my command, are you unable to appoint in his place one who will fulfil my command. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2627)"],[2528,"When people alighted at a place, they dispersed into the ravines and valleys. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Your dispersing in these ravines and valleys is only from Satan.' So after that they did not alight at a place except that they drew close to one another, so that it would be said, 'If a garment were spread over them, it would cover them all.'"],[2529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to lag behind the march, and he would urge on the weak, take someone up behind him, and supplicate for them. Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it."],[2530,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered his execution, and he was a spy for Abu Sufyan. He passed by the gathering of the Ansar and said, 'I am a Muslim.' So they took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'He claims that he is a Muslim.' He said, 'Among you are men whom we entrust to their faith; among them is Furat b. Hayyan.'"],[2531,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, disliked shouting while fighting. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2656)"],[2532,"He used to dislike shouting at the time of fighting."],[2533,"When the Prophet ﷺ met the polytheists on the day of Hunayn, he dismounted from his mule and went on foot. Sahih according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. And it is not authentically established that he ﷺ dismounted and fought on foot except from this report, according to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2534,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: if he did not fight at the beginning of the day, he would delay the fighting until the sun declined and the winds blew."],[2535,"Abu Talha was shooting on the day of Uhud in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was behind him. Abu Talha was an archer, and when he shot, the Prophet ﷺ would raise his person to see where his arrow fell. Abu Talha would raise his chest and say, \"Like this, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, let no arrow strike you; my neck is before your neck.\" Abu Talha would offer himself before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am the most sturdy of my people, so command me with whatever you wish.\""],[2536,"Umayyah ibn Khalaf said to me while I was between him and his son, holding their hands: \"O servant of God, who is the man among you marked with an ostrich feather on his chest?\" He said: I said, \"That is Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib.\" He said, \"That is the one who did such deeds against us.\""],[2537,"Ibn Mas'ud said: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and the people turned away from him, but I remained with him among eighty men of the Muhajirun and Ansar. We stood firm for about eighty feet and did not turn our backs. They were the ones upon whom Allah sent down tranquility. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on his mule, moving forward, and his mule swerved, so he leaned from the saddle and his chest was exposed. I said, \"Rise, may Allah raise you.\" He said, \"Hand me a handful of dust.\" I handed it to him, and he threw it in their faces, and their eyes filled with dust. He said, \"Where are the Muhajirun and Ansar?\" I said, \"They are here.\" He said, \"Call them.\" So they came, their swords in their right hands like flames, and the polytheists turned their backs."],[2538,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever says, 'I seek forgiveness from Allah, the One whom there is no deity worthy of worship except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence, and I repent to Him,' three times, his sins will be forgiven even if he was fleeing from the battlefield.\""],[2539,"I came to al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sitting on a chest from the chests of the money-changers, having removed a bone from it, intending to go on a military expedition. I said, \"Allah has excused you.\" He said, \"Recite Surah al-Buhuth (meaning Surah al-Tawbah): Allah ﷻ said, {Go forth, light and heavy} [al-Tawbah 41].\""],[2540,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called a tribe of Arabs to go forth, but they were sluggish, so it was revealed: {If you do not go forth, He will punish you with a painful punishment} [al-Tawbah 39]. He said: Their punishment was that rain was withheld from them."],[2541,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his expeditions and passed by some people of Muzaynah. A slave of a woman among them followed him. When he was on part of the road, he greeted him, and he said, \"So-and-so?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What is your business?\" He said, \"I will fight alongside you.\" He said, \"Has your mistress given you permission?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Return to her and inform her, for your likeness is the likeness of a slave who does not pray. If you die before returning to her, and convey peace to her.\" So he returned to her and told her the news. She said, \"By Allah, did he command you to convey peace to me?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"Return and fight alongside him.\""],[2542,"Every sin of the martyr is forgiven except debt."],[2543,"When the first blood of the martyr is shed, his sins are forgiven for him."],[2544,"Whoever meets the enemy and remains steadfast until he is killed or prevails will not be tried in his grave."],[2545,"I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed Hamzah when the people returned from the fighting. A man said, \"I saw him near those trees, saying: I am the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger. O Allah, I declare myself innocent before You of what these have brought — Abu Sufyan and his companions — and I apologize to You for what these have done by their defeat.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went towards him, and when he saw his side, he wept; and when he saw what had been done to him, he sobbed. Then he said, \"Is there not a shroud?\" A man of the Ansar stood and threw a garment over him, then another stood and threw a garment over him. He said, \"O Jabir, this garment is for your father, and this is for my uncle Hamzah.\" Then Hamzah was brought, and he prayed over him. Then the martyrs were brought and placed beside Hamzah, and he prayed over them, and they were raised, but Hamzah was left until he had prayed over all the martyrs. He said: I returned while I was burdened, for my father had left upon me a debt and dependents. When it was night, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for me and said, \"O Jabir, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has revived your father and spoken to him with words.\" I said, \"And He spoke to him with words?\" He said, \"He said to him: Make a wish. He said: I wish that You return my soul and create my form as it was and return me to Your Prophet so that I may fight in the way of Allah and be killed another time. He said: I have decreed that they shall not return.\" He said: And he ﷺ said, \"The master of the martyrs before Allah on the Day of Resurrection is Hamzah.\""],[2546,"Hamzah was shrouded in a striped cloak. When they stretched it over his head, his feet showed; and when they stretched it over his feet, his head showed. So the Prophet ﷺ commanded them to stretch it over his head and put idhkhir (a fragrant grass) over his feet. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Were it not that Safiyyah would grieve, we would have left Hamzah unburied until he is gathered from the bellies of birds and beasts.\""],[2547,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, then departed to al-Ta'if and besieged them for eight or seven days, then went forth in the morning or evening, then dismounted, then rested. Then he said, \"O people, I am your forerunner, and I enjoin you to treat my family well. Your appointment is at the Pond. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, you will establish prayer and give zakah, or I will send upon you a man from me or like myself who will strike the necks of their fighters and take their offspring captive.\" He said: The people thought he meant Abu Bakr or Umar, but he took Ali by the hand and said, \"This one, this one.\""],[2548,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, he will have the reward of freeing a slave, and whoever reaches (the enemy) with an arrow in the path of Allah, he will have a degree in Paradise.' And I reached (the enemy) with sixteen arrows in one day."],[2549,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Ta'if during the battle of Hunayn. When we reached Ji'ranah, he distributed silver among the people.\""],[2550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Hawazin with twelve thousand (men). On the day of Hunayn, as many people of al-Ta'if were killed as were killed on the day of Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a handful of pebbles and threw them in our faces, and we were defeated."],[2551,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on one of his expeditions. I and another man came to him before we had accepted Islam, and we said, 'We feel ashamed that our people should witness a scene without us.' He said, 'Have you two accepted Islam?' We said, 'No.' He said, 'We do not seek help from the polytheists against the polytheists.' So we accepted Islam and witnessed (the battle) with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I killed a man, and that man struck me a blow. Then I married his daughter, and she used to say, 'May you not lack a man who has fastened this sash upon you!' I would say, 'May you not lack a man who hastened your father to the Fire!'"],[2552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out until, when he left behind Thaniyyat al-Wada', there was a squadron. He said, 'Who are these?' They said, 'Banu Qaynuqa', and they are the kinsfolk of Abdullah b. Salam.' He said, 'Have they accepted Islam?' They said, 'No, rather they are upon their religion.' He said, 'Tell them to return, for we do not seek help from the polytheists.'"],[2553,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought a battle in which Khalid b. al-Walid was at the head of his vanguard. Rabah and his companions passed by a slain woman from those the vanguard had struck. They stopped at her, marveling at her appearance, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with them. They parted for him until he looked at her and said, 'Ha! This one was not fighting.' Then he looked at the faces of the people and said to one of them, 'Catch up with Khalid b. al-Walid and tell him: Do not kill any offspring or hired servant.' And thus it was narrated by al-Mughirah b. Abd al-Rahman and Ibn Jurayj from Abu al-Zinad: 'The hadith has become authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it.' Ibn Jurayj and others narrated it from Abu al-Zinad according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2554,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a secret troop on the day of Khaybar to fight the polytheists. They continued fighting until they reached a village. When they arrived, the Prophet ﷺ asked them, \"What led you to kill the villagers?\" They replied, \"O Messenger of Allah, they were the children of the polytheists.\" He said, \"And were your children any better than the children of the polytheists? By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, every child is born on the fitrah (natural inclination towards monotheism) until his tongue speaks for him.\""],[2555,"I was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Qurayzah, and they were uncertain about me. The Prophet ﷺ ordered that they look at me to see if I had grown pubic hair. They looked at me and did not find that I had, so he let me go and sent me with the captives. This is a hadith narrated by a group of the leading scholars of the Muslims from Abd al-Malik b. Umayr, but the two (al-Bukhari and Muslim) did not include it. It seems they did not consider the corroboration of Mujahid b. Jubayr for Abd al-Malik in his narration from Atiyyah al-Qurazi, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2556,"He informed him that the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ examined him on the day of Qurayzah and did not see that the razor had passed over his hair, meaning his pubic hair, so they spared him from execution. Thus, with the corroboration of Mujahid, the hadith became authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2557,"That he should kill every one of them upon whom the razor had passed, and that their properties and progeny should be divided. He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'He has judged among them today with the judgment of Allah, which He judged from above the heavens.' Authentic."],[2558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abdullah b. Ghalib al-Laythi on a military expedition, and I was among them. He ordered them to launch a raid on Banu al-Mulawwih at al-Kadid. We went out until, when we were at al-Kadid, we met al-Harith b. al-Barsa' al-Laythi. We seized him, and he said, 'I have only come seeking Islam, and I came out to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' We said, 'If you are a Muslim, our holding you for a day and a night will not harm you, and if you are otherwise, we will secure you.' So we bound him firmly."],[2559,"Al-Dahhak b. Qays wanted to appoint Masruq as a governor. Umarah b. Uqbah said to him, 'Will you appoint a man from the remnants of the killers of Uthman?' Masruq said to him..."],[2560,"The Prophet ﷺ set the ransom for the people of the Jahiliyyah on the day of Badr at four hundred."],[2561,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to sell two brothers from the captives, so I sold them. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of their sale, and he said, \"Did you separate them?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Take them back, then sell them, and do not separate them.\""],[2562,"He separated a mother from her child, so the Prophet ﷺ forbade that and prohibited the sale, according to the condition set by Bukhari and Muslim."],[2563,"Two slaves went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hudaybiyyah before the peace treaty, and their masters wrote to him saying, \"O Muhammad, by Allah, they did not go out to you out of desire for your religion; they only went out fleeing from slavery.\" Some people said, \"They spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah; return them to them.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and said, \"I see that you, O Quraysh, will not stop until Allah sends against you someone who will strike your necks over this.\" And he refused to return them, saying, \"They are Allah's freedmen.\""],[2564,"No people ever break a covenant except that killing occurs among them, and no immorality ever appears among a people except that Allah inflicts death upon them, and no people ever withhold zakat except that Allah withholds rain from them."],[2565,"I said, \"Did you used to take a fifth of the food during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"We obtained food on the day of Khaybar, and a man would come and take from it as much as sufficed him, then leave.\""],[2566,"The fragrance of Paradise can be found from a distance of a hundred years' journey, and no servant kills a person under a covenant except that Allah forbids Paradise and its fragrance to him, that he should find it."],[2567,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Whoever kills a person from among Ahl Adh-Dhimmah, he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance may be detected from a distance of forty years.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4750)"],[2568,"Indeed, whoever kills a person under a covenant who has the protection of Allah and the protection of His Messenger has violated the protection of Allah, and he will not smell the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance can be found from a distance of seventy autumns."],[2569,"A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ died on the day of Hunayn, and they mentioned him to the Messenger ﷺ, who said, \"Pray over your companion.\" The faces of the people changed at that, so he said, \"Your companion stole from the spoils in the path of Allah.\" We searched his belongings and found beads from the beads of the Jews, not worth two dirhams."],[2570,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took spoils, he would order Bilal to call out among the people, and they would bring their spoils, and he would take a fifth and divide it. Then a man came after that with a hair rope and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this was among the spoils we obtained.\" He said, \"Did you hear Bilal call out three times?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then what prevented you from bringing it?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah,\" and he made an excuse. He said, \"You will come with it on the Day of Resurrection, and I will never accept it from you.\""],[2571,"Maslamah entered the land of the Romans, and a man who had stolen from the spoils was brought to him. He asked Salim about him, and Salim said, \"I heard my father narrate from Umar b. al-Khattab from the Prophet ﷺ: 'If you find a man who has stolen from the spoils, burn his belongings and beat him.'\" He said, \"We found a mushaf among his belongings, so Salim was asked about it, and he said, 'Sell it and give its price in charity.'\""],[2572,"\" Iasked Al-Hasan bin Muhammad about the saying of Allah, the Might and Sublime: 'and know that whatever of spoils of war that you may gain, verily, one-fifth of it is assigned to Allah. He said: 'This is the key to the Speech of Allah. This world and the Hereafter belling to Allah. He said: 'They differed concerning these two shares after the death of the Messenger of Allah, the share of the Messenger and the share of the near relatives (of the Messenger of Allah). Some said that the share of the near relatives was for the relatives of the Messenger, and some said that the share of the near relatives was for the relatives of the Khalifah. Then they agreed that these two shares should be spent on horses and equipment in the cause of Allah, and they were allocated for this purpose during the Khalifah of Abu Bakr and' Umar.\"' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4143)"],[2573,"I heard Ali say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ put me in charge of the fifth of the fifth, and I placed it in its proper places during the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr and Umar.\""],[2574,"Safiyyah was of the chosen spoils."],[2575,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his sword Dhu al-Fiqar as extra share on the day of Badr. Ibn Abbas said, this was the one about which he saw a vision on the day of Uhud. That is, when the polytheists came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, the opinion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was to remain in Madinah and fight them there. Some people who had not been present at Badr said to him, \"Will you take us out, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to fight them at Uhud?\" They hoped to attain the virtue that the people of Badr had attained. They kept at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he put on his armor, then they regretted it and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, stay; the opinion is your opinion.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is not fitting for a prophet to take off his armor after putting it on until Allah judges between him and his enemy.\" He said, and among what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told them that day before putting on his armor was: \"I saw that I was in a strong coat of mail, and I interpreted it as Madinah. And I saw myself riding behind a ram, and I interpreted it as the ram of the battalion. And I saw that my sword Dhu al-Fiqar was notched, and I interpreted it as a wound among you. And I saw cows being slaughtered, and cows, by Allah, are good; cows, by Allah, are good.\""],[2576,"He passed by a gathering."],[2577,"Hawazin came on the day of Hunayn with women, children, camels, and sheep, and arranged them in rows to outnumber the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Muslims and the polytheists met, and the Muslims turned back in retreat, as Allah Almighty said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.' And he said, 'O assembly of Ansar, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger.' Then Allah defeated the polytheists without a spear thrust or a sword blow. That day, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Whoever kills a disbeliever, his spoils belong to him.' Abu Qatadah killed twenty men that day and took their spoils. Abu Qatadah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I struck a man on the shoulder strap, and he had armor on. I was too hurried to take his spoils. See who he is, O Messenger of Allah.' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I took it, so make him satisfied with something from it and give it to me.' The Prophet ﷺ remained silent, and he never was asked for something except that he gave it or remained silent. 'Umar said, 'No, by Allah, Allah will not give the spoils to one of His lions and then give them to you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled."],[2579,"I witnessed Hunayn with my masters, and they spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about me. He ordered for me, and I was girded with a sword. It was reported that I was a slave, so he ordered for me some of the odds and ends of the baggage."],[2580,"We witnessed al-Hudaybiyyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When we left there, the people were urging their camels. Some people said to others, 'What is with the people?' They said, 'Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' We went out with the people, urging our mounts, and found the Prophet ﷺ standing on his riding camel at Kura' al-Ghamim. When the people gathered around him, he recited to them, 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest' [al-Fath: 1]. A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is it a conquest?' He said, 'Yes, by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it is indeed a conquest.' Khaybar was divided among the people of al-Hudaybiyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divided it into thirteen shares. The army was one thousand five hundred, including three hundred horsemen. He gave the horseman two shares and the foot soldier one share."],[2581,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr, 'Whoever does such and such will have such and such from the extra spoils.' He said: The young men advanced, and the elders stayed with the banners and did not leave them. When Allah granted them victory, the elders said, 'We were your support; if you had been defeated, you would have returned to us. Do not take the spoils and leave us with nothing.' The young men refused and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned it to us.' Then Allah Almighty revealed: 'They ask you about the spoils of war. Say, \"The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger\"' [al-Anfal: 1] up to: 'Just as your Lord brought you out of your home in truth, while a party of the believers were unwilling' [al-Anfal: 5]. He said: That was better for them, and likewise also, so obey me, for I know the outcome of this better than you."],[2582,"Abu Bakr and 'Uthman, the two sons of Abi Shaybah, narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Mus'ab b. Sa'd, from his father, who said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Badr with a sword and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my heart has been satisfied today against the enemy, so give me this sword.' He said, 'This sword is not for me nor for you.' I went away saying to myself, 'Today it will be given to someone who has not endured what I have.' While I was like that, a messenger came to me and said, 'Respond.' I thought something had been revealed concerning me because of my words. I came, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'You asked me for this sword, and it was not for me nor for you. Allah has now made it mine, so it is yours.' Then he recited: 'They ask you about the spoils of war. Say, \"The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger\"' [al-Anfal: 1] to the end of the verse."],[2583,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Badr along with three hundred and fifteen (men). The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, they are on foot, provide mount for them; O Allah , they are naked, clothe them; O Allah, they are hungry, provide food for them. Allah then bestowed victory on them. They returned when they were clothed. There was no man of them but he returned with one or two camels; they were clothed and ate to their fill. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2747)"],[2584,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give extra spoils to some of those he sent on expeditions, specifically for themselves, apart from the general division of the army, and the fifth is obligatory in all of that."],[2585,"I was a slave in Egypt belonging to a woman from Hudhayl. She freed me, and I did not leave Egypt while it had any knowledge but that I gathered it, as far as I could. Then I came to Syria and sifted through it, all the while asking about the extra spoils. I found no one to tell me anything about it until I met an old man called Ziyad b. Jariyah al-Tamimi. I said to him, 'Have you heard anything about the extra spoils?' He said, 'Yes, I heard Habib b. Maslamah al-Fihri say: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give a quarter as extra spoils at the beginning of an expedition and a third on the return.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the summary."],[2586,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give a third as extra spoils after the fifth."],[2587,"The people of the mosque sent me to Ibn Abi Awfa to ask him what the Prophet ﷺ did with the food of Khaybar. I went to him and asked him about that. I said, 'Did he take a fifth of it?' He said, 'No, it was less than that, and when one of us wanted something, he took what he needed from it.'"],[2588,"The Arabs used to say, 'Whoever eats bread becomes fat.' When we conquered Khaybar, we seized a loaf of bread from them, and I sat down by it and ate from it until I was full. Then I began looking at my sides to see if I had become fat."],[2589,"I witnessed the conquest of Khaybar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the people were defeated we fell upon their camp and the people took what they found of slaughtered camels—Zayd said, that is, the livestock. The pots had no sooner come to a boil than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered the pots to be overturned. Then he divided among us and allotted one sheep to every ten men."],[2590,"Plunder is not lawful, so overturn the pots."],[2591,"On the day of Khaybar the people seized sheep as plunder, slaughtered them, and began cooking them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and ordered the pots to be overturned, and he said, \"Plunder is not proper.\""],[2592,"He is not one of us who plunders, robs, or points out something for robbery."],[2593,"He forbade seizing property by stealth, eating animals that have been tied up and used as targets, and having intercourse with female captives until they have given birth to what is in their wombs."],[2594,"I asked 'Ubadah b. al-Samit about the spoils of war (al-anfal). He said: It was revealed concerning us, the people of Badr."],[2595,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Khaybar. A raiding party went out and captured a man who had sheep which he was tending, and brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ spoke to him as much as Allah willed him to speak, and the man said to him, \"I have believed in you and in what you have brought, but what about the sheep, O Messenger of Allah? They are a trust, and they belong to the people—a ewe or two or more than that.\" He ﷺ said, \"Throw pebbles at their faces, and they will return to their owners.\" So he took a handful of pebbles or dust and threw it at their faces, and they rushed off until every sheep entered upon its owner. Then he advanced to the battle line and an arrow struck him and killed him, although he had never prostrated to Allah even once. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Bring him into the tent.\" He was brought into the tent of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished, he entered upon him and then came out and said, \"Your companion's Islam has been excellent. I entered upon him and found with him two wives from among the houris of Paradise.\""],[2596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a leather bag containing beads from the booty, and he divided it between free women and slave women equally."],[2597,"On the day of Khaybar the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling war booty until it has been divided; and he forbade approaching pregnant women until they have given birth to what is in their wombs. He said, \"Would you water another's crop?\" And he forbade eating the flesh of domestic donkeys and the flesh of every predator with fangs."],[2598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar forbade selling war booty until it has been divided. Part of this matn has been narrated with a sound chain meeting the criteria of the two shaykhs.Sahih."],[2599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Khaybar forbade the flesh of domestic donkeys, pregnant women being approached until they have given birth to what is in their wombs, every predator with fangs, and selling the fifth until it has been divided.According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2600,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, some people of Quraysh came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, we are your allies and your people, and some of our slaves have joined you. They have no desire for Islam; they only fled from work, so return them to us.' He consulted Abu Bakr about their matter, and Abu Bakr said, 'They have spoken the truth, O Messenger of Allah.' Then he said to 'Umar, 'What do you think?' 'Umar said the like of Abu Bakr's words. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, 'O company of Quraysh, Allah will surely send upon you a man from among you whose heart Allah has tested for faith, and he will strike your necks for the religion.' Abu Bakr said, 'Is it I, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'No.' 'Umar said, 'Is it I, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'No, but it is the one mending the sandal in the mosque.' He had given his sandal to 'Ali to mend it. Then he said, 'Indeed, I heard him say: Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire.'"],[2601,"The Prophet ﷺ gave two shares to two hundred horses on the day of Khaybar."],[2602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The best tribe are Asad and the Ash'aris. They do not flee in battle, and they do not betray. They are from me and I am from them.' I related this to Mu'awiyah, and he said, 'It is not like this. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only said: They are from me and to me.' I said, 'It is not like this. My father narrated to me, but he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: They are from me and I am from them.' He said, 'Then you know better the hadith of your father.'"],[2603,"When the Prophet ﷺ obtained spoils, he would order Bilal to call out three times, and the people would bring whatever they had taken. Then he would order it to be divided into fifths. A man came to him with a halter of hair after the spoils had already been divided, and he said to him, 'Did you hear Bilal calling out three times?' The man said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What prevented you from bringing it?' The man made an excuse, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'You will be the one to bring it on the Day of Resurrection, for I will never accept it from you.'"],[2604,"A prophet among the prophets fought against the people of a city until he was about to conquer it, but he feared the sun would set. He said to it, 'O sun, you are commanded and I am commanded. I adjure you by Allah to stand still for a while during the day.' So Allah held it back until he conquered the city. They used to bring the spoils and offer them as a sacrifice, and fire would come and consume it. But when they offered the sacrifice this time, the fire did not come to consume it. They said, 'O Prophet of Allah, why is our sacrifice not accepted?' He said, 'There is embezzlement among you.' They said, 'How can we know who has the embezzlement?' They were twelve tribes. He said, 'Let the head of each tribe pledge allegiance to me.' So the head of each tribe pledged allegiance to him, and the prophet's hand stuck to the hand of one man among them. He said, 'The embezzlement is with you.' The man said, 'How can I know in which tribe it is?' He said, 'Call your tribe and have them pledge allegiance to you one by one.' He did so, and his hand stuck to the hand of the man who had the spoils. Then the fire came and consumed it. Ka'b said, 'Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Thus, by Allah, it is in the Book of Allah, meaning in the Torah.' Then he said, 'O Abu Hurairah, did the Prophet ﷺ tell you which prophet it was?' He said, 'No.' Ka'b said, 'It was Yusha' b. Nun.' Then he said, 'Did he tell you which city it was?' He said, 'No.' Ka'b said, 'It was the city of Ariha.'"],[2605,"The Prophet ﷺ said concerning the captives on the day of Badr, 'If you wish, you may kill them, and if you wish, you may ransom them and enjoy the ransom, and a number of you equal to them will be martyred.' The last of the seventy was Thabit b. Qays, who was martyred at al-Yamamah."],[2606,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set the ransom for the captives of the people of the Jahiliyyah at four hundred."],[2607,"Some of the captives on the day of Badr had no ransom, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made their ransom that they teach the children of the Ansar writing. A boy from the children of the Ansar came to his father, who said, 'What is the matter with you?' He said, 'My teacher beat me.' He said, 'The wicked one seeks the blood-price of Badr! By Allah, you shall never go to him again.'"],[2608,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received fay', he would distribute it the same day, giving the married man two shares and the unmarried man one share."],[2609,"I and al-Ashtar entered upon 'Ali b. Abi Talib on the day of the Camel, and I said, 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give you any covenant apart from the general one?' He said, 'No, except this.' He took out from his sword's sheath a document, and in it was: 'The believers' blood is equal, and the lowest of them may give protection on their behalf, and they are one hand against others. A believer is not to be killed for a disbeliever, nor one who has a covenant while his covenant stands.'"],[2610,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He grants refuge to the weakest among my ummah.\""],[2611,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The blood of the Muslims is equal...' and the rest of the hadith."],[2612,"The protection of the Muslims is one. If the lowest of them grants protection, do not violate it, for every treacherous one will have a banner by which he will be known on the Day of Resurrection."],[2613,"\"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Do not reside with the polytheists nor engage in intimate relations with them, for whoever resides with them or engages in intimate relations with them is not of us.'\""],[2614,"There was a man from the Ansar who accepted Islam, then apostatized and joined the polytheists. Then he regretted it and sent word to his people: Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ if there is any repentance for me. He said: Then the verses were revealed: {How shall Allah guide a people who disbelieved after their belief} [Al 'Imran 86] up to His saying: {Except for those who repent after that and correct themselves, for indeed Allah is Forgiving and Merciful} [Al 'Imran 89]. He said: \"So his people sent word to him, and he accepted Islam.\""],[2615,"When he feared a people, he would say: \"O Allah, we place You before their throats, and we seek refuge in You from their evils.\""],[2616,"He would supplicate, saying: \"O Allah, let me enjoy my hearing and my sight, and make them my heirs. O Allah, grant me victory over my enemy and show me my vengeance upon him.\""],[2617,"\"Whoever kills a mu'ahad (one with a covenant) without just cause, Allah forbids Paradise to him.\""],[2618,"Musaylima wrote to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibn Ishaq narrated to me from Sa'd b. Tariq al-Ashja'i, from Salama b. Nu'aym b. Mas'ud al-Ashja'i, from his father Nu'aym, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to the two messengers of Musaylima when he read Musaylima's letter: \"What do you two say?\" They said: We say as he said. He said: \"By Allah, were it not that messengers are not to be killed, I would strike your necks.\""],[2619,"\"When the battle grew fierce and the people met the people, we would seek protection by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and none of us would be closer to the enemy than he.\""],[2620,"\"A military expedition at sea is better than ten expeditions on land. Whoever crosses the sea is as if he crossed all the valleys, and the one who becomes seasick in it is like one who wallows in his blood.\""],[2621,"\"Ribat (guarding the frontier) for one day in the cause of Allah is better than a thousand days elsewhere.\""],[2622,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Ribat for one day in the cause of Allah is better than a thousand days elsewhere. Have I conveyed to you?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"O Allah, bear witness.\""],[2623,"Whoever dies upon one of these stations will be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection: ribat, or Hajj, or other than that."],[2624,"There is no Arabian horse but that it is granted permission at every dawn to make two supplications, saying: O Allah, You have made me a possession of the children of Adam, so make me the most beloved of his family and wealth to him."],[2625,"He used to call the female horse a faras (horse)."],[2626,"Three are felicity for the son of Adam, and three are misery for the son of Adam. Among the felicity of the son of Adam are: a righteous woman, a good dwelling, and a good mount. Among the misery of the son of Adam are: a cramped dwelling, a bad woman, and a bad mount."],[2627,"Seek me among your weak ones, for you are only given provision and victory because of your weak ones."],[2628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the day of Badr with three hundred and fifteen fighting men, just as Talut went out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for them when he went out, saying: \"O Allah, they are barefoot, so carry them. O Allah, they are naked, so clothe them. O Allah, they are hungry, so fill them.\" Then Allah granted them victory on the day of Badr, and they returned, and there was not a man among them except that he had come back with a camel or two, and they were clothed and filled."],[2629,"He said during a journey of his: \"We are traveling by night, if Allah Almighty wills, so let no weak one or difficult one travel with us.\" A man traveled on a difficult camel of his, and it fell and broke his neck and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be buried, then he ordered Bilal to call out: \"Paradise is not lawful for a disobedient person.\""],[2630,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was dividing dates on the day of Khaybar and said: O Muhammad, be just. He said: \"Woe to you! Who will be just to you if I am not just? Or from whom will you seek justice after me?\" Then he said: \"Soon a people like this one will come, reciting the Book of Allah while they are its enemies, reciting the Book of Allah with shaved heads. When they emerge, strike their necks.\""],[2631,"There will be among my nation people who are severe, whose tongues are sharp with the Qur'an, but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game. So when you meet them, kill them, for the one who kills them will be rewarded."],[2632,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be in my nation a people who are enemies, whose tongues are sharp with the Qur'an. When you see them, put them to sleep [i.e., kill them]."],[2633,"I wanted to see a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who would narrate to me about the Kharijites. He said: I met Abu Barzah on the day of Arafah among a group of his companions and I said: O Abu Barzah, narrate to us something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying about the Kharijites. He said: I will narrate to you what my two ears heard and my two eyes saw. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought dinars from a land and he was distributing them. With him was a black man with closely cut hair, wearing two white garments, with the trace of prostration between his eyes. He confronted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and came to him from his front, but he did not give him anything. Then he came from his left, but he did not give him anything. Then he came from behind him and said: By Allah, O Muhammad, you have not been just in the distribution today. The Prophet ﷺ became angry and said: \"You will not find after me anyone more just to you than me.\" He said it three times. Then he said: \"A people will emerge from the direction of the east, their guidance is like this, reciting the Qur'an but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game, then they will not return to it.\" He placed his hand on his chest. \"Their mark is shaving. They will continue to emerge until the last of them emerges. When you see them, kill them.\" Hammad said it three times. \"They are the worst of creation and creatures.\" Hammad said it three times. And he said: \"He also said: They will not return to it.\""],[2634,"There will be in my nation disagreement and division, and a people will come who please you and are pleased with themselves. Those who kill them are closer to Allah than them. They speak well but act badly, and they call to Allah but they are not from Allah in anything. When you meet them, put them to sleep [i.e., kill them].\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them for us. He said: \"Their sign is shaving and tashbit [perhaps a term for their appearance]."],[2635,"There will be in my nation disagreement and division: a people who speak well but act badly, reciting the Qur'an but it does not go beyond their collarbones. One of you would consider his prayer insignificant compared to their prayer, and his fasting insignificant compared to their fasting. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game, not returning until the arrow is returned to its bowstring. They are the worst of creation and creatures. Blessed is the one who kills them and whom they kill. They call to the Book of Allah, but they are not from it in anything. Whoever fights them is closer to Allah than them.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their sign? He said: \"Shaving.\""],[2636,"There will be in my nation disagreement and division: a people who speak well but act badly, reciting the Qur'an but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of the religion as an arrow passes through the game, not returning until it is returned to its bowstring. They are the worst of creation and creatures. Blessed is the one who kills them and whom they kill. They call to the Book of Allah, but they are not from it in anything. Whoever fights them is closer to Allah than them.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is their sign? He said: \"Shaving.\""],[2637,"Their example is like a man who shoots an arrow and then seeks the arrow where it landed. He takes it and looks at its bow notch and does not see any grease or blood on it. Then he looks at its fletching and does not see any grease or blood on it. Then he looks at its arrowhead and does not see any grease or blood on it. Just as nothing of grease and blood clung to it, likewise these people do not cling to anything of Islam.\""],[2638,"I entered with Abu Sa‘id al-Khudri upon Hudhayfah, and we said, “O Abu ‘Abd Allah, tell us what you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the tribulation.” Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Turn with the Book of Allah wherever it turns.” We said, “If the people disagree, with whom should we be?” He said, “Look to the group in which Ibn Sumayyah is, and adhere to it, for he turns with the Book of Allah.” I said, “Who is Ibn Sumayyah?” He said, “Do you not know him?” I said, “Explain him to me.” He said, “Ammār b. Yāsir.” I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ammār, “O Abu al-Yaqzān, you will not die until the transgressing group that deviates from the path kills you.”"],[2639,"\"He said to him and his son Ali, 'Go to Abu Sa'id and listen to his words about the matter of the Khawarij.' So they went and found him fixing a wall. When he saw us, he took his cloak, covered himself with it, and then began to speak to us until he mentioned it in the mosque. He said, 'We used to carry one brick at a time, while the construction workers carried two bricks at a time.' The Prophet ﷺ saw him and began to shake the dust off his head, saying, 'O Ammar, why don't you carry one brick at a time as your companions do?' Ammar replied, 'I seek reward from Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ shook his head and said, 'Woe to Ammar, the opposing faction will kill him.' Ammar said, 'I seek refuge in Allah from trials and tribulations.'\""],[2640,"I witnessed Abu Umāmah al-Bāhilī while he was standing over the heads of the Ḥarūriyyah at the gate of Damascus, saying, “Dogs of the people of the Fire,” he said it three times, “the best of those killed are those they killed,” and his eyes shed tears. A man said to him, “O Abu Umāmah, do you consider your saying that these are the dogs of the Fire something you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or from your own opinion?” He said, “Then I would be bold indeed if I had not heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except once, twice, or three times,” and he counted seven times, “I would not have told it to you.” A man said to him, “I saw that your eyes shed tears.” He said, “When they were believers they disbelieved after their faith.” Then he recited, {And be not like those who became divided and differed after clear proofs came to them} [Āl ‘Imrān 105], the verse, “so it applies to them twice.”"],[2641,"I heard Abu Umāmah while he was standing over the heads of the Ḥarūriyyah at the gate of Ḥimṣ or the gate of Damascus, saying, “Dogs of the Fire, dogs of the Fire, the worst of those killed under the shade of the sky; the best of those killed are those they killed.”"],[2643,"I came to ‘Ā’ishah. While we were sitting with her after her return from Iraq, in the nights when ‘Alī was fought, she said, “O ‘Abd Allah b. Shaddād, will you be truthful with me about what I ask you? Tell me about these people whom ‘Alī killed.” I said, “Why would I not be truthful with you?” She said, “Tell me about their story.” I said, “When ‘Alī corresponded with Mu‘āwiyah and appointed the two arbitrators, eight thousand of the reciters of the people went out against him and encamped in a land on the side of Kufa called Ḥarūrā’. They disapproved of him and said, ‘You have stripped off a shirt that Allah clothed you with and named you by, then you went and appointed arbitration in Allah’s religion, while there is no judgment except Allah’s.’ When ‘Alī learned of their reproach and their separation from him, he ordered a caller to announce that no one should enter upon the Commander of the Believers except a man who had memorized the Qur’an. When the house was filled with reciters, he called for a large muṣḥaf and placed it before him, and he began to strike it with his hand, saying, ‘O muṣḥaf, speak to the people.’ The people called out to him, ‘O Commander of the Believers, what do you ask it about? It is only paper and ink, and we speak of what we have seen from it. What do you want?’ He said, ‘Your companions who went out—between me and them is the Book of Allah. Allah ﷻ says concerning a woman and a man: If you fear a breach between them, send an arbitrator from his family and an arbitrator from her family. The nation of Muhammad ﷺ has greater sanctity than a woman and a man. They condemned me for corresponding with Mu‘āwiyah and writing ‘Alī b. Abī Ṭālib, while Suhayl b. ‘Amr came and we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyyah when his people made peace with Quraysh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote, “In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.” Suhayl said, “Do not write ‘In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.’” He said, “How should I write?” He said, “Write: In Your name, O Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Write.” Then he said, “Write: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah.” They said, “If we knew that you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have opposed you.” So he wrote, “This is what Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah has made peace upon with Quraysh.” Allah says in His Book: {Indeed, in the Messenger of Allah you have a good example for whoever hopes in Allah and the Last Day} [al-Aḥzāb 21]. Then ‘Alī b. Abī Ṭālib sent him to them. I went out with them until we reached the middle of their camp. Ibn al-Kawwā’ stood up and addressed the people, saying, “O bearers of the Qur’an, this is ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abbās. Whoever does not know him, I know him from the Book of Allah: this is the one about whose people it was revealed: {Rather, they are a quarrelsome people} [al-Zukhruf 58]. Send him back to his companion and do not debate the Book of Allah with him.” Their orators stood up and said, “No, by Allah, we will debate the Book of Allah with him. If he brings the truth, we will recognize it and follow it; and if he brings falsehood, we will refute him with his falsehood and send him back to his companion.” So they debated the Book of Allah with him for three days. Four thousand of them returned, all repentant, among them Ibn al-Kawwā’, until ‘Alī brought them in. Then ‘Alī sent to the rest of them, saying, “You have seen what has happened regarding our affair and the affair of the people. Stay where you wish until the nation of Muhammad ﷺ gathers, and settle where you wish between us and you, provided that we protect you from our spears as long as you do not cut off a road or shed blood unjustly. If you do that, we have declared war against you on equal terms. Indeed, Allah does not love the treacherous.” ‘Ā’ishah said to him, “O Ibn Shaddād, so he killed them?” He said, “By Allah, he did not send against them until they cut off the road, shed blood without Allah’s right, killed Ibn Khabbāb, and violated the protected people.” She said, “By Allah?” I said, “By Allah, besides whom there is no god.” She said, “What about something that reached me from the people of Iraq, which they talk about, saying ‘the one with the breast, the one with the breast’?” I said, “I saw him and stood over him with ‘Alī among the slain. He called the people and said, ‘Do you recognize this one?’ Most of those who came said, ‘I saw him in the mosque of Banū So-and-so praying,’ and ‘I saw him in the mosque of Banū So-and-so praying,’ but no one brought a definite identification except that.” She said, “What did ‘Alī say when he stood over him, as the people of Iraq claim?” I said, “I heard him say, ‘Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.’” She said, “Did you hear anything else from him?” I said, “O Allah, no.” She said, “Yes, Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.”"],[2644,"I witnessed Ali on the day of Nahrawan asking for the mukhaddaj (a man whose arm had a deformity who was foretold to ʿAlī by the Prophet ﷺ), but he was unable to find one. His forehead began to sweat and he became distressed. Eventually, he was able to find him and he fell down in prostration, saying, \"By Allah, you have neither lied nor been lied to.\""],[2645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and began to strike with his hand in it, giving right and left. Among them was a man with short garments, having a mark between his eyes from prostration. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept striking his hand right and left until the wealth was exhausted. When the wealth was exhausted, he turned away and said, “By Allah, you have not been just since today.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began turning his palm and saying, “If I am not just, then who will be just after me? Indeed, a renegade group will emerge, passing through the religion as an arrow passes through the game, then they will not return to it until the arrow returns to its bow. They recite the Qur’an, but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They speak well but act badly. Whoever meets them should fight them. Whoever kills them will have the best reward, and whoever they kill will have the best martyrdom. They are the worst of creation. Allah is free from them. The most rightful of the two parties will kill them.”"],[2646,"“I witnessed Ṣiffīn. They would not finish off a wounded person, nor kill one who fled, nor plunder a slain person.”"],[2647,"The caller of Ammār proclaimed on the Day of the Camel, when the people had fled, “Indeed, no one is to be finished off if wounded, no one who flees is to be killed, and whoever lays down his weapon is safe.” That distressed us."],[2648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ‘Abd Allah b. Mas‘ūd, “O Ibn Mas‘ūd, do you know what Allah’s ruling is concerning those who transgress from this nation?” Ibn Mas‘ūd said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Allah’s ruling concerning them is that their fleeing ones are not pursued, their captives are not killed, and their wounded are not finished off.” [Kawthar b. Ḥakīm is abandoned.]"],[2649,"When Ammar ibn Yasir was killed, Amr ibn Hazm went to Amr ibn al-As and said, \"Ammar has been killed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The rebellious group will kill him.'\" Amr ibn al-As stood up in alarm and went to Muawiyah. Muawiyah asked him, \"What's the matter with you?\" Amr replied, \"Ammar has been killed.\" Muawiyah said, \"So, Ammar has been killed, what about it?\" Amr responded, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The rebellious group will kill him.'\" Muawiyah then said to him, \"Did your own urine delude you? Did we kill him? Ali and his companions are the ones who brought him here until they threw him amidst our spears.\" (or he said, \"amidst our swords\")."],[2650,"I have not seen the like of what this nation turned away from of this verse: {And if two parties of the believers fight, make peace between them; but if one of them transgresses against the other, fight the one that transgresses until it returns to Allah’s command}.[1]"],[2651,"\"The Prophet [SAW] said: 'After me there will be many calamities and much evil behavior.' He raised his hands (and said): 'Whomever you see trying to create division among the Ummah of Muhammad [SAW] when they are all united, kill him, no matter who he is among the people.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4021)"],[2652,"“O Abu Dharr, how will you be when a death strikes the people until a house is worth a servant?” meaning a grave. I said, “What Allah and His Messenger choose for me.” Then he said, “How will you be when a famine strikes the people until you come to your mosque and cannot return to your bed, and cannot rise from your bed to your mosque?” I said, “What Allah and His Messenger choose for me.” He said, “Keep to chastity.” Then he said, “How will you be when a killing strikes the people until the stones of al-Zayt are drowned in blood?” I said, “What Allah and His Messenger choose for me, or Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Stay in your house.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, should I not take my sword and strike with it those who do that?” He said, “Then you would have shared with the people.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what if someone enters my house?” He said, “If you fear that the flash of the sword will overwhelm you, say like this, and throw the edge of your garment over your face, so he will bear his sin and your sin, and he will be among the people of the Fire.”"],[2653,"Marwān b. al-Ḥakam said to Ayman b. Khuraym, “Will you not go out and fight with us?” He said, “My father and my uncle witnessed Badr, and they enjoined me not to fight anyone who says ‘There is no god but Allah.’ If you bring me a release from the Fire, I will fight with you.” He said, “Then leave us.” He left saying: [al-baḥr al-wāfir] “I am not one to kill a man who prays / to another ruler from Quraysh. His is his authority and upon me is my sin / I seek refuge with Allah from ignorance and recklessness. Should I kill a Muslim without crime? / Then my life, as long as I live, will not benefit me.”"],[2654,"‘Uthmān b. ‘Affān sent Sa‘īd b. al-‘Āṣ to Kufa on the Day of al-Jara‘ah. They went out to him and turned him back. I was sitting with Ibn Mas‘ūd and Ḥudhayfah. Ibn Mas‘ūd said, “I did not think that these would return without a cupping-glass of blood being spilled, and I know nothing of that except something I knew while Muhammad ﷺ was alive: ‘A man becomes a believer in the morning and in the evening has nothing with him, and becomes a believer in the evening and in the morning has nothing with him. He fights in tribulation today and Allah kills him tomorrow; his heart is turned upside down and his buttocks are raised above.’” I said, “His lower part?” He said, “Rather, his buttocks.”"],[2655,"A slave boy belonged to Baba, and Baba used to beat him over some matters and punish him, and the boy used to treat his master with enmity. So he sold him. Then one day the boy met him, and the boy had a sword with him, and that was during the governorship of Sa'id b. al-'As. The slave drew the sword against Baba and brandished it at him, but the people restrained him from him. So Baba entered upon 'A'ishah and informed her of what the slave had done. 'A'ishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever points a piece of iron at any of the Muslims intending to kill him, his blood has become lawful.\" She said: So Baba went out from her presence, went to the master of the slave who had bought him from him, asked him to rescind the sale, and he rescinded it, so he returned him to him. Then Baba took him and killed him."],[2656,"Whoever draws his sword, then puts it down, his blood is wasted."],[2657,"\"A time is about to come when people will be sifted with a sifting, and a residue of people will remain whose covenants and trusts have become corrupt, and they will differ, and they will be like this\" — and he interlaced his fingers. They said: \"So how will it be for us, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"You will take what you recognize and leave what you reject, and you will attend to your own private affairs and abandon the affairs of the common people.\""],[2658,"There is no morning except that two callers cry out: Woe to the men from the women, and woe to the women from the men."],[2659,"There is no monasticism in Islam."],[2660,"Marry, for the best of this nation, the nation of Muhammad ﷺ, is the one with the most wives, and whatever is entrusted in your loins will surely come out before the Day of Resurrection."],[2661,"Ibn 'Abbas said to me: \"O Sa'id, marry, for the best of this nation are those with the most wives.\""],[2662,"\"The Messenger of Allah said: 'Women and perfume have been made dear to me, but my comfort has been provided in prayer.'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3940)"],[2663,"Nothing like marriage has been seen for two who love each other."],[2664,"Three are a right upon Allah that He help them: the one striving in the path of Allah, the one marrying desiring to remain chaste, and the mukatab who wants to pay off his contract."],[2665,"Marry women, for they will bring you wealth."],[2666,"A woman is married for one of three qualities: a woman is married for her beauty, a woman is married for her religion and character, so upon you is the one with religion, may your hands be dusty."],[2667,"Whoever Allah has provided with a righteous wife, He has helped him with half of his religion, so let him fear Allah in the second half."],[2668,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked, \"Which of women is best?\" He said, \"The best of women is she who gladdens (her husband) when he looks at her, obeys him when he commands, and does not oppose him regarding herself or his wealth.\""],[2669,"From the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[2670,"Three are from happiness and three are from misery. From happiness are: a wife whom you see and she pleases you, and when you are absent you trust her with herself and your wealth; a mount that is compliant and catches you up with your companions; and a house that is spacious and has many conveniences. From misery are: a wife whom you see and she displeases you, and she wields her tongue against you, and if you are absent from her you do not trust her with herself and your wealth; a mount that is slow, and if you beat it, it tires you, and if you ride it, it does not catch you up with your companions; and a house that is cramped and has few conveniences."],[2671,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have found a woman of noble lineage, rank, and wealth, except that she does not bear children. Should I marry her?\" He forbade him. Then he came to him a second time and said the like of that, and he forbade him. Then he came to him a third time and said the like of that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Marry the loving, fertile woman, for I will boast of your great numbers before the nations.\""],[2672,"Three things, O 'Ali, do not delay: prayer when its time comes, the funeral when it is present, and the single woman when she finds a suitable match."],[2673,"\"Choose well for your seed; marry suitable spouses, and give in marriage to suitable spouses.\""],[2674,"About Hisham ibn Urwah, he mentioned it with his chain of narration similarly."],[2675,"\"Indeed, the nobility of the people of this world, which they look to, is this wealth.\""],[2676,"\"Nobility is wealth, and honor is piety.\""],[2677,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The honor of the believer is his religion, his manliness is his intellect, and his nobility is his character.\""],[2678,"Abu Hudhayfa b. 'Utba b. Rabi'a b. 'Abd Shams, who was one of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, adopted Salim as a son and married him to his brother's daughter, Hind bt. al-Walid b. 'Utba b. Rabi'a b. 'Abd Shams. Salim was a freedman of a woman of the Ansar. He adopted him as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ adopted Zayd. In the Jahiliyya, whoever adopted a man, people called him to that (adoptive father) and he inherited from his estate, until Allah the Exalted revealed concerning that: {Call them by their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah. But if you do not know their fathers, then they are your brothers in religion and your clients} [al-Ahzab 5]. So they returned them to their fathers; whoever had no known father became his client or brother in religion. 'A'isha said: Sahlah bt. Suhayl b. 'Amr al-Qurashi, then al-'Amiri, who was the wife of Abu Hudhayfa b. 'Utba b. Rabi'a, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after Allah revealed that. She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we used to regard Salim as a son, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had given him shelter, and he stayed with him and with Abu Hudhayfa in one house, and he sees me while I am unveiled. Allah has revealed about them what you know. What is your opinion concerning his matter, O Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Suckle him.\" So she suckled him with five sucklings, and he became forbidden by them, and he took the status of her son by suckling."],[2679,"\"O Banu Bayada, give Abu Hind in marriage, and marry to him.\" He said, and he was a cupper."],[2680,"\"Whoever gives for Allah, withholds for Allah, loves for Allah, hates for Allah, and gives in marriage for Allah, has completed faith.\""],[2681,"If someone whose character and religion please you comes to you, then marry him. If you do not, there will be tribulation on earth and widespread corruption."],[2682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When one of you proposes to a woman, if he is able to look at some of what invites him to marry her, then let him do so.\" He said: I proposed to a woman from Banu Sulaym, and I used to hide for her among the roots of palm trees until I saw from her what invited me to marry her, then I married her."],[2683,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go and look at her, for it is more likely to create affection between you.\" He said: So he went and looked at her, then he mentioned her suitability."],[2684,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Conceal the proposal, then perform ablution and do it well, then pray what Allah Most High has decreed for you, then praise your Lord and glorify Him, then say: O Allah, You have power and I have no power, and You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. If You see for me in so-and-so (naming her by her name) good in my religion, my worldly life, and my hereafter, then decree her for me. If someone else is better for me in my religion, my worldly life, and my hereafter, then decree her for me.\""],[2685,"That the Prophet ﷺ wanted to marry a woman, so he sent a woman to look at her. He said: \"Smell her molars and look at her Achilles tendons.\" He said: So she came to them, and they said: \"Shall we not feed you, O Umm so-and-so?\" She said: \"I will not eat except from food brought by so-and-so.\" He said: So I climbed onto a shelf of theirs and looked at her Achilles tendons, then she said: \"Comb my hair, O my little daughter.\" He said: So she began to comb her hair while smelling her molars. He said: Then she came and reported."],[2686,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, the fornicator who has been flogged should not marry except one like him.\""],[2687,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, should I marry 'Anaq?\" He said: He was silent, then it was revealed: \"The fornicator does not marry except a fornicatress or an idolatress, and the fornicatress does not marry except a fornicator or an idolater, and that has been made forbidden to the believers\" [Quran 24:3]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to me and said: \"Do not marry her.\""],[2688,"The Prophet ﷺ heard saying, \"The orphan girl is consulted regarding herself. If she remains silent, it is her consent. And if she disagrees, no compulsion is on her.\""],[2689,"Her mother went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"My daughter dislikes him, by Allah.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to separate from her, and he separated from her, and he said: \"Do not marry women until you seek their consent, and if they remain silent, that is their permission.\" Afterwards, al-Mughira b. Shu'ba married her."],[2690,"Khawla bt. Hakim b. Umayya b. al-Awqas, the wife of 'Uthman b. Maz'un, and that was in Makkah: she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry?\" He said: \"Who?\" She said: \"If you wish, a virgin; and if you wish, a previously married woman.\" He said: \"Who is the virgin?\" She said: \"The daughter of the most beloved of Allah's creation to you, 'A'isha bt. Abi Bakr.\" He said: \"Who is the previously married woman?\" She said: \"Sawda bt. Zam'a b. Qays, who has believed in you and followed you in what you are upon.\" He said: \"Go and mention them.\" So she came and entered the house of Abu Bakr and said: \"O Abu Bakr, what good and blessing has Allah brought upon you! The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to propose 'A'isha on his behalf.\" He said: \"Call the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me.\" So she called him, and he came and married her, and she was at that time a girl of seven years."],[2691,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She is young.\" Then 'Ali proposed to her, and he married her."],[2692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Any woman married without the consent of her guardian, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid, her marriage is invalid. If he has consummated with her, she is entitled to her dowry for what he has consummated. If they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian.\""],[2693,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ likewise."],[2694,"A woman is not to be married without the permission of her guardian; if she is married, then her marriage is invalid — three times — and if he has consummated with her, then she is entitled to her dowry for what he has had of her; and if they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."],[2695,"Any woman who is married without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid, and she is entitled to her dowry for what he has had of her; and if they dispute, then the ruler is the guardian of the one who has no guardian."],[2696,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2697,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” All these chains of transmission are authentic, and we have a high chain through Isra'il. The leading earlier imams, who in their narrations descend through Isra'il, such as 'Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi, Waki', Yahya b. Adam, Yahya b. Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah, and others, have connected it, and they have ruled this hadith to be authentic. I heard Abu Nasr Ahmad b. Sahl al-Faqih in Bukhara say: I heard Salih b. Muhammad b. Habib al-Hafiz say: I heard 'Ali b. 'Abd Allah al-Madini say: I heard 'Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi say: “Isra'il used to memorize the hadith of Abu Ishaq as he memorized the Surah al-Hamd.” I heard Abu al-Hasan b. Mansur say: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ishaq say: I heard Abu Musa say: “'Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi used to affirm the hadith of Isra'il from Abu Ishaq, meaning regarding marriage without a guardian.” Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Shaybani narrated to me: Ahmad b. Muhammad b. al-Hasan narrated to us: Hatim b. Yunus al-Jurjani narrated to us: He said: I said to Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi: What do you say about marriage without a guardian? He said: “It is not permissible.” I said: What is the proof for that? He said: Qays b. al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from his father. I said: But al-Thawri and Shu'bah narrate it as mursal. He said: Isra'il has followed Qays. Muhammad b. Salih b. Hani' narrated to me: Muhammad b. al-Mundhir b. Sa'id narrated to us: Ishaq b. Ibrahim b. Jabalah narrated to us: I heard 'Ali b. al-Madini say: The hadith of Isra'il is authentic regarding “There is no marriage except with a guardian.” I heard Abu al-Hasan b. Mansur say: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ishaq al-Imam say: I asked Muhammad b. Yahya about this chapter, and he said: The hadith of Isra'il is authentic according to me. I said to him: Sharik also narrated it. He said: Who narrated it? I said: 'Ali b. Hujr narrated it to us, and I mentioned to him the hadith of Yunus from Abu Ishaq, and I said to him: Shu'bah and al-Thawri narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: Yes, “They narrated it like that, but they used to narrate the hadith and send it as mursal until it was said to them: From whom? Then they would give its chain.” I heard Abu al-Hasan Ahmad b. Muhammad al-'Anazi say: I heard 'Uthman b. Sa'id al-Darimi say: I said to Yahya b. Ma'in: Is Yunus b. Abi Ishaq dearer to you, or his son Isra'il b. Yunus? He said: “Both are trustworthy.” Sahih."],[2698,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2699,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2700,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2701,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2702,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2703,"There is no marriage except with a guardian."],[2704,"I used to serve the Prophet ﷺ, then the Prophet ﷺ said to me, \"O Rabi'ah! Why don't you get married?\" I replied, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I don't want to get married. I don't have enough to provide for a wife, and I don't want anything to distract me from you.\" Then he turned away from me. After that, he asked me again, \"O Rabi'ah! Why don't you get married?\" I replied, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I don't want to get married. I don't have enough to provide for a wife, and I don't want anything to distract me from you.\" He turned away from me again. Then I revisited myself and said, \"By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, you know what is best for me in this life and the hereafter.\" He said, \"And I say to myself, if he asks me for the third time, I will say yes.\" Then he asked me for the third time, \"O Rabi'ah! Why don't you get married?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah, do whatever you think is best for me or whatever you like.\" He said, \"Go to the family of so and so in such and such place among the Ansar. Tell them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends his greetings to you and orders you to marry Rabi'ah the daughter of so and so.\" So I went to them and conveyed the message. They said, \"Welcome to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ does not ask us for something without a reason.\" They honored me, married me to her, treated me kindly, and did not ask for any proof. I returned feeling sad, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me, \"What's wrong?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I went to a noble people, they honored and treated me kindly, and did not ask for any proof. But where will I get the dowry?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Buraidah Al-Aslami, \"O Buraidah, collect the weight of a date seed in gold for him.\" So they collected the weight of a date seed in gold for me. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Take it to them and say, 'This is her dowry.'\" So I took it to them and said, \"This is her dowry.\" They said, \"It's a lot, but we accept it.\" Then I asked, \"Where should I stay?\" They said, \"O Buraidah, give him a sheep.\" So they gave me a fat sheep. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Go to Aishah and tell her to look at the dough in which the food is baked and send it to us.\" So I went to Aishah, told her about it, and she said, \"Here it is, the dough in which the food is baked. By Allah, we don't have any other food in the morning.\" So I took it and the sheep to the Prophet ﷺ. They accepted the food and said, \"You keep the sheep.\" Then some Muslims came, slaughtered, skinned, and cooked it. So we had bread and meat in the morning. I felt content and prayed for the blessings of the Muslims."],[2705,"From al-Hasan regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {So do not prevent them from remarrying their husbands} [al-Baqarah 232], he said: Ma'qil b. Yasar al-Muzani narrated to me that it was revealed concerning him. He said: I had married a sister of mine to a man, and he divorced her until when her waiting period ended, he came to propose to her. I said to him: I married you, prepared a bed for you, honored you, then you divorced her, and now you come to propose to her? No, by Allah, she will never return to you. He said: He was a man with no fault in him, and the woman wanted to return to him. He said: So Allah revealed this verse, and I said: “Now I will do it, O Messenger of Allah,” and I married her to him. Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ishaq said: “In this hadith there is clear evidence that Allah ﷻ placed the marriage contract in the hands of the guardians, not in their hands, and that women, even if they are previously married, have no role in the contract.”"],[2706,"Any woman whom two guardians marry, she belongs to the first of them; and any two men who purchase a sale, it belongs to the first of them."],[2707,"Whichever man sells to two men a sale, it belongs to the first of them; and whichever woman two guardians give in marriage, she belongs to the first."],[2708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If two guardians contract a marriage, it belongs to the first; and if two authorizers sell, it belongs to the first.\" And Qatadah was followed in his narration from al-Hasan by Ash'ath ibn 'Abd al-Malik al-Humrani."],[2709,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If two authorizers contract a marriage, then the first has more right.\" These clear paths that I have mentioned for this text are all sound according to the condition of al-Bukhari, but they did not include it on the condition of al-Bukhari."],[2710,"\"Our dower, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, was ten uqiyyahs.\""],[2711,"Verily, do not go to excess in the dowers of women, for if it were a mark of honor in this world or piety before Allah, then the most deserving of it and the most entitled to it among you would be Muhammad ﷺ. He did not give as dower to any woman among his wives more than twelve uqiyyahs. And indeed one of you goes to excess in the dower of his wife until there is enmity in his heart against her, and he says, 'I have been burdened for you with the sweat of the water-skin.'"],[2712,"That 'Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed the people and said: O people, do not go to excess in the dowers of women, for if it were a mark of honor, none of you would be more entitled to it or more deserving than the Prophet ﷺ. He did not give as dower to any of his wives, nor did he give as dower for any of his daughters, more than twelve uqiyyahs. And the uqiyyah is forty dirhams, so that is four hundred and eighty dirhams. And that is the most the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ever gave as dower. So I do not know of anyone who exceeded four hundred dirhams. And it has been narrated in a sound manner from 'Abdullah ibn 'Abbas from 'Umar."],[2713,"\"Do not go to excess in the dowers of women.\""],[2714,"That 'Umar ibn al-Khattab stood on his pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: Verily, do not go to excess in the dowers of women, for if it were a mark of honor in this world or piety before Allah, the most deserving of it among you would be your Prophet ﷺ. No woman among his wives or daughters was given more than twelve uqiyyahs, and that is four hundred and eighty dirhams; the uqiyyah is forty dirhams. The sound chains have become mutawatir for the authenticity of the sermon of the Commander of the Faithful 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, and this chapter I have compiled in a large volume, but they did not include it."],[2715,"That a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I have married a woman from the Ansar for eight uqiyyahs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was startled by that and said: \"It is as if you are carving silver from the side of this mountain. Have you seen her? For in the eyes of the Ansar there is something.\" He said: I have seen her. He said: \"We have nothing, but we will send you on an expedition, and I hope you will obtain good.\" So he sent him with a group of people to some people of Banu 'Abs, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered for them a she-camel. They loaded their belongings on it, and it had not gone but a little when it knelt down and was too exhausted to get up. There was no one among the people younger than the one who had married. He came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ while he was lying on his back in the mosque, and he stood by his head, disliking to wake him. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ woke up and said: O Prophet of Allah, the one you gave us – we would like you to rouse it. The Prophet ﷺ extended his right hand to him, took his cloak with his left hand, placed it on his shoulder, and went walking until he came to it. He struck it with the sole of his foot, and by the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, after that it would outstrip the leader. Then they camped in the presence of the enemy, and the enemy had lit fires, and they surrounded them, then they dispersed upon them and said the takbir with the takbir of one man, and Allah routed them and took captives from them."],[2716,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ seeking his assistance in obtaining the dowry for a woman. The Prophet ﷺ asked, \"How much did you marry her for?\" He replied, \"Two hundred dirhams.\" The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"If you were to scoop from the ocean, you would not increase.\""],[2717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the saying of Allah ﷻ {and heaps of gold and silver} [Al 'Imran 14]. He said: \"The qintar is two thousand uqiyyahs.\""],[2718,"\"The woman with the greatest blessing is the one with the lightest dower.\""],[2719,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a man to a woman for a ring of iron whose bezel was silver.\""],[2720,"Whoever is afflicted by a calamity should say: 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return. O Allah, with You I seek reward for my calamity, so reward me in it and give me something better in exchange.' When Abu Salamah died, I said it, and every time I reached 'give me something better in exchange,' I said to myself, 'Who is better than Abu Salamah?' Then I completed it. When her waiting period ended, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Umar b. al-Khattab to propose to her on his behalf. She said to her son, 'O Umar, get up and marry the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [to me],' so he married her. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to her to consummate the marriage, but when she saw him she would take her daughter Zaynab and place her in her lap, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would leave. Ammar b. Yasir, who was her foster brother, learned of this, so he came to her and said, 'Where is this ugly, repulsive one who has annoyed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He took her and went away. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, entered upon her, and looked around the corners of the house, saying, 'What happened to Zunab?' She said, 'Ammar came and took her away.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage, and said, 'I shall not reduce anything for you from what I gave to so-and-so: two hand mills, two jars, and a cushion stuffed with palm fiber.' And he said, 'If I grant you seven nights, I would have to grant my wives seven nights too.'"],[2721,"Abu Talhah proposed to Umm Sulaym, and she said, 'O Abu Talhah, do you not know that the god you worship is a piece of wood that grew from the earth, carved by an Abyssinian slave of Banu so-and-so? If you become Muslim, I will ask no other dowry from you.' He said, 'Let me consider my affair.' He went away, then came back and said, 'I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' She said, 'O Anas, marry Abu Talhah.'"],[2722,"Umm Sulaym married Abu Talhah for his [embracing] Islam."],[2723,"Some people came to Abdullah b. Masud and said to him, 'A man among us married a woman but did not assign her a dowry and did not consummate the marriage, and then he died.' Abdullah said to them, 'I have not been asked about anything since I parted from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that is harder on me than this. Ask someone else.' They kept coming back to him about it for a month. Finally they said to him, 'Whom shall we ask if we do not ask you? You are among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ in this land, and we find no one else.' He said, 'I will state my own judgment in this matter, with all my effort. If it is correct, it is from Allah alone, with no partner; if it is wrong, it is from me, and Allah and His Messenger are free of it.' [He said,] 'I hold that she should be given a dowry like that of her peers, with no reduction or excess; she has the inheritance, and upon her is the waiting period of four months and ten days.' He said, 'Some people from Ashja' heard that, and they stood up and said, 'We bear witness that you have judged as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged in the case of a woman of ours called Birwa' bt. Washiq.' Abdullah was never seen so overjoyed at anything as he was that day, except for his acceptance of Islam. Then he said, 'O Allah, if it is correct, it is from You alone, with no partner; if it is wrong, it is from me and from Satan, and Allah and His Messenger are free of it.'"],[2724,"Concerning a man who married a woman and then died without having consummated the marriage or assigned her a dowry, he [Ibn Masud] ruled that she receives the full dowry, the waiting period is upon her, and she inherits. Then Ma'qil b. Sinan stood up and said, 'I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judge likewise in the case of Birwa' bt. Washiq.' Thus the hadith became authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2725,"From the good fortune of a woman is that her proposal is easy, her dowry is easy, and her womb is easy. Urwah said, 'That is, her womb is easy for giving birth.' Urwah said, 'And I say, from my own opinion, one of the first signs of her ill fortune is that her dowry is large.'"],[2726,"Regarding the dowry of the Prophet ﷺ, she said, 'Twelve awqiyah and a nashsh.' I asked, 'What is a nashsh?' She said, 'Half an awqiyah.'"],[2727,"She had been married to Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh, who died in Abyssinia. The Negus married her to the Prophet ﷺ and paid a dowry on his behalf of four thousand, and sent her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with Shurahbil b. Hasanah."],[2728,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, 'Would you like me to marry you to so-and-so?' He said, 'Yes.' And he said to the woman, 'Would you like me to marry you to so-and-so?' She said, 'Yes.' So he married one of them to the other. He did not assign her a dowry, nor give her anything. The man was among those who attended al-Hudaybiyah, and whoever attended al-Hudaybiyah had a share in Khaybar. When death approached him, he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me to so-and-so, and I did not assign her a dowry or give her anything. I call upon you to witness that I give her my share in Khaybar as her dowry.' So she took the share and sold it for one hundred thousand. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The best dowry is the easiest one.'"],[2729,"Among the greatest sins in the sight of Allah are: a man marries a woman, and when he has satisfied his need of her, he divorces her and takes away her dowry; a man hires a worker and then withholds his wages; and another kills an animal in vain."],[2730,"He taught us the sermon of need: 'Praise be to Allah, we praise Him, seek His help and His forgiveness, and seek refuge in Allah from the evils of ourselves. Whomever Allah guides, none can mislead, and whomever He misleads, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' Then he recited three verses: {O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims} [Al Imran 102]; {O mankind, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul and from it created its mate and dispersed from both of them many men and women. And fear Allah, through whom you ask one another, and the wombs. Indeed Allah is ever, over you, an Observer} [An-Nisa 1]; {O you who believe, fear Allah and speak words of appropriate justice. He will amend for you your deeds and forgive you your sins. And whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has certainly attained a great attainment} [Al-Ahzab 71]. Then he mentioned his need. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2731,"When he congratulated someone on marriage, he would say: 'May Allah bless you, and bless upon you, and unite you both in goodness.'"],[2732,"From a man among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar called Basra, he said: I married a virgin woman while she was in her veil. Then I entered upon her and found her pregnant. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “She is entitled to the dower because you deemed her private parts lawful, and the child is a slave for you. When she gives birth, flog her.”"],[2733,"That he married a virgin woman and consummated the marriage with her and found her pregnant. “The Prophet ﷺ made her child a slave belonging to him and separated the two of them.”"],[2734,"“Announce the marriage publicly.”"],[2735,"We escorted a woman from the Ansar to her husband. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Did you have any entertainment with you? For the Ansar love entertainment.”"],[2736,"I said to Muhammad bin Hatib, \"I married two women, and there was no sound in either of them,\" meaning the sound of a drum. So Muhammad said, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The distinction between what is permissible and what is forbidden is the sound of the drum.\""],[2737,"From Abu Ishaq, explained and summarized, upon the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2738,"I entered upon Qaraza b. Ka'b and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari at a wedding, and there were slave girls singing. I said: You are companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and people of Badr, and this is done in your presence? They said: If you wish, stay with us, and if you wish, go. For he permitted us entertainment at weddings and weeping at calamity. Sharik said: I think he said: other than wailing. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2739,"The Prophet ﷺ heard people singing at a wedding of theirs, and he had gifted her a ram. They were reciting in a sheep pen: “And your love is in the gathering, and He knows what is tomorrow.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “No one knows what is tomorrow except Allah.”"],[2740,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, and I excused myself to him, and he accepted my excuse. Then it was revealed to him: {Indeed We have made lawful to you your wives} [al-Ahzab: 50] the verse. She said: I was not lawful for him because I had not emigrated with him, and I was among the released ones."],[2741,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ equipped Fatima with a velvet garment, a water skin, and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fiber.”"],[2742,"That she should fatten me for my entering upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I did not respond to her with any of what she wanted until she fed me cucumber and fresh dates, and I became fat upon that, the best of fatness.”"],[2743,"When one of you acquires a slave girl, a wife, or a riding beast, let him take hold of its forelock and supplicate for blessing, and say: O Allah, I ask You for its good and the good of what it was created upon, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil of what it was created upon. And if it is a camel, let him take hold of the top of its hump."],[2744,"That 'Ali hosted a man and prepared food for him. He said: If only we invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he ate with us. So they invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he came. Then he saw a bed that had been set up in a corner of the house, so he returned. Fatima said: Go back and ask him what made you return, O Messenger of Allah? He went and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is not for a prophet to enter a decorated house.”"],[2745,"«When a man has two wives and he does not treat them fairly, he will come on the Day of Resurrection with one of his sides drooping.»"],[2746,"She said to him: O son of my sister, «The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not favor some of us over others in the length of his stay with us, and seldom did a day pass but he would visit us, drawing near to each wife without engaging in intercourse, until he reached the one whose turn it was and spent the night with her.» And Sawdah bt. Zamʿah said when she grew old and feared that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would separate from her: O Messenger of Allah, my day is for ʿĀʾishah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted that from her. ʿĀʾishah said: Concerning that, Allah, glorified be He, revealed about her and her likes: {And if a woman fears from her husband contempt or evasion} [al-Nisāʾ 4:128]."],[2747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to divide [his time] and be just, and he would say: «O Allah, this is my division in what I possess, so do not blame me for what You possess and I do not possess.» Ismāʿīl al-Qāḍī said: «He means the heart, and this is regarding justice between his wives.»"],[2748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek permission when it was the day of one of us, after [the verse] was revealed: {You may defer whom you will of them and receive to you whom you will} [al-Aḥzāb 33:51]. Muʿādhah said: I said to ʿĀʾishah: What did you used to say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: I used to say: If that were up to me, I would not prefer anyone over myself."],[2749,"I came to al-Ḥīrah and saw them prostrating to a governor of theirs. I said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more worthy of being prostrated to. So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I came to al-Ḥīrah and saw them prostrating to a governor of theirs, and you, Messenger of Allah ﷺ, are more worthy of being prostrated to. He said: «Tell me, if you passed by my grave, would you prostrate to it?» I said: No. He said: «Then do not do so. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command women to prostrate to their husbands because of the right Allah has given them over them.»"],[2750,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the right of the wife of one of us upon him? He said: «That he feed her when he eats, clothe her when he dresses, not strike the face, not revile, and not abandon except within the house.»"],[2751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Do not strike the maidservants of Allah.» Then ʿUmar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, the women have become bold against their husbands. So he permitted striking them. Then many women went around the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about their husbands. The Prophet ﷺ said: «Many women have gone around the family of Muḥammad ﷺ complaining about their husbands. Those are not the best of you.»"],[2752,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah, he said to her: «I sent to the Negus ounces of musk and a garment, and I think he has died, and I think the gift that was sent to him will be returned. When it is returned to me, it is for you—or for all of you?» It was as he said: the Negus died. When the gift was returned to him, he gave each of his wives an ounce of that musk, gave the rest to Umm Salamah, and gave her the garment."],[2753,"From Nahār al-ʿAbdī, who was one of the companions of Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī, from Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī: A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a daughter of his and said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my daughter; she has refused to marry. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: «Obey your father.» She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry until you tell me what the right of the husband over his wife is. He said: The right of the husband over his wife is that if he had a wound and she licked it, she would not have fulfilled his right."],[2754,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so, daughter of so-and-so. He said: «I know you; what is your need?» She said: My need concerns my cousin, so-and-so the devout worshipper. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I know him.» She said: He has proposed to me. Tell me what the right of the husband over the wife is, for if it is something I can bear, I will marry him, and if I cannot bear it, I will not marry. He said: Part of the right of the husband over the wife is that if his nostrils flowed with blood, pus, and ichor, and she licked it with her tongue, she would not have fulfilled his right. If it were proper for a human being to prostrate to a human being, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband when he enters upon her because of the excellence Allah has given him over her. She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will not marry as long as I remain in this world."],[2755,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ for some need, and he said: «O this one, are you married?» I said: Yes. He said: «How are you toward him?» She said: I do not fall short except in what I am unable to do. He said: «Then where are you in relation to him? For he is your Paradise and your Hell.» This is how Mālik b. Anas, Ḥammād b. Zayd, and al-Darāwardī narrated it from Yaḥyā b. Saʿīd, and it is authentic, but they did not include it."],[2756,"«It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to give permission in her husband's house while he is unwilling, nor to go out while he is unwilling, nor to obey anyone therein, nor to be harsh toward him, nor to abandon his bed, nor to strike him. If he is more wrong, let her come to him until she pleases him. If he accepts, then it is good and blessed, and Allah accepts her excuse and makes her argument successful, and there is no sin upon him. But if he refuses to be pleased with her, she has indeed conveyed her excuse before Allah.»"],[2757,"«Allah does not look at a woman who does not thank her husband while she cannot do without him.»"],[2758,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O women, give in charity, even from your jewelry, for indeed you comprise the majority of the inhabitants of Hell.\" A woman who was not among the elite women asked, \"Why are we the majority of the inhabitants of Hell, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Because you curse frequently and show ingratitude towards your husbands. I have not seen anyone more deficient in intelligence and religious commitment than you. A wise man could be led astray by some of you.\" They asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the deficiency in our intelligence and religious commitment?\" He said, \"As for the deficiency in intelligence, the testimony of two women is equal to that of one man. As for the deficiency in religious commitment, one of you may stay without praying for many days and nights, not prostrating to Allah.\""],[2759,"He heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: «Indeed, the wicked are the people of the Fire.» They said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the wicked? He said: «Women.» They said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers, daughters, and sisters? He said: «Yes, but when they are given, they do not give thanks, and when they are tested, they do not have patience.»"],[2760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Do not strike the female servants of Allah.» Then Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, the women have become defiant toward their husbands. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted striking them. He said: Then seventy women surrounded the family of Muhammad ﷺ, all of them complaining about their husbands. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «Those are not the best of you.»"],[2761,"About striking women. Then they complained about them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he allowed them to strike them. Then he said: Tonight seventy women surrounded the family of Muhammad ﷺ, all of them having been struck. Yahya said: And I think that al-Qasim said: Then it was said to them afterwards: «And the best of you will never strike.»"],[2762,"I met my maternal uncle carrying the banner. I said: Where do you intend? He said: «The Prophet ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, and he ordered me to strike his neck.»"],[2763,"Some people passed by us leaving, so we said to them: Where are you going? They said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to a man who has intercourse with his father's wife, to kill him."],[2764,"I was searching for a lost camel of mine during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While I was wandering among tents, suddenly I saw a group of riders and horsemen come and surround a man. They did not ask him or speak to him until they struck his neck. When they left, I asked about him. They said: He had consummated marriage with his father's wife. Its chain is good."],[2765,"Ghaylan b. Salamah al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while he had ten wives, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to take four of them. Thus the earlier companions of Sa'id narrated it: Yazid b. Zuray', Isma'il b. 'Ulayyah, Ghundar, and the leading memorizers among the people of Basra. Imam Muslim b. al-Hajjaj ruled that this hadith is one in which Ma'mar erred in Basra. If a reliable narrator outside the Basrans narrated it from him, we would judge it authentic. I found that Sufyan al-Thawri, 'Abd al-Rahman b. Muhammad al-Muharibi, and 'Isa b. Yunus—all three of them Kufans—narrated it from Ma'mar."],[2766,"That Ghaylan b. Salamah accepted Islam while he had ten wives, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to choose four of them."],[2767,"Ghaylan b. Salamah al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while he had ten wives, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to choose four of them and leave the rest. And thus I found the hadith among the people of al-Yamamah from Ma'mar."],[2768,"Ghaylan b. Salamah al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while he had eight wives, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to choose four of them. And thus I found the hadith among the imams of Khurasan from Ma'mar. Ahmad b. Muhammad is a liar."],[2769,"Ghaylan b. Salamah al-Thaqafi accepted Islam while he had ten wives. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to keep four and separate from the rest. My judgment leads me to the conclusion that Ma'mar b. Rashid narrated it in both ways: he sent it once and connected it once. The evidence for this is that those who connected it from him among the people of Basra also sent it. Yet connection is preferable to transmission, for the addition of a trustworthy narrator is accepted, and Allah knows best."],[2770,"A man from the people of Kufa came to 'Amr b. Shu'ayb and said, 'Aren't you amazed that al-Hasan says: The fornicator who has been flogged may marry none but a flogged woman like him?' 'Amr said, 'What amazes you about that? Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated it to us from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. And 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr used to proclaim it publicly.'"],[2771,"A man among the Muslims asked permission of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ regarding a woman called Umm Muharwil who used to commit fornication and stipulated that he would spend on her. He asked permission of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ concerning her and mentioned her situation to him. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited: {The fornicator marries not but a fornicatress or an idolatress} [al-Nur 3]. And it was revealed: {The fornicatress none marries her except a fornicator or an idolater} [al-Nur 3]."],[2772,"Indeed, it is not marriage, but rather sexual intercourse. Only a person who commits adultery or practices polytheism engages in it."],[2773,"When a slave marries without the permission of his master, he is a fornicator."],[2774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Ali: O 'Ali, do not follow a glance with another glance. The first is for you, but the second is not for you."],[2775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a military expedition when he saw a woman who was heavily pregnant. He said, 'Perhaps her companion has had intercourse with her.' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I was determined to curse him with a curse that would enter the grave with him. How can he make him an heir when he is not lawful for him, and how can he employ him as a servant when he is not lawful for him?'"],[2776,"He said regarding the captives of Awtas: 'A pregnant woman is not to be sexually approached until she gives birth, nor a woman who is not pregnant until she has menstruated once.'"],[2777,"Ibn 'Umar, may Allah forgive him, made a mistake. This tribe of the Ansar, who were idolaters, lived alongside this tribe of the Jews, who were People of the Book. They considered the Jews to have superiority over them, so they imitated many of their practices. Among the practices of the People of the Book was that they did not approach women except in one position, which was the most concealing for the woman. This tribe of the Ansar adopted that from them. Meanwhile, this tribe of Quraysh used to spread women in a detestable manner, deriving pleasure from them facing forward and backward and lying on their backs. When the Emigrants came to Madinah, a man among them married a woman from the Ansar and went to do with her as he was accustomed. She objected and said, 'We are only approached in one position, so do that, otherwise stay away from me.' Their matter became widely known and reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: {Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth as you will} [al-Baqarah 223]."],[2778,"Three pronouncements of divorce were referred back to one during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'Yes.'"],[2779,"Divorce during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and the first two years of 'Umar's caliphate: a threefold divorce counted as one. Then 'Umar said, 'People have become hasty in a matter in which they had been given respite. If only we could enforce it upon them.' So he enforced it upon them."],[2780,"Allah has not made anything lawful more hateful to Him than divorce."],[2781,"He is not one of us who corrupts a wife against her husband or a slave against his master."],[2782,"When the Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsah, he was commanded to take her back, so he took her back."],[2783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ divorced Hafsah, then took her back."],[2784,"I had a wife whom I loved, and Umar disliked her. Umar said: Divorce her. I refused. He mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'Obey your father and divorce her.' So I divorced her."],[2785,"A man came to Abu al-Darda' and said: My mother kept pressing me until I married, and now she orders me to divorce her, insisting on that. He said: I am not the one to command you to disobey your mother, nor am I the one to command you to divorce your wife. But if you wish, I will tell you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The parent is the middle gate of Paradise, so preserve that gate if you wish or lose it.'"],[2786,"Three matters in which seriousness is serious and jest is serious: marriage, divorce, and taking back."],[2787,"Allah has overlooked for my community mistakes, forgetfulness, and what they are compelled to do."],[2788,"There is no divorce or manumission in a state of closure."],[2789,"There is no divorce or manumission in a state of closure."],[2790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not tell you about the borrowed billy goat?' They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'He is the one who makes lawful. Allah cursed the one who makes lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah cursed the one who makes lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful.'"],[2791,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Shall I not tell you about the borrowed billy goat?' They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'He is the one who makes lawful.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah cursed the one who makes lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful.'"],[2792,"About a man who divorced his wife three times, then his brother married her without his instigation to make her lawful for his brother—does she become lawful for the first? He said: 'No. Marriage is out of desire. We used to consider this fornication at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2793,"He divorced his wife irrevocably during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I asked the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he said: 'What did you intend by that?' He said: I intended one divorce. He said: 'By Allah?' He said: By Allah. He said: 'It is as you intended.'"],[2794,"That Rukana b. 'Abd Yazid divorced his wife Suhayma with an irrevocable divorce. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have divorced my wife Suhayma with an irrevocable divorce. By Allah, I only intended one.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned her to him. Then he divorced her a second time during the time of 'Umar and a third time during the time of 'Uthman. The hadith is authentic by this narration, for Imam al-Shafi'i mastered it and preserved it from his family. And al-Sa'ib b. 'Abd Yazid is Abu al-Shafi' b. al-Sa'ib, and he is the brother of Rukana b. 'Abd Yazid. And Muhammad b. 'Ali b. Shafi', the paternal uncle of al-Shafi'i, was the shaykh of Quraysh in his time. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2795,"Any woman who asks her husband for divorce without a strong reason, Allah forbids her from smelling the fragrance of Paradise."],[2796,"A woman became Muslim during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and then married. Her husband came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I became Muslim along with her, and she knew of my Islam along with her.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took her away from her other husband and returned her to her first husband."],[2797,"The Prophet ﷺ returned his daughter Zaynab to her husband Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' based on the first marriage and did not initiate anything new. Sahih."],[2798,"From 'A'isha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, his daughter Zaynab left Makkah with Kinana or the son of Kinana. They went out in pursuit of her, and Habbar b. al-Aswad caught up with her. He kept stabbing her camel with his spear until he made her fall, and she miscarried what was in her womb and lost blood. Banu Hashim and Banu Umayya disputed over her. Banu Umayya said, 'We have more right to her,' because she was married to their cousin Abu al-'As. She stayed with Hind bt. 'Utba b. Rabi'a, and Hind said to her, 'This is because of your father.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Zayd b. Haritha, 'Will you go and bring me Zaynab?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Take my ring,' and gave it to him. Zayd set out, made his camel kneel, and kept being gentle until he met a shepherd. He said, 'For whom do you graze?' He said, 'For Abu al-'As.' He said, 'For whom are these sheep?' He said, 'For Zaynab bt. Muhammad.' He walked with him a little, then said to him, 'Would you like me to give you something to give to her, and do not mention it to anyone?' He said, 'Yes.' He gave him the ring. The shepherd went, brought in his sheep, and gave her the ring. She recognized it and said, 'Who gave you this?' He said, 'A man.' She said, 'Where did you leave him?' He said, 'At such and such a place.' She remained silent until night fell, then she went out to him. When she came to him, he said to her, 'Ride in front of me on his camel.' She said, 'No, but you ride in front of me.' So he rode and she rode behind him until she came. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, 'She is the best of my daughters; she was afflicted because of me.' That reached 'Ali b. al-Husayn, so he went to 'Urwa and said, 'What is this hadith that has reached me from you which you narrate, in which you diminish the right of Fatima?' He said, 'By Allah, I would not love to have what is between the east and the west while I diminish Fatima's right that is hers. As for after this, you have it that I will never narrate it again.' 'Urwa said, 'This was before the revelation of the verse: Call them by their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah [al-Ahzab: 5].'"],[2799,"When Hilal b. Umayya accused his wife, it was said to him, 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will surely flog you eighty lashes.' He said, 'Allah is more just than that He would flog me eighty lashes when He knows that I saw until I was certain and heard until I was sure. No, by Allah, He will never flog me.' Then the verse of mutual cursing was revealed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them both when the verse was revealed and said, 'Allah knows that one of you is lying. Is there any of you who will repent?' Hilal said, 'By Allah, I am truthful.' He said, 'Swear by Allah, besides whom there is no deity, that I am truthful,' saying that four times, then 'If I am lying, then upon me be the curse of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Stop him at the fifth, for it is decisive.' Then she swore, then said four times, 'By Allah, besides whom there is no deity, he is indeed one of the liars,' and 'If he is truthful, then upon her be the wrath of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Stop her at the fifth, for it is decisive.' She hesitated and was about to confess, then said, 'I will not disgrace my people.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If she gives birth to a child with dark eyelids, wide black eyes, full buttocks, thick thighs, and slender legs, then he belongs to the one she was accused with. And if she gives birth to a fair, curly-haired, smooth-haired child, then he belongs to Hilal b. Umayya.' She gave birth to a child matching the description of the accused man. Ayyub said, and Muhammad b. Sirin said, 'The man whom Hilal b. Umayya accused her with was Sharik b. Sahma', and he was the brother of al-Bara' b. Malik, the brother of Anas b. Malik through his mother, and his mother was black, and Sharik used to stay at Hilal's house and be with him.'"],[2800,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ say when the verse of mutual cursing was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Any woman who introduces into a people someone who is not of them, she has nothing to do with Allah, and Allah will never admit her to His Paradise. And any man who denies his child while looking at him, Allah will veil Himself from him and disgrace him before the heads of all creatures, the first and the last.'"],[2801,"I was a man who had been given such ability in sexual intercourse with women as no one else had been given. When Ramadan entered, I made a declaration of zihar against my wife, fearing that I might have intercourse with her at night and continue doing so, unable to stop until morning overtook me. While she was serving me one night, something of her became visible to me, and I jumped on her. When morning came, I went to my people and told them my story. I said, 'Come with me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' They said, 'No, by Allah, we will not go with you. We fear that Qur'an will be revealed concerning us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will say something about us whose shame will remain upon us. Go yourself and do what you think best.' So I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him my story. He said, 'Are you that one?' I said, 'I am that one. So judge according to the ruling of Allah, for I am patient and seeking reward.' He said, 'Free a slave.' I struck the side of my neck with my hand and said, 'By the One who sent you with truth, I do not possess anything other than this.' He said, 'Fast two consecutive months.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, did what happened to me occur except during fasting?' He said, 'Then feed sixty poor people.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with truth, we spent this night hungry, finding no supper.' He said, 'Go to the collector of the sadaqa of Banu Zurayq, let him give it to you, and feed from it a wasq to sixty poor people, and use the rest for your family.' I came to my people and said, 'I found hardship with you.'"],[2802,"That Salman b. Sakhr al-Ansari made his wife like his mother's back to him, then he mentioned the hadith similarly. This is a sound chain according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it; according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2803,"That a man came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had made zihar against his wife and then had intercourse with her. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I made zihar against my wife and then had intercourse with her before I made expiation.' He said, 'What led you to that, may Allah have mercy on you?' He said, 'I saw her anklet in the moonlight.' He said, 'Do not approach her until you do what Allah, Exalted, has commanded.' Its witness is the hadith of Isma'il b. Muslim from 'Amr b. Dinar. The two shaykhs did not use Isma'il or al-Hakam b. Aban as authorities, except that al-Hakam b. Aban is truthful. Al-'Adani is not reliable."],[2804,"That a man made zihar against his wife, then he saw her anklet in the moonlight and it pleased him, so he had intercourse with her. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, 'Allah, Exalted, said: before they touch one another [al-Mujadila: 3].' He said, 'That already happened.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Refrain until you make expiation.' Isma'il is weak."],[2805,"There is no divorce for one who does not possess, and no manumission for one who does not possess."],[2806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"There is no divorce before marriage.\" Sahih."],[2807,"Allah ﷻ said: {O you who believe, when you marry believing women and then divorce them} [Al-Ahzab: 49], and He did not say: \"When you divorce believing women and then marry them.\""],[2808,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"The divorce of a slave woman is two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles.\" Abu 'Asim said: I mentioned it to Muzahir b. Aslam and said: Narrate to me as you narrated to Ibn Jurayj. Muzahir narrated to me from al-Qasim from 'A'ishah from the Prophet ﷺ: \"The divorce of a slave woman is two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles,\" similar to what Muzahir b. Aslam narrated. He is a shaykh from the people of Basra whom none of our earlier scholars mentioned with criticism, so the hadith is sahih, but they did not include it in the two Sahihs. A hadith contradicting it has been narrated from Ibn 'Abbas. Sahih."],[2809,"\"Yes, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged that.\" It contradicts the hadith of 'Ali."],[2810,"I said to Ayyub: Do you know anyone who holds the view of al-Hasan regarding \"your affair is in your hand\" that it is three? He said: No, except something Qatadah narrated to us from Kathir, the freed slave of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it. Ayyub said: Kathir came to us and he asked him, and he said: I never narrated this. I mentioned it to Qatadah, and he said: \"Yes, but he forgot.\""],[2811,"The wife of Thabit b. Qays obtained a khul' from him, \"and the Prophet ﷺ made her waiting period one menstrual cycle.\""],[2812,"The wife of Thabit b. Qays obtained a khul' from him, \"and the Prophet ﷺ made her waiting period one menstrual cycle.\""],[2813,"She wanted to free slaves, a husband and a wife. She asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"and he ordered her to begin with the man before the woman.\""],[2814,"She wanted to become Muslim. She came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: My daughter is weaned. Rafi' said: My daughter. The Prophet ﷺ said to Rafi': \"Sit aside,\" and said to his wife: \"Sit aside.\" He then seated the child between them and said: \"Call her.\" The child inclined to her mother. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Allah, guide her.\" She inclined to her father, and he took her."],[2815,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when a man from Yemen came to him and said: Three men from Yemen came to 'Ali disputing about a child born after they had intercourse with a woman during a single period of purity. He said to two of them: \"Give the child willingly to this one.\" They said: No. Then he said to two of them: \"Give the child willingly to this one.\" They said: No. Then he said to two of them: \"Give the child willingly to this one.\" They said: No. Then he said: \"You are quarrelsome partners. I will cast lots among you, and whoever wins the lot gets the child and owes his two companions two-thirds of the blood money.\" He cast lots among them and gave the child to the one who won. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars or his premolars appeared. \"The two shaykhs agreed to abandon using al-Ajlah b. 'Abd Allah al-Kindi as evidence, and they only criticized him for a single hadith from 'Abd Allah b. Buraydah, and three trustworthy narrators followed him in that hadith. So this hadith is therefore sahih, but they did not include it in the two Sahihs.\" This hadith is indeed sahih."],[2816,"A woman said: Messenger of Allah, my womb is a vessel to this son of mine, my breasts, a water-skin for him, and my lap a guard for him, yet his father has divorced me, and wants to take him away from me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You have more right to him as long as you do not marry. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2276)"],[2817,"My maternal aunt was divorced three times, so she went out to cut down her palm trees. A man met her and forbade her, so she came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Go out and cut them down; perhaps you may give charity from it or do good.\""],[2818,"Her husband went out in search of some of his workers and was killed at the edge of al-Qadum. Hammad said: It is a watering place. She said: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned my situation to him and mentioned moving to my brothers. She said: He gave me permission. When I had passed by, he called me and said: \"Stay in your house until the term reaches its appointed time.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[2819,"that she heard Furay'ah bt. Malik, sister of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, say: \"My husband went out in search of some slaves of his, and they caught up with him at the edge of al-Qadum and killed him. His death notification came to me while I was in a house far from the houses of my family. I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'The death notification of my husband has come to me while I am in a house far from the houses of my family. He did not leave me any maintenance or wealth, and the dwelling is not mine. If I were to move to my brothers and family, it would be easier for me in some of my affairs.' He said: 'Move.' When I went out to the mosque or the room, he called me, or ordered that I be called for him, and said: 'Stay in the house in which the death notification of your husband came to you until the prescribed period reaches its term.' So she observed her waiting period in it, four months and ten days.\" She said: \"Then Uthman b. Affan sent for me, and I went to him and related it to him, and he adopted it.\""],[2820,"that she said: \"A woman was divorced and remained for twenty-three nights, then she gave birth to her child. She then came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said to her: 'Marry.'\""],[2821,"that she was married to al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, but she disliked him and he was harsh toward women. She said to al-Zubayr: 'O Abu Abd Allah, relieve me with a divorce.' She said that was when she felt labor pains. He said: 'What benefit is it to you if I divorce you one divorce and then take you back?' She said: 'I find myself relieved by that.' He said: 'Then he divorced her one divorce and went out.' She said to her slave girl: 'Close the doors.' She then gave birth to a girl. Al-Zubayr came and was given the good news, and he said: 'The daughter of Abu Mu'ayt deceived me.' Then he went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he separated her from him."],[2822,"Do not make ambiguous for us the Sunnah of our Prophet Muhammad ﷺ regarding the mother of a child when her master dies: her waiting period is four months and ten days."],[2823,"While I was sleeping, two men came to me, took me by my upper arms, and brought me to a rugged mountain. They said to me: 'Climb.' I said: 'I cannot.' They said: 'We will make it easy for you.' So I climbed until I was on level ground of the mountain, and suddenly I heard loud voices. I said: 'What are these voices?' They said: 'This is the howling of the people of the Fire.' Then they took me further, and I saw people suspended by their Achilles tendons, their cheeks split, and blood flowing from their cheeks. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are those who break their fast before the time to break their fast.' Then they took me further, and I saw people most swollen, most foul smelling, and worst in appearance. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the male and female fornicators.' Then they took me further, and I saw women whose breasts were being bitten by snakes. I said: 'What is the matter with these?' He said: 'These are those who deny their children their milk.' Then they took me further, and I saw boys playing between two rivers. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are the offspring of the believers.' Then a high place was shown to me, and I saw three men drinking from their wine. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'These are Ja'far b. Abi Talib, Zayd b. Harithah, and Abdullah b. Rawahah.' Then another high place was shown to me, and I saw three men. I said: 'Who are these?' He said: 'Abraham, Moses, and Jesus (peace be upon them), waiting for you.'"],[2824,"that his father Thabit b. Qays separated from Jamilah bt. Abdullah b. Ubayy while she was pregnant with Muhammad. When she gave birth to him, she swore that she would not nurse him with her milk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for him, spat into his mouth, and rubbed his palate with a ripe date, and named him Muhammad, and said: 'Take him around, for Allah will provide for him.' So I brought him on the first, second, and third day, and there was an Arab woman asking about Thabit b. Qays. I said: 'What do you want from him? I am Thabit.' She said: 'I saw in my dream as if I were nursing a son of his called Muhammad.' He said: 'I am Thabit, and this is my son Muhammad.' He said: 'And her breastplate was dripping with her milk.'"],[2825,"Ata': If she wishes, she may observe her waiting period with her family and reside in her bequest, and if she wishes, she may go out, according to the saying of Allah Almighty: {There is no blame upon you for what they do} [al-Baqarah 234]. Ata' said: 'Then the inheritance came and abrogated the residence, so she observes her waiting period wherever she wishes.'"],[2826,"A poor man came to some of the Ansar and said: 'My master forces me into prostitution.' So concerning that it was revealed: {Do not compel your slave girls to prostitution}."],[2827,"Whoever frees a slave, Allah will free from the Fire for every limb of his a limb of his."],[2828,"Whoever frees a slave or a servant, it will be his ransom from the Fire, limb for limb."],[2829,"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with no addition or omission. He became angry and said: 'One of you has his mushaf hanging in his house, and he adds and omits.' We said: 'We did not mean that; we meant that you narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding a companion of ours who had obligated (i.e., earned) the Fire. He said: \"Free on his behalf; Allah will free from the Fire for every limb of his a limb of his.\"' Arif—this is a nickname for Abdullah b. al-Daylami. Sahih."],[2830,"This old man—meaning Wathilah—narrated to me. I said: 'What did he narrate to you?' He said: 'He narrated to me: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk, when a group from Banu Sulaym came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, our companion has obligated (the Fire).\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Free on his behalf; Allah will free from the Fire, for every limb of his, a limb of his.\"' Thus the hadith of Wathilah is sahih according to the criteria of the two shaykhs through these narrations. Muslim has already reported its wording from the hadith of Abu Hurayrah regarding a Muslim man freeing a Muslim man. Sahih."],[2831,"Whoever frees a Muslim will have his ransom from the Fire, for every limb of this one a limb of that one."],[2832,"My brother bequeathed to me a portion of his wealth, so I met Abu al-Darda' and said: My brother has bequeathed to me a portion of his wealth, so where should I put it? Among the poor, the needy, or the emigrants? He said: As for me, if I were in your place, I would not overlook the mujahidin, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The likeness of one who frees a slave at the time of death is like the likeness of one who gives a gift when he is full.'"],[2833,"I freed a slave-girl of mine, and the Prophet ﷺ came in to me, so I informed him of her emancipation. He said: 'If you had given her to your maternal uncles, it would have been greater for your reward.'"],[2834,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, while Sa'd was a slave belonging to him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased with his service: 'O Abu Bakr, free Sa'd.' He said: O Messenger of Allah, we have no one besides him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The men are coming to you, the men are coming to you.'"],[2835,"Umm Salamah said to me: I will free you, but I stipulate that you serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as you live. He (the narrator) said: I said: 'Even if you did not stipulate it, I would not part from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as I live.' He said: 'So she freed me and stipulated that I serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as I live.'"],[2836,"A man said: Should I free a slave on behalf of my son, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'Yes.'"],[2837,"Whoever owns a forbidden blood relative, he is free."],[2838,"Whoever owns a forbidden blood relative, he is free."],[2839,"'The child of adultery is the worst of the three.' Abu Hurayrah said: 'To be provided with a whip in the way of Allah is more beloved to me than to free a child of adultery.'"],[2840,"'The child of adultery is the worst of the three.'"],[2841,"That Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'To be provided with a whip in the way of Allah is more beloved to me than to free a child of adultery,' and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The child of adultery is the worst of the three,' and 'The dead is punished by the weeping of the living.' A'ishah said: May Allah have mercy on Abu Hurayrah; he heard wrongly and thus erred. As for his saying, 'To be provided with a whip in the way of Allah is more beloved to me than to free a child of adultery,' when the verse descended: 'But he has not attempted the steep path. And what can make you know what is the steep path?' (al-Balad 11-12), it was said: O Messenger of Allah, we have nothing to free except that one of us has a black slave-girl who serves him and works for him. If we commanded them to commit adultery and then they brought children, we would free them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'To be provided with a whip in the way of Allah is more beloved to me than to command adultery and then free the child.' Salamah: Muslim did not use him as evidence; he was considered trustworthy but weakened by Ibn Rahawayh."],[2842,"A slave-girl came to Umar b. al-Khattab and said: My master accused me, so he made me sit on a fire until my private part burned. Umar said to her: Did he see that from you? She said: No. He said: Did you confess to him about anything? She said: No. Umar said: Bring him to me. When Umar saw the man, he said: Do you punish with the punishment of Allah? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I suspected her in my mind. He said: Did you see that from her? The man said: No. He said: Did she confess to it? He said: No. He said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A slave is not to be retaliated against by his master, nor a parent by his child,' I would have retaliated against you from her. Then he brought him out and flogged him with a hundred lashes, and said to the slave-girl: Go, for you are free for the sake of Allah; you are the freedwoman of Allah and His Messenger."],[2843,"A group of captives from Khawlan arrived, and ‘A’ishah had an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Isma‘il. Then captives from Yemen arrived, and she wanted to free one of them, but the Prophet ﷺ forbade her. Then captives from Mudar arrived – I think he said from Banu al-‘Anbar – and he commanded her to free one. Shu‘bah concurred with him, from ‘Ubayd b. al-Hasan. The hadith is authentic."],[2844,"‘A’ishah had an obligation to free a slave from the descendants of Isma‘il. Captives from Banu al-‘Anbar were brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: “Free one from Banu al-‘Anbar or from Banu Lihyan, but do not free one from Banu al-Khawlan.”"],[2845,"Three are entitled to Allah’s help: the mukatib who intends to pay, the mujahid in the path of Allah, and the one who marries intending chastity."],[2846,"“Whoever helps a mujahid in the path of Allah, or a warrior, or a debtor in his hardship, or a mukatab in his ransom, Allah will shade him in His shade on the Day when there is no shade except His shade.”"],[2847,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, teach me something that will admit me to Paradise.” He said: “You have shortened the speech but broadened the request. Free the person and release the neck.” He said: “Are they not one and the same?” He said: “Freeing the person is to single out for freeing, and releasing the neck is to help with its price, and the milch animal given as a gift, and the return upon the wronged relative. If you cannot do that, then feed the hungry, give drink to the thirsty, enjoin good and forbid evil. If you cannot do that, then restrain your tongue except from good.”"],[2848,"To plant for them five hundred offshoots, and when they take root, I would be free. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: “Plant and stipulate for them, and when you intend to plant, notify me.” He came and began planting except one which I planted with my own hand. They all took root except that one."],[2849,"“Any mukatab who contracted for a thousand uqiyyahs and paid all but ten uqiyyahs is a slave, and any mukatab who contracted for a hundred dinars and paid all but ten dinars is a slave.”"],[2850,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled concerning the mukatab that he is to be [legally] killed for the blood money of a free person according to the amount he has paid.” Yahya said: ‘Ikrimah said from Ibn ‘Abbas: “The hadd punishment of a slave is inflicted upon him.”"],[2851,"“The mukatab pays according to the amount that has been freed from him by the reckoning of a free person, and what remains enslaved by the reckoning of a slave.”"],[2852,"“When a mukatab commits a hadd offense or inherits an inheritance, he inherits according to the amount he has been freed, and the punishment is inflicted upon him according to the amount that has been freed from him.”"],[2853,"I was leading it at al-Bayda’ or al-Abwa’. She said: “Who is this?” I said: “I am Nabhan.” She said: “I have left the remainder of your mukatabah to my nephew Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah; I helped him with it in his marriage.” He said: I said: “No, by Allah, I will never pay it to him.” She said: “If your oath is that you will enter upon me or see me, then by Allah you will never see me. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘When the mukatab has what he can pay, then veil yourself from him.’”"],[2854,"O Messenger of Allah, a man from the polytheists accepts Islam at the hands of a Muslim man. He said: “He has more right to him in his life and his death.”"],[2855,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a man who becomes Muslim at the hands of another man, and he said, \"He is more entitled to his life and his death.\""],[2856,"\"I witnessed, as a boy with my paternal uncles, the pact of al-Muṭayyabīn, and it would not please me to have red camels in exchange for breaking it.\""],[2857,"\"There is no alliance in Islam, and whatever alliance existed in the pre-Islamic era, Islam only increases it in strength.\""],[2858,"We learned the Qur'an in this mosque, meaning the mosque of al-Baṣrah, and we used to sit in circles. It is as if I am looking at him between two white garments, and from him I took this surah: {Recite in the name of your Lord who created} [al-ʿAlaq: 1]. He said: It was the first surah revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[2859,"The first surah to be revealed was {Recite in the name of your Lord who created}."],[2860,"The first thing of the Qur'an to be revealed was {Recite in the name of your Lord who created}."],[2861,"That you took al-Anfāl, which is one of the Mathānī, and al-Barā'ah, which is one of the Mi'īn, and you joined them together, and you did not write between them the line 'Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm', and you placed them among the seven long surahs. What led you to do that? ʿUthmān said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go through times when surahs of numerous verses were revealed to him, and when something was revealed to him, he would call one of those who used to write for him and say, \"Put this in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned.\" And a verse would be revealed to him and he would say, \"Put this in the surah in which such-and-such is mentioned.\" Al-Anfāl was among the first of what was revealed in Madinah, and Barā'ah was among the last of the Qur'an, and its story was similar to its story. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away without clarifying to us that it was part of it. For that reason, I joined them together and did not write between them the line 'Bismillāh al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm'."],[2862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr, \"Whoever kills a killed person will have such-and-such.\" As for the elders, they remained steadfast under the banners, but the young men rushed to killing and spoils. The elders said to the young men, \"Include us with you, for we were a support for you, and if something had befallen you, you would have come to us.\" They refused, so they brought their dispute to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Then {They ask you about the spoils of war} [al-Anfāl: 1] was revealed, and the spoils were divided among them equally."],[2863,"\"Allah sent down the Qur'an to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree, and whenever Allah willed to reveal something from it, He revealed it, or to bring about something from it on earth, He brought it about.\""],[2864,"Abū Bakr and ʿUthmān, the two sons of Abī Shaybah, narrated to us; Jarīr narrated to us from Manṣūr from Saʿīd b. Jubayr from Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Indeed, We sent it down on the Night of Decree} [al-Qadr: 1]. He said: The Qur'an was sent down all at once on the Night of Decree to the lowest heaven, and it was at the positions of the stars, and Allah used to send it down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ piece by piece. He said: And they said: {Why was the Qur'an not sent down to him all at once? Thus, that We may strengthen your heart thereby, and We have arranged it in a measured order} [al-Furqān: 32]."],[2865,"The Qur'an was sent down all at once to the lowest heaven on the Night of Decree, then it was sent down after that over twenty years: {And they do not come to you with an argument except that We bring you the truth and the best explanation} [al-Furqān: 33] and {And a Qur'an which We have divided so that you may recite it to the people at intervals, and We have sent it down in stages} [al-Isrā': 106]."],[2866,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received a revelation, none of us could even raise their gaze towards him until the revelation had been completed.\""],[2867,"\"The Qur'an was separated from the Remembrance and placed in the House of Might in the lowest heaven, then Jibrīl ﷺ began to send it down upon the Prophet ﷺ and recite it in a measured manner.\""],[2868,"Disputing about the Quran is disbelief."],[2869,"Quarreling about the Quran is disbelief."],[2870,"The Quran was sent down in three modes."],[2871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite Surah Ha-Mim. I went to the mosque in the evening and a group sat with me. I said to a man in the group: Recite to me. He recited passages I did not read. I asked: Who taught you? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me. We went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. There was a man with him. I said: They disagreed in our recitation. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed and he felt displeased when I mentioned the disagreement. He said: 'Those before you were destroyed by disagreement.' Then Ali whispered to me. Ali said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands each of you to recite as he was taught. We left, each man reciting passages the other did not read."],[2872,"In it: We went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and there was a man with him. Zirr said: They identify him, meaning Ali."],[2873,"Recitation is seven. Sulayman said: Meaning not to disagree with people by your opinion in following."],[2874,"We recited the Mufassal surahs in Makkah for years without 'O you who believe' in it."],[2875,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Allah commanded me to recite the Quran to you.' He recited: {Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book and the polytheists...} [al-Bayyinah 1]. From its description: If the son of Adam asked for a valley of wealth and I gave it, he would ask for a second. If I gave him a second, he would ask for a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. Allah turns to whoever repents. The religion with Allah is the Hanifiyyah, not Judaism or Christianity. Whoever does good will never be denied reward."],[2876,"From Nubayh al-Anazi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: While I was reciting a verse from the Book of Allah ﷻ as I walked on a road in Madinah, a man called from behind me: Follow Ibn Abbas. He was Amir al-Mu'minin Umar. I said: I follow you based on Ubayy b. Kab. He said: Did he teach you as I heard you recite? I said: Yes. He said: Send a messenger with me. He said: Go with him to Ubayy b. Kab and see if Ubayy recites like that. I went with his messenger to Ubayy b. Kab. I said: O Ubayy, I recited a verse from the Book of Allah and Umar b. al-Khattab called from behind: Follow Ibn Abbas. I said: I follow you based on Ubayy b. Kab. He sent his messenger with me. Did you teach it to me as I recited? Ubayy said: Yes. The messenger returned to him. I went about my business. Umar went to Ubayy. I found that he had finished washing his head while his slave girl was combing his beard with a comb. Ubayy said: Welcome, Amir al-Mu'minin. Have you come as a visitor or seeking a need? Umar said: Seeking a need. He sat with two servants until he finished his beard and she combed the right side of his forelock, then the left. When finished, he turned to Umar and said: What is the need of Amir al-Mu'minin? Umar said: O Ubayy, why do you make people despair? Ubayy said: Amir al-Mu'minin, I received the Quran from Jibril while it was fresh. Umar said: By Allah, you will not stop and I will not be patient, three times, then he stood and left."],[2877,"He used to recite: {When those who disbelieved put in their hearts pride, the pride of ignorance} [al-Fath 26] and if you had been as zealous as they were, the Sacred Mosque would have been corrupted. {So Allah sent down His tranquility upon His Messenger} [al-Fath 26]. This reached Umar and he was upset. He sent for him while he was treating a camel of his with tar. He entered upon him and called people from his companions, including Zayd b. Thabit. He said: Who recites Surah al-Fath among you? Zayd recited according to our reading today. Umar was harsh with him. Ubayy said: May I speak? He said: Speak. You know that I used to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ and he would teach me while you were at the door. If you wish that I teach people as he taught me, I will, otherwise I will not teach a single letter as long as I live. He said: Teach the people."],[2878,"I came to Madinah to learn knowledge. When I entered the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the people were in circles talking. I kept going until I reached a circle with a pale man wearing two garments as if he had arrived from a journey. I heard him say: The companions of the pact have perished, by the Lord of the Kabah, and I do not grieve for them, saying it three times. I sat with him and he talked as was decreed for him, then he stood. I asked about him. They said: This is the master of the people, Ubayy b. Kab. I followed him to his house. His house was shabby, his clothing worn, his appearance poor, all similar. I greeted him and he returned the greeting. He asked: From which people are you? I said: From Iraq. He said: The most questioning, and he became angry. I faced the qiblah, knelt on my knees, raised my hands like this, and stretched my arms. I said: O Allah, we complain about them to You. We spend our provisions, exhaust our bodies, and groom our mounts seeking knowledge. When we meet them, they frown at us and speak harshly. Ubayy wept and began to placate me, saying: Woe to you, I did not mean that. Then Ubayy said: I promise you, if I live until Friday, I will speak what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ without fearing the blame of any critic. I left him and waited for Friday. On Thursday, I went out for an errand and found the roads full of people. Whichever street I took, people met me. I asked: What is the matter? They said: We think you are a stranger. I said: Yes. They said: The master of the Muslims, Ubayy b. Kab, has died. I met Abu Musa in Iraq and told him. He said: If only he had remained until you conveyed his words to us."],[2879,"A man came to Umar while he was at Arafah and said: Amir al-Mu'minin, I came from Kufah and left there someone who writes out copies of the Quran from memory. Umar became angry and swelled until he almost filled the space between the man's shoulders. He said: Woe to you, who is he? He said: Abdullah b. Masud. He kept calming down until he returned to his former state. Then he said: Woe to you, by Allah, I do not know of any Muslim remaining who is more deserving of that than him. I will tell you about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to converse at night about affairs of the Muslims at Abu Bakr's house. One night he conversed there and I was with him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left and we walked with him. There was a man standing praying in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood listening to his recitation. When we could not identify the man, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever would like to recite the Quran as it was sent down, let him recite it as Ibn Umm Abd does.' Then the man sat down supplicating, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Ask and you will be given.' Umar said: I said: By Allah, I will go to him in the morning and give him good news. I went to him to give him good news and found Abu Bakr had preceded me and given him the news. By Allah, I never raced him to any good but he preceded me."],[2880,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said, \"Whoever wishes to recite the Quran as it was revealed, then let them recite it in the style of Ibn Umm Abd.\" This is the narration of Alqamah from Umar, and it is authentic according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim. However, they did not include it in their collections. Alqamah himself transmitted it from Umar, but its authenticity in their eyes is questionable. Allah knows best, and there is a witness who commented on it from the hadith of Ammar ibn Yasar."],[2881,"The translation of the provided Arabic sentence is: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Abdullah ibn Mas'ood while he was reciting letter by letter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an as it was revealed, then let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Mas'ood.'\""],[2882,"A man came to me while I was praying and said, 'May your mother be bereaved of you! Do I not see you praying when it has been commanded that the Book of Allah be torn to pieces, every piece?' He said, 'So I shortened my prayer, and I used to sit, but I entered the house without sitting, and I climbed without sitting, and there I found al-Ash'ari, Hudhayfah, and Ibn Mas'ud disputing, and Hudhayfah was saying to Ibn Mas'ud, \"Hand this mushaf over to them.\" He said, \"By Allah, I will not hand it over to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made me recite seventy-some surahs; shall I then hand it over to them? By Allah, I will not hand it over to them.\"'"],[2883,"\"Abdullah ibn Mas'ood said: 'I have read 70 chapters from the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ Quran.' And Zaid ibn Thabit, who had two weak calves, used to play with the children.\""],[2884,"I heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ood say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to me seventy Surahs, which I had memorized before Zaid ibn Thabit embraced Islam.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary."],[2885,"A group of us from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ sat down and said, 'If we only knew which deeds are most beloved to Allah, we would do them.' Then Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: {Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth exalts Allah, and He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise. O you who have believed, why do you say what you do not do? Great is hatred in the sight of Allah that you say what you do not do. Indeed, Allah loves those who fight in His cause in a row as though they are a [single] structure joined firmly} to the end of the surah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it to us. Muhammad b. Kathir added in his hadith, and al-Awza'i said to us, 'Yahya b. Abi Kathir recited it to us like this.' Muhammad b. Kathir said, 'And al-Awza'i recited it to us like this.' Ibrahim said, 'And Muhammad b. Kathir recited it to us to the end of the surah like this.' Abu 'Amr b. al-Sammak said, 'And Ibrahim b. al-Haytham recited it to us to the end of the surah like this.'"],[2886,"We were around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ compiling the Quran when he said, 'Blessed is Syria.' It was said to him, 'Why?' He said, 'Because the angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over them.' Jarir b. Hazim narrated it from Yahya b. Ayyub, according to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[2887,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ compiling the Quran from parchments when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Blessed is Syria.' We said, 'For what reason?' He said, 'Because the angels of the Most Merciful spread their wings over them.'"],[2888,"He said: I entered the mosque on Friday while the Prophet ﷺ was delivering the sermon, and I sat near Ubayy b. Ka'b. The Prophet ﷺ recited Surah Bara'ah. I said to Ubayy, 'When was this surah revealed?' He said, 'He frowned at me and did not speak to me.' He said, 'And he mentioned the hadith. Thus I found it in my book, and I searched for it in the musnads but did not find it in full. The hadith with its chain is authentic.' Sahih."],[2889,"Which of the two readings do you think was the last reading? They said, 'The reading of Zayd.' He said, 'No, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to present the Quran to Gabriel ﷺ every year, and in the year in which he was taken, he presented it to him twice, and the reading of Ibn Mas'ud was the last of them.'"],[2890,"The Quran was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ several times. They say that this reading of ours is the final presentation."],[2891,"Ibn 'Abbas said: 'Ubayy recited to the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Shafi'i said: I recited to Isma'il b. Qustantin, and he used to say: 'The Quran is a noun and is not hamzated, and it is not derived from \"I recited.\" If it were derived from \"I recited,\" everything recited would be Quran. Rather, it is a name for the Quran like the Torah and the Gospel. \"I recited\" is hamzated, but the Quran is not hamzated.'"],[2892,"A bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Nabi' of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am not Nabi' of Allah; rather, I am Nabi of Allah.'"],[2893,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pronounce hamzah, nor did Abu Bakr, nor 'Umar, nor the caliphs. Hamzah is an innovation they introduced after them. I heard Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad b. Ya'qub al-Shaybani al-Hafiz say: I heard Abu Zakariya Yahya b. Muhammad b. Yahya say: I heard Ahmad b. Hanbal say: 'I do not write the hadith of Musa b. 'Ubaydah al-Rabadhi, nor the hadith of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Ziyad al-Afriqi.'"],[2894,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'The Quran was revealed with tafkhim: {like the form of a bird} [Al 'Imran 49], as an excuse and as a warning, and the two barriers, and {Unquestionably, His is the creation and the command} [al-A'raf 54], and similar to this in the Quran.' Its chain is authentic, but they did not record it. No, by Allah, al-'Awfi is weak, and Bakkar is not reliable, and the hadith is weak and rejected."],[2895,"From Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pause in his recitation: {In the name of Allah, the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful. [All] praise is [due] to Allah, Lord of the worlds - the Entirely Merciful, the Especially Merciful, Sovereign of the Day of Recompense}.'"],[2896,"The Prophet ﷺ used to cut off his recitation verse by verse: \"Al-ḥamdu lillāhi rabbi al-ʿālamīn\" [al-Fātiḥah:2], then he would pause; \"al-Raḥmān al-Raḥīm\" [al-Fātiḥah:1], then he would pause. Ibn Abī Mulaykah said: \"Umm Salamah used to recite it as 'Maliki yawmi al-dīn.'\""],[2897,"He used to recite \"Maliki yawmi al-dīn\"."],[2898,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited \"Ihdinā al-ṣirāṭa al-mustaqīm\" [al-Fātiḥah:6] with ṣād."],[2899,"That he prayed with the Prophet ﷺ when he said \"ghayri al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim wa lā al-ḍāllīn\" [al-Fātiḥah:7], he said \"Āmīn,\" lowering his voice with it. The judge said: \"ghayri\" [al-Fātiḥah:7] with kasrah on the rāʾ; for in the reading of the people of Makkah it is \"ghayra al-maghḍūbi ʿalayhim\" [al-Fātiḥah:7]."],[2900,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ with a companion of mine but we did not find him. Aisha then fed us dates and porridge. Then, the Prophet ﷺ came, dragging his foot and tying his lower garment. He asked, \"Did you feed them anything?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"While we were like that, a shepherd came by with a sheep. The Prophet ﷺ asked him, \"Did she give birth?\" He said, \"Yes.\" The Prophet ﷺ asked, \"What did she deliver?\" He replied, \"A healthy lamb.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Slaughter a sheep instead of her.\" Then, he turned to me and said, \"Do not think that we slaughtered her only for your sake. We have a hundred sheep, and we do not want them to increase. So, whenever a shepherd is burdened with the sheep, we slaughter a sheep in its place.\" Ibn Juraij said, \"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do not think' and did not say, 'Do not assume.'\" This was narrated by Sufyan Ath-Thawri from Abu Hashim from Asim bin Laqit, but Adh-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[2901,"\"Lā taḥsabanna,\" and he did not say \"lā yaḥsabanna.\""],[2902,"\"From no soul does it accept any intercession, and no compensation can be taken from it\" [2:48]. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to me: \"No soul will be recompensed for any other, nor will intercession be accepted from it.\" [2:48] with تَاءْ (ta) and \"no compensation can be taken from it\" [2:48] with يَاء (ya)."],[2903,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and some of his companions had lagged behind in travel. He raised his voice with these two verses: \"Yā ayyuhā al-nāsu ittaqū rabbakum inna zalzalata al-sāʿati shayʾun ʿaẓīm. Yawma tarawnahā tadh-halu kullu murḍiʿatin ʿammā arḍaʿat wa taḍaʿu kullu dhāti ḥamlin ḥamlahā wa tara al-nāsa sukārā wa mā hum bi-sukārā wa lākinna ʿadhāba Allāhi shadīd\" [al-Ḥajj:2]. When his companions heard that, they urged on their mounts, and they knew that he had something to say. He said: \"Do you know which day that is?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"A day when Adam will call upon his Lord, and He will say: 'O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire.' He will say: 'O Lord, and what is the delegation of the Fire?' He will say: 'From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire, and one to Paradise.'\" So his companions were struck with despair, and they did not show a single smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what had befallen his companions, he said: \"Know and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations that have never been with anything except that they increased it: Gog and Magog, and those who perished from the children of Adam and the children of Iblis.\" Then some of what they were feeling was relieved. Then he said: \"Know and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among mankind only like a mole on the side of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a beast.\" The hadith of Hishām al-Dastuwāʾī is a sound hadith, for most of our early imams hold that al-Ḥasan did hear from ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn. But when Hishām and al-Ḥakam b. ʿAbd al-Malik differ, the word is that of Hishām. Al-Ḥakam b. ʿAbd al-Malik is weak."],[2904,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited \"kayfa nunshizuhā\" [al-Baqarah:259] with zāy."],[2905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me: \"Innī anā al-razzāqu dhū al-quwwati al-matīn.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[2906,"A man from Banū Sulaym passed by a group of the Prophet's companions ﷺ with some sheep of his, and he greeted them. They said: \"He did not greet you except to seek protection from you.\" So they went to him and killed him, and took his sheep, and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ. Then Allah, exalted is He, sent down: \"Yā ayyuhā alladhīna āmanū idhā ḍarabtum fī sabīli Allāhi fa-tabayyanū wa lā taqūlū li-man alqā ilaykumu al-salāma lasta muʾminan\" [al-Nisāʾ:94] up to His saying: \"kadhālika kuntum min qablu fa-manna Allāhu ʿalaykum fa-tabayyanū\" [al-Nisāʾ:94]."],[2907,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited \"wa mā kāna li-nabiyyin an yaghulla\" [Āl ʿImrān:161] with fatḥah on the yāʾ."],[2908,"And he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me: \"fa-ruhun maqbūḍatun\" without an alif."],[2909,"I said to ʿĀʾishah: \"O Mother of the Believers, how did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite this letter: 'wa alladhīna yuʾtūna mā ātaw' [al-Muʾminūn:60]?\" She said: \"Which of the two is dearer to you?\" I said: \"One of them is dearer to me than red camels.\" She said: \"Which one?\" I said: \"alladhīna yuʾtawna mā ataw.\" She said: \"This is how I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite it.\""],[2910,"That she heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting {Then rest and provision} [al-Waqi'ah 89]."],[2911,"I heard Abu Hurayrah reciting this verse: {Indeed, Allah commands you to render trusts to whom they are due and when you judge between people to judge with justice. Excellent is that which Allah instructs you. Indeed, Allah is ever Hearing and Seeing.}"],[2912,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to me, saying: 'Put on your clothes and your weapon, then come to me.' So I put on my clothes and my weapon and went to him. I found him sitting and performing ablution. He looked up at me, then lowered his gaze, then said: 'O 'Amr, I intend to send you on an expedition. May Allah grant you spoils and keep you safe, and I desire for you a righteous desire for wealth.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not embrace Islam for wealth; I embraced Islam out of desire for Islam and to be with you.' He said: 'O 'Amr, excellent is righteous wealth for a righteous man'—meaning with a fathah on the nun and a kasrah on the 'ayn. [This is] a sahih hadith according to the condition of Muslim due to the narration of Musa b. 'Ali b. Rabah, and according to the condition of al-Bukhari for Abu Salih. Sahih."],[2913,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to recite {And We ordained for them therein: a life for a life} [al-Ma'idah 45] with nasb, {and an eye for an eye} [al-Ma'idah 45] with raf'."],[2914,"That the Prophet ﷺ recited {And We ordained for them therein: a life for a life, an eye for an eye, a nose for a nose, an ear for an ear, a tooth for a tooth, and for wounds is legal retribution} [al-Ma'idah 45]. Muhammad b. Mu'awiyah is not of the standard of this book."],[2915,"About the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And We tried you with a trial} [Taha 40], in a hadith traced back to the Prophet ﷺ: {Two men from among those who feared} [al-Ma'idah 23] with a raf' on the ya'."],[2916,"When 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'All of it is in the scriptures of Ibrahim and Musa.' Then when 'By the star when it descends' was revealed, and he reached {And Ibrahim, who fulfilled} [al-Najm 37], he pronounced it with tashdid and said 'waffā,' {That no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another} [al-Najm 38] up to His saying {This is a warner from the warners of old} [al-Najm 56]."],[2917,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting {But yes, My signs came to you, and you denied them and were arrogant and were among the disbelievers} [al-Zumar 59]."],[2918,"\"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ recited, 'Among those who are deserving of the guardianship' [Al-Ma'idah 107].\""],[2919,"He used to recite {in a muddy spring}."],[2920,"Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali and Jubayr b. Hayyah al-Thaqafi were with Ibn Ziyad. He said: They mentioned this variant: {It has certainly broken apart between you} [al-An'am 94] until they placed bets. Aslam b. Zur'ah said: 'I heard Abu Musa reciting {It has certainly broken apart between you} [al-An'am 94].' One of them said: 'The first person to enter upon us will be the judge between me and you.' Then Yahya b. Ya'mar entered upon us, and they asked him. Yahya said: 'It has certainly broken apart between you' with raf'. Yahya said: 'Indeed, Abu Musa is not one of deception, and I do not accuse him.'"],[2921,"About the saying of the disciples: {Can your Lord} [al-Ma'idah 112] or 'Can you ask your Lord?' He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite it as 'hal tastati'u' with a ta'.'"],[2922,"Ibrahim will meet his father Azar on the Day of Resurrection, and on Azar's face will be darkness and dust. Ibrahim will say to him: 'Did I not tell you not to disobey me?' His father will say: 'Today I will not disobey you.' Ibrahim will say: 'O Lord, You promised me that You would not disgrace me on the Day they are resurrected. What disgrace is greater than my father, the distant one?' Allah will say: 'I have forbidden Paradise to the disbelievers.' Then He will say: 'O Ibrahim, what is beneath your feet?' He will look, and behold, it is a sacrificial animal covered in blood. It will be seized by its legs and thrown into the Fire."],[2923,"The Prophet ﷺ taught me to recite {They may say, \"You have studied\"} [al-Anʿām 105], meaning with jazm on the sīn and naṣb on the tāʾ."],[2924,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line and drew lines to the right and left of that line. Then he said, \"This is the straight path of your Lord, and these are the other paths, upon each of which there is a devil inviting to it.\" Then he recited, \"And, [moreover], this is My path, which is straight, so follow it; and do not follow [other] ways, for you will be separated from His way.\" [Surah Al-An'am 153]"],[2925,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite {the gates of heaven will not be opened for them} [al-Aʿrāf 40] lightly (mukhaffaf)."],[2926,"The Prophet ﷺ recited {dakkan} [al-Aʿrāf 143] with tanwīn and did not lengthen it."],[2927,"The Prophet ﷺ recited {Now Allah has lightened [the burden] for you and knows that there is weakness among you} [al-Anfāl 66] with rafʿ."],[2928,"The Prophet ﷺ recited {that he should have prisoners of war} — ṣaḥīḥṣaḥīḥ."],[2929,"He heard Abū Hurayrah and Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us while he was on the minbar and said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul,\" three times, then fell silent. Every man among us bowed his head weeping in grief at the oath of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said, \"There is no servant who performs the five prayers, fasts Ramadan, and avoids the seven major sins except that the gates of Paradise will be opened for him on the Day of Resurrection, so much so that they will clatter.\" Then he recited {If you avoid the major sins which you are forbidden, We will expiate your misdeeds} [al-Nisāʾ 31]."],[2930,"\"The people of two religions do not inherit from each other, and a Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor a disbeliever from a Muslim.\" Then he recited {And those who disbelieve are allies of one another. If you do not do so, there will be fitnah on earth and great corruption} [al-Anfāl 73] with yāʾ."],[2931,"From Ibn ʿAbbās, tracing it back to the Prophet ﷺ: He recited {There has certainly come to you a Messenger from among yourselves} [al-Tawbah 128], meaning from the greatest of you in rank. Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[2932,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite {Say, \"In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy — in that let them rejoice. It is better than what they accumulate\"} [Yūnus 58]."],[2933,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite (Indeed he did a deed other than righteous). Its chain is obscure."],[2934,"The Prophet ﷺ recited {Ask him what is the case of the women who cut their hands} [Yūsuf 50]. He said, \"If he had sent for me, I would have hastened to answer and would not have sought an excuse.\""],[2935,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to ʿAlī, \"O ʿAlī, people are from various trees, while I and you are from one tree.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited (And gardens of grapevines, and crops, and palm trees, [growing] clustered and unclustered, watered with one water)."],[2936,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"And We cause some of them to excel others in produce\" [Quran 13:4], with nūn."],[2937,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Allah erases whatever He wills and establishes what He wills.\" [Surah Ar-Ra'd 13:39], abbreviated."],[2938,"I heard Saʿd reciting: \"Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten\" [Quran 2:106, variant: nansāhā]. I said, \"Saʿīd recites it as 'or cause it to be forgotten' [nunsihā].\" He said, \"The Quran was not revealed according to al-Musayyib or his son.\" He said, \"And I recall that he recited: 'We will make you recite, so you will not forget,' and 'Remember your Lord when you forget' [Quran 18:24].\""],[2939,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The Quran was revealed with tafkhīm: 'like the form of a bird' [Quran 3:49], 'as an excuse or a warning' [Quran 77:6], 'the two barriers,' 'Unquestionably, His is the creation and the command' [Quran 7:54], and similar verses.\""],[2940,"When the people of the Fire gather in the Fire, along with those of the people of the Qiblah whom Allah wills, they will say: \"What did your Islam avail you, when you have ended up with us in the Fire?\" They will say: \"We had sins, so we were seized for them.\" Allah hears what they say. He said: Then He commands that those of the people of the Qiblah who are in the Fire be brought out. The disbelievers say: \"Would that we were Muslims, so that we might be brought out as they were brought out.\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"Alif Lām Rā. These are the verses of the Book and a clear Quran. Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish that they had been Muslims\" [Quran 15:1–2], with tashdīd."],[2941,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the Almighty's saying: \"On the Day We will call every people with their imam\" [Quran 17:71]: He said: \"One of them will be called and given his book in his right hand, and his body will be extended for him sixty cubits.\" He said: \"And his face will be made white, and a crown of gleaming pearls will be placed on his head.\" He said: \"Then he will go to his companions.\" He said: \"They will see him from afar and say: 'O Allah, bring him to us and bless us in this one,' until he comes to them and says: 'Rejoice, for each man among you will have the like of this.' As for the disbeliever, his face will be blackened, and his body will be extended for him sixty cubits in the form of Adam. His companions will see him and say: 'We seek refuge in Allah from this one. O Allah, do not bring him to us.' He said: \"Then he will come to them, and they will say: 'O Allah, keep him away.' He said: \"Then he will say: 'May Allah distance you, for each of you will have the like of this.'\""],[2942,"The Prophet ﷺ remained in Makkah for thirteen years as a prophet, then there was revealed to him: \"Cause me to enter a sound entrance and cause me to exit a sound exit\" [Quran 17:80], with fatḥah on the mīm, and he emigrated."],[2943,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"If I ask you about anything after this\" [Quran 18:76], with two hamzahs."],[2944,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: \"If you wished, you could have taken for it a payment\" [Quran 18:77], without tashdīd."],[2945,"He used to recite: \"And before them was a king who seized every sound ship by force.\""],[2946,"He used to recite: \"In a muddy spring\" [Quran 18:86, variant: ḥamiʾah]."],[2947,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on a donkey, and he saw the sun when it set and said: \"O Abu Dharr, where does this set?\" I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"It sets in a hot spring,\" without hamzah."],[2948,"\"I do not know how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: ʿitiyyan or jithiyyan, for both are with ḍammah.\""],[2949,"That ʿĀʾishah used to send something as charity for the people of the Ṣuffah and say: 'Do not give any of them to a Barbarī man or a Barbarī woman, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"They are the successors about whom Allah ﷻ said: {Then there succeeded after them a generation who neglected prayer} [Maryam: 59].\"'"],[2950,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: (The heavens almost rupture from it) with yāʾ and nūn, {and the mountains collapse} [Maryam: 90] with tāʾ, {because they invoke for the Most Merciful a son. And it is not appropriate for the Most Merciful to take a son} [Maryam: 92], one open (fatḥah) after another open (fatḥah)."],[2951,"A man recited to ʿAbdullāh {Ṭā Hā} [Ṭā Hā: 1] with an open (fatḥah), and ʿAbdullāh corrected him: {Ṭā Hā} [Ṭā Hā: 1] with a kasrah. The man said to him, 'It only means: put your foot down, with an open (fatḥah).' ʿAbdullāh said: 'Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it, and thus Jibrīl ﷺ brought it down.'"],[2952,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Yājūj and Mājūj will be opened, as Allah ﷻ said: {From every elevation they descend} [al-Anbiyāʾ: 96].' Ibn Isḥāq said, in the reading of ʿAbdullāh: 'From every grave they descend,' with jīm and thāʾ, like His saying: {From the graves to their Lord they rush} [Yā Sīn: 51], and that means the graves."],[2953,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {And you see the people intoxicated, yet they are not intoxicated} [al-Ḥajj: 2]. Al-Bukhārī has already transmitted this hadith from ʿUmar b. Ḥafṣ b. Ghiyāth, from his father, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Ṣāliḥ, from Abū Saʿīd, saying: Allah says: 'O Adam, bring out the delegation of the Fire,' and the hadith in its entirety, and at its end: {And you see the people intoxicated, yet they are not intoxicated} [al-Ḥajj: 2]. And the more authentic of the two hadiths is the hadith that Imam al-Bukhārī transmitted."],[2954,"When the Prophet ﷺ was expelled from Makkah, Abū Bakr said: 'They have expelled their Prophet. Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return. They will certainly be destroyed.' Then Allah the Exalted sent down: {Permission is given to those who are fought, because they were wronged, and indeed Allah is able to give them victory} [al-Ḥajj: 39]. He said: 'And it is the first verse revealed concerning fighting.'"],[2955,"I said to ʿĀʾishah: 'O Mother of the Believers, how did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite this letter: {And those who give what they give} [al-Muʾminūn: 60]?' She said: 'I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite it: {they give} [al-Muʾminūn: 60].'"],[2956,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: {In arrogance regarding it, talking by night, abandoning it} [al-Muʾminūn: 67]. He said: 'The polytheists used to forsake the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[2957,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, regarding {And they therein are grimacing} [al-Muʾminūn: 104]: He said: 'The Fire will disfigure them, and their upper lip will contract until it reaches the middle of his head, and their lower lip will hang down until it reaches his navel.'"],[2958,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ: {It was not proper for us to take} [al-Furqān: 18] — or 'to adopt' — he said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: {that we take besides You} [al-Furqān: 18], with the nūn in the accusative (naṣb)."],[2959,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ: {Alif Lām Mīm. The Romans have been defeated} [al-Rūm: 2] — or 'have defeated'? He said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite: {Alif Lām Mīm. The Romans have been defeated} [al-Rūm: 1].' We have not written these two hadiths except with this chain, although Muḥammad b. Saʿīd al-Shāmī is not of the standard of this book. Muḥammad b. Saʿīd is the one who was crucified, perished, and Bakr b. Khunays is abandoned."],[2960,"Ibn ʿUmar said: 'I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as you recited to me, and he corrected me as I corrected you.' ʿAṭiyyah al-ʿAwfī is alone in this, and they did not use him as proof, although Muslim used al-Fuḍayl b. Marzūq as proof. They did not use ʿAṭiyyah as proof."],[2961,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {No soul knows what is hidden for them of the joy of their eyes} [al-Sajdah 17]"],[2962,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he recited {and the sea, ever replenishing it} [Luqmān 27] in the nominative case"],[2963,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Uhud, he passed by Mus'ab b. 'Umayr, who lay slain on his path. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped over him and supplicated for him, then recited this verse: {Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah. Some of them have fulfilled their vow, and some are still waiting, and they have not changed in the least} [al-Ahzāb 23]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I bear witness that these are martyrs in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection. So come to them and visit them. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one greets them until the Day of Resurrection except that they return his greeting.\""],[2964,"The Prophet ﷺ recited \"Laqad kāna li-Saba' fī masākinihim\" [Indeed there was for Sheba a sign in their dwelling places]. This is a copy we have not written predominantly except from Abu al-'Abbās. The two Shaykhs did not use Ibn al-Baylamānī as evidence. It is not authentic."],[2965,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited: {Their hearts were startled; they said, \"What has your Lord said?\"} [Saba' 23]"],[2966,"The Prophet ﷺ recited {And indeed he led astray from among you a great multitude} [Yā Sīn 62] with a lightened reading. Its narrators are all trustworthy except Ismā'īl b. Rāfi', for the two Shaykhs did not use him as evidence. In its chain is Ismā'īl b. Rāfi', who is utterly unreliable."],[2967,"Al-Zubayr: When {Indeed you are to die, and indeed they are to die. Then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord, will dispute} [al-Zumar 31] was revealed, al-Zubayr said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will what was between us in this world, along with the particular sins, be repeated for us?\" He said: \"Yes, it will be repeated for them until they render to every possessor of a right his due.\" Al-Zubayr said: \"By Allah, the matter is surely severe.\""],[2968,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: {O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins, and He does not care}"],[2969,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite: {Indeed I am the Provider, possessor of strength, the Firm}"],[2970,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {Those who believed and whose descendants followed them in faith – We will join their descendants with them} [al-Tūr 21]"],[2971,"I recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"fa-hal min mudhdhakir\" with dhāl. The Prophet ﷺ said: {Then is there any who will remember?} [al-Qamar 15] with dāl."],[2972,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ recited, \"Reclining on green cushions and beautiful carpets.\" [Surah Ar-Rahman, verse 76]"],[2973,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: {Then you will drink as the thirsty camels drink} [al-Wāqi'ah 55]"],[2974,"That she was with her daughter, the daughter of al-ʿAjmāʾ, during the days of Hajj at Minā. He said: Budayl b. Warqāʾ came to them on the riding camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his saddle, and called out that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ says: “Whoever is fasting should break his fast, for these are days of eating and drinking.” This hadith is not part of this book."],[2975,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: “Then rest and fragrant basil” [al-Wāqiʿah: 89]."],[2976,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “Then divorce them at the beginning of their waiting period.” Muslim already transmitted this hadith in full from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn al-Zubayr, that he heard ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Ayman asking ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and I think he mentioned this wording. Muslim transmitted the hadith at greater length than this."],[2977,"I was holding the hand of al-Aʿmash, with Yūsuf al-Samtī on the other side, and he asked him about His ﷻ saying: “And the defilement” [al-Muddaththir: 5]. He said: “You have begun with this,” then he said: “I recited the Qurʾān to Yaḥyā b. Waththāb thirty times, and Yaḥyā recited to ʿAlqamah, and ʿAlqamah recited to ʿAbd Allāh, and ʿAbd Allāh recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: ‘And the rijs, so shun it,’ with kasrah on the rāʾ.”"],[2978,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite: “And the rujz, so shun it” [al-Muddaththir: 5] with ḍammah on the rāʾ, and he said: “They are the idols.”"],[2979,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was talking about the period of revelation. He said, \"So I said, 'Keep me company,' but they covered me up. Then Allah the Almighty revealed the verse {O you wrapped in garments} [Al-Muddathir 2]. Arise and warn, and your Lord glorify, and your clothing purify, and uncleanliness avoid.\" He said, \"They are the idols.\""],[2980,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ in a cave when “By those sent forth in succession” [al-Mursalāt: 1] was revealed. I took it directly from his mouth, and his mouth was still moist with it. I do not know with which of them he concluded: “Then in what statement after it will they believe?” [al-Mursalāt: 50] or “And when it is said to them, ‘Bow,’ they do not bow” [al-Mursalāt: 48]."],[2981,"“You will be gathered barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.” His wife said: “Will some of us look at the private parts of others?” He said: “O so-and-so, {Every man among them that Day will have concern enough of his own}.”"],[2982,"He used to recite: “And he is not concerning the unseen a ẓanīn,” with the ẓāʾ."],[2983,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite: ‘So He proportioned you and balanced you,’ with tashdīd.”"],[2984,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite: “Yes, My signs came to you, but you denied them and were arrogant, and you were among the disbelievers” [al-Zumar: 59]."],[2985,"“Do you know what the vastness of Hell is?” He said: I said: “I do not know.” He said: “Indeed, by Allah, you do not know. Between the lobe of their ear and their shoulder is a distance of seventy years’ journey, through which flow valleys of pus and blood.” I said: “Rivers?” He said: “No, valleys.” Authentic."],[2986,"That he asked Jibrīl ﷺ about this verse: {And the Trumpet will be blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth will fall dead except whom Allah wills}—who are those whom Allah did not will to fall dead? He said: “They are the martyrs of Allah ﷻ.”"],[2987,"“No doer of good—whether a Muslim or a disbeliever—does good except that Allah rewards him.” He said: We said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is Allah’s reward to a disbeliever?” He said, “If he has maintained ties of kinship, or given charity, or done a good deed, Allah rewards him with wealth, children, health, and the like of that.” He said: We said, “What is his reward in the Hereafter?” Then he said, “A punishment less than the punishment.” He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {Admit the people of Pharaoh into the severest punishment} [Ghaafir: 46]. Thus did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite it, with the alif omitted."],[2988,"“O Muhammad, are you better or ‘Abd Allah?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Have you finished?” He said, “Yes.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful: {Ha. Meem. A revelation from the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Fussilat: 2] until he reached: {But if they turn away, then say, “I have warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of ‘Ad and Thamud”} [Fussilat: 13]. Then ‘Utbah said to him, “Enough, enough! Do you have anything other than this?” He said, “No.” So ‘Utbah returned to Quraysh, and they said, “What is behind you?” He said, “I did not leave anything that I thought you would say to him except that I said it to him.” They said, “Did he answer you?” He said, “Yes. No, by the One who set it up with His Prophet, I did not understand anything of what he said except that he warned you of a thunderbolt like the thunderbolt of ‘Ad and Thamud.” They said, “Woe to you! A man speaks to you in Arabic and you do not know what he said?” He said, “No, by Allah, I did not understand anything of what he said except the mention of the thunderbolt.”"],[2989,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding {And indeed, he is knowledge of the Hour} [al-Zukhruf: 61]: he said, “The emergence of ‘Isa before the Day of Resurrection.”"],[2990,"When he traveled and mounted his riding beast, he would say “Allahu akbar” three times, then say: {Glory be to the One who subjected this to us, and we were not capable of it. And indeed to our Lord we will return} [al-Zukhruf: 13–14]."],[2991,"Allah created the creation, and when He finished with them, the womb (rahm) stood up and said, “This is the station of one who seeks refuge in You from being severed.” He said, “Yes. Are you not pleased that I join whoever joins you and cut off whoever cuts you off?” It said, “Yes, indeed.” He said, “Then that is for you.” He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Recite, if you wish: {So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth and sever your ties of kinship?} [Muhammad: 22] up to His saying, Exalted is He: {Or are there locks upon their hearts?} [Muhammad: 24]."],[2992,"I heard the Prophet (pbuh) recite, \"So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption on earth?\" [Surah Muhammad, 22]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent on this summarization."],[2993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {So remind—you are only a reminder. You are not over them a controller} [al-Ghashiyah: 21–22] with the letter sad, {except one who turns away and disbelieves} [al-Ghashiyah: 23]."],[2994,"He used to recite: No! But you do not honor the orphan, and you do not urge one another to feed the poor, and you consume and you love—all of them with the letter ya."],[2995,"From Abu Qilabah, from someone whom the Prophet ﷺ taught to recite: {So on that Day, none will punish as He punishes, and none will bind as He binds} [al-Fajr: 25–26]."],[2996,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was there, and opposite him was a burrow. He said, “If hardship were to come and enter this burrow, ease would come and enter upon it and drive it out.” He said: Then Allah, Exalted is He, revealed: {For indeed, with hardship comes ease. Indeed, with hardship comes ease} [al-Sharh: 5–6]."],[2997,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ubayy, “I will teach you a surah.” Ubayy said to him, “Have you been commanded to do that, may my father be your ransom?” He said, “Yes.” Then he recited: {Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book and the polytheists were not to desist until there came to them the clear proof—a messenger from Allah, reciting purified pages} [al-Bayyinah: 1–2]."],[2998,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {That Day, it will report its news} [al-Zalzalah: 4]. He said, “Do you know what its news is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Its news is that it will testify against every slave, male and female, about what he did on its surface, saying: ‘He did such-and-such a deed on such-and-such a day.’ This is its news.”"],[2999,"The Prophet ﷺ recited: He thinks that his wealth will make him immortal [al-Humazah: 3] with a kasrah under the seen."],[3000,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite: {For the security of Quraysh, their security for the caravan of winter and summer} [Quraysh:2]."],[3001,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ recited, \"Indeed, We have granted you, [O Muhammad], al-Kawthar.\" [Surah al-Kawthar, verse 1]."],[3002,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform Witr and recite: ‘Glorify the Name of your Lord the Most High.’, [Al-A’la (87)] ‘Say: O you disbelievers!” [Al-Kafirun (109)] and ‘Say: Allah is One.”. [Al-Ikhlas (112)] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1171)"],[3003,"When this surah, 'When the help of Allah and the victory comes,' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it until he completed it, then said: \"I and my companions are in one group, and the people are in another group. There is no emigration after the victory.\""],[3004,"{In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds} [Al-Fatihah:2]. I said to my father: Sa'id informed you that Ibn Abbas said: {In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful} [Al-Fatihah:1] is a verse. He said: \"Yes.\""],[3005,"\"Shall I not teach you a surah the like of which was not revealed in the Torah, nor in the Gospel, nor in the Psalms, nor in the Furqan?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"I hope that you will not leave through that door until you learn it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up and I stood up with him. He began to talk to me while my hand was in his hand. I started to slow down, disliking that he might leave before telling me it. When I came near the door, I said: O Messenger of Allah, the surah which you promised me. He said: \"How do you recite when you stand for prayer?\" I recited the Opening of the Book. He said: \"It is it, and it is the Seven Oft-Repeated Verses and the Great Quran which I have been given.\""],[3006,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Nasr narrated to us, Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Isa al-Qadi narrated to us, Abdullah b. Maslama narrated to us from what was read to Malik, from al-Ala' b. Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sa'id, the client of Amir b. Kuraiz, from Ubayy b. Ka'b, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, something similar, according to the condition of Muslim."],[3007,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds} [Al-Fatihah:2], he said: \"The jinn and mankind.\""],[3008,"(Master of the Day of Judgment) He said: \"It is the Day of Reckoning.\""],[3009,"From Abdullah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {The straight path} [Al-Fatihah:6], he said: \"It is the Book of Allah.\""],[3010,"{The straight path} [Al-Fatihah:6]: \"It is Islam, and it is wider than what is between the heaven and the earth.\""],[3011,"\"He is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions,\" I said. We mentioned this to Hassan, and he said, \"By Allah, he is truthful and sincere. He is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and Abu Bakr and Umar.\""],[3012,"\"Surah Al-Baqarah contains a verse which is the chief of the verses of the Quran. It is not recited in a house in which there is a devil except that he leaves it: the Verse of the Throne.\""],[3013,"\"Verily, everything has a summit, and the summit of the Quran is Surah Al-Baqarah.\""],[3014,"\"I was given Surah Al-Baqarah from the first Reminder.\""],[3015,"Recite Surat al-Baqarah in your houses, for Shaytan does not enter a house in which Surat al-Baqarah is recited."],[3016,"The mistress of the verses of the Quran is the Verse of the Throne."],[3017,"Indeed Allah wrote a book two thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth, and He sent down from it two verses with which He sealed Surat al-Baqarah. They are not recited in a house for three nights but Shaytan draws near it."],[3018,"{Alif Lam Mim. That is the Book} [al-Baqarah:2]. He said: {Alif Lam Mim} [al-Baqarah:1] is a letter of the name of Allah, and {the Book} [al-Baqarah:2] is the Quran. {No doubt in it} [al-Baqarah:2] means no uncertainty in it."],[3019,"The companions of Muhammad ﷺ and their faith were mentioned in the presence of Abdullah. He said: Abdullah said: The affair of Muhammad was clear to whoever saw him. By the One besides whom there is no deity, no believer has believed with a faith more excellent than faith in the unseen. Then he recited: {Alif Lam Mim. That is the Book, no doubt in it} [al-Baqarah:2] up to His saying, the Exalted: {who believe in the unseen} [al-Baqarah:3]."],[3020,"The stones that Allah mentioned in the Quran, whose fuel is people and stones, are stones of sulfur that Allah, the Exalted, created with Him however He willed, or as He willed."],[3021,"Allah brought Adam out of the Garden before anyone entered it. Allah, the Exalted, said: {Indeed, I am placing a vicegerent on the earth. They said: Will You place upon it one who will cause corruption therein and shed blood?} [al-Baqarah:30]. And there had been on it, two thousand years before he was created, the jinn, the Banu al-Jan. They caused corruption on the earth and shed blood. So when Allah, the Exalted, said: {Indeed, I am placing a vicegerent on the earth. They said: Will You place upon it one who will cause corruption therein and shed blood?} [al-Baqarah:30], meaning the jinn, the Banu al-Jan. When they caused corruption on the earth, He sent against them armies of angels, and they struck them until they drove them to the islands of the seas. He said: The angels said: {Will You place upon it one who will cause corruption therein} [al-Baqarah:30] as those jinn, the Banu al-Jan, did? He said: Allah said: {Indeed, I know what you do not know} [al-Baqarah:30]."],[3022,"When Allah finished creating Adam and sent the soul into him, he sneezed and said: Praise be to Allah. His Lord said to him: May your Lord have mercy on you."],[3023,"Allah created Adam from the surface of the whole earth. His offspring came forth according to that: among them are the white, the black, the brown, and the red; among them are those in between; and among them are the easy, the wicked, and the good."],[3024,"Adam was a tall man, as if he were a lofty palm tree, with much hair on his head. When he committed the sin, his private parts became visible to him, and he had not seen them before. He fled through the Garden, and a tree caught hold of him. He said to it: Release me. It said: I will not release you. He said: His Lord called him: O Adam, are you fleeing from Me? He said: O Lord, I felt shy before You."],[3025,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, was Adam a prophet? He said: Yes, taught and spoken to. He said: How many generations were between him and Nuh? He said: Ten generations. He said: How many between Nuh and Ibrahim? He said: Ten generations. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how many messengers were there? He said: Three hundred and fifteen, a great multitude."],[3026,"A forgiveness, but they said: Wheat. And they entered upon their backsides. That is His saying, the Exalted: {But those who wronged changed the saying to other than what was said to them} [al-Baqarah:59]."],[3027,"How can you be asked about something when you have the Book of Allah, the most recent of reports from Allah? He has already told you that they wrote a book with their own hands, altered and distorted it, and said, “This is from Allah,” and sold it for a small price. Yet you have the Book of Allah, pure and unmixed. By Allah, none of them will ask you about what was revealed to you."],[3028,"The Jews of Khaybar were fighting Ghatafan. Whenever they met, the Jews of Khaybar were defeated. So the Jews sought refuge in this supplication: “O Allah, we ask You by the right of Muhammad, the unlettered Prophet, whom You promised to bring forth for us at the end of time, to grant us victory over them.” He said: So whenever they met, they called with this supplication and defeated Ghatafan. But when the Prophet ﷺ was sent, they disbelieved in him, so Allah revealed: {And they used to seek victory before} [Al-Baqarah 89] — by you, O Muhammad, over the disbelievers. “ ” Necessity led to its inclusion in the tafsir, and it is strange from his narration. There is no necessity for that, i.e., for including it, for Abdullah is abandoned and doomed."],[3029,"“The Jews” {and those who associate others with Allah} [Al-Baqarah 96]. He said: “The non-Arabs.” “The two Shaykhs agreed on the chain of the Companion’s tafsir, and this is a sound chain according to their condition, but they did not include it.” According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3030,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, exalted is He, with additional wording."],[3031,"\"They are the people of the Book.\" \"And among those who associate partners with Allah, one of them wishes that if he could live a thousand years, he would not be freed from the torment. And Allah is seeing of what they do.\" [Al-Baqarah 96] He said, this is the statement of one of them to his companion. He sent joy and fragrance festival."],[3032,"My two viziers from heaven are Gabriel and Michael, and from the people of earth are Abu Bakr and Umar."],[3033,"I have two viziers from the people of heaven and two viziers from the people of earth. As for my two viziers from the people of heaven, they are Gabriel and Michael, and as for my two viziers from the people of earth, they are Abu Bakr and Umar."],[3034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the bearer of the trumpet and said: “Gabriel on his right and Michael on his left.” Abu Ubayd said: “Both are with hamzah in the hadith.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[3035,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Gabriel is on his right side and Michael is on his left side, and he is the companion of the images.\" Dahabi did not provide a summary for this."],[3036,"While we were with Ibn Abbas, a man came to him. He asked, “Where have you come from?” He replied, “From Iraq.” He asked, “From which of them?” He replied, “From Kufa.” He asked, “What is the news?” He replied, “I left them talking that Ali has come out against them.” He said, “What do you say? May you be bereft of your father! If we knew that, we would not have married his women or divided his inheritance.” Then he said: “I will tell you about that. The devils used to eavesdrop on the heaven, and one of them would come with a word of truth that people had heard, and he would add seventy lies to it, then instill it into people’s hearts. Allah informed Solomon son of David of that, so he took it and buried it under the throne. When Solomon died, a devil stood on the road and said, ‘Shall I guide you to Solomon’s treasure, the like of which no one has, the inaccessible treasure?’ They said, ‘Yes.’ So they brought it out, and it was sorcery. The nations inherited it, and its remnants are what the people of Iraq talk about. Then Allah revealed Solomon’s excuse, saying: {And they followed what the devils recited over Solomon’s kingdom, and Solomon did not disbelieve, but the devils disbelieved} [Al-Baqarah 102], up to the end of the verse."],[3037,"I heard Ali informing the people."],[3039,"It was revealed: {So wherever you turn, there is the face of Allah} [Al-Baqarah 115] — “that you may pray wherever your mount faces you in voluntary prayer.”"],[3040,"Regarding the saying of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted: {Those to whom We gave the Book recite it as it should be recited} [Al-Baqarah 121]. He said: “They make lawful its lawful and forbid its forbidden, and they do not distort it from its proper places.”"],[3041,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, may He be glorified and exalted: {And when his Lord tested Abraham with words} [Al-Baqarah 124]."],[3042,"Allah said to His Prophet ﷺ: \"Purify My House for those who circumambulate, those who seclude themselves, and those who bow and prostrate.\" So circumambulation is before prayer. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Circumambulation of the House is equivalent to prayer, except that Allah has permitted speech during it. So whoever speaks, let him speak only good.\""],[3043,"Allah, Exalted is He, said to His Prophet ﷺ: \"Purify My House for those who circumambulate, those who seclude themselves, and those who bow and prostrate.\" So circumambulation is before prayer. This is one part of the matn, and the second part is from the hadith of al-Qasim b. Abi Ayyub. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[3044,"\"Circumambulation of the House is a prayer, except that Allah has permitted speech during it. So whoever speaks during it, let him speak only good.\""],[3045,"Ibrahim, the Friend of the Most Merciful, came from Armenia with the Sakina as a guide for him to the location of the House, just as a spider establishes its house. Then Ibrahim dug beneath the Sakina and uncovered foundations, no base of which could be moved by fewer than thirty men. He said, then he said..."],[3046,"The first thing that was abrogated from the Quran, as was mentioned to us, was the matter of the qiblah. Allah said: {To Allah belong the east and the west, so wherever you turn, there is the Face of Allah} [Al-Baqarah 115]. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced it and prayed toward the Sacred House in Jerusalem, and left the Ancient House. Then Allah, Exalted is He, said: {The foolish among the people will say, 'What has turned them away from their qiblah, which they used to face?'} [Al-Baqarah 142], meaning the Sacred House in Jerusalem. So He abrogated it and turned him toward the Ancient House. Then Allah, Exalted is He, said: {And from wherever you set out, turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. And wherever you are, turn your faces toward it} [Al-Baqarah 150]."],[3047,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at a funeral among the Banu Salamah, and I was walking beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A man said, \"What a good man, as far as we know, if he was chaste and a Muslim, if he was.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Are you the one saying that?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, that is what appeared to us, and Allah knows best what is hidden.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is affirmed.\" He said, \"And we were with him at the funeral of a man from the Banu Harithah or from the Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal. A man said, \"What a bad man, as far as we know, if he was coarse and harsh, if he was.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Are you the one saying that?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah knows best what is hidden. As for what appeared to us from him, that is what it is.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"It is affirmed.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {And thus We have made you a just community that you will be witnesses over the people and the Messenger will be a witness over you} [Al-Baqarah 143]."],[3048,"On the authority of Abu Sa'id, regarding {And thus We have made you a just community} [Al-Baqarah 143], he said, \"Just.\""],[3049,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was directed toward the Ka'bah, they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while they were praying toward the Sacred House in Jerusalem?\" So Allah revealed: {And Allah would never let your faith be lost} [Al-Baqarah 143], to the end of the verse. 'Ubaydullah b. Musa said, \"This hadith informs you that prayer is part of faith.\""],[3050,"{So turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque} [Al-Baqarah 144]; he said, \"Its direction is toward it.\""],[3051,"\"Toward the water spout of the Ka'bah.\""],[3052,"On the authority of his mother, Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqbah, who was among the first emigrant women, regarding the words of Allah ﷻ {And seek help through patience and prayer} [Al-Baqarah 45], she said: 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf fainted, and they thought that he had died during it. So his wife Umm Kulthum went out to the mosque seeking help through the patience and prayer she had been commanded to use. When he regained consciousness, he said, \"Did I faint just now?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You are right. Two angels came to me and said, 'Come, let us take you to the Mighty, the Trustworthy for judgment.' Then another angel said, 'Return him, for this is one of those for whom you wrote happiness while they were still in their mothers' wombs, and his children will benefit from him for as long as Allah wills.'\" He lived for a month after that, then died."],[3053,"He received news from some of his family while he was traveling, so he performed two units of prayer. Then he said, \"We have done what Allah has commanded: seek help through patience and prayer.\" [Al-Baqarah 153]"],[3054,"What excellent two burdens, and what an excellent addition: those who, when affliction strikes them, say, 'Indeed we belong to Allah and indeed to Him we will return.' Those are the ones upon whom are blessings from their Lord and mercy—what excellent two burdens—and it is those who are guided—what an excellent addition."],[3055,"This verse was only revealed concerning the Ansar. In the pre-Islamic era, when they entered ihram, it was not permissible for them to circumambulate between al-Safa and al-Marwah. When we came, they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Allah revealed: {Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah} [al-Baqarah 158] to the end of the verse."],[3056,"They were among the rituals of the pre-Islamic era, so when Islam came we refrained from them. Then Allah revealed: {Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj to the House or performs Umrah, there is no blame upon him to walk between them. And whoever volunteers good...} the verse."],[3057,"A man came to him and said: Should I begin with al-Safa before al-Marwah, or begin with al-Marwah before al-Safa? And should I pray before I circumambulate, or circumambulate before I pray? And should I shave before I slaughter, or slaughter before I shave? Ibn Abbas said: Take that from the Book of Allah, for it is more deserving of being preserved. Allah Almighty said: {Indeed, al-Safa and al-Marwah are among the symbols of Allah} [al-Baqarah 158], so al-Safa is before al-Marwah. And He said: {Do not shave your heads until the offering reaches its place of sacrifice}, so slaughter is before shaving. And He said: {Purify My House for those who circumambulate, those who stay in retreat, and those who bow and prostrate} [al-Baqarah 125], so circumambulation is before prayer."],[3058,"He saw them circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah and said: This is from what your mother Ishmael bequeathed to you."],[3059,"In the pre-Islamic era, the devils used to play music all night long between Safa and Marwa. They had idols, which they worshipped. When Islam came, the Muslims said to the Prophet Muhammad, \"O Messenger of Allah, we will no longer perform the rite of Sa'y (walking) between Safa and Marwa, as it is something we used to do in the pre-Islamic era.\" Then Allah revealed the verse, \"Indeed, as for those who perform Hajj to the Ka'bah or 'umrah, there is no blame upon them for walking between them\" (Quran 2:158). This means that there is no sin upon them, but they will be rewarded."],[3060,"Were it not for a verse in the Book of Allah, I would not have informed anyone of anything. It was said: What is it, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: The verse: {Indeed, those who conceal what We sent down of clear proofs and guidance after We made it clear to the people in the Book – those are cursed by Allah and cursed by those who curse, except those who repent, correct themselves, and make clear}."],[3061,"Do not curse the wind, for it is from the breath of the Most Merciful. His saying, exalted is He: {and the directing of the winds and the clouds controlled between the heaven and the earth} [al-Baqarah 164]. But say: O Allah, we ask You for the good of this wind and the good of what is in it and the good of what it was sent with, and we seek refuge in You from its evil and the evil of what is in it and the evil of what it was sent with."],[3062,"\"Al-Mawaddah\" translates to \"love\" or \"affection\" in English."],[3063,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about faith, and he recited this verse: {Righteousness is not that you turn your faces toward the east and the west, but righteousness is [in] one who believes in Allah and the Last Day} [al-Baqarah 177] until he finished the verse. He said: Then he asked him again, and he recited it. Then he asked him again, and he recited it. Then he asked him, and he said: And when you do a good deed, your heart loves it; and when you do an evil deed, your heart hates it."],[3064,"A man gives while he is healthy, miserly, hoping for life and fearing poverty."],[3065,"Abdullah said: Al-ba'sa' is poverty, al-darra' is sickness, and 'when the distress' he said: at the time of fighting."],[3066,"He is the main pillar in the satisfaction of his family."],[3067,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He: {and payment to him with kindness} [al-Baqarah 178], he said: The debtor pays the claimant with kindness."],[3068,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled in favor of retaliation. On the condition of the two Shaykhs, and they did not include it. On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3069,"He stood and addressed the people here, meaning in Basra, and recited to them Surah al-Baqarah and explained what was in it. He came to this verse: {If he leaves wealth, the bequest is for the parents} [al-Baqarah 180] and said: This was abrogated. Then he mentioned what came after it."],[3070,"That ʿAlī entered upon a man of Banū Hāshim who was ill, to visit him, and he wanted to make a bequest, but he forbade him and said: “Allah says, ‘If he leaves good’ [al-Baqarah 180], meaning wealth. So leave your wealth to your heirs.”"],[3071,"As for the rulings of fasting: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah and began fasting three days of every month and the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ. Then Allah made fasting obligatory upon him, and Allah revealed, “O you who believe, fasting is prescribed for you as it was prescribed for those before you” [al-Baqarah 183] up to this verse, “And upon those who can afford it, a ransom of feeding a poor person” [al-Baqarah 184]. So whoever wished fasted, and whoever wished fed a poor person, and that sufficed for him. Then Allah revealed the other verse, “The month of Ramadan in which the Qur’an was sent down” [al-Baqarah 185] up to His saying, “So whoever of you witnesses the month, let him fast it” [al-Baqarah 185]. Thus Allah made fasting binding upon the resident healthy person, and granted a concession in it for the sick and the traveler, and the feeding remained established for the elderly person who is unable to fast. These are two states. They used to eat, drink, and go to women as long as they had not slept; but when they slept, they abstained. Then a man of the Anṣār called Ṣirmah was working while fasting until evening came. He went to his family, prayed the ʿIshāʾ, then slept and did not eat or drink until morning, so he woke up fasting. He exerted himself and slept, and woke up fasting. ʿUmar had had relations with women, with a slave-girl or a free woman, after he had slept, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. Then Allah revealed, “It has been made lawful for you, on the night of the fast, to go to your wives” [al-Baqarah 187] up to His saying, “Then complete the fast until nightfall” [al-Baqarah 187]."],[3072,"“Worship Me, and I will respond to you.”"],[3073,"“They are a tranquility for you, and you are a tranquility for them.”"],[3074,"We were at Constantinople, with ʿUqbah b. ʿĀmir al-Juhanī in charge of the people of Egypt and Faḍālah b. ʿUbayd al-Anṣārī in charge of the people of Syria. A great row of the Byzantines came out, and we formed a great row of Muslims against them. A man from the Muslims charged at the Byzantine row until he entered among them, then came out to us, advancing, and shouted at the people. They said, “He has thrown himself into destruction by his own hand.” Abū Ayyūb, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: “O people, you interpret this verse in this way, but it was revealed concerning us, the Anṣār. When Allah made His religion mighty and its supporters numerous, we said to one another secretly from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, ‘Our wealth has been lost. If only we could stay with it and put it right.’ Then Allah turned back upon us what we had intended.” He said: “Then Allah ﷻ revealed, ‘And spend in the way of Allah, and do not throw yourselves into destruction by your own hands’ [al-Baqarah 195]. The destruction was in staying with our wealth that we had intended. We were commanded to go on military expeditions.” Abū Ayyūb continued to fight in the way of Allah until Allah ﷻ took him."],[3075,"A man said to him: “O Abū ʿUmārah, ‘And do not throw yourselves into destruction by your own hands’ [al-Baqarah 195]—is it the man who meets the enemy and fights until he is killed?” He said: “No, rather it is the man who commits a sin and says, ‘Allah will not forgive me.’”"],[3076,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ, “And complete the ḥajj and the ʿumrah for Allah” [al-Baqarah 196], he said: “That you enter iḥrām from the dwelling of your family.”"],[3077,"He used to recite it: “So whoever does not find [an offering], then a fast of three days, consecutive.”"],[3078,"“Shawwāl, Dhū al-Qaʿdah, and ten [days] of Dhū al-Ḥijjah.”"],[3079,"\"I was walking with Ibn Abbas, who was performing the Hajj and he was riding on a camel, and he was saying, 'And they (the women) walk with us side to side.' I said, 'Do you joke while you are performing the Hajj?' He said, 'Playfulness is only what is allowed for women.'\""],[3080,"Al-rafath is sexual intercourse; al-fusūq is whatever one commits of disobedience to Allah, such as hunting and other things; and al-jidāl is reviling and quarreling."],[3081,"In the early days of the ḥajj, they used to trade at Minā, like the market of Majāz and the seasons of the ḥajj. When the Qur’an was revealed, they feared trading, so Allah ﷻ revealed, “There is no blame upon you in seeking bounty from your Lord” [al-Baqarah 198] during the seasons of the ḥajj."],[3082,"“The Sacred Monument” [al-Baqarah 198]: “all of Muzdalifah.”"],[3083,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us at 'Arafah. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"To proceed: the people of polytheism and idols used to depart from here at sunset, when the sun was on the mountain peaks like the turbans of men on their heads. Our ritual differs from their ritual. And they used to depart from al-Mash'ar al-Haram at sunrise, when the sun was on the mountain peaks like the turbans of men on their heads. Our ritual differs from their ritual.\""],[3084,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say between the Yamani Corner and the Black Stone: \"Our Lord, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and protect us from the punishment of the Fire\" [al-Baqarah 201]."],[3085,"I hired myself out to my people to carry me, and I set aside part of my wages for them on condition that they let me perform Hajj with them. Will that suffice? He said: \"You are among those of whom Allah ﷻ said: 'Those will have a share of what they earned, and Allah is swift in account' [al-Baqarah 202].\""],[3086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Hajj is 'Arafah, or 'Arafat. Whoever reaches 'Arafah before dawn has caught the Hajj. And the days of Mina are three. 'Whoever hastens [to leave] in two days, there is no sin upon him' [al-Baqarah 203], and whoever delays, there is no sin upon him.\""],[3087,"Umar ؓ"],[3088,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said: \"O people of Madinah, Allah is presenting to me concerning wine an allusion, and I do not know—perhaps He will send down to me a command about it.\" Then he stood and said: \"O people of Madinah, Allah has sent down the prohibition of wine. Whoever this verse reaches while he has some of it, let him not drink it or sell it.\" He said: So they poured it out in the streets of Madinah."],[3089,"When 'Do not approach the orphan's property except in the best way' [al-An'am 152] was revealed, they separated their property from the orphans' property, and food began to spoil and meat to rot. They complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Allah ﷻ sent down: 'Say: Setting things right for them is better, and if you mix with them, they are your brothers' [al-Baqarah 220]. He said: So they mixed with them."],[3090,"In it the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said something, so it is as he said, and if he did not say anything about it, then I say: 'Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish' [al-Baqarah 223]. \"If you wish, practice withdrawal, and if you wish, do not.\""],[3091,"This group of the Muhajirun used to approach women in an abominable manner, from the front and from the back, wherever they met them. When they came to Madinah, they married women from the Ansar and wanted from them what they used to do with the Muhajir women, but they rejected that and complained about it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So Allah ﷻ sent down: 'Your wives are a tilth for you, so come to your tilth however you wish' [al-Baqarah 223], meaning from the front or from the back, but only in the vagina. Ibn 'Abbas said: It was only from her back, in her front. [Al-Hakim said: It is according to the condition of Muslim]"],[3092,"A man used to divorce his wife as much as he wanted, even if he divorced her a hundred times or more, as long as he took her back before her waiting period ended. Until a man said to his wife: \"By Allah, I will not divorce you so that you become separated from me, nor will I keep you with me.\" She said: \"How is that?\" He said: \"I will divorce you, and whenever your waiting period is about to end, I will take you back, then divorce you, and do that repeatedly.\" The woman complained about that to 'A'ishah, and 'A'ishah mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he remained silent and did not say anything until the Qur'an was revealed: 'Divorce is twice; then either keep [her] in an acceptable manner or release [her] with kindness.'"],[3093,"His sister's husband divorced her, and he wanted to take her back, but Ma'qil prevented her. So Allah Almighty sent down: 'And when you divorce women and they have reached their term, do not prevent them from marrying their [former] husbands if they agree among themselves on an acceptable basis.'"],[3094,"\"If she carries him for nine months, she breastfeeds him for twenty-one months, and if she carries him for six months, she breastfeeds him for twenty-four months.\" Then he recited: 'And his carrying and weaning is thirty months' [al-Ahqaf 15]."],[3095,"This verse abrogated her waiting period in her family's home, so she may observe the waiting period wherever she wishes, according to the words of Allah Almighty: {without being forced to leave} [al-Baqarah 240]. 'Ata' said: If she wishes, she observes the waiting period in her family's home, and if she wishes, she may leave, according to the words of Allah ﷻ: {And if they leave, there is no blame upon you for what they do with themselves}."],[3096,"He stood and addressed the people here, reciting Surah al-Baqarah to them and explaining it to them. He came to this verse: {If he leaves wealth, the bequest is for the parents and near relatives} [al-Baqarah 180], and said: \"This has been abrogated.\" Then he recited until he came to this verse: {And those who are taken in death among you and leave wives behind} [al-Baqarah 234] up to the words of Allah Almighty: {without being forced to leave} [al-Baqarah 240], and said: \"And this too.\""],[3097,"From her: when her husband dies, she observes the waiting period wherever she wishes.\" According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3098,"When 'Guard strictly the prayers and the 'Asr prayer' was revealed, we recited it during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as Allah willed for us to recite it. Then Allah abrogated it and revealed: {Guard strictly the prayers and the middle prayer} [al-Baqarah 238]. A man said to him: Is it the 'Asr prayer? He said: \"I have informed you how it was revealed and how Allah abrogated it, and Allah knows best.\""],[3099,"Regarding the words of Allah Almighty: {Have you not considered those who left their homes in thousands, fearing death?} [al-Baqarah 243]. He said: They were four thousand who left fleeing from the plague. They said: We will go to a land where there is no death. Allah said to them: 'Die,' and they died. A prophet passed by them and asked Allah to revive them, so He revived them. They are the ones of whom Allah ﷻ said: {in thousands, fearing death} [al-Baqarah 243]."],[3100,"\"Do you marvel that intimate friendship was for Ibrahim, speech for Musa, and the vision for Muhammad ﷺ?\""],[3101,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque and sat with him. He mentioned the virtue of prayer, fasting, and charity. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which verse that Allah has revealed to you is greatest? He said: {Allah - there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence} [al-Baqarah 255], and he mentioned the verse until he completed it."],[3102,"\"The Footstool is the place of His two feet, and the Throne - its magnitude cannot be estimated.\""],[3103,"From 'Ali, ؓ ."],[3104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked al-Bara' b. 'Azib, saying: \"O Bara', how is your spending on your family?\" He said: He was generous to his family. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not consider it. He said: \"Indeed, your spending on your family, your children, and your servant is charity, so do not follow that with reproach or harm.\""],[3105,"He used to recite it as 'biribwah' with kasrah on the ra'. He said: Al-ribwah is an elevated place of the earth."],[3106,"He heard him saying, Umar asked the companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him, \"Do you know the meaning of the verse that says, 'Would any of you wish to have a garden with date-palms and vines...'\" [Al-Baqarah 266]? They replied, \"Allah knows best.\" Umar became angry and said, \"Say, 'We know' or 'We do not know.'\" Ibn Abbas said to himself, \"I have some knowledge about it, O commander of the faithful.\" Umar said, \"Say, 'O son of my brother, do not belittle yourself.'\" Ibn Abbas gave an example of a certain action and Umar asked, \"What kind of action?\" Ibn Abbas replied, \"A wealthy man who performs good deeds, then Allah sends devils to him, so he commits sins until his good deeds are completely destroyed.\""],[3107,"\"A strong, toxic wind.\""],[3108,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered the Zakat al-Fitr to be given in the form of a saa' of dates. A man came with inferior quality dates, so the Prophet ﷺ said to Abdullah ibn Rawaha, \"Do not give these dates as zakat.\" Then the Quran was revealed: \"O you who have believed, spend from the good things which you have earned and from that which We have produced for you from the earth. And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that] while you would not take it [yourself] except with closed eyes\" (Al-Baqarah 267)."],[3109,"\"Indeed, your children are a gift from Allah to you. He grants to whom He wills females and grants to whom He wills males. They and their wealth are for you when you need it.\""],[3110,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded that charity be given. A man came with some of this saḥl—Sufyān said: meaning the bad dates—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Who brought this?” And no one would bring anything except that it would be attributed to the one who brought it. Then the verse was revealed: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that] while you would not take it [yourself] except with closed eyes} [Al-Baqarah 267]. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two types of dates from being taken as charity: the Juʿrūr and the color of Ḥubayq. Al-Zuhrī said: “The two types from the dates of Madinah.” Sulaymān b. Kathīr concurred with him on the authority of al-Zuhrī."],[3111,"He forbade two types of dates: the Juʿrūr and the color of Ḥubayq. He said: “People used to aim for the worst of their fruits and bring them out as charity, so they were forbidden from two types of dates, and the verse was revealed: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that]}.”"],[3112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out with a staff in his hand. There were clusters of dates hanging in the mosque, one of which contained bad dates. He poked that cluster and said, “What harm would it do the owner of this if he were to give in charity something better than this? Indeed, the owner of this will eat bad dates on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he said, “By Allah, he will leave it debased for forty years for the ʿawāfī.” Then he said, “Do you know what the ʿawāfī are?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Birds and beasts of prey.”"],[3113,"It was revealed concerning the Anṣār. When the date palms were harvested, the Anṣār would bring out from their gardens clusters of unripe dates and hang them at the top of two pillars in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the poor among the Muhājirūn would eat from them. One of them would deliberately insert a cluster of bad dates, thinking that it was permissible amid the abundance of clusters that were placed. So it was revealed concerning those who did that: {And do not aim toward the defective therefrom, spending [from that] while you would not take it [yourself] except with closed eyes} [Al-Baqarah 267]. He says: If it were gifted to you, you would not accept it except with embarrassment toward its owner, out of annoyance that he sent you what he had no need for. {And know that Allah is Free of need} [Al-Baqarah 267] of your charities, {and Praiseworthy} [Al-Baqarah 267]."],[3114,"That they should give something to their relatives while they were polytheists. Then the verse was revealed: {Not upon you is their guidance, but Allah guides whom He wills} [Al-Baqarah 272] until it reached {and you will not be wronged} [Al-Baqarah 272]. He said: So He granted them a concession."],[3115,"From Jābir, may Allah be pleased"],[3116,"that the guaranteed forward loan for a specified term has been made lawful by Allah in the Book and He has permitted it. Allah ﷻ said: {O you who believe, when you contract a debt for a specified term, write it down} [Al-Baqarah 282] — the verse."],[3117,"Allah ﷻ said: {From among those whom you approve as witnesses} [Al-Baqarah 282], and they are not among those we approve. He said: So I sent to Ibn al-Zubayr asking him, and he said: “It is more fitting that when they are asked, they speak the truth.” He said: I have not seen judgment except according to what Ibn al-Zubayr said."],[3118,"When this verse was revealed: {If you disclose what is in your souls or conceal it, Allah will bring you to account for it} [Al-Baqarah 284], it weighed heavily upon them as nothing similar had before. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “Say: We hear and we obey.” So Allah cast faith into their hearts, and they said: We hear and we obey. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Allah does not burden a soul beyond its capacity. It will have what it earned and upon it what it incurred} [Al-Baqarah 286] until His saying: {or we erred} [Al-Baqarah 286]. He said: “I have done so” until the end of Al-Baqarah."],[3119,"May Allah have mercy on Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did something when it was revealed, and then the verse after it abrogated it: {It will have what it earned and upon it what it incurred} [Al-Baqarah 286]."],[3120,"When this verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: {The Messenger has believed in what was revealed to him from his Lord} [Al-Baqarah 285], the Prophet ﷺ said, “And he is more entitled to believe.”"],[3121,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Recite the two bright ones: Al-Baqarah and Āl ʿImrān.”"],[3122,"He led them in prayer and recited: “Alif Lām Mīm. Allah—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining.” Abu ʿUbayd said: As for the later reciters from the people of the two sanctuaries, Makkah and Madinah, the people of the two garrisons, Kufa and Basra, the people of Syria, Egypt, and others among the reciters, they recite it as “al-Qayyūm” [Āl ʿImrān:2], with no disagreement among them that I know of. Thus is the recitation with us, in conformity with the written text and what the community is upon, even though both forms have a basis in Arabic."],[3123,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Baṭḥāʾ when a cloud passed by. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Do you know what this is?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “It is clouds.” We said, “Clouds.” He said, “And rain-clouds.” We said, “And rain-clouds.” He said, “And high clouds.” We said, “And high clouds.” Then he fell silent. Then he said, “Do you know how much is between the heaven and the earth?” We said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Between them is a distance of five hundred years’ journey, and from each heaven to the next is a distance of five hundred years’ journey, and the thickness of each heaven is a distance of five hundred years’ journey. Above the seventh heaven is a sea, between its top and bottom is like what is between the heaven and the earth. Then above that are eight mountain goats, between their knees and hooves is like what is between the heaven and the earth, and Allah, exalted is He, is above that; nothing of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him.”"],[3124,"From Ibn ʿAbbās: “In it are precise verses” — these are the ones in Sūrat al-Anʿām: “Say: Come, I will recite what your Lord has forbidden to you: that you associate nothing with Him” to the end of the three verses."],[3125,"“Indeed, among what I fear for my community is that wealth will become abundant among them until they vie for it and fight over it. And among what I fear for my community is that the Qurʾān will be opened to them until the believer, the disbeliever, and the hypocrite recite it, and the believer will make its lawful lawful, seeking its interpretation” — to the end of the verse."],[3126,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say often: “O Turner of hearts, make our hearts firm upon Your religion.” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for us when we have believed in you?” He said, “Indeed, the hearts of the children of Adam are between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful, like a single heart; He turns it as He wills, like this.”"],[3127,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “The Balance is in the hand of the Most Merciful; He raises some people and lowers others, and the heart of the son of Adam is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; if He wills, He keeps it straight, and if He wills, He deviates it.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: “O Turner of hearts, make my heart firm upon Your religion.”"],[3128,"“The heart of the son of Adam is more changeable than a pot when it boils.”"],[3129,"I heard Ibn ʿAbbās reciting: “And no one knows its interpretation except Allah and those firmly rooted [Āl ʿImrān:7] in knowledge; they say, ‘We believe in it.’”"],[3130,"The first Scripture was revealed from one gate upon one mode, and the Qurʾān was revealed from seven gates upon seven modes: a restrainer, a commander, lawful, unlawful, precise, ambiguous, and parables. So make lawful its lawful, make unlawful its unlawful, do what you are commanded, refrain from what you are forbidden, take lesson from its parables, act upon its precise, believe in its ambiguous, and say: ‘We believe in it; all is from our Lord.’ And none will take heed except people of understanding."],[3131,"ʿUmar said: “Leave this; we believe in it; all is from our Lord.”"],[3132,"regarding Allah's statement, \"They kill the prophets unjustly and they kill those who enjoin justice among people\" [Āl ʿImrān 3:21]. He said, ʿĪsá (Jesus), the son of Mary was sent with twelve men from the disciples who taught people. He used to [teach them to] prohibit them from marrying their nieces. There was a king (Herod Antipas) who had a niece [named Herodias] who was taken by him so he desired her. He used to fulfill her needs every day.[Herodias'] mother said to her, \"If he asks you about your need, tell him to kill Yaḥyá (John), the son of Zakariyyah (Zachariah).\" King [Herod] asked her, \"[What is] your need?\" She replied, \"My need is for Yaḥyá, the son of Zakariyyah, to be killed.\" The king said, \"Ask for something else.\" She said, \"I ask for nothing else.\" When [Yaḥyá ] came, he gave the order, and he was beheaded on a tray.A drop of his blood continued to boil until Allah sent Bukhtanaṣṣar (Nebuchadnezzar). An old man directed him [to the boiling blood], and it entered his mind that the killing should not stop until this blood settles down. So he killed seventy thousand people in one day in one stroke, and in one house."],[3133,"\"Allah has revealed to your prophet ﷺ, 'I have killed seventy thousand people with the killing of Yahya bin Zakariya, and I will kill seventy thousand people with the killing of your grandson's son, seventy thousand and seventy thousand.'\""],[3134,"Polytheism is more hidden than the crawling of ants on a smooth rock in the dark night. Its least form is that you love for the sake of some injustice and hate for the sake of some justice, and that is the religion except love and hate. Allah, glorified is He, said: “Say: If you love Allah, then follow me; Allah will love you.”"],[3135,"“Unless you guard against them with precaution” [Āl ʿImrān:28]. He said: Precaution is speaking with the tongue while the heart is at rest with faith; he does not stretch forth his hand to kill, nor to sin, for that he has no excuse."],[3136,"Zakariyah took care of her, so he entered the sanctuary and found grapes with her out of season. Zakariyah said, \"How did you come by this?\" She replied, \"It is from Allah. Indeed, Allah provides for whom He wills without account.\" Zakariyah said, \"The One who provides you with grapes out of season is also capable of granting me a child, although I am old and my wife is barren.\" Thereupon, Zakariyah called upon his Lord. When he was given the glad tidings of Yahya (John), he said, \"My Lord, grant me a sign.\" Allah replied, \"Your sign is that you will not speak to people for three nights consecutively, except by gesture.\" Zakariyah said, \"My tongue shall remain restrained from speech without having any illness, while I am in a sound state.\""],[3137,"\"Every prophet has supporters from among the prophets, and my supporter among them is my father and intimate friend, Ibrāhīm.\" Then he recited: \"Indeed, the people most worthy of Ibrāhīm are those who followed him and this Prophet and those who believe, and Allah is the ally of the believers.\""],[3138,"Israel was afflicted by sciatica and would spend the night crying out. He vowed that if Allah healed him, he would not eat any meat containing veins. So the Jews made it forbidden, and then the verse was revealed: 'All food was lawful for the Children of Israel except what Israel made unlawful for himself before the Torah was sent down. Say, \"Bring the Torah and recite it, if you are truthful\"' (Al Imran 93). This was before the Torah."],[3139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, regarding sciatica: 'Take the tail fat of an Arabian ram, neither the largest nor the smallest, cut it into small pieces, then melt it thoroughly, and divide it into three parts. Drink one part each day on an empty stomach.' Anas b. Sirin said: 'I prescribed that to a large number of people, and all of them were cured by the permission of Allah Almighty.'"],[3140,"Regarding the verse 'The first House established for mankind is the one at Bakkah, blessed' (Al Imran 96): Was it the first house built on earth? He said: 'No, but it was the first house in which blessing, guidance, the Station of Ibrahim, and security for whoever enters it were placed. If you wish, I will tell you how Allah built it. Allah revealed to Ibrahim: \"Build Me a house on earth.\" He felt unable, so Allah sent down the Sakīnah, a swift wind with a head. One followed the other until it stopped, then coiled like a snake at the site of the House. Ibrahim built, raising a wall each day. When he reached the place of the Stone, he said to his son: \"Bring me a stone.\" The son searched for a stone and brought one, but found that the Black Stone had already been set in place. The son asked: \"Where did you get this?\" He said: \"One who does not rely on your building brought it—Jibril ﷺ brought it from heaven.\" Then he completed it."],[3141,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: 'O people, Allah has made the Hajj obligatory upon you.' Al-Aqraʿ b. Ḥābis stood up and said: 'Every year, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'If I said that, it would become obligatory, and if it were obligatory, you would not perform it—or you would not be able to perform it. The Hajj is once; whoever does more, it is voluntary.'"],[3142,"Al-Aqraʿ b. Ḥābis asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Is Hajj once every year?' He said: 'No, rather once; whoever does more, it is voluntary.' On this topic, there is also a narration from ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib with elaboration and clarification from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3143,"When this verse was revealed: 'And due to Allah from the people is the Hajj to the House for whoever is able to make a way to it' (Al Imran 97), they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is it every year?' He remained silent. Then they said: 'Is it every year?' He remained silent. Then they said: 'Is it every year?' He said: 'No, and if I had said yes, it would have become obligatory.' Then Allah Almighty sent down: 'O you who believe, do not ask about things which, if they are disclosed to you, will distress you' (Al-Ma'idah 101)."],[3144,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: 'O you who believe, fear Allah as He should be feared, and do not die except as Muslims' (Al Imran 102), then said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, if a single drop of zaqqūm were to fall into the seas of the earth, it would corrupt them.' In the narration of Wahb b. Jarīr: 'It would embitter the livelihoods of the people of the world, so how about the one whose food it is?'"],[3145,"That He is obeyed and not disobeyed, remembered and not forgotten."],[3146,"\"They are the ones who migrated with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Mecca to Medina.\""],[3147,"Whoever would like his building to be raised high and his ranks elevated, let him pardon the one who wrongs him, give to the one who withholds from him, and maintain ties with the one who cuts him off."],[3148,"Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq entered the mosque while ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb was addressing the people. He went to the room in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had died, uncovered his face from the striped Yemeni cloak with which he was shrouded, looked at him, leaned over to kiss his face, and said: 'By Allah, Allah will not cause you to die twice after this death of yours, after which you will never die.' Then he went out to the mosque while ʿUmar was speaking to the people. Abū Bakr said: 'Sit down, O ʿUmar.' He refused. He spoke to him twice or three times, but he refused. Then he stood up and recited the testimony of faith. When he finished, he said: 'Now then, whoever worshipped Muḥammad, Muhammad ﷺ has died; and whoever worshipped Allah, Allah is ever-living and never dies.' Then he recited: 'And We did not grant immortality to any human before you' (Al-Anbiyāʾ 34), and 'Muḥammad is but a messenger; messengers have passed away before him' (Āl ʿImrān 144), and he recited up to 'the grateful.' No sooner had he recited it than the people became certain of the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so much so that someone said: 'The people did not know that this verse had been revealed until Abū Bakr recited it.' Al-Zuhrī said: Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib informed me that ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb said: 'When Abū Bakr recited it, I was stunned and fell to the ground, and I became certain that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had died.'"],[3149,"He said: 'The Prophet ﷺ was not given victory in any battle as he was given on the day of Uḥud.' We objected to that, so Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'Between me and whoever disputes this is the Book of Allah Almighty. Allah Almighty says concerning the day of Uḥud: \"And Allah certainly fulfilled His promise to you when you were killing them by His permission\" (Āl ʿImrān 152). Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'Al-ḥiss means killing.' \"Until you lost courage and disputed about the command and disobeyed after He had shown you what you love. Among you are some who desire this world and among you are some who desire the Hereafter. Then He turned you away from them to test you, and He has pardoned you, and Allah is the possessor of bounty for the believers\" (Āl ʿImrān 152). He meant the archers by this. The Prophet ﷺ had stationed them in a position and said: \"Protect our rear. If you see us being killed, do not come to help us; and if you see us taking spoils, do not share with us.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions gained spoils and overran the camp of the polytheists, all the archers left their position and entered the camp to take booty. The ranks of the Prophet's Companions had engaged, and they were like this—and he interlaced his fingers—and they became entangled. When the archers abandoned that gap where they had been, the cavalry entered from that spot upon the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, and they struck one another, became entangled, and many Muslims were killed. At the beginning of the day, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Companions had the upper hand, until seven or nine of the banner-bearers of the polytheists were killed. The Muslims fell back toward the mountain, but they did not reach what people call al-Ghābah; rather, it was below al-Mihrās. Satan shouted: \"Muḥammad has been killed!\" They did not doubt that it was true. We remained in that state, not doubting that he had been killed, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appeared between the two Saʿds. We recognized him by his swaying gait when he walked. We rejoiced as if nothing had afflicted us. He climbed toward us, saying: \"Allah's anger is severe against a people who bloodied the face of their Prophet.\" And another time he said: \"O Allah, it is not for them to prevail over us,\" until he reached us. He stayed a while, then Abū Sufyān shouted from the foot of the mountain: \"Exalted be Hubal! Exalted be Hubal!\"—meaning his deity. \"Where is Ibn Abī Kabshah? Where is Ibn Abī Quḥāfah? Where is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb?\" ʿUmar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I answer him?\" He said: \"Yes.\" When he said \"Exalted be Hubal,\" ʿUmar said: \"Allah is most high and most mighty.\" Abū Sufyān said: \"O Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, this is a day of silence.\" He repeated: \"Where is Ibn Abī Kabshah? Where is Ibn Abī Quḥāfah? Where is Ibn al-Khaṭṭāb?\" ʿUmar said: \"This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this is Abū Bakr, and here I am, ʿUmar.\" Abū Sufyān said: \"A day for the day of Badr; days alternate, and war is a back-and-forth.\" ʿUmar said: \"Not equal! Our dead are in Paradise, and your dead are in the Fire.\" He said: \"You claim that; then we have been disappointed and lost.\" Then Abū Sufyān said: \"You will find mutilation among your dead, and that was not by the counsel of our chiefs.\" Then the zeal of the Age of Ignorance overtook him, and he said: \"As for that, if it happened, we did not dislike it.\""],[3150,"I raised my head on the day of Uhud and began to look, and there was none among them but he was swaying under his shield from drowsiness. That is His saying, Exalted is He: {Then He sent down upon you, after distress, security—drowsiness overcoming a party of you} [Al Imran 154]—the verse."],[3151,"When your brothers were struck at Uhud, Allah placed their souls in the crops of green birds that come to the rivers of Paradise, eat from its fruits, and shelter in lanterns of gold hanging in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food, drink, and resting place, they said: Who will convey to our brothers about us that we are alive in Paradise, being provided for, so that they will not renounce jihad or hold back in war? Allah, Exalted is He, said: I will convey it to them on your behalf. So Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: {And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah} [Al Imran 169]—the verse."],[3152,"Your father and grandfather—meaning Abu Bakr and al-Zubayr—were among those of whom Allah, Exalted is He, said: {Those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after the wound had befallen them} [Al Imran 172]."],[3153,"The last words of Ibrahim when he was cast into the fire were: 'Sufficient for me is Allah, and He is the best disposer of affairs.' And your Prophet ﷺ said the like of it: {Those to whom the people said, 'Indeed, the people have gathered against you, so fear them.' But it increased them in faith, and they said, 'Sufficient for us is Allah} [Al Imran 173]—Allah and the best disposer of affairs.'"],[3154,"By the One besides whom there is no deity, there is no soul on earth but that death is better for it. If it is a believer, Allah says: {But those who fear their Lord will have gardens beneath which rivers flow} [Al Imran 198]. And if it is a wicked person, Allah says: {We only prolong for them so that they may increase in sin}."],[3155,"\"Abdullah will be surrounded by what he was stingy with on the Day of Judgment,\" a snake will have two raisins that it will consume in his grave, and it will say, \"I am your wealth that you were stingy with.\" I heard Yahya ibn Mansur say, \"I heard Abu Amr Al-Mustamli say, 'I heard Abu Hisham Al-Rifai say, 'I heard Abu Bakr ibn Ayash say, 'By Allah, I never lied about Abu Ishaq, and I do not see Abu Ishaq lying about Abu Wail, and I do not see Abu Wail lying about Abdullah.'\" Ath-Thawri narrated it from Abu Ishaq upon the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3157,"The space of a whip in Paradise is better than this world and all that is in it. Recite, if you wish: {So whoever is drawn away from the Fire and admitted to Paradise has attained success. And what is the life of this world except the enjoyment of delusion}."],[3158,"By Allah, if every one of us who rejoiced in what he was given and was praised for what he did not do is punished, then we will all be punished. Ibn Abbas said: This verse was only revealed concerning the People of the Book. The Jews came to him—the Prophet ﷺ asked them about something, and they concealed it. Then they came to him and he asked them, and they informed him of something other than that. Then they went out, thinking that they had informed him of what he asked them about, and they sought praise for that and rejoiced in what they were given of concealing from him what he asked them about."],[3159,"\"It was hemorrhoid with him, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to pray on his side.\""],[3160,"They will wish to come out of the Fire, but they will not come out of it [al-Ma'idah 37]. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed me that they are the disbelievers. He said: I said to Jabir: What about His saying: {Indeed, whoever You admit to the Fire, You have disgraced him} [Al Imran 192]? He said: Allah has disgraced him when He burned him with the Fire, or less than that disgrace—by the sea of the water-skin, he is ruined."],[3161,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, I do not hear that Allah has mentioned women in the emigration at all. So Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: {And their Lord responded to them, 'Indeed, I will not allow the work of any worker among you to be lost, whether male or female; you are of one another} [Al Imran 195]."],[3162,"An enemy from their land descended upon the Negus. The emigrants came to him and said: We would love to march out against them to fight alongside you, so that you may see our courage and we may repay you for what you have done for us. He said: No. The remedy by Allah's help is better than the remedy by people's help. He said: And concerning him it was revealed: {And indeed, among the People of the Book are those who believe in Allah and what has been sent down to you and what was sent down to them, humble before Allah} [Al Imran 199]."],[3163,"It reached him that Abu Ubaydah was besieged in Syria and that the people had gathered against him. Umar wrote to him: Peace be upon you. Now then: No station of hardship befalls a believing servant but Allah makes after it relief, and hardship will never overcome two eases. {O you who believe, be patient, endure, and remain stationed, and fear Allah so that you may succeed} [Al Imran 200]. He said: So Abu Ubaydah wrote back to him: Peace be upon you. Now then: Indeed, Allah says in His Book: {Know that the life of this world is play and amusement and adornment and boasting among you and multiplication in wealth and children} [al-Hadid 20]—to the end of it. He said: So Umar went out with his letter, sat on the pulpit, and read it to the people of Madinah. Then he said: O people of Madinah, Abu Ubaydah is only alluding to you: desire jihad."],[3164,"I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: 'In the time of the Prophet ﷺ there was no military campaign in which one remained stationed, but rather waiting for prayer after prayer.'"],[3165,"\"Ask me about Surah An-Nisa, for I read the Quran while I was young.\""],[3166,"\"Verily, ties of kinship are severed, and verily, blessings are denied, and verily, when Allah brings hearts closer, nothing can ever separate them.\" Then he recited: \"If you were to spend all that is on Earth, you could not have brought their hearts together.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Family ties are a branch of mercy from the Most Merciful, and it will come on the Day of Resurrection speaking with a fluent tongue. Whoever maintains it, Allah will maintain him, and whoever severs it, Allah will sever him.\""],[3167,"There was some dispute between Abu Talha and Umm Sulaym, so Abu Talha wanted to divorce Umm Sulaym. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Indeed, divorcing Umm Sulaym is a grave sin.\""],[3168,"Three people call upon Allah but are not answered: a man who has a wife of bad character and does not divorce her; a man who has a debt owed to him by another man but does not take witnesses; and a man who gives his wealth to a fool, while Allah ﷻ has said, {And do not give the foolish your wealth} [An-Nisa: 5]."],[3169,"Regarding His saying, the Most High, {And whoever is rich, let him abstain} [An-Nisa: 6], meaning he should not take from the orphan's wealth. {And whoever is poor, let him eat with what is reasonable} [An-Nisa: 6], meaning he may eat from it to the extent of his needs, so that he does not take from the orphan's wealth."],[3170,"They are appeased by them, so if there is any shortfall in money, apologize to them."],[3171,"When Allah revealed {And do not approach the orphan's property except in the best way} [Al-An'am: 152] and {Indeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly are only consuming fire into their bellies, and they will burn in a Blaze} [An-Nisa: 10], those who had an orphan with them separated his food from their food and his drink from their drink. As a result, some of his food and drink would remain and be kept until he ate it or it spoiled. That became difficult for them, so they mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Allah revealed {And they ask you about orphans. Say, \"Improvement for them is best. And if you mix with them, they are your brothers\"} [Al-Baqarah: 220]. So they mixed their food with their food and their drink with their drink."],[3172,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit me while I was ill among Banu Salama. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how should I divide my wealth among my children?\" He did not reply to me. Then the verse {Allah instructs you concerning your children} [An-Nisa: 11] was revealed. The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting the hadith of Shu'ba from Muhammad b. al-Munkadir on this topic with different wording. This chain is authentic, but they did not include it, though they included its origin."],[3173,"If I had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about three things, it would be dearer to me than red camels: who would be the caliph after him; regarding a people who say, \"We acknowledge zakah on our wealth but will not pay it to you,\" is it lawful to fight them; and about kalalah."],[3174,"I was the last person to see Umar. I heard him say, \"The correct statement is what I said.\" I said, \"What did you say?\" He said, \"I said, 'Kalalah is one who has no child.'\""],[3175,"If the Prophet ﷺ had clarified them for us, it would be dearer to me than the world and all it contains: the caliphate, kalalah, and riba."],[3176,"Seven are forbidden by lineage and seven by marriage. Then he recited this verse: {Forbidden to you are your mothers, your daughters, your sisters, your paternal aunts, your maternal aunts, brother's daughters, sister's daughters} [An-Nisa: 23] - these are from lineage - {and your mothers who nursed you, your sisters through nursing, your wives' mothers, your stepdaughters under your guardianship from your wives with whom you have consummated marriage - but if you have not consummated marriage with them, there is no sin upon you - and the wives of your sons who are from your loins, and to gather two sisters in marriage, except what has already occurred; and do not marry women whom your fathers married}."],[3177,"\"Seven are forbidden by lineage and seven by marriage.\""],[3178,"He said regarding this verse {And [also prohibited are] the married women except those your right hands possess} [An-Nisa: 24]: \"Every woman with a husband, having intercourse with her is adultery, except for those taken captive.\""],[3179,"Abu Nadrah said: I said, 'We do not recite it that way.' Ibn Abbas said, 'By Allah, Allah sent it down that way.'"],[3180,"And she recited this verse: {And those who guard their private parts, except from their spouses or what their right hands possess, for indeed they are not blameworthy. But whoever seeks beyond that} [al-Mu'minun: 5] — what Allah has given in marriage or granted possession, then he has transgressed."],[3181,"Indeed in Surah al-Nisa' there are five verses that I would not trade for the world and all it contains: {Indeed, Allah does not wrong [even] an atom's weight, and if there is a good deed, He multiplies it and gives from Himself a great reward} [al-Nisa': 40]; {If you avoid the major sins that you are forbidden, We will remove from you your misdeeds and admit you to a noble entrance} [al-Nisa': 31]; {Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills} [al-Nisa': 48]; {And if, when they wronged themselves, they had come to you and asked forgiveness of Allah, and the Messenger had asked forgiveness for them, they would have found Allah Accepting of repentance and Merciful}; {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself then seeks forgiveness of Allah will find Allah Forgiving and Merciful} [al-Nisa': 110]. Abdullah said: 'I would not trade for them the world and all it contains.'"],[3182,"O Messenger of Allah, do men go to battle while we do not, and we do not fight so as to be martyred, and we have only half the inheritance? Then Allah revealed {And do not wish for that by which Allah has made some of you exceed others}."],[3183,"\"To those also, to whom your right hand was pledged, give your portion.\" When the Emigrants came to Medina. they inherited from the Helpers without any blood-relationship with them for the brotherhood which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established between them. When the following verse was revealed: \"To (benefit) everyone we have appointed shares and heirs to property left by parent and relatives.\" it abrogated the verse: \"To those also, to whom your right hand was pledged, give their due portion.\" This alliance was made for help, well wishing and cooperation. Now a legacy can be made for him. (The right to)inheritance was abolished. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2922)"],[3184,"Allah brought a servant from among His servants to whom He had given wealth, and said to him: 'What did you do in the world?' He said — {and they will not conceal from Allah any account} [al-Nisa': 42] — 'I did nothing, O Lord, except that You gave me wealth and I used to trade with people, and it was my nature to be lenient with the one who could pay and to give respite to the one in difficulty.' Allah Almighty said: 'I am more entitled to that than you. Forgive My servant.' Uqbah b. Amir al-Juhani and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari said: 'This is how we heard it from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his family and peace.'"],[3185,"About this verse: {By Allah, our Lord, we were not associators} [al-An'am: 23], and He said in another verse: {and they will not conceal from Allah any account} [al-Nisa': 42]. Ibn Abbas said: 'As for His saying {By Allah, our Lord, we were not associators} [al-An'am: 23], when they saw on the Day of Resurrection that none would enter Paradise except the people of Islam, they said: \"Come, let us deny.\" Then Allah sealed their mouths, and their hands and feet spoke, {and they will not conceal from Allah any account} [al-Nisa': 42].'"],[3186,"A man from the Ansar invited us before wine was forbidden. When the Maghrib prayer came, a man went forward and recited 'Say, O disbelievers,' but he became confused. Then it was revealed: {Do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying}."],[3187,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and some companions of his came to the Prophet ﷺ in Makkah and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, we were in honor while we were associators, but when we believed we became humiliated.' He said: 'I have been commanded to pardon, so do not fight; restrain yourselves.' Then Allah Almighty revealed: {Have you not seen those who were told, \"Restrain your hands and establish prayer and give zakah\"? Then when fighting was prescribed for them, at once a party of them feared people} [al-Nisa': 77]."],[3188,"The man used to come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and greet him, then he would return to his people who were polytheists. If the Muslims made a mistake in a secret mission or in a battle, the man would set a slave free as an atonement. If the man had a contract with a group between themselves, he would pay the blood money to them and set free the slave who was taken as a captive. (Surah An-Nisa 92) The Prophet ﷺ said: \"The man should fulfill his covenant and his people should fulfill theirs, and he should set free the captive slave who has been taken by his people.\""],[3189,"It was revealed concerning Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, who was wounded."],[3190,"I traveled to A'ishah about this verse: {It is not by your wishes or the wishes of the People of the Book; whoever does evil will be recompensed for it} [al-Nisa': 123]. She said: 'It is what afflicts you in this world,' according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3191,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And what is recited to you in the Book concerning orphan girls} [al-Nisa': 127] at the beginning of the surah, from the inheritance laws: they used not to give inheritance to a child until he reached puberty."],[3192,"He had a wife older than him, and he married a young woman in addition to her, and he preferred the virgin over her. His first wife refused to be content with that, so he divorced her with one divorce. Then when only a little of her waiting period remained, he said: 'If you wish, I will take you back and you will be patient with being less preferred; if you wish, I will leave you until your waiting period ends.' She said: 'Rather take me back; I will be patient with being less preferred.' He took her back, then again preferred the other over her, and she did not remain patient with being less preferred. Then he divorced the other one and preferred the young woman over her. That is the reconciliation about which it has reached us that Allah revealed: {And if a woman fears from her husband contempt or evasion, there is no sin upon them if they make terms of settlement between them}."],[3193,"I was with Ali b. Abi Talib when a man said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, what do you think of the words of Allah, Exalted is He: {Allah will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will never grant the disbelievers a way over the believers} [An-Nisa: 141], while they fight them and prevail and kill?\" Ali said, \"Come closer, come closer.\" Then he said, {Allah will judge between you on the Day of Resurrection, and Allah will never grant the disbelievers a way over the believers}.\""],[3194,"“And there is none of the People of the Book but will surely believe in him before his death” (An-Nisāʾ 4:159). He said: the coming forth (return) of Jesus, son of Mary—may God’s blessings be upon him."],[3195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to set out for the land of the Negus. This reached Quraysh, so they sent Amr b. al-As and Umarah b. al-Walid, and they gathered gifts for the Negus. We arrived, and they arrived at the Negus. They brought him a gift, and he accepted it, and they prostrated to him. Then Amr b. al-As said, \"A people from among us have turned away from our religion, and they are in your land.\" The Negus said to them, \"In my land?\" He said, \"Yes.\" So he sent for us. Ja'far said to us, \"Let none of you speak; I am your spokesman today.\" We came to the Negus while he was seated in his assembly, with Amr b. al-As on his right and Umarah on his left, and the priests and monks were seated in two rows. Amr and Umarah said to him, \"They do not prostrate to you.\" When we reached him, the priests and monks who were with him shouted at us, \"Prostrate to the king!\" Ja'far said, \"We prostrate only to Allah.\" The Negus said to him, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Allah sent among us His Messenger, and he is the Messenger whose coming Jesus announced, a Messenger who would come after him, whose name is Ahmad. He commanded us to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, to establish prayer, to give zakat, and he commanded us to do good and forbade us from evil.\" He said, \"The people were impressed by his words. When Amr saw that, he said to him, 'May Allah preserve the king, they disagree with you about Jesus son of Mary.' The Negus said to Ja'far, 'What does your companion say about the son of Mary?' He said, 'He says about him the word of Allah: he is the Spirit of Allah and His Word, which He brought forth from the chaste virgin, whom no human being touched.' He said, 'The Negus picked up a stick from the ground and raised it, saying, \"O assembly of priests and monks, what these people say about the son of Mary does not exceed what you say by the weight of this. Welcome to you and to the one from whom you have come. I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah, and that he is the one whose coming Jesus son of Mary announced. Were it not for the kingship I am in, I would come to him and carry his sandals. Stay in my land as long as you wish.\" He ordered food and clothing for them, and said, \"Return to these two their gift.\""],[3196,"A man died and left a daughter and a full sister. He said, \"The daughter gets half, and the sister gets nothing; whatever remains goes to his male relatives.\" A man said to him, \"But Umar b. al-Khattab ruled otherwise: he gave the daughter half and the sister half.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"Are you more knowledgeable or Allah?\" Ma'mar said, \"I did not understand the implication of that until I met Ibn Tawus and mentioned to him the hadith of al-Zuhri. He said, 'My father informed me that he heard Ibn Abbas say: Allah, Exalted is He, said: {If a man dies, having no child but a sister, she shall have half of what he leaves} [An-Nisa: 176]. Ibn Abbas said, \"So you say she gets half even if he has a child.\""],[3197,"He said to me, 'O Jubayr, do you recite Al-Ma'idah?' I said, 'Yes.' She said, 'Indeed, it is the last surah that was revealed. Whatever you find in it of permissible things, deem them permissible, and whatever you find of forbidden things, deem them forbidden.'"],[3198,"The last surah to be revealed was Surah Al-Ma'idah."],[3199,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to kill dogs. The people said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is made lawful for us from this community that you commanded to be killed?\" Then Allah revealed: {They ask you what is lawful for them. Say: Lawful for you are good things, and what you have trained of hunting animals, teaching them} [Al-Ma'idah: 4]."],[3200,"The slaughtered animals of the Jews and Christians were made lawful only because they believed in the Torah and the Gospel."],[3201,"From Ibn Abbas regarding His words, Exalted is He: {He made among you prophets} [Al-Ma'idah: 20] he said: He made from among you prophets. {And made you kings} [Al-Ma'idah: 20] he said: a wife and a servant. {And gave you what He had not given anyone among the worlds} [Al-Ma'idah: 20] he said: those who were among them at that time."],[3202,"Regarding His words, Exalted is He: {Our Lord, show us those two who led us astray from among the jinn and mankind, that we may put them under our feet} he said: Iblis and the son of Adam who killed his brother."],[3203,"He heard a reciter reciting {O you who believe, fear Allah and seek the means to Him} [Al-Ma'idah: 35]. He said: the nearness. Then he said: The knowledgeable ones among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ knew that Ibn Umm Abd (Abdullah b. Mas'ud) was among the closest of them to Allah as a means. On the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3204,"Two verses were abrogated from Surah Al-Ma'idah: {So judge between them or turn away from them} [Al-Ma'idah: 42]. Then Allah, Exalted is He, revealed: {And judge between them by what Allah has revealed, and do not follow their desires} [Al-Ma'idah: 49]. \"Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it.\" Sahih."],[3205,"We were with Ḥudhayfah, and they mentioned the verse, \"And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed – then it is those who are the disbelievers.\" [Māʾidah 5:44] Then a man from the people said, \"Indeed, this is concerning the Children of Israel.\" Ḥudhayfah responded [sarcastically], \"What an excellent example are ʿyour] brothers in the Children of Israel: that all sweetness is for you and all bitterness is for them? Not at all! By the One in whose hand is my soul, until you follow the Sunnah (their legacy) with the Sunnah (as your legacy), step by step, just as you follow the Qudhah with the Qudhah.\""],[3206,"Indeed, it is not the disbelief that they think it is. It is not a disbelief that removes one from the religion. {And whoever does not judge by what Allah has revealed, those are the disbelievers} [Al-Ma'idah: 44]. It is a disbelief less than disbelief."],[3207,"I heard ʿIyāḍ al-Ashʿarī say: When {Allah will bring a people whom He loves and who love Him} [Quran 5:54] was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “They are your people, O Abū Mūsā,” and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gestured with his hand toward Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī."],[3208,"The Prophet ﷺ was on guard until this verse was revealed, \"And Allah protects you from the people.\" [Hadeeth from Al-Ma'idah 67] So, the Prophet ﷺ removed his head from the dome and said to them, \"O people, go away, for Allah has protected me.\""],[3209,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {So record us among the witnesses} [Quran 3:53], he said, “With the community of Muhammad ﷺ. And his community bore witness for him to the conveyance [of the message], and they bore witness for the messengers that they had indeed conveyed.”"],[3210,"ʿAbdullāh was brought an udder, and he said to the people, “Come near,” and they began eating it. One man among them was in a corner, and ʿAbdullāh said, “Come near,” but he said, “I do not want it.” He said, “Why?” He said, “Because I have forbidden the udder [for myself].” ʿAbdullāh said, “This is from the steps of Satan.” Then ʿAbdullāh said: {O you who believe, do not forbid the good things which Allah has made lawful for you and do not transgress. Indeed, Allah does not like the transgressors} [Quran 5:87]. “Come near, eat, and expiate your oath, for this is from the steps of Satan.”"],[3211,"Two Christian men testified before him concerning the will of a Muslim man who had died among them. He said: The heirs of the will became suspicious, so they brought the two to Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī, and he made them swear after the afternoon prayer by Allah that they had not sold it for a price and had not concealed the testimony of Allah, [saying], “Indeed, we would then be among the sinful.” ʿĀmir said: Then Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī said, “By Allah, this is a story [a case].”"],[3212,"Quraysh said to the Prophet ﷺ, “Call upon Allah, your Lord, to make al-Ṣafā into gold for us, and we will believe in you.” He said, “Will you do it?” They said, “Yes.” So he called upon Allah, and Gabriel came to him and said, “Your Lord sends you greetings of peace and says: If you wish, al-Ṣafā will become gold for them by morning; then whoever disbelieves among them, I will punish him with a punishment with which I have not punished anyone in the worlds. And if you wish, I will open for them the gates of repentance and mercy.” He said, “O Lord, the gate of repentance and mercy.”"],[3213,"When Surah al-Anʿām was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ glorified Allah, then said, “So many angels escorted this surah that they filled the horizon.”"],[3214,"They are two terms: the term of this world and a term in the Hereafter, appointed with Him, known to none but Allah. And His saying: {And if We had sent down to you a book written on paper and they had touched it with their hands} [Quran 6:7] — he said, “Even if they touched it and looked at it, they would not believe in it.”"],[3215,"It was revealed concerning Abū Ṭālib: he used to forbid the polytheists from harming the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but he distanced himself from what he brought. Sahih."],[3216,"It was revealed concerning Abū Ṭālib: he used to forbid the polytheists from harming him and he kept away from him. The hadith of Ḥamza b. Ḥabīb is sahih according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[3217,"\"O Muhammad, we know that you maintain family ties and speak the truth, and we do not consider you a liar. However, we reject the message that you have brought. So Allah, the Almighty, revealed: 'We know that what they say grieves you. Indeed, they do not deny you [Muhammad], but it is the verses of Allah that the wrongdoers reject.'\" [Surah Al-An'am, verse 33]"],[3218,"From Abū Hurayrah, regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {nations like yourselves} [Quran 6:38], he said: All creatures will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection — beasts, riding animals, birds, and everything — and to the extent of Allah’s justice, He will exact retribution for the hornless animal against the horned one. Then He will say, “Be dust.” That is when {the disbeliever will say, “Would that I were dust”} [Quran 78:40]. Jaʿfar al-Jidhrī — this is Ibn Burqān — Muslim used him as evidence, and it is sahih according to his condition, but they did not include it. According to the condition of Muslim."],[3219,"“This concerns Abraham and his companions; it is not about this community.”"],[3220,"\"The settled (meaning a fetus) is what was in the womb, whether it is alive or has already died, and the entrusted is what is in the grave.\""],[3221,"Oh, for your mother! That is his light, and he is his light. When he manifests with his light, nothing can reach him."],[3222,"Al-ḥamūlah is what carries among camels, and al-farsh is the small ones."],[3223,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar."],[3224,"Ibn Abbas said: 'Inability and prudence are part of divine decree.'"],[3225,"Indeed, in the livestock there are clear signs; they are the Mother of the Book. Then he recited: {Say, 'Come, I will recite what your Lord has prohibited to you'} [Al-An'am 151] to the end of the verse."],[3226,"When Allah revealed {And do not approach the property of the orphan except in the way that is best} [Al-An'am 152] and {Indeed, those who devour the property of orphans unjustly are only consuming fire into their bellies, and they will be burned in a Blaze} [An-Nisa 10], whoever had an orphan under his care separated his food from his own food and his drink from his own drink. Then if something was left over from the orphan's food, it was kept for him until he ate it or it spoiled. That became difficult for them, so they mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then Allah ﷻ revealed {They ask you about orphans. Say, 'Improvement for them is best. And if you mix with them, they are your brothers'} [Al-Baqarah 220]. So they mixed their food with their food and their drink with their drink."],[3227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will pledge allegiance to me upon these verses?' Then he recited {Say, 'Come, I will recite what your Lord has prohibited to you'} [Al-An'am 151] until he finished the three verses. Whoever fulfills them, his reward is with Allah. Whoever omits anything from them, Allah will catch him with it in this world, and that will be his punishment. Whoever delays it to the Hereafter, his affair is with Allah; if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him."],[3228,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line for us, then he drew lines on his right and left. Then he said, \"This is the way of Allah, and these are different paths, on every path there is a devil calling towards it.\" [And, \"This is My path, which is straight, so follow it, and do not follow other paths, for they will lead you away from His path.\"] (Surah Al-An'am, 153)"],[3229,"They were created in the loins of men and formed in the wombs of women."],[3230,"Do not curse faces. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[3231,"Allah created four things with His Hand: the Throne, the Gardens of Eden, Adam, and the Pen. And He veiled Himself from creation with four things: fire, darkness, light, and darkness."],[3232,"The garment of Adam and Eve was like a fingernail. When they tasted the tree, they began to fasten over themselves from the leaves of Paradise. He said: 'That is the leaves of the fig tree.'"],[3233,"In the pre-Islamic era, a woman would circumambulate the House naked, with a piece of cloth over her private part, saying: 'Today part of it appears, or all of it; but whatever appears of it, I do not make lawful.' Then this verse was revealed: {Say, 'Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah?'}"],[3234,"The companions of the A'raf are people whose good deeds carried them past the Fire, but their evil deeds fell short of Paradise. When their eyes are turned toward the companions of the Fire, they say: 'Our Lord, do not place us with the wrongdoing people.' While they are in that state, your Lord looks upon them and says: 'Arise, enter Paradise, for I have forgiven you.'"],[3235,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed by al-Hijr, he said: 'Do not ask for signs. The people of Salih asked for them, and she—meaning the she-camel—used to come to drink from this mountain pass and leave from this mountain pass. But they defied the command of their Lord and hamstrung her. So the shout seized them, and Allah destroyed all of them under the sky except one man who was in the sanctuary of Allah.' It was said: 'Who was he?' He said: 'Abu Righal. When he left the sanctuary, what befell his people befell him.'"],[3236,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning the saying of Him, Exalted is He: {When his Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, He made it crumble to dust} [Al-A'raf 143]. Hammad said: Like this—and he placed his thumb on the joint of his right little finger. He said: Humayd b. Thabit said, \"Do you narrate something like this?\" He said: Thabit struck Humayd's chest with his hand and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated it, and I should not narrate it?\""],[3237,"\"Information is not like direct observation. Allah informed Musa of what his people had done with the calf, but he did not throw down the tablets; when he directly saw what they had done, he threw down the tablets.\""],[3238,"Harun came upon al-Samiri while he was making the calf and said to him, \"What are you making?\" He said, \"Something that neither benefits nor harms.\" Harun said, \"O Allah, give him what he asked for in his heart.\" When he left, he said, \"O Allah, I ask You to make it low.\" So it lowed. Whenever it prostrated, it lowed, and whenever it raised its head, it lowed. That was due to Harun's supplication."],[3239,"He said: The companions of the calf said, 'Hitta samqatha azabba mazabba,' which in Arabic means 'red, strong wheat containing a black hair.' That is the saying of Him, Exalted is He: {Then those who did wrong changed the word to something other than what was said to them} [Al-Baqarah 59]. When they refused to prostrate, Allah commanded the mountain to fall upon them. They looked at it and saw it covering them, so they fell down prostrating on one side and looked with the other side. Then Allah had mercy on them and lifted it from them. They said, 'No prostration is more beloved to Allah, Exalted is He, than the prostration by which He averted punishment from you.' So they prostrate on one side for that reason. That is the saying of Him, Exalted is He: {And when We raised the mountain above them as if it were a canopy} [Al-A'raf 171]."],[3240,"Moses called upon Allah, so Allah sent seventy and made his supplication when he called upon for those who believe in Muhammad and follow his words, \"So forgive us, have mercy upon us, and You are the best of forgivers\" [Al-A'raf: 155], \"So I will record it for those who fear Me and give zakah\" [Al-A'raf: 156], and those who follow Muhammad and his family and send blessings upon him."],[3241,"\"Do you know Aylah?\" I said, \"What is Aylah?\" He said, \"A village where some Jews lived. Allah forbade them fish on the Sabbath. Their fish used to come to them on their Sabbath, appearing at the surface—white, fat, like pregnant camels—near their courtyards and buildings. On other than the Sabbath, they could not find them or catch them except with hardship and great effort. Some of them said to others, or whoever among them said it: 'Perhaps if we caught them on the Sabbath and ate them on another day...' A household among them did that. They caught fish and grilled them. Their neighbors smelled the aroma of grilling and said, 'By Allah, we do not think the people of Banu So-and-so are doing anything.' Then others caught them, until the practice spread among them and became widespread. They split into three groups: a group that ate, a group that forbade, and a group that said: {Why do you admonish a people whom Allah will destroy or punish with a severe punishment?} [Al-A'raf 164]. The group that forbade said: 'We warn you of Allah's anger and His punishment—that He may strike you with a sinking of the earth, a pelting from the sky, or some of the punishment He has. By Allah, we will not stay overnight in a place where you are.' They left the walled town. The next morning, they went to the gate of the town and knocked, but no one answered. They brought a ladder, leaned it against the wall, and one of them climbed up. He said, 'O servants of Allah! Monkeys, by Allah, with tails, howling!' He said it three times, then descended from the wall and opened the gate. The people entered upon them. The monkeys recognized their human relatives, but the humans did not recognize their monkey relatives. A monkey would come to its human relative or kinsman, rub against him, and cling to him. The human would say, 'Are you So-and-so?' The monkey would nod its head, meaning yes, and weep. A female monkey would come to her human relative or kinswoman, and the human would say, 'Are you So-and-so?' She would nod her head, meaning yes, and weep. Then the humans said to them, 'We warned you of Allah's anger and His punishment—that He may strike you with a sinking of the earth, a metamorphosis, or some of the punishment He has.'\" Ibn Abbas said: \"Listen to what Allah says: 'We saved those who forbade evil and seized those who did wrong with a dreadful punishment because they were defiantly disobeying.' I do not know what happened to the third group.\" Ibn Abbas said: \"How many evil deeds have we seen and not forbidden?\" Ikrimah said: I said, \"What do you think, may Allah make me your ransom? They did disapprove and dislike it when they said: 'Why do you admonish a people whom Allah will destroy or punish with a severe punishment?'\" My words pleased him, and he ordered two thick cloaks for me and clothed me with them."],[3242,"He gathered them all that day, and it was nothing but existence until the Day of Resurrection. Then He made them souls, then formed them and gave them the power of speech. And He took from them the covenant and the pledge, and He made them testify upon themselves, \"Am I not your Lord?\" They said, \"Yes, we testify.\" [This] lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection, \"Indeed, we were unaware of this.\" Or [lest] you say, \"It was only that our fathers associated [others in worship] before, and we were but descendants after them. Then would You destroy us for what the falsifiers have done?\" [Allah] said, \"I swear by Myself, and I bear witness on you all the heavens and the earths, and I bear witness upon your father Adam, 'Am I not your Lord?' They said, 'Yes, we testify.' [This] lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection, 'Indeed, we were unaware of this.' Or lest you should say, 'It was only that our fathers associated [others in worship] before, and we were but descendants after them. Then would You destroy us for what the falsifiers have done?' He said, \"Indeed, I bear witness over all of you that I am free from whatever you associate with Me. Indeed, the Messengers will come to you with My reminders and My covenant, and they will present My Books to you.\" They said, \"We bear witness that You are our Lord and our God. You have no Lord besides You, and we have no god besides You.\" And their father Adam raised them, so He looked at them, and He saw richness and poverty, beauty and otherwise. He said, \"My Lord, if You had balanced Your servants.\" He said, \"I love to return the gratitude.\" And among them were seen prophets like bright lamps. They were given a separate covenant in regards to Prophet-hood and Messengership. This is the saying of Allah, the Exalted, \"[And mention] when We took from the prophets their covenant and from you and from Noah.\" (33:7) And His saying, \"So direct your face toward the religion, inclining to truth. [Adhere to] the fitrah of Allah upon which He has created [all] people. No change should there be in the creation of Allah.\" (30:30) And His saying, \"This is a warner of the warners of old.\" (53:56) And His saying, \"And We had not found for most of them any covenant, but indeed, We found most of them defiantly disobedient.\" (7:102) And His saying, \"Then We sent following their footsteps Our messengers and followed [them] with Jesus, the son of Mary, and gave him the Gospel. And We placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy and monasticism, which they innovated; We did not prescribe it for them except that they did so seeking the approval of Allah.\" So they did not observe it with due observance. (57:27) He knew in His knowledge those who would deny what He would affirm and those who would affirm what He would deny. So the soul of 'Isa was among those souls to which the covenant was taken in the time of Adam. And that soul was then sent to Maryam when He said, \"Settle in a place of worship wherein the sun does not rise, and you take a veil from them.\" So We sent to her Our soul, and it manifested to her in the form of a well-built man. (19:17) Until His saying, \"A determined appointment.\" (19:21) She conceived. He, who spoke to her, was the soul of 'Isa, peace be upon him. Abu Ja'far narrated to me that Ar-Rabi' bin Anas narrated to him from Abu Al-'Aliyah from Ubayy bin Ka'b who said, \"He entered it.\""],[3243,"Umar b. al-Khattab was asked about this verse: {And when your Lord took from the Children of Adam, from their loins, their descendants, and made them testify against themselves: \"Am I not your Lord?\" They said, \"Yes, we testify.\" Lest you should say on the Day of Resurrection, \"Indeed, we were unaware of this.\"} [Al-A'raf 172]. Umar b. al-Khattab said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was asked about it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah created Adam, then wiped his back with His right hand and extracted from it his descendants. He said, \"I created these for Paradise, and they will act with the deeds of the people of Paradise.\" Then He wiped his back again and extracted from it descendants. He said, \"I created these for the Fire, and they will act with the deeds of the people of the Fire.\"' A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then what is the point of action?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When Allah creates a man for Paradise, He makes him act with the deeds of the people of Paradise.'\""],[3244,"When Allah created Adam, He wiped his back, and every soul He would create until the Day of Resurrection fell from his back like tiny ants. Then He placed between the eyes of each human among them a glint of light. Then He presented them to Adam. Adam said, 'Who are these, O Lord?' He said, 'These are your descendants.' Adam saw a man among them whose glint between his eyes pleased him and said, 'O Lord, who is this?' He said, 'This is your son Dawud, who will be in the last of the nations.' Adam said, 'How much lifespan have You assigned to him?' He said, 'Sixty years.' Adam said, 'O Lord, add to him forty years from my lifespan, so that his lifespan will be one hundred years.' Allah, Exalted is He, said, 'Then it will be written and sealed, and it will not be changed.' When Adam's lifespan came to an end, the Angel of Death came to take his soul. Adam said, 'Do I not have forty years remaining of my lifespan?' The Angel of Death said, 'Did you not give them to your son Dawud?' He said: So he denied, and his descendants denied; he forgot, and his descendants forgot; he erred, and his descendants erred."],[3245,"He is Bal'am ibn Ba'ura'a according to the conditions of Bukhari and Muslim."],[3246,"I asked him about the spoils (al-anfal). He said: \"It was revealed concerning us on the day of Badr. The people were in three positions: one third fighting the enemy, one third gathering the goods and taking captives, and one third by the tent guarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When they gathered the goods, they disputed about them. Those who gathered and took them said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted each of us what he acquired; it is ours, not yours.' Those fighting the enemy and pursuing them said, 'By Allah, had it not been for us, you would not have obtained it. We occupied the enemy.' The guards said, 'By Allah, you are not more entitled to it than we are. We saw the chance to fight the enemy when Allah delivered their backs to us—to take the goods when no one could prevent it—but we feared the enemy's raid on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so we stood in front of him.'\" He said: \"So Allah took it out of our hands and gave it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who divided it equally. There was no one-fifth (khums) on that day. In it was fear of Allah, obedience to Him, obedience to His Messenger ﷺ, and reconciliation of hearts.\""],[3247,"\"Whoever does such and such, or comes to such and such a place, will have such and such.\" The young men rushed to that, while the elders remained steadfast under the banners. When Allah granted them victory, the young men came seeking what was assigned to them. The elders said, \"We were your support and we stayed under the banners.\" Then Allah, Exalted is He, revealed: {They ask you about the spoils of war. Say, \"The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger.\"} So fear Allah and amend what is between you."],[3248,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished with the slain, it was said to him, \"You should go after the caravan; there is nothing to stop you from it.\" Al-Abbas called out to him while he was in his bonds: \"It is not right for you.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"Because Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has fulfilled what He promised you.\""],[3249,"From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri regarding this verse: {And whoever turns his back to them on that day} [Al-Anfal 16]. He said: \"It was revealed concerning us on the day of Badr.\""],[3250,"Ubayy b. Khalaf came on the day of Uhud toward the Prophet ﷺ, intending to attack him. Men among the believers intercepted him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered them to clear his way. Then Mus'ab b. Umayr, the brother of Banu Abd al-Dar, confronted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Ubayy's collarbone through a gap between the long coat of mail and the helmet, so he thrust him with his spear. Ubayy fell from his horse, and no blood came from his wound; it broke one of his ribs. His companions came to him while he was bellowing like a bull. They said to him, \"What ails you? It is only a scratch.\" He mentioned to them the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Rather, I will kill Ubayy.\" Then he said, \"By Him in whose hand is my soul, if what I have were inflicted on the people of Dhu al-Majaz, they would all die.\" Ubayy died, heading to the Fire—so away with the companions of the Blaze—before reaching Makkah. Then Allah revealed: {You did not throw when you threw, but Allah threw} [Al-Anfal 17], the verse."],[3251,"Abu Jahl was the one who sought judgment. For when the two parties met, he said: 'O Allah, whichever of us was more severing of kinship and brought us what we do not know, then destroy him this morning.' That was his seeking of judgment. Then Allah revealed: {If you seek judgment, then judgment has come to you} [Al-Anfal 19] up to His saying {and that Allah is with the believers} [Al-Anfal 19]."],[3252,"Regarding His saying, may He be glorified: {He comes between a man and his heart} [Al-Anfal 24], he said: 'He comes between the disbeliever and faith, and He comes between the believer and disobedience.'"],[3253,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered Quraysh and said: 'Is there anyone among you other than yourselves?' They said: 'Among us is our sister's son, among us is our ally, and among us is our freed slave.' He said: 'Our ally is from us, our sister's son is from us, and our freed slave is from us. Indeed, my guardians among you are the pious.'"],[3254,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: {And prepare against them whatever you are able of power} [Al-Anfal 60]. 'Indeed, power is archery.'"],[3255,"Indeed, kinship ties are severed, blessings are denied, and when Allah brings hearts together, nothing can separate them. Then he recited: {Even if you spent all that is on earth, you could not have brought their hearts together}."],[3256,"I met Abu Ishaq after he had lost his sight and asked him: 'Do you recognize me?' He said: 'Indeed I recognize you and love you.' Then he said:"],[3257,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consulted Abu Bakr concerning the captives. He said: 'They are your people and your kin, so release them.' Then he consulted Umar, who said: 'Kill them.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ransomed them. Then Allah, may He be glorified, revealed: {It is not for a prophet to have captives until he has made a great slaughter in the land} [Al-Anfal 67] up to His saying {so eat of what you have taken as spoil, lawful and good} [Al-Anfal 69]. He said: The Prophet ﷺ then met Umar and said: 'A calamity almost befell us because of your opposition.'"],[3258,"From the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'We acquired worldly gains with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Allah, may He be glorified, revealed: {Had it not been for a prior decree from Allah, a tremendous punishment would have touched you for what you took} [Al-Anfal 68]. I hope that it was a mercy from Allah that preceded for us.' Then some of them said: 'By Allah, he used to hate you and call you Al-Akhnas.' Sa'd laughed until he was overcome by laughter, then said: 'Does not a man find fault with his brother in a matter between them, yet that does not reach his trustworthiness?' And he mentioned another word."],[3259,"I said to Uthman b. Affan: 'What prompted you to take Al-Anfal, which is among the Mathani, and Bara'ah, which is among the Mi'in, and join them together without writing Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim, and place them among the seven long surahs? What prompted you to do that?' Uthman said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to have periods when surahs of multiple verses were revealed to him. When something was revealed, he would call one of his scribes and say: \"Place these in the surah that contains such and such.\" Al-Anfal was among the first to be revealed in Madinah, and Bara'ah was among the last of the Quran, and its story was similar to its story, so I thought it was part of it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away without clarifying to us that it was part of it, so I did not write Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim between them.'"],[3260,"I asked Ali b. Abi Talib: 'Why was Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim not written in Bara'ah?' He said: 'Because Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim is a safeguard, while Bara'ah was revealed with the sword, and there is no safeguard in it.'"],[3261,"\"You do not recite even a quarter of it, meaning Bara'ah, yet you call it Surah al-Tawbah, while it is the Surah of Punishment.\""],[3262,"I was in the expedition that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent with Ali with Bara'ah to Makkah. His son or another man asked him: 'What did you announce?' He said: 'We declared: \"None shall enter Paradise except a believer, and no polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year, and no one shall circumambulate the House naked, and whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, its term is four months.\" I announced until my voice became hoarse.'"],[3263,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood on the Day of Sacrifice between the Jamarat during the Hajj that he performed, and said to the people, “Which day is this?” They said, “This is the Day of Sacrifice.” He said, “Which land is this?” They said, “This is the Sacred Land.” He said, “Which month is this?” They said, “The Sacred Month.” He said, “This is the day of the Greater Hajj. Your blood, your wealth, and your honor are sacred to you like the sanctity of this land on this day.” Then he said, “Have I conveyed?” They said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then began to say, “O Allah, bear witness.” Then he bade farewell to the people, and they said, “This is the Farewell Hajj.”"],[3264,"Whoever departs this world upon sincerity to Allah alone, with no partner, and upon establishing prayer and giving zakat, departs it while Allah is pleased with him. That is the religion of Allah with which the messengers came and which they conveyed from their Lord before the confusion of reports and the divergence of desires. Its confirmation is in the Book of Allah: “If they repent, establish prayer, and give zakat, then let them go their way” [At-Tawbah: 5]. And His ﷻ saying “If they repent” means they cast off idols and their worship, “and establish prayer and give zakat, then they are your brothers in religion.”"],[3265,"From Hudhayfah regarding His ﷻ saying: “Then fight the leaders of disbelief—indeed, they have no oaths” [At-Tawbah: 12]. He said: “They have no covenant.” Hudhayfah said: “They have not been fought yet.”"],[3266,"Regarding His saying: “Then fight the leaders of disbelief” [At-Tawbah: 12]. He said: “Abu Jahl b. Hisham, Umayyah b. Khalaf, Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Abu Sufyan b. Harb, and Suhayl b. 'Amr. They are the ones who broke the covenant of Allah and plotted to expel the Messenger from Makkah.”"],[3267,"When you see a man keeping to the mosque, do not hesitate to testify that he is a believer, for Allah says: “Only those who believe in Allah maintain the mosques of Allah.”"],[3268,"When the verse “Those who hoard gold and silver and do not spend them in the way of Allah” [At-Tawbah: 34] was revealed, it weighed heavily on the Muslims. They said, “None of us can leave wealth for his child to remain after him.” Umar said, “I will relieve you.” So they went, and Umar went, and Thawban followed him. They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Umar said, “O Prophet of Allah, this verse has weighed heavily on your companions.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, “Allah did not make zakat obligatory except to purify what remains of your wealth through it, and He made inheritance obligatory only in wealth that remains after you.” Umar then said takbir, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Shall I not tell you of the best thing a man hoards? It is a righteous woman: when he looks at her she pleases him, when he commands her she obeys him, and when he is absent she protects [his honor].”"],[3269,"We sat with Miqdad b. al-Aswad in Damascus while he was on a chest, with no extra space on it. A man said to him, “If only you would stay away from military campaigns this year.” He replied, “The call to arms came to us—meaning Surah At-Tawbah. Allah ﷻ said: ‘March forth, light and heavy’ [At-Tawbah: 41], and I find myself nothing but light.”"],[3270,"From Abu Hurayrah with wording other than this."],[3271,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the mosque founded on piety. He said, “It is this mosque of mine.”"],[3272,"He said: “The mosque founded on piety is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Sahih."],[3273,"Two men argued about the mosque founded on piety. One said, “It is the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,” and the other said, “It is the mosque of Quba.” They hastened to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The mosque founded on piety is this mosque of mine.” Its chain is good."],[3274,"When this verse was revealed: “In it are men who love to purify themselves” [At-Tawbah: 108], the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O assembly of the Ansar, Allah has praised you for purification with good. So what is this purification of yours?” They said, “We perform ablution for prayer, wash from janabah, and cleanse ourselves with water.” He said, “That is it, so adhere to it.”"],[3275,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the sa’ihin (those who journey), and he said, “They are the ones who fast.”"],[3276,"I heard a man asking forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists, and I said to him, ‘Do not ask forgiveness for your parents while they are polytheists.’ He said, ‘Did not Ibrahim ask forgiveness for his father while he was a polytheist?’ So I mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ, and there was revealed: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they were near relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are companions of the Blaze. And Ibrahim’s asking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him; but when it became clear to him that he was an enemy of Allah, he disowned him. Indeed, Ibrahim was compassionate and forbearing.} [At-Tawbah: 114]"],[3277,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May Allah have mercy on you and forgive you, O uncle. I will not cease asking forgiveness for you until Allah ﷻ forbids me.” Then the Muslims began asking forgiveness for their deceased who had died as polytheists, and Allah the Exalted revealed: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists, even if they were near relatives, after it has become clear to them that they are companions of the Blaze.} [At-Tawbah: 113]"],[3278,"When Abu Talib was near death, the Prophet ﷺ came to him while ‘Abd Allah b. Abi Umayyah and Abu Jahl b. Hisham were with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O uncle, you have the greatest right upon me and the best hand with me; indeed your right is greater upon me than that of my father. So say a word by which intercession will become binding for me for you on the Day of Resurrection: say, ‘There is no god but Allah.’” The two of them said to him, “Will you turn away from the religion of ‘Abd al-Muttalib?” He fell silent, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated it to him. He said, “I follow the religion of ‘Abd al-Muttalib,” and died. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, “I will surely seek forgiveness for you as long as I am not forbidden from it.” Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists} [At-Tawbah: 113] and the verse {And Ibrahim’s asking forgiveness for his father} [At-Tawbah: 114] to the end of the verse."],[3279,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to look at the graves, and we went out with him. He ordered us, so we sat down. Then he stepped over the graves until he reached one of them, and he confided with it for a long time. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ’s sobbing rose as he wept, and we wept because of his weeping. Then he came to us, and ‘Umar b. al-Khattab met him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, what made you weep? You have made us weep and alarmed us.” He came and sat with us and said, “Did my weeping alarm you?” We said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “The grave at which you saw me confiding is the grave of my mother Aminah bt. Wahb. I asked my Lord for permission to visit her, and He permitted me, then I asked Him for permission to seek forgiveness for her, but He did not permit me, and there came down to me: {It is not for the Prophet and those who believe to ask forgiveness for the polytheists} [At-Tawbah: 113] until the end of the verse, and {And Ibrahim’s asking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him} [At-Tawbah: 114]. There seized me what seizes a child for his parent of tenderness, and that is what made me weep.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it in this wording. Muslim only included the hadith of Yazid b. Kaysan from Abu Hazim from Abu Hurayrah in an abridged form. Ayyub b. Hani’ was deemed weak by Ibn Ma‘in."],[3280,"About His ﷻ saying {And His Throne was upon the water} [Hud: 7]: On what was the water? He said, “On the back of the wind.”"],[3281,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to go on a raid of his. He called Ja‘far and ordered him to stay behind in Madinah. He said, “I will never stay behind after you, O Messenger of Allah.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called me and adjured me to stay behind before I could speak. I wept, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “What makes you weep, O ‘Ali?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, more than one thing makes me weep: Tomorrow Quraysh will say, ‘How quickly he stayed behind from his cousin and abandoned him.’ And another thing that makes me weep is that I wanted to expose myself to jihad in the path of Allah, for Allah says {Nor do they tread any ground that enrages the disbelievers, nor do they inflict upon an enemy any infliction} to the end of the verse; I wanted to expose myself to Allah’s bounty.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “As for your saying that Quraysh will say, ‘How quickly he stayed behind from his cousin and abandoned him,’ you have in me a model: they have said ‘sorcerer, soothsayer, liar.’ Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? As for your saying that you wanted to expose yourself to Allah’s bounty, here are measures of pepper that came to us from Yemen; sell it and enjoy it, you and Fatimah, until Allah brings you from His bounty, for Madinah is only set right by me or by you.”"],[3282,"O Abu al-‘Aliyah, do not say, “You have departed from the prayer,” but say {You have completed the prayer} [An-Nisa’: 103], for Allah the Exalted says {They turned away—may Allah turn their hearts away} [At-Tawbah: 127]."],[3283,"The last of the Qur’an to be revealed is {There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves; what distresses you is grievous to him, he is eager for you, kind and merciful to the believers}."],[3284,"\"They have a foot of truth with their Lord\" [Yunus 2]. The predecessors have said so about their truth with their Lord."],[3285,"Do not transgress, and do not be a transgressor, for Allah says {Your transgression is only against yourselves}."],[3286,"I heard Abu Ja‘far Muhammad b. ‘Ali b. al-Husayn recite this verse {And Allah invites to the Home of Peace and guides whom He wills to a straight path} [Yunus: 25], then he said: Jabir b. ‘Abd Allah narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day and said, “I saw in a dream as if Jibril was at my head and Mika’il at my feet, one of them saying to his companion, ‘Strike a parable for him.’ He said to him, ‘Listen with your ear and understand with your heart: your likeness and the likeness of your ummah is that of a king who took a house, then built a home in it, then set a feast in it, then sent a messenger inviting the people to their food. Some of them responded to the messenger and some of them refused. Allah is the King, the house is Islam, the home is Paradise, and you, O Muhammad, are the messenger. Whoever responds to you enters Islam, and whoever enters Islam enters Paradise, and whoever enters Paradise eats from it.’”"],[3287,"‘Uthman b. ‘Affan heard that the delegation of the people of Egypt had set out, so he went out to meet them. When they heard of him they came toward him, and he disliked that they should enter Madinah upon him. They came to him and said to him, “Call for the mushaf and open the seventh,” for they used to call Surah Yunus the seventh. He recited it until he came to this verse: {Say, “Have you considered what Allah has sent down for you of provision, of which you have made some unlawful and some lawful?” Say, “Has Allah permitted you, or do you fabricate against Allah?”} [Yunus: 59]. They said to him, “Stop. Have you considered the protected pasture you have reserved? Has Allah permitted you, or do you fabricate against Allah?” He said, “Continue. It was revealed regarding such-and-such. As for the protected pasture, ‘Umar reserved it before me for the camels of zakah. When I was appointed and the zakah camels increased, I increased the protected pasture in proportion to the increase in zakah.”"],[3288,"Al-Hajjaj prolonged the sermon, so Ibn Umar placed his head in my lap. Al-Hajjaj said, \"Indeed Ibn al-Zubayr has altered the Book of Allah.\" Ibn Umar sat up and said, \"Neither you nor Ibn al-Zubayr can do that. There is no change in the words of Allah\" [Yunus 64]. Al-Hajjaj said, \"You have certainly been given knowledge, if it benefits you.\""],[3289,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the saying of Allah ﷻ: \"For them are good tidings in the worldly life and in the Hereafter\" [Yunus 64]. He said, \"It is the righteous dream which a man sees or is seen for him.\""],[3290,"Jibril kept stuffing mud into the mouth of Pharaoh for fear that he would say, 'There is no god but Allah.'"],[3291,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted at al-Hijr during the expedition of Tabuk, he stood and addressed the people, saying: \"O people, do not ask your Prophet about signs. These are the people of Salih; they asked their Prophet to bring them a sign, so Allah sent them the she-camel. It used to come from this mountain pass and drink their water on its day of drinking, and they would drink its milk just as they used to drink from their water. But they rebelled against the command of their Lord and hamstrung it. So Allah promised them three days—a promise from Allah that was not to be belied. Then the cry came upon them, and Allah destroyed all those among them who were under the eastern and western parts of the heavens, except a man who was in the sanctuary of Allah. The sanctuary of Allah protected him from the punishment of Allah.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who is he?\" He said, \"Abu Righal.\""],[3292,"From Abdullah, regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ: \"He knows its resting place and its depository\" [Hud 6]. He said, \"Its resting place is in the wombs, and its depository is where it dies.\""],[3293,"About His saying ﷻ: \"And His Throne was upon the water\" [Hud 7]. On what was the water? He said, \"On the back of the wind.\""],[3294,"A group of people entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and began asking him, saying, 'Give us,' until that distressed him. Then others entered and said, 'We have come to greet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to gain understanding in the religion, and to ask him about the beginning of this matter.' He said, \"Allah existed and nothing else besides Him. The Throne was upon the water, and He wrote in the Remembrance everything. Then He created seven heavens.\" He said, \"Then someone came to him and said, 'Your she-camel has gone.'\" He said, \"I wish I had left it.\""],[3295,"Until an appointed term."],[3296,"There is no one from this nation who hears of me, nor a Jew nor a Christian, and does not believe in me, except that he will enter the Fire. I began saying, 'Where is its confirmation in the Book of Allah?' until I found this verse: \"And whoever disbelieves in it from the parties, the Fire is his promised destination\" [Hud 17]. He said, \"The parties are all the religions.\""],[3297,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If Allah had shown mercy to anyone from the people of Nuh, He would have shown mercy to the mother of the child.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Nuh remained among his people for a thousand years less fifty, calling them, until at the end of his time he planted a tree. It grew large and spread in every direction. Then he cut it down and began making it into a ship. They would pass by and ask him, and he would say, 'I am making it into a ship.' They would mock him and say, 'You are making a ship on land? How will it sail?' He said, 'You will soon know.' When he finished it, the oven gushed forth and water increased in the streets. The mother of the child feared for him, and she loved him intensely. She went out to the mountain until she reached a cleft. When the water reached her, she carried him out until she stood on the mountain. When the water reached her neck, she raised him with her hand until the water took him away. If Allah had shown mercy to any of them, He would have shown mercy to the mother of the child.\"[1]"],[3298,"There were three hundred years between Noah and the destruction of his people. The furnace had already spread in India and Noah's ark circled around the Kaaba for a week."],[3299,"I heard Abu Dharr saying while holding the door of the Kaaba: \"O people, whoever knows me, I am the one you know; and whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The example of my household is like the ark of Nuh: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever lags behind it drowns.'\""],[3300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Wadi al-Azraq and said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"Wadi al-Azraq.\" He said, \"It is as if I can see Musa b. Imran descending, with a lowing sound, raising his voice to Allah with takbir.\" Then he came to a mountain pass and said, \"What is this pass?\" They said, \"Such-and-such pass.\" He said, \"It is as if I can see Yunus b. Matta on a red, curly-haired she-camel, its reins of palm fiber, and he is reciting the talbiyah, wearing a woolen jubbah.\""],[3301,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"I see that you have aged.\" He said, \"Sura Hud, al-Waqi'ah, 'Amma Yatasa'alun, and Idha al-Shamsu Kuwwirat have caused my hair to turn grey.\""],[3302,"\"Ibrahim al-Khalil ﷺ was inspired with this Arabic tongue by inspiration.\""],[3303,"From 'Ata' regarding the words of Allah ﷻ {The mercy of Allah and His blessings be upon you, O people of the house}: \"I was with 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas when a man came and greeted him, so I said, 'And upon you be peace, and the mercy of Allah, and His blessings, and His forgiveness.' Ibn 'Abbas said, 'Stop at what the angels stopped at.'\""],[3304,"When the messengers of Allah came to Lut, he thought they were guests who had come to him, so he brought them close and seated them nearby. He brought his daughters, who were three, and seated them between his guests and his people. Then his people came rushing to him. When he saw them, he said, {These are my daughters; they are purer for you, so fear Allah and do not disgrace me concerning my guests} [Hud 78]. They said, {We have no right to your daughters, and indeed you know what we want} [Hud 79]. {He said, If only I had strength against you or could take refuge in a strong support} [Hud 80]. Jibril ﷺ turned to him and said, {Indeed we are messengers of your Lord; they will never reach you} [Hud 81]. He said, \"So he blinded their eyes, and they retreated, climbing over one another, until they reached those at the door. They said, 'We have come to you from the most magical of people; he has blinded our sight.' So they went off, climbing over one another, until they entered the town. It was raised during part of the night until it was between the sky and the earth, so that they could hear the voices of birds in the air. Then it was turned upside down, and the baked clay stones came out upon them. Whoever the baked clay stone caught, it killed him, and whoever escaped, a stone followed him wherever he was and killed him.\" He said, \"Then he departed with his daughters, who were three. When he reached such-and-such a place in Syria, his eldest daughter died, and a spring called al-Wariyyah gushed forth at her grave. Then he went on as far as Allah willed him to go, and the youngest died, and a spring called al-Ru'unah gushed forth at her grave. None of them remained except the middle one.\""],[3305,"Some people saw a fire in the graveyard, so they went to it and found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the grave, saying, \"Hand me your companion,\" and he was the man al-Awwah who raised his voice in remembrance."],[3306,"The Quran was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he recited it to them for a time. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would tell us stories.\" So Allah ﷻ sent down {Alif Lam Ra. These are the verses of the clear Book} [Yusuf 1]. He recited until His saying {We relate to you the best of stories} [Yusuf 3], the verse. He recited to them for a time, and they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, if only you would speak to us.\" So Allah ﷻ sent down {Allah has sent down the best of speech, a book consistent within itself} [al-Zumar 23], the verse. All of that is commanded with the Quran."],[3307,"{O my father, hire him, for the best you can hire is the strong and trustworthy} [al-Qasas 26], and Abu Bakr when he discerned in 'Umar."],[3308,"{And she said, 'Come you'} [Yusuf 23]. It was said to him, so he said, \"Thus we were taught.\""],[3309,"Jacob was portrayed to him, so he hit his chest and his desire flowed from his fingers."],[3310,"Yusuf stumbled three stumbles: when he desired her and was imprisoned; his saying to the man, {Mention me to your lord} [Yusuf 42], so he remained in prison for several years because Satan made him forget the remembrance of his Lord; and his saying to them, {Indeed you are thieves} [Yusuf 70]."],[3311,"\"The matter about which you both inquire has been decided.\""],[3312,"The noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one: Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim, the friend of the Most Merciful. If I were to remain as long as Yusuf remained, then the caller came to me, I would have answered. When the messenger came to him and said, 'Return to your lord and ask him what was the matter with the women who cut their hands. Indeed my Lord is knowing of their scheme.'"],[3313,"A man asked permission to enter upon 'Umar, and he said, \"Ask permission for the son of the good ones.\" 'Umar said, \"Give him permission.\" When he entered, 'Umar said to him, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am so-and-so, son of so-and-so, son of so-and-so,\" and he began counting men from the nobles of the Jahiliyyah. 'Umar said to him, \"Are you Yusuf b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"That is the son of the good ones, and you are the son of the evil ones. You are only counting for me men of the people of the Fire.\""],[3314,"Umar said to me, “O enemy of God and enemy of Islam, you have betrayed God’s wealth.” He said: I said, “I am not an enemy of God nor an enemy of Islam; rather, I am an enemy of whoever is their enemy. I have not betrayed God’s wealth; rather, these are the prices of my camels and shares that have accumulated.” He said: So he repeated it to me, and I repeated these words to him. He said: So he fined me twelve thousand. He said: Then I stood in the dawn prayer and said, “O God, forgive the Commander of the Faithful.” Then after that he wanted to appoint me to a post, but I refused him. He said, “And why, when Joseph asked for office and he was better than you?” I said, “Joseph is a prophet, the son of a prophet, the son of a prophet, the son of a prophet; and I am the son of Umaymah, and I fear three and two.” He said, “Will you not say five?” I said, “No.” He said, “Then what are they?” I said, “I fear that I will speak without knowledge, and that I will give legal opinions without knowledge, and that my back will be beaten, and that my honor will be insulted, and that my wealth will be taken by beating.”"],[3315,"Jacob the prophet ﷺ had a brother who was a close friend for the sake of God. One day he said, “O Jacob, what took away your sight, and what bent your back?” He said, “As for what took away my sight, it was weeping over Joseph. As for what bent my back, it was grief over my son Benjamin.” He said: Then Gabriel ﷺ came to him and said, “O Jacob, God sends you greetings and says to you: Are you not ashamed to complain of Me to other than Me?” He said: Jacob said, “I only complain of my anguish and grief to God.” He said: Gabriel said, “I know what you complain of, O Jacob.” He said: Then Jacob said, “My Lord, will You not have mercy on an old man? You have taken away my sight and bent my back. Return to me my fragrant flower so I may smell him once before death, then do with me as You will.” He said: Gabriel came to him and said, “God sends you greetings and says to you: Rejoice, and let your heart be glad. By My might, if they were both dead, I would raise them. Prepare food for the poor, for the most beloved of My servants to Me are the prophets and the poor. Do you know why I took away your sight and bent your back, and what Joseph’s brothers did to him? Because you slaughtered a sheep, and an orphan poor man who was fasting came to you, and you did not feed him anything from it.” He said: After that, whenever Jacob wanted lunch, he would order a caller to announce, “Whoever among the poor wants lunch, let him have lunch with Jacob.” And when he was fasting, he would order a caller to announce, “Whoever among the poor is fasting, let him break his fast with Jacob.”"],[3316,"“Jacob had a brother who was a close friend.”"],[3317,"I said to her about His saying, the Exalted: “Until, when the messengers despaired and thought that they had been denied” [Yusuf 110]. I said, “Did they truly despair that they had been denied?” She said, “God forbid that the messengers would think that of their Lord. Rather, it is the followers of the messengers. When victory was delayed from them and affliction became severe upon them, the messengers thought that their followers had been denied.”"],[3318,"“If My servants obeyed Me, I would give them rain at night and bring the sun out over them by day, and I would not make them hear the sound of thunder.”"],[3319,"From one of the two books: they are two books. God erases what He wills from one of them, “and He confirms, and with Him is the Mother of the Book” [Ar-Ra'd 39], meaning the totality of the Book. “Muslim has used Hammad as evidence, and al-Bukhari has used Ikrimah as evidence.” And it is strange but sound from the hadith of Sulayman al-Taymi, but they did not include it. Sound, strange."],[3320,"“Caution does not avail against destiny, but God erases through supplication whatever He wills of destiny.”"],[3321,"Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Talha, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas regarding His saying, Exalted is He: “Have they not seen that We come to the land, reducing it from its borders?” [Ar-Ra'd 41]. He said: The death of its scholars and jurists."],[3322,"\"Allah the Almighty says: 'And whoever among them says, 'Indeed, I am a god besides Him,' then that person We will recompense with Hell. Thus do We recompense the wrongdoers.' [Surah Al-Anbiya 29] *And He said to Muhammad, peace be upon him: 'Indeed, We have granted you a clear conquest, that Allah may forgive for you what preceded of your sin and what will follow...' [Surah Al-Fath 2] They asked: What is the reason for Allah's preference of Muhammad over the people of the earth? He replied: Indeed, Allah the Almighty says, 'And We have not sent any messenger except in the language of his people.' [Surah Ibrahim 4] And He said to Muhammad, peace be upon him: 'And We have not sent you, [O Muhammad], except as a bringer of good tidings and a warner to all mankind.' [Surah Saba 28] So He sent him to the jinn and mankind.\""],[3323,"He said regarding the saying of God, Exalted is He: “So they thrust their hands into their mouths” [Ibrahim 9]. He said: They bit on them."],[3324,"From Abdullah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: “So they thrust their hands into their mouths” [Ibrahim 9]. Abdullah said: Thus, and he put his hand into his mouth and bit his hand, and said: They bit on their fingers in rage."],[3325,"When God, Exalted is He, sent down upon His Prophet ﷺ: “O you who believe, protect yourselves and your families from a Fire” [At-Tahrim 6], the Messenger of God ﷺ recited it to his companions one night — or he said one day — and a young man fell down unconscious. The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand on his chest, and it was trembling. He said, “O young man, say: There is no god but God.” So he said it, and he gave him glad tidings of Paradise. His companions said, “O Messenger of God, among us?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Have you not heard the saying of God, Exalted is He: ‘That is for whoever feared My station and feared My warning’ [Ibrahim 14]?”"],[3326,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying, Exalted is He: “And he will be given to drink from purulent water, which he will gulp” [Ibrahim 17]. He said: It is brought near to him, and he loathes it. When it is brought close to him, it scorches his face and the skin of his head falls off. When he drinks it, it cuts through his intestines until it comes out of his backside. God says: “And they will be given boiling water to drink, and it will cut their intestines” [Muhammad 15]. And God, Exalted is He, says: “And if they call for relief, they will be relieved with water like molten brass, which scalds the faces. Wretched is the drink” [Al-Kahf 29]."],[3327,"Ibn Hibban said: He cannot be used as evidence."],[3328,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a basket of unripe dates and he recited: \"The example of a good word is like a good tree.\" He said, \"It is the date-palm.\""],[3329,"I heard 'Ali stand up and say, 'Ask me before you lose me, for after me you will never ask the like of me.' Ibn al-Kawwa' stood up and said, 'Who are those who exchanged the favor of Allah for disbelief and led their people to the home of ruin?' He said, 'The hypocrites of Quraysh.' He said, 'Then who are those whose efforts are wasted in the life of this world while they think they are doing good?' He said, 'Among them are the people of Harura'.'"],[3330,"From 'Ali regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And they led their people to the home of ruin} [Ibrahim 28], he said, 'They are the two most wicked of Quraysh: Banu Umayyah and Banu al-Mughirah. As for Banu al-Mughirah, Allah cut off their last remnant on the day of Badr, and as for Banu Umayyah, they were granted enjoyment for a time.'"],[3331,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {On the Day the earth will be replaced by another earth, and the heavens [as well], and they will come forth before Allah, the One, the Prevailing.} I said, 'Where will the people be on that day?' He said, 'Upon the bridge.'"],[3332,"\"Allah continues to intercede, admit into paradise, have mercy, and intercede until He says, 'Whoever among the Muslims, let him enter paradise.' That is when He says, 'Perhaps those who disbelieved wish that they had been Muslims.' (Al-Hijr 2)\""],[3333,"“A woman used to perform prayer behind the Prophet ﷺ, and she was one of the most beautiful of people. Some of the people used to go into the first row so that they would not see her, and some of them used to lag behind so that they would be in the last row, and when they bowed, they would do like this so that they could see her from beneath their armpits. Then Allah revealed: “And indeed, We know the first generations of you who had passed away, and indeed, We know the present generations of you (mankind), and also those who will some afterwards.” [15:24] concerning her matter. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1046)"],[3334,"\"The forward rows are for those who come early and the back rows are for those who come late.\" - Al-Dhahabi did not mention it in the summary."],[3335,"\"Do you welcome me, O Amir al-Mu'minin, even though you have killed my father and taken my wealth?\" He replied, \"As for your wealth, it is in the treasury, so go tomorrow and take it. As for your claim that you have killed my father, I hope that both you and your father are among those whom Allah, the Almighty, has mentioned in the verse: 'And We have removed whatever was in their breasts of resentment, [while] brothers, on thrones facing each other' (Surah Al-Hijr 47).\" A man from Hamdan said, \"Indeed, Allah is more just than that.\" Upon hearing this, Ali let out a cry that could be heard throughout the palace. He said, \"Then who are we if we are not those mentioned in the verse?\" This narration is authentic and has not been narrated by anyone else."],[3336,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said, \"When the believers are saved from the Fire, they will be detained on a bridge between the Fire and Paradise to settle their disputes that existed among them in the world. When they are purified and have their sins expiated, permission will be granted for them to enter Paradise. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, one of them will be more generous in giving a place for his fellow believer in Paradise than what anyone of you gives of his dwelling in the world.\""],[3337,"\"Don't you see the man sending his ring to his family, saying, 'Bring me this and that,' and when they see it, they recognize that it is true.\""],[3338,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"The seven repeatedly-recited verses (Al-Fatiha) are the opening of the Book.\""],[3339,"\"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, was given seven mathānī (oft-repeated āyāt) and the long ones while Moses was given six.\""],[3340,"In His saying, exalted be He, \"And We have certainly given you, [O Muhammad], seven of the often repeated [verses] and the great Qur'an.\" [Al-Hijr: 87] Al-Baqarah, Ali 'Imran, An-Nisa', Al-Ma'idah, Al-An'am, Al-A'raf, and the Surah Al-Kahf."],[3341,"\"The Jews and the Christians are divided, and their saying, 'The Quran is false.' Allah says, 'They believe in some and disbelieve in some.'\""],[3342,"Regarding this verse: {You take from it intoxicant and good provision} [an-Nahl 67], he said, 'Intoxicant is what is forbidden of its fruit, and good provision is what is lawful of its fruit.'"],[3343,"From 'Abdullah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {sons and grandchildren} [an-Nahl 72], he said, 'Grandchildren are sons-in-law.'"],[3344,"'Abdullah regarding the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {We increased them in punishment upon punishment} [an-Nahl 88], he said, 'Scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees.'"],[3345,"I heard from Abdullah and I believe you or I'm telling you the truth. He said, \"I heard Abdullah say that indeed in the Quran there is a verse in Surah An-Nahl that encompasses both good and evil. [It says]: 'Indeed, Allah orders justice and good conduct and giving to relatives and forbids immorality and bad conduct and oppression. He admonishes you that perhaps you will be reminded.'\" He [the narrator] said, \"You spoke the truth.\""],[3346,"There is no sin more deserving of its perpetrator's punishment being hastened in this world, along with what is stored up for him in the Hereafter, than transgression and severing ties of kinship."],[3347,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate and say: 'O Allah, make me content with what You have provided me, bless it for me, and replace every absent thing of mine with something better.'"],[3348,"\"And He said in Surah An-Nahl, 'And when We substitute a verse in place of another verse' (16:101) and He said in His statement, glorified be He, 'Then indeed, your Lord, to those who emigrated after they had been compelled [to renounce their religion] and thereafter fought [for the cause of Allah] and were patient, indeed, your Lord, after that, is forgiving and merciful' (16:110). The verse means that it is Abdullah bin Sa'd or someone else who used to be the governor of Egypt and he used to write on behalf of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, but then he defected and joined the disbelievers. So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, ordered that he be killed on the Day of the Conquest. Uthman bin Affan sought his protection for him from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, granted him protection.\""],[3349,"The polytheists seized Ammar b. Yasir and would not release him until he reviled the Prophet ﷺ and spoke well of their gods. Then they released him. When he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"What happened to you?\" He replied, “Something terrible, O Messenger of Allah. I was not released until I spoke ill of you and spoke well of their gods.” He said, \"How do you find your heart?\" He replied, “At peace with faith.” He said, \"If they do it again, then do the same.\"[1]"],[3350,"\"Allah is the tongue to which the impenetrable speak, while this is a clear Arabic tongue. Indeed, those who do not believe in the signs of Allah fabricate lies.\""],[3351,"We were sitting with Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah in the mosque of al-Khayf in Mina when a man who was a storyteller stood up and said: 'Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah narrated to us from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn 'Abbas,' and then he commenced a long story. Ibn 'Uyaynah stood up, leaned on his stick, and said: {Only those who do not believe in the verses of Allah fabricate falsehood} [an-Nahl 105]. 'I never narrated this, nor do I know it.'"],[3352,"You will surely be presented with the opportunity to revile me, so revile me, but if you are presented with disavowal of me, then do not disavow me, for I am upon Islam. Let one of you stretch out his neck; may his mother be bereft of him, for there is no worldly life for him and no Hereafter after Islam. Then he recited: {except one who is forced while his heart is at rest in faith}."],[3353,"Hujr b. Qays al-Madari was among those specially devoted to the service of the Commander of the Faithful 'Ali b. Abi Talib. One day 'Ali said to him: 'O Hujr, you will be made to stand after me and be ordered to curse me, so curse me but do not disavow me.'"],[3354,"Ishaq narrated to us, 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us, al-Thawri informed us, from Firas, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, who said: I recited in the presence of 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud: {Indeed, Ibrahim was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah} [al-Nahl 120]. He said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Indeed, Mu'adh was a nation, devoutly obedient. He said: They repeated it to him, and he repeated it, then said: Do you know what al-ummah is? The one who teaches people good, and al-qanit is the one who obeys Allah and His Messenger."],[3355,"When the day of Uhud occurred, sixty-four men from the Ansar were struck, and six from the Muhajirun, and they mutilated them, among them Hamzah. The Ansar said: If we ever strike them on a day like this, we will certainly exceed them. When the day of the conquest of Makkah came, Allah ﷻ sent down: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of what you were punished with; but if you are patient, it is surely better for the patient} [al-Nahl 126]. A man said: No Quraysh after today. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Restrain from the people except four.\""],[3356,"I was in a gathering in which Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman was present, and I said: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was taken on the Night Journey, entered al-Masjid al-Aqsa. He said: Hudhayfah said: And how did you know that, O bald one? Indeed, I recognize your face but I do not know your name, so what is your name? I said to him: I am Zirr b. Hubaysh al-Asadi. He said: Then he said: How did you know that he entered the mosque? He said: I said: Through the Qur'an. Hudhayfah said: Whoever takes from the Qur'an has succeeded. He said: I recited: {Glory be to Him who took His servant by night from the Sacred Mosque to the Farthest Mosque, whose surroundings We have blessed} [al-Isra' 1]. Hudhayfah said: Do you see that he entered it? I said: Yes. He said: By Allah, he did not enter it, and had he entered it, prayer in it would have been prescribed upon you. He said: Then he said: He did not leave the back of al-Buraq until he saw Paradise and Hellfire and was promised the entirety of the Hereafter. He said: I said: O Abu 'Abd Allah, what is al-Buraq? He said: A beast above a donkey and below a mule, its stride is as far as its sight."],[3357,"from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: When we reached Bayt al-Maqdis (al-Aqsa), Jibril pointed with his finger causing a crack in the rock, and he tied Buraq to it."],[3358,"\"Nuh, when he ate food or wore a garment, praised Allah, so he was named a grateful servant.\""],[3359,"Is there anyone among the people from them? I said: If there were, what would you do with him? He said: If there were anyone among them from them, I would take him by his head, then recite to him such-and-such a verse: {And We decreed to the Children of Israel in the Book: You will surely cause corruption in the land twice, and you will surely rise to a great height} [al-Isra' 4]. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3360,"'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud often used to recite this verse: {Indeed, this Qur'an guides to that which is most upright and gives good tidings to the believers} [al-Isra' 9], lightly. 'Uthman said: This is the recitation of Hamzah."],[3361,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth and have family and children, so how should I act or spend? He said: \"Pay the obligatory zakah as a purification that purifies you, maintain ties of kinship, and acknowledge the right of the asker, the neighbor, the poor, and the wayfarer.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, reduce it for me. He said: \"Then give the relative his due, the poor, and the wayfarer, and do not squander wastefully.\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, if I pay the zakah to the Messenger of the Messenger of Allah, have I paid it to Allah and His Messenger? He said: \"Yes, if you pay it to His Messenger, you have paid it, and its reward is for you, and upon the one who changes it is its sin.\""],[3362,"Abu al-'Ubaydayn came to 'Abd Allah, and he was a man blind of sight, and 'Abd Allah used to be recognized for him. He said: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, whom do we ask if we do not ask you? He said: \"What is your need?\" He said: What is al-awwah? He said: \"The merciful.\" He said: What is al-ma'un? He said: \"What people help each other with among themselves.\" He said: What is al-tabdhīr? He said: \"Spending wealth in other than its right.\" He said: What is al-ummah? He said: \"The one who teaches people good.\""],[3363,"When {May the hands of Abu Lahab perish} [al-Masad 1] was revealed, al-'Awra' Umm Jamil bt. Harb approached, wailing, with a stone in her hand, and she was saying: Muzammam: we rejected him and his religion, we hated him and his affair, we disobeyed him. The Prophet ﷺ was sitting in the mosque, and with him was Abu Bakr. When Abu Bakr saw her, he said: O Messenger of Allah, she has approached, and I fear that she may see you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She will never see me,\" and he recited Qur'an and sought protection through it, as he said, and he recited: {And when you recite the Qur'an, We placed between you and those who do not believe in the Hereafter a hidden barrier} [al-Isra' 45]. She stood before Abu Bakr and did not see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: O Abu Bakr, I was informed that your companion has satirized me. He said: No, by the Lord of this House, he has not satirized you. She turned away, saying: Quraysh has known that I am the daughter of their chief."],[3364,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ: {Or a creation of what is great within your breasts} [al-Isra' 51], what does He mean by it? He said: \"Death.\""],[3365,"A group of humans used to worship a group of jinn. The group of jinn embraced Islam, but the humans clung to their worship of them. Allah ﷻ sent down: {Say: Call upon those you claim besides Him, for they do not possess the removal of harm from you, nor a change. Those whom they call upon seek the means to their Lord} [al-Isra' 57], \"both with ya'.\""],[3366,"The people of Makkah asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to make al-Safa into gold for them, and to move the mountains away from them so that they could cultivate them. Allah ﷻ said: If you wish, We will give them what they asked, but if they disbelieve, they will be destroyed as I destroyed those before them; and if you wish, I will grant them respite, perhaps We may spare them. Allah sent down this: {And nothing prevented Us from sending signs except that the former peoples denied them, and We gave Thamud the she-camel as a clear sign} [al-Isra' 59]."],[3367,"\"It is the vision of an eye that I saw on the night of my ascension.\""],[3368,"“It is the Zaqqūm.”"],[3369,"ʿAbdullāh used to pray Maghrib while we thought the sun was still risen. He said: One day we looked at that, and he said, “What are you looking at?” They said, “At the sun.” ʿAbdullāh said, “This, by the One besides whom there is no god, is the time for this prayer.” Then he recited: {Establish prayer at the sun’s decline until the darkness of the night} [al-Isrāʾ 78]. So this is the sun’s decline."],[3370,"“People will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection, and I and my community will be on a hill. My Lord will clothe me in a green robe. Then He will permit me, and I will say what Allah wills me to say. That is the Praiseworthy Station.”"],[3371,"\"That your Lord may raise you to a praised position.\" [Quran 17:79] He said, \"The people will be gathered in one plain where the caller will make them hear and the sight will reach them barefooted, unclothed, as they were created, silently, not speaking except with His permission. Then Muhammad will be called and he will say, 'Here I am, at your service, and your happiness and righteousness are in your hands. Evil is not yours. The guided ones are those whom You have guided and Your servant is in Your presence, and to You is his return, and there is no refuge or escape from You except to You. Blessed and exalted are You, O Lord of the House.' That is the praised position mentioned by Allah, 'That your Lord may raise you to a praised position.' [Quran 17:79]\""],[3372,"The two sons of Mulaykah came—they were from the Anṣār—and said, “O Messenger of Allah, our mother was protective of her husband and generous to guests, but she buried a daughter alive in the Jāhiliyyah. Where is our mother?” He said, “Your mother is in the Fire.” They rose, and that was hard on them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them back. They returned, and he said, “My mother is with your mother.” A hypocrite among the people said to himself, “This benefits his mother no more than the two sons of Mulaykah benefit their mother, while we tread on his heels.” A young man of the Anṣār—I never saw a man more given to questioning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than he—said, “O Messenger of Allah, I see that your parents are in the Fire.” He said, “I asked my Lord about them, and He did not grant me anything for them. On that day I will stand at the Praiseworthy Station.” The hypocrite said to the young Anṣārī, “Ask him what the Praiseworthy Station is.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the Praiseworthy Station?” He said, “The day when Allah descends upon His Throne, and it creaks under Him as a camel saddle creaks from the strain, by the space between heaven and earth. You will be brought barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. The first to be clothed will be Ibrāhīm. Allah ﷻ will say, ‘Clothe My friend in two white garments from the garments of Paradise.’ Then I will be clothed after him. I will stand at the right of Allah ﷻ in a position for which the first and the last will envy me. A river from al-Kawthar will be opened for me to my basin.” He said: The hypocrite said, “I have never heard anything like today. Rarely has a river flowed except in pottery or pebbles. Ask him in what the river flows.” He said, “In a basin of musk and pebbles.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard anything like today. Rarely has a river flowed except with plants.” He said, “Yes.” He asked, “What are they?” He said, “Rods of gold.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard anything like today. By Allah, no rod grows except with fruit. Ask him if those rods have fruits.” He said, “Yes: pearls and jewels.” The hypocrite said, “I have never heard anything like today. Ask him about the drink of the basin.” The Anṣārī said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is the drink of the basin?” He said, “Whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. Whoever Allah gives a drink from it will never thirst after it, and whoever is deprived of it will never be quenched after it.”"],[3373,"I have a friend of mine, and I am in Kufa. Do you have a man you are looking for? I said yes. He said, \"This is his ranking, and indeed he is Oways Al-Qarani. I think he will pass by now.\" He said, so we sat for him, and he passed, and there was a mark on him. He said, \"People tread on his heels.\" He said, \"He approaches them and speaks to them about it, but they don't stop. We walked with the people until we entered the mosque in Kufa, and we entered with him. He went to a wall and prayed two Rak'ahs, then he turned his face towards us and said, 'O people, why do you tread on my heels in every way? I am a weak person, and I have needs that I cannot fulfill with you. Do not do that, may Allah have mercy on you. Whoever has any need from me, let him tell me here.'\" The man said, and it was 'Umar ibn Al-Khattab who asked a delegation that came to him, \"Did someone from his family visit you, like this and like that?\" The man said, \"People have mentioned you, O Amir al-Muminin, and they did not mention that, as is commonly said. That is not from his mention, what I have told you. The man said, \"Oways has taken a covenant and a pledge from the man not to tell anyone else about it.\" Then he said, \"Oways said, 'This majlis (gathering) is attended by three people - a knowledgeable believer, a believer who is not knowledgeable, and a hypocrite. This is like rain that falls from the sky to the earth; it reaches the good and fruitful tree and increases its beauty, freshness, and produce. And it reaches the weak and fruitless tree, and increases its rot and makes its leaves fall. And it reaches the thorns that break and destroy them.'\" Then he recited the verse, \"And We send down of the Qur'an that which is healing and mercy for the believers, but it does not increase the wrongdoers except in loss.\" [Al-Isra 82] This Qur'an does not sit with anyone except that it either adds or decreases in him. This is the decree of Allah that He has decreed, healing and mercy for the believers, but it does not increase the wrongdoers except in loss. O Allah, grant me a martyrdom that precedes its pain and its safety precedes its fear, which gives life and sustenance. Then he became silent. The man said, \"I walked with him.\" He asked, \"My friend, how do you see the man?\" I said, \"I have not increased in him except a desire, and I am not one who can leave him.\" We remained with him, and we did not stay except for a short while until he struck the people again. The commander of the faithful, Ali, was sent, and Oways Al-Qarani was among them. We went out with him and traveled with him, and we would stay with him and descend with him until we reached the presence of the enemy.\""],[3374,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me until he brought me to the Kaʿbah. He said to me, “Sit.” So I sat beside the Kaʿbah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed onto my shoulder, then said, “Rise.” I rose, but when he saw my weakness beneath him, he said, “Sit.” So I descended and sat. Then he said, “O ʿAlī, climb onto my shoulder.” So I climbed onto his shoulders. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose with me. When he rose with me, it seemed to me that if I wished I could touch the horizon of the sky. I climbed above the Kaʿbah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stepped aside. He said to me, “Throw down their greatest idol, the idol of Quraysh.” It was made of brass, fastened with iron pegs to the ground. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Work on it,” while he kept saying, “Go on! Go on! {Truth has come, and falsehood has vanished. Indeed falsehood is bound to vanish} [al-Isrāʾ 81].” I kept working on it until I got a firm hold of it. He said, “Hurl it.” I hurled it, and it shattered. I fell from the top of the Kaʿbah. The Prophet ﷺ and I ran off, fearing that someone from Quraysh or others might see us. ʿAlī said: It was never put back up until this hour."],[3375,"Abū Zakariyyā al-ʿAnbarī informed us; Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Salām narrated to us; Isḥāq b. Ibrāhīm al-Ḥanẓalī narrated to us; Shabābah b. Sawwār reported it, and he mentioned it likewise."],[3376,"I heard Abū Dharr al-Ghifārī recite this verse: {And We will gather them on the Day of Resurrection on their faces, blind, dumb, and deaf} [al-Isrāʾ 97]. Abū Dharr said: The truthful, the believed one ﷺ told me: “People will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection in three groups: well-fed, clothed, and mounted; a group walking and running; and a group dragged by the angels on their faces.” We said, “We know these two. What about those who walk and run?” He said, “Allah will send a blight on all beasts so that no beast remains, until a man will give a wonderful garden for a stray she-camel with a saddle.”"],[3377,"The Qurʾān was sent down all at once to the lowest heaven, then it came down after that over twenty years. He ﷻ said: {They do not bring you any similitude but We bring you the truth and a better explanation} [al-Furqān 33]. He said: {And a Qurʾān which We have divided, that you may recite it to the people at intervals, and We have sent it down gradually} [al-Isrāʾ 106]."],[3378,"“Whoever memorizes ten verses from the beginning of Sūrat al-Kahf will be protected from the Dajjāl.”"],[3379,"The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, \"Whoever recites Surah Al-Kahf on Friday, he will be illuminated with light from between the two Fridays.\""],[3380,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His ﷻ saying: {and he will be given to drink from purulent water, which he will gulp but scarcely swallow} [Ibrāhīm 17]. He said: “It will be brought near to him, and he will loathe it. When it is brought close to his face, it will roast his face and the skin of his head will fall off. When he drinks it, it will sever his intestines until it comes out of his anus.” Allah ﷻ says: {They will be given boiling water to drink, and it will cut their intestines} [Muḥammad 15]. And Allah ﷻ says: {And if they call for help, they will be helped with water like molten brass, which scalds faces—evil the drink} [al-Kahf 29]."],[3381,"When Mūsā met al-Khiḍr (peace be upon them), a bird came and dipped its beak in the water. Al-Khiḍr said to Mūsā, “Reflect on what this bird says.” He said, “What does it say?” He said, “It says: Your knowledge and Mūsā’s knowledge in Allah’s knowledge are only like what my beak has taken from the water.”"],[3382,"“As a protection for the righteousness of their father, and He did not mention any righteousness about them.”"],[3383,"It was neither gold nor silver; it was pages of knowledge."],[3384,"From the Prophet ﷺ concerning the saying of Allah, Mighty and Sublime: {And beneath it was a treasure for them} [Al-Kahf: 82], he said: \"Gold and silver.\" But Yazid b. Yusuf is abandoned."],[3385,"Sufficient for you is what Musa and al-Khidr disputed about."],[3386,"The children of the believers in Paradise will be cared for by Ibrahim ﷺ ."],[3387,"I said to Ubayy: {Shall We inform you of the greatest losers in their deeds? Those whose effort is lost in the life of this world while they think they are doing good} [Al-Kahf: 104]—are they the Haruriyyah? He said: \"No, but they are the people of the monasteries. The Haruriyyah are a people who deviated, so Allah caused their hearts to deviate.\""],[3388,"I was reciting to my father until I reached this verse: {Say: Shall We inform you of the greatest losers in their deeds} [Al-Kahf: 103]—the verse—I said: O father, are they the Khawarij? He said: No, my son, recite the verse after it: {Those are the ones who disbelieve in the signs of their Lord and in the meeting with Him, so their deeds are nullified, and We will assign no weight to them on the Day of Resurrection} [Al-Kahf: 105]. He said: \"They are the devoted ones among the Christians; their disbelief in the signs of their Lord was in Muhammad and in the meeting with Him.\" And they said there is no food or drink in Paradise, but the Khawarij are the transgressors who break the covenant of Allah after its ratification and cut what Allah has commanded to be joined and spread corruption on the earth—those are the losers."],[3389,"Ask Allah for al-Firdaws, for it is the center of Paradise."],[3390,"It has been revealed to me that whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord should do righteous deeds and not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord, and he will have a light from Abyan to Makkah, attended by the angels."],[3391,"O Messenger of Allah, a man fights in the path of Allah while seeking some worldly gain. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"He has no reward.\" The people considered that grave, and the man repeated, and he said: \"He has no reward.\""],[3392,"Kaf is from Karim (Generous), Ha is from Hadi (Guide), Ya is from Hakim (Wise), 'Ayn is from 'Alim (All-Knowing), Sad is from Sadiq (Truthful)."],[3393,"Kaf, Ha, Ya, 'Ayn, Sad: Generous, Guide, Trustworthy, Mighty, Truthful."],[3394,"No one was named Yahya before him."],[3395,"He was asked about the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And I have reached old age} [Maryam 8]. What is old age? He said: \"The misery of old age.\" The poet said [al-khafīf meter]: Indeed the newborn is excused, and no excuse is given to one who has grown aged in time. Ahmad b. Hanbal said: Muhammad b. Ziyad al-Yashkuri al-Tahhan is a wicked liar who fabricates hadith, and Ibn Shuja' is among the weak narrators of Marw."],[3396,"\"He used to command them to pray morning and evening.\""],[3397,"\"Showing compassion through mercy.\""],[3398,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Every child of Adam will come on the Day of Resurrection with a sin, except what was from Yahya b. Zakariyya.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lowered his hand to the ground and took a small stick, then said: \"And that is because he had nothing of what men have except the like of this stick; for that reason Allah named him a chief, and chaste, and a prophet from among the righteous.\""],[3399,"{She said: How can I have a boy when no man has touched me and I have not been unchaste?} [Maryam 20]. Then she conceived from the one who spoke to her, and it entered from her mouth."],[3400,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Your Lord has placed beneath you a stream} [Maryam 24], he said: \"It is the small river, the little stream.\""],[3401,"\"He heard the sound of the pen as he wrote on the tablet.\""],[3402,"From Ibn 'Abbas regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And mention in the Book Ibrahim. Indeed, he was a man of truth, a prophet} [Maryam 41]. He said: \"The prophets were from the Children of Israel except ten: Nuh, Salih, Hud, Lut, Shu'ayb, Ibrahim, Isma'il, Ishaq, Ya'qub, and Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon them all). And no prophet had two names except Israel and 'Isa: Israel is Ya'qub, and 'Isa is the Messiah.\""],[3403,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he recited this verse: {Then there succeeded after them a succession} [al-A'raf 169]. He ﷺ said: \"There will be a succession after sixty years who will neglect the prayer and follow desires, and they will meet evil. Then there will be a succession who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. Three types recite the Quran: a believer, a hypocrite, and a wicked person.\" Bashir said: I said to al-Walid: What are these three? He said: The hypocrite is a disbeliever, the wicked person consumes by it, and the believer believes in it."],[3404,"\"People of the Book and people of the brick will perish from my nation.\" 'Uqbah said: Who are the people of the Book, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"A people who learn the Book of Allah and dispute with it against those who believe.\" He said: I said: Who are the people of the brick, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"A people who follow desires and neglect the prayers.\""],[3405,"From 'Abdullah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Then they will meet error} [Maryam 59]. He said: \"A river in Hell, deep-bottomed, foul-tasting.\""],[3406,"\"What Allah has made lawful in His Book is lawful, and what He has forbidden is forbidden, and what He has remained silent about is a pardon. So accept from Allah the pardon, for Allah is never forgetful.\" Then he recited this verse: {And your Lord is never forgetful}."],[3407,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Do you know of any namesake for Him?} [Maryam 65]. He said: \"No one has been named the Most Merciful other than Him.\""],[3408,"About the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And there is none of you except he will come to it. This is upon your Lord an inevitability decreed} [Maryam 71]. He narrated to me that 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud narrated to them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"People will enter the Fire, then they will emerge according to their deeds. The first of them like the flash of lightning, then like the passing of the wind, then like the galloping of a horse, then like a rider, then like the hastening of a traveler, then like their walking.\""],[3409,"The slogan of the Muslims on the bridge over Hell on the Day of Resurrection is: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety."],[3410,"From 'Abd Allah: \"{There is none of you but will pass over it} [Maryam: 71] — he said: The bridge over Hell is like the edge of a sword. The first group will pass like lightning, the second like the wind, the third like the finest horses, and the fourth like the finest camels and beasts. Then they will pass while the angels say: Lord, grant safety, grant safety.\""],[3411,"Allah will gather the people on the Day of Resurrection. A caller will call out: O people, are you not pleased that your Lord who created you, provided for you, and fashioned you should entrust every one of you to the one he used to take as a protector in the world? He said: A devil resembling 'Uzayr will be represented to those who worshipped 'Uzayr, until trees, sticks, and stones are represented to them. The people of Islam will remain kneeling, and it will be said to them: What is the matter with you that you do not go as the people go? They will say: We have a Lord whom we have not yet seen. He said: It will be said: How will you recognize your Lord if you see Him? They will say: Between us and Him there is a sign; if we see it, we will recognize Him. It will be said: What is it? They will say: He will uncover a shin. He said: Then a shin will be uncovered. He said: Then those whose backs were stiff will fall down prostrating, while a people whose backs are like the horns of cattle will remain, wanting to prostrate but unable. Then they will be commanded to raise their heads, and they will be given their light according to their deeds. Among them is one who is given his light like a mountain before him; among them is one given more than that; among them is one given his light like a palm tree in his right hand; and among them is one given less than that in his right hand, until the last of them is one whose light is on his big toe, shining at times and going out at times. When his foot shines, he walks; when it goes out, he stops. He will pass, and they will pass over the bridge. The bridge is like the edge of a sword, slippery and treacherous. It will be said: Pass according to your light. Among them is one who passes like a shooting star, one like the blink of an eye, one like the wind, one like a man running, and one who trots. They will pass according to their deeds, until the one whose light is on his big toe passes: he drags one hand and hangs the other, drags one foot and hangs the other, and the fire strikes his sides. He said: Then they will be saved. When they are saved, they will say: Praise be to Allah who saved us from you after what He showed us. Allah has given us what He has not given anyone. Masruq said: 'Abd Allah never reached this point in this hadith except that he laughed. A man said to him: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, you have narrated this hadith many times, and whenever you reach this point you laugh. 'Abd Allah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrate it many times, and he never reached this point except that he laughed until his uvula showed and the last of his molars appeared, because of the man's saying: Do You mock me when You are the Lord of the worlds? He says: No, but I am able to do that, so ask Me."],[3412,"From 'Ali regarding this verse: {On the Day We will gather the righteous to the Most Merciful as a delegation} [Maryam: 85]. 'Ali said: By Allah, the delegation will not be gathered on their feet nor driven like cattle. Rather, they will be brought she-camels the like of which no creature has seen, with saddles of gold and reins of chrysolite. They will ride them until they knock on the gates of Paradise. [The hadith]"],[3413,"He recited: {Except one who has taken from the Most Merciful a covenant} [Maryam: 87], and said: They have taken a covenant from the Most Merciful, for Allah will say on the Day of Resurrection: Whoever has a covenant with Me, let him stand. He said: We said: Teach us, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. He said: Say: O Allah, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Knower of the unseen and the witnessed, I pledge to You in this worldly life that I bear witness that there is no god but You alone, with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger. If You entrust me to myself, You will bring me near evil and remove me from good. I trust only in Your mercy, so make it for me a covenant with You that You will fulfill for me on the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, You do not break the promise."],[3414,"He is similar to your saying, O Muhammad, in the language of Abyssinia."],[3415,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in al-Batha' when a cloud passed by. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you know what this is?\" We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"The cloud.\" We said: The cloud. He said: \"And the rain-cloud.\" We said: And the rain-cloud. He said: \"And the high cloud.\" Then he was silent. Then he said: \"Do you know how much is between the heaven and the earth?\" We said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Between them is a journey of five hundred years, and between each heaven and the next is a journey of five hundred years, and the thickness of each heaven is a journey of five hundred years. Above the seventh heaven is a sea, between its top and bottom is like what is between the heaven and the earth. Then above that are eight mountain goats, between their knees and hooves is like what is between the heaven and the earth. And Allah is above that, and none of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him.\""],[3416,"From al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib regarding Allah's saying ﷻ {And eight will bear the Throne of your Lord above them that Day} [Al-Haqqah: 17]: Angels in the form of mountain goats, between their hooves and knees is a journey of sixty-three or sixty-five years."],[3417,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {He knows the secret and what is more hidden} [Taha: 7], he said: {The secret} is what you yourself know, and {what is more hidden} is what Allah casts into your heart of what you do not know."],[3418,"On the day Allah spoke to Musa, he was wearing a woolen jubbah, a woolen cloak, woolen trousers, woolen sleeves, and sandals made from the hide of an unslaughtered donkey."],[3419,"The Prophet ﷺ used to narrate to us most of the night about the Children of Israel, and he would not get up except for the great prayer."],[3420,"When Umm Kulthum bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was placed in the grave, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"From it We created you, and into it We will return you, and from it We will bring you out once again. In the name of Allah, and in the path of Allah, and upon the religion of the Messenger of Allah.\" When her niche was built, he began throwing clods to them and saying: \"Fill the gaps between the bricks.\" Then he said: \"This is nothing, but it comforts the living.\" He did not comment on it, and it is a weak report because 'Ali b. Yazid is abandoned."],[3421,"When Musa hastened to his Lord, al-Samiri went and gathered what he could of the jewelry of the Children of Israel and fashioned it into a calf. Then he threw the handful into its belly, and it became a calf that lowed. Al-Samiri said to them: This is your god and the god of Musa. Harun said to them: O my people, did not your Lord promise you a good promise? When Musa returned to the Children of Israel after al-Samiri had led them astray, he seized his brother by the head. Harun told him what he said, and Musa said to al-Samiri: What is your case? Al-Samiri said: I grasped a handful from the trace of the messenger and threw it, and thus my soul enticed me. He said: Musa went to the calf, placed files on it, and filed it down while it was at the bank of a river. None of those who worshipped the calf drank from that water except that his face turned yellow like gold. They said to Musa: What is our repentance? He said: Let some of you kill others. So they took knives, and a man would kill his father and brother, not caring whom he killed, until seventy thousand of them were killed. Then Allah revealed to Musa: Command them to raise their hands, for I have forgiven those who were killed and accepted the repentance of those who remain."],[3422,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on Musa. The one who sees with his own eyes is not like the one who is told. His Lord informed him that his people were tempted after him, so he did not throw down the tablets; but when he saw them and witnessed them, he threw down the tablets.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on Musa. Had he not been hasty, other things about his story would have been narrated besides what has been narrated.\""],[3423,"\"Allah created Adam from the surface of the entire earth, so he was named Adam.\""],[3424,"\"When Adam ate from the tree that he was forbidden from, Allah Almighty said, 'What led you to disobey Me?' Adam replied, 'My Lord, I was seduced by Eve.' Allah said, 'Then surely I will make it so that you both feel hatred towards each other. You will feel pain and discomfort in childbirth, and I will cause you to menstruate twice a month.' When Eve heard this, she felt remorse and Adam said to her, 'You will experience menstruation and your daughters will as well.'\""],[3425,"Whoever recites the Quran and follows what is in it, Allah will guide him from misguidance and protect him on the Day of Resurrection from an evil reckoning. That is because Allah, exalted is He, said: {So whoever follows My guidance will neither go astray nor suffer} [Taha: 123]."],[3426,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding {a narrow livelihood} [Taha: 124]: \"The punishment of the grave.\""],[3427,"Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan said: \"O Allah, let me enjoy my husband, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and my father Abu Sufyan, and my brother Muʿawiyah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"You have called upon Allah for fixed terms, apportioned provisions, and predetermined outcomes. None of them can be hastened before its time or delayed after its time. Had you asked Allah to grant you well-being, or asked Him to protect you, or to grant you well-being from the punishment of the Fire or the punishment of the grave, it would have been better, or it would have been more excellent.\""],[3428,"\"The trial of the grave is regarding me. So when you are asked about me, do not doubt.\""],[3429,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the words of Allah, exalted is He: {And they cannot intercede except for someone He is pleased with} [Al-Anbiya: 28], then said ﷺ: \"Indeed my intercession is for the people of major sins among my community.\""],[3430,"Regarding His statement, exalted is He: {Have those who disbelieved not considered that the heavens and the earth were a joined entity, and We split them apart} [Al-Anbiya: 30] – he said: \"The sky was split open by rain, and the earth was split open by vegetation.\""],[3431,"\"The supplication of Dhu al-Nun when he called upon Him while he was in the belly of the whale: 'There is no god but You; glory be to You. Indeed, I have been of the wrongdoers.' No Muslim man ever calls upon Allah with it for anything but that he is answered.\""],[3432,"From ʿAbd Allah b. Masʿud regarding His statement, exalted is He: {And he called out in the darknesses} [Al-Anbiya: 87] – he said: \"The darkness of the night, the darkness of the belly of the whale, and the darkness of the sea.\""],[3433,"From Ibn ʿAbbas regarding the words of Allah, exalted is He: {And We set right for him his wife} [Al-Anbiya: 90] – he said: \"There was a length in the tongue of Zakariyya's wife, and Allah, exalted is He, set it right.\""],[3434,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq delivered a sermon to us. He praised Allah and extolled Him with what He deserves, then said: \"I enjoin you to fear Allah, and to extol Him with what He deserves, and to combine hope with fear. For Allah praised Zakariyya and his household, saying: {Indeed, they used to hasten to good deeds and supplicate Us in hope and fear, and they were humbly submissive to Us} [Al-Anbiya: 90]. Then know, O servants of Allah, that Allah has taken your souls as a pledge for His right, and has taken your covenants for that, and has purchased from you the little that is perishable for the much that is enduring. This is the Book of Allah among you; its light is not extinguished, and its wonders do not cease. So seek light from its light, and take counsel from its Book, and seek light from it for the day of darkness. Indeed, He created you only for His worship and appointed over you noble recording angels who know what you do. Then know, O servants of Allah, that you go forth in the morning and return in the evening within a term whose knowledge is hidden from you. If you are able that your terms come to an end while you are in the work of Allah, then do so; and you will never be able to do that except with Allah's help. So race within the respite of your terms before your terms come to an end and He returns you to the evil of your deeds. For there are people who made their terms for other than themselves and forgot themselves. I forbid you to be like them. So hasten, hasten; then deliverance, deliverance. For behind you is a pursuer who is swift in his passing and quick.\""],[3435,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the night journey, he met Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa, and they discussed the Hour. They started with Ibrahim and asked him about it, but he had no knowledge of it. Then Musa, and he had no knowledge of it. Then the discussion returned to 'Isa, and 'Isa said: Allah entrusted me with knowledge of events before its occurrence, but not the Hour itself; we do not know it. He then mentioned the emergence of the Dajjal: I will descend and kill him, and the people will return to their lands. Then Ya'juj and Ma'juj will come out to meet them, and they will emerge from every slope. They will not pass by any water but they will drink it, nor pass by anything but they will corrupt it. The people will cry out to Allah and call upon Him, and He will cause them to die. Then the earth will cry out to Allah from their stench, and they will cry out to me, so I will call upon Allah, and He will send the sky with water that will carry their bodies and cast them into the sea. Then the mountains will be blown away, and the earth will be stretched out like the stretching of leather. And Allah entrusted me that when that happens, the Hour will be to the people like a pregnant woman at full term: her family does not know when she will surprise them with her delivery, night or day.' Abdullah b. Mas'ud said: I found confirmation of that in the Book of Allah ﷻ: {Until when Ya'juj and Ma'juj are let loose and they descend from every height, and the true promise draws near} [Al-Anbiya: 97]—the verse. He said: And all people from every place they came from on the Day of Resurrection, it is a slope."],[3436,"When {Indeed you and what you worship besides Allah are the firewood of Hell; you will come to it} [Al-Anbiya: 98] was revealed, the polytheists said: Are the angels, 'Isa, and 'Uzayr worshiped besides Allah? He said: If those who are worshiped had been gods, they would not have entered it. Then {Indeed, those for whom the best has preceded from Us, they will be far removed from it} [Al-Anbiya: 101] was revealed: 'Isa, 'Uzayr, and the angels."],[3437,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on one of his journeys and had outstripped his Companions in travel. He raised his voice with these two verses: {O people, fear your Lord. Indeed, the earthquake of the Hour is a tremendous thing. On the Day you see it, every nursing mother will forget what she nursed, and every pregnant woman will deliver her burden, and you will see the people as drunk, though they are not drunk; but the punishment of Allah is severe} [Al-Hajj: 2]. When his Companions heard that, they urged their mounts and knew that he had something to say. When they gathered around him, he said: \"Do you know which day that is?\" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"That is the day when Adam ﷺ will be called, and his Lord will call him and say: O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire. He will say: O Lord, what is the delegation of the Fire? He will say: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.\" They said: They were struck with despair until they did not even smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that, he said: \"Work and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations that, whenever they are with anything, they make it numerous: Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and those who perished from the children of Adam and the children of Iblis.\" That relieved the people, so he said: \"Work and rejoice, for by the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among the people only like a mark on the foreleg of a beast or a mole on the side of a camel.\""],[3438,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite {And you will see the people as drunk, though they are not drunk; but the punishment of Allah is severe} [Al-Hajj: 2]."],[3439,"\"The formed [fetus] is what was alive, and the unformed is what was a miscarriage.\""],[3440,"\"That Allah will not support Muhammad (Peace be upon him).\""],[3441,"He said concerning {These are two disputants who disputed concerning their Lord} [Al-Hajj: 19]: \"It was revealed about us and about those who fought in single combat on the day of Badr: 'Utbah, Shaybah, and al-Walid.\""],[3442,"I heard Abu Dharr swearing that this verse was revealed concerning these six men on the day of Badr: 'Ali, Hamzah, 'Ubaydah, Shaybah, 'Utbah—the two sons of Rabi'ah—and al-Walid b. 'Utbah: {These are two disputants who disputed concerning their Lord} [Al-Hajj: 19] up to His saying, exalted be He, {We will make him taste a painful punishment} [Al-Hajj: 25].[1]"],[3443,"'Ali said: I am the first who will kneel for the dispute on my knees before Allah on the Day of Resurrection. The hadith is authentic with these narrations from 'Ali, just as it is authentic from Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, even if they did not include it [in their collections]."],[3444,"This verse was revealed about Hamzah and his companions: {And do not think those who were killed in the way of Allah are dead; rather, they are alive with their Lord}."],[3445,"From Abu Hurayrah, and he recited the words of Allah ﷻ {As for those who disbelieve, garments of fire will be cut out for them} [Al-Hajj: 19] and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, boiling water will be poured upon their heads, and it will penetrate the skull until it reaches their inside, and it will strip away what is in their inside until it tears through their feet; that is the melting. Then he will be returned as he was.\""],[3446,"The Fire is black; its flame does not give light, nor does its ember. Then he recited this verse: {Whenever they try to come out of it from anguish, they will be returned into it}."],[3447,"\"That a man will be concerned about a sin, meaning that if he does not commit it, it will not be written against him. Even if a man intends to kill another man at his home while he is far away, Allah will make him taste a painful punishment. And Shu'bah narrated it from Isma'il ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Suddi from Murrata on the condition of Muslim.\""],[3448,"He traced it back to the Prophet ﷺ regarding the words of Allah ﷻ {And whoever intends therein deviation with wrongdoing, We will make him taste a painful punishment} [Al-Hajj: 25]: \"If a man intended therein deviation while he was in 'Adan Abyan, Allah would make him taste a painful punishment.\""],[3449,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"A man of Quraysh will commit deviation (ilḥād) in it, whose sins, were they weighed against the sins of the two weighty kinds (humans and jinn), would outweigh them.\""],[3450,"Tubba' came intending the Ka'bah, until when he was at Kurā' al-Ghamīm, Allah sent upon him a wind such that a standing person could hardly stand except with difficulty, and a standing person would go and then sit and be thrown down, and it rose against them, and they met from it great hardship. Tubba' called his two rabbis and asked them, \"What is this that has been sent upon me?\" They said, \"Will you grant us safety?\" He said, \"You are safe.\" They said, \"You intend a House which Allah protects from whoever intends it.\" He said, \"Then what will remove this from me?\" They said, \"Strip to two garments, then say 'Labbayka, labbayka,' then enter and circumambulate that House, and do not provoke any of its people.\" He said, \"If I resolve upon this, will this wind leave me?\" They said, \"Yes.\" So he stripped, then said the talbiyah. Ibn 'Abbās said, \"The wind turned away like pieces of dark night.\""],[3451,"When Ibrāhīm finished building the House, he said, \"Lord, I have finished.\" He said, \"Proclaim the pilgrimage among the people.\" He said, \"Lord, how far will my voice reach?\" He said, \"Proclaim, and upon Me is the delivery.\" He said, \"Lord, how shall I say?\" He said, \"Say: O people, the pilgrimage to the Ancient House has been prescribed for you.\" Then all between heaven and earth heard it. Do you not see that they come from the farthest parts of the earth, saying the talbiyah?"],[3452,"Allah called the House 'al-'Atīq' only because He freed it from tyrants, and no tyrant ever prevailed over it."],[3453,"I said to him regarding His saying, Exalted is He, {And the camels and cattle We have made for you among the symbols of Allah; for you therein is good. So mention the name of Allah upon them when lined up} [al-Ḥajj 36]. He said, \"When you want to slaughter a camel, make it stand, then say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, from You and to You, then mention the name, then slaughter it.\" I said, \"And do I say that for the sacrificial animal (uḍḥiyah)?\" He said, \"And for the sacrificial animal.\""],[3454,"We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are these sacrificial animals (aḍāḥī)?\" He said, \"The sunnah of your father Ibrāhīm.\" We said, \"What do we get from them?\" He said, \"For every hair, a good deed.\" We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and wool?\" He said, \"For every hair of wool, a good deed.\""],[3455,"Whoever has the means to offer a sacrifice but does not do so, let him not attend our place of prayer."],[3456,"He used to recite it: {Permission is given to those who are fought against, because they have been wronged, and indeed Allah is able to give them victory} [al-Ḥajj 39]. He said, \"It is the first verse revealed concerning fighting.\""],[3457,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is Sūrat al-Ḥajj distinguished by two prostrations?\" He said, \"Yes, and whoever does not prostrate for them, let him not recite it.\""],[3458,"He prayed the morning prayer with 'Umar, and he prostrated twice in al-Ḥajj."],[3459,"In Sūrat al-Ḥajj there are two prostrations."],[3460,"He prostrated twice in al-Ḥajj."],[3461,"\"They both used to prostrate two prostrations in Surat al-Hajj.\""],[3462,"\"He prostrated two prostrations in Surat al-Hajj, and he recited the prostration at the end of Surat al-Hajj and prostrated, and we prostrated with him.\""],[3463,"\"I saw Abu al-Darda' prostrate two prostrations in Surat al-Hajj.\""],[3464,"She asked the Prophet ﷺ about this verse: {And He has not placed upon you in the religion any hardship} [Al-Hajj 78] He said, \"Constriction.\""],[3465,"\"A sacrifice they will slaughter.\" Suhayl has rejected narrations, and Ibn 'Aqil is not strong."],[3466,"\"I heard 'Umar b. al-Khattab say: When the revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a buzzing like the buzzing of bees was heard near him. We waited for a while, then he faced the qiblah and raised his hands, saying: 'O Allah, increase us and do not decrease us; honor us and do not disgrace us; give us and do not deprive us; prefer us and do not prefer others over us; be pleased with us and make us pleased.' Then he said: 'Ten verses have been revealed to me; whoever establishes them will enter Paradise.' Then he recited: {The believers have certainly succeeded. Those who are humble in their prayers} [Al-Mu'minun 2] and the verses.\""],[3467,"\"Allah created the Garden of Eden and planted its trees with His own hand. He said to it: 'Speak,' and it said: 'The believers have certainly succeeded.'\""],[3468,"We said to 'A'ishah: O Mother of the Believers, how was the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? She said: \"The character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the Qur'an.\" Then she said: Do you recite Surat al-Mu'minun? Recite: {The believers have certainly succeeded} [Al-Mu'minun 1] until you reach the tenth verse. Then she said: \"Such was the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[3469,"Regarding His saying, Exalted be He, \"Who are humble in their prayers\" [Surah Al-Mu'minun, verse 2], He said: \"Humility is in the heart, and that your shoulders soften for the Muslim, and that you do not turn around in your prayer.\""],[3470,"The translation is as follows: \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to raise his gaze towards the sky when he prayed, and then the verse would descend upon him: 'Those who are humble in their prayers' [Al-Mu'minun 2]. And he would lower his head.\""],[3471,"And she recited this verse: {And those who guard their private parts, except from their spouses or those their right hands possess, for indeed they are not blameworthy. But whoever seeks beyond that} [Al-Mu'minun 6] - whoever seeks beyond what Allah has married him to or given him possession of has transgressed."],[3472,"It was narrated to us by Ishaq, who was informed by 'Abd al-Razzaq, who was informed by Ma'mar, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Those are the inheritors} [Al-Mu'minun 10]. He said: \"They will inherit their dwellings and the dwellings of their brothers that were prepared for them if they obeyed Allah.\""],[3473,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is the person who commits adultery, steals, and drinks alcohol, but still fears Allah Almighty, considered righteous?\" He said, \"No, but the person who fasts, prays, and gives charity, and still fears Allah Almighty, is considered righteous.\""],[3474,"\"Night conversation was disliked only when this verse was revealed: {In arrogance regarding it, conversing by night, speaking nonsense} [Al-Mu'minun 67]. He said: In arrogance regarding the House, saying: 'We are its people.' {Speaking nonsense} [Al-Mu'minun 67] He said: They used to abandon it and not maintain it.\""],[3475,"Abu Sufyan came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"O Muhammad, I adjure you by Allah and kinship. We have eaten 'alhaz (i.e., hair and blood).\" Then Allah, Exalted and Glorified, revealed: {And We had seized them with punishment, but they did not humble themselves to their Lord, nor did they supplicate} [Al-Mu'minun 76]."],[3476,"A man came to him and said, 'O Ibn Abbas, I have something in my soul about the Quran.' He said, 'What is it?' He said, 'Doubt.' He said, 'Woe to you! Have you asked anyone other than me?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'Bring it.' He said, 'I hear Allah saying, \"And Allah is ever, over all things, competent\" [Al-Ahzab 27]. Was this a matter that has already occurred? And He said, \"So no lineage will there be among them that Day, nor will they ask one another\" [Al-Mu'minun 101]. But He said in another verse, \"And they will approach one another, asking each other\" [As-Saffat 27]. Then he mentioned other things. Ibn Abbas said, 'As for His saying, \"And Allah is ever, over all things, competent\" [Al-Ahzab 27], He has always been and will always be; He is the First and the Last, the Outward and the Inward. As for His saying, \"So no lineage will there be among them that Day, nor will they ask one another\" [Al-Mu'minun 101], this is at the first blast, when nothing remains on the earth; so no lineage will there be among them that Day, nor will they ask one another. As for His saying, \"Then they will approach one another, asking each other\" [As-Saffat 50], when they enter Paradise, they will approach one another, asking each other.'\""],[3477,"\"And therein they will grimace in displace lips. -He will be grilled by the Fire until his upper lip is folded up reaching the middle of his head, And his bottom lip pains down, until it hits his navel.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2587)"],[3478,"\"Like a fully matured bunch of grapes\""],[3479,"The people of the Fire will call upon Malik, but he will not answer them for forty days. Then he will respond to them, 'Indeed, you will remain.' He said, 'Their call became insignificant, by Allah, to Malik and the Lord of Malik.' They will say, 'Our Lord, our wretchedness overcame us, and we were a people astray' [Al-Mu'minun 106]. He will say, 'Remain despised therein and do not speak to Me.'\""],[3480,"\"Learn Surat al-Baqarah, Surat an-Nisa, Surat al-Ma'idah, Surat al-Hajj, and Surat an-Nur, for in them are the obligatory duties.\""],[3481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not let women live in the upper rooms, nor teach them writing. Rather, teach them spinning and Surah al-Nur.\""],[3482,"\"Women used to be entrepreneurs in the city, so Muslim men would marry women from among them so that they could support them financially. However, this practice was later prohibited.\""],[3483,"In His saying, \"Do not enter houses other than your own until you have sought permission\" [Surah An-Nur 27], He said: The writer made a mistake, it should be \"until you have sought permission\" (instead of \"until you have made yourself known\")."],[3484,"\"Any woman who perfumes herself and passes by a group so that they smell her fragrance is an adulteress.\""],[3485,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the sudden glance, and he commanded me to avert my gaze."],[3486,"From Abdullah regarding \"and not expose their adornment\" [An-Nur 31]: He said, \"Not anklets, not earrings, not earrings, not necklaces.\" \"Except that which appears thereof\" [An-Nur 31]: He said, \"Clothing.\""],[3487,"When this verse was revealed, \"and to wrap their headcovers over their chests\" [An-Nur 31], the women of the Ansar took their waist-wrappers and tore them from the edges and covered their heads with them."],[3488,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding \"and give them from the wealth of Allah which He has given you\" [An-Nur 33]: He said, \"A quarter is left for the mukatab (contract slave).\""],[3489,"Musaykah belonged to one of the Ansar. She said, 'My master forces me into prostitution.' Then it was revealed, \"And do not compel your slave girls to prostitution if they desire chastity.\""],[3490,"\"And it is the grave, meaning the pit.\" The chain of narration is authentic and neither of them narrated it as authentic."],[3491,"\"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it is from a blessed tree.\""],[3492,"\"Eat olive oil and anoint yourselves with it, for it is good and blessed.\""],[3493,"That his name be raised and mentioned therein, the men glorify Him therein at morning and evenings. [He is] a light example - like a niche within which is a lamp, the lamp is within glass. [The niche is] as if it were a pearly [white] star lit from [the oil of] a blessed olive tree, neither of the east nor of the west, whose oil would almost glow even if untouched by fire. Light upon light. Allah guides to His light whom He wills. And Allah presents examples for the people, and Allah is Knowing of all things."],[3494,"\"The mosques have pegs; they are their pegs. They have companions from the angels. If they are absent, the angels ask about them; if they are sick, the angels visit them; and if they are in need, the angels help them.\""],[3495,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we used to take turns tending the animals. When it was my turn, I sent my camels out to graze and then returned. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was addressing the people, and I heard him say: \"There is no Muslim who performs wudu and performs the wudu thoroughly, then stands in his prayer knowing what he is saying, except that he turns away from sins like the day his mother gave birth to him, with no sin upon him.\" He said: I could not restrain myself at that point from saying, “Bakh, bakh!” Umar, while I was beside him, said: “Are you amazed at this? Before you came, he said something even better than it.” I said: “What is it? May my father and mother be your ransom.” He said: He said: \"There is no man who performs wudu and performs the wudu thoroughly, then says when he finishes his wudu, ‘I testify that there is no god but Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger,’ except that eight gates of Paradise are opened for him; he may enter through whichever of them he wishes.\" Then he said: \"The people will be gathered on one plain; sight will reach them all, and the caller will make them all hear. Then a caller will call out: The people of the gathering will surely know for whom honor is today.\" Three times. Then he will say: \"Where are those whose sides used to forsake their beds?\" Then he will say: \"Where are those whom ‘neither trade nor sale distracted from the remembrance of Allah’ [al-Nur 37], to the end of the verse?\" Then a caller will call out: The gathering will surely know for whom honor is today. Then he will say: \"Where are the frequent praisers, those who used to praise their Lord?\"[1]"],[3496,"He called for a drink and it was brought to him. He said, “Pass it to the people.” They said, “We are fasting.” He said, “But I am not fasting.” Then he ordered it and drank it, then recited: {They fear a Day on which hearts and eyes will be overturned.}"],[3497,"Concerning the saying of Allah ﷻ, \"Allah is the Light of the heavens and the earth,\" he recited the verse, then said: \"But those who disbelieve—their deeds are like a mirage in a lowland, which the thirsty one thinks is water, until, when he comes to it, he finds it to be nothing, and he finds Allah there, so He pays him his account in full; and Allah is swift in reckoning\" [al-Nur 39]. He said: “Likewise, the disbeliever will come on the Day of Resurrection thinking that he has some good with Allah that he will find, but Allah will admit him into the Fire.” He said: And He gave another parable for the disbeliever, saying: \"Or like darknesses in a deep sea, covered by waves, above which are waves, above which are clouds—darknesses, one above another. When he puts out his hand, he can hardly see it. And whoever Allah does not grant light has no light\" [al-Nur 40]. Thus He moves him through five kinds of darkness: his speech is darkness, his deed is darkness, his entrance is darkness, his departure is darkness, and his final destination is to the darknesses, to the Fire, on the Day of Resurrection.[1]"],[3498,"We went out for a funeral at the gate of Damascus with Abu Umamah al-Bahili. When he prayed over the funeral and they began to bury it, Abu Umamah said: O people, you have entered morning and evening in a dwelling where you divide good deeds and evil deeds, and you are about to depart from it to another dwelling, and it is this—he pointed to the grave—the house of solitude, the house of darkness, the house of worms, and the house of constriction, except what Allah expands. Then you move from it to the stations of the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, you are in some of those stations until a matter from Allah’s command overwhelms the people, and faces become white and faces become black. Then you move from it to another dwelling, and a severe darkness overwhelms the people. Then the light is divided, and the believer is given light, while the disbeliever and the hypocrite are left and given nothing. This is the parable that Allah, exalted is He, struck in His Book: {Or like darknesses in a deep sea covered by waves, above which are waves, above which are clouds—darknesses, some above others. When he stretches out his hand, he can hardly see it. And he to whom Allah has not granted light has no light} [al-Nur 40]. The disbeliever and the hypocrite do not benefit from the believer’s light, just as the blind do not benefit from the sight of the seeing. The hypocrite says to those who believe: {Wait for us, so that we may acquire some of your light. It will be said, “Go back behind you and seek light”} [al-Hadid 13]. This is the deception with which the hypocrite deceives. Allah, may He be glorified, said: {They seek to deceive Allah, but He deceives them} [al-Nisa' 142]. So they return to the place where the light was divided, but they find nothing, so they turn back to them while a wall with a gate has been struck between them; its interior contains mercy, and its exterior, from its direction, contains punishment. They call out to them: Were we not with you? Did we not pray with your prayers and raid with your raids? {They will say, “Yes, but you tempted yourselves, and you waited, and you doubted, and false hopes deceived you until the command of Allah came, and the Deceiver deceived you concerning Allah”} [al-Hadid 14]. He recited until His saying: {And wretched is the destination} [al-Hadid 15]."],[3499,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions arrived in Madinah and the Ansar sheltered them, the Arabs shot at them from a single bow. They would not spend the night except with weapons, nor rise in the morning except with them. They said: Do you think we will live until we spend the night safe and secure, fearing none but Allah? So it was revealed: {Allah has promised those of you who believe and do righteous deeds that He will surely make them successors in the land, as He made successors those before them, and that He will surely establish for them their religion which He has approved for them, and that He will surely change their state, after their fear, to security} [al-Nur 55] up to {And whoever disbelieves after that} [al-Nur 55], meaning by the blessing, {then those are the defiantly disobedient} [Al 'Imran 82]."],[3500,"From Ali regarding the saying of the Exalted: {Let those whom your right hands possess ask permission of you} [al-Nur 58]. He said, “Women, for men ask permission.”"],[3501,"\"He is the mosque; if you enter it, then say peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. It is authentic according to the condition of the two sheikhs (referring to Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim) and they did not discard it, according to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim.\""],[3502,"When you enter your houses, greet their inhabitants, and when you eat, mention the name of Allah. If one of you greets when he enters his house and mentions the name of Allah over his food, Satan says to his companions: “There is no lodging or dinner for you.” But if one of you does not greet and does not mention the name, Satan says to his companions: “You have attained lodging and dinner.”"],[3503,"From Ibn Mas'ud, ؓ ."],[3504,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: How will the people of Hell be gathered on their faces? He said, “Indeed, the One who made them walk on their feet is able to make them walk on their faces.” Sahih."],[3505,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, those who will be gathered on their faces—how will they be gathered? He said, “Indeed, the One who made them walk on their feet is able to gather them on their faces.”"],[3506,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Ma'add b. 'Adnan b. Adad b. Zand b. al-Bara' b. A'raq al-Thara.” She said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “He destroyed 'Ad and Thamud and the companions of the well and many generations between that—none knows them but Allah.” Umm Salamah said: A'raq al-Thara is Ishmael son of Abraham, Zand is Hamaysa', and Bara' is Nabt."],[3507,"There is no year with more rain than another year, but Allah turns it wherever He wills. Then he recited: {And We have distributed it among them} [al-Furqan 50], the verse."],[3508,"Regarding these two verses, their command is concerning those in Surah Al-Furqan who do not invoke any deity besides Allah and do not kill a soul which Allah has forbidden except for a just cause, and also in Surah An-Nisa, \"And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell.\" I asked Ibn Abbas about this, and he said, \"When the verse in Surah Al-Furqan was revealed, the polytheists of Makkah said, 'We have killed the soul which Allah has forbidden, and we have associated partners with Allah, and we have committed indecent actions.' Then the verse was revealed, 'Except for those who repent, believe, and do righteous deeds.'\" And he said, \"This is referring to those people.\" As for the verse in Surah An-Nisa, \"And whoever kills a believer intentionally,\" it refers to a man who embraced Islam, performed the deeds of Islam, and then intentionally killed a believer. His recompense is Hell, and there is no repentance for him. I mentioned this to Mujahid, and he said, \"It is correct according to the condition of the two sheikhs (referring to Bukhari and Muslim), as long as he has not been expelled.\" (According to the condition of Bukhari and Muslim)"],[3509,"A man from the people of polytheism said: O Messenger of Allah, and they have killed and done so abundantly, and fornicated and done so abundantly: how excellent is what you call us to! If only you told us that there is an expiation for what we have done. So Allah, may He be glorified, sent down: {And those who do not call upon another god with Allah} [al-Furqan 68], the verse. And it was revealed: {Say, “O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah”} [al-Zumar 53]. “Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it.” According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3510,"He recited the saying of Allah, may He be glorified: {And We revealed to Moses, “Travel by night with My servants; indeed, you will be pursued”} [al-Shu'ara' 52], the verses. Abu Burdah b. Abi Musa al-Ash'ari said from his father: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped with a Bedouin and honored him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Visit us; come to us.” The Bedouin came to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “What is your need?” He said: A she-camel with her saddle, and my family milks her milk. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Is this one incapable of being like the old woman of the Children of Israel?” His companions said to him: What is the old woman of the Children of Israel, O Messenger of Allah? He said: When Moses wanted to travel with the Children of Israel, the road was lost to him. He said to the Children of Israel: What is this? The scholars of the Children of Israel said to him: Joseph ﷺ , when death came to him, took from us a covenant from Allah that we would not leave Egypt until his bones were carried with us. Moses said: Which of you knows where Joseph’s grave is? The scholars of the Children of Israel said: No one knows the location of his grave except an old woman of the Children of Israel. Moses sent for her and said: Show us the grave of Joseph. She said: No, by Allah, not until you grant me my reward. He said to her: What is your reward? She said: My reward is that I be with you in Paradise. It was as if he disliked that. It was said to him: Give her her reward. So he gave her her reward. She took them to a lake of stagnant water and said to them: Drain this water. When they drained it, she said to them: Dig. They dug and extracted Joseph’s bones. When they lifted them from the ground, behold, the road was like the light of day."],[3511,"She said: O Messenger of Allah, 'Abd Allah b. Jud'an used to entertain guests, maintain family ties, and do such-and-such. Will that benefit him? He said: No, for he never once said, 'My Lord, forgive me my sin on the Day of Judgment.'"],[3512,"“The hoopoe used to guide Sulayman to water.” I said: How is that, when the hoopoe has a snare set for it and dirt thrown over it? He said: “May Allah deprive you of your father’s private parts! When destiny comes, does not sight depart?”"],[3513,"Ibn Abbas said, \"Indeed, fate comes when it is less than visible.\""],[3514,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “They now know that what I used to tell them in this world was true.” And Allah, exalted is He, said to His Prophet ﷺ: {Indeed, you will not make the dead hear, nor will you make the deaf hear the call when they turn their backs, retreating} [an-Naml 80]."],[3515,"From 'Abd Allah, regarding {Whoever comes with a good deed} [al-An'am 160], he said: “Whoever comes with 'there is no god but Allah'.” Regarding {and whoever comes with an evil deed} [al-An'am 160], he said: “with associating partners.” Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, and they did not include it. On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3516,"“Free from everything except the mention of Musa.” {She would almost have disclosed it} [al-Qasas 10] he said: “That she would say, 'O my son'.” {And she said to his sister, 'Trace him'} [al-Qasas 11] meaning 'seek his tracks.' {And We had forbidden foster mothers to him from before} [al-Qasas 12] he said: “No wet nurse would be brought to him but he would refuse her.”"],[3517,"From 'Umar, regarding {Then one of the two women came to him walking shyly} [al-Qasas 25]. He said: She used to come, frequently going in and out, placing her hand over her face. Then Musa stood up with her and said to her: 'Walk behind me and describe the way to me, for I will walk ahead of you, because we do not look at the backs of women.' Then she said: {O my father, hire him. Indeed, the best one you can hire is the strong and the trustworthy} [al-Qasas 26], because of the strength she saw in him and because of what he said to her. This increased his desire for him, so he said: {Indeed, I wish to marry you to one of these two daughters of mine on condition that you serve me for eight years; but if you complete ten, it will be from you. I do not wish to make it difficult for you. You will find me, if Allah wills, from among the righteous} [al-Qasas 27]—that is, in good companionship and fulfilling what I have said. Musa said: {That is between me and you. Whichever of the two terms I fulfill, there will be no injustice against me} [al-Qasas 28]. He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Allah is witness over what we say.' So he married him and stayed with him, working for him in tending his sheep and whatever he needed from him. He married him to Safura or her sister Sharqa, the two who used to drive away the flocks. Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, and they did not include it. On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked: Which of the two terms did Musa fulfill? He said: “The longer and better of them.” Hafs is weak."],[3519,"The Prophet ﷺ asked Jibril which of the two terms Musa fulfilled, and he said: “The most complete of them.”"],[3520,"I prayed 'Asr next to Ibn 'Umar and heard him say in his bowing: 'My Lord, because of the blessings You have bestowed on me, I will never be a supporter of the criminals.' When he finished, he said: 'I have never prayed a prayer except that I hope it will be an expiation for the one after it.'"],[3521,"Allah has not destroyed any people, generation, nation, or people of a town with a punishment from the sky since He sent down the Torah upon the face of the earth, except the people of the town that was transformed into apes. Do you not see the statement of Allah, exalted is He: {And We gave Musa the Scripture after We had destroyed the former generations, as enlightenment for the people and guidance and mercy that perhaps they might remember}?"],[3522,"From Abu Hurayrah, regarding {And you were not on the side of the mountain when We called} [al-Qasas 46], he said: “It was called out: 'O community of Muhammad, I answered you before you called upon Me, and I gave you before you asked Me.'”"],[3523,"When Musa came to his people, he commanded them to give zakah. Qarun gathered them and said: 'He has brought you prayer and other things, and you have borne them. Are you willing to give him your wealth?' They said: 'We cannot bear to give him our wealth. What do you think?' He said: 'I think I should send for the prostitute of the Children of Israel and send her to him so that she will accuse him of wanting her for himself.' Musa then supplicated against them, and Allah commanded the earth to obey him. Musa said to the earth: 'Seize them.' It seized them up to their ankles, and they began saying: 'O Musa, O Musa.' Then he said to the earth: 'Seize them.' It seized them up to their knees, and they began saying: 'O Musa, O Musa.' Then he said to the earth: 'Seize them.' It seized them up to their necks, and they began saying: 'O Musa, O Musa.' Then he said to the earth: 'Seize them.' It seized them and swallowed them. Allah then revealed to Musa: 'O Musa, My servants asked you and pleaded with you, but you did not answer them. By My might, if they had called upon Me, I would have answered them.' Ibn 'Abbas said: That is the statement of Allah, may He be glorified and exalted: {So We caused the earth to swallow him and his home} [al-Qasas 81]. He was swallowed down to the lowest earth."],[3524,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about the words of Allah, Exalted is He, {And you commit in your assemblies the evil deed} [Al-Ankabut 29]. He said: \"They used to pelt the people on the road with pebbles and mock them. That is the evil deed they used to commit.\" Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not record it."],[3525,"About the words of Allah, Exalted is He, {And the remembrance of Allah is greater} [Al-Ankabut 45]. I said, \"The remembrance of Allah is by glorification, tahlil, and takbir.\" He said: \"No; the remembrance of Allah is greater than your remembering Him.\" Sahih according to the condition of the two shaykhs, but they did not record it. Sahih al-isnad, and they did not record it."],[3526,"I heard Abu al-Darda' say: \"A people will come who recite {Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated} [Al-Rum 2], but it is only 'have been defeated' (ghulibat).\" Sahih al-isnad, and they did not record it."],[3527,"The Muslims used to love that the Romans prevail over Persia because they were People of the Book, while the polytheists used to love that Persia prevail over the Romans because they were people of idols. The Muslims mentioned that to Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr mentioned it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Indeed, they will soon be defeated.\" Abu Bakr mentioned that to them, and they said, \"Set a term between us and you. If they prevail, you will have such and such, and if we prevail, we will have such and such.\" So he set a term of five years, but they did not prevail. Abu Bakr mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Why did you not make it—I think he said—less than ten?\" He said, \"Then the Romans prevailed after that. That is His saying, Exalted is He: {Alif Lam Mim. The Romans have been defeated in the nearest land, and they, after their defeat, will prevail} [Al-Rum 2]. He said: The Romans were defeated, then they prevailed afterwards. To Allah belongs the command before and after. And on that day the believers will rejoice in Allah's victory.\""],[3528,"Yes. He recited {So glorify Allah when you reach the evening} [Al-Rum 17]. He said: \"The Maghrib prayer. {And when you rise in the morning} [Al-Rum 17]: the Fajr prayer. {And in the afternoon} [Maryam 11]: the Asr prayer. {And when you reach the noon} [Al-Rum 18]: the Zuhr prayer.\" And he recited {And after the Isha prayer, there are three times of privacy for you} [Al-Nur 58]."],[3529,"{And of the people is he who buys idle talk to mislead from the way of Allah} [Luqman 6]. He said: \"By Allah, it is singing.\""],[3530,"Luqman said to his son while advising him: \"O my son, beware of begging, for it is a fear by night and a humiliation by day.\""],[3531,"From Nubayh al-Anazi, from Jabir b. Abdullah, and he recited the words of Luqman to his son: {And be moderate in your pace and lower your voice} [Luqman 19]. He said: \"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out, they walked in front of him and left his back for the angels.\""],[3532,"The Prophet ﷺ would not sleep until he recited 'Alif Lam Mim. The revelation of the Book' (Al-Sajdah) and 'Blessed is He in whose hand is the dominion' (Al-Mulk). Abu al-Zubayr said: \"Safwan or Abu Safwan narrated it to me.\""],[3533,"\"Of the six days in which Allah created the heavens and the earth, then He established Himself above them.\""],[3534,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Batha' when a cloud passed by. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you know what this is?\" We said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"The cloud.\" We said, \"The cloud.\" He said: \"And the rain-cloud.\" We said, \"And the rain-cloud.\" He said: \"And the cloud-layer.\" Then he fell silent. Then he said: \"Do you know how much is between the heaven and the earth?\" We said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Between them is a distance of five hundred years' journey, and from each heaven to the next is a distance of five hundred years' journey, and the thickness of each heaven is five hundred years' journey. Above the seventh heaven is a sea between its top and bottom like what is between the heaven and the earth, and Allah is above that, and nothing of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him.\""],[3535,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and the heat had become intense, the people dispersed until I looked and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the closest of them to me. He said: I approached him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise and distance me from the Fire.\" He said: \"You have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for whom Allah makes it easy: worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, establish the prescribed prayers, give the obligatory zakat, and fast Ramadan.\" He said: \"And if you wish, I will tell you of the gates of Paradise.\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a man's standing in the depth of the night seeking the Face of Allah.\" He said: Then he recited this verse: {Their sides forsake their beds, calling upon their Lord in fear and hope, and from what We have provided them they spend} [Al-Sajdah 16]. He said: \"And if you wish, I will tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and its highest peak.\" He said: I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"As for the head of the matter, it is Islam; as for its pillar, it is prayer; and as for its highest peak, it is jihad in the way of Allah. And if you wish, I will tell you of the key to all of that.\" Then he fell silent. Then two riders appeared heading toward us, and I feared that they would distract him from my need. He said: I said, \"What is it, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"He pointed with his finger to his mouth.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will we be held accountable for what we say with our tongues?\" He said: \"May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Jabal! Does anything cast people on their faces into Hell except the harvests of their tongues?\" This is the wording of Jarir's hadith, and Abu Ishaq al-Fazari did not mention al-Hakam b. Utaybah in his hadith."],[3536,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was describing Paradise until he finished, then he said: \"In it there is what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined.\" Then he recited: {Their sides forsake their beds} [Al-Sajdah 16] to the end of the verse. Abu Sakhr said: I mentioned it to al-Qurazi, and he said: \"They concealed for Allah a deed, and He concealed for them a reward. They came to Allah, and those eyes were delighted.\""],[3537,"It is written in the Torah: Allah has prepared for those whose sides forsake their beds what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no human heart has imagined; no sent prophet knows it, nor any angel brought near. He said: We recite it: {No soul knows what is hidden for them of comfort for their eyes as reward for what they used to do} [Quran 32:17]."],[3538,"From 'Abd Allah regarding {And We will surely let them taste the nearer punishment before the greater punishment} [Quran 32:21], he said: \"The Day of Badr.\""],[3539,"\"No servant has been granted anything better or more expansive than patience.\""],[3540,"\"The Day of Badr: victory was granted to the Prophet ﷺ, but the faith of those who disbelieved did not benefit them after death.\""],[3541,"Surah Al-Ahzab used to equal Surah Al-Baqarah in length, and it contained: {The old man and the old woman, if they commit adultery, stone them absolutely}.[1]"],[3542,"He said: I said to Ibn 'Abbas about the saying of Allah ﷻ {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his interior} [Quran 33:4]: What is meant by that? He said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ stood up and had a thought. The hypocrites who prayed with him said: Do you not see that he has two hearts, one heart with them and one heart with you? So Allah ﷻ revealed {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his interior} [Quran 33:4]."],[3543,"\"He used to recite this verse: The Prophet is closer to the believers than their own selves, and he is a father to them, and his wives are their mothers.\""],[3544,"While 'A'isha bint Talha was saying to her mother Umm Kulthum bint Abi Bakr: My father is better than your father, 'A'isha the Mother of the Believers said: Shall I not judge between you? Abu Bakr entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"O Abu Bakr, you are the freed one of Allah from the Fire.\" I said: From that day he was named 'Atiq (freed one). And Talha entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"You, O Talha, are among those who have fulfilled their vow.\" The chain is authentic, but they [Bukhari and Muslim] did not record it; rather Ishaq b. Yahya b. Talha is abandoned, as Ahmad said."],[3545,"She said in my house that this verse was revealed: \"Indeed, Allah intends to keep away the impurity from you, O people of the household\" [Surah Al-Ahzab 33]. She said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husain, and said, \"O Allah, these are the people of my household.\" Umm Salamah said, \"O Messenger of Allah, am I not one of the people of the household?\" He replied, \"You are of my family, but the people of my household have more right to be considered as such.\""],[3546,"I came looking for Ali but did not find him. Fatimah said he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to call him, so I sat down. Then Ali came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they entered, and I entered with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Hasan and Husayn and seated each of them on his thigh. He brought Fatimah closer to him and her husband, then wrapped them with his cloak while I was present and said, \"Indeed, Allah desires to remove impurity from you, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.\" [Surah Al-Ahzab, 33:33] O Allah, these are the members of my household."],[3547,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, men are mentioned but women are not mentioned. So Allah ﷻ revealed {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women, the believing men and believing women} [Quran 33:35] to the end of the verse, and revealed {Indeed, I do not allow to be lost the work of any worker among you, male or female} [Quran 3:195]."],[3548,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When a man wakes up his wife at night, they should both pray two Rak'ahs, for they will be recorded among those who remember Allah frequently; and likewise, the same applies to women.\" This Hadith is not attributed to Abu Nuaim, and the Prophet ﷺ did not mention it in the chain of narrators. However, it is narrated by 'Isa bin Ja'far, who is trustworthy."],[3549,"I was in the mosque when Al-'Abbas and 'Ali came to me and said: O Usama, seek permission for us to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ and sought permission for them, saying: Al-'Abbas and 'Ali are seeking permission. He said: \"Do you know what they need?\" I said: No, by Allah, I do not know. He said: \"But I know. Permit them.\" They entered upon him and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have come to ask you which of your family is most beloved to you. He said: \"The most beloved of my family to me is Fatima bint Muhammad.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, we are not asking you about Fatima. He said: \"Then Usama b. Zayd, upon whom Allah has bestowed favor and upon whom I have bestowed favor.\"[1]"],[3550,"Zayd b. Haritha came to complain to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Zaynab bint Jahsh. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Keep your wife.\" Then was revealed {And you concealed within yourself what Allah would disclose} [Quran 33:37]. On the condition of Bukhari and Muslim."],[3551,"When the Prophet ﷺ married Zaynab, Umm Sulaym sent a dish of hays (a mixture of dates, butter, and dried curd) in a stone bowl. Anas said: The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Go and invite whomever you meet of the Muslims.\" I went and did not see anyone but I invited him. He said: The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand in the food and supplicated over it, saying: \"As Allah wills.\" He said: They began to eat and leave, but a group remained in the house. The Prophet ﷺ felt shy before them, and they prolonged the conversation. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left and left them in the house. Then Allah revealed {O you who believe, do not enter the houses of the Prophet unless you are given permission for a meal, without awaiting its time} [Quran 33:53], meaning without waiting, until {That is purer for your hearts and their hearts} [Quran 33:53]."],[3552,"A man came to Abu Umamah and said: O Abu Umamah, I saw in my dream that the angels pray for you whenever you enter, whenever you leave, whenever you stand, and whenever you sit. Abu Umamah said: O Allah, forgive me. Leave us be, for if you wished, the angels would pray for you. Then he recited: {O you who believe, remember Allah with much remembrance and glorify Him morning and evening. He it is who sends blessings upon you, and His angels, to bring you out from darkness into light, and He is ever merciful to the believers}."],[3553,"\"I am the servant of Allah and the seal of the prophets, and my father was embedded in his clay, and I will inform you about that. I am the supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of Isa, and the vision of my mother Aminah which she saw.\" And likewise the mothers of the prophets see visions, and the mother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw when she gave birth to him a light that illuminated for her the palaces of Sham. Then he recited: {O Prophet, indeed We have sent you as a witness, a bearer of glad tidings, and a warner, and one who invites to Allah by His permission, and an illuminating lamp}."],[3554,"He recited the saying of Allah Almighty: {O you who believe, when you marry believing women and then divorce them before you have touched them} [Al-Ahzab 49], and he said: \"There is no divorce until there is marriage.\""],[3555,"\"There is no divorce except after marriage.\""],[3556,"\"There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership.\""],[3557,"\"There is no divorce for one who does not possess.\""],[3558,"\"There is no divorce except after marriage, and no emancipation except after ownership.\""],[3559,"I am but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told me, Jabir b. Abdullah al-Ansari, that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no divorce for one who does not possess, and no emancipation for one who does not possess.\""],[3560,"\"There is no divorce before marriage.\""],[3561,"The Prophet ﷺ proposed to me, and I excused myself to him, and he excused me. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {O Prophet, indeed We have made lawful to you your wives} [Al-Ahzab 50] up to His saying: {those who emigrated with you} [Al-Ahzab 50]. She said: So I was not lawful for him because I had not emigrated with him; I was among the freed ones."],[3562,"He recited the saying of Allah Almighty: {Indeed, Allah and His angels send blessings upon the Prophet. O you who believe, send blessings upon him and greet him with peace} [Al-Ahzab 56]. Thabit said: Sulayman, the freed slave of al-Hasan b. Ali, came to us and narrated to us from Abdullah b. Abi Talhah al-Ansari, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came one day and glad tidings were visible in his face. We said: O Messenger of Allah, we see glad tidings in your face. He said: \"Indeed, the angel came to me and said: O Muhammad, your Lord says: Are you not pleased that no one from your Ummah sends blessings upon you except that I send ten blessings upon him, and no one from your Ummah greets you with peace except that I return it to him tenfold?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[3563,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"Verily, Allah has angels who travel about the earth, informing me about the greetings of my Ummah.\" This narration has an authentic chain of transmission, but it has not been narrated by anyone except Al-Thawri. It is well-known from him. As for the narration from Al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn As-Sa'ib, we have not written it except with this chain of transmission."],[3564,"\"Increase your prayers upon me on Friday, for there is no one who sends prayers upon me on Friday except that his prayer is presented to me.\""],[3565,"\"When a third of the night had passed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said: 'O you people! Remember Allah! Remember Allah! The Rajifah is coming, followed by the Radifah, death and what it brings is coming, death and what it brings is coming!'\" Ubayy said: \"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed I say very much Salat for you. How much of my Salat should I make for you?' He said: 'As you wish.'\" [He said:] \"I said: 'A fourth?' He said: 'As you wish. But if you add more it would be better for you.' I said: 'Then half?' He said: 'As you wish. And if you add more it would be better [for you].'\" [He said:] \"I said: 'Then two-thirds? 'He said: 'As you wish, but if you add more it would be better for you.' I said: 'Should I make all of my Salat for you?' He said: 'Then your problems would be solved and your sins would be forgiven.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2457)"],[3566,"His people had a well which dried up one day, so he went out to wash himself and placed his clothes on a rock. The rock then took hold of his clothes and Moses came out following it, naked, until it reached the gathering of the Children of Israel. They saw him, but no one rushed to cover him. That is what Allah, the Exalted, said: \"So Allah cleared him of what they said, and he was honored in the sight of Allah.\" [Qur'an 33:69]"],[3567,"{Indeed, We offered the Trust to the heavens and the earth and the mountains, and they declined to bear it and feared it} He said: It was said to Adam, \"Will you take it with all that it entails? If you obey, I will forgive, and if you disobey, I will warn you?\" He said, \"I accept.\" He said: It was only as long as between the afternoon prayer and sunset before he committed the sin."],[3568,"From him, Al-Dhahabi in summarizing."],[3569,"From Anas regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And We made iron soft for him, [saying], \"Make full coats of mail\"} [Saba' 11]. Anas said: Luqman was with Dawud while he was weaving a coat of mail, and he began twisting it with his hand like this. Luqman began to wonder and wanted to ask him, but his wisdom prevented him from asking. When he finished it, he poured it over himself and said, \"What an excellent coat of mail for war this is!\" Luqman said, \"Silence is part of wisdom, and few practice it. I wanted to ask you, but I remained silent until you sufficed me.\" \"Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it.\" According to the conditions of Muslim."],[3570,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And determine precisely in the weaving} [Saba' 11]. He said: \"Do not make the nails thin and the links wide, lest it become loose, and do not make the nails thick and the links narrow, lest it break; make it in due proportion.\" This is a rare expression in exegesis, and 'Abd al-Wahhab is among those whom they did not include. 'Abd al-Wahhab: they did not include him due to his weakness."],[3571,"Sulayman b. Dawud, upon them be peace, died while standing in prayer, and the devils did not know of it until a termite ate his staff and he fell. Whenever a tree grew, he would ask it, \"For what ailment are you?\" He said: It would inform him, as Allah, Exalted is He, told: {And to Sulayman [We subjected] the wind—its morning course was a month and its evening course was a month, and We made flow for him a spring of molten copper} [Saba' 12]—all the verses. When the carob tree grew, he asked it, \"For what purpose have you grown?\" It said, \"For the ruin of this mosque.\" He said, \"The ruin of this mosque will only occur at my death,\" so he stood up to pray."],[3572,"I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ about Saba': \"What is it—a man, a woman, or a land?\" He said: \"He was a man who had ten children: six of his descendants were in Yemen and four in Syria. As for the Yemenis: Madhhij, Kindah, al-Azd, al-Ash'ariyyun, Anmar, and Himyar—all of them are good. As for the Syrians: Lakhm, Judham, 'Amilah, and Ghassan.\""],[3573,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about Saba', saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, is Saba' a man, a mountain, or a valley?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, he was a man who had ten children. Four went to Syria and six to Yemen. Those who went to Syria were Lakhm, Judham, 'Amilah, and Ghassan. Those who went to Yemen were Himyar, Madhhij, al-Azd, Kindah, al-Ash'ariyyun, and al-Anmar, from whom are Bajilah.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[3574,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And We have not sent you except comprehensively to all people as a bringer of good tidings and a warner} [Saba' 28]. He said: Al-A'mash narrated to us, from Mujahid, from 'Ubayd b. 'Umayr, from Abu Dharr, who said: I sought the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night and found him standing in prayer. He prolonged the prayer, then said: \"I was given five things tonight that no prophet before me was given: I was sent to the red and the black.\" Mujahid said: That is, humans and jinn. \"And I was aided with terror, so the enemy is struck with terror even at a month's distance. And the earth was made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification. And spoils of war were made lawful for me, but they were not lawful for anyone before me. And it was said to me, 'Ask and you shall be given,' so I reserved it as intercession for my community. It will reach whoever does not associate anything with Allah.\""],[3575,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And how can they have attainment from a distant place} [Saba' 52]. He said: \"They ask for return, but it is not the time for returning.\""],[3576,"When we relate a report to you, we bring you confirmation of it in the Book of Allah: Indeed, when a servant says, “Glory be to Allah, and praise be to Allah, and there is no deity but Allah, and Allah is the Greatest, and blessed is Allah,” an angel takes hold of them, enfolds them beneath his wing, and ascends with them. He does not pass by any gathering of angels with them except that they seek forgiveness for the one who said them, until he brings them before the Face of the Most Merciful. Then ʿAbdullāh recited: “To Him ascends the good word, and the righteous deed raises it.” (Fāṭir 10)"],[3577,"I set out with my father toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. My father greeted him, and we sat for a while and conversed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to my father, \"Is this your son?\" He said, \"Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.\" He said, \"Truly?\" He said, \"I bear witness to it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled, laughing at the confirmed resemblance between me and my father and at my father's oath about that. He said: Then he said, \"Indeed, this son of yours will not commit a crime against you, nor will you commit a crime against him.\" He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {That no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another} [al-Najm 38] up to His saying, Exalted is He: {This is a warner from the warners of old} [al-Najm 56]. \"Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it.\" Sahih."],[3578,"When \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High\" was revealed, he said: \"All of it is in the scriptures of Ibrahim.\" When \"By the star when it descends\" was revealed and he reached {And Ibrahim, who fulfilled} [al-Najm 37], he said: And in {That no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another} [al-Najm 38] up to His saying, Exalted is He: {This is a warner from the warners of old} [al-Najm 56]."],[3579,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say regarding His statement, Exalted and Majestic is He, \"So among them is one who wrongs himself, and among them is one who is balanced, and among them is one who outstrips in [good] deeds.\" [Quran 35:32] He said, \"The one who outstrips and the one who is balanced will enter Paradise without being held to account, and the one who wrongs himself will be held to a slight account and then enter Paradise.\" Narrations differ from Al-A'mash in the chain of this hadith, it is narrated from Ath-Thawri from Al-A'mash from Abu Thabit from Abu Ad-Darda, and it is also said from Shu'bah from Al-A'mash from a man from Ta'if from Abu Ad-Darda, and it is also said from Ath-Thawri likewise from Al-A'mash. He said, Abu Thabit mentioned from Abu Ad-Darda, \"And when the narrations become many in a hadith, it appears that the hadith has a basis.\""],[3580,"I said to 'A'ishah, \"O Mother of the Believers, what do you think of the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {Then We caused to inherit the Book those whom We have chosen of Our servants; and among them is he who wrongs himself, and among them is he who is moderate, and among them is he who is foremost in good deeds by permission of Allah. That is the great bounty} [Fatir 32]?\" 'A'ishah said: \"As for the foremost, they are those who passed away during the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he bore witness to their life and provision. As for the moderate, they are those who followed their traces and acted according to their deeds until they joined them. As for the one who wrongs himself, he is like me and like you and whoever followed us, and all are in Paradise.\" Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it. Al-Salt: al-Nasa'i said he is not trustworthy, and Ahmad said he is not strong."],[3581,"The Prophet ﷺ recited the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {Gardens of perpetual residence which they will enter. They will be adorned therein with bracelets of gold} [Fatir 33], then said: \"Indeed, upon them will be crowns; the least pearl among them would illuminate what is between the east and the west.\""],[3582,"“Sorrow is the Fire.”"],[3583,"\"Sixty years\" with an authentic chain of narration, and it has not been classified as authentic."],[3584,"“When a man from my community reaches sixty years of age, Allah has excused him regarding his lifespan.”"],[3585,"“The lifespans of my community are between sixty and seventy, and the fewest of them are those who exceed that.”"],[3586,"“Allah has indeed excused a servant whom He has given a life of sixty or seventy years. Allah has indeed excused him regarding his lifespan.”"],[3587,"“Allah has indeed excused a servant whom He has kept alive until he reached sixty or seventy. Allah has indeed excused him.”"],[3588,"“Whoever from my community reaches seventy years of age, Allah has excused him regarding his lifespan.”"],[3589,"“The dung beetle was nearly punished in its hole because of the sin of the son of Adam.” Sound chain of narration, authentic."],[3590,"“Whoever finds hardness in his heart should write ‘Yā Sīn. By the Qur’an’ in a bowl with saffron and then drink it.”"],[3591,"The Banū Salamah were in one part of Madinah and wanted to move near the mosque. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Indeed, it is We who bring the dead to life and record what they have put forth and what they left behind} [Yā Sīn: 12]. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called them and said: “Indeed your footprints are being recorded.” Then he recited the verse to them, and they stayed."],[3592,"The man of Yā Sīn: “O my people, follow the messengers.” He said: They strangled him so that he would die, so he turned to the prophets and said: {Indeed, I have believed in your Lord, so listen to me} [Yā Sīn: 25], that is, “bear witness for me.”"],[3593,"Al-ʿĀṣ b. Wā’il came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a decayed bone and crushed it, then said: “O Muhammad, will Allah resurrect this after it has crumbled to dust?” He said: “Yes, Allah will resurrect this. He will cause you to die, then give you life, then enter you into the Fire of Hell.” He said: Then the verses were revealed: {Does man not see that We created him from a drop of fluid, then behold, he is an open adversary} [Yā Sīn: 77] until the end of the surah."],[3594,"\"The Angels\""],[3595,"ʿAbdullāh recited: {Rather, you wonder, and they mock} [al-Ṣāffāt: 12]. Shurayḥ said: “Indeed, Allah does not wonder at anything; only those who do not know wonder.” Al-Aʿmash said: So I mentioned that to Ibrāhīm, and he said: “Indeed Shurayḥ was pleased with his own opinion. ʿAbdullāh was more knowledgeable than Shurayḥ, and ʿAbdullāh used to recite it as {Rather, you wonder} [al-Ṣāffāt: 12].”"],[3596,"\"Their example is like those who are similar to them.\""],[3597,"There is no caller who calls a man to something except that he will be made to stand with him on the Day of Resurrection, cleaving to him and driven with him. Then he recited this verse: {And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned}."],[3598,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever calls his Muslim brother to something—even if a man calls another man—he will be made to stand with him on the Day of Resurrection, cleaving to him and driven with him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {And stop them; indeed, they are to be questioned} [Al-Ṣāffāt: 24]."],[3599,"From the followers of Noah to Ibrahim, following his method and his Sunnah, he reached the age of maturity until his actions were comparable to the actions of Ibrahim. When they submitted to what they were commanded, Allah commanded Ibrahim to present his forehead and he placed his face towards the ground. Ibrahim said, \"Do not slaughter me while you are looking at me. Perhaps you will have mercy on me, so do not prepare yourself to slaughter me. Tie my hands to my neck and then place my face on the ground.\" When he put his hand to slaughter him, the blade did not cut until the call came, \"O Ibrahim, you have indeed fulfilled the vision.\" (Surah As-Saffat, 105) So he held his hand and raised his words, \"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice.\" (Surah As-Saffat,107) With a great ram that was accepted. Ibn 'Abbas claimed that the sacrificed one was Ismael."],[3600,"The dreams of the prophets are revelation."],[3601,"The Prophet ﷺ would sleep with his eyes while his heart would not sleep."],[3602,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Ṣād while he was on the pulpit. When he reached the prostration, he descended and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him. On another day, he recited it, and when he reached the prostration, the people prepared to prostrate. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is the repentance of a prophet, but I saw you preparing to prostrate.\" So he descended and prostrated, and the people prostrated with him."],[3603,"I saw in a dream, as a sleeper sees, as if I began reciting Sūrat Ṣād until I reached the prostration, and the inkwell, the pen, and everything around it prostrated. I informed the Prophet ﷺ of that, and he prostrated in it. [Satisfying the condition of Muslim]"],[3604,"Abū Ṭālib fell ill, so the Quraysh came, and the Prophet ﷺ came. At the head of Abū Ṭālib there was a place for one man to sit, so Abū Jahl stood up to prevent him from that. They complained about him to Abū Ṭālib, who said: \"O son of my brother, what do you want from your people?\" He said: \"O uncle, I only want from them one word by which the Arabs will be humbled before them and by which the tribute of the non-Arabs will be brought to them.\" He said: \"One word?\" He said: \"One word.\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"Lā ilāha illā Allāh.\" They said: \"Has he made the gods one god? Indeed, this is a strange thing.\" And it was revealed concerning them: {Ṣād, by the Qur’ān full of remembrance} [Ṣād: 1] until it reached {This is nothing but an invention} [Ṣād: 7]."],[3605,"{Ṣād, by the Qur’ān full of remembrance} [Ṣād: 1] was revealed concerning them and their gathering—that is, the gathering of Abū Ṭālib and Abū Jahl and the assembly of the Quraysh to them when they disputed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3606,"The translation into English for the given Arabic sentence is: \"It is neither delusion nor escape, correct in its chain of narration and has not been mentioned in any authentic collection.\""],[3607,"Nothing befell Dāwūd after the decree except because of self-admiration he felt within himself. That was because he said: \"O Lord, there is no hour of night or day except that a worshipper from the family of Dāwūd worships You, praying to You, glorifying You, or magnifying You,\" and he mentioned other things. Allah disliked that and said: \"O Dāwūd, that was only through Me. Were it not for My help, you would not have had strength for it. By My majesty, I will leave you to yourself one day.\" He said: \"O Lord, then inform me of it.\" So the trial befell him on that day."],[3608,"Dāwūd ﷺ said: \"O Lord, I ask You for Your love and the love of those who love You, and for the deed that brings me to Your love. O Lord, make Your love dearer to me than myself, my family, and cold water.\" And when the Prophet ﷺ mentioned Dāwūd and spoke of him, he said: \"He was the most devout of human beings.\""],[3609,"Dāwūd ﷺ died suddenly on Saturday, and he used to observe the Sabbath. Birds gathered over him and shaded him. [Satisfying the condition of Al-Bukhārī and Muslim]"],[3610,"He is the devil who used to rule from his throne for forty days, and Solomon had a servant called \"Jaradah.\" There was a dispute between some of her people and his people, so he judged between them with justice, except that he wished for the truth to be in favor of her people. Allah then revealed to him that he would be afflicted with a test. He did not know whether it would come to him from the sky or from the earth."],[3611,"Solomon son of David (peace be upon them both) asked Allah for three things, and He gave him two, and I hope He has given him the third. He asked Him for judgment that coincides with His judgment, and He gave him that. He asked Him for a kingdom that no one after him should have, and He gave him that. He asked Him that any man who leaves his house intending only to pray in this mosque—meaning the House of the Sanctuary—would depart from his sins as on the day his mother gave birth to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"We hope that Allah has given him that.\""],[3612,"I heard 'A'isha saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to fast until we said, 'He does not intend to break his fast,' and he would break his fast until we said, 'He does not intend to fast.' And he used to recite every night Surah Bani Isra'il and Surah Az-Zumar. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[3613,"When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: {Indeed, you are to die, and indeed, they are to die. Then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord, will dispute} [Az-Zumar: 31], I said, 'Will what was between us in this world, along with the specific sins, be repeated against us?' He said, 'Yes, it will surely be repeated against you until every rightful owner receives his due.' Al-Zubayr said: By Allah, the matter is indeed severe. [Authentic according to the conditions of Muslim]"],[3614,"When this verse was revealed, he mentioned the hadith but did not mention Al-Zubayr in its chain. [Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it]"],[3615,"We used to say: There is no repentance for one who is tested (by falling into sin), and Allah will not accept anything from him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, the verse was revealed about them: {Say, 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.'} [Az-Zumar: 53] and the verses after it. 'Umar said: So I wrote them down, then I sat on my camel, then I went around Madinah, then... The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed in Makkah waiting for Allah to permit him to migrate, and his companions among the emigrants. Abu Bakr stayed waiting for permission to be given to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that he could leave with him."],[3616,"Every inhabitant of the Fire will see his place in Paradise and will say, 'If only Allah had guided me,' and it will become a regret for him. And every inhabitant of Paradise will see his place in the Fire and will say, 'Had it not been that Allah guided me,' and it will become gratitude for him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {Lest a soul should say, 'Oh [how great is] my regret over what I neglected in regard to Allah'} [Az-Zumar: 56]."],[3617,"Ibn 'Abbas said to me: Do you know the vastness of Hell? I said: No. He said: Indeed, by Allah, you do not know that between the lobe of one of their ears and his shoulder is a journey of seventy years, valleys of pus and blood. I said to him: Rivers? He said: No, rather valleys. Then he said: Do you know the vastness of Hell? I said: No. He said: Indeed, by Allah, you do not know. 'A'isha told me that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the saying of Allah Almighty: {And the earth entirely will be [within] His grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be folded in His right hand} [Az-Zumar: 67]. I said: Where will the people be on that day, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'On the bridge of Hell.'"],[3618,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying, Exalted be He: {And the trumpet will be blown} [Az-Zumar: 68]. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'It is a horn into which it is blown.'"],[3619,"She used to say to the wives of the Prophet ﷺ: Does a woman not feel ashamed to offer herself? Then Allah revealed this verse about the wives of the Prophet ﷺ: {You may defer [the turn of] whom you will of them, and you may receive to yourself whom you will} [Al-Ahzab: 51]. 'A'isha said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'I see your Lord hastens to fulfill your desire.'"],[3620,"In the words of Allah ﷻ {It is not lawful for you to marry other women after this, nor to replace them} [Al-Ahzab 52], Ibn Jurayj narrated to me from Ata, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Aisha, who said, \"The Prophet ﷺ did not pass away until Allah made it lawful for him to marry.\""],[3621,"The Hawamim are the silk brocade of the Quran. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[3622,"He passed by Abu al-Darda' while he was building a mosque and said: What is this? He said: 'This is for the family of Ha-Meem.'"],[3623,"In His statement, Glory be to Him, \"Our Lord, You caused us to die twice and You gave us life twice\" [Surah Al-Ghafir: 11], He said, \"It is similar to that which is in Surah Al-Baqarah, 'You were lifeless, then We gave you life; then We caused you to die; then We revived you' [Surah Al-Baqarah: 28].\""],[3624,"A caller will call out before the Hour: O people, the Hour has come to you. The living and the dead will hear it. And Allah will descend to the lowest heaven and call out: To whom belongs the dominion today? To Allah, the One, the Prevailing."],[3625,"From a man among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ who heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding retribution, but I did not hear it. So I bought a camel, loaded my saddle onto it, then traveled for a month until I reached Egypt. I went to 'Abd Allah b. Unays and said to the doorkeeper: Tell him Jabir is at the door. He said: Ibn 'Abd Allah? I said: Yes. He went to him and informed him. He stood up, stepping on his garment, until he came out to me. He embraced me and I embraced him. I said to him: A hadith reached me from you that you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding retribution, which I did not hear. I feared that I might die or you might die before I heard it. 'Abd Allah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah will gather the servants—or he said the people—naked, uncircumcised, and buhman. He said: We said: What is buhman? He said: They will have nothing with them. Then He will call them with a voice that the far one hears as the near one hears: I am the King, I am the Judge. It is not fitting for anyone from the people of Paradise to enter Paradise, and it is not fitting for anyone from the people of the Fire to enter the Fire, while there is an injustice owed by him, until I exact retribution for it from him, even a slap. He said: We said: How is that, when we will come to Allah naked, uncircumcised, and buhman? He said: 'By good deeds and bad deeds.' He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {This Day every soul will be recompensed for what it earned. No injustice today} [Ghafir: 17]. [Sahih chain, but they did not include it] Sahih."],[3626,"\"There is no god but Allah\"—so let him say after it \"Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,\" meaning His saying ﷻ {So call upon Him, being sincere to Him in religion. Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds} [Ghafir: 65]."],[3627,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If a bullet of this [metal]—the size of this\"—and he pointed to something like a skull—\"were sent from the heaven to the earth, a distance of five hundred years' journey, it would reach the earth before nightfall.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {When the shackles are around their necks and the chains; they will be dragged in the boiling water} [Ghafir: 72]—the verses."],[3628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited {An Arabic Qur'an for a people who know} [Fussilat: 3], then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Isma'il was inspired with this tongue by direct inspiration.\""],[3629,"On the authority of his father {in a clear Arabic tongue} [Al-Shu'ara': 195] he said: \"In the tongue of Jurhum.\""],[3630,"The Prophet ﷺ heard a man recite and make a grammatical mistake, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Guide your brother.\" Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[3631,"Parse the Qur'an grammatically and seek out its rare expressions."],[3632,"\"They will come on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles on their mouths, and the first part of a human being to speak will be his thigh and his palm.\""],[3633,"\"You will be gathered here\"—and he gestured with his hand toward Syria—\"on foot and riding, and upon your faces, and you will be presented before Allah with muzzles on your mouths. The first part of any of you to speak will be his thigh.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {And you were not concealing yourselves lest your hearing, your eyes, or your skins testify against you}\""],[3634,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {Our Lord, show us those who led us astray from among the jinn and humans} [Fussilat: 29] he said: \"The son of Adam who killed his brother, and Iblis.\""],[3635,"What do you say about the saying of Allah ﷻ {Indeed, those who say, 'Our Lord is Allah' and then remain steadfast} [Fussilat: 30] and His saying, exalted is He, {Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing} [Al-An'am: 82]? They said: \"Those who say, 'Our Lord is Allah' and then remain steadfast and do not turn away.\" And His saying, \"and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing\" means with sin. Then Abu Bakr said: \"You have interpreted it in a way other than its correct interpretation. 'Then remain steadfast' means they did not turn to any deity other than Him, and 'do not mix their faith with wrongdoing' means with shirk.\""],[3636,"Two men insulted each other near the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became intensely angry. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"I know a word which, if he said it, would cause his anger to go away: 'I seek refuge in Allah from the accursed Satan.'\" The man said: \"Do you consider me mad?\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {And if a provocation from Satan should provoke you, then seek refuge in Allah. Indeed, He is the Hearing, the Knowing} [Fussilat: 36]."],[3637,"He \"used to prostrate at the last two verses of Ha-Mim Al-Sajdah, and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Mas'ud, used to prostrate at the first of them.\""],[3638,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, \"Indeed those who disbelieve in the Reminder when it comes to them—and indeed it is a mighty Book. Falsehood cannot come to it from before it or from behind it; a revelation from One Wise and Praiseworthy.\" [Fussilat 42] So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will never return to Allah with anything more beloved to Him than something that came from Him,\" meaning the Qur'an."],[3639,"I was a neighbor of al-Khabbab b. al-Aratt. We once left the mosque and he took my hand and said, \"O so-and-so, draw near to Allah as much as you are able, for you will never draw near to Him with anything more beloved to Him than His speech.\""],[3640,"Regarding His ﷻ saying, \"The heavens almost break apart from above them,\" he said, \"From the weight.\""],[3641,"\"Between Adam and Noah there were ten generations, all of them upon a law of truth. When they differed, Allah sent the prophets and messengers, and sent down His Book, and they became one community.\""],[3642,"\"People, after Adam, fell into polytheism, they took these idols and worshipped other than Allah. So the angels made supplication against them and said, 'Our Lord, You created Your servants and You perfected their creation and You provided for them and You provided them with good provisions. They disobeyed You and worshipped other than You, O Allah. O Allah, they make supplication against them.' So the Lord, the Exalted and Majestic, said to them, 'Indeed, they are in error, so they shall not be excused.' He said, 'Choose two from among you who will descend to the earth and I will order them and they will be forbidden. So they chose Harut and Marut. He said, and the narration mentions their trial and it says, 'So when they drank alcohol and became intoxicated and they fell into unlawful sexual intercourse and they killed a soul, the commotion increased between them and the angels. So they looked at what they were doing and in response to that, (the verse) was revealed, 'And the angels exalt ( Allah) with praise of their Lord and ask forgiveness for those on earth' (Surah Ash-Shura, 42:5). He said, 'So afterward the angels made excuses for the people of the earth and supplicated for them.'"],[3643,"That he was standing at Arafat and looked at the sun when it had declined like a shield toward setting, and he wept and his weeping intensified, and he recited the saying of Allah ﷻ: \"Allah is the One who sent down the Book in truth and the Balance. And what can make you know? Perhaps the Hour is near\" [al-Shura 17] up to \"the Strong, the Mighty\" [Hud 66]. His servant said to him, \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I have stood with you many times and you did not do this.\" He said, \"I remembered the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing in this place of mine, and he said, 'O people, nothing remains of this world of yours compared to what has passed except as what remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed of it.'\""],[3644,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “Whoever desires the harvest of the Hereafter, We will increase for him his harvest; and whoever desires the harvest of this world, We will give him of it, but he will have no share in the Hereafter” [Ash-Shura 20]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah, the Exalted, says: “Son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship; I will fill your chest with richness and I will alleviate your poverty. But if you do not do so, I will fill your chest with preoccupation and I will not alleviate your poverty.”"],[3645,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whosoever makes all [his] concerns into one concern (meaning, the concern of the Hereafter), Allah will relieve him of [all] concerns of his world. And whosoever is indulged [only] in concerns [of this world], Allah will not care in which of the valleys of this world he dies.\"[1]"],[3646,"\"I do not ask you for any reward for the clear proofs and guidance I have brought you, except that you love Allah and draw near to Him through obedience to Him.\""],[3647,"About that, Ibn Abbas wrote: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"was of the middle house of Quraysh; there was no clan of theirs except that it had given birth to him.\" So Allah ﷻ said, \"Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it\" [al-An'am 90] up to what I call you to, except that you love me because of my kinship with you and protect me through it. Hushaym said: And Husayn reported to me from Ikrimah from Ibn Abbas something similar to that."],[3648,"Mu'adh b. Jabal addressed us and said, \"You are the believers and you are the people of Paradise. By Allah, I hope that the majority of those you strike down among the Persians and the Romans will be in Paradise, for one of them does a good deed and someone says, 'You have done well, may Allah bless you. You have done well, may Allah have mercy on you.' And Allah says, 'And He responds to those who believe and do righteous deeds, and increases them from His bounty.'\""],[3649,"The sun never rises except that two angels are sent with it, and they make the people of the earth hear—except the two heavy kinds (jinn and humans)—\"O people, come to your Lord, for what is little and sufficient is better than what is abundant and distracting.\" And the sun never sets except that two angels are with it calling, \"O Allah, hasten a replacement for the one who spends, and hasten ruin for the one who withholds.\""],[3650,"There is no one in Kufa in the morning except that he is comfortable; the lowest of them in status drinks from the water of the Euphrates, sits in the shade, and eats wheat. This verse was only revealed concerning the people of the Suffah: \"If Allah were to extend provision to His servants, they would surely transgress in the land, but He sends down in measure whatever He wills\" [al-Shura 27]. That is because they said, \"If only we had,\" and they longed for the world."],[3651,"\"Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah is more just than to repeat his punishment upon His servant. And whoever commits a sin and Allah conceals it and forgives him, Allah is too generous to return to something He has forgiven.\""],[3652,"Some of his companions entered upon him after he had been afflicted in his body. One of them said to him, \"We grieve for you because of what has befallen you.\" He said, \"Do not grieve for what you see, for it only befell due to a sin, and what Allah forgives is more.\" Then Imran recited this verse: \"Whatever misfortune befalls you is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much\" [al-Shura 30] to the end of the verse."],[3653,"We were reviewing the masahif in the presence of 'Alqamah, and he recited this verse: \"Indeed in that are signs for those who are certain [in faith]\" and said: 'Abdullah said: Certainty is the whole of faith. And he recited this verse: \"Indeed in that are signs for every patient and grateful one\" [Ibrahim: 5]. He said: 'Abdullah said: \"Patience is half of faith.\""],[3654,"On the day of Uhud, sixty-four of the Ansar were killed, among them six including Hamzah, and they were mutilated. The Ansar said: If we ever inflict a day like this on them, we will certainly exceed them. Then on the day of the conquest of Makkah, Allah revealed: \"And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted. But if you endure patiently, verily, it is better for the patient.\""],[3655,"\"The straight path is Islam, and it is as wide as the distance between the heaven and the earth.\""],[3656,"On the authority of 'Abdullah regarding His saying, may He be exalted: \"And indeed, you guide to a straight path\" [Al-Shura: 52]. He said: \"The Book of Allah.\" According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3657,"I said to Ibn 'Abbas: \"And they made the angels, who are servants of the Most Merciful, females\" or \"servant of the Most Merciful\"? He said: \"Servants of the Most Merciful.\" I said: \"In my masahif it is 'servant of the Most Merciful'.\" He said: \"Erase it and write 'servants of the Most Merciful'.\""],[3658,"On the authority of 'Abdullah regarding: \"Do they distribute the mercy of your Lord? It is We who distribute among them\" [Al-Zukhruf: 32] - the verse. 'Abdullah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed Allah has distributed your characters among you just as He distributed your provisions among you. And indeed Allah gives the world to whom He loves and to whom He does not love, but He does not give the religion except to whom He loves. So whoever He gives the religion, He has loved him.\""],[3659,"On the authority of Qatadah regarding His saying, the Exalted: \"And whether We take you away [in death], verily We will exact retribution from them\" [Al-Zukhruf: 41]. Anas said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went away and the retribution remained, and Allah did not show His Prophet ﷺ anything in his nation that he disliked until he passed away. And there was no Prophet except that he saw punishment in his nation, except your Prophet ﷺ.\" The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[3660,"Some people from my companions will be taken to the left side, and I will say: 'My companions, my companions.' It will be said: 'They did not cease turning back on their heels after you.' I will say as the righteous servant 'Isa ibn Maryam said: 'And I was a witness over them as long as I was among them. But when You took me up, You were the Watcher over them.'\""],[3661,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"No people have gone astray after being guided except that they were given to argumentation.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, \"{They did not harm you except [for some] annoyance. But they have been disputing people}.\" [Surah Az-Zukhruf, 58]"],[3662,"\"The Departure of Jesus, the son of Mary\""],[3663,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding: \"And indeed, it is knowledge of the Hour\" [Al-Zukhruf: 61]: \"The stars are a security for the inhabitants of the heaven. When they go, there will come to them what they are promised. And I am a security for my companions as long as I am present. When I go, there will come to them what they are promised. And my household is a security for my nation. When my household goes, there will come to them what they are promised.\" The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not include it. I think it is fabricated."],[3664,"You are staying."],[3665,"\"Indeed you will see a man walking in the markets while his name has already fallen among the dead.\" Then he recited: \"Indeed, We sent it down in a blessed night. Indeed, We are ever warning. In it every wise matter is made distinct\" [Al-Dukhan: 4] - meaning the Night of Decree. In that night the matter of the world is made distinct until the like of it in the coming year. \"The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not include it.\" Sahih according to the condition of Muslim."],[3666,"\"The loss of a believer is mourned for forty mornings\" - Authentic chain of narration and it has not been excluded from the authentic collection."],[3667,"Jarir [Al-Bahr Al-Kamil] recited: \"The winds effaced the traces of their abodes, as if they had been on an appointed time.\" 'Ali said to me: \"How did you say, O brother of Banu Tamim?\" The man repeated the verse to him. 'Ali said: \"Why did you not say: 'How many gardens and springs did they leave behind, and crops and noble sites, and comforts wherein they used to delight? Thus it was. And We made another people inherit them' [Al-Dukhan: 26]. Then he said: 'O my brother, these people were inheritors, then they became inherited. Indeed they disbelieved in the blessings, so the calamities befell them.' Then he said: 'Beware of disbelieving in blessings, lest calamities befall you.'\" Abu Hatim said: I said to Muhammad b. Yazid b. Sinan: \"Your grandfather Sinan was very old and met 'Ali?\" He said: \"Yes, he witnessed the battles with him.\""],[3668,"She said: \"Tubba' was a righteous man. Do you not see that Allah, may He be exalted, condemned his people but did not condemn him?\""],[3669,"“I do not know whether Tubba‘ was accursed or not, and I do not know whether Dhu al-Qarnayn was a prophet or not, and I do not know whether the prescribed punishments are expiations for those who incur them or not.”"],[3670,"Ibn ʿAbbās was asked: “In how many days were the heavens and the earth created?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah created the first of days, Sunday, and the earth was created on Sunday and Monday. The mountains were created, the rivers were carved, fruits were planted in the earth, and the sustenance of every land was decreed on Tuesday and Wednesday. Then He turned to the heaven while it was smoke and said to it and to the earth: ‘Come willingly or unwillingly.’ They said: ‘We come willingly’ [Q 41:11]. He completed them as seven heavens in two days and revealed to each heaven its command on Thursday and Friday. The last creation was at the end of the hours of Friday. When Saturday came, there was no creation in it, so the Jews said what they said, and Allah ﷻ sent down its denial: ‘And We created the heavens and the earth and all that is between them in six days, and no weariness touched Us’ [Q 50:38].”"],[3671,"A man recited in his presence: “Indeed, the tree of Zaqqūm is food for the sinful” [Q 44:44]. Abū al-Dardāʾ said: “Say: food for the sinful.” The man said: “food for the orphan (al-yathīm).” Abū al-Dardāʾ said: “Say: food for the wicked (al-fājir).”"],[3672,"“Allah has three garments: He wraps Himself in might, He clothes Himself in mercy, and He covers Himself in grandeur. Whoever seeks might without what Allah has given him of might is the one to whom it is said: ‘Taste, indeed you are the mighty, the noble’ [Q 44:49]. Whoever shows mercy to people by the mercy of Allah is the one who has clothed himself in the garment that befits him. Whoever contends with Allah over the cloak that befits Him, Allah says: It is not fitting for one who contends with Me that I should admit him to Paradise.”"],[3673,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: “Fear Allah as He should be feared and do not die except as Muslims” [Q 3:102]. “By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if a single drop of Zaqqūm were to fall upon the earth, it would ruin the livelihoods of the people of this world. So how about the one whose food it is?”"],[3674,"A man came to ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ and asked him: “From what were the creation created?” He said: “From water, light, darkness, wind, and dust?” The man said: “From what were these created?” He said: “I do not know.” Then the man came to ʿAbd Allāh b. al-Zubayr and asked him, and he said the same as ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAmr. Then the man came to ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās and asked him: “From what was creation created?” He said: “From water, light, darkness, wind, and dust.” The man said: “From what were these created?” ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās recited: “And He subjected to you all that is in the heavens and all that is on earth, all from Him” [Q 45:13]. The man said: “No one could have given us this except a man from the household of the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[3675,"“Every servant will be resurrected upon that upon which he died.”"],[3676,"A man among the Arabs would worship a stone, and if he found one better than it, he would take it and discard the other. So Allah ﷻ sent down: “Have you seen him who takes his own desire as his god?” [Q 45:23]."],[3677,"“The son of Adam hurts Me by insulting time, and I am time. I turn its night and day, and when I will, I seize them both.”"],[3678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah ﷻ said: “I asked My servant for a loan but he refused to lend to Me, and My servant insulted Me without knowing. He says: ‘Woe to time! Woe to time!’ and I am time.”"],[3679,"“The son of Adam hurts Me by saying: ‘O failure of time!’ Let none of you say: ‘O failure of time!’ for I am time; I turn its night and day, and when I will, I seize them both.”"],[3680,"“The first thing Allah created was the Pen. He created it from hajā before the alif and the lām, and it took the form of a pen of light. It was said to it: ‘Flow upon the Preserved Tablet.’ It said: ‘O Lord, with what?’ He said: ‘With all that will be until the Day of Resurrection.’ When Allah created the creation, He appointed guardians over them to record their deeds. When the Resurrection occurs, their deeds will be shown to them and it will be said: ‘This is Our record speaking about you in truth; indeed, We used to have transcribed whatever you used to do’ [Q 45:29]. He compared the two records, and they were identical. Ibn ʿAbbās said: ‘Are you not Arabs? Is a copy taken except from a record?’”"],[3681,"He is the line."],[3682,"About him, Al-Dhahabi in summarizing."],[3683,"From Umm al-ʿAlāʾ al-Anṣāriyyah, who had given allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: ʿUthmān b. Maẓʿūn was allotted to us for lodging when the Anṣār drew lots for lodging the Emigrants. She said: He fell ill, and we nursed him until he passed away, and we wrapped him in his garments. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and I said, “May Allah have mercy on you, Abū al-Sāʾib. My testimony is that Allah has honored you.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “And what makes you know that?” She said, “By Allah, I do not know, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “As for him, certainty has come to him, and I hope for good for him from Allah.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “Say, ‘I am not the first of the messengers, and I do not know what will be done with me or with you’” [al-Aḥqāf: 9]. Umm al-ʿAlāʾ said: By Allah, I will never vouch for anyone after him. Umm al-ʿAlāʾ said: I saw a spring flowing for ʿUthmān in a dream, so I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that. He said, “That is his deeds flowing for him.”"],[3684,"Sa'd sought permission from Ibn 'Amir, and underneath him was a servant made of silk. He commanded her to be lifted up, so I lifted her up and he entered upon him and underneath him was a bed made of straw. He said to him, \"You have sought permission on me, and underneath me is a servant made of silk, so I commanded her to be lifted up.\" She was then lifted up, and he said to him, \"Indeed, you are a noble man, O Ibn 'Amir, if you are not among those whom Allah Almighty has described in the Quran saying, 'Have you exchanged the good things of this worldly life for the Hereafter?' And by Allah, lying on hot embers is more beloved to me than lying on it.\""],[3685,"\"To buy meat for my family with a dirham, so they threw it to him. Umar said, 'You have eaten what you desired, and you bought it. None of you wants his cousin and neighbor to be deprived of this verse: 'Have you taken your pleasures in the life of the world and forgotten the Hereafter?'\" [Surah Al-A'raf (46:20), Qasim Wah]."],[3686,"\"What Allah sent upon 'Ad from the wind was nothing but the predetermined punishment of my Lord.\" This hadith is narrated with an authentic chain according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs (Bukhari and Muslim). They did not include it in their compilations, but Muslim singled out the narration of Mas'ud ibn Malik according to the conditions of Bukhari and Muslim."],[3687,"From ʿĀʾishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughing with a full laugh so that I could see his uvula; he would only smile. She said: When he saw clouds or wind, it was recognized in his face. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, when people see clouds, they rejoice, hoping that there is rain in them, but I see that when you see them, displeasure is recognized in your face.” He said, “O ʿĀʾishah, what assures me that there is no punishment in them? A people were punished with the wind, and it brought punishment upon a people.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: “And when they saw it as a cloud approaching their valleys, they said, ‘This is a cloud bringing us rain’” [al-Aḥqāf: 24], the verse."],[3688,"They landed on the Prophet ﷺ while he was reciting the Quran in the shade of a palm tree. When they heard him, they said, \"Listen!\" They said, \"Silence!\" They were nine, one of them was Zoba'ah. Allah (Glorified and Exalted be He) revealed: \"And (remember) when We sent towards you (Muhammad صلى الله عليه وسلم) a group (of the jinn) to listen to the Qur'an...\"; until \"...clear misguidance\", Surah Al-Imran (3:164). It is an authentic Hadith with a sound chain of narrators and they have not reported it."],[3689,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The jinn are of three types: (1) one type has wings and they fly in the air, (2) another type are snakes and dogs, and (3) another type camp [at a place] and then [later] move [away].\""],[3690,"\"Those who have gone astray from the path of Allah\" [Surah Muhammad 1] He said, \"Among them are the people of Mecca\" [Surah Muhammad 1] And those who believe and do righteous deeds\" [Surah Muhammad 2] He said, \"They are the Ansar\" [Surah Muhammad 2] He said, \"He has corrected their condition\" [Surah Muhammad 2] He said, \"He has commanded them\""],[3691,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying, Exalted is He: “And he will be given to drink of purulent water, which he will sip” [Ibrāhīm: 17]. He said: It will be brought near to him, and he will find it repugnant. When it is brought close to him, it will roast his face and the skin of his head will fall off. When he drinks it, it will sever his intestines until it comes out of his anus. Allah, Exalted is He, says: “And they will be given to drink boiling water, and it will sever their intestines” [Muḥammad: 15]. Allah, Exalted is He, says: “And if they call for relief, they will be relieved with water like molten brass, which scalds the faces—wretched is the drink” [al-Kahf: 29]."],[3692,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: “Until when they have gone out from you, they say to those who were given knowledge, ‘What did he say just now?’” [Muḥammad: 16]. He said: “I was among those who were asked.”"],[3693,"I heard Ḥudhayfah, having recited the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: “So know that there is no god but Allah and ask forgiveness for your sin” [Muḥammad: 19], say: I was a man of sharp tongue toward my family, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I fear that my tongue may cause me to enter the Fire.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “What about seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from Allah a hundred times a day.”"],[3694,"The master of seeking forgiveness is that the servant says: O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me, and I am Your servant, and I am upon Your covenant and Your promise as much as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. I acknowledge to You Your favor upon me, and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You."],[3695,"I was sitting with Umar ibn Al-Khattab when he heard a scream. He said, \"Oh Yarfaa, look, what is this sound?\" He got up, looked, and then came back and said, \"It is a girl from the Quraysh being sold by her mother.\" Umar said, \"Pray for me, or he said, \"Upon me are the Mujahideen (emigrants) and the Ansar.\" He did not wait more than an hour until the house and the room were filled. Umar praised and thanked Allah, then he said, \"Do you know what this was? It was one of the things that the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ forbade.\" They said, \"No.\" He said, \"Verily, it has become rampant among you.\" Then he recited, \"Then do you think that if you turned away you could cause corruption on earth and break your ties of lineage?\" [Muhammad 22]. Then he said, \"And what kind of breaking off is worse than a mother being sold among you, while Allah has granted you a broader scope?\" They said, \"So do what you find necessary.\" He said, \"He wrote in the horizons that a free woman should not be sold, for it is a breaking off and it is not permissible.\""],[3696,"When it was sent down: “And if you turn away, He will replace you with another people” [Muḥammad: 38], they said, “O Messenger of Allah, who are these who would replace us if we turn away?”—and Salmān was beside him—He said, “They are the Persians, this one and his people.”"],[3697,"The Surah al-Fath was revealed between Mecca and Medina regarding the incident of Hudaybiyah, from the beginning to the end."],[3698,"I heard Mujammiʿ b. Jāriyah say: We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from al-Ḥudaybiyyah until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm, when people were making marks (or drawing lines) toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some people said to others, “What is with the people?” They said, “Revelation has come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Some people said, “We urged our mounts until we found the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing at Kurāʿ al-Ghamīm.” When the people gathered around him, he recited to them: “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory” [al-Fatḥ: 1]. Some people said, “Is it a victory?” He said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, it is indeed a victory.”"],[3699,"Opening of Khaybar, so that Allah may forgive you for what preceded of your sin and what follows. (Surah Al-Fath, 48:2) So they said, \"O Messenger of Allah, congratulations to you! But what is for us?\" So Allah revealed, \"So that He may admit the believing men and believing women to gardens beneath which rivers flow.\" (Surah Al-Fath, 48:5)"],[3700,"When we returned from al-Ḥudaybiyyah, the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ were mixed with grief and dejection, since they had slaughtered their sacrificial animals in their places. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A verse has been sent down to me that is more beloved to me than the whole world—three times.” We said, “What is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, and he recited: “Indeed, We have granted you a clear victory, that Allah may forgive you your former and latter sins and complete His favor upon you and guide you to a straight path” [al-Fatḥ: 2], to the end of the two verses. We said, “May it be pleasant for you, O Messenger of Allah. So what is for us?” Then he recited: “That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, to abide therein forever, and to remove from them their misdeeds—and that is, in the sight of Allah, a great triumph” [al-Fatḥ: 5]. When we came to Khaybar, they saw the army of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, meaning his troops, and they fled in retreat to the fortress. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Khaybar is ruined. Indeed, when we descend upon the courtyard of a people, then evil is the morning of those who were warned.” Al-Ḥakam b. Mālik is weak; he adduced it as a corroborating report."],[3701,"About Ali, who is the one who sent down tranquility in the hearts of the believers. [Al-Fath 4] He said, \"Tranquility has a face like the face of a human, then it is a gentle breeze.\""],[3702,"I said to Ibn ʿAbbās, “What is His saying, Exalted is He: ‘and honor him’ [al-Fatḥ: 9]?” He said, “Striking before the Prophet ﷺ with the sword.”"],[3703,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Ḥudaybiyyah at the base of the tree that Allah, Exalted is He, mentioned in the Qurʾān. A branch of that tree was over the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so I raised it from his back, while ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib and Suhayl b. ʿAmr were sitting before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ʿAlī, “Write.” Then he mentioned lines from the ḥadīth that are transmitted in the two books, from the mention of Suhayl b. ʿAmr. ʿAbd Allāh b. Mughaffal said: While we were thus, thirty young men bearing arms came out against us and charged at our faces. The Prophet ﷺ supplicated against them, and Allah took away their sight. We rose to them and seized them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “Have you come under a covenant with anyone, or has anyone granted you protection?” They said, “O Allah, no.” So he released them. Then Allah, Exalted is He, sent down: “And it is He who withheld their hands from you and your hands from them in the hollow of Makkah, after He had given you victory over them—and Allah is ever Seeing of what you do” [al-Fatḥ: 24]."],[3704,"From ʿAlī regarding His saying, Exalted is He: “and bound them to the word of piety” [al-Fatḥ: 26]. He said, “There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater.”"],[3705,"A man recited Surah al-Fath to ʿAbd Allāh, and when he reached {Like a seed that puts forth its shoot, then strengthens it, then it becomes thick and stands straight upon its stem, delighting the sowers—so that He may enrage by them the disbelievers} [al-Fath 29], he said: \"Allah enrages the disbelievers by the Prophet ﷺ and his Companions.\" He said: Then ʿAbd Allāh said: \"You are the crop, and its harvest has drawn near.\" A sound hadith according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3706,"From ʿĀʾishah: {so that He may enrage by them the disbelievers} [al-Fath 29]. She said: \"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were commanded to seek forgiveness for them, so they reviled them.\""],[3707,"When {Indeed, those who lower their voices in the presence of the Messenger of Allah} [al-Hujurat 3] was revealed ﷺ, Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq said: \"By the One who sent down the Book upon you, O Messenger of Allah, I will not speak to you except as a confidant whispers, until I meet Allah ﷻ.\" This is a sound hadith according to the criterion of Muslim, but they did not include it. According to the condition of Muslim."],[3708,"He was asked: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about what we do—is it something already decreed, or something we initiate?\" He said: \"Every person is facilitated for what he was created.\""],[3709,"While he was sitting with ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar, a man from the people of Iraq came to him and said: \"O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, by Allah, I have set out to follow your way and emulate you in the matter of the people's division, and to avoid evil as much as I can, and to recite a clear verse from the Book of Allah that has taken hold of my heart. So tell me about it. What do you think of Allah's saying ﷻ: {And if two factions among the believers fight, then make peace between them. But if one of them oppresses the other, then fight against the one that oppresses until it returns to the command of Allah. And if it returns, then make peace between them with justice and act equitably. Indeed, Allah loves those who act equitably}?\""],[3710,"Regarding His saying ﷻ {And do not defame yourselves} [al-Hujurat 11], he said: \"Do not revile one another.\""],[3711,"Nicknames existed in the pre-Islamic era. The Prophet ﷺ called a man among them by his nickname, and it was said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, he dislikes it.\" So Allah ﷻ revealed: {And do not call each other by offensive nicknames} [al-Hujurat 11]."],[3712,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ will say on the Day of Resurrection: 'I commanded you, but you neglected what I entrusted to you, and I raised your lineages. Today I raise My lineage and lower your lineages. Where are the righteous? Where are the righteous? Indeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous.'\""],[3713,"He recited Allah's saying ﷻ: {Indeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous} [al-Hujurat 13], then said: \"Allah says on the Day of Resurrection: 'O people, I established a lineage and you established a lineage. I made the most noble of you the most righteous, but you refused except to say: So-and-so son of so-and-so is more noble than so-and-so son of so-and-so. Today I raise My lineage and lower your lineages. Where are the righteous? Where are the righteous?'\" Ṭalḥah said: ʿAṭāʾ said to me: \"O Ṭalḥah, how many names on the Day of Resurrection will be like mine and yours? When one is called, only the one intended will stand.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[3714,"\"A mountain of emerald encircles the world, upon it lies the canopy of the sky.\""],[3715,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the morning prayer. When he reached this verse, \"And by the date-palm trees, bearing clusters of dates\" [Quran 50:10], Qutbah said, \"I used to say to him, 'What does 'clusters' mean?' He replied, 'Its branches are long.' Muslim reported this hadith without mentioning the explanation of 'clusters' and it is authentic according to its conditions.\""],[3716,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Maʿd b. ʿAdnān b. Adad b. Zand b. Barrī b. Aʿrāq al-tharā.\" She said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"He destroyed ʿĀd and Thamūd and the companions of al-Rass and many generations between that—none knows them except Allah.\" Umm Salamah said: \"Aʿrāq al-tharā is Ismāʿīl b. Ibrāhīm, Zand is the son of Humaysaʿ, and Barrī is Nabt.\""],[3717,"Regarding this verse: \"Not a word does he utter but there is a watcher by him ready\" [Quran 50:18], Ibn Abbas said: \"Only the good and the evil are written. O boy, saddle the horse for me and O boy, give me water to drink. Only the good and the evil are written.\""],[3718,"I heard Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating and reciting the words of Allah ﷻ: {And the intoxication of death will bring the truth; that is what you were trying to avoid.} [Qaf 19] Then he said, Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, told me: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on his deathbed. He had a cup containing water, and he used to dip his hand into the cup and then wipe his face with the water, saying, \"O Allah, help me with the throes of death.\""],[3719,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the first for whom the earth will split open, then Abū Bakr, then ʿUmar. Then I will come to the people of al-Baqīʿ and they will be gathered with me. Then I will await the people of Makkah.\" And ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿUmar recited: \"On the Day the earth splits open from them, hastening forth—that is a gathering easy for Us.\""],[3720,"A man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ trembling with fear. He said: \"Take it easy, for I am only the son of a woman from Quraysh who used to eat dried meat in this valley.\" Then Jarīr b. ʿAbd Allāh al-Bajalī recited: {And you are not over them a tyrant—so remind by the Qur'an whoever fears My threat} [Qaf 45]."],[3721,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit the sick, follow funerals, accept the invitation of a slave, and ride a donkey. On the day of Khaybar and the day of Qurayzah, he was on a donkey whose halter was a rope of palm fiber, and beneath him was a saddle pad of palm fiber."],[3722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to the weak among the Muslims and visit them, visit their sick, and attend their funerals."],[3723,"I saw the Commander of the Faithful, Ali ibn Abi Talib, standing on the pulpit. He said, \"Ask me before you are unable to ask me, and you will not ask anyone like me after me.\" Then Ibn Al-Kawwa stood up and asked, \"O Commander of the Faithful, what is {By those [winds] scattering [dust]} [Al-Dhariyat 1]?\" He said, \"The winds.\" He asked, \"What is {And those [clouds] carrying a load}?\" He said, \"The clouds.\" He asked, \"What is {And those [ships] sailing with ease}?\" He said, \"The ships.\" He asked, \"What is {And those [angels] apportioning each matter}?\" He said, \"The angels.\" He then asked, \"Who are {the ones who exchanged the favor of Allah for disbelief and settled their people in the home of ruin, Hell} [Ibrahim 28]?\" He said, \"The hypocrites of Quraysh.\""],[3724,"From Anas regarding this verse: {They used to sleep but little of the night} [Adh-Dhariyat 17], he said: 'They used to pray between the evening prayer and the sunset prayer.'"],[3725,"In His saying ﷻ {They used to sleep but little of the night} [Al-Dhariyat 17], it is said: \"Not a night passes by them without praying in it until morning comes.\""],[3726,"Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ was: 'O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the evil of the wind, from the evil of what the wind brings, and from the north wind, for it is the barren wind.'"],[3727,"The passage translates to English as follows:In His saying, Almighty Allah, {And in 'Aad [was a sign], when We sent against them the barren wind.} [Al-Dhariyat 41], it is said, \"the one that does not fertilize anything.\""],[3728,"\"Jabal\" translates to \"mountain\" in English."],[3729,"The Much-Frequented House is in the seventh heaven. Seventy thousand angels enter it every day and do not return to it until the Hour comes."],[3730,"\"The sky\""],[3731,"\"Indeed, Allah raises the ranks of the believing offspring with Him in Paradise, even if they are lower in deeds than Him.\" Then He recited: \"And those who believed and whose descendants followed them in faith - We will join with them their descendants, and We will not deprive them of anything.\" (Surah At-Tur, 21) He (Al-Dhahabi) did not mention it in his summary."],[3732,"The Prophet ﷺ prostrated in it, meaning 'An-Najm', and the Muslims, the polytheists, humans, and jinn prostrated in it. Sahih according to the condition of al-Bukhari, but they did not include it with this wording on the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3733,"From Abdullah regarding His saying, exalted is He: {The heart did not lie [about] what it saw} [An-Najm 11], he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Jibril in a garment of fine silk, filling what is between the heaven and the earth.' Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it on the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3734,"That close friendship (khullah) was for Ibrahim, speech (kalam) for Musa, and the vision (ru'yah) for Muhammad ﷺ, and the blessings of Allah be upon them all."],[3735,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ describing the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary. He said: 'A rider travels in its shade for a hundred years; a hundred riders can take shade in its branches; in it are moths of gold.'"],[3736,"\"He did not go right or left\" {and he did not transgress} [Surah An-Najm 17] He said, \"He did not exceed.\""],[3737,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He: {Those who avoid major sins and immoralities, except the small faults} [An-Najm 32], he said: 'He commits them occasionally, then repents from them.' Ibn Abbas said: The Prophet ﷺ used to say: '[Rajaz meter] If You forgive, O Allah, You forgive much; and which servant of Yours has not committed small faults?'"],[3738,"Ishaq narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, Ma'mar informed us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, that Ibn Mas'ud said regarding His saying, exalted is He: {Except the small faults} [An-Najm 32]: 'The adultery of the eyes is looking, the adultery of the lips is kissing, the adultery of the hands is touching, and the adultery of the feet is walking. The private part confirms that or denies it. If he proceeds with his private part, he is an adulterer; otherwise, it is a small fault.'"],[3739,"Upon every soul of the son of Adam is written a share of adultery that he will inevitably encounter. The eye's adultery is looking, the foot's adultery is walking, the ear's adultery is listening, the hand's adultery is touching, the tongue's adultery is speaking, and the heart desires and longs, and the private part confirms that or denies it."],[3740,"The arrows of Islam are thirty arrows; no one completed them before Ibrahim ﷺ . Allah ﷻ said: {And Ibrahim, who fulfilled} [al-Najm: 37]."],[3741,"When 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' was revealed, he said: 'All of it is in the scriptures of Ibrahim.' Then when 'By the star when it descends' was revealed, and he reached {And Ibrahim, who fulfilled: that no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another} [al-Najm: 38] up to His saying {This is a warner from the warners of old} [al-Najm: 56]."],[3742,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed the dead is punished by the weeping of the living.' And when she says: O my support, O my defender, O my helper, O my clothier—how beloved is the dead! So it is said: Are you her helper? Are you her clothier? Are you her supporter? He said: I said: Glory be to Allah. He said: Allah ﷻ said: {And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another} [al-An'am: 164]. So he said: Woe to you! I narrate to you from Abu Musa from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you say this? Which of us lied? By Allah, I did not lie about Abu Musa, and Abu Musa did not lie about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[3743,"About Abdullah's statement in his words, may Allah be glorified and exalted: \"And the moon split\" [Surah Al-Qamar, verse 1]. He said, \"I saw the moon split, and I saw the mountain between the two parts of the moon.\""],[3744,"\"I saw the moon split into two halves twice in Makkah before the Prophet's ﷺ migration, with one half over Abu Qubays and the other half over the Suwayda.\" They said, \"The moon is bewitched,\" then came the verse, \"The Hour has come near, and the moon has split [in two].\" (Quran 54:1) He said, \"Just as you saw it split, what I have informed you about the approaching Hour is true.\""],[3745,"\"The moon split during the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. And as for the narration of Abdullah son of Amr, it is authentic.\""],[3746,"In the saying of Allah, the Exalted, \"{The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split.}\" [Surah Al-Qamar 54:1], it is said that this occurred during the time of the Prophet ﷺ when the moon split into two halves: one half was on one side of the mountain and the other half was on the other side. The Prophet ﷺ then said, \"O Allah, bear witness.\"[1]"],[3747,"In His words, the Almighty (ﷻ), \"{The Hour has come near, and the moon has split}\" [Quran, Al-Qamar 54:1], it is said, \"The moon split while we were in Mecca during the time of the Prophet ﷺ .\""],[3748,"The people of Mecca asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a sign, and the moon was split in Mecca twice. Allah (the Exalted) said, \"The Hour has drawn near, and the moon has split\" [Al-Qamar 54:1].[1]"],[3749,"He used to recite (khashi'an absaruhum) with an alif."],[3750,"I heard Aban b. Taghlib recite (khashi'an absaruhum) like Hamzah."],[3751,"There were three hundred years between the call of Noah and the destruction of Noah's people, and the oven persisted in India, and Noah's ark sailed for a week. The chain of narrators is authentic, and it was not included in the authentic collections."],[3752,"\"The last speech about qadar is for the worst of this ummah.\""],[3753,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surah al-Rahman to his companions until he finished, he said: 'Why do I see you silent? The jinn were better than you in response. I did not recite to them even once {So which of the favors of your Lord will you deny?} [al-Rahman: 13] except that they said: And not any of your blessings, our Lord, do we deny, so to You is praise.' Authentic according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not record it. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3754,"No one is named the Merciful except Him. This is an authentic chain of narration and it was not excluded from being authentic."],[3755,"\"With a reckoning and stages.\" Its chain of narration is authentic, but they did not record it. Authentic."],[3756,"\"An-najm is what the earth produces, and ash-shajar is what is on a trunk.\" Its chain of narration is authentic, but they did not record it. Minhal b. Khalifah was deemed weak by Ibn Ma'in."],[3757,"\"As-samum, from which Allah created the jann, is one part of seventy parts of the fire of Jahannam.\""],[3758,"Indeed, among what Allah has created is a preserved Tablet made of white pearl, its covers are made of red ruby, its pen is light, and its written words are light. Every day, it is looked upon three hundred and sixty times or more. In each look, Allah creates, provides, gives life, causes death, honors, humiliates, and does whatever He wills. This is the saying of the Most High: \"Every day, He is upon a matter.\" [Surah ar-Rahman 29] \"Authentic chain of narrators, and they did not exclude it.\" The name of Abu Hamzah Thabit is mentioned, and he erred once."],[3759,"From his father regarding {But for him who fears the standing before his Lord are two gardens} [al-Rahman: 46], he said: 'Two gardens of gold for the forerunners, and two gardens of silver for the followers.' According to the condition of Muslim."],[3760,"\"You have been informed about the hidden matters, so how about the evident ones?\" It is correct according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but it has not been narrated based on the conditions of Bukhari and Muslim."],[3761,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding His saying ﷻ {As though they were rubies and coral} [al-Rahman: 58], he said: 'He looks at his face in her cheek, clearer than a mirror. And the least pearl upon her would illuminate what is between the east and the west. And upon her are seventy garments; his sight penetrates them until he sees the marrow of her shin from behind that.' Its chain of narration is authentic, but they did not record it. Durayj has strange reports."],[3762,"The Throne of Allah was upon the water, then He took for Himself a screen, then He took another screen below it, until He covered it with a single pearl.” So the Mighty One, from His saying, said: {And besides these two are two gardens} (55:62). He said: “And it is the one regarding which creation does not know what is in it.” He said: And it is the one about which Allah ﷻ said: {And no soul knows what has been hidden for them of comfort for eyes as reward for what they used to do} (32:17). Every day a gift comes to them from it."],[3763,"\"The date palm of Paradise, its trunks are emerald green, and its branches are red gold, and its leaves are clothing for the people of Paradise among which their garments, necklaces, and their fruits are like pots or water pitchers, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and softer than butter, and it does not have thorns.\""],[3764,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: I asked the Prophet ﷺ: What has made you gray? He said: “Surah Hud, al-Waqi'ah, al-Mursalat, 'Amma yatasa'alun, and Idha al-shamsu kuwwirat.”"],[3765,"The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: Indeed Allah benefits us through the Bedouins and their questions. One day a Bedouin came and said: O Messenger of Allah, Allah has mentioned in the Quran a harmful tree, and I did not think that in Paradise there is a tree that harms its owner. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “And what is it?” He said: The lote tree, for it has thorns. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: {In lote trees with thorns removed} (56:28). Allah removes its thorns, and in place of every thorn He puts a fruit, for it produces fruit; each fruit opens with it into seventy-two colors, no color resembling another.” [Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it] Sahih."],[3766,"“From black smoke.”"],[3767,"Rather, You, O Lord,” three times. Then he recited: {Have you seen that which you sow? Is it you who makes it grow, or are We the grower?} (56:63). He said: “Rather, You, O Lord; rather, You, O Lord; rather, You, O Lord.” Then he recited: {Have you seen the water that you drink? Is it you who brought it down from the clouds, or are We the bringer down?} (56:68). He said: “Rather, You, O Lord,” three times. Then he recited: {Have you seen the fire that you kindle? Is it you who produced its tree, or are We the producer?} (56:72). He said: “Rather, You, O Lord,” three times."],[3768,"The Quran was sent down in the Night of Decree from the highest heaven to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was divided over the years.” He said: And he recited this verse: {But nay! I swear by the setting of the stars} (56:75). He said: “It came down in portions.”"],[3769,"We were with Salman, and he went off for a need and disappeared from us. Then he came out to us, and there was no water between us and him. He said: We said to him: O Abu 'Abd Allah, if you perform ablution, we would ask you about some things from the Quran. He said: “Ask, for I do not touch it; only the purified touch it.” Then he recited: {Indeed it is a noble Quran, in a hidden Book; none touch it except the purified} (56:77-79)."],[3770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: “Place it in your bowing.” Then when {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} (87:1) was revealed, he said: “Place it in your prostration.”"],[3771,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the first to be permitted to prostrate on the Day of Resurrection, and the first to be permitted to raise his head. So I raise my head and look in front of me, and I recognize my community from among the nations. I look to my right and recognize my community from among the nations. I look to my left and recognize my community from among the nations.” A man said: O Messenger of Allah, how do you recognize your community from among the nations from Noah to your community? He said: “They are bright-faced with white limbs from the traces of ablution. No one among the nations besides them is like that. I recognize them because they are given their books in their right hands. I recognize them by their marks on their faces from the traces of prostration. I recognize them by their light that is before them and on their right and on their left.”"],[3772,"From 'Abd Allah regarding His saying ﷻ: {Their light running before them} (57:12), he said: “They are given their light according to the measure of their deeds. Among them is one whose light is like a mountain, and the least of them in light is one whose light is on his thumb; it goes out at times and is lit at other times.”"],[3773,"I saw 'Ubadah b. al-Samit in the mosque of Jerusalem, facing east, or the wall – I am uncertain – and he was weeping while reciting this verse: {So a wall will be put between them with a gate, its interior containing mercy} (57:13). Then he said: Here the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed us Hell."],[3774,"“There was not between their acceptance of Islam and the revelation of this verse, by which Allah reproached them, except four years: {And do not be like those who were given the Scripture before, and a long period passed over them} (57:16) to the end of the verse.”"],[3775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say: The people of the pre-Islamic era used to say, 'Indeed, ill omens are only in the woman, the riding beast, and the dwelling.' Then she recited: {No disaster strikes upon the earth or among yourselves except that it is in a register before We bring it into being. Indeed that, for Allah, is easy.} [Al-Hadid 22]"],[3776,"\"Is there not anyone who does not experience sadness and happiness? But it is those who make calamity a source of patience and make joy a reason for gratitude.\" It is a soundly-narrated Hadith, and it has not been excluded from being valid."],[3777,"{And We placed in the hearts of those who followed him compassion and mercy, and monasticism which they innovated. We did not prescribe it for them except seeking the pleasure of Allah, but they did not observe it with its due observance. So We gave those who believed among them their reward, but many of them are defiantly disobedient.} [Al-Hadid 27] Ibn Mas'ud said: The Prophet ﷺ said to me, 'O Abdullah b. Mas'ud.' I replied, 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah,' three times. He said, 'Do you know which handhold of faith is most trustworthy?' I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'The most trustworthy handhold of faith is allegiance for the sake of Allah, loving for His sake and hating for His sake. O Abdullah b. Mas'ud.' I said, 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah,' three times. He said, 'Do you know which people are best?' I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'Indeed, the best of people are those best in deeds when they have understanding in their religion. O Abdullah b. Mas'ud.' I said, 'At your service and at your command,' three times. He said, 'Do you know which people are most knowledgeable?' I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said, 'Indeed, the most knowledgeable of people are those most perceptive of the truth when people differ, even if he is deficient in deeds, even if he crawls on his backside. Those before us divided into seventy-two sects; three of them were saved and the rest perished. One sect confronted the kings and fought them for the religion of Allah and the religion of Jesus son of Mary until they were killed. A sect did not have the strength to confront the kings, so they remained among their people and called them to the religion of Allah and the religion of Jesus son of Mary, and the kings killed them and sawed them with saws. A sect did not have the strength to confront the kings nor to remain among their people calling them to Allah and to the religion of Jesus son of Mary, so they wandered in the mountains and became monks therein. They are the ones about whom Allah said: {and monasticism which they innovated. We did not prescribe it for them except seeking the pleasure of Allah, but they did not observe it with its due observance} [Al-Hadid 27] up to His saying {defiantly disobedient} [Al-Hadid 27]. So the believers are those who believed in me and affirmed me, and the defiantly disobedient are those who disbelieved in me and rejected me.'"],[3778,"Aisha said: Blessed is the One whose hearing encompasses all things. Indeed, I could hear the words of Khawla bt. Tha'laba, though some of it was hidden from me, as she complained about her husband to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, he consumed my youth and I bore children for him, until when my age advanced and my bearing ceased, he declared zihar against me. O Allah, I complain to You.' Aisha said: She did not leave until Jibril ﷺ descended with these verses: {Allah has certainly heard the statement of the one who pleads with you concerning her husband.} [Al-Mujadila 1] He said: Her husband was Aws b. al-Samit."],[3779,"That Jamila was the wife of Aws b. al-Samit, and Aws was a man afflicted with a touch of madness. When his madness became severe, he declared zihar against his wife, so Allah revealed concerning him the expiation for zihar."],[3780,"[regarding the ayah] “Allah will raise those who have believed among you and those who have been given knowledge in ranks.” [Al-Mujādilah 11] He said: “Allah raises those believers who have been given knowledge above those who have not been given knowledge by ranks.”"],[3781,"Indeed, there is a verse in the Book of Allah that no one has ever acted upon and no one after me will ever act upon: the verse of private consultation. {O you who have believed, when you privately consult the Messenger, offer before your private consultation a charity.} [Al-Mujadila 12] He said: I had a dinar, so I sold it for ten dirhams. Then I privately consulted the Prophet ﷺ, and every time I privately consulted the Prophet ﷺ, I offered before my private consultation a dirham. Then it was abrogated, and no one acted upon it, so it was revealed: {Do you fear to offer charities before your private consultation?} [Al-Mujadila 13]"],[3782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the shade of a room, and the shade was about to recede. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, a man will come to you and look at you with the eye of a devil. When he comes to you, do not speak to him.' It was not long before a blue-eyed, one-eyed man appeared. When he saw him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and said: 'For what do you revile me, you and your companions?' He said: 'Let me go and I will bring them to you.' So he went and called them, and they swore that they had not said anything and had not done anything, until they were deemed treacherous. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {On the Day when Allah resurrects them all, they will swear to Him as they swear to you, and they think they are on something. Unquestionably, it is they who are the liars.} [Al-Mujadila 18]"],[3783,"Abu al-Darda' said to me: 'Where is your dwelling?' I said, 'In a village near Homs.' Abu al-Darda' said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There are no three people in a village or a desert where the prayer is not established among them except that Satan has gained mastery over them. So adhere to the congregation, for indeed the wolf eats the stray sheep.'"],[3784,"\"About Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her\""],[3785,"From Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas that they both testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gourds, green jars, glazed jars, and varnished jars. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {And whatever the Messenger gives you, take it; and whatever he forbids you, refrain from it.} [Al-Hashr 7]"],[3786,"A sheep's head was gifted to a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: 'Indeed, my brother so-and-so and his family are more in need of this than us.' He said: So he sent it to him, and it kept being sent from one to another until it circulated among seven households and returned to the first. Then it was revealed: {And they give preference over themselves, even though they are in privation.} [Al-Hashr 9] to the end of the verse."],[3787,"People are on three stations; two of them have passed and one remains. The best state you can be upon is to be upon this remaining station. Then he recited: {For the poor emigrants who were expelled from their homes and properties.} [Al-Hashr 8] Then he said: 'These are the emigrants, and this is a station that has passed.' Then he recited: {And those who had established the home and faith before them.} Then he said: 'These are the Helpers, and this is a station that has passed.' Then he recited: {And those who came after them, saying, 'Our Lord, forgive us and our brothers who preceded us in faith.'} He said: 'Those two stations have passed, and this station remains. The best state you can be upon is to be upon this remaining station.'"],[3788,"There was a monk who worshipped in a hermitage, and a woman adorned herself for him, and he had intercourse with her, and she became pregnant. Then Satan came to him and said, 'Kill her, for if they find out about you, you will be disgraced.' So he killed her and buried her. Then they came to him and seized him and took him away. While they were walking, Satan came to him and said, 'I am the one who adorned her for you. Prostrate to me once and I will save you.' So he prostrated to him. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Like the example of Satan when he says to man, 'Disbelieve.' But when he disbelieves, he says, 'Indeed, I am disassociated from you.'} [Al-Hashr 16]"],[3789,"\"To seek inspiration from the forgiveness of Ibrahim for his father, so that they may seek forgiveness for the polytheists. And His saying, \"Our Lord, do not make us a trial for those who disbelieve,\" [Al-Mumtahanah 5], \"Do not punish us with their hands, nor with a punishment from You,\" (Lord) they say, \"If these (believers) were upon the truth, they would not have been afflicted.\""],[3790,"\"In the making of the idols of Ibrahim and those with him, except for seeking forgiveness for his father while he was still a polytheist.\""],[3791,"That she should take from her and accept from her and admit her into her home, until she sent to Aisha to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about this. She informed him, and he commanded her to accept her gifts and admit her into her home. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Allah does not forbid you from those who do not fight you because of religion and do not expel you from your homes from being righteous toward them.} [Al-Mumtahina 8] to the end of the two verses."],[3792,"That Abu Hudhayfa b. 'Utba brought her and Hind bt. 'Utba to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to give him allegiance. She said: \"He took from us and stipulated upon us.\" She said: \"I said to him: 'O cousin, have you seen in your people any of these faults or vices?' Abu Hudhayfa said: 'Enough! Give him allegiance, for with this he accepts allegiance and thus he stipulates.' Hind said: 'I will not give you allegiance upon theft, for I steal from my husband's wealth.' The Prophet ﷺ withheld his hand and she withheld her hand until he sent to Abu Sufyan, who made it lawful for her from it. Abu Sufyan said: 'As for what is fresh, yes; as for what is dry, no, and no blessing.' She said: Then we gave him allegiance. Then Fatima said: 'There was no dome more hateful to me than your dome, nor did I love that Allah should lay it open and what is in it. By Allah, there is no dome I love more that Allah should maintain it and bless it than your dome.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'And also, by Allah, none of you believes until I am more beloved to him than his child and his parent.'\""],[3793,"We gathered and reminded one another, saying: 'Which of you will go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him which deeds are most beloved to Allah?' Then we separated and were in awe that any of us should go to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for us and gathered us, and some of us began gesturing to others. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited to us: 'Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, and He is the Mighty, the Wise. O you who believe, why do you say what you do not do?' to the end of the surah. Abu Salama said: 'Abdullah b. Salam recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Yahya said: Abu Salama recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Al-Awza'i said: Yahya b. Abi Kathir recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Abu Ishaq al-Fazari said: Al-Awza'i recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Mu'awiya b. 'Amr said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Nadr said: Mu'awiya b. 'Amr recited it to us from its beginning to its end. Abu Bakr b. Balawayh said: Muhammad b. Ahmad b. al-Nadr recited it to us from its beginning to its end.\""],[3794,"Jesus ﷺ promised his companions twelve men in a house, and he came out to them from a side other than the side of the house, shaking his head, and he mentioned a hadith. He said at its end: Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {So We supported those who believed against their enemy, and they became dominant} [al-Saff 14]."],[3795,"\"This verse is written in the Torah with seven hundred verses: {Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth glorifies Allah, the King, the Holy, the Mighty, the Wise} - the opening of Surah al-Jumu'ah.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[3796,"Abu Jahl passed by the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying and said, \"Didn't I forbid you from praying, O Muhammad? You know that no one else has called people to prayer more than me.\" The Prophet ﷺ scolded him. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, said, \"Let him make his call, we will call the Zabaniyah.\" By Allah, if he had made his call, the angels of punishment would have seized him.[1]"],[3797,"\"Lengthen this prayer and shorten this sermon\" - meaning the Friday prayer."],[3798,"\"Whoever abandons the Friday prayer three times without necessity, Allah seals his heart.\""],[3799,"We went on a military expedition with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with us were some people from the bedouins. We used to race to the water, and the bedouins would get there before us. A bedouin would outrun his companions, fill the basin, place stones around it, and put a leather mat over it until his companions came. A man from the Ansar came to the bedouin and loosened the halter of his camel to let it drink, but he refused to let him. He pulled out a stone and the water overflowed. The bedouin raised a piece of wood and struck the Ansari's head with it, wounding him. He went to 'Abdullah b. Ubayy, the head of the hypocrites, and told him, as he was one of his companions. 'Abdullah b. Ubayy became angry and said: 'Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they disperse from around him' - meaning the bedouins. They used to talk to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at meals. 'Abdullah said to his companions: 'When they disperse from Muhammad, then go to Muhammad for food; let him and those with him eat.' Then he said to his companions: 'If you return to Madinah, the mightier will surely expel the humbler from it.' Zayd said: I was riding behind my uncle, so I heard 'Abdullah, and we were his maternal uncles. I told my uncle, and he went and told the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him, and he swore, denied, and made excuses, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ believed him and called me a liar. He came to my uncle and said: 'What did you intend? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has hated you and called you a liar, and the Muslims have called you a liar.' Such grief fell upon me as had never fallen upon anyone. While I was walking with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and I had nodded off with grief, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me, pulled my ear, and smiled in my face. Nothing would have pleased me more than to have eternal life or the world in exchange for that. Then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?' I said: 'He did not say anything to me except that he pulled my ear and smiled in my face.' He said: 'Rejoice.' Then 'Umar caught up with me and said: 'What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you?' I said to him the same as I said to Abu Bakr. When morning came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited Surah al-Munafiqun: {When the hypocrites come to you, they say: We bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah} [al-Munafiqun 1] until he reached {those who say: Do not spend on those who are with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse} [al-Munafiqun 7] until he reached {the mightier will surely expel the humbler from it} [al-Munafiqun 8]. \"The two Shaykhs agreed on extracting a few words of this hadith from the hadith of Abu Ishaq al-Sabi'i from Zayd b. Arqam.\" Al-Bukhari extracted it as a corroboration for Abu Ishaq from the hadith of Shu'ba from al-Hakam from Muhammad b. Ka'b al-Qurazi from Zayd b. Arqam, but they did not extract it in full, and the chain is authentic. They extracted part of it from it."],[3800,"\"Every servant will be resurrected upon what he died upon.\""],[3801,"This verse was revealed: {Indeed, among your spouses and your children are enemies to you, so beware of them} [al-Taghabun 14] concerning a group of people from Makkah who embraced Islam and wanted to come to the Prophet ﷺ, but their spouses and children refused to let them go. They came to Madinah, and when they arrived to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, they saw that they had gained understanding, so they intended to punish them. Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {But if you pardon and overlook} [al-Taghabun 14] - the verse."],[3802,"About this verse: {And whoever is protected from the stinginess of his soul - it is those who will be the successful} [al-Hashr 9]. He said: \"I am a man who has not been able, and nothing leaves my hand, and I feared that this verse might have struck me.\" 'Abdullah said: \"You mentioned miserliness, and what a bad thing miserliness is. As for what Allah mentioned in the Quran, it is not as you said. That is that you intend the wealth of another or the wealth of your brother and consume it.\""],[3803,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ says: I asked My servant for a loan, but he refused to lend Me. My servant reviled Me without knowing: he says 'Woe to time, woe to time,' and I am time.\" Then Abu Hurayra recited the word of Allah ﷻ: {If you lend Allah a goodly loan, He will multiply it for you} [al-Taghabun 17]."],[3804,"From Muhammad b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi', the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from 'Ikrima, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: 'Abd Yazid, the father of Rukana, divorced the mother of Rukana, then married a woman from Muzayna. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, he is of no more use to me than this hair is to another hair' - she had taken a hair from her head. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became zealous at that, so he called Rukana and his brothers, then said to those sitting with him: 'Do you see such-and-such from such-and-such?' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Abd Yazid: 'Divorce her.' He did so. Then he said to Abu Rukana: 'Take her back.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I divorced her three times.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I knew that, so take her back.' Then it was revealed: {O Prophet, when you divorce women, divorce them for their waiting period} [al-Talaq 1]."],[3805,"Her going out of her house is a clear obscenity."],[3806,"Abu Dharr: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to recite this verse: {And whoever fears Allah, He will make a way out for him and provide for him from where he does not expect} [al-Talaq 3]. He said: He kept repeating it until I became drowsy. Then he ﷺ said: 'O Abu Dharr, if the people acted upon it, it would suffice them.'"],[3807,"This verse was revealed: {And whoever fears Allah, He will make a way out for him and provide for him from where he does not expect} [al-Talaq 3] concerning a man from Ashjaʿ who was poor, with little means and many dependents. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him. He ﷺ said to him: 'Fear Allah and be patient.' He returned to his companions and they said: What did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give you? He said: He did not give me anything, but he said to me: 'Fear Allah and be patient.' It was only a short while before his son came with some sheep of his that the enemy had seized. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him about them and told him what had happened. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Eat them.' So the verse was revealed: {And whoever fears Allah, He will make a way out for him and provide for him from where he does not expect} [al-Talaq 2]."],[3808,"When the verse was revealed in Surah al-Baqarah concerning a number of women, they said: There remain a number of women who have not been mentioned – the young and the old, those whose menstruation has ceased, and those who are pregnant. So Allah ﷻ revealed the verse in Surah al-Nisaʾ: {And those of your women who despair of menstruation, if you doubt, their period is three months, and those who have not menstruated. And for pregnant women, their term is until they deliver their burden} [al-Talaq 4]. Its chain of narration is authentic, but the two shaykhs did not include it. Authentic."],[3809,"He said: {Allah is the One who created seven heavens and of the earth the like thereof} [al-Talaq 12]. He said: Seven earths, in every earth there is a prophet like your prophet, and Adam like Adam, and Noah like Noah, and Abraham like Abraham, and Jesus like Jesus."],[3810,"\"In every land, towards Ibrahim.\""],[3811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a female slave with whom he had relations. ʿAʾishah and Hafsah kept at him until he made her forbidden upon himself. So Allah revealed this verse: {O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you, seeking the pleasure of your wives?} [al-Tahrim 1] to the end of the verse."],[3812,"A man came to him and said: 'I have made my wife forbidden to me.' He said: 'You have lied; she is not forbidden to you.' Then he recited this verse: {O Prophet, why do you forbid what Allah has made lawful for you, seeking} [al-Tahrim 1] the verse."],[3813,"\"Teach yourself and your family the good.\""],[3814,"The stones that Allah has named in the Qurʾan: {Its fuel is people and stones} [al-Tahrim 6] are stones of sulfur that Allah created with Him as He willed, or as He willed."],[3815,"A young man from the Ansar was overcome by fear of the Fire. He would weep whenever the Fire was mentioned, until that kept him confined to his house. This was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he came to the house. When he entered upon him, the young man embraced him and fell down dead. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Prepare your companion for burial, for fear of the Fire has split his liver.'"],[3816,"I performed the Hajj once and stayed in one of the streets of Kufa. I went out on a dark night, and suddenly there was a caller crying out in the middle of the night, saying: 'My God, by Your might and majesty, I did not intend by disobeying You to oppose You. I disobeyed You when I disobeyed You, and I am not ignorant of that, but a sin presented itself, aided by my wretchedness, and Your covering that You let down over me deceived me. I disobeyed You in my ignorance, and I opposed You in my ignorance. Now who can rescue me from Your punishment, and to whose rope can I cling if You cut Your rope from me? Alas for my youth, alas for my youth!' When he finished his words, I recited a verse from the Book of Allah: {Protect yourselves and your families from a Fire whose fuel is people and stones, over which are angels, stern and severe} [al-Tahrim 6]. Then I heard a violent movement, and after that I heard no sound. I went on. The next day I returned to my path, and there I saw a funeral bier that had been laid out, and an old woman. I asked her about the matter of the deceased, and she did not know me. She said: 'A man passed by here last night – may Allah not reward him except with what he deserves for my son. My son was standing praying, and he recited a verse from the Book of Allah. When my son heard it, his bile vessel burst, and he fell down dead.'"],[3817,"That a servant commits a sin, then repents and does not return to it. Its chain of narration is authentic, but the two shaykhs did not include it. Authentic."],[3818,"Sincere repentance expiates every sin, and it is in the Qurʾan. Then he recited: {O you who believe, turn to Allah in sincere repentance; perhaps your Lord will expiate for you your evil deeds} [al-Tahrim 8]."],[3819,"From Ibn Abbas regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ: {On the Day when Allah will not disgrace the Prophet and those who believed with him. Their light will run before them and on their right; they will say, ‘Our Lord, perfect for us our light’} [al-Tahrim 8]. He said, “There is no one among the monotheists but will be given a light on the Day of Resurrection. As for the hypocrite, his light will be extinguished, and the believer will be fearful because of what he sees of the extinguishing of the hypocrite’s light, so he will say, {‘Our Lord, perfect for us our light’} [al-Tahrim 8].”"],[3820,"{The two betrayed them} [al-Tahrim 10]. He said, “They did not commit adultery. As for the wife of Noah, she used to tell people that he was insane; and as for the wife of Lot, she used to point out the guests. That was their betrayal.”"],[3821,"The wife of Pharaoh used to be tortured in the sun; when they left her, the angels shaded her with their wings, and she saw her house in Paradise."],[3822,"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \"When I was taken on the Night Journey, I passed by a pleasant fragrance and asked: 'What is this fragrance?' They replied: 'This is the fragrance of the comb of the daughter of Pharaoh, and her children used to comb her hair. When the comb fell from her hand, she said: 'In the name of Allah!' Her daughter asked: 'Is it for my father?' She replied: 'No, not for your father, but for my Lord and your Lord, and the Lord of your father.' Her daughter said: 'I will inform my father about this.' So she told Pharaoh, who summoned her and her children, and asked her: 'What do you want?' She replied: 'Gather my bones and the bones of my children, and bury us all together.' He acknowledged the truth in her request and brought her children to throw them one by one into the grave, until the last one was her young breastfeeding son. He said to her: 'Be patient, O mother, for you are upon the truth.' Then she was thrown into the grave along with her son.\" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: \"Four people spoke while still children: this child (referring to the son of the woman of Pharaoh), the witness of Joseph, the companion of Jurayj, and Jesus son of Mary, peace be upon them.\""],[3823,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines, then said, “Do you know what this is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “The best of the women of Paradise are Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. Imran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh, along with what Allah has narrated to us of her story in the Quran: {She said, ‘My Lord, build for me a house near You in Paradise, and save me from Pharaoh and his deeds, and save me from the wrongdoing people’} [al-Tahrim 11].”"],[3824,"“The best of its women is Maryam bt. Imran, and the best of its women is Khadijah.”"],[3825,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A surah of the Book of Allah ﷻ, which is only thirty verses, interceded for a man and brought him out of the Fire and admitted him into Paradise.”"],[3826,"A man is brought in his grave, and his legs are approached, and his legs say, “You have no way over what is on my side; he used to stand and recite Surah al-Mulk with me.” Then he is approached from the side of his chest—or he said, his belly—and it says, “You have no way over what is on my side; he used to recite Surah al-Mulk with me.” Then his head is approached, and it says, “You have no way over what is on my side; he used to recite Surah al-Mulk with me.” He said: “So it is the protector; it prevents the punishment of the grave. And in the Torah it is Surah al-Mulk. And whoever recites it in a night has done much and been extensive.”"],[3827,"Indeed, the first thing that Allah created was the pen. He said to it, \"Write.\" It asked, \"What should I write?\" He replied, \"Write the destiny.\" From that day, everything that exists will continue until the Day of Judgment. It is said that His throne was over the water, and the steam from the water rose and the skies were created. Then He created the \"Noon\" and spread the earth upon it. The earth rested upon the back of the Noon and the Noon shuddered. The earth solidified and was established with mountains. Indeed, the mountains elevate on the surface of the earth."],[3828,"“And what they write.”"],[3829,"I asked Aishah, “O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” She said, “Do you recite the Quran?” I said, “Yes.” She said, “The character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the Quran.”"],[3830,"\"He is known for his evil deeds, just as a sheep is known by its wool.\""],[3831,"He recited this verse: {withholder of good, transgressor, sinful, churlish, and after all that, an ignoble outcast} [al-Qalam 13], then said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, “The people of the Fire are every cruel, arrogant, self-conceited hoarder; and the people of Paradise are the weak and the oppressed.”"],[3832,"that he (Ibn ʿAbbās) asked regarding [Allah's] statement ﷻ, 'The day the shin will be exposed' (Qalam 68:42), he said: 'If something is hidden from the Quran for you then seek it in poetry, for it is the dīwān (register) of the Arabs.'As you've heard the poet saying: [..poetry omitted..], Ibn ʿAbbās said: 'This is the day of distress and severity.'[1]"],[3833,"\"Mutatābi‘ātin\" translates to \"successive\" in English."],[3834,"“They will have upon them dust of humility and disgrace. This is their recompense, the words of Allah Almighty: 'On the Day the faces will be humbled, burdened by dust.'” [Surah Abasa, 41]"],[3835,"\"Eight angels in the form of wheels, with their rims reaching to their knees, journeyed for a distance of sixty-three years.\""],[3836,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Bathaʾ when a cloud passed by. He looked at it and said to them, “Do you know the name of this?” They said, “Yes, it is a cloud (al-saḥāb).” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “And al-muzn.” They said, “And al-muzn.” He said, “And al-ʿanānah.” Then he said, “Do you know the distance between heaven and earth?” They said, “No.” He said, “The distance between them is one, or two, or seventy-three years. And the heaven above it is like that, and Allah is above that; nothing of the deeds of the children of Adam is hidden from Him. And in the seventh heaven there are eight mountain goats; between their hooves and their knees is like the distance between one heaven and the next.”"],[3837,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding {with water like molten brass} [al-Kahf 29]. He said, “Like the dregs of oil; when it is brought near him, the skin of his face falls off. If a bucket of ghislin were poured into this world, it would stink for the people of the world.”"],[3838,"\"Then We will cut from it the [life] artery.\" [Al-Haqqah 46]He said, \"The arteries of the heart.\""],[3839,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Then We would have cut from him the aorta} [al-Haqqah 46]. He said, “It is the vein of the heart that is in the back.”"],[3840,"\"What are the khātūn? They are khāti'ūn (sinners). What are the ṣābūn? They are ṣābi'ūn.\""],[3841,"\"O Allah, if this is the truth from You, then rain upon us stones from the sky.\""],[3842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {So what is [the matter] with those who disbelieve, hastening [from] before you, [O Muhammad], [divided] to the right and to the left in groups? Does every person among them aspire to enter a garden of pleasure? No! Indeed, We have created them from that which they know.} Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat on his palm and said: \"Allah says: O son of Adam, how can you defy Me when I created you from something like this, until when I fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked between two garments [i.e., with arrogance], and the earth [resounds] with your heavy tread—meaning a complaint—so you gathered and withheld, until when it [the soul] reaches the collarbones, you say, 'I will give charity,' but how [can there be] a time for charity?\""],[3843,"“His face was toward the Throne and the back of his neck toward the earth.”"],[3844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not recite upon the jinn nor did he see them. However, he set out with a group of his companions, intentionally, to the market of `Ukaz, which was blocked off by the Shayateen (devils). The shooting stars were sent upon them, so they returned to their people and said, \"What is wrong with you?\" They replied, \"There is a barrier between us and the news from the heavens, and shooting stars were sent upon us.\" They said, \"This is nothing but something that has happened. So go forth to every corner of the earth and look at what has happened.\" So, they went forth in all directions, striking the eastern and western parts of the earth, seeking to find out what had happened between them and the news from the sky. When they returned to their people, they said, \"Indeed, we have heard a wonderful Quran which guides to righteousness, so we have believed in it and will never associate anything with our Lord. Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, then revealed, \"Say: It has been revealed to me that a group of jinn listened and said, 'Indeed, we have heard a wonderful Quran which guides to righteousness, so we have believed in it and will never associate anything with our Lord.'\" (Quran, Surah Al-Jinn, ayah 2)"],[3845,"He heard Abdullah bin Mas'ood saying: \"Verily, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions while he was in Makkah: 'Whoever of you wants to meet the emissaries of the jinn tonight, let him do so.' None of them (except me) came, so we set out until we reached the highest point in Makkah. He drew a line with his foot and commanded me to sit on it. Then he went on until he stood and began reciting the Quran. A cloud overshadowed him and covered him with so many dark layers that I could not hear his voice. Then they departed and dispersed like pieces of scattered clouds, going away. Only a few of them remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished praying before dawn and left. He appeared again and asked me, 'What happened to the emissaries?' I replied, 'They are there, O Messenger of Allah.' So he took bones and the dung and gave them to them as provisions. Then he forbade anyone of them to use bones or dung for personal use.'"],[3846,"\"Regarding the remembrance of his Lord, he (the disbeliever) will be subjected to an escalating torment.\" [Quran 17:47] He said, \"A mountain in Hell.\""],[3847,"Regarding His saying, the Most High: {They were almost upon him in crowds} [Al-Jinn 19], he said: “They would bow when he bowed and prostrate when he prostrated—meaning the jinn.”"],[3848,"About the reading of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , she said, when the verse {O you who wraps himself [in clothing], arise [to pray] the night, except for a little -} [Al-Muzzammil 2] was revealed, they stood in prayer for a year until their feet swelled. So, Allah, the Exalted and Mighty, revealed {So recite what is easy [for you] of the Qur'an. He knew that there would be among you those who are ill.}"],[3849,"About the standing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: “Do you not recite, 'O you who wraps himself'?” I said, “Yes.” She said: “That is his standing.”"],[3850,"“You have been wrapped in this matter, so arise with it.”"],[3851,"When the first part of Al-Muzzammil was revealed, they would stand [in prayer] approximately like their standing during the month of Ramadan, until its last part was revealed. He said: “And between its first and last part was about a year.”"],[3852,"The Prophet ﷺ, when revelation came to him while he was on his she-camel, she would place her neck on the ground and could not move. She recited the word of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime: {Indeed, We will cast upon you a heavy word} [Al-Muzzammil 5]."],[3853,"From ʿAbd Allāh: {Indeed, the night rising} [Al-Muzzammil 6], he said: “It is, in Ethiopian, standing at night.”"],[3854,"“A thorn that seizes the throat, neither entering nor exiting.” And regarding His saying, the Most High: {a heap of sand pouring down} [Al-Muzzammil 14], he said: “Al-mahīl is that which, when you take something from it, the rest follows it; and al-kathīb is [a heap] of sand.”"],[3855,"\"You mentioned this matter, so please handle it.\""],[3856,"“From sin.”"],[3857,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “What is the ṣūr?” He said: “A horn that is blown.”"],[3858,"From him, al-Dhahabī in the Talkhīṣ."],[3859,"That al-Walid b. al-Mughirah came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited the Quran to him, and it seemed that he softened towards it. That reached Abu Jahl, so he came to him and said, \"O uncle, your people see that they should gather wealth for you.\" He said, \"Why?\" He said, \"To give it to you, for you went to Muhammad to expose yourself to what he has.\" He said, \"Quraysh knows that I am among the wealthiest of them.\" He said, \"Then say something about him that will reach your people, that you are a denier of him or that you dislike him.\" He said, \"What should I say? By Allah, there is no man among you more knowledgeable about poetry than I, nor more knowledgeable about rajaz or qasidah than I, nor about the poetry of the jinn. By Allah, what he says resembles nothing of this. By Allah, his speech has sweetness, and upon it is a beauty, and it is fruitful at its top and abundant at its bottom, and it ascends and is not ascended upon, and it crushes what is beneath it.\" He said, \"Your people will not be pleased with you until you say something about it.\" He said, \"Leave me so that I may think.\" When he thought, he said, \"This is magic transmitted; he learns it from someone else.\" Then was revealed: {Leave Me with the one I created alone} [Al-Muddaththir: 11]."],[3860,"\"Woe is a valley in Hell into which the disbeliever falls for forty autumns before reaching its bottom. And Sa'ud is a mountain in the Fire, upon which he climbs for seventy autumns, then he falls, and so it is.\""],[3861,"From Ali regarding His ﷻ saying: {Every soul is a pledge for what it has earned, except the companions of the right} [Al-Muddaththir: 39], he said, \"They are the children of the Muslims.\""],[3863,"From Abu Musa regarding His ﷻ saying: {fled from a lion} [Al-Muddaththir: 51], he said, \"The 'qaswarah' are the archers, men of the hunt.\""],[3864,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite: {And you do not will except that Allah wills, He is the One worthy of piety and worthy of forgiveness}. He said, \"Your Lord ﷻ says: I am worthy to be feared, that another god should be made with Me, and I am worthy for whoever fears to make another god with Me, that I forgive him.\""],[3865,"\"From which of them?\" I said, \"From Banu Asad.\" He said, \"From their Haruriyah, or from those whom Allah has blessed?\" I said, \"From those whom Allah has blessed.\" He said, \"Ask.\" I said, \"{I swear by the Day of Resurrection} [Al-Qiyamah: 1].\" He said, \"Your Lord swears by whatever He wills of His creation.\" I said, \"{And I swear by the self-reproaching soul} [Al-Qiyamah: 2].\" He said, \"From the blamed soul.\" I said, \"{Does man think that We will not assemble his bones? Yes, We are Able to restore his fingertips} [Al-Qiyamah: 4].\" He said, \"If He willed, He would make it a hoof or a solid hoof.\" I said, \"{So a dwelling place and a repository} [Al-An'am: 98].\" He said, \"The dwelling place is in the womb, and the repository is in the loins.\""],[3866,"From Ibn Abbas: {Rather man desires to continue in sin} [Al-Qiyamah: 5], he says, \"I will repent later.\" {He asks, 'When is the Day of Resurrection?'} [Al-Qiyamah: 6], \"It will become clear to him when the vision is dazzled.\""],[3867,"From Abdullah regarding His ﷻ saying: {On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come, the faith of a soul will not benefit it if it had not believed before} [Al-An'am: 158], he said, \"The rising of the sun from its west.\" Then he recited this verse: {And the sun and the moon are brought together; on that day man will say, 'Where is the escape?'} [Al-Qiyamah: 10]."],[3868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The lowest rank of the people of Paradise is for a man who looks at his kingdom for a thousand years, seeing its furthest reaches as he sees its closest parts. He looks at his wives, servants, and palaces. The highest rank of the people of Paradise is for the one who looks at the face of Allah Almighty twice every day.\" Israel ibn Yunus transmitted from Thawr from Ibn Umar, who said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The lowest rank of the people of Paradise is for the one who looks at his kingdom for a thousand years, and the highest rank is for the one who looks at the face of Allah Almighty twice every day.' Then he recited: 'Faces that Day will be radiant, looking at their Lord' (Quran 75:22), and 'To their Lord, on that Day, the gazes will be cast' (Quran 75:23). He said, 'They will look at the face of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, every day.'\""],[3869,"I said to Ibn Abbas: {Woe to you, then woe} [Al-Qiyamah: 34], is it something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said or something Allah revealed? He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it, then Allah revealed it.\""],[3870,"Indeed, when the Prophet ﷺ read the verse \"Is not He capable of reviving the dead?\" (Qiyamah 40), he said \"yes.\" And when he read the verse \"Is not Allah the wisest of judges?\" (At-Tin 8), he also said \"yes.\""],[3871,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: \"Has there come upon man a period of time when he was not a thing mentioned?\" until he completed it. Then he said, \"I see what you do not see, and I hear what you do not hear. The heaven creaked, and it rightfully creaked, for there is no space in it the width of four fingers except that an angel is placing his forehead prostrating to Allah. By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would not enjoy women on beds, and you would go out to the open spaces crying out to Allah. By Allah, I wish I were a tree that is cut down.\""],[3872,"Regarding His ﷻ saying: {And its clusters will be made to hang low} [Al-Insan: 14], he said, \"They will be made low for them, so they will take from them as they wish.\""],[3873,"He mentioned the mounts of the people of Paradise, then recited: {And when you look there, you will see bliss and a great kingdom} [Al-Insan: 20]."],[3874,"On the authority of Abu Hurayrah regarding His ﷻ saying: {And those sent forth in goodness} [al-Mursalāt: 1], he said: “They are the angels sent with what is right.”"],[3875,"\"The Winds\""],[3876,"Regarding this verse: {Indeed, it throws off sparks [as big] as palaces} [al-Mursalāt: 32], he said: “In the pre-Islamic era we used to cut wood into two or three cubits and raise it up in winter, and we called it a palace (al-qaṣr).” He said: And I heard Ibn ʿAbbās when he was asked about {Yellow camels} [al-Mursalāt: 33], he said: “The ropes of ships, joined one to another until they become like the middles of camel saddles.”"],[3877,"“When Allah wanted to create the creation, He sent the wind, and it drew the water until it exposed a projection, which is beneath the Kaʿbah. Then He spread out the earth until it reached whatever length and breadth Allah willed.” He said: It extended like this—and Ibn ʿAbbās showed me with his hand, like this and like this—he said: “Then Allah made the mountains as firm anchors and pegs.” Abu Qubays was among the first mountains placed on the earth."],[3878,"Regarding His, the Exalted's, saying: {They will remain therein for ages} [al-Nabaʾ: 23], he said: “An age (ḥuqb) is eighty years.”"],[3879,"I heard Al-Abbas say, \"Give us the water and quench our thirst.\""],[3880,"“The speech of the son of Adam is not for him except commanding what is right, forbidding what is wrong, or remembering Allah.”"],[3881,"“Death.” Authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not record it according to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3882,"The Prophet ﷺ, when a quarter of the night had passed, used to say, \"O people, remember Allah's favor on you. O people, remember that the shaking (of the Hour) will come after which comes calmness. Then the second shaking comes after which comes calmness. Then a third shaking will come and it will be followed by a calamity whose magnitude is beyond description. Then the Hour will be established with its signs.\" Ubayy bin Ka'b said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I invoke salutations upon you frequently. How much of my supplication should I devote to you?\" He said, \"As you like.\""],[3883,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the Hour until it was revealed to him: {They ask you about the Hour, when is its arrival? In what [capacity] are you to mention it? To your Lord is its final end} [al-Nāziʿāt: 43]. He said: “So it ceased.”"],[3884,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and kept saying, “Guide me.” She said: And with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were some of the prominent polytheists. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to turn away from him and face the other, saying, “Do you see any harm in what I say?” and the other would say “No.” So concerning this was revealed: {He frowned and turned away}."],[3885,"“All of this we have already known, so what is al-abb?” Then he broke a stick that was in his hand and said: “This, by the life of Allah, is artificiality. Follow what has been made clear to you from this Book.”"],[3886,"“People will be resurrected barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised. Sweat will bridle them and reach the lobes of their ears.” She said: I said: “O Messenger of Allah, how terrible! Some of us will look at one another.” He said: “People will be too preoccupied for that.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {On the Day a man will flee from his brother, and his mother and his father, and his wife and his children. For each one of them that Day will be a matter occupying him.}"],[3887,"\"They will be covered with dust on the faces of the disbelievers, not on the faces of the believers.\" And this is the saying of Allah Almighty, \"On the Day the faces will be covered with dust, covered with darkness.\" [Surah 'Abasa, 41]"],[3888,"“Whoever loves to look at the Day of Resurrection, let him recite: {When the sun is wrapped up}.”"],[3889,"“The gathering of beasts is their death, and the gathering of every thing is death except for the jinn and mankind.”"],[3890,"\"They are the two men who are doing the work that leads them to enter both Paradise and Hell. The wicked will be with the wicked, and the righteous will be with the righteous.\""],[3891,"Regarding His ﷻ saying: {So I swear by the receding stars, the running ones, the hidden} [al-Takwīr 16], he said: \"They are the wild cattle.\""],[3892,"When 'Uthman was killed, that terrified me greatly, so I came to 'Ali. While I was with him, a man asked him: What are {the running ones, the hidden} [al-Takwīr 16]? He said: \"The stars.\""],[3893,"\"Yes, this is the time of Witr prayer, then recite (And by the night when it passes away, and by the dawn when it breathes) [Al-Takweer, 18]. 'It is correct with the condition of a Muslim and they did not leave it.'\""],[3894,"A beggar stood during the time of the Prophet ﷺ and asked, and the people remained silent. Then a man gave him something, so the people gave him. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever initiates a good practice and it is followed, he will have its reward and the like of the rewards of those who follow him, without diminishing their rewards in any way. And whoever initiates an evil practice and it is followed, he will bear its burden and the like of the burdens of those who follow him, without diminishing their burdens in any way.\" He said: Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman then recited: {A soul will know what it has sent forward and left behind} [al-Infiṭār 5]."],[3895,"\"It is a man who hires another man or a measurer, knowing that he will be unfair in his measuring, so his sin is upon him.\" Ibrahim b. Yazid is weak."],[3896,"“When the believer commits sin, a black spot appears on his heart. If he repents and gives up that sin and seeks forgiveness, his heart will be polished. But if (the sin) increases, (the black spot) increases. That is the Ran that Allah mentions in His Book: “Nay! But on their hearts is the Ran (covering of sins and evil deeds) which they used to earn.” [83:14] (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4244)"],[3897,"\"A mixture, not a seal that seals.\""],[3898,"Regarding His ﷻ saying: {When the sky is split open and it has listened to its Lord and has been made fit} [al-Inshiqāq 2], he said: I heard: {And when the earth is spread out} [al-Inshiqāq 3], he said: \"On the Day of Resurrection.\" {And it casts out what is in it and becomes empty} [al-Inshiqāq 4], he said: \"It brings out the dead that are in it.\""],[3899,"The House was two thousand years before the earth. \"So when the earth is spread out,\" he said, \"from beneath it, an extension.\""],[3900,"\"Three qualities: whoever has them, Allah will reckon him with an easy reckoning and admit him to Paradise by His mercy.\" They said: For whom, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"You give to the one who deprived you, you pardon the one who wronged you, and you maintain ties with the one who cut you off.\" He said: If I do that, what will I get, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"You will be reckoned with an easy reckoning and Allah will admit you to Paradise by His mercy.\""],[3901,"From 'Abdullah regarding His ﷻ saying: {You will surely ride stage after stage} [al-Inshiqāq 19], he said: \"The sky.\""],[3902,"Regarding His ﷻ saying: {You will surely ride stage after stage} [al-Inshiqāq 19], he said: meaning your Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"State after state.\""],[3903,"From Abū Hurayrah: As for 'Ali, he raised it to the Prophet ﷺ, and as for Yūnus, he did not count Abū Hurayrah in this verse: {And a witness and one witnessed} [al-Burūj 3]. He said: \"The witness is the Day of 'Arafah and the Day of Jumu'ah, and the one witnessed is the promised Day of Resurrection.\" The hadith of Shu'bah from Yūnus b. 'Ubayd is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it on the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[3904,"An oath: {By the sky with its constellations} [al-Burūj 1], {Indeed, the seizure of your Lord is severe} [al-Burūj 12] until the end of it."],[3905,"Indeed, among what Allah created is a Preserved Tablet of a white pearl, whose two covers are of red ruby; its pen is light and its writing is light. He looks into it every day three hundred and sixty looks—or times—and in each of those times He creates, provides, gives life, causes death, honors, humbles, and does whatever He wills. That is His saying: {Every day He is upon a task}."],[3906,"\"The crucifixion\" [Al-Tariq 7] is the crucifixion, and \"the bars\" [Al-Tariq 7] are four sides beneath the ribs."],[3907,"Al-maṭar (the rain). {And by the earth that cracks open} [86:12] he said, \"That which produces plants.\""],[3908,"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in Witr prayer, in the first Rak'ah, \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High.\" In the second Rak'ah, he would recite \"Say: O disbelievers.\" In the third Rak'ah, he would recite \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak.\" Lastly, he would recite \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.\""],[3909,"We asked Aisha, \"What used to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite during the Witr prayer?\" She replied, \"In the first Rak'ah, he used to recite Surah Al-A'la (the Most High), in the second Rak'ah, Surah Al-Kafirun (the Disbelievers), and in the third Rak'ah, Surah Al-Ikhlas (the Unity) along with Surah Al-Falaq (the Dawn) and Surah An-Nas (Mankind).\" Sa'id ibn Kathir ibn 'Ufair, who is a narrating authority among the people of Egypt, mentioned this Hadith and narration. I requested it at the time when I was writing a book about Witr prayer, but I did not find it. Later, I found it after Adh-Dhahabi stopped commenting on it in his summary."],[3910,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform two units of prayer, followed by Witr prayer wherein he would recite after them \"Exalt the name of your Lord, the Most High\" and \"Say: O disbelievers!\" And in Witr prayer, he would recite \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak\" and \"Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind.\""],[3911,"When he recited {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} [87:1], he said, \"Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, who created and proportioned.\" He said, \"And this is the recitation of Ubayy b. Kaʿb.\""],[3912,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, when he recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' [87:1], would say, {We will make you recite, so you will not forget} [87:6]—he said, \"He remembers the Qur'an out of fear of forgetting it.\" He said: And I heard Saʿd recite {Whatever verse We abrogate or cause to be forgotten} [2:106]. I said, \"But Saʿīd b. al-Musayyib recites 'or cause it to be forgotten'.\" Saʿd said, \"The Qur'an did not descend upon al-Musayyib nor upon the family of al-Musayyib. Allah, Exalted is He, said, {We will make you recite, so you will not forget} [87:6], and He said, {And remember your Lord when you forget} [18:24].\""],[3913,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb passed by a monk's monastery and called out, \"O monk! O monk!\" He said: So the monk looked down at him, and ʿUmar began to look at him and weep. He said: It was said to him, \"O Commander of the Faithful, what makes you weep over this man?\" He said, \"I remembered the saying of Allah, Exalted is He, in His Book: {Laboring, exhausted, entering a blazing Fire, given to drink from a boiling spring} [88:3–5]. That is what made me weep.\" This is an anecdote in its proper place, for Abū ʿImrān al-Jawnī did not meet the time of ʿUmar. Al-Jawnī did not meet ʿUmar, but it is an anecdote in its proper place."],[3914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I have been commanded to fight the people until they say, 'There is no god but Allah.' When they say it, they protect from me their blood and their property, except for its due right, and their reckoning is upon Allah.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {You are not over them a tyrant, except for those who turn away and disbelieve—Allah will punish them with the greatest punishment} [88:21–24]."],[3915,"The dawn of the day. {And by ten nights} [89:2] he said, \"The ten of al-Aḍḥā (the Festival of Sacrifice).\""],[3916,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about \"Ash-Shafi' and Al-Witr\" [Al-Fajr 3], he said, \"They are both parts of the prayer.\""],[3917,"\"And Pharaoh commanded his wife to be tied to four stakes, then he placed a massive millstone on her back until she died.\""],[3918,"The oath: {Indeed, your Lord is ever on the watch} [89:14]. The crossing of the Ṣirāṭ consists of three bridges: a bridge over which is the trust, a bridge over which is the ties of kin, and a bridge over which is the Lord, Exalted is He."],[3919,"\"To create whatever he wishes in it.\""],[3920,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And by the parent and what he begot} [90:3], he said, \"By 'the parent' He means Adam, and 'what he begot' means his offspring.\""],[3921,"In the hardship of his creation: in his birth, the growth of his teeth, his stages, his livelihood, and his circumcision."],[3922,"On the authority of ʿAbd Allāh: {And We guided him to the two paths} [90:10], he said, \"Good and evil.\""],[3923,"Among the things that make forgiveness obligatory is feeding a hungry Muslim."],[3924,"\"The destitute one who has no home.\""],[3925,"\"The dust that nothing protects from dust.\""],[3926,"Regarding His ﷻ saying {And by the sun and its brightness} [Ash-Shams:1], he said: \"Its light.\" {And by the moon when it follows it} [Ash-Shams:2]: \"It follows it.\" {And by the day when it displays it} [Ash-Shams:3], he said: \"It illuminates it.\" {And by the sky and He who built it} [Ash-Shams:5], he said: \"Allah built the sky.\" {And by the earth and He who spread it} [Ash-Shams:6], he said: \"He spread it out.\" He said: {And by the soul and He who proportioned it, and inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness} [Ash-Shams:8]: \"He made it know its wretchedness and its happiness.\" {He has succeeded who purifies it, and he has failed who buries it} [Ash-Shams:9], he said: \"He led it astray.\""],[3927,"Regarding His ﷻ saying {And inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness} [Ash-Shams:8], he said: \"He made it adhere to its wickedness and its righteousness.\""],[3928,"\"Six whom I have cursed and Allah has cursed, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: the one who adds to the Book of Allah, the one who denies Allah's decree, the one who dominates with tyranny to humiliate those whom Allah has honored and honor those whom Allah has humiliated, the one who abandons my Sunnah, the one who makes lawful from my progeny what Allah has forbidden, and the one who makes lawful the sanctuary of Allah.\""],[3929,"\"Six whom I have cursed and Allah has cursed, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: the one who adds to the Book of Allah, the Exalted, the one who denies Allah's decrees, the one who dominates with tyranny to humiliate those whom Allah has honored and honor those whom Allah has humiliated, the one who makes lawful the sanctuary of Allah, the one who makes lawful from my progeny what Allah has forbidden, and the one who abandons my Sunnah.\""],[3930,"Abu Quhafah said to Abu Bakr: \"I see you freeing weak slaves. If you do what you do, you should free strong men who can protect you and stand in your defense.\" Abu Bakr said: \"O my father, I only desire what I desire because of what was revealed about this: {As for him who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the best, We will ease him toward ease} [Al-Layl:6] up to His ﷻ saying {And no one has with him any favor to be repaid, except seeking the face of his Lord, the Most High. And he will soon be pleased}.\""],[3931,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shown what would be opened for his nation after him, and he rejoiced at that.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: \"By the morning brightness and by the night when it covers,\" up to His saying {And your Lord will soon give you, and you will be pleased} [Ad-Duha:5]. He said: \"So He gave him a thousand palaces in Paradise of pearl, whose dust is musk, in each palace what is fitting for him.\""],[3932,"I asked Allah for something that I wish I had not asked. I mentioned the messengers of my Lord and said: \"O Lord, You subjected the wind to Solomon and You spoke to Moses.\" Then He, Blessed and Exalted, said: \"Did I not find you an orphan and give you refuge, and found you lost and guided you, and found you poor and enriched you?\" I said: \"Yes,\" so I wished I had not asked Him."],[3933,"When {May the hands of Abu Lahab perish, and he perished} was revealed up to {and his wife, the carrier of firewood, around her neck} [Al-Masad:5], a rope of palm fiber. It was said to the wife of Abu Lahab: \"Muhammad has satirized you.\" She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting in the assembly and said: \"O Muhammad, why do you satirize me?\" He said: \"By Allah, I have not satirized you; only Allah has satirized you.\" She said: \"Have you seen me carrying firewood or seen around my neck a rope of palm fiber?\" Then she left. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained for days without revelation coming to him. She came to him and said: \"O Muhammad, I think your companion has abandoned you and hated you.\" Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {By the morning brightness and by the night when it covers} [Ad-Duha:1]: \"Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor has He hated you.\""],[3934,"When {May the hands of Abu Lahab perish} was revealed, then he mentioned the hadith exactly like it word for word."],[3935,"O youth, seize the opportunity. Rarely does a night pass me except that I recite in it a thousand verses, and I recite Al-Baqarah in a single rak'ah, and I fast the sacred months and three days of every month, and Mondays and Thursdays. Then he recited {And as for the favor of your Lord, report it}."],[3936,"A man from his brothers would meet him and say: \"Allah provided me last night with such-and-such prayer, and provided such-and-such good.\""],[3937,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was approached by Jibril while he was playing with the boys. He seized him, threw him down, split open his heart, and extracted from it a clot of blood, saying, \"This is the share of Satan in you.\" He said: Then he washed it in a basin of gold with Zamzam water, then repaired it and returned it to its place. He said: The boys came running to his mother—meaning his wet nurse—and said, \"Muhammad has been killed.\" His wet nurse came forward, intending him, and met him returning while his color was drained. Anas said: \"We used to see the mark of the stitching on his chest.\" \"Its chain is correct, but they did not record it.\" And the report from Umar b. al-Khattab and Ali b. Abi Talib is established: \"A hardship will never overpower two eases.\" And it has been narrated with a mursal chain from the Prophet ﷺ, authentic according to the condition of Muslim."],[3938,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Exalted and Glorified be He, “Indeed, with hardship there is ease” [Ash-Sharh 6], it is related that the Prophet ﷺ went out one day cheerful and happy, laughing, and saying: “One hardship will never overcome two eases: ‘So indeed, with hardship there is ease. Indeed, with hardship there is ease’” [Ash-Sharh 6].[1]"],[3939,"Regarding His ﷻ saying {By the fig and the olive} [al-Tin 1], he said: \"The fruit that people eat.\" {And Mount Sinin} [al-Tin 2], he said: {the Mount} [al-Baqarah 63] is the mountain, and {Sinin} [al-Tin 2], he said: \"The blessed.\""],[3940,"Whoever recites the Quran will not be sent back to the worst of age, such that he would not know after having knowledge anything. That is His ﷻ saying {Then We returned him to the lowest of the low, except those who believe} [al-Tin 6]. He said: except those who recite the Quran."],[3941,"\"The first surah revealed of the Quran was 'Read in the name of your Lord who created.'\""],[3942,"\"The first surah revealed of the Quran was 'Read in the name of your Lord.'\""],[3943,"He was at Hira when the angel came to him with a piece of silk brocade, on which was written: Read in the name of your Lord who created, up to {what he did not know}."],[3944,"He was at Hira, and he mentioned the first connected hadith, all of whose narrators are trustworthy. I built this book on the principle that an addition from a trustworthy narrator is accepted. As for prostration in {Read in the name of your Lord} [al-Alaq 1], Muslim recorded it from Abu al-Tahir, from Ibn Wahb, from Amr b. al-Harith, from Ubayd Allah b. Abi Ja'far, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, as mursal."],[3945,"\"The decisive prostrations in the Quran are: Alif Lam Mim Tanzil, Ha Mim Tanzil al-Sajdah, al-Najm, and 'Read in the name of your Lord who created.'\" And I am astonished at the one who told me that he does not prostrate in the Mufassal. Authentic."],[3946,"\"The Quran was revealed in one complete sentence on the night of Al-Qadr to the sky of this world, which was in the position of the stars. Allah would reveal it to His Messenger ﷺ bit by bit. Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: 'And those who disbelieved say, \"Why was the Qur'an not revealed to him all at once?\" Thus [it is] that We may strengthen thereby your heart. And We have spaced it distinctly.' [Surah Al-Furqan: 32].\""],[3947,"The Quran was sent down on the Night of Decree from the highest heaven to the lowest heaven all at once, then it was divided over the years. He said: And he recited this verse {No! I swear by the positions of the stars, and indeed it is an oath, if you knew, great.}"],[3948,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Night of Decree? He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about the Night of Decree: is it in Ramadan or outside Ramadan?\" He said, \"Rather, in Ramadan.\" I said, \"Tell me, O Messenger of Allah, is it with the prophets as long as they exist, and when the prophets are taken it is lifted, or is it until the Day of Resurrection?\" He said, \"No, rather until the Day of Resurrection.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me in which Ramadan it is.\" He said, \"In the last ten; do not ask me about anything after this.\" I said, \"I adjure you by my right upon you, O Messenger of Allah, in which ten is it?\" He said: Then he became angry with me, severe anger, such as he had never been angry with me before or after, and he said, \"If Allah willed, He would have informed you of it. Seek it in the last seven; do not ask me about anything after this.\""],[3949,"The Quraysh said to the Jews, \"Give us something we can ask this man about.\" They said, \"Ask him about the Spirit.\" So it was revealed {And they ask you about the Spirit. Say, 'The Spirit is from the command of my Lord, and you have not been given of knowledge except a little.'} [al-Isra 85]. They said, \"We have not been given of knowledge except a little, yet we have been given the Torah, in which is the judgment of Allah. And whoever has been given the Torah has been given much good.\" He said: Then it was revealed {Say, 'If the sea were ink for the words of my Lord, the sea would be exhausted before the words of my Lord are exhausted, even if We brought the like of it as replenishment.'}\""],[3950,"That the Prophet ﷺ recited to him \"Lam yakun\" and recited therein: \"Indeed the religion with Allah is the Hanifiyyah, not Judaism, nor Christianity, nor Zoroastrianism. And whoever does good will never be denied it.\""],[3951,"“Whoever says, ‘I am a believer,’ let him say, ‘I am in Paradise.’” So he said, “Yes.” Then al-Mughirah said: Abu Wa’il Shaqiq b. Salamah recited, “Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book…” up to His statement: {And they were not commanded except to worship Allah, [being] sincere to Him in religion} [al-Bayyinah:5], until His statement, the Most High: {And that is the upright religion} [al-Bayyinah:5]. He recited it while alluding to the Murji’a."],[3952,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Teach me to recite, O Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Recite three of the ones that begin with al-Ra’.” The man said, “I have grown old, my heart has hardened, and my tongue has become thick.” He said, “Recite three of those that begin with Ha-Mim.” He said the same as his first statement. He said, “Recite three of the Musabbihat.” He said the same thing. Then the man said, “O Messenger of Allah, teach me a comprehensive surah.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught him {When the earth is shaken} [al-Zalzalah:1] until he finished it. The man said, “By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never add anything to it.” Then the man turned away, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “The little man has succeeded.” Then he mentioned what would preserve him."],[3953,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {That day it will relate its news} [al-Zalzalah:4]. He said, “Do you know what its news is?” They said, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said, “Indeed, its news is that it will testify against every male and female servant regarding what they did on its surface. It will say, ‘He did such-and-such on such-and-such a day.’ That is its news.”"],[3954,"While Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was eating lunch with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this verse was revealed: {So whoever does an atom’s weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom’s weight of evil will see it} [al-Zalzalah:8]. Abu Bakr stopped and said, “O Messenger of Allah, will we see every evil we have done?” He said, “What you see of what you dislike is how you are repaid. Good is deferred for its recipients in the Hereafter.” Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. It is mursal."],[3955,"\"She is the horse.\" (Al-Adiyat 2) He said, \"When a man covers his horse.\" (Al-Adiyat 3) The horses charge at the enemy, leaving a mark. (Al-Adiyat 4) He said, \"The dust.\" (Al-Adiyat 5) The enemy, indeed, is ungrateful to his Lord. (Al-Adiyat 6) He said, \"Disbelief.\" According to the condition of Bukhari and Muslim."],[3956,"When a believing servant dies, the souls of the believers meet his soul and ask him, “What did so-and-so do?” When he says, “He died,” they say, “He has been taken to his mother, the pit. What a terrible mother and what a terrible nurse.”"],[3957,"He said: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reciting {The mutual rivalry for increase diverts you} [al-Takathur:1], and he was saying: “The son of Adam says, ‘My wealth, my wealth.’ But do you have from your wealth anything except what you ate and consumed, or wore and wore out, or gave in charity and sent forth?”"],[3958,"“I do not fear poverty for you, but I fear for you the rivalry over increase. I do not fear mistakes for you, but I fear deliberate wrongdoing for you.”"],[3959,"He recited: “By time, and the vicissitudes of fate. Indeed, mankind is in loss.”"],[3960,"From Abu Sa’id al-Khudri: {Woe to every scorner and mocker} [al-Humazah:1]. He said, “Woe is a valley in Hell into which the disbeliever falls for forty autumns before the reckoning of people is finished.”"],[3961,"He mentioned the Fire and magnified its matter, and mentioned of it what Allah willed him to mention. Then he said, “Indeed, it will be closed over them in extended columns.”"],[3962,"The companions of the elephant advanced until they drew near Makkah, and ‘Abd al-Muttalib met them and said to their king, “What has brought you to us? We have nothing for you, O our Lord. Did You not send us so that we might bring You whatever You wanted?” He said, “I was told about this House which no one enters except that he is safe, so I came to frighten its people.” He said, “We will bring you whatever you want, so go back.” But he refused except to enter it, and he went on advancing toward it. ‘Abd al-Muttalib stayed behind and stood on a mountain, saying, “I will not witness the destruction of this House and its people.” Then he said: “O Allah, every deity has a sacred place, so protect Your sacred place; let their cunning never overcome Your plan. O Allah, if You act, then command whatever You will.” Then birds in flocks, like a cloud, approached from the direction of the sea until they overshadowed them—the birds that Allah, Exalted is He, mentioned: {Striking them with stones of baked clay} [al-Fil:4]. He said: The elephant began to bellow loudly, {and He made them like eaten straw}."],[3963,"“Allah favored Quraysh with seven qualities: that I am among them, that prophethood is among them, that the Hijabah (care of the Ka’bah) is among them, that the Siqayah (providing water to pilgrims) is among them, that Allah aided them against the elephant, that they worshiped Allah for ten years when no one else worshiped Him, and that Allah revealed a surah of the Quran concerning them.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. {For the security of Quraysh, their security in the winter and summer journeys, let them worship the Lord of this House, who fed them against hunger and secured them from fear}.”"],[3964,"Al-Ma'un is the loaned item. [It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim.]"],[3965,"It is the obligatory zakah. They show off their prayer and withhold their zakah. [This chain is authentic but mursal, for Mujahid did not hear from 'Ali. It is disconnected.]"],[3966,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Al-Kawthar, to which he replied, \"It is a river that Allah has granted me in Paradise. Its soil is musk, its taste is sweeter than honey, and its birds have necks like the necks of camels.\" Abu Bakr said, \"O Messenger of Allah, it is beautiful indeed.\" The Prophet ﷺ replied, \"Its drink is more beautiful than its appearance.\" This hadith was narrated by Muslim from the narration of Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas, when the verse \"Indeed, We have granted you, [O Muhammad], al-Kawthar\" [Quran 108:1] was revealed. It is complete and longer than this, but I have narrated it in the chains of Asim ibn Ali, for Abu Uwais is trustworthy, and Az-Zuhri does not preserve a Mursal hadith from his brother Abdullah. The well-known version of this hadith is from the narration of Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah ibn Muslim, from his father. This hadith is authenticated by Muslim."],[3967,"Al-Kawthar is the abundant good that Allah has given him. Abu Bishr said: I said to Sa'id, 'Some people claim that it is a river in Paradise.' He said, 'The river is part of the abundant good.'"],[3968,"\"From Ali, he said: 'Pray and sacrifice for your Lord.' [Al-Kawthar 2] He said, 'His placement is your right hand over your left hand during salah.' And the second narration, Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the summary.\""],[3969,"\"When this verse was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , it says, 'Indeed, We have granted you, [O Muhammad], al-Kawthar. So pray to your Lord and sacrifice [to Him alone].'\" (Al-Kawthar 2) The Prophet ﷺ asked Gabriel, \"O Gabriel, what is this 'nahirah' that my Lord has commanded me to do?\" Gabriel replied, \"It is not a 'nahirah,' but rather, it is a command that whenever you enter a state of ritual consecration for prayer, you should raise your hands when you say the takbir (saying \"Allahu Akbar\"), when you bow, and when you raise your head after bowing. This is our prayer and the prayer of the angels in the seven heavens.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Raising the hands from the 'istikana' position is what Allah, the Almighty, said, 'But they did not prostrate to Allah when they were able, and they did not do humility.'\" (Al-Mu'minun 76) As for Israel, he is the owner of wonders that should not be relied upon. And the term \"asbigh\" refers to a group of abandoned Shia individuals according to An-Nasai.\""],[3970,"He said to the Prophet ﷺ, 'Command me with something I should say.' He said, 'When you retire to your bed, recite: {Say, O disbelievers} [Al-Kafirun:1] to its end, for it is a disavowal of polytheism.'"],[3971,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to frequently say: 'Glory be to You, our Lord, and praise be to You.' When {When comes the help of Allah and the victory} was revealed, he said: 'Glory be to You, our Lord, and praise be to You. O Allah, forgive me; indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.'"],[3972,"\"Lahab ibn Abi Lahab used to insult the Prophet ﷺ , so the Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Allah, send upon him your dog.'\" Then he went on a caravan intending to go to Sham. He stopped at a place and said, \"I fear the supplication of Muhammad ﷺ .\" They said to him, \"No, do not worry.\" So they set up their belongings around him and sat guarding him. Then a lion came and snatched him and took him away. (This hadith has a sound chain of narration, but it was not included by the compilers of the hadith collections) - Sahih Al-Isnad.\""],[3973,"That he heard it from 'Umar b. Habib. 'Amr b. Habib is weak."],[3974,"I was with Ibn 'Abbas one day when the sons of Abu Lahab came to him disputing about something among themselves. He got up to reconcile between them, and one of them pushed him, so he fell onto the bed. Ibn 'Abbas became angry and said: 'Get out of my sight, you vile earnings!' meaning his offspring, {His wealth and what he has earned will not avail him}."],[3975,"The polytheists said: 'O Muhammad, describe your Lord to us.' Then Allah ﷻ revealed: {Say: He is Allah, the One. Allah, the Eternal Refuge} [Al-Ikhlas:2]. He said: Al-Samad is the One who did not beget {and was not begotten, and there is none comparable to Him} [Al-Ikhlas:3], because nothing is born except that it will die, and nothing dies except that it will be inherited from, and indeed Allah does not die and is not inherited from. {And there is none comparable to Him} [Al-Ikhlas:4]: He said: He has no likeness and no equal, and there is nothing like Him."],[3976,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, shall I recite from Surah Yusuf and Surah Hud?' He said: 'O 'Uqbah, recite with: I seek refuge in the Lord of the daybreak. For you will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah and more effective with Him than it. So if you are able to not let it miss you, then do so.'"],[3977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took her hand and pointed with it to the moon, and said: 'Seek refuge in Allah from the evil of this, for it is the darkness when it settles.' [Its chain is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. It is authentic.]"],[3978,"The Prophet ﷺ came to visit me and said: 'Shall I not treat you with a ruqya with which Jibril ﷺ treated me?' I said: 'Yes, may my father and mother be ransomed for you.' He said: 'In the name of Allah, I treat you, and Allah heals you from every disease in you, from the evil of the blowers on knots, and from the evil of an envier when he envies.' He performed this ruqya three times. [Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis.]"],[3979,"There is no newborn except that on his heart is the whisperer. If he remembers Allah, it withdraws, and if he is heedless, it whispers. That is His saying, Exalted is He: {The whisperer, the withdrawer}."],[3980,"When Allah shaped Adam, He left him, so Iblis began to circle around him, looking at him. When he saw that he was hollow, he said, \"I have gained mastery over him—a creature that cannot control itself.\""],[3981,"Adam dwelt in Paradise only for the time between the afternoon prayer and sunset."],[3982,"\"The first place that Allah sent Adam down to is the land of India.\""],[3983,"\"The most pleasant smell on earth is found in India, where Prophet Adam, peace be upon him, descended. Its trees are made of the fragrance of paradise.\" This is an authentic Hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and Al-Dhahabi did not mention anything about it in his summary."],[3984,"Indeed, when Allah brought Adam out of Paradise, He provisioned him with fruits of Paradise and taught him the craft of everything. So these fruits of yours are from the fruits of Paradise, except that these change while those do not change."],[3985,"The Jews came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the creation of the heavens and the earth. He ﷺ said, \"Allah created the earth on Sunday and Monday, and He created the mountains on Tuesday, and whatever beneficial things are in them. He created the trees, the water, the mines, and the buildings on Wednesday. These are four days.\" Then Allah (ﷻ) said, \"Are you really denying the One who created the earth in two days and make for Him partners? He is the Lord of the worlds. He placed on the earth firm mountains above it and bestowed blessings in it, and determined in it its provisions in four days, equally for those who ask.\" He created the heavens on Thursday and He created the stars, the sun, the moon, and the angels on Friday until the remaining three hours. In the first of these three hours, He decrees the death of those who died, in the second, He inflicts affliction upon everything from which people benefit, and in the third, He admitted Adam into Paradise, ordered Iblis to prostrate to him, and expelled him from Paradise in the last hour. Then the Jews said, \"And what about Muhammad?\" He ﷺ said, \"Then Allah established Himself above the Throne.\" They said, \"You have spoken the truth, if you had completed it.\" He said, \"Then He became angry with a severe anger.\" Then, the verse was revealed: \"And certainly We created the heavens and the earth, and whatever is between them, in six days, and We were not touched with fatigue.\" So have patience over what they say."],[3986,"Adam was a tall man with much hair on his head, as if he were a lofty palm tree."],[3987,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best day on which the sun has risen is Friday. On this day, Adam was created and on this day he was descended to the earth.\""],[3988,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah took the covenant from the back of Adam at 'Arafah, meaning by mentioning the mountain of 'Arafah. Then, He extracted from his loins all of the offspring that He would create and dispersed them before Him like seeds, and then He addressed them from all sides and said: 'Am I not your Lord?' They replied: 'Indeed, we bear witness to it.' [This] He did lest they should say on the Day of Resurrection: 'We were not aware of this.' [This is mentioned] in His saying: 'Or [lest] you say, 'It was only that our fathers associated [others in worship] with Allah before, and we were but descendants after them. Then would You destroy us for what the falsifiers have done?' [Al-A'raf: 172-173] This is an authentic Hadith, and they did not exclude it from their collections.\""],[3989,"Omar ibn al-Khattab was asked about this verse, \"And when your Lord took from the children of Adam - from their loins - their descendants.\" [Al-A'raf: 172]. Omar ibn al-Khattab said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Indeed, Allah created Adam, then He wiped his back with His right hand and brought forth from him his descendants. Then He said, \"I have created these for Paradise and they will do the deeds of the people of Paradise.\" Then He wiped his back and brought forth from him his descendants. He said, \"I have created these for Hellfire, and they will do the deeds of the people of Hellfire.\" Then a man said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about the actions?\" He said, \"When Allah creates a servant for Paradise, He employs him with the deeds of the people of Paradise until he dies upon the actions of the people of Paradise and enters Paradise. And when Allah creates a servant for the Hellfire, He employs him with the deeds of the people of Hellfire until he dies upon the actions of the people of Hellfire and enters the Hellfire.\""],[3990,"\"O Lord, did you not blow into me from Your soul?\" He said, \"Indeed, yes.\" He said, \"O Lord, did You not make me dwell in Your paradise?\" He said, \"Indeed, yes.\" He said, \"O Lord, did Your mercy not precede Your anger?\" He said, \"Indeed, yes.\" He said, \"So if I repent and mend my ways, will I return to Paradise?\" He said, \"Indeed, yes.\" So His saying, \"Then Adam received from his Lord words\" [Quran 2:37]."],[3991,"Hawa's children did not survive for her, so she made a vow that if a child survived for her, she would name him 'Abd al-Harith. Then a child survived for her, and she named him 'Abd al-Harith. That was only from an inspiration of Satan."],[3992,"When Adam died, the angels washed him with water an odd number of times, dug a grave for him, and said, \"This is the sunnah of Adam for his descendants.\""],[3993,"Allah sent Nuh at the age of forty, and he remained among his people for a thousand years less fifty, calling them. He lived after the flood for sixty years until people multiplied and spread.[1]"],[3994,"The children of Nuh are three: Sam, Ham, and Yafith, the father of the Romans.[1]"],[3995,"the leaders of the Prophets are five, and Muḥammad ﷺ is the leader of those five. The five are: Nūḥ, Ibrāhīm, Mūsá, ʿĪsá, and Muḥammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon them all."],[3996,"He mentioned the saying of Allah, exalted is He: {Indeed, We sent Nuh to his people} [Nuh: 1]. He mentioned that Nuh bathed and saw his son looking at him, so he said, \"You look at me while I am bathing? May Allah change your color!\" He said, \"So he turned black, and he is the father of the blacks.\"[1]"],[3997,"Between Nuh and Adam there were ten generations, all of them upon a law of truth. Then they differed, so Allah sent the prophets as bearers of glad tidings and warners.\" He said, \"And likewise in the recitation of 'Abdullah: 'The people were one community, then they differed.'\"[1]"],[3998,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If Allah were to show Mercy to anyone from among the nation of Nūḥ, he would show Mercy to Umm al-Ṣabī (mother of the young boy).\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Nūḥ remained with his nation for a thousand years save fifty inviting them [to the Message] until the end of his time. He planted trees and they became plentiful/large and they [grew] in all different ways. Then he cut them and began to make his ship. [The people] used to pass by and say that he is making a ship on land, how would it sail?' The he would said, 'You will soon find out.'When he was finished with it and 'fār al-tannūr' (commonly interpreted as the bursting of springs from the ground) and the flooding started in the pathways. Umm al-Ṣabī feared for [her child] and she loved him intensely. She left toward the mountain until she reached a third of it. When the water reached it, she left from there until she settled on the two-thirds of the mountain. Then when the water reached it, she left from there until settled on [top] of the mountain. When the water reached up to her neck, she lifted him in her arms until the water washed him away. So if Allah were to show Mercy to anyone among them, he would show Mercy to Umm al-Ṣabī.\"[1]"],[3999,"Our Lord, exalted is He, gathered for Nuh the knowledge of all the past peoples and supported him with a spirit from Him. He called his people secretly and openly for nine hundred and fifty years. Whenever a generation passed, another generation followed it, and it increased them in disbelief and tyranny.[1]"],[4000,"they all attributed this ḥadīth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Allah will call Nūḥ and nation on the Day of Resurrection as the first among the people, and He will say, \"How did you respond to Nūḥ?\" They will say, \"He did not invite us [to Islam], nor he had conveyed [the Message], nor had commanded us to do [works], nor had prohibited us [to do other works.] Then Nūḥ will say, \"O Lord, I called my people with an open Call to the first of them to the last of them, Ummah after Ummah until it reached the end with the seal of the Prophets, Aḥmad. He scribed [the Message], recited it, and believed in it.Then Allah will say to the angels, call Aḥmad and his Ummah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his Ummah will rush with light terminating in front of them. Then Nūḥ will say to Muḥammad and his Ummah, \"Do you know that I conveyed the message to my nation and strove to give them counsel and tried my best that they be saved from the Hellfire [preaching] then privately and publically and 'they did nothing but increasingly avoid my call' (Nūḥ 71:6)?\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his followers will testify, \"We bear witness that you are indeed among the truthful in all that you have said.\"So, the nation of Nūḥ will ask, \"O Aḥmad, how did you and you Ummah come to know this when you and your Ummah are the last of the nations?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ will respond, \"In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful, 'Indeed, We sent Nūḥ to his people, [saying], warn your people before there comes to them a painful punishment. (Nūḥ, 71:1).'\" He will recite the entire Sūrah. When he finishes it, the nation of Nūḥ will say, \"We bear witness 'that this is indeed the true account, and there is no deity except Allah, and Allah is indeed the All-Mighty, the All-Wise. (Āl ʿImrān 3:62)\" Thereupon, Allah ﷻ will say, \"But stand apart today, you criminals. (Yā Sīn 36:59)\" and thus they will be the first to be separated [from the rest destined toward] the Hellfire."],[4001,"He recited this verse: {And do not display yourselves as was the display of the former times of ignorance} [Al-Ahzab: 33]. He said, \"It was between Nuh and Idris, a thousand years. Two clans of the children of Adam, one of them dwelt in the plain and the other dwelt in the mountain. The men of the mountain were handsome, while the women were ugly; and the women of the plain were beautiful, while the men were ugly. Iblis came to a man of the people of the plain in the form of a shepherd boy and produced a sound the like of which the people had never heard. So they adopted a festival to which they gathered once a year. A man from the people of the mountain came upon them while they were at their festival and saw the women and their beauty. He went to his companions and told them about that, so they moved to those women and settled with them, and immorality appeared among them. That is the saying of Allah, exalted is He: {And do not display yourselves as was the display of the former times of ignorance} [Al-Ahzab: 33].\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the summary."],[4002,"He was asked about Idris: who is he, and in what time was he? He said: \"He is the grandfather of Nuh, who is called Khanukh, and he is alive in Paradise.\""],[4003,"Then Allah's Prophet Idris was a fair-skinned man, tall, with a large belly, broad chest, little body hair, and thick hair on his head. One of his eyes was larger than the other, and on his chest there were three white spots that were not leprosy. When Allah saw from the people of the earth what He saw of their oppression and transgression in the matter of Allah, Allah raised him to the sixth heaven. He is the one about whom He says: {And We raised him to a high station}."],[4004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his hand on my head and said: \"This boy will live a century.\" He said: So he lived a hundred years. Al-Waqidi said: Allah ﷻ says: {And many generations between that} [Al-Furqan: 38]. So there were ten generations between Nuh and Adam, and between him and Ibrahim were ten generations. Ibrahim, the Friend of Allah, was born at the beginning of two thousand years from the creation of Adam. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4005,"They will say: O Ibrahim, you are the Friend of the Most Merciful. The inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth have heard of your friendship."],[4006,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say before he passed away: \"Indeed, Allah has taken me as a friend, just as He took Ibrahim as a friend.\""],[4007,"When the Prophet ﷺ saw the images in the House, he did not enter until he ordered them to be erased. He saw Ibrahim and Ismail with divining arrows in their hands, so he said: \"May Allah fight them! By Allah, they never sought omens with divining arrows.\""],[4008,"\"And Ibrahim is the Friend of the Most Merciful, His chosen one, and His Prophet ﷺ, son of Azar, son of Majur, son of Sarugh, son of Ra'u, son of Malih, son of 'Abir, son of Salikh, son of Arfakhshadh, son of Sam, son of Nuh, may the blessings of Allah be upon him.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4009,"A palm appeared from the sky, and between two of its fingers there was a white hair. It began to draw near to Ibrahim's head, then drew nearer, and cast it onto his head, and said: \"Ignite with dignity.\" Then Allah revealed to him to purify himself. He was the first to have gray hair and to be circumcised. Allah sent down to Ibrahim some of what He sent down to Muhammad in the Qur'an. Among what Allah sent down to him were: {The repentant, the worshippers, the praisers, the travelers, the bowers, the prostrators, the commanders of good and the forbidders of evil, and the keepers of Allah's limits; and give glad tidings to the believers} [Al-Tawbah: 112], and {Indeed, the believers have succeeded} [Al-Mu'minun: 1] up to His saying: {Who will inherit Paradise; they will abide therein eternally} [Al-Mu'minun: 11], and the one in Al-Ahzab: {Indeed, the Muslim men and Muslim women} [Al-Ahzab: 35] to the end of the verse, and the one in Sa'ala: {Those who are constant in their prayer} [Al-Ma'arij: 23] up to His saying: {And those who stand firm in their testimonies} [Al-Ma'arij: 33]. No one fulfilled these portions except Ibrahim, the Friend of Allah, and Muhammad, may Allah's blessings be upon them both and upon his family and peace."],[4010,"\"Ibrahim ﷺ was circumcised after one hundred and twenty years with an adze, and he died at the age of two hundred years.\""],[4011,"\"Ibrahim was circumcised after one hundred and twenty years with an adze, then he lived after that eighty years.\""],[4012,"When Ibrahim ﷺ was commanded to build the House, Ismail and Hajar went out with him. When he arrived in Makkah, he saw above his head, in the place of the House, something like a cloud in which there was something like a head. It spoke to him and said: \"O Ibrahim, build upon my shadow or upon my measure, and do not add or subtract.\" When he had built, he left and left behind Ismail and Hajar. That is where Allah ﷻ says: {And when We assigned to Ibrahim the site of the House, saying: Do not associate anything with Me, and purify My House for those who circumambulate, and those who stand, and those who bow and prostrate}."],[4013,"Ibrahim, upon him be blessings and peace, came and found Ismail repairing a house for him behind Zamzam. Ibrahim said to him: \"O Ismail, your Lord has commanded me to build the House.\" Ismail said to him: \"Then obey your Lord in what He has commanded you.\" He said: \"So help me with it.\" He said: So he stood with him. Ibrahim began to build it, and Ismail handed him the stones, and they both said: {Our Lord, accept from us; indeed, You are the Hearing, the Knowing} [Al-Baqarah: 127]."],[4014,"When Ibrahim built the House, Allah revealed to him: 'Proclaim the pilgrimage to the people.' He said: 'Ibrahim said: Verily, your Lord has taken a House and commanded you to perform pilgrimage to it.' So everything that heard him from stone, tree, hill, or dust responded: 'Labbayk Allahumma Labbayk.'"],[4015,"Islam is thirty portions, and no one was tested with this religion and upheld it except Ibrahim ﷺ . Allah Almighty said: {And Ibrahim who fulfilled} [al-Najm: 37], so Allah wrote for him acquittal from the Fire."],[4016,"I heard 'Ali say: 'A man sought forgiveness for his parents while they were polytheists, so I said: Do you seek forgiveness for them while they are polytheists? He said: Ibrahim sought forgiveness for his father. I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Allah revealed: {And Ibrahim's seeking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him} [al-Tawbah: 114]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4017,"The first to speak Arabic and upon whose wording and speech the Book was placed, then made into a single book like 'Bismillah al-Rahman al-Rahim' connected, until his son Isma'il b. Ibrahim (may Allah's blessings be upon them both) separated it."],[4018,"Indeed, for every prophet there are allies from among the prophets, and my ally and close friend is my father Ibrahim. Then he recited: {Indeed, the people most deserving of Ibrahim are those who followed him} [Al 'Imran: 68]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4019,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Indeed, for every prophet there are allies from among the prophets, and my ally and close friend among them is my father Ibrahim.' Then the Prophet ﷺ recited: {Indeed, the people most deserving of Ibrahim} [Al 'Imran: 68] 'to the end of the verse.' The hadith of Abu Nu'aym, if combined with the hadith of al-Waqidi, is authentic, for it must be from Masruq."],[4020,"When you conquer a region, treat the Copts well, for they have a covenant and a tie of kinship. Al-Zuhri said: The kinship is that the mother of Isma'il was from them."],[4021,"Ismail (son of Ibrahim) was a prophet of Allah, who was named \"Sadiq al-Waad\" (the truthful in promise). He was a man of strength who fought against the enemies of Allah, and Allah granted him victory over them. He was fierce in his war against the disbelievers, and he did not fear any blame from anyone when it came to fulfilling the commands of Allah. He had a small head, a thick neck, long arms and legs. He would strike his knees with his hands while standing, and he had small eyes, a long nose, broad shoulders, long fingers, and a prominent physique. He was strong, fierce, and harsh towards the disbelievers. He used to command his family to pray and give Zakaat, and he was pleasing to his Lord. It is said, \"His Zakaat was his sacrifice to Allah from his wealth, and he would not promise anyone anything except that he would fulfill it, so Allah named him Sadiq al-Waad (the truthful in promise). He was a messenger and a prophet.\" The isnad (chain of narration) is weak."],[4022,"The one who was sacrificed is Isma'il."],[4023,"Regarding \"And We ransomed him with a great sacrifice\" [al-Saffat 37:107], he said: \"Isma'il, at the time when Abraham slaughtered the ram.\"[1]"],[4024,"We attended the gathering of Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, and the people discussed Isma'il and Ishaq b. Ibrahim. Some said the sacrificed one is Isma'il, and others said rather Ishaq is the sacrificed one. Mu'awiyah said: 'You have fallen upon an expert. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Bedouin came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I left the lands dry and the water dried up, wealth has perished and families are lost, so give me from what Allah has granted you as spoils, O son of the two sacrificed ones. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and did not object. We said: O Commander of the Faithful, who are the two sacrificed ones? He said: When 'Abd al-Muttalib was ordered to dig Zamzam, he vowed to Allah that if Allah facilitated its matter, he would slaughter one of his children. He brought them out and cast lots among them, and the lot fell upon 'Abdullah. He intended to slaughter him, but his maternal uncles from Banu Makhzum prevented him and said: Appease your Lord and ransom your son. He said: So he ransomed him with one hundred camels. He said: He is the first sacrificed one, and Isma'il is the second.'"],[4025,"The ransomed one is Isma'il, and the Jews claimed that he is Ishaq, and the Jews lied."],[4026,"He said concerning the one whom Allah ransomed with a great sacrifice: 'He is Isma'il.'"],[4027,"Indeed, the one whom Allah commanded Ibrahim to sacrifice from his two sons was Isma'il, and we find that in the Book of Allah in the story of the report about Ibrahim and what he was commanded concerning the sacrifice of his son, that it was Isma'il. That is because Allah says when He finished the story of the sacrificed one from Ibrahim's two sons: {And We gave him glad tidings of Ishaq, a prophet from among the righteous}, then He says: {So We gave her glad tidings of Ishaq, and after Ishaq, Ya'qub}, meaning a son and a son of a son. So He would not command the sacrifice of Ishaq while He had a promise for him from Allah as He had promised, and the one He commanded to sacrifice is none other than Isma'il."],[4028,"I asked Khawwat b. Jubayr al-Ansari about God's sacrifice, which of the two it was. He said: Ishmael. When Ishmael reached seven years, Abraham saw in a dream in his dwelling in Syria that he was sacrificing Ishmael, so he rode to him upon al-Buraq until he came to him and found him with his mother. He took him by the hand and went off with him as he was commanded. Satan came to him in the likeness of a man he recognized and said, \"O Abraham, where are you heading?\" Abraham said, \"For my need.\" He said, \"You intend to sacrifice Ishmael?\" Abraham said, \"Have you seen a father sacrifice his child?\" He said, \"Yes, you.\" Abraham said, \"And why?\" He said, \"You claim that God commanded you to do that.\" Abraham said, \"If God commanded me, we obey God and I do well.\" So he turned away from him. Iblis came to Hagar and said, \"Where has Abraham gone with your son?\" She said, \"He went for his need.\" He said, \"He intends to sacrifice him.\" She said, \"Have you seen a father sacrifice his child?\" He said, \"He claims that God commanded him to do that.\" She said, \"He has done well to obey God.\" Then he caught up with Ishmael and said, \"O Ishmael, where is your father taking you?\" He said, \"For his need.\" He said, \"He is taking you to sacrifice you.\" He said, \"Have you ever seen a father sacrifice his child?\" He said, \"Yes, he.\" He said, \"And why?\" He said, \"He claims that God commanded him to do that.\" Ishmael said, \"He has done well to obey his Lord.\" He said, \"He set out with him until he brought him to Mina where he was commanded, then to the place of slaughtering the sacrificial camels today. He said, 'My son, God has commanded me to sacrifice you.' Ishmael said, 'Obey, for obedience to your Lord is all good.' Then Ishmael said, 'Did you inform my mother of this?' He said, 'No.' He said, 'You did right. I fear she would grieve. But when you bring the knife near my throat, turn away from me, for it is more likely that you will be patient and not see me.' So Abraham did that, and he began to cut his throat, but the cutting was on copper; the blade did not bite. He sharpened it twice or three times on a stone, all that while unable to cut. Abraham said, 'This matter is from God,' and raised his head. There was a mountain goat standing before him. Abraham said, 'Rise, my son, for your ransom has come down.' So he slaughtered it there at Mina. What is wrong with al-Waqidi and the sound collections?"],[4029,"The Prophet of God David said: \"O Lord, I hear people say 'Lord of Isaac'.\" He said: \"Isaac was generous to Me with his own self.\""],[4030,"Sarah was ninety years old and Abraham one hundred and twenty. When the fear left Abraham and the good news of Isaac came to him and he was safe from the one he feared, he said: \"Praise be to God who bestowed upon me in old age Ishmael and Isaac; indeed my Lord hears supplication.\" Gabriel ﷺ came to Sarah with the good news and said: \"Rejoice in a son called Isaac, and after Isaac, Jacob.\" She struck her forehead in amazement, and that is His saying, exalted: {She struck her face} [Al-Dhariyat 29]. She said: \"Shall I bear a child when I am an old woman and this my husband is an old man? This is indeed a strange thing.\" They said: \"Are you amazed at God's command? The mercy of God and His blessings be upon you, people of the house. He is praiseworthy, glorious.\""],[4031,"Then Isaac son of Abraham was the one whom God made a light, a radiance, and a comfort to his parents. He was among the most handsome of people, the most beautiful, and the most eloquent in speech. He was fair, with curly hair and beard, resembling Abraham in form and character. To Isaac were born Jacob and Esau. Jacob was the better of the two, more eloquent, more beautiful, and more charming. Esau had much hair on his head, body, and face."],[4032,"{And We gave him good tidings of Isaac} He said: \"Good news of prophethood; he was given good tidings twice: when he was born and when he was made a prophet.\""],[4033,"Ka'b said to Abu Hurayrah: \"Shall I not tell you about Isaac son of Abraham the prophet?\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"Yes.\" Ka'b said: \"When Abraham saw that he should sacrifice Isaac, Satan said: 'By God, if I do not tempt the family of Abraham at this, I will never tempt any of them.' Satan took the form of a man they recognized. He came until when Abraham went out with Isaac to sacrifice him, he entered upon Sarah, Abraham's wife, and said to her: 'Where has Abraham gone with Isaac this morning?' Sarah said: 'He went for some need of his.' Satan said: 'No, by God, he did not go for that.' Sarah said: 'Then why did he go with him?' He said: 'He went to sacrifice him.' Sarah said: 'There is nothing in that; he would not sacrifice his son.' Satan said: 'Yes, by God.' Sarah said: 'And why would he sacrifice him?' He said: 'He claims that his Lord commanded him to do that.' Sarah said: 'He has done well to obey his Lord if He commanded him that.' Satan left Sarah and caught up with Isaac while he was walking behind his father. He said: 'Where has your father gone with you this morning?' He said: 'He went with me for some need of his.' Satan said: 'No, by God, he did not go with you for some need of his; rather he went to sacrifice you.' Isaac said: 'My father would never sacrifice me.' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'He claims that God commanded him to do that.' Isaac said: 'By God, if He commanded him, he will obey Him.' Satan left him and hurried to Abraham. He said: 'Where have you gone with your son this morning?' He said: 'I went for some need of mine.' He said: 'No, by God, you did not go with him except to sacrifice him.' He said: 'And why would I sacrifice him?' He said: 'You claim that God commanded you to do that.' He said: 'By God, if God has commanded me, I will do it.' He said: 'When Abraham took Isaac to sacrifice him and Isaac submitted, God spared him and ransomed him with a great sacrifice. Abraham said to Isaac: \"Rise, my son, for God has exempted you.\" And God revealed to Isaac: \"I have granted you a supplication that I will answer for you.\" Isaac said: \"I supplicate You to answer me: any servant who meets You from the first and the last, not associating anything with You, admit him to Paradise.\""],[4034,"He said: \"He is Isaac, meaning the sacrificed one.\""],[4035,"\"The sacrificed one is Isaac.\""],[4036,"\"The rock at the foot of Thabir upon which Abraham sacrificed Isaac: a dusty ram descended upon him from Thabir, with a bleating that echoed.\" Then he mentioned a long hadith."],[4037,"The account of Isaac when God commanded Abraham to sacrifice him. God granted Abraham Isaac on the night the angels left him. When he was seven years old, God revealed to Abraham to sacrifice him and make him an offering. In those days the offering was accepted and taken up. Abraham concealed that from Isaac and all people and confided it to a close friend of his. Al-Ghazir al-Siddiq said—and he was the first to believe in Abraham—Siddiq said to him: \"God does not test the likes of you with such a thing, but He wants to try and test you. Do not think ill of God, for God will make you a leader for mankind. There is no might and no power for Abraham and Isaac except with God, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.\""],[4038,"His saying: {And when his Lord tested Abraham with words and he fulfilled them} [Al-Baqarah 124]. He said: \"The rites of Hajj.\""],[4039,"When Sarah died, Abraham married a woman called Hajura. She bore him seven persons: Bafis, Midian, Kaysan, Lut, Sarkh, Umaym, and Na'shan. Wahb also mentioned in this book: Midian is among the ranks of Abraham, and Lut was from them."],[4040,"\"And Lut the Prophet ﷺ was the son of the brother of Ibrahim al-Khalil ﷺ .\" This is a sound chain of transmission, sahih."],[4041,"\"And Lut the Prophet ﷺ is Lut b. Faran b. Azar b. Bakhur, the son of the brother of Ibrahim al-Khalil, and al-Mu'tafikah—they are the people of Lut.\""],[4042,"From Abu Hurayrah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {Or that I could take refuge in a strong support} [Hud 11:80], he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah have mercy on Lut; he used to take refuge in a strong support. And Allah did not send any prophet after him except among a numerous group of his people.\""],[4043,"\"No prophet was ever sent after Lut except among a numerous group of his people.\""],[4044,"\"Lut set out and settled among the people of Sodom, and he found them having intercourse with men. So he settled among them, and Allah sent him to them. He called them and admonished them, and of their story is what Allah narrated in His Book.\""],[4045,"Lut was the Prophet of Allah and the son of the brother of Ibrahim. He was a fair-skinned man with a handsome face, a fine nose, small ears, long fingers, and excellent front teeth. He had the most beautiful smile when he laughed, and he was the most beautiful, most dignified, most judicious, and least harmful to his people. This was when he heard about his people what he heard about the great harm that they intended for him, where he says: {If only I had against you some power or could take refuge in a strong support} [Hud 11:80]."],[4046,"When Ibrahim migrated to the land of Syria and they expelled him from it as a fugitive, he departed with Sarah. She said to him, \"I have given myself to you,\" and Allah revealed to him that he should marry her. That was the first revelation He sent down to him, and Lut believed in him along with a group from his people. He said, \"Indeed, I will emigrate to my Lord. Indeed, He is the Exalted in Might, the Wise.\" So they expelled him from the land of Babylon to the Holy Land until he reached Harran, and they expelled him from there until they pushed him to the Jordan, where there was a tyrant among the tyrants, until Allah crushed him. Then Ibrahim returned to Syria with Lut, and Allah made Lut a prophet and sent him to the Mu'tafikat as a messenger calling to Allah. They were five cities, the greatest of which was Sodum, then 'Amud, then Arum, then Sa'ur, then Sabur. The people of these cities numbered four million. Lut settled in Sodum and stayed among them for more than twenty years, commanding them and forbidding them, calling them to Allah and to His worship, and to abandon the abominations and filthy acts they were upon. Hospitality was made obligatory upon Lut as it was made obligatory upon Ibrahim and Isma'il. His people did not entertain any guest, and they approached the males of the worlds and disregarded women. So Allah reproached them for that through the tongue of their Prophet in the Qur'an, saying: {Do you approach males among the worlds and leave what your Lord has created for you as mates?} [Ash-Shu'ara 26:166]. Wahb said: 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas mentioned that what led them to approach men instead of women was that they had orchards and fruits inside their homes, and orchards and fruits outside along the roadside. A severe drought and famine struck them, so they said to one another, \"If you prevent these exposed fruits from the wayfarers, you will have a livelihood from them.\" They said, \"How can we prevent them?\" Some of them turned to others and said, \"Make it your custom regarding anyone you find in your lands as a stranger whom you do not know: rob him, have intercourse with him, and drag him along. For people will not set foot in your lands if you do that.\" Then Iblis came to them on those mountains in the form of a handsome boy, the sweetest boy people had ever seen, and marked him. They seized him, had intercourse with him, robbed him, and dragged him along. Then he left. So no person came to them except that they did that to him. That remained their custom until Allah sent Lut to them. Lut forbade them from that and warned them of the punishment, and he made excuses to them, saying, \"O my people, indeed you commit an immorality that no one in the worlds has preceded you with.\" Then he mentioned the rest of the hadith from Ibn 'Abbas."],[4047,"When the angels departed from Ibrahim toward the town of Lut and reached it at midday, when they arrived at the river of Sodum, they met the daughter of Lut drawing water for her family (he had two daughters). They said to her, \"O girl, is there a place to stay?\" She said, \"Yes, stay where you are; do not enter until I come to you.\" She went to her father and said, \"O my father, help some young men at the gate of the city; I have not seen faces of people more handsome than theirs. Do not let your people take them and disgrace them.\" His people had forbidden him from hosting any man, to the point that they said, \"If he hosts someone among us, let him host the men.\" So he went to them without informing anyone except the household of Lut. His wife went out and told his people, saying, \"In the house of Lut there are men whose like I have never seen.\" His people came rushing to him. When they came, Lut said to them, \"O my people, fear Allah and do not disgrace me regarding my guest. Is there not among you a right-minded man? These are my daughters; they are purer for you than what you want.\" They said to him, \"Did we not forbid you from hosting men? You know that we have no right to your daughters, and you know what we want.\" When they did not accept what he offered them, he said, \"If only I had against you some power or could take refuge in a strong support,\" meaning, may Allah's prayers be upon him, \"If only I had supporters to help me against you or a clan to protect me from you, they would come between you and what you came wanting from my guests.\" When Lut said, \"If only I had against you some power or could take refuge in a strong support,\" Jibril then spread his wings and blinded their eyes. They left, some stumbling over the tracks of others, blind, saying, \"Flee, flee! In the house of Lut are the most skilled sorcerers on earth.\" That is the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And they had sought from him his guests, so We obliterated their eyes} [Al-Qamar 54:37]. They said, \"O Lut, indeed we are messengers of your Lord; they will never reach you. So set out with your family during a portion of the night and let not any of you turn back, except your wife. Follow the tracks of your family,\" meaning, \"And proceed where you are commanded.\" So Allah brought them out to Syria. Lut said, \"Destroy them now.\" They said, \"We have not been commanded except for the morning. Is not the morning near?\" When it was the time before dawn, Lut and his family went out, except his wife. That is the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {Except the family of Lut; We saved them before dawn} [Al-Qamar 54:34]."],[4048,"\"Hud the Prophet ﷺ was a tough, enduring man.\""],[4049,"\"No nation was destroyed except that its prophet joined them in Makkah and worshiped there until he died. And the grave of Hud is between al-Hijr and Zamzam.\""],[4050,"I heard 'Ali b. Abi Talib say to a man from Hadramawt: \"Have you seen a red sand hill mixed with red clay and many lote trees in such-and-such a region?\" The man said, \"By Allah, O Commander of the Faithful, you describe it as one who has seen it.\" He said, \"No, but I was told about it.\" The Hadrami said, \"What is its matter, O Commander of the Faithful?\" He said, \"In it is the grave of Hud ﷺ.\""],[4051,"Wahb b. Munabbih was asked about Hud: \"Was he the father of al-Yaman who begot them?\" Wahb said: \"No, but he was the brother of al-Yaman, and in the Torah he is traced back to Nuh. When tribalism arose among the Arabs and Mudar boasted of its father Isma'il, al-Yaman claimed Hud as a father so that they would be descendants of the prophets and his offspring among them. But he is not their father; rather, he is their brother. He was sent only to 'Ad.\" Wahb did not name 'Ad, nor did he trace their tribes, nor did he mention their poetry. There was no nation on earth greater in number than them, nor larger in bodies, nor stronger in might. When they saw the wind approaching them, they said to Hud, \"You frighten us with the wind.\" So they gathered their children, wealth, and livestock into a mountain pass, then stood at the entrance of that pass to keep the wind away from their wealth and families. But the wind entered from beneath their feet, between them and the ground, until it uprooted them. Wahb said: When Allah sent to them Hud b. 'Abd Allah b. Rabah b. al-Harith b. 'Ad b. 'Aws b. Iram b. Sam b. Nuh, every sand dune that Allah placed in any part of the lands was a dwelling of 'Ad in its sands. The land of 'Ad was the most fertile land of the Arabs, with the most abundance of water, rivers, and gardens. When Allah became angry with them and they became arrogant toward Allah—and they were people of idols that they worshiped besides Allah—Allah sent upon them the barren wind."],[4052,"«Allah's Prophet Hud was the most resembling of people to Adam (peace be upon them both).»"],[4053,"«That Salih the Prophet ﷺ was from the Arabs. When Allah destroyed 'Ad and their affair came to an end, Thamud flourished after them and were made successors in the earth, and they spread. Then they became arrogant against Allah. When their corruption appeared and they worshipped other than Allah, Allah sent Salih to them. They were an Arab people, and he was of their middle in lineage and their best in position. Their dwellings were al-Hijr to Qar', which is Wadi al-Qura, eighteen miles between al-Hijr and al-Hijaz. Allah sent him to them as a young lad, and he called them to Allah until he became gray-haired and old, and none followed him from among them except a few who were deemed weak. Then 'Ad and Thamud perished, and those of those nations who were from them. They were from the offspring of Lawidh b. Sam b. Nuh, and there was no prophet between Nuh and Ibrahim before him — meaning before Ibrahim — except Hud and Salih.»"],[4054,"«Then Salih was Allah's Prophet ﷺ, and he resembled 'Isa son of Maryam: reddish tending to whiteness, with lank hair.»"],[4055,"«Indeed Allah sent Salih to his people when he had reached the age of puberty. He was a man reddish tending to whiteness, with lank hair. He used to walk barefoot as 'Isa son of Maryam (peace be upon them both) did, not taking sandals, nor anointing himself, nor taking a house or dwelling. He remained with his Lord's she-camel: wherever she turned he turned with her, and wherever she halted he halted with her. He had fasted forty days before the she-camel was hamstrung. On his right hand there was a mole as a sign. He stayed among them forty years calling them to Allah from when he was a lad until he became gray-haired, while they only increased in tyranny.»"],[4056,"The Prophet ﷺ said: «Whoever has prepared food from this water, let him throw it away.» He said: So among them were some who had kneaded dough and some who had mixed hais, and they threw it away."],[4058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, when he came to al-Hijr, after praising and extolling Allah: «To proceed: do not ask your Messenger for signs. These are the people of Salih; they asked their Messenger for a sign, so Allah sent them a she-camel. It used to come down from this mountain pass and go out from this mountain pass, and it drank their water on the day of its watering.» On the condition of Muslim."],[4059,"And Shu'aib b. Mika'il the Prophet ﷺ, Allah sent him as a prophet. Of his account and the account of his people was what Allah mentioned in the Qur'an. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned him, he said: «That is the orator of the prophets,» because of his arguing with his people. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4060,"Regarding His saying ﷻ {And indeed we see you among us as weak} [Hud 91], he said: «Shu'aib was blind.»"],[4061,"Indeed Allah sent Shu'aib to the people of Madyan, and they are the companions of the Aikah. The Aikah was of tangled trees. They were a people who disbelieved in Allah, cheated people in measures and weights, and corrupted their wealth. Allah the Exalted had expanded their provision and spread out their livelihood as a gradual drawing of them, despite their disbelief in Him. Shu'aib said to them: «O my people, worship Allah; you have no god other than Him, and do not diminish the measure and the scale. Indeed I see you in good, and I fear for you the punishment of an encompassing Day.» Of Shu'aib's words to his people and his people's reply to him was what Allah has mentioned in His Book. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4062,"I asked 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas about the destruction of the people of Shu'aib and Allah's saying concerning them: Then the punishment of the Day of Shadow seized them; indeed it was the punishment of a great day. 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas said: «Allah sent upon them severe heat, and it seized their breaths, so they entered the interiors of houses, and it entered upon them the interiors of the houses and seized their breaths, so they went out from the houses fleeing to the desert. Then Allah sent a cloud and it shaded them from the sun, and they found in it coolness and pleasure. So they called to one another until when they gathered beneath it, Allah sent upon them fire.» 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas said: «So that is the punishment of the Day of Shadow; indeed it was the punishment of a great day.»"],[4063,"Allah sent Shu'aib the Prophet ﷺ to two nations: to his people, the people of Madyan, and to the companions of the Aikah. The Aikah was of tangled trees. When Allah willed to punish them, He sent upon them severe heat and raised for them the punishment as if it were a cloud. When it drew near them, they went out to it hoping for its coolness. When they were beneath it, it rained upon them. He said: That is His saying ﷻ {Then the punishment of the Day of Shadow seized them} [al-Shu'ara' 189]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4064,"From Mujahid regarding His saying {the punishment of the Day of Shadow} [al-Shu'ara' 189], he said: «Shadows of the punishment.» Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4065,"that we do with our wealth as we please} [Hud 87] He said: It was part of what he forbade them from clipping dirhams, or he said: cutting dirhams. Then the punishment of the day of the shadow seized them; indeed it was the punishment of a great day. He said: Allah sent to them a shadow of clouds, and Allah sent to the sun, so it burned on the earth, and they all went out to that shadow until when they had all gathered, Allah removed the shadow from them and heated the sun upon them, so they burned as locusts burn in a frying pan. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4066,"“Whoever among the scholars tells you what the punishment of the day of the shadow is, then declare him a liar.”"],[4067,"“Ya'qub, son of Ishaq, son of Ibrahim, is Isra'il (peace be upon them).”"],[4068,"As for the Asbat, they are the sons of Ya'qub: Yusuf, Binyamin, Rubil, Yahudha, Sham'un, Lawi, Dan, and Fahat. They were twelve men from whom Allah spread twelve tribes, whose lineages no one knows except Allah, may He be exalted. Allah Most High said: {And We divided them into twelve tribes, as nations} [Al-A'raf 160]."],[4069,"Ishaq, son of Ibrahim al-Khalil, married a woman and she became pregnant with two boys in one womb. When she was about to give birth, the two boys fought in her womb. Ya'qub wanted to come out before 'Isa, but 'Isa said: By Allah, if you come out before me, I will obstruct the womb of my mother and kill her. So Ya'qub held back and 'Isa came out before him. Ya'qub grabbed the heel of 'Isa and came out, so he was named 'Isa because he disobeyed, and he was named Ya'qub because he came out holding the heel of 'Isa. He was the elder of the two in the womb, but he disobeyed and came out before him. The two boys grew, and 'Isa was the more beloved of them to his father, while Ya'qub was the more beloved of them to his mother. 'Isa was a hunter. When Ishaq grew old, he became blind."],[4070,"“Yusuf and his mother were given half of all beauty.”"],[4071,"“The noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one, son of the noble one: Yusuf, son of Ya'qub, son of Ishaq, son of Ibrahim, the prophet of Allah, son of the prophet of Allah, son of the prophet of Allah, son of the friend of Allah.”"],[4072,"Asma' b. Kharija came to the door of 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud and said: I am the son of noble elders. 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud said: “That is Yusuf, son of Ya'qub, son of Ishaq, son of Ibrahim.”"],[4073,"“Indeed Yusuf ﷺ was thrown into the well when he was twelve years old, and he met his father after eighty years.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4074,"“Beauty was divided: half was given to Yusuf and Sarah, and half to the rest of mankind.”"],[4075,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, while describing Yusuf (Joseph) when he saw him in the third heaven, \"I saw a man whose image resembled that of the full moon on a moonlit night. So I asked Jibril (Gabriel), 'Who is this?' He replied, 'This is your brother Yusuf.' Ibn Ishaq said, 'Allah had granted Yusuf such beauty and dignity that no one before him or after him has been given. It is even said, and Allah knows best, that he was given half of all beauty, and the other half was divided among the people.'\" (There is no mention of this narration by Al-Dhahabi in his summarization)"],[4076,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at the home of a bedouin, who honored him. He said to him: “O bedouin, ask for your need.” He said: O Messenger of Allah, a she-camel with her saddle and some goats for my family to milk. He said it twice. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Are you incapable of being like the old woman of the Children of Israel?” His companions said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the old woman of the Children of Israel? He said: When Musa wanted to travel with the Children of Israel, he lost his way. The scholars of the Children of Israel said to him: We tell you that Yusuf took from us covenants by Allah that we would not leave Egypt until we carried his bones with us. He said: Who among you knows where the grave of Yusuf is? They said: No one knows where the grave of Yusuf is except an old woman of the Children of Israel. So he sent for her and said: Show me the grave of Yusuf. She said: No, by Allah, I will not do it until I am with you in Paradise. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked what she said, but it was said to him: Give her what she asked. So he gave her what she asked. She came to a lake and said: Drain this water. When they drained it, she said: Dig here. When they dug, there were the bones of Yusuf. When they lifted them from the ground, the road became like the light of day."],[4077,"The knowledge and wisdom of Allah remained among the heirs of Ibrahim. Then Allah gave Yusuf b. Ya'qub dominion over the holy land, and he ruled for seventy-two years. That is His saying in what He revealed of His Book: {My Lord, You have given me some sovereignty and taught me some interpretation of events} [Yusuf 101], the verse. It is not authentic."],[4078,"There were eighty years between Joseph's separation and Jacob's embrace until they met."],[4079,"Joseph was bought for only twenty dirhams. His family, when he sent for them while they were in Egypt, numbered three hundred ninety people: their men were prophets and their women were truthful ones. By Allah, they did not leave with Moses until they reached six hundred and seventy thousand."],[4080,"Then to Jacob was born Joseph the truthful, whom Allah chose, selected, and honored, and allotted him two-thirds of beauty and allotted one-third among His servants. He resembled Adam on the day Allah created him, formed him, and breathed into him of His spirit before sin touched him. When Adam disobeyed, light, radiance, and beauty were stripped from him. Allah had given Adam beauty, comeliness, light, and radiance on the day He created him, but when he did what he did and fell into sin, that was taken from him. Then Allah granted Adam one-third of beauty along with the repentance He accepted from him. Thereafter Allah gave Joseph the beauty, comeliness, light, and radiance that He had stripped from Adam when he sinned. That is because Allah loved to show His servants that He is capable of whatever He wills. He gave Joseph such beauty and comeliness as He gave no one among people. Then Allah gave him knowledge of dream interpretation. He would report a matter he had seen in his sleep that it would come to be, and before it came to be, Allah taught him as He taught Adam all the names. When he smiled, you would see light in his front teeth; when he spoke, you would see rays of light in his speech, blazing between his incisors."],[4081,"Moses son of Misha son of Joseph son of Jacob was born and became a prophet among the Children of Israel before Moses son of Imran, as they claim. Those who are certain of it claim that he is the one who sought the learned man to learn from him until he reached the learned man who scuttled the ship, killed the boy, and built the wall, with Moses son of Misha accompanying him. Then he turned away from him until he reached what he reached."],[4082,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Moses son of Imran stood as a preacher among the Children of Israel,\" and he mentioned the hadith in full."],[4083,"{And We wrote for him on the Tablets of everything an admonition and a detailed explanation of all things} [Al-A'raf: 145]. He said: Moses thought that all things had been recorded for him just as you see that your scholars have recorded for you everything they record. When Moses reached the seashore, he met the learned man and questioned him. The learned man acknowledged his superior knowledge and did not envy him. Moses said to him, entreating him: \"May I follow you so that you teach me of the right guidance you have been taught?\" The learned man knew that Moses could not endure his company nor be patient with his knowledge, so he said to him: \"Indeed you will not be able to have patience with me. And how can you be patient about what you do not encompass in knowledge?\" Moses said, excusing himself: \"You will find me, if Allah wills, patient, and I will not disobey any of your commands.\" But he knew that Moses could not endure his company nor be patient with his knowledge, so he said to him: \"If you follow me, do not ask me about anything until I mention it to you.\" Then they boarded the ship and the learned man scuttled it. Scuttling it was pleasing to Allah and displeasing to Moses. Then he met the boy and killed him, which was pleasing to Allah. Then he mentioned part of the story and the speech, and Ibn Abbas did not go beyond that."],[4084,"\"May Allah have mercy on us and on Moses.\" He began with himself. Had he been patient, more of his story would have been related to us, but he said: \"If I ask you about anything after this, do not keep me as a companion. You have received from me an excuse.\""],[4086,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Verily, Allah chose Musa with His speech and Ibrahim with His close friendship.\""],[4087,"Allah ﷻ divided His vision and His speech between Muhammad ﷺ and Moses: Muhammad saw Him twice, and Moses spoke to Him twice.[According to the condition of Muslim]"],[4088,"Moses son of Imran is the chosen one of Allah."],[4089,"Moses remained forty days after Allah spoke to him, and no one saw him except that he died."],[4090,"When Moses son of Imran's Lord spoke to him, he wished to look at Him. He said: \"My Lord, show me that I may look at You.\" He said: \"You will never see Me, but look at the mountain; if it remains firm in its place, then you will see Me.\" So He surrounded the mountain with angels, surrounded the angels with fire, surrounded the fire with angels, and surrounded the angels with fire. Then your Lord manifested Himself to the mountain, then manifested from it something like a little finger, and He made the mountain level. Moses fell down thunderstruck for as long as Allah willed. Then he recovered and said: \"Glory be to You, I repent to You, and I am the first of the believers,\" meaning the first of the Children of Israel to believe."],[4091,"Mention was made to me of the tree to which Moses, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, took shelter, so I traveled to it for two days and two nights. Then I reached it in the morning and found it green and flourishing. I prayed for the Prophet ﷺ and greeted him. My camel, being hungry, stretched toward it and took a mouthful while hungry. It chewed but could not swallow it, so it spat it out. I prayed for the Prophet ﷺ and departed."],[4092,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse: {When his Lord appeared to the mountain, He made it crumble to dust} [Al-A'raf 143]. Hammad gestured, placing his thumb on the joint of the little finger, and said: \"So the mountain sank.\""],[4093,"From the Prophet ﷺ—if Allah wills; Abu Salamah Musa b. Isma'il was uncertain—{When his Lord appeared to the mountain, He made it crumble to dust} [Al-A'raf 143], he said: \"The mountain sank.\" Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz narrated it to us: al-Hasan b. Sufyan, 'Imran b. Musa al-Jurjani, and Ahmad b. 'Ali b. al-Muthanna informed us, saying: Hudbah b. Khalid narrated to us, Hammad b. Salamah narrated to us, similar to the hadith of al-Khuza'i, and Hudbah did not doubt it."],[4095,"That he should return that to them, so He gave them dominion over the eastern and western parts of the earth and granted them a great kingdom, until they asked to look at their Lord. They said, \"Show us Allah plainly,\" and that was when they saw Moses and his Lord spoke to him, and they heard, so they sought the vision. Moses had selected the best of them to testify for him before the Children of Israel that his Lord had indeed spoken to him, but they said, \"We will never testify for you until you show us Allah plainly.\" So the thunderbolt seized them while they were looking on."],[4096,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The Angel of Death used to come to people openly. He came to Moses son of Imran, and Moses slapped him and gouged out his eye. The Angel of Death ascended and said: 'O Lord, Your servant Moses did such and such to me, and were it not for his honor with You, I would have made it hard for him.' Allah said: 'Go to My servant Moses and give him the choice between placing his hand on the back of an ox, for every hair covered by his palm he gets a year, and dying now.' So he came to him and gave him the choice. Moses said: 'What comes after that?' He said: 'Death.' He said: 'Then now.' So he took a whiff of him and seized his soul, and Allah restored his sight to him. After that he used to come to people in concealment.\""],[4097,"Allah announced the death of Aaron to Moses when Allah willed to take him. When He announced it to him, he grieved. When he was taken, he became extremely distressed and wept for a long time. When he returned to that, Allah, Exalted be He, turned to him consoling and admonishing him, saying to him: \"O Moses, it was not befitting for you to long for the loss of anything with Me, nor to find comfort in other than Me, nor to bind your knees except to Me, nor that this distress of yours now over Aaron should be except for Me. How can you feel lonely for any of the things while you hear My words? Or how can you long for the loss of any worldly thing after I have chosen you for My messages and My speech?\" And he mentioned a long intimate conversation. He said: Aaron was taken while Moses was one hundred and seventeen years old, three years before the end of the wandering. Aaron was taken at one hundred and twenty years old; Moses remained after him three years until he completed one hundred and twenty years, while the Children of Israel were divided concerning him, sometimes gathering around him and other times separating."],[4098,"From some of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ: Allah revealed to Moses son of Imran, \"I am going to take Aaron, so bring him to such-and-such a mountain.\" Moses and Aaron set out toward that mountain, and there they found a tree shaped like a built house, and inside it a bed with coverings, and in it a pleasant fragrance. When Aaron looked at that mountain, the house, and what was in it, it pleased him, and he said: \"O Moses, I would love to sleep on this bed.\" Moses said to him: \"Then sleep on it.\" He said: \"I fear that the Lord of this house may come and be angry with me.\" Moses said to him: \"Do not be afraid; I will suffice you against the Lord of this house, so sleep.\" He said: \"O Moses, rather sleep with me, for if the Lord of this house comes, He will be angry with both me and you.\" When they lay down, death took Aaron. When he felt it, he said: \"O Moses, you deceived me.\" When he was taken, that house was lifted, that tree disappeared, and the bed was raised to heaven. When Moses returned to the Children of Israel without Aaron, they said: \"Moses killed Aaron out of jealousy for the Children of Israel's love for him.\" Aaron was more affectionate and gentler to them than Moses, and Moses had some harshness toward them. When that reached him, he said to them: \"Woe to you! He was my brother; do you think I would kill him?\" When they persisted against him, he stood, prayed two rak'ahs, then called upon Allah, and the bed descended until they saw it between heaven and earth, and they believed him."],[4099,"From 'Ali regarding His saying, Exalted be He: {O you who believe, do not be like those who hurt Moses, and Allah cleared him of what they said} [Al-Ahzab 69]. He said: Moses and Aaron went up the mountain, and Aaron died. The Children of Israel said to Moses: \"You killed him; he was more loving to us than you and gentler to us than you.\" So they hurt him in that. Allah commanded the angels, and they carried him and passed him by the gatherings of the Children of Israel until they knew of his death, and they buried him. None knew his grave except the vultures, and Allah made them deaf and dumb."],[4100,"The chosen one of Allah, Moses, disliked death and regarded it as great. When he disliked it, Allah willed to make death beloved to him and life hateful to him. Prophethood was transferred to Joshua son of Nun, who used to come to him morning and evening. Moses would say to him: \"O Prophet of Allah, what has Allah revealed to you?\" Joshua son of Nun would say to him: \"O Prophet of Allah, did I not accompany you for such and such years? Did I ever ask you about anything Allah revealed to you until you were the one to begin and mention it?\" When Moses saw that, he disliked life and loved death."],[4101,"It was mentioned to me that concerning the death of the chosen one of Allah, Moses ﷺ: he used to shade himself in a booth and eat and drink from a hollowed-out stone, lapping from it like an animal, out of humility for Allah, until Allah honored him with what He honored him with of His speech. Regarding his death: he went out one day from his booth for some need, unknown to any of Allah's creation. He passed by a group of angels digging a grave. He recognized them and approached them until he stood over them, and they were digging a grave the like of which he had never seen anything more beautiful in its greenery, freshness, and splendor. He said to them: \"O angels of Allah, for whom are you digging this grave?\" They said: \"By Allah, we are digging it for a servant noble to his Lord.\" He said: \"This servant has a standing with Allah such that I have never seen a resting place or entrance like today.\" That was when what was to come from Allah regarding his taking came. The angels said to him: \"O chosen one of Allah, would you like to be that one?\" He said: \"I wish it.\" They said: \"Then descend and lie in it, and turn to your Lord, then breathe the easiest breath you have ever breathed.\" He descended, lay in it, turned to his Lord, then breathed, and Allah took his soul. Then the angels prayed over him. The chosen one of Allah, Moses ﷺ, was ascetic in this world, desirous of the hereafter."],[4102,"Job son of Amush was the patient prophet of Allah, upon whom Iblis, the enemy of Allah, brought his troops, cavalry, and infantry to tempt him and divert him from the remembrance of Allah, but Allah protected him and Iblis found no way to him. Allah cast upon Job tranquility and patience over the affliction with which He tested him, so Allah named him {an excellent servant, indeed he was oft-returning} [Sad 44]. Job was a tall man with curly hair, wide eyes, and handsome appearance. On his forehead was written 'the afflicted, the patient.' He had a short neck, broad chest, thick calves and forearms. He used to give to widows and clothe them, striving and sincere for Allah, Exalted be He."],[4103,"The wife of Job said to him: \"By Allah, I have been stricken with such hardship and poverty that my people would send a loaf of bread and I would feed you. So call upon Allah to heal you.\" He said: \"Woe to you! We were in prosperity for seventy years, so we are in affliction for seven years.\""],[4104,"Job, the prophet of Allah, remained in his affliction for fifteen years; relatives and strangers abandoned him except two men from his brothers, who were among his closest brothers. They used to come to him morning and evening. One day one of them said to his companion: \"By Allah, we know that Job has committed a sin that no one in the worlds has committed.\" His companion said to him: \"And what is that?\" He said: \"For eighteen years Allah has not had mercy on him and removed what he has.\" When they went to Job, the man could not restrain himself until he mentioned that to him. Job said to him: \"I do not know what you are saying, except that Allah knows that I used to pass by two men disputing and mentioning Allah, and I would return to my house and make expiation for them, disliking that Allah be mentioned except in truth.\" And he used to go out for his need, and when he finished his need, his wife would hold his hand until he reached home. One day he was late for her, and Allah revealed to Job in his place: \"Strike with your foot; this is a cool bathing place and a drink.\" She found him late and went to meet him, and he came to her, Allah having removed the affliction from him, and he was the most handsome he had ever been. When she saw him, she said: \"O you, may Allah bless you, have you seen the prophet of Allah, this afflicted one? By Allah, I have never seen a man more resembling him than you when he was healthy.\" He said: \"I am he.\" He said: He had two threshing floors, one for wheat and one for barley. Allah sent two clouds: when one was over the wheat threshing floor, it poured gold into it until it overflowed, and the other poured silver into the barley threshing floor until it overflowed."],[4105,"When Allah restored Ayyub to health, He rained upon him locusts of gold, and he began to take them with his hand and put them in his garment. It was said to him, \"O Ayyub, are you not satisfied?\" He said, \"And who can be satisfied with Your mercy?\""],[4106,"Ayyub was afflicted for seven years, thrown on the dung heap of Bayt al-Maqdis."],[4107,"The age of Ayyub was ninety-three years, and at his death he appointed his son Hawmal as his successor. After him, Allah sent his son Bishr b. Ayyub as a prophet and named him Dhu al-Kifl, and commanded him to call to His oneness. He remained in al-Sham his whole life until he died, and his age was seventy-five years. Bishr appointed his son Abdan as his successor. Then after them Allah sent Shu'ayb."],[4108,"Then Ilyas, the Prophet of Allah, was a man of mountains and wilderness, secluding himself therein to worship his Lord. He had a large head, a lean belly, and thin legs, and on his head was a red mole. Allah raised him only to the land of al-Sham and did not ascend with him to heaven, and he bequeathed prophethood after him to al-Yasa'."],[4109,"And Yunus b. Matta, whom Allah named Dhu al-Nun, said: {And Dhu al-Nun, when he went off in anger and thought that We would not decree for him, then he called out in the darkness: \"There is no god but You, glory be to You; indeed I have been of the wrongdoers\"} [al-Anbiya' 87]. Allah answered him and saved him from distress, from three darknesses: the darkness of night, the darkness of the sea, and the darkness of the belly of the whale. He spent the night with his people, and He sent him to a hundred thousand or more, and they believed, so Allah let them enjoy until their appointed terms which He had written for them, and did not destroy them with punishment."],[4110,"The supplication of Dhu al-Nun with which he called in the belly of the whale: \"There is no god but You, glory be to You; indeed I have been of the wrongdoers.\" No Muslim calls with it in distress except that Allah answers him."],[4111,"Whoever says, \"I am better than Yunus b. Matta\" has lied."],[4112,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a mountain pass and said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"The pass of such-and-such.\" He said, \"It is as if I am looking at Yunus b. Matta on a she-camel whose halter is of palm fiber, wearing a woolen jubbah, and he is saying, 'Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk.'\""],[4113,"Yunus remained in the belly of the whale for forty days."],[4114,"He used to pray much in the darkness. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4115,"Yunus b. Matta was swallowed by the whale in the forenoon and it cast him out in the evening."],[4116,"Whoever calls with the supplication of Yunus with which he called in the belly of the whale will be answered."],[4117,"Yunus bin Matta was a righteous servant, but he was of narrow character. When the burdens of prophethood were placed upon him and they were burdens that only a few could bear, he cracked under their weight, just as a single straw breaks under the burden. He expelled them from his body and fled from them, saying to his Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , \"Therefore be patient, as the messengers endowed with determination were patient.\" \"So be patient with the decree of your Lord and do not be like the companion of the fish when he called out while he was distressed.\" [Quran 68:48] It means, do not throw in another burden as you have thrown it away. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[4118,"When Yunus fell into the belly of the whale, he thought it was death, so he moved his legs and found they could move. Then he prostrated and said, 'O Lord, I have taken for You a place of prostration where no one has ever prostrated before.'"],[4119,"The Prophet of Allah, Dawud b. Isha b. 'Awbad b. Ba'ir b. Salmun b. Yahsun b. Yarib b. Ram b. Hadrun b. Faris b. Yahuda b. Ya'qub b. Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Khalil, was a short, blue-eyed man with little hair, pure of heart and a jurist."],[4120,"From his father regarding the words of Allah Almighty: {Have you not considered those who left their homes in thousands, fearing death?} [Qur'an 2:243] up to His words {And Allah is Knowing of the wrongdoers} [Qur'an 2:95]. He said: Allah Almighty revealed to their prophet that among the children of so-and-so there is a man by whom Allah will slay Goliath. Of his signs is this horn: if it is placed on his head, it will grasp whatever it misses. So he came to him and said, 'Allah has revealed to me that among your children there is a man by whom Allah will slay Goliath.' He said, 'Yes, O Prophet of Allah.' He said, 'Then he brought out twelve men like pillars, among them a man outstanding above them. He began presenting them to the horn, but he saw nothing.' Then he said, 'Do you have a child other than these?' He said, 'Yes, O Prophet of Allah, I have a short son whom I was ashamed for people to see, so I put him with the sheep.' He said, 'Where is he?' He said, 'He is in such-and-such a mountain pass.' So he went out to him and said, 'This is he, no doubt about it.' Then he placed the horn on his head and it fitted. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4121,"When Allah created Adam, He wiped his back, and from his back came forth every soul He would create of his progeny until the Day of Resurrection. He placed between the eyes of every human among them a glint of their light. Then He presented them to Adam, who said, 'O Lord, who are these?' He said, 'These are your progeny.' He saw a man among them whose glint between his eyes pleased him. He said, 'O Lord, who is this?' He said, 'This is a man from the last of the nations from your progeny, called Dawud.' He said, 'O Lord, how long have You made his lifespan?' He said, 'Sixty years.' He said, 'O Lord, increase him from my lifespan forty years.' He said, 'Then it will be written and sealed and not changed.' When Adam's lifespan ended, the Angel of Death came to him. He said, 'Is there not left of my lifespan forty years?' He said, 'Did you not give them to your son Dawud?' So he denied, and his progeny denied. He forgot, and his progeny forgot. He erred, and his progeny erred."],[4122,"\"And between Moses and David were five hundred and sixty-nine years.\" Al-Dhahabi did not mention it in his summary."],[4123,"Four thousand guarded him every day and night. Al-Suddi said: Dawud had divided time into three days: one day to judge among the people, one day to devote himself to worship, and one day to devote himself to his wives. He had ninety-nine wives. In what he read of the scriptures, he found the excellence of Ibrahim, Ishaq, and Ya'qub. When he found that in what he read, he said, 'O Lord, I see that all good has been taken by my forefathers who were before me. Give me the like of what You gave them and do with me as You did with them.' Then Allah revealed to him: Your forefathers were tried with afflictions that you have not been tried with. Ibrahim was tried with the sacrifice of his son, Ishaq with the loss of his sight, and Ya'qub with his grief over Yusuf, and you have not been tried with any of that. He said, 'O Lord, try me with the like of what You tried them and give me the like of what You gave them.' Then Allah revealed to him: You will be tried, so beware. After that, he remained as long as Allah willed, when Satan came to him in the form of a dove of gold and landed between his legs while he was standing praying. He reached out his hand to take it, but it flew from the window. He watched where it landed and sent someone after it. Then he saw a woman bathing on her roof, one of the most beautiful of women in form. She glanced and saw him, so she let down her hair and covered herself with it. That increased his desire for her. He inquired about her and was told that she had a husband and that her husband was away at such-and-such a garrison. He sent to the commander of the garrison and ordered him to send the husband to such-and-such an enemy. He sent him, and he achieved victory. He kept sending him until he was killed on the third occasion. Then he married his wife. When he entered upon her, he had not stayed long before Allah sent two angels in human form. They asked to enter upon him and found him on his day of worship. The guards prevented them from entering, so they climbed over the wall into his prayer niche. He was unaware while praying when suddenly they were sitting before him. He was startled by them, and they said, 'Do not fear. We are two disputants; one of us has wronged the other, so judge between us with truth and do not be unjust.' He said, 'Do not fear,' and he mentioned the hadith at length concerning his acknowledgment of his sin. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4124,"Allah chose for His prophethood and selected for His message Dawud b. Isha. Allah gathered for him that light and wisdom and gave him additionally the Psalms from Himself. Dawud b. Isha ruled for seventy years. He dealt fairly among people, judged between them with finality by what Allah taught him and gave him of His wisdom. Our Lord commanded the mountains, and they obeyed him, and made iron soft for him by Allah's permission. Our Lord commanded the angels to carry the Ark for him. Dawud continued to manage by Allah's knowledge and light, judging by what He made lawful and forbidding what He made unlawful, until when Allah willed to take him to Himself, He revealed to him: Entrust Allah's light and wisdom, both apparent and hidden, to your son Sulayman b. Dawud. And he did so."],[4125,"From al-Sha'bi regarding His words, exalted is He: {And We have written in the Psalms after the reminder} [Qur'an 21:105]. He said: In the Psalms of Dawud after the reminder of Musa: {That the earth will be inherited by My righteous servants} [Qur'an 21:105]. He said: Paradise. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4126,"I walked with my uncle Muhammad b. 'Ali b. al-Husayn to Ja'far and I said, 'People claim that Sulayman b. Dawud asked his Lord to grant him a kingdom that would not befit anyone after him, and that it is the twenty.' He said, 'I do not know what people's traditions are, but...'"],[4127,"A vineyard had produced its grapes, but the sheep ruined it. Dawood (David) decided to grant the vineyard to the owner of the sheep. Sulaiman (Solomon) said, \"This is not fair, O Prophet of Allah.\" Dawood asked, \"Why?\" Sulaiman replied, \"You should transfer the vineyard to its owner, and the sheep to its owner, until the vineyard returns to its previous state.\" Allah, the Almighty, says, \"So We made Sulaiman understand it, and to each [of them] We gave judgement and knowledge.\" (Quran 21:79). Adh-Dhahabi remained silent regarding the summary."],[4128,"Sulayman b. Dawud was given the kingdom of the easts and wests of the earth. Sulayman b. Dawud ruled for seven hundred years and six months. He ruled all the people of the world from jinn, humans, devils, beasts, birds, and wild animals. He was given knowledge of everything and the speech of everything. In his time, the marvelous crafts that people had never heard of were made and subjected to him. He continued to manage by Allah's command, light, and wisdom, until when Allah willed to take him, He revealed to him: Entrust Allah's knowledge and wisdom to his brother and the children of Dawud, and they were four hundred and eighty men without a message. This is false."],[4129,"The Children of Ishaq dated from the sending of Musa to the reign of Sulayman b. Dawud. He said: Sulayman inherited Dawud. He said: Prophethood and message were taken to him that He would grant him a kingdom that would not befit anyone after him. So He subjected to him the jinn, humans, birds, and wind."],[4130,"It has reached us that Sulayman b. Dawud's army was one hundred parasangs: twenty-five of them for humans, twenty-five for jinn, twenty-five for wild beasts, and twenty-five for birds. He had a thousand houses of glass on wood, three hundred of them for free women and seven hundred for concubines. He commanded the strong wind, and it lifted him, then he commanded the wind, and it carried him. Allah revealed to him while he was traveling between heaven and earth: I have increased your kingdom so that no one of the creatures speaks anything but the wind comes and informs you of it."],[4131,"So he travels in a single morning the distance of a month. Sahih."],[4132,"Four ruled the earth: Sulayman b. Dawud, Dhu al-Qarnayn, a man from the people of Hulwan, and another man.\" It was said to him, \"Was it al-Khidr?\" He said, \"No.\""],[4133,"The last of the prophets of the Children of Israel was Zakariya b. Adna b. Muslim, and he was from the progeny of Ya'qub. He said, \"He will inherit my kingdom and inherit prophethood from the family of Ya'qub.\""],[4134,"Zakariya was a carpenter."],[4135,"Zakariya called upon his Lord in secret, saying: \"My Lord, indeed my bones have weakened, and my head has flared with gray hair, and I have never been disappointed in supplicating You, my Lord. Indeed, I fear the successors after me, and they are the 'asaba, and my wife has been barren, so grant me from Yourself a heir who will inherit me and inherit prophethood, and inherit from the family of Ya'qub, inheriting the prophethood of the family of Ya'qub, and make him, my Lord, pleasing.\" And His saying, \"Grant me from Yourself a good offspring\"—He says its positions—\"indeed You are the Hearer of supplication.\" And He said, \"My Lord, do not leave me alone, and You are the best of inheritors.\" Then the angels called him—he is Jibril—while he was standing praying in the mihrab: \"Allah gives you glad tidings of a boy whose name is Yahya; We have not assigned to him before any namesake,\" no one before him was named Yahya. And the angels said, \"Indeed Allah gives you glad tidings of Yahya, confirming a word from Allah, confirming 'Isa, and a hasur,\" and the hasur is the one who does not desire women. When he heard the call, Satan came to him and said, \"O Zakariya, the voice you heard is not from Allah; it is only from Satan mocking you. If it were from Allah, He would have revealed it to you as He reveals other matters to you.\" Then he doubted in his place and said, \"How can I have a boy\"—he says from where—\"when old age has reached me and my wife is barren?\" He said, \"Thus Allah does what He wills, and I created you before, and you were nothing.\""],[4136,"{\"My Lord, grant me from Yourself a good offspring. Indeed, You are the Hearer of supplication\"} [Al 'Imran: 38]. {\"Indeed, my bones have weakened, and my head has flared with gray hair\"} [Maryam: 4] and the following verses. Then He said, {\"How can I have a boy when my wife has been barren and I have reached extreme old age?\"} [Maryam: 9]. He said, \"Thus your Lord says, 'It is easy for Me, and I created you before, and you were nothing.'\" He said, \"My Lord, make for me a sign.\" He said, \"Your sign is that you will not speak to people for three nights, [being] sound.\" So his tongue was sealed for three days and their nights, while he was healthy and did not speak. {\"Then he came out to his people from the mihrab and inspired them to glorify in the morning\"} [Maryam: 11] and in the evening. \"O Yahya, take the Scripture with strength,\" and We gave him judgment as a boy, and the verses until {\"he will be raised alive\"} [Maryam: 15]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4137,"Zakariya and 'Imran married two sisters. The mother of Yahya was with Zakariya, and the mother of Maryam was with 'Imran. Then 'Imran died while the mother of Maryam was pregnant with Maryam, and she was a fetus in her womb. And she was, as they claim, one from whom Allah withheld children until she despaired; and they were a household from Allah in a [high] station."],[4138,"There is no human being except that he has erred, or thought of a sin, or committed it, except Yahya b. Zakariya; he neither thought of a sin nor committed it."],[4139,"Yahya b. Zakariya was a master and hasur; he did not approach women nor desire them. He was a young man, handsome of face and form, gentle of wing, with little hair, short fingers, a long nose, joined eyebrows, and a thin voice, much in worship, strong in obedience to Allah."],[4140,"Jesus, the son of Mary, and John, the son of Zachariah, were sent with twelve thousand disciples to teach people. It is said that they prohibited the marriage of the niece of their king, [Herodias], who was fond of her and intended to marry her. She had a daily request which he fulfilled for her. When her mother learned of this, she advised her daughter [Herodias] to ask King [Herod] for a favor when she visited him. She said, \"Ask him to have John, the son of Zachariah, beheaded for me.\" When she went in to see King [Herod], he asked her what she wanted, and she said that she wanted John, the son of Zachariah to be beheaded. However, King [Herod] asked her to request something else, but she that she did not want anything other than this.When she persisted, the king called for John, the son of Zachariah, and ordered him to be beheaded. A drop of his blood fell on the ground, and it continued to boil until Allah sent a Nebuchadnezzar upon them. An old man from the Children of Israel guided him to that blood, and God placed in his heart the idea that they should be killed in revenge for that blood. As a result, seventy thousand of them were killed in a single day, and then the violence ceased."],[4141,"Allah revealed to Muhammad ﷺ: 'I killed seventy thousand for Yahya b. Zakariya, and I will kill for the son of your daughter seventy thousand and seventy thousand.'"],[4142,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I am the nearest of people to 'Isa b. Maryam in this world and the Hereafter. The prophets are brothers from different mothers; their mothers are diverse but their religion is one, and there is no prophet between me and 'Isa b. Maryam.'"],[4143,"Hannah gave birth to Maryam, and Maryam gave birth to 'Isa."],[4144,"'Isa b. Maryam was born on the day of 'Ashura'."],[4145,"From 'Abd Allah, they both said: Maryam went out to the side of the prayer niche with a menstrual impurity that had befallen her. When she became pure, there was a man with her. That is His saying: {Then We sent to her Our Spirit, and he represented himself to her as a well-proportioned man} [Maryam:17], and he is Jibril ﷺ . She was frightened by him and said: {I seek refuge in the Most Merciful from you, if you should be righteous} [Maryam:18]. He said: {I am only the messenger of your Lord to give you a pure boy} [Maryam:19]—the verse. She went out with her outer garment on, and he took hold of her sleeve and blew into the opening of her chemise, which was slit from the front, and the breath entered her chest, and she conceived. Her sister, the wife of Zakariyya, came to visit her one night. When she opened the door for her, she embraced her. The wife of Zakariyya said: O Maryam, did you realize that I am pregnant? Maryam likewise said: Did you realize that I am pregnant? The wife of Zakariyya said: Indeed I have found that what is in my womb prostrates to what is in your womb. That is His saying, may He be glorified: {confirming a word from Allah} [Al 'Imran:39]. The wife of Zakariyya gave birth to Yahya. When Maryam was about to give birth, she went out to the side of the prayer niche, and the pains of childbirth drove her to the trunk of a palm tree. She said, out of shame before the people: {I wish I had died before this and been completely forgotten} [Maryam:23]. Jibril called to her {from beneath her: Do not grieve; your Lord has placed beneath you a stream. And shake toward you the trunk of the palm tree; it will drop upon you ripe, fresh dates} [Maryam:25]. She shook it, and He caused a river to flow for her in the prayer niche—and al-sariyy is the river—and the palm tree dropped ripe, fresh dates. When she gave birth to him, the devil went and informed the Children of Israel that Maryam had given birth. When they wanted her to speak, she pointed to 'Isa, and 'Isa spoke and said: Indeed I am the servant of Allah; He has given me the Book and made me a prophet and made me blessed. When 'Isa was born, no idol on earth that was worshipped besides Allah remained except that it fell prostrate on its face."],[4146,"The delegation of Najran came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: What do you say about 'Isa son of Maryam? He said: \"He is the spirit of Allah and His word, and the servant of Allah and His messenger.\" They said to him: Would you like us to invoke a mutual curse with you that it is not so? He said: \"And is that more beloved to you?\" They said: Yes. He said: \"Whenever you wish.\" The Prophet ﷺ came and gathered his children, al-Hasan and al-Husayn. Their chief said: Do not invoke a mutual curse with this man, for by Allah, if you do, one of the two parties will be swallowed up. They came and said: O Abu al-Qasim, it was only our foolish ones who wanted to invoke a mutual curse with you, and we would like you to excuse us. He said: \"I have excused you.\" Then he said: \"Indeed, the punishment has overshadowed Najran.\""],[4147,"Every child of Adam is touched by Satan with that poke, and for it the newborn cries out—except what was with Maryam and her son. For when her mother gave birth to her—meaning her mother—she said: I seek refuge for her and her offspring in You from the accursed Satan. So a veil was struck before her, and he poked at it. Her Lord accepted her with gracious acceptance and made her grow in a good manner. Her mother died, and she was given into the care of her maternal aunt, the mother of Yahya."],[4148,"They will come to 'Isa for intercession, and he will say: Do you know anyone who is the word of Allah and His spirit, who heals the blind and the leper and gives life to the dead, other than me? They will say: No."],[4149,"\"The best of the women of the worlds are Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, Fatimah bt. Muhammad, Maryam bt. 'Imran, and Asiyah bt. Muzahim, the wife of Pharaoh.\""],[4150,"\"No one spoke in the cradle except three: 'Isa son of Maryam, the witness of Yusuf, the companion of Jurayj, and the son of the hairdresser of Pharaoh's daughter.\""],[4151,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"'Isa son of Maryam will certainly descend as a just judge and a fair imam, and he will certainly travel a mountain pass as a pilgrim for Hajj or 'Umrah or with the intention of both, and he will certainly come to my grave until he greets me, and I will certainly return his greeting.\" Abu Hurayrah says: O my brother's son, if you see him, say: Abu Hurayrah sends you greetings of peace."],[4152,"\"Indeed, the spirit of Allah, 'Isa son of Maryam, is descending among you. When you see him, recognize him: a man of medium height, of reddish-white complexion, wearing two garments dyed with saffron, as if water were dripping from his head though it is not wet. He will break the cross, kill the pig, abolish the jizyah, and call the people to Islam. In his time, Allah will destroy the false messiah, the Dajjal, and security will descend upon the people of the earth so that lions graze with camels, leopards with cattle, and wolves with sheep, and children play with snakes without them harming them. He will remain for forty years, then he will die, and the Muslims will pray over him.\""],[4153,"Allah caused 'Isa son of Maryam to die for three hours of the day when He raised him to Himself, while the Christians claim that He caused him to die for seven hours of the day, then revived him. Wahb said: The Christians claimed that Maryam gave birth to 'Isa three hundred sixty-three years after the birth of Alexander. They claimed that the birth of Yahya b. Zakariyya was six months before the birth of 'Isa. They claimed that Maryam became pregnant with 'Isa when she was thirteen years old, and that 'Isa lived until he was raised at the age of thirty-two, and that Maryam remained after his raising for six years, so her total lifespan was fifty-six years. They claimed that Zakariyya b. Barkhiyya, the father of Yahya b. Zakariyya, was two hundred years old when the mother of Maryam was pregnant with Maryam. When Maryam was born, Zakariyya took charge of her after the death of her mother, because her maternal aunt, the sister of her mother, was married to him. The name of Maryam's mother was Hannah bt. Faqudh b. Qil."],[4154,"He said to a man sitting near him while he was narrating to his companions: Come close to me. The man said to him: May Allah preserve you. By Allah, I do not know how to ask you as these people have asked. He said: Come close to me, and I will tell you about the prophets mentioned in the Book of Allah. I tell you about Adam: he was a servant, a farmer. I tell you about Nuh: he was a servant, a carpenter. I tell you about Idris: he was a servant, a tailor. I tell you about Dawud: he was a servant, a maker of armor. I tell you about Musa: he was a servant, a shepherd. I tell you about Ibrahim: he was a servant, a farmer. I tell you about Salih: he was a servant, a merchant. I tell you about Sulayman: he was a servant to whom Allah gave kingship. He used to fast six days at the beginning of the month, three in the middle, and three at the end. He had nine hundred concubines and three hundred free wives. I tell you about the son of the virgin, the pure, 'Isa son of Maryam: he would not store anything for tomorrow and would say: The One who gave me my morning meal will give me my evening meal, and the One who gave me my evening meal will give me my morning meal. He worshipped Allah all night, praying until the sun rose, and during the day he was a wanderer. He fasted all time and stood in prayer all night. I tell you about the chosen Prophet ﷺ: he used to tend the sheep of his household in Ajyad. He used to fast, and we would say he does not break his fast; and he would break his fast, and we would say he does not fast—but all of it: we never saw him fasting. He fasted three days of every month. He was the gentlest of people in disposition, the best in conduct, and the most knowledgeable. And I inform you about Hawwa': she used to spin hair and transform it with her hands, and she would clothe herself and her children with it. And Maryam bt. 'Imran used to do that."],[4155,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was in the mosque, and I seized the opportunity of his privacy. He said to me: \"O Abu Dharr, indeed the mosque has a greeting.\" I said: What is its greeting, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Two rak'ahs.\" I prayed them, then he turned to me and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you commanded me to pray, but what is prayer? He said: \"Goodness placed; whoever wishes may do little, and whoever wishes may do more.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, which deeds are most beloved to Allah? He said: \"Faith in Allah.\" Then he mentioned the hadith until he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how many are the prophets? He said: \"One hundred twenty-four thousand prophets.\" I said: How many messengers are among them? He said: \"Three hundred and thirteen.\" And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[4156,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent after eight thousand prophets, of whom four thousand were from the Children of Israel.\""],[4157,"“I am the seal of a thousand prophets or more.”"],[4158,"“Seventy prophets have traversed the mountain pass of al-Rawḥāʾ as pilgrims, wearing woolen garments, and seventy prophets have prayed in the mosque of al-Khayf.”"],[4159,"“Among my brethren of the prophets who passed before were eight thousand prophets, then ʿĪsā son of Maryam, then I came after him.” Its chain is weak."],[4160,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah while the Jews were saying: “This world is only seven thousand years.” Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[4161,"“The lifespan of Adam was a thousand years.”"],[4162,"A man from Banū ʿAbs called Khālid b. Sinān said to his people: “I shall extinguish for you the fire of al-Ḥadathān.” ʿUmārah b. Ziyād, a man of his people, said to him: “By Allah, you have never told us anything but the truth, O Khālid. So what is your business with the fire of al-Ḥadathān? You claim that you will extinguish it.” So he set out, and ʿUmārah b. Ziyād set out with him along with thirty of his people until they came to it, and it was emerging from a fissure in a mountain of a lava field called Ḥarrat Ashjaʿ. Khālid drew a line for them and seated them within it, and said: “If I am delayed from you, do not call me by my name.” It came out as if it were chestnut horses following one another. Khālid faced it and struck it with his staff, saying: “Badaʾ, badaʾ, badaʾ, all guidance. The son of the shepherd of goats claimed that I would not come out of it while my incisors are in my hand,” until he entered the fissure with it. He was delayed from them, and ʿUmārah b. Ziyād said: “By Allah, if your companion were alive, he would have come out to you by now.” They said: “Call him by his name.” They said: “He forbade us to call him by his name.” But they called him by his name. He came out to them holding his head, and said: “Did I not forbid you to call me by my name? By Allah, you have killed me. So bury me, and when donkeys pass by you, among them a tailless donkey, then dig me up, for you will find me alive.” So they buried him. Then donkeys passed by them, among them a tailless donkey, and we said: “Dig him up, for he commanded us to dig him up.” ʿUmārah b. Ziyād said: “Do not let Muḍar say that we dig up our dead. By Allah, we will never dig him up.” He had told them that in the saddlebag of his wife there were two tablets, and if any matter became unclear to them, they should look at them, for they would see what they asked about. And he said: “No menstruating woman should touch them.” When they returned to his wife, they asked her about them, and she brought them out while she was menstruating, so the knowledge that was in them was lost. Abū Yūnus said: Simāk b. Ḥarb said: The Prophet ﷺ was asked about him, and he said: “That was a prophet whom his people neglected.” And Abū Yūnus said: Simāk b. Ḥarb said: The son of Khālid b. Sinān came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “Welcome to the son of my brother.” Al-Ḥākim said:"],[4163,"They said: “O Messenger of Allah, tell us about yourself.” He said: “I am the supplication of my father Ibrāhīm, the glad tidings of ʿĪsā, and my mother saw when she was pregnant with me that a light came out of her that illuminated Buṣrā, and Buṣrā is in the land of Syria.”"],[4164,"“Indeed, in the first of the Book I am with Allah as the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still prostrate in his clay. And I will inform you of the interpretation of that: the supplication of my father Ibrāhīm, the glad tidings of ʿĪsā to his people, and the vision of my mother, who saw that a light came out of her that illuminated the palaces of Syria.” He said: “Yes.”"],[4165,"ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib said: “We came to Yemen in the winter journey and stopped at a Jewish rabbi. A man of the people of the Psalms said to me: ‘O ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, will you permit me to look at your body, except for what is private?’ He opened one of my nostrils and looked into it, then looked into the other. Then he said: ‘I bear witness that in one of your hands there is kingship and in the other prophethood, and I see that in Banū Zuhrah. How is that?’ I said: ‘I do not know.’ He said: ‘Do you have a wife (shaʿah)?’ I said: ‘What is shaʿah?’ He said: ‘A wife.’ I said: ‘Not at present.’ He said: ‘When you return, marry among them.’ So ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib returned to Makkah and married Hālah bt. Wahb b. ʿAbd Manāf, and she bore him Ḥamzah and Ṣafiyyah. And ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib married Āminah bt. Wahb, and she bore the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Quraysh said when ʿAbd Allāh married Āminah: ‘ʿAbd Allāh has surpassed his father.’”"],[4166,"There was a Jew who had settled in Makkah and traded there. On the night in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born, he said in a gathering of Quraysh: “O assembly of Quraysh, has a child been born among you tonight?” They said: “By Allah, we do not know.” He said: “Allah is greater. If it has escaped you, no harm, so look and remember what I say to you: tonight the Prophet of this last community has been born. Between his shoulders there is a mark, in which there are dense hairs like the mane of a horse. He will not suckle for two nights, because an ʿifrīt from the jinn inserted his two fingers into his mouth and prevented him from suckling.” The people dispersed from their gathering, amazed at his words and talk. When they reached their homes, each one of them told his family, and they said: “A boy has been born to ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and they have named him Muḥammad.” The people met and said: “Have you heard the words of the Jew, and has the birth of this boy reached you?” They went to the Jew and told him the news. He said: “Go with me so that I may look at him.” They went out and brought him to Āminah. He said: “Bring out your son to us.” She brought him out, and they uncovered his back, and he saw that mole. The Jew fell down unconscious. When he recovered, they said: “Woe to you, what is the matter?” He said: “By Allah, prophethood has departed from the Children of Israel. You have rejoiced with him, O assembly of Quraysh. By Allah, he will launch an assault upon you whose news will spread from the east to the west.” Among the group that day to whom the Jew said what he said were Hishām b. al-Walīd b. al-Mughīrah, Musāfir b. Abī ʿAmr, ʿUbaydah b. al-Ḥārith b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and ʿUtbah b. Rabīʿah—a youth above the age of puberty—among a group of Banū Manāf and others from Quraysh."],[4167,"“O Messenger of Allah, will you stay in your house in Makkah?” He said: “Has ʿAqīl left us any dwellings or houses?” ʿAqīl had inherited Abū Ṭālib, while ʿAlī and Jaʿfar did not inherit him, because they were Muslims."],[4168,"A Bedouin asked the Prophet ﷺ about fasting on Monday. He said: “That is the day on which I was born and on which revelation was sent down to me.” It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. Muslim only cited the hadith of Shuʿbah from Qatādah with this chain: “Fasting the day of ʿArafah expiates the previous year and the year before,” according to the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[4169,"The Prophet ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant."],[4170,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was born on the Day of the Elephant.\" Humayd b. al-Rabi' was alone in this wording in this hadith, and he was not followed in it."],[4171,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born on the twelfth night that had passed of the month of Rabi' al-Awwal.\""],[4172,"\"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were born in the Year of the Elephant, like two agemates.\" Ibn Ishaq said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was twenty years old in the year of Ukaz.\""],[4173,"He said: \"O my little son, I have grieved over you as I have never grieved over anything. By Allah, I shall never send you on an errand again, and you will never part from me after this.\""],[4174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named himself to us with names, some of which we have remembered and some of which we have forgotten. He said: \"I am Muhammad, and I am Ahmad, and al-Muqaffa, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of the great battle.\""],[4175,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Muqaffa, and al-Hashir, and al-Khatam, and al-Aqib.\""],[4176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am Abu al-Qasim; Allah gives, and I distribute.\""],[4177,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, was born, Gabriel came to him and said: \"Peace be upon you, O Abu Ibrahim.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[4178,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"Who am I?\" We said: \"The Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Yes, but who am I?\" We said: \"You are Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Abdul-Muttalib b. Hashim b. Abd Manaf.\" He said: \"I am the master of the children of Adam, and there is no pride.\""],[4179,"The stepdaughter of the Prophet ﷺ, Zaynab, narrated to me, and I said to her: \"Tell me about the Prophet ﷺ: was he from Mudar?\" She said: \"From whom else could he be but from Mudar, from the descendants of al-Nadr b. Kinanah?\""],[4180,"He mentioned the birth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"His father died while his mother was pregnant with him.\""],[4181,"The Prophet ﷺ visited his mother's grave with a thousand veiled men, and no one was seen weeping more than on that day."],[4182,"I heard Ka'b b. Malik saying: When I greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said while his face was radiant—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was pleased, his face would light up as though it were a piece of the moon, and that was recognized from him."],[4183,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was neither tall nor short, with rough palms and feet, a large head and beard, tinged with redness, large joints, and a long line of hair from chest to navel. When he walked, he leaned forward as though descending a slope. I have not seen anyone like him before or after, ﷺ."],[4184,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had eyes with a reddish tinge and a wide mouth. I asked, 'What does \"ashkal al-ʿaynayn\" mean?' He said, 'Long and narrow with a reddish tinge.'"],[4185,"\"The two shins of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were thin, and he would not laugh except as a smile, and whenever I looked at him I would say: \"He put kohl on his eyes,' but he ﷺ did not use kohl.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3645)"],[4186,"I saw the seal of prophethood on the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, like a pigeon's egg."],[4187,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'O Abu Zayd, come close and wipe my back.' So I approached him and wiped his back, placing my fingers on the seal and pressing them. It was said to him, 'And what is the seal?' He said, 'Hair gathered together at his shoulders.'"],[4188,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ let his forelock hang down as long as Allah willed, then afterward he parted it."],[4189,"Hariz b. ʿUthman narrated: I said to ʿAbd Allah b. Busr al-Sulami, 'Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Was he an old man?' He said, 'There were white hairs in the hair under his lower lip.'"],[4190,"And he said to the messenger: Ask him whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dyed his hair, for I saw a hair of his that had been colored. Anas said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been favored with black hair, and if I were to count the white hairs that appeared on his head and beard, I would not add more than eleven white hairs. As for what has been colored, it is from the perfume with which he used to scent the hair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[4191,"There were only a few white hairs on the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, at the parting of his hair. When he applied oil, the oil concealed them."],[4192,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was wearing two green garments, and his hair had become gray, and his gray hair was red, dyed with henna."],[4193,"I asked ʿAʾishah, 'Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have gray hair?' She said, 'Allah did not disfigure him with white hair.'"],[4194,"It was said to Anas: What was the Prophet's ﷺ gray hair like? He said: \"Allah did not disfigure him with gray hair; there were only seventeen or eighteen [gray hairs] on his head.\""],[4195,"Aisha brought out to us a coarse woolen cloak and a thick lower garment, and she said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away in these two.\""],[4196,"\"The Prophet ﷺ had a horse named Al-Murtajiz.\""],[4197,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a horse called al-Murtajiz, a she-camel called al-Qaswa', a mule called Duldul, a donkey called 'Ufayr, a coat of mail called al-Fusul, and a sword called Dhu al-Fiqar.\" Hibban b. 'Ali was considered weak by them."],[4198,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: When were you a prophet? He said: \"While Adam was between the spirit and the body.\""],[4199,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: When did prophethood become incumbent for you? He said: \"Between the creation of Adam and the blowing of the spirit into him.\""],[4200,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do not insult Waraqah, for I have seen that he will have a garden, or two gardens.”"],[4201,"Waraqah b. Nawfal b. Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza, regarding what Khadijah mentioned to him about the affairs of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, recited poetry: \"[meter: al-basit] O for men, and the turns of time and destiny, and what is there for anything Allah has decreed of change; even Khadijah calls me to inform her, but she has no knowledge of the hidden unseen. She came to ask me about him, to tell her of a matter I see will come to people of later times. She told me of something I had heard of in the ancient past and ages: that Ahmad will come and Gabriel will tell him that you are sent to mankind. I said: Perhaps what you hope for, Allah will fulfill for you, so hope for good and wait. Send him to us so that we may question him about his affair, what he sees in sleep and wakefulness. Then when he came to us, he spoke amazing words at which the skin and hair stood on end: 'I saw the Trusted One of Allah facing me in a form perfected of the most majestic forms.' Then it continued, and fear would terrify me from what it greeted of the trees around me. I said: I think, though I do not know if he will prove me true, that you will be sent reciting the revealed surahs, and I will come to you if you proclaim their call to jihad without reproach or distress.\""],[4202,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent as a prophet at the age of forty after the [Year of the] Elephant.\""],[4203,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, regarding the revelation: he became extremely distressed about that. I said, because of what I saw of his distress: Your Lord has surely forsaken you due to the distress He sees in you. Then Allah revealed: {Your Lord has not forsaken you, nor has He become displeased} [al-Duha: 3]."],[4204,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Gabriel: \"What prevents you from visiting us more than you do?\" Then Allah, glorified and exalted, revealed: {And we do not descend except by the command of your Lord} [Maryam: 64], up to His saying: {And your Lord is never forgetful} [Maryam: 64]."],[4205,"The Qur'an was separated from the Remembrance and placed in the House of Might in the lowest heaven. Gabriel ﷺ then brought it down to the Prophet ﷺ gradually, {and We have recited it in a measured recitation} [al-Furqan: 32]. Sufyan said: \"Five verses or so.\""],[4206,"\"We used to compile the Qur'an from parchment fragments in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4207,"When Gabriel ﷺ descended and said: 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful,' he knew it was a surah."],[4208,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pass by the market of Dhul-Majaz while I was among my merchandise. He passed wearing a red hulla, and I heard him saying: \"O people, say: There is no god but Allah, and you will succeed.\" A man was following him, throwing stones at him, and had made his heel bleed, while he was saying: \"O people, do not obey this one, for he is a liar.\" I said: \"Who is this?\" It was said: \"A young man from Banu Abdul-Muttalib.\" When Allah made Islam prevail, we left al-Rabadha with a woman of ours in a litter until we stopped near Madinah. While we were sitting, a man came to us wearing two garments and greeted us. He said: \"Where are the people from?\" We said: \"From al-Rabadha, and we have a red camel with us.\" He said: \"Will you sell me this camel?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"For how much?\" We said: \"For such-and-such a measure of dates.\" He said: \"I take it,\" and he did not haggle. He took the camel's halter and went away until he disappeared among the walls of Madinah. Some of us said to others: \"Do you know the man?\" None of us knew him. The people blamed one another, saying: \"You give your camel to someone you do not know!\" The woman in the litter said: \"Do not blame one another, for we have seen a man who will not betray you; I have never seen anything more like the full moon at night than his face.\" In the evening a man came to us and said: \"Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Are you the ones who came from al-Rabadha?\" We said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I am the messenger of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to you. He commands you to eat from these dates until you are full, and to measure until you receive in full.\" We ate dates until we were full and measured until we received in full. Then we came to Madinah the next day, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ standing and preaching to the people on the pulpit. I heard him say: \"The upper hand is the giving hand, and begin with those you support: your mother, your father, your sister, your brother, then your nearest, then your nearest.\" Then a man from the Ansar said: \"O Messenger of Allah, these are Banu Tha'laba ibn Yarbu' who killed so-and-so in the Jahiliyyah, so avenge us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his hands until I saw the whiteness of his armpits and said: \"A mother does not bear the crime of her child; a mother does not bear the crime of her child.\""],[4209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to present himself to the people in a certain situation and say, \"Is there anyone who can take me to his people? The Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the words of my Lord.\" So a man from the Bani Hamdan came to him and said, \"I can.\" He asked, \"Are there any restrictions among your people?\" The man replied, \"Yes.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then asked, \"Where are you from?\" He said, \"From Hamdan.\" Then the man from Hamdan feared that his people might harm him, so he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I will go to my people and inform them, and then I will meet you in 'Aam Qabil.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"Yes.\" So he set off and the delegation of the Ansar came in the month of Rajab."],[4210,"\"I was sent to perfect righteous character.\""],[4211,"About the character of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , she said, \"Don't you read the Quran?\" He said, \"Indeed, yes.\" She said, \"Verily, the character of the Prophet of Allah ﷺ is the Quran.\""],[4212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never cursed a Muslim with a curse that is remembered, never struck anything with his hand except when striking in the path of Allah, never was asked for something and refused it unless he was asked for a sin, in which case he was the farthest of people from it, never took revenge for himself for anything brought to him unless the sacred limits of Allah were violated, in which case he took revenge for Allah, and never was given a choice between two matters but chose the easier of them. And when he renewed his covenant with Jibril to study with him, he was more generous with good than the sent wind.\""],[4213,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is described in the Gospel: not harsh, nor hard-hearted, nor noisy in the markets; he does not repay evil with its like, but he pardons and overlooks."],[4214,"I heard Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah much, speak little nonsense, lengthen the prayer, shorten the sermon, and not disdain to walk with a slave or a widow until he fulfilled their need for them.\""],[4215,"I heard Abu Sa'id al-Khudri say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to remember Allah much, speak little nonsense, lengthen the prayer, shorten the sermon, and not disdain to walk with a slave or a widow until he fulfilled their need for them.\""],[4216,"\"Allah revealed to Jesus ﷺ , 'O Jesus, believe in Muhammad and instruct those from your nation who will meet him to believe in him. If it were not for Muhammad, I would not have created Adam, and if it were not for Muhammad, I would not have created Paradise and Hell. Indeed, I created the Throne upon water, and it shook. So I wrote on it: There is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, and it became still.'\""],[4217,"When Adam committed the sin, he said: \"O Lord, I ask You by the right of Muhammad that You forgive me.\" Allah said: \"O Adam, how did you know Muhammad when I have not created him?\" He said: \"O Lord, because when You created me with Your hand and breathed into me of Your spirit, I raised my head and saw written on the legs of the Throne: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. So I knew that You would not attach to Your name except the most beloved of creation to You.\" Allah said: \"You have spoken the truth, O Adam. Indeed, he is the most beloved of creation to Me. Call upon Me by his right, for I have forgiven you. And were it not for Muhammad, I would not have created you.\""],[4218,"Abu Talib went out to Syria, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went with him among elders of Quraysh. When they came in sight of the monk, they descended and changed their saddles. The monk came out to them, whereas before that they used to pass by him and he would not come out to them nor pay attention. He was walking among them while they were unloading their saddles, until he came and took the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: \"This is the master of the worlds; this is the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds; this is one whom Allah will send as a mercy to the worlds.\" Elders of Quraysh said to him: \"What is your knowledge of that?\" He said: \"When you appeared from the mountain pass, there remained no tree or stone but fell down prostrating, and they prostrate only to a prophet. I recognize him by the seal of prophethood below the cartilage of his shoulder, like an apple.\" Then he went back and prepared food for them, then came to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among the camel herds. He said: \"Send for him.\" He came with a cloud shading him. He said: \"Look at him, a cloud shades him.\" When he drew near the people, he found that they had preceded him to the shade of the tree. When he sat down, the shade of the tree inclined over him. He said: \"Look at the shade of the tree, it inclined over him.\" While he was standing with him, he adjured them not to take him to the Byzantines, for if the Byzantines saw him they would recognize him by description and kill him. Then he turned and saw seven men coming from the Byzantines. He met them and said: \"What has brought you?\" They said: \"We have come because this prophet is emerging in this month, and no road remains but people have been sent to it, and we have been sent to this road of his.\" The monk said to them: \"Have you left behind anyone better than you?\" They said: \"No. We were only informed of his news, so we were sent to this road of yours.\" He said: \"Do you think that if Allah wills a matter to be decreed, any of the people can repel it?\" They said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then pledge allegiance to him.\" They pledged allegiance to him and stayed with him. Then the monk came to them and said: \"I adjure you by Allah, which of you is his guardian?\" Abu Talib kept adjuring him until he sent him back. Abu Bakr sent Bilal with him, and the monk provisioned him with cakes and oil."],[4219,"That a man asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"How was the beginning of your affair, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"My wet nurse was from Banu Sa'd ibn Bakr. I went with a son of hers to tend some lambs of ours, and we did not take any provisions with us. I said: 'O my brother, go and bring us provisions from our mother.' My brother went, and I remained with the lambs. Two white birds came like two eagles. One of them said to the other: 'Is it he?' The other said: 'Yes.' They came hastening to me, took me, laid me on my back, split my belly, then extracted my heart and split it, and took out two black clots from it. One of them said to the other: 'Cleanse it,' meaning 'mark it,' and 'seal it with the seal of prophethood.' Then one of them said to the other: 'Put him in one scale and put a thousand of his nation in the other scale.' I looked at the thousand above me, fearing they would fall on me. They said: 'If his entire nation were weighed against him, he would outweigh them.' Then they went away and left me. I was terrified with a great fear. Then I went to my mother and told her what I had seen. She feared that I had been afflicted, so she said: 'I seek refuge for you with Allah.' She saddled a camel of hers, placed me on the saddle, and rode behind me until we reached my mother. She said: 'I have fulfilled my trust and my duty,' and told her what I had encountered. That did not alarm her, and she said: 'I saw a light come out of me that illuminated the palaces of Syria.'\""],[4220,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey and stopped at a place. Suddenly there was a man in the valley saying: \"O Allah, make me from the nation of Muhammad, the one shown mercy, forgiven, and rewarded for it.\" He said: I looked over the valley, and there was a man whose height was more than three hundred cubits. He said to me: \"Who are you?\" I said: \"Anas ibn Malik, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: \"Where is he?\" I said: \"There he is, hearing your words.\" He said: \"Go to him and convey my greetings of peace to him, and say: Your brother Ilyas conveys greetings of peace to you.\" I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He came until he met him, embraced him, and greeted him. Then they sat talking. He said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, I eat only one day each year, and this is my day of breaking fast, so I and you will eat.\" A table descended upon them from the sky with bread, fish, and celery on it. They ate and fed me. We prayed the afternoon prayer, then he bade him farewell. Then I saw him pass on the clouds towards the sky."],[4221,"I traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and saw something amazing from him. We stopped at a place, and he said: \"Go to these two trees and say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ says to you to come together.\" I went and said that to them. Each one of them was uprooted from its root, and each went to its companion until they met together. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ relieved himself behind them, then said: \"Go and say to them: Let each one return to its place.\" I came to them and said that, and each one returned to its place. Sahih."],[4222,"That he narrated to him that \"a bowl was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people kept eating from it. Whenever a group was full, another group sat in their place. He said: 'Thus it was until the first prayer.' A man said: 'Was it replenished with something?' Samura said: 'It was not replenished except from the sky.'\""],[4223,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, and the people were afflicted with severe hunger. The people asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to slaughter some of their riding camels, and they said, 'Allah will help us reach our destination by means of them.' When Umar b. al-Khattab saw that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was about to grant them permission to slaughter some of their riding camels, he said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how will we be tomorrow when we meet the enemy hungry and on foot? But if you see fit, O Messenger of Allah, call upon the people to bring the remnants of their provisions.' So the people began to come with a handful of food and more than that. The one who brought the most came with a sa' of dates. He gathered it all. Then he stood and supplicated as Allah willed him to supplicate. Then he called the army with their vessels, then he ordered them to fill up whatever remained of the army. They did not leave any vessel without filling it, and the like of it remained. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed until his molars appeared."],[4224,"I sailed the sea on a ship, and it broke apart, so I rode upon a plank from it, and it cast me onto a thicket in which there was a lion. Nothing frightened me except it, so I said, “O Abu al-Harith, I am a client of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then it lowered its head and nudged my side with its shoulder, and it kept nudging me and guiding me to the road until it set me upon the road. When it set me down, it murmured, and I thought that it was bidding me farewell."],[4225,"We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a desert Arab—an eloquent Bedouin from Yemen—entered on a red she-camel. He made it kneel at the door of the mosque, then came in, greeted us, and sat down. When he had finished, they said, “O Messenger of Allah, the she-camel under the Bedouin is stolen.” He said, “Is there proof?” They said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “O ʿAlī, take Allah’s due from the Bedouin if the proof is established against him; and if it is not established, then return him to me.” The Bedouin lowered his head for a while. Then the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Stand, O Bedouin, for Allah’s matter; otherwise present your argument.” Whereupon the she-camel spoke from behind the door: “By Him who sent you with honor, O Messenger of Allah, this man did not steal me, and no one has owned me other than he.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “O Bedouin, by Him who made her speak in your defense—what was it that you said?” He replied, “I said: O Allah, You are not a Lord whom we have newly invented, nor is there with You a god who aided You in creating us, nor is there with You any lord such that we would doubt Your lordship. You are our Lord as we say, and above what those who speak can say. I ask You to send blessings upon Muhammad and to clear me by my innocence.” The Prophet ﷺ said to him, “By Him who sent me with honor, O Bedouin, I have indeed seen the angels racing to the mouths of the alleys, writing down your words—so increase your prayers for blessings upon me.”[1]"],[4226,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'By what do I know that you are the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'What do you think? If I call this date stalk from this palm tree, will you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then he called the date stalk, and the date stalk began to descend from the palm tree until it fell to the ground, then it began to hop until it came to the Prophet ﷺ.' He said, 'Then he said to it, \"Return,\" and it returned until it went back to its place.'"],[4227,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah, and he went out to one of its outskirts. No tree or mountain faced him except that it said, 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.'"],[4228,"I fell ill, and the Prophet ﷺ came to me while I was saying, 'O Allah, if my appointed time has come, then give me rest; and if it is delayed, then raise me; and if it is a trial, then give me patience.' He said, 'What did you say?' I repeated it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Allah, heal him. O Allah, grant him well-being.' Then he said, 'Stand up.' I stood up, and that pain never returned to me afterwards."],[4229,"There is no believing man or believing woman on the face of the earth but that he loves me. He said: I said, 'And what is your knowledge of that, O Abu Hurayrah?' He said, 'I used to call my mother to Islam, but she refused. One day I called her, and she made me hear about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I disliked. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I used to call my mother to Islam, but she refuses. One day I called her, and she made me hear about you what I dislike. So supplicate to Allah, O Messenger of Allah, to guide the mother of Abu Hurayrah to Islam.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for her. I returned to my mother to give her the good news of the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When I was at the door, the door was locked. I knocked on the door, and she heard my sound, so she put on her clothes and placed her head covering, and said, \"Gently, O Abu Hurayrah.\" She opened the door for me. When I entered, she said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ weeping from joy as I used to weep from sorrow, and I said, \"Rejoice, O Messenger of Allah, Allah has answered your supplication and guided the mother of Abu Hurayrah to Islam.\" I said, \"Supplicate to Allah to make me and my mother beloved to His believing servants and to make them beloved to us.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, make this servant of Yours and his mother beloved to Your believing servants, and make them beloved to them.\" So there is no believer, man or woman, on the earth but that he loves me and I love him.'"],[4230,"A certain man used to sit with the Prophet ﷺ, and whenever the Prophet ﷺ spoke something, his face would twitch. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'Be like that.' He continued to twitch until he died."],[4231,"A Jew called Jurayjirah had some dinars owed to him by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He demanded payment from the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him, 'O Jew, I do not have what I can give you.' He said, 'Then I will not leave you, O Muhammad, until you give it to me.' He ﷺ said, 'Then I will sit with you.' So he sat with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in that place the noon prayer, the afternoon prayer, the sunset prayer, the night prayer, and the dawn prayer. The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were threatening him and intimidating him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed, and said, 'What are you doing to him?' They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, a Jew is detaining you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'My Lord has forbidden me from wronging a person under treaty, or anyone else.' When the day declined, the Jew said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger.' And he said, 'Half of my wealth is in the cause of Allah. By Allah, I did what I did to you only to look at your description in the Torah: Muhammad b. Abdullah, his birthplace is Makkah, his migration is to Taybah, and his kingdom is in Syria. He is not harsh or coarse, nor does he shout in the markets, nor does he adorn himself with obscenity or foul speech. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are the Messenger of Allah. This is my wealth, so judge in it as Allah has shown you.' The Jew was very wealthy. This hadith is utterly rejected."],[4232,"Quraysh remained weak and submissive until Abu Talib died."],[4233,"The name of the Negus was Mashamah, and in Arabic it is Atiyyah. Indeed, al-Najashi is the title of the king, like saying Khusraw and Heraclius."],[4234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to the Negus, and we were about eighty men. He mentioned the hadith in full as I have narrated it in the commentary."],[4235,"Uthman b. Affan and his wife Ruqayyah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out as emigrants from Makkah to the first Abyssinia. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah, then they emigrated to Madinah. The two Shaykhs agreed on the transmission of the hadith of Ibn Abi Shaybah and others from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Ubayd Allah b. Adi, from al-Miswar b. Makhramah about the departure of Uthman b. Affan to the land of Abyssinia, and they narrated the hadith in full. Therefore, I abbreviated the narration of Musa b. Uqbah from Ibn Ishaq, and he mentioned in the Maghazi that Ruqayyah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, as they mentioned, was not seen among the Arabs or the Abyssinians as more beautiful than her. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4236,"Abu Talib recited verses to the Negus urging them to treat them well as neighbors and to defend them: 'Let the best of people know that Muhammad is a vizier to Moses and the Messiah, son of Mary. He brought us guidance like what they brought, and each, by Allah's command, guides and protects. And you recite it in your book with truthful speech, not the speech of the mubarjim. No band comes to you seeking your favor but that they are returned with honor.'"],[4237,"I came from the land of Abyssinia while I was a young girl, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed me with a khamīṣa that had markings. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began wiping the markings with his hand and saying, 'Sanāh, sanāh,' meaning 'Good, good.'"],[4238,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I do not know which of the two I am more delighted about: the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Jaʿfar.'"],[4239,"'We were eleven at the first ʿAqaba in the coming year, and we gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the pledge of women before war was made obligatory upon us.'"],[4240,"Indeed, the Prophet ﷺ spent ten years following people in their homes during the season of Manazil, Muzdalifah, and 'Ukaz. He would ask, \"Who will shelter me? Who will support me until I convey the messages of my Lord, and for him is Paradise?\" Yet, he would find no one to support him or shelter him. And there would be a man who would leave from Egypt or Yemen to bring him back to his people, and they would warn him, \"Beware of the young Quraishi boy who will tempt you.\" He would walk among their tents, calling them to Allah Almighty, and they would point at him with their fingers. Then Allah sent us from Yathrib (Medina), and the man from among us would meet him, believe in him, and teach him the Quran. He would then return to his people, and they would embrace Islam until there was not a single house among the houses of the Ansar without Muslims in it. We sent a message to Allah, and He allowed us to gather and meet. We said, \"How long will the Messenger of Allah ﷺ be expelled in the mountains of Makkah and live in fear?\" So we set out until we reached him in Muzdalifah during the pilgrimage season. We made an agreement with him at 'Aqabah, and his uncle, al-'Abbas, said to him, \"O son of my brother, I do not know who these people who have come to you are. I have knowledge of the people of Yathrib, so we gathered with a man, and when al-'Abbas looked at our faces, he said, 'These are people we do not know. They are young men.' So we said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do we pledge allegiance to you on?' He said, 'Pledge allegiance to me on hearing and obeying, in times of energy and times of laziness, on spending in times of ease and times of hardship, on commanding good and forbidding evil, and on not blaming us for what we do in the name of Allah. Pledge allegiance to me on supporting me when I come to you, and withholding from what you withhold from yourselves, your wives, and your children. And for you is Paradise.' So we pledged allegiance to him, and Sa'd bin Zurarah, the youngest among the seventy, took his hand and said, 'O people of Yathrib, none of us withholds his hand from this pledge, and we will never quit it.' So we went to him, each man one by one, and he took our pledge to grant us Paradise.\""],[4241,"'Between the night of ʿAqaba and the emigration of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there were three months or close to that. The pledge of the Ansar to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on the night of ʿAqaba in Dhu al-Hijja, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah in the month of Rabiʿ al-Awwal.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4242,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to the leaders from the Ansar, 'Will you shelter me and protect me?' They said, 'Yes, so what is for us?' He said, 'Paradise.'"],[4243,"He said: The first of the emigrants to come to us in Madinah were Musʿab b. ʿUmayr and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they used to teach us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived after I had read 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' and some surahs from the Mufassal. Then Saʿd b. Malik and ʿAmmar b. Yasir came. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khattab came with twenty. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and we were not delighted with anything as much as we were delighted with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The women and children began running about saying, 'This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[4244,"I said to ʿUrwa b. al-Zubayr, 'How long did the Prophet ﷺ stay in Makkah?' He said, 'Ten years.' I said, 'But Ibn ʿAbbas says, \"He stayed for fifteen years.\"' He said, 'He took it from the saying of the poet.' Sufyan b. ʿUyayna said: Yahya b. Saʿid narrated to us, he said: I heard an old woman from the Ansar say: I saw Ibn ʿAbbas frequenting Ṣirma b. Qays to learn from him these verses [al-baḥr al-ṭawīl]: \"He stayed in Quraysh for fifteen years, reminding, if only he had found a congenial friend. He would present himself to the people at the gatherings, but he saw no one to shelter him and no one to call. When he came to us and the journey's goal settled with him, he became happy and content with Ṭayba. He no longer feared the injustice of any wrongdoer, far away, nor feared any aggressor among people. We gave him our wealth from the best of what we owned, and ourselves in battle and in consolation. We show enmity to all those among people who show enmity to him, with justice, even if that loved one is congenial. We know that God is the only reality besides Him, and that the Book of God has become a guide.'\""],[4245,"'The Prophet ﷺ stayed in Makkah for fifteen years: seven and eight, seeing the light and hearing the sound. And he stayed in Madinah for ten.' According to the condition of Muslim."],[4246,"'That Allah ﷻ kept His Prophet ﷺ in Makkah for thirteen years.'"],[4247,"The Prophet said: 'Allah ﷻ revealed to me, \"Whichever of these three lands you settle in, it is your abode of emigration: Madinah, al-Bahrayn, or Qinnasrīn.\"'"],[4248,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in Makkah when he was commanded to emigrate, and it was revealed to him: {And say, \"My Lord, cause me to enter a truthful entrance and to exit a truthful exit, and grant me from Yourself a supporting authority\"} [Al-Isra 80]."],[4249,"From Qatada regarding His saying, the Exalted, {And say, \"My Lord, cause me to enter a truthful entrance and to exit a truthful exit\"} [Al-Isra 80]: 'So Allah brought him out of Makkah to Madinah as a truthful exit, and He brought him into Madinah as a truthful entrance.' He said: 'And the Prophet of Allah ﷺ knew that he had no power over this matter except with authority, so he asked for a supporting authority for the Book of Allah, the limits of Allah, the obligations of Allah, and the establishment of the Book of Allah. Indeed, authority is a might from Allah which He placed among His servants. Were it not for that, some of them would raid others, and the strong among them would devour the weak.'"],[4250,"O Allah, You have brought me out of the most beloved land to me, so settle me in the most beloved land to You."],[4251,"The Prophet ﷺ said to the Muslims: \"I have been shown the abode of your emigration: a salty land with date palms between two lava tracts,\" namely the two harrahs."],[4252,"Ali purchased his own self and wore the garment of the Prophet ﷺ, then slept in his place. The polytheists were shooting arrows at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had clothed him in a striped cloak. Quraysh wanted to kill the Prophet ﷺ, so they kept shooting at Ali, thinking he was the Prophet ﷺ because he had put on the striped cloak. Ali began to writhe, and when it became clear that he was Ali, they said: \"You are indeed despicable; you are writhing, whereas your companion would not writhe, and we have disapproved of that in you.\""],[4253,"Ali said when he spent the night on the bed of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, in verse (meter: al-tawil):I protected with my own self the best of those who have trodden the pebbles,And who circumambulated the Ancient House and the Stone;A Messenger of a god who feared they would plot against him,So the God of bounty saved him from the plot.The Messenger of Allah spent the night in the cave safe and protected,In the keeping of God and under a veil;While I spent the night watching them, and they did not suspect me,And I had resolved myself upon death or capture.Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4254,"On the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to sleep on his bed and he left Makkah as an emigrant, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me to the idols and said: \"Sit.\" So I sat beside the Kaaba. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed onto my shoulder and said: \"Rise.\" So I rose with him. When he saw my weakness beneath him, he said: \"Sit.\" So I sat and let him down from me. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat for me and said: \"O Ali, climb onto my shoulder.\" So I climbed onto his shoulders. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rose with me, and it seemed to me that if I wished I could touch the sky. I climbed onto the Kaaba, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ moved aside. I threw down their greatest idol, which was of copper, fastened to the ground with iron pegs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Work at it.\" So I worked at it, and I kept working at it while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Go on, go on.\" I kept working at it until I got a firm hold of it. Then he said: \"Smash it.\" So I smashed it and broke it, and I came down."],[4255,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Jibril ﷺ : \"Who will emigrate with me?\" He said: \"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq.\""],[4256,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out from Mecca to Medina and Abu Bakr was with him, Abu Bakr carried all his wealth, which was five or six thousand dirhams. Then my grandfather, Abu Qhafa, came to me, although he had lost his sight, and he said, \"By Allah, he has saddened you with his wealth, taking it with him.\" I said, \"No, father, he has left us with plenty of goodness.\" I went to some rocks and placed them in a corner of the house, and Abu Bakr used to store his wealth there. I covered the rocks with a cloth and then I took my grandfather by the hand and placed it on the cloth. He said, \"Indeed, if he has left all this, then it is good.\" She said, \"By Allah, he did not leave a little or a lot.\""],[4257,"Some men mentioned, during the caliphate of Umar, that they considered Umar superior to Abu Bakr. That reached Umar, and he said: \"By Allah, a single night of Abu Bakr is better than the family of Umar, and a single day of Abu Bakr is better than the family of Umar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out to go to the cave with Abu Bakr. He would walk for a while in front of him and for a while behind him, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ noticed it and said: 'O Abu Bakr, why do you walk sometimes in front of me and sometimes behind me?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I remember the pursuers and walk behind you; then I remember the ambush and walk in front of you.' He said: 'O Abu Bakr, if anything were to happen, would you prefer it to befall you rather than me?' He said: 'Yes, by the One who sent you with the truth, no affliction would befall but that I would wish it upon myself rather than you.' When they reached the cave, Abu Bakr said: 'Stay where you are, O Messenger of Allah, until I inspect the cave for you.' He entered and inspected it. When he was in its upper part, he remembered that he had not inspected a side chamber, so he said: 'Stay where you are, O Messenger of Allah, until I inspect the side chamber.' He entered and inspected it, then said: 'Come down, O Messenger of Allah.' So he came down. Umar said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, that night is better than the family of Umar.'\""],[4258,"He informed him that he heard Suraqah b. Ju'shum say: \"The messengers of the disbelievers of Quraysh came to us, offering a bloodwit for each of the two, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, to whoever killed or captured them. While I was sitting in one of the gatherings of my people, the Banu Mudlij, a man from among them came and stood over us and said: 'O Suraqah, I have just seen some dark figures by the shore; I think they are Muhammad and his companions.' Suraqah said: 'I knew that they were indeed they, so I said to them: \"They are not them; rather I saw so-and-so and so-and-so. Go as seekers.\"' He said: 'Then I stayed in the gathering only a short while before I got up, entered my house, and ordered my slave girl to bring out my horse, which was behind a hillock, and hold it for me. I took my spear and went out from the back of the house, drawing the butt of the spear on the ground and holding the spearhead high, until I came to my horse and mounted it. I urged it on, and it galloped with me until I saw their two dark figures. When I drew near them, close enough for them to hear my voice, my horse stumbled and I fell off. I got up and reached for my quiver, took out the divining arrows, and drew lots with them, and the one I disliked came out: that I should not harm them. But I disobeyed the arrows and mounted my horse, urging it on until, when I drew near them, I heard the recitation of the Prophet ﷺ, and he was not turning around, while Abu Bakr was turning around often. Then the forelegs of my horse sank into the ground up to the knees, and I fell off. Then I spurred it and rose, and it could hardly pull out its forelegs. When it stood upright, there was a column of smoke rising from the tracks of its forelegs into the sky.'\" Abdullah (the transmitter) said: \"That is the smoke that appears without fire.\" \"Then I took out the divining arrows and cast lots, and the one I disliked came out: that I should not harm them. So I called out to them for safety, and they stopped. I rode my horse until I came to them. It occurred to me, because of the obstacle I had encountered in reaching them, that the affair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would prevail. I said to him: 'Your people have set a bloodwit for you.' I told them the news of their journey and what the people intended against them, and I offered them provisions and goods, but they took nothing from me and asked only that I conceal their whereabouts. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to write for me a document of peace by which I would be safe, and he ordered Amir b. Fuhayrah, the freedman of Abu Bakr, and he wrote it for me on a piece of leather. Then they went on.\""],[4259,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was on his mount at al-Hazwarah, saying: \"By Allah, you are the best of Allah's land and the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah; and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.\""],[4260,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah, Abu Bakr said, \"Indeed, to Allah we belong and to Him we shall return.\" [Quran 2:156] The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was expelled to be destroyed, so this verse was revealed, \"Permission [to fight] has been granted to those who are being fought, because they were wronged. And indeed, Allah is competent to give them victory. Those who have been expelled from their homes unjustly\" [Quran 22:39-40]. Abu Bakr realized that there would be a battle."],[4261,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out of the cave as an emigrant, with Abu Bakr and Amir b. Fuhayrah, Abu Bakr riding behind him and Abd Allah b. Urayqit al-Laythi behind them, he took them by the lower route of Makkah, then went on with them until he descended with them to the coast below Usfan, then crossed with them below Amaj, then crossed the road after passing Qudayd, then took them through al-Hijaz, then crossed with them Thaniyyat al-Mirar, then took them through al-Hafya', then crossed with them Mudlijat Liqf, then descended with them into Mudlijat Majah, then took them through Madhhij, then through Batn Madhhij from Dhu al-Ghusn, then through Batn Dhi Kashd, then took al-Jubajib, then took Dhi Salm from Batn A'la Mudlijah, then took al-Qahah, then descended al-Arj, then took Thaniyyat al-Gha'ir to the right of his mount, then descended Batn Rim, and arrived at Quba' among the Banu Amr b. Awf."],[4262,"When the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr set out in concealment, they passed by a slave tending sheep and asked him for milk to drink. He said: \"I have no ewe that can be milked, except that here is a young she-goat that conceived at the beginning of winter and has miscarried, and no milk remains for her.\" He said: \"Bring her.\" So he brought her, and the Prophet ﷺ tied her legs, wiped her udder, and prayed until she let down milk. He said: \"Abu Bakr came with a leather shield, and Abu Bakr milked; then he milked and gave the shepherd to drink; then he milked and drank.\" The shepherd said: \"By Allah, who are you? For by Allah, I have never seen the like of you.\" He said: \"Do you think you can keep my secret until I tell you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I am Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"Are you the one whom Quraysh claim is a Sabian?\" He said: \"They do say that.\" He said: \"I bear witness that you are a prophet, and I bear witness that what you have brought is true, and that no one does what you have done except a prophet; and I will follow you.\" He said: \"You cannot do that today; but when you hear that I have prevailed, come to us.\""],[4263,"From his father Hisham b. Hubaysh b. Khuwaylid, a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left Makkah as an emigrant to Madinah, with Abu Bakr and the freedman of Abu Bakr, Amir b. Fuhayrah, and their guide al-Laythi, Abd Allah b. Urayqit. They passed by the tent of Umm Ma'bad al-Khuza'iyyah. She was a sturdy, hardy woman who would sit on her knees in the courtyard of the tent and then serve water and food. They asked her for meat and dates to buy, but they found none of that with her. The people were exhausted and emaciated. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at a sheep in the corner of the tent and said: \"What is this sheep, O Umm Ma'bad?\" She said: \"A sheep left behind by weakness from the flock.\" He said: \"Does it have any milk?\" She said: \"She is too weak for that.\" He said: \"Will you permit me to milk her?\" She said: \"May my father and mother be your ransom; if you see any milk in her, milk her.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for her, wiped her udder with his hand, mentioned the name of Allah Almighty, and prayed for her sheep. She spread her legs for him and let down milk abundantly; she chewed her cud. He called for a vessel large enough for a group to sit around, and milked into it a copious flow until froth appeared on top. Then he gave her to drink until she was satisfied, and gave his companions to drink until they were satisfied, and he himself drank last, until they were all refreshed. Then he milked into it a second time after a pause until he filled the vessel, and left it with her. Then he took a pledge from her, and they departed from her. She had not waited long before her husband Abu Ma'bad came, driving some lean goats that staggered from emaciation, with little marrow. When Abu Ma'bad saw the milk, he was amazed and said: \"Where did you get this, O Umm Ma'bad, when the sheep is away and barren, and there is no milking animal in the house?\" She said: \"No, by Allah, except that a blessed man passed by us, and his condition was such and such.\" He said: \"Describe him to me, O Umm Ma'bad.\" She said: \"I saw a man of evident cleanliness, bright-faced, handsome in form; no stoutness marred him, nor did leanness diminish him. He was comely and well-proportioned; in his eyes there was deep blackness, in his eyelashes there was thickness, in his voice there was a slight hoarseness, in his neck there was a fine length, in his beard there was fullness. He had arched eyebrows and joined eyebrows. When he was silent, dignity surrounded him; when he spoke, he captivated and was crowned with splendor. He was the most beautiful of people and most radiant from a distance, and the finest and most beautiful from near. His speech was sweet and distinct, neither scanty nor verbose; his words were like strung pearls flowing down. He was of medium height; tallness did not make him unattractive, nor did shortness disappoint the eye. He was a branch between two branches, the freshest of the three in appearance and the best in stature. He had companions surrounding him: if he spoke, they listened to his words; if he commanded, they hastened to his command. He was served and honored; he was not frowning nor weak-minded.\" Abu Ma'bad said: \"By Allah, this is the man of Quraysh whose affair was mentioned to us, and I intended to accompany him, and I will do so if I find a way.\" In the morning, a voice in Makkah rose high, they could hear the voice but did not know its owner, saying (meter: al-tawil):May God, the Lord of mankind, reward with the best reward two companionsWho alighted at the tent of Umm Ma'bad.They stopped there with guidance, and by him she was guided;So he has triumphed who became a companion of Muhammad.O Banu Qusayy, what has God withheld from youOf deeds that cannot be recompensed, and of sovereignty?May Abu Bakr be congratulated on the good fortune of his ancestorBy accompanying him; whom God makes happy, he is happy.May Banu Ka'b be congratulated on the standing of their maidenAnd her seat as a lookout for the believers.Ask your sister about her sheep and her vessel,For if you ask the sheep, it will testify.He called for a barren sheep, and it yieldedFor him pure milk, the udder of the sheep frothing.He left it as a pledge with her for a milkerWho returns it again after coming to drink.When Hassan heard the caller saying that, he composed verses in response, saying (meter: al-tawil):A people have failed from whom their prophet departed,And blessed is he who travels to them and comes.He departed from a people whose minds went astray,And settled among a people with a renewed light.Their Lord guided them with it after misguidance,And He directs them; whoever follows the truth is rightly guided.Are the misguided of a people who behaved foolishly in blindness equalTo guides who are guided by one rightly guided?Upon the people of Yathrib have alightedThe mounts of guidance, descending upon them with the most fortunate.A prophet who sees what the people around him do not see,And recites the Book of Allah in every gathering.If he speaks one day about an unseen matter,Its confirmation comes that day or the next morning."],[4264,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one night as an emigrant. He then mentioned the hadith at length, similar to the hadith of Sulayman b. al-Hakam. As for the hadith of the two tents, well known by its narrators, it has"],[4265,"From his father, they mentioned the hadith at length, similar to the hadith of Abu Ma'bad. I said to our shaykh Abu Bakr al-Qati'i: Did the shaykh hear it from Mukram? He said: Yes, by Allah, my father took me on Hajj when I was seven years old and brought me to Mukram b. Muhriz. There is nothing in these chains that meets the criteria of the Sahih."],[4266,"He met the caravan of Muslims—they were merchants returning from Syria, heading back from Makkah—they intercepted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr with white garments when they heard of their departure. When the Muslims in Madinah heard of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ departure, they would go out every morning to the Harrah and wait for him until the heat of midday became unbearable. One day they returned after waiting a long time. When they had gone into their homes, a Jew climbed to the top of one of their forts to look out, and he caught sight of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions, dressed in white, with the mirage shimmering around them. The Jew could not help but cry out at the top of his voice: 'O assembly of Arabs, this is your companion whom you have been waiting for!' The Muslims rushed to their weapons and met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the edge of the Harrah."],[4267,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque of Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, which is the mosque of Quba, and prayed in it. Some men of the Ansar entered upon him, greeting him. Ibn 'Umar said: Suhayb entered with them. I asked him: How did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ respond when someone greeted him while he was praying? He said: 'He would gesture with his hand.'"],[4268,"'Whoever goes out until he comes to this mosque—meaning the mosque of Quba—and prays in it, it is like the reward of an 'umrah.'"],[4269,"'That I pray in the mosque of Quba is dearer to me than that I pray in the mosque of Jerusalem.'"],[4270,"From him, he said: 'I witnessed the day the Prophet ﷺ entered Madinah, and I have never seen a day more beautiful or more radiant than it.'"],[4271,"\"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued until he reached Medina, and the people came out until we entered the road, and the women, servants, and young boys were shouting, \"Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, Allah is the Greatest! Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah!\" When he woke up in the morning, he set out and stopped where he was commanded.\""],[4272,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Al-Madinah, the people rushed towards him and it was said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come!’ I came along with the people to see him, and when I looked at the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I realized that his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing he said was: “O people, spread (the greeting of) Salam, offer food to people and pray at night when people are sleeping, you will enter Paradise in peace.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1334)"],[4273,"From Safinah, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ built the mosque, Abu Bakr came with a stone and placed it. Then 'Umar came with a stone and placed it. Then 'Uthman came with a stone and placed it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'These are the rulers of affairs after me.' This hadith has a sound chain, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[4274,"'The people erred regarding the calendar. They did not count from his pledge of allegiance nor from his death; they only counted from his arrival in Madinah.'"],[4275,"'The calendar began in the year in which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, and in that year 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr was born.'"],[4276,"'Ali b. Abi Talib: 'From the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated and left the land of polytheism.' And 'Umar put it into practice."],[4277,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, he established brotherhood between his companions. 'Ali came with tears flowing from his eyes and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you have established brotherhood between your companions but you have not established brotherhood between me and anyone.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O 'Ali, you are my brother in this world and the Hereafter.' Salim b. Abi Hafsah followed him in narrating from Jumay' with an addition in the wording."],[4278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between his companions. He established brotherhood between Abu Bakr and Umar, between Talhah and al-Zubayr, and between Uthman b. Affan and Abd al-Rahman b. Awf. Ali said: O Messenger of Allah, you have established brotherhood between your companions, so who is my brother? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Are you not pleased, O Ali, that I should be your brother?\" Ibn Umar said: Ali was tough and brave. Ali said: Indeed, O Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You are my brother in this world and the Hereafter.\" Jami' b. Umayr is accused, and Ishaq b. Bishr al-Kahili is perished."],[4279,"When a man among us arrived in Madinah and had an acquaintance there, he would stay with his acquaintance; if he had no acquaintance there, he stayed in the Suffah. I arrived and stayed in the Suffah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would provide us daily a mudd of dates between two people and clothe us with rough cloth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in some of the daytime prayer. When he said the salam, the people of the Suffah called to him from right and left: O Messenger of Allah, the dates have burned our bellies and the rough cloth has worn out from us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to his pulpit, ascended it, praised Allah and extolled Him, then mentioned the hardship he met from his people until he said: \"There passed over me and my companion ten and some [days] when I and he had no food except berir (fruit of the arak tree).\" The narrator said: I said to Abu Harb: What is berir? He said: The food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, dates of the arak tree. \"Then we came to these brothers of ours from the Ansar, and the main part of their food was dates, and they shared them with us. By Allah, if I could find bread and meat for you, I would satisfy you with it. But perhaps you will live to a time when a large bowl will be brought to one of you in the morning and another in the evening.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, are we better today or on that day? He said: \"Rather you are better today. Today you love one another, but on that day some of you will strike the necks of others.\" I think he said: \"hating one another.\""],[4280,"The people of the Suffah were the guests of Islam; they had no family or wealth to take refuge with. By Allah, besides whom there is no god, I would press my liver to the ground from hunger and tie a stone on my belly from hunger. One day I sat at the side of their path from which they came out. Abu Bakr passed by me, so I asked him about a verse from the Book of Allah, only asking him so that he would take me along, but he passed and did not do so. Then Umar passed by, and I asked him about a verse from the Book of Allah, the Exalted, only asking him so that he would take me along, but he passed and did not do so. Then Abu al-Qasim ﷺ passed by and smiled when he saw me and said: \"Abu Hurayrah.\" I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Come along\" and went on. I followed him. He entered his house, and I sought permission and he permitted me. He found milk in a bowl and said: \"Where did you get this milk?\" It was said: So-and-so gifted it to us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Abu Hurayrah.\" I said: At your service. He said: \"Go to the people of the Suffah and call them. They are the guests of Islam; they have no family or wealth to take refuge with.\" When charity came to him, he would send it all to them and take nothing from it; when a gift came to him, he would send for them and take some of it and include them in it. That saddened me, and I said: What is this bowl among the people of the Suffah while I am his messenger to them? He will order me to pass it around among them, so what might I get from it? I had hoped to get from it something that would suffice me. But there was no escape from obeying Allah and obeying His Messenger ﷺ. So I went to them and called them. When they entered upon him and took their seats, he said: \"Abu Hirr, take the bowl and give it to them.\" I took the bowl and began handing it to a man who would drink until quenched, then return it, and I handed it to another who would drink until quenched, until I finally came with it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and all the people had drunk their fill. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the bowl and placed it on his hands, then raised his head to me and smiled and said: \"Abu Hirr.\" I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Sit and drink.\" I drank. Then he said: \"Drink.\" I drank. Then he said: \"Drink.\" I drank, and I kept drinking while he said \"Drink\" until I said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I find no passage for it. He took the bowl, praised Allah, mentioned His name, and then drank."],[4281,"\"The companions of the Suffah were seventy men who had no cloaks.\""],[4282,"I heard Sahl b. Abdullah al-Tustari say: When Allah, may He be exalted, sent the Prophet ﷺ, there were in the world seven categories of people: kings, farmers, livestock owners, merchants, artisans, laborers, and the weak and poor. He did not command any of them to leave what he was in, but He commanded them to knowledge, certainty, piety, and trust in all that they were in. Sahl, may Allah have mercy on him, said: It is fitting for a rational person to say: It is not fitting for me, after knowing that I am Your servant, to hope and expect other than You, nor to imagine about You, since You created me and formed me as a servant to You, that You would entrust me to myself or hand over my affairs to other than You."],[4283,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of my nation, as the Highest Assembly informed me, are a people who laugh openly in the expanse of the mercy of their Lord, may He be exalted, and weep secretly from fear of the severity of the punishment of their Lord, may He be exalted. They remember their Lord in the morning and evening in the good houses, the mosques, and call upon Him with their tongues in hope and fear, and ask Him with their hands lowered and raised, and turn with their hearts again and again. Their burden on people is light, and on themselves heavy. They walk on the earth barefoot on their feet like the creeping of ants, without vanity or arrogance. They walk with tranquility and draw near through the means, recite the Quran, bring offerings, and wear worn-out garments. Over them are witnesses present from Allah, the Exalted, and a preserving eye. They discern the servants and reflect on the lands. Their spirits are in this world and their hearts in the Hereafter. They have no concern except their leader. They have prepared provisions for their graves, the passage for their path, and readiness for their standing.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {That is for him who fears My station and fears My threat} [Ibrahim: 14]."],[4284,"Whatever was revealed as 'O you who believe' was in Madinah, and whatever was revealed as 'O mankind' was in Makkah."],[4285,"\"We recited the Mufassal at a certain time, and we performed Hajj while in Makkah there was no 'O you who believe' in it.\""],[4286,"Atika, the daughter of Abdul Muttalib, saw a dream that alarmed her. It was about a man named Dammam bin Amr Al-Ghifari. He appeared to be a terrifying figure to the Quraysh in Makkah for three consecutive nights. Atika became greatly disturbed by this dream and sent a message to her brother, Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib, informing him about it.She said, \"Oh, my brother, I had a dream last night that frightened me. It indicated that your people will face harm and calamity. The man in the dream approached on a camel and stopped at Aabtah. He then called out, 'O deceitful family of Ghadr, prepare yourselves in three.' I saw people gathering around him, and then he entered the mosque with his camel. The people gathered around him again. Suddenly, he reached the top of the Kāba and called out, 'O deceitful family of Ghadr, prepare yourselves in three.' Then his camel appeared on top of Abi Qubays, and he called out once again, 'O deceitful family of Ghadr, prepare yourselves in three.' He then picked up a rock and sent it rolling down the mountain. It kept rolling until it reached the bottom, destroying every house and building of your people.Al-Abbas said, \"By Allah, this is indeed a vision. Conceal it.\" She said, \"And you, conceal it. If this reaches the people of Quraysh, they will harm us.\" So Al-Abbas left her and met Walid ibn Utbah, who was his friend. He mentioned it to him and entrusted him with it. Walid mentioned it to his father, and the news spread. Al-Abbas said, \"By Allah, I will go to the Kāba to circumambulate it.\" When I entered the mosque, there was Abu Jahl with a group from Quraysh talking about Aatikah's vision.Abu Jahl said, \"O Abu al-Fadl, when did this prophetess say this to you?\" I replied, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"A vision seen by Atika, the daughter of Abdul-Muttalib. Have you, sons of Abdul-Muttalib, consented that your men should prophesy until even your women prophesy? We will wait for these three that Atika mentioned. If it is true, it will happen, and if not, we will write a document against you, for you are the most lying household in the Arab land. By Allah, there is no significant matter except that I have denied what she said. I said, 'She saw nothing, and I heard nothing like this.'\"By evening, every woman from the Banu Abdul Muttalib came to me, blaming me for not preventing this corrupted man from causing harm to our men and approaching our women. They said, \"Didn't you have any sense of honor?\" I replied, \"By Allah, you speak the truth. I had doubts, but if he repeats this, I will handle him.\" I sat there, waiting for the third day to confront him and make him say something. I cursed him in my heart, thinking that it was better to confront him than to curse him. Suddenly, I heard Ḍamḍam bin Amr reciting verses while standing on his camel at Aabtah. He had unraveled his turban and torn his shirt. He referred to the people of Mecca, saying, \"Oh, deceitful and sinful Quraysh, your wealth is with Abu Sufyan, and your trade has been taken by Muhammad and his companions. Seek help from the devil.\" He then continued to recite for some time. This distracted me, and I only had my device until we left the city.Quraish suffered a great loss that day, as they had in the Battle of Badr. They lost many noble people and their best warriors. Atika, the daughter of Abdul Muttalib, said, \"Wasn't the dream true and did it not warn you? You said that it wasn't true, and I didn't lie. Whoever denies the truth is indeed a liar.\""],[4287,"\"There were with us only two horses: a horse for al-Zubayr and a horse for al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad, meaning on the day of Badr.\""],[4288,"On the day of Badr, every three of us were on one camel. He said: Ali and Abu Lubabah were the two companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: When it was his turn to ride, we said: Ride until we walk. He would say: \"You two are not stronger than I, and I am not more in need of the reward than you.\""],[4289,"Regarding the Night of Decree, he said: \"Seek it for the eleventh [night] remaining, the morning of which is the day of Badr.\""],[4290,"\"Seek the Night of Decree for the nineteenth, the morning of which is the day of Badr, the day of the Criterion, the day the two armies met.\""],[4291,"The Muhājirūn on the day of Badr were eighty-something, and the Anṣār were two hundred and forty-something."],[4292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr when we were lined up for battle against Quraysh and they were lined up against us: \"When they close in on you, shoot them with arrows.\""],[4293,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them: \"What do you say about these captives?\" ʿAbd Allāh b. Rawāḥah said: \"Go to a valley with much firewood, light a fire, then throw them into it.\" Al-ʿAbbās said: \"May Allah sever your womb ties.\" ʿUmar said: \"Their leaders and chiefs fought you and called you a liar, so strike their necks.\" Then Abū Bakr said: \"They are your kinsmen and your people.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered for some need, and a group said: \"The right view is what ʿUmar said.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: \"What do you say about these? The likeness of these is as the likeness of brothers of theirs who were before them: Noah said, 'My Lord, do not leave upon the earth any of the disbelievers' [Nūḥ:26], and Moses said, 'Our Lord, obliterate their wealth and harden their hearts' [Yūnus:88] to the end of the verse, and Abraham said, 'Whoever follows me is of me, and whoever disobeys me, You are Forgiving, Merciful' [Ibrāhīm:36], and Jesus said, 'If You punish them, they are Your servants, and if You forgive them, You are the Mighty, the Wise' [al-Māʾidah:118]. You are a people among whom there is treachery. None of you should depart except with a ransom or by striking the neck.\" ʿAbd Allāh said: \"I said: 'Except Suhayl b. Bayḍāʾ, for he should not be killed; I have heard him speak of Islam.' He fell silent, and there was no day I feared more that stones would fall on me from the sky than that day until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Except Suhayl b. Bayḍāʾ.'\""],[4294,"When the captives were brought to Madinah, Sawdah bt. Zamʿah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, was with the family of ʿAfrāʾ in their mourning for ʿAwf and Muʿawwidh, the two sons of ʿAfrāʾ, and that was before the veil was imposed on them. Sawdah said: \"By Allah, I was with them when news came: 'These captives have been brought.' I returned to my house and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in it, and there was Abū Yazīd Suhayl b. ʿAmr in a corner of the room with his hands tied to his neck with a rope. By Allah, when I saw Abū Yazīd like that, I could not stop myself from saying: 'Abū Yazīd, you surrendered! Why did you not die honorably?' I was only startled by the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from inside the house: 'O Sawdah, by Allah and His Messenger!' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with truth, when I saw Abū Yazīd with his hands tied to his neck with a rope, I could not stop myself from saying what I said.'\""],[4295,"When the people of Makkah sent ransom for their captives, Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for the ransom of Abū al-ʿĀṣ wealth including a necklace that Khadījah had given her to wear when she married Abū al-ʿĀṣ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he felt intense compassion for her and said: \"If you see fit to release her captive and return to her what belongs to her.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had taken a promise from Abū al-ʿĀṣ and he had promised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to send Zaynab to him."],[4296,"From Ibn ʿAbbās regarding His ﷻ saying: {If you have believed in Allah and what We sent down upon Our servant on the day of al-Furqān} [al-Anfāl:41], meaning by al-Furqān the day of Badr, the day Allah distinguished between truth and falsehood."],[4297,"On the day of Uḥud, when the polytheists retreated, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Line up so that I may praise my Lord ﷻ.\" They formed rows behind him, and he said: \"O Allah, to You belongs all praise. O Allah, none can withhold what You extend, none can extend what You withhold, none can guide whom You lead astray, none can lead astray whom You guide, none can give what You withhold, none can withhold what You give, none can bring near what You distance, none can distance what You bring near. O Allah, spread over us from Your blessings, Your mercy, Your bounty, and Your provision. O Allah, I ask You for enduring bliss that does not change or cease. O Allah, I ask You for security on the day of fear. O Allah, I seek refuge from the evil of what You have given us and the evil of what You have withheld. O Allah, make faith beloved to us and beautify it in our hearts, and make disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience hateful to us, and make us among the rightly guided. O Allah, cause us to die as Muslims and live as Muslims and join us with the righteous, not disgraced or tempted. O Allah, fight the disbelievers who deny Your messengers and turn away from Your path, and place upon them Your wrath and punishment. O God of truth, Amen.\""],[4298,"ʿAlī came with his sword on the day of Uḥud, bent, and said to Fāṭimah: \"Take this sword, for it has satisfied me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you fought well with your sword, Sahl b. Ḥunayf, Abū Dujānah, ʿĀṣim b. Thābit al-Aflaḥ, and al-Ḥārith b. al-Ṣimmah also fought well.\""],[4299,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, he gave his sword to his daughter Fāṭimah and said: \"My daughter, wash this blood off.\" ʿAlī gave her his sword and said: \"And this, wash its blood off. By Allah, it served me well in fighting today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you fought well today, Sahl b. Ḥunayf and Simāk b. Kharashah, Abū Dujānah, also fought well with you today.\" Ibn Isḥāq said: ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib said when he handed the sword to Fāṭimah (peace be upon her): \"O Fāṭimah, take the sword, not blameworthy; I am no coward nor base. By my life, I have striven in support of Aḥmad and in pleasing a Lord merciful to His servants.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[4300,"On the day of Uḥud, he chanted this poetry: [rajaz meter] \"We are the protectors of Ghālib and Mālik; we defend our blessed Messenger. We strike for him today in the battles, striking like the broadswords on the honored steeds.\" When the Prophet ﷺ returned on the day of Uḥud, he said to Ḥassān: \"Speak about Ṭalḥah.\" Ḥassān composed: [ṭawīl meter] \"Ṭalḥah on the day of the mountain pass consoled Muḥammad on a path that was narrow and difficult for him. He protected him with his hands from the spears, and his limbs surrendered beneath the swords and were paralyzed. He was the leader of the people except Muḥammad; he kept the mill of Islam turning until it stood firm.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[4301,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he went to climb onto a rock, and he had put on two coats of mail, so he could not climb onto it. Then Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh sat beneath him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ climbed until he stood on it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ṭalḥah has made it obligatory [Paradise for himself].\""],[4302,"Ṭalḥah returned with thirty-seven or thirty-five wounds between strikes, stabs, and shots. His forehead was scarred, his index finger was cut off, and the finger next to it was paralyzed."],[4303,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"That rout on the day of Uhud—I withdrew and said, 'I will defend myself; either I will be martyred or I will escape until I meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' While I was in that state, there was a man with his face covered, and I did not know who he was. The polytheists advanced until I thought they had mounted him. He filled his hand with pebbles and threw them in their faces, and they retreated on their heels backwards until they reached the mountain. He did that repeatedly, and I did not know who he was, while between me and him was al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad. While I was about to ask al-Miqdad about him, al-Miqdad said, 'O Sa'd, this is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ calling you.' I said, 'Where is he?' Al-Miqdad pointed to him, and I stood up as if no harm had afflicted me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Where were you today, O Sa'd?' I said, 'Where I saw the Messenger of Allah.' He seated me in front of him, and I began shooting and saying, 'O Allah, Your arrow—shoot Your enemy with it,' and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was saying, 'O Allah, answer Sa'd; O Allah, make Sa'd's aim true. Shoot, Sa'd, may my father and mother be your ransom.' There was no arrow I shot but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Allah, make his aim true and answer his supplication. Shoot, Sa'd,' until when I had emptied my quiver, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shook out what was in his quiver and gave me a bright-feathered arrow.\" He said: \"It was the one that had been feathered, and it was sharper than the others.\" Al-Zuhri said: \"The arrows that Sa'd shot on that day were a thousand arrows.\""],[4304,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: \"When the people were routed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud, I was the first to return to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I caught sight of him from afar, and there was a man who had embraced me from behind like a bird, intending to reach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah. And there was a man lifting him up once and setting him down another time. I said, 'Since I was not the one with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then let it be Talhah—that would be me.' I passed on, and we reached him, and there was Talhah lifting him up once and setting him down another time. Talhah had sixty-six wounds, one of which had cut his median vein. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had been struck on his cheeks, and two rings of the helmet had stuck into his cheeks. When Abu Ubaydah saw what was on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he adjured me by Allah to let him get to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He pulled out one of them with his front tooth, and it came out and his front tooth fell out. Then he looked at the other one and adjured me by Allah to let him get to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he seized it with his other front tooth and pulled it, and it came out and his front tooth fell out. Thus Abu Ubaydah became broken-toothed.\""],[4305,"\"By Allah, I saw myself looking at Hind bt. Utbah and her companions with their garments tucked up, fleeing, and there was little or nothing preventing their capture when the archers inclined toward the camp, so that the people uncovered it, seeking the spoils, and they left our rear exposed to the cavalry. We were attacked from behind, and a crier shouted, 'Indeed Muhammad has been killed.' We turned back, and the people turned back after we had struck the banner, until none of the people came near it.\""],[4306,"Amr b. Qays had a debt from the time of ignorance, and that debt prevented him from embracing Islam until he could collect it. One day he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions at Uhud and said, \"Where is Sa'd b. Mu'adh?\" It was said, \"At Uhud.\" He said, \"Where are his brother's sons?\" It was said, \"At Uhud.\" He asked about his people, and they said, \"At Uhud.\" He took his sword and spear, put on his armor, and went to Uhud. When the Muslims saw him, they said, \"Get away from us, O Amr.\" He said, \"I have believed.\" He charged and fought, and was carried to his family wounded. Sa'd b. Mu'adh entered upon him and said, \"Did you come out of anger for Allah and His Messenger, or out of zeal for your people?\" He said, \"Rather, I came out of anger for Allah and His Messenger.\" Abu Hurayrah said: \"He entered Paradise without having prayed a single prayer to Allah.\" According to the condition of Muslim."],[4307,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he mentioned the companions of Uhud, say: \"By Allah, I would love to have been left with my companions in the hollow of the mountain\"—he said—\"killed with them.\""],[4308,"\"That Fatimah, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, used to visit the grave of her uncle Hamzah ibn Abdul-Muttalib during the days, and she would pray and cry at his grave.\""],[4309,"The Prophet ﷺ visited the graves of the martyrs at Uhud and said: \"O Allah, Your servant and Your Prophet bears witness that these are martyrs, and that whoever visits them and greets them until the Day of Resurrection, they will return his greeting.\" Al-Attaf said: \"My maternal aunt narrated to me that she visited the graves of the martyrs. She said: 'I had with me only two servant boys guarding the mount. I greeted them and heard the return of the greeting: \"By Allah, we know you as we know one another.\"' She said: 'I shuddered and said, \"O boy, bring my mule close,\" and I mounted.'\" This is a sound Madinan chain, but they did not include it. It is mursal."],[4310,"Allah, exalted is He: {Those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after the wound had befallen them} [Al Imran 172]."],[4311,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fought Muharib Khasafah at Nakhl. They saw an opening among the Muslims, and a man from among them called Ghawrath b. al-Harith came until he stood over the head of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a sword and said, \"Who will protect you from me?\" He said, \"Allah.\" The sword fell from his hand, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and said, \"Who will protect you?\" He said, \"Be the best taker.\" He said, \"Will you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"I give you my covenant that I will not fight you and will not be with a people who fight you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ let him go. He went to his people and said, \"I have come to you from the best of people.\" When the time for prayer came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the prayer of fear. The people were two groups: one group facing the enemy and one group praying with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He prayed two rak'ahs with those who were with him, and they departed and took the place of those facing the enemy. Those others came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs with them. Thus the people prayed two rak'ahs each, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed four rak'ahs."],[4312,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on a campaign and met the polytheists at Usfan. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Zuhr, they saw him bowing and prostrating, he and his companions. Some of them said to others, 'This was an opportunity for you; if you had attacked them, they would not have known about you until you fell upon them.' A speaker among them said, 'They have another prayer that is dearer to them than their families and their wealth. Prepare to attack them during it.' Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed to His Prophet ﷺ: {And when you are among them and lead them in prayer} [Al-Nisa 102] to the end of the verse, and informed him of what the polytheists had plotted. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Asr, and they were facing him in the direction of the qiblah, he placed the Muslims behind him in two rows, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the takbir, and they said the takbir with him.\" He mentioned the prayer of fear and said at the end: \"When the polytheists saw them, some prostrating and some standing to guard them, they said, 'They have been informed of what we intended.'\""],[4313,"I heard Jabir b. Abd Allah say: \"When the trench was being dug, I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suffering from severe hunger. I went to my wife and said, 'I have seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suffering from severe hunger.' She brought out a sack containing a sa' of barley, and we had a tame animal. She slaughtered it and ground the sa'. I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and consulted him, saying, 'O Messenger of Allah, we have slaughtered an animal of ours and ground a sa' of barley that we had. Come, you and a small group with you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out, 'O people of the trench, Jabir has prepared a meal, so come on!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not take down your cooking pot and do not bake your dough until I come.' I came, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and the people came forward until I went to my wife. She brought out dough, and he spat in it and blessed it. Then he said, 'Call a woman baker to bake with you, and ladle from your cooking pot, but do not take it down.' They were a thousand. Jabir swore by Allah, exalted is He, that they ate until they left it and departed, while our cooking pot was still bubbling as it was, and our dough was being baked as it was.\" This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Amr; in the wording of Abu al-Abbas it is abridged."],[4314,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Confederates: \"Only twelve men remained with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was crouching from the cold and said, 'O Ibn al-Yaman, get up and go to the camp of the Confederates and see their condition.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, by the One who sent you with the truth, I only stood up for you out of modesty because of the cold.' He said, 'Go out to the black stony ground and the cold of the morning. Go, O Ibn al-Yaman, no harm will befall you from heat or cold until you return to me.' I went to their camp and found Abu Sufyan kindling a fire among a small group around him, the Confederates having dispersed from him. When I sat among them, Abu Sufyan thought that someone from outside had entered among them. He said, 'Let each man of you take the hand of his companion.' I struck my hand on the one to my right and took his hand, then I struck my hand on the one to my left and took his hand. I remained among them for a little while, then I got up and came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was standing praying. He gestured to me with his hand to come close, so I came close. Then he gestured again to come close, so I came close until he let part of the garment that was on him fall over me while he was praying. When he finished his prayer, he said, 'O Ibn al-Yaman, sit. What is the news?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the people have dispersed from Abu Sufyan, and only a small group kindling a fire remains. Allah has poured upon him cold like that which He poured upon us, but we hope from Allah what he does not hope.'\""],[4315,"A man from the polytheists was killed on the day of the trench, and they asked to bury him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ refused until they gave him the blood money. And from Banu Amir b. Luayy, Amr b. Abd Wudd was killed; Ali b. Abi Talib killed him in single combat."],[4316,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The duel between Ali ibn Abi Talib and Amr ibn Abd Wudd on the day of the trench is better than the deeds of my ummah (followers) until the Day of Judgment.\" May Allah curse the one who fabricated it, the Rafidi."],[4317,"\"Amr ibn Abdud was killed among the polytheists on the Day of the Trench. Ali ibn Abi Talib killed him. The chain of transmission of this battle is considered authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs.\""],[4318,"Amr b. Abd Wudd was the third of Quraysh. He had fought on the day of Badr until wounds disabled him, and he did not witness Uhud. When the day of the Trench came, he went out marked for battle to witness his moment. When he and his cavalry halted, Ali said to him, \"O Amr, you used to pledge to God for Quraysh that no man would invite you to two qualities but you would accept one of them from him.\" Amr said, \"Yes.\" Ali said to him, \"Then I invite you to God (mighty and sublime) and His Messenger ﷺ and Islam.\" He said, \"I have no need of that.\" He said, \"Then I invite you to single combat.\" He said, \"O son of my brother, why? By God, I would not like to kill you.\" Ali said, \"But I would like to kill you.\" Amr became angry, dismounted from his horse, hamstrung it, then came forward to Ali and said, \"Who will duel?\" Ali stood up while he was masked in iron and said, \"I will face him, O Prophet of God.\" He said, \"It is Amr b. Abd Wudd. Sit down.\" Amr called out, \"Will no man [come]?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ gave him permission. Ali walked toward him saying: [al-Kamil] \"Do not be hasty, for a responder to your call has come to you, not incapable; possessed of insight and discernment, and truthfulness is the salvation of every victor. I hope to establish over you the wailing of funeral mourners from a wide-cutting blow whose remembrance will remain in the convulsions of battle.\" Amr said to him, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am Ali.\" He said, \"Son of whom?\" He said, \"Son of Abd Manaf; I am Ali b. Abi Talib.\" He said, \"You have, O son of my brother, among your paternal uncles those older than you, so turn back, for I dislike shedding your blood.\" Ali said, \"But I, by God, do not dislike shedding your blood.\" He became angry, dismounted, drew his sword as if it were a flame of fire, then came toward Ali enraged. Ali met him with his shield. Amr struck the shield, split it, and the sword stuck in it, and it hit his head and wounded him. Ali struck him on the vein of the shoulder, so he fell and dust rose. The Messenger of God ﷺ heard the takbir and knew that Ali had killed him. Then Ali ؓ said: \"Do the horsemen charge upon me thus? Away from me and from them! Hold back my companions. Today zeal and a sword fixed in the head, not useless, prevent me from flight—except against the son of Abd when he charged him. And I swore—so listen from the Book—that I would vindicate whoever declares God's oneness through piety: two men striking every striker. I returned when I left him laid low like a palm trunk between rugged ground and hills. I refrained from his garments, though if I had been the one stripped, my garments would weigh me down. He worshipped stones out of folly of mind, and I worshipped the Lord of Muhammad with truth.\" Then Ali came toward the Messenger of God ﷺ with his face shining. Umar b. al-Khattab said, \"Why did you not plunder his coat of mail? The Arabs have no coat better than it.\" He said, \"I struck him, and he shielded himself with his private parts, and I was ashamed of my cousin's son to strip him.\" And his cavalry fled defeated until they were forced into the trench."],[4319,"[al-Basit] \"If the killer of Amr were other than his killer, I would weep for him as long as the soul remains in my body. But his killer is one who is not faulted by it, and he was called of old the egg of the land.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4321,"\"And among the disbelievers of Quraysh killed on the day of the Trench, from Banu Amir b. Lu'ayy, then from Banu Malik b. Hasal: Amr b. Abd Wudd b. Nasr b. Malik b. Hasal. Ali b. Abi Talib killed him.\""],[4322,"From Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her when a man from the People of the House greeted us while we were in the house. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up startled, and I followed him. It was Dihya al-Kalbi. He said, \"This is Gabriel, commanding me to go to Banu Qurayza.\" He said, \"You have laid down your weapons, but we have not. We sought the polytheists until we reached Hamra' al-Asad.\" That was when the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from the Trench. The Prophet ﷺ stood up startled and said to his companions, \"I adjure you not to pray the Asr prayer until you come to Banu Qurayza.\" The sun set before they reached them. One group of Muslims said, \"The Prophet ﷺ did not intend that they should abandon the prayer,\" so they prayed. Another group said, \"We are under the Prophet's adjuration, and we bear no sin,\" so one group prayed out of faith and seeking reward, and another group left it out of faith and seeking reward. The Prophet ﷺ did not criticize anyone from either party. The Prophet ﷺ went out and passed by gatherings between him and Qurayza and said, \"Did anyone pass by you?\" They said, \"Dihya al-Kalbi passed by us on a gray mule, beneath him a velvet saddlecloth.\" He said, \"That was not Dihya, but Gabriel, sent to Banu Qurayza to shake them and cast terror into their hearts.\" The Prophet ﷺ besieged them and ordered his companions to shield themselves with their shields so that he could make them hear his words. He called to them, \"O brothers of apes and pigs!\" They said, \"O Abu al-Qasim, you were not foul-mouthed.\" He besieged them until they came down to the judgment of Sa'd b. Mu'adh, for they were his allies. He judged among them that their fighting men be killed and their women and children taken captive."],[4323,"\"We were presented to the Messenger of God ﷺ at the time of Qurayza. Whoever among us had reached puberty or had pubic hair was killed. They looked at me, and my pubic hair had not grown, so I was left.\""],[4324,"She said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ never killed any woman of Banu Qurayza except one woman. By God, she was with me, laughing with her belly exposed, while the Messenger of God ﷺ was killing their men with swords, when a caller called her name: 'Where is so-and-so?' She said, 'I am, by God.' I said, 'Woe to you, what is with you?' She said, 'I will be killed, by God.' I said, 'Why?' She said, 'Because of an act I committed.' So they took her and struck her neck. I will never forget my amazement at her good spirits and much laughter, though she knew she would be killed.\""],[4325,"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed Abu Bakr over us, and we raided people from Banu Fazara. When we approached a watering place, Abu Bakr ordered us, and we halted for rest. When we prayed the morning prayer, Abu Bakr ordered us, and we launched the raid. We reached the water and killed there whom we killed. A group of people turned away, including women and children, and they almost reached the mountain. We shot an arrow between them and the mountain, and when they saw the arrow, they stopped. I brought them, driving them to Abu Bakr. Among them was a woman from Banu Fazara wearing a worn leather garment, and with her was a daughter of hers, one of the most beautiful of the Arabs. Abu Bakr gave me her daughter as booty. I came to Madinah, and the Messenger of God ﷺ met me in the market and said, \"O Salama, may your father be for God's sake; give me the woman.\" I said, \"By God, O Messenger of God, I have not uncovered a garment for her; and she is yours, O Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ sent her to Makkah and ransomed with her Muslim captives who were in the hands of the polytheists. [Muslim extracted it with a different wording.]\" Muslim extracted it with another wording."],[4326,"He informed him that the Messenger of God ﷺ was at al-Hudaybiya and said, \"Do not light a fire at night.\" Then later he said, \"Light fires and prepare food, for no people after you will attain your sa' or your mudd.\""],[4327,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to Khaibar, he employed Siba' bin 'Urfutah al-Ghifari in Medina.\""],[4328,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abu Bakr to some of the fortresses of Khaybar. He fought and exerted himself, but there was no conquest.\""],[4330,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ would sometimes be afflicted with migraine, and he would remain a day or two without going out. When he encamped at Khaybar, migraine afflicted him, and he did not go out to the people. Abu Bakr took the banner of the Messenger of God ﷺ, then rose and fought fiercely, then returned.\""],[4331,"\"The Prophet ﷺ marched to Khaybar. When he reached it, he sent Umar ؓ and sent people with him to their town or fortress, and they fought them. They did not wait long before they routed Umar and his companions. They came back, and he was calling them cowards and they were calling him a coward. Then the Prophet ﷺ marched on.\" The hadith."],[4332,"\"The Prophet ﷺ gave the banner on the day of Khaybar to Umar. He went and returned, calling his companions cowards and they calling him a coward.\""],[4333,"On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man, but he showed cowardice. Muhammad b. Maslama came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have never seen a day like today. Mahmud b. Maslama has been killed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not wish to meet the enemy, and ask Allah for well-being, for you do not know what you will be tested with alongside them. When you meet them, say: O Allah, You are our Lord and their Lord, and our forelocks and their forelocks are in Your hand; You alone kill them. Then keep to the ground, sitting. If they overwhelm you, rise up and say Allahu akbar.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Tomorrow I shall send a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom they both love. He will not turn his back; Allah will grant victory at his hands.' The people craned their necks for it, while Ali that day had sore eyes. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Go.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I cannot see a place.' He spat into his eyes, tied a banner for him, and handed it to him. Ali said, 'O Messenger of Allah, on what basis shall I fight them?' He said, 'On the basis that they testify that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. When they do that, they have protected their blood and property from me except for what is due, and their reckoning is with Allah ﷻ.' He said, 'He met them and Allah granted victory at his hands.' The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting the hadith of the banner, but they did not transmit it with this wording. They transmitted the mention of the banner from it."],[4334,"We witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Khaybar when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into the eyes of Ali and he was cured, and he gave him the banner. Marhab came forward, saying in rajaz verse: 'Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, fully armed, a tried hero; when wars come, they blaze.' Ali came forward to him, saying in rajaz verse: 'I am the one my mother named Haydara, like a lion of the thickets with a fearsome look; I will give you full measure like the measuring of the largest container.' He struck Marhab and split his skull, killing him, and the victory was achieved."],[4335,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took as booty his sword Dhu al-Fiqar on the day of Badr."],[4336,"Safiyya was among the select booty."],[4337,"I heard Ali say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ put me in charge of the fifth of the fifth, and I placed it in its rightful places during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr, and Umar.'"],[4338,"We returned with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Khaybar to Wadi al-Qura, and with him was a servant of his whom Rifa'a b. Zayd al-Hizami had gifted to him. While he was setting down the saddle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the setting of the sun, a stray arrow came to him and killed him—the arrow whose shooter is unknown. We said, 'Congratulations to him for Paradise.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No, by the One in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, his cloak is now burning on him in the Fire; he stole it from the spoils of the Muslims on the day of Khaybar.' A man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in alarm when he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I took two shoe straps for a pair of shoes of mine.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The like of it will be cut for you in the Fire.'"],[4339,"When news of the killing of Ja'far came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, grief entered him because of that. Gabriel came to him and said, 'Allah, Exalted is He, has given Ja'far two wings dyed with blood, with which he flies among the angels.'"],[4340,"When news of Ja'far's death came to him, we recognized sadness in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Someone entered upon him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, the women have overcome us or defeated us.' He said, 'Go back to them and silence them.' He went, then came back to him, and he sent him back three times. He said, 'Go back to them, and if they refuse, throw dust in their mouths.' Aisha said, 'I said to myself about the man: May Allah distance you. I know that you are not going to obey the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you will not leave yourself until you know you cannot throw dust in their mouths.'"],[4341,"No one after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore sandals, put on sandals, or rode mounts better than Ja'far b. Abi Talib."],[4342,"When the grief of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over those killed on the day of Mu'ta became severe, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said three times: 'The Dajjal will certainly encounter a people like you or better than you, and Allah will never disgrace a nation of which I am the first and Isa b. Maryam is the last.'"],[4343,"Peace be upon you, O son of the two-winged one."],[4344,"Abdullah b. Rawaha fainted, and his sister Amra began weeping, saying, 'O my brother, O such and such,' enumerating his qualities. When he regained consciousness, he said, 'You did not say anything except that it was said to me: You are like that.'"],[4345,"«On the day of Mu'ta, nine swords were broken in my hand, and nothing remained in my hand except a Yemeni blade.»"],[4346,"She said to the wife of Salama b. Hisham b. al-Mughira: «Why do I not see Salama attending the prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and with the Muslims?» She said: By Allah, he is not able to go out. Whenever he goes out, the people shout at him: O runaway, did you flee in the cause of Allah ﷻ? So he stayed in his house and does not go out. He was in the expedition of Mu'ta with Khalid b. al-Walid."],[4347,"There was an argument between me and a cousin of mine, and he said: Except for your fleeing on the day of Mu'ta. I did not know what to say to him."],[4348,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Amr b. al-'As on the expedition of Dhat al-Salasil, and among them were Abu Bakr and 'Umar. When they reached the place of fighting, 'Amr ordered them not to light a fire. 'Umar became angry and wanted to take him to task, but Abu Bakr forbade him and told him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not appointed him over you except because of his knowledge of war. So 'Umar calmed down.»"],[4349,"«The conquest was on the thirteenth of Ramadan.»"],[4350,"similarly is reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ[1]"],[4351,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, 'Abd Allah b. Sa'd b. Abi Sarh hid with 'Uthman b. 'Affan, who brought him and made him stand before the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, accept the pledge of 'Abd Allah. He raised his head and looked at him three times, then he turned to his companions and said: «Was there not among you a righteous man who would stand up to this one when he saw me holding back my hand from his pledge and kill him?» They said: We do not know, O Messenger of Allah, what is in your heart. Could you not have signaled to us with your eye? He said: «It is not fitting for a prophet to have a treacherous eye.»"],[4352,"«'Abd Allah b. Abi Sarh used to write for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he joined the disbelievers. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that he be killed, but 'Uthman sought protection for him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him protection.»"],[4353,"«It was revealed about 'Abd Allah b. Abi Sarh: {And who is more unjust than one who invents a lie against Allah or says: It was revealed to me, while nothing was revealed to him, and who says: I will send down the like of what Allah has sent down} [al-An'am: 93]. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah, he fled to 'Uthman b. 'Affan, who was his foster brother, and 'Uthman hid him until the people of Makkah became calm, then he brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sought amnesty for him.»"],[4354,"In the year of the conquest, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped at Dhu Tuwa, Abu Quhafa said to a daughter of his, who was the youngest of his children: O my little daughter, help me to look over Abu Qubays, for his sight had failed. So she helped him to look over it, and he said: O my little daughter, what do you see? She said: I see a gathered black mass, and I see a man moving in front of that black mass, approaching. He said: Those are the horses, my little daughter. Then he said: What do you see? She said: I see the black mass has spread out. He said: Then, by Allah, the horses have been driven forward, so hurry with me to my house. She went quickly, and when she descended with him to al-Abtah, she had a necklace of silver on her neck, and a person snatched it from her neck. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque, Abu Bakr went out and brought his father, leading him. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he said: «Why did you not leave the old man in his house until I came to him?» He said: He walking to you, O Messenger of Allah, is more appropriate than you walking to him. So he seated him before him, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped his chest and said: «Submit, and you will be safe.» So he submitted. Then Abu Bakr stood up and took his sister by the hand and said: I adjure you by Allah and Islam, the necklace of my sister. By Allah, no one brought it. Then he said a second time: I adjure you by Allah and Islam, the necklace of my sister. No one brought it. He said: O my little sister, consider your necklace as a loss, for by Allah, trustworthiness among people is indeed scarce."],[4355,"We were at a passage of people, and the riders would tell us, so we asked them: What is this matter and what is with the people? They said: A prophet who claims that Allah Almighty sent him, and that Allah revealed to him such and such. The Arabs were waiting for the conquest to accept Islam, and they used to say: Wait for him; if he prevails, then he is a prophet, so believe him. After the event of the conquest, every people hastened to accept Islam to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came and stayed with him for such and such, then he came from him, and we met him. He said: I have come to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ truly, and he «commands you with such and such. When the prayer is due, let one of you give the adhan, and let the one among you with the most Qur'an lead you.» They looked and did not find anyone with more Qur'an than me, so they put me forward, and I was a boy of seven or six years. I used to pray, and when I prostrated, my cloak would become tight on me. He said: A woman from the tribe said: Cover from us the private part of your reciter. He said: So I was given a Yemeni garment with knots for six or seven dirhams, and I was never happier with anything than I was with that."],[4356,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Makkah on the day of the conquest with his chin on his saddle, humbly.»"],[4357,"A man spoke to the Prophet ﷺ on the Day of the Conquest, and trembling seized him. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Calm down, for I am only the son of a woman of Quraysh who used to eat dried meat.”"],[4358,"On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called upon the Ansar, saying, “O company of Ansar!” They responded, “At your service, may our fathers and mothers be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Turn your faces to Allah and to His Messenger; He will admit you into gardens beneath which rivers flow.” So they advanced, with a fervor like Hunayn, until they surrounded him in a dense throng, their shoulders pressing together, fighting until Allah defeated the polytheists."],[4359,"On the day of Hunayn, the people of Makkah and the people of Madinah met, and the fighting intensified, and they turned back in retreat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called upon the Ansar, saying, “O company of Muslims, I am the Messenger of Allah.” They said, “To you, by Allah, we have come.” So they bowed their heads and fought until Allah granted them victory."],[4360,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched to Hunayn after completing the conquest of Makkah, Malik b. 'Awf al-Nasri gathered from Banu Nasr, and Jusham, and from Sa'd b. Bakr, and groups from Banu Hilal, and people from Banu 'Amr b. 'Asim b. 'Awf b. 'Amir, and the confederates from Thaqif and Banu Malik joined with them. Then he marched with them against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, accompanied by wealth, women, and children. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of them, he sent 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, saying, “Go and infiltrate the people so that you may learn for us something of their situation.” So he entered and stayed among them for a day or two, then returned and reported the news to him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Umar b. al-Khattab, “Do you not hear what Ibn Abi Hadrad says?” 'Umar said, “Ibn Abi Hadrad has lied.” Ibn Abi Hadrad said, “If you accuse me of lying, then you have often accused one better than me of lying.” 'Umar said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Ibn Abi Hadrad says?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “You were astray, O 'Umar, and Allah guided you.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to Safwan b. Umayya and asked him for one hundred coats of mail and whatever equipment was needed for them. He said, “By force, O Muhammad?” He said, “Rather as a guaranteed loan, until we return them to you.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out marching.[Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it.] Sahih."],[4361,"From Abu Sallam al-Bahili, a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from 'Ubada b. al-Samit, who said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a piece of camel hair from the side of a camel, then said, “O people, it is not lawful for me of what Allah has granted you as spoils even the amount of this, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you. So pay back the thread and the needle, and beware of misappropriation, for it is a disgrace upon its perpetrator on the Day of Resurrection. And upon you is jihad in the path of Allah, for it is a gate among the gates of Paradise by which Allah removes worry and grief.”"],[4362,"We besieged the fortress of al-Ta'if with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, “Whoever reaches the enemy with an arrow, for him is a degree in Paradise.” On that day I reached with sixteen arrows. Sahih."],[4363,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed four 'umrahs: the 'umrah of al-Hudaybiyya, the 'umrah of al-Qada' the following year, the third from al-Ji'irrana, and the fourth which was with his Hajj."],[4364,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ marched to Tabuk, a man would continually lag behind, and they would say, “O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so has lagged behind.” He would say, “Leave him. If there is good in him, Allah will cause him to catch up with you, and if it is otherwise, Allah has relieved you of him.” Until it was said, “O Messenger of Allah, Abu Dharr has lagged behind, and his camel delayed him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Leave him. If there is good in him, Allah will cause him to catch up with you, and if it is otherwise, Allah has relieved you of him.” Abu Dharr waited for his camel, but it delayed him. When it delayed him, he took his belongings and placed them on his back, and set out following the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on foot. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dismounted at one of his halting places, and a Muslim lookout saw him and said, “O Messenger of Allah, this is a man walking on the road.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Be Abu Dharr.” When the people examined him, they said, “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, it is Abu Dharr.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “May Allah have mercy on Abu Dharr. He walks alone, dies alone, and will be resurrected alone.” Then time passed, and Abu Dharr was sent to al-Rabadha. When death approached him, he instructed his wife and his servant, “When I die, wash me and shroud me, then carry me and place me on the main road. The first riders who pass by you, say, 'This is Abu Dharr.'” When he died, they did that with him. A group of riders appeared and did not know of him until their mounts nearly trampled his bier. There was Ibn Mas'ud among a group of people from Kufa. They said, “What is this?” It was said, “The funeral of Abu Dharr.” Ibn Mas'ud burst into tears and said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth: 'May Allah have mercy on Abu Dharr. He walks alone, dies alone, and will be resurrected alone.'” So he dismounted and took charge of him personally until he buried him. When they arrived in Madinah, the words of 'Abdullah and what he had undertaken were mentioned to 'Uthman."],[4365,"From 'Ali? This is the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque, and this is the house of 'Ali. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr and 'Umar with Bara'a to the people of Makkah. They set out and met a rider. They said, “Who is this?” He said, “I am 'Ali. O Abu Bakr, give me the letter that is with you.” He said, “And what about me?” He said, “By Allah, I know nothing but good.” So 'Ali took the letter and went with it, and Abu Bakr and 'Umar returned to Madinah. They said, “What about us, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Nothing but good for you two, but it was said to me that none should convey from you except you or a man from your family.”"],[4366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Bakr and commanded him to proclaim these words. Then 'Ali followed him. While Abu Bakr was on part of the road, he heard the grumbling of the camel of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr came out alarmed, thinking it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but it was 'Ali. He handed over to him the letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which appointed him over the pilgrimage season, and 'Ali was commanded to proclaim these words. 'Ali stood during the days of Tashriq and proclaimed: “Allah is free from obligation to the polytheists, and His Messenger. So travel freely in the land for four months. No polytheist shall perform Hajj after this year, and no one shall circumambulate the House naked, and none shall enter Paradise except a believer.” 'Ali kept proclaiming it, and when his voice became hoarse, Abu Hurayra stood up and proclaimed.[Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it. The narration from 'Ali has been authenticated with an explanation of this proclamation.] Sahih."],[4367,"We asked 'Ali, “With what were you sent in the Hajj?” He said, “I was sent with four things: none shall enter Paradise except a believing soul, and no one shall circumambulate the House naked, and no believer and disbeliever shall gather in the Sacred Mosque after this year of theirs, and whoever had a treaty with the Prophet ﷺ, his treaty lasts until its term, and whoever had no treaty, his respite is four months.”"],[4368,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say when the two messengers of Musaylima the Liar came to him with his letter, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to them, “Do you two say the like of what he says?” They said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “By Allah, were it not that messengers are not to be killed, I would strike your necks.”"],[4369,"Yā Abā ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, there are people here who recite according to the recitation of Musaylima. ʿAbdullāh said: \"Is there a book other than the Book of Allah, or a messenger other than the Messenger of Allah after the spread of Islam?\" So he sent him back. Then he came to him later and said: \"O ʿAbdullāh, by the One besides whom there is no god, they are in the house reciting according to the recitation of Musaylima, and they have a muṣḥaf containing the recitation of Musaylima.\" That was during the time of ʿUthmān. ʿAbdullāh said to Qaraẓa, who was a cavalry commander: \"Go and surround the house and seize those inside.\" He did so and brought him eighty men. ʿAbdullāh said to them: \"Woe to you! Is there a book other than the Book of Allah, exalted is He, or a messenger other than the Messenger of Allah?\" They said: \"We repent to Allah, for we have wronged ourselves.\" So ʿAbdullāh left them and did not fight them, and he sent them to Syria, except their leader Ibn al-Nawwāḥa, who refused to repent. ʿAbdullāh said to Qaraẓa: \"Go and strike his neck and throw his head into his mother's lap, for I think she knew of his deed.\" So he did."],[4370,"Musaylima came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him: \"Do you testify that I am the Messenger of Allah?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I believe in Allah and His messengers.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"This is a man whose destruction has been delayed for the destruction of his people.\""],[4371,"The Banū Saʿd ibn Bakr sent Ḍimām ibn Thaʿlaba to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came to us, made his camel kneel at the gate of the mosque, hobbled it, then entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting in the mosque with his companions. He said: \"Which of you is the son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I am the son of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.\" He said: \"Muḥammad?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"O Muḥammad, I am going to question you and be harsh in questioning, so do not take it personally against me, for I will not take it personally.\" He said: \"Ask whatever seems fit to you.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will come after you: Did Allah send you to us as a messenger?\" He said: \"O Allah, yes.\" He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, your God and the God of those before you and the God of those who will come after you: Did Allah command you that we should worship Him and not associate anything with Him, and that we should cast off these idols and rivals that our forefathers used to worship?\" He ﷺ said: \"O Allah, yes.\" Then he began to mention the obligatory duties of Islam one by one—prayer, zakāt, fasting, ḥajj, and all the obligatory duties of Islam—adjuring him at each obligation as he had adjured him in the previous one. When he finished, he said: \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that you are His servant and messenger. I will perform these obligations and avoid what you have forbidden me; I will not add or subtract.\" Then he turned away to his camel. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when he turned: \"If the man with the two braids speaks the truth, he will enter Paradise.\" Ḍimām was a sturdy, hairy man with two locks of hair. Then he went to his camel, untied its hobble, and returned to his people. They gathered around him, and the first thing he said was while cursing al-Lāt and al-ʿUzzā. They said: \"Stop, O Ḍimām! Beware of leprosy, elephantiasis, and madness.\" He said: \"Woe to you! By Allah, they can neither harm nor benefit. Allah has sent a messenger and revealed to him a book by which He has rescued you from what you were in. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muḥammad is His servant and messenger. I have come to you from him with what he commanded you and forbade you.\" By Allah, by the evening of that day there was no man or woman in his settlement who was not a Muslim. Ibn ʿAbbās said: \"We have not heard of any delegate of a people better than Ḍimām ibn Thaʿlaba.\" [The two Shaykhs agreed on the arrival of Ḍimām in Madinah, but neither of them reported the ḥadīth in full, and this is authentic.]"],[4372,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ḥajj in the year ten after his arrival in Madinah, and he performed ḥajj alone (ifrād).\" [Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ.]"],[4373,"\"The Prophet ﷺ performed ḥajj several times before he emigrated, and after he emigrated he performed the Farewell ḥajj. The total number of sacrificial camels he brought was one hundred, among them a camel with a silver nose ring. The Prophet ﷺ slaughtered sixty-three with his own hand, and ʿAlī slaughtered the rest.\" It was said to al-Thawrī: \"Who mentioned it?\" He said: \"Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad from his father from Jābir, and Ibn Abī Laylā from Miqsam from Ibn ʿAbbās.\""],[4374,"Narrated Abu Muayhibah, who was a guardian of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke me up one night and said, 'O Abu Muayhibah, go and seek forgiveness, for I have been commanded to seek forgiveness for the people of Baqi' (the graveyard in Medina).' So I went with him. When we reached Baqi', he said, 'Peace be upon you, O people of Baqi', may what you are in this morning be good for you. If you knew what Allah has saved you from, the trials would have approached you like thick darkness following after darkness. Then he said, 'O Abu Muayhibah, Allah has chosen for me to be given the treasures of the earth, eternal life in it, and then Paradise, and the meeting with my Lord Almighty.' I said, 'May I be your sacrifice, both my parents are offered to you. Take the keys of the treasures of this earth, and eternal life in it, then Paradise.' He said, 'No, O Abu Muayhibah, I have chosen to meet my Lord Almighty.' Then he sought forgiveness for the people of Baqi' and left. When he began the prayer in the morning, he would begin his prayer by complaining about that day when he was taken (from this world).\" (Source: Al-Bukhari)"],[4375,"similarly is reported from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ[1]"],[4376,"From ʿĀʾisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ: \"The illness from which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died began in the house of Maymūna. He came out with his head bandaged and entered upon me between two men, his feet dragging on the ground—on his right al-ʿAbbās and on his left a man.\" ʿUbaydullāh said: Ibn ʿAbbās informed me that the one on his left was ʿAlī."],[4377,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dying, and there was a bowl of water near him. He would dip his hand into the bowl and then wipe his face with the water, then say: \"O Allah, help me against the agonies of death.\""],[4378,"The last thing he spoke was: \"The glory of my Lord, the Exalted. I have conveyed.\" Then he passed away ﷺ."],[4379,"The last advice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when death approached him was: \"The prayer, the prayer,\" twice, \"and what your right hands possess.\" He kept gurgling with it in his chest, and his tongue could not utter it. [They agreed on reporting this ḥadīth and on reporting the ḥadīth of ʿĀʾisha that the last word he spoke was \"the Highest Companion.\"]"],[4380,"\"On the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, everything in Madinah became dark.\""],[4381,"\"I witnessed the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, and I have never seen a day more ugly than it.\""],[4382,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, angels offered them condolences; they heard the voice but did not see the person. They said: \"Peace be upon you, O people of the household, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. In Allah there is consolation for every calamity and a replacement for every loss. So trust in Allah and hope in Him. The truly deprived is the one deprived of reward. Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings.\""],[4383,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, his companions gathered around him and wept, and they assembled. Then a man entered, reddish of beard, large-bodied and handsome. He stepped over their necks, wept, then turned to the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'In Allah there is consolation from every affliction, compensation for every loss, and a successor for every perished one. So to Allah turn in repentance, and to Him turn your desire. The real bereaved is one who is not recompensed.' Then he departed. Some of them said to one another, 'Do you know the man?' Abu Bakr and Ali said, 'Yes, this is the brother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, al-Khidr ﷺ .' This is a witness for what preceded, even though Abbad b. Abd al-Samad is not up to the standard of this book. This is a witness for what preceded it."],[4384,"Aisha used to say, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say during the illness in which he passed away, 'O Aisha, I feel the pain of the food that I ate at Khaybar. This is the time when the aorta will be severed from that poison.'\""],[4385,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was killed is dearer to me than that I swear one oath that he was not killed, because Allah took him as a prophet and as a martyr."],[4386,"I heard al-Sha'bi say: 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was poisoned, and Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was poisoned, and Umar b. al-Khattab was killed patiently, and Uthman b. Affan was killed patiently, and Ali b. Abi Talib was killed patiently, and al-Hasan b. Ali was poisoned, and al-Husayn b. Ali was killed patiently. So what hope remains after them?' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4387,"Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept over the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O father, how close he is to his Lord! O father, to Jibril we announce his death. O father, the Garden of Firdaws is his abode.'"],[4388,"I washed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I looked for what normally occurs to a corpse, but I saw nothing. He was fragrant alive and dead ﷺ."],[4389,"We wanted to wash the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the people differed about it. Some said, 'Should we strip the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as we strip our dead, or wash him with his clothes on?' Then Allah cast sleep upon them until every man among them was asleep with his chin on his chest. Then a voice from the side of the house said, 'Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is to be washed with his clothes on?' So they washed him with his shirt on, pouring water over him and rubbing him from above it. Aisha said: 'By Allah, if I had known beforehand what I came to know afterward, none would have washed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except his wives.'"],[4390,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became seriously ill, we said, 'Who will pray over you, O Messenger of Allah?' He wept and we wept, and he said: 'Gently, may Allah forgive you and reward you well on behalf of your Prophet. When you have washed me, embalmed me, and shrouded me, place me on the edge of my grave, then leave me for a while. The first to pray over me will be my intimate friend and companion Jibril, then Mikail, then Israfil, then the Angel of Death with armies of angels. Then let the men of my household begin the prayer over me, then their women. Then enter in groups and singly, and do not harm me with wailing, lamentation, or shouting. Convey my greetings of peace to any of my companions who is absent, for I call you as witnesses that I have sent peace upon everyone who enters Islam and follows me in my religion from this day until the Day of Resurrection.' Abd al-Malik b. Abd al-Rahman in this chain is unknown; we do not know him as reliable or unreliable, and the rest are all trustworthy. Abd al-Malik is unknown."],[4391,"I saw as if three moons fell into my chamber. I asked Abu Bakr, and he said, 'O Aisha, if your dream is true, the best of the people of the earth will be buried in your house, three of them.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died and was buried, Abu Bakr said to me, 'O Aisha, this is the best of your moons, and he is one of them.'"],[4392,"The Prophet ﷺ used to like dreams. He said, 'Has anyone of you seen a dream today?' Aisha said, 'I saw as if three moons fell into my chamber.' The Prophet ﷺ said to her, 'If your dream is true, three will be buried in your house, they are the best, or the most excellent, of the people of the earth.' When the Prophet ﷺ died and was buried in her house, Abu Bakr said to her, 'This is one of your moons, and he is the best of them.' Then Abu Bakr and Umar died and were buried in her house."],[4393,"I used to enter my house where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was while I had taken off my outer garment, saying, 'He is only my husband and my father.' But when Umar was buried with them, by Allah, I never entered except with my clothes fastened tightly, out of modesty before Umar."],[4394,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq's name is Abdullah b. Uthman b. Amir b. Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Taym b. Murrah b. Ka'b b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr."],[4395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever desires to see a person from the those saved from the Hellfire, let him look at Abu Bakr. And indeed, his name, which his family named him, is Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Amr ibn Amr where he was born. But the name 'Atiq overwhelmed him.\""],[4396,"The passage translates to: \"Ali heard someone swear, 'By Allah, the Exalted has sent down the name of Abu Bakr from the heavens as 'Siddiq' (the truthful).' If it were not for the ignorance of Muhammad ibn Sulaiman al-Saeedi, I would have judged this chain of narration as authentic. There is also supporting evidence in the hadith of al-Nazzal ibn Sabra from Ali. If it were not for the ignorance of Muhammad ibn Sulaiman al-Saeedi, the teacher of Ishaq al-Sululi, I would have judged it as authentic.\""],[4397,"We met Ali in good spirits while he was joking, and we said, 'Tell us about your companions.' He said, 'All the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are my companions.' We said, 'Tell us about Abu Bakr.' He said, 'That is a man whom Allah named Siddiq on the tongue of Jibril and Muhammad, peace be upon them both.' Hilal b. al-Ala is munkar al-hadith."],[4398,"When the Prophet Muhammad (pbuh) was taken on the Night Journey to the Al-Aqsa Mosque, people began talking about it. Some people turned away from believing it, but those who believed and confirmed it went to Abu Bakr and asked him, \"Does your friend claim that he was taken on this journey to Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa last night?\" Abu Bakr asked, \"Did he say that?\" They replied, \"Yes.\" Abu Bakr said, \"If he said that, then he has spoken the truth.\" They asked him, \"Do you believe him when he says that he went to Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa last night and returned before morning?\" Abu Bakr replied, \"Yes, I believe him even in something far greater than that. I believe him when he receives revelation from the heavens, either during the morning or while at rest.\" That is why Abu Bakr was given the title \"As-Siddiq\" (the Truthful)."],[4399,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was to the Prophet ﷺ in the position of a vizier. He would consult him in all his affairs. He was the second in Islam, the second in the cave, the second in the shelter on the day of Badr, and the second in the grave. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never put anyone ahead of him. Among its narrators is one unknown."],[4400,"Abu Bakr died on Tuesday night, eight nights remaining of Jumada al-Ula in the year thirteen. He was then sixty-three years old. His illness lasted fifteen days. The cause of his illness was that he bathed on a cold day and developed a fever, so for fifteen nights he did not go out for prayer. Umar led the people in prayer while he was in the house that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had allotted to him, facing Uthman's house today. He instructed that his wife Asma' bt. Umays wash him. She became weak, so she sought help from Abd al-Rahman. He was shrouded in two garments, one of which was washed — and it is said in three garments. He was carried on the bier of the Prophet ﷺ, which was the bier of A'ishah upon which she used to sleep. Abu Bakr was carried on it, and Umar prayed over him in the mosque between the grave and the pulpit. He was buried at night in the room with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his head was placed between the shoulders of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4401,"The cause of the death of Abu Bakr was the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . His body continued to deteriorate until he died. Its chain of narration is weak."],[4402,"One day a man gave Abu Bakr a bowl of khazirah as a gift. With him was a man called al-Harith b. Kaladah, who had knowledge. When they had eaten from it, Ibn Kaladah said, \"In it is a poison that acts within a year.\" By the One in whose hand is my soul, a year had not passed before they both died on the same day, at the head of the year."],[4403,"He said: \"What is to be expected from this lowly world when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was poisoned, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq was poisoned, Umar b. al-Khattab was killed outright, and likewise Uthman and Ali were killed, al-Hasan was poisoned, and al-Husayn was killed outright.\" Al-Sari is abandoned."],[4404,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Hassan b. Thabit: \"Have you said anything about Abu Bakr?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Say it so that I may hear.\" He said, I recited: [al-Basit meter] \"And the second of two in the lofty cave, while the enemy circled around him when he climbed the mountain. And he was the beloved of the Messenger of Allah, they knew, among all creatures none was equal to him as a substitute.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled. Amr b. Ziyad fabricates hadith."],[4405,"You heard the saying of Hassan: [al-Basit meter] \"When you recall the grief of a trusted brother, remember your brother Abu Bakr for what he did. The best of creation, its most pious and most just after the Prophet, and its most faithful to what he bore. The second, the follower, the praised one in his presence, and the first of the people among them to believe the messengers.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4406,"She said: Abu Bakr asked me, \"In how many garments did you shroud the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" I said, \"In three garments.\" He said, \"Shroud me in them too.\""],[4407,"In how many garments did you shroud the Prophet ﷺ? I said, \"In three white Yemeni new garments, with no shirt and no turban among them.\" He said, \"Wash this garment of mine — it has a trace of saffron and reddish dye — and put it with two new garments.\" I said, \"It is worn out.\" He said, \"The living is more entitled to the new than the dead; it is only for the discharge.\" According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4408,"Abu Bakr held the caliphate for two years and seven months."],[4409,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the beginning of his prophethood while he was in Makkah and at that time he was in disguise, so I asked him, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am a Prophet.\" I asked, \"What is a Prophet?\" He said, \"A Messenger of Allah.\" I asked, \"Did Allah send you?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I asked, \"What did Allah send you with?\" He said, \"To worship Allah alone, break the idols, and maintain family ties.\" I said, \"Yes, I believe in that which Allah has sent you. So who has followed you in this?\" He said, \"A slave and a free man,\" meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. 'Umar used to say, \"I remember that I was a quarter of Islam.\" Then I became Muslim and said, \"Shall I follow you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"No, rather convey the truth to your people. When you hear that I have left Makkah, then follow me.\""],[4410,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was descending in 'Ukaz. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, who follows you in this matter?\" He said, \"Two free men and a slave: Abu Bakr and Bilal.\" I embraced Islam at that moment. As for the narration of Abu 'Amr"],[4411,"Abu Umamah said: O Amr b. Abasah, by what do you claim that you are a quarter of Islam?"],[4412,"Abu Bakr was our master, our best, and the most beloved of us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It is sahih according to their condition, but they did not include it. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4413,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf was with Umar b. al-Khattab, and Muhammad b. Maslamah broke the sword of al-Zubayr. Then Abu Bakr stood and addressed the people, apologizing to them. He said: By Allah, I was never eager for authority for a single day or night, nor desirous of it, nor did I ask Allah ﷻ for it in secret or openly. But I feared tribulation. I have no comfort in authority, but I have been entrusted with a momentous matter for which I have no strength or means except with the strengthening of Allah ﷻ. I would wish that the strongest of people to bear it were in my place today. The Muhajirun accepted from him what he said and his apology. Ali and al-Zubayr said: We were not angry except because we were delayed from consultation, and we see Abu Bakr as the most deserving of the people for it after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he is the companion of the cave and the second of two, and we know his honor and his seniority. And indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to lead the people in prayer while he was still alive."],[4414,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Ansar said: A leader from among us and a leader from among you. ‘Umar went to them and said: O Ansar, do you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer? Which of you would like himself to be given precedence over Abu Bakr? The Ansar said: We seek refuge with Allah from being given precedence over Abu Bakr. (Using translation from Aḥmad 133)"],[4415,"They struck the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he fell unconscious. Abu Bakr stood up and began calling out, saying: \"Woe to you! Would you kill a man for saying, 'My Lord is Allah'?\" They said: \"Who is this?\" They said: \"This is Ibn Abi Quhafah, the madman.\""],[4416,"He informed him that he heard Suraqah b. Ju'shum say: \"The messengers of the disbelievers of Quraysh came to us, offering a blood-money payment for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and for Abu Bakr, and for whoever kills or captures them, a blood-money payment for each of the two.\""],[4417,"I heard 'Ali say: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came first, Abu Bakr was second, 'Umar was third, then a trial befell us, and Allah forgives whom He wills.\""],[4418,"When 'Umar b. al-Khattab was placed on his bier, the people gathered around him, supplicating for him, and I was among them. Then 'Ali b. Abi Talib came and said: \"I used to think that Allah the Exalted would place you with your two companions. That is because I used to hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say most often: 'I went, with Abu Bakr and 'Umar; I entered, with Abu Bakr and 'Umar; I came out, with Abu Bakr and 'Umar.' And I used to think that Allah would place you with them.\""],[4419,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the mosque with one of his hands on Abu Bakr and the other on 'Umar, and said: \"Thus shall we be raised on the Day of Resurrection.\" Sa'id b. Maslamah al-Qurashi is weak."],[4420,"\"The first over whom the earth will split open will be me, then Abu Bakr, then 'Umar. Then I will come to the people of al-Baqi', and it will split open over them, and I will be raised among them.\""],[4421,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me and to Abu Bakr: \"With one of you is Jibril, and with the other is Mika'il and Israfil, a mighty angel who witnesses the fighting and is in the ranks.\""],[4422,"\"While I was drawing water from the well of Badr, a strong wind came the like of which I had never seen, then it passed. Then another strong wind came, the like of which I had never seen except the previous one, then it passed. Then a third strong wind came, the like of which I had never seen except the previous one. The first wind was Jibril descending with a thousand angels alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The second wind was Mika'il descending with a thousand angels on the right of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr was on his right. The third wind was Israfil descending with a thousand angels on the left of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was on the left. When Allah the Exalted defeated his enemies, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mounted me on his horse; it galloped with me and I fell on my heels. I called upon Allah ﷻ, and He held me firm. When I sat upright upon it, I thrust with this hand of mine into the enemy until this part of me was stained with blood.\" And he pointed to his armpit."],[4423,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he looked at Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: \"These two are the hearing and the sight.\""],[4424,"Regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ: {For Allah is his protector, and Jibril, and the righteous believers} [at-Tahrim 4], he said: Abu Umamah narrated to me that it is as He said: \"Allah is his protector, and Jibril, and the righteous believers are Abu Bakr and 'Umar.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. Musa b. 'Umayr is weak."],[4425,"\"If you entrust authority to Abu Bakr, you will find him abstemious in this world and desirous of the Hereafter. If you entrust authority to 'Umar, you will find him strong and trustworthy; the blame of a critic does not affect him regarding Allah the Exalted. If you entrust authority to 'Ali, you will find him a guide and rightly guided, who will lead you along the path.\""],[4426,"They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, would that you appointed a successor over us?\" He said: \"If I appoint a successor over you and you disobey him, punishment will descend upon you.\" They said: \"Would that you appointed Abu Bakr over us.\" He said: \"If I appoint him over you, you will find him strong in the affair of Allah, weak in his body.\" They said: \"Would that you appointed 'Umar over us.\" He said: \"If I appoint him over you, you will find him strong and trustworthy; the blame of a critic does not affect him regarding Allah.\" They said: \"Would that you appointed 'Ali over us.\" He said: \"You will not do so, and if you do, you will find him a guide and rightly guided, who will lead you along the straight path.\""],[4427,"\"Abu Bakr and Umar.\""],[4428,"“Who among you saw a dream?” A man said, “I did. I saw as if a balance descended from the sky, and you and Abu Bakr were weighed, and you outweighed Abu Bakr. Then Umar and Abu Bakr were weighed, and Abu Bakr outweighed. Then Umar and Uthman were weighed, and Umar outweighed. Then the balance was raised.” He said, “We saw displeasure on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[4429,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he had prayed the morning prayer, would turn to his companions and say, “Which of you saw a dream last night?” One day he prayed and then said, “Which of you saw a dream?” A man said, “I did, O Messenger of Allah. I saw as if a balance was let down from the sky, and you were placed in one pan and Abu Bakr in the other, and you outweighed Abu Bakr. Then you were raised and Abu Bakr was left in his place. Then Umar b. al-Khattab was brought and placed in the other pan, and Abu Bakr outweighed him. Then Abu Bakr was raised and Uthman was brought and placed in the other pan, and Umar outweighed Uthman. Then Umar and Uthman were raised and the balance was raised.” He said, “Then the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed, and he said, ‘The caliphate of prophethood is thirty years, then it will become kingship.’” Saʿid b. Jumhan said: Safinah said to me, “Hold fast: two years of Abu Bakr, ten of Umar, twelve of Uthman, and six of Ali, all together.” These transmissions have been narrated with a sound chain elevated to the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4430,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Tonight a righteous man was shown that Abu Bakr was tied to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Umar was tied to Abu Bakr, and Uthman was tied to Umar.” Jabir said: When we arose from the Prophet ﷺ, we said, “The righteous man is the Prophet ﷺ. As for what was mentioned of their being tied to one another, they are the guardians of this matter with which Allah sent His Prophet ﷺ, and for the final outcome.” “The chain of this hadith is sound from Abu Hurayrah, and they did not include it.” Sahih."],[4431,"“The caliphate is in Madinah, and the kingship is in Syria.”"],[4432,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah have mercy on Abu Bakr, who married me to his daughter and carried me to the place of emigration.\""],[4433,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered in the year of the conquest, he saw women striking the faces of horses with their veils. He smiled at Abu Bakr and said, “O Abu Bakr, how did Hassan b. Thabit put it?” Abu Bakr recited to him [wafir meter]: “I would lose my little daughter if you did not see them raising the dust from the shoulders of Kada; they vie for the reins, hastening, while the women strike them with their veils.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Enter from where Hassan said.”"],[4434,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the Prophet ﷺ said, “A man from the people of Paradise will appear to you.” Then Abu Bakr appeared, greeted, and sat down."],[4435,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Gabriel took my hand and showed me the gate of Paradise through which my ummah will enter.” Abu Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, I wish I had been with you so that I could see it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed, you will be the first of my ummah to enter it.”"],[4436,"Aisha reported: When Khadijah died, Khawlah bt. Hakim came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Will you not marry?” He said, “Whom?” She said, “If you wish, a virgin, and if you wish, a previously married woman.” He said, “Who is the virgin, and who is the previously married woman?” She said, “As for the virgin, the daughter of the most beloved of Allah’s creation to you, Aisha bt. Abu Bakr. As for the previously married woman, Sawdah bt. Zamʿah.”"],[4437,"I said to Aisha, “Which of the people was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” She said, “Abu Bakr, then Umar, then Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah.”"],[4438,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Abu Bakr and Umar appeared. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Praise be to Allah who has strengthened me with you two.”"],[4439,"“I considered sending men to the horizons to teach the people the sunnahs and the obligatory duties, just as Jesus son of Mary sent the disciples.” It was said to him, “What about Abu Bakr and Umar?” He said, “I cannot do without them. They are to the religion like hearing and sight.”"],[4440,"When the verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ: {Indeed, those who lower their voices in the presence of the Messenger of Allah—those are the ones whose hearts Allah has tested for righteousness} [al-Hujurat 3], Abu Bakr said, “I resolved upon myself that I would not speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except as one confiding a secret.”"],[4441,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, how can there be success after this verse: {Whoever does evil will be recompensed for it} [al-Nisa': 123]? For every evil we have done, we will be recompensed for it.' He said, 'May Allah forgive you, O Abu Bakr,' saying it three times. 'O Abu Bakr, do you not fall ill? Do you not grieve? Do you not become weary? Do you not suffer hardship?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'That is how you are recompensed in this world.'"],[4442,"Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and Umar, and be guided by the guidance of Ammar, and hold fast to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd."],[4443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and Umar, and be guided by the guidance of Ammar, and hold fast to the covenant of Ibn Umm Abd.'"],[4444,"Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and Umar, and be guided by the guidance of Ammar, and when Ibn Umm Abd narrates to you, believe him."],[4445,"Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and Umar."],[4446,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Follow in the footsteps of those who came after me, namely Abu Bakr and Umar, and seek guidance from the teachings of Ammar. Hold onto the covenant of Ibn Umme Abd. This is a hadith for the sake of narrating the virtues of the two honorable companions, and this chain of narration has been established from Ath-Thawri and Mas'ar Yahya al-Himmani. It has also been established from Mas'ar and Wakie', as well as Hafs ibn Umar al-Ayli. Then, [this hadith] was summarized in its narration from Ibn Uyaynah al-Humaidi and others. This chain of narration was established from Ibn Uyaynah to Ishaq bin Isa bin At-Tabbaa'. Thus, the authenticity of this hadith has been confirmed even though they did not mention it specifically, and we have found a supporting witness for it through a reliable chain of narration from Abdullah ibn Mas'ood.\""],[4447,"Follow the two who come after me: Abu Bakr and Umar, and be guided by the guidance of Ammar, and hold fast to the covenant of Ibn Mas'ud."],[4448,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, the orators of the Ansar stood up. Some of them began saying, 'O company of Muhajirun, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed a man from among you, he paired with him a man from among us. So we think that this matter should be undertaken by two men, one from you and one from us.' The orators of the Ansar followed one another in saying that. Then Zayd b. Thabit stood up and said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was from the Muhajirun, and the Imam should be from the Muhajirun, and we are his supporters as we were supporters of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then Abu Bakr stood up and said, 'May Allah reward you well, O company of Ansar, and make firm your speaker.' Then he said, 'But if you did otherwise, we would not have made peace with you.' Then Zayd b. Thabit took Abu Bakr by the hand and said, 'This is your companion, so give him allegiance.' Then they departed. When Abu Bakr sat on the pulpit, he looked into the faces of the people and did not see Ali. He asked about him, and some of the Ansar went and brought him. Abu Bakr said, 'Cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his son-in-law, did you intend to split the staff of the Muslims?' He said, 'No blame, O successor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' and gave him allegiance. Then he did not see al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam, so he asked about him until they brought him. He said, 'Cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his disciple, did you intend to split the staff of the Muslims?' He said something similar: 'No blame, O successor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' and they both gave him allegiance."],[4449,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey to Al-Aqsa Mosque, people started talking about it. Some people who used to believe in him and trust him turned away, while men from the polytheists went to Abu Bakr and asked him, \"Does your companion claim that he was taken on a journey to Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa last night?\" Abu Bakr asked them, \"Did he say that?\" They replied, \"Yes.\" Abu Bakr then said, \"If he indeed said that, then he has spoken the truth.\" They asked him, \"Do you believe him when he claims that he went to Al-Masjid Al-Aqsa and came back before morning?\" Abu Bakr answered, \"Yes, I believe him in something even more miraculous than that. I believe him in the news of the heavens in the early morning or evening. That is why he is called Abu Bakr As-Siddiq.\""],[4450,"That evil had occurred among them until they threw stones at each other. The Prophet ﷺ came to them and said, 'O Abu Bakr, if the prayer is established, step forward and lead the people in prayer.' He said, 'Yes.'"],[4451,"Banu al-Mustaliq sent me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for us: to whom should we give our sadaqah after you?' He said, 'So I went to him and asked him, and he said, \"To Abu Bakr.\" I came back to them and informed them. They said, 'Return to him and ask him: if something happens to Abu Bakr, then to whom?' I went to him and asked him, and he said, 'To Umar.' I came back to them and informed them. They said, 'Return to him and ask him: if something happens to Umar, then to whom?' I went to him and asked him, and he said, 'To Uthman.' I came back to them and informed them. They said, 'Return to him and ask him: if something happens to Uthman, then to whom?' I went to him and asked him, and he said, 'If something happens to Uthman, then may you have ruin for all time, ruin!'"],[4452,"I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he said to Hassan b. Thabit, 'Have you said anything about Abu Bakr?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Say it so that I may hear.' He said: I recited: 'And the second of two in the lofty cave, when the enemy roamed about it as he climbed the mountain. And he was the beloved of the Messenger of Allah, as they knew, among all creatures, no one equaled him.' Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4453,"Abu Sufyan b. Harb came to Ali b. Abi Talib and said, 'Why is this matter in the hands of the least numerous and most humiliated of Quraysh,' meaning Abu Bakr? 'By Allah, if I wished, I would fill it against him with cavalry and infantry.' Ali said, 'For a long time you have been hostile to Islam and its people, O Abu Sufyan, but it has not harmed it at all. We found Abu Bakr worthy of it.' Its chain is authentic."],[4454,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to him. Some of them spoke with words that were mistaken in speech. The Prophet ﷺ turned to Abu Bakr and said, 'O Abu Bakr, did you hear what they said?' He said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and I understood it.' He said, 'Then answer them.' Abu Bakr answered them with a response and excelled in the answer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Abu Bakr, Allah has given you the greatest good pleasure.' Some of the people said to him, 'What is the greatest good pleasure, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Allah will manifest Himself to His servants in general in the Hereafter, and He will manifest Himself to Abu Bakr in particular.'"],[4455,"If the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were to appoint a successor, he would have appointed Abu Bakr and Umar."],[4456,"\"What Muslims see as good, it is considered good in the eyes of Allah. And what Muslims see as bad, it is considered bad in the eyes of Allah. The companions unanimously agreed to appoint Abu Bakr as the successor.\""],[4457,"When the Prophet ﷺ died, the Muhajirun and the Ansar gathered at the Saqifah of Banu Sa'idah for the pledge of allegiance to Abu Bakr. I came to Umm Salamah and said to her, \"The people have pledged allegiance to Abu Bakr.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not appoint a successor, so I will not appoint one. But if Allah wills good for the people, He will unite them after me upon the best of them, just as He united them after their Prophet upon the best of them."],[4459,"Abu Bakr took charge of us and he was the best of Allah's vicegerents, the most merciful to us, and the kindest to us."],[4460,"We circumambulated a room in which Abu Bakr was, when he was afflicted with the illness of which he died. He looked out at us once and said, \"Are you not pleased with what I am doing?\" We said, \"Yes, O Khalifa of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4461,"When Abu Bakr al-Siddiq dispatched the armies toward Syria—Yazid b. Abi Sufyan, Amr b. al-As, and Shurahbil b. Hasanah—he walked with them until he reached Thaniyyat al-Wada'. They said, \"O Khalifa of the Messenger of Allah, you walk while we are riding?\""],[4462,"I entered upon Abu Bakr during his caliphate."],[4463,"The wealth of Bahrain came to us during the caliphate of Abu Bakr."],[4464,"Uyaynah b. Hisn and al-Aqra' b. Habis came to Abu Bakr and said, \"O Khalifa of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4465,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I participated in a military campaign during the caliphate of Abu Bakr. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4466,"We were with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and he wept. We said, \"O Khalifa of the Messenger of Allah, what is this weeping?\""],[4467,"The Companions of the Prophet ﷺ unanimously agreed and appointed Abu Bakr as successor. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4468,"Mus'ab b. 'Abd Allah al-Zubayri narrated to me: They both said: 'Umar b. al-Khattab b. Nufayl b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Riyah b. 'Abd Allah b. Qurt b. Razah b. 'Adi b. Ka'b b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr, in one wording. They both said: His mother was Hantama bt. Hashim b. al-Mughira b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum, and her mother was al-Shifa' bt. 'Abd Qays b. 'Adi b. Sa'd b. Taym. He was given the kunya Abu Hafs. He was appointed as successor on the day Abu Bakr died, which was Tuesday, eight nights remaining of Jumada al-Akhira."],[4469,"“Abu Bakr died and 'Umar was appointed as successor at the head of two years, three months, and twenty-two days from the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4470,"I went out with the people of Madinah on a day of 'Id and saw 'Umar b. al-Khattab walking barefoot, an old man, bald, brown-skinned, left-handed, tall, towering over the people as if he were on a mount, wearing a Qatari cloak, saying: “O servants of Allah, emigrate and do not become like the Bedouins. Let one of you be wary of the rabbit which he kills by throwing pebbles or stones at it and then eats it. Rather, let the spear-points, lances, and arrows make it lawful for you.”"],[4471,"'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz asked Abu Bakr b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathma: For what reason was it written “from the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ” during the era of Abu Bakr, then 'Umar initially wrote “from the Caliph of Abu Bakr”? Who was the first to write “from the Commander of the Believers”? He said: Al-Shifa' narrated to me—and she was among the first emigrant women—that 'Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to the governor of Iraq to send him two sturdy men whom he could ask about Iraq and its people. The governor of Iraq sent Labid b. Rabi'a and 'Adi b. Hatim. When they arrived in Madinah, they made their mounts kneel in the courtyard of the mosque, then entered the mosque. They met 'Amr b. al-'As and said: Seek permission for us, O 'Amr, from the Commander of the Believers. 'Amr said: You two, by Allah, have hit upon his name: he is the commander and we are the believers. 'Amr jumped up and entered upon 'Umar, Commander of the Believers, and said: Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Believers. 'Umar said: What made you come up with this name, O Ibn al-'As? My Lord knows—you must explain what you said. He said: Labid b. Rabi'a and 'Adi b. Hatim have arrived. They made their mounts kneel in the courtyard of the mosque, then entered upon me and said: Seek permission for us, O 'Amr, from the Commander of the Believers. They, by Allah, hit upon your name: we are the believers and you are our commander. He said: “So the correspondence continued with that from that day onward.” Al-Shifa' was the grandmother of Abu Bakr b. Sulayman. Sahih."],[4472,"When 'Umar came to Syria, a ford presented itself to him. 'Umar dismounted from his camel, took off his leather socks—or he said his boots—then took hold of his mount's halter and waded through the ford. Abu 'Ubayda b. al-Jarrah said to him: You have done, O Commander of the Believers, a great deed in the eyes of the people of the land: you took off your leather socks, led your mount, and waded through the ford. He said: 'Umar struck his hand against Abu 'Ubayda's chest and said: “Oh, if only someone other than you had said it, O Abu 'Ubayda! You were the fewest of people, and Allah honored you with Islam. So whatever you seek honor through other than it, Allah will humiliate you, the Exalted.”"],[4473,"I went on a military expedition with 'Umar to Syria. We stopped at a place, and a village chief came, asking to be directed to the Commander of the Believers, until he reached him. When the village chief saw 'Umar, he prostrated. 'Umar said: “What is this prostration?” He said: This is how we do with kings. 'Umar said: “Prostrate to your Lord who created you.” He said: O Commander of the Believers, I have prepared food for you, so come to me. 'Umar said: “Is there any of the Persians' images in your house?” He said: Yes. He said: “We have no need of your house, but go and send us a type of food, and do not add anything more to it.” He said: So he went and sent food to him, and he ate from it. Then 'Umar said to his servant: “Is there any of that nabidh in your water-skin?” He said: Yes. He said: “Send it to us.” He brought it and poured it into a vessel, then smelled it and found its smell repugnant. He poured water over it, then smelled it and found its smell repugnant. He poured water over it three times, then drank it. Then he said: “If something troubles you in your drink, do with it like this.” Muslim al-A'war—they abandoned him."],[4474,"“O Allah, support the religion with 'Umar b. al-Khattab.”"],[4475,"“O Allah, strengthen Islam with 'Umar.”"],[4476,"“O Allah, strengthen Islam especially with 'Umar b. al-Khattab.”"],[4477,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, strengthen Islam with 'Umar b. al-Khattab or with Abu Jahl b. Hisham.” So Allah made the supplication of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for 'Umar, and upon him He built the dominion of Islam and through him He demolished the idols. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4478,"“By Allah, we were not able to pray at the Ka'ba openly until 'Umar accepted Islam.”"],[4479,"“Islam during the time of 'Umar was like a man approaching, only increasing in nearness. When 'Umar was killed, it was like a man retreating, only increasing in distance.”"],[4480,"The first one whom the Truth will embrace on the Day of Resurrection is Umar, and the first one whom the Truth will shake hands with on the Day of Resurrection is Umar, and the first one whose hand will be taken and led to Paradise is Umar b. al-Khattab."],[4481,"We have remained mighty ever since Umar embraced Islam."],[4482,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said when Umar embraced Islam: Jibril came to me and said, 'The people of heaven have rejoiced at Umar's Islam.' [Sahih] Abdullah b. Khurash - al-Daraqutni deemed him weak."],[4483,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck Umar b. al-Khattab's chest with his hand when he embraced Islam three times, saying: 'O Allah, bring out what is in his chest of rancor and replace it with faith,' saying that three times."],[4484,"Umar fought the polytheists in the mosque of Makkah, and he kept fighting them from morning until the sun was above his head. He said: He became exhausted and sat down. Then a man entered upon him wearing a red cloak and a Qumisi shirt, handsome of face. He came and dispersed them, saying: 'What do you want from this man?' They said: 'By Allah, nothing except that he has apostatized.' He said: 'What an excellent man, he chose a religion for himself. Leave him and what he chose for himself. Do you think Banu 'Adi would be pleased if Umar were killed? No, by Allah, Banu 'Adi would not be pleased.' He said: And Umar said that day: 'O enemies of Allah! By Allah, if we reached three hundred, we would drive you out of it.' I said to my father afterwards: 'Who was that man who turned them away from you that day?' He said: 'That was al-'As b. Wa'il, Abu 'Amr b. al-'As.'"],[4485,"When Umar embraced Islam, the polytheists said: 'Today the people have become equal with us.'"],[4486,"If there were a prophet after me, it would be Umar b. al-Khattab."],[4487,"I saw in a dream that I was given a large wooden bowl full of milk, and I drank from it until I was full, until I saw it in a vein between the skin and the flesh. Then there remained a leftover, so I gave it to Umar b. al-Khattab. They said: 'O Prophet of Allah, this is knowledge that Allah gave you, and you were filled with it, then a leftover remained and you gave it to Umar b. al-Khattab.' He said: 'You have spoken correctly.'"],[4488,"If the knowledge of Umar were placed in one pan of a scale and the knowledge of the people in another, Umar's knowledge would outweigh."],[4489,"Umar was the most pious of us toward the Lord and the most read of us of the Book of Allah."],[4490,"There were inspired individuals among the nations before; if there is one in my nation, it is Umar b. al-Khattab."],[4491,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a brief sermon. When he finished, he said: 'O Abu Bakr, stand and preach.' Abu Bakr stood and preached, and he was shorter than the Prophet ﷺ. When Abu Bakr finished his sermon, he said: 'O Umar, stand and preach.' Umar stood and preached, and he was shorter than the Prophet ﷺ and shorter than Abu Bakr."],[4492,"Indeed, Allah has placed truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart."],[4493,"The narrator said: \"Get up and pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Two men stood up, but Abu Jahsh refused to stand. Umar said to him, \"Pray, O Abu Jahsh, with the Prophet ﷺ.\" He replied, \"I will not stand until a man comes to me who is stronger in arm than I and harder in grip than I, so he throws me down and rubs my face in the dust.\" Umar said, \"So I rose to him, and I was stronger in arm and harder in grip than him, and I threw him down and rubbed his face in the dust. Then Uthman came to me and held me back. Umar ibn al-Khattab went out angry until he reached the Prophet ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ saw him and saw the anger in his face, he said, 'What troubles you, O Abu Hafs?' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I came upon a group sitting at the door of the mosque while the prayer had been established, and among them was Abu Jahsh al-Laythi. The two men stood up,' and he repeated the story. Then Umar said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, Uthman's help to him was only because he hosted him one night and he wanted to repay that favor.' Uthman heard him and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, do you not hear what Umar says about us in your presence?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'If Umar is pleased, by the mercy of Allah, I would wish that you had brought me the head of the wicked one.' Umar got up, and when he had gone far, the Prophet ﷺ called him and said, 'Come here, O Umar, where did you intend to go?' He said, 'I intended to bring you the head of the wicked one.' He said, 'Sit down until I inform you of the self-sufficiency of the Lord from the prayer of Abu Jahsh al-Laythi. Indeed, Allah has in the lowest heaven angels in humility who do not raise their heads until the Hour is established. When the Hour is established, they raise their heads and say, \"Our Lord, we have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped.\"' Umar ibn al-Khattab said to him, 'And what do they say, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'As for the people of the lowest heaven, they say, \"Glory be to the One with sovereignty and dominion.\" As for the people of the second heaven, they say, \"Glory be to the Living who does not die.\" So say it, O Umar, in your prayer.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what about what you taught me and commanded me to say in my prayer?' He said, 'Say this once and that once.' And what he had commanded him was to say, 'I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and I seek refuge in You from You. Glorified be Your Face.'"],[4494,"I never heard Umar ibn al-Khattab say about anything at all, 'I think such and such,' except that it was as he thought. While Umar ibn al-Khattab was sitting, a handsome man passed by him. He said to him, 'My guess is wrong, or you are still upon your religion from the Jahiliyyah, and you were their soothsayer.' He said, 'I have never seen anything like today, how a Muslim man is confronted.' Umar said, 'I adjure you to tell me.' He said, 'I was their soothsayer in the Jahiliyyah.' He said, 'Then what was the most amazing thing that came to you?' And he mentioned a long hadith without a chain."],[4495,"We traveled with Umar ibn al-Khattab on his last journey to Syria. When he approached it, he was informed that the plague was in it. It was said to him, 'O Commander of the Faithful, it is not appropriate for you to rush into it, just as if it had occurred while you were there, it would not be for you to leave it.' So he turned back toward Madinah. While we were traveling at night, he said to me, 'Turn off the road.' So he turned off and I turned off. He dismounted from his camel, then placed his head on the arm of his camel and slept, and I could not sleep. Then he went on saying to me, 'What is it with me and them? They turned me back from Syria.' Then he mounted, and I did not ask him about anything until I thought we were about to mingle with people. I said to him, 'Why did you say what you said when you woke from your sleep?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Seventy thousand will be resurrected from between the wall of Hims and the olives in the red earth, upon whom there is no reckoning.\" If Allah returns me from this journey of mine, I will carry my family and my people and my wealth until I settle in Hims.' He returned from that journey and was killed, ؓ ."],[4496,"Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: 'Take for the Muslims a place of emigration and a lodging for jihad.' Sa'd sent a man from the Ansar called al-Harith ibn Salama, and he chose for them the site of Kufa today. Sa'd settled there with the people and marked out our mosque and marked out the plots in it. Al-Sha'bi said: In Kufa there grew lavender, wormwood, oxeye daisies, and anemones. In the Jahiliyyah the Arabs used to call it Khadd al-Adhra (the virgin's cheek). They chose it and wrote to Umar ibn al-Khattab, and he wrote: 'Leave it.' So the people moved to Kufa. Al-Haytham ibn Adi is unreliable."],[4497,"Kufa is the dome of Islam and the land of affliction."],[4498,"His mistress proposed to dye his beard, so he said, \"I can only see you extinguishing my light, just as so-and-so extinguishes his light.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent in summarizing this."],[4499,"Umar ibn al-Khattab said one day to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, 'O best of people after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Abu Bakr said, 'If you say that, then indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The sun has not risen on a man better than Umar.\"'"],[4500,"The most perceptive of people are three: al-Aziz when he discerned about Yusuf and said to his wife, 'Make his stay comfortable'; the woman who saw Musa ﷺ and said to her father, 'O my father, hire him'; and Abu Bakr when he appointed Umar as successor."],[4501,"Umar was struck on Wednesday, four nights remaining in Dhul-Hijjah."],[4502,"He said on the pulpit: 'I saw in a dream as if a rooster pecked me three pecks. I said, \"A non-Arab.\" I have entrusted my affairs to these six with whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was pleased when he passed away: Uthman, Ali, Talha, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. Whoever is chosen as successor is the caliph.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4503,"Abu Lu'lu'a belonged to al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba, and he used to make millstones. Al-Mughira used to employ him every day for four dirhams. Abu Lu'lu'a met Umar and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, al-Mughira has increased my burden. Speak to him to lighten it for me.' Umar said to him, 'Fear Allah and treat your master well.' He said, and Umar intended to meet al-Mughira and speak to him about lightening it. Abu Lu'lu'a became angry, and his name was Fayruz and he was a Christian. He said, 'His justice encompasses all people except me.' He became angry and resolved to kill him. He made a dagger with two heads, sharpened it, and poisoned it. Umar said the takbir. Umar would not say the takbir when the prayer was established until he spoke and said, 'Straighten your rows.' He came and stood in the row opposite him, next to Umar, in the dawn prayer. When the prayer was established, Umar spoke and said, 'Straighten your rows,' then said the takbir. When he said the takbir, he stabbed him in his shoulder, stabbed him in another place, and stabbed him in his side. Umar fell. He also stabbed thirteen men with him: seven of them recovered and six of them died. Umar was carried away, and the people were in commotion until the sun almost rose. Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf called out, 'O people, the prayer, the prayer!' They rushed to the prayer. Abd al-Rahman went forward and led them in prayer, reciting the two shortest surahs in the Quran. When he finished, the people turned to Umar ibn al-Khattab. He called for a drink to see the extent of his wound. Nabidh was brought and he drank it, and it came out of his wound, and it was not known whether it was blood or nabidh. Then he called for milk and it was brought and he drank it, and it came out of his wound. They said, 'No harm upon you, O Commander of the Faithful.' He said, 'If being killed is harm, then I have been killed.'"],[4504,"From Mina in the last Hajj, he made his camel kneel at al-Batha, then he gathered a heap of sand at al-Batha, then threw over it a piece of his cloak, then lay down on his back and stretched his hands toward the sky and said, 'O Allah, my age has advanced, my strength has weakened, and my flock has spread. So take me to You without being negligent or wasteful.' Then he arrived in Dhul-Hijjah and addressed the people, saying, 'O people, I have established for you the sunnahs and ordained for you the obligations, and I have left you upon the clear path,' and he struck one hand upon the other, 'unless you turn the people right and left.' Dhul-Hijjah had not ended before Umar was killed. And I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib say, 'Abu Lu'lu'a, who killed Umar, stabbed twelve men along with Umar: six of them died and six recovered. He had a knife with two ends, and he stabbed himself with it and killed himself.'"],[4505,"Umar lived three days after he was stabbed, then he died, so he was washed and shrouded."],[4506,"He was stabbed, so I said, “Rejoice in Paradise, O Commander of the Faithful. You embraced Islam when the people disbelieved, and you waged jihad with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the people let him down, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while he was pleased with you, and not two men differed concerning your caliphate, and you have been killed as a martyr.” He said, “Repeat that to me,” so I repeated it to him. Then he said, “By Allah, besides whom there is no god, if I had whatever is on the earth of yellow and white, I would ransom myself with it from the terror of the rising.”"],[4507,"that the funeral prayer for Umar was held in the mosque, and Suhayb ؓ led the prayer."],[4508,"When Umar was killed, Ali and Uthman hastened to pray over him, but Suhayb said to them, “Leave that to me, for I have been entrusted with more of your affair than the prayer over Umar, and I lead you in the prescribed prayer.” So Suhayb prayed over him."],[4509,"Umar performed Hajj with the people for ten consecutive years, one of them during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and nine during his own caliphate, and he was buried beside Abu Bakr in Aisha's house. His caliphate lasted ten years, five months, and twenty-nine days."],[4510,"He was stabbed, so he said to Abdullah, “Go to Aisha and convey my greetings to her, and say that Umar says to you: If it does not harm you or constrain you, then I would love to be buried with my two companions. But if that harms you or would be constraining for you, then by my life, there have been buried in this Baqi from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the mothers of the believers those who are better than Umar.” The messenger came to her, and she said, “That does not harm me or constrain me.” He said, “Then bury me with them.”"],[4511,"I looked into the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar from Aisha's room, and I saw red pebbles on it."],[4512,"Umar passed away at the age of sixty-three years."],[4513,"Umar was a fortified fortress into which Islam entered and from which it did not leave. But when Umar was struck, the fortress was breached, and now Islam leaves from it and does not enter it. When the righteous are mentioned, then come quickly with Umar."],[4514,"Ali entered upon Umar while he was shrouded and said, “May Allah have mercy on you.” Then he said, “There is no one among the people more beloved to me that I meet Allah with what is in his record than this shrouded one.”"],[4515,"A voice was heard at Mount Tabalah when Umar b. al-Khattab was killed, reciting poetry [al-tawil meter]: “Let whoever is weeping weep over Islam, for they are on the verge of destruction and the era has grown old. The world has turned away and its good has turned away, and it has wearied those who were certain of the promise.” They looked, but they saw nothing."],[4516,"(Poetry) [al-khafif meter]: “Weep, O eye, with tears and wailing, do not tire over the imam, the steadfast. Fate has bereaved us of the knight renowned on the day of battle and rebuke, the protector of the faith and the helper against time, the rain of the distressed and the afflicted. Say to the people of hardship and misery: die, since fate has given us the cup of annihilation.” Atikah also said [al-tawil meter]: “Fayruz bereaved me—may his fortune not flow—of a white one, a follower of the Book, repentant, kind to the near, harsh to the enemies, a brother of trust in calamities, responsive. Whenever he says something, his action does not belie his word, quick to good deeds and not frowning.” “The hadith of al-Thawri is included in the two Sahihs, but I have cited here some phrases with sound chains that are beneficial and rare.”"],[4517,"Umar said to the members of the shura, “How excellent they are! If they were to entrust it to the little bald one, how he would carry them upon the truth, even if the sword were held to his neck.” I said, “You know that of him and yet you would not appoint him?” He said, “If I appoint a successor, then one better than me appointed a successor, and if I leave it, then one better than me left it.”"],[4518,"I heard 'Ali on the Day of the Camel saying: 'O Allah, I disavow to You the blood of 'Uthman. My mind was overwhelmed the day 'Uthman was killed, and my soul rejected it. They came to me for the pledge of allegiance, so I said: By Allah, I would be ashamed before Allah to pledge allegiance to a people who killed a man about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Should I not feel shy before one of whom the angels feel shy?\" And I would be ashamed before Allah to pledge allegiance while 'Uthman lies slain on the ground, not yet buried.' So they went away. When he was buried, the people returned and asked me for the pledge, so I said: 'O Allah, I am apprehensive about what I am undertaking.' Then resolve came, and I pledged allegiance. When they said, 'O Amir al-Mu'minin,' it was as if my heart was split, and I said: 'O Allah, take from me for 'Uthman until You are pleased.'\""],[4519,"'Uthman b. 'Affan b. Abi al-'As b. Umayyah b. 'Abd Shams b. 'Abd Manaf b. Qusayy b. Kilab. The mother of 'Uthman was Arwa bt. Kariz, and the mother of Arwa was Umm Hakim, who is al-Bayda', the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They differed about the kunyah of 'Uthman: it was said Abu 'Abd Allah, and it was said Abu 'Amr. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4520,"I heard Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah say: \"'Uthman b. 'Affan was given the kunyah Abu 'Amr and Abu 'Abd Allah. He was killed in Dhu al-Hijjah in the year thirty-five.\""],[4521,"\"'Uthman b. 'Affan was killed at the age of ninety, or eighty-eight.\""],[4522,"'Uthman b. 'Affan was killed on Friday, when twelve days remained of Dhu al-Hijjah, in the year thirty-five. His caliphate lasted twelve years."],[4523,"\"I saw 'Uthman b. 'Affan on the pulpit on Friday wearing a thick Adani waist-wrapper worth four or five dirhams and a Kufan dyed cloak. He was muscular, with a long beard and a handsome face.\""],[4524,"The first stone the Prophet ﷺ carried for building the mosque; then Abu Bakr carried another stone; then 'Uthman carried another stone. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you not see how these are helping you?' He said: \"O 'A'ishah, these are the caliphs after me.\""],[4525,"\"The pledge of allegiance to 'Uthman took place on Monday, ten of Muharram, in the year twenty-four.\""],[4526,"The pledge of allegiance to 'Uthman came. 'Abd Allah said: \"I do not fail to prefer our highest one of great merit.\""],[4527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Let every man among you rise to his peer.\" The Prophet ﷺ rose to 'Uthman, embraced him, and said: \"You are my friend in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[4528,"I witnessed 'Uthman on the day he was besieged, in the place of the funerals. He said: \"I adjure you by Allah, O Talhah, do you remember the day when you and I were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in such-and-such a place, and there was no one with him from his Companions except me and you? He said to you: 'O Talhah, there is no prophet but he has a companion from his nation with him in Paradise, and 'Uthman is my companion and with me in Paradise.'\" Talhah said: \"O Allah, yes.\" He said: \"Then Talhah left.\""],[4529,"Some of the people said to him: \"This one now claims that you fell into error regarding 'Uthman.\" He said: \"That is what he says.\" He said: \"Bring the man back to me.\" Then he said: \"Did you understand what I said to you?\" He said: \"Yes. I asked you whether 'Uthman witnessed the Pledge of al-Ridwan, and you said no. I asked you whether he witnessed Badr, and you said no. I asked you whether he was among those whom Satan caused to slip, and you said yes.\" He said: \"As for the Pledge of al-Ridwan, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and said: 'Uthman has gone on an errand for Allah and His Messenger,' and he allotted a share for him, but did not allot for any other absent person. As for those who turned away on the day the two hosts met, Satan only caused them to slip because of some of what they had earned, but Allah has pardoned them. Indeed, Allah is Forgiving, Forbearing.\""],[4530,"\"One day you will come upon a man wrapped in a cloak, giving allegiance to the people, from the people of Paradise.\" So I came upon Uthman, and he was wrapped in a striped cloak, giving allegiance to the people."],[4531,"A man asked the Prophet ﷺ, \"Is there lightning in Paradise?\" He said, \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, Uthman will move from one abode to another and Paradise will flash with lightning for him.\" If this Husayn b. Ubayd Allah preserved it from Abd al-Aziz b. Abi Hazim, then it is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, though they did not include it. This is the subject."],[4532,"Musa, Muhammad, and Ibrahim, the sons of Uqba, narrated to us. They said: The brother of our mother, Abu Hasana, narrated to us. He said: I witnessed Abu Hurayra while Uthman was besieged in the house, and I sought his permission to speak. Abu Hurayra said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"There will be a trial and dissension, or dissension and trial.\" He said: We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us?\" He said, \"Cling to the commander and his companions,\" and he gestured toward Uthman."],[4533,"Uthman b. Affan dozed off on the day he was killed, then woke up and said, \"Were it not that people would say Uthman wished for the trial, I would tell you.\" He said: We said, \"May Allah set you right, tell us, for we will not say what people say.\" He said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this dream of mine, and he said, 'You will attend the Friday prayer with us.'\""],[4534,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Call for me, or would that I had with me, a man from my companions.\" She said: I said, \"Abu Bakr?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"Umar?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"Your cousin Ali?\" He said, \"No.\" I said, \"Then Uthman?\" He said, \"Yes.\" She said: Uthman came, and he said, \"Arise.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ began whispering to Uthman, and Uthman's color changed. He said: When the day of the house came, we said, \"Will you not fight?\" He said, \"No, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entrusted me with a matter, and I will patiently endure it.\""],[4535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Uthman, \"Allah will clothe you with a shirt, and if the hypocrites want you to take it off, do not take it off.\""],[4537,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, the people of Makkah began bringing their children, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wipe their heads and supplicate for them. My father brought me to him, and I was perfumed with khaluq. He did not wipe my head, nor touch me, and nothing prevented him from that except that my mother had perfumed me with khaluq, so he did not touch me because of the khaluq.\" Ahmad b. Hanbal said: \"It has been narrated that he embraced Islam on that day, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ found him repulsive and did not touch him or supplicate for him. Khaluq does not prevent supplication, nor is there any fault in a child for the action of another, but he was deprived of the blessing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ due to Allah's prior knowledge of him, and Allah knows best.\""],[4538,"Uthman b. Affan appointed al-Walid b. Uqba b. Abi Mu'ayt, and he was his maternal brother, over Kufa and its land, while Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas was there. He came to Sa'd and seated him with him, not knowing his purpose. Then he said, \"Abu Wahb, what brought you?\" He said, \"I have come as an agent.\" He said, \"Over what?\" He said, \"Over your post.\" He said, \"By Allah, I do not know whether I have become foolish after you or you have become foolish after me.\" He said, \"By Allah, neither have I become foolish after you nor have you become foolish after me, but the people have favored themselves over you with their authority.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4539,"\"Whoever is saved from three things is saved.\" They said, \"What are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"My death, the killing of a caliph who steadfastly upholds the truth and gives it, and from the Dajjal.\""],[4540,"\"The mill of Islam will turn after thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it is the path of those who perished; and if their religion remains, it will endure for seventy.\" Umar said, \"O Prophet of Allah, with what has passed or with what remains?\" He said, \"No, rather with what remains.\""],[4541,"\"Al-Walid b. Uqba b. Abi Mu'ayt b. Amr b. Umayya b. Abd Shams, and he was Uthman's maternal brother; their mother was Arwa bt. Kurayz b. Rabi'a b. Abd Shams, and her mother was Umm Hakim al-Bayda' bt. Abd al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ killed Uqba b. Abi Mu'ayt on his return, and al-Walid was a man during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was given the kunya Abu Wahb.\""],[4542,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A righteous man was shown tonight that Abu Bakr was attached to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Umar was attached to Abu Bakr, and Uthman was attached to Umar.\" When we rose from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we said, \"As for the righteous man, he is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; and as for what was mentioned of their being attached to one another, they are the guardians of this matter with which Allah sent His Prophet ﷺ.\" Al-Darimi said: I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: Muhammad b. Harb with the chain of this hadith, while the people narrate it from al-Zuhri as mursal; it is only Amr b. Aban, and Aban b. Uthman did not have a son called Amr."],[4543,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention a trial and he acknowledged it. A veiled man wrapped in a garment passed by him, and he said, \"This one is upon guidance on that day.\" So I went up to him and behold, it was Uthman b. Affan. I turned to him with his face and said, \"Is it this one?\" He said, \"Yes.\""],[4544,"Uthman came to the Prophet ﷺ with a thousand dinars when he was equipping the army of hardship, and Uthman poured them into the Prophet's ﷺ lap. He said, \"The Prophet ﷺ began turning them over and saying, 'What harm can come to Uthman after what he has done today?' He said it repeatedly.\""],[4545,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ in a dream last night, and he said, 'O Uthman, break your fast with us.' So Uthman woke up fasting, and he was killed that same day.\""],[4546,"\"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Uthman b. Affan approached. When he drew near, he said, 'O Uthman, you will be killed while reciting Surat al-Baqarah, and your blood will fall upon {Allah will suffice you against them, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing} [al-Baqarah: 137]. You will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as a commander over every forsaken one, envied by the people of the east and the west, and you will intercede for the number of Rabi'ah and Mudar.'\""],[4547,"\"I witnessed Ali on the Day of the Camel saying: 'O Allah, I declare my innocence to You from the blood of Uthman. My mind was overwhelmed on the day Uthman was killed, and I disapproved of myself. They wanted me to accept allegiance, but I said: By Allah, I would be ashamed before Allah to pledge allegiance to a people who killed a man about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Should I not be shy of one before whom the angels are shy?\" And I am ashamed before Allah to pledge allegiance while Uthman lies slain on the ground, not yet buried.' So they left. When he was buried, the people returned to me and asked me for allegiance. I said: 'O Allah, I am apprehensive about what I am undertaking.' Then a firm resolve came, and I pledged allegiance. When they said, 'O Commander of the Faithful,' it was as if my heart was shattered. I said: 'O Allah, take from me for Uthman until You are pleased.'\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4548,"\"On the Day of the Camel, I went out to look at the slain. Ali, al-Hasan b. Ali, Ammar b. Yasir, Muhammad b. Abi Bakr, and Zayd b. Suhan stood up and went around among the slain. Al-Hasan b. Ali saw a slain man lying face down. He turned him onto his back, then cried out and said, 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. Quraysh rejoiced, by Allah.' His father said to him, 'Who is he, my son?' He said, 'Muhammad b. Talha b. Ubayd Allah.' He said, 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. By Allah, he was a righteous young man.' Then he sat down gloomy and sad. Al-Hasan said to him, 'O father, I had forbidden you from this march, but so-and-so and so-and-so overcame your judgment.' He said, 'That was so, my son. I wish I had died twenty years before this.' Muhammad b. Hatib said: I stood up and said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, we are returning to Madinah and people will ask us about Uthman. What do you say about him?' Then Ammar b. Yasir and Muhammad b. Abi Bakr spoke, saying this and that. Ali said to them, 'O Ammar and O Muhammad, you say that Uthman was self-seeking and mismanaged authority, and you punished him, by Allah, but you did wrong in the punishment. You will come before a just Judge who will judge between you.' Then he said, 'O Muhammad b. Hatib, when you arrive in Madinah and are asked about Uthman, say: By Allah, he was among those who believed and did righteous deeds, then feared and believed, then feared and did good. And Allah loves the doers of good. And upon Allah let the believers rely.'\""],[4549,"\"To proceed: this authority—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not leave us any covenant regarding it whose trace is to be followed, but we saw it as our own matter. Abu Bakr was appointed successor, and he established and remained upright. Then Umar was appointed successor, and he established and remained upright. Then time struck with its full weight.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[4550,"\"Eighty participants of Badr and two hundred fifty of those who pledged allegiance under the tree fought alongside Ali at Siffin.\""],[4551,"\"He fought alongside Ali at Siffin.\""],[4552,"\"I went to Hudhayfah in al-Mada'in during the nights when the people marched against Uthman. He said, 'O my son, what did your people do?' I said, 'Which of their conditions do you ask about?' He said, 'Who among them went out against this man?' I named for him a man who had gone out. He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever separates from the community and takes up leadership will meet Allah with no argument in his favor.\"\""],[4553,"\"It would not please me to take my sword in killing Uthman even if I had the world and all it contains.\""],[4554,"Allah, Exalted is He, {And We shall remove whatever rancor is in their breasts, as brothers, on couches facing one another} [al-Hijr: 47]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4555,"that Umm Habiba bt. Abi Sufyan, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sent a messenger to Abdullah b. Abi Rabi'a, the brother of Ayyash b. Abi Rabi'a, informing him of the killing of Uthman, and she sent to him his shirt in which he was killed and his garments stained with his blood. When the messenger reached him, he went out to the people, ascended the minbar, informed them of his killing, spread his shirt on the minbar, wept, and the people wept with him, and he began to recite: [al-tawil] 'A matter came to me in which there is grief for the people, and in it long weeping for the eyes; in it is the enjoyment of life with humiliation, and in it a firm cutting off of noses. The calamity of the Commander of the Faithful, and for these the mountain peaks would shift. A band in Madinah fell upon him; two parties among them: a killer and a deserter. I shall weep for Abu Amr with every Indian sword and with white ones that have a ringing among the armored. And no sleep until the people are imprisoned by the spears, and the rancor of the misguided people is healed. I am not staying as long as I live in a town where I drag a hem while you are slain.'\" He said: So he went out with those with him, and when he drew near Makkah he fell from his mount and died. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[4556,"And he said to the people of the house: Do not kill them; may Allah pardon every person who did not fight. So how have you seen Allah pour enmity and hatred upon them after mutual affection? And how have you seen good turn away from people after him like the turning away of the pregnant winds?\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4557,"that he was asked about Uthman: What was on the stone of his ring? He said: Indeed, on the stone of his ring, out of the sincerity of his intention, was: O Allah, make me live happy and make me die as a martyr. By Allah, he lived happy and died a martyr."],[4558,"Ali said: \"Be quiet, or be silent, for by Allah, you will not ask me about anything but that I will inform you.\" Zayd said: I adjure you by Allah, did you kill Uthman? Ali bowed his head for a while, then said: \"By the One who split the grain and created the soul, I did not kill him, nor did I order his killing.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4559,"And al-Walid b. Uqba said: [al-tawil] \"Indeed, the best of people after their Prophet is the one killed by the Tujibi who came from Egypt,\" meaning by the Tujibi the killer of Uthman. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4560,"that he proposed to Umar for his daughter, and he rejected him. That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and when Umar came to him, he said: \"O Umar, shall I not direct you to a son-in-law better for you than Uthman, and direct Uthman to one better for him than you?\" He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"Marry me to your daughter, and I will marry Uthman to my daughter.\""],[4561,"Uthman b. Affan bought Paradise from the Prophet ﷺ twice: the sale of the right when he dug the well of Ma'una, and when he equipped the army of hardship. \"The chain is sahih, but they did not record it.\" Isa b. al-Musayyab was weakened by Abu Dawud and others."],[4562,"Ali wanted to march to Syria to Siffin, and the Nakha' gathered until they entered upon al-Ashtar in his house. He said: \"Is there in the house anyone but a Nakha'i?\" They said: No. He said: \"This ummah deliberately went to the best of its people and killed him, meaning Uthman. We fought the people of Basra on the basis of a pledge about which we interpreted, and you are marching to a people over whom we have no pledge. Let every man consider where he places his sword.\""],[4563,"I heard Ahmad b. Hanbal say: \"No virtues have come for any of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ like what has come for Ali b. Abi Talib.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4564,"Fatima bt. Asad b. Hashim was the first Hashimite woman born of a Hashimite, and she had a great standing among the notables during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She died during the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he prayed over her. Ali's name was Asad, and therefore he says: [al-rajaz] \"I am the one whom my mother named Haydara.\""],[4565,"We were sitting with Sa'id b. al-Musayyib when Ali b. al-Husayn passed by us, and I have never seen a Hashimite more devoted to Allah than him. Sa'id b. al-Musayyib stood up to him, and we stood with him. We greeted him, and he returned our greeting. Sa'id said to him: O Abu Muhammad, tell us about Fatima bt. Asad b. Hashim, the mother of Ali b. Abi Talib. He said: Yes, my father told me; he said: I heard the Commander of the Faithful Ali b. Abi Talib say: When Fatima bt. Asad b. Hashim died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shrouded her in his shirt, prayed over her, and said seventy takbirat over her. He descended into her grave and began gesturing in the corners of the grave as if widening it and leveling it for her. He came out of her grave with his eyes flowing with tears, and he threw dust into her grave. When he left, Umar b. al-Khattab said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I saw you do for this woman something you have not done for anyone. He said: \"O Umar, this woman was my mother who gave birth to me. Abu Talib used to prepare food, and he would have a feast, and he would gather us for his food, and this woman would set aside from all of it a share for me, and I would return to it. Jibril ﷺ informed me from my Lord ﷻ that she is among the people of Paradise, and Jibril ﷺ informed me that Allah Almighty commanded seventy thousand angels to pray over her.\""],[4566,"Mu'awiya said to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas: What prevents you from reviling the son of Abi Talib? He said: I do not revile him as long as I remember three things that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, for one of them would be dearer to me than red camels. Mu'awiya said to him: What are they, O Abu Ishaq? He said: I do not revile him as long as I remember when the revelation descended upon him, and he took Ali, his two sons, and Fatima, and brought them under his garment, then said: \"My Lord, these are the people of my household.\" And I do not revile him as long as I remember when he left him behind in the campaign of Tabuk, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ undertook. Ali said to him: You have left me with the children and women. He said: \"Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophethood after me?\" And I do not revile him as long as I remember the day of Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I will surely give this banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah will grant victory through his hands.\" We stretched our necks toward the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Where is Ali?\" They said: He has sore eyes. He said: \"Call him.\" They called him, and he spat in his face, then gave him the banner, and Allah granted victory through him. He said: By Allah, Mu'awiya did not mention him with a single letter until he left Madinah."],[4567,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from the Farewell Pilgrimage and camped at Ghadir Khumm, he ordered for a pulpit to be set up. Then he said, 'It seems that I have been called, and I have responded. I have left among you two weighty things: the Book of Allah, the Almighty and my progeny. Look carefully at how you will treat them after me, for they will never separate until they meet me at the Pool.' The narration is abbreviated by Al-Dhahabi.\""],[4568,"That he heard Zayd b. Arqam say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ halted between Makkah and Madinah by five large trees. The people swept what was beneath the trees. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went in the evening and prayed, then stood as a preacher, praised Allah and extolled Him, and reminded and exhorted. He said whatever Allah willed that he say, then said, \"O people, I am leaving among you two matters; you will not go astray if you follow them: the Book of Allah and my Household, my progeny.\" It was not related by Muhammad b. Salama b. Kuhayl, and al-Sa'di deemed it weak."],[4569,"I fought along with ʿAlī to Yemen and I sensed estrangement from him. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned ʿAlī and talked down about him. I then saw the [color] on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change and he said, \"O Buraydah, am I not more prefered to the believers than themselves?\" I said, \"Yes O Messenger of Allah.\" He then said, \"For whomever I am his mawlá (leader), then ʿAlī is his mawlá.\" and he mentioned the ḥadīth.[1]"],[4570,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an army and he put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of it. He left on the expedition and he entered upon a female slave. So four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ scolded him, and they made a pact saying: \"[If] we meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ we will inform him of what 'Ali did.\" When the Muslims returned from the journey, they would begin with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and give him Salam, then they would go to their homes. So when the expedition arrived, they gave Salam to the Prophet ﷺ, and one of the four stood saying: \"O Messenger of Allah! Do you see that 'Ali bin Abi Talib did such and such.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him. Then the second one stood and said as he said, and he turned away from him. Then the third stood before him, and said as he said, and he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said as they had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ faced him, and the anger was visible on his face, he said: \"What do you want from 'Ali?! What do you want from 'Ali?! What do you want from 'Ali?! Indeed 'Ali is from me, and I am from him, and he is the ally of every believer after me.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3712)"],[4571,"From him, al-Dhahabi in the Talkhis."],[4572,"Ali became Muslim when he was ten or sixteen years old. This chain of transmission is more appropriate than the first, and I only presented that because I have a higher chain in it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4573,"Ali had four qualities that no one else had: he was the first Arab and non-Arab to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he was the one whose banner was with him in every battle; he was the one who stood firm with him on the day of al-Mihras; and he was the one who washed him and placed him in his grave. In it is Zakariyya b. Yahya al-Waqqar, and he is suspect."],[4574,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed the banner to Ali on the day of Badr when he was twenty years old."],[4575,"I am the servant of Allah and the brother of His Messenger, and I am the greatest truthful one. No one after me will say it except a liar. I prayed before the people by seven years, before anyone of this ummah worshipped Him."],[4576,"I worshipped Allah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for seven years before anyone of this ummah worshipped Him. And this is false."],[4577,"Abu Dharr and Nu'aym, the paternal cousin of Abu Dharr, set out, and I was with them, seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was concealed in the mountain. Abu Dharr said, \"O Muhammad, we have come to you to hear what you say and to what you call.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I say: there is no god but Allah, and I am the Messenger of Allah.\" Abu Dharr and his companion believed in him, and I believed in him. Ali was on an errand for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, to which he had sent him. Revelation came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Monday, and Ali prayed on Tuesday. \"Sahih al-isnad, but they did not record it.\" Sahih."],[4578,"The Prophet ﷺ was called to prophethood on Monday, and Ali became Muslim on Tuesday. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4579,"Ali was killed on Friday, seventeen nights having passed of the month of Ramadan, in the year forty. His caliphate lasted five years except three months. Abd al-Rahman b. Muljam al-Muradi killed him. On the day he was killed, he was sixty-three or sixty-four years old. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4580,"I heard Abu Bakr b. Abi Shayba say: Ali b. Abi Talib governed for five years and was killed in the year forty of the Hijrah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he was sixty-three years old. He was killed on Friday, the twenty-first of the month of Ramadan, and he died on Sunday and was buried in Kufa. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4581,"That he visited Ali during an illness he complained of. He said: I said to him, \"We have feared for you, O Commander of the Faithful, in this illness of yours.\" He said, \"But I, by Allah, have not feared for myself from it, because I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the truthful and the believed, say: 'You will be struck a blow here and a blow here'—and he pointed to his temples—'and its blood will flow until your beard is dyed, and its perpetrator will be the most wretched of them, just as the one who hamstrung the she-camel was the most wretched of Thamud.'\""],[4582,"I came to Damascus intending to go on a military expedition, so I went to 'Abd al-Malik to greet him. I found him in a dome on a bed near the standing person, and beneath him were two rows. I greeted him and sat down. He said to me, 'O Ibn Shihāb, do you know what was in Jerusalem on the morning 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib was killed?' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Come.' I arose from behind the people until I came behind the dome. He turned his face toward me and leaned over me and said, 'What was it?' I said, 'No stone was lifted from Jerusalem except that blood was found beneath it.' He said, 'No one remains who knows this except me and you. Let no one hear it from you.' I did not narrate it until he died, and the report is mursal."],[4584,"'The millstone of Islam will turn for thirty-five or thirty-six years. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perish; but if their religion remains for them, then for seventy years.' 'Umar said, 'O Messenger of Allah, with what remains or with what has passed?' He said, 'With what remains.'"],[4585,"That 'Uthmān was buried, then allegiance was pledged to 'Alī on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ openly. The first to pledge allegiance to him was Ṭalḥah, and he said, 'This is a pledge that will be broken.'"],[4586,"When allegiance was pledged to 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib on the pulpit of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Khuzaymah ibn Thābit said while standing before the pulpit: \"[al-baḥr al-ṭawīl] If we pledge allegiance to 'Alī, then Abū Ḥasan suffices us from the turmoils we fear. We found him the most worthy of people for the people, for he is the most knowledgeable of Quraysh in the Book and the Sunnahs. And Quraysh cannot stir his dust when he runs one day on the lean, stout camels. In him is all the good that is in them, and not in them is all the good that is in him of excellence.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[4587,"When the pledge of allegiance to 'Alī came to Ḥudhayfah, he said, 'I will not pledge allegiance after him except to one with a tilted neck or one cut short.'"],[4588,"I saw 'Alī on a worn-out saddle at al-Rabadhah, saying to al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, 'Why do you whimper like a slave girl? By Allah, I have turned this matter over and over, and I found no escape from fighting the people or disbelieving in what was revealed to Muḥammad ﷺ.' Al-Dhahabī omitted it from the Talkhīṣ due to its weakness."],[4589,"That while he was sitting with 'Abdullāh ibn 'Umar, a man from the people of Iraq came to him and said, 'O Abū 'Abd al-Raḥmān, by Allah, I have been eager to follow your way and imitate you in the matter of the division of the people, and to keep away from evil as much as I can. I recite a decisive verse from the Book of Allah that has taken hold of my heart, so tell me about it. What do you think of the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And if two factions among the believers fight, make peace between them. But if one of them transgresses against the other, then fight against the one that transgresses until it returns to the command of Allah. And if it returns, then make peace between them with justice and act equitably. Indeed, Allah loves those who act equitably.}?'"],[4590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me in a military detachment with some of his companions. A man from the Anṣār and I raced toward the enemy. I attacked a man, and when I approached him, he said 'Allāhu akbar,' so I thrust at him and killed him. I thought he only did that to protect his blood. When we returned, he preceded me to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, there is no horseman better than your horseman. We pursued a man, and he got to him before me, so he said Allāhu akbar, and that did not prevent him from killing him.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O Usāmah, what did you do today?' I said, 'I attacked a man, and he said Allāhu akbar, and I thought he only did that to protect his blood, so I killed him.' He said, 'How, after Allāhu akbar? Why did you not split open his heart?' I said, 'What did he say?' He kept saying to me that day, 'I will not fight a man who says Allāhu akbar,' from what he prohibited me, until I meet him ﷺ."],[4591,"Abū Aḥmad Muḥammad ibn Muḥammad al-Ḥāfiẓ narrated to us: Aḥmad ibn Ja'far ibn Naṣr narrated to us: Hārūn ibn al-Mughīrah narrated to us: 'Amr ibn Abī Qays narrated to us, from Ibrāhīm ibn Muhājir, from Ibrāhīm al-Nakha'ī, from Abū al-Sha'thā', from his uncle, from Usāmah ibn Zayd, and he mentioned the ḥadīth in a similar manner. Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[4592,"I heard Sa'd ibn Mālik when a man said to him, 'Indeed 'Alī criticizes you because you stayed behind from him.' Sa'd said, 'By Allah, it was an opinion I held, and my opinion was mistaken. 'Alī ibn Abī Ṭālib was given three things; if I had been given one of them, it would be more beloved to me than the world and all it contains. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him on the day of Ghadīr Khumm, after praising Allah and extolling Him: \"Do you know that I am closer to the believers than their own selves?\" We said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"O Allah, whoever I am his mawlā, then 'Alī is his mawlā. Befriend whoever befriends him and be hostile to whoever is hostile to him.\" And he was brought on the day of Khaybar while he was suffering from ophthalmia and could hardly see. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have ophthalmia.\" So he spat in his eyes and supplicated for him, and he did not suffer from ophthalmia until he was killed, and Khaybar was conquered at his hands. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ expelled his uncle al-'Abbās and others from the mosque, so al-'Abbās said to him, \"You expel us while we are your close relatives and uncles, and you let 'Alī live in it?\" He said, \"It is not I who expelled you and settled him, but Allah expelled you and settled him.\"' Al-Ḥākim remained silent about its authentication."],[4593,"'When 'Uthmān was killed and allegiance was pledged to 'Alī, Abū Mūsā gave a sermon while he was in charge of Kufa and forbade the people from fighting and entering into the turmoil. So 'Alī dismissed him from Kufa from Dhū Qār and sent to him 'Ammār ibn Yāsir and al-Ḥasan ibn 'Alī. They dismissed him and appointed Qaraẓah ibn Ka'b, who remained governor until 'Alī arrived from Basra after some months, and he dismissed him when he arrived. When he marched to Ṣiffīn, he appointed 'Uqbah ibn 'Amr, Abū Mas'ūd al-Anṣārī, as his deputy when he arrived from Ṣiffīn.' Al-Haytham ibn 'Adī is abandoned."],[4594,"Abū Mūsā al-Ash'arī and Abū Mas'ūd al-Badrī entered upon 'Ammār while he was urging the people to mobilize. They said to him, 'We have not seen from you, since you embraced Islam, any matter more hateful to us than your hastening in this affair.' 'Ammār said, 'I have not seen from you two, since you embraced Islam, any matter more hateful to me than your delaying in this affair.' He said, 'Then 'Ammār clothed each of them with a full suit, and he went out to the Friday prayer.' Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[4595,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what should I do when the worshippers differ?' He said, 'Take your sword to the Harrah and strike it with it, then enter your house until a decreeing death comes to you or a sinning hand.'"],[4596,"He gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a sword from Najran. When he came to him, he gave it to Muhammad b. Maslamah and said, 'Strive with this in the path of Allah. When the necks of people differ, strike the rock with it, then enter your house, and be like a discarded saddlecloth until a sinning hand kills you or a decreeing death comes to you.'"],[4597,"I heard al-Hasan say: Talhah and al-Zubayr came to Basrah, so the people said to them, 'What brought you?' They said, 'We seek the blood of Uthman.' Al-Hasan said, 'Glory be to Allah! Did the people not have any intellects to say, \"By Allah, none killed Uthman but you\"?' He said, then when Ali came to Kufah, and the people had no intellects to say, 'O man, we indeed, by Allah, did not guarantee you.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[4598,"I saw Talhah, and the most beloved of gatherings to him was the emptiest of them, and he was striking his beard against his chest. He said, so I said to him, 'O Abu Muhammad, I see you, and the most beloved of gatherings to you is the emptiest of them, while you are striking your beard against your chest. If you dislike this affair, then leave it, for no one compels you to it.' He said, 'O Alqamah b. Waqqas, do not blame me. Yesterday we were one hand against those besides us, but today we have become two mountains of iron, one of us crawling toward the other.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[4599,"Allah protected me by something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Khosrow died, he said, 'Whom did they appoint as successor?' They said, 'His daughter.' He said, 'A people will never succeed who entrust their affairs to a woman.' He said, when Aishah came, I remembered the statement of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Allah protected me by it. It is upon the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4600,"'I wish I had been bereaved of ten like al-Harith b. Hisham and that I had not undertaken my march with Ibn al-Zubayr.'"],[4601,"The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the departure of one of the Mothers of the Believers, so Aishah laughed. He said, 'Look, O Humayra, that you are not the one.' Then he turned to Ali and said, 'If you are given charge of any of her affairs, be gentle with her.' Abd al-Jabbar: They did not narrate from him."],[4602,"When Ali marched to Basrah, he entered upon Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, to bid her farewell. She said, 'Go in Allah's protection and under His care. By Allah, you are upon the truth and the truth is with you. Were it not that I hate to disobey Allah and His Messenger, for he commanded us ﷺ to remain in our houses, I would have marched with you. But by Allah, I will send with you someone better in my sight and dearer to me than myself, my son Umar.' These three hadiths are all authentic upon the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include them. Upon the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4603,"Umar said, 'Sit in your house, for you have fought alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, he repeated that to him, so Umar said to him on the third time or the one after it, 'Stay in your house. By Allah, I find at the edge of Madinah that you and your companions would go out and corrupt the companions of Muhammad ﷺ.' Sahih."],[4604,"When Aisha reached some of the houses of the Bani 'Amir, the dogs barked at her. She asked, \"What water is this?\" They said, \"It is Al-Hawab.\" Aisha said, \"I think I should go back.\" Az-Zubair said, \"No, do not turn back, and the people would see you and Allah will correct the matter between them.\" Aisha said, \"I think I should go back.\" I heard Allah's Messenger ﷺ saying, \"How (regrettable) is the situation of one of you who is startled by the barking of a dog belonging to Al-Hawab (tribe).\" Adh-Dhahabi remained silent about a conclusion to this narration."],[4605,"When we left Makkah, the daughter of Hamzah followed us, calling out, 'O uncle, O uncle.' So I took her by the hand and handed her to Fatimah, saying, 'Take care of your cousin.' When we arrived in Madinah, Zayd, Ja'far, and I disputed about her. I said, 'I took her and she is my cousin.' Zayd said, 'She is my brother's daughter.' Ja'far said, 'She is my cousin and her maternal aunt is with me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ja'far, 'You resemble me in appearance and character,' and to Zayd, 'You are our brother and our ally,' and to me, 'You are from me and I am from you. Give her to her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is like a mother.' I said, 'Will you not marry her, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'"],[4606,"I said, 'Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being reviled among you?' I said, 'I seek refuge in Allah,' or 'Glory be to Allah,' or something like that. She said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever reviles Ali has reviled me.\"'"],[4607,"I heard Abu Abdullah al-Jadali say: I performed Hajj as a boy, and I passed by Madinah, and the people were a single neck, so I followed them. They entered upon Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and I heard her say, 'O Shabib b. Rib'i,' and a rough, coarse man answered her, 'At your service, O mother.' She said, 'Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reviled in your gathering?' He said, 'How could that be?' She said, 'Ali b. Abi Talib.' He said, 'We say things desiring the goods of this world.' She said, 'For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Whoever reviles Ali has reviled me, and whoever reviles me has reviled Allah the Exalted.\"' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[4608,"«Whoever obeys me has obeyed God, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed God; and whoever obeys Ali has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys Ali has disobeyed me.»"],[4609,"O enemy of God, you have harmed the Messenger of God ﷺ. {Indeed, those who harm God and His Messenger – God has cursed them in this world and the Hereafter, and has prepared for them a humiliating punishment.} [al-Ahzab 57]. Had the Messenger of God ﷺ been alive, you would have harmed him."],[4610,"\"We went with Ali to Yemen, and his long journey tired me until I found it in myself. When I arrived, I expressed my complaint to him in the mosque until the messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed. I entered the mosque one morning and the messenger of Allah ﷺ was with some of his companions. When he saw me, he fixed his gaze on me and said, 'He says he has a complaint against me.' So I sought refuge in Allah from causing harm to you, O Messenger of Allah. He said, 'Indeed, whoever harms Ali has harmed me.'\""],[4611,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to Ali, «You will clarify for my community what they differ about after me.»"],[4612,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ when his sandal strap broke. Ali lagged behind to mend it, and he walked a little, then said: «Indeed, among you is one who will fight for the interpretation of the Quran just as I fought for its revelation.» The people craned their necks for it, and among them were Abu Bakr and Umar. Abu Bakr said, \"Is it I?\" He said, «No.» Umar said, \"Is it I?\" He said, «No, but it is the mender of the sandal,» meaning Ali. So we went to him and gave him the good news, but he did not raise his head, as if he had already heard it from the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[4613,"The Messenger of God ﷺ called me and said, «O Ali, in you there is a likeness of Jesus (peace and blessings be upon him): the Jews hated him until they slandered his mother, and the Christians loved him until they placed him in a station that was not his.» He said, and Ali said, «Indeed, there will perish concerning me two [types]: a loving exaggerator who attributes to me what is not in me, and a hating fabricator whose hatred of me drives him to slander me. Indeed, I am not a prophet, and revelation does not come to me, but I act according to the Book of God and the Sunnah of His Prophet ﷺ as much as I am able. Whatever I command you of obedience to God Almighty, then obedience to me is incumbent upon you, whether you like it or dislike it; and whatever I or others command you of disobedience to God, then there is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to God ﷻ. Obedience is only in what is right.» «The chain is authentic, but they did not record it.» Al-Hakam b. Abdul-Malik: Ibn Ma'in declared him weak."],[4614,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, «O Ali, you have a treasure in Paradise, and you are its two-horned one. Do not follow a glance with another glance, for the first is yours and the second is not yours.»"],[4615,"«O Ali, whoever separates from me has separated from God, and whoever separates from you, O Ali, has separated from me.»"],[4616,"That the Prophet ﷺ said, «I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs.»"],[4617,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Pray for me, the leader of the Arabs.\" So I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, aren't you the leader of the Arabs?\" He said, \"I am the leader of the offspring of Adam, and Ali is the leader of the Arabs.\""],[4618,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said, «Summon for me the master of the Arabs.» Aisha said, \"Are you not the master of the Arabs, O Messenger of God?\" He said, «I am the master of the children of Adam, and Ali is the master of the Arabs.» Ibn Ulwan fabricated it."],[4619,"\"I was with Ali on the Day of Camel, and when I saw Aisha standing, I felt a sense of unease. Allah then revealed to me the reason for that during the Dhuhr prayer. I fought alongside the Commander of the Believers, and when it was over, I went to the city and visited Umm Salamah. I said to her, 'By Allah, I did not come to ask for food or drink, but I am a supporter of Abu Dhar.' She welcomed me and I narrated my story to her. She asked, 'Where were you when hearts flew like birds?' I replied, 'I went to the place where Allah revealed to me the reason for that when the sun had set.' She said, 'Well done! I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Ali is with the Quran, and the Quran is with Ali. They will never separate until they return to me at the Pond.'\""],[4620,"«May God have mercy on Ali. O God, make the truth revolve with him wherever he revolves.»"],[4621,"I heard Ali say, «When I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, he gave me, and when I was silent, he began with me.»"],[4622,"Some of the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ had doors opening into the mosque. One day he said, «Close these doors except the door of Ali.» He said, so people spoke about that. The Messenger of God ﷺ stood up, praised God and extolled Him, then said: Now then, I was commanded to close these doors except the door of Ali. One of you said about it: By God, I closed nothing and opened nothing, but I was commanded with something and I followed it."],[4623,"Umar b. al-Khattab said: Ali b. Abi Talib was given three qualities; if I had one of them, it would be dearer to me than being given red camels. It was said: What are they, O Commander of the Believers? He said: His marriage to Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; his dwelling in the mosque with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, being permitted therein what was permitted for him; and the banner on the day of Khaybar."],[4624,"I asked Qutham b. al-Abbas: How did Ali inherit the Messenger of Allah ﷺ apart from you? He said: Because he was the first of us to join him and the closest of us in attachment to him."],[4625,"The heir inherits only through kinship or clientage, and there is no disagreement among the people of knowledge that a paternal cousin does not inherit together with a paternal uncle. Thus it becomes clear by this consensus that Ali inherited knowledge from the Prophet ﷺ apart from them, and by the soundness of what the judge mentioned.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4626,"During the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Ali used to say: Allah says: {If he dies or is killed, will you turn back on your heels?} [Al Imran 144]. By Allah, we will not turn back on our heels after Allah has guided us. By Allah, if he dies or is killed, I will surely fight for what he fought for until I die. By Allah, I am his brother, his ally, his paternal cousin, and the inheritor of his knowledge, so who is more entitled to it than me?” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4627,"The Prophet ﷺ said in a sermon he delivered during the Farewell Pilgrimage: “I will surely kill the Amalekites in a battalion.” Then Jibril ﷺ , or Ali, said to him: “Or Ali b. Abi Talib.” Ismail b. Yahya b. Salamah b. Kuhayl and his father are abandoned."],[4628,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the city of knowledge and Ali is its gate, so whoever wants the city, let him come to the gate.”"],[4629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the city of knowledge and Ali is its gate, so whoever wants the city, let him come to the gate.” Al-Husayn b. Fahm said: Abu al-Salt al-Harawi narrated it to us from Abu Muawiyah."],[4630,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “I am the city of knowledge and Ali is its gate, so whoever wants knowledge, let him come to the gate.”"],[4631,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at me and said: “O Ali, you are a master in this world and a master in the Hereafter. Your beloved is my beloved, and my beloved is the beloved of Allah; your enemy is my enemy, and my enemy is the enemy of Allah; and woe to him who hates you after me.”"],[4632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali b. Abi Talib: “Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah. Whoever obeys you has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys you has disobeyed me.”"],[4633,"“Whoever wants to live my life, die my death, and dwell in the Garden of Eternity which my Lord promised me, let him be a devotee of Ali b. Abi Talib, for he will never take you out of guidance, nor bring you into error.”"],[4634,"“We used not to know the hypocrites except by their denying Allah and His Messenger, their staying away from the prayers, and their hatred of Ali b. Abi Talib.”"],[4635,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was holding the upper arm of 'Ali b. Abi Talib and saying: \"This is the commander of the virtuous, the slayer of the wicked; supported is he who supports him, forsaken is he who forsakes him.\" Then he raised his voice with it."],[4637,"Fatima married me from a family that had no money"],[4638,"From 'Ali: {You are only a warner, and for every people there is a guide} [al-Ra'd 7]. 'Ali said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is the warner, and I am the guide.\""],[4639,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ became angry, none of us dared to speak to him except 'Ali b. Abi Talib.\""],[4640,"A man said to Salman: \"How intense is your love for 'Ali!\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever loves 'Ali has loved me, and whoever hates 'Ali has hated me.'\""],[4641,"\"Allah commanded me to love four of my Companions and informed me that He loves them.\" He said: \"We said: 'Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? All of us would love to be among them.' He said: 'Indeed, 'Ali is among them.' Then he fell silent. Then he said: 'Indeed, 'Ali is among them.' Then he fell silent.\""],[4643,"Anas b. Malik was ill, and Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj came to visit him with some companions. The conversation turned to 'Ali, and Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj belittled him. Anas said: \"Who is this? Sit me up.\" They sat him up, and he said: \"O Ibn al-Hajjaj, do I see you belittling 'Ali b. Abi Talib? By the One who sent Muhammad ﷺ with the truth, I was the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before him, and each day a boy from the sons of the Ansar served before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. That day was my turn, and Umm Ayman, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, came with a bird and I placed it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Umm Ayman, what is this bird?' She said: 'This is a bird I caught and prepared for you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Allah, bring me the most beloved of Your creation to You and to me, to eat with me from this bird.' Then someone knocked at the door, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Anas, see who is at the door.' I said: 'O Allah, make him a man from the Ansar.' I went, and there was 'Ali at the door. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is busy.' I came back and stood in my place. Soon he knocked again, and the Prophet said: 'O Anas, see who is at the door.' I said: 'O Allah, make him a man from the Ansar.' I went, and there was 'Ali at the door. I said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is busy.' I came back and stood in my place. Soon he knocked, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Anas, go and let him in, for you are not the first man to love his people; he is not from the Ansar.' So I went and let him in. He said: 'O Anas, bring the bird near to him.' I placed it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they both ate.\" Muhammad b. al-Hajjaj said: \"O Anas, was this in your presence?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"I give a covenant by Allah that I will never belittle 'Ali after this sitting of mine, and I do not know anyone who belittles him except that I will show him his face (i.e., confront him).\" Ibrahim b. Thabit is dropped."],[4644,"I was sitting with Ibn 'Abbas when nine men came to him and said: \"O Ibn 'Abbas, either you come with us, or you give us privacy from these people.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"Rather, I will come with you.\" He said, while he was then healthy before he became blind. They began to talk, and we do not know what they said. Then he came shaking his garment and saying: \"Uff and tuff! They have criticized a man who has more than ten virtues that no one else has. They criticized a man to whom the Prophet ﷺ said: 'I will send a man whom Allah will never disgrace, who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.' So everyone present hoped for it. He said: 'Where is 'Ali?' They said: 'He is at the mill grinding.' He said: 'None of you would have ground.' He came with sore eyes, hardly able to see. He spat into his eyes, then shook the banner three times and gave it to him. Then 'Ali brought Safiyya bt. Huyayy.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent so-and-so with Surat al-Tawbah, then sent 'Ali after him and took it from him, saying: 'No one should take it except a man who is from me and I am from him.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And the Prophet ﷺ said to his cousins: 'Which of you will take me as a friend in this world and the Hereafter?' 'Ali was sitting with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to a man among them and said: 'Which of you will take me as a friend in this world and the Hereafter?' They refused. Then he said to 'Ali: 'You are my friend in this world and the Hereafter.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And 'Ali was the first person to believe after Khadijah.\" He said: \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his garment and placed it over 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn, and said: {Indeed Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O People of the House, and to purify you with a thorough purification} [al-Ahzab 33].\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And 'Ali sold himself, so he wore the Prophet's ﷺ garment and slept in his place.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"The polytheists were shooting at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Abu Bakr came while 'Ali was sleeping. Abu Bakr thought he was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said: 'O Prophet of Allah.' 'Ali said to him: 'The Prophet of Allah ﷺ has gone toward the well of Maymun, so catch up with him.' Abu Bakr went and entered the cave with him.\" He said: \"And 'Ali began throwing stones as the Prophet of Allah ﷺ used to be thrown at, and he was writhing, having wrapped his head in the garment, not taking it out until morning. Then he uncovered his head, and they said: 'You are indeed cowardly; your companion did not writhe when we threw at him, but you writhe, and we found that strange.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out on the expedition of Tabuk and went out with the people. 'Ali said to him: 'Should I go out with you?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'No.' 'Ali wept, so he said to him: 'Are you not pleased that you are to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no prophet after me? It is not fitting that I should go except with you as my successor.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'You are the guardian of every believer after me, male and female.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ closed the doors of the mosque except for 'Ali's door, so he would enter the mosque in a state of major impurity, and it was his path, having no other path.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever's mawla I am, then 'Ali is his mawla.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And Allah ﷻ has informed us in the Qur'an that He was pleased with the Companions of the Tree, and He knew what was in their hearts. So has He informed us that He was displeased with them after that?\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"And the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to 'Umar when he said: 'Permit me to strike his neck.' He said: 'Would you do it? And what would make you know? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: Do what you wish.'\""],[4645,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr to me and Abu Bakr: \"On the right of one of you is Jibril, and on the other is Mika'il, and Israfil, a mighty angel, is witnessing the battle and is in the rank.\""],[4646,"The people complained about 'Ali b. Abi Talib to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he stood among us as a preacher, and I heard him say: \"O people, do not complain about 'Ali, for by Allah, he is indeed stern in the cause of Allah and in the path of Allah.\""],[4647,"\"Which of you will take me as a friend in this world and the Hereafter?\" He said to each man among them: \"Will you take me as a friend in this world and the Hereafter?\" He said no, until he passed by most of them. Then 'Ali said: \"I will take you as a friend in this world and the Hereafter.\" He said: \"You are my friend in this world and the Hereafter.\""],[4648,"\"We used to say that the best judge among the people of Madinah was 'Ali b. Abi Talib.\""],[4649,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to ʿAlī: \"O ʿAlī, blessed is the one who loves you and believes in you, and woe to the one who hates you and denies you.\""],[4650,"ʿAlī sent me — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ — to Yemen. He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man, and cases will come to me for judgment about which I have no knowledge.\" He said: He placed his hand on my chest and said: \"O Allah, make his tongue firm and guide his heart.\" So I never doubted in judgment — or in any judgment — after that."],[4651,"While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from the people of Yemen came to him and began to talk to the Prophet ﷺ and inform him. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, three men came to ʿAlī disputing over a child; they had intercourse with a woman during a single period of purity. He said to two of them: 'Give up willingly this child.' Then he said: 'You are quarrelsome partners. I will cast lots among you, and whoever the lot falls to, the child is his, and he owes two-thirds of the blood money to his two companions.' So he cast lots among them, and the lot fell to one of them, and he handed the child over to him.\" He said: \"The Prophet ﷺ laughed until his molars showed\" — or he said: \"his back teeth.\""],[4652,"\"I know nothing concerning it except what ʿAlī said.\""],[4653,"I walked with the Prophet ﷺ to a woman, and she slaughtered a sheep for us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A man from the people of Paradise will certainly enter.\" Then Abū Bakr entered. Then he said: \"A man from the people of Paradise will certainly enter.\" Then ʿUmar entered. Then he said: \"A man from the people of Paradise will certainly enter. O Allah, if You will, make him ʿAlī.\" He said: Then ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib entered."],[4654,"\"The first of you to reach the Basin will be the first of you in Islam: ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib.\""],[4655,"\"The first to embrace Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib.\""],[4656,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Fāṭimah and said: \"I, you, this sleeping one — meaning ʿAlī — and these two — meaning al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn — will surely be in one place on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[4657,"I asked Saʿīd b. Jubayr, saying: \"O Abū ʿAbd Allāh, who was the bearer of the banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: He looked at me and said: \"You seem to be at ease.\" I became angry and complained about him to his brothers among the Qurʾān reciters, saying: \"Are you not amazed at Saʿīd? I asked him who was the bearer of the banner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he looked at me and said: 'You are indeed at ease.'\" They said: \"You asked him while he was in fear of al-Ḥajjāj and had taken refuge at the House. Ask him now.\" So I asked him, and he said: \"Its bearer was ʿAlī. Thus I heard it from ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbās.\""],[4658,"\"Paradise longed for three: ʿAlī, ʿAmmār, and Salmān.\""],[4659,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I asked my Lord, Mighty and Exalted is He, that I not marry anyone from my community, nor marry anyone off, except that he will be with me in Paradise, and He granted me that.\""],[4660,"It was revealed to me concerning ʿAlī three things: that he is the master of the Muslims, the imam of the God-fearing, and the leader of the radiant, marked ones."],[4661,"We performed Hajj and passed by al-Hasan b. 'Ali in Madinah, and with us was Mu'awiya b. Hudayj. It was said to al-Hasan, \"This is Mu'awiya b. Hudayj, the reviler of 'Ali.\" He said, \"Bring him to me.\" So he was brought, and he said, \"Are you the reviler of 'Ali?\" He replied, \"I did not do that.\" He said, \"By Allah, if I meet him—and I do not think you will meet him on the Day of Resurrection—you will find him standing at the Pool of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, driving away from it the banners of the hypocrites with a stick of 'awsaj in his hand. The truthful and trusted one ﷺ narrated this to me, and whoever fabricates has failed.\""],[4662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O 'Ali, shall I not teach you words which, if you say them, Allah will forgive you, although you are already forgiven? 'There is no god but Allah, the Most High, the Magnificent. There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous. Glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne, and praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.'\""],[4663,"\"And I swear by the One whom I have taken an oath of allegiance to, if Ali were to make a covenant with the people, he would be the closest to the Prophet ﷺ. We returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the morning, and he was saying, 'Has Ali come? Has Ali come?' repeatedly. Fatimah said, 'It is as if you have sent him on an errand.' She then said, 'He came afterwards.' Abi Salamah said, 'I thought he had some urgent need for him.' So we left the house and sat by the door, and I was closest to the door. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and poured his left hand on him and spoke to him privately. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away that day. So Ali was the closest to the people in commitment.\""],[4664,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was holding my hand and we were in the streets of Madinah, we passed by a garden. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how beautiful a garden it is!\" He said, \"You have in Paradise something more beautiful than it.\""],[4665,"I entered with the Prophet ﷺ upon 'Ali b. Abi Talib, visiting him while he was ill, and with him were Abu Bakr and 'Umar. They moved aside so that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down. One of them said to his companion, \"I think he is only going to die.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"He will not die except being killed, and he will not die until he is filled with rage.\" This chain is weak."],[4666,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded 'Ali b. Abi Talib to fight the renegers, the deviators, and the apostates.\" It is not authentic."],[4667,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say to 'Ali b. Abi Talib, \"You will fight the renegers, the deviators, and the apostates on the roads, at Nahrawan, and on the highlands.\" Abu Ayyub said, \"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, with whom will you fight these peoples?' He said, 'With 'Ali b. Abi Talib.'\""],[4668,"Indeed, among what the Prophet ﷺ entrusted to me is that the community will betray me after him."],[4669,"The Prophet ﷺ said to 'Ali, \"Indeed, you will face hardship after me.\" He said, \"While my religion remains safe?\" He said, \"While your religion remains safe.\""],[4670,"'Abdullah b. Sallam came to me when I had put my foot in the stirrup, intending Iraq. He said, \"Do not go to Iraq, for if you go there, the strike of the sword will befall you.\" 'Ali said, \"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said that to me before you.\" Abu al-Aswad said, \"I said to myself, 'O Allah, I have never seen a warrior on a day like this telling people such a thing.'\""],[4671,"'Ali and I were companions in the expedition of Dhu al-'Ashirah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped there and stayed, we saw some people from Banu Mudlij working at a spring of theirs among palm trees. 'Ali said to me, \"O Abu al-Yaqzan, would you like to go to those people and see how they work?\" We went to them and observed their work for a while, then sleep overcame us. So 'Ali and I went off and lay down in a hollow of palm trees on fine dust, and we slept. By Allah, nothing woke us except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who was shaking us with his foot, and we had become dusty from that fine dust. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Abu Turab,' because of the dust he saw on him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Shall I not tell you about the two most wretched of people?' We said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'The red one of Thamud who hamstrung the she-camel, and the one who will strike you here—meaning your head—until this becomes wet with blood—meaning his beard.'\""],[4672,"When 'Ali marched to Siffin, I disliked fighting, so I came to Madinah and entered upon Maymuna bt. al-Harith. She said, \"Where are you from?\" I said, \"From the people of Kufa.\" She said, \"From which of them?\" I said, \"From Banu 'Amir.\" She said, \"Welcome upon welcome, and nearness upon nearness. What has brought you?\" He said, \"I said, 'Ali has marched to Siffin and I disliked fighting, so I came here.' She said, \"Did you pledge allegiance to him?\" He said, \"I said, 'Yes.' She said, \"Then return to him and be with him, for by Allah, he has not gone astray nor led astray.\""],[4673,"\"Looking at 'Ali is worship.\""],[4674,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Looking at the face of Ali is an act of worship.\" This statement was transmitted by Amr ibn Murrah from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i."],[4675,"Looking at the face of Ali is an act of worship."],[4676,"Umar b. al-Khattab proposed to Ali for Umm Kulthum, and said: Marry her to me. Ali said: I am reserving her for my nephew Abdullah b. Jafar. Umar said: Marry her to me, for by Allah, there is no one among the people who reserves for her what I reserve. So Ali married her to him. Then Umar came to the Muhajirun and said: Will you not congratulate me? They said: For whom, O Commander of the Believers? He said: For Umm Kulthum bt. Ali, the daughter of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Every lineage and tie will be severed on the Day of Resurrection except my lineage and my tie.' So I loved that there be between me and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a lineage and a tie."],[4677,"If you entrust it (the caliphate) to Abu Bakr, he is one who abstains from this world and desires the Hereafter, and in his body there is weakness. If you entrust it to Umar, he is strong, trustworthy, and does not fear the blame of any blamer in Allah. If you entrust it to Ali, he is a guide, rightly guided, and will keep you on a straight path."],[4678,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'The nation will betray you after me, while you live upon my creed and will be killed upon my sunnah. Whoever loves you loves me, and whoever hates you hates me. And this will be dyed from this' – meaning his beard from his head. Sahih."],[4679,"A delegation from the people of Basra came to Ali, and among them was a man from the Kharijites called al-Ja'd b. Na'jah. He praised and extolled Allah, and invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, then said: Fear Allah, O Ali, for you will die. Ali said: 'No, but I will be killed, struck on this, dyeing this.' Ali pointed to his head and his beard with his hand. 'A decree decreed and a covenant made, and he who fabricates has failed.' Then he criticized Ali's clothing, saying: If only you wore clothing better than this. Ali said: 'This clothing of mine is farther from pride for me and more deserving that the Muslims follow my example.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4680,"Al-Harith b. Makhshi reported that Ali was killed on the morning of the twenty-first of Ramadan. He said: I heard al-Hasan b. Ali say while delivering a sermon, mentioning the virtues of Ali: 'He was killed on the night the Quran was sent down, on the night Jesus was taken up, and on the night Moses passed away.' He said: And al-Hasan b. Ali prayed over him, peace be upon them."],[4681,"Al-Hasan prayed over Ali and said four takbirs over him."],[4682,"It is said that she was called Qatam. She was married and divorced, and her dowry was 3,000 dirhams. Ali was killed. In this regard, Al-Farazdaq said in Al-Bahr Al-Taweel, \"I have never seen a dowry carried by a commendable person like the dowry of Qatam, which was three thousand dirhams, a slave, a freed slave, and Ali was killed with a designated sword.\" So there is no dowry more valuable than Ali, even if it becomes expensive. And there is no killing except by the killing of Ibn Muljam.\""],[4683,"When Ibn Muljam struck Ali that blow, Ali gave instructions concerning him, saying: 'He has struck me, so treat him well and soften his bedding. If I live, it is retaliation or pardon; if I die, then deal with him, for I will dispute with him before my Lord, exalted be He.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4684,"When they brought Ibn Muljam to Ali, he said: 'Do with him what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did with a man who was given a chance to kill him, so he ordered that he be killed and burned with fire.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4685,"\"I saw the killer of Ali ibn Abi Talib being burned by fire among the companions of spears.\""],[4686,"No stone was lifted in Jerusalem on the night Ali was killed except that fresh blood was found beneath it."],[4687,"Regarding Al-Dhahabi in summarization"],[4689,"The caliphate of prophethood is thirty years."],[4690,"We leave you as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left us. We said: O Messenger of Allah, appoint a successor over us. He said: 'If Allah knows good in you, He will appoint over you the best of you.' Ali said: 'Allah knew good in us, so He appointed Abu Bakr over us.' Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4691,"Sa'sa'a b. Suhan entered upon Ali and said, 'O Amir al-Mu'minin, whom will you appoint as successor over us?' He said, 'If Allah knows good in your hearts, He will appoint the best of you as successor over you.'"],[4692,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali, 'These Shi'a claim that Ali will be resurrected before the Day of Resurrection.' He said, 'They lie, by Allah. These are not his Shi'a. If we knew that he would be resurrected, we would not have married off his wives or divided his wealth.'"],[4693,"They said to Abu Mahdi, 'Peace be upon you, O Mahdi.' He said, 'Glory be to Allah! Did I not forbid you from this? The Mahdi is only the one whom Allah guides.'"],[4694,"Abdullah b. al-Kawwa', Shabib b. Rib'i, and people with them withdrew from Ali after his return from Siffin to Kufa, because they objected to his cursing of Abu Bakr and Umar and those after them among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They opposed him and revolted against him. Ali went out to them, argued with them, and then returned without fighting. In the hadith of Abu Ishaq al-Fazari, from Shu'ba, from Salama b. Kuhayl, from Abu Juhayfa, there is an addition of some wording, including Ali's saying: 'I will not live with you in a town until I meet Allah ﷻ.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4695,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ali, 'Whoever parts from me has parted from Allah, and whoever parts from you has parted from me.' Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4696,"A man from the extremists called out to Ali while he was in prayer, the dawn prayer, reciting: 'And it was already revealed to you and to those before you that if you associate others with Allah, your work will surely become worthless, and you will surely be among the losers' (Quran 39:65). Ali answered him while in prayer: 'So be patient. Indeed, the promise of Allah is truth. And let not those who have no certainty make you impatient' (Quran 30:60). 'These are hadiths with sound chains of narrators but are not musnad, so I judged them according to what the convention requires.' Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4697,"\"In my house, the verse 'Indeed, Allah desires to repel from you filth, O People of the Household' [33:33] was revealed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn are the People of my Household.'\""],[4698,"I went to Ali and did not find him, so Fatima said to me, \"Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and call him.\" So he came with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they entered, and I entered with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Hasan and Husayn and seated each of them on his thighs, brought Fatima closer to him, along with her husband, then wrapped them with a cloak and said, \"Indeed, Allah only desires to remove impurities from you, O people of the household, and to purify you thoroughly.\" [Quran 33:33] Then he said, \"These are my household. O Allah, they are more deserving.\""],[4699,"The Prophet ﷺ went out in the morning, wearing a cloak of black hair. Al-Hasan and al-Husayn came, and he brought them in with him. Then Fatima came, and he brought her in with them. Then Ali came, and he brought him in with them. Then he said: 'Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with thorough purification' (Quran 33:33)."],[4700,"Saad received the revelation from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . Then, he brought Ali, Fatimah, and their two sons under his robe. He said, \"O Allah, these are my family and the people of my household\" - Ali and Al-Bakir - and spoke about them."],[4701,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw mercy descending, he said, 'Call them for me, call them for me.' Safiyya said, 'Whom, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'My household: Ali, Fatima, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn.' They were brought, and the Prophet ﷺ threw his cloak over them. Then he raised his hands and said, 'O Allah, these are my family, so bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.' And Allah ﷻ revealed: 'Allah intends only to remove from you the impurity, O people of the household, and to purify you with thorough purification' (Quran 33:33)."],[4702,"Ka'b ibn 'Ujrah met me and said, \"Should I not give you a gift that I heard from the Prophet ﷺ?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Say, 'O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad, as You have sent prayers upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are commendable and glorious. O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad, as You have blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim. Indeed, You are praiseworthy and glorious.'\" This hadith has been narrated by Imam Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Bukhari from Musa ibn Ismail in his authentic compilation. I have mentioned it so that the beneficiary may know that all the Ahl al-Bayt (Family of the Prophet) and the descendants, as well as Abu Farwah and Urwah ibn al-Harith al-Hamdani, are among the reliable companions in Kufa."],[4703,"'I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my household. They will never separate until they return to me at the Basin.'"],[4704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O children of Abd al-Muttalib, indeed I have asked Allah for three things for you: that He strengthens your leader, guides your misguided ones, and teaches knowledge to your ignorant ones. And I have also asked Allah to make you generous, noble, and compassionate. So, if a man stands in prayer and in fasting and then meets Allah while harboring hatred towards the family of Muhammad, he shall enter the fire.\""],[4705,"The Prophet ﷺ looked at Ali, Fatima, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn and said, 'I am at war with those who fight you, and at peace with those who make peace with you.'"],[4706,"He said to Ali, Fatima, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn, 'I am at war with those who fight you, and at peace with those who make peace with you.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4707,"'The stars are a safeguard for the people of the earth from drowning, and my household is a safeguard for my community from discord. If any tribe of the Arabs opposes them, they will differ and become the party of Iblis.'"],[4708,"Love Allah for the blessings He nourishes you with, love me for the love of Allah, and love my household for my love."],[4709,"By Him in whose hand is my soul, none hates us, the people of the household, but Allah will cause him to enter the Fire."],[4710,"My Lord promised me concerning my household that whoever of them affirms the oneness of Allah and affirms my conveyance of the message will not be punished."],[4711,"When this verse was revealed: 'Come, let us call our sons and your sons, our women and your women, ourselves and yourselves' [Al 'Imran: 61], the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called 'Ali, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn and said, 'O Allah, these are my family.'"],[4712,"I heard Abu Dharr saying while holding the door of the Ka'bah: 'Whoever knows me, I am who he knows; whoever does not know me, I am Abu Dharr. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the likeness of my household among you is like the ark of Noah among his people: whoever boards it is saved, and whoever stays behind drowns.\"' Mufaddal b. Salih is weak."],[4713,"An angel descended from heaven and asked Allah's permission to greet me, having never descended before. He gave me glad tidings that Fatimah is the mistress of the women of Paradise."],[4714,"An angel descended from heaven and asked Allah's permission to greet me, having never descended before. He gave me glad tidings that Fatimah is the mistress of the women of Paradise."],[4715,"The first to enter Paradise will be I, Fatimah, Hasan, and Husayn. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about those who love us? He said: 'Behind you.'"],[4716,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and placed his foot between me and Fatimah, and taught us what to say when we went to bed. He said: 'O Fatimah, when you are both in your places, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and magnify Him thirty-four times.' 'Ali said: 'By Allah, I have not left it since.' A man who had something in his heart against him said: 'Not even on the night of Siffin?' 'Ali said: 'Not even on the night of Siffin.' Sahih according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Fatimah while I was with him, and she had taken a gold chain from her neck and said: 'This was given to me as a gift by Abu Hasan.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Fatimah, would it please you that people say Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad, and in your hand is a chain of fire?' Then he left and did not sit. Fatimah then took the chain, bought a slave with it, and freed him. When that reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Praise be to Allah who saved Fatimah from the Fire.' Sahih according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Fatimah safeguarded her chastity, so Allah has made her descendants forbidden from the Hellfire.\""],[4719,"The prophets will be raised on the Day of Resurrection on mounts to meet the believers of their people at the gathering place. Salih will be raised on his she-camel, and I will be raised on al-Buraq, whose stride is as far as its farthest glance. Fatimah will be raised in front of me."],[4720,"On the Day of Resurrection a caller will call from behind the veil: 'O people of the gathering, lower your eyes from Fatimah, daughter of Muhammad ﷺ, until she passes.'"],[4721,"From Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: The daughter of Hubayrah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a large ring of gold or gold rings on her hand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began striking her hand. She then went to Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and complained to her about what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had done to her. Thawban said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Fatimah while I was with him, and she had taken a gold chain from her neck and said, \"This was given to me as a gift by Abu Hasan,\" while the chain was in her hand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Fatimah, would it please you that people say 'Fatimah, the daughter of Muhammad,' while in your hand is a chain of fire?\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ left without sitting down. Fatimah took the chain, bought a slave with it, and freed him. When this reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"Praise be to Allah who saved Fatimah from the Fire.\""],[4722,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah, \"Indeed, Allah becomes angry when you become angry, and He becomes pleased when you are pleased.\""],[4723,"I entered with my mother upon Aishah, and I heard her from behind the veil while she was asking her about Ali. She said, \"You ask me about a man? By Allah, I do not know any man who was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than Ali, nor any woman on earth who was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than his wife.\""],[4724,"She said: \"I have not seen anyone whose speech and conversation more closely resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than Fatimah. When she entered upon him, he would welcome her, stand up for her, take her hand, kiss her, and seat her in his place.\""],[4725,"\"Fatimah is the chief of the women of Paradise, except for Maryam bt. Imran.\""],[4726,"\"Fatimah is a part of me; whatever pleases her pleases me, and whatever displeases her displeases me.\""],[4727,"\"Fatimah was the beloved of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ among women, and Ali was among the men.\""],[4728,"He entered upon Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said, \"O Fatimah, by Allah, I have not seen anyone more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you, and by Allah, no one among the people after your father ﷺ is more beloved to me than you.\""],[4729,"I heard Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani say: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from a military expedition or journey, he would go to the mosque and pray two rak'ahs, then he would go to Fatimah before going to his wives. When he returned, he came out of the mosque and Fatimah met him at the door of the house, kissing his mouth while her eyes wept. He said to her, \"O my daughter, what makes you weep?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I see you disheveled and exhausted, and your clothes have become worn.\" He said, \"Do not weep, for Allah ﷻ has sent your father for a matter by which no house of mud or hair on the face of the earth will remain except that Allah will bring it honor or humiliation, until it reaches wherever the night reaches.\""],[4730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Gabriel ﷺ brought me a quince from Paradise, and I ate it on the night I was taken on the Night Journey, and Khadijah conceived Fatimah. Whenever I longed for the fragrance of Paradise, I would smell the neck of Fatimah.\""],[4731,"When he traveled, the last person he would see before departing was Fatimah, and when he returned from a journey, the first person he would see was Fatimah ؓ ."],[4733,"From Aishah, may Allah be pleased"],[4734,"Fatimah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asking him for a servant. He said to her, \"What you have come seeking is dearer to you, or something better than it?\" He said: I think she asked Ali. He said: \"Say: O Allah, Lord of the heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, our Lord and Lord of all things, Revealer of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Quran, Splitter of the grain and the date-stone, I seek refuge in You from the evil of everything whose forelock You hold. You are the First, so there is nothing before You; You are the Last, so there is nothing after You; You are the Outward, so there is nothing above You; You are the Inward, so there is nothing below You. Settle our debt and enrich us from poverty.\""],[4735,"The polytheists of Quraysh gathered in the Hijr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O my daughter, be still.\" Then he went out and entered the mosque upon them. They raised their heads, then lowered them. He took a handful of dust and threw it toward them, then said, \"May the faces be disfigured!\" Not a man among them was struck but he was killed on the day of Badr."],[4736,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married his daughter Fatimah to Ali b. Abi Talib and ordered him not to enter upon Fatimah until he came to him.» And he mentioned the hadith. Its chain is authentic, but they did not record it. Mursal."],[4737,"I entered with my aunt upon Aisha, and she was asked, \"Which of the people was most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" She said, \"Fatimah.\" It was said, \"And among the men?\" She said, \"Her husband, if what I knew of him was that he fasted much and prayed much.\""],[4738,"Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are four: Maryam bt. Imran, Asiya the wife of Pharaoh, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad."],[4739,"«Sufficient for you among the women of the worlds are Maryam bt. Imran, Asiya the wife of Pharaoh, Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, and Fatimah bt. Muhammad.»"],[4740,"That he sent Hasan b. Hasan to him to propose to his daughter. He said to him, \"Tell him to meet me at nightfall.\" He said, \"So he met him, and al-Miswar praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, 'Now then, by Allah, there is no lineage, no tie, no relation by marriage more beloved to me than your lineage, your tie, and your relation by marriage. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fatimah is a piece of me; what constricts her constricts me, and what expands her expands me. And lineages will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection except my lineage, my tie, and my relation by marriage.\" And with you is her daughter, and if I married you to her, that would constrict her.'\" So he departed excusing him."],[4741,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pass by the door of Fatimah for six months when he went out for the dawn prayer, saying, \"Prayer, O people of the house! {Allah only desires to remove impurity from you, O people of the house, and to purify you thoroughly} [al-Ahzab 33].\""],[4742,"Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl to her uncle al-Harith b. Hisham. He consulted the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"Are you asking me about her lineage?\" Ali said, \"I know her lineage, but do you command me to marry her?\" He said, \"No. Fatimah is a piece of flesh from me, and I think only that she will grieve or become distressed.\" Ali said, \"I will not do anything you dislike.\""],[4743,"From Abu Hanzalah, a man from the people of Makkah, that Ali proposed to the daughter of Abu Jahl. Her family said to him, \"We will not marry you off in addition to the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" That reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Fatimah is only a piece of flesh from me; whoever harms her has harmed me.\""],[4744,"That Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl, and that reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said, \"Fatimah is only a piece of me; what harms her harms me, and what exhausts her exhausts me.\""],[4745,"I was at the wedding procession of Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When morning came, the Prophet ﷺ came to the door and said, \"O Umm Ayman, call for me my brother.\" She said, \"He is your brother and you marry him off?\" He said, \"Yes, O Umm Ayman.\" Then Ali came, and the Prophet ﷺ sprinkled water on him and supplicated for him. Then he said, \"Call for me Fatimah.\" She said, \"She came stumbling from shyness.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Be calm, for I have married you to the most beloved of my household to me.\" She said, \"And the Prophet ﷺ sprinkled water on her.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and saw darkness before him and said, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"I am Asma' bt. Umays.\" He said, \"You came to the wedding procession of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah?\" I said, \"Yes.\" Then he supplicated for me. The hadith is erroneous."],[4746,"That she said, \"I have not seen anyone closer in speech and conversation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than Fatimah. When she entered upon him, he would stand for her, kiss her, welcome her, take her by the hand, and seat her in his place. And when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her, she would stand to meet him, and kiss his hand.\""],[4747,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines on the ground, and then he said, \"Do you know what this is?\" They replied, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best women of the people of Paradise are four: Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, and two others.\""],[4748,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"I am the tree, Fatimah is its branch, Ali is its pollen, al-Hasan and al-Husayn are its fruit, and our followers are its leaves. The root of the tree is in the Garden of Eden, and all the rest of it is in the rest of Paradise.\" This is an anomalous text, and even if it is so, Ishaq al-Dabari is truthful, and Abd al-Razzaq, his father, and his grandfather are trustworthy, and Mina', the client of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, met the Prophet ﷺ and heard from him. And Allah knows best. No one said this except al-Hakim, but this is a weak follower."],[4749,"When Fatimah bt. the Prophet ﷺ was mentioned, she said: \"I never saw anyone more truthful in speech than her, except the one who fathered her.\""],[4750,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"When the Day of Resurrection comes, it will be said: 'O people of the gathering, lower your gaze so that Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ may pass.' She will pass wearing two green garments.\" Abu Muslim said: Abu Qilabah said to me, while Abd al-Hamid was with us, that he said: \"Two red garments.\""],[4751,"Khadijah gave birth to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two boys and four girls: al-Qasim, Abdullah, Fatimah, Umm Kulthum, Ruqayyah, and Zaynab."],[4752,"On the authority of Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: \"She was like the moon on the night of the full moon, or the sun when it emerges from behind the clouds, white with a tinge of red. She had black hair, and she resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than any other person. By Allah, as the poet said: 'Fair, trailing her hair as she stands; she disappears in it, and it is thick and jet-black. It is as if she is a bright day within it, and it is as if it is a dark night upon her.'\""],[4753,"\"Fatimah was born in the forty-first year of the birth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4754,"\"Fatimah bt. Muhammad ﷺ died on the third night of Ramadan, at the age of twenty-nine or thereabouts.\" There is disagreement about the time of her death. It is narrated from Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ali that he said: \"Fatimah died three months after the Prophet ﷺ.\" As for Aisha, she said in what is narrated from her: \"She died six months after the Prophet ﷺ.\" As for Abdullah b. al-Harith, he said in what Yazid b. Abi Ziyad narrated from him: \"Fatimah died eight months after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4755,"\"Fatimah remained six months after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Salih b. Kaysan, Uqayl, Ibn Uyaynah, al-Waqidi, Muhammad b. Abdullah the nephew of al-Zuhri, and Ibn Jurayj all followed him with something similar."],[4756,"Fatimah became severely ill, so she said to Asma' bt. Umays: \"Do you not see what I have come to? I will be carried on a bier in public view.\" Asma' replied: \"Indeed, by my life. But I will make for you a covered bier like what I saw made in the land of Abyssinia.\" She said: \"Show it to me.\" Asma' sent for fresh palm stalks, which were cut from the palm groves, and they were made into a covered bier on the bier. That was the first covered bier ever made. Fatimah smiled, and I never saw her smile after her father except on that day. Then we carried her and buried her at night."],[4757,"\"Fatimah bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was buried at night. Ali buried her, and Abu Bakr was not aware of it until she had been buried. Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ prayed over her.\""],[4758,"\"Fatimah died at the age of twenty-one, and she was born at the beginning of the forty-first year of the birth of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[4759,"\"Between the Prophet ﷺ and Fatimah there were two months.\""],[4760,"\"Fatimah remained only two months after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4761,"That Fatimah, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, used to say: 'O my father, how near he is to his Lord! O my father, the Gardens of Eternity are his abode. O my father, his Lord honors him when he comes to Him. O my father, the Lord and His messengers greet him when they meet him.' When Fatimah died, Ali b. Abi Talib said: '[Al-Bahr al-Tawil] For every meeting of two close friends there is a parting, and everything short of parting is little. And my losing one after another is a proof that no close friend lasts forever.'"],[4762,"\"I and Ali washed Fatimah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\""],[4763,"'For every children of a mother there are paternal relatives to whom they are attributed, except the two sons of Fatimah, for I am their guardian and their paternal relatives.'"],[4764,"Al-Hasan and al-Husayn came racing to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he embraced them and then said: 'Indeed a child is a cause of miserliness, cowardice, and grief.'"],[4765,"Al-Hajjaj said: 'He was not from the progeny of the Prophet ﷺ,' while Yahya b. Ya'mar was with him. He said to him: 'You have lied, O commander.' He said: 'You must bring me clear proof and confirmation from the Book of Allah ﷻ for what you say, or I will surely kill you.' He said: '{And from his progeny, Dawud, Sulayman, Ayyub, Yusuf, Musa} up to His ﷻ saying {and Zakariyya, Yahya, Isa, and Ilyas} [Al-An'am 85]. So Allah ﷻ informed that Isa is from the progeny of Adam through his mother, and al-Husayn b. Ali is from the progeny of Muhammad ﷺ through his mother.' He said: 'You have spoken the truth. So what made you contradict me in the assembly?' He said: 'What Allah took upon the prophets: to make it clear to the people and not conceal it. Allah ﷻ said: {But they threw it away behind their backs and purchased with it a small price} [Al 'Imran 187].' He said: So he exiled him to Khurasan. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4766,"When Fatimah gave birth to al-Hasan, the Prophet ﷺ came and said: 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' He said: I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said: 'Rather, he is Hasan.' When she gave birth to al-Husayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' He said: I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said: 'Rather, he is Husayn.' Then when she gave birth to the third, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said: 'Rather, he is Muhsin.' Then he said: 'I have named them after the names of the sons of Harun: Shabar, Shubayr, and Mushbir.'"],[4767,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her one day and said: 'Where are my two sons?' She said: 'Ali took them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned and found them playing in an upper room, with some leftover dates before them. He said: 'O Ali, will you not turn my son away before the heat?' And he mentioned the rest of the hadith. 'This Muhammad b. Musa is Ibn Mashmul, a Madinan, trustworthy. This Awn is Ibn Muhammad b. Ubayd Allah b. Abi Rafi'; he and his father are trustworthy. Umm Ja'far is the daughter of al-Qasim b. Muhammad b. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq, and her grandmother is Asma' bt. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq. All of them are noble and trustworthy.' But Muhammad was deemed weak."],[4768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us during one of the afternoon prayers, Zuhr or Asr, carrying one of his two sons, al-Hasan or al-Husayn. He came forward and placed him at his right foot, then prostrated for a long prostration. My father said: I raised my head from among the people, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating, with the boy riding on his back. So I returned to prostration. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, the people said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you prostrated in this prayer of yours a prostration you never used to prostrate. Was it something you were commanded to do, or was it revealed to you?' He said: 'None of that. But my son rode on me, and I disliked to hurry him until he finished his need.'"],[4769,"'Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are my two sons. Whoever loves them loves me, and whoever loves me, Allah loves him, and whoever Allah loves, He will admit him to Paradise. Whoever hates them hates me, and whoever hates me, Allah hates him, and whoever Allah hates, He will admit him to the Fire.'"],[4770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us with al-Hasan and al-Husayn, one on one shoulder and the other on the other, kissing this one sometimes and that one sometimes, until he came to us. A man said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you love them?' He said: 'Yes. Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.'"],[4771,"'Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, except for the two sons of the maternal aunt.'"],[4772,"'Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.'"],[4773,"'Al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of the people of Paradise, and their father is better than them.'"],[4774,"The Prophet ﷺ used to seek protection for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, saying: \"I seek protection for you both with the perfect words of Allah from every devil and venomous creature and from every envious evil eye.\" Then he would say: \"This is how Ibrahim used to seek protection for his two sons Ismail and Ishaq.\""],[4775,"We used to pray the Isha prayer with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he prostrated, al-Hasan and al-Husayn would jump onto his back, and when he raised his head he would take them and set them down gently. When he returned to prostration they would return. When he finished the prayer, he placed one here and one there. I came to him and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I not take them to their mother?\" He said: \"No.\" Then a flash of lightning flashed, and he said: \"Go to your mother.\" They kept walking in its light until they entered."],[4776,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"What have you named my son?\" I said: \"Harb (war).\" He said: \"He is al-Hasan.\" Then when al-Husayn was born I named him Harb, and the Prophet ﷺ said: \"What have you named my son?\" I said: \"Harb.\" He said: \"He is al-Husayn.\" Then when Muhsin was born, he said: \"What have you named my son?\" I said: \"Harb.\" He said: \"He is Muhsin.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said: \"I have named these sons of mine with the names Harun gave his sons: Shabbar, Shubayr, and Mushabbir.\""],[4777,"Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq met Al-Hasan ibn Ali, embraced him, and said, \"He resembles the Prophet, not resembling Ali.\" And Ali laughed."],[4778,"He met Hasan ibn Ali and said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kiss your stomach.\" So he asked Hasan to reveal the spot that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed so that he could kiss it too. Hasan revealed it to him, and he kissed it."],[4779,"I heard Wahb Abu Juhayfah say: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and al-Hasan b. Ali resembled him.\""],[4780,"\"There was none among the children of Ali resembling the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more than Al-Hasan.\" Sahih."],[4781,"The passage translates to: \"Al-Hasan ibn Ali performed Hajj twenty-five times on foot, and indeed the camels were led alongside him.\""],[4782,"\"Fatima gave birth to Hassan two and a half years after Uhud, and Hassan gave birth four years and six months from that date.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent on it in the summary."],[4783,"Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib passed away in Rabi' al-Awwal in the year forty-nine, and Sa'id ibn al-As prayed over him."],[4784,"\"I still love this man after seeing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing what he was doing. I saw Al-Hasan come to the Prophet's room ﷺ while he was putting his fingers in the Prophet's beard ﷺ and the Prophet ﷺ was putting his tongue in his mouth, then he said, 'O Allah, I love him, so you should love him.'\""],[4785,"We were with Abu Hurairah when Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib came to us and greeted us with peace. We returned the greeting, but Abu Hurairah did not notice him. So we said to him, \"O Abu Hurairah, Hasan ibn Ali greeted us with peace.\" He followed him and said, \"And peace be upon you, my master.\" Then he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'He is a master.'\""],[4786,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed Hasan, hugged him to himself, and began to sniff him, while a man from the Ansar was with him. The Ansari said: \"I have a son who has grown up and I have never kissed him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"What do you think—if Allah has removed mercy from your heart, what is my sin?\""],[4787,"The Prophet ﷺ came carrying al-Hasan b. Ali on his neck. A man met him and said: \"What an excellent mount you have ridden, O boy!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"And what an excellent rider he is!\""],[4788,"I said to Al-Hasan ibn Ali that people are saying you want the caliphate. He replied, \"The leaders of the Arabs were in my hands; they would fight whoever I fought and make peace with whoever I made peace with. I abandoned it seeking the pleasure of Allah Almighty and to spare the blood of the nation of Muhammad ﷺ . Then it was taken from me by the deceit of the people of Hijaz.\" This is a sound chain of narration according to the criteria of the two Sheikhs (al-Bukhari and Muslim), but they did not include it."],[4789,"A man approached Hasan ibn Ali and said, \"O you who have blackened the face of the believers!\" Hasan replied, \"Do not rebuke me, may Allah have mercy on you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the Umayyads delivering sermons on his pulpit, one man after another, and it displeased him. Then the verse 'Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar'—a river in Paradise—was revealed. And the Surah 'Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Decree. And what can make you know what is the Night of Decree? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months' was revealed, over which the Umayyads would rule. This is sufficient for us, and it neither increases nor decreases.\" This is a sound chain of narration, and the one who said this to Hasan ibn Ali was Sufyan ibn al-Layl, a companion of his father."],[4790,"I went to Al-Hasan ibn Ali when he pledged allegiance to Muawiyah, and I said, \"Oh, the one who darkens the face of the believers.\" Then, the secret was mentioned by him, (reference to the secret conversation between Al-Hasan and Muawiyah)."],[4791,"When the matter between Hasan ibn Ali and Mu'awiya occurred, I came to him in Medina while he was sitting with his companions. He mentioned the hadith at length. We then discussed the adhan (call to prayer) in his presence. Some of us said that the adhan began as a vision experienced by Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Asim. Hasan ibn Ali replied, \"The matter of the adhan is greater than that. Gabriel, ﷺ , called the adhan in the heavens two by two and taught it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and in one instance he called the iqama (second call to prayer) one by one and taught it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Hasan called the adhan when he was appointed.\""],[4792,"I was a witness on the day Hasan ibn Ali died, and I saw Husayn ibn Ali saying to Sa'id ibn al-As, while gesturing at his neck, \"Step forward. If it were not a tradition, I would not have asked you to precede.\" There was an issue among them, and Abu Hurairah said, \"Are you begrudging the son of your Prophet ﷺ a grave to bury him in? I heard the Messenger of Allah say, 'Whoever loves them has loved me, and whoever despises them has despised me.'\""],[4793,"“My grandfather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, taught me some words to say in Qunut of Witr: Allahumma ‘afini fiman ‘afait, wa tawallani fiman tawallait, wahdini fiman hadait, wa qini sharra ma qadait, wa barik li fima a’tait. Innaka taqdi wa la yuqda ‘alaik, innahu la yudhillu man walait. Subhanaka rabbana tabarakta wa ta’alait (O Allah, pardon me along with those whom You have pardoned, be an ally to me along with those whom You are an ally to, guide me along with those whom You have guided, protect me from the evil that You have decreed, and bless for me that which You have bestowed. For verily You decree and none can decree over You. He whom You support can never be humiliated. Glory is to You, our Lord, You are Blessed and Exalted).” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1178)"],[4794,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me these words in witr. He said: Say: Allahumma ihdini fiman hadayta wa 'afini fiman afayta wa tawallani fiman tawallayta wa barik li fima a'tayta, wa qini sharra ma qadayta, fa innaka taqdi wa la yuqda 'alayk, wa innahu la yadhilluman walayta, tabarakta Rabbana wa at'alayt. Wa salla Allahu ala al-Nabi Muhammad (O Allah, guide me among those whom You have guided, pardon me among those You have pardoned, turn to me in friendship among those on whom You have turned in friendship, and bless me in what You have bestowed, and save me from the evil of what You have decreed. For verily You decree and none can influence You; and he is not humiliated whom You have befriended. Blessed are You, O Lord, and Exalted. And may Allah (SWT) send salah upon the Prophet Muhammad)'\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1746)"],[4795,"\"A man has been taken away tonight, whom the first and the last cannot surpass in deeds and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to give him his banner and he would fight while Jibril stood on his right and Mika'il on his left. He does not turn back until Allah grants him victory, and he does not leave anything on the people of the earth, whether it be yellow or white, except for seven hundred dirhams from his gifts. He wanted to buy a servant for his family with them.\" \"Then he said, 'O people, whoever knows me has known me, and whoever does not know me, I am Al-Hasan ibn Ali, I am the son of the Prophet, I am the son of the appointed successor, I am the son of the bearer of glad tidings, I am the son of the warner, I am the son of the caller to Allah by His permission, I am the son of the shining lamp, and I am from the people of the household to whom Jibril used to descend and ascend from among us. I am from the people of the household whom Allah has removed impurity from and purified an absolute purification. I am from the people of the household whom Allah has made their love obligatory upon every Muslim.' And Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, said to His Prophet ﷺ, 'Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except love of the near relatives.' And whoever does a good deed, We will increase for him in good over it.' [42:23] So, the doing of a good deed is love for us, the people of the household, is not correct.\""],[4796,"The Prophet ﷺ named Al-Hasan ibn Ali on his seventh day, and he derived the name Husayn from his name. It is mentioned that there was nothing between them except affection."],[4797,"Al-Hasan ibn Ali was poisoned several times, each time surviving until the last time when he died. His liver was affected, and when he died, the women of Banu Hashim mourned him for a month."],[4798,"\"Abu Muhammad al-Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib was pledged allegiance to in Kufa shortly after the killing of the Commander of the Faithful, Ali. He received the pledge from his companions. Haritha ibn Mudarrib narrated to me, saying, 'I heard al-Hasan ibn Ali say, \"By God, I will not pledge allegiance to you except on what I tell you.\"' They asked, 'What is it?' He replied, 'You will make peace with whomever I make peace, and you will fight whomever I fight.' And when the pledge was completed, he addressed them.\""],[4799,"When Ali was killed, Hasan stood up to address the people. A man from the tribe of Azd Ash-Shanu'ah stood up and said, \"I bear witness that I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding him (Hasan) in his lap and saying, 'Whoever loves me, let him love him and inform the absent ones.' If it were not for the honor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , I would never have mentioned it.\""],[4800,"After the allegiance was pledged to Hasan ibn Ali, he seriously confronted Mu'awiya and advanced towards him, appointing Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Tayyar at the front with ten thousand men. He then followed him with Qays ibn Sa'd leading a great army. Mu'awiya corresponded with Abdullah ibn Ja'far, promising him a million dirhams if he came to Hijaz, to which he agreed, abandoned his course, and went to Mu'awiya, who fulfilled his promise. The army dispersed, and Qays ibn Sa'd remained separate with many joining him. Those who were with Abdullah ibn Ja'far were also approached by Mu'awiya and enticed, but they did not comply until Hasan made peace with Mu'awiya, relinquishing authority to him. Hasan and his companions proceeded to meet Mu'awiya, and Hasan was treacherously wounded in the Sabat Pass by Sinan ibn al-Jarrahi al-Asadi, an ally of Banu Nasr, who stabbed him in the thigh with an abhorrent strike. Sinan held the views of the Khawarij. Hasan clutched him and fell to the ground with him. Abdullah ibn Zubyan ibn Amarah al-Tamimi leapt upon Sinan, biting his face until he severed his nose and crushed his head with a stone, killing him instantly. Thus, away with the companions of the Blaze. Hasan was carried on a stretcher to Mada'in and was hosted by Sa'd ibn Mas'ud al-Thaqafi, the uncle of al-Mukhtar, who was Ali's governor in Mada'in. He brought a doctor to treat Hasan until he recovered."],[4801,"Al-Hasan ibn Ali received Muawiya with battalions like mountains. Amr ibn al-As said, \"By God, I see battalions that will not retreat unless their peers are killed.\" Muawiya, being the better man of the two, replied, \"What if these kill those? Who will be responsible for their blood? Who will handle their affairs? Who will take care of their women?\" So Muawiya sent Abd al-Rahman ibn Samura ibn Habeeb ibn Abd Shams. Sufyan said he was a companion. Al-Hasan agreed to peace with Muawiya, surrendered leadership to him, and pledged allegiance to him on conditions and covenants. Muawiya sent a great sum of money to Al-Hasan, reportedly five hundred thousand dirhams, in Jumada al-Awwal of the year forty-one. Al-Hasan had led before surrendering leadership to Muawiya for seven months and eleven days. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in \"Al-Talkhis.\""],[4802,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about al-Hasan b. Ali: \"This son of mine is a sayyid, and perhaps Allah will reconcile through him two great factions of the Muslims.\""],[4803,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was addressing the people, al-Hasan b. Ali came and climbed up to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hugged him and said: \"Indeed, this son of mine is a sayyid, and perhaps Allah ﷻ will reconcile through him two great factions of the Muslims.\" Al-Bukhari recorded both through Abu Musa Isra'il from al-Hasan."],[4804,"A man criticized Hasan ibn Ali when he pledged allegiance to Muawiya, saying that Hasan had brought shame to the believers and had done this and that. Hasan replied, \"Do not blame me, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the Umayyads taking turns on his pulpit, one after another, and it distressed him and concerned him, so Allah Almighty revealed: 'Indeed, We have granted you Al-Kawthar,' a river in Paradise. And He also revealed: 'Indeed, We sent it down during the Night of Decree. And what will make you know what the Night of Decree is? The Night of Decree is better than a thousand months' during which they will rule after you.” This was omitted by Al-Dhahabi from his summary due to its weakness."],[4805,"We were at the forefront with Hasan ibn Ali, numbering twelve thousand, with our swords dripping with sharpness ready to fight the people of Sham, led by Abu al-Umr Taha. When the peace agreement between Hasan ibn Ali and Muawiya reached us, it was as if our backs were broken from anger and rage. When Hasan ibn Ali arrived in Kufa, a man from among us, known as Abu Amir Sufyan ibn al-Layl, stood up and said, \"Peace be upon you, O debaser of the believers.\" Hasan replied, \"Do not say that, O Abu Amir. I have not debased the believers, but I disliked killing them in pursuit of power.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in the summary."],[4806,"\"The wisest among the wise is the pious, and the weakest among the weak is immorality. As for this matter in which Muawiya and I differed, it is a rightful matter for each of us. However, Muawiya had more right to it than me, so I left it for him to decide, to seek the satisfaction of the Muslims and preserve their lives. Though I do not know, it may be a trial for you and a temporary enjoyment. I say this and seek forgiveness from Allah for me and for you.\" - This was omitted by Al-Dhahabi from his summary due to its weakness."],[4807,"The passage translates to: \"Ali used to say to Al-Hasan, 'He is taking off his robe.'\""],[4808,"\"The daughter of Al-Ash'ath bin Qays, Al-Hasan bin Ali, was named, and wealth was bestowed upon her.\""],[4809,"\"I have certainly voided a portion of my liver, and I have been given poison to drink several times, but never the like of this.\""],[4810,"Hasan ibn Ali saw in a dream a vision with the words \"{Say, He is Allah, [who is] One}\" [Al-Ikhlas 1] written between his eyes. He shared this vision with Said ibn al-Musayyib, who said, \"If your vision is true, then your time has come.\" He was poisoned that year and passed away, may Allah have mercy on him. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from his summary due to its weakness."],[4811,"She entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I had a distressing dream last night.\" He asked, \"What was it?\" She replied, \"It was severe.\" He asked again, \"What was it?\" She said, \"I saw as if a piece of your body was cut off and placed in my lap.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have seen a good dream. Fatimah will give birth to a son, if Allah wills, and he will be placed in your lap.\" Fatimah then gave birth to Al-Husayn, and he was indeed placed in her lap as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said. One day, I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed Al-Husayn in his lap. Then, I noticed that the Prophet's eyes were shedding tears. So, I said, \"O Prophet of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is the matter?\" He replied, \"Gabriel came to me and informed me that my Ummah will kill this son of mine.\" I asked, \"This one?\" He replied, \"Yes, and he brought me a handful of his red soil.\""],[4812,"\"Fatimah gave birth to Husayn after Hasan by one year and ten months. She gave birth to him five months and a half into the sixth year of the Hijrah. Husayn was killed on Friday, the day of Ashura, ten days into Muharram in the year sixty-one, at the age of fifty-four years.\" I have mentioned these reports with their explanation in the Book of the Maqtal of al-Husayn, in which there is sufficiency for whoever hears and understands it. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4813,"He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to a meal to which they had been invited. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was met by the leader of the people while Husayn was with the boys playing. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wanted to take hold of him, but the boy began to flee—here once and there once—and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept jesting with him until he caught him. Then he placed one hand under the back of his head and the other under his chin, and put his mouth on his mouth, kissing him, and said: \"Husayn is from me and I am from Husayn. May Allah love whoever loves Husayn. Husayn is a sibt among the asbat.\""],[4814,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ carrying al-Husayn b. Ali, and he was saying: \"O Allah, I love him, so love him.\""],[4815,"“Allah, the Most High, revealed to Muhammad ﷺ that I have killed seventy thousand through Yahya bin Zakariyya and I will kill seventy thousand through the son of your granddaughter. This is the wording of the narration of Ash-Shafi'i. And in the narration of Al-Qadi Abu Bakr bin Kamal, I have killed in revenge for the blood of Yahya bin Zakariyya, and I will kill in revenge for the blood of the son of your granddaughter.”"],[4816,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out one day and found me in the mosque, took my hand and leaned on me. I went with him until he came to the market of Banu Qaynuqa'. He said: He did not speak to me. He went around and looked, then returned, and I returned with him. He sat in the mosque and drew up his legs, then said to me: \"Call for me the little one (Luka').\" Husayn came running until he fell into his lap. Then he put his hand into the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to open Husayn's mouth and put his mouth into his, saying: \"O Allah, I love him, so love him.\""],[4817,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me while Husayn was in his lap: \"Jibril ﷺ informed me that my community will kill Husayn.\" Ibn Abi Samina abridged this hadith, and others narrated it in full from Muhammad b. Mus'ab. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4818,"Ali said: \"O people of Iraq, love us with the love of Islam. I heard my father say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O people, do not raise me above my station, for Allah took me as a servant before He took me as a prophet.'\" I mentioned that to Sa'id b. al-Musayyib, and he said: \"And after He took him as a prophet.\""],[4819,"\"We and the people of the house had no doubt that Hussein ibn Ali would be killed at Karbala.\""],[4820,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ call the adhan in the ear of Husayn when Fatimah gave birth to him."],[4821,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Fatimah and said, \"Adorn the hair of Al-Hussein and give as charity its weight in silver, and give the midwife a gift of a sheep for the newborn's 'Aqiqah.\""],[4822,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was nursing Husayn b. Ali with the milk of a son called Qutham. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached for him, so I handed him over, and he urinated on him. She said: I reached out my hand to him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not interrupt my son.\" She said: So he sprinkled him with water. Ibn Abbas said: \"The urine of a boy who has not eaten is sprinkled, and the urine of a girl is washed.\""],[4823,"When Fatimah gave birth to al-Hasan, the Prophet ﷺ came and said: 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' He said: I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said: 'Rather, he is Hasan.' When she gave birth to al-Husayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' He said: I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said: 'Rather, he is Husayn.' Then when she gave birth to the third, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said: 'Show me my son. What have you named him?' I said, 'I have named him Harb.' He said: 'Rather, he is Muhsin.' Then he said: 'I have named them after the names of the sons of Harun: Shabar, Shubayr, and Mushbir.'"],[4824,"\"Al-Husayn was killed on the day of Ashura, on Friday.\"Hakim said, \"We will explain this news in the Book of the Killing of Al-Husayn, and it is sufficient for those who hear it.\"Hakim said, \"This is the last that has been reached through diligence concerning mentioning the virtues of the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with authentic chains of narration that have not been compiled by the two esteemed Imams (Bukhari and Muslim). I have dictated what my diligence has led to regarding the virtues of the four caliphs and the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, authenticated by chains of narration. Then I saw that it was better to organize this book chronologically after them for all the companions, from the beginning of Islam to the last one who died among them, and Allah is the one who aids in that with His mercy.\""],[4825,"When Abu al-Haysar Anas b. Rafi' came to Makkah with a group of young men from Banu Abd al-Ashhal, among them Iyas b. Mu'adh, seeking an alliance with Quraysh against their own people from Khazraj, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard of them and went to them. He sat with them and said: \"Would you like something better than what you came for?\" They said: \"And what is that?\" He said: \"I am the Messenger of Allah. Allah sent me to the servants, calling them to worship Allah and not associate anything with Him, and He revealed to me the Book.\" Then he mentioned Islam to them and recited the Qur'an to them. Iyas b. Mu'adh, who was a young boy, said: \"O people, by Allah, this is better than what you came for.\" He said: Abu al-Haysar took a handful of pebbles and struck the face of Iyas b. Mu'adh with them, saying: \"Leave us alone. By my life, we have come for other than this.\" Iyas fell silent, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and they departed to Madinah. Then the battle of Bu'ath took place between the Aws and the Khazraj. He said: Iyas b. Mu'adh did not remain long before he died. Mahmud b. Labid said: One of my people who attended his death informed me that they kept hearing him declaring the oneness of Allah, magnifying Him, praising Him, and glorifying Him until he died. He said: They had no doubt that he had died a Muslim, for he had embraced Islam in that gathering when he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he heard."],[4826,"The death of al-Bara' b. Ma'rur was in Safar, one month before the arrival of the Prophet ﷺ, and he was the first of the nuqaba' to speak."],[4827,"Al-Bara' b. Ma'rur was the first to strike the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in allegiance to him on the Night of al-Aqaba among the seventy of the Ansar. Al-Bara' b. Ma'rur stood up, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: \"Praise be to Allah who honored us with Muhammad ﷺ and brought him to us. He was the first to answer and the last to call, so we answered Allah ﷻ, and we heard and obeyed. O assembly of Aws and Khazraj, Allah has honored you with His religion. If you take listening, obedience, and support with gratitude, then obey Allah and His Messenger.\" Then he sat down."],[4828,"Khadijah ؓ hired the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for two journeys to Jarash, each journey for a young she-camel."],[4829,"The first woman whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married was Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. Abd al-Uzza. He married her in the Jahiliyyah, and her father Khuwaylid b. Asad gave her in marriage."],[4830,"Khadijah died one year before the Hijrah."],[4831,"Abu Talib and Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid died in the same year, which was three years before the Prophet's ﷺ migration to Madinah. Khadijah was buried in al-Hajun, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended into her grave. She was twenty-eight years old when he married her. Muhammad said: \"Khadijah's kunya was Umm Hind. She had a son and a daughter when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her. Khadijah's mother was Fatimah bt. Za'idah b. al-Asamm, and her mother was Halah bt. Abd Manaf.\""],[4832,"Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid died when she was sixty-five years old.” This is an anomalous statement, for what I hold is that she had not reached sixty years."],[4833,"Khadijah bore the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two boys and four girls: al-Qasim, ʿAbd Allah, Fatimah, Zaynab, Ruqayyah, and Umm Kulthum."],[4834,"Praise be to Allah who fed me leavened bread, clothed me in silk, and married me to Khadijah, and I was in love with her.”"],[4835,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed on Monday, and Khadijah prayed with him. Then on Tuesday he presented the prayer to ʿAli, and he accepted Islam. He said, “Let me consult Abu Talib about the prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “It is but a trust.” ʿAli said, “Then I will pray.” So he prayed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on Tuesday."],[4836,"I was a merchant and a friend of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib during the time of ignorance. I came on a trading journey and stayed with al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib at Mina. A man came, looked at the sun when it had passed its zenith, and stood to pray. Then a woman came and stood to pray. Then a boy who was approaching puberty came and stood to pray. I asked al-Abbas, “Who is this?” He replied: “This is Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Abd al-Muttalib, my nephew. He claims that he is a prophet, and no one besides this woman and this boy has followed him in his affair. This woman is Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid, his wife, and this boy is his cousin, Ali b. Abi Talib.” Afif al-Kindi, who embraced Islam and became a good Muslim, said: “I wish that I had embraced Islam that day, so that a quarter of Islam would have belonged to me.”[1]"],[4837,"Narrated Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ , said that the first thing that Allah's Messenger ﷺ started receiving from Allah was true dreams during his sleep. And he would not see any dream but it would come true like bright daylight. Then solitude was made dear to him and he used to go in seclusion in the cave of Hira where he used to worship (Allah alone) continuously for many nights before coming back to his wife Khadija. She informed him of her conviction of his Prophethood and supported him through her wealth and efforts. Then Allah's Messenger ﷺ returned with that experience of true inspiration, his heart was beating violently, and then he went to Khadija and said, \"Cover me! Cover me!\" They covered him until his fear was over and then he told Khadija everything that had happened and said, \"I fear that something may happen to me.\" Khadija replied, \"Never! But have the glad tidings, for by Allah, Allah shall never disgrace you as you keep good relations with your kith and kin, speak the truth, help the poor and the destitute, serve your guests generously, and assist the deserving calamity-afflicted ones.\" Then Khadija went along with him to her cousin Waraqa bin Naufal bin Asad bin 'Abdul 'Uzza bin Qusai. Waraqa was the son of her paternal uncle, i.e., her father's brother, who during the Pre-Islamic Period became a Christian and used to write the writing with Hebrew letters. He would write from the Gospel in Hebrew as much as Allah wished him to write. He was an old man and had lost his eyesight. Khadija said to him, \"O my cousin! Listen to the story of your nephew.\" Waraqa asked, \"O my nephew! What have you seen?\" The Prophet ﷺ described whatever he had seen. Waraqa said, \"This is the same Namus (i.e., Gabriel, the Angel who keeps the secrets of Allah) whom Allah had sent to Moses ﷺ . I wish I were young and could live till the time when your people would turn you out.\" Allah's Messenger ﷺ asked, \"Will they drive me out?\" Waraqa replied in the affirmative and said, \"Anyone (man) who came with something similar to what you have brought was treated with hostility; and if I should remain alive till the day when you will be turned out then I would support you strongly.\" But after a few days of Waraqa's death, Allah's Messenger ﷺ received the Divine Inspiration and the Verse of Al-Qur'an, 2.286 (Surat Al-Baqarah) was revealed to him."],[4838,"Khadijah was the first of the women to believe in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4839,"\"Khadijah was the first person to believe in Allah and believe in His Messenger ﷺ, before prayer was obligatory.\" This statement was deleted by Al-Dhahabi from the summary [of narrators] due to its weakness."],[4840,"I came to Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman while he was in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard him say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid is the foremost of the women of the worlds in faith in Allah and in Muhammad ﷺ.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4841,"The best of its women is Maryam bt. ʿImran, and the best of its women is Khadijah.”"],[4842,"I was commanded to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, wherein there is no clamor nor toil.”"],[4843,"I was commanded to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, wherein there is no clamor nor toil.”"],[4844,"I was commanded to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl.”"],[4845,"I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Jibril came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, here is Khadijah coming to you with a vessel containing condiment, or food, or drink. When she comes to you, convey to her peace from her Lord and give her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of hollow pearl, wherein there is no clamor nor toil.”"],[4846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew four lines in the ground and said, \"Do you know what this is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best women of the people of Paradise are Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, Fatimah bint Muhammad, and Maryam bint Imran,\" and I think he said, \"and the wife of Pharaoh.\""],[4847,"I found in my father's book in his own handwriting: Sa'd b. Ibrahim b. Sa'd and Ya'qub b. Ibrahim narrated to us, they said: My father narrated to us, from Salih, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, who said: A'ishah said to Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Shall I give you glad tidings that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The mistresses of the women of the people of Paradise are four: Maryam bint Imran, Fatimah bint the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, and Asiyah.\" According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4848,"\"I never felt jealous of any woman as I felt jealous of Khadijah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry me until after she had died. That was because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of reeds, in which there is no clamor or toil.\""],[4849,"\"The Prophet ﷺ did not marry any other wife alongside Khadijah until she died.\" A'ishah said, \"I never saw Khadijah at all, but I was not jealous of any of his wives as much as I was of Khadijah, because of how often he mentioned her.\""],[4850,"Jibril ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ while Khadijah was with him and said, \"Allah sends greetings of peace to Khadijah.\" She said, \"Allah is al-Salam, and upon you be peace and the mercy of Allah.\""],[4851,"As'ad b. Zurarah died in Shawwal, nine months after the Hijrah, while the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was being built that day; that was before Badr. The Banu al-Najjar came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Our naqib has died, so appoint a naqib for us.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am your naqib.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4852,"I was my father's guide after he lost his sight. Whenever he heard the call to prayer on Friday, he would say, \"May Allah have mercy on As'ad b. Zurarah.\" After some time, I thought I should ask my father why, whenever he heard the call to prayer, he said, \"May Allah have mercy on As'ad b. Zurarah.\" So I said, \"O my father, it amazes me that you pray for Abu Umamah every time you hear the call for Friday prayer.\" He said, \"O my son, he was the first to lead the Friday prayer for us in Madinah, in a depression of the Harrah of Banu Bayadah, in a place called al-Khadimat.\" I said, \"How many were you that day?\" He said, \"Forty men.\""],[4853,"\"The Prophet ﷺ cauterized As'ad b. Zurarah for a thorn wound.\""],[4854,"From Zaynab bint Nubayt, she said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adorned her mother and her maternal aunt.\" Their father, Abu Umamah As'ad b. Zurarah, had entrusted them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"so he adorned them with earrings of pure gold containing pearls.\" Zaynab said, \"I reached the jewelry or some of it.\" Its chain is sahih, but they did not record it. Sahih."],[4855,"\"The first banner the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied was for Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib, then the banner of Ubaydah b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib to Rabigh, between al-Juhfah and Qudayd.\""],[4856,"And Utbah b. Rabi'ah killed Ubaydah b. al-Harith in single combat: Utbah struck him on his leg and cut it off. \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ carried him, and he died at al-Safra' on his return from Badr, and he buried him there.\""],[4857,"Utbah and Ubaydah exchanged two blows, each of which wounded the other. Hamzah and Ali returned upon Utbah and killed him, and they carried their companion Ubaydah and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. His leg had been cut off and its marrow was flowing. When they brought Ubaydah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said, \"Am I not a martyr, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Ubaydah said, \"If Abu Talib were alive, he would know that we are more deserving of what he said when he recited: 'We surrender him until we are struck down around him, and we become heedless of our children and wives.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4858,"The army of Badr was presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sent back Umair b. Abi Waqqas. Umair wept, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed him to go and fastened the straps of his sword upon him."],[4859,"\"We are the smallest with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, me and Sa'd bin Khaythama.\""],[4860,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out to Badr, Sa'd b. Khaythamah and his father both wanted to go out with him. They mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that one of them should go out, so they cast lots. Khaythamah b. al-Harith said to his son Sa'd, \"One of us must stay behind, so stay with your wives.\" Sa'd said, \"If it were anything other than Paradise, I would have preferred you with it. I hope for martyrdom in this expedition of mine.\" They cast lots, and Sa'd's arrow came out, so he went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Badr, and Amr b. Abd Wadd killed him. It is mursal and its chain is weak."],[4861,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to seek out a burial ground for his companions in which they would be buried. He had sought the areas and outskirts of Madinah, then said, \"I was commanded with this place,\" meaning al-Baqi', which used to be called Baqi' al-Khabkhabah. Most of its vegetation was al-gharqad (boxthorn), and the first to be buried there was Uthman b. Maz'un. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed a stone at his head and said, \"This is the grave of our forerunner.\" Whenever a Muhajir died after him, it was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, where shall we bury him?\" and he would say, \"Near our forerunner Uthman b. Maz'un.\" Its chain is weak."],[4862,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kissed Uthman b. Maz'un after he had died."],[4863,"His wife said, \"Congratulations on Paradise, O Uthman b. Maz'un!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at her and said, \"And what makes you know that?\" She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, your horseman and your companion.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed I am the Messenger of Allah, and I do not know what will be done with me.\" The people became worried for Uthman. When Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Join her to our righteous predecessor Uthman b. Maz'un.\" The women wept, and Umar began to strike them with his whip. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his hand and said, \"Gently, O Umar.\""],[4864,"Mus'ab and Ja'dah—the one who says [al-tawil]: \"And who is the one who would refuse me on account of his maternal uncle? My maternal uncle is Ali, possessor of generosity, and Aqil.\" Mus'ab said, \"Hubayrah died in Najran as a polytheist. As for Ja'dah, he married his maternal cousin Umm al-Hasan bt. Ali, and she bore him Abdullah b. Ja'dah b. Hubayrah, about whom it was said in Khurasan [al-basit]: 'Were it not for Ibn Ja'dah, your Quhunduz would not have been conquered, nor Khurasan, until the trumpet is blown.'\" Mus'ab said, \"Ali appointed Ja'dah b. Hubayrah al-Makhzumi over Khurasan, and he returned to Iraq, then performed Hajj and died in Madinah.\" He narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ confirming the soundness of what Mus'ab mentioned."],[4865,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them, then the later ones are worse.\""],[4866,"I said to Ali, \"O maternal uncle, did you kill Uthman?\" He said, \"No, by Allah, I did not kill him, nor did I order it, but I was overpowered.\" Ja'dah b. Hubayrah died after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ali confused it with the death of his father Hubayrah b. Abi Hubayrah."],[4867,"Sa'd b. Malik prepared to go out to Badr, but he fell ill and died. The place of his grave is near the house of Ibn Qariz. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned him his share and his reward."],[4868,"From Banu Hashim b. Abd Manaf, those who witnessed Badr were the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib, Ali b. Abi Talib, Zayd b. Harithah, Anasah the mawla of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Kabshah, Abu Marthad, and his son Marthad."],[4869,"Hamzah used to fight in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with two swords, saying, \"I am the lion of Allah.\""],[4870,"\"The best of creation on the day when Allah gathers the messengers, and the best of people after the messengers are the martyrs, and the best of martyrs is Hamza ibn Abdul-Muttalib.\""],[4871,"\"Indeed Amina bint Wahb, the mother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , was in the chamber of her uncle Ahyaab ibn Abdul Manaf ibn Zuhrah. And indeed Abd al-Muttalib ibn Hashim brought his son Abdullah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, the father of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and Abdullah married Amina bint Wahb. And Abd al-Muttalib married Hala bint Ahyaab ibn Abdul Manaf ibn Zuhrah, who was the mother of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib, in the same gathering. And he (Abd al-Muttalib) was close in age to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his foster brother.\""],[4872,"Abu Jahl confronted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Safa, harmed him, insulted him, and said about him what is disliked of faulting his religion and belittling him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not speak to him. A freedwoman of Abdullah b. Jud'an al-Taymi was in her dwelling above al-Safa, hearing that. Then he left him and went to the assembly of Quraysh at the Kaaba and sat with them. It was not long before Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib came, wearing his bow over his shoulder, returning from a hunt of his. When he did that, he would not pass by the assembly of Quraysh—and they were the most formidable—without stopping. That day he was a polytheist upon the religion of his people. The freedwoman came to him while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had risen to return to his house. She said to him, \"O Umarah, if only you had seen what your nephew Muhammad encountered from Abu al-Hakam just now. He found him here, harmed him, insulted him, and reached what is disliked, then left him and went to the assembly of Quraysh at the Kaaba and sat with them, and did not speak to Muhammad.\" Hamzah was overcome with anger for what Allah willed of his honor. He went out quickly, not stopping at anyone as he used to do, intending to circumambulate the House, making for Abu Jahl to fall upon him. When he entered the mosque, he saw him sitting among the people, so he approached him until he stood over his head, raised the bow, and struck him on the head with a full blow. Men of Quraysh from Banu Makhzum stood up to Hamzah to help Abu Jahl. They said, \"We see you, O Hamzah, have turned renegade.\" Hamzah said, \"And what prevents me, when it has become clear to me from him? I bear witness that he is the Messenger of Allah and that what he says is true. By Allah, I will not desist, so stop me if you are truthful.\" Abu Jahl said, \"Leave Abu Umarah alone, for I insulted his nephew with a foul insult.\" Hamzah continued in his Islam and followed, easing the burden of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Hamzah embraced Islam, Quraysh knew that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had become strong and protected, and that Hamzah would defend him, so they refrained from some of what they had been doing and inflicting upon him. Sa'd said about that when he struck Abu Jahl, and he mentioned some rajaz verse that is not established, beginning with: \"Taste, O Abu Jahl, what has covered you.\" Then Hamzah returned to his house, and Satan came to him and said, \"You are the chief of Quraysh, you followed this renegade and left the religion of your forefathers. Death is better for you than what you have done.\" A doubt came upon Hamzah, and he said, \"What have I done? O Allah, if it is right guidance, then make its confirmation in my heart; otherwise, make for me a way out from what I have fallen into.\" He spent a night such as he had never spent before from the whispering of Satan until morning. Then he went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O son of my brother, I have fallen into a matter from which I do not know the way out, and a situation like mine upon what I do not know whether it is right guidance or something else severe. Tell me a narration, for I have desired, O son of my brother, that you narrate to me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward and reminded him, admonished him, warned him, and gave him glad tidings. Allah cast faith into his soul as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. He said, \"I bear witness that you are truthful, with the testimony of one who affirms and acknowledges. So proclaim, O son of my brother, your religion. For by Allah, I would not love to have all that the sun shines upon while I am upon my former religion.\" Thus Hamzah was among those through whom Allah strengthened the religion."],[4873,"Ali and Hamza came to the Prophet ﷺ after they had performed ghusl. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"How did you two do it?\" One of them said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I covered myself with a garment.\" The other said, \"And I did the same.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you two had done otherwise, I would have covered you both.\""],[4874,"On the day of Uhud, Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib was fighting in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"I am the lion of Allah.\" [Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it.] Sahih."],[4875,"From his shaykhs, they said: When Hamza was struck down, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying, \"I will never be afflicted with the like of you.\" Then he said to Fatima and his paternal aunt Safiyya, \"Rejoice: Jibril ﷺ came to me and informed me that Hamza is written among the inhabitants of the heavens as Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib, the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[4876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Call Hamza.\" He was the closest of them to the polytheists, by the owner of the red camel. Hamza said to me, \"That is Utba b. Rabi'a, and he is forbidding fighting, saying, 'O people, I see a people you will not reach, and there is good among you. O people, bind it to me today and say that Utba b. Rabi'a has become cowardly, for you know I am not the most cowardly of you.' Abu Jahl heard that and said, 'You say this? If it were anyone else...' He said, 'You are filled with terror.' He said, 'Do you mean me, O yellowed one?' The narrator said: Then Utba, his brother Shayba, and his son al-Walid came forward and said, 'Who will duel?' Some youths from the Ansar went out, but Utba said, 'We do not want these; rather, who will duel us from the uncles of Banu Abd al-Muttalib?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Rise, O Hamza; rise, O Ubayda; rise, O Ali.' So Hamza faced Utba, Ubayda faced Shayba, and Ali faced al-Walid. Hamza killed Utba, Ali killed al-Walid, and Ubayda killed Shayba, while Shayba struck Ubayda's leg and cut it off, and Hamza and Ali rescued him until he died at al-Safra'. [Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it.] They did not include it because of Haritha, and Ibn al-Madini deemed him unreliable."],[4877,"On the day of Uhud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned and heard the women of Banu Abd al-Ashhal weeping over their dead. He said, \"But Hamza has no weepers.\" So the women of the Ansar came and wept over Hamza in his presence. He slept, then woke up while they were weeping, and said, \"Woe to them! They are still here until now? Tell them to go back and not weep over any dead after today.\" Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it."],[4878,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"The master of the martyrs is Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib, and a man who stood before a tyrannical ruler, enjoining good and forbidding evil, and the ruler killed him.\" Sahih isnad, but they did not include it. Al-Saffar is unknown."],[4879,"Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was killed while in a state of janaba. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The angels washed him.\" Sahih isnad, but they did not include it. Mu'alla b. Abd al-Rahman is perished."],[4880,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out intending to visit Hamza's daughter Qabisa, until he stood at the door and said, \"Peace be upon you. Is Abu Umara there?\" She said, \"No, by Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He went out intending to come to you, and I think he missed you in one of the alleys of Banu al-Najjar. Will you not enter, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Do you have anything?\" She said, \"Yes.\" So he entered, and she brought him some hays and said, \"Eat, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, may it be wholesome and pleasant for you. You have come while I wanted to come to you to congratulate you and wish you well. Abu Umara told me that you have been given a river in Paradise called al-Kawthar.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"And its vessels are more numerous than the stars of the sky, and the most beloved of those who come to it to me are your people.\" Sahih isnad, but they did not include it."],[4881,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Hamza on the day of Uhud after he had been mutilated and disfigured, and he said, \"Were it not that Safiyya would grieve, I would leave him so that Allah would gather him from the bellies of birds and beasts.\" So he shrouded him in a namira. [Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it.] According to the condition of Muslim."],[4882,"A son was born to a man among us, and they said, \"What shall we name him?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Name him after the most beloved of names to me: Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib.\" Sahih isnad, but they did not include it. Ya'qub b. Kasib is weak."],[4883,"He heard a man in Madinah say: My grandfather brought my father to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"This is my son; what shall I name him?\" He said, \"Name him after the most beloved of people to me: Hamza b. Abd al-Muttalib.\" This unknown narrator fell short in reporting the hadith from Ibn Uyayna, and the statement about it is the statement of Ya'qub b. Humayd. Abu Ahmad al-Hafiz used to debate with me that al-Bukhari narrated from him in the Sahih, but I refused. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis because of his weakness."],[4884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I entered Paradise last night and looked around, and there was Ja'far flying with the angels, and Hamza reclining on a couch.\" Sahih isnad, but they did not include it. Salama b. Wahram was deemed weak by Abu Dawud."],[4885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned on the day of Uhud and heard the women of Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal weeping over their slain. He said, \"But Hamza has no weepers.\" The hadith."],[4886,"From 'Urwah: 'Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, and he was killed on the day of Uhud at the age of fifty-four.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about him in the Talkhis."],[4887,"'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stripped Hamza, he wept, and when he saw his mutilation, he sobbed.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about him in the Talkhis."],[4888,"The Prophet ﷺ looked on the day of Uhud at Hamza, who had been killed and mutilated, and he saw a sight that he had never seen more painful to his heart or more frightening. He said, 'May Allah's mercy be upon you. You were one who maintained ties of kinship and did much good. Were it not for the grief after you, it would please me to leave you until you are gathered from scattered mouths.' Then he swore while standing in his place: 'By Allah, I will mutilate seventy of them in your place.' Then the Qur'an was revealed while he was standing in his place, and he did not move: {And if you punish, then punish with the like of that with which you were afflicted, but if you endure patiently, it is better for the patient} [al-Nahl 126] until he completed the surah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ expiated his oath and refrained from what he intended. Salih and weak."],[4889,"When Hamza was killed, Safiyya came looking for him, not knowing what had been done to him. She met 'Ali and al-Zubayr. 'Ali said to al-Zubayr, 'Mention it to your mother,' and al-Zubayr said to 'Ali, 'No, you mention it to your aunt.' She said, 'What happened to Hamza?' They made it seem as though they did not know. She came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'I fear for her mind.' He placed his hand on her chest and supplicated, and she said, 'We belong to Allah and to Him we return,' and wept. Then he came and stood over him, and he had been mutilated. He said, 'Were it not for the distress of the women, I would leave him until he is gathered from the crops of birds and the bellies of beasts.' Then he ordered the slain, and he began to pray over them. He would place nine and Hamza, and he would say seven takbirs over them. Then they would be lifted, and Hamza would be left. Then nine more would be brought, and he would say seven takbirs over them. Then they would be lifted, and Hamza would be left. Then nine more would be brought, and he would say seven takbirs over them, until he finished with them. Abu Bakr b. 'Ayyash heard it from Yazid. I say: they are not reliable."],[4890,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in a dream: He said, 'I saw as if I was riding behind a ram, and as if the pommel of my sword broke. I interpreted it as that I would kill the ram of the people, and I interpreted the pommel of my sword as a man from my kin.' Then Hamza was killed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed Talha, who was the bearer of the banner of the polytheists."],[4891,"'Abd al-Muttalib married Hala bt. Uhayb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhra, and she gave birth to Hamza and Safiyya."],[4892,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, it is written with Him in the seventh heaven: Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger ﷺ.' Yahya b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Labiba is weak."],[4893,"'Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib was given the kunya Abu 'Umara.'"],[4894,"I heard Jabir b. 'Abd Allah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed Hamza on the day of Uhud when the people returned from the fighting. He said: A man said, 'I saw him at that tree, saying: I am the lion of Allah and the lion of His Messenger. O Allah, I disavow to You what these have brought to Abu Sufyan and his companions, and I apologize to You for what these have done in their retreat.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went toward him. When he saw his forehead, he wept, and when he saw the mutilation done to him, he sobbed. Then he said, 'Should he not be shrouded?' A man from the Ansar stood up and threw a garment. Jabir said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The master of the martyrs with Allah, Exalted is He, on the Day of Resurrection is Hamza.'"],[4895,"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Every prophet was given seven companions, and I was given more than ten.' It was said to 'Ali, 'Who are they?' He said, 'I, Hamza, and my two sons,' then he mentioned them."],[4896,"That I meet the enemy tomorrow, and they kill me, then they split open my belly, and cut off my nose and my ear, then You ask me, 'For what was that?' and I say, 'For You.' Sa'id b. al-Musayyib said, 'I hope that Allah will fulfill the last of his oath as He fulfilled the first.'"],[4897,"The first banner raised in Islam belonged to Abdullah b. Jahsh."],[4898,"Mus‘ab ibn ‘Umayr was the youth of Mecca in his prime and beauty. His parents loved him, and his mother dressed him in the finest and most delicate of clothes. He was the most fragrant among the people of Mecca. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned him and said, \"I have not seen in Mecca anyone with a more beautiful hair, more elegant outfit, or greater comfort than Mus‘ab ibn ‘Umayr.\"[1]"],[4899,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished [the Battle of] Uhud, he passed by Mus'ab Al-Ansari, who had been killed on his path, and recited: \"Among the believers are men who have been true to what they promised Allah\" [Al-Ahzab 33:23]."],[4900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on the day of Uhud to look for Sa'd b. al-Rabi' and said to me: 'If you see him, convey to him my greetings and tell him the Messenger of Allah says: How do you find yourself?' He said: So I went around among the slain and found him in his last breaths, with seventy wounds, between spear thrusts, sword blows, and arrow shots. I said to him: 'O Sa'd, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sends you greetings and says: Tell me how you find yourself.' He said: 'Upon the Messenger of Allah be peace, and upon you be peace. Tell him: O Messenger of Allah, I find myself smelling the fragrance of Paradise. And tell my people the Ansar: You have no excuse before Allah if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is harmed while there is an eye blinking among you.' He said: Then his soul departed, may Allah have mercy on him."],[4901,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who will check for me what has happened to Sa'd b. al-Rabi'?' Then he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner, and said: Sa'd said: 'Inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I am among the dead, and convey my greetings to him, and tell him Sa'd says: May Allah reward you on our behalf and on behalf of the entire Ummah with the best reward.' Mursal."],[4902,"We were prevented from witnessing Badr except that my father and I had set out wanting to reach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the disbelievers of Quraysh intercepted us and said: 'You are seeking Muhammad.' We said: 'We do not seek him; we only want to go to Madinah.' So they took from us a covenant by Allah and a pledge that we would go to Madinah and not fight alongside Muhammad ﷺ. When we passed them, we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned to him what they said and what we said to them. He said: 'We will seek Allah's help against them and keep our covenant with them.' So we went on to Madinah, and that is what prevented us from witnessing Badr."],[4903,"Muhammad b. Umar narrated to us."],[4904,"By Allah, my father drank wine in the morning on the day of Uhud, then went forth and fought until he was killed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Uhud as a martyr."],[4905,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Jabir: 'O Jabir, shall I give you glad tidings?' He said: 'Yes, give me glad tidings, may Allah give you glad tidings of good.' He said: 'Do you realize that Allah, Exalted is He, brought your father back to life and seated him before Him, then said: Wish upon Me, My servant, whatever you wish and I will grant it to you.' He said: 'O Lord, I have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped. I wish that You return me to the world so that I may be killed fighting alongside the Prophet ﷺ once again.' He said: 'It has already been decreed by Me that to it you shall not return.'"],[4906,"My father said to me: 'O my son, I do not know, perhaps I will be among the first to be struck down tomorrow, that being the day of Uhud. I enjoin you to take good care of Abdullah's daughters.' Then they met in battle, and he was struck down that day."],[4907,"When the fighting of Uhud drew near, my father called me at night and said: 'I do not consider myself anything but killed among the first of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to be killed. By Allah, I do not leave anyone more dear to me than you after the person of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I have a debt, so pay off my debt, and take good care of your sisters.' He said: So the next morning we arose, and he was the first to be killed. I buried him with another person in one grave, then my soul was not at ease to leave him with another in one grave, so I exhumed him after six months, and there he was, as on the day I laid him, except for his ear."],[4908,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'Indeed Allah, the Exalted, does not speak to anyone except from behind a veil, but He spoke to your father face to face and said: Wish upon Me.' And he mentioned the hadith."],[4909,"In Paradise we roam as we wish. I said to him: 'Were you not killed on the day of Badr?' He said: 'Yes, then I was brought back to life.' I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is martyrdom, O Abu Jabir.'"],[4910,"That he joined the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Its chain is obscure."],[4911,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say at the killing of Hanzala b. Abi Amir, after he and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith met when Shaddad b. al-Aswad overpowered him with the sword and killed him, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your companion is being washed by the angels.\" They asked his wife, and she said: \"He went out when he heard the alarm while he was junub.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"For that reason the angels washed him.\""],[4912,"\"Yes, for I saw his father on the day of Uhud brandishing his sword as a camel brandishes.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4913,"Muhammad b. Umar narrated to us."],[4914,"From his shaykhs."],[4915,"Sa'd, may Allah make your face sweat in the Fire. Then Sa'd lived after being struck by an arrow for about a month, until he passed judgment on Banu Qurayza by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and returned to the city of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then his wound burst open and he died at night. Jibril ﷺ came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said to him: \"Who is this for whom the gates of heaven were opened and the Throne of the Most Merciful shook?\" The Prophet ﷺ went out to Sa'd and found that he had died. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4916,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.\""],[4917,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said of Sa'd while he was being buried: \"This righteous servant—the Throne moved for him, and the gates of heaven were opened for him.\" Sahih."],[4918,"The Throne—meaning the bier—shook for love of meeting Allah. He said: And he raised his parents upon the Throne; its planks dislocated. He said: And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered his grave and was detained. When he came out, it was said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what detained you?\" He said: \"Sa'd was squeezed in the grave with a squeeze, so I called upon Allah to relieve him of it.\""],[4919,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Will your tears not cease and your grief depart? For your son is the first at whom Allah smiled and for whom the Throne shook.\" Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[4920,"The hypocrites said: \"How light his funeral is! That is only because of his judgment concerning Banu Qurayza.\" This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"No, rather the angels were carrying him.\""],[4921,"I said to him: \"Glory be to Allah! You are one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you have precedence—why do you weep over a woman?\" He uncovered his head and said: \"You have spoken truly. By the life of Allah, by Allah, it is not right for me to weep over anyone after Sa'd b. Mu'adh, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said.\" She said to him: \"And what did he say?\" He said: \"He said: 'The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.'\" She said: \"And he was walking between me and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[4922,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.\" He said: A man said to Jabir: \"But al-Bara' says: 'The bier shook.'\" He said: \"There were grudges between these two tribes, al-Aws and al-Khazraj. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The Throne of the Most Merciful shook for the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.'\""],[4923,"The Prophet ﷺ said: I entered Paradise and heard in it a recitation. I said, “Who is this?” They said, “Harithah b. al-Nu'man.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Thus is righteousness, thus is righteousness.”"],[4924,"Haritha, the son of my paternal aunt, went out as an observer on the day of Badr, and he did not go out to fight. An arrow struck him and killed him. My aunt came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, my son Haritha—if he is in Paradise, I will be patient and seek reward; otherwise, you will see what I do.” He said, “O mother of Haritha, indeed there are many gardens, and indeed Haritha is in the highest Firdaws.”"],[4925,"A man from the Romans struck Ja'far b. Abi Talib and cut him into two halves. One of his halves fell into a vineyard, and in his half were found thirty or thirty-some wounds. He had emigrated to the land of Abyssinia in the second emigration, and with him was his wife Asma' bt. 'Umays. He remained in the land of Abyssinia until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ emigrated to Madinah; then he emigrated to him while he was at Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I do not know which of the two I am more delighted about: the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Ja'far.” He said, “And Ja'far was given the kunya Abu 'Abd Allah.”"],[4926,"My father, who had nursed me, from Banu Murrah, informed me. He said: “It is as if I am looking at Ja'far b. Abi Talib on the day of Mu'tah. He dismounted from a horse of his and hamstrung it, then went forward and fought until he was killed.”"],[4927,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I entered Paradise last night and looked around in it, and there was Ja'far flying with the angels, and there was Hamzah reclining on a couch.”"],[4928,"“No one has worn sandals, nor put on shoes, nor ridden mounts, nor ridden the camel saddle after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ more excellent than Ja'far b. Abi Talib.”"],[4929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I saw Ja'far b. Abi Talib as an angel flying with the angels with two wings.”"],[4930,"From 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: “When the news of Ja'far's death came, we recognized grief on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[4931,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting and Asma' bt. 'Umays was near him, he returned the greeting and then said, “O Asma', this is Ja'far b. Abi Talib with Jibril, Mika'il, and Israfil. They greeted us, so return the greeting to them.” He had already informed me that he met the polytheists on such-and-such a day, three or four days before his passing before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ [perhaps meaning: before the news reached him]. He said: I met the polytheists, and I was struck in my body from my front with seventy-three wounds, between arrow shots, spear thrusts, and sword blows. Then I took the banner with my right hand, and it was cut off. Then I took it with my left hand, and it was cut off. So Allah compensated me for my hands with two wings with which I fly with Jibril and Mika'il. I descend from Paradise wherever I wish and eat of its fruits whatever I wish. Asma' said, “Congratulations to Ja'far for the good that Allah has granted him, but I fear that people will not believe it. So ascend the minbar and inform them.” He ascended the minbar, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, “O people, indeed Ja'far is with Jibril and Mika'il, and he has two wings with which Allah compensated him for his hands. He greeted me.” Then he informed them of how his affair was when he met the polytheists. And it became clear to the people after the day on which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed them that Ja'far had met them; therefore he was named al-Tayyar in Paradise. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I saw as if I entered Paradise, and I saw for Ja'far a degree above the degree of Zayd. I said, “I did not think that Zayd would be below anyone.” It was said to me, “O Muhammad, do you know by what Ja'far's degree was raised?” He said, I said, “No.” It was said, “By the kinship that is between you and him.”"],[4933,"Ja'far said, “I am more entitled to her, for her maternal aunt is with me.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “As for you, O Ja'far, you resemble me in my physical appearance and my character, and you are from my tree from which I am.” He said, “I am content, O Messenger of Allah, with that.” As for the girl, I judge her for Ja'far, for her maternal aunt is with him, and the maternal aunt is a mother. Abu Hurayrah used to say: The sky has not shaded a face more beloved to me after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than Ja'far b. Abi Talib, because of the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “You resemble me in my physical appearance and my character.”"],[4934,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: We are the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, the masters of the people of Paradise: I, 'Ali, Ja'far, Hamzah, al-Hasan, al-Husayn, and the Mahdi."],[4935,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived from Khaybar, Ja'far arrived from Abyssinia. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him and kissed his forehead, then said: \"By Allah, I do not know which of the two makes me happier: the conquest of Khaybar or the arrival of Ja'far.\" Isma'il b. Abi Khalid and Zakariyya b. Abi Za'idah transmitted it, as narrated to us by 'Ali b. 'Isa al-Hiri: Ibrahim b. Abi Talib narrated to us: Ibn Abi 'Umar narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Ibn Abi Khalid and Zakariyya from al-Sha'bi, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived from Khaybar, and he mentioned the hadith."],[4936,"You are an excellent people, were it not that you preceded us in emigration, for we are more virtuous than you. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; he carried your pedestrians and taught your ignorant, so we fled with our religion. She said: I will not return until I enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So I entered upon him, and she said: O Messenger of Allah, I met 'Umar, and he said such and such. He said: Rather, you have two emigrations: your emigration to Abyssinia and your emigration to Madinah."],[4937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Ja'far passed by me tonight in a company of angels, his wings dyed with blood, white of heart.\""],[4938,"\"We were at Mu'tah with Ja'far b. Abi Talib, and we found him among the slain. We found on him more than seventy wounds.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4939,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with Asma' bt. 'Umays near him, he returned the greeting and gestured with his hand, then said: \"O Asma', this is Ja'far b. Abi Talib with Jibril ﷺ and Mika'il; they passed by and greeted us, so return the greeting to them.\" And he told me that he met the polytheists on such and such a day, three or four before his passing before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: I met the polytheists, and I was struck in my body from my front with seventy-three wounds, between stabs and shots. I took the banner with my right hand, and it was cut off; then I took it with my left hand, and it was cut off. Allah compensated me for my hands with two wings with which I fly in Paradise with Jibril and Mika'il, may Allah's prayers be upon them, and I eat of its fruits whatever I wish. Asma' said: Congratulations to Ja'far for what Allah has granted him of good. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and informed the people. He said: It became clear to the people afterward what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had told them, so Ja'far was named al-Tayyar. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4941,"What we have is better for them. They agreed until he carried Jabalah and Asma' and left Zayd behind. Then horsemen from Tihamah, from Banu Fazarah, came and raided Tayyi', capturing Zayd and taking him to the market of 'Ukaz. The Prophet ﷺ saw him before he was sent, and said to Khadijah: \"O Khadijah, I saw in the market a boy of such and such description,\" describing intelligence, manners, and beauty. \"If I had money, I would buy him.\" She instructed Waraqah b. Nawfal, and he purchased him with her money. He said: \"O Khadijah, give me this boy willingly.\" She said: O Muhammad, I see a handsome boy, and I fear you may sell him or give him away. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O blessed one, I only intend to adopt him as a son.\" She said: Yes, O Muhammad. So he raised him and adopted him, and he was called Zayd b. Muhammad. Then a man from the tribe came and looked at Zayd and recognized him. He said: You are Zayd b. Harithah. He said: No, I am Zayd b. Muhammad. He said: No, rather you are Zayd b. Harithah, from the description of your father and your paternal uncles and maternal uncles, such and such. They have exhausted their bodies and spent their wealth in seeking you. Zayd said: [al-tawil] I long for my people even though I am far away, for I am a resident of the House near the sacred sites. And restrain yourselves from the way that has grieved you, and do not act in the land like wild camels. For I, by Allah's praise, am in the best of families, the choice of Ma'add, generation after generation. Harithah said, when it reached him: [al-tawil] I wept for Zayd and did not know what happened to him. Is he alive, to be hoped for, or has death come upon him? By Allah, I do not know, though I ask: Did the plain swallow you or the mountain? Would that I knew if time would bring you back, for my sufficiency from this world is your return to me. The sun reminds me of him at its rising, and his memory comes to me when the evening darkens. And when the winds blow, they stir his memory, so how long are my sorrows for him, and how great my fear! I will exert the camels' utmost in the land, and I will not tire of wandering unless the camels tire. So that he may come, or my death may come to me, for every man perishes even if hope deceives him. Harithah b. Sharahil came to Makkah with his brothers and family, and he came to the Prophet ﷺ in the courtyard of the Ka'bah among a group of his companions, including Zayd b. Harithah. When they looked at Zayd, they recognized him and he recognized them, but he did not get up for them out of respect for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said to him: O Zayd, but he did not answer them. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Who are these, O Zayd?\" He said: O Messenger of Allah, this is my father, this is my paternal uncle, this is my brother, and these are my kin. The Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"Get up and greet them, O Zayd.\" He got up and greeted them, and they greeted him. Then they said to him: Come with us, O Zayd. He said: I do not want a substitute for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor anyone else. They said: O Muhammad, we will give you blood money for this boy, so name whatever you wish, and we will bring it to you. He said: \"I ask you to bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that I am the seal of His prophets and messengers, and I will send him with you.\" They hesitated, wavered, and stammered, then said: Will you accept from us what we offered of dinars? He said to them: \"Here is another matter: I have placed the affair in his hands. If he wishes, let him get up, and if he wishes, let him enter.\" They said: Is there anything left? They said: O Zayd, Muhammad has now permitted you, so go with us. He said: Far be it, far be it! I do not want a substitute for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor do I prefer over him any father or son. They tried to persuade him, coax him, and appeal to his sympathy, and they told him of their longing for him, but he refused and swore that he would not follow them. Harithah said: As for me, I will support you with my own self. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and messenger. The rest refused."],[4942,"Harithah b. Sharahil, when he lost his son Zayd, wept for him and said: I wept for Zayd and did not know what happened. Then he mentioned the poem in full. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4943,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, send my brother Zayd with me. He said: \"Here he is; if he wishes, I will not prevent him.\" Zayd said: No, by Allah, I will not choose anyone over you. Jabalah said: I said: My brother's opinion is better than mine. \"Sahih al-isnad, though they did not include it, and it is a witness for the preceding hadith.\" Sahih."],[4944,"From Ibn Ishaq: \"Among those who witnessed Badr with the Prophet ﷺ was Zayd b. Harithah b. Sharahil al-Kalbi, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[4945,"\"The first to embrace Islam was Zayd b. Harithah.\""],[4946,"I heard 'A'ishah say: \"When Zayd b. Harithah, Ja'far b. Abi Talib, and 'Abdullah b. Rawahah were killed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat weeping for them, and grief was evident in him.\""],[4947,"Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us."],[4948,"Aisha used to say, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never sent Zayd b. Haritha in an army without appointing him as its commander. Had he lived after him, he would have appointed him as his successor.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it."],[4949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do not blame us for loving Zayd,\" meaning Ibn Haritha. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[4950,"The Messenger of Allah said, \"The best commanders of expeditions is Zayd b. Haritha; he is the most equitable among them in distributing spoils and the most just among them toward his subjects.\" Its chain contains al-Waqidi."],[4951,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out, with me riding behind him, toward one of the stone idols. We slaughtered a sheep for him and placed it in the oven. When it was cooked, we took it out and put it in our provision basket. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proceeded riding with me behind him during the hot days of Makkah, until we reached the upper part of the valley. There he met Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl. One of them greeted the other with the greeting of the Jahiliyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Why do I see your people have rejected you?\" He replied, \"By Allah, that is because of a change in a matter between me and them, but I see them are upon misguidance.\" He said, \"So I went out seeking this religion until I came to the rabbis of Yathrib. I found them worshipping Allah and associating partners with Him. I said to myself, 'This is not the religion I seek.' Then I went out until I came to the rabbis of Ayla. I found them worshipping Allah and associating partners with Him. I said to myself, 'This is not the religion I seek.' Then a rabbi among the rabbis of Syria said to me, 'You are asking about a religion in which we know no one who worships Allah by it except an old man in al-Jazirah.' So I went out until I came to him and told him what I had set out for. He said, 'Everyone you have seen is upon misguidance. You are asking about a religion which is the religion of Allah and the religion of His angels. A prophet has emerged in your land, or is about to emerge, calling to it. Return to him, believe him, follow him, and have faith in what he brings.' So I returned, but I did not comprehend anything after that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made the camel he was riding kneel down. Then we presented to him the provision basket containing the roasted meat. He said, 'What is this?' We said, 'This is a sheep we slaughtered for such-and-such an idol.' He said, 'I do not eat what is slaughtered for other than Allah.' It was an idol made of brass called Isaf and Na'ilah, which the polytheists would touch when they performed tawaf. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed tawaf and I performed tawaf with him. When I passed by it, I touched it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do not touch it.' Zayd said, 'We performed tawaf. I said to myself, \"I will certainly touch it to see what he says.\" So I touched it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Were you not forbidden?\" Zayd said, 'By the One who honored him and revealed the Book to him, I did not touch an idol after that, until Allah honored him with what He honored him and revealed the Book to him.' Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl died before the Prophet ﷺ was sent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'He will come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation by himself.' It is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it. Whoever reflects on this hadith will recognize the virtue of Zayd and his preceding in Islam before the call. According to the condition of Muslim."],[4952,"Ja'far said, 'I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Ali said, 'I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Zayd said, 'I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'So take us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said, 'I went out, then returned and said, \"This is Ja'far, Ali, and Zayd b. Haritha seeking permission to enter.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Give them permission.\" So they entered and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have come to ask you who is the most beloved of people to you?\" He said, \"Fatimah.\" They said, \"We ask you about men.\" He said, \"As for you, O Ja'far, your physical appearance resembles my physical appearance and your character resembles my character. You are from me and from my tree. As for you, O Ali, you are my brother and the father of my children, from me and to me. As for you, O Zayd, you are my client, from me and to me, and the most beloved of the people to me.\""],[4953,"From the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , it is narrated that, \"In the early stages of revelation, he was taught the methods of ablution, prayer, and the principles of Islam.\" Al-Dhahabi excluded this from his summary due to its weakness."],[4954,"Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us."],[4955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he did not go on a campaign, would not give his weapons except to Ali or Zayd."],[4956,"I participated in seven campaigns with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and nine campaigns with Zayd b. Haritha. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to appoint him as our commander. It is authentic according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. It is in al-Bukhari among the three-narrator chains."],[4957,"The Prophet ﷺ never sent Zayd on a military expedition without appointing him as commander over them. It is authentic according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[4958,"Two suits of clothing were gifted to the Prophet ﷺ. He took one of them and gave the other to Zayd. It is authentic according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4959,"Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us."],[4960,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked, \"Who is your leader, O Bani Salamah?\" They replied, \"Al-Jadd ibn Qays, except that he is stingy.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What disease is worse than stinginess? Rather, your leader should be Bashir ibn Al-Bara' ibn Ma'rur.\" This hadith is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but he (Muslim) did not include it in his book."],[4961,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during his illness in which he passed away. I said, 'May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what do you suspect about yourself? For I do not suspect for my son anything except the food he ate with you at Khaybar.' Her son was Bishr b. al-Bara' b. Ma'roor, who died before the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And I do not suspect anything else. This is the time of the severing of my aorta.' It is authentic according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4962,"A Jewish woman invited the Prophet ﷺ and some of his companions to a roasted sheep. When they sat down to eat, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took a morsel, put it down, then said to them, \"Hold back! This sheep is poisoned.\" He said to the Jewish woman, \"Woe to you! For what reason did you poison me?\" She said, \"I wanted to know if you were a prophet, for it would not harm you; and if you were otherwise, to relieve the people of you.\" Bishr b. al-Bara' ate from it and died, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ killed her. \"Sahih according to Muslim's criterion, but they did not include it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4963,"\"Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, Kanaz b. al-Husayn, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, died in Madinah during the caliphate of Abu Bakr. It is said that the one who died in Madinah during the caliphate of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq in the year twelve was Marthad b. Abi Marthad.\" Others said he was killed at Ajnadayn."],[4964,"\"Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them.\""],[4965,"From 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib.\""],[4966,"I heard Mus'ab b. 'Abd Allah al-Zubayri say, \"Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi died in the year twelve of the Hijrah, at the age of sixty-six.\""],[4967,"\"Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi's name is Kanaz b. Husayn b. Yarbu' b. 'Amr b. Yarbu' b. Kharashah b. Sa'd b. Tarif b. Jallan b. Ghanm b. A'sar b. Sa'd b. Qays 'Aylan.\""],[4968,"\"Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, Kanaz b. al-Husayn, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, died and was buried in Madinah during the caliphate of Abu Bakr in the year twelve.\""],[4969,"\"Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them.\""],[4970,"I heard Wathilah b. al-Asqa', the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, say, \"Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them.\" Sadaqah b. Khalid concurred with him on it."],[4971,"\"Do not sit on graves and do not pray toward them.\""],[4972,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him as a guard. When the face of dawn appeared, he came forward. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This companion of yours has come, interrupting you.\" Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him, \"Did you dismount from your horse tonight?\" He said, \"No, by Allah, O Prophet of Allah, except for a call of nature.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not mind if you do no work after this.\" Yahya b. Hamzah said, \"I mentioned this hadith to Abu 'Amr al-Awza'i, and al-Awza'i told me that Hassan b. 'Atiyyah used to narrate it. This is a noble virtue of Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi, transmitted solely by the sons of Yahya b. Hamzah al-Dimashqi from their fathers from al-Awza'i, and all of them are trustworthy; its narrators are trustworthy.\""],[4973,"On the day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had two horses: one belonged to Marthad b. Abi Marthad and the other to al-Zubayr. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[4974,"That some people from 'Adal and al-Qarah—and they are two tribes of Jadilah—came to the Prophet ﷺ after Uhud and said, \"In our land there is Islam, so send with us a number of your Companions to teach us the Qur'an and instruct us in Islam.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent with them six men, among them Marthad b. Abi Marthad, the ally of Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, and he was their leader; Khalid b. al-Bukayr al-Laythi, the ally of Banu 'Adi; 'Abd Allah b. Tariq al-Zafari; Zayd b. al-Dathinah; Khubayb b. 'Adi; and 'Asim b. Thabit b. Abi al-Aflah. They set out, with Marthad b. Abi Marthad as their leader, until when they were at al-Raji', Hudhayl came upon them. The people were not startled in their camps except by men with swords in their hands who had surrounded them with them. So the people took up their swords to fight, but they said, \"By Allah, we do not want to kill you, but we want to capture some of the people of Makkah for ransom. You have the covenant of Allah and His pledge.\" As for 'Asim, Marthad, and Khalid, they fought until they were killed, and they said, \"By Allah, we will never accept from a polytheist a covenant or a pact ever.\" [Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness]"],[4975,"He, i.e., Marthad b. Abi Marthad, was present on the Day of Badr on a horse called al-Subul."],[4976,"\"If it pleases you that your prayer be accepted, let the best among you lead you in prayer, for they are your delegation between you and your Lord, exalted is He.\""],[4977,"From 'Urwah, \"In the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Jubar b. Sakhr b. Umayyah b. Khansa' b. Sinan.\""],[4978,"\"Jubar b. Sakhr died in Madinah in the year thirty, and he was sixty-two years old.\""],[4979,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"We have been forbidden to look at our private parts.\" [Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis]"],[4980,"The Islam of Abu Hudhayfah existed before the Prophet Muhammad (Peace be upon him) entered the home of Arqam. He was one of those who migrated twice. This narration was deleted by Al-Dhahabi due to its weakness."],[4981,"\"Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah was a tall man with a handsome face, and his mother was Umm Safwan.\""],[4982,"\"Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah was killed as a martyr on the Day of Yamamah.\""],[4983,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the Day of Badr, \"Whoever of you encounters al-'Abbas, let him hold back from him, for he has come out under compulsion.\" Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah said, \"Shall we kill our fathers, brothers, and kinsmen, and leave al-'Abbas? By Allah, I will certainly strike him with the sword.\" This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said to 'Umar b. al-Khattab, \"O Abu Hafs.\" 'Umar said, \"It was the first day he called me by the kunya Abu Hafs.\" \"The face of the uncle of the Messenger of Allah is to be struck with the sword?\" 'Umar said, \"Let me strike his neck, for he has become a hypocrite.\" And Abu Hudhayfah used to say, \"I am not safe from that word I said, and I remain fearful until Allah expiates it from me through martyrdom.\" He said: So he was killed as a martyr on the Day of Yamamah. [Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it]"],[4984,"Mu'awiyah entered upon Abu Hashim. [What makes you weep? Is it pain or desire for the world?] He said, \"No, indeed I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ make a covenant with me.\" I said, \"What is it?\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Perhaps a time will overtake you when they will gather a host and you will be in it.' And I have gathered as he said ﷺ.\" [In the hadith there is an obscenity, which is that Abu Hudhayfah 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah was martyred before Mu'awiyah accepted Islam, and Mu'awiyah said this statement to his uncle Abu Hashim b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah on the Day of Siffin.]"],[4985,"Mu'awiyah entered upon Abu Hashim."],[4986,"Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, his name is Hushaym, and it is said the name of Abu Hudhayfah is Hisl."],[4987,"He erred in this, for al-Yaman, the father of Hudhayfah, was nicknamed Hisl, and it is said his name was 'Isl."],[4988,"He was called Hisl or 'Isl, and it is said his name was Miqsam."],[4989,"And it is said Miqsam."],[4990,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered (them) into the well, so they were thrown into it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood over them and said, “O people of the well, have you found what your Lord promised to be true? Indeed, I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.” His companions said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to people who are dead?” He said, “They have come to know that what your Lord promised you is true.” When he ordered (them), they were dragged, and a look of displeasure was recognized on the face of Abu Hudhayfah b. 'Utbah while his father was being dragged to the well. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “O Abu Hudhayfah, by Allah, it seems that what has befallen your father has distressed you.” He said, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not doubt Allah or His Messenger, but if he had been forbearing, upright, and of sound judgment, I had hoped that he would not die until Allah ﷻ guided him to Islam. When I saw that that hope had passed and he fell where he fell, it saddened me.” He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for good for him. (Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it) according to the condition of Muslim."],[4991,"Qutbah b. 'Amir b. Hadidah was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Badr, and he is the one about whom it was revealed: {It is not righteousness that you enter houses from their backs} [al-Baqarah: 189]. And his brother was Yazid b. 'Amir b. Hadidah, and Yazid was called Abu al-Mundhir."],[4992,"From elders of his people, they said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in the season in which he met the party from the Ansar, and he presented himself to the tribes of the Arabs. Then they turned away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returning to their lands, having believed and affirmed—among them Qutbah b. 'Amir b. Hadidah.”"],[4993,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Qutbah b. 'Amir b. Hadidah with twenty men to a clan of Khath'am in Safar of the year seven.”"],[4994,"Take the Qur'an from four: from 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, and from Mu'adh, and from Ubayy, and from Salim the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah."],[4995,"Musa b. 'Utbah said, “He is Salim b. Ma'qil from the people of Istakhr.” Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[4996,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the night prayer. Then I came, and he said to me, “Where were you?” I said, “We were listening to the recitation of a man among your companions in the mosque; I have never heard a voice or recitation like his from any of your companions.” He stood up and I stood with him until he listened to him, then he turned to me and said, “This is Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah. Praise be to Allah who has placed in my nation someone like this.” (Sahih according to the condition of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it) thus according to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[4997,"The wife of Abu Hudhayfah mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, used to enter upon her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, “Breastfeed him.” So she breastfed him after he had witnessed Badr, and he used to enter upon her. (Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it) according to the condition of Muslim."],[4998,"Umm Salim al-Ansariyyah made Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, a sa'ibah for Allah, and he was killed on the Day of Yamamah. She inherited weapons and a horse, so 'Umar b. al-Khattab sent to her: “Take it, for you are the most entitled of the people to it.” She said, “I have no need of it; I had made it for Allah the Exalted when I freed him.” So 'Umar took it and made it in the path of Allah ﷻ. This is not authentic."],[4999,"When Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, was killed, they said, \"A quarter of the Qur'an has gone.\""],[5000,"He said to his companions, \"Make wishes.\" Some of them said, \"I wish that this house were filled with gold and I would spend it in the cause of Allah and give charity.\" A man said, \"I wish that it were filled with chrysolite and jewels and I would spend it in the cause of Allah and give charity.\" Then Umar said, \"Make wishes.\" They said, \"We do not know, O Commander of the Faithful.\" Umar said, \"I wish that it were filled with men like Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah, Muadh b. Jabal, Salim the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfah, and Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman.\""],[5001,"Zaid ibn Al-Khattab carried the banner of the Muslims on the day of Yamamah, and the Muslims were exposed until Hanifah became visible among the men. Then Zaid ibn Al-Khattab began to say, \"As for the men, there are no more men, and as for the men, there are no more men.\" He then shouted at the top of his voice, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You from the flight of my companions, and I disassociate myself from what Musaylimah and Muhkam ibn At-Tufayl have brought.\" He held onto the banner and advanced with it to confront the enemy, and he struck with his sword until Rahmah ibn Al-Khattab, may Allah have mercy on him, was killed. The banner fell, and it was taken by Salim, the servant of Abu Hudhayfah. The Muslims said, \"O Salim, we fear that we will be betrayed by you.\" He replied, \"Woe to the one carrying the Quran, if you are given to me.\" Zaid ibn Al-Khattab was killed in the twelfth year of Hijrah."],[5002,"Ibn Umar was the fifth of a group of five companions in the expedition against Musaylimah, and they killed other than him. It was said: Zayd b. al-Khattab, Abdullah b. Makhramah, and two others."],[5003,"\"He said, 'Woe to you! You have killed my brother, and whenever the cool breeze blows, I always remember him.' Adh-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the summary.\""],[5004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when Ukkashah was forty years old, and he was killed a year after that at Buzakhah during the caliphate of Abu Bakr in the year twelve. Ukkashah was one of the most handsome of people."],[5005,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The first group to enter Paradise will have faces shining like the full moon on a night of a lunar eclipse. Then those who follow them will have faces as bright as the brightest star in the sky.\" Ukasha ibn Muhsin stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me one of them.\" He said, \"O Allah, make him one of them.\" Another person stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to make me one of them.\" He said, \"Ukasha has already reached that position.\""],[5006,"We were the vanguard, two hundred horsemen, and over us was Zayd b. al-Khattab. Thabit b. Aqram and Ukkashah b. Mihsan were ahead of us. When we passed by the two of them slain, we moved on, and Khalid and the Muslims were behind us. They stopped at the two of them, and Khalid ordered that a grave be dug for them, and he buried them with their blood."],[5007,"Ma'n b. Adi b. al-Jadd b. al-Ajlan, an ally of Banu Amr b. Awf, witnessed the Aqabah pledge, Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the battle scenes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was martyred on the day of al-Yamamah during the caliphate of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ."],[5008,"Ma'n b. Adi at al-Yamamah on the day of Musaylimah the Liar."],[5009,"And he was called Abu al-Rabi'."],[5010,"Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Bishr b. Umarah said: \"He was given the kunya Abu al-Rabi'. He accepted Islam in Madinah at the hands of Mus'ab b. Umayr, and that was before the conversion of Sa'd b. Muadh. Abbad b. Bishr witnessed Badr and was among those who killed Ka'b b. al-Ashraf. He also witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the battle scenes with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He also witnessed the day of al-Yamamah, and on that day he showed great valor, hardship, and direct engagement in fighting until he was martyred. That was in the year twelve, and he was forty-five years old.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5011,"Abbad b. Abdullah b. al-Zubayr: By Allah, my father named me Abbad only because of him."],[5012,"From his shaykhs, they said: \"The name of Abu Dujanah is Simak b. Kharashah b. Lawdhan b. Abd Wadd b. Zayd b. Tha'labah b. al-Khazraj. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Utbah b. Ghazwan. Abu Dujanah witnessed Badr and Uhud and stood firm on that day with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him unto death. He witnessed al-Yamamah and was among those who participated in the killing of Musaylimah, and Abu Dujanah was martyred on that day.\""],[5013,"The Prophet ﷺ took a sword on the day of Uhud while his Companions were around him and said, \"Who will take this sword?\" They stretched out their hands, each saying, \"I will, I will.\" He said, \"Who will take it with its right?\" The people hesitated. Simak Abu Dujanah said, \"I will take it with its right.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed it to him, and with it he split the heads of the polytheists on that day. [According to the condition of Muslim]"],[5014,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ presented a sword on the day of Uhud and said, “Who will take this sword with its due?” I stood up and said, “I, O Messenger of Allah.” He turned away from me, then said, “Who will take this sword with its due?” I said, “I, O Messenger of Allah.” He turned away from me, then said, “Who will take this sword with its due?” Abu Dujanah Simak b. Kharashah stood up and said, “I will take it, O Messenger of Allah, with its due. What is its due?” He said, “That you do not kill a Muslim with it and do not flee with it from a disbeliever.” He said, “So he handed it to him. And whenever he intended to fight, he would signal with a band.” He said, “I said, ‘I will certainly watch him today to see what he does.’” He said, “So he began not to encounter anything without tearing it apart and ripping it open, until he reached some women at the foot of the mountain, who had tambourines with them. Among them was a woman saying [in rajaz meter]: ‘We are the daughters of Tariq; we walk upon cushions. If you advance, we embrace and spread the cushions; or if you retreat, we part, a parting without love.’” He said, “He raised the sword toward a woman to strike her, then held back from her. When the fighting was over, I said to him, ‘I saw all that you did, except that you raised the sword against the woman and did not strike her.’ He said, ‘By Allah, I honored the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ too much to kill a woman with it.’” [Its chain is authentic, but they (al-Bukhari and Muslim) did not include it.] Sahih."],[5015,"From 'Urwah: “In naming those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu 'Adi: Tha'labah b. 'Anamah b. 'Adi, and he was martyred on the day of the Trench.”"],[5016,"Tha'labah b. 'Anamah came as a delegate to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting. He greeted, and on his finger was a ring of gold, so he did not return the greeting. Then he greeted again, and he did not return it. It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, Tha'labah greets you three times and you do not return it.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Do you not see him splashing my face with a live coal of fire in his hand?' So Tha'labah threw away the ring. Haram b. 'Uthman is perishing."],[5017,"From Ibn Ishaq: “In naming those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Zurayq b. 'Amir, then from Banu al-'Ajlan: Rafi' b. Malik b. al-'Ajlan al-Zurqi.”"],[5018,"I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I sneezed, and I said, 'Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, blessed therein, blessed upon it, as our Lord loves and is pleased with.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished the prayer, he turned and said, 'Who spoke during the prayer?' I said, 'I, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'How did you say?' He said, I said, 'Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, blessed therein, blessed upon it, as our Lord loves and is pleased with.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, more than thirty angels vied to ascend with it.' Muhammad b. Salih b. Hani' narrated to us; Ahmad b. Salamah narrated to us; Muhammad b. Yahya narrated to us; Qutaybah b. Sa'id narrated to us, and we did not write it except from him, and he mentioned the hadith similarly. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5019,"On the day of Badr, the people gathered around Umayyah b. Khalaf. I approached him and noticed a piece of his armor had broken from under his armpit. He said, 'I thrust at him with the sword in that spot and killed him. I was shot with an arrow on the day of Badr and it put out my eye.' 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat in it and supplicated for me, and it never harmed me thereafter.' Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. 'Abd al-'Aziz b. 'Imran—they weakened him."],[5020,"I set out on the day of Badr, and we lost the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The groups called to one another, 'Is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among you?' They stopped until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and with him was 'Ali b. Abi Talib. They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we lost you.' He said, 'Abu Hasan found a cramp in his stomach, so I stayed behind for him.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5021,"'Urwah narrated to us: “In naming those who witnessed the 'Aqabah from the Ansar, from Banu Zurayq: Rifa'ah b. Rafi' b. Malik b. al-'Ajlan b. Zurayq, and he was a naqib. He also mentioned him in naming those who witnessed Badr.”"],[5022,"“Rifa'ah b. Rafi' b. Malik b. al-'Ajlan b. 'Amr b. 'Amir b. Zurayq b. 'Abd Harithah. His mother and the mother of his brother Khallad b. Rafi' were Umm Malik bt. Ubayy b. Salul. Rifa'ah b. Rafi' died when Mu'awiyah took power.”"],[5023,"“Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas b. Imri' al-Qays b. Malik, the khatib of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and was killed as a martyr on the day of Yamamah.”"],[5024,"“Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas was martyred on the day of Yamamah. Abu Bakr had put him in command of the Ansar along with Khalid b. al-Walid ؓ.”"],[5025,"I heard Ahmad b. Sayyar say, “The kunyah of Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas is Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.”"],[5026,"What an excellent man Abu Bakr is! What an excellent man Umar is! What an excellent man Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah is! What an excellent man Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas is! What an excellent man Muadh ibn Jabal is! What an excellent man Muadh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh is! What a wretched man so-and-so and so-and-so are—seven men whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named, but Suhayl did not name them for us. Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of Muslim."],[5027,"When it was the Day of al-Yamama, I came to Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas while he was applying hanut (perfuming himself for burial). I said, 'O uncle, do you not see what the people are facing?' He put on his shrouds, then advanced saying, 'Now, now!' He began saying about the hanut, like this—and the Ansari gestured to his shin, like this—in the faces of the people, fighting the people: 'Evil is what you have accustomed your peers to! It was not like this that we used to fight alongside the Prophet ﷺ.' He fought until he was killed. Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5028,"Thabit ibn Qays gave a speech when the Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah, saying, 'We will protect you from what we protect ourselves and our children from. So what is for us?' He said, 'Paradise.' He said, 'We are content.' Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5029,"O Messenger of Allah, I fear that I have perished. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'And why?' He said, 'Allah forbade us to love being praised for what we have not done, and I find that I love praise. He forbade us from arrogance, and I find that I love beauty. He forbade us from raising our voices above your voice, and I have a loud voice.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Thabit, are you not content to live praiseworthy, be killed as a martyr, and enter Paradise?' He said, 'Yes indeed, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Then he lived praiseworthy and was killed as a martyr on the day of Musaylima the Liar.' Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it with this wording. Muslim alone included the hadith of Hammad ibn Salama and Sulayman ibn al-Mughira from Thabit from Anas, who said: When it was revealed, 'Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet' (Quran 49:2), Thabit ibn Qays came, and he mentioned the hadith in abbreviated form. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5030,"Thabit ibn Qays came on the Day of al-Yamama, having applied hanut and put on his shrouds, while his companions had fled. He said, 'O Allah, I declare my innocence to You of what these people have brought, and I apologize to You for what these people have done. Evil is what you have accustomed your peers to! Leave us and our peers alone for a while.' Then he charged and fought for a while until he was killed. His coat of mail had been stolen, and a man saw him in a dream, and he said, 'My coat of mail is in a pot under a saddle at such-and-such a place,' and he made some bequests. So they searched for the coat of mail and found it where he had said, and they carried out his bequest."],[5031,"When Allah revealed to His Messenger ﷺ, 'Do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet' (Quran 49:2), and the verse, 'And Allah does not love every arrogant boaster' (Quran 57:23), my father sat in his house weeping. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ missed him and asked about his situation. He said, 'I am a man with a loud voice, and I fear that my deeds have become worthless.' He said, 'Rather, you will live praiseworthy, die as a martyr, and Allah will admit you to Paradise in peace.' When it was the Day of al-Yamama with Khalid ibn al-Walid, he was martyred. A man among the Muslims saw him in a dream, and he said, 'When I was killed, a man among the Muslims took my coat of mail and hid it at the far end of the army. It is with him, and he has placed a cooking pot over the coat of mail and put a saddle on the pot. Go to the commander and inform him, and beware of saying this is a dream and thus wasting it. When you come to Madinah, go and tell the Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I owe such-and-such a debt, and that my slave so-and-so is free. Beware of saying this is a dream and thus wasting it.' He said, 'So he went to him and informed him of the news, and he found the matter as he had described. He went to Abu Bakr and informed him, and he carried out his bequest. We know of no one after his death whose bequest was carried out except Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5032,"Abu al-As ibn al-Rabi' ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf ibn Qusayy. Abu al-As's name was Miqsam, and his mother was Hala bint Khuwaylid ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy. His maternal aunt was Khadija bint Khuwaylid, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ had married him to his daughter Zaynab before Islam. She bore him Ali and Umama. Ali died while young, and Umama remained until Ali ibn Abi Talib married her after the death of Fatima. Abu al-As was among those who witnessed Badr with the polytheists. He was captured by Abdullah ibn Jubayr ibn al-Nu'man al-Ansari. When the people of Makkah sent to ransom their captives, his brother Amr ibn al-Rabi' came to ransom Abu al-As with wealth that Zaynab had given him. I have mentioned previously what occurred between him and Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, until Zaynab was martyred. Now listen to the good outcome of Abu al-As and the excellence of his Islam and his migration to Madinah until he died in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5033,"From Aisha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, she said: When the people of Makkah sent to ransom their captives, Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sent to ransom Abu al-As with wealth, and she sent with it a necklace that Khadija had given her when she married Abu al-As. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw that necklace, he felt great tenderness and said, 'If you see fit to release her captive and return to her what belongs to her, then do so.' They said, 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' So they released him and returned to her what belonged to her. Abu al-As remained in his polytheism until just before the conquest of Makkah, when he went out with merchandise to Syria with funds belonging to Quraysh that they had entrusted to him. When he finished his trade and was returning, a raiding party of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met him. It is said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was the one who dispatched the raiding party against the caravan in which Abu al-As was returning from Syria. They were one hundred and seventy riders, led by Zayd ibn Haritha, in Jumada al-Ula in the year six of the Hijra. They seized the goods in that caravan and captured some of its people, but Abu al-As eluded them by flight. When the raiding party arrived with what they had taken, Abu al-As came by night seeking his property until he entered upon Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and sought her protection, and she granted it. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out for the dawn prayer and said the takbir, the people said the takbir with him."],[5034,"Dirar ibn al-Azwar the poet—the name of al-Azwar was Malik ibn Aws ibn Jadhima ibn Rabi'a ibn Malik ibn Tha'laba ibn Asad ibn Khuzayma. Dirar was a horseman and a poet. He witnessed the Day of al-Yamama and fought the fiercest fighting until both his legs were cut off. He then kneeled on his knees and fought on, and the horses trampled him until death overcame him."],[5035,"Dirar ibn al-Azwar al-Asadi was killed on the Day of Ajnadayn."],[5036,"I brought the Prophet ﷺ a milch camel from my family. He said, 'Milk it.' I went to exhaust it (by milking fully), and he said, 'Do not exhaust it; leave some milk for the calf.' Sahih isnad. Nothing else is preserved from Dirar from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As for his virtue, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed for him when he recited his poem to him, which..."],[5037,"When Dirar ibn al-Azwar embraced Islam, he came to the Prophet ﷺ and began reciting [meter: al-mutaqarib]: 'I have abandoned gambling arrows and the music of singing-girls, and wine in fervor and supplication. And my charge of the fine horse in the thick of battle, and my striving against the Muslims in fighting. Jamila said, \"You have scattered us and cast your family to the far north.\" O Lord, may I not be cheated in my bargain, for I have sold my family and wealth for my faith.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Your bargain is not cheated, O Dirar.' Sahih."],[5038,"Abu Kabshah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died in the year thirteen (AH)."],[5039,"From his teachers, they said: Abu Kabshah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, his name was Sulaym, and he was among those born in the land of Daws. Abu Kabshah was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Badr, Uhud, and all the battles. He died on the first day of 'Umar b. al-Khattab's caliphate, which was Tuesday, eight nights remaining of Jumada al-Ula, in the year thirteen of the Hijrah. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5040,"Among those who were present at Badr from Banu Hashim b. 'Abd Manaf was Abu Kabshah, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5041,"Muhammad b. 'Umar narrated to us."],[5042,"I followed Muhammad and I submitted to Allah, the Lord of the worlds, may His mention be glorious. Then his mother said: \"Indeed, no one has more right to be supported and helped by you than your cousin, Ibn Khalik. By Allah, if we were capable of doing what men can do, we would have followed him and protected him.\" So I said, \"Oh my mother, what prevents you from submitting and following him? Indeed, your brother Hamza has already submitted.\" She said, \"I will see what my sisters do, then I will decide whether to join them.\" I said, \"I ask you by Allah, won't you go to him, greet him and believe in him, and testify that there is no god except Allah?\" She said, \"Indeed, I testify that there is no god except Allah, and I testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.\" After that, she pledged her allegiance to the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ verbally and encouraged her son to support him and follow his orders. This statement is reported to be authentic but not compiled in the collection of Sahih Al-Bukhari."],[5043,"Concerning his religion, and he kept close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. His son 'Amr b. Sa'id remained upon his religion. When 'Amr accepted Islam and joined his brother Khalid in the land of Abyssinia, with him was his wife Fatimah bt. Safwan b. Umayyah."],[5044,"Khalid b. Sa'id, Aban b. Sa'id, and 'Amr b. Sa'id were among the foremost in Islam. Uhayhah and al-'As, the two sons of Sa'id b. al-'As, were killed on the day of Badr as disbelievers; both of them were killed by 'Ali b. Abi Talib, as I mentioned in the account of Khalid b. Sa'id."],[5045,"Hisham b. al-'As: his mother was Harmalah bt. Hisham b. al-Mughirah b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Umar b. Makhzum."],[5046,"Hisham b. al-'As b. Wa'il b. Hashim b. Sa'id b. Sahm. His mother's name was Harmalah bt. Hisham b. al-Mughirah. Hisham was an early Muslim in Makkah, before his brother 'Amr. He migrated to the land of Abyssinia. Then he came to Makkah when he heard of the Prophet's ﷺ migration to Madinah and wanted to join him, but his father and his people detained him in Makkah until he came to the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah after the Battle of the Trench. He then witnessed all the battles after that. He was younger than his brother 'Amr b. al-'As."],[5047,"Hisham b. al-'As b. Wa'il was a righteous man. On the day of Ajnadayn, he saw some of the Muslims retreating from their enemy, so he threw off his helmet and said: 'O assembly of Muslims, these uncircumcised ones have no endurance against the sword, so do as I do.' Then he plunged into their midst, killing a number of them, and advanced against the enemy, shouting: 'To me, O assembly of Muslims, to me! I am Hisham b. al-'As b. Wa'il. Are you fleeing from Paradise?' until he was killed."],[5048,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The two sons of al-'As are believers: Hisham and 'Amr.' Sahih according to Muslim's criterion, but they did not record it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5049,"We used to say that there is no repentance for anyone who abandons his religion after accepting Islam and knowing it. Then Allah revealed concerning them: 'O My servants who have transgressed against themselves, do not despair of the mercy of Allah' [al-Zumar 53]. I wrote it with my own hand and sent it to Hisham b. al-'As b. Wa'il. He cried out with it, then mounted his camel and joined Madinah. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Bashir is munkar al-hadith."],[5050,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, 'Ikrimah b. Abi Jahl fled. His wife, Umm Hakim bt. al-Harith b. Hisham, was a sensible woman who had accepted Islam. She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for protection for her husband, and he instructed her to bring him back. She went out seeking him and said to him: 'I have come to you from the most upholding of people, the most righteous of people, and the best of people. I have sought protection for you, and he has granted you protection.' So he returned with her. When he drew near to Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: 'Ikrimah b. Abi Jahl will come to you as a believer and an emigrant, so do not insult his father, for insulting the dead hurts the living and does not reach the dead.' When he reached the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ rejoiced and sprang up to his feet out of joy at his arrival. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5051,"Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl fled on the day of the conquest heading to Yemen. Umm Hakim bt. al-Harith b. Hisham came forward—she was at that time a Muslim and married to Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl—and sought permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to go after her husband, and he granted her permission and gave him security. She set out with a Byzantine servant of hers, and he tried to seduce her, but she kept enticing him and drawing near to him until she reached some people from Makkah, then sought their help against him, and they bound him. She caught up with her husband in part of Tihamah, and he had boarded a ship. When he sat in it, he called upon al-Lat and al-Uzza. The people of the ship said: No one here may call upon anything except Allah alone sincerely. Ikrimah said: By Allah, if He is alone in the sea, then He is alone on land. I swear by Allah I will return to Muhammad ﷺ. So Ikrimah returned with his wife, entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and pledged allegiance to him, and he accepted it from him. A man from Hudhayl entered when Banu Bakr defeated his wife, fleeing, and she blamed him, declared him incapable, and reproached him for fleeing, so he said [rajaz verse]: If only you had seen us at al-Khandamah, when Safwan fled and Ikrimah fled, and they pressed upon us with surrendered swords, cutting every forearm and skull—you would not utter in blame even the slightest word. Urwah said: Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl was martyred on the day of Ajnadayn, among the Muslims, then of Quraysh, then of Banu Makhzum."],[5052,"Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl said: When I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I said: O Muhammad, this woman has informed me that you have granted me security. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: You are secure. I said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone with no partner, and that you are the servant of Allah and His Messenger, and you are the most righteous of people, the most truthful of people, and the most faithful of people. Ikrimah said: I said that while lowering my head out of shyness before him. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me for every enmity with which I opposed you, or every expedition in which I hastened, intending thereby to manifest polytheism. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Allah, forgive Ikrimah for every enmity with which he opposed me, or every expedition in which he hastened, intending to turn people away from Your path. I said: O Messenger of Allah, command me with the best of what you know so that I may learn it. He said: Say: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger, and strive in His path. Then Ikrimah said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave any expenditure I spent in obstructing the path of Allah except that I will spend double its like in the path of Allah, and I will not have fought any battle in obstructing the path of Allah except that I will strive twice as hard in the path of Allah. Then he exerted himself in fighting until he was killed as a martyr on the day of Ajnadayn during the caliphate of Abu Bakr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed him in the year of his farewell pilgrimage over Hawazin to collect their zakat, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while Ikrimah was at Tabalah."],[5053,"Al-Harith b. Hisham, Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl, and Ayyash b. Abu Rabiah were wounded on the day of al-Yarmuk. Al-Harith called for water to drink, and Ikrimah looked at him, so al-Harith said: Give it to Ikrimah. Then Ayyash b. Abu Rabiah looked at him, so Ikrimah said: Give it to Ayyash. It did not reach Ayyash nor any of them until they died, and they did not taste it."],[5054,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me on the day I came as an emigrant: Welcome to the emigrant rider, welcome to the emigrant rider, welcome to the emigrant rider. I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I will not leave any expenditure I spent except that I will spend its like in the path of Allah, exalted be He."],[5055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I saw in a dream as if Abu Jahl came to me and pledged allegiance to me. When Khalid b. al-Walid embraced Islam, it was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Allah has made your dream true, O Messenger of Allah—this was the Islam of Khalid. He said: There will certainly be another, until Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl embraced Islam, and that was the confirmation of his dream."],[5056,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I saw for Abu Jahl a cluster of dates in Paradise. When Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl embraced Islam, he said: O Umm Salamah, this is the one."],[5057,"Ikrimah b. Abu Jahl would take the mushaf, place it on his face, weep, and say: The speech of my Lord, the Book of my Lord."],[5058,"As for Abu Quhafah al-Taymi, he is Uthman b. Amir b. Amr b. Kab b. Sad b. Taym b. Murrah. He embraced Islam on the day of the conquest of Makkah and died in Makkah in Muharram of the year fourteen of the Hijrah, being then ninety-seven years old."],[5059,"Abu Bakr came on the day of the conquest of Makkah with his father Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Had you left the old man in his house, we would have come to him."],[5060,"I brought my father Abu Quhafah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: Why did you not leave the old man until I came to him? I said: Rather, it is more fitting for him to come to you. He said: We will certainly preserve him because of the favors of his son upon us."],[5061,"The name of Abu Quhafah is Uthman b. Amir b. Amr b. Kab b. Sad b. Taym b. Murrah b. Kab b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr. He embraced Islam on the day of the conquest and died in Muharram of the year fourteen, being then ninety-seven years old."],[5062,"Abu Quhafah, the father of Abu Bakr, died in the year seventeen, being then one hundred and four years old."],[5063,"Umar b. al-Khattab took Abu Quhafa by the hand and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. When he stood with him before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Change it and do not bring him near blackness.” — On the condition of Muslim."],[5064,"On the day of the conquest, the Prophet ﷺ was brought Abu Quhafa while his head and beard were like the thaghamah plant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Dye his beard.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5065,"It is as if I am looking at the beard of Abu Quhafa, as if it were the blazing of an arfaj bush from the intensity of its redness. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: “If you had let the old man remain in his house, we would have come to him, as an honor to Abu Bakr.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5066,"When the Prophet ﷺ was taken, the news reached the people of Makkah. Abu Quhafa heard the clamor and said: “What is this?” They said: “The Prophet ﷺ has died.” He said: “A momentous affair. Who has undertaken the matter after him?” They said: “Your son.” He said: “And Banu Makhzum and Banu al-Mughirah are pleased?” They said: “Yes.” He said: “O Allah, there is no one to lower what You have raised, nor to raise what You have lowered.” When at the head of the year Abu Bakr died, the news reached the people of Makkah, and Abu Quhafa heard the clamor. He said: “What is this?” They said: “Your son has died.” He said: “A momentous affair, and the one before it was greater. Who has undertaken the matter after him?” They said: “Umar b. al-Khattab.” He said: “He is his companion.” — Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, though they did not record it. They did not record anything by Umarah b. Abd Allah b. Sayyad."],[5067,"Umar b. al-Khattab was appointed as successor after a year and three months, and Umar prayed over him, then walked with him to al-Baqi until he was buried there.”"],[5068,"“Nawfal b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib, whose kunya was Abu al-Harith, died in Madinah two years after the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab.”"],[5069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Ransom yourself, O Nawfal.” He said: “I have nothing with which to ransom myself, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Ransom yourself with your spears that are in Juddah.” He said: “By Allah, no one knew that I had spears in Juddah besides Allah and myself. I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.” So he ransomed himself with them, and they were a thousand spears. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Nawfal and al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib; before that they had been partners in the Jahiliyyah, sharing their wealth and loving each other. Nawfal witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the conquest of Makkah, Hunayn, and al-Ta'if, and he stood firm on the day of Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “It is as if I am looking at your spears being broken in the backs of the polytheists.”"],[5070,"He sought help from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in marrying, and he married him to a woman. He then looked for something but did not find it, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Rafi and Abu Ayyub with his armor, and they pawned it with a man from the Jews for thirty measures of barley. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave it to me, and we ate from it for half a year. Then we measured it and found it as we had first stored it. Nawfal said: I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “If you had not measured it, you would have eaten from it as long as you lived.” As for Rabiah b. al-Harith and Ubaydah b. al-Harith, they were killed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Badr. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5071,"“Among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Quraysh and the Ansar were three hundred and thirteen men.” He said: “And from the Banu Abd al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf were Ubaydah, al-Tufayl, and Husayn, the sons of al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib. They differed about Rabiah b. al-Harith: it was said that he lived after that and lived to the days of Umar b. al-Khattab and narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5072,"It reached the Prophet ﷺ that a people spoke ill of him and said: “The likeness of Muhammad is only that of a palm tree that grew in a rubbish heap.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry, then said: “O people, Allah created His creation and made them into two groups, and He placed me in the better of the two groups. Then He made them into tribes, and He placed me in the best tribe. Then He made them into houses, and He placed me in the best house.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I am the best of you in tribe and the best of you in house.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5073,"From Hisham b. al-Kalbi regarding the Prophet’s ﷺ saying: “The first blood I abolish is the blood of Rabiah b. al-Harith. He was being nursed among Banu Layth, and Hudhayl killed him.” Hisham said: “Rabiah was not killed, for he lived after the Prophet ﷺ until the caliphate of Umar. The one whom Hudhayl killed was someone else.” Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5074,"He came to Syria during the reign of Muawiyah, and a group of people from Syria met him and said: “Is there kinship between you and Muadh?” He said: “I said: He is my cousin.” They said: “Shall we not tell you a hadith?”"],[5075,"Among those from the people of Makkah who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Banu Umayyah ibn Abd Shams, was Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As ibn Umayyah ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf, and with him was his wife. She gave birth to him in the land of Abyssinia his son Sa'id ibn Khalid."],[5076,"The mother of Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As was Lubaynah, known as Umm Khalid, daughter of Hubab ibn Abd Yalil ibn Nashib ibn Ghayrah ibn Sa'd ibn Layth ibn Bakr ibn Abd Manah ibn Ali ibn Kinanah ibn Khuzaymah."],[5077,"Khalid's Islam was early, and he was the first of his brothers to accept Islam. The beginning of his Islam was that he saw in a dream that he was standing at the edge of the Fire, as if his father was pushing him into it, and he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding him by the waist so that he would not fall. He woke up frightened and said, 'I swear by Allah, this is a true vision.' He met Abu Bakr ibn Abi Quhafah and mentioned that to him. Abu Bakr said, 'Good is intended for you. This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so follow him. You will follow him and enter with him into Islam, and Islam will prevent you from entering it, while your father will fall into it.' He met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was at Ajyad and said, 'O Muhammad, to what do you call?' He said, 'I call to Allah alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that you abandon what you were upon of worshipping a stone that does not harm or benefit and does not know who worships it from who does not.' Khalid said, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So he accepted Islam. His father sent in search of him those of his remaining children who had not accepted Islam, and Rafi', his freedman. They found him and brought him to his father Abu Uhayhah. He rebuked him and reproached him and struck him with a staff in his hand until he broke it on his head. Then he said, 'You have followed Muhammad when you see his people oppose him, and what he has brought of defaming their gods and the faults of their forefathers.' Khalid said, 'He has spoken the truth, by Allah, and I have followed him.' His father Abu Uhayhah became angry and reviled him, then said, 'Go, you lowly one, wherever you wish. By Allah, I will deny you sustenance.' Khalid said, 'If you deny me, Allah ﷻ will provide me with what I live on.' So he expelled him and said to his sons, 'None of you speak to him or I will do to him what I did to him.' Khalid went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he honored him and stayed with him. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5078,"Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5079,"Khalifah said, 'And it was in the year thirteen.' He said, 'And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was his governor over Yemen.'"],[5080,"About their offices when the news of the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached them, Abu Bakr said, 'No one has a greater right to the office than the governors of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Return to your offices.' They said, 'We will not work for anyone after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' So they went out to Syria and were all killed. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5081,"It was Abu Bakr who called him to Islam until he accepted Islam."],[5082,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed Khalid ibn Sa'id over Yemen, he arrived after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and delayed his pledge for two months, saying, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed me, then did not dismiss me until Allah ﷻ took him.' He met Ali ibn Abi Talib and Uthman ibn Abd Manaf and said, 'O Banu Abd Manaf, are you pleased that someone other than you should take charge of your affair?' Umar conveyed this to Abu Bakr. As for Abu Bakr, he did not hold it against him, but Umar held it against him. Then Abu Bakr sent armies to Syria. The first one to be appointed over a quarter of it was Khalid ibn Sa'id. Umar began to say, 'Will you appoint him when he did what he did and said what he said?' He kept at Abu Bakr until he dismissed him and appointed Yazid ibn Abi Sufyan. 'Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not record it.' This is interrupted."],[5083,"I heard Ahmad ibn Sayyar say: 'Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As was born to his father Sa'id, who had twenty sons and twenty daughters. As for Khalid ibn Sa'id, he was killed on the day of Marj al-Suffar in Muharram of the year fourteen in the caliphate of Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ.'"],[5084,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ with a ring on his hand. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'What is this ring?' He said, 'A ring I have taken.' He said, 'Throw it away.' So I threw it to him, and it was a ring of iron. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'What did you engrave on it?' I said, 'Muhammad, Messenger of Allah.' The Prophet ﷺ took it and wore it until he died. It is the ring that was on his hand. 'Sahih al-isnad, but they did not record it.' Yahya al-Himmani is weak."],[5085,"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he came from the land of Abyssinia, and with him was his daughter Umm Khalid. He brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she had on a yellow shirt. The girl was pleased with her shirt. She had understood some of the speech of Abyssinia, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to her in the language of Abyssinia, 'Sanah sanah,' which in Abyssinian means 'beautiful, beautiful.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, 'Wear it out and make it old, wear it out and make it old.' He said, 'She wore it out, by Allah, then made it old.' Then she leaned towards the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed her hand on the place of the seal of prophethood. Her father took her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Leave her.' Sahih al-isnad. The two shaykhs agreed on recording hadiths from Ishaq ibn Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Sa'id from his fathers and uncles. This is Umm Khalid, daughter of Khalid ibn Sa'id ibn al-'As, whom her father carried when she was young to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ afterwards, and she narrated from him, but it is interrupted."],[5086,"From Banu Zuhayr, Safwan ibn Makhrama ibn Nawfal, and by him Makhrama is given the kunya. He is the brother of al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, and his mother is Atikah bint Awf, sister of Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf."],[5087,"He said: \"Cool down the Zuhr prayer, for the intense heat is from the scorching wind of Hell.\""],[5088,"From al-Waqidi."],[5089,"Then Salamah b. Hisham escaped after that and rejoined the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Madinah, and that was after the Battle of the Trench. His mother Duba'ah bt. 'Amir b. Qaraz b. Salamah b. Qushayr b. Ka'b b. 'Amir b. Rabi'ah said (in rajaz verse):\"O Allah, Lord of the sacred Ka'bah, grant Salamah victory over every enemy. He has two hands in obscure affairs: one hand by which he gives and a generous hand.\"He remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away. Then he went out with the Muslims to Syria when Abu Bakr dispatched the armies to fight the Romans. Salamah was killed as a martyr at Marj al-Suffar in Muharram of the year 14 during the caliphate of 'Umar ؓ."],[5090,"From 'Urwah: \"Concerning the naming of those who attended al-'Aqabah from the Ansar, from Banu Sa'idah b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj: Sa'd b. 'Ubadah b. Dulaym b. Harithah b. 'Ubaydah b. Huzaymah. He was a naqib (representative) and he attended Badr.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5091,"From 'Urwah: \"Concerning the naming of those who attended al-'Aqabah, and from Banu Sa'idah b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj: Sa'd b. 'Ubadah was the bearer of the banner of the Ansar with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr and elsewhere.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5092,"\"That Sa'd b. 'Ubadah b. Dulaym b. Harithah b. al-Nu'man b. Abi Huzaymah b. Tha'labah b. Tarif b. al-Khazraj b. Sa'idah b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5093,"\"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, whose kunyah was Abu Thabit, died in Hawran in the land of Syria two and a half years into the caliphate of 'Umar, and that was at the end of the fifteenth year.\""],[5094,"I heard Yahya b. 'Abd Allah b. Bukayr say: \"Sa'd b. 'Ubadah died in Hawran in the year 16.\""],[5095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Bring out to me twelve naqibs (representatives).\" So we brought out to him Sa'd b. 'Ubadah b. Dulaym b. Harithah b. Huzaymah b. Tha'labah b. Tarif b. al-Khazraj b. Sa'idah, and he was the naqib of Banu Sa'idah. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5096,"Quraysh heard a speaker saying at night on Abu Qubays (in tawil verse):\"If the two Sa'ds become Muslims, Muhammad will awake in Makkah not fearing the opposition of any opponent.\"Quraysh thought that they were Sa'd of Tamim and Sa'd of Hudhaym. When it was the second night, they heard him saying:\"O Sa'd, Sa'd of al-Aws, be you a supporter, and O Sa'd, Sa'd of the generous Khazrajis, answer the caller to guidance and wish upon Allah in Paradise the wish of a knower. For the reward of Allah for the seeker of guidance is gardens of Paradise with raised couches.\"When they woke up, Sufyan said: \"By Allah, it is Sa'd b. Mu'adh and Sa'd b. 'Ubadah.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5097,"The jinn said (in sari' verse):\"We killed the master of the Khazraj, Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, and we shot him with two arrows that did not miss his heart.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5098,"\"I indeed feel something in my back.\" He did not stay long before he died, and the jinn lamented, saying (in sari' verse):\"We killed the master of the Khazraj, Sa'd b. 'Ubadah, and we shot him with two arrows that did not miss his heart.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5099,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ learned of Abu Sufyan's approach, he spoke, but Abu Bakr turned away from him, then Umar spoke, but he turned away from him. Sa'd b. Ubadah said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One in whose hand is my soul, if you ordered us to plunge into the sea we would plunge, and if you ordered us to strike their livers to Bark al-Ghimad we would do it. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned the people, and they set out until they stopped at Badr. Authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5100,"Sa'd b. Ubadah used to say: O Allah, grant me glory, and there is no glory except through deeds, and no deeds except through wealth. O Allah, little does not suffice me, nor am I suited to it. If there were a caller calling from a fortress: Whoever wants fat and meat, let him come to Sa'd."],[5101,"The polytheists captured Sa'd b. Ubadah, tied his hand to his neck, and brought him into Makkah, beating him and dragging him by his forelock, and he had long hair. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis because of its weakness."],[5102,"So I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he commanded me to repay it on her behalf. The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting this hadith that the mother of Sa'd b. Ubadah died, but they did not connect it from him. This is authentic according to their conditions. Al-Madayini is weak."],[5103,"Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, and he was the milk-brother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his paternal cousin. Halimah nursed him for some days, and he used to be close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. But when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sent, he became hostile to him, satirized him, and satirized his companions, and he remained for twenty years opposed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, never absent from any place where Quraysh set out to fight the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then when the departure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Makkah in the year of the conquest was mentioned, Allah ﷻ cast Islam into his heart, and he met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he reached al-Abwa, and he and his son Ja'far embraced Islam. He went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and witnessed the conquest of Makkah and Hunayn. Abu Sufyan said: When we met the enemy at Hunayn, I dismounted from my horse with a drawn sword in my hand, and Allah knows that I intended death in his defense while he was looking at me. Al-Abbas said: O Messenger of Allah, this is your brother and your cousin Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith, so be pleased with him. He said: 'I have done so; may Allah forgive him every enmity with which he opposed me.' Then he turned to me and said: 'My brother, by my life.' So I kissed his foot in the stirrup. They said: Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith died in Madinah after his brother Nawfal b. al-Harith by four months less thirteen nights. It is said he died in the year 20, and Umar b. al-Khattab prayed over him, and he was buried in the house of Aqil b. Abi Talib in al-Baqi'. He is the one who dug his own grave three days before he died. 'I have mentioned the Islam of Abu Sufyan at the conquest of Makkah previously.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5104,"I heard Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir say, \"Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Muttalib, whose name was al-Mughirah, passed away in the year twenty. Umar ibn al-Khattab performed the funeral prayer for him.\""],[5105,"Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib was the most beloved of Quraysh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was severe against him; but when he embraced Islam, he became the most beloved of people to him. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5106,"Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith is the best of my family."],[5107,"The master of the youths of Paradise is Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib."],[5108,"\"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. I saw him with no one except me and Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith ibn Abdul-Muttalib. He was holding the reins of the Messenger of Allah's mule while he was riding it, and Abu Sufyan was eager to rush towards the polytheists.\" This hadith is authentic according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs (i.e., Abu Bakr and Umar), but it has not been included in Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim."],[5109,"A man had dates owed to him by the Prophet ﷺ, and he came to demand them. The Prophet ﷺ borrowed dates from Khawlah bt. Hakim and gave them to him, saying: 'Indeed, I had dates, but they were athariyy (inferior),' then he said: 'Thus do the believing servants of Allah act. Allah does not have mercy on a community where the weak among them cannot take their right from the strong without stammering.' Abu Sufyan did not narrate from the Prophet ﷺ any hadith other than this single one, and no one established its chain from Shu'bah except Ghundar. Abu al-Abbas al-Sayyari informed us, Abu al-Muwajjih narrated to us, Abdan narrated to us, my father informed me from Shu'bah from Simak, who said: We were with Mudrik b. al-Muhallab in Sijistan, and I heard a shaykh narrating from Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith from the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned it. But Abd Allah b. Abi Sufyan did not hear from his father."],[5110,"Among those who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the descendants of al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib was Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'He is among the best of my family.' And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He is the master of the youths of the people of Paradise.' He stood firm with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him in the dimness of dawn and said: 'Who is this?' He replied: 'The son of your mother, O Messenger of Allah.' And he said: 'The barber shaved him and cut a wart from his head, and the blood did not stop until he died, and that was in the year 20. Umar b. al-Khattab prayed over him. He had met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on part of the road while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was going out to Makkah for the conquest, and he embraced Islam before the conquest.'"],[5111,"Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib, his name was al-Mughirah. He died in the year 20, and Umar b. al-Khattab prayed over him."],[5112,"Indeed, Allah does not sanctify a community where the weak does not take his right from the strong without stammering."],[5113,"A man had dates owed to him by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he came to him demanding payment. The Prophet ﷺ borrowed dates from Khawlah bt. Hakim and gave them to him, saying: “Indeed, I had dates, but they were of poor quality (ʿathariyy).” Then he said: “Thus do the believing servants of Allah act. Indeed, Allah does not show mercy to a nation where the weak among them cannot take their right without difficulty.”"],[5114,"I was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in my childhood wearing a rag, and my private parts were uncovered. He said: “Cover the sanctity of his private parts, for the sanctity of the private parts of the young is like the sanctity of the private parts of the old, and Allah does not look at one who uncovers private parts.” Its chain is obscure and its text is rejected."],[5115,"From ʿUrwah: “Among those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia with Jaʿfar from the Banū Zuhrah b. Kilāb were ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd and his brother ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd ؓ.”"],[5116,"“My brother and companion with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the third, and the most beloved of people to me except for what was from ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb.” Its chain is authentic."],[5117,"“When ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd died, ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb waited for Umm ʿAbd, and she came and prayed over him.”"],[5118,"“ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd is not higher in our estimation than his brother ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd, but he died early.”"],[5119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to pray the morning prayer, and he reached out with his hand in front of him. A man from the people asked him when he finished the prayer, and he said: “Satan came, and I rebuked him. Had I seized him, I would have tied him to one of the pillars of the mosque until the children of the people of Madinah could go around him.”"],[5120,"I heard Yaḥyā b. Bukayr say: “ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd died in the year forty-four.” He has only one hadith."],[5121,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a black slave girl and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing slave; will this one suffice for me?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who is your Lord?” She said: “My Lord is Allah.” He said: “What is your religion?” She said: “Islam.” He said: “Who am I?” She said: “You are the Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Do you pray the five prayers and affirm what I have brought from Allah?” She said: “Yes.” So he struck her on the back and said: “Free her.” And ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd met the Prophet ﷺ and heard from him. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5122,"I heard my father Ḥamzah b. ʿAbdullāh say: I asked my father ʿAbdullāh b. ʿUtbah b. Masʿūd: “What do you remember of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He said: “I remember that he took me when I was five or six years old, seated me in his lap, wiped my head, and supplicated for blessing for me and my offspring.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5123,"Nuʿaym al-Naḥḥām is Nuʿaym b. ʿAbdullāh b. Khālid b. Usayd b. ʿAbd ʿAwf b. ʿUbayd b. ʿAwīj b. ʿAdī b. Kaʿb. He embraced Islam before the Hijrah and was among those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia. He is the one called al-Naḥḥām, and he was called that only because the Prophet ﷺ said: “I heard a soft sound (naḥmah) from Nuʿaym in Paradise.” And al-naḥmah means the voice."],[5124,"“And that was in the year thirteen.”"],[5125,"The Prophet's ﷺ mu'adhdhin called the adhan on a cold night while I was under my blanket, and I wished that Allah Almighty would put on his tongue \"and no harm\" – meaning, the phrase \"no harm\" that would permit staying home. When he finished, he said: \"And no harm.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not record it. Sahih"],[5126,"Tufayl ibn 'Amr embraced Islam and followed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in Makkah. Then he returned to his people in the land of Daws and remained there until he emigrated to Madinah after Badr, Uhud, and the Khandaq, when he came with those of his people who had embraced Islam along with him, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at Khaybar. Then he joined the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Khaybar, and he allotted them shares with the Muslims."],[5127,"We said: O Messenger of Allah, make us your right flank, and make our battle cry \"O blessed one!\" So he did ﷺ. The battle cry of the whole tribe of Asad to this day is \"O blessed one!\" Its chain is authentic but they did not record it, if it is not mursal. 'Amr ibn al-Tufayl ibn 'Amr met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Sahih mursal"],[5128,"And 'Amr ibn al-Tufayl ibn 'Amr ibn Tarif ibn al-'As ibn Tha'labah al-Azdi. His father al-Tufayl ibn 'Amr was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he passed away. When the Arabs apostatized, he went out and fought until the Muslims finished with Tulayhah and all the land of Najd. Then he marched with the Muslims to al-Yamamah, accompanied by his son 'Amr ibn al-Tufayl. 'Amr ibn al-Tufayl went out and was wounded, and his hand was cut off. Then he recovered and his hand healed. While he was with 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, food was brought, and he moved away from it. 'Umar said: \"Why do you move away because of your hand?\" He said: \"Yes.\" 'Umar said: \"No, by Allah, I will not taste it until you stir it with your hand. By Allah, there is no one among the people a part of whom is in Paradise other than you.\" Then he went out in the year of al-Yarmuk during the caliphate of 'Umar with the Muslims and was killed as a martyr ؓ."],[5129,"Sa'd ibn 'Ubayd ibn al-Nu'man ibn Qays ibn 'Amr ibn Zayd ibn Umayyah ibn Zayd, who is called Sa'd the reader and is given the kunyah Abu Zayd, was one of the six who collected the Qur'an during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Khandaq, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was killed as a martyr on the day of al-Qadisiyyah in the year sixteen, when he was sixty-four years old ؓ."],[5130,"'Utbah ibn Ghazwan ibn Jabir ibn Wuhayb ibn Nasib ibn Malik ibn al-Harith ibn Mazin ibn Mansur ibn 'Ikrimah ibn Khasafah ibn Qays 'Aylan ibn Mudar ibn Nizar."],[5131,"From his teachers regarding the mention of 'Utbah ibn Ghazwan, they said: \"His kunyah was Abu 'Abdullah, and it is said Abu Ghazwan. He was, as mentioned, a tall, handsome man. He was an early Muslim and emigrated to the land of Abyssinia in the second emigration. He was among the renowned archers of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He is the one who founded Basra. He died during the caliphate of 'Umar ibn al-Khattab at the mine of Banu Sulaym while on his way to Basra as its governor appointed by 'Umar ibn al-Khattab. His servant Suwayd brought his belongings and estate to 'Umar.\" Ibn 'Umar said: \" 'Utbah ibn Ghazwan died in the year fifteen, and it is said seventeen, when he was fifty-seven years old.\""],[5132,"'Utbah ibn Ghazwan witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5133,"'Utbah ibn Ghazwan died in the year seventeen, at the age of fifty-seven ؓ."],[5134,"'Utba b. Ghazwan delivered us a sermon and he praised Allah and lauded Him, then said: Now coming to the point, verily the world has been given the news of its end and that too quite early. Nothing would be left out of it but only water left in the utensil which its owner leaves, and you are going to shift to an abode which knows no end, and you should shift with the good before you, for we have been told that a stone would be thrown at one side of the Hell and it would go down even for seventy years but would not be able to reach its bottom. By Allah, it would be fully packed. Do you find it something strange, and it has been mentioned that there yawns a distance which one would be able to cover in forty years from one end to another of Paradise, and a day would come when it would be fully packed and you must be knowing that I was the seventh amongst seven who had been with Messenger of Allah ﷺ and we had nothing to eat but the leaves of the tree until the corners of the mouth were injured. We found a sheet which we tore in two and divided between myself and Sa'd b. Malik. I made the lower garment with halt of it and so did Sa'd make the lower garment with half of it and today there is none amongst us who has not become the governor of a city from amongst the cities (of the Islamic Commonwealth) and I seek refuge with Allah that I should consider myself great whereas I am insignificant in the eye of Allah. Prophethood does not remain for ever and its impact fades with the result that it changes eventually into kingship, and you would soon come to know and experience those rulers who would come after us and see (how far they are from religion). (Using translation from Muslim 2967a)"],[5135,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said one day to Quraysh: \"Is there among you anyone from other than you?\" They said: \"The son of our sister, 'Utbah ibn Ghazwan.\" He said: \"The son of a people's sister is one of them.\" The mention of 'Utbah ibn Ghazwan in this hadith is very rare, and his virtues are many. This is among his noblest virtues. The musnads of 'Utbah ibn Ghazwan from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are scarce. We have written from that a hadith that we found very rare, so I will mention it, even though al-Ghallabi is not among the criteria of this book. Its chain is obscure."],[5136,"\"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[5137,"Abu 'Ubaydah 'Amir ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Jarrah ibn Hilal ibn Uhayb ibn Dabbah ibn al-Harith ibn Fihr ibn Malik ibn al-Nadr ibn Kinanah. His mother was Umm Ghanm bint Jabir ibn al-'Adl ibn 'Amir ibn 'Umayrah ibn Wari'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Fihr."],[5138,"Khalifah b. Khayyat narrated to us, and he mentioned this lineage."],[5139,"Umar said to his companions, \"Wish for something.\" Each man among them began to wish for something. He said, \"But I wish for a house full of men like Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah.\" They said to him, \"You have not spared Islam any good.\" He said, \"That is what I intended.\""],[5140,"Abdullah used to say: My closest friends among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were three: Abu Bakr, Umar, and Abu Ubaidah."],[5141,"Umar's letter came to us when the plague struck Syria. Umar wrote to Abu Ubaidah that he had a need for which he could not do without him. Abu Ubaidah said, \"May Allah have mercy on the Commander of the Faithful; he wants the survival of a people who are not to remain.\" Then Abu Ubaidah wrote back to him, \"I am in an army of the Muslim armies. I do not wish to spare myself from what has befallen them.\" When he read the letter, he said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return.\" The people said, \"Abu Ubaidah has died.\" He said, \"No.\" And he had written to him with firm resolution: \"Move out from the land of al-Urdunn, for it is deep and pestilential, to the land of al-Jabiyah, for it is pleasant and moist.\" When the letter with firm resolution reached him, he ordered his caller to announce to the people to depart. When he was brought his mount to ride, he placed his foot in the stirrup, then folded his leg and said, \"I think your disease has afflicted me.\" He said, \"And Abu Ubaidah died, and the plague turned away from the people.\""],[5142,"Muadh b. Jabal sent al-Harith b. Umayrah to Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah to ask him how he was, for he had been struck by the plague. Abu Ubaidah showed him a plague sore that had appeared on his palm. He described its condition and was frightened when he saw it. Abu Ubaidah swore to him by Allah that he would not love to have in its place red camels."],[5143,"When Abu Ubaidah was struck by the plague, he said, \"O Muadh, lead the people in prayer.\" So Muadh led the people in prayer. Then Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah died. Muadh stood among the people and said, \"O people, turn to Allah in sincere repentance from your sins. A servant does not meet Allah repentant from his sin except that it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him.\" Then he said, \"O people, you have been afflicted by the loss of a man. By Allah, I do not claim that I have ever seen among the servants of Allah a servant less complaining, more pure-hearted, farther from malice, more loving of the Hereafter, or more sincere in advising the common people than him. So ask mercy for him; may Allah have mercy on him.\" Then he said, \"Come out to pray over him, for by Allah, no one like him will ever be placed over you again.\" The people gathered, and Abu Ubaidah was brought out. Muadh came forward and prayed over him. When he was brought to his grave, Muadh b. Jabal, Amr b. al-As, and al-Dahhak b. Qais entered his grave. When they placed him in his niche and came out, they poured earth over him. Muadh b. Jabal said, \"O Abu Ubaidah, I will praise you and not speak falsely, fearing that wrath from Allah might befall me for it. By Allah, as far as I know, you were among those who remember Allah much, among those who walk humbly on the earth, and when the ignorant address them, they say, 'Peace,' and among those who, when they spend, are neither extravagant nor stingy, but between that is a just balance. By Allah, you were among the humble, the meek, who show mercy to the orphan and the needy and detest the treacherous and the arrogant.\""],[5144,"He described Abu Ubaidah, saying: A thin man, gaunt-faced, light-bearded, tall, slightly stooped, with a gap between his two front teeth."],[5145,"Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah died at Fahl in al-Urdunn in the year eighteen."],[5146,"Among those who witnessed Badr from the Banu al-Harith b. Fihr was Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah, and he was forty-one years old."],[5147,"The father of Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah began to set up the idol for Abu Ubaidah on the day of Badr, and Abu Ubaidah kept turning away from him. When he persisted in fighting, Abu Ubaidah went straight for him and killed him. Then Allah, exalted is He, revealed this verse about him when he killed his father: {You will not find a people who believe in Allah and the Last Day loving those who oppose Allah and His Messenger, even if they were their fathers or their sons} [al-Mujadilah: 22]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5148,"We entered upon Abu Ubaidah ibn al-Jarrah to visit him, and his wife was sitting thin at his head while he faced the wall. We said to her, \"How did Abu Ubaidah pass the night?\" She said, \"He passed the night with reward.\" He turned his face toward us and said, \"I did not pass the night with reward.\" Then he said, \"Will you not ask me about what I said?\" We said, \"We were not amazed by what you said, so we would ask you about it.\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever spends an expenditure in the path of Allah, it is multiplied seven hundred times. And whoever spends on himself and his family, or visits a sick person, or anything more, the good deed is multiplied ten times. Fasting is a shield as long as it is not rent. And whoever Allah tests with an affliction in his body, it is an expiation for him.'\""],[5149,"I heard Yahya b. Said say, \"Abu Ubaidah died at the age of fifty-eight years.\""],[5150,"Abu Ubaidah al-Jarrah died in Jordan in the year eighteen, and Mu'adh b. Jabal ؓ led the funeral prayer over him."],[5151,"I did not seek leadership, nor did I love it, except that some people from Najran came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and complained to him about their governor. He said, \"I will certainly send over you the trustworthy one.\" Umar said, \"So I was among those who strove, hoping that he would send me, but he sent Abu Ubaidah. [Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not record it] according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5152,"There is none among my companions but that if I wished I could find some fault in his character, except Abu Ubaidah b. al-Jarrah."],[5153,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to Abu Ubaidah when he dispatched him to Syria: \"I would like you to know your honor with me and your standing with me. By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no man on earth among the Muhajirun or others whom I consider equal to you, and not even this one—meaning Umar—and his standing with me is below yours.\""],[5154,"I was among the first to return on the day of Uhud, and in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there was a man fighting on his behalf—and I think he said protecting him. He said: I said, \"Would that you were Talha, since what passed me by has passed me by.\" He said: Between me and the east was a man I did not recognize, and I was closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than he, yet he was rushing forward swiftly in a way I could not. Then behold, it was Abu Ubaidah b. al-Jarrah. We both reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ together, and his front tooth had been broken and he had been wounded in the face, and two rings of the helmet had entered his cheeks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, \"Attend to your companion,\" meaning Talha, who had bled profusely, and he did not look at him. So we turned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I wanted what Abu Ubaidah wanted, but he asked me to let him, and he did not cease until I left him. One of the rings had become stuck, and he disliked to shake it with his hand lest he hurt the Prophet ﷺ, so he gripped it with his front tooth, rose up, and pulled it out, and his front tooth fell out. Then he asked me, and did not let me, until I left him. Then he turned to the other ring and did the same, pulling it out, and his other front tooth fell out. Thus Abu Ubaidah became the most broken-toothed of men."],[5155,"Abu Ubaidah Amir b. al-Jarrah embraced Islam along with Uthman b. Maz'un, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, and their companions before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house of al-Arqam. Abu Ubaidah migrated to the land of Abyssinia in the second migration. Abu Ubaidah witnessed Badr and Uhud, and he remained firm on the day of Uhud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the people fled. He is the one who pulled out with his two front teeth the two rings of the helmet of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that had entered his cheeks, and the two front teeth of Abu Ubaidah fell out by that pulling, so Abu Ubaidah became the most broken-toothed of men. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5156,"The inscription on the seal of Abu Ubaidah b. al-Jarrah was 'Fulfillment is precious.'"],[5157,"Al-Aqib and al-Sayyid, the two leaders of Najran, came to the Prophet ﷺ intending to invoke a mutual curse with him. One of them said to his companion, \"Do not do it, for by Allah, if he is a prophet and curses us, we will never prosper, nor will our descendants after us.\" So they said, \"Rather, we will give you what you asked, and send with us a man who is truly trustworthy.\" He said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stretched their necks for it. He said, \"Arise, O Abu Ubaidah b. al-Jarrah.\" When he turned away, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"This is the trustworthy one of this nation.\" The two Shaykhs agreed on recording this hadith in abbreviated form in the two Sahihs from the hadith of al-Thawri and Shu'bah, from Abu Ishaq, from Silah b. Zufar, from Hudhayfah. Israel differed from them, saying it is from Silah b. Zufar, from Abdullah, and he narrated the hadith more completely than what al-Thawri and Shu'bah have. So I recorded it because it is according to their conditions. Sahih according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5158,"The people of Yemen came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Send with us a man to teach us the Qur'an.\" He took the hand of Abu Ubaidah and sent him with them, and said, \"This is the trustworthy one of this nation.\" Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not record it with the mention of the Qur'an. According to the conditions of Muslim."],[5159,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to Abu Ubaidah, \"Shall I give you the oath of allegiance? For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'You are the trustworthy one of this nation.'\" Abu Ubaidah replied, \"How can I pray before a man whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded to lead us in prayer when he passed away?\" [Sahih chain, but they did not record it] Munqati' (disconnected)."],[5160,"From him: I said, \"He has appointed as successor the trusted one of Allah and the trusted one of His Messenger ﷺ.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5161,"What an excellent man is Abu Bakr! What an excellent man is Umar! What an excellent man is Abu Ubaidah b. al-Jarrah! What an excellent man is Usayd b. Hudayr! What an excellent man is Thabit b. Qays! What an excellent man is Mu'adh b. Jabal! What an excellent man is Mu'adh b. Amr b. al-Jamuh!"],[5162,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Abu Talhah and Abu 'Ubaidah. It is sahih according to Muslim's criterion, but they did not record it. Fahd b. 'Awf: they abandoned him."],[5163,"From Ibn Ishaq, regarding naming those who attended al-'Aqabah: Mu'adh b. Jabal b. 'Amr b. Aws b. 'A'idh b. 'Adiyy b. Ka'b b. Ghanm b. Sa'd b. 'Aliyy b. Asad b. Saridah b. Yazid b. Jusham. He was among the Banu Salamah. He attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and all the expeditions. He died at 'Amwas in the year of the plague during the caliphate of 'Umar b. al-Khattab. The Banu Salamah claimed him only because he had established brotherhood with a man from among them."],[5164,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: The kunyah of Mu'adh b. Jabal is Abu 'Abd al-Rahman."],[5165,"Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight years old, and he was the imam of the scholars by a degree."],[5166,"Mu'adh b. Jabal b. 'Amr b. 'A'idh b. 'Adiyy b. Ka'b b. 'Amr b. Adda b. Sa'd b. 'Aliyy b. Asad b. Saridah b. Yazid b. Jusham. He attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5167,"Mu'adh b. Jabal b. 'Amr, one of the Banu Salamah b. al-Khazraj, whose kunyah is Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, died in the year eighteen during the plague of 'Amwas, and he was thirty-eight years old."],[5168,"From him, al-Dhahabi in the Talkhis."],[5169,"He was thirty-two years old. Al-Dhahabi omitted it due to its weakness."],[5170,"Mu'adh b. Jabal died when he was twenty-eight, and he was the imam of the scholars by a degree."],[5171,"Mu'adh b. Jabal passed away when he was thirty-three or thirty-four years old. This statement of Yahya b. Sa'id is closer to correctness than the preceding one."],[5172,"I entered the mosque of Damascus and saw a man with glistening front teeth, very silent. People were with him; when they disagreed about something, they referred it to him and acted upon his opinion. I asked about him and was told: Mu'adh b. Jabal."],[5173,"Mu'adh b. Jabal was buried at Qasr Khalid."],[5174,"Mu'adh b. Jabal was a handsome, generous young man, among the best youth of his people. He was not asked for anything except that he gave it, until he incurred a debt that consumed his wealth."],[5175,"He passed by Mu'adh b. Jabal while he was standing at his door, gesturing with his hand as if talking to himself. 'Abdullah said to him: \"What is the matter with you, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman? It is as if you are talking to yourself.\""],[5176,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed Mu'adh b. Jabal over the people of Makkah when he went out to Hunayn, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded him to teach the people the Qur'an and to give them understanding in the religion. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed, heading to Madinah, and left Mu'adh b. Jabal over the people of Makkah."],[5177,"A hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"The slightest ostentation is shirk, and the most beloved of servants to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, are the pious, the hidden ones, who, when they are absent, are not missed, and when they are present, are not recognized. Those are the leaders of guidance and the lamps of knowledge.\""],[5178,"When death came to Mu'adh b. Jabal, it was said to him: \"Advise us, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.\" He said: \"Sit me up, for knowledge and faith are in their place; whoever seeks them will find them.\" He said that three times. \"Seek knowledge from four: from 'Uwaymir, Abu al-Darda', from Salman al-Farisi, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and from 'Abdullah b. Salam, who was a Jew and then embraced Islam, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say that he is the tenth of ten in Paradise.\""],[5179,"Mu'adh b. Jabal is the most knowledgeable of the first and the last, after the prophets and messengers, and Allah boasts of him to the angels."],[5180,"Mu'adh b. Jabal spat to his right, then said: \"I have not done this since I embraced Islam and accompanied the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[5181,"Mu'adh b. Jabal stood among the army under his command when the plague struck and said: \"O people, this is a mercy from your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet, and the death of the righteous before you.\" Then Mu'adh said while delivering a sermon: \"O Allah, grant the family of Mu'adh their fullest share of this mercy.\" While he was so, someone came and said: \"Your son 'Abd al-Rahman has been stricken.\" When 'Abd al-Rahman saw his father Mu'adh, he said: \"O father, {The truth is from your Lord, so do not be among the doubters} [al-Baqarah 147].\" Mu'adh said: {You will find me, if Allah wills, among the patient} [al-Saffat 102]. Then from one Friday to the next, the entire family of Mu'adh died, and he was the last of them."],[5182,"'Umar b. al-Khattab addressed the people and said: \"Whoever wants to ask about the Qur'an, let him go to Ubayy b. Ka'b. Whoever wants to ask about the lawful and the unlawful, let him go to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Whoever wants to ask about wealth, let him come to me, for Allah, Exalted, has made me a treasurer.\""],[5183,"Allah, Exalted, said: {Indeed, Abraham was a nation, devoutly obedient to Allah} [al-Nahl 120] — the verse. He said: \"Do you know what the ummah is? And what the qanit is?\" I said: \"Allah knows best.\" He said: \"The ummah is the one who teaches good, and the qanit is the one obedient to Allah and to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. And such was Mu'adh b. Jabal: he was a teacher of good and was obedient to Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[5184,"'Abdullah said: \"Whoever forgets, forgets. We used to liken him to Abraham.\" And 'Abdullah was asked about the ummah, and he said: \"A teacher of good, and the qanit is the one obedient to Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\" Then 'Abdullah said: \"Whoever forgets, forgets. We used to liken him to Abraham.\" And 'Abdullah was asked about the ummah, and he said: \"A teacher of good, and the qanit is the one obedient to Allah and His Messenger ﷺ.\""],[5185,"When the Prophet ﷺ passed away and they appointed Abu Bakr as successor, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent Mu'adh to Yemen. Abu Bakr appointed 'Umar over the pilgrimage season, and he met Mu'adh in Makkah, and with him were slaves. He said: \"What are these?\" He said: \"These were gifted to me, and these to Abu Bakr.\" 'Umar said to him: \"I think you should bring them to Abu Bakr.\" He said: \"The next day he met him and said: 'O Ibn al-Khattab, last night I saw myself leaping into the Fire while you were holding me by my waistband, and I think I will only obey you.'\" He said: \"So he brought them to Abu Bakr and said: 'These were gifted to me, and these to you.' He said: 'We have accepted your gift.' Then Mu'adh went out to pray, and there they were praying behind him. Mu'adh said: 'For whom do you pray?' They said: 'For Allah, Exalted.' He said: 'Then you are for Him,' and he freed them.\""],[5186,"Umar b. al-Khattab addressed the people and said: “Whoever wishes to ask about the Qur'an, let him go to Ubayy b. Ka'b. Whoever wishes to ask about the lawful and the unlawful, let him go to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Whoever wishes to ask about the shares of inheritance, let him go to Zayd b. Thabit. Whoever wishes to ask about wealth, let him come to me, for I am its treasurer.”"],[5187,"Mu'adh b. Jabal was a young man, forbearing, generous, among the best youths of his people. He did not hold on to anything, and he kept borrowing until he drowned all his wealth in debt. His creditors came to the Prophet ﷺ. Had they left anyone for the sake of anyone, they would have left Mu'adh for the sake of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sold his property for them until Mu'adh stood with nothing."],[5188,"A son of his died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to him consoling him: “In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Mu'adh b. Jabal. Peace be upon you. I praise Allah to you, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: May Allah magnify your reward, inspire you with patience, and grant us and you gratitude. For our souls, our wealth, our families, and our children are among the pleasant gifts of Allah, the Exalted, and His entrusted loans. He let you enjoy him in happiness and joy, and He took him from you with a great reward of prayer, mercy, and guidance, if you seek recompense for him. So be patient, and do not let your anxiety nullify your reward, lest you regret. Know that anxiety does not bring back anything, nor does it ward off grief, and what is to come will be as if it had already been. And peace.” This is strange but good, except that Mujashi' b. Amr is not among the criteria of this book. This is from the fabrications of Mujashi' b. Amr."],[5189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took me by the hand one day and said: “O Mu'adh, by Allah, I love you.” I said to him, “May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, and by Allah I love you.” He said: “I enjoin you, O Mu'adh, not to fail after every prayer to say: O Allah, help me to remember You, thank You, and worship You well.” Mu'adh enjoined this upon al-Sunabihi, and al-Sunabihi enjoined it upon Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, and Abu Abd al-Rahman enjoined it upon Uqbah b. Muslim. Its chain is authentic, but they did not record it. Authentic."],[5190,"Mu'adh b. Jabal was one of the most handsome people in face, the best in character, and the most generous with what he had. He incurred a large debt, and his creditors pressed him until he hid from them for some days in his house. His creditors sought help from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for Mu'adh, calling him. He came with his creditors. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, take our rights from him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “May Allah have mercy on whoever gives charity to him.” Some people gave him charity, but others refused and said, “O Messenger of Allah, take our rights from him.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be patient with them, O Mu'adh.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stripped him of his property and gave it to his creditors, and they divided it among themselves. They received five-sevenths of their rights. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, sell him for us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Leave him alone, for you have no way against him.” Mu'adh went to Banu Salamah. Someone said to him, “O Abu Abd al-Rahman, if only you had asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for today you have become destitute.” He said, “I would not ask him.” He stayed for some days, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called him and sent him to Yemen, saying: “Perhaps Allah will restore you and pay off your debt on your behalf.” Mu'adh went to Yemen and remained there until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died. He arrived in the year in which Umar b. al-Khattab performed Hajj in Makkah. Abu Bakr had appointed him over the Hajj. They met on the Day of Tarwiyah there, embraced, and each consoled the other for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then they sat on the ground talking. Umar saw servants with Mu'adh and said, “Who are these?” Then he mentioned the words which I mentioned previously. Al-Dhahabi omitted this from the summary due to its weakness."],[5191,"Al-Fadl b. al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, whose kunyah was Abu Muhammad, fought with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Makkah and Hunayn, and stood firm with him when the people turned in defeat. He witnessed the Farewell Pilgrimage with him, and he was among those who washed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took charge of his burial. Then he went to Syria as a warrior in the region of Jordan during the plague of Amwas in the year eighteen of the Hijrah, during the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ."],[5192,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: “Al-Fadl b. Abbas was killed on the day of al-Yarmuk during the era of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq ؓ.”"],[5193,"From al-Fadl b. Abbas."],[5194,"From al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib."],[5195,"Al-Fadl was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of Muzdalifah. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed, he said: “O people, be calm, for righteousness is not in making horses and camels hurry.” Al-Dhahabi omitted this from the summary due to its weakness."],[5196,"It is said of Jamil 'Dhu al-Qalbayn' because of his intelligence, until Allah said: {Allah has not made for any man two hearts in his interior} [al-Ahzab 4]. He witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Shurahbil b. Hasanah died on the day of al-Yarmuk during the caliphate of Umar in the year eighteen."],[5197,"\"Shurahbil, the son of Hassanah and his mother Hassanah, who was from the Adwaliyah tribe. And Abu Shurahbil, Abdullah ibn al-Muta' ibn Amr from the Kindah tribe, an ally of the Banu Zahrah, known as Abu Abdullah. He was one of the second wave of emigrants from Abyssinia.\""],[5198,"From Muhammad b. Ishaq: “In naming those who migrated to Abyssinia: Shurahbil b. Hasanah. His mother Hasanah migrated to the land of Abyssinia with her husband Sufyan b. Ma'mar b. Habib b. Wahb b. Hudhafah b. Jumah.”"],[5199,"Shurahbil b. Abdullah b. al-Muta' b. Amr b. Abd al-Aziz, and his mother is Hasanah, and her clientage belongs to Uthman b. Habib. Shurahbil ibn Hasanah died in the plague of Amawas in the year eighteen, and he was sixty-seven years old."],[5200,"The Negus sent Umm Habibah to the Prophet ﷺ with Shurahbil ibn Hasanah."],[5201,"Shurahbil ibn Hasanah was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he campaigned with him in several expeditions. He was one of the commanders whom Abu Bakr al-Siddiq appointed over Syria."],[5202,"The plague struck Syria, and Amr b. al-As addressed us, saying: 'This plague is a defilement, so flee from it into the valleys and ravines.' That reached Shurahbil ibn Hasanah, and he said: 'Amr has lied. I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Amr is more astray than his family's camel. Rather, it is a mercy from your Lord, the supplication of your Prophet ﷺ, and the death of the righteous before you.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5203,"Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. Amr, his name is Abdullah b. Suhayl b. Amr b. Abd Shams b. Nadr b. Malik b. Hisl b. Amir b. Lu'ayy. The mother of Abu Jandal is Fakhitah from Banu Nawfal b. Abd Manaf. He witnessed Badr and was with the polytheists. When he camped at Badr, he fled to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was martyred on the day of al-Yamamah. Thus I found his death in the history of Shabbab, and I think he is mistaken regarding the time of his death."],[5204,"Abu Jandal b. Suhayl b. Amr embraced Islam early in Makkah, but his father Suhayl b. Amr imprisoned him, bound him in iron, and prevented him from emigrating. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped at al-Hudaybiyyah and Suhayl b. Amr came to him and made a treaty with him as he did, Abu Jandal came dragging his chains to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned him to his father because the peace agreement was between them. Afterwards he escaped and joined Abu Basir, who was at al-Is, where a group of Muslims had gathered around him. Whenever a caravan of Quraysh passed by them, they intercepted it, killed those they could, and seized what goods they could. Abu Jandal remained with Abu Basir until Abu Basir died. Then Abu Jandal and the Muslims with him came to Madinah during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He continued to campaign with him and strive in the cause of Allah after him until he died in Syria in the plague of Amawas in the year eighteen, during the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ."],[5205,"She said: 'You do this to me among all the people? You will begin with me before them.' He said: 'Will you grant protection to polytheists?' She went out. Umm Hani said: 'I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, what I encountered from my mother's son Ali! I barely escaped from him. I granted protection to two of my in-laws who were polytheists, and he fell upon them to kill them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That was not for him. We have granted protection to the one you protected and granted security to the one you secured.' I returned to the two men and informed them, so they departed to their homes. It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Al-Harith b. Hisham and Abdullah b. Abi Rabiah are sitting in their gathering, shooting arrows in saffron-dyed cloaks.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There is no way against them; we have granted them security.' Al-Harith b. Hisham said: 'I became ashamed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ should see me, remembering his seeing me in every place among the polytheists. Then I remember his kindness and mercy. I met him while he was entering the mosque, and he received me with cheerfulness and stopped until I came to him. I greeted him and bore witness to the testimony of truth.' He said: 'Praise be to Allah who guided you. Someone like you would not be ignorant of Islam.' Al-Harith said: 'By Allah, I have never seen the like of Islam being unknown.'"],[5206,"Al-Harith b. Hisham departed from Makkah, and the people of Makkah grieved deeply. Not one remained but went out to bid him farewell, until when he was at the upper part of al-Batha or wherever he chose, he stopped, and the people stopped around him weeping. When he saw the people's grief, he said: 'O people, I did not depart out of preference for myself over you or choosing one land over your land. But this affair has come to pass, and men of Quraysh went out in it. By Allah, they were not of its elders or its noble houses. By Allah, even if the mountains of Makkah were gold and we spent them in the cause of Allah, we would not catch up with one day of their days. By Allah, if they have preceded us in this world, let us strive to share with them in the Hereafter. Let a man who goes out as a warrior fear Allah.' So he went out as a warrior to Syria and was struck down as a martyr. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5207,"He fought on their behalf and escaped with the head of his horse Tamrah and its bridle. Al-Harith b. Hisham said, excusing his flight that day [in al-tawil meter]: 'Allah knows I did not cease fighting them until they struck my horse with a frothing chestnut stallion. Then I knew that if I fought one more, I would be killed without harming my enemy in that scene. So I turned away from them while loved ones were among them, hoping for their punishment on a day of watch.' Then he fought at Uhud with the polytheists, and he did not cease adhering to polytheism until he embraced Islam on the day of the conquest of Makkah. Aisha narrated from al-Harith."],[5208,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'How does revelation come to you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Like the ringing of a bell, and when it departs from me, I have retained what he said. That is the hardest upon me. Sometimes the angel comes to me in the form of a man and speaks to me, and I retain what he says.' I do not know anyone who said in this hadith from Aisha from al-Harith other than Amir b. Salih. The companions of Hisham narrated it from his father from Aisha that al-Harith b. Hisham asked the hadith."],[5209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood as a preacher and commanded the charity of breaking the fast, a sa' of dates or a sa' of barley for every individual, or for every head, young and old, a sa' of dates or two mudds of wheat."],[5210,"Abdullah b. Tha'labah b. Su'ayr b. Abi Su'ayr al-Adawi was born four years before the Hijrah. He was carried to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who wiped his face and blessed him in the year of the conquest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was fourteen. Abdullah b. Tha'labah died, and his kunyah was Abu Muhammad, in the year eighty-nine, at the age of ninety-three."],[5211,"That the Prophet ﷺ wiped over his head."],[5212,"On the authority of Abdullah b. Tha'alaba b. Su'ayr al-Udhri, who was born in the year of the conquest. He was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who wiped his face and blessed him."],[5213,"Among the allies of Quraysh was Abdullah b. Adi b. al-Hamra al-Zuhri. His mother was the daughter of Shariq b. Amr b. Wahb b. Shariq. The kunya of Abdullah b. Adi was Abu Amr."],[5214,"Ibn Umar said: \"Abdullah b. Adi died during the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ.\""],[5215,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood at al-Hazwara and said: \"By Allah, I know that you are the best of Allah's land and the most beloved of Allah's land to me. Had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.\""],[5216,"And Khalid b. Urfuta b. Abraha b. Shayban b. Hisl b. Hind b. Abdullah b. Ghaylan b. Aslam b. Udhra, the ally of Banu Zuhra. Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas appointed him over al-Qadisiyya."],[5217,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[5218,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"There will be calamities, tribulation, division, and discord. When that happens, if you are able to be the one killed and not the killer, then do so.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5219,"Suhail b. Amr was given the kunya Abu Yazid."],[5220,"I captured Suhail and did not seek anyone else in exchange for him from all the nations. Khindif knows that the youth Suhail is her youth when he is in order. I struck with the sharp sword until it bent, and I forced myself upon the owner of the cattle. He said: Among his descendants are Abdullah, who was among the first emigrants and witnessed Badr, and Abu Jandal, and he accompanied the Prophet ﷺ, and Utbah the Younger. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5221,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"The status of one in the path of Allah for an hour is better for him than his entire life with his family.\" Suhail said, \"And I will remain stationed (in the battlefield) until I die and never return to Mecca.\" So, he remained stationed in the Levant until he died from the plague of ‘Amawas. Indeed, this plague occurred in the Levant in the year eighteen after the Hijrah.\" Al-Dhahabi excluded it from the summary due to its weakness."],[5222,"Some people were present at Umar's door, among them Suhail b. Amr, Abu Sufyan b. Harb, and elders from Quraysh. His doorkeeper came out and began to admit the people of Badr, such as Suhayb, Bilal, and Ammar. He said: By Allah, he was a Badri and he loved them, and he had been enjoined regarding them. Abu Sufyan said: \"I have never seen anything like today. These slaves are admitted while we sit here and no one pays attention to us.\" Suhail b. Amr said: \"What a man he was, how wise he was! O people, by Allah, I see what is in your faces. If you are angry, then be angry with yourselves. The people were called and you were called; they hastened and you delayed. By Allah, what they have surpassed you in of virtue, as they see, is more grievous for you to miss than this door of yours over which you compete.\" Then he said: \"These people have surpassed you in what you see, and by Allah you have no way to what they have surpassed you in. Look to this jihad and cling to it; perhaps Allah ﷻ will grant you jihad and martyrdom.\" Then he shook his garment, stood up, and went to Syria."],[5223,"Umar said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"O Messenger of Allah, let me pull out the two front teeth of Suhail b. Amr so that he will never stand as a speaker among his people.\" He said: \"Leave him, for perhaps he will please you one day.\" Sufyan said: When the Prophet ﷺ died, the people of Makkah were on the verge of abandoning Islam. Suhail b. Amr stood at the Kaaba and said: \"Whoever worshipped Muhammad ﷺ, Muhammad has died. But Allah is alive and does not die.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5224,"Bilal b. Rabah, the freed slave of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, was known by the kunya Abu Abdullah. He was among those born in the Sarat region. He died in Damascus in the year 20 AH and was buried near the Bab al-Saghir in the cemetery of Damascus. He was sixty-some years old."],[5225,"I heard Shu'ayb ibn Talhah saying, \"Bilal was the servant of Abu Bakr, and Shu'ayb was more knowledgeable about Bilal's birth.\""],[5226,"Someone who saw Bilal narrated to me: \"He was a man of very dark complexion, thin, tall, with a slight stoop. He had abundant hair, light sideburns, and much gray hair, which he did not dye. Bilal was present at Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Ubayda b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib.\""],[5227,"Bilal b. Rabah, Abu Amr. Bilal's mother was Hamama. He reached the age of sixty-seven and was buried near the Bab al-Saghir in the cemetery of Damascus."],[5228,"He was present at Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was a black man, born into slavery. Abu Bakr bought him from Umayya b. Khalaf; Abu Bakr gave a slave boy in exchange and took Bilal instead. His mother's name was Hamama, and both of them became Muslims. His kunya was Abu Abdullah. He died in Damascus in the year 20 AH, though it is also said 18 AH."],[5229,"I passed by Bilal while he was in the mosque and said, 'O Abu Abdullah, what keeps you sitting here?' He replied, 'I am waiting for the sun to rise.'"],[5230,"It is also said: Abu Amr, the freed slave of Abu Bakr ؓ."],[5231,"It is said: Umar b. Abdullah al-Madani, the freed slave of Ufra."],[5232,"A brother of Bilal claimed Arab descent and asserted that he was one of them. He proposed to an Arab woman, and they said, 'If Bilal attends, we will marry her to you.' So Bilal attended and said, 'I am Bilal b. Rabah, and this is my brother. He is a man of bad character and religion. If you wish to marry him, then do so; and if you wish to leave the matter, then leave it.' They said, 'Whoever is your brother, we will marry to him.' So they married her to him."],[5233,"The first seven to openly proclaim Islam were: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whom Allah protected through his uncle Abu Talib; Abu Bakr, whom Allah Almighty protected through his people; and the rest, whom the polytheists seized, clad in iron armor, and made to stand in the sun. Every one of them gave in to what they wanted, except Bilal, for his soul became insignificant to him in the cause of Allah ﷻ, and he became insignificant to his people. They handed him over to the children, who paraded him through the mountain paths of Makkah while he kept saying, 'One, One.' [Authentic chain, though they did not record it.] Sahih."],[5234,"Abu Bakr is our master, and he freed our master."],[5235,"Umar mentioned the excellence of Abu Bakr and began describing his virtues, then said, 'And this Bilal, our master, is one of the good deeds of Abu Bakr.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5236,"Abu Bakr freed seven of those who were tortured for the sake of Allah ﷻ, among them Bilal and Amir b. Fuhayra. Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, though they did not record it. According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5237,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The best of the black people are three: Luqman, Bilal, and Mihja', the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Its chain is sahih, but they did not record it."],[5238,"The foremost are four: I am the foremost of the Arabs, Salman is the foremost of the Persians, Bilal is the foremost of the Abyssinians, and Suhayb is the foremost of the Romans."],[5239,"How excellent a man is Bilal; he is the chief of the muezzins, and none follows him except a muezzin, and the muezzins will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection."],[5240,"One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ woke up and called Bilal, saying: O Bilal, how did you precede me to Paradise last night? I heard the rustling of your footsteps ahead of me, and I came upon a palace of gold, square and lofty. I said: For whom is this palace? They said: For a man of Quraysh. I said: I am a Qurayshi; for whom is this palace? They said: For Umar b. al-Khattab. Bilal said: O Messenger of Allah, I have never given the call to prayer except that I prayed two rak'ahs, and no ritual impurity ever befell me except that I performed ablution at that time. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Because of this.' It is sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not record it, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5241,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ while he was encamped at Ukaz. I said: Who is with you in this matter? He said: Two men, Abu Bakr and Bilal. So I embraced Islam, and I saw myself as a quarter of Islam. Its chain is sahih, but they did not record it. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5242,"Bilal died in the year twenty."],[5243,"Sa'id b. 'Amir b. Hudhaym b. Salaman b. Rabi'ah b. Sa'd b. Jumah. Umar appointed him over some of the armies of Syria, and he died while in his post in Syria in the year twenty."],[5244,"He attended the first and second Aqabah pledges from the Ansar, then from Banu Abd al-Ashhal: Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan, whose name is Malik, an ally of theirs. He was a naqib (representative) and witnessed Badr, and he has no descendants."],[5245,"And he said: Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan and As'ad b. Zurarah were among the first of the Ansar to embrace Islam in Makkah, and among the first to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before their people. They brought this to Madinah. Abu al-Haytham attended the Aqabah pledge with the Muslim Ansar, and he was one of the twelve representatives, with no disagreement among them about that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan and Uthman b. Maz'un. Abu al-Haytham witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5246,"Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan died in Madinah during the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab."],[5247,"I heard the elders of the people of the district, meaning Banu Abd al-Ashhal, saying: Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayhan died in Madinah in the year twenty."],[5248,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day from his house at noon and saw Abu Bakr sitting in the mosque. He said: 'What brought you out at this hour, O Abu Bakr?' He replied: 'What brought you out brought me out, O Messenger of Allah.' Then Umar came, and he said: 'What brought you out, O Ibn al-Khattab?' He said: 'What brought you two out, O Messenger of Allah.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat down talking with them, then said: 'Do you two have strength to go to these palm trees'—and he gestured with his hand toward the houses of the Ansar—'to get food, drink, and shade, if Allah wills?' We said: 'Yes.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out, and they set out with him. And he mentioned the hadith. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5249,"Sa'id b. 'Amir b. Hudhaym b. Salaman b. Rabi'ah b. Sa'd b. Jumah. Umar appointed him over some of the armies of Syria, and he died while in his post in Syria in the year twenty."],[5250,"ʿUmar said to Saʿid ibn ʿAmir ibn Hidhyam, “Why do the people of Syria love you?” He replied, “I look after them and I console them.” So he gave him ten thousand, but he returned it and said, “I have servants and horses, and I am well off, and I want my work to be charity for the Muslims.” ʿUmar said, “Do not do that. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me wealth less than that, and I said something like what you have said. He said to me: ‘If Allah gives you wealth that you did not ask for and you did not set your heart upon, then take it, for it is only Allah’s provision He has given you.’”"],[5251,"\"And Anas ibn Marthad ibn Abi Marthad al-Ghanawi, also known as Abu Yazid, was a companion of Hamza ibn Abd al-Muttalib. He passed away in the year twenty, in the month of Rabi al-Awwal. He had a twenty-one-year age difference with his father, as I mentioned before when talking about Abu Marthad al-Ghanawi. After him, his son Marthad came, and this is his grandson. All of them are from the companions, as Al-Dhahabi mentioned in his summary of their weakness.\""],[5252,"And Usayd b. Hudayr b. Simak b. 'Atik b. Rafi' b. Imri' al-Qays b. Zayd b. 'Abd al-Ashhal, and he was given the kunya Abu Yahya. He died in the year twenty."],[5253,"Abu Yahya Usayd b. Hudayr died in the year twenty. He had attended al-'Aqaba, then was a naqib. 'Umar b. al-Khattab prayed over him in Madinah, and he was buried in al-Baqi'. He had two kunyas: Abu Yahya and Abu Hudayr. His father was Hudayr the scribe. Usayd left no descendants."],[5254,"And Usayd b. al-Hudayr b. Simak was given the kunya Abu Yahya, and it is said Abu al-Husayn, and it is said Abu Bahr. Usayd was a nobleman among his people in the Jahiliyya and in Islam, counted among their sages and men of opinion. He was one of the scribes, and his father al-Hudayr the scribe had been the same before him. He was the chief of the Aws on the day of Bu'ath, and Hudayr was killed that day. Usayd b. Hudayr was one of the seventy of the Ansar who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of al-'Aqaba, according to a narration that includes all of them, and one of the twelve nuqaba'. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Usayd b. Hudayr and Zayd b. Haritha. Usayd did not attend Badr; he and others of the senior Companions among the nuqaba' and others stayed behind from Badr because they did not think that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would meet war or fighting. Usayd attended Uhud and was wounded that day with seven wounds, and he remained steadfast with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the people were routed. He attended al-Khandaq and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi omitted this from al-Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5255,"He used to recite on the roof of his house, and he had a beautiful voice. He said: While I was reciting, something like a cloud overshadowed me while the woman was in the house and the horse in the courtyard. I feared that the woman would fall, so I stopped. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Recite, for it was only an angel listening to the Qur'an.\""],[5256,"Usayd b. Hudayr was one of the most virtuous of people. He used to say: If I could be as I am in any one of three states, I would be among the people of Paradise, and I would have no doubt about that: when I recite the Qur'an, or when I hear it, or when I hear the sermon of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, or when I attend a funeral. I have never attended a funeral and then spoken to myself about anything other than what is being done to it and what it is heading to."],[5257,"Usayd b. Hudayr and 'Abbad b. Bishr were with the Prophet ﷺ on a dark, pitch-black night. When they departed, the staff of one of them lit up, so they walked in its light. When they separated, the staff of the other lit up. Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it."],[5258,"Usayd b. Hudayr was a righteous man, cheerful and handsome. While he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, talking to the people and making them laugh, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ poked him in his side. He said, 'You have hurt me.' He said, 'Get even.' He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you are wearing a shirt and I am not wearing a shirt.' He said: So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lifted his shirt, and he embraced him and began kissing his flank, saying, 'May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. This is what I wanted.' This is the wording of the hadith of Jarir from Husayn, for the hadith of Warqa' is abridged. Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[5259,"\"How excellent a man is Usayd b. Hudayr!\""],[5260,"He was ill and used to lead us in prayer, and he prayed sitting. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited him, and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, Usayd is our imam, and he is sick, and he prayed sitting with us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'So pray behind him sitting, for the imam is to be followed. If he prays sitting, then pray behind him sitting.' Sahih al-isnad, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[5261,"We came from a journey and were met at Dhu al-Hulayfa. The boys of the Ansar used to meet them when they arrived. They met Usayd b. Hudayr and informed him of the death of his wife, so he covered his head and wept. She said: I said to him, 'Glory be to Allah! You are one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and you have precedence; why do you weep over a woman?' He uncovered his head and said, 'You have spoken the truth. By the life of Allah, by Allah, it is right that I should not weep over anyone after Sa'd b. Mu'adh, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said.' I said to him, 'And what did he say?' He said, 'The Throne shook at the death of Sa'd b. Mu'adh.' 'A'isha said: And Usayd b. Hudayr was riding between me and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it. Al-Dhahabi omitted this from al-Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5262,"'Iyad, and what 'Iyad b. Ghanm! He was among the best of those whom women conceived. He was the first to cross the pass to Byzantium."],[5263,"From his shaykhs that they said: 'Iyad b. Ghanm b. Zuhayr b. Abi Shaddad b. Rabi'a b. Hilal b. Ahyab b. Dabba b. al-Harith b. Fihr. He embraced Islam before al-Hudaybiyya and attended al-Hudaybiyya with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was married to Umm al-Hakam bt. Abi Sufyan b. Harb. When death approached Abu 'Ubayda b. al-Jarrah, he appointed 'Iyad as his successor over what he was responsible for. 'Iyad was a righteous man. When 'Umar was told of the death of Abu 'Ubayda, he repeatedly said 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return' and asked for mercy upon him, and said, 'No one will fill your place.' He asked who was appointed successor over his work, and they said, ''Iyad b. Ghanm.' He confirmed him and wrote to him: 'I have appointed you over what Abu 'Ubayda b. al-Jarrah was in charge of, so act with what God is due from you.' 'Iyad died on the day he died with no wealth, nor did he owe anyone a debt. He died in Syria in the year twenty, and he was sixty years old. Al-Dhahabi omitted this from al-Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5264,"‘Ayyad b. Ghanm died in the year twenty."],[5265,"‘Ayyad b. Ghanm al-Ash‘ari took possession of a house belonging to a man when it was conquered. Hisham b. Hakim came to him and spoke harshly to him. Hisham stayed away for some nights, then came to ‘Ayyad apologizing. He said to ‘Ayyad, “Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘The people most severely punished on the Day of Resurrection are those most severe in punishing people in this world’?” ‘Ayyad said to him, “O Hisham, we have heard what you heard and seen what you saw and accompanied whom you accompanied.” Ibn Zurayq, and he is unreliable."],[5266,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me one day, “O ‘Ayyad, do not marry an old woman or a barren one, for I will boast of your large numbers.”"],[5267,"Al-Bara’ b. Malik b. al-Nadr b. Damdam b. Zayd b. Haram b. Jundub b. ‘Amir b. Ghanm b. ‘Adi b. al-Najjar. His mother was Umm Sulaym bt. Milhan, and he was the brother of Anas b. Malik through his father and mother. He witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was brave and held a prominent position in war."],[5268,"He entered upon his brother al-Bara’ while he was lying on his back with one leg over the other, singing. He forbade him, and he said, “Do you fear that I might die on my bed when I have single-handedly killed a hundred disbelievers, besides those in whose killing others shared with me?”"],[5269,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: Al-Bara’ b. Malik was a man with a good voice, and he used to chant verses for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during some of his journeys. While he was chanting, he drew near the women, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, “Beware of the glass vessels.” He said, “So he stopped.” Muhammad said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that the women should hear his voice.”"],[5270,"“How many a weak and oppressed person in two worn garments, if he swore by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath! Among them is al-Bara’ b. Malik. Al-Bara’ met a company of the polytheists, and the polytheists had inflicted heavy losses on the Muslims.” They said, “O Bara’, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ‘If you swore by Allah, He would fulfill your oath,’ so swear by your Lord.” He said, “I adjure You, O Lord, to grant us victory over them.” Then they met at the bridge of al-Sus and inflicted heavy losses on the Muslims. They said to him, “O Bara’, swear by your Lord.” He said, “I adjure You, O Lord, to grant us victory over them and to join me with Your Prophet ﷺ.” So they were granted victory over them, and al-Bara’ was killed as a martyr."],[5271,"On the day of al-‘Aqaba in Persia, when the people had withdrawn, al-Bara’ b. Malik stood up, mounted his horse while it was slowly moving, then said to his companions, “Evil is what you have accustomed your peers to.” Then he charged at the enemy, and Allah granted victory to the Muslims, and al-Bara’ was martyred that day."],[5272,"“Al-Nu‘man b. ‘Amr b. Muqarrin b. ‘Amir b. Bakr b. Hujayn b. Nasr al-Muzani.”"],[5273,"“Al-Nu‘man b. Muqarrin al-Muzani was killed while he was commander of the people in the year twenty-one.”"],[5274,"“I came to Ibn ‘Umar with the news of the death of al-Nu‘man b. Muqarrin. He placed his hand over his face and began to weep.”"],[5276,"We, the Banu Muqarrin, were seven during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We had one servant, and one of us slapped him. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Set him free.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5277,"And Qatada b. al-Nu'man b. Yazid b. Amr b. Sawwad b. Zafar, and the name of Zufur is Ka'b b. al-Khazraj b. Amr, and he is al-Nabit b. Malik b. Aws. Qatada was given the kunya Abu Amr, and he is the grandfather of Asim and Ya'qub, the two sons of Umar b. Qatada. Asim b. Umar was one of the scholars of siyar and other subjects."],[5278,"Because he came from Hadramawt, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had appointed him over al-Bahrayn. Then Umar appointed him over al-Bahrayn, and he died there, so he appointed in his place Abu Hurayra al-Dawsi. Indeed, al-Ala b. al-Hadhrami died in al-Bahrayn in the year twenty-one.\""],[5279,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ accepting the people's allegiance on the day of the conquest. He said: He sat near Samura's house. Al-Aswad said: I saw the Prophet ﷺ sit, and the people came to him, young and old, men and women, and gave him allegiance upon Islam and the shahada. I said: What is Islam? He said: \"Faith in Allah.\" I said: What is the shahada? He said: \"The testimony that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5280,"The Prophet ﷺ took Hussain and kissed him. Then, he approached them (the people) and said, 'Verily, this child is a source of stinginess, cowardice, ignorance, and sadness.'"],[5281,"\"Muhammad b. al-Aswad b. Khalaf b. Abd Yaghuth al-Qurashi, counted among the Makkans.\""],[5282,"Khalid b. al-Walid died in the year twenty-one at Hims."],[5283,"Khalid b. al-Walid b. al-Mughira b. Abd Allah b. Umar b. Makhzum, and his mother was Lubaba bt. al-Harith b. Hazn al-Hilaliyya, the sister of Maymuna bt. al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. Khalid was given the kunya Abu Sulayman. Umar b. al-Khattab appointed him over al-Ruha, Harran, al-Rabba, and Amid, and he remained for a year, then asked to be excused, so he excused him. He then came to Madinah and stayed there in his house until he died in Madinah in the year twenty-two."],[5284,"I heard Yahya b. Bukayr say: \"Khalid b. al-Walid was given the kunya Abu Sulayman.\""],[5285,"It was said to Umar b. al-Khattab: \"Some women of Banu al-Mughira have gathered in the house of Khalid b. al-Walid weeping, and we dislike that they should disturb you. Would you forbid them?\" Umar said: \"What harm is there if they shed a bucket or two of their tears, as long as there is no laq' or laqlaqa?\" He meant by laq' slapping and by laqlaqa wailing. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5286,"\"When the Prophet ﷺ returned from the Confederates, Khalid b. al-Walid stayed at the abode of the Confederates and sent word to the Prophet ﷺ of his Islam.\" He narrated to us confirming what al-Zubaydi mentioned about Khalid b. al-Walid's Islam before Khaybar."],[5287,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Khaybar, and he sent me to call out: \"Prayer is congregational. None shall enter Paradise except a submitted soul.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5288,"\"The conquest of Khaybar was in the year six.\""],[5289,"I set out heading to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I met Khalid b. al-Walid shortly before the conquest, while he was coming from Makkah. I said: Where are you heading, O Abu Sulayman? He said: By Allah, the brand has straightened, and indeed the man is a prophet; I am going to submit. Until when? He said: \"We arrived in Madinah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and Khalid b. al-Walid went forward, submitted, and pledged allegiance. Then I approached, pledged allegiance, and departed.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5290,"And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned Khalid b. al-Walid, saying: \"Yes, a servant of Allah and brother of the tribe, and a sword among the swords of Allah.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5291,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the deaths of the people of Mu'tah, he said: \"Then the banner was taken by a sword among the swords of Allah, Khalid b. al-Walid, and Allah granted victory through him.\""],[5292,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced the deaths of the people of Mu'tah from the pulpit, then said: \"Then Khalid b. al-Walid took the standard, and he is a sword among the swords of Allah.\""],[5293,"\"Do not harm Khalid, for he is a sword among the swords of Allah that He has unleashed upon the disbelievers.\""],[5294,"\"There was no one more hostile to the Arabs than Hurmuz. When we finished with Musaylimah and his companions, we headed towards the direction of Basra, and Hurmuz met us at Kazimah with a great army. Khalid went out to him and called for single combat, and Hurmuz went out to him, and Khalid b. al-Walid killed him. He wrote about that to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, who granted him his spoils. His cap reached a value of one hundred thousand dirhams, for the Persians, when a man was noble, would value his cap at one hundred thousand dirhams.\""],[5295,"They sought it but did not find it. Then they sought it and found it, and it was a worn cap. Khalid said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed 'umrah and shaved his head. The people rushed to the sides of his hair, but I got to his forelock before them and put it in this cap. I have not witnessed a battle with it with me except that I was granted victory.\" It is mursal."],[5296,"Khalid b. al-Walid wrote to Rustam, Mihran, and the nobles of Persia: \"Peace be upon those who follow guidance. To proceed: We call you to Islam. If you refuse, then give the jizyah from the hand while you are humbled. If you refuse, then with me is a people who love death in the path of Allah as the Persians love wine and peace.\""],[5297,"\"Khalid b. al-Walid died in Madinah in the year twenty-two.\""],[5298,"Yahya b. Bukayr: \"He died in Madinah in the year seventeen or eighteen.\""],[5299,"From 'Urwah: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr from Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza: Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, an ally of theirs.\""],[5300,"\"Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah had the kunyah Abu Muhammad.\""],[5301,"\"Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah, whose kunyah is Abu Muhammad, is said to be from Lakhm, then one of Banu Rashidah. He witnessed Badr, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to al-Muqawqis, the ruler of Alexandria. He was among the mentioned archers from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He died in Madinah at the age of sixty-five, and 'Uthman b. 'Affan prayed over him. He was a merchant who sold food, had a good body, a light beard, inclined towards shortness, and was not rough-fingered.\""],[5302,"I heard Yahya b. Bukayr say: “Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah died in the year thirty, and Uthman b. Affan prayed over him, and he was given the kunya Abu Muhammad.”"],[5303,"He looked upon the Prophet ﷺ at Uhud while he was in pain, and in the hand of Ali b. Abi Talib was a shield containing water, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was washing his face from that water. Hatib said to him: “Who did this to you?” He said: “Utbah b. Abi Waqqas smashed my face and broke my front tooth with a stone he threw at me.” I said: “I heard a crier crying out on the mountain, ‘Muhammad has been killed,’ so I came to you, and my soul had almost left me.” I said: “Where did Utbah go?” He pointed to where he went, so I went until I caught him and struck him with the sword and threw down his head. Then I descended, took his head, his spoils, and his horse, and brought them to the Prophet ﷺ, who granted that to me and prayed for me, saying “ ؓ ” twice."],[5304,"A slave of Hatib came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ complaining about Hatib, saying: “O Prophet of Allah, Hatib will surely enter the Fire.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You lie. He will never enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Hudaybiyyah.”"],[5305,"He narrated to him that his father wrote a letter to the disbelievers of Quraysh while he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and had witnessed Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ali and al-Zubayr and said: “Go until you catch up with a woman who has a letter with her, and bring it to me.” They went until they reached her and said: “Give us the letter that is with you,” and they told her that they would not leave until they stripped every garment from her. She said: “Are you not two Muslim men?” They said: “Yes, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that you have a letter.” When she was certain that she could not escape them, she untied the letter from her head and handed it to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Hatib and read the letter to him, saying: “Do you recognize this letter?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “What made you do this?” He said: “My children and relatives are there, and I was a bedouin man among you, the people of Quraysh.” Umar said: “Permit me, O Messenger of Allah, to kill Hatib.” The Messenger of Allah said: “No, for he witnessed Badr, and you do not know—perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.’”"],[5306,"“Ubayy b. Ka'b b. Qays b. Ubayd b. Zayd b. Mu'awiyah b. Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar witnessed Badr.”"],[5307,"Khalifah b. Khayyat narrated to us, mentioning this lineage and adding: “The mother of Ubayy b. Ka'b was Suhaylah bt. al-Aswad b. Haram b. Amr b. Zayd Manat b. Adi b. Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar, and she was the paternal aunt of Abu Talhah.”"],[5308,"“Ubayy b. Ka'b died during the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab in the year twenty-two.”"],[5309,"Muhammad b. Umar narrated to us, mentioning the lineage similarly and adding: “He witnessed the Aqabah among the seventy from the Ansar, and he used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. There is disagreement about the time of his death: it is said he died during the caliphate of Umar in the year twenty-two, and it is said he died during the caliphate of Uthman in the year thirty. The latter is the more reliable of the statements, because Uthman ordered him to compile the Quran.”"],[5310,"“I saw Ubayy b. Ka'b with a white head and beard, not dyeing it.”"],[5311,"“The judges among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were six: Umar, Ali, Abdullah, Ubayy, Zayd, and Abu Musa—thus he narrated to us, and in most and the most authentic narrations, Mu'adh b. Jabal is in place of Abu Musa.”"],[5312,"I heard Abu Mushir say: “Ubayy b. Ka'b—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him the master of the Ansar, and he did not die until they said, ‘Master of the Muslims.’”"],[5313,"“And Ubayy died during the caliphate of Umar in the year twenty-two.”"],[5314,"Ubay b. Ka'b died during the caliphate of Uthman in the year thirty-two. The disagreement is apparent regarding the time of the death of Ubay b. Ka'b."],[5315,"He died during the caliphate of Uthman in the year thirty. It was mentioned that he had the kunya Abu al-Tufayl, and he had two kunyas. His death was in the city of the Prophet ﷺ after the criticism of Uthman had appeared."],[5316,"Ubay had a harshness."],[5317,"When the people fell into the affair of Uthman, I said to Ubay b. Ka'b: Abu al-Mundhir, what is the way out of this affair? He said: \"The Book of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet. What is clear to you, act upon it, and what is unclear to you, entrust it to its knower.\""],[5318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between his companions, and he established brotherhood between Ubay b. Ka'b and Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl."],[5319,"I witnessed Madinah. When the prayer was established, I advanced and stood in the first row. Then Umar b. al-Khattab came out and split the rows, then advanced, and with him came a dark-skinned man with a light beard. He looked at the faces of the people, and when he saw me, he pushed me and stood in my place. That distressed me greatly. When he finished, he turned to me and said: Do not let it grieve you or sadden you. Would it be hard for you that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"None stands in the first row except the Muhajirun and the Ansar\"? So I said: Who is this? They said: Ubay b. Ka'b."],[5320,"\"A surah was sent down to me, and I was commanded to recite it to you.\" He said: I said: Was I named to you? He said: \"Yes.\" I said to Ubay: Did you rejoice at that, O Abu al-Mundhir? He said: And what prevents me, while Allah, exalted and blessed, says: \"Say: In the bounty of Allah and in His mercy – in that let them rejoice.\""],[5321,"I heard Ikrimah bin Sulaiman saying, \"I read upon Ismail bin Abdullah bin Qustantini. When I reached the verse of Ad-Duha, he said to me, 'Say Allahu Akbar at the end of every chapter until you finish.' Abdullah bin Kathir informed him that Mujahid had read upon him and commanded him to do so. Mujahid informed him that Ibn Abbas had commanded him to do so. Ibn Abbas informed him that Ubayy bin Ka'b had commanded him to do so. And Ubayy bin Ka'b informed him that the Prophet ﷺ had commanded him to do so.\""],[5322,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Abu al-Mundhir, which verse in the Book of Allah that you have is the greatest?\" He said: I said: \"Allah – there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of existence\" [Al-Baqarah 255]. He said: Then he struck my chest and said: \"May knowledge be pleasing to you, O Abu al-Mundhir.\""],[5323,"I came to Madinah seeking knowledge. I entered the mosque and found a man with people gathered around him. I said: Who is this? They said: This is Ubay b. Ka'b. I followed him, and he entered his house. I knocked on the door, and he came out and rebuked me and glared at me. I faced the qibla and said: \"O Allah, we complain about them to You. We spend our provisions, weary our bodies, and drive our mounts seeking knowledge, but when we meet them, they dislike us.\" He said: If you give me until Friday, I will certainly speak with what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not fearing therein the blame of any blamer. When Thursday came, I went out early, and the streets were crowded. I said: What is the matter with the people today? They said: It seems you are a stranger. I said: Yes. They said: The master of the Muslims, Ubay b. Ka'b, has died."],[5324,"Ali is the best judge among us, and Ubay is the best reciter among us. We leave some of what Ubay says."],[5325,"Umar said to him: Who taught you this verse? He said: Ubay b. Ka'b taught it to me. He said: Take us to him. So they went to him, and he was leaning on a cushion, combing his hair. He greeted him, and he returned the greeting. He said: O Abu al-Mundhir. He said: \"At your service.\" He said: This man told me that you taught him this verse. He said: \"He spoke the truth. I received it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Umar said: You received it from the Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Yes, I received it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,\" three times, each time saying it, and the third time he was angry: \"Yes, by Allah, Allah sent it down to Jibril, and Jibril sent it down to Muhammad, and He did not consult al-Khattab about it, nor his son.\" Then Umar left, raising his hands and saying: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5326,"He said to him: O Commander of the Believers, that is only shirk. Have you not heard the saying of Luqman to his son: \"O my son, do not associate partners with Allah. Indeed, association is a great wrong\" [Luqman 13]? Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5327,"\"Abdul Rahman ibn Awf ibn Abdul Rahman ibn Abd ibn Al-Harith ibn Zuhrah ibn Kilab ibn Murrah ibn Kaab ibn Luayy ibn Ghalib ibn Fihri ibn Malik\" translates to \"Abdul Rahman, the son of Awf, the son of Abdul Rahman, the son of Abd, the son of Al-Harith, the son of Zuhrah, the son of Kilab, the son of Murrah, the son of Kaab, the son of Luayy, the son of Ghalib, the son of Fihri, the son of Malik.\""],[5328,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf b. Abd al-Rahman b. al-Harith b. Zuhra. His mother and the mother of his brother al-Aswad b. Awf were al-Shifa bt. Awf b. Abd b. al-Harith b. Zuhra b. Kilab. She had emigrated before the conquest. Abd al-Rahman's name was Abd Amr, so the Prophet ﷺ named him Abd al-Rahman."],[5329,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf died in the ninth year of Uthman's caliphate, and Uthman prayed over him. He had reached seventy-five years of age."],[5330,"From him, al-Dhahabi in the Talkhis."],[5331,"Khalifa b. Khayyat narrated to us and mentioned this lineage, adding: \"Abd al-Rahman's kunya was Abu Muhammad, and his name in the Jahiliyya was Abd al-Ka'ba, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Abd al-Rahman.\" [It is] according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5332,"\"My name in the Jahiliyya was Abd Amr, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Abd al-Rahman.\""],[5333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abd al-Rahman, \"What did you do, O Abu Muhammad, in touching the corner—meaning the Black Stone?\" Abd al-Rahman said, \"I touched it and left off.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You did right.\""],[5334,"I saw Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas at the funeral of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf say, \"Go, Ibn Awf, with your fill of this world, having taken nothing from it.\""],[5335,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abd al-Rahman, \"How did you do, O Abu Muhammad, in touching the Stone?\" He said, \"I touched it and left off.\" He said, \"You did right, O Abu Muhammad.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5336,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, whose kunya was Abu Muhammad, died in the year thirty-two, and he was seventy-five years old."],[5337,"Abd al-Rahman b. Awf fainted during his illness, a faint in which they thought he had passed away, until they rose from his side, covered him with a cloth, and Umm Kulthum bt. Uqba, his wife, went out to the mosque to seek help in what she was commanded of patience and prayer. They waited a while while he was in the faint; then he regained consciousness. The first thing he said was to say takbir, so the people of the house and those near them said takbir. Then he said to them, \"Did I faint just now?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then he said, \"Two men took me away in my faint, one of them stern and rough. They said, 'Come, let us take you to judgment before the Almighty, the All-Knowing.' Then [one] said, 'Return him, for he is among those for whom Allah wrote happiness and forgiveness in their mothers' wombs, and his sons will enjoy him as long as Allah wills.'\" He lived after that for a month, then died, and Uthman led the pilgrimage that year."],[5338,"Umayya b. Khalaf said, \"Write to me with your name by which you used to write to me: Abd Amr.\""],[5339,"I heard Sa'd b. Malik say, when Abd al-Rahman b. Awf died, \"Alas for the mountain!\""],[5340,"On his authority, al-Dhahabi in the Talkhis."],[5341,"On his authority, al-Dhahabi in the Talkhis."],[5342,"I heard Anas ibn Malik saying, \"Abdul Rahman ibn Auf migrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ formed a brotherhood between him and Sa'd ibn Ar-Rabi'.\""],[5343,"I heard ʿAli say to ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf on the day he died: \"Go, O Ibn ʿAwf, for you have attained its clear portion and outstripped its dregs.\""],[5344,"\"I have heard that ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf freed thirty thousand households.\""],[5345,"From Abu al-Aswad, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Banu Zuhrah b. Kilab b. Murrah: ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf b. Zuhayr."],[5346,"The passage translates to: “’Abdur-Rahman ibn 'Awf left behind a thousand camels and three thousand sheep in Naqee', and one hundred horses grazing in Naqee'. He used to farm in Al-Jurf with twenty irrigating camels, and he would reserve a year's worth of provisions for his household from that. 'Abdur-Rahman ibn 'Awf had embraced Islam before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the house of Al-Arqam or called therein. He witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the battles of Badr, Uhud, and Al-Khandaq, and all the other battles, and he remained steadfast with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when others fled.’ Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary.”"],[5347,"He was called the disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5348,"\"Othman said: 'Here, oh Miswar! Who claimed to be better than your uncle Abdul Rahman in the first migration has indeed lied.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summarization.\""],[5349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Busrah while she was combing ʿAʾishah's hair and said: \"O Busrah, who is asking for Umm Kulthum's hand?\" She said: I heard one or two men. He said: \"Then where are you concerning the leader of the Muslims, ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf?\""],[5350,"ʿAli said: I am the first to be pleased, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to you: \"You are trustworthy among the people of heaven, trustworthy among the people of earth.\" Abu al-Muʿalla is Furat b. al-Saʾib; they abandoned him."],[5351,"I said to ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar..."],[5352,"ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf sold land of his for forty thousand dinars and divided it among the Banu Zuhrah, the poor of the Muslims, the Muhajirun, and the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. He sent some of that wealth to ʿAʾishah, and she said: \"Who sent this wealth?\" I said: \"ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf.\" He said: And he related the story. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None will be tender to you after me except the patient ones. May Allah give Ibn ʿAwf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise.\""],[5353,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to his wives: \"The one who will be tender to you after me is the truthful, the righteous. O Allah, give ʿAbd al-Rahman b. ʿAwf to drink from Salsabil of Paradise.\" The hadith has been authenticated from ʿAʾishah and Umm Salamah, from ʿAʾishah and Umm Salamah."],[5354,"\"O Ibn ʿAwf, you are among the wealthy, and you will not enter Paradise except crawling. So lend to Allah; He will release your feet.\" He said: \"What shall I lend to Allah?\" He said: \"You should free yourself from what you possess.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, from all of it entirely?\" He said: \"Yes.\" So Ibn ʿAwf went out intending to do that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him and said: \"Gabriel came to me and said: Command Ibn ʿAwf to host the guest, feed the poor, give to the beggar, and begin with those he supports, for if he does that, it will be purification for what he possesses.\""],[5355,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best of you is the best to your family after me.\" Quraysh said, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me from Abu Salama ibn Abdur Rahman that his father left a will to the wives of the believers and left them a garden worth forty thousand dinars."],[5356,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to me, \"Your affairs are among what concerns me after me, and none will be patient with you except the patient ones.\" Then she said, \"May Allah give your father to drink from Salsabil of Paradise.\" And 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf had connected them with wealth, so it was sold for forty thousand. Sakhr b. 'Abd Allah, truthful, but they did not narrate from him."],[5357,"Musa b. 'Awn b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Awn dictated to me: \"'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud b. Kahil b. Habib b. Tamir b. Makhzum b. Sahilah b. Kahil b. al-Harith b. Taym b. Sa'd b. Hudhayl b. Mudrikah b. Ilyas b. Mudar b. Nizar.\""],[5358,"\"'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud b. al-Harith b. Shamkh b. Makhzum b. Kahil b. al-Harith b. Sa'd b. Hudhayl, from the allies of Banu Zuhrah.\" Al-Waqidi opposed both of them regarding this lineage."],[5359,"That 'Ammar b. Yasir was prayed over and buried in al-Baqi' at night, and he was some sixty-odd years old."],[5360,"That the Prophet ﷺ gave him the kunyah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, and no son was born to him."],[5361,"The mother of 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud is Umm 'Abd bt. 'Abd b. al-Harith b. Zuhrah."],[5362,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: The kunyah of 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud is Abu 'Abd al-Rahman."],[5363,"'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud was slender and delicate, and his mother was Umm 'Abd bt. 'Abd b. al-Harith b. Zuhrah, and it is said that she was from al-Qarah."],[5364,"I saw myself as the sixth of six, and there was no Muslim on earth other than us."],[5365,"'Urwah said: \"Among those who emigrated to Abyssinia in the first emigration, before the departure of Ja'far b. Abi Talib, was 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud.\""],[5366,"I was with 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, and he was a dark-skinned man with a slight touch of something, slender in body, thin in flesh."],[5367,"'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud died in Madinah, and al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam prayed over him."],[5368,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām and ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd. Its chain is authentic, but they did not record it. Authentic."],[5369,"A mention of what ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd instructed if something happened to him during this illness of his: that his will should return to Allah, then to al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām and his son ʿAbdullāh b. al-Zubayr, and that they are released and absolved from what they took charge of and decided; and that the daughters of ʿAbdullāh should not marry except with their permission, and that this does not apply specifically to Zaynab."],[5370,"ʿAbdullāh would have a year pass without narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day he narrated a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and grief overcame him, and sweat began to trickle down his forehead, and he said: “Something like this, or close to this.”"],[5371,"That he heard Abū Mūsā say: “My brother and I arrived from Yemen, and we stayed for a while, seeing nothing except that ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd was a man from the household of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, because of what we saw of his entering and his mother’s entering upon him.”"],[5372,"“Ibn Umm ʿAbd is one of those closest in means to Allah on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[5373,"“ʿAbdullāh, when eyes fell still, I would hear a humming from him like the humming of bees until morning.”"],[5374,"“ʿAbdullāh would give us a sermon every Thursday on his feet, speaking a few words, while we wished he would add more.”"],[5375,"I read in ʿUmar’s letter to the people of Yemen and Kufa: “To proceed: you are the head of the Arabs and their cranium, and you are my arrow which I shoot with, whether something comes from here or there. I have sent ʿAbdullāh to you and chosen him for you, preferring you over myself with him.” Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[5376,"That some people came to ʿAlī and praised ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd, so he said: “I say about him what they said, and more: he read the Qur’an, made lawful its lawful, and made forbidden its forbidden; a jurist in religion, knowledgeable of the Sunnah.”"],[5377,"Abū Mūsā said: “If you say that, then he used to hear when we did not hear, and enter when we did not enter.” Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[5378,"“If you knew my sins, no two men would tread upon my heel, and you would throw dust upon my head. I would wish that Allah forgave me a sin among my sins, and I was called ʿAbdullāh b. Rawtha.”"],[5379,"I arrived in Syria and prayed two rakʿahs, then I said: “O Allah, make easy for me a righteous companion.” I met a group of people and sat, and then one of them came and sat beside me. I said: “Who is this?” He said: “Abū al-Dardāʾ.” I said: “I supplicated Allah to make easy for me a righteous companion, and He made it easy for me.” He said: “From whom are you?” I said: “From the people of Kufa.” He said: “Is not among you Ibn Umm ʿAbd, the owner of the sandals, the cushion, and the purification vessel? And among you is the one whom Allah protected from Satan by the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ. And among you is the keeper of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which no one else knows.”"],[5380,"Ten are in Paradise. He mentioned Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talha, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman b. Awf, Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, Sa'id b. Zayd, and Abdullah b. Mas'ud."],[5381,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they are both heavier in the Balance than Uhud.\""],[5382,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ, and with him were Abu Bakr and those of his Companions whom Allah willed. We passed by Abdullah b. Mas'ud while he was praying. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Who is this?\" It was said, \"Abdullah b. Mas'ud.\" He said, \"Abdullah recites the Qur'an freshly as it was revealed.\" Abdullah praised his Lord and extolled Him, and he did well in his praise of his Lord. Then he asked Him, and he made his request concise, and he asked Him as the best request a servant could ask his Lord. Then he said, \"O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not waver, and bliss that never ends, and the companionship of Muhammad ﷺ in the highest Illiyyin, in Your gardens, the gardens of eternity.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept saying, \"Ask and you shall be given, ask and you shall be given,\" twice. So I went to give him the glad tidings, but I found that Abu Bakr had preceded me, and he was always foremost in good."],[5383,"He said: \"I am pleased for my community with what Ibn Umm Abd is pleased for it.\""],[5384,"He said: \"I am pleased for my community with what Ibn Umm Abd is pleased for it.\""],[5385,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If I were to appoint anyone to a position of authority without consulting (the believers), I would have appointed Ibn Umm ʿAbd (ʿAbdullah bin Masʿood).ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 739)"],[5386,"He said: \"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an freshly as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd.\""],[5387,"I was sitting with Umar when a thin man came to him, and he began to look at him and his face beamed. Then he said, \"How filled with knowledge he is! How filled with knowledge he is!\" meaning Abdullah b. Mas'ud."],[5388,"\"Tell us about the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"About which of them?\" He said, \"Tell us about Abdullah b. Mas'ud.\" He said, \"He learned the Book and the Sunnah, then he stopped, and that is sufficient for him.\" And the rest of the hadith mentions: \"It is authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it,\" according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5389,"It was revealed concerning five men of Quraysh, and I and Ibn Mas'ud were among them. Quraysh said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"If you would drive away these people, we would sit with you. You bring these close instead of us.\" Then it was revealed: {And do not drive away those who call upon their Lord morning and evening, seeking His countenance} [al-An'am 52] up to His saying {of the thankful} [al-An'am 53]."],[5390,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abdullah b. Mas'ud, \"Recite.\" He said, \"Should I recite while it was revealed to you?\" He said, \"I love to hear it from someone else.\" He said: He began Surah al-Nisa' until he reached: {So how will it be when We bring from every nation a witness, and We bring you as a witness against these?} [al-Nisa' 41]. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wept, and Abdullah stopped. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Speak.\" So he praised Allah at the beginning of his speech, extolled Allah, sent blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ, bore the testimony of truth, and said, \"We are pleased with Allah as Lord and Islam as religion, and I am pleased for you with what Allah and His Messenger are pleased.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I am pleased for you with what Ibn Umm Abd is pleased for you.\""],[5391,"Shaqiq used to mention the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, but he did not mention Ibn Mas'ud. I said to him, \"I see that you do not mention Ibn Mas'ud.\" He said, \"That is a man over whom I do not prefer anyone.\""],[5392,"He said: \"Abdullah resembled the Prophet ﷺ in his guidance, his manner, and his conduct.\" Ibrahim said: \"And Alqama resembled Abdullah.\""],[5393,"While I was in my house in Kufa, I heard at the door of the house: 'Peace be upon you, may I enter?' I said: 'And upon you be peace, enter.' When he entered, it was Abdullah b. Mas'ud. I said: 'O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what hour is this for a visit?' That was at midday. He said: 'The day seemed long to me, so I remembered with whom I could converse.' Then he began to narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I narrated to him. Then he started to tell me, saying: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There will be a tribulation in which the one lying down is better than the one reclining, the one reclining is better than the one sitting, the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one riding. Its slain will all be in the Fire.\"' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, when is that?' He said: 'That is the days of killing (al-harj).' I said: 'When are the days of killing?' He said: 'When a man does not trust his companion.' I said: 'What do you command me to do if I reach that time?' He said: 'Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what if someone enters my house upon me?' He said: 'Then enter your inner room.' I said: 'What if someone enters my inner room upon me?' He said: 'Then enter your mosque and do like this—or he grasped with his right hand on the wrist—and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that.'"],[5394,"It was said to al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib: 'Which of you is older, you or the Prophet ﷺ?' He said: 'He is older than I, but I was born before him.'"],[5395,"'Al-Abbas was older than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ by three years.' He was brought to my mother, and it was said to her: 'Aminah has given birth to a boy.' So she went out with me in the morning, holding my hand, until we entered upon her. It is as if I am looking at him kicking his legs in his courtyard, and the women began talking to me, saying: 'Kiss your brother.' He said: 'Al-Abbas died in the year thirty-four, and he was eighty-eight years old.'"],[5396,"That Abbas bin Abdul-Muttalib bin Hashim bin Abd Manaf is a cousin of Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. His mother is Nuteila bint Khabbab bin Kulayb bin Malik bin Amr bin Amr bin Zaid bin Manat bin Amir Al-Khazrajiya. Abbas was also known as Abu Al-Fadl. Al-Fadl was his eldest son. Abbas was three years older than Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. Abbas witnessed the conquests of Mecca, Hunayn, Taif, and Tabuk with Prophet Muhammad ﷺ. He stayed with him on the day of Hunayn with his family when people abandoned him."],[5397,"'The mother of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib is Nutaylah bt. Khabbab b. Kulayb b. Malik b. Amr b. Amir b. al-Namir b. Qasit. Al-Abbas was born three years before the Elephant.'"],[5398,"'Al-Abbas freed seventy slaves at his death.'"],[5399,"I was a servant of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, and I had embraced Islam, and Umm al-Fadl had embraced Islam, and al-Abbas had embraced Islam, but he was concealing his Islam out of fear of his people. Abu Lahab had stayed behind from Badr and sent in his place al-As b. Hisham, for he owed him a debt. He said to him: 'Take care of this raid for me, and I will leave you what you owe me.' So he did. When the news came and Allah disgraced Abu Lahab, and I was a weak man, carving these wooden bowls in a room. By Allah, I was sitting in the room carving my bowls, and Umm al-Fadl was with me, when the wicked Abu Lahab came dragging his feet—I think he said—at the rope of the room, and his back was to my back. The people said: 'This is Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith.' Abu Lahab said: 'Come to me, O son of my brother.' Abu Sufyan came and sat by him, and the people came and stood over them. He said: 'O son of my brother, how was the affair of the people?' He said: 'Nothing. By Allah, we met them and we gave them our shoulders; they killed us as they wished and captured us as they wished. By Allah, I do not blame the people.' He said: 'Why?' He said: 'I saw white men on piebald horses. By Allah, they do not miss anything, and nothing can stand against them.' He said: 'Then I lifted the rope of the room and said: By Allah, those are the angels.' Abu Lahab raised his hand and struck my face, and I fought with him, but he overpowered me and threw me to the ground until he knelt on my chest. Then Umm al-Fadl stood up, tucked up her garment, took one of the poles of the room, and struck him with it, causing a severe wound on his head. She said: 'O enemy of Allah, you thought him weak because you saw his master absent from him.' He stood up humiliated. By Allah, he lived only seven nights until Allah struck him with the adasah (a plague sore), and it killed him. His two sons left him for two or three nights without burying him until he stank. A man from Quraysh said to his two sons: 'Are you not ashamed? Your father has stunk in his house.' They said: 'We fear this sore.' Quraysh used to fear the adasah as they feared the plague. A man said: 'Go, and I will be with you.' By Allah, they did not wash him except by throwing water on him from a distance. Then they carried him and threw him in upper Makkah against a wall, and they threw stones on him."],[5400,"'Al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib had embraced Islam and remained in charge of his water distribution (siqayah), and did not migrate.'"],[5401,"That I should shoot a stone at the seventy riders from the Ansar who came as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us, and with him was his uncle al-Abbas. He said: 'O uncle, take for me from your maternal uncles.' He said: 'O Muhammad, ask for your Lord and for yourself whatever you wish.' He said: 'As for what I ask you for myself, you are to protect me from what you protect your wealth and yourselves.' They said: 'What is for us if we do that?' He said: 'Paradise.' These narrations are all with one wording, and in the hadith of Musa b. Imran, he did not hear it except from him."],[5402,"We, the family of al-Abbas, had entered Islam, and we were concealing our Islam. I was a servant of al-Abbas, carving wooden bowls. When Quraysh marched to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr, we began to await news. Then al-Daman al-Khuza'i came to us with the news, and we found strength in ourselves, and what came to us of the news of the victory of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pleased us. By Allah, I was sitting in the portico of Zamzam carving bowls, and Umm al-Fadl was sitting with me, and we were pleased with the news of the victory of the Messenger of Allah, when the news reached us about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the wicked Abu Lahab came dragging his feet, and Allah had disgraced and humiliated him because of the news that came to him, until he sat on the rope of the room. The people said: 'This is Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith, he has arrived.' The people gathered around him. Abu Lahab said to him: 'Come to me, O son of my brother.' He sat before him. He said: 'Tell me about the people.' He said: 'Yes, by Allah, these people—when we met them, we gave them our shoulders; they placed their weapons in us wherever they wished. By Allah, with that, I do not blame the people. We met white men on piebald horses. By Allah, they did not leave anything.' He said: 'Then I lifted the rope of the room and said: Those, by Allah, are the angels.' He said: 'Abu Lahab raised his hand and struck my face with a severe blow, and I fought with him, but I was a weak man. He overpowered me and threw me to the ground and knelt on my chest and beat me. Umm al-Fadl went to one of the poles of the tent, took it, and said: You thought him weak because his master is absent from him, and she struck him with the pole on his head, causing a severe wound. He stood up dragging his feet, humiliated. Allah struck him with the adasah, and by Allah, he remained only seven days until he died. His two sons left him in his house for three days without burying him until he stank. Quraysh used to fear this adasah as they feared the plague, until a man from Quraysh said to them: Woe to you both, are you not ashamed? Your father has stunk in his house and you do not bury him. They said: We fear the infection of this sore. He said: Go, and I will help you with him. By Allah, they did not wash him except by throwing water from a distance, not coming near him. Then they carried him to upper Makkah, leaned him against a wall, and then threw stones on him. Husayn b. Abdullah b. Ubaydullah is weak."],[5403,"'I was a servant of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, and Islam had entered us, the people of the house. Al-Abbas embraced Islam, Umm al-Fadl embraced Islam, and I embraced Islam. Al-Abbas used to fear his people and disliked opposing them, and he concealed his Islam.'"],[5404,"Some men from the Ansar asked permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'Permit us to leave the ransom of our nephew al-Abbas.' He said: 'By Allah, you will not leave a single dirham.'"],[5405,"When the people of Makkah came to ransom their captives, Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for the ransom of Abu al-As, and she sent with it a necklace that Khadijah had given her when she was married to Abu al-As. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he felt intense compassion for her and said: 'If you see fit to release her captive and return to her what belongs to her, then do so.' They said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah,' and they returned to her what belonged to her. This is on the condition of Muslim."],[5406,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to honor al-Abbas with the reverence a child has for his father, especially, a reverence Allah singled out al-Abbas for among all people."],[5407,"Al-Abbas is from me and I am from him."],[5408,"O Abu al-Fadl, you have from Allah until you are satisfied."],[5409,"One day I was in the mosque when Abu Jahl came and said: 'I vow by Allah that if I see Muhammad prostrating, I will step on his neck.' So I went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and entered upon him and informed him of Abu Jahl's words. He went out angry until he came to the mosque. He hurried before entering from the gate and leapt over the wall. I said: 'This is a day of evil.' I wrapped my lower garment and followed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while reciting: 'Read in the name of your Lord who created, created man from a clinging clot.' When he reached the matter of Abu Jahl, {No! Indeed, man transgresses because he sees himself self-sufficient} [al-'Alaq: 7], a man said to Abu Jahl: 'O Abu al-Hakam, this is Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Abu Jahl said: 'Do you not see what I see? By Allah, he has filled the horizon of the sky against me.' When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached the end of the surah, he prostrated."],[5410,"I heard al-Abbas say: I was with the Prophet ﷺ one night when he said to me: 'Look at the sky.' I looked. He said: 'Do you see anything in the sky?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'What do you see?' I said: 'The Pleiades.' He said: 'Indeed, this nation will be ruled by a number equal to its stars from your loins.'"],[5411,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in the time of intense heat and stopped at a place. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood to bathe, and al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib stood and screened him with a woolen cloak. Sahl said: I looked at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the side of the cloak while he raised his head to the sky and said: 'O Allah, screen al-Abbas and his descendants from the Fire.'"],[5412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'O Abu Wahb, upon whom have you stayed?' He said: 'Upon al-Abbas.' He said: 'You have stayed upon the one among Quraysh who has the strongest love for Quraysh.'"],[5413,"I heard my grandfather Khurayim b. Aws b. Harithah b. Lam say: I emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon his return from Tabuk and became Muslim. I heard al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib say: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to praise you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Speak, may Allah not cause your mouth to chatter.' Al-Abbas then recited: [al-bahr al-munsarih] 'Before it, you were good in the shadows and in the repository where leaves are stitched. Then you descended to the lands; you are not a human, nor a lump of flesh, nor a clot. Rather, a drop that rides the ship, and Nasr and his people were bridled with drowning. You are transferred from loins to wombs; when one world passes, another generation appears. Until your house, the Guardian, encompassed from Khindif the heights beneath which are the girdles. And when you were born, the earth shone and the horizons lit up with your light. So we, in that radiance and in the light and the paths of right guidance, traverse.'"],[5414,"Al-Abbas said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and I and Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Muttalib kept close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and did not leave him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a white mule of his, a gift from Farwah b. Na'amah al-Judhami. When the Muslims and the disbelievers met, the Muslims turned in retreat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ began spurring his mule toward the disbelievers. Al-Abbas said: I was holding the bridle of the Messenger of Allah's mule, pulling it back to keep it from going fast, and Abu Sufyan was holding the stirrup of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Abbas, call out: O companions of the Samurah (the tree under which the pledge was taken).' So I called them. By Allah, when they heard my voice, they turned back like cows turning to their calves, saying: 'At your service, at your service.' They fought the disbelievers, and the call was among the Ansar, saying: 'O company of the Ansar, O company of the Ansar.' Then the call was restricted to Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, saying: 'O Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, O Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked while on his mule, as if stretching over it to watch their fighting, and said: 'This is when the battle grows hot.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took some pebbles and threw them in the faces of the disbelievers, then said: 'They are defeated, by the Lord of Muhammad.' I went to look and saw the fighting as it was, as far as I could see. By Allah, it was only when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw his pebbles at them that I kept seeing their strength weakening and their affair retreating."],[5415,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was equipping, or reviewing, an army at Baqi' al-Khayl when al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib appeared. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'This is al-Abbas, the uncle of your Prophet, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most compassionate toward it.'"],[5416,"The Prophet ﷺ went out equipping an army and looked at al-Abbas and said: 'This is al-Abbas, the uncle of the Prophet ﷺ, the most generous of Quraysh in hand and the most maintaining of kinship ties with it.'"],[5417,"A man mentioned Abu Al-Abbas, so Al-Abbas slapped him. They gathered and said, \"By Allah, we will also slap Al-Abbas as he slapped him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was informed of this, so he delivered a sermon and said, \"Who is the most honorable person in the sight of Allah?\" They replied, \"You, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Indeed, Al-Abbas is from me, and I am from him. Do not insult our dead, for it hurts our living.\""],[5418,"Abd Allah b. al-Abbas entered upon Mu'awiyah b. Abi Sufyan while the clans of Quraysh had gathered in circles around him. Mu'awiyah asked him about their forefathers until he said: 'What do you say about your father al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib?' He said: 'May Allah have mercy on Abu al-Fadl. By Allah, he was the uncle of the Prophet of Allah and the delight of the eye of the Messenger of Allah, the master of uncles and close friends, the grandfather of grandfathers; his fathers were the most generous and his ancestors the most courageous. He had knowledge of affairs, adorned by forbearance and elevated by understanding. Every sharp sword earned his spoils, and every opposing coward earned his opinion. Close friends vanished at the mention of his virtue, and lineages receded at the mention of his clan. He was the keeper of the House, the water-giving, the lineage, and the kinship. And why should he not be so? How could he not be so? The planner of his policy was the most noble of those who planned and the most understanding of those who grew up from Quraysh and rode.'"],[5419,"That al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from al-Baḥrayn eighty thousand, and no wealth greater than it came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, neither before it nor after it. He commanded regarding it, and it was scattered on a mat, and the call to prayer was announced. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, leaning over the wealth while standing. The people came and he began giving them, and on that day there was no counting nor weighing; it was nothing but handfuls. Then al-ʿAbbās came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I gave my ransom and the ransom of ʿAqīl on the day of Badr, and ʿAqīl had no wealth. Give me from this wealth.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Take.\" So he scooped into a cloak that was on him, then went to leave but could not, so he raised his head to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, lift it for me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and said, \"As for one of them, what Allah promised, He has fulfilled for me, and I do not know about the other. Say to those in your hands of the captives: If Allah knows any good in your hearts, He will give you better than what was taken from you, and He will forgive you. This is better than what was taken from me, and I do not know what will be done with forgiveness.\" Abu ʿAlī al-Ḥusayn b. ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ informed me, ʿAbdān al-Ahwāzī informed us, al-Ḥusayn b. al-Ḥārith al-Ahwāzī narrated to us, Hāshim b. al-Qāsim narrated to us, Sulaymān b. al-Mughīrah narrated to us, from Ḥumayd b. Hilāl, from Abū Burdah, from Abū Mūsā, that al-ʿAlāʾ b. al-Ḥaḍramī sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wealth from al-Baḥrayn, and he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[5420,"Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib approached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a dress and with two braids, and he was wearing white. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him, he smiled. Al-Abbas said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what made you smile? May Allah make your teeth laugh!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied, \"I admired the beauty of the uncle of the Prophet.\" Al-Abbas then asked, \"What beauty is there in men?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ answered, \"The tongue.\""],[5421,"Al-ʿAbbās was in Madinah, and the Anṣār sought a garment to clothe him, but they found no shirt that would fit him except the shirt of ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy, so they clothed him with it. Jābir said: Al-ʿAbbās was the prisoner of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr, and he was brought out only reluctantly, so he was taken to Madinah, and ʿAbd Allāh b. Ubayy clothed him with his shirt. For that reason, \"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shrouded him in his shirt as a reward for what he had done to al-ʿAbbās.\""],[5422,"\"When al-ʿAbbās was taken prisoner, no shirt was found for him that would fit except the shirt of Ibn Ubayy.\""],[5423,"I entered upon Abū Jaʿfar al-Manṣūr and saw that he had a jumma (long hair reaching the shoulders). I began looking at its beauty, and he said, \"Abū Muḥammad b. ʿAlī had a jumma, and he told me that his father ʿAlī b. ʿAbd Allāh had a jumma, and he told me that his father ʿAbd Allāh b. al-ʿAbbās had a jumma, and al-ʿAbbās had a jumma, and he told me that the Prophet ﷺ had a jumma, and Hāshim b. ʿAbd Manāf had a jumma.\" I said to my father, \"I am amazed at its beauty.\" He said, \"That is the light of the caliphate.\" He said: My father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: \"When Allah intends to create a creature for the caliphate, He wipes His hand over its forelock, so no eye falls upon it except that it loves it.\" The narrators of this hadith, to the last of them, are all Hāshimites known for noble lineage. Its narrators are Hāshimites, not relied upon."],[5424,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"We are expanding the mosque,\" and your house is close to the mosque, so give it to us to expand the mosque with it, and I will grant you a larger one instead. He said, \"I will not do it.\" He said, \"Then I will take it from you by force.\" He said, \"That is not for you. So appoint between me and you someone who judges by the truth.\" He said, \"And who is he?\" He said, \"Ḥudhayfah b. al-Yamān.\" He said, so they came to Ḥudhayfah and told him the story. Ḥudhayfah said, \"I have knowledge about this.\" He said, \"And what is that?\" He said, \"Indeed, the Prophet Dāwūd, may Allah's blessings be upon him, wanted to expand the Bayt al-Maqdis, and there was a house near the mosque belonging to an orphan. He requested it from him, but he refused. Dāwūd wanted to take it from him, but Allah ﷻ revealed to him: 'The most pure of houses from wrongdoing is My house.'\" He said, so he left it. Then al-ʿAbbās said to him, \"Is there anything left?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, so he entered the mosque, and there was a water spout belonging to al-ʿAbbās, protruding into the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so that rainwater would flow from it into the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. ʿUmar said with his hand, and he pulled out the water spout, saying, \"This water spout will not flow into the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-ʿAbbās said to him, \"By the One who sent Muḥammad with the truth, it was he who placed the water spout in this place, and you, O ʿUmar, have removed it.\" ʿUmar said, \"Place your feet on my neck to restore it to what it was.\" So al-ʿAbbās did that. Then al-ʿAbbās said, \"I have given you the house to expand the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with it.\" So ʿUmar expanded the mosque with it, then granted al-ʿAbbās a house larger than it in al-Zawrāʾ."],[5425,"He wanted to expand the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and a dispute arose over the house of al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, and he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[5426,"I said to al-ʿAbbās, \"Ask the Prophet ﷺ to appoint you over the alms.\" So he asked him, and he said, \"I would not appoint you over the washing of people's sins.\" Authentic."],[5427,"Al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about paying his alms in advance before it became due, \"and he permitted him to do that.\""],[5428,"Al-ʿAbbās came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was angry. He said, \"What is the matter with you?\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is between us and Quraysh?\" He said, \"What is between you and them?\" He said, \"They meet each other with radiant faces, but when they meet us, they meet us with something else.\" He said, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry until a vein between his eyes throbbed. He said, when it cleared from him, he said, \"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he judges for Allah and His Messenger.\" He said, then he said, \"What is the matter with men who harm me regarding al-ʿAbbās, the uncle of a man, the equal of his father?\""],[5429,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, when Quraysh meet each other, they meet with good cheer, but when they meet us, they meet with faces we do not recognize.\" He said, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became intensely angry and said, \"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muḥammad, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for Allah and His Messenger.\" I have mentioned in the virtues of al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn a portion of the excellences of the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and clarified the defects of this hadith by mentioning al-Muṭṭalib b. Rabīʿah and those who dropped him from the chain, so that suffices from repeating it in this place."],[5430,"He said to al-ʿAbbās b. ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, \"The best of this nation, the heir of the Prophet, and his uncle.\""],[5431,"That your messenger came to me while I was having breakfast, so I fed them, then I came.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[5432,"Indeed, his father was a chief of the Quraish tribe. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[5433,"God enjoined me regarding the near of kin and commanded me to begin with al-Abbas."],[5434,"Umar b. al-Khattab sought rain in the Year of Ashes through al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, saying: 'O God, this is the uncle of Your Prophet, al-Abbas. We turn to You through him, so give us rain.' They did not leave until God gave them rain. Then Umar addressed the people, saying: 'O people, the Messenger of God ﷺ regarded al-Abbas as a son regards his father, honoring him, magnifying him, and fulfilling his oath. So, O people, follow the Messenger of God ﷺ in regard to his uncle al-Abbas and take him as a means to God ﷻ in whatever befalls you.'"],[5435,"Abdullah b. al-Arqam b. Abd Yaghuth b. Ahyab b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah. His mother was Amrah bt. al-Arqam b. Hashim b. Abd Manaf. He had become blind before his death. He died in the year thirty-five."],[5436,"He was a scribe for the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar ؓ."],[5437,"The Prophet ﷺ received a letter from a man, so he said to Abdullah ibn Arqam, \"Answer me.\" He wrote his response and then read it to him. He said, \"You are right, and you did well. O Allah, grant him success.\" When Umar became the Caliph, he used to consult him."],[5438,"The translation of the passage is: \"In charge of the treasury during the time of Umar and the early part of Uthman's rule until he passed away, and he had companionship.\""],[5439,"When the prayer is established and one of you needs to relieve himself, let him begin with relieving himself."],[5440,"From Ibn Ishaq, in naming those who were present at Badr and al-Aqabah from Banu Jusham b. al-Harith and Zayd b. al-Harith, and they are the twins: Abdullah b. Zayd b. Abd Rabbihi b. Tha'labah, and he is the one who was shown the call to prayer, so the Messenger of God ﷺ came with it and ordered him to do it."],[5441,"Abdullah b. Zayd, the companion of the call, was called Abu Muhammad."],[5442,"From Urwah, among those who witnessed Badr and al-Aqabah from Banu Jusham b. al-Harith and Zayd b. al-Harith, and they are the twins: Abdullah b. Zayd b. Abd Rabbihi b. Tha'labah b. Zayd b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and his brother Harith b. Zayd. Abdullah b. Zayd is the one who was shown the call to prayer."],[5443,"Abdullah b. Zayd b. Abd Rabbihi b. Tha'labah b. Zayd b. al-Harith, and he was called Abu Muhammad. Abdullah b. Zayd was present among the seventy of the Ansar on the night of al-Aqabah, according to the narration of all of them, and he was present at Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of God ﷺ. He carried the banner of Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj in the campaign of the conquest. He is the one who was shown the call to prayer, which the jurists of Islam have accepted and transmitted. It was not included in the two Sahihs due to the disagreement of the transmitters regarding its chains. The best of the narrations about it is the narration of Sa'id b. al-Musayyib. Some of our imams mistakenly thought that Sa'id did not meet Abdullah b. Zayd, but that is not so, for Sa'id b. al-Musayyib was among those who interceded between Ali and Uthman, and Abdullah b. Zayd died only in the latter part of Uthman's caliphate. The hadith of al-Zuhri from Sa'id b. al-Musayyib is well-known, narrated by Yunus b. Yazid, Ma'mar b. Rashid, Shu'ayb b. Abi Hamzah, Muhammad b. Ishaq, and others. As for the reports of the Kufans in this chapter, their basis is the hadith of Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Layla. Some of them said it is from Mu'adh b. Jabal or Abdullah b. Zayd, and some of them said Abd al-Rahman from Abdullah b. Zayd. As for the reports of the children of Abdullah b. Zayd from their fathers from him, their chains are not sound. Abdullah b. Zayd attributed this hadith to the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[5444,"\"He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this wall of mine is a charity for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.' Then his parents came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it has been our source of livelihood.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to them. Then they both died and their son inherited it.\""],[5445,"Abu al-Darda' was Uwaymir b. Zayd b. Qays b. Khunasah b. Umayyah b. Malik b. Amir b. Adi b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj. It is said that the name of Abu al-Darda' was Amir, but it was made diminutive, so he was called Uwaymir. His mother was Muhibbah bt. Waqid b. Amr b. al-Aznabah b. Amir b. Zayd Manat b. Malik b. Tha'labah b. Ka'b. Abu al-Darda' was, as mentioned, the last of his household to accept Islam. He continued to cling to an idol of his, over which he had placed a cloth. Abdullah b. Rawahah used to invite him to Islam, but he refused. Then Abdullah b. Rawahah came to him, for he was his brother in the pre-Islamic era, regarding Islam. When he saw that he had gone out of his house, he went in instead, entered his house, and hurried his wife while she was combing her hair. He said, 'Where is Abu al-Darda'?' She said, 'Your brother went out a little while ago and entered his house where the idol was, and with him was an adze. He took it down and began to chop it into pieces, piece by piece, while he was reciting rajaz secretly against all the names of the devils: Indeed, everything that is called upon besides God is false.' Then he went out, and his wife heard the sound of the adze as he was striking that idol. She said, 'You have destroyed me, O Ibn Rawahah.' He went out after that. It was not long before Abu al-Darda' came to his dwelling and entered. He found the woman sitting and weeping out of fear for him. He said, 'What is the matter with you?' She said, 'Your brother Abdullah b. Rawahah entered upon me and did what you see.' He became very angry, then he thought to himself and said, 'If there were any good in this, it would have defended itself.' So he went until he came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and with him was Ibn Rawahah, and he became a Muslim. It is said that the Messenger of God ﷺ looked at Abu al-Darda' while the people were fleeing in every direction on the day of Uhud and said, 'What an excellent horseman Uwaymir is, except that he is not a transient.' Ibn Umar said, 'I heard someone mention that Abu al-Darda' did not witness Uhud, but he was among the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he witnessed many battles with him.' Ibn Umar said, 'Abu al-Darda' died in Damascus in the year thirty-two, during the caliphate of Uthman b. Affan.'"],[5446,"He was called Abu Ishaq al-Ajrab, a freedman of Banu Habbar al-Qurashi. He said: 'I saw Abu al-Darda' Uwaymir b. Qays b. Khunasah, the companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He had eyes with a reddish tinge and a prominent nose, and he dyed with yellow. I saw on him a small padded cap, and I saw on him a turban which he had thrown over his shoulders.' Al-Abbas said: 'I heard a man who was with me say to him, \"Since when have you seen him?\" He said, \"I have seen him for more than a hundred years.\"' He said: 'He had on socks and sandals.' He said: 'Abu Ishaq had reached about a hundred and twenty years.'"],[5447,"Abu Dharr was Jundub b. Junadah, and it is said Yazid b. Junadah. He died at al-Rabadhah in the year thirty-two. They differed over who prayed over him: it is said Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and it is said Jarir b. Abdullah al-Bajali."],[5448,"Abu Dharr said to a group with him, \"Death has come upon me as you see, and if I had a garment that would suffice me as a shroud or for my companion, I would not be shrouded except in that. I adjure you that none of you who was an 'arif, a naqib, an amir, or a bard should shroud me.\" The people were nobles: Hujr al-Midri, Malik al-Ashtar, and a group among whom was a man from the Ansar. All the people had attained some rank except the Ansari. He said, \"I will shroud you in this cloak of mine and in two garments in my bag woven by my mother for me to wear in ihram.\" Abu Dharr said, \"That suffices me.\""],[5449,"It is said his name was Yazid."],[5450,"The Prophet ﷺ named him that."],[5451,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Abu Dharr, \"How will you be, O Yazid?\" in a long hadith."],[5452,"\"Shall I tell you about the Islam of Abu Dharr?\" He said, \"We said, 'Yes.'\" He said, \"Abu Dharr said: I was a man from Ghifar, and it reached us that a man had appeared in Makkah claiming to be a prophet. I said to my brother, 'Go to this man and speak with him, and bring me his news.' He went and met him, then returned. I said, 'What do you have?' He said, 'By Allah, I saw a man who commands good and forbids evil.' I said to him, 'You have not satisfied me with the news.' So I took a provision bag and a staff, then set out for Makkah. I did not recognize him and disliked asking about him, and I drank from Zamzam water and stayed in the mosque. Ali passed by me and said, 'The man seems like a stranger.' I said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Come to the house.' I went with him, and he did not ask me about anything, nor did I inform him. Then when morning came, I went to the mosque to ask about him, but no one told me anything about him. Ali passed by me and said, 'Does the man still not know his place?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'Come with me.' He said, 'What brought you to this town?' I said to him, 'If you keep it secret, I will tell you.' He said, 'I will.' I said to him, 'It reached us that a man has appeared here claiming to be a prophet. I sent my brother to speak with him, and he returned without satisfying me with the news, so I wanted to meet him.' He said, 'You have been guided. This is my direction, so follow me and enter where I enter. If I see anyone I fear for you, I will stand by the wall fixing my sandal, and you proceed.' So he went, and I went with him until he entered, and I entered with him upon the Prophet ﷺ. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, present Islam to me.' He presented Islam to me, and I embraced Islam on the spot. He said to me, 'O Abu Dharr, keep this matter secret and return to your land. When you hear of our emergence, come forward.' I said, 'By the One who sent you with truth, I will proclaim it among them.' He went to the mosque while Quraysh were in it and said, 'O assembly of Quraysh, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.' They said, 'Rise against this Sabian.' They rose and beat me to near death. Al-Abbas caught me and leaned over me, then turned to them and said, 'Woe to you! You kill a man from Banu Ghifar, while your trade route and passage are through Ghifar.' So they left me. When morning came, I returned and said the same as I said yesterday. They said, 'Rise against this Sabian.' Al-Abbas caught me and leaned over me and said the same as he had said yesterday. Thus was the beginning of Abu Dharr's Islam.\""],[5454,"Abu Dharr used to say, \"I saw myself as a quarter of Islam. No one embraced Islam before me except the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Bilal.\""],[5455,"I was a quarter of Islam. Three people embraced Islam before me, and I was the fourth. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and messenger.' I saw joy in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. On the condition of Muslim."],[5456,"The earth has not carried, nor the sky shaded, anyone more truthful in speech and more faithful than Abu Dharr, who resembles Isa ibn Maryam. Umar ibn al-Khattab stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, should we recognize that for him?\" He said, \"Yes, recognize it for him.\""],[5457,"The sky has not shaded, nor the earth carried, a man more truthful in speech than Abu Dharr."],[5458,"The sky has not shaded, nor the earth carried, anyone more truthful in speech than Abu Dharr."],[5459,"From the Prophet ﷺ that he said, \"The people most severely tested are the prophets, then the scholars, then the next best and the next best.\""],[5460,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Abu Dharr, how will you be when you are among the dregs?\" and he interlaced his fingers. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me?\" He said, \"Be patient, be patient, be patient. Treat people according to their character, and differ from them in their deeds.\""],[5461,"When time draws near, wearing of tayalisah becomes widespread, trade increases, wealth increases, the owner of wealth becomes great because of his wealth, indecency increases, there will be the rule of boys, women become numerous, the ruler oppresses, short measure is given in the measuring vessel and the scale, and a man raising a puppy is better for him than raising a child of his own. The old are not respected, the young are not shown mercy, and children of adultery become so many that a man will have intercourse with a woman on the main road, and the best of them in that time will say, 'If only you two had withdrawn from the road.' They will wear sheepskins over wolves' hearts; the best of them in that time will be the sycophant."],[5462,"I came to Abu Dharr and found him in the mosque, hiding alone under a black cloak. I said, 'O Abu Dharr, what is this solitude?' He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Solitude is better than a bad companion, and a righteous companion is better than solitude; uttering good is better than silence, and silence is better than uttering evil.\"' It is not authentic."],[5463,"I was with Abu al-Darda' when a man came from the direction of Madinah and asked him, and he informed him that Abu Dharr had been sent to al-Rabadhah. Abu al-Darda' said, 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. If Abu Dharr had cut off a limb of mine or a hand, I would not have disparaged him after I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"The green sky has not shaded, nor the dusty earth carried, a man more truthful in speech than Abu Dharr.\"'"],[5464,"Umm Dharr, by Allah, 'Uthman did not send Abu Dharr away, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When construction reaches Sal', leave it.' Abu Dharr said, 'When construction reached Sal' and passed beyond it, Abu Dharr left for Syria.' And he mentioned the rest of the hadith in full."],[5465,"He was among the group from the people of Kufah who stood to pray over him."],[5466,"When death approached Abu Dharr, I wept. He said to me, 'What makes you weep?' I said, 'Why should I not weep when you are dying in a desolate land, and I do not have a garment large enough to serve as a shroud for you and me, and there is no escape from a bier for you.' He said, 'Rejoice and do not weep, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No two Muslim parents lose two or three children and seek reward, but they will never see the Fire.\"' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5467,"He heard from the Prophet ﷺ, and he was called Habib al-Rum because of his frequent raids against them. He said, 'And about him Shurayh b. al-Harith said [in tawil meter]: Indeed, everyone who claims to be Habib, even if his manliness appeared, would ransom Habib of Banu Fihr, a chief leading the horses as if they trampled with small pebbles the one who cups the embers.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5468,"The Byzantines marched against Habib b. Maslama while he was in Armenia. He wrote to Mu'awiya asking for reinforcements. Mu'awiya wrote to 'Uthman about that, and 'Uthman wrote to the commander of Iraq ordering him to reinforce Habib. He reinforced him with the people of Iraq and appointed over them Salman b. Rabi'a al-Bahili. They set out intending to aid Habib, but they did not reach them until he and his companions had met the enemy and Allah granted them victory. When Salman and his companions arrived at Habib's, they asked them to share in the spoils, saying, 'We reinforced you.' The people of Syria said, 'You did not witness the fighting; you have no share with us.' Habib refused to share with them, and he and his companions kept their spoils. The people of Syria and the people of Iraq disputed over that until it almost led to fighting between them. Some of the people of Iraq said, 'If you kill Salman, we will kill your Habib, and if you go to Ibn 'Affan, we will go.'"],[5469,"I heard my father say, 'The kunya of Habib b. Maslama is Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.'"],[5470,"I witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ that he gave a third as extra share."],[5471,"Abu Dharr al-Ghifari and the people used to call Habib b. Maslama 'Habib al-Rum' because of his frequent fighting against the Byzantines."],[5472,"Habib b. Maslama died in Armenia in the year forty-two, at the age of fifty."],[5473,"Visit sparingly and you will increase in love."],[5474,"He was appointed commander over an army and he trained the troops. When he came to the enemy, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"No group gathers and some of them supplicate while others say 'Amin' except that Allah answers them.\" Then he praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"O Allah, preserve our blood and make our rewards the rewards of martyrs.\" While they were in that state, the Hunbat, the commander of the enemy, descended and entered Habib's tent. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5475,"And among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Zuhra and their allies was al-Miqdad b. Amr b. Tha'laba b. Malik b. Zam'a b. Thumama b. Matrud b. Amr b. Rabi'a b. Zuhayr b. Namir b. Tha'laba b. Malik."],[5476,"From 'Urwa: \"In naming those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Zuhra and their allies: al-Miqdad b. Amr.\""],[5477,"And it is said: to al-Aswad b. Abi Qays b. Abd Manaf."],[5478,"I was a companion of al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad in the pre-Islamic era. He had shed blood among them and fled to Kinda, and he allied himself with them. Then he shed blood among them and fled to Makkah, and he allied himself with al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth, and for that reason he was attributed to him."],[5479,"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad was given the kunya Abu Ma'bad. He died in the year thirty, having reached about seventy years of age. He used to dye his beard yellow. He died at al-Jurf and was carried on the shoulders of men, and Uthman b. Affan prayed over him, and he was buried in al-Baqi'."],[5480,"Al-Miqdad b. Amr b. Tha'laba b. Malik b. Rabi'a, and he mentioned up to Quda'a. His kunya was Abu Ma'bad. In the pre-Islamic era he had allied himself with al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth al-Zuhri, who adopted him, and he was called al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad. When the Qur'an was revealed: {Call them by their fathers} [al-Ahzab 5], he was called al-Miqdad b. Amr. Al-Miqdad emigrated to Abyssinia in the second emigration according to the narration of Ibn Ishaq. Al-Miqdad witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was one of the noted archers among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5481,"Al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad came to Makkah and said: I will ally myself with the mightiest of its people, so he allied himself with al-Aswad b. Abd Yaghuth. Thus he was called Miqdad b. al-Aswad, but he is Miqdad b. Amr al-Bahrawi, and he is not the son of al-Aswad al-Kindi."],[5482,"That I be his companion is dearer to me than anything equivalent to it. He came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was supplicating against the polytheists and said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we will not say as the people of Musa said to Musa: {Go, you and your Lord, and fight; we are sitting here} [al-Ma'ida 24]. Rather, we will fight on your right, on your left, in front of you, and behind you. I saw the Prophet ﷺ's face light up for that, and it pleased him."],[5483,"I saw al-Miqdad b. al-Aswad, the guard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sitting on a chest of the money-changers' chests in Hims, his bulk overflowing the chest because of his size, intending to go on a military expedition. I said to him: Allah has excused you. He said: The Sura of Mobilization has compelled us: {Go forth, light or heavy} [al-Tawba 41]. Baqiyya said: The Sura of Mobilization is Surat al-Tawba."],[5484,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an expedition. When I returned, he said to me: \"How do you find yourself?\" I said: I continued until I thought that those with me were my servants. By Allah, I will never act as a governor over two men after them."],[5485,"From Ibn Ishaq: \"Among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj b. Amr b. Malik b. Aws: Abu Abs b. Jabr b. Amr b. Zayd b. Jusham b. Harithah b. al-Harith.\""],[5486,"\"Abu Abs b. Jabr b. Amr b. Zayd b. Jusham b. Harithah witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5487,"I recited to Ya'qub: Among those who witnessed Badr was Abu Abs b. Jabr, whose name was Abd al-Rahman b. Jabr."],[5488,"\"Abu Abs Abd Allah b. Jabr b. Amr b. Zayd al-Ansari died in the year thirty-three.\""],[5489,"\"Abu Abs Abd al-Rahman b. Jabr died in the year thirty-four, at the age of seventy.\""],[5490,"\"Abu Abis ibn Jabr and Khunays ibn Hudhaafah al-Sahmi were among the noble companions. Abu Abis witnessed the battles of Badr, Uhud, the Battle of the Trench, and all other major events along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . He was also among those who participated in the killing of Ka'b ibn Ashraf.\""],[5491,"Abd al-Majid b. Abi Abs al-Ansari, from the descendants of Abi Abs, narrated to us: \"He used to pray the prescribed prayers with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then he would go out to Banu Harithah. One dark, rainy night he went out, and it was lit up for him in his staff until he entered the dwellings of Banu Harithah.\" Mursal."],[5492,"Abu Abs b. Jabr al-Ansari invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to food he had prepared for them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Remove your sandals when eating, for it is a beautiful sunnah.\" Yahya and his shaykh are abandoned."],[5493,"\"The two men whose homes were farthest from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were Abu Lubabah b. Abd al-Mundhir and his family in Quba', and Abu Abs b. Jabr, whose dwelling was among Banu Harithah. They used to pray the afternoon prayer with the Prophet ﷺ, then come to their people, and they had not prayed, due to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastening his prayer.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5494,"\"Abu Talhah Zayd b. Sahl b. al-Aswad b. Haram b. Zayd Manat b. Adi b. Malik b. al-Najjar witnessed Badr and has descendants. He was among the notable archers of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It is said that he was a brown-skinned man of medium height. He died in Madinah in the year thirty-four, and Uthman b. Affan prayed over him; he was then seventy years old.\""],[5495,"From Urwah: \"In naming those who witnessed the Aqabah pledge and then witnessed Badr from Banu Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar: Abu Talhah, who is Zayd b. Sahl b. al-Aswad b. Haram b. Amr b. Zayd Manat.\""],[5496,"\"Abu Talhah Zayd b. Sahl used to dig.\""],[5497,"I heard Yahya b. Main say: \"Abu Talhah al-Ansari is Zayd b. Sahl.\""],[5498,"\"This is my maternal uncle, so whoever of you wishes, let him bring out his maternal uncle.\""],[5499,"\"The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a thousand men.\""],[5500,"\"The voice of Abu Talhah in the army is better than a troop.\""],[5501,"The Prophet ﷺ said on the day of Uhud: \"Whoever kills an unbeliever, the spoils are his.\" On that day Abu Talhah killed twenty men."],[5502,"\"Abu Talhah fasted after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for forty years, breaking the fast only on the day of Fitr or Adha.\""],[5503,"Abu Talhah said: \"I will not be put in command over two men nor will I blame them.\""],[5504,"Abu Talhah recited this verse: {Go forth, light and heavy} [al-Tawba 41], then said: \"Allah has called us to go forth, Allah has commanded us, and we call forth our elders and youth. Equip me.\" His sons said, \"May Allah have mercy on you. You have fought in the time of the Prophet ﷺ, Abu Bakr, and Umar, and now we will fight on your behalf.\" So he fought in the naval expedition and died. They sought an island to bury him on but could not find one until after seven days, and he had not changed."],[5505,"Abu Talhah would shoot in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ would raise his back from behind him to see where his arrow fell. Abu Talhah would stretch out his chest, shielding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with it, and say: \"Like this, O Prophet of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom; my throat before your throat.\""],[5506,"From Banu Salim b. Awf b. Amr b. Awf b. al-Khazraj: Ubada b. al-Samit b. Qays b. Asram b. Bahz b. Tha'laba b. Ghanm b. Salim, a Naqib who attended Badr and all the expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5507,"I heard Sufyan b. Uyayna say: \"Ubada b. al-Samit was a Badri, an Uhudi, an Aqabi, a Shajari, and he was a Naqib.\""],[5508,"I heard Ahmad b. Hanbal say: \"Ubada b. al-Samit was a Badri, an Uhudi, a Shajari, an Aqabi, a Naqib.\""],[5509,"From Urwa, in naming those who attended al-Aqaba and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"From Banu Awf, then from Banu Salim b. Ja'far: Ubada b. al-Samit, and he was a Naqib and he attended Badr.\""],[5510,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him [i.e., 'Ubada b. al-Samit] to collect the zakat, and he said: \"O Abu al-Walid.\""],[5511,"It was said to 'Ubada b. al-Samit: \"O Abu al-Walid.\""],[5512,"Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Zahid informed us; Ahmad b. Mihran al-Asbahani narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us from Thawr b. Yazid from Makhul, who said: \"'Ubada b. al-Samit and Shaddad b. Aws used to live in Jerusalem, and 'Ubada was given the kunya Abu al-Walid.\""],[5513,"\"We set out for the Hajj in which we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-'Aqaba. The representative of Banu 'Awf b. al-Harith was 'Ubada b. al-Samit.\""],[5514,"Mu'awiya said to them: \"O company of the Ansar, why do you not come to me along with your brothers from Quraysh?\" 'Ubada said: \"Need.\" He said: \"Then why not on the camels used for carrying water?\" He said: \"We spent them on the day of Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5515,"\"The grave of 'Ubada b. al-Samit and 'Umar b. 'Abd Allah is in Jerusalem.\""],[5516,"\"Whenever I came to Jerusalem, I would stay with 'Ubada b. al-Samit.\""],[5517,"\"'Ubada b. al-Samit died in Syria, in the land of Palestine, at al-Ramla, in the year thirty-four, and he was seventy-two years old.\""],[5518,"\"'Ubada b. al-Samit died in Jerusalem and was buried there in the year thirty-four, and he was seventy-two years old.\""],[5519,"'Ubada b. al-Samit disapproved of some things about Mu'awiya, then said to him: \"I will not live with you in the same land.\" So he departed to Madinah. 'Umar said to him: \"What has brought you to me? May Allah not open a land in which you and your like are not present. So go back; Mu'awiya has no authority over you.\""],[5520,"\"He had participated in six military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5521,"\"I entered upon 'Ubada b. al-Samit, and he had become knowledgeable in the religion of Allah.\""],[5522,"We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that we would not fear the blame of any blamer concerning Allah."],[5523,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was occupied. When a man arrived who had accepted Islam at the hands of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would hand him over to one of us to teach him the Quran. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ handed over to me a man who stayed with me in the house, and I taught him the Quran. He saw that he owed me something, so he gifted me a bow, the like of which I have never seen better or more beautiful in its curve. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"What do you think, O Messenger of Allah, about it?\" He said, \"A live coal between your shoulders which you have hung around your neck or attached to yourself.\""],[5524,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"After me, rulers will govern you who will make you recognize what you disapprove and will disapprove of what you recognize. Whoever among you lives to see that, then there is no obedience to the one who disobeys Allah.\""],[5525,"From Isma'il b. Ubayd, similar to it. As for the hadith of Muslim b. Khalid, 'Abdullah b. Waqid was alone in narrating it, and he is weak."],[5526,"'Ubada b. al-Samit stood up in the middle of the courtyard of the Commander of the Faithful 'Uthman b. 'Affan and said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Muhammad Abu al-Qasim, say, 'After me, men will govern your affairs who will make you recognize what you disapprove and will disapprove of what you recognize. So there is no obedience to the one who disobeys Allah, and do not blame yourselves. By the One in whose hand is my soul, Mu'awiya is one of those.'\" 'Uthman did not reply to him with a single word. This hadith has been narrated with a sound chain according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs regarding 'Ubada b. al-Samit's coming to 'Uthman b. 'Affan complaining, with an abridged text."],[5527,"'Ubada b. al-Samit came back from the Levant intending to perform Hajj. He performed Hajj, then arrived in Madinah and went to 'Uthman b. 'Affan complaining."],[5528,"From Ibn Ishaq: \"The first of the Emigrants to arrive in Madinah was Abu Salama, and the first to arrive after Abu Salama was 'Amir b. Rabi'a.\""],[5529,"Al-Dhahabi commented on it in the Talkhis."],[5530,"When the people began to criticize 'Uthman, my father got up at night, prayed, and supplicated, saying, \"O Allah, protect me from the trial just as You protected Your righteous servants from it.\" He did not go out nor did morning come except with his funeral."],[5531,"'Amir b. Rabi'a al-'Adawi died in the year thirty-three, and it is said in the year thirty-two."],[5532,"Among those who emigrated to Abyssinia, the ones who left the first time before Ja'far and his companions from the Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b was 'Amir b. Rabi'a from the people of Yemen. He was present at Badr."],[5533,"Badr took place on the morning of the sixteenth of Ramadan."],[5534,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a funeral procession passed by. A man from the Jews said, 'O Muhammad, does this funeral speak?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. The Jew said, 'I bear witness that it speaks.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When the People of the Book narrate something to you, say: We believe in Allah, His angels, His books, and His messengers.'"],[5535,"When the funeral of Rafi' b. Khadij was placed, and he mentioned the hadith."],[5536,"Abu al-Aswad Muhammad b. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Nawfal b. 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr narrated to us."],[5537,"From his father."],[5538,"The mother of al-Zubayr was Safiyyah bt. 'Abd al-Muttalib, and her mother was Halah bt. Uhayb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah, and her mother was 'Aliyah bt. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf."],[5539,"Al-Zubayr embraced Islam when he was sixteen years old, and he was killed when he was sixty-something years old."],[5540,"Talhah and al-Zubayr each reached sixty-four years."],[5541,"Al-Zubayr was killed when he was sixty-seven years old, and he was given the kunyah Abu al-Tahir."],[5542,"I heard al-'Abbas say to al-Zubayr, 'O 'Abd Allah, here the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded you to plant the standard.'"],[5543,"Al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam embraced Islam when he was eight years old, and he migrated when he was eighteen years old. Al-Zubayr's paternal uncle would hang al-Zubayr in a mat and smoke him with fire, saying, 'Return to disbelief,' and al-Zubayr would say, 'I will never disbelieve.'"],[5544,"Al-Zubayr embraced Islam and migrated to the land of Abyssinia for both migrations together, and he did not stay behind from any expedition that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ undertook. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between him and Ibn Mas'ud. He was a man neither tall nor short, with a light beard, brown-skinned, and hairy."],[5545,"Concerning his blood, Ali and his companions, and it was indeed Amr ibn Jurmuz who killed him in the month of Rajab in the year thirty-six. The Banu Mujashi were led by the Arabs in their efforts to hide Zubayr, and that is why Jareer says [in Al-Bahr Al-Taweel]. After Zubayr, Mujashi wore the clothes that were stained with blood and did not wash them."],[5546,"I accompanied al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam on one of his journeys, and he became junub in a barren land. He said, 'Cover me.' So I covered him, and I happened to glance at him and saw him scarred by swords. I said, 'By Allah, I have seen marks on you that I have never seen on anyone else.' He said, 'Have you seen that? By Allah, there is no wound among them except it was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the path of Allah.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5547,"Az-Zubayr heard about that when he was eleven years old, so he went out with his sword unsheathed until he stood before the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"What is the matter with you?\" He replied, \"I wanted to strike whoever took you.\" The Prophet ﷺ supplicated for him and for his sword, and it was the first sword unsheathed in the cause of Allah ﷻ."],[5548,"The first battle in Islam was Badr. We had only two horses with us: a horse belonging to Az-Zubayr and a horse belonging to Al-Miqdad."],[5549,"\"By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not go out on any expedition or military detachment except that I was in it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5550,"\"On the day of Badr, Az-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam wore a yellow turban wrapped around his head, and the angels descended wearing yellow turbans.\""],[5551,"\"The inheritance of Az-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam was divided among forty thousand thousand dirhams.\""],[5552,"\"The inheritance of Az-Zubayr was divided among forty thousand thousand dirhams.\""],[5553,"He said, \"Tell me about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ so that I may narrate from you, for all the sons of the Companions narrate from their fathers.\" He said, \"My son, there is no one who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with any companionship except that I accompanied him with the like of it or better. You know that your mother Asma' daughter of Abu Bakr was my wife, and that your maternal aunt 'A'ishah daughter of Abu Bakr [is also related to me]. You know that my mother is Safiyyah daughter of 'Abd al-Muttalib, and that my maternal uncles are Hamzah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, Abu Talib, and 'Abbas, and that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is my maternal cousin. You know that my paternal aunt Khadijah daughter of Khuwaylid was his wife, and that her daughter Fatimah is the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. You know that Khadijah's mother is Habibah daughter of Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza. You know that the mother of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is Aminah daughter of Wahb b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah. I accompanied him with the best companionship, praise be to Allah, and I heard him say: 'Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5554,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is Az-Zubayr.\" It was said to him, \"O Abu 'Abd Allah, do you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it to anyone other than you?\" He said, \"No, by Allah, I do not know.\" [Al-Hakim said:] \"Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it with this wording.\" According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5555,"Zubayr ibn al-Awwam passed by a gathering of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and Hassaan recited poetry to them while they were not paying much attention. Zubayr sat with them and said, \"Why do I see you not giving more attention to the poetry of Ibn al-Furai'ah? The Prophet ﷺ used to appreciate it, listen to it carefully, and generously reward him for it. He would not be distracted from it by anything.\" Hassaan replied, \"He stood by the Prophet's covenant and his guidance. His words matched his actions. He was a loyal advocate for the truth, the most famous knight and warrior who would lead battles. Even if he was from a noble lineage and his mother was Safiyyah, he would not be protected from the Messenger of Allah's nearness. He was also a supporter of Islam, a source of honor and glory. How many hardships did Zubayr endure and how many battles did he fight for the sake of the chosen one? Allah rewards abundantly when hardships are revealed. He hastens towards death with noble and courageous readiness. There is no match for him among them, nor was there before him. As long as you continue to praise him, it is better than any worldly gain. Your actions, O son of Hashim, are superior.\""],[5556,"Uthman suffered a nosebleed in the year of the nosebleeds, so much so that he made a will and stayed behind from the Hajj. A man from Quraysh entered upon us and said, \"Appoint a successor.\" He said, \"And they said that?\" He replied, \"Yes.\" He said, \"And who is he?\" The man fell silent. Then another man entered upon him and said, \"Appoint a successor,\" and mentioned something similar to what the first had said. Uthman said, \"Az-Zubayr?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Uthman said, \"Indeed, by the One in whose hand is my soul, if it were not for the best of them, as far as I know, and the most beloved of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, [I would not say this].\""],[5557,"A'ishah said to me, \"My son, your father is among those who responded to Allah and the Messenger after the wound had befallen them.\""],[5558,"\"Talhah and Az-Zubayr are my two neighbors in Paradise.\""],[5559,"From Nubayh al-'Anazi, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that he said, \"Do not revile the disciple of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for their expiation is being killed.\""],[5560,"\"The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, sent me on a cold morning. So I came to him and he was with some of his wives under his blanket. He admitted me into the blanket, and we became three.\""],[5561,"A man from the Ansar brought a complaint before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ against me concerning the irrigation channels of the Harrah. He said, 'O Zubayr, irrigate, then release the water to your neighbor.' The Ansari said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is it because he is your cousin?' The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed color and he said, 'O Zubayr, irrigate, then withhold the water until it reaches the wall, then release it to your neighbor.' Thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted Zubayr his full right. Zubayr said, 'I think this verse was revealed concerning my dispute: {But no, by your Lord, they will not believe until they make you judge in what arises between them} [an-Nisa' 65].'"],[5562,"On the Day of the Camel, Zubayr called his son Abdullah and made a bequest to him, saying, 'O my son, this is a day on which either an oppressor or an oppressed person will be killed, and by Allah, if I am killed, I will be killed as an oppressed one. By Allah, I did not do it, nor did I do it. Look, O my son, after my religion, for I leave nothing more important than it, and it is one million and two hundred thousand.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5563,"Zubayr turned back in defeat on the Day of the Camel, and Ibn Jurmuz, a man from Banu Tamim, caught up with him and killed him."],[5564,"When Zubayr left on the day of the Battle of the Camel, he said, \"I know if my knowledge were of any benefit, life would be close to death.\" Then it did not occur to him that he would be killed by Ibn Jurumuz."],[5565,"I heard Al-Fadl ibn Dakin saying, \"Talha and Zubair ibn Al-Awam were killed in the month of Rajab in the year sixty-three.\""],[5566,"Zubayr went out on the Day of the Camel, which was Thursday, ten nights having passed of Jumada al-Akhirah of this year, after the battle, on a horse called Dhu al-Khimar, heading toward Madinah. He was killed in Wadi al-Siba' and buried there."],[5567,"These are the best ones; they were killed. Then he wept and said: Zubayr approached his killer after he had overpowered him and said, 'I remind you of Allah,' so Zubayr refrained from him until he did that several times. Then when he betrayed Zubayr and struck him, Zubayr said, 'May Allah fight you! You remind me of Allah and then you forget Him.'"],[5568,"Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5569,"Ali said to Zubayr, 'Do you remember the day when you and I were in the portico of a group of the Ansar, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to you, \"Do you love him?\" I said, \"What prevents me?\" He said, \"Indeed, you will go out against him and fight him while you are an oppressor.\" He said, so Zubayr turned back. The hadith contains some doubt."],[5570,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'You will fight him while you are an oppressor to him'? He said, 'I did not remember.' Then Zubayr went on, turning away."],[5571,"I witnessed Ali and Zubayr when Zubayr returned on his mount, piercing through the ranks. His son Abdullah confronted him and said, 'What is the matter with you?' He said, 'Ali reminded me of a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying, \"You will fight him while you are an oppressor to him,\" so I will not fight him.' He said, 'And did you come for fighting? You came only to reconcile between the people, and Allah will set this matter right through you.' He said, 'I have sworn not to fight.' He said, 'Then free your slave Girgis and stop until you reconcile between the people.' So he freed his slave Girgis and stopped, but the people's affair became confused, so he went on his horse."],[5572,"I heard Ali and Zubayr, and Ali was saying to him, 'I adjure you by Allah, O Zubayr, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"You will fight me while you are an oppressor to me?\"' He said, 'Yes, but I forgot.'"],[5573,"I heard Ali while he was adjuring Zubayr, saying to him, 'I adjure you by Allah, O Zubayr, did you not hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"You will fight me while you are an oppressor to me?\"' He said, 'Yes, but I forgot.'"],[5574,"We were with Ali when Ibn Jurmuz came to seek permission from him. Ali said, \"Do you intend to kill the son of Safiyyah to show off?\" Grant him permission and give him glad tidings of Hell. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Every prophet has a disciple, and indeed Zubair is my disciple, and the son of my cousin.\""],[5575,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'For every prophet there is a disciple, and my disciple is Zubayr.'"],[5576,"I was sitting with 'Ali when the head of al-Zubayr was brought, along with his killer. 'Ali said to the doorkeeper, \"Give the killer of the son of Safiyya tidings of the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr.'\" These hadiths are authentic from the Commander of the Believers, 'Ali, even if they did not record them with these chains. These are sound hadiths."],[5577,"Ibrahim: \"Because they were born in the same year.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5578,"Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5579,"Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Taym b. Murra, and he was in Syria. He spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about his share, so He allotted him his share. He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"And your reward from the day of Badr.\""],[5580,"\"The mother of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the mother of 'Uthman, the mother of Talha, the mother of 'Ammar b. Yasir, the mother of 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, and the mother of al-Zubayr accepted Islam, and Sa'd and his mother accepted Islam while she was alive.\""],[5581,"Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Tamim b. Murra arrived from Syria after the Prophet ﷺ returned from Badr, and he spoke to the Prophet ﷺ about his share. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"You shall have your share.\" He said, \"And my reward, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"And you shall have your reward.\""],[5582,"Talha b. 'Abd Allah said to me: I attended the market of Busra, and there was a monk in his cell saying, \"Ask the people of this season whether any of them is from the people of the Haram.\" Talha said: I said, \"Yes, I am.\" He said, \"Has Ahmad appeared yet?\" He said: I said, \"Who is Ahmad?\" He said, \"The son of 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. This is the month in which he will emerge. He is the last of the prophets, his emergence is from the Haram, and his emigration is to a place of palm trees, rocky land, and a salt marsh. Beware lest anyone beat you to him.\" Talha said: What he said fell into my heart, so I departed quickly until I arrived in Makkah. I said, \"Has anything happened?\" They said, \"Yes, Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Amin has declared prophethood, and Ibn Abi Quhafa has followed him.\" He said: I went out until I entered upon Abu Bakr and said, \"Have you followed this man?\" He said, \"Yes, so go to him and enter upon him and follow him, for he calls to the truth.\" Talha informed him of what the monk had said. Abu Bakr went out with Talha and brought him in to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Talha accepted Islam and informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what the monk had said, and it pleased the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When Abu Bakr and Talha had accepted Islam, Nawfal b. Khuwaylid b. al-'Adawiyya seized them and bound them with a single rope, and Banu Taym did not protect them. Nawfal b. Khuwaylid was called the strongest of Quraysh, and for that reason Abu Bakr and Talha were called the Two Companions. Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah did not witness Badr, because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sent him and Sa'id b. Zayd to spy on the caravan. They returned after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had finished fighting the polytheists he encountered, and they met him between Zulal and Sabala on the curtained litter as he was returning from Badr. But he did witness Uhud and other battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was among those who stood firm with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud when the people turned back, and he pledged allegiance to him unto death. Malik b. Zuhayr shot at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that day, and Talha shielded the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with his hand. It struck his little finger and it was paralyzed. He said, \"Hass! Hass!\" when the arrow struck him, and he mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Had he said 'In the name of Allah,' he would have entered Paradise,\" while the people were looking at him. Talha was struck on his head that day—the hard head—by a man among the polytheists who struck him twice: once when he was advancing and once when he was turning away from him. Dirar b. al-Khattab al-Fihri used to say, \"By Allah, I struck him that day.\""],[5583,"\"Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah was killed while his treasurer had one million dirhams and two hundred thousand dirhams, and his capital and real estate were valued at thirty million dirhams. He was, as mentioned, generous with wealth, clothing, and food. He was killed on the day he was killed at the age of sixty-two.\""],[5584,"\"Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah was fair-skinned, inclining to redness, of medium height, closer to being short, broad-chested, wide-shouldered; when he turned, he turned his whole body; he had large feet, a handsome face, and a thin nose. When he walked, he walked quickly, and he did not dye his hair.\""],[5585,"We were fighting 'Ali alongside Talha, and Marwan was with us. He said: We were routed. He said: Marwan said, \"I will not attain my revenge from Talha after today.\" He said: He shot him with an arrow and killed him. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5586,"Nafi': \"Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah was killed by Marwan b. al-Hakam.\""],[5587,"\"I saw Marwan b. al-Hakam when Talha b. 'Ubayd Allah was shot that day, and it struck his knee. He did not cease glorifying Allah until he died.\""],[5588,"\"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and in his hand was a small pouch. He threw it towards me or he said, 'He tossed it to me' and said, 'Keep it, O Abu Muhammad, for it soothes the heart.'\""],[5589,"When the Day of the Camel came, Ali called out among the people: \"Do not shoot anyone with an arrow, do not thrust with a spear, do not strike with a sword, and do not pursue the people, for this is a station where whoever succeeds in it will succeed on the Day of Resurrection.\" He said: So we faced each other. Then the people all said: \"O vengeance for Uthman!\" He said: And Ibn al-Hanafiyya was our imam on a hillock, with the banner with him. He said: Ali called him, and he came toward us, turning his face, and said: \"O Commander of the Believers, they are saying: 'O vengeance for Uthman!'\" Ali stretched out his hands and said: \"O Allah, throw the killers of Uthman down today on their faces.\" Then al-Zubayr said to the cavalrymen who were with him: \"Shoot them with a volley,\" as if he wanted the fighting to break out. When his companions saw it break out, they did not wait and charged, and Allah defeated them. Marwan b. al-Hakam shot Talha b. Ubaidullah with an arrow, and it pierced his leg against the side of his horse, and the horse pulled him along until he caught up with it and slaughtered it. Marwan turned to Aban b. Uthman, who was with him, and said: \"I have spared you one of the killers of your father.\""],[5590,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, saying, \"Whoever I am his master, then Ali is his master. O Allah, be a supporter of whoever supports him and an enemy of whoever opposes him\"? He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then why did you fight against me?\" He said, \"I did not remember.\" So Talha Al-Hasan, who is Al-Arni and is not trustworthy, turned away."],[5591,"And I saw him, and the dearest of gatherings to him was the emptiest one, while he was striking his beard against his chest. I said to him: \"O Abu Muhammad, I see you, and the dearest of gatherings to you is the emptiest one, and you are striking your beard against your chest. Do you dislike this day? Then leave it, for no one compels you to it.\" He said: \"O Alqama b. Waqqas, do not blame me. We were one hand against those besides us, but today they have become two mountains, one of us creeping toward the other. However, I had something to do with the affair of Uthman for which I see no expiation except that my blood be shed in seeking his blood.\" I said: \"And Muhammad b. Talha, why do you bring him out while you have small children? Leave him, so that if something happens, he may succeed you in your estate.\" He said: \"He knows better. I dislike to see anyone who has an intention in this matter and then I would prevent him.\" Then I spoke with Muhammad b. Talha about staying behind, and he said: \"I dislike to ask the baggage about my father.\""],[5592,"Talha was the Prophet's in-law through four marriages. The Prophet ﷺ had Aisha bt. Abi Bakr, and her sister Umm Kulthum bt. Abi Bakr was married to Talha, and she bore him Zakariyya, Yusuf, and Aisha. The Prophet ﷺ had Zaynab bt. Jahsh, and Hamna bt. Jahsh was under Talha b. Ubaidullah, and she bore him Muhammad, who was killed on the Day of the Camel with his father. Umm Habiba bt. Abi Sufyan was under the Prophet ﷺ, and her sister al-Rifa'a bt. Abi Sufyan was under Talha b. Ubaidullah. And Umm Salama bt. Abi Umayya was under the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and her sister Qurayba bt. Abi Umayya was under Talha b. Ubaidullah, and she bore him Maryam bt. Talha."],[5593,"Ali seated Talha on the Day of the Camel, wiped the dust from his head, then turned to al-Hasan b. Ali and said: \"I wish I had died thirty years before this.\""],[5594,"Ali said on the Day of the Camel, when he saw the slain and the heads flying: \"O Hasan, what good can be hoped for after this?\" He said: \"I forbade you from this before we entered into it.\""],[5595,"I said: \"O Abu Muhammad, did Talha and al-Zubayr pledge allegiance to Ali?\" He said:"],[5596,"The poet [al-tawil meter]: A young man whom wealth brought close to his friend when he was rich, and poverty distanced him, as if the Pleiades were hung upon his brow, and in one cheek Sirius, and in the other the full moon."],[5597,"I passed by Talha b. Ubaidullah on the Day of the Camel, and he was lying wounded in his last moments. I stopped by him, and he raised his head and said: \"I see the face of a man like the moon. Who are you?\" I said: \"From the companions of the Commander of the Believers, Ali.\" He said: \"Extend your hand, I pledge allegiance to you.\" I extended my hand, and he pledged allegiance to me, then his soul departed. I came to Ali and told him what Talha had said, and he said: \"Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth: Allah refused that Talha enter Paradise except with my allegiance upon his neck.\""],[5598,"On the Day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ had on two coats of mail, and he rose toward the rock but could not manage it, so Talha sat beneath him until he settled on the rock. Al-Zubayr said: I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Talha has made it obligatory.\""],[5599,"\"Talha has made it obligatory.\""],[5600,"Talha slaughtered a camel and dug a well on the Day of Dhu Qarad, and he fed them and gave them water. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Talha the Generous.\" So he was named Talha al-Fayyad."],[5601,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me on the Day of Uhud Talha al-Khayr, in the expedition of al-Ushayra Talha al-Fayyad, and on the Day of Hunayn Talha al-Jawwad.\""],[5602,"When Muhammad b. Talha was born, we brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"What have you named him?\" We said, \"Muhammad.\" He said, \"This is my name, and his kunya is Abu al-Qasim.\" Abu Shayba is weak."],[5603,"I heard Mus'ab al-Zubayri say: Muhammad b. Talha b. Ubaidullah—his mother is Hamna bt. Jahsh."],[5604,"When we finished the fighting of the Camel, Ali, al-Husayn b. Ali, Ammar b. Yasir, Sa'sa'a b. Suhan, al-Ashtar, and Muhammad b. Abi Bakr stood up and went around among the slain. Al-Hasan b. Ali saw a slain man lying face down, so he turned him onto his back and said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return—a fledgling of Quraysh, by Allah!\" His father said to him, \"What is it, my son?\" He said, \"Muhammad b. Talha.\" He said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return. As far as I knew, he was a righteous young man.\" Then he sat down gloomy and sad."],[5605,"And he said, \"Whoever sees the man with the black burnous, let him not kill him—meaning Muhammad.\" Muhammad said to Aisha that day, \"O mother, what do you command me?\" She said, \"I think you should be like the better of the two sons of Adam: restrain your hand.\" So he restrained his hand, and a man from Banu Asad b. Khuzayma called Talha b. Mudlij, from Banu Munqidh b. Tarif, killed him. It is also said that Shaddad b. Mu'awiya al-Absi killed him, and it is said that rather Isam b. Mis'ar al-Basri killed him, and most reports say this. He is the one who said about killing him [al-bahr al-tawil]: \"A disheveled one, standing in prayer with the verses of his Lord, little harm in what people see, a Muslim. I turned the spear to him from beneath his armor, and he fell down slain upon his hands and mouth. You pierced his shirt to him with the spearhead, and I made him fall from the back of a marked horse. You set his back straight in the charge of the cavalry with a spearhead like the forepart of a swift wild ass. He reminds me of Ha-Mim when I thrust him, but would that he had recited Ha-Mim before advancing. No guilt upon him except that he did not follow Ali, and whoever does not follow the truth wrongs.\" He said: Ali said when he saw him slain, \"His head brought him to this fall.\""],[5606,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq: I was the first to return to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was Talha b. Ubaidullah. Talha was overcome by the cold, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was more wet than him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, \"Take care of your companion.\" So we left him and went to him, and there was a helmet stuck to his cheeks. Between him and the east was a man, and I was closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was Abu Ubaida b. al-Jarrah. I went to remove the helmet, and Abu Ubaida said, \"I implore you by Allah, O Abu Bakr, will you not leave me?\" So I left him, and he pulled it, and Abu Ubaida's front tooth was pulled out. He said: I went to remove the other ring, and Abu Ubaida said the same to me, so he removed the other ring, and Abu Ubaida's other front tooth was pulled out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, your companion has earned, or made Talha earn.\" Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it. No, by Allah."],[5607,"I entered upon the Mother of the Believers, while Aisha bt. Talha was saying to her mother Asma, \"I am better than you, and my father is better than your father.\" Her mother began to revile her and say, \"You are better than me?\" The Mother of the Believers Aisha said, \"Shall I judge between you two?\" She said, \"Yes.\" She said, \"Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'O Abu Bakr, you are the freed one of Allah from the Fire.'\" She said, \"From that day he was named Atiq, and he had not been named Atiq before that.\" She said, \"Then Talha b. Ubaidullah entered, and he said, 'You, O Talha, are among those who have fulfilled their vow.'\""],[5608,"\"Whoever wants to look at a martyr walking on the face of the earth, let him look at Talha b. Ubaidullah.\""],[5609,"I entered upon Ali with Umar b. Talha after he had finished with the companions of the Camel. He said: He welcomed him and drew him near. He said, \"I hope that Allah will make me and your father among those of whom Allah, exalted is He, said: 'And We shall remove whatever rancor is in their breasts, as brothers, on couches, facing one another' (al-Hijr 47).\" He said, \"O son of my brother, how is so-and-so? How is so-and-so?\" He said: He asked him about the mothers of his father's children. He said: Then he said, \"We did not seize your lands this year except for fear that the people would plunder them. O so-and-so, go with him to Banu Qurayza and order him to give him this year's produce and hand over his land to him.\" Two men sitting to one side, one of them al-Harith al-A'war, said, \"Allah is more just than that—that we kill them and they be our brothers in Paradise.\" He said, \"A people farthest and most remote in the land of Allah. Who is it then, if not I and Talha? O son of my brother, if you have a need, come to us.\""],[5610,"Umar b. al-Khattab proposed to Umm Aban bt. Utba b. Rabi'a b. Abd Shams, and she refused him. It was said to her, \"Why?\" She said, \"If he enters, he enters with harshness, and if he goes out, he goes out with harshness. The affair of his hereafter has distracted him from the affair of his world, as if he were looking at his Lord with his two eyes.\" Then al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam proposed, and she refused him. It was said to her, \"Why?\" She said, \"His wife has no say from him in her hair extensions.\" Then Ali proposed to her, and she refused. It was said to her, \"Why?\" She said, \"His wife has nothing from him except the fulfillment of his need, and he says 'such and such' and 'it was and it was.'\" Then Talha proposed to her, and she said, \"A husband indeed.\" They said, \"How is that?\" She said, \"I know his character. If he enters, he enters laughing, and if he goes out, he goes out smiling. If I ask, he gives, and if I am silent, he initiates. If I work, he thanks, and if I sin, he forgives.\" When he consummated the marriage with her, Ali said, \"O Abu Muhammad, will you permit me to speak to Umm Aban?\" He said, \"Speak to her.\" He said: He took hold of the curtain of the bridal canopy, then said, \"Peace be upon you, O one who holds herself dear.\" She said, \"And upon you be peace.\" He said, \"The Commander of the Believers proposed to you and you refused him.\" She said, \"That happened.\" He said, \"Al-Zubayr, the cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and one of his disciples, proposed to you and you refused.\" She said, \"And that happened.\" He said, \"I proposed to you, with my kinship to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you refused.\" She said, \"And that happened.\" He said, \"By Allah, you have married the most handsome of us and the most open-handed of us. He gives like this and like this.\""],[5611,"\"Talha entered upon me, and I found him distressed.\" I said, \"Why do I see you with a grim face? Has something in our affair troubled you?\" He said, \"No, by Allah, nothing in your affair troubled me, and you are an excellent wife, but wealth has accumulated with me.\" She said, \"Then send to your household and your people and distribute it among them.\" She said: He did so, and I asked the treasurer how much he distributed. He said, \"Four hundred thousand, and his income every day was one thousand dirhams.\" He said: He was called Talha the Generous. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5612,"When the war laid down its burdens, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ boasted, while Talha was silent and Simak b. Kharasha Abu Dujana was silent, not speaking. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I saw myself on the day of Uhud, and there was no creature near me on the earth except Gabriel on my right and Talha on my left.\" Poetry was said about that [al-bahr al-tawil]: \"Talha on the day of the mountain pass sheltered Muhammad at an hour when it was hard and straitened for him. He protected him with his two hands from the spears, so his fingers were cut off beneath the spears and were paralyzed. And he was the imam of the people after Muhammad, he established the mill of Islam until it became stable.\""],[5613,"Hassan b. Thabit, about Talha, without excluding anyone [al-bahr al-munsarih]: \"He stood firm when the Prophet gave the greeting, and when all the servants turned away and were exposed. He defended the life-blood of the Prophet while the enemy had drawn near to him and mounted behind. Smeared with blood was his life-blood, for fear that it would be said: their rising turned them back.\""],[5614,"I heard my father saying: \"I was wounded on the day of Uhud all over my body, even in my private part.\""],[5615,"Umar b. al-Khattab appointed Qudamah b. Maz'un over al-Bahrayn, and he was the maternal uncle of Hafsah and Abdullah b. Umar."],[5616,"Qudamah b. Maz'un died in the year thirty-six, at the age of sixty-eight, and he did not dye his white hair."],[5617,"The polytheists captured Hudhayfah and his father before Badr and wanted to kill them. They took from them a covenant by Allah and His pact that they would not help against them, so the two swore to them, and they released them. They came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him, saying: \"We have sworn to them, so if you wish, we will fight alongside you.\" He said: \"We fulfill their covenant and seek Allah's help against them.\""],[5618,"Urwah said: Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman was one of the Banu Abs and was an ally among the Ansar. His father was killed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Uhud. The Muslims mistook him that day, thinking he was one of the polytheists, and Hudhayfah began saying: 'My father, my father,' but they did not understand him until they killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that blood money be paid for him."],[5619,"Because he had shed blood among his people, he fled to Madinah and became an ally of the Banu Abd al-Ashhal, so his people called him al-Yaman because he allied with the Yemenis. Hudhayfah, his father Husayl, and his brother Safwan witnessed Uhud. As for his father, some of the Muslims killed him that day, thinking he was one of the polytheists, so Hudhayfah gave his blood money as charity to the Muslims. As for Hudhayfah, he witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ his battles after Badr and lived until the beginning of the caliphate of Ali in the year thirty-six. Some claimed that he was at al-Mada'in in the year thirty-five, forty nights after the killing of Uthman."],[5620,"Hudhayfah died in the year thirty-six, and it was said that he died forty days after Uthman."],[5621,"This statement is an error, and I think its author either did not know the time when Uthman was killed or did not know how to calculate. There is no disagreement among all the biographers that Uthman was killed in Dhu al-Hijjah of the year thirty-five of the Hijrah, and a group of them said he was killed when twelve nights remained of it. Since the killing of Uthman was in Dhu al-Hijjah and Hudhayfah lived after him forty nights, that would be in the following year."],[5622,"When death approached Hudhayfah, and he had lived forty nights after Uthman, he said to us: \"I enjoin you to fear Allah and to obey the Commander of the Faithful, Ali b. Abi Talib.\""],[5623,"A man came to Hudhayfah and said: O Abu Abdullah."],[5624,"When Hudhayfah was brought his shroud, and he was leaning against Ibn Mas'ud, a new shroud was brought. He said: \"What will you do with this? If your companion is righteous, Allah will surely replace it for him, and if he is otherwise, Allah will surely strike his face with it on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[5625,"Hudhayfah lost consciousness at the beginning of the night, then regained consciousness and said: \"Which part of the night is this?\" I said: \"The last part before dawn.\" He said: \"I seek refuge in Allah from Hell\" two or three times, then said: \"Buy for me two garments and shroud me in them, and do not withhold anything from me, for if your companion is pleasing to Allah, he will wear better than them, and otherwise He will strip them from him quickly.\""],[5626,"ﷺ said: Jibril ﷺ came to me and said: 'Indeed, al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise.' Sahih."],[5627,"Ali was asked about Ibn Mas'ud, and he said: 'He recited the Qur'an, then stopped at its ambiguities, so he made lawful its lawful and forbade its forbidden.' He was asked about Ammar, and he said: 'A believer who forgot; when reminded, he remembered.' He was asked about Hudhayfah, and he said: 'He was the most knowledgeable of people about the hypocrites.'"],[5628,"That he is a mawla of Banu Zuhrah."],[5629,"Khabbab b. al-Aratt was a mawla of Banu Zuhrah, and it was said: a mawla of Thabit b. Umm Anmar."],[5630,"Khabbab b. al-Aratt was a mawla of Thabit b. Umm Anmar, and Thabit was a mawla of al-Akhnas b. Shariq al-Thaqafi. And it was said: Khabbab was a mawla of Utbah b. Ghazwan."],[5631,"'Khabbab b. al-Aratt was a mawla of Utbah b. Ghazwan.' 'And the soundest of these opinions is the saying of al-Zuhri, for the narration to him is authentic.'"],[5632,"I heard Kurdus say, \"Indeed, Khabbab ibn al-Aratt embraced Islam in the sixth year, so he was one-sixth of Islam.\""],[5633,"'Khabbab b. al-Aratt was given the kunyah Abu Abdullah.'"],[5634,"From Urwah, regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr, he said: 'Khabbab b. al-Aratt.'"],[5635,"Khabbab b. al-Aratt died in the year thirty-seven, and he was the first of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whom Ali buried in al-Kufah, and the first over whom he prayed after the return of the Commander of the Faithful from Siffin. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5636,"'From his father, Khabbab, a mawla of Banu Zuhrah, and he had witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5637,"The people used to bury their dead in al-Kufah until Khabbab came to them. When he became gravely ill, he said to me: 'O my son, bury me in al-Zuhr, for if you bury me in al-Zuhr, it will be said: a man from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been buried.' When Khabbab died, he was buried in al-Zuhr, and he was the first to be buried in al-Zuhr, so the people then buried their dead in al-Zuhr."],[5638,"He was taken captive in Makkah, and Umm Anmar bt. Siba' al-Khuza'iyyah purchased him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Khabbab and Jabr b. Atik. Khabbab witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Khabbab died in the year thirty-seven, and on that day he was seventy-three years old."],[5639,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was lying under a tree, with his hand under his head. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will you not supplicate against these people who we fear may turn us away from our religion?” He turned his face away from me three times, each time I said it to him and he turned his face away. Then he sat up on the third time and said, “O people, fear Allah and be patient. For by Allah, a man among the believers before you would have a saw placed on his head and be split in two, yet he would not turn back from his religion. Fear Allah, for Allah will surely open for you and bring about good.”"],[5640,"that our rewards go with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; whatever of this world we acquired after him [is the concern].”"],[5641,"I heard Mus'ab b. 'Abd Allah al-Zubayri say: “'Ammar b. Yasir b. 'Amir b. Malik b. Kinana b. Qays b. al-Husayn b. al-Wadhim b. Tha'laba b. 'Amr b. Haritha b. Malik b. 'Ans b. Zayd.”"],[5642,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Patience, O family of Yasir, for your appointment is Paradise.” He said, “And the name of the mother of 'Ammar b. Yasir was Sumayya bt. Muslim b. Lakhm.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5643,"'Ali said to 'Ammar, “O Abu al-Yaqzan.”"],[5644,"Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad b. 'Ali b. 'Abd al-Hamid al-San'ani informed me in Makkah: Ishaq b. Ibrahim narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us: Ma'mar informed us, from Ziyad b. Jabal, from Abu Ka'b al-Harithi, that he entered upon 'Uthman, and a tall, bald man with a few hairs at the front of his head came. I said, “Who is this?” They said, “'Ammar b. Yasir.”"],[5645,"“I saw 'Ammar b. Yasir on the day of Siffin: dark-skinned, tall, with a spear in his hand.”"],[5646,"I saw 'Ammar b. Yasir at al-Kunasa: dark-skinned, with curly hair, and he was reciting this verse: {And of His signs is that He created you from dust; then, behold, you are human beings spreading [throughout the earth]}."],[5647,"“By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have fought with this [spear] alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times, and this is the fourth.” Then he said, “By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they were to strike us until they drive us to the palm fronds of Hajar, I would know that we are upon the truth and they are upon falsehood.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5648,"From 'Urwa: “In the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the allies of Banu Makhzum: 'Ammar b. Yasir.”"],[5649,"“Abu Salama and Umm Salama emigrated, and 'Ammar b. Yasir went out with them, and he was an ally of theirs.”"],[5650,"“I was a peer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; no one was closer to him in age than I.”"],[5651,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah, the first time he came to it, and 'Ammar ibn Yasir said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ must have a place where, when he wakes from his midday nap, he can seek shade in it and pray in it.\" So 'Ammar gathered stones and leveled the Mosque of Quba, and it is the first mosque that was built, and 'Ammar built it."],[5652,"The first to build a mosque and pray in it was 'Ammar ibn Yasir."],[5653,"From 'Asim ibn 'Umar regarding the naming of those between whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood among the Muhajirun and the Ansar, they said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between 'Ammar ibn Yasir and Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman.\""],[5654,"I was in Wasit al-Qasab in the house of 'Abd al-A'la ibn 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir. The doorkeeper said, \"This is Abu Ghadiyah al-Juhani seeking permission.\" 'Abd al-A'la said, \"Let him in.\" He was admitted, wearing tattered clothes, and behold, he was a tall, lean man, as if he were not from this ummah. When he sat down, he said, \"We used to count 'Ammar ibn Yasir among the best of us.\" He said, \"By Allah, I was in the Mosque of Quba when he said—and he mentioned a word—if I had found helpers against him, I would have trampled him until I killed him.\" He said, \"On the day of Siffin, he came walking at the head of the battalion on foot until he was between the two ranks. He thrust a man with a spear and brought him down, and the helmet fell away from him, and he struck him, and behold, it was the head of 'Ammar ibn Yasir.\" He said, \"A client of ours said: I have not seen a man more clearly astray than him.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5655,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"He will be killed by the rebellious group.\" So 'Amr stood up in alarm and went to Mu'awiyah and said to him, \"What is the matter with you?\" Mu'awiyah said, \"Just now 'Ammar ibn Yasir has been killed.\" 'Amr said, \"Has 'Ammar been killed?' Mu'awiyah replied, \"Yes, he has been killed, but by 'Ali and his companions.\" They brought him until they threw him among our spears or swords, according to their agreement, and did not kill him by this method (i.e. crucifixion), as stated in the conditions of both Bukhari and Muslim."],[5656,"We witnessed Siffin, and when we made a truce, these would enter the camp of those and those would enter the camp of these. I saw four men moving along: Mu'awiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, Abu al-A'war al-Sulami, 'Amr ibn al-'As, and his son. I heard 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr say to his father 'Amr, \"We have killed this man, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about him what he said.\" He said, \"Which man?\" He said, \"'Ammar ibn Yasir. Do you not remember the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was building the mosque, and we were carrying one brick at a time while 'Ammar was carrying two bricks at a time? He passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ carrying two bricks at a time, and you were among those present.\" He said, \"Indeed, the transgressing party will kill you, and you are among the people of Paradise.\" Then 'Amr went in to Mu'awiyah and said, \"We have killed this man, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about him what he said.\" He said, \"Be quiet! By Allah, you keep wallowing in your own urine. Did we kill him? It was 'Ali and his companions who brought him and threw him among us.\" It is, as you see, an error."],[5657,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"O Allah, Quraysh have become fond of [harming] 'Ammar. Indeed, the killer of 'Ammar and the one who strips him are in the Fire.\" This was narrated solely by 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak, who is trustworthy and reliable, from Mu'tamir, from his father. If it is preserved, then it is sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. However, the people narrated it from Mu'tamir, from Layth, from Mujahid. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5658,"'Ammar ibn Yasir asked permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him. He said, \"Give him permission.\" When he entered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Welcome to the good one, the perfumed one.\""],[5659,"'Umar ibn al-Khattab wrote to us: \"I have sent to you 'Ammar ibn Yasir as commander and 'Abdullah ibn Mas'ud as teacher and minister. They are among the nobles of the companions of Muhammad ﷺ from the people of Badr, so listen and obey. I have placed Ibn Mas'ud over your treasury, so listen to them, learn from them, and follow them. I have preferred you over myself by [sending] 'Abdullah.\" Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5660,"Ibn Sumayyah: Never were two matters presented to him but that he chose the more rightly guided of them."],[5661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Amr (a companion) was never given the choice between two matters except that he would choose the one that was more virtuous.\" Adh-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summarization."],[5662,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by 'Ammar and his family while they were being tortured and said, \"Rejoice, O family of 'Ammar and family of Yasir, for your appointment is Paradise.\" Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it. According to the condition of Muslim."],[5663,"There was something between me and 'Ammar, so I complained about him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever reviles 'Ammar, Allah reviles him; whoever is hostile to 'Ammar, Allah is hostile to him.\" The chain is sahih, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[5664,"Indeed, the last of your provision from this world will be a drink of mixed milk.\" Sahih according to their conditions, but they did not include it. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5665,"Indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The last drink I will drink when I die is this.\""],[5666,"I heard Khalid b. al-Walid say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a military expedition, and with me was 'Ammar b. Yasir. We came upon some people, among them a household who had mentioned Islam. 'Ammar said, \"These people have declared the oneness of God,\" but I paid no attention to his words. Then they suffered what the people suffered. 'Ammar began to warn me that if I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would inform him. So he went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. When he saw that the Prophet did not support him, he turned away with his eyes flowing with tears. He said: Then he called me and said: \"O Khalid, do not revile 'Ammar, for whoever reviles 'Ammar, Allah reviles him; whoever hates 'Ammar, Allah hates him; and whoever belittles 'Ammar, Allah belittles him.\" Khalid said: \"Seek forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah. By Allah, nothing prevented me from answering him except that I belittled him.\" Khalid said: \"There is nothing I fear more than my belittling of 'Ammar b. Yasir that day.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. This is how it was narrated by Mas'ud b. Sa'd al-Ju'fi and Muhammad b. Fudayl b. Ghazwan from al-Hasan b. 'Ubayd Allah al-Nakha'i. As for the hadith of Mas'ud b. Sa'd..."],[5667,"Mas'ud b. Sa'd narrated to us. As for the hadith of Muhammad b. Fudayl..."],[5668,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on a military campaign, and we defeated them. 'Ammar b. Yasir said, \"They have shielded themselves from us with tawhid,\" but I paid no attention to his words. And he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner."],[5669,"There occurred between me and 'Ammar b. Yasir some words, so I complained about him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Khalid, whoever insults 'Ammar, Allah insults him; whoever is hostile to 'Ammar, Allah is hostile to him; and whoever despises 'Ammar, Allah despises him.\" This was narrated by al-'Awwam b. Hawshab from Salamah b. Kuhayl, and Shu'bah differed in its chain, for he said: from Salamah, from 'Alqamah, from Khalid b. al-Walid."],[5670,"There was between me and 'Ammar b. Yasir some words, so I was harsh to him. 'Ammar went off to complain about me to the Prophet ﷺ. Khalid came while he was complaining about him, and he kept being harsh to him and did not increase except in harshness, while the Prophet ﷺ remained silent. 'Ammar wept and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you not see him?\" The Prophet ﷺ raised his head and said: \"Whoever is hostile to 'Ammar, Allah is hostile to him; and whoever hates 'Ammar, Allah hates him.\" Khalid said: \"So I went out, and there was nothing more beloved to me than the pleasure of 'Ammar. I met him and he was pleased.\" This is the hadith of al-'Awwam b. al-Hawshab."],[5671,"No day ever came upon me that was greater upon me than the matter of 'Ammar. On the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me with some of his companions and put me in command over them, and among the people was 'Ammar, we came upon a people among whom were a Muslim household. 'Ammar and some Muslims spoke to me about them, saying, \"Let them go.\" I said, \"No, by Allah, I will not do so until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sees them and forms his opinion about them.\" 'Ammar became angry with me. When I arrived, I asked permission to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was asking me for news while I was telling him. Then 'Ammar asked permission, and he granted it to him. 'Ammar entered and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, did you not see what Khalid did, such and such?\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, were it not for your gathering, Ibn Sumayyah would not have reviled me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O 'Ammar, leave.\" So 'Ammar left, weeping and saying, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not support me against Khalid.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Did you not answer the man?\" I said, \"Nothing prevented me from answering him except contempt for him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ became angry and said: \"Whoever hates 'Ammar, Allah hates him; whoever reviles 'Ammar, Allah reviles him; and whoever belittles 'Ammar, Allah belittles him.\" So I went out from the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and continued to seek 'Ammar until he sought forgiveness for me."],[5672,"We entered with Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari upon Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman, and I asked him about the trials. He said: \"Go around with the Book of Allah wherever it goes, and look to the group in which is Ibn Sumayyah, and follow it, for he goes around with the Book of Allah wherever it goes.\" We said to him, \"Who is Ibn Sumayyah?\" He said, \"'Ammar. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to him: 'You will not die until the transgressing group kills you, and you will drink a drink of pure white milk that will be the last provision of this world for you.'\""],[5673,"It is not possible that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died on the day he died while loving a man who would enter the Fire forever.\" They said, \"We used to think that he loved you, sought your help, and appointed you.\" He said, \"By Allah, He knows best about my love, but it is enough for him that we used to think he loved a man.\" He said, \"Who is that?\" He said, \"'Ammar b. Yasir.\" They said, \"That is the one you killed on the day of Siffin.\""],[5674,"\"By the One in whose hand is my soul, I have fought with this alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times, and this is the fourth.\" \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if they were to strike us until they drove us to the palm branches of Hajar, we would know that our righteous ones are upon the truth and that they are upon misguidance.\" It is authentic according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[5675,"I came to Madinah and asked Allah to make easy for me a righteous companion to sit with, and He made easy for me Abu Hurayrah. He said to me: \"From which people are you?\" I said, \"From the land of Kufah; I came seeking knowledge and good.\" He said, \"Is there not among you Sa'd b. Malik, whose supplication is answered; and 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud, the keeper of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ's purification and his sandals; and Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman, the keeper of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ's secret; and 'Ammar b. Yasir, whom Allah protected from Satan upon the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ; and Salman, the possessor of the two books?\" Qatadah said: \"The two books are the Injil and the Furqan.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. The hadith is authentic."],[5676,"\"'Ammar is filled with faith up to his very core.\""],[5677,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was suffering from a fever, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Shall I teach you a ruqya with which Jibril treated me?\" I said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: Then he taught him: \"(In the name of Allah I perform ruqya for you, and Allah heals you from every ailment that harms you) Take it, may it be beneficial for you.\""],[5678,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and with him were only five slaves, two women, and Abu Bakr. \"Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs.\""],[5679,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, the length of the prayer and the shortness of the khutba are a sign of a man's understanding of the religion, so prolong the prayer and shorten the khutba.\" Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not record it with this wording according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5680,"A man disparaged 'A'isha in the presence of 'Ali, so 'Ammar b. Yasir said to him: \"Be quiet, you repulsive, reviled one! Do you harm the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" Sahih according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not record it according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5681,"\"Look at Ammar bin Yasir, for he dies upon fitrah (natural disposition), unless a slip of old age overtakes him.\""],[5682,"\"I do not know anyone who went out during the fitna seeking the countenance of Allah the Exalted and the abode of the Hereafter except 'Ammar b. Yasir.\""],[5683,"We witnessed Siffin with 'Ali. We had appointed two men so that when the enemy was heedless, he attacked them and did not return until he dyed his sword with blood. Then he said: \"Excuse me, for by Allah, I did not return until my sword rebounded upon me.\" He said: And I saw 'Ammar and Hashim b. 'Utba while he was walking between the two ranks, and 'Ammar said: \"O Hashim, this, by Allah, will surely betray his command and forsake his army.\" Then he said: \"O Hashim, Paradise is beneath the flashing swords today; I meet the beloved ones Muhammad and his party. O Hashim, one-eyed, and there is no good in a one-eyed man who does not face hardship.\" He said: Then Hashim shook the banner and said [rajaz meter]: \"A one-eyed man seeking a dwelling for his people; he has struggled with life until he is weary; he must either blunt or be blunted.\" He said: Then he entered one of the valleys of Siffin. Abu 'Abd al-Rahman said: And I saw the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ following 'Ammar as if he were a banner for them. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5684,"'Abdullah b. Budayl b. Warqa' b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Rabi'a b. Jazi' b. 'Amir b. Mazin b. 'Adi b. 'Amr b. Rabi'a: he witnessed with the Prophet ﷺ the conquest of Makkah, Hunayn, and Tabuk, and he was killed fighting alongside 'Ali on the day of Siffin."],[5685,"I saw Abu 'Amra al-Ansari on the day of Siffin; he had participated in Badr, the 'Aqaba pledge, and Uhud. He was fasting and writhing from thirst, and he said to a servant of his: \"Woe to you, sprinkle water on me,\" and the servant sprinkled him. Then he shot an arrow, drawing it weakly until he shot three arrows, then he said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of Allah, whether it reaches or falls short, that arrow will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection.'\" Then he was killed before sunset."],[5686,"\"The Muslims will prevail over the Arabian Peninsula, and the Muslims will prevail over Persia, and the Muslims will prevail over the Byzantines, and the Muslims will prevail over the one-eyed Dajjal.\""],[5687,"to blunt or be blunted."],[5688,"I was Mu'awiya's envoy to 'A'isha during the Battle of Siffin. 'A'isha said: \"Who among the people was killed?\" I said: \"'Ammar b. Yasir.\" 'A'isha said: \"That is the leader whom people followed for his religion.\" She said: \"And who else?\" I said: \"Hashim b. 'Utba b. Abi Waqqas, the one-eyed.\" She said: \"That is a man whose mount almost never stumbled.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5689,"As for \"Hashim the one-eyed,\" he is the son of 'Utba b. Abi Waqqas. He embraced Islam on the day of the conquest of Makkah. He was one-eyed; his eye was gouged out on the day of al-Yarmuk. He is the nephew of Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. He witnessed Siffin with 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and on that day he was in command of the infantry."],[5690,"And Khuzaymah b. Thabit b. al-Fakih b. Tha'labah b. Sa'idah b. 'Amir b. Ghayyan b. 'Amir b. Khatmah b. Jusham, and he is Dhu al-Shahadatayn (the one of the two testimonies), his kunyah was Abu 'Umarah, the bearer of the banner of Khatmah on the day of the conquest."],[5691,"Khuzaymah b. Thabit b. al-Fakih b. Tha'labah b. Sa'idah b. 'Amir b. Ghayyan b. 'Amir b. Khatmah, and he is Dhu al-Shahadatayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ made his testimony equal to the testimony of two men. And he informed the Prophet ﷺ that he saw in a dream as if he prostrated on the forehead of the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ lay down for him until he prostrated on his forehead. Ibn Ishaq said: 'He was killed with 'Ali at Siffin after the killing of 'Ammar b. Yasir.'"],[5692,"One of them was called Dahraj and the other 'Abd Allah."],[5693,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The transgressing party will kill 'Ammar.' He said: So he drew his sword and fought until he was killed. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5694,"His uncle recited: \"I adjure by Allah the Namari youth, the Romans took him as a child, but my family is in al-Nabi.\" He said: Al-Nabi is the name of the village where his family was. So Suhaib grew up among the Romans, and Kalb purchased him from them. Then she brought him to Makkah, and 'Abd Allah b. Jud'an al-Taymi bought him and freed him. He stayed with him in Makkah until 'Abd Allah b. Jud'an died, and the Prophet ﷺ was sent."],[5695,"Suhaib's kunyah was Abu Yahya. He is Suhaib b. Sinan al-Namari, from al-Namir b. Qasit. He had been taken captive and fell into the land of the Romans. So it was said, 'Suhaib al-Rumi.' He reached seventy years and used to dye with henna. He died in Madinah in Shawwal of the year thirty-eight and was buried in al-Baqi'."],[5696,"When Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) migrated, the people of Makkah followed him and confiscated his belongings. So, he took out forty arrows from his possessions and said, \"You are not allowed to approach me until I have put an arrow in each of you. Then, I will turn to my sword, and you will know that I am a man who left behind two valuable assets in Makkah, which are now yours.\" Adh-Dhahabi remained silent about this incident in his summary."],[5697,"\"And Allah, Exalted and Mighty, said, 'We did not make for him before this a name.' (Surah Maryam, 19:7) He (Prophet Muhammad) said, 'Certainly, He (Allah) said, 'And indeed, you do not withhold [superfluously] anything but that you spent it, and He also said, 'Indeed, you are called to the collector of sadaqah (zakah), and you are among the emigrants from whom Allah has favored.' (Surah At-Tawbah, 9:75) So, Suhaib said, 'Regarding the statement, 'Indeed, I used to go by the name Abu Yahya, for surely Allah's Messenger ﷺ used to call me Abu Yahya. As for the statement, 'I do not withhold anything but that I spend it,' indeed Allah the Exalted says, 'And whatever you spend of anything, He will replace it. And He is the best of providers.' (Surah Saba, 34:39) And as for the statement, 'Indeed, I am called to the collector of sadaqah (zakah),' surely among the Arabs, they curse each other. So a group of Arabs cursed me after I had known my family and upbringing. They sold me for a black slave in Kufa (Iraq). So, I took their language, and if I were to belong to a lowly family, I would not be associated with anything except them.' He (the narrator) said, 'You have spoken the truth.'\""],[5698,"\"I never placed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between myself and the enemy. I was only on his right, or in front of him, or on his left.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[5699,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as an emigrant while he was eating dates. I approached and began eating from the dates, while I had an inflammation in my eye. He said: 'Do you eat dates while you have an inflammation?' I replied: 'I only eat on my healthy side, which has no inflammation.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed. \"Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it.\" Sahih."],[5700,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say regarding the first emigrants: \"They are the foremost, the intercessors, those who draw near to their Lord, Blessed and Exalted. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they will come on the Day of Resurrection with weapons on their shoulders, and they will knock on the gate of Paradise. The keepers will say to them: 'Who are you?' They will say: 'We are the emigrants.' The keepers will say to them: 'Have you been brought to account?' They will kneel on their knees, scatter what is in their quivers, and raise their hands to the sky, saying: 'O Lord, what account are we to give? We went out and left family, wealth, and children.' So Allah will fashion for them wings of gold, inlaid with chrysolite and rubies, and they will fly until they enter Paradise. That is His saying: {And they said, Praise be to Allah who has removed from us sorrow} [Fatir 34] to the verse {nor fatigue} [Fatir 35].\" Abu Hudhayfah said: Hudhayfah said: Sayfi said: Suhaib said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They will know their dwellings in Paradise better than they know their dwellings in this world.\" Its chain and text are strange. \"I mentioned it in the virtues of Suhaib because he was among the first emigrants, and the narrator of the hadith is his descendants. The hadith belongs to his companions, and we did not write it except from our shaykh, the ascetic Abu 'Amr, may Allah have mercy on him.\" Rather, it is a lie and its chain is dark."],[5701,"\"I accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before revelation came to him.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[5702,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I was shown the place of your emigration, a land with date-palms between two lava tracts, either Hajar or Yathrib.\" He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out to Madinah. Abu Bakr went out with him. I had intended to go out with him, but some young men of Quraysh prevented me. That night, I kept standing and did not sit down. They said: 'Allah has occupied him with his stomach,' and I was not ill. Then they left, and some people caught up with me after I had traveled a barid to bring me back. I said to them: 'Will you accept that I give you a few uqiyyahs of gold and let me go, and keep your word to me?' So I followed them back to Makkah. I said to them: 'Dig under the threshold of the door, for under it are the uqiyyahs. And go to such-and-such a woman and take the two garments.' Then I left until I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ before he left Quba'. When he saw me, he said: 'O Abu Yahya, the transaction has profited,' three times. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, no one preceded me to you, and none told you except Jibril ﷺ .'"],[5703,"Suhaib ransomed his family from Makkah with his wealth, then went out as an emigrant. They caught up with him on the road, and he brought out for them what remained of his wealth."],[5704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call: “O Allah, indeed You are not a god we have invented, nor a Lord we have originated, nor was there before You anyone for us to resort to and forsake [others], nor did anyone assist You in our creation that we might associate him with You. Blessed and exalted are You.” Ka'b al-Ahbar said: “The Prophet ﷺ used to call with it.” Its chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not include it."],[5705,"“Do not hate Suhaib.” Its chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not include it."],[5706,"“Love Suhaib like the love of a mother for her child.”"],[5707,"“Come, let us tell you about our campaigns. As for saying, ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,’ then no.”"],[5708,"I said to Abu Suhaib: “What is the matter with you that you do not narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as your companions narrate?” He said: “O my dear son, I heard as they heard, but I am prevented from narrating because I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Whoever lies about me deliberately will be tasked on the Day of Resurrection to tie two ends of a barley grain, and he will never be able to tie it.’” Amr is weak."],[5709,"“When Umar was stabbed, he ordered Suhaib, the freedman of Banu Jud'an, to lead the people in prayer.”"],[5710,"“Suhaib ibn Sinan, the ally of Abdullah ibn Jud'an al-Taymi.”"],[5711,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are four who excelled. I am the foremost among the Arabs, Suhaib is the foremost among the Romans, Salman is the foremost among the Persians, and Bilal is the foremost among the Abyssinians.\" [Sources: [Jami` al-Tirmidhi]]"],[5712,"I heard Yahya ibn Ma'in say: “Uwais al-Qarni was killed before the Commander of the Faithful Ali ibn Abi Talib on the day of Siffin.”"],[5713,"\"When it was the day of Siffin, a caller from the companions of Muawiyah called out to the companions of Ali, 'Is Uwais al-Qarni among you?' They replied, 'Yes.' He then struck his mount until he reached them, and then said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"The best of the followers is Uwais al-Qarni.\"' The Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary.\""],[5714,"I witnessed Ali on the day of Siffin while he was saying: “Who will pledge allegiance to me upon death?” or he said: “upon fighting?” Then ninety-nine pledged allegiance to him. He said: “Where is the completion? Where is the one I was promised?” Then a man came wearing ragged woolen clothes with a shaved head and pledged allegiance to him upon death and fighting. He said: “It was said: This is Uwais al-Qarni.” He kept fighting before him until he was killed."],[5715,"Is there amongst you Uwais b. 'Amir? (He continued finding him out) until he met Uwais. He said: Are you Uwais b., Amir? He said: Yes. He said: Are you from the tribe of Qaran? He said: Yes. He (Hadrat) 'Umar (again) said: Did you suffer from leprosy and then you were cured from it but for the space of a dirham? He said: Yes. He ('Umar) said: Is your mother (living)? He said: Yes. He ('Umar) said: I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: There would come to you Uwais b. Amir with the reinforcement from the people of Yemen. (He would be) from Qaran, (the branch) of Murid. He had been suffering from leprosy from which he was cured but for a spot of a dirham. His treatment with his mother would have been excellent. If he were to take an oath in the name of Allah, He would honour that. And if it is possible for you, then do ask him to beg forgiveness for you (from your Lord). So he (Uwais) begged forgiveness for him. Umar said: Where do you intend to go? He said: To Kufa. He ('Umar) said: Let me write a letter for you to its governor, whereupon he (Uwais) said: I love to live amongst the poor people. When it was the next year, a person from among the elite (of Kufa) performed Hajj and he met Umar. He asked him about Uwais. He said: I left him in a state with meagre means of sustenance. (Thereupon) Umar said: I heard Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: There would come to you Uwais b. 'Amir, of Qaran, a branch (of the tribe) of Murid, along with the reinforcement of the people of Yemen. He had been suffering from leprosy which would have been cured but for the space of a dirham. His treatment with his mother would have been very kind. If he would take an oath in the name of Allah (for something) He would honour it. Ask him to beg forgiveness for you (from Allah) in case it is possible for you. So he came to Uwais and said.: Beg forgiveness (from Allah) for me. He (Uwais) said: You have just come from a sacred journey (Hajj) ; you, therefore, ask forgiveness for me. He (the person who had performed Hajj) said: Ask forgiveness for me (from Allah). He (Uwais again) said: You have just come from the sacred journey, so you ask forgiveness for me. (Uwais further) said: Did you meet Umar? He said: Yes. He (Uwais) then begged forgiveness for him (from Allah). So the people came to know about (the status of religious piety) of Uwais. He went away (from that place). Usair said: His clothing consisted of a mantle, and whosoever saw him said: From where did Uwais get this mantle? (Using translation from Muslim 2542c)"],[5716,"As the people of Yemen approached, Umar began to gather companions and asked them, \"Is there anyone among you from Qaran?\" Until a man from Qaran came to him and Umar asked, \"Who are you?\" They replied, \"I am Qaran.\" Umar then held him by the collar and recognized him by his distinctive appearance. Umar asked him, \"What is your name?\" He replied, \"My name is Uwais.\" Umar asked him, \"Do you have a mother?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Umar asked, \"Do you have any white spots on your body?\" He replied, \"Yes, I prayed to Allah to remove it from my body except for the size of a dirham, so that I may remember my Lord with it.\" Umar said to him, \"Ask forgiveness for me.\" He replied, \"You are more deserving to ask forgiveness for me. You are the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .\" Umar said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'The best follower is a man named Uwais Al-Qarni. He has a mother and he has white spots on his body. He supplicated to his Lord, and he was cured except for the size of a dirham on his shin, which he uses to remember his Lord with.'\" Umar then requested forgiveness from him. Uwais went among the people, but Umar did not know where he went. Uwais arrived in Kufa and we used to gather in a circle to remember Allah, and he would sit among us. When he mentioned something, it remained fixed in our hearts, and no other speech could take its place. One day, I lost him, so I asked my companion, \"What happened to the man who used to join us?\" He said, \"Who are you referring to?\" I asked, \"Who is that?\" He said, \"That is Uwais Al-Qarni.\" I then found out where he was staying and I went to see him. I said to him, \"May Allah have mercy on you, where have you been and why did you leave us?\" He replied, \"I did not have a garment, so it prevented me from coming to you.\" I then took off my own garment and threw it to him. He threw it back to me saying, \"I delayed wearing it for an hour.\" Then he said, \"If I had taken this garment from you and worn it, my people would have seen me in it, and they would have thought, 'This is the one they accuse of being a self-indulgent.' So I took off my own garment and threw it back to him and said, \"Leave until I hear what they say.\" So he wore the garment and we left together. When he passed by his people's gathering, they said, \"Look at this self-indulgent one, he has not stopped with anyone until he deceived him and took his garment.\" I said to him, \"Are you not ashamed? Why did you harm him?\" By Allah, I presented it to him and he refused to accept it.\" Uwais replied, \"Delegations from various Arab tribes came to Umar and their leader said to him, 'O Umar bin Khattab, is there anyone among you from Qaran?' Umar asked him, 'Are you their leader?' He replied, 'Yes, I am.' Umar then asked him, 'Do you know a man from Qaran named Uwais who has such and such characteristics?' The leader of the delegation said, 'O Amir-ul-Mu'minin, why do you mention this person and his matters?' Umar said to him, 'May your mother be bereaved of you! I encountered him two or three times.' Then Umar said, 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned him to us, he said, 'A man named Uwais bin 'Amir from Qaran will come to you, and he has such and such characteristics.' When the man came, he did not start with anyone before Umar, so he went to him and asked for forgiveness. Umar asked him, 'What prayer have you made for me?' He replied, 'Umar said such and such to me.' Umar said, 'I am not asking for forgiveness for you until you make three promises.' Uwais asked, 'What are they?' Umar said, 'Do not afflict me with what remains for you, and do not inform anyone about what Umar said to you, and forget the third one.'\""],[5717,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man from my Ummah will enter Paradise with the intercession of a man named Rabiahah and Mudar, more than them.\" Hisham narrated to me from Hawshab, from Al-Hasan, that he was Uwais Al-Qarni. Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash said, \"So I said to a man from his people, Uwais, 'By what means did he achieve this?' He said, 'It is the favor of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills.'\" Al-Dhahabi did not comment on this in his summary."],[5718,"Uwais al-Qarni had a cloak that when he sat it touched the ground, and he used to say: “O Allah, I excuse myself to You for every hungry liver and naked body, and I have nothing except what is on my back and in my belly.”"],[5719,"Awais Al-Qarni said, \"Be in the command of Allah as if you have killed all the people.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it when summarizing."],[5720,"\"A man from Murad came to Uwais Al-Qarani and greeted him saying, 'Peace be upon you.' Uwais replied, 'And upon you.' The man asked, 'How are you, Uwais?' Uwais replied, 'Praise be to Allah.' The man asked, 'How is the time treating you?' Uwais replied, 'Do not ask a man who has not experienced the evening if it has become morning, and do not ask a man who has not experienced the morning if it has become evening. O brother of Murad, there is no joy remaining for a believer in death. O brother of Murad, the recognition of a believer with the rights of Allah does not leave him with any silver or gold. O brother of Murad, if a believer fulfills the command of Allah, he will have no companion left. By Allah, we command them to do good and forbid them from evil, but they consider us enemies. And verily, among the evildoers, they find support. By Allah, they accuse us of great sins, but that will not prevent me from speaking the truth.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary.\""],[5721,"They mentioned Hajj and asked Uwais Al-Qarani, \"Did you perform Hajj?\" He replied, \"No.\" They asked him, \"Why?\" He remained silent. Then, one of them said, \"I have a riding animal,\" another said, \"I have provisions,\" and another said, \"I have equipment.\" So, he accepted from them and performed Hajj with it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this incident in the summary."],[5722,"I came to Kufa, and I had no concern there except Uways al-Qarani: I searched for him and asked about him until I happened upon him sitting alone on the bank of the Euphrates at midday, performing ablution and washing his garment. I recognized him by the description. There he was: a fleshy man, dark-complexioned, intensely so; hairy, with a shaved head—meaning he had no forelock—thick-bearded, wearing a woolen waist-wrapper and a woolen cloak, without shoes; large-faced, and very awe-inspiring in appearance. I greeted him, and he returned my greeting and looked at me and said, “May God give you life—who are you?” I extended my hand to him to shake his, but he refused to shake my hand and said, “And you—may God give you life.” I said, “May God have mercy on you, O Uways, and forgive you. How are you—may God have mercy on you?” Then jealousy choked me, from my love for him and my tenderness toward him because of what I saw of his condition, until I wept and he wept. Then he said, “And you—may God have mercy on you, O Harim ibn Hayyan. How are you, my brother? Who guided you to me?” I said, “God.” He said, “There is no god but God. Glory be to our Lord: surely the promise of our Lord is to be fulfilled,” when he named me. By God, he had never seen me, nor had I seen him. Then I said, “How did you recognize me, and know my name and my father’s name? For by God I had never seen you before this day.” He said, “The All-Knowing, the All-Aware informed me. My spirit recognized your spirit when my soul spoke to your soul: spirits have breaths like the breaths of the living. The believers recognize one another and converse by God’s Spirit even if they have not met, and even if they have not spoken; they come to know one another, even if lands are distant from them and homes separate them.” He said: I said, “Tell me a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ that I may memorize from you.” He said, “I did not meet the Messenger of God ﷺ, nor did I have companionship with him. I have seen men who saw him, and what has reached me of his hadith is as what has reached you. I do not like to open this door upon myself—so that I become one who relates traditions, or a judge, or one who gives legal opinions; a person has enough to occupy him, O Harim ibn Hayyan.” He said: I said, “My brother, recite to me verses from the Book of God so I may hear them from you, for I love you for God with a strong love. And supplicate with prayers and give counsel with an admonition that I may preserve from you.” He said: he took my hand on the bank of the Euphrates and said, “I seek refuge in God, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from Satan the accursed. In the name of God, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate.” He gasped once, then wept in his place, then said: “My Lord—exalted be His mention—has said, and most rightful of speech is His speech, most truthful of discourse is His discourse, and best of words is His word: {And We did not create the heavens and the earth and what is between them in play; We created them only in truth} [al-Dukhan 39],” until he reached, “{except whom God has mercy upon; indeed He is the Mighty, the Merciful} [al-Dukhan 42].” Then he gasped again and fell silent. I looked at him, thinking he had fainted. Then he said, “O Harim ibn Hayyan, your father has died, and you are soon to die; and Abu Hayyan has died—either to Paradise or to the Fire. Adam has died, and Eve has died, O son of Hayyan; and Noah has died, and Abraham, the intimate friend of the Most Merciful, O son of Hayyan; and Moses, the one spoken to by the Most Merciful, has died, O son of Hayyan; and David, the vicegerent of the Most Merciful, has died, O son of Hayyan; and Muhammad, the Messenger of the Most Merciful, has died, and Abu Bakr, the caliph of the Muslims, has died, O son of Hayyan; and my brother, my chosen one, and my friend, ‘Umar ibn al-Khattab, has died.” Then he said, “Oh ‘Umar!” May God have mercy on ‘Umar—while ‘Umar at that time was still alive, and that was at the end of his caliphate. He said: I said to him, “May God have mercy on you—‘Umar ibn al-Khattab is still alive.” He said, “Yes, if you understand: you have already understood what I said— I and you are among the dead; it has already been.” Then he invoked blessings upon the Prophet ﷺ and made brief supplications. Then he said, “This is my counsel to you, O Harim ibn Hayyan: the Book of God; keeping company with the righteous among the Muslims; and prayer and peace upon the Prophet ﷺ. I have announced death to myself and announced it to you; so keep remembrance of death—do not let it leave you even for a moment. Warn your people when you return to them, and advise all the people of your religion. Strive for your own soul, and beware, beware of separating from the جماعت (the community), lest you separate from your religion without realizing and enter the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he said, “O God, this man claims that he loves me for Your sake and has visited me for Your sake. O God, show me his face in Paradise, and admit him to me as a visitor in Your abode, the Abode of Peace. Preserve him so long as he remains in the world, wherever he may be; gather up for him what he has lost; make him content in this world with little; and whatever You give him of this world, make it easy for him; and make him, for what You give him of Your blessing, among the grateful; and reward him with the best reward. I entrust you to God, O Harim ibn Hayyan. Peace be upon you and the mercy of God.” Then he said to me, “You will not see me after today—may God have mercy on you—for I dislike fame, and solitude is dearer to me, because I am deeply sorrowful and heavily burdened with care so long as I remain alive in this world among these people. Do not ask about me, and do not seek me. Know that you are in my mind even if I do not see you and you do not see me; remember me and pray for me, for I will remember you and pray for you, God willing, exalted is He. Go—here,” until he took this way. He said: I was eager to walk with him for an hour, but he refused, so I parted from him—he weeping and I weeping. He said: I kept looking at his back until he entered one of the alleys. How often I sought him after that and asked about him, yet I found no one who could tell me anything about him. May God have mercy on him and forgive him. No week passed over me except that I saw him in my sleep once or twice—or as he said."],[5723,"He said: They mentioned Uways al-Qarani in his gathering, and he said, “He was killed with Ali ibn Abi Talib among the foot soldiers.”"],[5724,"\"I saw a woman in the mosque of Uwais Al-Qarni, and she said, 'He used to gather with his companions in their mosque, where they prayed and recited from their scriptures. Then I would bring them their lunch and dinner here until they finished their prayers.' She said, 'This was their habit whenever they were present, until they participated in a war and Uwais and a group of his companions were martyred before Ali ibn Abi Talib.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary.\""],[5725,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"A man from my nation will enter Jannah (Paradise) through the intercession of a man from the tribe of Banu Tamim more than the tribe of Banu Tamim themselves.\" Al-Thaqafi said, Hisham said, \"I heard Al-Hasan saying, 'Indeed, he is Uwais al-Qarni.' It has a Sahih Isnad (authentic chain of narration), but they did not mention it.\" Al-Dhahabi said in his summary, it is Sahih (authentic)."],[5726,"From Ibn Ishaq in naming those who attended Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Dubay'ah: Sahl ibn Hunaif ibn Wahib ibn Ghanim ibn Tha'labah ibn Mujadda'ah ibn al-Harith ibn Amr, and Amr who is called Bakhraj."],[5727,"That he is called Bajda'."],[5728,"Sahl ibn Hunaif ibn Wahb ibn 'Ukaim ibn Tha'labah, Abu Thabit, died in Kufah in the year thirty-eight, and 'Ali ibn Abi Talib ؓ prayed over him."],[5729,"I passed by a flood and entered it and bathed in it, and I came out of it feverish. That was reported to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Tell Abu Thabit to give charity.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his Talkhis."],[5730,"From 'Asim ibn 'Umar: \"Regarding the brotherhood established by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ between the Muhajirun and the Ansar, among Banu Hashim were 'Ali ibn Abi Talib and Sahl ibn Hunaif ؓ.\""],[5731,"Ali prayed over Sahl ibn Hunaif and pronounced six takbirs over him, then turned to us and said, \"He was one of the people of Badr.\""],[5732,"My father said to me, \"O my son, we saw ourselves on the day of Badr when one of us would point his sword at the head of a polytheist, and his head would fall from his body before he even reached him.\""],[5733,"Ali entered with his sword upon Fatimah while she was washing the blood from the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, \"Take it, for I fought well with it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you fought well today, then Sahl ibn Hunaif, 'Asim ibn Thabit, al-Harith ibn al-Simmah, and Abu Dujanah fought well too.\""],[5734,"Ali entered upon Fatimah while she was washing the blood from the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he mentioned the hadith as I dictated it. I heard Abu 'Ali al-Hafiz say, \"We did not write it as a connected report except from Abu Ya'qub with his chain. The well-known version is from the hadith of Ibn 'Uyaynah, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from 'Ikrimah, as a mursal report. This particular text is known only from the hadith of Abu Ma'shar, from Ayyub ibn Abi Umamah ibn Sahl, from his father, from his grandfather.\""],[5735,"Ali came to Fatimah on the day of Uhud and said, \"Hold this sword of mine, for I struck well with it today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you fought well with it, then 'Asim ibn Thabit, Sahl ibn Hunaif, and al-Harith ibn al-Simmah also fought well.\""],[5736,"Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf informed me, and he was one of the prominent Ansar who participated in the Battle of Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , \"It is authentic according to the conditions of the two scholars (referring to Imam Bukhari and Imam Muslim), and they did not exclude it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[5737,"'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, a man from Banu 'Adi ibn Ka'b, saw Sahl ibn Hunaif with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bathing at al-Kharrar and said, \"By Allah, I have never seen anything like today, nor the skin of a hidden maiden.\" Sahl fell down and collapsed. It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, can you do anything for Sahl ibn Hunaif?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah, became angry with him, and said, \"Why would one of you kill his brother or his companion? Why does he not invoke blessing? Bathe for him.\" So 'Amir bathed for him, and Sahl recovered with no harm. And the washing: a vessel with water is brought, he inserts both hands into the vessel, pours water from the vessel over his face, then washes his right hand in it, rinses his mouth into the vessel, inserts his hand to wash his back, then takes water with his left hand and does the same, then washes his chest in the vessel, then washes his right knee and fingertips in the vessel, does the same with the left leg, reaches inside his waist-wrapper, then covers the vessel before placing it on the ground, scoops water from it with his hand, rinses his mouth, pours it over his face, then pours it over his head, and then throws the vessel behind him."],[5738,"My father, Sahl ibn Hunaif, bathed and took off a cloak he had on the day of Hunain when Allah defeated the enemy, while 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah was watching. Sahl was a fair-skinned man, well-built. 'Amir ibn Rabi'ah said to him, \"I have never seen anything like today,\" and he looked at him and admired his beauty when he removed his cloak. He said, \"Not even a maiden behind her curtain has a more beautiful body than Sahl ibn Hunaif.\" Sahl fell ill on the spot and his illness became severe. Someone came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him that Sahl ibn Hunaif was ill and would not be going with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to him and they told him what had happened with 'Amir. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Why would one of you kill his brother? Why did you not invoke blessing? The evil eye is real. Perform ablution for him.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When one of you sees something that pleases him, let him invoke blessing, for the evil eye is real.\" These additions in both hadiths are among what they (al-Bukhari and Muslim) did not include. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his Talkhis."],[5739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"You are my messenger to Makkah. Convey my greetings to them and tell them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commands you three things: do not swear by your fathers; when you relieve yourselves, do not face the qiblah or turn your backs to it; and do not clean yourselves with bones or dung.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his Talkhis."],[5740,"Khawwat ibn Jubair ibn al-Nu'man ibn Imri' al-Qais — who is al-Burak ibn Tha'labah ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted him his share and reward on the day of Badr."],[5741,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"O Abu 'Abd Allah.\""],[5742,"\"Khawwat b. Jubayr b. al-Nu'man b. Umayya b. al-Barak b. Imri' al-Qays b. Tha'laba b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Malik died in Madinah in the year forty, and he was seventy-four years old.\""],[5743,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent Khawwat b. Jubayr to Banu Qurayza on a horse of his called al-Janah. \"Sahih according to the conditions of al-Bukhari, but they did not include it. 'Abd al-'Aziz b. Yahya is weak.\""],[5744,"\"Whatever intoxicates in large quantity, a small quantity of it is unlawful.\""],[5745,"That Khawwat b. Jubayr was among those who went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Badr. When he was at al-Rawha', a stone splinter struck him and broke his leg. \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him back to Madinah, allotted him a share and his reward, and he was like one who witnessed it.\" They said: Khawwat witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5746,"My father Khawwat b. Jubayr: I fell ill and the Prophet ﷺ visited me. When I recovered he said, \"Your body is healthy, O Khawwat. So fulfill for Allah, Exalted be He, what you promised Him.\" I said, \"I did not promise Allah anything.\" He said, \"There is no sick person who falls ill but that he vows something or intends something. So fulfill for Allah ﷻ what you promised Him.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5747,"The name of 'Abd Allah b. Salam was al-Husayn. \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him 'Abd Allah.\""],[5748,"'Abd Allah b. Salam was given the kunya Abu Yusuf. His name before Islam was al-Husayn. When he embraced Islam, \"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him 'Abd Allah.\" He was from the Children of Israel, from the descendants of Yusuf b. Ya'qub (peace be upon them both), and an ally of the Qawaqila from Banu 'Awf b. al-Khazraj. 'Abd Allah b. Salam died in Madinah, according to all their statements, in the year forty-three during the caliphate of Mu'awiya."],[5749,"\"The clientage of 'Abd Allah b. Salam belonged to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he died in the year forty-three.\""],[5750,"From al-Dahhak regarding His saying ﷻ {And a witness from the Children of Israel has testified to its like} [al-Ahqaf 10]: He said, \"The witness is 'Abd Allah b. Salam, and he was among the best of the scholars of the Children of Israel.\""],[5751,"I was sitting in a circle in the Mosque of Madinah. In it was an old man of fine appearance, who was 'Abd Allah b. Salam. He began narrating to them an excellent hadith. When he stood up, the people said, \"Whoever would like to look at a man from the people of Paradise, let him look at this one.\" I said, \"By Allah, I will follow him and learn the location of his house.\" I followed him, and he went until he was about to leave Madinah, then he entered his house. I asked permission to enter, and he permitted me. He said, \"What do you need, O son of my brother?\" I said to him, \"I heard the people saying such and such, and I was pleased to be with you.\" He said, \"Allah knows best who are the people of Paradise. I will tell you about what they said. They said that while I was sleeping, a man came to me and said, 'Get up.' He took me by the hand, and I went with him. Then I saw a wide road on my left, and I started to take it. He said, 'Do not take it, for it is the path of the people of the left.' Then there was a clear, straight road on my right. He said, 'Take this one.' Then I came to a mountain, and he said, 'Climb.' Whenever I wanted to climb, I fell on my backside.\" He said, \"That happened to me several times. Then he went on until he brought me to a pillar whose top was in the sky and whose bottom was in the earth, with a ring at its top. He said, 'Climb on top of this.' I said, 'How can I climb when its top is in the sky?' He took me by the hand and threw me, and I found myself clinging to the ring until morning. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and related it to him. He said, 'As for the road you saw on your left, it is the path of the people of the left. As for the road on your right, it is the path of the people of the right. As for the ring, it is the firm handle of Islam. You will continue to hold fast to it until you die.'\""],[5752,"The Prophet ﷺ set out while I was with him until we entered the synagogue of the Jews. He said, \"O assembly of Jews, show me twelve men who testify that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. Allah will remove from every Jew under the surface of the sky the wrath that has fallen upon them.\" They fell silent, and no one answered him. Then he repeated it to them, and no one answered him. He said, \"You refuse. By Allah, I am the Gatherer, I am the Final Prophet, and I am the Chosen Prophet, whether you believe or reject.\" Then he left, and I was with him, until we were about to go out. Then a man from behind us said, \"Stay where you are, O Muhammad.\" That man said, \"What kind of man do you know me to be among you, O assembly of Jews?\" They said, \"By Allah, we do not know that there has ever been among us a man more knowledgeable in the Book of Allah than you, nor more understanding than you, nor than your father before you, nor than your grandfather before your father.\" He said, \"Then I bear witness to him by Allah that he is the Prophet of Allah whom you find in the Torah.\" They said, \"You have lied.\" Then they rejected his statement and spoke evil of him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have lied. Your statement will never be accepted. Just now you praised him with the good you mentioned, but when he believed, you called him a liar and said about him what you said. Your statement will never be accepted.\" So we went out, and we were three: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, myself, and 'Abd Allah b. Salam. And Allah, Exalted be He, revealed concerning him {Say: Have you considered if it is from Allah and you disbelieve in it} [al-Ahqaf 10] - the verse. \"Sahih according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it. They only agreed on the hadith of Humayd from Anas: 'What kind of man is 'Abd Allah b. Salam among you?' in abbreviated form.\" According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5753,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “No one will enter Paradise who has in his heart an atom's weight of a mustard seed of pride.” This has a sound chain of transmission, but they did not record it, in the mention of Abdullah b. Salam. Salim b. Ibrahim is weak."],[5754,"When Mu'adh b. Jabal was on his deathbed, it was said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, advise us. He said: Sit me up. Then he said: Indeed, knowledge and faith are in their place; whoever seeks them will find them. He said it three times. And seek knowledge from four men: Uwaymir Abu al-Darda', Salman al-Farisi, Abdullah b. Mas'ud, and Abdullah b. Salam, who was a Jew and then embraced Islam. For I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “He is the tenth of ten in Paradise.” This has a sound chain of transmission, but they did not record it. Sahih."],[5755,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a bowl, and he ate from it. Some of it remained, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A man from this mountain pass, from the people of Paradise, will come and eat this.” Sa'd said: I had left my brother Umayr performing ablution, and I said: It is Umayr. Then Abdullah b. Salam came and ate it. “This has a sound chain of transmission, but they did not record it.” Sahih."],[5756,"“Salamah b. Salamah b. Waqsh b. Zughbah b. Za'ura' b. Abd al-Ashhal b. Jumah b. Jusham b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj b. Amr b. Malik b. Aws.”"],[5757,"From Urwah regarding the naming of those of the Ansar who attended the Aqabah, then from the Aws, then from the Banu Abd al-Ashhal: “Salamah b. Waqsh attended Badr.”"],[5758,"And Salamah b. Salamah b. Waqsh, whose kunyah was Abu Awf, attended the first Aqabah and the last Aqabah with the seventy, according to all of them. And all of them said: Salamah attended Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He died in the year forty-five, at the age of seventy, and was buried in Madinah."],[5759,"“Abu Awf Salamah b. Salamah b. Waqsh died in the year forty-five and was buried in Madinah ؓ.”"],[5760,"We had a Jewish neighbor among the Banu Abd al-Ashhal. One day he came out of his house and stood before the Banu Abd al-Ashhal. Salamah said: “I was at that time a young boy, wearing a burdah of mine, lying in it in the courtyard of my family. He mentioned the Resurrection, the rising, the reckoning, the scales, Paradise, and Hell.” He said: He said that regarding the people of Yathrib, while the people were idol worshippers and did not believe in any resurrection after death. They said to him: Woe to you! Do you think this will happen, O so-and-so? That people will be raised after their death to a Garden and a Fire, and they will be requited therein for their deeds? He said: Yes, by the One by whom I swear. They said: O so-and-so, woe to you! What is the sign of that? He said: A prophet sent from the direction of this land—and he pointed with his hand toward Makkah. They said: And when will we see him? He said: He looked at me, and I was the youngest of them in age, and said: If this boy lives out his lifespan, he will meet him. Salamah said: “By Allah, night and day had not passed before Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sent the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was alive among us. We believed in him, but he disbelieved out of envy and jealousy.” We said to him: Woe to you, O so-and-so! Were you not the one who told us about him what you told? He said: Yes, but it is not him."],[5761,"From Salamah b. Salamah b. Waqsh, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while in a state of ablution. They ate and then left. Salamah performed ablution, so Jubayrah said to him: Were you not in a state of ablution? He said: Yes, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we came out from an invitation to which we were invited, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a state of ablution. He ate and then performed ablution. I said to him: Were you not in a state of ablution, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, but the matter occurs, and this is among what has occurred. Al-Layth b. Sa'd said: Zayd b. Jubayrah narrated to me from his father Jubayrah b. Mahmud that his grandfather Salamah was the last of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to die, unless it was Anas b. Malik, for he remained after him. On the condition of Muslim."],[5762,"“O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the clients of the Ansar.”"],[5763,"Abu al-Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us: Ahmad b. Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us: Yunus b. Bukayr narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq: Yazid b. Ruman and Asim b. Umar b. Qatadah narrated to me from Urwah b. al-Zubayr."],[5764,"Asim b. Adi b. al-Jadd b. Ajlan went out on the day of Badr, “and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him back and allotted him a share along with the companions of Badr.”"],[5765,"And 'Asim ibn 'Adi ibn al-Jadd ibn 'Ajlan ibn Dubay'ah, who was from Bali, an ally of the Banu 'Abd ibn Zayd ibn Malik ibn 'Awf ibn 'Amr ibn 'Awf ibn Malik ibn al-Aws, went out to Badr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him back and allotted him his share."],[5766,"He is called Abu 'Abd Allah."],[5767,"My brother and I bought one hundred shares of the shares of Hunayn. The Prophet ﷺ learned of that and said, \"O 'Asim, two ravenous wolves that attack a flock of sheep whose owner has lost it are not more destructive to it than love of wealth and status is to a person.\" This hadith is well-known from 'Asim from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5768,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to camel herders to spend the night away from Mina; they may throw pebbles on the Day of Sacrifice, then throw on the next day, then throw on the Day of Departure. Its chain is authentic; Malik ibn Anas deemed it sound, while others slipped regarding it. Al-Bukhari and Muslim did not include it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted a concession to herders to throw pebbles one day and tend their flocks another day. Yahya said, \"This is a mistake; it is only as Malik said.\" Yahya said, \"When Sufyan narrated this hadith to us, he said, 'Something has slipped my mind regarding this hadith.'\""],[5770,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah on Monday, twelve nights having passed of the month of Rabi' al-Awwal, and he stayed in Madinah for ten years. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5771,"From Ibn Ishaq: Among those who witnessed the Trench was Zayd ibn Thabit ibn al-Dahhak ibn Lawdhan ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd 'Awf ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, and he was among those who carried earth that day with the Muslims."],[5772,"He is called Abu Kharijah: Zayd ibn Thabit ibn al-Dahhak ibn Zayd ibn Lawdhan ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd 'Awf ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar, the Ansari. He died in the year forty-five."],[5773,"Abu Sa'id Zayd ibn Thabit ibn al-Dahhak died in the year forty-five."],[5774,"Zayd ibn Thabit said: The Battle of Bu'ath took place when I was six years old, and it was five years before the Hijrah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah when I was eleven years old. I was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they said, 'A boy from the Khazraj who has read sixteen surahs.' I was not allowed to participate in Badr or Uhud, but I was allowed in the Trench."],[5775,"Zayd ibn Thabit ibn al-Dahhak ibn Zayd ibn Lawdhan ibn 'Amr ibn 'Abd 'Awf ibn Ghanm ibn Malik ibn al-Najjar. He died in the year forty-four or forty-five."],[5776,"My father Zayd ibn Thabit died before the sun turned yellow, and it was my opinion to bury him before morning. The Ansar came and said, 'He will not be buried except in daylight so that people may gather for him.' Marwan heard the voices and came walking until he entered upon me and said, 'It is my firm resolve that he will not be buried until morning.' When morning came, we washed him three times: the first with water, the second with water and lote leaves, and the third with water and camphor. We shrouded him in three garments, one of which was a cloak that Mu'awiyah had given him. We prayed over him after sunrise, and Marwan ibn al-Hakam prayed over him. Marwan sent a camel to be slaughtered, and it was slaughtered and the people were fed. The women wept for three days."],[5777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Do you know Syriac?” I said: “No.” He said: “Then learn it, for letters come to us.” So I learned it in seventeen days. Al-A'mash said: “Letters used to come to him that he did not want anyone to read except someone he trusted.” It is authentic if Thabit b. Ubayd heard it from Zayd b. Thabit, but they did not record it. Authentic if Thabit heard it from Zayd."],[5778,"“I said to Zayd b. Thabit: O Abu Kharijah.”"],[5779,"\"I attended the funeral of Zaid ibn Thabit, and when he was buried in his grave.\" And he mentioned the hadith."],[5780,"“The most merciful of my Ummah to my Ummah is Abu Bakr, and the strictest of them in the matter of Allah is Umar, and the most truthful of them in modesty is Uthman, and the best reciter of them of the Book of Allah is Ubayy b. Ka'b, and the most learned of them in the obligatory shares is Zayd b. Thabit, and the most knowledgeable of them in the lawful and the unlawful is Mu'adh. Indeed, every Ummah has a trustworthy one, and the trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah.” This is a chain that is authentic according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs, but they did not record it with this wording. Rather, they only agreed on mentioning Abu Ubaydah with this chain. I have mentioned its defect in the book al-Talkhis, upon the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5781,"To him: “Step aside, O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: “This is how we treat our elders and scholars.” The chain is authentic according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not record it. It would have been appropriate in the merits of Zayd b. Thabit to begin with the hadith about the compilation of the Quran, for he has many merits, but the two Shaykhs agreed on recording it, so I left it out. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[5782,"“And among the allies of Banu Nawfal b. Abd Manaf is Ya'la ibn Munyah. Munyah is his mother, and she is Munyah bt. Ghazwan b. Jabir from Banu Mazin. His father is Umayyah b. Abi Ubayd b. Hammam b. al-Harith b. Bakr.”"],[5783,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: “Ya'la b. Umayyah: Umayyah is his father, and Munyah is his mother.”"],[5784,"Ya'la ibn Umayyah had three sons; Safwan, Uthman, and Abdul Rahman."],[5785,"I spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about my father Umayyah on the day of the conquest, and I said: “O Messenger of Allah, accept my father’s pledge for emigration.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I accept his pledge for jihad, for emigration has ceased.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[5786,"The first person to date documents was Ya'la b. Umayyah, and he was in Yemen. The Prophet ﷺ arrived in Madinah in the month of Rabi' al-Awwal, and the people dated from the beginning of the year; indeed, the people dated from the arrival of the Prophet ﷺ."],[5787,"From his two paternal uncles, Ya'la and Salamah, the two sons of Umayyah, who said: “We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and with us was a companion of ours. A man fought him and bit his forearm, so he pulled it out of his mouth, and his two front teeth fell out. He went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking blood money. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Would one of you go to his brother and bite him like a stallion bites, then come after that seeking blood money? Go away, for you have no blood money.’” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invalidated it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[5788,"“And from Banu Jusham b. al-Khazraj, then from Banu Salimah b. Sa'd b. Saridah b. Yazid b. Jusham: Mu'adh, Mu'awwidh, and Khallad, the sons of Amr b. al-Jamuh b. Zayd b. Haram b. Ka'b. They witnessed Badr. Mu'adh killed Abu Jahl, and Ikrimah b. Abi Jahl cut off his hand, and he lived until the time of Uthman. His mother is Hind bt. Amr b. Tha'labah b. Haram, and his paternal uncle is Jabir b. Abd Allah al-Ansari, an Aqabi and a Badri.”"],[5789,"“And Mu'adh b. Amr b. al-Jamuh was afflicted with a wound on the day of Badr and remained ill until the era of Uthman. Then he died in Madinah in the year fourteen, and Uthman b. Affan prayed over him, and he was buried in al-Baqi'.”"],[5790,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr: “In naming those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Aqabah from Banu Haram b. Ka'b: Mu'adh b. Amr b. al-Jamuh.”"],[5791,"What an excellent man is Mu'adh ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh."],[5792,"\"While I was standing in line on the day of Badr, I looked to my right and left and saw two young boys from the Ansar. Their teeth were new, and I wished to be among them, so one of them nudged me and said, 'Do you know Abu Jahl?' I replied, 'Yes, and what do you need him for, O son of my cousin?' He said, 'I have been informed that he insults the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, if I see him, he will not leave my sight until he dies.' I was amazed by this, so the other one also nudged me and said the same thing. Before I could respond, I saw Abu Jahl moving among the people, so I told them, 'Behold, this is your companion whom you are asking about.' They immediately drew their swords and struck him until they killed him. Then they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He asked, 'Which one of you killed him?' Each of them said, 'I killed him.' He then asked, 'Did you both wipe your swords?' They replied, 'No.' So he looked at their swords and said, 'Both of you killed him, and the spoils have been rightfully decided for Mu'adh ibn 'Amr ibn Al-Jamuh.'\" (This hadith has been summarized by Adh-Dhahabi.)"],[5793,"From Urwah b. al-Zubayr: “In naming those who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Aqabah from Banu Haram b. Ka'b: Mu'adh b. Amr b. al-Jamuh.”"],[5794,"That Umayr ibn al-Hammam from Banu Salimah, then from Banu Haram ibn Ka'b ibn Ghanm ibn Salimah, was among those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the day of Badr: 'Arise to a Garden whose width is the heavens and the earth.' Umayr ibn al-Hammam al-Ansari said: 'O Messenger of Allah, its width is the heavens and the earth? Excellent! Excellent! By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I must be among its people.' He said: 'Then you are among its people.' He took out some dates and began to eat them, then he said: 'If I live until I eat these dates of mine, that would be a long life indeed.' He threw away what he had of dates, then fought them until he was killed. Sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it. According to the condition of Muslim."],[5796,"From Ibn Ishaq regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Jusham ibn al-Khazraj: Khirash ibn al-Simmah ibn Amr ibn al-Jamuh."],[5797,"From Urwah regarding those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Haram ibn Ka'b: al-Hubab ibn al-Mundhir ibn al-Jamuh ibn Zayd ibn Haram."],[5798,"I advised the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Badr with two matters, and he accepted them from me. I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the expedition of Badr, and he encamped behind the water. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, did you do this by revelation or by opinion?' He said: 'By opinion, O Hubab.' I said: 'Then the opinion is that you place the water behind you, so that if you retreat, you retreat to it.' He accepted that from me. A rejected hadith and its chain."],[5799,"Gabriel ﷺ descended upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'The opinion is what al-Hubab indicated.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Hubab, you have indicated the right opinion.' A rejected hadith and its chain."],[5800,"And Gabriel ﷺ descended upon Muhammad ﷺ and said: 'Which of the two matters is more beloved to you: that you remain in this world with your companions, or that you return to your Lord to what He promised you of gardens of bliss, with houris, everlasting bliss, whatever your soul desires, and whatever delights your eyes?' He consulted his companions, and they said: 'O Messenger of Allah, that you remain with us is more beloved to us, so that you may inform us of the weaknesses of our enemy, supplicate to Allah to grant us victory over them, and tell us news from the heavens.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is the matter with you that you do not speak, O Hubab?' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, choose what your Lord has chosen for you.' He accepted that from me. A rejected hadith and its chain."],[5801,"Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib heard someone claiming that the one who said on the day of the Saqifah, 'I am its seasoned little palm trunk,' was a man from Banu Salimah called al-Hubab ibn al-Mundhir."],[5802,"When Zayd ibn Thabit died, Abu Hurayrah said: 'Today the learned scholar of this nation has died, and perhaps Allah will make Ibn Abbas a successor to him.'"],[5803,"From six of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Umar, Abdullah, and Zayd—their knowledge resembled one another, and they used to take from one another. He said: I said to al-Sha'bi, 'And was al-Ash'ari among these?' He said: 'He was one of the jurists.'"],[5804,"That he attended the funeral of Zayd ibn Thabit, and when he was buried, Ibn Abbas shed tears over his grave and said: 'Thus does knowledge depart.'"],[5805,"Ibn Abbas and Zaid b. Thabit attended a funeral. When Zaid wanted to mount, Ibn Abbas took hold of his stirrup. He said, \"Step aside, O son of my brother.\" He said, \"Thus is done to the scholars.\""],[5806,"When Zaid b. Thabit was buried, Ibn Abbas threw dust upon him, then said, \"Thus is knowledge buried.\""],[5807,"When Zaid b. Thabit died, we sat with Ibn Abbas in the shade of a palace. He said, \"Thus is the departure of knowledge. Today much knowledge has been buried.\""],[5808,"\"And Abu Ahyab Safwan b. Umayyah b. Khalaf b. Wahb b. Hudhafah b. Jumah died. His Islam was at the conquest; he died in the year forty-three.\""],[5809,"\"Uthman b. Talhah b. Abi Talhah b. Abd al-Uzza b. Uthman b. Abd al-Dar, and his mother was the daughter of Sa'id b. Sumayyah from Banu Amr b. Awf from the people of Quba'. His Islam and the Islam of Amr b. al-As and Khalid b. al-Walid were at one time, and he died in Makkah in the year forty-three.\""],[5810,"\"And from Banu Abd al-Dar b. Qusayy\" and he mentioned this lineage. \"His mother was Salamah bt. Sa'id from Banu Amr b. Awf from the people of Quba'. His Islam was before the conquest, along with the Islam of Amr b. al-As and Khalid b. al-Walid. He came to Madinah in Safar of the year eight of the Hijrah, and he died in Makkah in the year forty-two when Mu'awiyah assumed power.\""],[5811,"\"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enter the Ka'bah, he and Usamah b. Zaid, Bilal, and Uthman b. Talhah; no one entered with them.\" Bilal informed me that he asked Uthman b. Talhah, \"Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?\" He said, \"Between the two Yemeni pillars.\" And Shaybah b. Uthman narrated it from his uncle Uthman b. Talhah."],[5812,"Three things win for you the love of your brother: that you greet him when you meet him, that you make room for him in the gathering, and that you call him by the dearest of his names to him."],[5813,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Abdullah is the one who saw the Prophet ﷺ, and Buhaynah is his mother.\""],[5814,"\"...from his sides.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped at Lahy Jamal. And Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Ali b. al-Hussein al-Baqir and Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman b. Thawban narrated from Abdullah b. Malik b. Buhaynah."],[5815,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the morning prayer, and with him was Bilal. He established the prayer. He passed by me and said, \"Will you pray the morning prayer as four?\" Sheikh Abu Bakr b. Ishaq informed us, al-Hasan b. Ali b. Ziyad informed us, Abu Humah narrated to us, Abu Qurrah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj and Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ja'far b. Muhammad, and he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[5816,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by him while he stood upright praying the morning prayer before me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do not make this prayer before noon and after it, and make a separation between them.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5817,"Nafi' b. 'Utbah b. Malik b. Ahyab b. 'Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah, and his mother was from Kinanah, her name being Zaynab bt. Jabir."],[5818,"And it is said his mother was 'Atikah bt. 'Awf, the sister of 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf."],[5819,"Some Arabs came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to greet him, wearing woolen garments. I stood up and said: 'I will certainly come between these people and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then I said to myself: 'He is the confidant of the people.' Then my soul refused anything but that I stand before him. He said: 'I heard him say: \"They will raid the Arabian Peninsula and Allah will grant it conquest. Then they will raid Persia and Allah will grant it conquest. Then they will raid the Dajjal and Allah will grant him conquest.\"' Musa b. 'Abd al-Malik is weak."],[5820,"'Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar b. 'Awf b. 'Abd al-Harith b. Zuhrah b. Kilab, whose kunya is Abu Zubayr, and his mother was Bukayrah bt. 'Abd Yazid b. Hashim b. al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf. He witnessed Hunayn with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5821,"The likeness of a servant when he is afflicted with pain or fever is like an iron that is put into the fire: its dross goes away and its goodness remains."],[5822,"And 'Abd Allah b. 'Adi b. al-Hamra' b. Rabi'ah b. Abi 'Amr b. Ahyab b. 'Ilaj b. 'Abd al-'Uzza, and his mother was the daughter of Shariq b. 'Amr b. Ahyab, the sister of al-Akhnas b. Shariq."],[5823,"And 'Abd Allah b. 'Adi b. al-Hamra' al-Thaqafi, whose kunya is Abu 'Amr."],[5824,"He informed him that he heard the Prophet ﷺ while he was standing at al-Hazwarah in Makkah: 'By Allah, you are the best of Allah's land and the most beloved land to Allah, and had I not been expelled from you, I would not have left.'"],[5825,"And Abu 'Abd al-Rahman Habib b. Maslamah b. Malik b. Wahb b. Tha'labah b. Wathilah b. 'Amr b. Sinan al-Fihri."],[5826,"I heard Habib b. Maslamah say: 'I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ grant an extra third (of the spoils).'"],[5827,"When 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samurah b. Habib conquered Sijistan, and with him was Abu Rifa'ah 'Abd Allah b. al-Harith b. Asad b. 'Adi b. Malik b. Tamim b. al-Du'il b. Jabal b. 'Adi b. 'Abd Manah b. Udd b. Tabikhah, who was a Companion, he traveled with the army. When night came, he stood to pray, then slept in the latter part of the night. His companions forgot him, and a group of the enemy came and slaughtered him."],[5828,"'Abd Allah b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Abi Mulaykah heard from him."],[5829,"He married Umm Yahya bt. Abi Ihab, and his mother Thuwaybah came and said: 'I have suckled both of you.' So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that, and he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[5830,"From 'Urwah, in naming those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Banu Za'ura' b. 'Abd al-Ash-hal: Muhammad b. Maslamah b. Khalid b. 'Adi b. Mujadda'ah b. Harithah b. al-Harith."],[5831,"Al-Dhahabi commented on it in the Talkhis."],[5832,"Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari died in the year forty-three."],[5833,"Muhammad b. Maslamah died in Madinah in the year forty-six, and he was then seventy-seven years old. He was tall and bald."],[5834,"Indeed I know a man whom the trial will not harm: Muhammad b. Maslamah. So we came to Madinah, and there was a tent pitched with Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari inside it. I asked him, and he said: I will not settle in any of their cities until this trial clears away from the community of the Muslims. Sahih."],[5835,"Indeed I know a man whom the trial will not harm. So we came to Madinah, and there was a tent pitched and Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Ansari was there. We asked him, and he said: We will not attach ourselves to any bad thing from their cities until the matter clears away from what it has cleared."],[5836,"I was sitting with Muhammad b. Maslamah when the daughter of al-Dahhak b. Khalifah passed by, and he began following her with his gaze. I said: Glory be to Allah! You do this while you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When Allah casts the proposal of a woman into a man's heart, there is no harm in his looking at her.'"],[5837,"The Prophet ﷺ, when he looked at them, said: 'The faces have prospered.' The chain is sahih, but they did not record it. Sahih."],[5838,"From the Prophet ﷺ, and he went out among Ghatafan. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Who will deal with Ibn al-Ashraf for me? He has harmed Allah and His Messenger.' Muhammad b. Maslamah al-Harithi said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. Would you like me to kill him? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent. Then he said: 'Go to Sa'd b. Mu'adh and consult him.' He said: I went to Sa'd b. Mu'adh and mentioned that to him. He said: Proceed with the blessing of Allah, and take with you my nephew al-Harith b. Aws b. Mu'adh, 'Abbad b. Bishr al-Ash-hali, Abu 'Abs b. Jabr al-Harithi, and Abu Na'il Silkan b. Qays al-Ash-hali. He said: I met them and mentioned that to them. They all came to me except Silkan. He said: O nephew, you are believed by me, but I do not like to do anything of that until I speak directly with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So that was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'Proceed with your companions.' He said: We went out to him at night until we came to him in a fortress. 'Abbad b. Bishr said poetry about that, explaining in verse their killing and their course. He said: [Wafir meter]I called out to him, but he paid no heed to my voice, and he appeared, emerging from above a wall.I called to him again, and he said: 'Who is the caller?' I said: 'Your brother 'Abbad b. Bishr, and this is our armor as a pledge, so take it for two months, fulfilled, or half a month.'He said: 'People who are hungry and starving, yet they have never lacked wealth without poverty.'He came toward us descending quickly and said to us: 'You have certainly come for some matter.'In our right hands were white, sharp swords, tested, with which we cauterize and cut.I said to my companion when he appeared to me, as the swords rushed upon him like the slaughter of a donkey:Ibn Maslamah al-Muradi embraced him, shouting over him like a mighty lion.He struck with his sword, unsheathed, upon him, and Abu 'Abs b. Jabr made him fall in drops.Allah was our sixth, a guardian, with the best blessing and the mightiest victory.And a noble group brought his head, to whom came guidance from truth and righteousness. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5839,"\"To strike with this upon what is in this,\" Muhammad ibn Muslimah said to him, \"Sit down, for we have struck with this upon what is in this before you were born.\" He continued to speak to him until he returned, \"With a sound chain of narration according to the conditions of the two famous sheikhs (Al-Bukhari and Muslim) and they did not exclude it.\" According to the condition of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[5840,"'Who will deal with this wicked one, Marhab?' Muhammad b. Maslamah said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Rise against him; O Allah, help him.' Muhammad b. Maslamah stood up. Jabir said: By Allah, I never saw a battle between two men that I witnessed like theirs. When one of them drew near to the other, a tree came between them, and each one began taking cover from his opponent behind it. When he hid behind something from it, his opponent found what was next to him from it until he reached him. They kept maneuvering with their swords, and Muhammad b. Maslamah struck Marhab's sword against the shield, so his sword became stuck in it, and Marhab could not pull his sword out. Then Muhammad struck him and killed him."],[5841,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped near Khaybar, he said: 'Tomorrow I will give the banner to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.' When the next day came, a group of his companions stretched their necks for it. But he called 'Ali, who was suffering from eye inflammation, spat in his eyes, gave him the banner, and the people advanced with him. They met the people of Khaybar, and there was Marhab before them reciting rajaz, saying: [Rajaz meter]Khaybar knows that I am Marhab, armed with sharp weapons, a tried hero.When swords come forth blazing, I thrust at times and at times I strike.He and 'Ali exchanged two blows, and 'Ali struck him on his head until the sword bit into his molars, and the people of the army heard the sound of his strike. He killed him, and the last of the people had not arrived before it was opened for the first of them. 'This is a large chapter that I have included in the chapters.'"],[5842,"Indeed, 'Amr b. Nufayl and al-Khattab b. Nufayl, the father of 'Umar, were paternal brothers."],[5843,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl came from Syria after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned from Badr. He spoke to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he allotted him his share. He said: And my reward, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And your reward."],[5844,"From Ibn Ishaq in naming those who witnessed Badr among the Muslims with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu 'Adi b. Ka'b b. Fihr b. Malik, he said: 'And Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Rabah b. Qurt b. Razah b. 'Adi b. Ka'b b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr b. Malik, and his mother was Fatimah bt. Ba'jah from Khuza'ah.'"],[5845,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl was given the kunya Abu al-A'war."],[5846,"Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl was dark-skinned, tall, and hairy, and he was given the kunya Abu al-A'war."],[5847,"He was summoned for the funeral of Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl while he was leaving Madinah on Friday, so he went out to it and did not attend the Friday prayer."],[5848,"It was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that a nation would be raised for five years. It is reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Sa'id ibn Zaid ibn 'Amr will embrace Islam before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ enters the house of Al-Arqam and before he calls people to Islam.\" Sa'id ibn Zaid witnessed the battles of Uhud, Al-Khandaq (the Trench), and all the other scenes with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , but he did not witness the Battle of Badr."],[5849,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas washed Sa'id b. Zayd at the tree."],[5850,"Mu'awiyah sent to Marwan b. al-Hakam in Madinah to take the oath of allegiance for his son Yazid, and Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl was absent. He kept waiting for him. A man from the people of Syria said to Marwan: What is holding you back? He said: Until Sa'id b. Zayd comes, for he is the elder of the people of Madinah; when he pledges allegiance, the people will pledge allegiance. He said: Sa'id b. Zayd was delayed until Marwan took the oath of allegiance, and Sa'id withheld from the oath of allegiance."],[5851,"Sa'd washed Sa'id b. Zayd and embalmed him, then he went to the house and bathed, then said: Indeed, I did not bathe from washing him, but I bathed because of the heat."],[5852,"His grandfather Sa'id b. Zayd asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about his father Zayd, saying: O Messenger of Allah, my father Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl was as you saw and as you have heard, and if he had reached you he would have believed in you, so seek forgiveness for him. He said: Yes. So he sought forgiveness for him and said: Indeed, he will come on the Day of Resurrection as a nation by himself. He was, as they mentioned, seeking the religion and died while seeking it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5853,"'Umar b. al-Khattab and Sa'id b. Zayd said: O Messenger of Allah, will you seek forgiveness for Zayd? He said: Yes. So they both sought forgiveness for him, and he said: Indeed, he will be resurrected as a nation by himself."],[5854,"I saw myself with 'Umar binding me and my mother—meaning the mother of Sa'id b. Zayd—wanting me to embrace Islam. If anyone had broken apart or dispersed, he would have been deserving of what you did to 'Uthman."],[5855,"“Ten are in Paradise: Abu Bakr, ‘Umar, ‘Uthman, ‘Ali, al-Zubayr, Talhah, ‘Abd al-Rahman, Sa‘d, and Abu ‘Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah—these are nine.” Then he fell silent. They said, “We adjure you by Allah, will you not tell us who the tenth is?” He said, “You adjured me by Allah: Abu al-A‘war is in Paradise.”"],[5856,"I saw Zayd b. ‘Amr b. Nufayl standing, leaning his back against the Ka‘bah, saying, “O people of Quraysh, none of you today is upon the religion of Abraham but me.” He used to revive the buried infant girl: he would say to the man who wanted to kill his daughter, “Wait, do not kill her; I will bear her upkeep for you.” So he would take her, and when she grew up he would say to her father, “If you wish I will hand her over to you, and if you wish I will bear her upkeep for you.”"],[5857,"From ‘Urwah b. al-Zubayr concerning “those of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who stayed behind at Tabuk: Ka‘b b. Malik b. al-Qayn b. Ka‘b b. Sawwad b. Ghanm b. Sa‘d. He narrated to us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[5858,"And Ka‘b b. Malik b. Abi Ka‘b b. al-Qayn b. Ka‘b b. Sawwad b. Ghanm b. Ka‘b b. Salamah—he is the poet of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was said that he was given the kunyah Abu ‘Abd Allah. Ka‘b witnessed Uhud and was wounded there with more than ten wounds, and he was carried off among the slain. He did not witness Badr, but he witnessed the Khandaq and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except Tabuk, for he stayed behind from it. He is one of the three who stayed behind during the expedition of Tabuk and then were forgiven. Ka‘b b. Malik died in the year fifty during the governorship of Mu‘awiyah b. Abi Sufyan, being then seventy-seven years old."],[5859,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ “commanded Ka‘b b. Malik, when he was forgiven together with his companions, to pray two rak‘ahs—or two prostrations.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5860,"Ka‘b b. Malik was present at al-‘Aqabah and gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there. He said: We set out among pilgrims from Madinah. Al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur said to us, “O you people, I have seen a dream, and by Allah I do not know whether you will agree with me about it or not.” He said: We said, “What is that?” He said: “I have seen that I should not leave this building behind me.” And he mentioned the hadith at length. “I think I have already related it in the account of al-Bara’ b. Ma‘rur ؓ.”"],[5861,"“Al-Hakam b. ‘Amr b. Mujadda‘ b. Hidhyam b. al-Harith b. Nu‘aylah b. Mulayk b. Damrah b. Bakr b. ‘Abd Manah b. Kinanah.”"],[5862,"“Al-Hakam b. ‘Amr b. Mujadda‘ b. Hidhyam b. Hulwan b. al-Harith b. Nu‘aylah b. Mulayk b. Damrah. His mother was Umamah bt. Malik b. al-Ashhal b. ‘Abd Allah b. Ghifar. He died in Khurasan while he was governor there in the year fifty-one.”"],[5863,"“Al-Hakam b. ‘Amr b. Mujadda‘ b. Hidhyam b. al-Harith b. Nu‘aylah b. Mulayk b. Damrah b. Bakr b. ‘Abd Manah b. Kinanah. Nu‘aylah was the brother of Ghifar b. Mulayk. He accompanied the Prophet ﷺ until he passed away, then moved to al-Basrah and settled there. Ziyad b. Abi Sufyan appointed him over Khurasan until he died there in the year fifty.”"],[5864,"I was with al-Hakam b. ‘Amr al-Ghifari when a messenger from ‘Ali b. Abi Talib came to him and said, “The Commander of the Faithful says to you: You are the most deserving of those who should help us in this matter.” He replied, “I heard my close friend, your cousin, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘When the matter is like this—or similar to this—then take a sword of wood.’”"],[5865,"I heard Ahmad b. Shayban say: “Al-Hakam b. ‘Amr, Rafi‘ b. ‘Amr, and ‘Ulayyah b. ‘Amr accompanied the Prophet ﷺ. Then Ziyad appointed al-Hakam over Khurasan. The cause of his death was that he prayed against himself while he was in Marw, regarding a letter that was read to him and sent back to him from Ziyad, and another from Mu‘awiyah. His supplication was answered, and he died in Marw. Buraydah al-Aslami had died before him, and they were both buried together in the cemetery of Husayn in Marw, opposite the bathhouse of Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari. I have visited their graves.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5866,"That he should reserve for himself the white and the yellow (silver and gold) and not divide among the Muslims any gold or silver. So al-Hakam wrote to him: “To proceed: You wrote mentioning the letter of the Commander of the Faithful. I found the Book of Allah prior to the letter of the Commander of the Faithful. I swear by Allah, if the heavens and the earth were closed off against a servant, and he feared Allah, He would make for him a way out from between them. Peace.” Al-Hakam ordered a crier to proclaim: “Go early to your spoils,” and he divided it among them. When al-Hakam did what he did in dividing the spoils, Mu‘awiyah sent someone who shackled and imprisoned him, and he died in his shackles and was buried in them, and he said, “I will be a disputant.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5867,"\"Do you not know why I came to you? Do you not remember that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ received the command from his commander to stand and then fall into the fire, the man was about to fall into it but he managed to grab hold of him? Then the Prophet ﷺ said, 'If he had fallen into it, he would have entered the Hellfire. There is no obedience in the disobedience of Allah.' Al-Hakam said, 'Yes.' 'Imran said, 'I only wanted to remind you of this hadith.'\""],[5868,"A man from the people said to him: 'Why do you say this, when you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"None of you should wish for death because of harm that befalls him\"?' He said: 'I heard what you heard, but I am hastening towards six things: the sale of al-Hakam, the abundance of stipulations, the rule of youths, the shedding of blood, the severing of kinship ties, and a generation that will come at the end of time who will take the Qur'an as musical instruments.'"],[5869,"\"Rafi' b. 'Amr b. Mujadda' b. Hidhyam b. al-Harith al-Ghifari; he died in Basra in the year fifty.\""],[5870,"\"After me there will be a people from my Ummah who recite the Qur'an, but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will depart from the religion as an arrow departs from the game, then they will not return to it. Their distinguishing mark is shaving (the head).\" 'Abdullah b. al-Samit said: I met Rafi' b. 'Amr, the brother of al-Hakam b. 'Amr al-Ghifari, and said to him: 'What is the hadith that you heard from Abu Dharr, such-and-such?' I mentioned the hadith to him. He said: 'What amazes you about this? I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[5871,"I was throwing stones at the date-palm trees of the Ansar while I was a boy. The Prophet ﷺ saw me and said: \"O boy, why are you throwing stones at the date-palms?\" I said: 'I eat (from them).' He said: \"Do not throw stones at the date-palms, but eat what falls beneath them.\" Then he wiped my head and said: \"O Allah, fill his belly.\""],[5872,"I was throwing stones at the date-palm trees of the Ansar, so they seized me and took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said: 'This one throws stones at our date-palms.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Rafi', why do you throw stones at their date-palms?\" I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, hunger.' He said: \"Then eat what has fallen. May Allah fill you and quench your thirst.\""],[5873,"\"Abu Sa'id 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samura b. Habib b. 'Abd Shams; his mother was Arwa bt. Abi al-Fara'a b. Ka'b b. 'Amr b. Tarif b. Khuzayma b. 'Alqama b. Khidash b. Ghanm b. Malik b. Kinana. He died in Basra in the year fifty, and Ziyad prayed over him and walked in his funeral procession.\""],[5874,"I went out in the funeral procession of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Samura, and Ziyad was walking in front of the bier. Some men from his freedmen started walking on their heels in front of the bier, saying: 'Slowly, slowly, may Allah bless you.' He said: Abu Bakra caught up with us on part of the road to al-Mirbad. When he saw those people and what they were doing, he charged at them forcefully and raised his whip towards them, saying: \"Make way! By the One who honored the face of Abu al-Qasim ﷺ, I saw us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when we would almost trot with it (the bier) at a quick pace.\""],[5875,"(empty)"],[5876,"\"'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Taym b. Murra; he is the nephew of Talha b. 'Ubaydullah. His mother was 'Umira bt. Jud'an b. 'Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Taym b. Murra. He is the son of the sister of 'Abdullah b. Jud'an al-Qurashi.\""],[5877,"I embraced Islam on the day of the conquest, \"and I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[5878,"My father 'Abd al-Rahman was struck down with Ibn al-Zubayr. \"Ibn al-Zubayr ordered that he be buried in the mosque of the Ka'ba, then he ordered the horses (to be walked) over his grave at night to conceal its trace.\""],[5879,"\"It was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ fragrance of medicine, and they mentioned the frog as a medicine, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade killing it.\""],[5880,"\"'Uthman b. Abi al-'As b. 'Abd Rahaman b. 'Abdullah b. Hammam al-Thaqafi, his kunya is Abu 'Abdullah. He died in the year fifty.\""],[5881,"And he said: \"I saw us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performing ramal (a brisk walk).\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5882,"Sufyan b. Awf al-Ghamidi was from the people of Hims. He accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was brave, courageous, and generous. He is the one who raided Hit and al-Anbar during the days of Ali, killing and taking captives. He was among those who killed Hassan b. Hassan al-Bakri, the brother of al-Harith b. Hassan, who came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ with Qayla bt. Makhrama. Ali gave a sermon and said in his sermon: \"The brother of Ghamid has raided Hit and al-Anbar.\" He was in charge of the summer expeditions during the days of Muawiya. Muawiya used to honor his position and say: \"He would carry out raids in a single gathering against a thousand fully mature horses.\" After him, Muawiya appointed Ibn Masud al-Fazari over the summer expeditions, and it was said: [al-Bahr al-Tawil]\"Set up, O Ibn Masud, a firm spear, as Sufyan b. Awf used to set it up. And raid, O Ibn Masud, the cities of Caesar, as Sufyan b. Awf used to raid them. Sufyan is a chief among the chiefs of a tribe by whom Taym is protected, and there is no people among the people who can oppress them.\""],[5883,"Al-Mughira b. Shuba was given the kunya Abu Abdullah. He governed Kufa and died there in the year fifty."],[5884,"Al-Mughira b. Shuba b. Abi Amir b. Masud b. Muattib b. Malik b. Amr b. Sa'd b. Amr b. Qays b. Shayba b. Bakr b. Hawazin b. Mansur b. Ikrima b. Khasafa b. Qays."],[5885,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Isa."],[5886,"Al-Mughira b. Shuba b. Abi Amir b. Masud b. Muattib b. Malik b. Ka'b b. Amr b. Sa'd b. Awf b. Thaqif, whose name is Qusayy b. Munabbih b. Bakr b. Hawazin b. Mansur b. Ikrima b. Khasafa b. Qays b. Ghaylan b. Mudar b. Nizar. He was given the kunya Abu Abdullah and was called 'Mughira of opinion.' He was clever; he never found himself facing two matters without finding a way out of one of them. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and stayed with him until he performed the Umrah of al-Hudaybiyya in Dhu al-Qa'dah in the year six of the Hijra. Al-Mughira said: It was the first journey I went on with him, and I used to be with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq and keep close to the Prophet ﷺ among those who kept close to him. After that, al-Mughira witnessed the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The delegation of Thaqif arrived, and he lodged them and honored them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Abu Sufyan b. Harb to al-Ta'if, and they defeated the banners."],[5887,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, Abu Bakr al-Siddiq sent me to the people of al-Buhayra. Then I witnessed al-Yamama, then I witnessed the conquests of Syria with the Muslims, then I witnessed al-Yarmuk, and my eye was injured on the day of al-Yarmuk. Then I witnessed al-Qadisiyya, and I was Sa'd's envoy to Rustam. I was appointed by Umar b. al-Khattab to some conquests, and I conquered Hamadhan. I was on the left wing of al-Numan b. Muqarrin on the day of Nahawand. Umar had written: If al-Numan is killed, the commander is Hudhayfa; if Hudhayfa is killed, the commander is al-Mughira. I was the first to establish the diwan of Basra, and I gathered the people to be given stipends. I governed Kufa for Umar b. al-Khattab, and Umar was killed while I was its governor. Then I governed it for Muawiya. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5888,"Ali, when al-Mughira b. Shuba threw his ring into the grave of the Prophet ﷺ, said: \"Do not let people say that you went down into the grave of the Prophet ﷺ, and do not tell people that your ring is in his grave.\" So Ali went down, saw where it lay, picked it up, and gave it back to him. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5889,"We were sitting at the small gate that is in the mosque, meaning the gate of Ghaylan: Abu Bakra, his brother Nafi, and Shibl b. Ma'bad. Al-Mughira b. Shuba came walking in the shade of the mosque, and the mosque at that time was made of reeds. He came to Abu Bakra and greeted him. Abu Bakra said to him: \"O governor, what brought you out of the governor's residence?\" He said: \"I came to talk with you.\" Abu Bakra said to him: \"That is not for you. The governor sits in his house and sends for whomever he wishes and talks with them.\" He said: \"O Abu Bakra, there is no harm in what I do.\" So he entered through the smaller gate and went on until he came to the door of Umm Jamil, a woman from Qays. He said: Between the house of Abu Abdullah and the woman's house there was a road. He entered upon her. Abu Bakra said: \"I have no patience for this.\" So he sent for a servant of his and said to him: \"Climb up to my room and look from the window.\" The servant went, looked, and before long returned and said: \"I found them under one blanket.\" Abu Bakra said to the people: \"Get up with me.\" They got up. Abu Bakra began by looking, and he said: \"To Allah we belong and to Him we return.\" Then he said to his brother: \"Look.\" He looked and said: \"What did you see?\" He replied: \"I saw adultery.\" Then he said: \"What raised your suspicion? Look.\" He looked and said: \"What did you see?\" He replied: \"I saw adultery by a married person.\" He said: \"I call Allah as witness over you.\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: Then he went back to his family and wrote to Umar b. al-Khattab about what he had seen. A terrible matter came to him: a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Before long, he sent Abu Musa al-Ashari as governor of Basra. Abu Musa sent to al-Mughira: \"Stay for three days during which you are your own governor. On the fourth day, set out, you and Abu Bakra and his witnesses. How fortunate for you if you were lied about, and woe to you if you were truthfully reported.\" So the people set out: Abu Bakra and his witnesses and al-Mughira b. Shuba until they came to Madinah to the Commander of the Faithful. He said: \"Bring what you have, O Abu Bakra.\" He said: \"I bear witness that I saw adultery by a married person.\" Then they brought forward Abu Abdullah, his brother, and he testified, saying: \"I bear witness that I saw adultery by a married person.\" Then they brought forward Shibl b. Ma'bad al-Bajali, and he asked him, and he testified likewise. Then they brought forward Ziyad, and he said: \"What did you see?\" He said: \"I saw them under a blanket, and I heard heavy breathing. I do not know what was beyond that.\" Umar said \"Allahu Akbar\" and rejoiced that al-Mughira was saved. He flogged the people except Ziyad. He said: The Commander of the Faithful Umar b. al-Khattab had appointed Utba b. Ghazwan over Basra. He arrived there in the year sixteen, and his death was in the year nineteen. Utba disliked that and prayed to Allah to relieve him of it. He fell from his mount on the road and died, may Allah have mercy on him. Then what happened with al-Mughira happened."],[5890,"Egypt was conquered in the year twenty, and in it the Euphrates was conquered by force. It was said that al-Mughira b. Shuba conquered it, and Utba b. Ghazwan had left him as his deputy and gone to Umar. Umar appointed al-Mughira b. Shuba over Basra and wrote to him after that. Then what happened between him and Umm Jamil al-Qaysiyya happened."],[5891,"We attended the funeral of al-Mughira b. Shuba. When he was lowered into his grave, a man stood over it and said: \"Who is this buried one?\" We said: \"The governor of Kufa, al-Mughira b. Shuba.\" By Allah, it was not long before he said: [al-Bahr al-Tawil]\"Is it the trace of a dwelling of al-Mughira that is known? Over it the hills of jinn and humans are known. If you have left behind Haman after us and Pharaoh, then know that the Lord of the Throne is just.\" He said: They turned on him and reviled him. By Allah, I do not know which way he went. The governorship of al-Mughira b. Shuba over Kufa lasted seven years."],[5892,"I heard Jarir say at the funeral of al-Mughira b. Shuba: \"Ask forgiveness for your governor, for he loved well-being.\""],[5893,"A man came and called out, seeking permission: \"Abu 'Isa is at the door of the Commander of the Faithful, 'Umar.\" 'Umar said, \"And who is Abu 'Isa?\" He said, \"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, I am he.\" 'Umar said, \"Does 'Isa have a father? Is there not among the kunyas of the Arabs what you can use as kunyas, like Abu 'Abd Allah and Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?\" A man said, \"I testify that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ give him the kunya of Abu 'Isa.\" 'Umar said, \"The Prophet ﷺ has been forgiven his past and future sins, but we are in confusion; we do not know what will be done with us.\" So he gave him the kunya Abu 'Abd Allah.Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5894,"Al-Mughirah governed Kufa in the year 41 and died in the year 50."],[5895,"Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah used to revile 'Ali in his sermon, and he appointed preachers who reviled him. While he was delivering a sermon and reviling 'Ali, and next to me was Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl al-'Adawi, he struck me with his hand and said, \"Do you not see what this one says?—or he said, 'these ones'—I bear witness that the nine are in Paradise, and if I were to swear about the tenth, I would be truthful. We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Hira': I, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf. The mountain shook, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Be still, Hira', for upon you are none but a prophet, a siddiq, or a martyr.'\""],[5896,"We traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one night, and he tapped my mount's neck with his hand and said, \"Do you have water with you?\" I said, \"Yes, here is a small waterskin with me.\" He dismounted, relieved himself, then came to me and said, \"Do you need to relieve yourself?\" I said, \"No.\" Then he washed his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, sniffed water three times, and washed his face three times. Then he wanted to expose his forearms, but he was wearing a narrow woolen jubbah and could not get his forearms out of it, so he brought his hands out from beneath the jubbah and washed his forearms three times each. Then he wiped his head and wiped over his khuffs. Then we traveled on and caught up with the people, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf led them in prayer. I wanted to inform him of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ location, but he prevented me. So we prayed, then made up the second one.\"Gharib, sahih al-isnad, but they did not record it in this wording.\"Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5897,"I witnessed al-Qadisiyyah. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah went, and when he came to Ibn Rustam, who was on a throne, he leapt up and sat with him on his throne. They were bewildered. Al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah said to them, \"What are you alarmed about from this? I will now get up and return to what I was, and your companion will return to what he was.\" They said."],[5898,"On the day of al-Qadisiyyah, al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah was sent to the ruler of Persia. He said, \"They sent ten men with me, and they were sent. He tightened his garments, took a shield, and set off until they reached him.\" He said, \"Throw me a shield,\" and he sat on it. The 'ilj said, \"You Arabs, we know what has brought you to us. You are a people who cannot find enough food in your lands to satisfy yourselves, so take, for we will give you the food you need. We are Magians, and we dislike killing you, for you defile our land for us.\" Al-Mughirah said, \"By Allah, that is not what brought us. We were a people who worshiped stones and idols; when we saw a stone better than another, we threw it away and took another, and we did not know a Lord until Allah sent to us a messenger from among ourselves. He called us to Islam, and we followed him. We did not come for food. We have been commanded to fight our enemy among those who have abandoned Islam. We did not come for food, but we came to kill your warriors and take your offspring captive. As for what you mentioned about food, by my life, we do not find food to satisfy ourselves, and sometimes we do not even find enough water to quench our thirst. So we came to this land of yours and found abundant food and abundant water. By Allah, we will not leave it until it is ours or yours.\" The 'ilj said in Persian, \"He has spoken the truth.\" He said, \"And your eye will be gouged out.\" His eye was gouged out the next day; an arrow struck him.\"Gharib, sahih al-isnad, but they did not record it.\"Sahih."],[5899,"\"Rukanah b. 'Abd Yazid b. Hashim b. al-Muttalib b. 'Abd Manaf died in Madinah at the beginning of Mu'awiyah's rule, in the year 40.\""],[5900,"He \"wrestled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ threw him.\" Rukanah said, \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, 'The difference between us and the polytheists is the turbans over the caps.'\""],[5901,"'Amr b. al-'As died in the year 51, and Allah knows best."],[5902,"The two sons of al-'As are believers: Hisham and 'Amr."],[5903,"When 'Amr was near death, he said to his son 'Abd Allah, \"When I die, wash me, shroud me, and fasten my izar—or my lower garment—for I will be disputing. When you have washed me, hasten with me in walking. When you place me in the prayer area—and that is on a day of 'Id, either Fitr or Adha—look at the mouths of the roads, and when no one remains and the people have gathered, begin and pray over me, then pray the 'Id. When you place me in my grave, pour the earth over me, for my right side is not more entitled to the earth than my left side. When you have leveled the earth over me, sit by my grave for about the time it takes to slaughter a camel and cut it up, so that I may feel comforted by you.\""],[5904,"When death approached 'Amr b. al-'As, he said, \"Measure my wealth.\" They measured it and found it to be fifty-two mudds. He said, \"Who will take it with all that it entails? Would that it were dung.\" He said, \"And the mudd was sixteen uqiyyahs, and each uqiyyah from it was two makkuks.\"Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5905,"Amr b. al-As b. Wa'il b. Hashim b. Sa'id b. Sahm, and his kunya was Abu Abd Allah. His mother was al-Nabigha bt. Harmala, a captive from Anaza. His maternal brothers were Amr b. Uthatha b. Abbad b. Abd al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf b. Qusayy and Unayf b. Abi al-As b. Umayya b. Abd Shams. There is disagreement about the time of his death."],[5906,"that he died in the year fifty-one. And the most correct thing I have heard about the time of Amr b. al-As's death"],[5907,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: 'Amr b. al-As died in the year forty-three and was buried in Egypt.'"],[5908,"Amr b. al-As b. Wa'il came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year eight, with the kunya Abu Abd Allah, and died in Egypt on the day of Fitr in the year forty-two, while he was governor there."],[5909,"\"I went intentionally to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to convert (to Islam). I encountered Khalid ibn Al-Walid before the conquest (of Mecca), while he was approaching from Mecca. I asked, 'Where are you heading, O Abu Sulayman?' He replied, 'By Allah, the landmark (Meesam) has been established, and indeed, the man is a Prophet. I will go and, by Allah, I will convert.' I asked him, 'Until when?' He said, 'And I, by Allah, have come only to convert.' So we proceeded to meet the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . Khalid ibn Al-Walid took the lead and accepted Islam and pledged his allegiance. Then I approached and pledged allegiance to him, and then I left.\""],[5910,"Amr b. al-As was short and stout."],[5911,"Umar b. al-Khattab saw Amr b. al-As and he had dyed his gray hair so it was like a crow's wing, so he said: 'What is this, O Abu Abd Allah?' He replied: 'O Commander of the Faithful, I love that you see in me some remnant [of youth].' Umar did not forbid him from that nor fault him for it. Amr b. al-As died when he was about one hundred years old. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5912,"Amr b. al-As used to say: 'I wonder at one whom death befalls while his intellect is with him, how he cannot describe it.' When death befell him, his son Abd Allah said to him: 'Describe death for us while your intellect is with you.' He said: 'O my son, death is too great to be described, but I will describe for you something of it. I find myself as if the mountains of Radwa are on my neck, I find myself as if the thorns of weapons are in my inside, and I find myself as if my soul is coming out of the eye of a needle.'"],[5913,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Amr b. al-As to al-Bahrayn, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out in a military expedition and we went out with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dozed, then woke and said: 'May Allah have mercy on Amr.' He said: We recalled every person whose name was Amr. Then he dozed a second time and woke and said: 'May Allah have mercy on Amr.' Then he dozed a third time and woke and said: 'May Allah have mercy on Amr.' We said: 'Who is Amr, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Amr b. al-As.' They said: 'What is the matter with him?' He said: 'I remembered him. When I called people to give charity, he came with charity and gave generously, and I said to him: \"Where did you get this?\" He said: \"From Allah.\" Amr spoke truly. Indeed Amr has much good.' Zuhayr said: When the fitna occurred, I said: 'I will follow this one about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said what he said,' so I did not part from him."],[5914,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not equate anyone of his companions with me and Khalid b. al-Walid in his war since we embraced Islam. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5915,"He was a descendant of Banu al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf: Qays b. Makhrama b. al-Muttalib b. Abd Manaf. His mother was Asma bt. Amir, a woman from the Ansar."],[5916,"I and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were born in the Year of the Elephant, so we are of the same age."],[5917,"Abd Allah b. Hisham b. Zuhra b. Uthman b. Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Taym b. Murra. His mother was a woman from Banu Asad b. Khuzayma b. Sa'd b. Layth b. Bakr b. Abd Manat. His mother took him to the Prophet ﷺ when he was small, and he wiped his head, but did not take his pledge of allegiance."],[5918,"From Abdullah b. Hisham—who met the Prophet ﷺ—that his mother brought him to the Prophet ﷺ, and he wiped his head and supplicated for him. He used to slaughter a single sheep as sacrifice on behalf of all his household."],[5919,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was holding the hand of Umar b. al-Khattab. Umar said, 'By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, you are more beloved to me than everything except myself.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Now, O Umar.' Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[5920,"Al-Munkadir b. Abdullah b. al-Hudayr b. Muhriz b. Abd al-Uzza b. Amir b. al-Harith b. Haritha b. Sa'd b. Taym b. Murra met the Prophet ﷺ and heard from him."],[5921,"The first thing that comes to me I will send to you. Then ten thousand dirhams came to her, and she sent them to him. He took a slave girl from it, and she bore him his sons Muhammad, Abu Bakr, and Umar. All of them were mentioned for righteousness, and hadith was transmitted from them."],[5922,"Whoever circumambulates the House seven circuits without engaging in vain talk in it, it is like the reward of freeing a slave."],[5923,"That one night he went out after delaying the Isha prayer until a short while or an hour of the night had passed, while the people were waiting in the mosque. He said, 'What are you waiting for?' They said, 'We are waiting for the prayer.' He said, 'You will remain in prayer as long as you wait for it.' Then he said, 'Indeed, it is a prayer that no one from the nations before you has prayed.'"],[5924,"Among the names of the companions of the Aqaba who pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ from the Banu Ghanm b. Malik b. al-Najjar was Abu Ayyub, and he is Khalid b. Zayd b. Kulayb b. Tha'laba."],[5925,"We raided Constantinople and Abu Ayyub al-Ansari was with us. We formed two rows, and I never saw two rows longer than them. Abu Ayyub al-Ansari died during this raid, and he had instructed to be buried at the foot of the wall of Constantinople and that a debt owed by him be paid, and so it was done."],[5926,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ established brotherhood between Abu Ayyub and Mus'ab b. Umayr. Abu Ayyub witnessed Badr, Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He died in the year Yazid b. Mu'awiya raided Constantinople, during the caliphate of his father Mu'awiya, in the year fifty-two. His grave is at the foot of the fortress of Constantinople in the land of the Romans; it is mentioned that they tend to his grave, visit it, and seek rain through it when they suffer drought."],[5927,"Abu Ayyub fought at Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he did not miss any campaign of the Muslims except that he was in it, except one year, when a young man was appointed over the army and he stayed behind that year. After that he began to regret it and say, 'What concern is it to me who is appointed?' He fell ill while Yazid b. Mu'awiya was in command of the army. Yazid entered to visit him and said, 'What is your need?' He said, 'My need is that when I die, you mount and then advance into enemy territory as far as you find a passage. If you find no passage, then bury me and return.' He said: Abu Ayyub used to say: Allah, exalted is He, said: 'Go forth, light and heavy' [Qur'an 9:41], so I find myself only light or heavy. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5928,"He witnessed with him the day of Harura'."],[5929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was staying with Abu Ayyub al-Ansari in an upper room, and his food was in a basket in a closet. A cat would come through the opening and take the food from the basket. Abu Ayyub complained about that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'That is a ghoul. When it comes, say to it: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adjures you not to return.' He said: It came, and Abu Ayyub said to it: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ adjures you not to return. It said, 'O Abu Ayyub, let me off this time, for by Allah I will not return.' So he left it. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. It said that twice, then it said, 'Would you like me to teach you words which, if you say them, no devil will approach your house that night, that day, and the next day?' He said, 'Yes.' It said, 'Recite the Verse of the Throne: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer [Qur'an 2:255].' He said: He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him, and he said, 'It spoke the truth, though it is a liar.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5930,"Abu Ayyub al-Ansari had a date-drying yard in a garden in his house."],[5931,"He had a storeroom, and a ghoul used to come and take from it."],[5932,"Abu Ayyub came to Mu'awiya and mentioned a need to him. He said, 'Are you not the companion of 'Uthman?' He said, 'Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that after him we would experience selfishness.' He said, 'And what did he command you?' He said, 'He commanded us to be patient until we meet him at the Pond.' He said, 'Then be patient.' Abu Ayyub became angry and swore never to speak to him again. Then Abu Ayyub came to 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas and mentioned this to him, and he left his house for him just as Abu Ayyub had left his house for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and said, 'What do you want?' He said, 'Four young slaves to be in my place.' He said, 'You have from me twenty slaves.'"],[5933,"And he said, 'I will surely do for you as I did for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' And he said, 'How much debt do you owe?' He said, 'Twenty thousand.' He said, 'Then he gave him forty thousand and twenty slaves, and said, 'You may have what is in the house.'' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5934,"Abu Ayyub was in a gathering saying, 'Can any of you recite a third of the Qur'an?' Then the Prophet ﷺ came to them and heard Abu Ayyub, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Abu Ayyub has spoken the truth.'"],[5935,"I heard Jabir b. Samura say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with Abu Ayyub, and when he ate food, he would send him the leftovers. Abu Ayyub would look at the place where the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ hand had been and eat from where his hand had been. One day he made food containing garlic and sent it to him, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it. Abu Ayyub came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not see the traces of your fingers.' He said, 'It had garlic in it.' Shu'ba said in his narration: 'Is it forbidden?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No.' Hammad said in his narration: 'O Messenger of Allah, you sent back to me what you did not eat.' He said, 'You are not like me; the angel comes to me.'"],[5936,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me, I said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom, I dislike being above you while you are below me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'It is more comfortable for me to be on the lower floor because of the people coming to us.' He said: I saw a jar of ours break and its water spill, so I and Umm Ayyub stood with a velvet cloth of ours—we had no other blanket—drying the water with it, fearing that something harmful might reach the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5937,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me for a month, and I observed his every action. I saw him, when the sun set or moved away, reject worldly possessions if they were in his hands, and if he was sleeping, he would be awakened and stand up to perform ablution and pray. Then he would perform four units of prayer, perfecting and beautifying them. When he intended to depart, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, you stayed with me for a month, and I wished that you stayed longer. So, I observed your every action, and I saw you, when the sun set or moved away, reject worldly possessions if they were in your hands and focus on prayer.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, the gates of heaven are opened at that hour. So, do not miss the opportunity to have the gates of heaven and the gates of Paradise opened for you until you perform this prayer.\" He then said, \"I loved to ascend to my Lord in those hours, as it is better and my actions would be raised at the beginning of the actions of the worshippers.\" [This hadith has been narrated by Al-Dhahabi, who excluded it from the summarization as it is considered weak.]"],[5938,"Abu Ayyub Khalid b. Zayd, in whose house the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had stayed, went on a campaign to the land of the Romans. He passed by Mu'awiya, and Mu'awiya treated him harshly. Then he returned from his campaign, and Mu'awiya treated him harshly and did not raise his head to him. Abu Ayyub said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ informed us that after him we would see selfishness.' Mu'awiya said, 'And what did he command you?' He said, 'He commanded us to be patient.' He said, 'Then be patient.' So he came to 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas in Basra, whom 'Ali, ؓ , had appointed over it, and said, 'O Abu Ayyub, I want to leave my dwelling for you as you left yours for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He ordered his family, and they left, and he gave him everything that was in the house. When it was time for his departure, he said, 'Your need?' He said, 'My need is my stipend and eight slaves to work on my land.' His stipend was four thousand, and he multiplied it for him five times, giving him twenty thousand and forty slaves. 'This hadith has already been mentioned with a connected, authentic chain, and I repeated it for the additions in it with this chain.' It has already been mentioned with an authentic chain."],[5939,"I never prayed behind your Prophet ﷺ except that I heard him, when he finished his prayer, say: 'O Allah, forgive me my errors and all my sins; bless me, give me life, provide for me, and guide me to righteous deeds and character, for none guides to its righteousness but You, and none turns away its evil but You.' Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[5940,"He took something from the beard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'May no harm come to you, O Abu Ayyub.'"],[5941,"'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas and al-Miswar b. Makhrama differed about a person in ihram washing his head with water without being in a state of major ritual impurity. They sent me to Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who was at some of the waters of Makkah, to ask him about that."],[5942,"Al-Tufayl b. 'Abd Allah, the nephew of 'A'isha, said to her mother that he saw in a dream that he met a group of Christians and said, 'You would be the best people if you did not claim that the Messiah is the son of God.' They said, 'And you would be the best people if you did not say, \"Whatever God wills and whatever Muhammad wills.\"' He said: Then he met some Jews and said, 'You would be the best people if you did not claim that 'Uzayr is the son of God.' They said, 'And you would be the best people if you did not say, \"Whatever God wills and whatever Muhammad wills.\"' So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'Have you told anyone about this?' He said, 'Yes.' Then he praised God and extolled Him, and said, 'Your brother has seen what has reached you, so do not say, \"Whatever God wills and whatever Muhammad wills,\" but say, \"Whatever God alone wills, He has no partner.\"'"],[5943,"I saw in what the sleeper sees, then he mentioned the hadith exactly like it: \"This is more worthy of being the preserved version than the first.\""],[5944,"\"Nubayshah b. Abdullah b. Shayban b. Attab b. al-Harith b. Husayn b. al-Harith b. Abd al-Uzza, and he is Nubayshah al-Khayr, whose kunyah is Abu Tarif; he settled in Basra.\""],[5945,"Nubayshah entered upon us, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had named him Nubayshah al-Khayr. He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he had captives, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, either you show them favor or you ransom them.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You have commanded what is good; you are Nubayshah al-Khayr after that.\""],[5946,"\"And Abu Ayyub is Khalid b. Zayd b. Kulayb b. Tha'labah b. Abd Awf, from the Banu Tamim b. Malik b. al-Najjar. He was present at al-Aqabah, Badr, and all the battles, and the conquests of Iraq. He was present with Ali at Siffin, then went to Syria and entered the land of the Byzantines as a raider and camped at Constantinople.\""],[5947,"Abu Ayyub al-Azdi passed by Muawiyah."],[5948,"\"And Jarir b. Abdullah b. Malik b. Nasr b. Tha'labah b. Jusham b. Awf b. Shulayl b. Khuzaymah b. Sakan b. Ali b. Malik b. Zayd b. Qays b. Abqar b. Anmar. He had stayed during the fitnah at Qarqisiya, then moved from there to Kufa, and died there in the year fifty-one.\""],[5949,"\"Abu Musa al-Ashari is Abdullah b. Qays, an ally of the family of Utbah b. Rabiah b. Abd Shams.\""],[5950,"\"Abu Musa al-Ashari's name is Abdullah b. Qays b. Sulaym b. Haddar b. Hurayth b. Amir b. Bakr b. Amir b. Udhrah b. Wa'il b. Najiyah b. al-Muhajir b. al-Ashari, and he is Nabt b. Udad b. Yashjub b. Ya'rub b. Qahtan. Abu Musa's mother was Taybah bt. Wahb b. Atik; she had become Muslim and died in Madinah. Abu Musa had come to Makkah and allied himself with Abu Uhayhah Said b. al-As, became Muslim in Makkah, migrated to the land of Abyssinia, then came with the people of the two ships while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at Khaybar.\""],[5951,"\"Abu Musa al-Ashari was among those who migrated to the land of Abyssinia and remained there until the Prophet ﷺ sent Amr b. Umayyah al-Damri to the Negus, and he carried them in two ships and brought them to him at Khaybar after al-Hudaybiyyah.\""],[5952,"\"A man of light body, short, and small.\""],[5953,"Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari died in the year fifty-two when he was sixty-three years old."],[5954,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say, \"Abu Musa al-Ashari's name is Abdullah b. Qays.\""],[5955,"\"Abu Musa al-Ashari came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ supplicated for the oldest of the people of the ship and the youngest of them.\" Abu Amir al-Ashari said, \"I am the oldest of the people of the ship, and my son is the youngest of them.\" Said said, \"Among them were Abu Amir, Abu Malik, Abu Musa, and Ka'b b. Asim; I think they went out via al-Abwa'.\""],[5956,"I heard Al-Sha'bi saying, \"The judges among the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were six individuals; three in Al-Madinah and three in Al-Kufa. In Al-Madinah, they were Umar, Ubay ibn Ka'b, and Zaid ibn Thabit. In Al-Kufa, they were Ali, Abdullah, and Abu Musa.\" Al-Shaybani said, \"So I asked Al-Sha'bi, 'Is Abu Musa included with them?' He said, 'He was one of the scholars.' Then Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Abbas ibn Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Asim al-Shahidi narrated it to me.\""],[5957,"The knowledge of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ culminated in these persons: Umar b. al-Khattab, Ali b. Abi Talib, Abdullah b. Masud, Ubayy b. Kab, Muadh b. Jabal, Zayd b. Thabit, Abu al-Darda, and Abu Musa al-Ashari."],[5958,"Abu Musa al-Ashari addressed us saying: “By Allah, if you obey Allah outwardly and Abdullah b. Qays secondly, I will surely carry you upon the way.”"],[5959,"No rider ever came to al-Basra better for its people than Abu Musa al-Ashari."],[5960,"Indeed Ali was the first to embrace Islam along with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5961,"Regarding the Prophet ﷺ , Ibn Abbas wrote to him asking about it. Al-Ash'ari wrote to him, \"Indeed, you are a man of your time, and I have not heard anything from the Prophet ﷺ about it except that I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he wanted to urinate. He stood up and urinated against a wall there and said, 'Indeed, the Children of Israel used to collect their urine with a qarad (vessel). So, when one of you wants to urinate, let him turn away from his urine.'\""],[5962,"I witnessed Abu Musa al-Ashari, Ammar b. Yasir, and Abu Masud al-Badri. I heard Abu Musa and Abu Masud say to Ammar: “We have not seen from you in Islam a matter more hateful to us than your hastening in this affair.” Ammar said: “And I have not seen from either of you since you embraced Islam a matter more hateful to me than your tardiness concerning it.” Then they all went out to the mosque together."],[5963,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by Abu Musa one night while Aisha was with him, and Abu Musa was reciting. They stopped and listened to his recitation, then moved on. When morning came, Abu Musa came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said: “I passed by you, O Abu Musa, last night while you were reciting, and we listened to your recitation.” Abu Musa said: “O Prophet of Allah, had I known you were there, I would have embellished it for you beautifully.”"],[5964,"“Is our Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, our emigration with him, our jihad with him, and our deeds with him to be returned to us? And that every deed we did after him we escaped from it equally, head for head.” Your father said to my father: “No? By Allah, we indeed strove after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, prayed, fasted, and did much good, and we hope for that.” He said: My father said to your father: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I would love that it be returned to me, and that everything after that we escaped from it head for head.” He said: I said: Indeed your father is better than my father."],[5965,"The Prophet ﷺ appointed Abu Musa over the naval expedition. While it was sailing with them at night, a caller from above called out to them: “Shall I not inform you of a decree Allah has ordained upon Himself? Whoever thirsts for Allah on a hot day, it is binding upon Allah to give him drink on the Day of the greatest thirst.”"],[5966,"Muawiya appointed Uqba b. Amir al-Juhani over Egypt after the death of his brother Utba b. Abi Sufyan, and that was in the year forty-four, and Muawiya led the pilgrimage that year."],[5967,"Uqba b. Amir al-Juhani was given the kunya Abu Amr. He died in the year fifty-two."],[5968,"I passed by people who had gathered around an old man while he was narrating. They made way for me, and behold, an old man was narrating, saying: “O people, three things among you are a trust. Whoever preserves them is a believer, and whoever does not preserve them is not a believer: if he says, 'I prayed,' but did not pray; 'I fasted,' but did not fast; and 'I performed ghusl from janaba,' but did not perform ghusl.” He said: Then someone to my right said: “Who is this?” He said: “Uqba b. Amir al-Juhani, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[5969,"Ziyad sent me to Hujr bin 'Adi, and it is said [that he was known as] Ibn al-Adbar. He refused to come to him. Then he sent me again a second time, and he still refused to come to him. He [Ziyad] said, so he sent to him: \"I warn you not to embark on the ends of affairs, for those who embarked on their beginnings have perished.\"[1]"],[5970,"I saw Hujr b. al-Adbar when Ziyad sent him to Muawiya, with his legs on one side while he was on a camel."],[5971,"Hujr b. 'Adi al-Kindi, whose kunya was Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, had come as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ and was present at al-Qadisiyya, and was present at the Camel and Siffin with 'Ali. Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan killed him at Marj 'Adhra'. He had two sons, 'Abd Allah and 'Abd al-Rahman; Mus'ab b. al-Zubayr killed them both in retaliation, and Hujr was killed in the year 53."],[5972,"When it was the nights of Hujr's dispatch to Mu'awiya, the people began to be bewildered and say, 'What has Hujr done?' News of him reached Ibn 'Umar while he was hiding in the market, so he loosened his garment and jumped up and departed, and I began to hear his weeping as he turned away."],[5973,"I saw Hujr b. 'Adi saying, 'Indeed I am upon my pledge of allegiance; I will not revoke it nor seek to be released from it, as Allah and the people hear.'"],[5974,"When Ziyad sent Hujr b. 'Adi to Mu'awiya, Mu'awiya ordered his imprisonment at a place called Marj 'Adhra'. Then he consulted the people concerning him. He said, 'They began to say, \"Killing, killing.\"' He said, 'Then 'Abd Allah b. Zayd b. Asad al-Bajali stood up and said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, you are our shepherd and we are your flock; you are our pillar and we are your supports. If you punish, we say you have acted rightly, and if you pardon, we say you have done well. Pardon is closer to piety, and every shepherd is responsible for his flock.\"' He said, 'So the people dispersed after his statement.'"],[5975,"Hadiya b. Fayyad al-A'war ordered the killing of Hujr b. 'Adi, so he walked to him with a sword, and his sides trembled. He said, 'O Hujr, did you not claim that you would not show fear of death? We will leave you.' He said, 'Why would I not show fear when I see a dug grave, a spread shroud, and an unsheathed sword? But by Allah, I will never say what displeases the Lord.' He said, 'Then he killed him, and that was in Sha'ban of the year 51.'"],[5976,"Do not wash blood from me, and do not release my shackle, and bury me in my clothes, for we will meet tomorrow on the main road."],[5977,"Jarir never came as a delegate but I came with him, and he never entered upon Mu'awiya but I entered with him, and we never entered upon him except that he mentioned the killing of Hujr b. 'Adi."],[5978,"Ziyad prolonged the sermon, so Hujr b. 'Adi said, 'The prayer!' He continued in his sermon, so he said to him, 'The prayer!' and struck his hand toward the pebbles, and the people struck their hands toward the pebbles. So he descended and prayed, then he wrote to Mu'awiya about him, and Mu'awiya wrote: 'Send him to me.' So he sent him to him. When he came before him, he said, 'Peace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful.' He said, 'Am I the Commander of the Faithful? I will not release you nor seek your release.' Then he ordered his killing. When they took him, he asked them to let him pray two rak'as, so they allowed him, and he prayed two rak'as. Then he said, 'Do not release iron from me, do not wash blood from me, and bury me in my clothes, for I will be a disputant.' He said, 'Then he was killed.'"],[5979,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed them and said, 'What day is this?' They said, 'A sacred day.' He said, 'What land is this?' They said, 'The sacred land.' He said, 'What month?' They said, 'A sacred month.' He said, 'Indeed your blood, your wealth, and your honor are inviolable to you like the sanctity of this day of yours, like the sanctity of this month of yours, like the sanctity of this land of yours. Let the one present convey to the absent. Do not return after me as disbelievers, striking one another's necks.'"],[5980,"I heard Ibrahim ibn Ya'qub saying, \"Hudhur ibn 'Adiyy lived during the era of ignorance (pre-Islamic era) and he consumed blood while doing so. Then he accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and heard from him, and witnessed battles alongside 'Ali ibn Abi Talib; such as the battles of Jamala and Siffin. He was killed in the allegiance to Ali.\""],[5981,"\"I entered with Muawiyah to the Mother of the Believers, Aisha, and she said, 'O Muawiyah, you killed someone and his companions, and you did what you did.' And she mentioned the whole incident in detail.\""],[5982,"Ziyad said to 'Imran b. Husayn, 'O Abu Nujayd.'"],[5983,"'Imran b. Husayn b. 'Ubayd b. Khalaf b. 'Abd Nahm b. Huzma b. Jahma b. Ghadira, whose kunya was Abu Nujayd, accepted Islam early, he and his father and his sister, and he went on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ several times. He remained in the lands of his people, then he moved to al-Basra and settled there until he died there, and his children were there. 'Imran b. al-Husayn died in al-Basra one year before Ziyad, and Ziyad died in the year 55."],[5984,"Abu Nujayd 'Imran b. al-Husayn b. Khalaf b. 'Abd Nahm al-Khuza'i died in al-Basra in the year 52."],[5985,"I went to Basra and entered the mosque, and there was an old man leaning against a pillar, narrating. He was saying: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come people who give testimony before they are asked for it.\" I said: Who is this old man? They said: Imran ibn Husain."],[5986,"Ziyad, or some other governor, sent Imran ibn Husayn to collect sadaqah (i.e. zakat). When he returned, he asked Imran: Where is the property? He replied: Did you send me to bring the property? We collected it from where we used to collect in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we spent it where we used to spend during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1625)"],[5987,"Imran ibn al-Husain was among the most diligent of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in worship. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5988,"No one among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ who came to Basra surpassed Imran ibn Husain. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[5989,"We set out with Imran ibn al-Husain from Basra to Kufa, and not a day passed but he composed poetry."],[5990,"A she-camel belonging to Nujayd ibn Imran ibn Husain kicked while Imran was ill, and it hurt him, so Imran cursed it. Nujayd went out exclaiming 'Indeed we belong to Allah' and his she-camel pleased him. It was said to him: What is the matter with you? He said: Abu Nujayd cursed my she-camel, and it was not long before its neck broke."],[5991,"Know, O Mutarrif, that the angels used to greet me at my head, at the House, and at the door of the Hijr. But when I cauterized myself, that ceased. When he recovered, he spoke to him, saying: Know, O Mutarrif, that what I used to miss has returned to me. Keep it secret about me, O Mutarrif, until I die."],[5992,"I have not touched my private part with my right hand since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[5993,"A man came to Imran ibn Husain while he was in the mosque and said: A man divorced his wife three times in one sitting. He said: A sin has attached to him and his wife has become forbidden to him. The man went and mentioned that to Abu Musa, intending to find fault with him. Abu Musa said: May Allah increase among us the like of Abu Nujayd."],[5994,"And it is said: a year after it."],[5995,"[meter: al-bahr al-basit] May God bless a grave and purify it, near al-Thawiyya, watered above it by al-mawr. Quraysh escorted to it the bier of its master, for generosity and prudence are buried in it today. O Abu al-Mughira, the world is stricken with grief, and among the deceived by the world's splendor is the deceived one. You had knowledge of what is good, and you had rejection of what is evil. You used to visit and give wealth out of abundance, even if your door became blocked and inaccessible. After you, people's minds have become light, as if sparrows were woven into them."],[5996,"The name of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq in the pre-Islamic era was Abd al-Uzza, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Abd al-Rahman."],[5997,"Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr was given the kunya Abu Abd Allah, and it is said Abu Muhammad. His mother was Umm A'isha, Umm Ruman bt. Amir ibn Uwaymir ibn Abd Shams ibn Abd Manaf. Umm Ruman embraced Islam and her Islam was good."],[5998,"I heard Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah say: The name of Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr was Abd al-Uzza, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Abdur-Rahman. He was given the kunya Abu Muhammad. He witnessed the conquest of Damascus, and Umar gave him Layla bt. al-Judi as spoils when Damascus was conquered, for he was in love with her."],[5999,"They set out to Syria in a caravan from the people of Makkah to procure provisions. They came to a woman called Layla, and they saw her appearance and beauty. Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr returned while he was courting her in verse: [al-tawil meter] I remembered Layla while al-Samawah lay between us. What is it to me about the daughter of al-Judi, Layla, and what is mine? I would give a Harithi kiss that settles in Busra or settles in al-Jawabiya. When it was the time of Khalid b. al-Walid and he conquered Syria, they captured her among the captives. Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr spoke to Khalid about her, so Khalid wrote to Abu Bakr about it, and Abu Bakr wrote that they should give her to him."],[6000,"Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr was among a group of young men of Quraysh who emigrated to the Prophet ﷺ before the conquest."],[6001,"Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq remained upon the religion of his people in idolatry until he witnessed Badr with the polytheists. He called for single combat, and his father Abu Bakr rose to duel him, but it is mentioned that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: “Spare us yourself.”"],[6002,"Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr said to Abu Bakr: “I saw you on the day of Uhud and turned away from you.” Abu Bakr said: “But if I had seen you, I would not have turned away from you.”"],[6003,"Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr died suddenly, and his kunya was Abu Abdullah. He died in the year 53."],[6004,"“May Allah have mercy on my brother. The greatest thing I find in my soul is that he was not buried where he died.” She said: Her brother had died in Abyssinia, so a group of Quraysh went out to him and carried him to the upper part of Makkah."],[6005,"We know of no four in Islam who met the Prophet ﷺ, the fathers together with the sons, except Abu Quhafa, Abu Bakr, Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, and his son Abu Atiq Muhammad b. Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr."],[6006,"Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq died suddenly."],[6007,"No lie was ever attached to Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr in Islam."],[6008,"A woman entered Aisha’s house and prayed near the Prophet’s ﷺ chamber while she was healthy. She prostrated and did not raise her head until she died. Aisha said: “Praise be to Allah who gives life and causes death. In this there is a lesson for me regarding Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr. He slept in a noon resting place of his, and they went to wake him and found that he had died.” Into Aisha’s soul came the suspicion that some evil had been done to him and that he had been hastened upon and buried while still alive. She saw that this was a lesson for her, and what was in her soul about that departed."],[6009,"Abdur-Rahman b. Abi Bakr died in the year 53 and witnessed the Battle of the Camel with his sister Aisha, and he came to Ibn Amir in Basra."],[6010,"And she said [in the meter al-Tawil]: “We were like the two cup-companions of Jadhima for a long span of time, until it was said they would never part. But when we separated, it was as if I and Malik, despite our long togetherness, had not spent a single night together.” Then she returned to Makkah and said, “By Allah, had I witnessed you, I would have buried you where you died.”"],[6011,"“No lie ever clung to Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr in Islam.”"],[6012,"And he said, “I sell my religion for my worldly life,” and he went out to Makkah until he died there. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6013,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Bring me an inkpot and a shoulder blade so that I may write for you a document after which you will never go astray.” Then he turned his back to us, then he faced us and said, “Allah and the believers refuse anyone but Abu Bakr.” Its chain is sahih."],[6014,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him, “Take your sister A’ishah behind you and let her perform Umrah from al-Tan’im. When she descends the hill, tell her to enter ihram, for it is an accepted Umrah.” Its chain is strong."],[6015,"“And on the day of al-Ta’if, among the Muslims from Banu Taym b. Murrah, Abdullah b. Abi Bakr was killed. He was struck by an arrow and died fifty days after that.”"],[6016,"“The one who used to bring food to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr in the cave was Abdullah b. Abi Bakr.”"],[6017,"“Abdullah b. Abi Bakr died in the same year in which Fatimah died, after the passing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[6018,"Abdullah b. Abi Bakr was struck by an arrow on the day of al-Ta’if, and it reopened his wound forty nights after the passing of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he died. Abu Bakr entered upon A’ishah and said, “O my little daughter, by Allah, it is as if he was taken by the ear of a sheep and brought out of our house.” She said, “Praise be to Allah who bound your heart and gave you resolve to follow right guidance.” He went out, then entered and said, “O my little daughter, do you fear that you have buried Abdullah while he was alive?” She said, “Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return, O my father.” He said, “I seek refuge in Allah, the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing, from Satan the accursed. O my little daughter, there is no one except that he has two promptings: a prompting from an angel and a prompting from Satan.” He said: The delegation of Thaqif came to him, and that arrow had not ceased to concern him, so he brought it out to them and said, “Does any of you recognize this arrow?” Sa’d b. Ubayd, the brother of Banu al-Ajlan, said, “This is an arrow that I shaped, feathered, and notched, and I shot it.” Abu Bakr said, “This arrow is the one that killed Abdullah b. Abi Bakr. Praise be to Allah who honored him by your hand and did not disgrace you by his hand, for He is the One who protects.”"],[6019,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was shrouded in two striped garments that belonged to Abdullah b. Abi Bakr, and he was wrapped in them, then they were removed from him.” Abdullah b. Abi Bakr had kept that shroud for himself so that he might be shrouded in it when he died. Then after he had kept it, he said, “I would not keep for myself something that Allah withheld from His Messenger ﷺ to be shrouded in,” so Abdullah gave it as charity. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6020,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When a Muslim man reaches forty years, Allah turns away from him three types of affliction: insanity, leprosy, and vitiligo. When he reaches fifty years, Allah forgives his sins, the earlier and the later, and he becomes a prisoner of Allah on earth and an intercessor for his household on the Day of Resurrection.” Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis due to its weakness."],[6021,"“We do not know of four in Islam who attained the Prophet ﷺ with fathers along with sons except Abu Quhafah, Abu Bakr, Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr, and Abu Atiq Muhammad b. Abd al-Rahman.”"],[6022,"He was called 'the gold-drinker.' His mother was Hind bt. al-Harith from Banu Ghanm b. Malik b. 'Abd Manat b. 'Ali b. Lubanah. Al-Muhajir came to Basra and died there."],[6023,"\"I passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was performing ablution, and I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting.\" When he finished, he returned it to me and apologized to me, saying, \"Nothing prevented me from returning your greeting except that I disliked mentioning Allah, the Exalted, while I was not in a state of purity.\""],[6024,"And his forefathers were called al-Qawaqil. He had entered the state of ihram from Syria when the Prophet ﷺ set out for Hudaybiyyah, intending 'umrah. His arrival coincided with the Prophet's departure, so he went out with him. Ka'b b. 'Ujrah was an ally of Banu 'Awf b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj.\""],[6025,"From his father: I said, 'O Abu Muhammad, what did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command you at the time of Hudaybiyyah regarding your ihram?' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Shave, shave.\"'"],[6026,"\"Ka'b b. 'Ujrah died in Madinah in the year fifty-two, and he was then seventy-five years old.\""],[6027,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Ka'b b. 'Ujrah: \"O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, I seek refuge for you with Allah from the rule of the foolish.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the rule of the foolish?\" He said, \"Rulers who will come after me. Whoever enters upon them, believes their lies, and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me, and I am not of him, and he will never come to me at the Pond.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6028,"And some of them said: 'Amr b. Rib'i. He witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and the subsequent expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6029,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with me on the day of Dhu Qarad and looked at me, then said, \"O Allah, bless him in his hair and his skin,\" and said, \"May your face prosper.\" I said, \"And your face, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Was Mas'adah killed?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then what is this on your face?\" I said, \"An arrow that struck me, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Come closer.\" So I drew near to him, and he spat on it, and it never hurt me afterwards, nor did it fester."],[6030,"\"Abu Qatadah b. Rib'i, one of Banu Salamah, died in Madinah in fifty-four, and he was seventy years old.\""],[6031,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: \"Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, is Abu 'Abd Allah.\""],[6032,"\"Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was originally from Yemen. He was taken captive, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set him free. His kunyah is Abu 'Abd Allah. He died in Homs in the year fifty-four.\""],[6033,"\"And from what reached us regarding the news of Hims, and from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and from the allies of Quraysh, Thawban ibn Budjdud, who was also known as Abu Abdullah, was a man from the Alhân tribe. He was captured as a prisoner, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set him free and said to him: 'Oh Thawban, if you wish to join those whom you were with, then you are one of them. And if you wish to remain with us, the household of the Messenger of Allah, upon the allegiance to the Messenger of Allah.' Thawban responded: 'Rather, I will remain on the allegiance to the Messenger of Allah.' He then passed away in Hims during the reign of Abdullah ibn Qurt.\""],[6034,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"If you swear to do a sin, then abandon it. Cast the grudges of the Jahiliyyah beneath your feet. And beware of drinking wine, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, does not sanctify the one who drinks it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6035,"Supplication repels the divine decree, righteousness increases provision, and a servant is deprived of provision because of a sin he commits."],[6036,"Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to me: I was standing before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a scholar from among the Jewish rabbis came to him and said, \"Peace be upon you, O Muhammad.\" I pushed him with a shove that almost knocked him down. He said, \"Why do you push me?\" I said, \"Why do you not say, 'O Messenger of Allah'?\" The Jew said, \"We call him by the name his family gave him.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"My name, which my family gave me, is Muhammad.\" The Jew said, \"I have come to ask you.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Will it benefit you if I tell you?\" He said, \"I will listen with my ears.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ scratched the ground with a stick he had and said, \"Ask.\" The Jew said, \"Where will the people be on the Day when the earth is changed to another earth and the heavens too?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"In darkness, before the gathering.\" He said, \"Who will be the first of the people to pass?\" He said, \"The poor among the emigrants.\" He said, \"What will be their gift when they enter Paradise?\" He said, \"An extra portion of the liver of the whale.\" He said, \"What will be their food after that?\" He said, \"The bull of Paradise, which ate from its outskirts, will be slaughtered for them.\" He said, \"What will be their drink with it?\" He said, \"A river called Salsabil.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth. It is according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim.\""],[6037,"I heard Ibrahim b. al-Mundhir al-Hizami say: \"Hakim b. Hizam b. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy, whose kunya was Abu Khalid, died in the year fifty-four at the age of one hundred and twenty years. He was born thirteen years before the Year of the Elephant and died in Madinah.\""],[6038,"I heard 'Ali b. Ghannam al-'Amiri say: \"Hakim b. Hizam was born inside the Ka'bah. His mother entered the Ka'bah, went into labor there, and gave birth in the House.\""],[6039,"Abu Khalid Hakim b. Hizam died in the year sixty at the age of one hundred and twenty years."],[6040,"That he intended to slaughter his son 'Abd Allah, and that was five years before the birth of the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6042,"The translation of the passage is: \"Hakim bin Hizam did not accept anything from Abu Bakr until he passed away, nor from Umar until he passed away, nor from Uthman, nor from Muawiyah until he died.\""],[6043,"I freed forty slaves in the pre-Islamic era. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, 'Is there any reward for me in them?' He said, 'You accepted Islam with the good you had previously done.' It is authentic according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[6044,"I said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Do you think that any good I did in the pre-Islamic era, by which I sought closeness to God, will earn me any reward?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'You accepted Islam with the reward of what you had previously done.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6045,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he gave me, and I persisted in asking him. He said, 'I do not disapprove of your asking, O Hakim. This wealth is green and sweet. It is but the dirt of people's hands. The hand of Allah is above the hand of the giver, and the hand of the giver is above the hand of the asker, and the hand of the asker is the lowest of hands.'"],[6046,"On the day of Badr, I saw that a mist from the sky had fallen into the valley and filled the horizon. Then the valley flowed with water. It occurred to me that this was something from the sky with which Muhammad ﷺ was supported. It was nothing but the defeat, and it was the angels. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6047,"Muhammad the Prophet was the most beloved of people to me in the pre-Islamic era. When he became a prophet and went out to Madinah, Hakim b. Hizam went out to the market of 'Ukaz and found a suit of clothing belonging to Dhu Yazan being sold for fifty dirhams. He bought it to give as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He brought it to him and wanted him to accept it, but he refused. 'Ubayd Allah said: I think he said, 'We do not accept anything from the polytheists, but we will take it for a price.' So I sold it to him until he came to Madinah. He wore it, and I saw it on him on the pulpit. I never saw anything more beautiful than him in it that day. Then he gave it to Usamah b. Zayd. Hakim saw it on Usamah and said, 'O Usamah, are you wearing the suit of Dhu Yazan?' He said, 'Yes, for I am better than Dhu Yazan, and my father is better than his father, and my mother is better than his mother.' Hakim said, 'So I went to Makkah and amazed them with Usamah's words.'"],[6048,"When the Prophet ﷺ sent him as governor to Yemen, he said, 'Do not touch the Qur'an unless you are in a state of purity.'"],[6049,"From Dawud b. al-Husayn, regarding those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia in the second emigration: Khalid b. Hizam, a snake bit him on the road and he died."],[6050,"From 'Urwah and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Abd al-Qari, that they both heard 'Umar b. al-Khattab say: I passed by Hisham b. Hakim b. Hizam while he was reciting Surah al-Baqarah during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—the full hadith. He said: 'According to the arrangement of this book, the mention of Khalid b. Hizam should come before Hakim, and the mention of Hisham b. Hakim should come after the two of them, but I gathered them in this place at the mention of Hakim so that it would be closer to the understanding of the seeker of benefit.'"],[6051,"Hassan b. Thabit lived sixty years in the Jahiliyyah—his kunyah was Abu al-Walid—and sixty years in Islam. He was Hassan b. Thabit b. al-Mundhir b. Haram b. 'Amr b. Zayd Manat b. 'Adi b. 'Amr b. Malik b. al-Najjar, the poet of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Hassan's mother was al-Furay'ah bt. Khalid b. Khunays b. Lawdhan b. 'Abd Wadd. It is said that he died before the age of forty, and it is said he died in the year fifty-five."],[6052,"I came to Hassan and said, 'O Abu al-Husam.'"],[6053,"By Allah, I was a young boy, seven or eight years old, understanding what I heard, when I heard a Jew on the elevated fortress of Yathrib crying out, 'O assembly of Jews!' When they gathered, they said, 'Woe to you! What is the matter with you?' He said, 'The star of the one who is to be sent tonight has risen.'"],[6054,"And if a man seeks his worldly life desirously, he clings to a rope of deception from it."],[6055,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would place a pulpit in the mosque for Hassan, upon which he would stand, boasting on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say, 'Indeed, Allah supports Hassan with the Holy Spirit as long as he defends or boasts on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[6056,"From the Prophet ﷺ something similar to it."],[6057,"Indeed, my father and my mother and my honor are a protection for the honor of Muhammad from you."],[6058,"I saw Hassan b. Thabit with a forelock that he had tied between his eyes."],[6059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Hassaan ibn Thabit, \"Indeed, the Holy Spirit is with you whenever you confront them.\""],[6060,"Hassan b. Thabit asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to satirize the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What about my lineage among them?' Hassan said, 'I will draw you out from them as a hair is drawn out from dough.'"],[6061,"'Abd Allah b. Rawahah and Hassan b. Thabit came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Ta-Sin-Mim, the poets, was revealed, weeping while he recited to them, 'And the poets—the deviators follow them,' until he reached, 'and did righteous deeds.' He said, 'You.' 'And remembered Allah often.' He said, 'You.' 'And defended themselves after they were wronged.' He said, 'You.'"],[6062,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was approached and it was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Muttalib is satirizing you.\" Ibn Rawaha stood up and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, permit me to deal with him.\" He said, \"Are you the one who says, 'May Allah make firm'?\" He said, \"Yes, I said, O Messenger of Allah: [al-bahr al-basit] 'May Allah make firm the good He has given you, as firm as Musa was made firm, and grant victory like the victory they were granted.'\" He said, \"And may Allah do good to you likewise.\" Sahih."],[6063,"Makhrama b. Nawfal b. Uhayb b. 'Abd Manaf, and he was among those whose hearts were to be reconciled."],[6064,"Makhrama b. Nawfal accepted Islam at the conquest of Makkah. He was knowledgeable in the genealogy of Quraysh and its traditions, and he had knowledge of the boundary markers of the Haram. Makhrama's son was Safwan, by whom he was given the kunya, and he was the eldest of his children."],[6065,"I heard Yahya b. 'Abd Allah b. Bukayr say, \"Makhrama b. Nawfal was given the kunya Abu al-Miswar.\""],[6066,"The Prophet ﷺ said to my father, \"O Abu Safwan.\""],[6067,"Makhrama b. Nawfal was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn, and he gave him fifty camels from the spoils of Hunayn. Makhrama died in Madinah in the year fifty-four, and on the day he died he was one hundred and fifteen years old."],[6068,"I heard Sa'id b. 'Uqba say, \"Makhrama b. Nawfal al-Qurashi died at the age of one hundred and fifteen. He had accepted Islam on the day of the conquest, and he was among those whose hearts were to be reconciled.\""],[6069,"Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan said, while 'Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar was with him, \"Who will deal with Makhrama b. Nawfal for me, to give me justice from his tongue's disparagement?\" 'Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar said to him, \"I will suffice you against him.\" That reached Makhrama, and he said, \"'Abd al-Rahman has made me an orphan in his care, claiming by his strength that he can suffice against me.\" Ibn al-Barsa' al-Laythi said to him, \"He is 'Abd al-Rahman b. Azhar.\" So he raised a stick in his hand and struck him, splitting his head, and said, \"Our enemy in the Jahiliyya, and you envy us in Islam, and you come between me and Ibn al-Azhar.\""],[6070,"When death came to Makhrama b. Nawfal, his daughter wept for him and said, \"O father, he was gentle and soft.\" He regained consciousness and said, \"Who is the mourner?\" They said, \"Your daughter.\" He said, \"Come here.\" She came, and he said, \"One like me is not mourned like that. Say: O father, he was an arrow that hit the mark; he was a fortified father.\""],[6071,"Some cloaks were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he distributed them among his companions. My father said to me, \"Come with me to him, for cloaks have come to him.\" My father spoke at the door, and the Prophet ﷺ recognized his voice and came out with a cloak, saying, \"I kept this for you, I kept this for you.\""],[6072,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made Islam public, all the people of Makkah accepted Islam, and that was before prayer was made obligatory, until when he recited the prostration, he could not prostrate until the leaders of Quraysh arrived: al-Walid b. al-Mughira, Abu Jahl b. Hisham, and others. They had been in al-Ta'if on their lands. They said, \"Will you abandon the religion of your forefathers?\" and they disbelieved. Ya'qub b. Sufyan said, \"We do not know of any hadith with a chain from Makhrama b. Nawfal other than this.\""],[6073,"Sa'id b. Yarbu' b. 'Ankatha b. 'Amir b. Makhzum, whose kunya was Abu Hud, accepted Islam on the day of the conquest of Makkah and was present with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Hunayn. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him fifty camels from the spoils of Hunayn."],[6074,"Sa'id b. Yarbu' b. 'Ankatha b. 'Amir al-Makhzumi died in the year fifty-five, and he was one hundred and eighteen years old."],[6075,"From 'Urwa: Among those who gave the pledge to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-'Aqaba from Banu 'Amr b. Sawada was Abu al-Yasar Ka'b b. 'Amr b. 'Abbad b. 'Amr b. Tamim b. Sawwad b. Ghanim b. Ka'b b. Salama, one of the people of Badr. He witnessed al-'Aqaba, and he is the one who captured al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib."],[6076,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: Abu al-Yasar Ka'b b. 'Amr died in the year fifty-five in Madinah, and he was the last of the people of Badr to die."],[6077,"Abu al-Yasar Ka'b b. 'Amr b. 'Abbad b. 'Amr b. Sawwad b. Ghanim b. Ka'b b. Salama b. Sa'd b. Ghanim b. Asad b. Jusham b. al-Khazraj died in the year fifty-five in Madinah."],[6078,"Abu al-Yasar Ka'b b. 'Amr b. 'Abbad b. 'Amr b. Sawwad b. Ghanim b. Ka'b b. Salama b. Ghanim b. Asad b. Jusham b. al-Khazraj."],[6079,"And what are forty thousand dinars to a man who has four dependents?"],[6080,"We were sitting one day in the courtyard of the Ka'ba in the Jahiliyya when a woman came seeking refuge with the Ka'ba from her husband. Her husband came and stretched his hand toward her, and his hand withered. I saw him in Islam, and he was indeed paralyzed."],[6081,"Huwaytib b. 'Abd al-'Uzza lived one hundred and twenty years: sixty in the Jahiliyya and sixty in Islam. When Marwan b. al-Hakam became governor of Madinah in his first year, Huwaytib entered upon him with venerable elders: Hakim b. Hizam and Makhrama b. Nawfal. They conversed in his presence and dispersed. Then Huwaytib entered upon him one day after that and conversed with him. Marwan said to him, 'What is the matter with you?' He told him. Marwan said to him, 'Your acceptance of Islam was delayed, O Shaykh, until the young ones preceded you.' Huwaytib said, 'By Allah, I intended to embrace Islam more than once, but each time your father prevented me and forbade me, saying: Would you abandon the nobility of your people and the religion of your forefathers for a new religion and become its follower?!' He said: So Marwan fell silent and regretted what he had said to him. Then Huwaytib said, 'Did not 'Uthman tell you what he met from your father when he embraced Islam?' Marwan's distress increased. Then Huwaytib said, 'There was no one among the elders of Quraysh who remained upon the religion of their people until Makkah was conquered who was more averse to what it was conquered upon than I, but the decrees [of Allah prevail]. I witnessed Badr with the polytheists and saw a lesson: I saw the angels killing and taking captives between the heaven and the earth. I said: This is a man who is protected. When what I saw at Uhud was mentioned, we fled back to Makkah and stayed there, while Quraysh embraced Islam one man after another. When the day of al-Hudaybiyya came, I attended and witnessed the treaty, and I worked for it until it was completed. All of that while Islam increased, and Allah ﷻ willed only what He willed. When we wrote the treaty of al-Hudaybiyya, I was the last of its witnesses, and I said: Quraysh will see from Muhammad only what displeases her. She has accepted to defend herself with spears. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came for the 'Umra of al-Qada' and Quraysh left Makkah, I was among those who stayed behind in Makkah, I and Suhayl b. 'Amr, so that we might expel the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the time elapsed. When the three days ended, Suhayl b. 'Amr and I approached and said: Your condition has elapsed, so leave our land. He called out: O Bilal, let not the sun set while any Muslim who came with us remains in Makkah.'"],[6082,"Abu Shajara Yazid b. Shajara al-Rahawi, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died in the land of the Romans in the year fifty-eight."],[6083,"\"The swords are the keys of Paradise.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6084,"Yazid b. Shajara al-Rahawi, who was one of the commanders of al-Sham and whom Mu'awiya used to appoint over the armies, delivered a sermon to us one day and said: O people, remember the blessing of Allah upon you. If you could see what I see of black and red and green and white, and in the saddles what is in them: when the prayer is established, the gates of heaven, the gates of Paradise, and the gates of Hell are opened, and the houris are adorned and look forth. When one of them turns his face toward the fighting, they say: O Allah, make him firm; O Allah, grant him victory. When he turns back, they veil themselves from him and say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him. So strike the faces of the enemy, may my father and mother be your ransom. For when one of you advances, the first gush of his blood removes his sins as leaves fall from a tree, and two of the wide-eyed houris descend to him and wipe the dust from his face. He says to them: I am for you, and they say: We are for you. And he is clothed with one hundred garments; if they were placed between these two fingers of mine—meaning the index and middle fingers—they would fit, not of the weaving of the children of Adam but of the garments of Paradise. You are recorded with Allah by your names, your marks, your adornments, your private conversations, and your gatherings. On the Day of Resurrection it will be said: O so-and-so, this is your light; and O so-and-so, you have no light. Hell has a shore like the shore of the sea, in which are creeping creatures and serpents like palm trees and scorpions like mules. When the people of Hell cry out for relief, it is said: Go out to the shore. They go out, and the creeping creatures seize their lips and faces and whatever Allah wills, and they strip them. They cry out, fleeing from them back to the Fire. And mange is inflicted upon them, so that one of them scratches his skin until the bone appears. One of them says: O so-and-so, does this harm you? He says: Yes. He says: That is because you used to harm the believers."],[6085,"Ma'n: It is said he died in Egypt, and it is said in Madinah, in the year sixty. He witnessed Uhud and all the battles. About him Hassan b. Thabit said (in the meter al-bahr al-mutaqarib): \"Indeed this is my maternal uncle; I boast of him, so let every man show me his maternal uncle.\""],[6086,"I prayed behind Maslamah b. Makhlad in Egypt, and he recited al-Baqarah and did not omit a single wāw or alif from it."],[6087,"The Prophet ﷺ was born when he was ten years old."],[6088,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, who am I?” He replied, “You are Saʿd b. Mālik b. Uhayb b. ʿAbd Manāf b. Zuhrah.” He asked, “Who else?” He said, “Anyone who claims otherwise, upon him be the curse of Allah.”"],[6089,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ was appointed over Kufah by ʿUmar and ʿUthmān. His mother was Ḥamnah bt. Abī Sufyān b. Umayyah b. ʿAbd Shams b. ʿAbd Manāf."],[6090,"ʿUmar said to Saʿd, “O Abū Isḥāq.”"],[6091,"I heard that Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ, ʿUmayr, ʿĀmir, and ʿUqbah were brothers, and Abū Waqqāṣ was Mālik b. Uhayb b. ʿAbd Manāf b. al-Ḥārith b. Zuhrah."],[6092,"Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ died during the time of Muʿāwiyah, after his first ḥajj, at the age of eighty-three."],[6093,"Abū Isḥāq Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ died at the age of seventy-five in Madinah, and Marwān b. al-Ḥakam, who was its governor, led his funeral prayer."],[6094,"My father was the last of the Muhājirūn to die."],[6095,"My father was a short, stocky man, thick-set, with a large head and coarse fingers. He was given the kunyah Abū Isḥāq. He died in his palace at al-ʿAqīq, ten miles from Madinah, and was carried to Madinah on the shoulders of men."],[6096,"Saʿd used to dye his hair black."],[6097,"When Saʿd b. Abī Waqqāṣ was near death, he called for an old woolen jubbah of his and said, “Shroud me in it, for I met the polytheists in it on the day of Badr, and I was saving it for this day.”"],[6098,"Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas was the last of the Muhajirun to pass away."],[6099,"Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas was the last of the Muhajirun to pass away."],[6100,"Abu 'Abd Allah: 'Sa'd embraced Islam when he was nineteen years old.'"],[6101,"The mother of Sa'd and the mother of his two brothers 'Umayr and 'Amir was Hamnah bint Abi Sufyan ibn Umayyah ibn 'Abd Shams. 'Umayr was martyred at Badr, and 'Amir was among those who emigrated to Abyssinia. He used to dye his hair with black—meaning Sa'd."],[6102,"My father: 'Sa'd passed away ten miles from Madinah and was carried on the shoulders of men to Madinah, while Marwan was governor over it at that time.'"],[6103,"The sons of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas: 'Umar ibn Sa'd, whom al-Mukhtar ibn Abi 'Ubayd killed; Muhammad ibn Sa'd, whom al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf killed—he was among those taken captive from the companions of 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn al-Ash'ath; their mother was Mariyah bint Qays ibn Ma'di Karib of Kindah. 'Amir ibn Sa'd, whose mother was Bahra'. Salih ibn Sa'd, who settled in al-Hirah because of something that occurred between him and his brother 'Umar ibn Sa'd, and his mother was Khawlah bint 'Umayr ibn Taghlib ibn Wa'il. Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, Ishaq ibn Sa'd, Yahya ibn Sa'd, and 'A'ishah bint Sa'd."],[6104,"'Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas were said to be of the same age.' Ibrahim said: 'They were born in the same year.'"],[6105,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6106,"Sa'd was asked about something or a hadith, and he hesitated, then said: 'I dislike relating to you a hadith to which you would add a hundred.'"],[6107,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except one hadith Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6108,"I embraced Islam on the day I embraced Islam, and Allah had not yet prescribed the prayer."],[6109,"Shall I inform the Messenger of Allah that I protected my companions with the chests of my arrows, driving away their enemy with them, over every rugged terrain and every plain? No archer of Ma'add can count a single arrow shot alongside the Messenger of Allah before me."],[6110,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas approached. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This is my maternal uncle, so let any man show me his maternal uncle.\""],[6111,"\"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas was the first to shed blood in the cause of Allah.\""],[6112,"\"The first to shoot an arrow in the cause of Allah was Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas.\""],[6113,"\"I saw myself as one-third of Islam.\""],[6114,"The Prophet ﷺ sat in the mosque for three nights saying, \"O Allah, admit through this gate a servant who loves You and whom You love.\" Sa'd entered through it."],[6115,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O Allah, answer him when he calls upon You.\""],[6116,"Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas said: [in the perfect meter] I am the son of the one whose supplication is answered and the repairer of the breach for the Chosen One among the Arabs, who guards it for the Prophet, seeking reward, singled out for it above every reward-seeker. The people differed among themselves, but he refused to fight the people of monotheism and the scriptures. May Allah keep him safe; none of them was struck by an arrow then, nor was he struck."],[6117,"\"A man disparaged 'Ali, so Sa'd b. Malik supplicated against him. A she-camel or a camel came to him and killed him. Sa'd then freed a slave and swore never to supplicate against anyone again.\""],[6118,"\"Why do you insult Ali ibn Abi Talib? Wasn't he the first to embrace Islam? Wasn't he the first to pray with the Messenger of Allah? Wasn't he the most ascetic of people? Wasn't he the most knowledgeable of people?\" He continued, saying, \"Wasn't he the one whom the Messenger of Allah circumcised his daughter? Wasn't he the companion of the Messenger of Allah in his expeditions?\" Then he turned towards the Qibla and raised his hands and said, \"O Allah, this person insults one of Your close allies, so do not disperse this gathering until You show them Your power.\" Qays said, \"By Allah, we did not disperse until his beast screamed and threw him upon his forehead in those rocks, and his brain split and he died.\""],[6119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O Allah, make his arrow hit the mark and answer his supplication.\""],[6120,"I was sitting with Sa'd when a man called al-Harith b. Barsa' came while he was in the market. He said to him, \"O Abu Ishaq, I was just now with Marwan, and I heard him saying, 'This wealth is our wealth; we give it to whomever we wish.'\" He said, \"Sa'd raised his hand and said, 'Shall I supplicate?' Marwan jumped up from his couch, embraced him, and said, 'I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Ishaq, not to supplicate, for it is only Allah's wealth.'\""],[6121,"Al-Harith b. al-Barsa' came while he was in the market and said to him, \"O Abu Ishaq, I heard Marwan claiming that Allah's wealth is his wealth; he gives it to whomever he wishes and withholds it from whomever he wishes.\" He said to him, \"Did you hear him say that?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Sa'id said, \"Sa'd took me by the hand and al-Harith by the hand until he entered upon Marwan and said, 'O Marwan, do you claim that Allah's wealth is your wealth; you give it to whomever you wish and withhold it from whomever you wish?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'Then I shall supplicate,' and Sa'd raised his hands. Marwan jumped up to him and said, 'I adjure you by Allah not to supplicate. It is Allah's wealth; He gives it to whomever He wishes and withholds it from whomever He wishes.'\""],[6122,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had insomnia one night and said, \"Would that a man from my companions guard me tonight.\" She said, \"We heard the sound of weapons. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Who is this?' Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas said, 'It is I, O Messenger of Allah; I have come to guard you.'\" 'A'ishah said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then slept until I heard his snoring.\""],[6123,"When the first fitna came, it became problematic for me. I said, 'O Allah, show me from the truth a matter I can hold onto.' Then I saw in a dream the world and the Hereafter, and between them was a wall, not tall, and I was beneath it. I said, 'If I climb this wall until I can look at the bravest of the dead, they will inform me.' He said: 'I was brought down to a land with trees, and there was a group of people sitting. I said, \"Are you the martyrs?\" They said, \"We are the angels.\" I said, \"Where are the martyrs?\" They said, \"Go forward to the ranks.\" So I ascended a rank, Allah knows best its beauty and vastness, and there I was with Muhammad ﷺ, and Ibrahim was an old man, and he was saying to Ibrahim, \"Seek forgiveness for my nation,\" and Ibrahim was saying, \"You do not know what they innovated after you; they shed their blood and killed their imam. Why did they not do as Sa'd, my friend, did?\" I said, \"By Allah, I have seen a dream; perhaps Allah will benefit me by it. I will go and look for Sa'd's position and be with him.\" So I came to Sa'd and told him the story. He said: 'He was not overjoyed by it.' And he said, 'Whoever is not a friend of Ibrahim has failed.' I said, 'With which of the two factions are you?' He said, 'I am not with either of them.' I said, 'What do you command me?' He said, 'Do you have sheep?' I said, 'No.' He said, 'Buy sheep and stay with them until it clears.'"],[6124,"From 'Urwah b. al-Zubayr, in the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Quraysh, then from Banu Makhzum: al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam."],[6125,"The Makhzumis said: 'The mother of al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam is Tumadir bt. Hidhyam from Banu Sahm b. 'Amr b. Husays.'"],[6126,"\"He used to say, 'I am the son of Subu' al-Islam. My father embraced Islam on the seventh day, and his house was on As-Safa, which was the house where the Prophet ﷺ used to be in during the early days of Islam. He invited people to Islam there, and many embraced Islam in that house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the night of Monday while there, 'O Allah, give honor to Islam through the two dearest men to You, either Umar ibn al-Khattab or Amr ibn Hisham.' The following morning, Umar ibn al-Khattab embraced Islam in the house of Arqam, and they left from there, glorifying and circumambulating the Kaaba openly. The house of Arqam was then known as the house of Islam, and Arqam gave it as charity to his son. I read a copy of the charity document in the house of Arqam, which began with 'In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. This is what Arqam decreed, his share of the Sadaqah. It was his right to have a portion of Safa, and it is a charity in its place in the Haram that cannot be sold or inherited.' Hisham ibn al-Aas and Fulan ibn Hisham's client testified to this. This house continued to function as a standing charity, with his children residing in it, leasing it, and benefitting from it, until the time of my father Ja'far bin Muhammad.\""],[6127,"From his grandfather al-Arqam, who was at Badr: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sheltered in his house near al-Safa until forty Muslim men were complete, the last of them in Islam being 'Umar b. al-Khattab. When they became forty, they went out to the polytheists. Al-Arqam said: 'I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to bid him farewell, intending to go to Jerusalem. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"Where do you intend?\" I said, \"Jerusalem.\" He said, \"What takes you there? Is it for trade?\" I said, \"No, but to pray in it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A prayer here is better than a thousand prayers there.\""],[6128,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the Day of Badr: 'Put down the heavy baggage you have.' Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi raised the sword of Ibn 'A'idh al-Marzuban, and al-Arqam b. Abi al-Arqam recognized it and said, 'Give it to me, O Messenger of Allah.' So he gave it to him."],[6129,"Indeed, the one who steps over people's necks on Friday and separates them is like one dragging his intestines into the Fire."],[6130,"I heard Ishaq b. Ibrahim al-Hanzali say: 'Abu al-Yasar al-Ansari's name is Ka'b b. 'Amr b. 'Abbad b. 'Amr b. Tamim b. Shaddad b. 'Uthman b. Ka'b b. Salama, one of the people of Badr, and he witnessed al-'Aqaba, and he is the one who captured al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib.'"],[6131,"From 'Urwah, in the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Abu al-Yasar Ka'b b. 'Amr."],[6132,"Abu al-Yasar's name is Ka'b b. 'Amr, brother of Banu Salima, died in the year 55 in Madinah. He was a short, stocky man with a belly."],[6133,"Abu al-Yasar's name is Ka'b b. 'Amr b. 'Abbad b. 'Amr b. Ghaziyya b. Sawwad. Abu al-Yasar witnessed al-'Aqaba in all the narrations, and he witnessed Badr when he was twenty years old, and he witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was a short, stocky man with a belly, and he died in Madinah in the year 55."],[6134,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was accepting people's allegiance. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, stretch out your hand so I may pledge allegiance to you, and stipulate conditions for me, for you know best the conditions.' He said, 'I accept your allegiance on condition that you worship Allah, establish prayer, give zakat, advise the Muslim sincerely, and separate from the polytheist.'"],[6135,"From 'Urwah, in the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Mu'attib b. 'Awf b. 'Amir b. al-Fadl b. 'Afif."],[6136,"Shaddad b. Aws b. Thabit b. al-Mundhir b. Haram, whose kunyah was Abu Ya'la, settled in Palestine and died in the year fifty-eight at the age of seventy-five."],[6137,"Abu Mashar said, \"Abu Hurayrah and Shaddad ibn Aws died in the year fifty-eight.\""],[6138,"My name in the Jahiliyyah was 'Abd Shams b. Sakhr, but in Islam I was named 'Abd al-Rahman. They gave me the kunyah Abu Hurayrah only because I used to tend sheep for my family and I found kittens of a wild cat, so I put them in my sleeve. When I returned to them, they heard the sounds of the kittens from my lap and said, 'What is this, O 'Abd Shams?' I said, 'Kittens I found.' They said, 'Then you are Abu Hurayrah,' and it stuck to me ever since."],[6139,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call me Abu Hirr, while the people called me Abu Hurayrah. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6140,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to call me Abu Hirr, while the people called me Abu Hurayrah."],[6141,"That you give me the kunyah of a male is dearer to me than that you give me the kunyah of a female."],[6142,"The name of my father was Abu Abd Amr ibn Abd Ghannam."],[6143,"My name in the Jahiliyyah was 'Abd Shams b. Sakhr, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me 'Abd al-Rahman."],[6144,"The name of Abu Hurayrah was 'Abd Ghanim."],[6145,"I heard Abu Mushir say: Abu Hurayrah's name was 'Ali b. 'Abd Shams."],[6146,"The name of Abu Hurayrah was 'Abd Nuhm b. 'Amir."],[6147,"Abu Hurayrah died at al-'Aqiq. His name was 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr, though some people say Ibn 'Abd al-'Uzza."],[6148,"And it is also said: Sikkin."],[6149,"The name of Abu Hurayrah is Sikkin. Thus the disagreement concerning the name of Abu Hurayrah has settled on nine forms, the most correct of which, in my view, is 'Abd Shams in the Jahiliyyah and 'Abd al-Rahman in Islam. Likewise, the year of his death is also disputed."],[6150,"Abu Hurayrah perished during the governorship of Mu'awiyah in the year fifty-eight, and in that same year died Sa'id b. al-'As, 'A'ishah, and Sa'd b. Malik."],[6151,"Abu Hurayrah died in the year fifty-eight; it is also said he died in the year fifty-nine, and he was seventy-eight years old."],[6152,"Abu Hurayrah died in the year fifty-seven."],[6153,"Abu Hurayrah died in the year fifty-five."],[6154,"Abu Hurayrah passed away in the year fifty-nine, at the end of Mu'awiyah's governorship; on the day he died he was seventy-eight years old, and al-Walid b. 'Utbah prayed over him while he was governor of Madinah, and Marwan was at that time dismissed from the governorship of Madinah."],[6155,"A man came to Zayd b. Thabit and asked him about something, so Zayd said to him: 'Go to Abu Hurayrah, for while I, Abu Hurayrah, and so-and-so were in the mosque one day supplicating Allah Almighty and remembering our Lord, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and sat with us.' He said: 'He sat down and we fell silent.' He said: 'Return to what you were doing.' Zayd said: 'So I and my companion supplicated before Abu Hurayrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began saying ameen to our supplication.' He said: 'Then Abu Hurayrah supplicated, saying: O Allah, I ask You for the like of what these two companions of mine asked You, and I ask You for knowledge that will not be forgotten.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ameen.' So we said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we also ask Allah for knowledge that will not be forgotten.' He said: 'The Dawsi has beaten you to it.'"],[6156,"Abu Hurayrah is the vessel of knowledge."],[6157,"He said to him: 'O Abu Hurayrah, what are these hadiths that have reached us, that you narrate from the Prophet ﷺ? Did you hear except what we heard? And did you see except what we saw?' He said: 'O my mother, the mirror, the kohl, and adorning oneself for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to occupy you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and by Allah, nothing used to occupy me from him.'"],[6158,"Abu Hurayrah was among the most retentive of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6159,"I heard Abu Hurayrah say: 'I memorized from the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ hadiths that I have not narrated to you, and if I narrated one of them to you, you would stone me with rocks.'"],[6160,"No one among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ narrated more hadith from him than Abu Hurayrah, and Marwan sent him over Madinah and wanted his hadith, so he said: 'Narrate as we narrated.' When he refused, he took him unawares and seated a scribe for him, and Abu Hurayrah began narrating while the scribe wrote until he exhausted all his hadith. Then Marwan said: 'Do you know that we have written all of your hadith?' He said: 'You have done it? If you obey me, you will erase it.' So he erased it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6161,"Marwan summoned Abu Hurayrah and seated me behind the couch, and began asking him while I wrote; when it was the beginning of the year, he summoned him and seated him behind a screen and began asking him about that, and he neither added nor omitted, nor brought forward nor delayed."],[6162,"A man said to Ibn Umar that Abu Hurairah narrates many hadiths from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibn Umar replied, \"I seek refuge with Allah for you from being in doubt about what he brings. But he was bold while we were timid.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6163,"\"Abu Hurairah was bold with the Prophet ﷺ, asking him about things we would not ask him about.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6164,"From the Prophet ﷺ: \"Whoever follows a funeral procession will have a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he will have two qirats, greater than Uhud.\" Ibn Umar said, \"O Abu Hurairah, consider what you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Abu Hurairah stood up and went to Aisha and said to her, \"O Mother of the Believers, I adjure you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever follows a funeral procession and prays over it will have a qirat, and if he witnesses its burial, he will have two qirats'?\" She said, \"O Allah, yes.\" Abu Hurairah said, \"Neither weddings nor trading in the markets distracted us from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I only sought from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a word he would teach me or a meal he would feed me.\" Ibn Umar said, \"O Abu Hurairah, you were the most constant of us in accompanying the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the most knowledgeable of us of his hadith.\""],[6165,"\"Ink on the garment of a seeker of knowledge is like perfume on the garment of a virgin girl.\""],[6166,"I narrated a hadith from Abu Hurairah and he denied it. I said, \"I heard it from you.\" He said, \"If you heard it from me, then it is written down with me.\" He took me by the hand to his house and showed me a book of his books containing the hadith of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he found that hadith. He said, \"I told you that if I narrated it to you, it is written down with me.\""],[6167,"When you hear in a hadith, 'he would say', it is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6168,"He sat in a gathering where Abu Hurairah was narrating to them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Some of them denied it and some recognized it, until that happened repeatedly. On that day I knew that Abu Hurairah was the most retentive of people regarding the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6169,"O Abu Muhammad, by Allah, we do not know whether this Yemeni knows more about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or you? He has said about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say, meaning Abu Hurairah. Talhah said, \"By Allah, there is no doubt that he heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what we did not hear and knew what we did not know. We were wealthy people with houses and families; we used to come to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ at the two ends of the day and then return. Abu Hurairah was poor, with no wealth, no family, and no child. His hand was with the hand of the Prophet ﷺ, and he went around with him wherever he went. There is no doubt that he knew what we did not know and heard what we did not hear. None of us ever accused him of saying about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say.\""],[6170,"I saw Abu Hurairah come out on Friday, grasp the two pommels of the pulpit while standing, and say..."],[6171,"From him, a narration regarding what has spread of his narrations and the narrations of others among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, with sound sources.\" Abu Bakr said, \"And Abu Ayyub al-Ansari narrated from him, despite his lofty status and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ staying with him.\""],[6172,"I came to Madinah and found Abu Ayyub narrating from Abu Hurairah. I said, \"You narrate from Abu Hurairah while you are a man of high standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He replied, \"To narrate from Abu Hurairah is dearer to me than to narrate from the Prophet ﷺ.\" Imam Abu Bakr said, \"Among Abu Hurairah's eagerness for knowledge is his narration from those who narrated less from the Prophet ﷺ than him, out of eagerness for knowledge. He narrated from Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi.\""],[6173,"\"None of you should brandish a sword at his brother, for perhaps Satan will cause it to slip from his hand and he will fall into a pit of the pits of the Fire.\""],[6174,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ promised us the campaign of India. If I am martyred, I will be among the best of martyrs, and if I return, I am Abu Hurayrah, the freed one."],[6175,"Mus'ab al-Zubayri, and it has been said his name is Samurah b. Mi'yar."],[6176,"And it is said his name is Samurah b. Mi'yar."],[6178,"Mi'yar b. Muhayriz."],[6179,"Abu Mahdhurah had a forelock on the front of his head; when he sat, he would let it down and it would reach the ground. They said to him, 'Will you not shave it?' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over it with his hand, so I will not shave it until I die.' So he did not shave it until he died. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6180,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ assigned the watering to the Banu 'Abd al-Muttalib, the veiling to the Banu 'Abd al-Dar, and made the call to prayer for us and our clients."],[6181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Abu Mahdhurah to give the call to prayer and to perform the Iqamah. The mention of this was omitted by Al-Dhahabi in the summary."],[6182,"He informed him: 'He was an orphan under the care of Abu Mahdhurah b. Mi'yar until he equipped him for Syria.'"],[6183,"The muezzin of Mu'awiyah called the adhan, so Abu Mahdhurah carried him and threw him into Zamzam."],[6184,"The name of Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi is Malik b. Rabi'ah."],[6185,"Abu Usayd is Malik b. Rabi'ah b. al-Badan b. 'Amir b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Harithah b. 'Amr b. al-Khazraj b. Sa'idah."],[6186,"From Abu Usayd Malik b. Rabi'ah: He had been present at Badr, then he lost his sight afterwards."],[6187,"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi lost his sight before the killing of 'Uthman, and he said: 'Praise be to Allah who gave me enjoyment of my sight during the life of the Prophet ﷺ, then when Allah willed the trial for His servants, He withheld my sight from it.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6188,"In the year of the community, the year forty, died Abu Usayd Malik b. Rabi'a b. 'Amir b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj b. Sa'ida, and he was the last of the people of Badr to die; and he was among those who saw the angels on the day of Badr, then his sight was taken away, and he was the keeper of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ over his women.\" This is an error."],[6189,"Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi died in the year sixty, and he was ninety-two years old."],[6190,"I saw Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi after his sight had gone, short and squat, white-haired and white-bearded, and I saw his head with much hair. Abu Usayd died in Madinah in the year sixty, and he was ninety-eight years old, and he was the last of the people of Badr to die."],[6191,"Abu Usayd al-Ansari brought captives from al-Bahrayn and they were lined up. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and looked at them, and behold, a woman was weeping. He said, 'What makes you weep?' She said, 'My son was sold among the Banu 'Abs.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Usayd, 'You shall ride and bring him.' So Abu Usayd rode and brought him."],[6192,"About the Messenger of Allah ﷺ giving the Ansar the choice, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The best of the tribes of the Ansar are the houses of the Banu al-Najjar, then the Banu 'Abd al-Ashhal, then the Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, then the Banu Sa'ida; and in every house of the Ansar there is good.' Abu Usayd said: 'If I were to accept other than the truth, I would begin with my own clan, the Banu Sa'ida.'"],[6193,"Bilal al-Muzani, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, is Bilal b. al-Harith b. Mazin b. Subayh b. Khalawah b. Tha'labah b. Thawr b. Hadmih b. Latim b. 'Amr b. Muzaynah."],[6194,"I heard Harun b. 'Abd Allah say: 'Bilal b. al-Harith al-Muzani was given the kunya Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.'"],[6195,"Bilal b. al-Harith al-Muzani died in the year sixty."],[6196,"Bilal b. al-Harith al-Muzani was one of those who carried one of the three banners which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ tied for them on the day of the conquest of Makkah. Bilal was given the kunya Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, and he used to dwell in the two mountains of Muzaynah, al-Ash'ar and al-Ajrad, and he came to Madinah often. He died in the year sixty, and on that day he was eighty years old."],[6197,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted him a piece of land and wrote for him: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, gave to Bilal b. al-Harith: He gave him the mines of al-Qabaliyyah, both its lowlands and its highlands, and al-Jashimah, and Dhat al-Nusub, and where cultivation is suitable in Quds, if it is thriving. And Mu'awiyah wrote."],[6198,"The Muslim is he from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe."],[6199,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, is the dissolution of the Hajj (tamattu') for us in particular or for the people in general? He said: 'Rather for us in particular.'"],[6200,"Safwan b. al-Mu'attal b. Rahada b. Khuza'i b. Muharib b. Murra b. Hilal b. Falij b. Dhakwan b. Tha'laba b. Bahta b. Sulaym. He had a house in Basra in the lane of al-Mirbad. He died in al-Jazira in the area of Shimshāt, and his grave is there."],[6201,"Safwan b. al-Mu'attal was given the kunya Abu 'Amr. He embraced Islam before the expedition of al-Muraysi' and took part in it with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. After that, he took part with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in al-Khandaq and all the battles. He was with Kurz b. Jabir al-Fihri in pursuit of the 'Uraynis who raided the milch-camels of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Dhu al-Jadr. Safwan b. al-Mu'attal died at Shamshāt in the year sixty."],[6202,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: \"O Prophet of Allah, I am asking you about a matter which you know and I do not.\" He said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"Are there any hours of the night and day in which prayer is disliked?\" He said: \"When you have prayed the morning prayer, then refrain from praying until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of a devil. Then pray, for prayer is attended and accepted until the sun is directly above your head like a spear. When it is above your head like a spear, then refrain from praying, for that is the hour in which Hell is stoked and its gates are opened, until the sun declines. When it declines, prayer is attended and accepted until you pray the afternoon prayer. Then refrain from praying until the sun sets.\" The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not record it. Authentic."],[6203,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to announce: 'Do not make nabidh in the earthenware jar.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6204,"Safwan said when he struck him [al-bahr al-tawil]: Receive the tip of the sword from me, for I am a young man who, when insulted, is not a poet. But I protect what I protect and take revenge on the slanderer who accuses the innocent, pure ones. 'A'isha said: Safwan fled, and Hassan came seeking redress with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him to grant him Safwan's blow against him, and he granted it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ compensated him with a large garden of palm trees and a Roman slave girl called Sirin. Hassan sold the garden to Mu'awiya b. Abi Sufyan during his governorship for a great sum of money."],[6205,"We set out as pilgrims. When we were at al-'Arj, we came upon a snake writhing. It did not take long before it died. A man among us took out a piece of cloth from his saddlebag, wrapped it in it, hid it in the ground, and buried it. Then we arrived in Makkah. While we were in the Sacred Mosque, a person stood before us and said: 'Which of you is the companion of 'Amr b. Jabir?' We said: 'We do not know 'Amr b. Jabir.' He said: 'Which of you is the companion of the jinni?' They said: 'This one.' He said: 'May Allah reward you well. He was the last of the nine to die, those who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to listen to the Qur'an.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6206,"The food of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was provided by his companions on a rotating basis, one night and another night. He said: It came around to me, so I prepared food for the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took it to him. Sufyan b. Hamza said: \"Hamza b. 'Amr al-Aslami had the kunya Abu Muhammad. He died in the year sixty-one, at the age of seventy-one.\""],[6207,"Hamza had the kunya Abu Muhammad. He died in the year sixty-one.\""],[6208,"Abdullah b. Zayd b. 'Asim was killed on the Day of al-Harra.\""],[6209,"Abdullah b. Zayd b. 'Asim b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Mabdhul b. 'Amr b. Ghunaym b. Mazin b. al-Najjar. His mother was 'Umara, and her name was Nusayba bt. Ka'b b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Mabdhul. He witnessed Uhud, al-Khandaq, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was the paternal uncle of 'Abbad b. Tamim. Abdullah b. Zayd was among those who killed Musaylima the liar on the Day of al-Yamama. Abdullah b. Zayd was killed on the Day of al-Harra, which was at the end of Dhu al-Hijja in the year sixty-three, during the governorship of Yazid b. Mu'awiya.\""],[6210,"He was present at Badr. This is a mistake."],[6211,"Abdullah b. Zayd b. 'Asim was a Khazraji from the Banu Mazin b. al-Najjar. He was the killer of Musaylima.\""],[6212,"I heard my father say: 'Abdullah b. Zayd has the kunya Abu Muhammad.'"],[6213,"When the time of al-Harrah came, a man went to Abdullah b. Zayd and said: 'This is Ibn Hanzalah pledging allegiance to the people upon death.' He said: 'I will not pledge allegiance to anyone upon this after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.'"],[6214,"\"Rabi'ah bin Ka'b al-Aslami embraced Islam and was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ from the early days, belonging to the As-Suffah (a group of poor companions who lived in the Mosque of the Prophet). He used to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and remained in his company in Madinah, participating in battles with him until he passed away. After his death, Rabi'ah left Madinah and settled near a well in the lands of Aslam, which was close to Madinah. He remained there until the days of Harrah, where he perished. The Harrah occurred in the month of Dhul-Hijjah of the year sixty-three.\""],[6215,"I used to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and he said to me, \"O Rabee'ah, why don't you get married?\" I replied, \"No, by Allah, I do not want to get married.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent on this issue in the summary."],[6216,"Mu'adh b. al-Harith al-Qari, of the Banu al-Najjar, had the kunya Abu al-Harith b. al-Hubab b. al-Arqam b. 'Awf b. Malik b. al-Najjar; he is Mu'adh al-Qari, kunya Abu al-Harith. He was killed on the day of al-Harrah in Dhu al-Hijjah, year sixty-three ؓ."],[6217,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say: 'Ma'qil b. Sinan al-Ashja'i witnessed the conquest with the Prophet ﷺ and was killed on the day of al-Harrah in the year sixty-three.'"],[6218,"Ma'qil b. Sinan b. Muzahhir b. 'Araki b. Fattan b. Subay' b. Bakr b. Ashja' witnessed the conquest with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6219,"Abu Bakr b. Abi Shaybah and Muhammad b. Abdullah b. Numayr narrated to us, they both said: 'Abu Muhammad al-Ash'ath b. Qays al-Kindi, of the Banu al-Harith b. Mu'awiyah, died in Kufa, and al-Hasan b. Ali was there after Mu'awiyah made peace with him, so al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ prayed over him.'"],[6220,"When al-Ash'ath b. Qays died, al-Hasan b. Ali said: 'When you wash him, do not stir him up until you bring him to me.' He said: So he was brought to him, and he called for hanut and performed ablution with it on his hands, face, and feet, then said: 'Wrap him.'"],[6221,"Al-Miswar b. Makhramah b. Nawfal b. Ahyab b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah. His mother was 'Atikah bt. 'Awf, sister of Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf."],[6222,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ delivering a sermon on his pulpit, and I was then a boy who had reached puberty."],[6223,"It is said that he died at al-Hajun; a stone from a mangonel struck him while he was in the Hijr at Makkah. He lingered for five days, then died. Abdullah b. al-Zubayr prayed over him, and he was sixty-eight years old."],[6224,"From him, he said: 'Al-Miswar b. Makhramah died in the year seventy-three.' And this is a mistake in the saying."],[6225,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fed me dates in a dish, not of this barni of yours. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when I was eleven years old."],[6226,"Some cloaks were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he distributed them among his companions. My father said to me, \"Come with me to him, for cloaks have come to him.\" My father spoke at the door, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recognized his voice and came out with a cloak, saying, \"I kept this for you, I kept this for you.\" This hadith is included in the book of Muslim, and I repeated it so that it may be known that he used to come with his father to the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Miswar had memorized the sermons of the Prophet ﷺ."],[6227,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered a sermon to us at Arafat. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"To proceed: indeed, the people of polytheism and idols used to depart from this place when the sun was on the tops of the mountains like turbans of men on their faces. But we depart after it has set. And they used to depart from al-Mash'ar al-Haram when the sun was fully risen.\""],[6228,"\"Al-Dahhak b. Qays b. Khalid b. Wahb b. Tha'labah b. Wathilah b. Amr b. Sinan b. Muharib b. Fihr. His mother was Umaymah bt. Rabi'ah from Kinanah, and she was also the mother of his sister Fatimah bt. Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak b. Qays; they were full siblings.\""],[6229,"Ibn Ziyad came to Syria after the people of Syria had pledged allegiance to Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, except for the people of al-Jabiyah. So they pledged allegiance to Ibn Ziyad. From then on, among Banu Umayyah and their clients were Marwan b. al-Hakam and after him Khalid b. Yazid b. Mu'awiyah. That was in the middle of Dhu al-Qa'dah in the year 64 AH. Then he marched against al-Dahhak b. Qays, and they met at Marj Rahit and fought for twenty days. Then defeat came upon al-Dahhak b. Qays and his companions, and that was in Dhu al-Hijjah of the year 64 AH. Al-Dahhak b. Qays and many people from Qays were killed."],[6230,"\"Al-Dahhak b. Qays al-Akbar was given the kunya Abu Unays. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away while al-Dahhak was a boy who had not yet reached puberty.\""],[6231,"\"There will never cease to be a ruler from Quraysh.\""],[6232,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, before the Hour there will be trials like patches of dark smoke, in which a man's heart will die just as his body dies. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. In them, people will sell their religion for a small portion of this world.\" Yazid had already died, and you are our brothers and our equals, and among them."],[6233,"When a man comes to a people and they say, \"Welcome,\" then welcome to him on the day he meets his Lord. And when a man comes to a people and they say to him, \"May you have drought,\" then drought for him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6234,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: \"Trim and do not over-cut, for it is more radiant for the face and more pleasing to the husband.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6235,"\"Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As b. Wa'il b. Hashim b. Sa'id b. Sahm b. Amr b. Husays b. Ka'b. Abdullah b. Amr embraced Islam before his father. Among what was mentioned about him: he was a tall, reddish man with large calves, white hair and beard. He became blind at the end of his life. Abdullah b. Amr died in Syria in the year 65 AH, when he was seventy-two years old. He was given the kunya Abu Muhammad.\""],[6236,"\"The death of Abu Muhammad Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As — his mother was Rayta bt. Munabbih b. al-Hajjaj b. Amir b. Hudhayfah b. Sa'd b. Sahm — occurred in the year 65 AH. He used to dye his hair black. Amr b. al-As was twelve years older than his son.\""],[6237,"Abdullah b. Umar entered upon Abdullah b. Amr, who had dyed his beard black. Abdullah b. Umar said, \"Peace be upon you, O little gray-haired one.\" Ibn Amr said to him, \"Do you not recognize me, O Abu Abd al-Rahman?\" He said, \"Yes, I recognize you as an old man, but today you are a youth. Indeed, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Yellow is the dye of the believer, red is the dye of the Muslim, and black is the dye of the disbeliever.'\""],[6238,"Three persons came to Abdullah ibn Amr and said: O Abu Muhammad."],[6239,"Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As—his mother was Rayta bt. Munabbih ibn al-Hajjaj ibn Amir ibn Hudhayfah ibn Sa'd ibn Sahm ibn Amr ibn Husays ibn Ka'b ibn Lu'ayy."],[6240,"Take the Quran from four: two men from the Muhajirun and two men from the Ansar—from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, Salim the mawla of Abu Hudhayfah, Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and Mu'adh ibn Jabal. And he said: And he singled out Abdullah ibn Mas'ud with a word."],[6241,"Umm Abdullah, the daughter of Raita bin Munabbih bin Al-Hajjaj, was kind to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . One day he came to her and said, \"How are you, Umm Abdullah?\" She replied, \"I am fine, and Abdullah is a man who has renounced the world.\" His father told him on the day of Siffin, 'Go out and fight.' He said, 'O my father, are you commanding me to go out and fight, even though I have heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ things that I have never heard before? He said, 'I adjure you by Allah, do you know that what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to you was true? He took your hand and put it in mine and said, 'Obey your father Amr bin Al-As.' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I am commanding you to fight.' So he went out and fought. When the war was over, Abdullah bin Amr said, 'If you had seen the position and the scene of my station at Siffin, when in the evening the people of Iraq came like clouds in spring, and the Zawahir shook them. If you say that they have changed overnight, we have battalions of them that have stood firm, and other battalions shook. They said to us, 'We think that you should give your allegiance to Ali.' We said, 'No, we think that you should fight each other.'"],[6242,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in one of his expeditions, and the people panicked. I went out with my weapon upon me, and I looked at Salim, the mawla of Abu Hudhayfah, with his weapon upon him, walking with tranquility upon him. I said: I will certainly follow the example of this righteous man, until he came and sat at the door of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I sat with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out angry and said: 'O people, what is this haste? What is this luxury? Are you unable to do as these two believing men did?'"],[6243,"I was with my father at Huwarin when a man approached. When the people saw him, they rushed to him. He said: I was among those who rushed to his sitting place. I said: Who is this man? They said: This is Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As."],[6244,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you permit me to write down what I hear from you? He said: 'Yes.' I said: In pleasure and in anger? He said: 'Yes, for it is not fitting that I should say in pleasure or in anger anything but the truth.'"],[6245,"Ka'b al-Ahbar saw Abdullah ibn Amr giving fatwas to the people and said: Who is this? They said: This is Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As. So he sent a man from his companions to him and said: Tell him: O Abdullah ibn Amr, do not fabricate lies against Allah, lest He destroy you with a punishment; and indeed he who fabricates has failed. He said: The man came to him and said that to him. Ibn Umar said: And Ka'b spoke the truth: 'He who fabricates has failed,' and he did not become angry. He said: Then Ka'b sent the man back to him and said: Ask him about the gathering—what is it? And about the souls of the Muslims—where do they assemble? And the souls of the people of polytheism—where do they assemble? So he came to him and asked him, and he said: 'As for the souls of the Muslims, they assemble at Ariha; as for the souls of the people of polytheism, they assemble at San'a; and as for the first gathering, it is a fire that drives the people—they see it at night and do not see it by day.' So Ka'b's messenger returned to him and informed him of what he had said, and he said: He has spoken the truth. This is a scholar, so ask him."],[6246,"Asma ibn Harithah ibn Hind ibn Abdullah ibn Ghiyath ibn Sa'd ibn Amr ibn Amir ibn Afsa, mawla of Banu Harithah."],[6247,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Ashura, and he said: 'Have you fasted today, O Asma?' I said: No. He said: 'Then fast.' I said: I have already eaten lunch, O Messenger of Allah. He said: 'Fast what remains, and command your people to fast.' Asma said: So I took my sandals in my hand and entered my camp until I came to my people, and I said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ commands you to fast. They said: We have already eaten lunch. I said: He has commanded you to fast the rest of your day."],[6248,"Asma ibn Harithah died in the year sixty-six, and he was eighty years old."],[6249,"I did not consider Asma and Hind, the two sons of Harithah, to be anything but servants of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because of how long they kept to his door and served him, and they were in need. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6250,"Hind ibn Harithah al-Aslami was present at al-Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Hind ibn Harithah died in Madinah during the caliphate of Amir al-Mu'minin Ali. It is said that they were eight brothers, all of whom accompanied the Prophet ﷺ and were present at the Pledge of al-Ridwan: Asma, Hind, Khirash, Dhu'ayb, Humran, Fadalah, Salamah, and Malik—the sons of Harithah ibn Sa'id."],[6251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from Aslam on the day of Ashura and said: “Whoever has eaten or drunk, let him complete his fast, and whoever has not eaten, let him fast the remainder of his day.” The narration has already been mentioned that Asma was the messenger for that, and it is also narrated that he was Hind."],[6252,"The Prophet ﷺ sent him on the day of Ashura. He said: “Command your people to fast this day.” He said: What do you think, O Messenger of Allah, if I find them having already eaten? He said: “Let them complete the rest of their day.”"],[6253,"“Sulayman b. Surad b. al-Jawn b. Abi al-Jawn – who is Abd al-Uzza b. Munqidh b. Rabi’ah – and he was given the kunya Abu Mutarrif. He embraced Islam and accompanied the Prophet ﷺ. His name was Yasar, and when he embraced Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Sulayman. He had advanced age and nobility among his people. He settled in Kufa when the Muslims settled there, and he witnessed with the Commander of the Faithful Ali the battle of Siffin. Then he went out seeking vengeance for the blood of al-Husayn b. Ali, and under his banner were four thousand men. Sulayman b. Surad was killed in that battle, and his head was carried to Marwan b. al-Hakam. On the day he was killed, Sulayman was ninety-three years old.”"],[6254,"“Al-Mukhtar b. Abi Ubayd killed Sulayman b. Surad – this one – after Sulayman b. Surad had killed Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad.”"],[6255,"“Sulayman b. Surad killed Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad.”"],[6256,"“Abu Shurayh, Ka’b b. Amr al-Khuza’i, died in the year sixty-eight, and his name is disputed; it is said he was Khuwaylid b. Amr.”"],[6257,"“Al-Nu’man b. Bashir b. Sa’d b. Tha’laba b. Khilas b. Zayd b. Malik al-Agharr b. Tha’laba b. Ka’b b. al-Khazraj b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and his mother was Amra bt. Rawaha, the sister of Abd Allah b. Rawaha. To al-Nu’man was born Abd Allah, and by him he was given the kunya Abu Abd Allah.”"],[6258,"We sat with him and he mentioned the first child born among the Ansar after the coming of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to Madinah. He said: “Al-Nu’man b. Bashir was born a year or less than a year after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah.” He said: Then they mentioned Abd Allah b. Abi Talha, and he said: “If Umm Sulaym was pregnant with him and gave birth after arriving in Madinah.”"],[6259,"I heard Abu Mushir say: “Al-Nu’man b. Bashir was killed between Salamiyeh and Hims; he was assassinated.”"],[6260,"“When al-Dahhak b. Qays was killed at Marj Rahit on the fifteenth of Dhu al-Hijja in the year sixty-four during the caliphate of Marwan b. al-Hakam, al-Nu’man b. Bashir wanted to flee from Hims, where he was governor, so he feared and called for Ibn al-Zubayr. The people of Hims sought him and killed him and cut off his head.”"],[6261,"“Before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of dark night. In them a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, or a believer in the evening and a disbeliever in the morning. People will sell their religion in them for a paltry portion of this world.”"],[6262,"“Abu Waqid al-Laythi – his name is al-Harith b. Awf b. Usayd b. Jabir b. Abda Manah b. Yashju’ b. Amir b. Layth.”"],[6263,"I heard Sa'id b. Kathir b. 'Ufayr say: \"Abu Waqid al-Laythi, al-Harith b. 'Awf b. Usayd b. Jabir b. 'Awthara b. 'Abd Manat b. Yashju' b. 'Amir, was an early Muslim. He carried the banner of Banu Layth, Damra, and Sa'd b. Bakr on the day of the conquest. Abu Waqid remained after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for a long time, then he went to Makkah and stayed there for a year as a neighbor, and he died there.\""],[6264,"\"We visited al-Laythi during the illness in which he died, and he died, so we buried him in Makkah in the cemetery of the Muhajirun at Fakhkh. It was called the cemetery of the Muhajirun because those who had come to Madinah and then performed Hajj and stayed as neighbors and died in Makkah were buried there. Among them were Abu Waqid al-Laythi, 'Abdullah b. 'Umar, and others. Abu Waqid al-Laythi died in the year sixty-eight, at the age of eighty-five.\""],[6265,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, my knee touching his knee, when a man came to him and clung to his ear. The face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ changed and the blood rushed to the lines of his face ﷺ. Then he said: \"This is the messenger of 'Amir b. al-Tufayl, threatening me and threatening those who seek refuge with me. But Allah ﷻ has sufficed me against him through the children of Isma'il and Banu Qayla,\" meaning the Ansar."],[6266,"\"Indeed, the legs of my pulpit are firmly rooted in Paradise.\""],[6267,"\"Zayd b. Arqam b. Zayd b. Qays b. al-Nu'man b. Malik b. al-Agharr b. Tha'laba b. Ka'b b. al-Khazraj. He was called Abu 'Amr. He died in Kufa during the time of al-Mukhtar b. Abi 'Ubayd in the year sixty-eight.\""],[6268,"I said to Zayd b. Arqam: \"O Abu 'Amr...\""],[6269,"The people went out to pray for rain, and among them was Zayd b. Arqam. There was only one man between him and me. I said to him: \"O Abu 'Amr, how many expeditions did the Prophet ﷺ undertake?\" He said: \"Nineteen.\" I said: \"How many did you participate in with him?\" He said: \"Seventeen.\""],[6270,"We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until we reached Ghadir Khumm. He ordered a tree to be cleared, and it was swept on a day that was intensely hot, the like of which we had never experienced. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: \"O people, no prophet was ever sent but he lived half as long as the one before him. I am about to be called and to respond. I am leaving among you that with which, if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray after me: the Book of Allah ﷻ.\" Then he stood up, took 'Ali by the hand, and said: \"O people, who is more entitled to you than yourselves?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said: \"Am I not more entitled to you than yourselves?\" They said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Whoever I am his mawla, then 'Ali is his mawla.\""],[6271,"\"The Prophet ﷺ died when I was fifteen years old.\" This is how Ibrahim b. Tahman, Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi, and al-Walid b. Khalid narrated from Shu'ba; as for the hadith of Abu Dawud..."],[6272,"Shu'ba narrated to us."],[6273,"Staying at Al-Mahassab is not one of the ceremonies (of Hajj), but Al-Mahassab is a place where Messenger of Allah ﷺ camped (during his Hajjat-al-Wida). (Using translation from Bukhārī 1766)"],[6274,"On the authority of Ibn 'Abbas ؓ."],[6275,"\"Abu al-'Abbas 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas died at the age of seventy-one. He was born in the mountain pass three years before the Hijra.\""],[6276,"I said to Ibn Abbas, \"O Abu al-Abbas,\""],[6277,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was praying at the end of the night, and I stood behind him. He took me and made me stand beside him. When he turned back to his prayer, I moved back. When he finished, he said, \"What is the matter with you? I make you stand beside me and you move back?\" I said, \"It is not proper for anyone to pray beside you while you are the Messenger of Allah.\" This pleased him, and he supplicated to Allah to increase me in understanding and knowledge."],[6278,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the house of Maymunah. She placed water for his ablution. Maymunah said to him, \"Abdullah b. al-Abbas placed water for your ablution.\" He said, \"O Allah, give him understanding in religion and teach him interpretation.\""],[6279,"\"The most compassionate of my Ummah toward it is Abu Bakr; the firmest of them in the command of Allah is Umar; the most modest of them is Uthman; the best reciter of them is Ubayy b. Ka'b; the most knowledgeable of them in inheritance is Zayd b. Thabit; the best judge of them is Ali b. Abi Talib; the most knowledgeable of them in lawful and unlawful is Muadh b. Jabal; the most truthful of them in speech is Abu Dharr; the trustworthy one of this Ummah is Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah; and the scholar of this Ummah is Abdullah b. Abbas.\""],[6280,"It was mentioned to Jabir about the red meat and he said: \"That sea, meaning Ibn Abbas, recited: 'Say, \"I do not find within that which was revealed to me [anything] forbidden to one who would eat it\"' (Quran 6:145).\" Al-Dhahabi did not comment on it in his summary."],[6281,"\"Ibn Abbas was called al-Bahr (the Sea) because of the abundance of his knowledge.\""],[6282,"\"Ibn Abbas was the scholar (ḥabr) of this Ummah.\""],[6283,"\"Ibn Abbas was called al-Bahr (the Sea) because of the abundance of his knowledge.\""],[6284,"I spent a night with the family of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I went to the mosque, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the later Isha prayer until no one remained in the mosque except him. He then passed by me and said, \"Who is this?\" I said, \"Abdullah.\" He said, \"So what is it?\" I said, \"My father commanded me to spend the night with you tonight.\" He said, \"Then follow.\" When he entered, he said, \"Spread a bed for Abdullah.\" I was brought a cushion made of sackcloth. Al-Abbas had instructed me not to sleep until I had memorized his prayer. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came forward and slept until I heard his snoring. Then he sat upright on his bed, raised his head to the sky, and said, \"Glory be to the King, the Most Holy,\" three times. Then he recited this verse from the end of Surah Al Imran until he completed it: {Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth} [Quran 2:164]. Then he got up, urinated, cleaned his teeth with his siwak, performed ablution, then entered his prayer place and prayed two rak'ahs that were neither short nor long. Then he prayed and performed witr. When he finished his prayer, I heard him say, \"O Allah, place light in my sight, place light in my hearing, place light in my tongue, place light in my heart, place light on my right, place light on my left, place light in front of me, place light behind me, place light above me, place light below me, and grant me light on the day I meet You, and magnify light for me.\""],[6285,"Al-Abbas sent his son Abdullah to the Prophet ﷺ, and he slept behind him. There was a man with the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ turned and said, \"When did you come, my beloved?\" He said, \"A short while ago.\" He said, \"Did you see anyone with me?\" He said, \"Yes, I saw a man.\" He said, \"That was Jibril ﷺ , and no creature saw him except my cousin, unless he is a prophet, but that will be placed in the latter part of your life.\" Then he said, \"O Allah, teach him interpretation and give him understanding in religion and make him among the people of faith.\""],[6286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the privy and found a covered basin. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Who made this?\" I said, \"I did.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, teach him the interpretation of the Quran.\""],[6287,"\"If Ibn Abbas had reached our age, none of us would have accompanied him.\""],[6288,"Ibn Abbas delivered a sermon while he was at the pilgrimage season. He began Surah al-Nur, reciting and explaining it. I kept saying, \"I have never seen or heard the speech of a man like him. If the Persians and Romans had heard it, they would have embraced Islam.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6289,"Yes, the interpreter of the Qur'an is Ibn Abbas."],[6290,"I performed Hajj along with a companion of mine while Ibn Abbas was leading the Hajj. He began reciting Surah al-Nur and explaining it. My companion said, 'Glory be to Allah! What comes out of this man's head! If the Turks had heard this, they would have embraced Islam.'"],[6291,"I saw a gathering of Ibn Abbas such that if all of Quraysh had boasted of it, it would have been a source of pride for them. I saw the people assemble until the road became too narrow for them, and no one could come or go. He said: I entered upon him and informed him that they were as if at his door. He said to me, 'Prepare for me water for ablution.' He performed ablution and sat down, then said to me, 'Go out and tell them: Whoever wishes to ask about the Qur'an and its letters and what he intends from it, let him enter.' I went out and informed them, and they entered until they filled the house and the room. They did not ask him about anything except that he informed them about it and added for them the like of what they asked or more. Then he said, 'Your brothers.' So they left. Then he said to me, 'Go out and say: Whoever wishes to ask about the lawful and the unlawful and jurisprudence, let him enter.' I went out and told them, and they entered until they filled the house and the room. They did not ask him about anything except that he informed them about it and added for them the like of it. Then he said, 'Your brothers.' So they left. Then he said to me, 'Go out and say: Whoever wishes to ask about the obligatory shares of inheritance and what resembles them, let him enter.' I went out and informed them, and they entered until they filled the house and the room. They did not ask him about anything except that he informed them about it and added for them the like of it. Then he said, 'Your brothers.' So they left. Then he said to me, 'Go out and say: Whoever wishes to ask about Arabic, poetry, and unusual expressions in speech, let him enter.' He said: So they entered until they filled the house and the room. They did not ask him about anything except that he informed them about it and added for them the like of it. Abu Salih said: If all of Quraysh had boasted of that, it would have been a source of pride for them. He said: I have not seen the like of this for anyone among the people. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6292,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died, I said to a man from the Ansar, 'Come, O so-and-so, let us seek knowledge, for the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are alive.' He said, 'How strange of you, O Ibn Abbas! Do you think the people will need you while among the people are Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said: So I left that and set out seeking. If a hadith reached me from a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who had heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would go to him and sit at his door, and the wind would blow dust on my face. He would come out to me and say, 'O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what brought you? What is your need?' I would say, 'A hadith reached me that you narrate from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He would say, 'Why did you not send for me?' I would say, 'I am more deserving of coming to you.' He said: That man remained until the people gathered around me, and he said, 'This young man was more intelligent than I.'"],[6293,"If it were up to me, I would have killed them because of the saying of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, 'Whoever changes his religion, kill him,' and I would not have burned them, because I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Do not punish with the punishment of Allah.' That reached Ali, and he said, 'Woe to Ibn Abbas!'"],[6294,"Umar used to ask me along with the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf said to him, 'Do you ask him while we have sons like him?' Umar said, 'He is from where you know.' Then he asked them about 'When comes the help of Allah and victory.' Some of them said, 'Allah commanded us to praise Him and seek His forgiveness,' and some said, 'We do not know.' Then he said to me, 'O Ibn Abbas, what do you say?' I said, 'It is the appointed term of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' And he recited the surah to its end: {Indeed, He is ever accepting of repentance} [al-Nasr: 3]. Umar said, 'By Allah, I know nothing of it except what you know.'"],[6295,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said regarding the Night of Decree: \"Whatever you have been able to ascertain, seek it in the last ten nights. And in which odd night do you see it?\" Some of them said: 'The ninth night', some said 'The seventh night', and some said 'The fifth night' and 'The third night'. He said, \"What is wrong with you, Ibn Abbas, that you do not speak?\" I said, \"If you wish, I will speak.\" He said, \"I did not call you except for you to speak.\" So I said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed, Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, mentions the number 'seven' most.' He said: 'The heavens are seven, and the earths are seven.' And he said, 'Indeed, we have split the earth open, so We caused in it grains, grapes, green fodder, olives, dates, and gardens of dense shrubbery, and fruits, and herbage, and palm trees, and gardens of dense shrubbery, as sustenance for you and your livestock.' And the gardens of dense shrubbery are intertwined and each intertwined garden is a garden, and the herbage is whatever the earth has grown that people do not eat.' Umar said, 'Are you amazed that you say the same as this boy who has not reached the age of having wet dreams?' Then he said, 'Indeed, I forbade you from speaking, so when I call you along with them, speak.'\""],[6296,"The Muhajirun said to Umar b. al-Khattab, 'Call our sons as you call Ibn Abbas.' He said, 'That is the young man of the elders; he has an inquisitive tongue and a discerning heart.' Munqati' (disconnected)."],[6297,"I, Huyayy b. Ya'la, and Sa'id b. Jubayr would come to Ibn Abbas. I would ask him about genealogy, Huyayy would ask him about the days of the Arabs, and Sa'id b. Jubayr would ask him about legal rulings. It was as if we were drawing from a sea."],[6298,"O Ibn Shaddad, will you not be amazed? The boy came to me while I had taken my place for the midday nap, and said, 'There is a man at the door seeking permission.' I said, 'Nothing brought him at this hour except a need; give him permission.' He entered and said, 'Will you not tell me about that man?' I said, 'Which man?' He said, 'Ali b. Abi Talib.' I said, 'About which of his affairs?' He said, 'When will he be resurrected?' I said, 'Glory be to Allah! He will be resurrected when those in the graves are resurrected.' He said, 'Do I not see you saying as these fools say?' So I said, 'Take this one away from me; he shall never enter upon me, or I will strike him.'"],[6299,"That the people of Kufa, such-and-such number of them have recited the Qur'an. So he said 'Allahu Akbar,' may Allah have mercy on him. I said, 'Have they differed?' He said, 'Uff! What do you know?' He became angry, so I went to my home. Then he sent for me afterward, and I made an excuse to him. He said, 'I adjure you not to come?' So I went to him, and he said, 'You said something.' I said, 'I seek Allah's forgiveness; I will not return to anything after it.' He said, 'I adjure you not to repeat to me what you said.' I said, 'I said: It was written to me that such-and-such number have recited the Qur'an, and I said, Have they differed?' He said, 'From what did you know that?' I said, 'I recited: {And of the people is he whose speech pleases you in worldly life, and he calls Allah to witness as to what is in his heart} [al-Baqarah: 204] until it ended at {And Allah does not like corruption} [al-Baqarah: 205]. When they do that, the companion of the Qur'an will not be patient. Then I recited: {When it is said to him, 'Fear Allah,' pride in sin takes hold of him. Sufficient for him is Hell, and how wretched is the resting place. And of the people is he who sells himself seeking the pleasure of Allah. And Allah is kind to His servants.}' He said, 'You have spoken the truth, by the One in whose hand is my soul.'"],[6300,"Umar said, 'I see that the Qur'an has become widespread among the people.' I said, 'I do not like that, O Commander of the Faithful.' He pulled his hand from mine and said, 'Why did you say that?' I said, 'Because when they recite, they will become disputatious; when they become disputatious, they will differ; and when they differ, they will strike one another's necks.' He then sat away from me and left me, and I stayed away from him for a day that only Allah knows. Then his messenger came to me at noon and said, 'Answer the Commander of the Faithful.' I went to him, and he said, 'How did you say?' I repeated my statement. Umar said, 'I used to conceal it from the people.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6301,"A mule was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, which Chosroes had given him. He rode it with a halter of hair, then seated me behind him. Then he traveled with me for a long while, then turned and said, 'O boy.' I said, 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Preserve Allah and He will preserve you. Preserve Allah and you will find Him before you. Become acquainted with Allah in times of ease, and He will know you in times of hardship. When you ask, ask Allah; when you seek help, seek help from Allah. The pen has dried with what is to be. If people were to strive to benefit you with something Allah has not decreed for you, they would not be able to do it. If people were to strive to harm you with something Allah has not written against you, they would not be able to do it. If you are able to act with patience along with certainty, do so; if you cannot, then be patient, for in patience over what you dislike there is much good. Know that with patience comes victory, with distress comes relief, and with hardship comes ease.'"],[6302,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Guard Allah, and He will guard you. Guard Allah, and you will find Him before you. Draw near to Allah in ease, and He will know you in hardship. And know that what has missed you was never to befall you, and what has befallen you was never to miss you. And know that if all the creation were to gather to give you something that Allah does not will to give you, they would not be able to do it. And if they were to gather to turn away from you something that Allah wills to befall you, they would not be able to do it. So when you ask, ask Allah, and when you seek help, seek help from Allah. And know that victory comes with patience, relief comes with distress, and with hardship comes ease. And know that the pen has already written what is to be.\" 'Isa b. Muhammad al-Qurashi is not relied upon."],[6303,"He saw Mu'awiyah circumambulating the Ka'bah, with 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas on his left, and I was following them on their backs, hearing their speech. Mu'awiyah began to touch the two corners of the Black Stone, so Ibn 'Abbas said to him: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not touch these two corners.\" Mu'awiyah said: \"O Ibn 'Abbas, nothing of it is abandoned.\" So Ibn 'Abbas did not leave him alone; every time he placed his hand on either of the two corners, he said that to him."],[6304,"I heard Ibn Abbas three days before his death saying, \"O Allah, I repent to You for the fatwas I used to give to people regarding exchange transactions.\"[1]"],[6305,"\"Would any of you like to have a garden of date palms and grapevines, with rivers flowing beneath it, in which he has every kind of fruit?\" [al-Baqarah 266] up to here: \"Then a whirlwind with fire struck it and it was burned.\" [al-Baqarah 266] He asked the people about it and said: \"In your opinion, was it revealed about 'Would any of you like to have a garden'?\" They said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" 'Umar became angry and said: \"Say: 'We know,' or 'We do not know.'\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"I have something in my mind about it, O Commander of the Believers.\" He said: \"O son of my brother, speak and do not belittle yourself.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"It was struck as a parable for a deed.\" 'Umar said: \"For a wealthy man who does good deeds, then Allah sends Satan to him and he commits sins until he drowns all his deeds. He had a garden, and it burned when he was most in need of it, when children were many and he had reached old age.\" He said: \"Would any of you like to meet the Day of Resurrection as a servant most in need of his deed, with nothing to show for it?\""],[6306,"Muharib b. Dithar said to me: \"Have you heard Sa'id b. Jubayr mention anything from Ibn 'Abbas about al-Kawthar?\" I said: \"Yes, he is the abundant good.\" He said: \"Glory be to Allah. Say what falls short of Ibn 'Abbas.\" I said: \"He said: I heard Ibn 'Abbas say: I heard Ibn 'Umar say: When 'Indeed, We have granted you al-Kawthar' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'It is a river in Paradise, its banks of gold, flowing over pearls and rubies. Its drink is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey.'\" He said: \"By Allah, Ibn 'Abbas has spoken the truth. This, by Allah, is the abundant good.\""],[6307,"I heard Abu Nu'aym say: \"'Abdullah b. 'Abbas died in the year sixty-eight.\""],[6308,"He said the takbir over Ibn 'Abbas four times and said: \"The rabbani of this ummah has perished.\""],[6309,"Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6310,"He came out of his bier, and when he was buried, this verse was recited at the edge of the grave, and no one knew who recited it: \"O reassured soul, return to your Lord, pleased and pleasing. Enter among My servants and enter My Paradise.\" [al-Fajr 28] He said: Isma'il b. 'Ali and 'Isa b. 'Ali mentioned that it was a white bird. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6311,"Approximately four hundred hadiths were narrated from him.\""],[6312,"I heard Shu'bah, the mawla of Ibn 'Abbas, say: \"Ibn 'Abbas died in the year sixty-eight in al-Ta'if, and he was seventy-five years old. He used to dye his beard yellow.\""],[6313,"Yazid b. 'Utbah b. Abi Lahab mentions the clouds that watered the grave of Ibn 'Abbas: \"[al-Bahr al-Basit] The sky of Allah poured His mercy three times with water over the grave of Ibn 'Abbas. He used to tell us this, and we knew it with certainty, but some remember and some forget. The sky waters the grave with His mercy. This, by my life, is a matter in the hands of people. If the people had an opinion to protect them in calamities, they would have thrown you Ibn 'Abbas—may Allah have mercy on his understanding—and what a man he was! Is there anyone like him at the decisive moment among the people? But they threw you an old man of blessed lineage, who does not know the division of fifths into sixths.\""],[6314,"\"We, the Ansar, requested from 'Umar or 'Uthman—Ibn Abi al-Zinad was uncertain—so we went with 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas and a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with him. Ibn 'Abbas spoke, and they spoke, mentioning the Ansar and their merits. The governor made excuses.\" Hassan said: \"It was a serious matter that we sought.\" He said: \"He kept debating with them until they stood up and excused him, except 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas, who said: 'No, by Allah, the Ansar have a high station. They supported and sheltered.' He mentioned their virtue and said: 'This is the poet of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his defender.' 'Abdullah kept arguing with comprehensive words that closed every need for him, until he had no choice but to fulfill our need.\" He said: \"We left, and Allah ﷻ had fulfilled our need through his speech. I took 'Abdullah by the hand, praising him and praying for him. I passed through the mosque with the group who had been with him, and they did not achieve what he achieved. I said, so that they could hear: 'He was more deserving of us than you.' They said: 'Indeed.' I said to 'Abdullah: 'By Allah, it is the remnants of prophethood, and its heir is Ahmad ﷺ, who was more deserving of it than you.'\" Hassan said: \"And I point to 'Abdullah: [al-Bahr al-Tawil] When he speaks, he leaves no room for a speaker, with eloquent words that show no gap between them. He suffices and heals what is in the chests, and leaves no one with a purpose in speech, serious or jest. I ascended to the heights without hardship, and reached their peaks, not lowly nor high.\""],[6315,"I saw Ibn Abbas wearing a mirt (garment) of brocaded silk with upright borders at Muzdalifah, and he took it for a thousand."],[6316,"And it is said: He was born in the Year of the Camel, in the year thirty-six. He was the most handsome of the Quraysh on earth, the most distinguished of them, and the most given to prayer among them. He was called al-Sajjad (the one who prostrates much), and in his offspring lies the caliphate. [His son] Abbas was his eldest child, and by him he was given his kunya. [He also had] Muhammad, Ubayd Allah, al-Fadl, and Lubaba, whose mother was Zur'ah daughter of Musarrih b. Ma'di Karib b. Wali'ah. Musarrih was one of the four kings. There is no surviving progeny for al-Abbas, Ubayd Allah, al-Fadl, and Muhammad, the sons of Abdullah b. Abbas. As for Lubaba daughter of Abdullah, she was married to Ali b. Abdullah b. Ja'far b. Abi Talib, and she bore him children, and her descendants have numerous offspring. Asma' daughter of Abdullah was married to Abdullah b. Abdullah b. al-Abbas, and she bore him Hasan and Husayn. Their mother was an umm walad."],[6317,"When Ibn Abbas lost his sight, a man came to him and said to him, \"If you endure for seven days without praying except lying on your back and making gestures, I will treat you and you will be cured, if Allah Almighty wills.\" So he sent to Aisha, Abu Hurayrah, and others among the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. Each of them said, \"What do you think? If I die within these seven days, how will you handle the prayer?\" So he left his eye alone and did not treat it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6318,"And it is said: Abu Amr from the inhabitants of Sham."],[6319,"Awf b. Malik al-Ashjai was given the kunya Abu Muhammad, and his dwelling was in Hims."],[6320,"Awf b. Malik al-Ashjai: When the zakat was revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he sent Abu Bakr al-Siddiq to him. Abu Bakr said to Awf, \"Allah Almighty has revealed the zakat.\" He said, \"And what is the zakat?\" He said, \"From every forty camels, one camel.\" He said, \"Then select for us, and take a camel.\" So Abu Bakr selected a camel and took a camel for his riding saddle. Awf said, \"Indeed, that is my riding camel.\" Abu Bakr said to him, \"Indeed, it is greater for your reward.\" He said, \"Then drive its young one.\" So Abu Bakr drove it and its young one to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of Awf's deed and statement. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Return to him and inform him that Allah has built a house for him in Paradise.\""],[6321,"Awf b. Malik al-Ashjai was present at Khaybar with the Muslims, and he carried the banner of Ashja' on the day of the conquest of Makkah. Then Awf moved to Sham during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and settled in Hims. He remained until the beginning of the caliphate of Abd al-Malik b. Marwan, then died in the year seventy-three. He was given the kunya Abu Amr."],[6322,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition to Tabuk at the end of the night while he was in his tent. I greeted him and said, \"Shall I enter, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Enter.\" I said, \"All of me?\" He said, \"All of you.\" Then he said ﷺ, \"Six things before the Hour. The first of them is the death of your Prophet. Say 'one.'\" I said, \"One.\" \"The second is the conquest of the House of the Sanctuary (Jerusalem). Say 'two.'\" I said, \"Two.\" Then he said, \"The third is a death that will take you like the sudden death of sheep. Say 'three.'\" I said, \"Three.\" He said, \"The fourth is that wealth will overflow among you, so that a man will be given a hundred dinars and he will remain displeased with it. Say 'four.'\" I said, \"Four.\" \"The fifth is a trial that will occur among you, such that scarcely a house of hair or clay will remain among you but it will enter it. Say 'five.'\" I said, \"Five.\" \"And the sixth is a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar (Byzantines). They will gather against you with the force of a pregnant woman's full term, then they will betray you and come upon you in eighty banners, each banner with twelve thousand men.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6323,"Regarding the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , he said, \"My nation will divide into seventy-three sects, the largest of which is a group that causes trials and tribulations for my nation. They make their own opinions the basis for judging matters and they declare what is forbidden to be permissible, and what is permissible to be forbidden.\" The mention of this hadith was omitted by Al-Dhahabi in his summarization."],[6324,"The first child born after the Hijrah was Abdullah b. al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam b. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. Abd al-Uzza. His mother was Asma' daughter of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and her mother was Qaylah daughter of Abd al-Uzza b. Abd Asad b. Nasr b. Malik b. Hisl b. Amir b. Lu'ayy. Abdullah was given the kunya Abu Bakr."],[6325,"The Prophet ﷺ named Abdullah b. al-Zubayr 'Abdullah.'"],[6326,"The calendar was [established] from the year in which the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah, and in that year Abdullah b. al-Zubayr was born."],[6327,"\"I was named after my grandfather Abu Bakr and given his kunya.\" Abdullah had two kunyas: Abu Bakr and Abu Khubayb."],[6328,"Asma' bt. Abi Bakr set out when she emigrated to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while she was pregnant with 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, and she gave birth to him. She brought him to the Prophet ﷺ for him to perform tahnik. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him and placed him in his lap. A date was brought, and he sucked it, then chewed it, then placed it in his mouth and performed tahnik with it. The first thing to enter his belly was the saliva of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped him and named him 'Abdullah. Later he came, when he was seven or eight years old, to give allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ; al-Zubayr had ordered him to do that. The Prophet ﷺ smiled when he saw him approaching and accepted his allegiance. He was the first born in Islam in Madinah upon the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Jews used to say: We have bewitched them, so no male child will be born to them in Madinah. The Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said takbir when 'Abdullah was born. 'Abdullah b. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said, when he heard the takbir of the people of Syria after they had killed 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr: Those who said takbir at his birth are better than those who said takbir at his killing."],[6329,"Ibn al-Zubayr was mentioned in the presence of Ibn 'Abbas, and he said: He was chaste in Islam, devout to Allah. His father was al-Zubayr, his mother Asma', his grandfather Abu Bakr, his paternal aunt Khadijah, his grandmother Safiyyah, and his maternal aunt 'A'ishah. By Allah, I will call myself to account for him in a way I have not called myself to account for Abu Bakr or 'Umar. But he deliberately preferred the Humaydat, the Asamat, and the Tuwaytat."],[6330,"Ibn al-Zubayr erased his own name from the register when 'Uthman ؓ was killed."],[6331,"The courier who brought Ibn al-Zubayr the head of al-Mukhtar told me: When he saw it, Ibn al-Zubayr said: Ka'b never told me anything but that I found it to be true, except that he told me that a man of Thaqif would kill me. Al-A'mash said: He did not know that Abu Muhammad—may Allah forsake him—had hidden it for him."],[6332,"Ibn al-Zubayr used to practice wisal for seven days, and on the third day he would arise as the most vigorous of us."],[6333,"Ibn al-Zubayr had a hundred slaves, each of whom spoke a different language, and Ibn al-Zubayr would speak to each of them in his own language. When you looked at him in a worldly matter, you would say: This is a man who has not desired Allah for the blink of an eye. And when you looked at him in a matter of the Hereafter, you would say: This is a man who has not desired this world for the blink of an eye."],[6334,"'Umar b. 'Abd al-'Aziz said to me: You have something in your heart against Ibn al-Zubayr. He said: I said: I have not seen anyone like him in intimate prayer, nor in prayer, nor harsher in the cause of Allah, nor more generous of soul."],[6335,"Yazid b. Mu'awiyah wrote to 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr: I have sent you a chain of silver, a shackle of gold, and a fetter of silver, and I have sworn that you will come to me in them. He threw the letter aside and said: [bahr al-basit] I will not soften a fingertip for other than the truth, until the stone softens for the tooth of the chewer."],[6336,"When Mu'awiyah died, 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr delayed obedience to Yazid b. Mu'awiyah and openly reviled him. That reached Yazid, so he sent orders that he be brought. It was said to Ibn al-Zubayr: He is having shackles made for you of gold; you will drape a garment over them and fulfill his oath, for reconciliation is better. He said: May Allah not fulfill his oath. Then he said: [bahr al-basit] I will not soften a fingertip for other than the truth, until the stone softens for the tooth of the chewer. Then he said: By Allah, a blow with a sword in honor is dearer to me than a blow with a whip in humiliation. Then he called people to himself and openly opposed Yazid b. Mu'awiyah. Yazid b. Mu'awiyah sent against him Muslim b. 'Uqbah al-Muzani with the army of the people of Syria, and ordered him to fight the people of Madinah, and when he finished that, to march to Makkah. Muslim b. 'Uqbah entered Madinah, and the remnants of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fled from him that day. He rampaged there and went to excess in killing. Then he left, and when he was partway to Makkah, he died and appointed Husayn b. Numayr al-Kindi as his successor, saying to him: O pack-saddle of a donkey, beware of the tricks of Quraysh and deal with them only with hypocrisy then severity. Husayn went on until he reached Makkah and fought Ibn al-Zubayr there for days."],[6338,"May Allah forgive you three times. By Allah, I knew you only as one who fasted much, prayed much, and maintained family ties. Indeed, by Allah, I do not hope, despite the evils you committed, that Allah will not punish you after them ever. Then he turned to me and said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever does an evil deed will be requited for it in this world. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6339,"'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan sent the head of 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr to Ibn Hazim in Khurasan, and he shrouded it and prayed over it. Al-Sha'bi said: He erred; one does not pray over a head."],[6340,"Peace be upon you, Abu Khubayb—he said it three times. I had forbidden you from this—he said it three times. You used to fast much, pray much, and maintain family ties. The stance of 'Abdullah b. 'Umar reached al-Hajjaj, so he had him brought down and cast into the Jewish graves. He sent to Asma' bt. Abi Bakr, who had lost her sight, ordering her to come to him, but she refused. He sent to her: You will come, or I will send someone to drag you by your forelock. She said: By Allah, I will not come to you until you send someone to drag me by my forelock. His messenger came and told him, and he said: Boy, hand me my horse's forelock. He mounted his mule and went to her, seething, until he reached her and said: How do you find what Allah has done to the enemy of Allah? She said: I find that you have ruined his worldly life and ruined your own Hereafter. As for what you used to taunt him with, Dhat al-Nitaqayn—yes, I had two waist-belts: one with which I covered the food of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from ants, and my other belt, which women must have. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: In Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer. As for the liar, we have seen him; as for the destroyer, you are he. Then he left. The narrations are sound that 'Abdullah b. al-Zubayr heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, entered upon him, and left his presence when he was eight years old. I will mention, by Allah's will, his reports that indicate that in this place, for what is recorded in his Musnad from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is more than seventy hadiths."],[6341,"That he came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was being cupped, and when he had finished he said, “O Abdullah, take this blood and pour it out where no one can see you.” When I had gone away from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I took the blood and drank it. Then when I returned to the Prophet ﷺ, he said, “What did you do, O Abdullah?” He said, “I put it in a place I thought was hidden from the people.” He said, “Perhaps you drank it?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Who commanded you to drink blood? Woe to you from the people, and woe to the people from you.”[1]"],[6342,"Whoever recites the Qur'an aloud or looking at it is given a tree in Paradise such that if a crow were to hatch beneath one of its leaves, and then that fledgling flew, old age would overtake it before it could cross that leaf."],[6343,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ twice in one day."],[6344,"He was asked: Which of the two sons of al-Zubayr was braver? He said: \"There is none of the two but a brave one. Both of them walked toward death while seeing it.\" In its chain there is a narrator who is abandoned."],[6345,"On the Day of the Trench, I and Umar b. Abi Salamah were on a tower. He would lower himself for me so I could look at the fighting, and I would lower myself for him so he could look at the fighting. I saw my father moving about in the salt marsh, charging at these once and charging at those once. When he returned, I said: O father, I saw you. He said: O my little son, did you really see me? I said: Yes. He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has today joined his parents for me.\""],[6346,"He said when Abdullah b. al-Zubayr was killed: I heard Abdullah b. al-Zubayr say: \"Whoever denies calamity, I do not deny it. It has been mentioned to me that Yahya b. Zakariyya was only killed because of an adulteress who was a slave girl.\""],[6347,"Abdullah b. al-Zubayr said to Abdullah b. Ja'far: \"Do you remember the day we met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I and you, and he carried me and left you?\""],[6348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the call to prayer.\" It was said: And why that? He said: \"They will have the longest necks of all people on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[6349,"I and Dharr al-Murhibi differed about al-Hajjaj. He said: A believer. And I said: A disbeliever."],[6350,"By Allah, I heard al-Hajjaj b. Yusuf say: How amazing is the servant of Hudhayl who claims that he recites a Qur'an from Allah. By Allah, it is nothing but rajaz poetry from the rajaz of the Bedouins. By Allah, if I had caught the servant of Hudhayl, I would have struck his neck."],[6351,"Ibn Umar witnessed Badr."],[6352,"We left the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day he died, and there was none among us except that he changed from what he was upon, except Umar and Abdullah b. Umar. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6353,"It is said he was buried at Fakhkh in the cemetery of the Muhajirun. He was buried in the year seventy-four, and on the day he died he was eighty-four years old."],[6354,"I said to a client of Ibn ʿUmar: How was the death of Ibn ʿUmar? He said: He disapproved of al-Ḥajjāj b. Yūsuf's actions in killing Ibn al-Zubayr, so he stood up to him and made him hear it. Al-Ḥajjāj said: Be silent, O old man, you have become senile. When they dispersed, al-Ḥajjāj ordered a man from the people of Syria, and he struck him with his spear on his leg. Then al-Ḥajjāj entered to visit him and said: If I knew who struck you, I would strike his neck. He said: \"You are the one who struck me.\" He said: How? He said: \"On the day you brought weapons into the sanctuary of Allah.\""],[6355,"Ibn ʿUmar said to him: \"You have killed me, and now you come to me as a visitor. Allah suffices as a judge between me and you.\" ʿUmara is weak."],[6356,"ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar came to al-Baṣra as a warrior heading to Fāris. He came to it and died in Makkah in the year 74."],[6357,"My father instructed me to bury him outside the sanctuary, but we were not able, so we buried him in the sanctuary at Fakhkh in the cemetery of the Emigrants."],[6358,"“I held back my hand and did not advance, while the one who fights upon the truth is better.”[1]"],[6359,"The people did not doubt that Ibn ʿUmar \"pledged allegiance to ʿAlī on the condition that he would not fight alongside him, and ʿAlī accepted that from him.\""],[6360,"I and Ibn ʿUmar were presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Badr, and he deemed us too young, but we witnessed Uḥud."],[6361,"Regarding the opinion of Ibn ʿUmar, for he remained after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for sixty years, and nothing of the affair of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the affair of his Companions was hidden from him."],[6362,"Ibn ʿUmar was in his time better than ʿUmar was in his time."],[6363,"I have not seen anyone more adherent to the first matter than ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar."],[6364,"If I were to testify for anyone that he is from the people of Paradise, I would testify for Ibn ʿUmar."],[6365,"\"You have spoken the truth, my son, but I testify that his father was more beloved of the people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than your father, and he was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you.\" Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. If someone imagines that this virtue is for Usama, let him know that I only included this hadith for two reasons: one of them is ʿUmar's testimony regarding his son that Usama did not witness any scene except that he witnessed it, and this is among the most excellent virtues of Ibn ʿUmar; the second is that the two Shaykhs have included most of what has been narrated of the virtues of Ibn ʿUmar according to their conditions from the musnads, so I strive to obtain a sound hadith with a connected chain that they did not include. Authentic."],[6366,"\"I pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ twice on the day of Hudaybiyah. 'Umar saw people gathered and said, 'Go and see what they are up to.' When I saw that the Prophet ﷺ was pledging allegiance on the verge of death, I pledged allegiance to him as well. Then I returned to 'Umar and informed him, and he came and pledged allegiance after me. This is due to the virtues of Ibn 'Umar, who was not asked to leave, and 'Ubaidullah ibn 'Umar Al-'Umari (may Allah have mercy on him) was only mentioned for poor memory.\""],[6367,"None of us who attained the world but that it swayed him and he swayed with it, except ʿAbd Allah b. ʿUmar."],[6368,"Ibn Umar entered the Kaaba, and I heard him say while prostrating: 'You know what prevents me from vying with Quraysh over this worldly life except fear of You.'"],[6369,"Ibn Umar was the best of this nation."],[6370,"I heard Ali ibn Hussein saying, \"Indeed, Ibn Umar is the most ascetic of the people and has the most accurate opinion.\""],[6371,"Al-Dhahabi commented on it in the Talkhis."],[6372,"There was no one among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ who, when he heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was more cautious not to add to it or subtract from it than Ibn Umar. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6373,"I recited this verse: 'You will not attain righteousness until you spend from what you love' [Al Imran 92], and I remembered what Allah Almighty had given me. I found nothing dearer to me than my slave girl Radiyyah, so I said: 'She is free for the sake of Allah ﷻ.' Were it not that I do not go back on anything I have devoted to Allah ﷻ, I would have married her. Then Nafi' married her, and she became the mother of his child."],[6374,"If you saw Ibn Umar following the traces of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, you would say: 'This is a madman.'"],[6375,"Abdullah ibn Umar accepted Islam before his father."],[6376,"A man asked him about a matter, and he said: 'I have no knowledge of it.' When the man turned away, Ibn Umar said: 'How well Ibn Umar spoke: he was asked about what he did not know, so he said I have no knowledge of it.'"],[6377,"And Rafi' b. Khadij b. Rafi' b. 'Adi b. Zayd b. Jusham b. Harithah b. al-Harith b. al-Khazraj b. 'Amr, who is al-Nabit b. Malik b. Aws. Rafi' witnessed Uhud, the Trench, and all the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Rafi' was struck on the day of Uhud by an arrow in his collarbone, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'If you wish, I will remove the arrow and leave the velvet, and I will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr.' Rafi' left it because of the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and for a long time he felt nothing from it. When he laughed heartily, it would show. Then, during the caliphate of Uthman, that wound reopened and he died from it. This is not authentic, and its meaning is not sound."],[6378,"Rafi' b. Khadij al-Harithi, whose kunya was Abu Abdullah, died in Madinah in the year seventy-four."],[6379,"I saw Ibn Umar standing between the two legs of the bier of Rafi' b. Khadij."],[6380,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed him on the day of Uhud and placed him among the archers. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6381,"He said: 'I went on seven military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and nine with Zayd b. Harithah, whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed as commander over us.'"],[6382,"And Salamah b. al-Akwa' was given the kunya Abu Sinan. He died in Madinah in the year seventy-four."],[6383,"Malik b. Sinan b. Tha'laba b. 'Ubayd b. al-Abjar, whose name was Khudra b. 'Awf, and he is the father of Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Sa'd b. Malik."],[6384,"From Umm 'Abd al-Rahman bt. Abi Sa'id, from her father Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wounded in his face on the day of Uhud. My father Malik b. Sinan met him, licked the blood from his face with his mouth, then swallowed it. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at one whose blood has mingled with my blood, let him look at Malik b. Sinan.\" Its chain is obscure."],[6385,"And Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, Sa'd b. Malik b. Sinan b. Tha'laba b. 'Ubayd b. al-Abjar, whose name was Khudra b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj. Qatada b. al-Nu'man was his maternal brother. And Abu Sa'id al-Khudri died in the year seventy-four."],[6386,"\"I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq.\" Ibn 'Umar said: \"He was then fifteen years old.\" Ibn 'Umar said: \"Abu Sa'id also witnessed the Battle of the Trench and the battles after that.\""],[6387,"I was presented to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Uhud when I was thirteen years old. My father took me by the hand and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, he is big-boned, even though he is a muezzin.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ raised his gaze to me and lowered it, then said: \"Send him back.\" So he sent me back."],[6388,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri died in the year seventy-four."],[6389,"Talk to one another, for one hadith reminds of another."],[6390,"My father said to me: \"I have grown old and my companions and my group have gone, so take my hand.\" He said: So he leaned on me until he came to the farthest part of al-Baqi', a place where no one was buried. Then he said: \"O my son, when I die, bury me here. Do not pitch a tent over me, do not walk with me with fire, let no wailing woman weep over me, do not inform anyone of my death, take me through the lane of 'Amqa, and let your walking be at a trot.\" He died on Friday. I disliked informing the people because he had forbidden me, so they came to me and said: \"When will you take him out?\" I said: \"When I finish preparing him, I will take him out.\" He said: So the people filled al-Baqi'. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6391,"We said to Abu Sa'id: \"You tell us wonderful hadiths, and we fear that we may add or subtract, so if only we could write them down.\" He said: \"You will never write it down, and you will never make it a Qur'an, but memorize from us as we memorized.\" Then another time he said: \"Take from us as we took from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6392,"On the day of Uhud, the Prophet ﷺ was wounded in his forehead. Malik b. Sinan, the father of Abu Sa'id, came to him, wiped the blood from the Prophet's ﷺ face, then swallowed it. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at one whose blood has mingled with my blood, let him look at Malik b. Sinan.\" Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us: Abu Ja'far Ahmad b. 'Abd al-Hamid al-Harithi narrated to us: Abu Usama narrated to us: Yazid b. 'Abd Allah narrated to me. And they both (al-Bukhari and Muslim) included it."],[6393,"Abu Bakr and 'Uthman, the two sons of Abu Shayba, narrated to us, they said: 'Abda b. Sulayman narrated to us, from Hisham b. 'Urwa, from Wahb b. Kaysan, who said: It was said to Jabir b. 'Abd Allah: \"O Abu 'Abd Allah...\""],[6394,"Jabir b. Abdullah b. Amr b. Haram b. Tha'labah b. Haram b. Ka'b b. Ghanm b. Ka'b b. Salamah b. Sa'd b. Ali b. Asad b. Saridah b. Yazid b. Jusham b. al-Khazraj, and he was given the kunyah Abu Abdullah."],[6395,"I heard Abu Nu'aym say: \"Jabir b. Abdullah died in the year seventy-nine.\""],[6396,"Jabir b. Abdullah witnessed al-Aqabah among the seventy of the Ansar who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ there, and he was among the youngest of them that day. He wanted to witness Badr, but his father left him behind to care for his sisters, who were nine, and he also left him behind when he went out to Uhud. He witnessed the battles after that."],[6397,"I was drawing water for my companions on the day of Badr from the well."],[6398,"He said: \"I was drawing water for my companions on the day of Badr from the well.\" Muhammad b. Umar said: \"This is a mistake from the narration of the people of Iraq regarding Jabir and Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, making them among those who witnessed Badr. Neither Musa b. Uqbah, nor Muhammad b. Ishaq, nor Abu Ma'shar, nor anyone who narrated the sirah reported that.\""],[6399,"Jabir b. Abdullah came to us with his head and beard dyed yellow."],[6400,"I entered upon al-Hajjaj and did not greet him."],[6401,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sought forgiveness for me on the night of al-Aqabah twenty-five times."],[6402,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on twenty-one military expeditions, and I witnessed nineteen with him. The last expedition the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went on was Tabuk."],[6403,"Others said he was given the kunyah Abu Talhah."],[6404,"From his father and Muhammad b. al-Hijazi al-Hajabi, they said: \"Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani died in Madinah in the year seventy-eight, and he was eighty-five years old.\""],[6405,"Zayd b. Khalid al-Juhani was given the kunyah Abu Abd al-Rahman. He died in Madinah in the year seventy-eight, and he was eighty-five."],[6406,"Asma' bt. 'Umays gave birth to 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far b. Abi Talib in the land of Abyssinia, and he died in the year eighty, and that was the day he died at the age of eighty years."],[6407,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"For the people there is one emigration, but for you there are two.\""],[6408,"That 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr and 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far pledged allegiance to the Prophet ﷺ when they were seven years old, and that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw them he smiled and stretched out his hand and accepted their pledge. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6409,"If only you could have seen me, 'Ubayd Allah, and Qutham while we were playing when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by us. He said: \"Lift this one up to me.\" So he placed me in front of him, and he said to Qutham: \"Lift this one up to me.\" So he placed him behind him. Then he supplicated for us. 'Ubayd Allah was dearer to 'Abbas than Qutham, but he was not too shy before his uncle. He said: I said: \"What happened to Qutham?\" He said: \"He was martyred.\" He said: I said: \"Allah and His Messenger know best what is good.\""],[6410,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died when he was ten years old."],[6411,"'Abd Allah b. Ja'far went as a delegate to Mu'awiya, and he ordered for him two million dirhams."],[6412,"Ziyad entered upon Abdullah Ibn Ja'far speaking in five paragraphs. He gave him and he started saying, \"We asked him a great deal and he gave us more than what we desired and increased it and improved it, then improved it again, then we returned and he improved it again, and I continued to go back to him repeatedly. I do not return to this world except that he smiled at me in amusement and folded the pillow.\" Al-Bukhari and Muslim agreed upon hearing Abdullah Ibn Ja'far Ibn Abu Talib from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was ten years old, and I remember by the will of Allah, in this place stating what they agreed upon with their chains of narrators."],[6413,"I saw on the Prophet ﷺ two garments dyed with saffron, a cloak, and a turban. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6414,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the price of a dog and the earnings of a cupper. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6415,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ command a man, saying: \"Ask Allah for pardon and well-being in this world and the Hereafter.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6416,"What is between the navel and the knee is 'awrah."],[6417,"The best of its women is Maryam bt. 'Imran, and the best of its women is Khadija bt. Khuwaylid."],[6418,"\"وَاثِلَةُ بْنُ الْأَسْقَعِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الْعُزَّى بْنِ عَبْدِ يَالِيلَ بْنِ نَاشِبِ بْنِ غَيْرَةَ بْنِ سَعْدِ بْنِ لَيْثٍ قَدِ اخْتَلَفُوا فِي كُنْيَتِهِ\" translates to \"Wathila bin Al-Asqaa bin Abdul Azza bin Abdul Yaleel bin Naseeb bin Ghayrah bin Saad bin Laith, their nickname differed.\""],[6419,"Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in which there is no error, no addition, and no forgetfulness. He said: \"Did any of you recite anything from the Qur'an tonight?\" We said: \"Yes, but we are not memorizers of it.\" He said: \"This Qur'an is written among you; you do not fail to memorize it, yet you claim that you add and subtract. So how about hadiths we heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, which perhaps we heard only once? It is enough for you if we bring you the hadith according to its meaning.\" It has also been said that his kunya was Abu Qirsafa. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6420,"Do not fast Ramadan during travel; whoever fasts it must make it up. Abu al-Fayd said: I met Abu Qirsafa Wathilah b. al-Asqa and asked him, and he said, \"If I fasted and fasted and fasted, I would not make it up.\""],[6421,"\"Wathila ibn al-Asqa' is known as Abu Qirsaftah. He had a house in Basra and it was said that his nickname was Abu Shaddad.\""],[6422,"I met Wathila ibn al-Asqa' and said, \"How are you, Abu Shaddad?\""],[6423,"Wathilah b. al-Asqa died at the age of one hundred and five years, and that was in the year eighty-three."],[6424,"I heard Yahya b. Ma'in say, \"Wathilah b. al-Asqa died in the year eighty-three, and he was one hundred and five years old.\""],[6425,"When my father prayed the morning prayer, he would sit facing the qiblah until the sun rose; often I would speak to him about a need and he would not speak to me. I said, \"What is this?\" He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever prays the morning prayer, then recites Qul huwa Allahu ahad one hundred times before speaking to anyone, his sins of a year are forgiven.\""],[6426,"When I embraced Islam, I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to me, \"Go and wash with water and sidr, and remove from yourself the hair of disbelief.\" And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over my head."],[6427,"I heard al-Abbas b. Muhammad al-Duri say, \"Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, Abu Mu'awiyah.\""],[6428,"Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, and the name of Abu Awfa is Alqamah b. Khalid b. al-Harith b. Abi Usayd b. Rifa'ah b. Tha'labah b. Hawazin b. Aslam b. Afsa. Abdullah is given the kunya Abu Mu'awiyah. The first battle that Abdullah b. Abi Awfa witnessed with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, according to us, was Khaybar, and then the battles after that. Abdullah b. Abi Awfa remained in Madinah until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, then he moved to Kufa and settled there when the Muslims settled there, and he built a house in the Aslam quarter. He had lost his sight, and he died in Kufa in the year eighty-six."],[6429,"I heard Abu Nu'aym say, \"Abdullah b. Abi Awfa died in the year eighty-seven or eighty-eight.\""],[6430,"It has also been said that the last of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to die in Kufa was Abdullah b. Abi Awfa."],[6431,"I saw on the hand of Ibn Abi Awfa a wound. I said, \"When did you get this?\" He said, \"On the day of Hunayn.\" I said, \"You witnessed Hunayn?\" He said, \"Yes, and before that.\""],[6432,"From Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, \"He was one of the Companions of the Tree, one thousand and four hundred, and Aslam was an eighth of the Muhajirun that day.\""],[6433,"I came to Abdullah b. Abi Awfa, the Companion of the Prophet ﷺ, and greeted him while he had lost his sight. He said to me, \"Who are you?\" I said, \"I am Sa'id b. Jumhan.\" He said, \"What has happened to your father?\" I said, \"The Azariqah killed him.\" He said, \"May Allah curse the Azariqah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us that they are the dogs of Hell.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6434,"His name was Huzn, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named him Sahl."],[6435,"I said to Sahl ibn Saad al-Sa'idi, \"O father of Abbas.\""],[6436,"I heard Abu Nu'aym say: 'Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi died in the year eighty-eight.'"],[6437,"From Sahl b. Sa'd al-Ansari, who had reached the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was fifteen years old."],[6438,"I saw al-Hajjaj b. Yusuf striking Abbas b. Sahl b. Sa'd during the governorship of Ibn al-Zubayr. Sahl came out, wearing a yellow waist-wrapper and cloak. When he approached, al-Hajjaj gestured with his hand to stop [the striking] of his son."],[6439,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while they say this and that. If I had arrived, they would not have heard anyone say, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ...' [The hadith is] authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[6440,"I saw Sahl b. Sa'd with a white beard and he had trimmed his mustache."],[6441,"He was present with the Prophet ﷺ on the day of..."],[6442,"Sahl b. Sa'd al-Sa'idi, whose kunya was Abu al-Abbas, died in Madinah in the year ninety-one. He was the last of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ to die in Madinah, and he was one hundred years old."],[6443,"Abdullah b. Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, whose kunya was Abu Muhammad, died in the year seventy-one, at the age of eighty-one. The name of Abu Hadrad was Salama, and he was from Banu Rifa'a, a clan of Aslam."],[6444,"I said to Anas b. Malik, 'Did you witness Badr?' He said, 'May your mother be bereft of you! How could I be absent from Badr?'"],[6445,"I saw Anas b. Malik with a seal on his neck; al-Hajjaj had sealed it, intending to humiliate him by that."],[6446,"Anas b. Malik died in the year ninety-three."],[6447,"Anas b. Malik b. al-Nadr b. Damdam b. Zayd b. Haram b. Jundub b. Amir b. Ghanm b. Adi b. al-Najjar; his mother was Umm Sulaym bt. Milhan."],[6448,"The Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah when I was ten years old, and he died when I was twenty."],[6449,"Thabit al-Bunani and I entered upon Anas b. Malik, and Thabit said, “O Abu Hamzah...”"],[6450,"“This I heard from the Prophet ﷺ, so I wrote it down and presented it to him.” The hadith is rejected."],[6451,"When Anas entered upon al-Hajjaj, he ordered that his neck be struck. Then he said, “O people of Syria, do you know this man? This is the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Then he said, “Do you know why I struck his neck?” They said, “The governor knows best.” He said, “He was among the affliction in the first fitnah and he harbored rancor in the last fitnah.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6452,"Abd al-Malik said, “Write to al-Hajjaj: O boy, woe to you! I feared that no one would be set right at your hands. When this letter of mine reaches you, rise and apologize to Anas b. Malik.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6453,"Anas said, “O Abu Muhammad, take from me, for I took from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took from Allah, Mighty and Exalted, and you will never take from anyone more trustworthy than me.”"],[6454,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ he would say, “or as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6455,"I said to Musa b. Anas, “How many expeditions did the Prophet ﷺ undertake?” He said, “He undertook twenty-three expeditions, and eight expeditions in which he stayed for months.” I said, “How many expeditions did Anas undertake with the Prophet ﷺ?” He said, “Eight expeditions.”"],[6456,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A man said, “Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” He became very angry and said, “By Allah, not everything we narrate to you did we hear from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but some of us would narrate to others, and we do not accuse one another.”"],[6457,"Hamal b. Malik b. al-Nabighah b. Jabir b. Ubayd b. Rabi'ah b. Ka'b b. al-Harith b. Kathir b. Hind b. Tabikhah b. Lihyan b. Hudhayl al-Hudhali. He had a house in al-Basrah."],[6458,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave judgment concerning the fetus. Hamal b. Malik b. al-Nabighah al-Hudhali stood up and said, “O Commander of the Believers, I was between two slave girls, meaning co-wives. I went out and one of them struck the other with the pole of her tent and killed her and killed what was in her belly. The Prophet ﷺ gave judgment concerning the fetus with a ghurrah, a male or female slave.” Umar said, “Allah is greater. Had we not heard this, we would not have judged otherwise.”"],[6459,"Abu Talib fathered Aqeel, Ja'far, and 'Ali, each of them being ten years older than the next, in succession."],[6460,"Aqeel b. Abi Talib came to Kufa, Basra, and Syria, and died during the caliphate of Mu'awiya."],[6461,"Among the blessings of Allah upon 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and the good that Allah willed for him, was that Quraysh was afflicted by a severe famine. Abu Talib had many dependents, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his uncle al-'Abbas, who was among the wealthiest of Banu Hashim: 'O Abu al-Fadl, your brother Abu Talib has many dependents, and the people have been struck by this famine as you see. Come with us to him so that we may relieve him of some of his dependents. I will take one of his sons, and you take another, and we will support them on his behalf.' Al-'Abbas said, 'Yes.' So they both went until they came to Abu Talib and said, 'We want to relieve you of some of your dependents until the people are relieved of what they are suffering.' Abu Talib said to them, 'If you leave 'Aqeel for me, then do as you wish.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took 'Ali and gathered him to himself, and al-'Abbas took Ja'far and gathered him to himself. 'Ali remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until Allah sent him as a prophet, and he followed him and believed him. Al-'Abbas took Ja'far, and Ja'far remained with al-'Abbas until he became Muslim and no longer needed him."],[6462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Aqeel b. Abi Talib: 'O Abu Yazid, I love you with two loves: a love for your kinship to me, and a love for what I knew of my uncle's love for you.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6463,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say to 'Aqeel: 'I love you, O 'Aqeel, with two loves: a love for you, and a love for Abu Talib's love for you.' The clarification of these two hadiths is in the hadith that..."],[6464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked out from a house, and with him were his two uncles al-'Abbas and Hamza, and 'Ali, Ja'far, and 'Uqayl, while they were in a field working. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his two uncles: 'Choose from among these?' One of them said, 'I have chosen Ja'far,' and the other said, 'I have chosen 'Ali.' He said: 'You both have chosen, and Allah has chosen 'Ali for me.'"],[6465,"Quraysh came to Abu Talib and said, 'Your nephew harms us in our gathering and our assembly, so forbid him from harming us.' He said to me, 'O 'Aqeel, bring Muhammad.' So I went to him and brought him out from a small plant called jils - Talha said it is a small plant - and he came at noon in the intense heat, seeking shade by walking in it because of the intense heat of the ground. So we came to them, and Abu Talib said, 'Your cousins claim that you harm them in their gathering and their assembly, so desist from that.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky and said, 'Do you see this sun?' They said, 'Yes.' He said, 'I am no more able to abandon that than you are able to take a flame from it.' Abu Talib said, 'We have never found our nephew to lie, so go back.'"],[6466,"'Aqeel b. Abi Talib came to us and married a woman from Banu Jusham b. Sa'd, and he consummated the marriage. Then he came out, and they said, 'With harmony and children.' He said, 'Rather, say: May Allah bless you and may He bestow blessings upon you.'"],[6467,"Ma'qil b. Yasar b. 'Abd Allah b. Harraq b. Lu'ayy b. Ka'b b. 'Abd b. Thawr b. Hadma b. Latim b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr b. Add b. Tabikha. He is given the kunya Abu 'Ali, and he had a plot of land in Basra. Ma'qil b. Yasar died during the governorship of Ibn Ziyad in the year fifty-eight."],[6468,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to judge among my people, so I said, 'I do not know how to judge.' He said, 'Decide between them.' I said, 'I do not know how to decide.' He said, 'Judge between them, for Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is with the judge as long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6469,"Act according to the Book of Allah and do not deny anything from it. Whatever is unclear to you from it, ask the people of knowledge about it, and they will inform you. Believe in the Torah and the Gospel, and believe in the Furqan, for in it is the clear explanation, and it is the intercessor and the one whose intercession is accepted, and the advocate and the confirmer."],[6470,"\"O commander of the faithful, Asbahan has been hit on the head.\""],[6471,"\"Abdullah son of Mughaffal, son of Abd Nahim, son of Afif, son of Suhaim, son of Rabia, son of Adi, son of Tha'laba, son of Dhuayb, son of Saad, son of Adi, son of Uthman, son of Amr, son of Add, son of Tabikha.\""],[6472,"And 'Abd Allah b. Mughaffal al-Muzani, whose kunya is Abu Sa'id - and he mentioned this lineage and added to it: His mother was al-'Atila bt. Mu'awiya b. Qurra b. Muzayna, and he had a house in Basra near the mosque."],[6473,"\"When I die, put camphor in the last of my washing, and shroud me in two cloaks and a shirt, for that is what was done with the Prophet ﷺ.\" [Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis]"],[6474,"\"Ka'b b. Zuhayr and Bujayr b. Zuhayr b. Abi Sulma — and Abi Sulma's name is Rabi'a b. Riyah b. Qurt b. al-Harith b. Qatada b. Halawa b. Tha'laba b. Thawr b. Hadma b. Latim b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr b. Add b. Tabikha — both came as a delegation to the Prophet ﷺ, embraced Islam, and accompanied him.\""],[6476,"Ka'b b. Zuhayr b. Abi Sulma recited to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the mosque: \"Su'ad has departed, and my heart today is smitten, enslaved by her, unredeemed, shackled.\""],[6477,"Ka'b b. Zuhayr recited to the Prophet ﷺ \"Banat Su'ad\" in his mosque in Madinah. When he reached his words: \"Indeed the Messenger is a sword by which light is sought, a drawn blade from among the swords of Allah, among a band of Quraysh — their spokesman said in the belly of Makkah, when they embraced Islam: 'They departed'\" — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ signaled with his sleeve to the people to listen to him. He said: Bujayr b. Zuhayr had written to his brother Ka'b b. Zuhayr b. Abi Sulma, frightening him and calling him to Islam, and he said in it some verses: \"Who will convey to Ka'b: Will you accept that which you persist in falsely, while it is more resolute? Turn to Allah alone, not al-'Uzza nor al-Lat, then you will be saved when salvation comes and you will be secure. At a day when none will be saved, and none will escape the Fire except one pure of heart, a Muslim. The religion of Zuhayr — and it is nothing — is false, and the religion of Abi Sulma is forbidden to me.\""],[6478,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah upon his return from al-Ta'if, Bujayr b. Zuhayr b. Abi Salma wrote to his brother Ka'b b. Zuhayr b. Abi Sulma, informing him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ \"had killed men in Makkah who had satirized and harmed him,\" and that the remaining poets of Quraysh — Ibn al-Ziba'ra and Hubayra b. Abi Wahb — had fled in every direction. \"So if you have any need for yourself, hasten to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he does not kill anyone who comes to him repentant. But if you do not do so, then save yourself by any means of escape.\" Ka'b had composed some verses in which he had spoken against the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so much so that they were reported from him and became well-known. What he said was: \"Will you two convey a message from me to Bujayr? And woe to you, is there any good in what I said? You told me — though I was not going to do it — upon what basis, woe to you, did someone other than you guide you? To a created being for whom you will find neither mother nor father, and you will not find a father for yourself upon him. If you do not do it, you will not be regretful, nor will you say, when you stumble, 'May he be raised!' With it the trusted one gave you a satisfying cup to drink, and the trusted one made you drink from it and gave you a second draught.\" He said: Ka'b only said \"the trusted one\" because Quraysh used to call the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that. When this reached Ka'b, the earth became constrained for him, he feared for his life, and his enemies among those present began to spread rumors about him, saying, \"He is as good as killed.\" When he found no way out, he composed his ode in which he praises the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned his fear and the rumors the slanderers spread about him. Then he set out until he arrived in Madinah and stayed with a man from Juhayna with whom he had an acquaintance, as was mentioned to me. The man brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he had prayed the morning prayer, and he prayed with the people. Then he pointed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"This is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; go to him and ask for protection.\" It was mentioned to me that he went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and placed his hand in his, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not recognize him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Ka'b b. Zuhayr has come to ask for your protection, repentant and Muslim. Will you accept him if I bring him to you?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I am Ka'b b. Zuhayr.\" [Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis]"],[6479,"\"Qurra b. Iyas b. Hilal b. Rabab b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Dhu'ayb b. Aws b. Sawwara b. 'Amr b. Sariya b. Tha'laba b. Dinar b. Sulayman b. Aws b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr — he is Abu Mu'awiya b. Qurra. He had a house in al-Basra in the presence of al-'Awfa. The Azariqa killed him along with Ibn 'Ubays in the year sixty-four.\""],[6480,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I take a sheep to slaughter it, and I feel compassion for it.\" He said, \"And the sheep — if you show it compassion, may Allah show you compassion.\""],[6481,"\"The excellence of 'A'isha over other women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.\""],[6482,"\"Whoever says 'Allahu akbar' once at sunset on the seashore, raising his voice, Allah will give him ten good deeds for every drop in the sea, wipe away ten evil deeds from him, and raise him ten degrees, the distance between each two degrees being a hundred years' journey for a swift horse.\""],[6483,"\"'A'idh b. 'Amr b. Hilal b. 'Ubayd b. Rawaha b. Labiba b. 'Adi b. 'Amir b. 'Abd Allah b. Tha'laba b. Hadma b. Latim b. 'Uthman b. 'Amr. He is given the kunya Abu Hubayra. He died during the governorship of Ibn Ziyad and had a well-known house in al-Basra.\""],[6484,"I was struck by an arrow in my face while I was fighting in front of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn. When the blood flowed over my face, beard, and chest, \"the Prophet ﷺ reached out and wiped the blood from my face and chest up to my two nipples, then prayed for me.\" Hajraj said: 'A'idh used to tell us about that during his lifetime. When he died and we washed him, we looked at what he used to describe to us of the trace of the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ up to the end of what he used to tell us on his chest, and there was a flowing white blaze like the blaze of a horse. Its chain contains two unknown narrators."],[6485,"\"The rock and the 'ajwa date are from Paradise.\""],[6486,"From 'Urwah, \"Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from the Ansar, from the Banu al-Khazraj: 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy ibn Salul.\" 'Urwah said, \"And he is 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy b. Malik b. Salim b. Ghanm b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj.\""],[6487,"\"'Abd Allah b. 'Abd Allah b. Ubayy ibn Salul was martyred on the day of al-Yamamah in the year twelve.\""],[6488,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, shall I kill my father?\" He said, \"Do not kill your father.\""],[6489,"That he sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ to kill his father, and he forbade him from that."],[6490,"That two of his teeth were injured on the day of Uhud with the Prophet ﷺ. He said, \"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to have two teeth made of gold.\""],[6491,"The translation of the given phrase \"ابْنُ إِسْحَاقَ وَسَلُولُ امْرَأَةٌ وَهِيَ أُمُّ أَبِي وَهُمْ بَنُو الْحُكْبَلَى\" is: \"Ishaaq's son along with Salul, a woman who is my mother, and they are the children of Al-Hukbla.\" (Note: The phrase \"عاصم بن سليمان الكوري كذاب\" does not seem to be a part of the given phrase. If you want it translated, it means \"Aasim ibn Sulayman Al-Koree is a liar\".)"],[6492,"\"And al-Nu'man b. Qawqal, and Qawqal's name was Malik b. Tha'labah b. Da'd b. Fahm b. Tha'labah b. Ghanim b. Salim b. 'Awf b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. al-Khazraj. And al-Qawaqil are the kinsfolk of 'Ubadah b. al-Samit.\""],[6493,"\"From al-Nu'man b. Qawqal.\""],[6494,"That he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you think that if I pray the prescribed prayers, fast Ramadan, deem lawful what is lawful, deem unlawful what is unlawful, and do not add anything to that, will I enter Paradise?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"By Allah, I will not add anything to that.\""],[6495,"\"Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: 'Itban b. Malik.\" He said, \"Some affliction befell my eyesight, so I sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ...\" the hadith."],[6496,"\"We were with Anas b. Malik, and he said to his son...\""],[6497,"\"Regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from the Ansar: Ziyad b. Labid b. Tha'labah b. Sinan b. 'Amir b. 'Adi b. Umayyah b. Bayadah b. 'Amir b. Zurayq. His mother was the daughter of 'Abd Mudarrib b. al-Harith b. Zayd b. 'Ubayd b. 'Amr b. 'Awf. And he died at the beginning of the caliphate of Mu'awiyah, according to what I heard from the history of Shabab.\""],[6498,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was narrating to his companions, and he was saying, \"The time of knowledge has gone.\" I said, \"By my father and mother, how can the time of knowledge go while we recite the Qur'an and teach it to our sons, and our sons teach it to their sons until the Hour stands?\" He said, \"May your mother be bereft of you, O Ibn Labid! I considered you one of the most understanding of the people of Madinah. Do not the Jews and Christians recite the Torah and the Gospel, yet they do not benefit from them at all?\""],[6499,"From 'Urwah, regarding the naming of those from the Ansar who attended Badr and al-'Aqabah: 'Umarah b. Hazm b. Zayd b. Lawdhan b. 'Amr b. 'Abd 'Awf b. Ghanim b. Malik b. al-Najjar. He was martyred on the Day of Yamamah, from the Ansar, then from Banu Malik b. al-Najjar: 'Umarah b. Hazm.'"],[6500,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me sitting on a grave. He said: \"Get down from the grave; do not harm the occupant of the grave, and he will not harm you.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6501,"\"Yazid b. Thabit b. al-Dahhak b. Zayd b. Lawzan b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Ghanim b. Malik b. al-Najjar. His mother and the mother of his brother Zayd b. Thabit was al-Nawwar bt. Malik b. 'Amir b. 'Adi b. al-Najjar. He attended Badr and was martyred on the Day of Yamamah.\""],[6502,"He was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions when a funeral procession appeared. When they saw it, \"he stood up, and his companions stood up as well, and they remained standing until it had gone far. I think it was only a Jew or a Jewess.\""],[6503,"From his paternal uncle Yazid b. Thabit, that they went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one day with a funeral procession until they reached al-Baqi'. He said: \"What is this?\" They said: \"This is so-and-so, a freedwoman of Banu so-and-so.\" He recognized her and said: \"Why did you not inform me of her?\" They said: \"We buried her at noon, and you were taking a nap and sleeping, so we did not like to inform you of her.\" He stood up, and the people lined up behind him, and he said the takbir over her four times. Then he said: \"Let no one among you die without informing me, for my prayer for them is a mercy.\""],[6504,"\"Busr b. Abi Artat'ah, and the name of Abu Artat'ah is 'Umayr b. 'Amr b. 'Uwaymir b. 'Imran b. al-Halbas b. Sayyar b. Nizar b. Ma'is b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy.\""],[6505,"\"Busr b. Abi Artat'ah died during the caliphate of Mu'awiyah, and he had become old in age until he became senile. He was given the kunyah Abu 'Abd al-Rahman. He died in Madinah, while his children were in Basra.\""],[6506,"He used to \"supplicate: O Allah, make good the outcome of all our affairs, and protect us from the disgrace of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter.\""],[6507,"\"Al-Mustawrid b. Shaddad b. 'Amr b. Hisl b. al-Ahabb b. Habib b. 'Amr b. Shayban b. Muharib b. Fihr b. Malik. He died in Egypt during the governorship of Mu'awiyah.\""],[6508,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The likeness of this world in comparison to the Hereafter is only as when one of you dips his finger in the sea; let him see what it brings back.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6509,"\"Khufaf b. Iyma' b. Rahadah b. Harbah b. Khufaf b. Harithah b. Ghifar. His father Iyma' b. Rahadah had accepted Islam and was among the leaders of his people. Khufaf b. Iyma' attended al-Hudaybiyah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6510,"Abu Dharr said: \"We came to our people, Ghifar, and some of them accepted Islam before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived in Madinah. Iyma' b. Rahadah used to lead them in prayer, and he was their chief.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6511,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicating in the Morning Prayer: “O Allah, curse Banu Lihyan, Ri‘l, Dhakwan, and ‘Usayyah—they disobeyed Allah and His Messenger—and Ghifar—may Allah forgive them—and Aslam—may Allah keep them safe.”"],[6512,"From Abu Basrah, a group of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reported that they heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"Indeed, Allah Almighty has increased your prayer, so pray it from the time after the Isha prayer until the Fajr prayer, and it is the Witr prayer.\" Abu Nasrah al-Ghifari said, \"Abu Tamim and I were sitting, and Abu Dhar took my hand and we went to Abu Basrah. We found him at the door of the house of Amr. Abu Dhar said to him, 'O Abu Basrah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Indeed, Allah Almighty has increased your prayer, so pray it from the time after the Isha prayer until the Fajr prayer, and it is the Witr prayer'?' He replied, 'Yes.'\""],[6513,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “As for the child, he is your slave. When she gives birth, flog her one hundred lashes, and she is entitled to the dowry because he had made lawful her private parts.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6514,"It is also said: Kulthum b. Husayn b. ‘Ubayd b. Khalid—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed him as his deputy over Madinah when he set out for the conquest of Makkah.”"],[6515,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out for the conquest of Makkah, he appointed Abu Ruhm Kulthum b. Husayn al-Ghifari as his deputy over Madinah.” Sahih."],[6516,"That he heard Abu Ruhm Kulthum b. Husayn, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who pledged allegiance under the tree, say: I went on the campaign of Tabuk with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One night, I traveled with him while we were close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Drowsiness overcame us, and I kept waking up while my mount had drawn near the mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I began to keep my mount away from his, until sleep overpowered me on part of the road while we were in part of the night. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The dearest of my people to me that they should not stay behind from me are the Muhajirun of Quraysh, the Ansar, Aslam, and Ghifar.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6517,"Hudhayfah b. Usayd b. al-Aghwas b. Waqi‘ah b. Haram b. Ghifar—and it is said Ibn Usayd b. Khalid b. al-Aghwaz—his kunyah is Abu Sarihah. He moved from Madinah to Kufah and died there."],[6518,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “There will come the wind in which Allah takes the soul of every believer, then the rising of the sun from the west, and that is the sign which Allah, may He be exalted, mentioned in His Book…” the hadith."],[6519,"The Prophet ﷺ used to bring near two white sheep with black markings and slaughter one of them, saying: “O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and the family of Muhammad.” He would bring the other near and say: “O Allah, this is on behalf of my Ummah—whoever bears witness to Your Oneness and to my conveying the message.”"],[6520,"“‘Attab b. Usayd b. Abi al-‘Is b. Umayyah b. ‘Abd Shams b. ‘Abd Manaf, and the mother of ‘Attab b. Usayd and Khalid b. Usayd is Zaynab bt. Abi ‘Amr b. Umayyah b. ‘Abd Shams. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed ‘Attab as governor over Makkah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while ‘Attab was his governor over Makkah. ‘Attab b. Usayd died in Makkah in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year thirteen.”"],[6521,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the night he drew near to Makkah during the campaign of the Conquest: “There are in Makkah four men of Quraysh whom I hold back from shirk and for whom I strongly desire Islam.” It was said: And who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “‘Attab b. Usayd, Jubayr b. Mut‘im, Hakim b. Hizam, and Suhayl b. ‘Amr.”"],[6522,"I heard ‘Attab b. Usayd, while he was leaning his back against the House of Allah, say: “By Allah, I have not obtained from this work of mine, which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ appointed me to, except two striped garments, and I clothed my freedman Kaysan with them.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6523,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the zakat on vines: “They are to be estimated as palm trees are estimated, then their zakat is to be paid as raisins just as the zakat on palm trees is paid as dates.”"],[6524,"And among the allies of Banu Hashim who were not from the people of Badr was Shaddad b. al-Had. Shaddad was a relative by marriage of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; Salma bt. 'Umays was with him, and he married her after Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib ؓ."],[6525,"A man from the Bedouins believed in the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"Shall I emigrate with you?\" The Prophet ﷺ enjoined his Companions to look after him. When the expedition of Khaybar or Hunayn took place, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired some booty and distributed it, and he allotted a share for him. He gave his Companions what he had allotted for him, and the man was tending their riding animals. When he came, they handed it over to him. He said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted it for you.\" He took it and went to him and said, \"O Muhammad, this is not what I followed you for. Rather, I followed you so that I might be shot here\"—and he pointed to his throat with an arrow—\"and die and enter Paradise.\" He said, \"If you are true to Allah, He will be true to you.\" They stayed a little while, then they advanced to fight the enemy. He was brought carried, having been struck by an arrow where he had pointed. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Is it he?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He was true to Allah, so He was true to him.\" The Prophet ﷺ shrouded him, then brought him forward and prayed over him. Among what appeared of his prayer over him was: \"O Allah, this is Your servant who went out as an emigrant in Your path and was killed as a martyr, and I am a witness over him.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6526,"Usama b. Zayd b. Haritha b. Sharahil b. Ka'b b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Yazid b. Imri' al-Qays al-Kalbi. Allah and His Messenger bestowed favor upon him. Ahmad b. Ya'qub informed me with this lineage: Musa b. Zakariyya narrated to us, Shabab narrated to us, and he added in it: His mother was Umm Ayman, the freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He died in Madinah at the end of Mu'awiya's caliphate, and he was sixty years old. He was given the kunya Abu Muhammad."],[6527,"The most beloved of my family to me is the one upon whom Allah has bestowed favor and upon whom I have bestowed favor: Usama."],[6528,"Usama is the most beloved of people to me."],[6529,"The date palm reached a thousand dirhams in the time of 'Uthman b. 'Affan. Usama b. Zayd went to a date palm, cut out its heart, and fed it to his mother. Someone said to him, \"What made you do this, when you see that the date palm has reached a thousand?\" He said, \"My mother asked me for it, and she does not ask me for anything I am able to do but that I give it to her.\""],[6530,"The inscription on the ring of Usama b. Zayd was \"The beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6531,"Usama b. Zayd was addressed as 'the commander' until he died. They would say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6532,"I was riding behind the Prophet ﷺ at 'Arafa."],[6533,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When a believer is praised to his face, faith grows in his heart.\""],[6534,"Abu Rafi' was a freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, belonging to al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib. When al-'Abbas embraced Islam, he gave him to the Prophet ﷺ. His name was Aslam, and it is also said Ibrahim. He embraced Islam before Badr, but he was residing in Makkah with al-'Abbas. He died after the killing of 'Uthman in the year thirty-five."],[6535,"The Prophet ﷺ sent 'Ali to Yemen and tied a banner for him. When he went on, he said, \"O Abu Rafi', catch up with him and do not leave him from behind. Let him stop and not turn around until I come to him.\" So he went to him and enjoined him with certain things, and said, \"O 'Ali, for Allah to guide a man through your hands is better for you than everything upon which the sun rises.\""],[6536,"He (Abu Raafi') informed him that he came with a letter from Quraysh to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: When I delivered the letter, Islam was cast into my heart. I said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I will never return to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I do not break a covenant, nor do I fail to return a messenger, but go back to them. If what is in your heart now remains in your heart, then come back.\" He said: So I returned to them, then I came back to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and embraced Islam. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6537,"\"Salman is one of us, the People of the House.\""],[6538,"\"Salman al-Farisi died in the year thirty-seven.\""],[6539,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ marked out the trench in the year of the Battle of the Confederates until he reached Madhahij. He allotted forty cubits for every ten men. The Muhajirun argued: Salman is from us. And the Ansar said: Salman is from us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Salman is one of us, the People of the House.\" Its chain is weak."],[6540,"Salman spoke the truth; Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Umar said: Tell us, O Abu Abd Allah. He said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining on a cushion. He tossed it to me, then said: \"O Salman, no Muslim enters upon his Muslim brother and he throws him a cushion out of honor for him except that Allah forgives him.\""],[6543,"\"The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever.\""],[6544,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I read in the Torah that the blessing of food is ablution before it and after it.\""],[6545,"Zayd ibn Saʿnah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out one day from the apartments, and with him was Ali ibn Abi Talib. A man came to him on his mount, like a Bedouin, and said: O Messenger of Allah, the village of Busra of Banu So-and-so has embraced Islam and entered into Islam. I had told them that if they embraced Islam, provision would come to them abundantly. A year of drought, hardship, and lack of rain has befallen them. I fear, O Messenger of Allah, that they may leave Islam out of greed just as they entered it out of greed. If you see fit to send them something to help them, do so. A man beside him, whom I think was Ali, looked at me and said: O Messenger of Allah, nothing of it remains. Zayd ibn Saʿnah said: I approached him and said: O Muhammad, will you sell me a known amount of dates from the orchard of Banu So-and-so, to be delivered at such-and-such a time? He said: \"No, O Jew, but I will sell you a known amount of dates to be delivered at such-and-such a time, and I will not specify the orchard of Banu So-and-so.\" I said: Yes. He made a deal with me. I loosened my money belt and gave him eighty mithqals of gold for a known amount of dates to be delivered at such-and-such a time. He gave it to the man and said: \"Be fair to them and help them with it.\" Zayd ibn Saʿnah said: When it was two or three days before the due date, I came to him and grabbed the collar of his shirt and his cloak, looked at him with a harsh face, and said: Will you not pay me my due, O Muhammad? By Allah, I have known you, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, as poor at repaying debts, delaying. I have had experience of mixing with you. I looked at Umar, and his eyes were rolling in his face like a revolving sphere. Then he looked at me and said: O enemy of Allah, do you say to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I hear and do to him what I see? By the One who sent him with the truth, were it not for what I fear of his strength, I would strike your head with my sword. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at Umar with calm and deliberation, then smiled and said: \"O Umar, he and I were in greater need of something other than this: that you command me to pay well and command him to demand well. Take him, O Umar, and give him his due, and add twenty saʿs of dates.\" I said: What is this increase, O Umar? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to increase you in place of my harshness toward you. I said: Do you know me, O Umar? He said: No, who are you? I said: Zayd ibn Saʿnah. He said: The rabbi? I said: The rabbi. He said: What made you do to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what you did and say to him what you said? I said: O Umar, there was no sign of prophethood that I did not recognize in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I looked at him except two that I had not tested in him: \"Does his forbearance overcome his ignorance, and does the intensity of ignorance against him only increase him in forbearance?\" I have now tested them. I call you to witness, O Umar, that I am pleased with Allah as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad ﷺ as Prophet. And I call you to witness that half of my wealth—for I am the wealthiest of them—is charity for the community of Muhammad ﷺ. Umar said: Or for some of them, for you cannot encompass them all. I said: Or for some of them. Zayd returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. He believed in him, affirmed him, pledged allegiance to him, and witnessed with him many battles. Then Zayd died in the expedition of Tabuk, advancing, not retreating. May Allah have mercy on Zayd."],[6546,"He said: \"Indeed I will tell you my name. My name was Qays, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Safinah.\" I said: Why did he name you Safinah? He said: He went out with his companions, and their baggage became heavy for them. He said: Spread your cloak. I spread it, and he put their baggage in it, then placed it on me and said: \"Carry, for you are nothing but a ship (safinah).\" He said: If I had carried that day the load of a camel or two or five or six, it would not have been heavy for me. The chain of transmission is authentic, but they did not record it. Sahih."],[6547,"\"That I serve the Prophet ﷺ as long as he lives.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6548,"That the ship of the Master of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I rode the sea and my ship in which I was broke. So I rode a plank from its planks, so the plank threw me into a place where lions were. So the lion came towards me wanting me, so I said, 'O Abu al-Harith, I am the slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ .' So he lowered his head and came towards me and pushed me with his shoulder until he took me out of the place where the lions were and put me on the road. And he made sounds, so I thought that he was bidding me farewell, so that was my last covenant with him.\""],[6549,"From Urwah: \"In naming the Muslims who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Aqabah from the Ansar, from al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Saʿd ibn al-Rabiʿ, and he was a naqib, and he witnessed Badr.\""],[6550,"From Ibn Shihab: \"In naming those who were martyred on the day of Uhud from the Ansar, from Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj: Saʿd ibn al-Rabiʿ.\""],[6551,"O deputy of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who is this? He said, \"This is the daughter of one who is better than me and you.\" He said, \"And who is better than me and you except the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" Abu Bakr said, \"A man who passed away during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and took his seat in Paradise, while I and you remained.\""],[6552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded Bilal to put his finger in his ear and said, \"It is louder for your voice.\" Bilal's adhan was in pairs and his iqamah was single, and \"Prayer has been established\" once. He used to give the adhan on Friday during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when the shade was like a shoelace. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the two Eids, he would take the road past the house of Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, then past the people of the tents, then he would begin with the prayer before the sermon, then he would say the takbir seven times in the first (rak'ah) before the recitation and five times in the second before the recitation, then he would address the people, then he would return by the other road, the road of Banu Zurayq. He slaughtered a sacrificial animal at the edge of al-Riqaq with his own hand using a blade, then he went out to the house of 'Ammar b. Yasir and the house of Abu Hurayrah in al-Balat. He used to go out to the two Eids walking and return walking, and he used to say the takbir between the parts of the sermon and say the takbir frequently during the sermon, and he would deliver the sermon leaning on a staff. When Bilal said the takbir for the adhan, he would face the qiblah, then say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, ashhadu an la ilaha illa Allah twice, ashhadu anna Muhammadan rasul Allah twice, and he would face the qiblah, then turn away from the qiblah and say: Hayya 'ala al-salah twice, then turn to the left of the qiblah and say: Hayya 'ala al-falah twice, then face the qiblah and say: Allahu akbar, Allahu akbar, la ilaha illa Allah."],[6553,"Sa'd al-Qaraz was the mu'adhdhin for the people of Quba', and 'Umar b. al-Khattab moved him and appointed him as the mu'adhdhin for the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6554,"\"Junadah b. Abi Umayyah b. Nizar b. Ka'b b. al-Harith b. Ka'b b. 'Abd Allah b. Malik b. Nasr al-Azdi; he died in the year eighty.\""],[6555,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with a group of Azd on a Friday, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invited us to food that was before him. We said, \"We are fasting.\" He said, \"Did you fast yesterday?\" We said, \"No.\" He said, \"Will you fast tomorrow?\" We said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then break your fast.\" Then he said, \"Do not fast on Friday alone.\""],[6556,"While 'Umar b. al-Khattab was sitting in the mosque, a man passed by at the back of the mosque. A man said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, do you know this passer-by?\" He said, \"No, who is he?\" He said, \"Sawwad b. Qarib, a man from the people of Yemen, from a household of nobility and standing. He is the one whose familiar spirit came to him with the appearance of the Prophet ﷺ.\" 'Umar said, \"Bring him to me.\" He was summoned, and 'Umar said, \"Are you Sawwad b. Qarib?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Are you the one whose familiar spirit came to you with the appearance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Are you still upon your soothsaying?\" He became very angry and said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, no one has confronted me with this since I became Muslim.\" 'Umar said, \"Glory be to Allah! By Allah, what we were upon of polytheism was greater than what you were upon of soothsaying. Tell me about your familiar spirit coming to you with the appearance of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"Yes, O Commander of the Faithful. One night, while I was between sleep and wakefulness, my familiar spirit came to me and struck me with his foot and said: 'Arise, O Sawwad b. Qarib, understand and comprehend if you can comprehend. A Messenger from Lu'ayy b. Ghalib has been sent, calling to Allah and to His worship.' Then he began to recite: [al-sari'] I marvel at the jinn and their searching, and their tightening the camels with their saddlecloths, rushing to Makkah seeking guidance; the best of the jinn are not like their impure ones. So depart to the chosen one of Hashim, and direct your eyes to its head.\" He said, \"I did not raise my head at his words and said, 'Let me sleep, for I have become drowsy.' When the second night came, he came to me and struck me with his foot and said: 'Did I not tell you, O Sawwad b. Qarib, arise, understand and comprehend? If you can comprehend, a Messenger from Lu'ayy b. Ghalib has been sent, calling to Allah and to His worship.' Then the jinn began to say: 'I marvel at the jinn and their seeking, and their tightening the camels with their saddles, rushing to Makkah seeking guidance; the truthful of the jinn are not like their liars. So depart to the chosen one of Hashim, between its ropes and its veils.'\" He said, \"I did not raise my head. When the third night came, he came to me and struck me with his foot and said: 'Did I not tell you, O Sawwad b. Qarib, understand and comprehend if you can comprehend? A Messenger from Lu'ayy b. Ghalib has been sent, calling to Allah and to His worship.' Then he began to say: 'I marvel at the jinn and their reports, and their tightening the camels with their saddles, rushing to Makkah seeking guidance; the believers among the jinn are not like their disbelievers. So depart to the chosen one of Hashim; its front is not like its rear.'\" He said, \"Love of Islam fell into my heart and I desired it. When morning came, I saddled my mount and set out for Makkah. When I was partway, I was told that the Prophet ﷺ had emigrated to Madinah. I came to Madinah and asked about the Prophet ﷺ. I was told he was in the mosque. I reached the mosque, hobbled my she-camel, and entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was there with people around him. I said, 'Hear my words, O Messenger of Allah.' Abu Bakr said, 'Come closer.' He kept saying that until I was before him. He said, 'Speak, and tell me about your familiar spirit coming to you.' He said: [al-tawil] A confidant came to me after stillness and a nap, and he was not, in what I have experienced, a liar. Three nights, his words each night: 'A Messenger of Allah from Lu'ayy b. Ghalib has come to you.' So I tucked up the hem of my lower garment, and the swift, strong she-camel carried me across the deserts. I bear witness that there is no Lord other than Allah, and that you are entrusted over every conqueror, and that you are the closest of the messengers in means to Allah, O son of the most noble and pure. So command us with what comes to you, O best of those who walked, even if in what has come there is graying of the forelocks, and be an intercessor for me on a day when no intercessor besides you will avail Sawwad b. Qarib.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions rejoiced greatly at my Islam, so much that it was seen in their faces. 'Umar leapt up and embraced him and said, \"I had wished to hear this from you.\" The chain is interrupted."],[6557,"\"Salman b. 'Amir b. Aws b. 'Amr b. Hujr b. 'Amr b. al-Harith b. Taym b. Dhuhl b. Malik b. Bakr b. Sa'd b. Dabba. He settled in Basra and had a house near the congregational mosque, and he died there during the caliphate of 'Uthman ؓ.\""],[6558,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my father used to maintain family ties, host guests, and fulfill obligations, but he did not live to see Islam. Does he have any reward for that?\" He said, \"No.\" When I turned away, he said, \"Bring the old man to me,\" and said to me, \"That will be in your descendants, so they will never be humiliated, never disgraced, and never become poor.\""],[6559,"\"'Iqal b. Muhammad b. Sufyan b. Mujashi' b. Darim, the grandfather of al-Farazdaq b. Ghalib, came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[6560,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he presented Islam to me, so I became Muslim, and he taught me verses of the Qur'an. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I did deeds in the Jahiliyyah. Do I have any reward for them?\" He said, \"What did you do?\" I said, \"Two ten-year-old she-camels of mine went astray, so I went out looking for them on a camel of mine. Two tents appeared to me in an open area, so I headed toward them. In one of them I found an old man. I said, 'Have you seen two ten-year-old she-camels?' He said, 'Miqsam b. Darim: we found your two she-camels and sold them, and Allah has revived with them two households of your people, Arabs of Mudar.' While he was talking to me, a woman from the other tent called out, 'She gave birth, she gave birth!' He said, 'What did she give birth to? If it is a boy, he will share in our people; if it is a girl, bury her.' She said, 'A girl.' I said, 'What is this newborn?' He said, 'My daughter.' I said, 'I will buy her from you.' He said, 'O brother of Banu Tamim, would you sell your daughter? I am a man of the Arabs of Mudar.' I said, 'I do not buy her neck from you, but I buy her spirit from you, that you not kill her.' He said, 'With what will you buy her?' I said, 'With these two she-camels and their offspring.' He said, 'Will you add this camel of yours?' I said, 'Yes, on condition that you send a messenger with me, and when I reach my family I will return the camel to him.' When part of the night passed, I thought to myself that this is a noble deed that no Arab has preceded me to. Islam appeared and I had revived three hundred and sixty buried girls, buying each one with two ten-year-old she-camels and a camel. So do I have any reward for that?\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Its reward is complete for you, since Allah has bestowed Islam upon you.\" 'Abbad said: The confirmation of Sa'sa'a's words is the saying of al-Farazdaq: [al-mutaqarib] And my grandfather who prevented the burial of girls, so he revived the buried one and it was not buried. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6561,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, sometimes I have surplus food that I store for the distant relative and the wayfarer.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Your mother and your father, your sister and your brother, then the nearest, then the nearest.\""],[6562,"\"Qays b. 'Asim b. Sinan b. Khalid b. Minqar b. 'Ubayd b. Muqai's b. 'Amr b. Ka'b b. Sa'd b. Zayd Manat b. Tamim. He came as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'This is the chief of the people of the wilderness.'\""],[6563,"I witnessed Qays ibn ʿĀṣim at his death while he was making his will. He gathered his sons, and they were thirty-two males. He said: “O my sons, when I die, make the eldest of you your leader, and you will succeed your fathers. Do not make the youngest of you your leader, lest that bring you disgrace among your peers. Do not set up a wailing woman for me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbid wailing. And maintain your wealth, for it is an honor for the noble and a means of independence from the vile. Do not give away the necks of camels without their due, and do not withhold them from their due. Beware of every vein of evil, for whatever pleases you one day, what will grieve you is greater. And beware of the sons of your enemies, for they are enemies to you on the path of their fathers. When I die, bury me in a place that this quarter of Bakr ibn Wāʾil cannot overlook, for there were scratches between me and them in the pre-Islamic era, and I fear they will dig me up from my grave, so you will corrupt their world and they will corrupt your hereafter.” Then he called for his quiver and ordered his eldest son—who was called ʿAlī—and said: “Take out an arrow from my quiver.” He took it out. He said: “Break it.” He broke it. Then he said: “Take out two arrows.” He took them out. He said: “Break them.” He broke them, but he could not break them. He said: “O my son, thus are you in unity, and thus are you in division.” Then he began to recite: [light meter] “Glory is only what the truthful father built and the offspring revived his deeds. Glory, courage, and forbearance suffice when adorned by chastity and generosity. Thirty, O my sons, when you bind covenants for calamities, are like thirty arrows; when a strong knot binds them for time, they are not broken, even if the other arrows are cut apart; scattering destroys their gathering. Those of age and honor are more worthy, even if leadership among you is theirs. Upon you is care for the young, until the youngest reaches the utmost of his effort.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6564,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and when he saw me, I heard him say: “This is the chief of the people of the desert.” When I dismounted, I came to him and began speaking to him. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, what wealth is there for which I will not bear any consequence from a guest who stays with me or from numerous dependents?” He said: “What an excellent wealth is forty, and the most is sixty, and woe to the owners of hundreds except the one who gives in its abundance and its fatness, lends its back, and feeds the contented and the beggar.” I said: “O Prophet of Allah, how noble and how excellent are these character traits! O Prophet of Allah, may the valley in which I live not be settled by the abundance of my camels.” He said: “Then what do you do?” I said: “They count the camels and they count the people, and whoever wishes takes the head of a camel and goes away with it.” He said: “Then what do you do with lending their backs?” I said: “I do not lend the young or the old worn-out she-camel.” He said: “Is your wealth more beloved to you or the wealth of your heirs?” I said: “My wealth is more beloved to me than the wealth of my heirs.” He said: “Indeed, you have from your wealth what you eat and consume, or what you wear and wear out, or what you give and send forth; otherwise it is for your heirs.” I said: “By Allah, if I remain, I will indeed exhaust their number.” Al-Ḥasan said: “By Allah, he did so. When death came to Qays, he enjoined his sons, saying: ‘Beware of asking, for it is the last earning of a man. No one asks except that he leaves his earning.’”"],[6565,"“ʿAmr ibn al-Ahtam ibn Sumayy ibn Sinān ibn Khālid ibn Minqar ibn ʿUbayd ibn Muqāʿis ibn ʿAmr ibn Kaʿb ibn Saʿd ibn Zayd Manāt ibn Tamīm. The name of al-Ahtam was Sinān; his two front teeth were broken on the day of al-Kilāb.”"],[6566,"Qays ibn ʿĀṣim, al-Zibriqān ibn Badr, and ʿAmr ibn al-Ahtam, the Tamīmīs, sat with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Zibriqān boasted and said: “O Messenger of Allah, I am the chief of Tamīm, obeyed among them, and followed among them. I protect them from injustice and take their rights for them, and this one knows that—meaning ʿAmr ibn al-Ahtam.” ʿAmr ibn al-Ahtam said: “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he is sharp-tongued, protective of his side, and obeyed in his assembly.” Al-Zibriqān said: “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he knows about me other than what he said, and nothing prevented him from speaking it except envy.” ʿAmr said: “I envy you? By Allah, you are of vile maternal uncle, newly rich, foolish in your origins, and negligent toward your kinsfolk. By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I spoke the truth in what I said first, and I did not lie in what I said last. But I am a man who was pleased, so I said the best of what I knew, and I became angry, so I said the worst of what I found. By Allah, you spoke the truth in both matters.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery; indeed, some eloquence is sorcery.” It has been narrated from Abū Bakrah al-Anṣārī that he attended this gathering."],[6567,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when a delegation of Banū Tamīm came to him, among them Qays ibn ʿĀṣim, ʿAmr ibn al-Ahtam, and al-Zibriqān ibn Badr. The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAmr ibn al-Ahtam: “What do you say about al-Zibriqān ibn Badr?” He said: “O Messenger of Allah, he is obeyed in his assembly, sharp-tongued, and protective of what is behind his back.” Al-Zibriqān said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he knows about me more than what he described, but he envied me.” ʿAmr said: “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, he is deficient in manliness, narrow in his enclosure, vile in maternal uncle, and foolish in his origins. By Allah, I did not lie at first, and I spoke the truth at last. But I was pleased, so I said the best of what I knew, and I became angry, so I said the worst of what I knew.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, some eloquence is sorcery, and indeed, some poetry is wisdom.”"],[6568,"“Ṣaʿṣaʿah ibn Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥuṣayn ibn ʿUmayr ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Nazzāl ibn Murrah ibn ʿUbayd ibn Muqāʿis ibn ʿAmr ibn Kaʿb ibn Saʿd ibn Zayd Manāt ibn Tamīm, the paternal uncle of al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays.”"],[6569,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and heard him reciting this verse: {So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it} [al-Zalzalah: 8]. I said: “I do not care if I hear nothing besides it; it suffices me, it suffices me.”"],[6570,"And al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays ibn Ḥuṣayn ibn al-Nazzāl ibn ʿUbaydah was a mukhaḍram; he met the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him and supplicated for him. He said: “The name of al-Aḥnaf is al-Ḍaḥḥāk, and it is said Ṣakhr ibn Qays ibn Muʿāwiyah ibn Ḥuṣayn. He was born with a curvature in his legs.” His mother said: “By Allah, were it not for a curvature in his leg, there would be no boy in the tribe like him.” He was the most forbearing of the Arabs."],[6571,"While I was circumambulating the House in the time of ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān, a man from Banū Layth came and took my hand. He said: “Shall I give you good news?” I said: “Yes.” He said: “Do you remember when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to your people, Banū Saʿd, and I began presenting Islam to them and calling them to it? You said: ‘You call to good and command good.’ I conveyed that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: ‘O Allah, forgive al-Aḥnaf ibn Qays.’” So al-Aḥnaf used to say: “There is nothing in my deeds that gives me more hope than that.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6572,"“Al-Aswad ibn Sarīʿ ibn Ḥimyar ibn ʿUbādah ibn al-Nazzāl ibn Murrah ibn ʿUbaydah. He had a house in Basra in the presence of the mosque, adjacent to Banū Tamīm. He died during the reign of Muʿāwiyah ؓ .”"],[6573,"“O Messenger of Allah, shall I recite to you praises with which I praised my Lord, Blessed and Exalted?” He said: “Indeed, your Lord, Blessed and Exalted, loves praise,” and he did not ask for more than that."],[6574,"I came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of Allah, I have composed poetry in which I praise Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and praise you.” He said: “As for what you praised Allah, the Exalted, then bring it, and as for what you praised me with, leave it.” So I began to recite it. A tall, aquiline-nosed man entered, and he said to me: “Stop.” When he left, he said: “Continue.” I began reciting again, and it was not long before he returned, and he said to me: “Stop.” When he left, he said: “Continue.” I said: “Who is this, O Prophet of Allah, who when he enters you say stop, and when he leaves you say continue?” He said: “This is ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb, and he is not one for falsehood in anything.”"],[6575,"Jariyyah b. Qudamah b. Zuhayr b. Husayn b. Rabah b. Sa'd b. Yahya b. Rabi'ah b. Ka'b, whose kunyah was Abu al-Walid and Abu Yazid, had a house in Basra in the Bahariyyah street."],[6576,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me a saying that will benefit me, and make it brief for me so that I may grasp it. He said: \"Do not get angry.\" He repeated it to me several times, saying: \"Do not get angry.\""],[6577,"When the people came for Hajj in the year nine, 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi, the paternal uncle of al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for permission to return to his people. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I fear that they will kill you.\" He said: \"Even if they find me sleeping, they would wake me.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him permission, and he returned to his people as a Muslim. He arrived at night, and Thaqif came to him. He called them to Islam, but they accused him, disobeyed him, and made him hear what he had not expected. Then they left him, and when it was late night and dawn broke, 'Urwah stood in his house, called the adhan for prayer, and recited the tashahhud. A man from Thaqif shot him with an arrow and killed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The example of 'Urwah is like the example of the companion of Ya-Sin: he called his people to Allah, the Exalted, and they killed him.\""],[6578,"Mujashi' b. Mas'ud b. Tha'labah b. Wahb b. 'A'idh, whose kunyah was Abu Sulayman. His mother and the mother of his brother Mujalid were Mulaykah bt. Sufyan b. al-Harith b. Labid b. Khuzaymah. Mujashi' was killed on the day of the lesser Jamal in the year thirty-six and was buried in his house among the Banu Sulaym, in the presence of Banu Sadus. He had more than one house in Basra, among them his house by the congregational mosque."],[6579,"I brought my brother Mujalid to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after the conquest and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have brought you my brother Mujalid so that you may accept his pledge for emigration. He said: \"The people of emigration have taken what it entails.\" I said: Then upon what do you accept his pledge, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"I accept his pledge upon Islam, faith, and jihad.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6580,"'Amr b. 'Abasah b. 'Amir b. Khalid b. Ghadirah b. 'Attab b. Imri' al-Qays, whose mother was Ramlah bt. al-Waqi'ah from Banu Hizam. He was the maternal half-brother of Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, one of the inhabitants of Syria, and his kunyah was Abu Yahya."],[6581,"I heard 'Amr b. 'Abasah say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in prayer facing a camel from the spoils. When he said the taslim, he took a hair from the side of the camel and said: \"It is not lawful for me to have from this spoil even the like of this hair, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you.\""],[6582,"\"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was still an ordinary person. I asked him, 'Who are you?' He replied, 'I am a prophet.' I asked, 'What is a prophet?' He replied, 'I am the Messenger of Allah.' I asked him, 'Did Allah send you?' He replied, 'Yes.' I asked, 'Why did Allah send you?' He replied, 'To worship Allah alone, break the idols, and maintain family ties.' I said, 'Indeed, Allah has sent you. So who follows you in this?' He replied, 'A free man and a slave,' meaning Abu Bakr and Bilal. Then 'Amr ibn Abasa said, 'I saw myself as one-fourth of Islam, so I embraced Islam.' I then asked the Prophet, 'Can I follow you, O Messenger of Allah?' He replied, 'No, but go back to your people. When I make my appearance, come to me.'\""],[6583,"And it is said: Abu 'Abd Allah. He died during the governorship of Bishr b. Marwan."],[6584,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I heard him saying, \"The affairs of this nation will remain apparent until twelve caliphs rise.\" Then he said something that I couldn't understand, and my father was closer to him than me, so I asked him, \"What did he say?\" He replied, \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\" Jabir ibn Samurah also narrated another hadith from his father."],[6585,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: We are people of the desert and livestock; should we perform ablution from the meat of sheep and their milk? He said: \"No.\""],[6586,"Abu Juhayfah Wahb b. 'Abd Allah al-Suwa'i died during the governorship of Bishr b. Marwan."],[6587,"I was with my uncle in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and he said, \"The affair of my Ummah (nation) will continue to be righteous as long as there are twelve caliphs.\" Then he said a word and lowered his voice with it. So, I asked my uncle, who was in front of me, what did he say, O uncle? He said, \"He said, O my son, 'All of them will be from Quraysh.'\""],[6588,"'Uthman b. Abi al-'As b. Kathir b. Dahman b. 'Abd Allah b. Hammam b. Aban b. Yasar b. Malik, whose kunyah was Abu 'Abd Allah, died in the year fifty."],[6589,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered him to make the mosque of Ta'if where their idol had been. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6590,"‘Āmir b. Wāthilah b. ‘Abd Allāh b. ‘Amr b. Jaḥsh b. Ḥayyān b. Sa‘d b. Layth. He was born in the year of Uḥud and lived eight years of the life of the Prophet ﷺ. He settled in Kufa, then resided in Makkah until he died, and he was the last of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to die. He died in the year one hundred and two. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6591,"Abū al-Ṭufayl said: “I lived eight years of the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I was born in the year of Uḥud.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6592,"Abū al-Ṭufayl ‘Āmir b. Wāthilah died in the year one hundred."],[6593,"He reported to him: I was a boy carrying the limb of a camel, and I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributing meat at al-Ji‘rānah. A woman came to him and he spread his cloak for her. I said, “Who is this?” They said, “His mother who suckled him.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6594,"Muḥammad b. ‘Umar said: Surāqah b. Mālik used to live in Qudayd. He died in the year twenty-four."],[6595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “O Surāqah, shall I not tell you about the people of Paradise and the people of the Fire?” I said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “As for the people of the Fire, they are every coarse, arrogant, haughty person. And as for the people of Paradise, they are the weak and the downtrodden.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us at al-Baṭḥā’ and said: “The ‘umrah has entered into the ḥajj until the Day of Resurrection.” Surāqah b. Mālik is the brother of Ka‘b b. Mālik. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6597,"He asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about a stray camel that comes to his watering trough: is there a reward for him if he gives it its fill? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In every living creature with a warm liver there is a reward.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “In every living creature with a warm liver there is a reward.”"],[6599,"Ḍirār b. al-Azwar, and the name of al-Azwar is Mālik b. Aws b. Khuzaymah b. Rabī‘ah b. Mālik b. Tha‘labah b. Dūdān b. Usayd b. Khuzaymah b. Mudrikah b. Ilyās b. Muḍar. He lived in Kufa and died there."],[6600,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said to him: “Stretch out your hand so that I may pledge allegiance to you upon Islam.” So I pledged allegiance to him. Then I said: [al-baḥr al-mutaqārib] “I have abandoned gambling arrows and the singing of slave-girls, and wine, seeking blessing and supplication; and my charging of the caparisoned horse in the midst of battle, and my bearing arms against the Muslims. O Lord, let not my pledge be cheated, for I have sold my family and my property out of dedication.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Your pledge has not been cheated, O Ḍirār.”"],[6601,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was milking and said: “Leave the milk for the one who calls for it.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6602,"Wabisa b. Ma'bad b. Qays b. Ka'b b. Fahd b. Munqidh b. al-Harith b. Tha'laba b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzayma settled in Kufa, then moved to al-Jazira and died there."],[6603,"Do not take the backs of beasts as pulpits, and the worst of these beasts is the mule."],[6604,"Khuraim b. Fatik b. al-Akhram b. Shaddad b. 'Amr al-Asadi."],[6605,"I went out with some camels of mine, and lightning at 'Uraqa struck them, so I hobbled them and used the foreleg of one of them as a pillow. That was at the time of the Prophet's ﷺ emergence. Then I said, \"I seek refuge in the great one of this valley.\" He said, \"That is what they used to do in the Jahiliyya.\" Then a caller called out to me, saying: [rajaz] \"Woe to you! Seek refuge in Allah, Possessor of Majesty, who sends down the sacred and the lawful. Declare Allah's oneness and do not care about the horrors of the resolute, when they mention Allah over the miles, in the plains and the mountains. The trustee of truth in the lowly is none but piety and righteous deeds.\" I said: [rajaz] \"O you who call with what changes: is it guidance seen with you or misguidance?\" He said, \"This is Allah's Messenger, possessor of good, who has come with Ya Sin and the Ha Mim surahs, in surahs thereafter detailed, making things forbidden and lawful. He commands fasting and prayer and restrains people from sins that were abominable in those days.\" I said, \"Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?\" He said, \"I am Malik b. Malik. Allah's Messenger ﷺ sent me from the land of the people of Najd.\" I said, \"If only someone would take care of these camels of mine, I would go to him and believe in him.\" He said, \"I will take care of them until I deliver them to your family safe, if Allah Almighty wills.\" So I mounted one of them and came to Madinah. I found the people on Friday while they were in prayer, so I said, \"They will finish their prayer, then I will enter.\" As I was about to make my mount kneel, Abu Dharr came out and said, \"Allah's Messenger ﷺ tells you: 'Enter.'\" So I entered. When he saw me, he said, \"What did the old man who guaranteed to deliver your camels to your family safe do? Indeed, he has delivered them safe.\" I said, \"May Allah have mercy on him.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Yes, may Allah have mercy on him.\" Khuraim said, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah,\" and his Islam became good. It is not authentic."],[6606,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"O Khuraim b. Fatik, were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man.\" He said, \"What are they, may my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Your abundant hair and your trailing lower garment.\" So Khuraim went and cut his hair and shortened his garment. Its chain is dark."],[6607,"Usama b. 'Umayr b. 'Asim b. 'Ubayd Allah b. Hunayf b. Yasar b. Naji b. 'Amr b. al-Harith b. Tabikha b. Lihyan b. Hudhayl, and he is the father of Abu al-Malih. He settled in Basra."],[6608,"He prayed the two rak'ahs of dawn with the Prophet ﷺ and prayed close to him. The Prophet ﷺ prayed two light rak'ahs, and he heard him say, \"O Allah, Lord of Jibril, Mika'il, Israfil, and Muhammad ﷺ, I seek refuge in You from the Fire,\" three times. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6609,"Abi al-Lahm's name is 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Malik b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Affan. He was a noble poet and witnessed the conquest of Hunayn with his freedman 'Umayr. Abu 'Ubayda said, \"He was called Abi al-Lahm (the one who refuses meat) because he refused to eat meat.\""],[6610,"Abi al-Lahm used to dwell at al-Safra', three [nights' journey] from Madinah, and 'Umayr his freedman used to dwell with him."],[6611,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us: Hatim b. Isma'il narrated to us: Yazid b. Abi 'Ubayd narrated to us: I heard 'Umayr, the freedman of Abi al-Lahm, say: My master ordered me to cut meat into strips for him. A poor person came to me, and I fed him some of it. My master beat me, so I went to Allah's Messenger ﷺ and mentioned it to him. He summoned him and said, \"Why did you beat him?\" He said, \"He fed my food without my order.\" Allah's Messenger ﷺ said, \"The reward is between you two.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6612,"I saw Allah's Messenger ﷺ on the stones of al-Zayt seeking rain, raising his hands."],[6613,"'Amr b. Umayya b. Khuwaylid b. 'Abd Allah b. Iyas b. 'Ubayd b. Nashira b. Ka'b b. Jaddi b. Damra b. Bakr b. 'Abd Manat b. Kinana."],[6614,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, should I let my mount loose and rely on Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Rather, hobble it and rely on Allah.\" Its chain is good."],[6615,"ʿUmayr ibn Salamah ibn Muntāb ibn Ṭalḥah ibn Jaddī ibn Ḍamrah."],[6616,"While we were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he was in a state of ihrām, in one of the areas of al-Rawḥāʾ, we came upon a wild donkey that had been hamstrung. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Leave it.\" Then its owner who had hamstrung it, a man from Bahz, came and said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, this donkey is yours. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered Abu Bakr to divide it among the traveling companions. Then he went on. When he was at al-Ithābah, he passed by a gazelle curled up in the shade of a tree with an arrow in it. The Prophet ﷺ ordered a man to call out that no one should take it, so the people went on and left it. Its chain is authentic."],[6617,"Abu al-Jaʿd al-Ḍamrī, ʿAmr ibn Bakr ibn Junādah ibn Murād ibn Kaʿb ibn Ḍamrah."],[6618,"\"Whoever abandons the Friday prayer three times out of negligence, Allah will seal his heart.\""],[6619,"Al-Ṣaʿb ibn Jaththāmah ibn Qays ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn Wahb ibn Yaʿmar ibn ʿAwf ibn Kaʿb ibn Sulmā ibn Layth. The mother of al-Ṣaʿb was Zaynab bt. Ḥarb ibn Umayyah ibn ʿAbd Shams ibn ʿAbd Manāf, the sister of Abu Sufyān, and her name was Fākhitah bt. Ḥarb. He used to reside in Waddān."],[6620,"It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that some cavalry had raided at night and struck some of the children of the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They are from their fathers.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6621,"Qabāth ibn Ashyam ibn ʿĀmir ibn al-Mulawwiḥ ibn Yaʿmar ibn ʿAwf ibn Kaʿb ibn ʿĀmir ibn Layth al-Ḍibābī."],[6622,"I heard ʿAbd al-Malik ibn Marwān say to Qabāth ibn Ashyam: O Qabāth, are you older or is the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is greater than me, and I am older than him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born in the Year of the Elephant, and he received prophethood at the end of the fortieth year after the Elephant. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6623,"The conversion of Qabāth ibn Ashyam to Islam occurred when men from his people and other Arabs came to him and said: Muhammad ibn ʿAbd Allāh ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib has come out calling to a religion other than our religion. So Qabāth got up and went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he entered upon him, he said to him: \"Sit down, O Qabāth.\" Qabāth was struck speechless, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Are you the one who said: If the women of Quraysh went out with all their might, they would repel Muhammad and his companions?\" Qabāth said: By the One who sent you with the truth, my tongue never uttered it, nor did my lips whisper it, nor did anyone hear it from me. It was nothing but a thought that crossed my mind. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, and I bear witness that you are His servant and messenger, and that what you have brought is the truth."],[6624,"\"The prayer of two men, one of whom leads the other, is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of forty men praying individually, one after another. The prayer of four men, one of whom leads them, is purer in the sight of Allah than the prayer of eighty praying individually, one after another. The prayer of eight men, one of whom leads them, is purer in the sight of Allah, the Exalted, than the prayer of one hundred praying individually, one after another.\""],[6625,"ʿUmayr ibn Qatādah ibn Saʿd ibn ʿĀmir ibn Junduʿ ibn Layth al-Laythī."],[6626,"There was a matter in my heart that saddened me: that I had not asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, nor had I heard anyone ask him about it. So I kept watching for an opportunity. One day I entered upon him while he was performing ablution, and I found him in two conditions I loved to find him in: free (unoccupied) and in good spirits. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, will you permit me to ask you?” He said, “Yes—ask whatever occurs to you.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is faith?” He said, “Generosity and patience.” I said, “Then which of the believers is best in faith?” He said, “The one with the best character.” I said, “Then which of the Muslims is best in Islam?” He said, “The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe.” I said, “Then which jihad is best?” He lowered his head and remained silent for a long time, until I feared I had burdened him, and I wished I had not asked him—especially since I had heard him the day before say: “Indeed, the greatest of the Muslims in wrongdoing against the Muslims is the one who asks about something that was not prohibited for them, and then it is prohibited for them because of his question.” So I said, “I seek refuge in Allah from the anger of Allah and the anger of His Messenger ﷺ.” He raised his head and said, “What did you say?” I said, “Which jihad is best?” He said, “A word of justice in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.”[1]"],[6627,"Shaddad b. al-Had b. Amr b. Abd Allah b. Jabir b. Numayr b. Utwarah b. Amir b. Layth b. Bakrah. The name of al-Had was Usamah. He is Abu Abd Allah b. Shaddad b. al-Had. He moved to Kufa."],[6628,"He said: He was only named al-Had."],[6629,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us during one of the two daytime prayers, Zuhr or Asr, carrying al-Hasan or al-Husayn. He came forward and placed him by his right foot, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrated with a long prostration. I raised my head amid the people, and there was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrating while the boy was riding on his back. So I sat back and prostrated. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished, some people said: O Messenger of Allah, you prostrated in this prayer a prostration that you do not usually make. Was it something you were commanded, or was it revealed to you? He said: 'No, it was not. But my son mounted me, and I disliked to hurry him until he finished his need.' Its chain is good."],[6630,"Al-Harith b. al-Barsa is al-Harith b. Malik b. Qays b. Uwaydh b. Abd Allah b. Jabir b. Abd Manaf b. Ashja b. Amir b. Layth. His mother was al-Barsa bt. Abd Allah b. Rabiah al-Hilaliyyah. He stayed in Makkah, then settled in Kufa."],[6631,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the day of the conquest of Makkah: 'Makkah will never be invaded after this year, ever.' Sufyan said: I heard it from Zakariyya; its interpretation is regarding disbelief. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6632,"He is Malik b. al-Huwayrith b. Ashyam b. Zabalah b. Hashish b. Abd Yalil b. Nashib b. Ghayrah b. Sa'd b. Layth b. Bakr."],[6633,"The Prophet ﷺ made him recite: 'So on that Day, none will punish as He punishes, and none will bind as He binds' [al-Fajr: 26]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6634,"Fadalah b. Wahb b. Bahrah b. Buhayrah b. Malik b. Qays b. Amir b. Layth. His mother was the daughter of Kaysan b. Amir al-Utwari. He is Abu Abd Allah Fadalah b. Wahb. He moved to Basra."],[6635,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me, and among what he taught me was: 'Guard the prayers.' I said: These are hours in which I have occupations, so command me with a comprehensive matter that, if I do it, will suffice me. He said: 'Guard the two afternoon prayers.' I said: What are the two afternoon prayers? He said: 'A prayer before sunrise and a prayer before sunset.'"],[6636,"Mus'ab al-Habr is Ibn Umayr b. Ubayd b. Hashim b. Abd Manaf b. Abd al-Dar b. Qusayy. He is the reciter whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the Ansar to teach them the Quran in Madinah before the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Many people embraced Islam with him, and he witnessed Badr."],[6637,"The first of the Muhajirun who came to us was Mus'ab b. Umayr ؓ."],[6638,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting in Quba with a group of people. Mus'ab b. Umayr stood up wearing a burdah that barely covered him, and the people lowered their heads. He came and greeted, and they returned his greeting. The Prophet ﷺ said good about him and praised him, then said: 'I saw this one with his parents in Makkah; they honored him and pampered him, and there was no young man of Quraysh like him. Then he left all that seeking the pleasure of Allah and the support of His Messenger. Indeed, it will not be long before Persia and Rome are conquered for you, and one of you will go out in a fine garment and return in a fine garment, and a large bowl will be brought to you in the morning and another in the evening.' They said: O Messenger of Allah, are we better today or on that day? He said: 'Rather, you today are better than you on that day. If you knew of this world what I know, your souls would find rest from it.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6639,"Abu Salamah, Abdullah b. Abd al-Asad b. Hilal b. Abdullah b. Umar b. Makhzum b. Yaqazah b. Murrah b. Kab b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr b. Malik, and he was among the emigrants to Abyssinia, and he emigrated to Madinah, and he witnessed Badr, and Umm Salamah was his wife, and Abu Salamah died in Shawwal, in the year four of the Hijrah."],[6640,"When a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return. O Allah, with You I seek reward for my calamity.'"],[6641,"Suhail b. Bayda' is Suhail b. Wahb b. Rabi'ah b. Hilal b. Ahyab b. Dabbah b. al-Harith b. Fihr b. Malik b. al-Nadr, and Bayda' is his mother, and her name is Da'd bt. Sa'id b. Sahm."],[6642,"From Urwah, regarding the naming of those who emigrated to the land of Abyssinia in the first emigration before the departure of Ja'far b. Abi Talib: Suhail b. Bayda'. And regarding the naming of those who witnessed Badr from Quraish, then from Banu al-Harith b. Fihr: Suhail b. Bayda'."],[6643,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not pray over Suhail b. Bayda' except in the mosque. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6644,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Suhail b. Bayda' were riding, with Suhail behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a camel, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Suhail b. Bayda',' and raised his voice two or three times, each time Suhail answered him. The people heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and knew that he wanted them, so those who were in front of him sat down and those who were behind him caught up, until when they had gathered, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah, Allah has forbidden him to the Fire and obligated Paradise for him.' Its chain is good but contains an interruption."],[6645,"Iyad b. Zuhair b. Abi Shaddad b. Rabi'ah b. Hilal b. Wuhaib b. Dabbah b. al-Harith b. Fihr, the Fihri. He witnessed Badr and died in Syria in the year thirty."],[6646,"Abdullah b. Hudhafah b. Qais b. Adi b. Sa'id b. Sahm."],[6647,"The Prophet ﷺ sent Alqamah b. Muhriz on an expedition. When we reached the head of our destination, he gave permission to a group of the army and appointed over them Abdullah b. Hudhafah b. Qais al-Sahmi, and he was one of the people of Badr, and he had a sense of humor, for he would make the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ camel kneel during one of his journeys to make him laugh by that. The Romans had captured him during the time of Umar b. al-Khattab and wanted him to disbelieve, but Allah ﷻ protected him until Allah, Blessed and Exalted, saved him from them. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6648,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to announce among the people of Mina: 'No one should fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking.'"],[6649,"'O Messenger of Allah, who is my father?' He said: 'Your father is Hudhafah. The child belongs to the bed and the stone belongs to the adulterer.' He said: 'If you had called me to an Abyssinian, I would have followed him.' His mother said to him: 'You have exposed me.' He said: 'I wanted to rest.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6650,"Abu Burdah Hani' b. Niyar b. Amr b. Ubaid b. Kilab b. Dahman b. Ghanim b. Dhubyan b. Humaym b. Kahil b. Dhuhl b. Bala b. Amr b. al-Harith b. al-Haf b. Quda'ah."],[6651,"From 'Urwah: In naming those who witnessed Badr: Abu Burdah b. Niyar."],[6652,"I met my maternal uncle Abu Burdah, and he had a banner. I said, 'Where are you heading?' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife after him, to strike his neck and take his property.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6653,"It is said that he was an ally of Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, and it is also said that he was one of them."],[6654,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, chose me and chose for me companions, and made among them ministers, supporters, and in-laws. So whoever reviles them, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Neither an obligatory nor a supererogatory deed will be accepted from him on the Day of Resurrection."],[6655,"Abu Lubabah Bashir b. 'Abd al-Mundhir and al-Harith b. Hatib went out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and went out with him to Badr, but he sent them back and appointed Abu Lubabah over Madinah, and allotted them two shares along with the people of Badr."],[6656,"When Allah accepted the repentance of Abu Lubabah, Abu Lubabah said, 'I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I will abandon the dwellings of my people in which I committed the sin, and I will divest myself of all my wealth as charity for Allah ﷻ and His Messenger ﷺ.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Abu Lubabah, a third will suffice you.\"' He said, 'So I gave a third in charity.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6657,"Abu Habbah Thabit b. al-Nu'man b. Umayyah b. Tha'labah b. 'Amr b. 'Awf b. Malik b. al-Aws, and he was martyred on the day of Uhud."],[6658,"He heard Abu Habbah al-Badri giving a legal verdict to the people that there is no harm in whatever pebbles a man throws at the Jamarat. 'Abdullah b. 'Amr b. 'Uthman said, 'I mentioned that to 'Abdullah b. 'Umar, and he said, \"Abu Habbah spoke the truth, and Abu Habbah was a Badri.\"'"],[6659,"I was taken up until I passed by a level place where I could hear the scratching of the pens."],[6660,"Al-Muttalib b. Abi Wada'ah b. Sabirah b. Sa'id b. Sa'd b. Sahm b. 'Amr b. Husays b. Ka'b b. Lu'ayy b. Ghalib b. Fihr b. Malik accepted Islam on the day of the conquest."],[6661,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prostrate in [Surah] al-Najm. He said, 'So the people prostrated with him.' Al-Muttalib said, 'I did not prostrate with them that day, for he was then a polytheist.' Al-Muttalib said, 'So I will never omit prostrating in it.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6662,"'Abdullah b. al-Harith b. Jaz' b. Ma'di Karib b. 'Amr b. 'Usaym b. 'Amr b. 'Uwayj b. 'Amr b. Zubayd died in the year eighty-six."],[6663,"“There will be after me sultans of tribulation; at their gates are like the kneeling places of camels. They will not give anyone anything except that they take from his religion the like of it.”"],[6664,"“The name of Ibn Umm Maktūm was ʿAmr b. Qays.”"],[6665,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ circumambulated during his farewell pilgrimage on his she-camel al-Jadʿāʾ, while ʿAbd Allāh b. Umm Maktūm held its halter, reciting rajaz verses.”"],[6666,"“ʿAbd Allāh b. Umm Maktūm — his mother was Umm Maktūm, and her name was ʿĀtikah bt. ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAnkathah b. ʿĀmir b. Makhzūm — and he was ʿAmr b. Qays b. Zāʾidah b. al-Aṣamm b. Harim b. Rawāḥah b. ʿAbd Maʿīṣ b. ʿĀmir b. Luʾayy. The correct view is what Muṣʿab said, and I have produced for him both names together.”"],[6667,"“The first of the Emigrants to arrive was Muṣʿab b. ʿUmayr; then after him ʿAmr b. Umm Maktūm, the blind, came to us.”"],[6668,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah while Ibn Umm Maktūm was with her, and she was cutting citron for him, which he was eating with honey. She said, “This one has continually had this from the family of Muḥammad ﷺ since Allah reproached His Prophet ﷺ regarding him.” By that the Mother of the Believers meant the revelation of Sūrat ʿAbasa wa-tawallā."],[6669,"I entered upon ʿĀʾishah while a blind man was with her, and she was cutting citron for him and feeding it to him with honey. I said, “Who is this, O Mother of the Believers?” She said, “This is Ibn Umm Maktūm, the one about whom Allah, Blessed and Exalted, reproached His Prophet ﷺ.” She said: “Ibn Umm Maktūm came to the Prophet ﷺ while ʿUtbah and Shaybah were with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned to face those two, and it was revealed: ‘He frowned and turned away because the blind man came to him’ — that is, Ibn Umm Maktūm.”"],[6670,"The Prophet ﷺ went out one morning and said, “The Fire has been kindled for the people of the Fire, and trials have come like the dark patches of night. If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much.”"],[6671,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am an elderly man, blind, living far away, and I have no guide to lead me. Between me and the mosque there are trees and rivers. Is there any excuse for me to pray in my house?” He said, “Do you hear the call?” I said, “Yes.” He said, “Then respond to it.”"],[6672,"From Abū Razīn — as for the ḥadīth of Shaybān."],[6673,"From Abū Razīn — as for the ḥadīth of Ḥammād b. Salamah."],[6674,"\"From Abu Razin\""],[6675,"“Al-Ḥaḍramī, Abū al-ʿAlāʾ — his name was ʿAbd Allāh b. ʿAbbād b. Akbar b. Rabīʿah b. Mālik b. ʿArīf b. Mālik b. al-Khazraj b. Iyād b. al-Ṣadaf b. Ḥaḍramawt b. Kindah. Al-ʿAlāʾ died while returning from al-Baḥrayn in the year twenty-one.”"],[6676,"«The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me concerning the two allies, one of them being a Muslim and the other a polytheist, to take the tithe from the Muslim and the jizya from the polytheist.» Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6677,"«He wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and began with himself.» Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6678,"«And Abdullah b. Jahsh b. Rabab b. Ya'mar b. Sabira b. Kabir b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzaymah; his mother was Umayma bt. Abd al-Muttalib, the paternal aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.»"],[6679,"«He was an ally of Banu Umayya b. Abd Shams.»"],[6680,"From Urwa: «In the naming of those who were martyred on the day of Uhud with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Banu Umayya: Abdullah b. Jahsh, an ally of theirs, and he was from Banu Asad b. Khuzaymah.»"],[6681,"\"Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Jash bin Rabbab bin Ya'amir bin Sabirah bin Kabir bin Ghanm bin Doudan bin Asad bin Khuzaymah bin Mudrikah bin Ilyas bin Mudar Halif bin Umayyah bin Ummu Abihi Umaymah bint Abdul-Muttalib Amatul Rasulullah ﷺ wa'amatuhu Zainab bint Jash zawjunnabiyyi ﷺ .\" Translation: \"Muhammad, the son of Abdullah, the son of Jash, the son of Rabbab, the son of Ya'amir, the son of Sabirah, the son of Kabir, the son of Ghanm, the son of Doudan, the son of Asad, the son of Khuzaymah, the son of Mudrikah, the son of Ilyas, the son of Mudar, the relative of Banu Umayyah, and his grandmother is Ummu Abihi Umaymah bint Abd al-Muttalib who is the aunt of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and his adopted mother is Zainab bint Jash, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ .\""],[6682,"«I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he passed by Ma'mar while he was sitting at his house in the market, his thighs uncovered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Cover your thigh, O Ma'mar, for the thigh is awrah.» Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6683,"«And Yazid b. Abdullah b. Sa'd b. al-Aswad b. Thumama b. Yaqzan b. al-Harith b. Amr b. Mu'awiya b. al-Harith, an ally of Banu Mu'ayqib. The Prophet ﷺ had appointed him over al-Yamama.»"],[6684,"«Let none of you take the goods of his companion in jest or in earnest; and if one of you finds his companion's stick, let him return it to him.»"],[6685,"«My father performed Hajj with the Prophet ﷺ in the Farewell Pilgrimage while I was a boy of seven years.»"],[6686,"«And in it al-Sa'ib b. Yazid died, meaning the year ninety-one.»"],[6687,"«I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ bring out Abdullah b. Khatal from behind the curtains of the Ka'bah and kill him in retaliation; then he said: No one of Quraysh will be killed in retaliation after this.»"],[6688,"«Abu Hashim b. Utba b. Rabi'a b. Abd Shams b. Abd Manaf; his mother was Khunas bt. Malik b. al-Mudarrib b. Hujr b. Abd b. Ma'is b. Amir b. Lu'ayy. He was one-eyed; his eye was gouged out on the day of al-Yarmouk. Abu Hashim died in the time of Mu'awiya.»"],[6689,"Abu Hurayrah came to Damascus and stayed with Abu Kulthum al-Sadusi. We came to him and discussed the middle prayer, and we differed about it. Abu Hurayrah said, \"You have differed about it just as we differed about it while we were at Quba, near the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Among us was the righteous man Abu Hashim b. 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah. He stood up and entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, being bold with him, then he came out to us and informed us that it is 'Asr.\""],[6690,"O uncle, what makes you weep? Is it pain or sorrow over the world? He said, \"Not at all, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a covenant with me that I did not fulfill. He said to me, 'O Abu Hashim, wealth will reach you, given to some people.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6691,"\"Abu al-'As b. al-Rabi' was the husband of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the son of her maternal aunt; his mother was Halah bt. Khuwaylid, the sister of Khadijah. Abu al-'As's name was Muhashsham, and he was nicknamed Jirw al-Batha'. Zaynab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, bore to Abu al-'As 'Ali b. Abi al-'As and Umamah bt. Abi al-'As. Abu al-'As died in the year eleven during the caliphate of Abu Bakr ؓ.\""],[6692,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned Zaynab to Abu al-'As by the original marriage and did not renew anything.\" This is a chain that is sahih according to Muslim's criterion, but it has been narrated that the Prophet ﷺ returned her to him with a new marriage. That is not sahih."],[6693,"Zaynab, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, became Muslim a year before her husband Abu al-'As; then Abu al-'As became Muslim. \"So the Prophet ﷺ returned her to him with a new marriage.\" This is false; perhaps he meant that she emigrated a year before him."],[6694,"Abu Musa said: \"A young man of Quraysh has come to you, noble in mothers, paternal aunts, and maternal aunts. He speaks about wealth among you thus and thus,\" or he had many virtues, and he is the one who conquered Khurasan and entered ihram from Naysabur in gratitude to Allah, Exalted is He, and made the water stations at 'Arafah."],[6695,"\"Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr.\""],[6696,"\"Hind b. Abi Halah bt. Malik, one of Banu Usayd b. 'Amr b. Tamim, an ally of Banu 'Abd al-Dar, and he is the son of Khadijah.\""],[6697,"\"Abu Halah, the husband of Khadijah, his name was Hind b. al-Nabbash b. Zurarah. His two sons were Hind and Halah; Hind witnessed Uhud.\""],[6698,"About the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he mentioned the hadith in full."],[6699,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was lying down, so the Prophet ﷺ woke up and embraced Hala, bringing her closer to his chest and said, \"Hala, Hala, Hala,\" as if he ﷺ was delighted by her resemblance to Khadijah."],[6700,"\"'Abd Allah b. Zama'ah b. al-Aswad b. al-Muttalib b. Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy. His mother was Quraybah bt. Abi Umayyah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum, and her mother was 'Atikah bt. 'Abd al-Muttalib.\""],[6701,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken ill and I was with him in a group of Muslims, Bilal was called for prayer. He said, 'Choose someone to lead the people in prayer.' So I went out and found Umar among the people, and Abu Bakr was absent. I said to Umar, 'Stand up and lead the people in prayer.' He stood up and when he said the takbeer (the opening phrase of prayer), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard his voice. Umar was a loud speaker. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Where is Abu Bakr? May Allah not blame him or the Muslims for that.' He sent for Abu Bakr and after Umar had finished that prayer, Abu Bakr led the people in prayer. Abdullah ibn Zam'a said, 'Umar said to me, \"What did you do to me, O Ibn Zam'a? By Allah, when you told me to lead the people in prayer, I did not think that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had commanded it. If it were not for that, I would not have led the people in prayer.\" I said, 'By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not command me. But when I did not see Abu Bakr, I thought that you were the most entitled to lead the people in prayer.'\""],[6702,"Shabab b. Khayyat said: Abu Umamah died in the year eighty-six."],[6703,"The Messenger of Allah sent me to my people to call them to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and to present to them the laws of Islam. I came to them after they had watered their camels, milked them, and drunk. When they saw me, they said, 'Welcome to al-Suddi b. 'Ajlan.' Then they said, 'We have heard that you have turned to this man.' I said, 'No, but I have believed in Allah and His Messenger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to you to present Islam and its laws to you.' While we were thus, they brought a large bowl of blood and placed it, and they gathered around it to eat it. They said, 'Come, O Suddi.' I said, 'Woe to you! I have come to you from one who forbids this to you, according to what Allah has revealed to him.' They said, 'And what is that?' I said, 'This verse was revealed to him: {Forbidden to you are the dead, blood, and the flesh of swine} [al-Ma'idah: 3] up to His saying {except that which you have properly slaughtered} [al-Ma'idah: 3].' I kept calling them to Islam, but they refused. I said to them, 'Woe to you! Bring me some water, for I am severely thirsty.' They said, 'No, but we will leave you to die of thirst.' He said: 'I wrapped my head with my turban and lay down on the scorching ground in intense heat. Then someone came to me in my sleep with a glass cup, the like of which people had never seen more beautiful, and in it a drink, the like of which people had never tasted more delicious. He gave it to me, and I drank it. As soon as I finished my drink, I woke up, and by Allah, I was not thirsty, nor did I know thirst after that drink.' Then I heard them saying, 'A man from the nobles of your people has come to you, and you have not given him even a sip of milk mixed with water. Bring me their mixed drink.' I said, 'I have no need of it. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has fed me and given me drink.' I showed them my stomach, and they all embraced Islam, to the last one of them."],[6704,"Mu'awiya b. Hayda b. Mu'awiya b. Qushayr b. Ka'b b. Rabi'a b. 'Amir, his lineage traced to 'Abd Allah b. al-Jarud."],[6705,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, whom should I treat well?' He said, 'Your mother.'"],[6706,"He said to his brother Malik b. Hayda: 'Come with us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, for he knows you but does not know me. He has detained some people from my neighbors.' We came to him, and Malik b. Hayda said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I have embraced Islam, and my neighbors have embraced Islam, so release them.' He did not answer him. Then he repeated, and he did not answer him. Then he stood up in anger and said, 'If I do that, they will claim that you call to the matter but conflict with something else.' I started to rebuke him and forbid him. He said, 'What does he say?' They said, 'He says such and such.' He said, 'If I do that, then that is upon me, not upon them in any way. Release his neighbors for him.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6707,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I am absent for months from water, and my family is with me; may I have intercourse with them?' He said, 'Yes, even if you are absent twenty years.'"],[6708,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married twelve Arab women who were muhsanat. 'Abd Allah b. Muhammad b. 'Aqil concurred with him on that. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6709,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married twelve women. Qatada b. Di'ama and other imams differed with them on that. As for the statement of Qatada about it: Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6710,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married fifteen women: six of them from Quraysh, one from the allies of Quraysh, seven from Arab women, and one from the Children of Israel. He did not marry in the pre-Islamic era except one. Abu 'Ubayda Ma'mar b. al-Muthanna differed with them, and his statement, may Allah have mercy on him, is closer to correctness. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6711,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married eighteen women: seven of them from the tribes of Quraysh, one from the allies of Quraysh, nine from the rest of the Arab tribes, and one from the Children of Israel, from the Children of Aaron b. Imran, the brother of Moses b. Imran. Abu 'Ubayda said: 'The first of his wives whom he married ﷺ in the pre-Islamic era was Khadija. Then after Khadija he married Sawda bt. Zam'a in Makkah in Islam. Then he married 'A'isha two years before the Hijra. Then he married in Madinah after the Battle of Badr, in the year two of the calendar, Umm Salama. Then he also married Hafsa bt. 'Umar in the year two of the calendar. These five are from Quraysh. Then he married in the year three of the calendar Zaynab bt. Jahsh. Then he married in the year five of the calendar Juwayriyya bt. al-Harith. Then he married in the year six of the calendar Umm Habiba bt. Abi Sufyan. Then he married in the year seven of the calendar Safiyya bt. Huyayy. Then he married Maymuna bt. al-Harith. Then he married Fatima bt. Shurayh. Then he married Zaynab bt. Khuzayma. Then he married Hind bt. Yazid. Then he married Asma' bt. al-Nu'man. Then he married Qutayla bt. Qays, the sister of al-Ash'ath. Then he married Sana' bt. al-Salt al-Sulamiyya.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6712,"The Prophet ﷺ married 'A'isha when she was seven years old, consummated the marriage when she was nine, and he died when she was eighteen. She died during the time of Mu'awiya in the year fifty-seven. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6713,"Urwa wrote to Al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Aisha after the death of Khadijah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Aisha in a dream three times, and it was said to him, 'This is your wife Aisha.' Aisha was six years old on the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her and he consummated the marriage with her. He then brought her to Medina when she was nine years old. Aisha, the mother of the believers, passed away on a Tuesday night after the Witr prayer. She was buried on the same night at Baqi' cemetery, fifteen nights into Ramadan. Abu Huraira performed her funeral prayer, while Marwan was absent, and Abu Huraira took charge after him.\""],[6714,"'A'isha bt. Abi Bakr al-Siddiq. Her mother was Umm Ruman bt. 'Amir b. 'Uwaymir b. 'Abd Shams b. 'Attab b. Udhayna b. Subay' b. Duhman b. al-Harith b. Ghanm b. Malik b. Kinana. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her in Shawwal of the tenth year after prophethood, three years before the Hijra. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with her in Shawwal, eight months after the Hijra. On the day he consummated, she was nine years old."],[6715,"To be buried in her house with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr, but she said: 'I have committed an innovation after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Bury me with his wives.' So she was buried in al-Baqi'."],[6716,"She is his wife ﷺ in this world and the Hereafter."],[6717,"She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house, on my day and night, while he was between my chest and my neck. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr entered with a fresh siwak of arak wood. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at it, so I said, 'O 'Abd al-Rahman, break it for me from that place.' He handed it to me, I took it, and he returned it to me. I broke it, straightened it, and gave it to the Prophet ﷺ, and he used it as a tooth-stick."],[6718,"'A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in my house, on my day, while he was between my chest and my neck. 'Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr entered upon him with a fresh siwak, and he looked at it until I thought he needed it. I took it, chewed it, broke it, and softened it, then gave it to him. He used it as a tooth-stick in the best manner I ever saw him use one. Then he went to hand it back to me, but his hand fell. I began to supplicate for him with a supplication that Jibril ﷺ used to make for him, and he used to make it when he was ill, but he did not make it during that illness. He raised his gaze to the sky and said, 'The Highest Companion,' and his soul departed ﷺ. Praise be to Allah who joined my saliva with his saliva on the last day of this world."],[6719,"He said: 'I used to enter the room in which 'Umar was buried with the two of them. By Allah, I never entered except with my garments wrapped tightly around me out of shyness before 'Umar.'"],[6720,"'A'isha said: I saw Jibril ﷺ standing in this room of mine while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was conversing privately with him. When he entered, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is this?' He said, 'To whom did you liken him?' I said, 'To Dihya al-Kalbi.' He said, 'You have seen much good. That is Jibril ﷺ .' It was not long before he said, 'O 'A'isha, this is Jibril conveying peace to you.' She said: I said, 'And upon him be peace. May Allah reward him well as a visitor.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6721,"'Umar allotted ten thousand to the Mothers of the Believers and added two thousand for 'A'isha, saying, 'She is the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6722,"The stipend of the people of Badr was six thousand, six thousand. The stipend of the Mothers of the Believers was ten thousand, ten thousand for each of them, except for three women: 'A'isha, for 'Umar said, 'I favor her with two thousand because of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ love for her,' and Safiyya and Juwayriyya, who received seven thousand, seven thousand."],[6723,"A chest arrived to 'Umar from Iraq containing jewels. He said to his companions, 'Do you know its value?' They said, 'No,' and they did not know how to divide it. He said, 'Do you permit me to send it to 'A'isha because of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ love for her?' They said, 'Yes.' So he sent it to her. She opened it and said, 'What has been opened for Ibn al-Khattab after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? O Allah, do not keep me alive for his gift next year.'"],[6724,"Her brother's sons said to her: 'Grant him permission, for he is among the best of your children.' She said, 'Leave me from praising him.' They kept at her until she permitted him. When he entered upon her, Ibn 'Abbas said: 'You were named Mother of the Believers so that you may be felicitous, and it was your name before you were born. You were among the most beloved of the Prophet's ﷺ wives to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ loved only what is good. Between you and meeting the beloved ones is nothing but the soul's departure from the body. Your necklace fell on the night of al-Abwa', and Allah made for the Muslims a choice in that, so Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed the verse of tayammum. Verses of the Qur'an were revealed concerning you, so there is no mosque among the mosques of the Muslims in which your exoneration is not recited during the hours of the night and the hours of the day.' She said, 'Leave me from your praise of me, O Ibn 'Abbas. I wish I were a thing forgotten, utterly forgotten.'"],[6725,"'A'isha said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry me until Jibril came to him with my image and said, 'This is your wife.' He married me while I was a young girl wearing a hawf. When he married me, Allah cast modesty upon me, and I was young. Sufyan said: Al-Zuhri said, 'Al-hawf is leather straps in its middle.'"],[6726,"Umm Salama said: I wanted to speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him to command the people to send him gifts wherever he was, for the people sought to send their gifts on 'A'isha's day, and we too love good as 'A'isha loves it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent and did not answer me. My female companions came to me, and I informed them that he ﷺ did not speak to me. They said, 'By Allah, do not leave him, and this is not the time to leave him.' She said: He came around, and I spoke to him. I said, 'My female companions told me to speak to you, asking you to command the people to send you gifts wherever you are.' I said to him the same statement two or three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent each time. Then he said, 'O Umm Salama, do not harm me regarding 'A'isha, for by Allah, revelation has not descended upon me while I was in the garment of any of my wives except 'A'isha.' She said: I said, 'I seek refuge in Allah from displeasing you regarding 'A'isha.'"],[6727,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned Fatima. She said: I spoke, and he said, 'Are you not pleased to be my wife in this world and the Hereafter?' I said, 'Yes, by Allah.' He said, 'Then you are my wife in this world and the Hereafter.' Abu al-'Anbas is Sa'id b. Kathir, a trustworthy Medinan. The hadith is sahih, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[6728,"That ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣafwān came to ʿĀʾishah with another man. ʿĀʾishah said to one of them, 'Did you hear the ḥadīth of Ḥafṣah, O so-and-so?' He said, 'Yes, O Mother of the Believers.' ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣafwān said to her, 'And what is that, O Mother of the Believers?' She said, 'I have nine qualities that no woman before me had, except what Allah ﷻ gave Maryam bt. ʿImrān. By Allah, I do not say this to boast over any of my companions.' ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṣafwān said to her, 'What are they, O Mother of the Believers?' She said, 'The angel brought my image to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me when I was seven years old, and I was given to him when I was nine years old. He married me as a virgin, which no other person had. Revelation came to him while he and I were under one blanket. I was among the most beloved of people to him. Verses of the Qur'an were revealed concerning me, which the ummah almost perished over. I saw Jibrīl ﷺ , and no one among his wives saw him except me. He passed away in my house, and no one attended him except the angel and I.'"],[6729,"It was revealed specifically concerning ʿĀʾishah."],[6730,"I never heard speech from the mouth of any creature more magnificent or more beautiful than that from the mouth of ʿĀʾishah. Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6731,"I have not seen anyone more knowledgeable than ʿĀʾishah, the Mother of the Believers, regarding the lawful, the unlawful, knowledge, poetry, and medicine. Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6732,"If the knowledge of all people were gathered, then the knowledge of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, ʿĀʾishah would be the most expansive of them in knowledge. Upon the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[6733,"I have not seen anyone more eloquent than ʿĀʾishah ؓ ."],[6734,"That he was asked, 'Was ʿĀʾishah proficient in the shares of inheritance?' He said, 'Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul. I saw the elders among the companions of Muḥammad ﷺ asking her about the shares of inheritance.'"],[6735,"I said to ʿĀʾishah, 'You recite poetry, being the daughter of al-Ṣiddīq, and you do not care, and you speak about medicine. What is your knowledge of it?' She said, 'The Prophet ﷺ used to fall ill, and delegations of the Arabs would come to him and describe remedies, and I would memorize that.' Al-Dhahabī omitted it from the Talkhīṣ."],[6736,"That she came with her parents, Abū Bakr and Umm Rūmān, to the Prophet ﷺ. They said, 'We would like you to supplicate for ʿĀʾishah with a supplication while we listen.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'O Allah, forgive ʿĀʾishah bt. Abī Bakr al-Ṣiddīq with a forgiveness that is obligatory, apparent, and hidden.' Her parents marveled at the excellence of the Prophet's ﷺ supplication for her. He said, 'Do you marvel? This is my supplication for whoever bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah.' Munkar despite the quality of its isnad."],[6737,"That the Prophet ﷺ was asked, 'Who is the most beloved of people to you?' He said, 'ʿĀʾishah.' It was said, 'We do not mean your family.' He said, 'Then Abū Bakr.'"],[6738,"The Prophet ﷺ sent me on an army that included Abū Bakr and ʿUmar. When I returned, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, who is the most beloved of people to you?' He said, 'What do you want with that?' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I want to know.' He said, 'ʿĀʾishah.' I said, 'I mean among men.' He said, 'Her father.' Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6739,"To the Prophet ﷺ when he returned from the expedition of Dhāt al-Salāsil: 'O Messenger of Allah, who is the most beloved of people to you?' He said, 'ʿĀʾishah.' He said, 'I mean among men.' He said, 'Her father.' Upon the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[6740,"To me every Mother of the Believers is dearer than Aisha. I said, \"As for you, you have contradicted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Aisha was the dearest of them to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6741,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which of your wives will be in Paradise?\" He said, \"Indeed, you are among them.\" She said, \"It occurred to me that that was because he did not marry a virgin other than me.\""],[6742,"Aisha said to me, \"I saw myself on a hill with cows being slaughtered around me.\" I said to her, \"If your dream is true, there will surely be a great battle around you.\" She said, \"I seek refuge in Allah from your evil; how bad is what you have said.\" I said to her, \"Perhaps, if it is something, it will grieve you.\" She said, \"By Allah, falling from the sky is dearer to me than doing that.\" Later, it was mentioned to her that Ali had killed Dhu al-Thudayya. She said to me, \"When you go to Kufa, write down for me the names of people who witnessed that from among those you know of the people of the town.\" When I arrived, I found the people divided into factions, so I wrote down for her from each faction ten who witnessed that. He said, \"I brought her their testimonies.\" She said, \"May Allah curse Amr b. al-As, for he claimed to me that he killed him in Egypt.\""],[6743,"Barīra, are you fasting? Why did you not buy us meat for a dirham? Aisha said, \"Had I been reminded, I would have done it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6744,"She heard the cry over Aisha and said to a servant girl, \"Go and look.\" She came back and said, \"She has passed away.\" Umm Salama said, \"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, she was the dearest of people to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except her father.\""],[6745,"Muawiya said, \"O Ziyad, who is the most knowledgeable of people?\" He said, \"You, O Commander of the Faithful.\" He said, \"I adjure you.\" He said, \"Since you adjure me, then Aisha.\""],[6746,"\"Aisha was the most knowledgeable of people, the most learned of people, and the best in judgment among the common people.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6747,"\"Hafsa bint Umar b. al-Khattab b. Nufayl b. Abd al-Uzza b. Rabah b. Abdullah b. Qurt b. Razah b. Adi b. Kab b. Luayy b. Ghalib. Her mother was Zaynab bint Mazun b. Habib b. Wahb b. Hudhafa b. Jumah. She was among the emigrants.\""],[6748,"\"Then the Prophet ﷺ married Hafsa bint Umar b. al-Khattab. Before him, she had been married to Khunays b. Hudhafa al-Sahmi.\""],[6749,"\"Would you like Hafsa?\" He turned away from me and did not answer me. Umar went to the Prophet ﷺ and complained about him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Better than that: I will marry Hafsa, and I will marry Uthman to Umm Kulthum.\" So the Prophet ﷺ married Hafsa, and Uthman married Umm Kulthum, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6750,"\"Hafsa was born while Quraysh was building the House, five years before the Prophet's ﷺ mission began.\""],[6751,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsa bint Umar. Her maternal uncles Qudama and Uthman, the two sons of Mazun, entered upon her. She wept and said, \"By Allah, he did not divorce me out of satiety.\" The Prophet ﷺ came and said, \"Jibril ﷺ said to me: Take back Hafsa, for she fasts and prays, and she is your wife in Paradise.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6752,"The Prophet ﷺ divorced Hafsah. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, \"O Muhammad, you divorced Hafsah while she is a woman who fasts often and stands in prayer often, and she is your wife in Paradise, so take her back.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6753,"Umm Salamah was the first woman to emigrate among the women."],[6754,"\"And among those who migrated with the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ from Makkah to Medina was Abu Salama, Abdullah ibn Abdul Asad, and his wife Umm Salama bint Abi Umaya.\""],[6755,"Umm Salamah's name was Ramlah, and she was the first woman to enter Madinah as an emigrant. Before the Prophet ﷺ, she was married to Abu Salamah 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Asad b. Hilal b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum. He was among the first to emigrate to Abyssinia, and he participated in Badr. He died during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She bore Abu Salamah children: Salamah, 'Umar, Durrah, and Zaynab. Their mother was Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ married her after Abu Salamah. Her son 'Umar b. Abi Salamah narrated from the Prophet ﷺ."],[6756,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When you are present with a dying person or a sick person, say good words, for the angels say ameen to what you say.\" When Abu Salamah died, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"What should I say?\" He said, \"Say: O Allah, forgive us and him, and grant me a good replacement after him.\" I said it, and Allah gave me Muhammad ﷺ in his place. It meets the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim if they did not include it."],[6757,"When a calamity befalls one of you, let him say: 'Indeed we belong to Allah, and indeed to Him we return. O Allah, with You I seek reward for my calamity, so reward me in it.' I used to want to say, 'And replace it for me with something better than it,' but I would say, 'Who is better than Abu Salamah?' I kept saying this until I finally said it. When her waiting period ended, Abu Bakr proposed to her, but she refused him. 'Umar proposed to her, but she refused him. Then the Prophet ﷺ sent someone to propose to her. She said, 'Welcome to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and to his messenger. Convey my greetings to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and tell him that I am a woman with children, that I am very jealous, and that none of my guardians is present.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent back to her: 'As for your saying that you have children, Allah will suffice you regarding your children. As for your saying that you are very jealous, I will supplicate Allah to remove your jealousy. As for the guardians, none of them, present or absent, will disapprove of me.' She said to her son, 'Arise, O 'Umar, and marry the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to me.' So he married her to him. He said to her, 'I will not give you less than what I gave your sister so-and-so: two vessels, two millstones, and a leather cushion stuffed with palm fibers.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to visit her while she was nursing Zaynab. When the Prophet ﷺ came, she would take Zaynab and place her in her lap to nurse her. She said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was modest and noble, so he would leave.' 'Ammar b. Yasir, who was her foster brother, noticed this. One day, when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to visit her, 'Ammar came and entered upon her. He snatched Zaynab from her lap and said, 'Leave this ugly, cross-eyed one who has caused annoyance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came in and looked around the house, saying, 'Where is Zunab? Why do I not see Zunab?' She said, ''Ammar came and took her away.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with his wife and said, 'If you wish, I will spend seven nights with you, and if I do that, I will spend seven nights with the other wives.'"],[6758,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah bint Abi Umayyah, she held onto his garment, preventing him from leaving her house. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you wish, I will give you more time and will count it: for a virgin, seven nights; for a previously married woman, three nights.\""],[6759,"Umm Salamah's name was Hind bint Abi Umayyah. The name of Abu Umayyah was Suhayl b. al-Mughirah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum. Her mother was 'Atikah bint 'Amir b. Rabi'ah b. Malik b. Khuzaymah b. 'Alqamah b. Firas b. Ghanm b. Malik b. Kinanah. Abu Salamah 'Abd Allah b. 'Abd al-Asad b. Hilal married her, and she emigrated with him to Abyssinia during both emigrations. There she bore him Zaynab, and later she bore him Salamah, 'Umar, and Durrah, the children of Abu Salamah."],[6760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Aisha has a branch from me that no one else has.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, what happened to the branch?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent, so it was known that Umm Salamah had taken its place. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[6761,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Salamah before the Battle of Badr, in the year two of the calendar. Her name was Hind bint Abi Umayyah b. al-Mughirah b. 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar b. Makhzum. The first of the Prophet's ﷺ wives to die was Zaynab, and the last of them to die was Umm Salamah. Saying year two is an error."],[6762,"I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was weeping. I asked, \"What makes you weep?\" She said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a dream, weeping, with dust on his head and beard. I said, 'What is wrong with you, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'I have just witnessed the killing of al-Husayn.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6763,"I came to Umm Salamah to offer condolences for the killing of al-Husayn b. 'Ali."],[6764,"When she arrived in Madinah, she told them that she was the daughter of Abu Umayyah b. al-Mughirah, but they disbelieved her and said, \"How deceitful strangers are!\" Eventually some people set out for the Hajj, and it was said to her, \"Write to your family.\" She wrote with them, and when they returned to Madinah, they believed her and held her in even greater esteem. Umm Salamah said, \"When I gave birth to Zaynab, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married me.\" Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[6765,"Umm Salamah bequeathed that Sa'id b. Zayd should pray over her, for fear that Marwan b. al-Hakam might pray over her."],[6766,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan. She had previously been married to 'Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh al-Asadi, of the Asad of Khuzaymah. He died while she was in the land of Abyssinia, having taken her there as an emigrant from Makkah. Then he was tried and became a Christian, and died a Christian, while Allah confirmed Islam and the emigration for Umm Habibah. Her husband became a Christian and died a Christian, but Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan refused to become a Christian, and Allah, exalted is He, completed Islam and the emigration for her until she arrived in Madinah. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her, and 'Uthman b. 'Affan gave her in marriage to him.\" Al-Zuhri said: \"They claimed that the Prophet ﷺ wrote to the Negus, and he gave her in marriage to him and paid on his behalf forty uqiyyahs.\""],[6767,"It is also said Aminah bt. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Harban b. 'Awf b. 'Ubayd b. 'Uwayj b. 'Adi b. Ka'b, and she died a year before Mu'awiyah."],[6768,"Umm Habibah's name was Ramlah bt. Abi Sufyan b. Harb. Her mother was Safiyyah bt. Abi al-'As b. Umayyah b. 'Abd Shams, the paternal aunt of 'Uthman b. 'Affan. 'Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh b. Rabab, the ally of Harb b. Umayyah, married her, and she bore him a daughter named Habibah, by which she was given her kunyah. Dawud b. 'Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi married Habibah."],[6769,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent 'Amr b. Umayyah al-Damri to the Negus to propose on his behalf to Umm Habibah bt. Abi Sufyan, who was then married to 'Ubayd Allah b. Jahsh. The Negus gave her in marriage to him and paid on behalf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a dowry of four hundred dinars from his own wealth.\" Abu Ja'far Muhammad b. Jarir said: \"We do not think 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan set the dowry of women at four hundred dinars except for that reason.\""],[6770,"He asked 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, how much the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave as dowry to his wives. She said: \"His dowry to his wives was twelve and a half uqiyyahs, which equals five hundred dirhams. This was the dowry of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to his wives.\""],[6771,"The Negus prepared Umm Habibah for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and sent her with Shurahbil b. Hasanah."],[6772,"Zaynab bt. Jahsh b. Rabab b. Ya'mar b. Sabirah b. Murrah b. Kathir b. Ghanm b. Dudan b. Asad b. Khuzaymah. Her mother was Umaymah bt. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim b. 'Amr b. 'Abd Manaf. Zaynab was married to Zayd b. Harithah, but he separated from her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her. Concerning her the verse was revealed: {So when Zayd had accomplished what he would of her, We gave her to you in marriage} [al-Ahzab 37]. She used to boast over the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, saying: \"Allah married me to His Messenger, while your fathers and relatives married you.\" Hamnah bt. Jahsh was the one with chronic vaginal bleeding; she was married to 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf and was the sister of Zaynab bt. Jahsh."],[6773,"Zaynab bt. Jahsh b. Rabab was the sister of 'Abd al-Rahman b. Jahsh.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his wives: \"The swiftest of you to join me is the one with the longest hand among you.\" Aisha said: \"After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whenever we gathered in the house of one of us, we would stretch our hands against the wall, trying to measure. We continued doing that until Zainab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, died. She was a short woman, and she was not the tallest of us. Then we knew that the Prophet ﷺ meant by the length of the hand charity.\" He said: \"Zainab was a woman skilled with her hands; she used to tan, sew, and give charity in the way of Allah ﷻ.\""],[6775,"Zainab bint Jahsh used to say to the Prophet ﷺ: \"I am the greatest of your wives in right upon you. I am the best of them in marriage, the most observant of concealment, and the closest of them in kinship.\" Then she would say: \"The Most Merciful ﷻ married me to you from above His Throne, and Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him) was the emissary for that. I am the daughter of your paternal aunt, and you have no close relative among your wives besides me.\" [Al-Hakim said:] \"I mentioned at the beginning of the biographical entry that the mother of Zainab bint Jahsh is Umaymah bint Abdul-Muttalib b. Hashim, and she is the paternal aunt of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[6776,"Juwayriyah bint al-Harith said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Your wives boast over me, saying: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not marry you; you are only a possession of the right hand.'\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Did I not make your dowry great? Did I not free forty slaves from your people?\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6777,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took captives from Banu al-Mustaliq, Juwayriyah bint al-Harith b. Abi Dirar fell to the share of Thabit b. Qays b. al-Shammas. He made a contract of manumission with her for herself. She was a sweet and beautiful woman; hardly anyone saw her except that she captivated him. She came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking his help with her contract of manumission. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6778,"Juwayriyah bint al-Harith b. Abi Dirar b. Habib b. A'idh b. Malik b. Jadhimah b. al-Mustaliq, from Khuza'ah. Musafi' b. Safwan had married her, and he was killed on the day of al-Muraysi'."],[6779,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took captives from Banu al-Mustaliq. He extracted the fifth from it, then divided it among the people, giving the horseman two shares and the foot soldier one share. Juwayriyah bint al-Harith b. Abi Dirar fell to the share of Thabit b. Qays b. Shammas al-Ansari. She had been under a paternal cousin of hers named Safwan b. Malik b. Jadhimah, who was killed, leaving her. Thabit b. Qays made a contract of manumission with her for herself for nine uqiyyah. She was a sweet woman; hardly anyone saw her except that she captivated him. While the Prophet ﷺ was with me, Juwayriyah entered asking him about her contract of manumission. By Allah, as soon as I saw her, I disliked her entering upon the Prophet ﷺ, and I knew that he would see in her what I saw. She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I am Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, chief of his people. You know what has befallen me. I fell to the share of Thabit b. Qays, and he made a contract with me for nine uqiyyah for my ransom.\" He said: \"Or better than that?\" She said: \"What is it?\" He said: \"I will pay your contract of manumission and marry you.\" She said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"I have done it.\" The news spread to the people, and they said: \"The in-laws of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are being enslaved!\" So they freed whoever was in their hands from the captives of Banu al-Mustaliq. Their manumission reached one hundred households because of his marriage to her. Aisha said: \"I know of no woman who was a greater blessing to her people than her.\" That was upon his return from the expedition of al-Muraysi'."],[6780,"He is called Musaafir, son of Safwan, son of Dhi al-Shaffar."],[6781,"Her name was Barrah, and he ﷺ changed it, naming her Juwayriyah. He disliked it being said: 'He came out from Barrah.' [Al-Hakim said:] \"Sahih according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not include it.\" According to the condition of Muslim."],[6782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ imposed the veil on Juwayriyah and used to allocate for her as he allocated for his wives."],[6783,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and said: \"Is there any food?\" She said: \"No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we have no food except a bone from a sheep that I gave to my freed slave as charity.\" He said: \"Bring it, for it has reached its proper place.\""],[6784,"He heard Anas b. Malik say: \"When the Prophet ﷺ conquered Khaybar, he chose Safiyyah bint Huyayy for himself. The Prophet ﷺ set out with her, placing her behind him.\" Then he said: \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placing his leg so that she could step on it and mount. When he reached Sadd al-Sahba', he stopped with her and made hais in a leather mat. He ordered me, and I invited those around him. That was the wedding feast of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Mus'ab said: \"She is Safiyyah bint Huyayy b. Akhtab b. Sa'id b. Tha'labah b. Ubayd b. al-Khazraj b. Abi Habib b. al-Nadr b. al-Nahham b. Yanhum, from the Children of Israel, from the tribe of Musa (peace and blessings be upon him). Her mother was Barrah bint al-Samaw'al; she died during the time of Mu'awiyah.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6785,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated his marriage with Safiyyah, Abu Ayyub spent the night at the door of the Prophet ﷺ. When morning came and he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said takbir, and Abu Ayyub had a sword with him. He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, she was a young girl newly married, and I had killed her father, her brother, and her husband, so I did not feel safe for you from her.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed and said to him, \"Good.\""],[6786,"I heard Anas b. Malik say, \"The Prophet ﷺ fed bread and meat for Safiyyah bt. Huyayy.\""],[6787,"I am one of the women who escorted Safiyyah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard her say, \"I had not reached seventeen, and I strove to reach seventeen years old on the night I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"Safiyyah died in the year fifty-two during the time of Mu'awiyah and was buried in al-Baqi'.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6788,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me while I was crying. He said, \"O daughter of Huyayy, what makes you cry?\" I said, \"It has reached me that Hafsah and A'ishah disparage me and say: We are better than her; we are the daughters of the paternal uncle of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wives.\" He said, \"Why did you not say: How can you be better than me when my father is Harun, my uncle is Musa, and my husband is Muhammad, may Allah's blessings and peace be upon them?\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6789,"Mis'ar b. Kidam narrated to me: \"The wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Maymunah bt. al-Harith b. Hazn b. Bujayr b. al-Harim b. Ruwaybah b. 'Abd Allah b. Hilal b. 'Amir b. Sa'sa'ah, narrated to me. Her mother was Hind bt. 'Awf b. Zuhayr b. al-Harith b. Hamatah b. Harith from Himyar.\""],[6790,"\"Maymunah bt. al-Harith b. Hamatah b. Harith, and she is the maternal aunt of 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas and the sister of Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith. She had married in the Jahiliyyah Mas'ud b. 'Amr b. 'Umayr al-Thaqafi, then he separated from her. Then Abu Ruhm b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Abi Qays from Banu Malik b. Hisl b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy married her, and he died leaving her. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her; al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib gave her in marriage to him, and he was her guardian. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with her at Sarif, ten miles from Makkah. She was the last woman the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married, and that was in the year seven during the Umrah of the Qadiyyah.\" Ibn 'Umar said, \"Maymunah died in the year sixty-one, and she was the last of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ to die. On the day she died she was eighty or eighty-one years old, and despite her advanced age she was vigorous.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6791,"\"My maternal aunt Maymunah's name was Barrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Maymunah.\" Sahih. Al-Dhahabi said: Sahih."],[6792,"\"Maymunah's name was Barrah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named her Maymunah.\" Sahih."],[6793,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ set out the following year, the year of Hudaybiyyah, to perform Umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah in the year seven, which is the month in which the polytheists had turned him away from the Sacred Mosque. When he reached Ya'jaj, he sent Ja'far b. Abi Talib ahead of him to Maymunah bt. al-Harith b. Hazn al-'Amiriyyah to propose to her on his behalf. She placed her affair in the hands of al-'Abbas b. 'Abd al-Muttalib, for her sister Umm al-Fadl was married to him. Al-'Abbas married her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ stayed at Sarif for a while after that until Maymunah arrived, and he consummated the marriage with her at Sarif. Allah Almighty ordained that Maymunah bt. al-Harith's death should occur after that by a while, so she died where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ consummated the marriage with her.\""],[6794,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymunah bt. al-Harith and stayed in Makkah for three nights. Then Huwaytib b. 'Abd al-'Uzza came to him with a group of Quraysh on the third day and said to him, \"Your term has ended, so depart from us.\" He said, \"What harm would it do you if you left me to hold a wedding feast among you, prepare food for you, and you attended it?\" They said, \"We have no need for your food, so depart from us.\" So he departed with Maymunah bt. al-Harith until he consummated the marriage with her at Sarif."],[6795,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her while he was not in ihram and consummated the marriage with her while not in ihram. He consummated it with her at Sarif, and she died at Sarif on the night in which he consummated the marriage. She was my maternal aunt, so I and Ibn 'Abbas descended into her grave. When we placed her in the niche, her head tilted, so I took my cloak, folded it, and placed it by her head. Ibn 'Abbas took it and threw it away, and he placed a piece of limestone by her head.\" He said, \"She had shaved her head during the Hajj, and her hair was gathered up. Between Sarif and Makkah there are twelve miles.\""],[6796,"\"The Prophet ﷺ married while he was in ihram.\" 'Amr said, \"I mentioned that to al-Zuhri.\" Then he said, \"O 'Amr, who do you think she was?\" I said, \"They say Maymunah.\" Ibn Shihab said, \"Yazid b. al-Asamm informed me that the Prophet ﷺ married her while he was not in ihram.\" 'Amr said to Ibn Shihab, \"Do you make a bedouin who urinates on his heels like Ibn 'Abbas?\" Ibn Shihab said, \"She is his maternal aunt.\" 'Amr said, \"She is also Ibn 'Abbas's maternal aunt.\""],[6797,"I met Aisha while she was returning from Makkah, myself and a son of Talha b. Ubayd Allah, who was her nephew. We had entered one of the walled gardens of Madinah and taken something from it. News of that reached her, and she turned to her nephew, blaming and reproaching him. Then she turned to me and gave me an eloquent admonition, then said: \"Do you not know that Allah, exalted is He, drove you until He placed you among the household of His Prophet? By Allah, Maymuna has gone, and your nose rope has been thrown onto your withers. She was among the most pious of us toward Allah, may He be glorified, and among the most devoted of us to maintaining family ties.\""],[6798,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one night from my place, and I locked the door behind him. He came asking for permission to enter, but I refused to open. He said, \"I swear that you will not open for me.\" I said to him, \"You go to your wives on my night?\" He said, \"I did not do that, but I felt a need to urinate.\" (Al-Dhahabi omitted this from the Talkhis.)"],[6799,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The sisters are believers: Maymuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ; her sister Umm al-Fadl bt. al-Harith; her sister Salma bt. al-Harith, the wife of Hamza; and Asma' bt. Umays, their maternal sister.\""],[6800,"Ibn Abbas said: \"This is Maymuna. When you lift her bier, do not shake it or jolt it, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had nine wives. He used to apportion his time among eight of them, and one he did not apportion for.\" Ata' said: \"She was Safiyya.\""],[6801,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Maymuna bt. al-Harith b. Farwa, who was the sister of Umm al-Fadl, the wife of al-Abbas b. Abd al-Muttalib, when he performed the Umrah in Makkah. She gave herself to the Prophet ﷺ, and about her was revealed: {And a believing woman if she gives herself to the Prophet, if the Prophet desires to marry her, exclusively for you, not for the believers} [al-Ahzab 50]. Then she returned with him to Madinah. Before him, she had been married to Farwa b. Abd al-Uzza b. Asad of the Banu Tamim b. Dudan. (Al-Dhahabi omitted this from the Talkhis.)"],[6802,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Khuzayma, one of the Banu Hilal b. Amir. Before him, she had been married to Abd Allah b. Jahsh, who was killed in the Battle of Uhud.\""],[6803,"\"Zaynab bt. Khuzayma b. al-Harith b. Abd Allah b. Amr b. Abd Manaf b. Hilal b. Amir b. Sa'sa'a died. She was Umm al-Masakin (Mother of the Poor), as she was called in the pre-Islamic era. She died in Madinah after the Hijrah during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" (Al-Dhahabi was silent about this in the Talkhis.)"],[6804,"\"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Zaynab bt. Khuzayma, and she was Umm al-Masakin of the Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'a. Before him, she had been married to al-Tufayl b. al-Harith. She died while with the Prophet ﷺ, and she stayed with him only a short while.\" (Al-Dhahabi was silent about this in the Talkhis.)"],[6805,"\"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married al-Aliyah, a woman of the Banu Bakr b. Kilab.\""],[6806,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a woman from the Banu Ghifar. When she entered upon him and took off her clothes, he saw a whiteness on her flank. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: \"Put on your clothes and return to your family,\" and he ordered that she be given her dower. \"This is not the Kalbiyya; rather, she is Asma' bt. al-Nu'man al-Ghifariyya.\" (Ibn Ma'in said: Zayd is not trustworthy.)"],[6807,"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married from the people of Yemen Asma' bt. al-Nu'man al-Ghifariyya, who was the daughter of al-Nu'man b. al-Harith b. Sharahil b. al-Nu'man. When he consummated the marriage with her, he called her, and she said, \"You come to me.\" So he divorced her. (Al-Dhahabi was silent about this in the Talkhis.)"],[6808,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Sharik al-Ansariyya of the Banu al-Najjar, and he said: \"I love to marry among the Ansar.\" Then he said: \"But I dislike their jealousy.\" So he did not consummate the marriage with her. (Al-Dhahabi was silent about this in the Talkhis.)"],[6809,"«The Prophet ﷺ married Sanaa, the daughter of Asma b. al-Salt al-Sulamiyya, and she died before he consummated the marriage with her.»"],[6810,"And regarding al-Kilabiyya, there has been a difference concerning her name. Some of them said: She is Fatima bt. al-Dahhak b. Sufyan al-Kilabi. Others said: She is 'Amra bt. Zayd b. 'Ubayd b. Ruwas b. Kilab b. 'Amir. Others said: She is Saba' bt. Sufyan b. 'Awf b. Ka'b b. 'Ubayd b. Abi Bakr b. Kilab. Others said: She is al-'Aliya bt. Zabyan. Others said: There was only one Kilabiyya, and the difference is only in her name. Others said: Rather, they were all [Kilabiyyat], but each one of them has a story different from the story of her companion."],[6811,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married al-Kilabiyya. When she entered upon him and he approached her, she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: «You have sought refuge in a great one; join your family.» Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6812,"The daughter of Abu al-Jawn, when she entered upon him and he approached her, she said: I seek refuge in Allah from you. He said: «You have sought refuge in a great one; join your family.»"],[6813,"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married a woman from Kinda, and she is al-Shaqiyya, the one who asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to return her to her people and to separate from her. So he did, and he sent her back with a man from the Ansar called Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6814,"Al-Nu'man b. Abi al-Jawn al-Kindi came forward. He and the sons of his father used to dwell in Najd, in the area adjacent to al-Sharba. He came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a Muslim and said: O Messenger of Allah, shall I not marry you to the most beautiful previously married woman among the Arabs? She had been under a cousin of hers who died, leaving her a widow, and she has desired you and has been proposed to on your behalf. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her for twelve uqiyyas and a nashsh. He said: O Messenger of Allah, do not be remiss with her regarding the dowry. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: «I have not given as a dowry to any of my wives more than this, nor will I give as a dowry to any of my daughters more than this.» Al-Nu'man b. Abi al-Jawn said: In you there is the medicine [or: the cure]. He said: So send, O Messenger of Allah, to your family someone who will bring them to you, for I am going out with your messenger and will send your family with him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi. When they arrived at her place, she sat in her house and gave him permission to enter. Abu Usayd said: The wives of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are not seen by men. Abu Usayd said: And that was after the hijab had been revealed. She sent to him: Make my affair easy for me. He said: A screen between you and any men you speak to, except for one who is a mahram of yours. She accepted. Abu Usayd said: I stayed three days, then I set out with the woman in a howdah on a camel, and I brought her until I arrived in Madinah. I lodged her among the Banu Sa'ida. The women of the neighborhood entered upon her, welcomed her, and made things easy, then left her, mentioning her beauty. That spread in Madinah, and they talked about her arrival. Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi said: I returned to the Prophet ﷺ while he was among the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf and informed him. A woman entered upon her, for the women had heard of her beauty, and she was among the most beautiful of women. She said: You are one of the royal women, so if you want to be favored with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, seek refuge from him, for you will be favored with him and he will desire you. Its chain is weak."],[6815,"Abu 'Ubayda Ma'mar b. al-Muthanna said: «Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married, when the delegation of Kinda came to him, Qutayla bt. Qays, the sister of al-Ash'ath b. Qays, in the year ten. Then he fell ill in the middle of Safar, then he passed away on Monday, two days having passed of the month of Rabi' al-Awwal, and she had not arrived to him and he had not consummated the marriage with her.» Some of them specified the time of his marriage to her and claimed that he married her a month before his death. Others claimed that he married her during his illness. Others claimed that he instructed that Qutayla be given a choice, and if she wished, [she could choose marriage], so she chose marriage, and 'Ikrima b. Abi Jahl married her in Hadramawt. This reached Abu Bakr, and he said: I have considered burning the two of them. 'Umar b. al-Khattab said: She is not one of the Mothers of the Believers, the Prophet ﷺ did not consummate the marriage with her, nor did he impose the hijab on her. And some of them claimed that she apostatized."],[6816,"«And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Maria al-Qibtiyya as a concubine, and she bore him Ibrahim.»"],[6817,"Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Mariah b. Shamun, who was gifted to him by the Muqawqis (Cyrus, man of the Caucasus), the ruler of Alexandria. She came with her sister Sirin and a eunuch called Mabur. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gifted Sirin to Hassan b. Thabit. Coptic Muqawqis and them were Christians. Mariah bore Ibrahim to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the month of Dhu al-Hijjah in the eighth year of Hijrah. Ibrahim died in Madinah when he was eighteen months old."],[6818,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, died, he said: «He has a wet nurse in Paradise.» Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[6819,"Maria was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with her was a cousin of hers. She said: He had intercourse with her once, and she became pregnant. She said: Then he secluded her with her cousin. She said: The people of falsehood and slander said: Because of his need for a child, he claimed the child of another. His mother had little milk, so she bought for him a milking ewe, and he was fed with its milk, and his flesh became good. Aisha said: One day he was brought in to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: «How do you see him?» I said: Whoever is fed with the flesh of sheep, his flesh becomes good. He said: «And the resemblance?» She said: What carries women of jealousy carried me, so I said: I do not see a resemblance. She said: What the people were saying reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he said to Ali: «Take this sword and go and strike the neck of Maria's cousin wherever you find him.» She said: He went, and there he was in a garden on a palm tree, harvesting fresh dates. She said: When he saw Ali with the sword, trembling came upon him, and the cloth fell, and he was one for whom Allah ﷻ had not created what men have—he was emasculated. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6820,"«Abu Bakr used to spend on Maria until he died, then Umar took over spending on her until she died during his caliphate.»"],[6821,"«The mother of Ibrahim was accused of [an affair with] a man, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered his neck to be struck. They looked, and he was a eunuch.» I said to Yahya: Who narrated to you? He said: 'Affan, from Hammad b. Salama."],[6822,"A man was accused in connection with Umm Ibrahim (Maria), the son of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to ‘Ali, “Go and strike his neck.” ‘Ali came to him and found him in a well cooling himself. ‘Ali said to him, “Come out,” and he extended his hand, so he pulled him out, and he was mutilated, having no male organ."],[6823,"The Prophet ﷺ took me by the hand, and I went with him to Ibrahim, his son, who was playing by himself. The Prophet ﷺ took him into his room and kept him there until his soul departed. He then placed him down and cried. I said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, you cry even though you have forbidden crying?\" He said, \"I have not forbidden crying, but I have forbidden two foolish and sinful voices: a voice produced during idle entertainment, play, and the devil's flutes, and a voice produced during a calamity that involves striking faces and tearing garments. This is mercy, and whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy. If it were not for the fact that it is a true promise and a true saying, and that the first will join the latter, we would have been more sorrowful for you than this. Indeed, O Ibrahim, our eyes shed tears, our hearts grieve, but we do not say anything that angers the Lord.\" (This part has been excluded by Al-Dhahabi in his summary.)"],[6824,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked barefoot behind the funeral procession of his son Ibrahim."],[6825,"Maria, the mother of the Prophet's ﷺ son, died in Madinah in the year seventeen, and the Commander of the Faithful ‘Umar b. al-Khattab prayed over her, and she was buried in al-Baqi‘."],[6826,"Rarely did a person come to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining of pain but that he said to him, “Get cupped,” nor of pain in his legs but that he said to him, “Dye them with henna.”"],[6827,"From Maymuna bt. Sa‘d, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the child of adultery. He said, “Two sandals with which I wage jihad are dearer to me than freeing the child of adultery.”"],[6828,"I entered upon Umm Imama, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and she said, \"I was once pouring water onto his (the Prophet's) hands while he was performing ablution when a man entered and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I want to return to my family, so give me some advice that I can hold on to.' He (the Prophet) said, 'Do not associate anything with Allah, even if you are cut into pieces and burned in fire. Do not disobey your parents, even if they command you to leave your family and worldly possessions behind, so obey them and do not neglect intentionally performing prayers, for whoever intentionally neglects it has no guarantee from Allah the Almighty or from His Messenger ﷺ . Do not consume alcohol, as it is the root of every sin. Do not exceed limits in your boundaries, for you will come on the Day of Resurrection with the weight of seven earths on your neck. Do not flee on the day of battle, for whoever flees on that day has earned the wrath of Allah, and his abode will be Hellfire, and what an evil destination it is. Spend on your family according to your means, and do not raise your stick (to harm them) and hide them from Allah the Almighty.'\" According to the transmitted chain."],[6829,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took Rayhana from Banu Qurayza as a concubine, and she joined her family."],[6830,"Abu Ubaidah Ma'mar ibn al-Muthanna mentioned that Rayhana bint Zayd ibn Sam'un from the Banu al-Nadir, whom some said belonged to the Banu Qurayza, was one of the milk yamin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ . She used to be among the palm trees, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes take a nap with her. He captured her in Shawwal in the fourth year. Abu Ubaidah stated that they were four: Maria al-Qibtiyya, Rayhana, and Jumeila, whom he acquired as captives and his wives feared they would have dominance over them. He also had another concubine, Nafisa, who was gifted to him by Zainab bint Jahsh. He had distanced himself from her concerning the matter of Safiyya bint Huyayy in the months of Dhu al-Hijjah, Muharram, and Safar. When the month of Rabi' al-Awwal came, during which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away, he became pleased with Zainab and visited her. She said, 'I do not know how to repay you,' and gifted her to him ﷺ . Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in \"Al-Talkhis.\""],[6831,"The eldest of the Prophet's ﷺ daughters was Zaynab bt. Khadijah."],[6832,"I heard ‘Ubayd Allah b. Muhammad b. Sulayman al-Hashimi say, “Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was born in the year thirty of the Prophet's ﷺ birth in Makkah, and she died in the year eight of the Hijra.”"],[6833,"While I was preparing to travel from Makkah to my father, Hind bt. ‘Utba b. Rabi‘a followed me and said, “O daughter of Muhammad, has it not reached me that you want to join your father?” I said, “I did not intend that.” She said, “O cousin, do not do it. If you need any supplies for your journey to help you reach your father, I have what you need.” Zaynab said, “By Allah, I do not think she said that except to make me do it. But I feared her and denied that I intended that. So I prepared myself. When I finished my preparations, my brother-in-law Kinana b. al-Rabi‘, the brother of my husband, came and brought me a camel. I mounted it, and he took his bow and quiver and set out with me in daylight, leading the camel while she was in her howdah. The men of Quraysh talked about it and went out in pursuit of her until they caught up with her at Dhu Tuwa. The first to reach her were Habbar b. al-Aswad b. al-Muttalib b. Asad b. ‘Abd al-‘Uzza and Nafi‘ b. ‘Abd Qays al-Fihri, due to kinship from Banu Abi ‘Ubayd in Ifriqiya. Habbar frightened her with a spear while she was in her howdah. The woman was pregnant, as they claim. When she was frightened, she miscarried her unborn child. Her brother-in-law knelt down and emptied his quiver, then said, “No man comes near me except that I put an arrow in him.” The people held back from him. Abu Sufyan came with a group of Quraysh and said, “O man, withhold your arrows from us until we speak to you.” He withheld them. Abu Sufyan approached until he stood before him and said, “You have not done right. You went out with the woman openly before the people, and you know our calamity and disaster and what Muhammad ﷺ has brought upon us. The people will think, since his daughter has been taken out to him openly before the people from among us, that this is due to humiliation that befell us because of our calamity, and that it is weakness and impotence on our part. By my life, we have no need to keep her from her father. But return with the woman until the clamor subsides and people talk that we have sent her back; then take her secretly and deliver her to her father.” He did so. He returned and she stayed for some nights. When the clamor subsided, he went out with her at night until he handed her over to Zayd b. Haritha and his companion, and they brought her to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6834,"From ‘A’isha, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, his daughter Zaynab left Makkah with Kinana or Ibn Kinana. They went out in her pursuit, and Habbar b. al-Aswad caught up with her. He kept thrusting her camel with his spear until he threw her down, and she miscarried and bled. She was carried away, and Banu Hashim and Banu Umayya disputed over her. Banu Umayya said, “We have more right to her,” because she was married to their cousin Abu al-‘As. She ended up with Hind bt. ‘Utba b. Rabi‘a, and Hind kept saying to her, “This is because of your father.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Zayd b. Haritha, “Will you not go and bring me Zaynab?” He said, “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Take my ring and give it to her.” Zayd went, leaving his camel, and kept being gentle until he met a shepherd. He said, “For whom do you tend sheep?” He said, “For Abu al-‘As.” He said, “For whom are these sheep?” He said, “For Zaynab bt. Muhammad.” He walked with him a little, then said to him, “Would you like me to give you something to give to her, and do not mention it to anyone?” He said, “Yes.” He gave him the ring. The shepherd went, brought his sheep in, and gave her the ring. She recognized it and said, “Who gave you this?” He said, “A man.” She said, “Where did you leave him?” He said, “At such-and-such a place.” She remained silent until night came, then she went out to him. When she came to him, he said to her, “Ride.” She said, “No, but you ride in front of me.” He rode and she rode behind him until she arrived. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “She is the best of my daughters; she was afflicted because of me.” That reached ‘Ali b. al-Husayn, so he went to ‘Urwa and said, “What is this hadith that has reached me from you, which you narrate and by which you diminish the right of Fatima?” ‘Urwa said, “By Allah, I would not like to have everything between the east and the west while diminishing Fatima’s right that belongs to her. Henceforth, I will never narrate it again.”"],[6835,"Imam Abu Bakr, at the end of this expression “the best of my daughters,” meant “one of the best of my daughters,” because the reports are firmly established and authentic from the Prophet ﷺ that Fatima (peace be upon her) is the mistress of the women of this community. Likewise, it is established from the Prophet ﷺ that he said, “Fatima is the mistress of the women of Paradise except Maryam bt. ‘Imran.” I have dictated from this genre that the Arabs may say “afdal” meaning “min afdal,” and in my books there is what suffices, Allah Almighty willing. Imam Abu Bakr has sufficiently clarified this expression, and we do not add to what he says since he is truly the foremost imam. However, under this word there is a nuance that leads to another meaning different from what he said: that knowledge encompasses that Zaynab was older than Fatima in age, born before her. It is possible to say that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ meant by his saying “afdal” i.e., the eldest and earliest of my children, and Allah knows best."],[6836,"Zaynab bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ died in the year eight of the Hijra."],[6837,"Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was the eldest of his daughters. The cause of her death was that when she left Makkah to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Habbar b. al-Aswad and another man caught up with her. One of them pushed her, as was said, so she fell onto a rock and miscarried her fetus, as she was pregnant, and bled. Her pain did not cease until she died from it."],[6838,"When the people of Makkah sent ransoms for their captives, Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, sent a necklace to ransom Abu al-As. Khadijah had given it to her for Abu al-As when he consummated the marriage with her. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, he felt great compassion for her and said: “If you see fit to release her captive and return to her what belongs to her.”"],[6839,"Zainab, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, the wife of Abu al-As, gave protection to her husband Abu al-As b. al-Rabi. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ validated her protection."],[6840,"“Zainab, I have granted protection to Abu al-As.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “We have granted protection to whom Zainab has protected. Indeed, the lowliest of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims.”"],[6841,"From Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, that Abu al-As b. al-Rabi sent to Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: “Obtain for me a guarantee of safety from your father.” She went out and looked out from the door of her room while the Prophet ﷺ was in the morning, praying with the people, and she said: “O people, I am Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I have granted protection to Abu al-As.” When the Prophet ﷺ finished the prayer, he said: “O people, I had no knowledge of this until you heard it. Indeed, the lowliest of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims.”"],[6842,"“I saw on Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a silk garment with stripes.”"],[6843,"Zainab, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died. He went out with her funeral procession and we went out with him. We saw him gloomy and sad. When the Prophet ﷺ entered her grave, he came out with a bright face. We asked him about that and he said: “She was a sickly woman, and I remembered the severity of death and the squeezing of the grave, so I supplicated to Allah to lighten it for her.”"],[6844,"“The Prophet ﷺ returned his daughter Zainab to her husband Abu al-As after two years, according to her first marriage contract, and he did not renew a dower.”"],[6845,"In naming those who went out in the first migration to Abyssinia before the departure of Ja'far and his companions: “Uthman b. Affan with his wife Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[6846,"I heard Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Sulayman b. Ja'far b. Sulayman al-Hashimi say: “Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was born in the thirty-third year after the Prophet's ﷺ birth.”"],[6847,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Go out with Ruqayyah with you.” He said: “I think one of you two will be patient with the other.” Then the Prophet ﷺ sent Asma' bt. Abi Bakr and said: “Bring me news of them.” Asma' returned to the Prophet ﷺ while Abu Bakr was with him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, he brought out a saddled donkey, mounted her on it, and took her toward the sea.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Abu Bakr, they are indeed the first to migrate after Lot and Abraham (peace be upon them).”"],[6848,"“Ruqayyah lived until Uthman married her. A boy named Abdullah was born to Uthman from Ruqayyah, and he died while young. After that, Uthman was called Abu Abdullah.” Ibn Ishaq said: “Some of the people of knowledge told me that some young men of Abyssinia saw Ruqayyah, the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, while she was there with Uthman. She was one of the most beautiful of mankind, and they used to go to her and be amazed at her beauty, until Allah killed them in battle when the Negus marched against his enemy.” Ibn Ishaq said: “It is said that Abdullah b. Uthman died in Jumada al-Ula in the year four, when he was six years old.”"],[6849,"The Prophet ﷺ left Uthman and Usamah b. Zayd behind with Ruqayyah during her illness and went out to Badr while she was sick. Zayd b. Harithah came on al-Adba' with the glad tidings, and Ruqayyah had died. We heard the clamor, and by Allah, we did not believe the glad tidings until we saw the captives."],[6850,"When Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"No man who approached his wife last night should enter the grave.\" So Uthman did not enter the grave."],[6851,"I witnessed the burial of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was sitting at the grave, and I saw his eyes shedding tears. He said, \"Is there among you a man who did not approach his wife last night?\" Abu Talhah said, \"I, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Then descend into her grave.\""],[6852,"I entered upon Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wife of Uthman, and in her hand was a comb. She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left from me just now; I combed his hair, and he said to me, 'How do you find Abu Abdullah?' I said, 'Well.' He said, 'Honor him, for he is among the most resembling of my companions to me in character.'\""],[6853,"I entered upon Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and in her hand was a comb. She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left from me just now; I combed his hair, and he said to me, 'How do you find Uthman?'\" She said, \"I said, 'Well.' He said, 'Honor him, for he is among the most resembling of my companions to me in character.'\""],[6854,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ allotted to Uthman his share on the day of Badr, and he had stayed behind with his wife Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she had contracted measles. Zayd b. Harithah came as a bearer of good news of the victory, and with him was a sacrificial camel, while Uthman was at the grave of Ruqayyah burying her."],[6855,"And the name of Umm Kulthum, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, was Umayyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her to Uthman after Ruqayyah in the month of Rabi' al-Awwal, and she entered upon him in Jumada al-Akhirah in the year eight, and she died while she was with Uthman in Sha'ban in the year nine. And Umm Atiyyah al-Ansariyyah was the one who washed her along with some women of the Ansar."],[6856,"Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, and Uthman married Umm Kulthum, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6857,"When Ruqayyah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, died, Umar passed by Uthman and said, \"Would you like Hafsah, daughter of Umar?\" But he did not answer him anything. So Umar came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Perhaps Allah, the Exalted, O Umar, will bring you an in-law who is better for you than Uthman.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married the daughter of Umar, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Umm Kulthum to Uthman. And before that, Abu Bakr had proposed to her and Umar had proposed to her, but he did not marry her to them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The best intercessor for Uthman is that I do not marry my daughters, but Allah, the Exalted, marries them.\""],[6858,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ met Uthman b. Affan while he was grieved. He said, \"What is the matter with you, O Uthman?\" He said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah. Has anyone among the people suffered what has befallen me? The daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, may Allah have mercy on her, has died, and the in-law relationship between me and you is cut off forever.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you say that, O Uthman, while this is Jibril ﷺ commanding me by the command of Allah, may He be exalted, to marry you to her sister Umm Kulthum with a dowry like hers and a waiting period like hers?\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her to him."],[6859,"About silk, do women wear it or not? He claimed that Anas b. Malik narrated to him that he saw on Umm Kulthum, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a garment of striped silk."],[6860,"From Umm Kulthum, daughter of the Prophet ﷺ, that she said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is my husband better or the husband of Fatimah?\" She said, \"The Prophet ﷺ was silent, then he said, 'Your husband is among those who love Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.'\" She turned away, and he said to her, \"Come, what did I say?\" She said, \"You said, 'My husband is among those who love Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love.'\" He said, \"Yes, and I will increase you: I entered Paradise and saw his station, and I did not see any of my companions surpassing him in his station.\""],[6861,"No one among the daughters of Abd al-Muttalib lived to see Islam except Safiyyah. He said, \"And the Prophet ﷺ allotted her two shares.\" She was the full sister of Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib, sharing both father and mother."],[6862,"\"Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib, the mother of Zubayr b. al-Awwam, died in the year 20 AH, and on the day she died she was seventy-three years old. Umar b. al-Khattab prayed over her and buried her in al-Baqi'.\""],[6863,"\"Safiyyah bt. Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, and her mother was Halah bt. Wuhaib b. Abd Manaf b. Zuhrah b. Kilab. She was the maternal sister of Hamzah b. Abd al-Muttalib. In the pre-Islamic era, al-Harith b. Harb b. Umayyah b. Abd Shams married her, and she bore him Safi. Then al-Awwam b. Khuwailid b. Usaid succeeded in marrying her, and she bore him al-Zubayr, al-Sa'ib, and Abd al-Ka'bah. She embraced Islam and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and she emigrated to Madinah and lived after him until the caliphate of Umar b. al-Khattab. She narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[6864,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the Trench, he placed his wives in a fortress called Fari', and he placed Hassan b. Thabit with them. Then the Jews came to the fortress seeking an opportunity against the wives of the Prophet ﷺ. A man from the fortress climbed up upon us, so I said to him, \"O Hassan, get up to him and kill him.\" He said, \"By Allah, that is not in me. If that were in me, I would have been with the Prophet ﷺ.\" I said to him, \"Tie this sword to my arm.\" So he tied it, and I got up to him and struck his head until I severed it. I said to him, \"Take him by his ears and throw him at them.\" He said, \"By Allah, that is not in me.\" So I took his head and threw it at them, and they fell back, saying, \"We knew that Muhammad would not leave his family as a rear guard with no one with them.\" She said, \"When the polytheists pressed hard, Hassan went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was with us in the fortress, and when he returned, he returned behind him just as the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned, while he was there. Sa'd b. Mu'adh passed by us, having taken some yellow dye, and he was at a wedding celebration a few days before that, and he was reciting rajaz poetry: 'Slowly, a little; the battle will catch up with the camel. No harm in death when the appointed time arrives.'\" A'ishah said, \"I never saw a man more handsome than him on that day.\""],[6865,"Urwah said: I heard her say, \"I was the first woman to kill a man. I was in Fari', the fortress of Hassan b. Thabit, and Hassan was with us among the women and children when the Prophet ﷺ dug the Trench.\" Safiyyah said, \"A man from the Jews passed by us and began to circle the fortress. I said to Hassan, 'This Jew is at the fortress as you see, and I do not trust that he will point out our vulnerable spots. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions are occupied away from us. So get up to him and kill him.' He said, 'May Allah forgive you, O daughter of Abd al-Muttalib. By Allah, you know that I am not a man for this.'\" Safiyyah said, \"When he said that and I saw nothing with him, I girded myself, took a post from the fortress, then descended from the fortress to him and struck him with the post until I killed him. Then I returned to the fortress and said, 'O Hassan, go down and strip him, for nothing prevented me from stripping him except that he is a man.' He said, 'I have no need of his spoils.'\""],[6866,"Quraysh did not disapprove of the Duha prayer; they only disapproved of the time. \"When the time of Asr came, they dispersed to the mountain passes and prayed singly and in pairs.\" Tulayb b. Umayr and Hatib b. Abd Shams went out praying in the pass of Ajnad, some of them looking at others, when Ibn al-Usaydi and Ibn al-Qibtiyyah, who were two obscene men, attacked them and pelted them with stones for a while until they left and departed, fleeing. They went to Abu Jahl, Abu Lahab, and Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt and mentioned the news to them, so they set out against them at dawn. They used to go out in the darkness of dawn, perform ablution, and pray. While they were in a pass, Abu Jahl, Uqbah, Abu Lahab, and a number of their fools attacked them, seized them, and harmed them. The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ then showed their Islam, spoke openly about it, called to them, and defended themselves. Tulayb b. Umayr deliberately went for Abu Jahl and struck him, wounding his head. They seized him and bound him, but Abu Lahab stood up for him until he untied him, because he was his nephew. It was said to Arwa bt. Abd al-Muttalib, \"Do you not see your son Tulayb? He has followed Muhammad and has become a target for him.\" Arwa had already embraced Islam, so she said, \"The best of Tulayb's days is a day when he defends his maternal cousin. He has brought the truth from Allah the Exalted.\" They said, \"So you have followed Muhammad?\" She said, \"Yes.\" Some of them went out to Abu Lahab and informed him, so he came until he entered upon her and said, \"I am amazed at you and at your following Muhammad, and you have abandoned the religion of Abd al-Muttalib.\" She said, \"That has happened. So stand up for your nephew, support him, and protect him. If his affair prevails, then you have the choice: if you wish, you may enter with him, or you may remain upon your religion. And if it does not prevail, you will have excused yourself before your nephew.\" He said, \"We have the strength to face all the Arabs. Then they will say that he has brought a newly invented religion.\" Then Abu Lahab departed. I did not find her Islam except in the book of Abu Abdullah al-Waqidi."],[6867,"That her name was Fakhitah."],[6868,"From Fakhitah, who is Umm Hani' bt. Abi Talib: She said, \"I saw the Prophet ﷺ pray the morning prayer on the day of the conquest in a single garment, having wrapped its two ends opposite each other, eight rak'ahs.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6869,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to his uncle Abu Talib for Umm Hani' before revelation came to him, and Hubayrah b. Abi Wahb proposed to her along with him, so he married her to Hubayrah. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"O Umar, you married Hubayrah and left me.\" He said, \"O nephew, I made a marriage alliance with them, and the noble man rewards the noble man.\" Then she embraced Islam, and Islam separated her from Hubayrah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to her for herself, and she said, \"By Allah, I used to love you in the pre-Islamic era, so how much more in Islam? However, I am a woman with young children, and I dislike that they should annoy you.\" Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the Talkhis."],[6870,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed to me, and I excused myself to him, and he accepted my excuse.\" Then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: \"O Prophet, indeed We have made lawful to you your wives to whom you have given their due compensation\" (Al-Ahzab 50) up to His saying, \"those who emigrated with you\" (Al-Ahzab 50). She said, \"I was not made lawful for him, because I did not emigrate with him; I was among the Tulaqa' (those freed on the day of the conquest).\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6871,"Umm Hani': \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered my house and prayed the Duha prayer, eight rak'ahs.\" Ibn Abbas went out saying, \"I have read what is between the two boards, but I did not know the Ishraq prayer until this moment: 'They glorify in the evening and the Ishraq' (Sad 18).\" Then Ibn Abbas said, \"This is the Ishraq prayer.\" Abdullah b. Abbas also narrated another hadith from Umm Hani'. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6872,"She said, \"O Messenger of Allah, my maternal cousin Ali claims that he will kill someone I have granted protection to.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"We have granted protection to whomever you have granted protection.\""],[6873,"From Umm Hani."],[6874,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon Umm Hani while a waterskin was hanging, so he drank while standing.\" And a hadith has been narrated by the children of Umm Hani from their forefathers from her."],[6875,"Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, favored the Quraysh with seven qualities that He had not given to anyone before them, nor will He give to anyone after them: among them is prophethood, among them is the guardianship of the Kaaba, among them is the provision of water to the pilgrims, and He granted them victory over the elephant while they worshipped none but Allah, and they worshipped Allah for ten years during which no one other than them worshipped Him, and a surah was revealed concerning them in which no one else was associated, 'For the familiarity of the Quraysh' (Surah Quraysh)."],[6876,"I would surely hear the recitation of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at night while I was on the roof of my family's house.\""],[6877,"The Quraysh did not disapprove of praying the Duha prayer; they only disapproved of the time."],[6878,"Mus'ab b. Abdullah al-Zubayri narrated to us.\""],[6879,"I entered upon Marwan b. al-Hakam and said to him, 'A woman from your family was divorced, and I passed by her while she was moving, so I found fault with her for that.' They said, 'Fatimah bt. Qays ordered us, and she informed us that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her to move, when her husband divorced her, to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum.' Marwan said, 'Yes, she ordered them to do that.' Urwah said, 'I said, By Allah, Aisha found fault with that most severely, and she said, Fatimah was with her husband in a desolate place, so there was fear for her safety, and for that reason the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a dispensation.'"],[6880,"That Fatimah bt. Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak b. Qays, informed him, and she had been married to a man from Banu Makhzum, and he mentioned the hadith in full, and said at the end of it: When her waiting period ended, Abu Jahm and Muawiyah b. Abi Sufyan proposed to her, so she consulted the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, 'As for Muawiyah, he is a poor man with no wealth, and as for Abu Jahm, I fear for you his beating of women.' So he ordered me to marry Usamah b. Zayd, and I married Usamah b. Zayd."],[6881,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the woman with istihadah, and he said, 'She should refrain from prayer for the days of her regular periods, then perform ghusl and pray when she is pure.'\" And Aisha and Umm Salamah narrated from Fatimah bt. Qays. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6882,"Fatimah bt. Qays came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'I have istihadah.' He said, 'That is not menstruation; it is only a vein. Let her refrain from prayer for the days of her regular periods, then perform ghusl, then fasten a cloth and pray.'"],[6883,"That Fatimah bt. Qays consulted the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I have istihadah and do not become pure; should I abandon prayer?' He said, 'That is only a vein, not menstruation, and a single ghusl is more complete than wudu.'"],[6884,"Among the women of Quraysh who accompanied the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is al-Shifa' bt. Abdullah, who is the mother of Sulayman b. Abi Hathmah al-Qurashi and the grandmother of Abu Bakr b. Sulayman b. Abi Hathmah.\""],[6885,"And al-Shifa' bt. Abdullah embraced Islam before the conquest and pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6886,"A man from the Ansar developed a namla (a type of sore), and he was told that al-Shifa' bt. Abdullah performs ruqya for namla. He came to her and asked her to perform ruqya for him. She said: By Allah, I have not performed ruqya since I embraced Islam. The Ansari went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what al-Shifa' had said. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ summoned al-Shifa' and said: Show me (your ruqya). She presented it to him, and he said: Perform ruqya for him and teach it to Hafsa as you taught her writing."],[6887,"She used to perform ruqya with an incantation in the pre-Islamic era. When Islam came, she said: I will not perform ruqya until I seek the permission of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said to her: Perform ruqya as long as it does not involve associating partners with Allah ﷻ."],[6888,"When she migrated to the Prophet ﷺ, she came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, I used to perform ruqya with incantations in the pre-Islamic era, and I thought I should present them to you. He said: Present them. She presented them to him, and among them was the ruqya for namla. He said: Perform ruqya with it and teach it to Hafsa: In the name of Allah, a hard object when it returns from its mouths, and it does not harm anyone. O Allah, remove the affliction, Lord of the people. He said: Perform ruqya with it on a vine branch seven times, place it in a clean spot, then rub it on a stone and apply it to the quicklime. Ibn Ma'in was asked about Uthman and did not recognize him."],[6889,"Namla is sores that appear on the side and elsewhere."],[6890,"I came one day and entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, and I asked him and complained to him. He began to apologize to me, and I began to blame him. She said: Then the first prayer time came, and I entered the house of my daughter, who was married to Shurahbil b. Hasana. I found her husband in the house, and I began to blame him, saying: The prayer time has come and you are here? He said: O aunt, do not blame me. I had two garments, one of which the Prophet ﷺ borrowed. I said: May my father and mother be ransomed for him! I blame him while this is his situation? Shurahbil said: One of them was actually a coat of mail that we patched. Al-Dhahabi omitted this from the Talkhis."],[6891,"Among those who migrated to Abyssinia was Amir b. Rabi'a, and with him was his wife Layla bt. Abi Hathma b. Ghanim b. Awf b. Ubayd b. Uwayj b. Adi b. Ka'b."],[6892,"No woman among the female emigrants arrived in Madinah before Layla bt. Abi Hathma, who came with my father, her husband Amir b. Rabi'a."],[6893,"By Allah, we were about to depart for the land of Abyssinia. Amir had gone for some of our needs when Umar b. al-Khattab approached and stood over me while he was still upon his polytheism. We used to suffer hardship and severity from him. He said: Is it departure, O Umm Abdullah? I said: Yes, by Allah, we will surely go forth in Allah's land. You have harmed us and oppressed us until Allah grants us a way out. He said: May Allah accompany you. I saw in him a tenderness I had never seen before. Then he left, and I could see that our departure had saddened him. Then Amir b. Rabi'a came back from that errand, and I said: O Abu Abdullah, if only you had seen Umar just now, his tenderness and his sadness for us. He said: Do you hope for his Islam? I said: Yes. He said: The one you saw will not embrace Islam until the camel of al-Khattab embraces Islam. He said this out of despair for him, because of the harshness and severity he used to see from him toward Islam."],[6894,"Among them was Fatimah bt. al-Khattab b. Nufayl, the wife of Sa'id b. Zayd b. Amr b. Nufayl. She had embraced Islam before Umar and was among the first women to pledge allegiance in Makkah."],[6895,"A man from Banu Zuhra met Umar before he embraced Islam, while Umar was girded with a sword. He said: Where are you heading? Umar said: I want to kill Muhammad. He said: Shall I not point you to something astonishing, O Umar? Your brother-in-law Sa'id and your sister have apostatized and left the religion they were upon. Umar walked to them in anger, and when he approached the door, there was a man with them called Khabbab who was teaching them Surah Ta-Ha. When Khabbab heard Umar's footsteps, he hid under a bed of theirs. Umar entered and said: What is this murmuring I heard from you two? They said: Nothing but a conversation we had between ourselves. He said: Perhaps you two have apostatized and left the religion you were upon. His brother-in-law Sa'id b. Zayd said to him: O Umar, tell me, if the truth were in other than your religion? Umar turned to his brother-in-law and trampled him severely. His sister pushed him away from her husband, and he struck her face, making it bleed. She said, while angry: O Umar, tell me, if the truth were in other than your religion? I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. When Umar despaired, he said: Give me this book that you have so I may read it. His sister said: You are impure, and none but the purified may touch it. Get up and perform ghusl or wudu."],[6896,"When my sister opened the door for me, I said: O enemy of herself, have you apostatized? She said, and he raised something, then she said: O son of al-Khattab, whatever you intended to do, do it, for I have embraced Islam. He said: I entered and sat on the bed, and there was a sheet in the middle of the house. I said: What is this sheet here? She said: Leave it, O son of al-Khattab. You do not perform ghusl from janaba and do not purify yourself, and this is not touched except by the purified."],[6897,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"There is no prayer for one who does not have ablution, and there is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah the Almighty upon it, and he does not believe in Allah who does not believe in me, and he does not love the Ansar.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the summary in this context."],[6898,"Umm Nubayh bint al-Hajjaj, the mother of Abdullah b. Amr, was a woman who used to send gifts to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and show him kindness. One day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to her as a visitor and said, \"How are you, O Umm Abdullah?\" She said, \"Well, may my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"And how is Abdullah?\" She said, \"Well, may my father and mother be your ransom. Abdullah is a man who has withdrawn from the world.\" He said, \"How so?\" She said, \"He has forbidden himself sleep, so he does not sleep, nor does he break his fast. He has forbidden himself meat, so he does not eat meat, and he does not fulfill the rights of his family.\" He said, \"Where is he?\" She said, \"He went out a short while ago; he is likely to return soon, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"When he comes to you, keep him for me.\" Abdullah did not delay in coming, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, \"Indeed, your soul has a right over you, and your family has a right over you.\""],[6899,"Among the women of Banu Amir b. Lu'ayy was Sahla bint Suhayl b. Amr b. Abd Shams b. Abd Wudd b. Nasr b. Malik b. Hisl. She was among those who emigrated with her husband Abu Hudhayfa to the land of Abyssinia, and she bore him in Abyssinia Muhammad b. Abi Hudhayfa."],[6900,"She mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfa, and his entering upon her. She claimed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded her to suckle him, so she suckled him while he was a grown man, after he had witnessed Badr. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6901,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded Sahla, the wife of Abu Hudhayfa, to suckle Salim, the freed slave of Abu Hudhayfa, so that Abu Hudhayfa's jealousy would go away. So she suckled him while he was a man.\" Rabi'a said: \"It was a concession for Salim.\" Sahih."],[6902,"\"Among the women of Quraysh was Umm Habiba, whose name was Hamna bint Jahsh, the sister of Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. She was from Asad b. Khuzayma, an ally of Banu Abd Shams.\""],[6903,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in the mosque a rope stretched between two pillars and said, \"What is this rope?\" It was said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Hamna bint Jahsh prays, and when she gets tired she holds on to the rope.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let her pray as long as she is able, and when she gets tired, let her sit.\" And Ali narrated to me, Isma'il narrated to us, Abu al-Nu'man narrated to us, Hammad b. Salama narrated to me from Humayd from Anas something similar. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6904,"\"May Allah have mercy on him. Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return.\" Then it was said to her, \"Your maternal uncle Hamza has been killed.\" She said, \"Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we return.\" Then it was said to her, \"Your husband has been killed.\" She said, \"Woe for my grief!\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, for the husband over the wife there is a branch that is not for anything else.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6905,"Umm Habiba bint Jahsh, who was the wife of Abd al-Rahman b. Awf and the sister of Zaynab bint Jahsh, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him that she had been suffering from prolonged vaginal bleeding (istihada) for seven years. She asked him for a religious ruling about that, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"This is not menstruation, but it is a vein, so wash yourself and pray.\" She used to wash in a large basin until the water was red with blood, then she would stand and pray."],[6906,"His maternal aunt, Fatima bint Abi Hubaysh, came to Aisha and said, \"I fear that I may be among the people of the Fire, for I have not prayed for about two years.\" She asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Let her leave prayer each month for the days of her menstrual periods, then perform ablution for each prayer, for it is only a vein.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6907,"I brought you until, when I was within a night or two of Madinah, I cooked for you a dish, and the firewood ran out. So I went out to look for firewood, and I took hold of the pot, and it overturned onto your forearm. Then I arrived in Madinah and brought you to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this is Muhammad b. Hatib, and he is the first to be named after you.\" He wiped your head, prayed for blessing, then spat into your mouth and began to spit on your hand, saying, \"Remove the affliction, O Lord of the people; cure, for You are the Healer. There is no cure but Your cure, a cure that leaves no sickness.\" She said: \"I did not get up with you from his presence until your hand was healed.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6908,"\"Among them was Umm Ayman, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his caretaker. Her name was Baraka. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ bequeathed her five camels and a flock of sheep. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed Umm Ayman when he married Khadija. She then married Ubayd b. Yazid from Banu al-Harith b. al-Khazraj, and she bore him Ayman, who was killed as a martyr on the day of Khaybar. Zayd b. Haritha belonged to Khadija, and she gave him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ freed him and married him to Umm Ayman after the prophethood, and she bore him Usama b. Zayd.\""],[6909,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ used to say to Umm Ayman, \"O my mother,\" and whenever he looked at her, he would say, \"This is the remaining member of my family.\""],[6910,"From Nubayh Al-Anazi, from Umm Ayman, she said: The Prophet ﷺ came to me in the night and saw a water container beside the house. He dipped his hand in it and splashed some water on his face. I also got up during the night while feeling thirsty, so I drank from the water container without realizing. When the morning came, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Umm Ayman, go and pour out what is in the water container.\" I said, \"By Allah, I have already drunk from it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled until his molars were visible and then said, \"Surely, your stomach will never feel discomfort because of it anymore.\" Adh-Dhahabi remained silent regarding summarizing it."],[6911,"\"Umm Ayman, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his caretaker, died in the beginning of the caliphate of Uthman b. Affan ؓ.\""],[6912,"Ibn Abi al-Furat, the mawla of Usama b. Zayd, disputed with al-Hasan b. Umayya and quarreled with him. Ibn Abi al-Furat said to him in the course of their exchange, \"O son of Baraka,\" meaning Umm Ayman. Al-Hasan said, \"Bear witness,\" and brought the matter before Abu Bakr b. Muhammad b. 'Amr b. Hazm, who was then the qadi of Madinah, and related the story to him. Abu Bakr said to Ibn Abi al-Furat, \"What did you intend by your saying to him, 'O son of Baraka'?\" He said, \"I called her by her name.\" Abu Bakr said, \"You only intended by this to belittle her, while her standing in Islam is what it is, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say to her, 'O my mother, O Umm Ayman, may Allah ﷻ never let me off if I let you off.'\" So he had him flogged with seventy lashes. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[6913,"Arwa, the daughter of Kariz bin Rabia bin Habib bin Abd Shams, embraced Islam and migrated to Al-Madinah. She passed away during the caliphate of Uthman."],[6914,"Asma' bt. Abi Bakr, her mother was Qutayla bt. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. As'ad b. Jabir b. Malik b. Hisl b. 'Amir b. Lu'ayy. She was the full sister of 'Abd Allah b. Abi Bakr. She embraced Islam early in Makkah and gave allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam married her, and she bore him 'Abd Allah, 'Urwa, 'Asim, al-Muhajir, Khadija al-Kubra, Umm al-Hasan, and 'A'isha bt. al-Zubayr, seven."],[6915,"She took a dagger during the time of Sa'id b. al-'As in the fitna and placed it under her pillow. She was asked, \"What are you doing with this?\" She said, \"If a thief enters upon me, I will rip open his belly.\" And she was blind. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[6916,"Asma' bt. Abi Bakr died a few nights after the killing of her son 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr. His killing was on Tuesday, when seventeen nights had passed of Jumada al-Ula in the year seventy-three."],[6917,"Duba'a bt. al-Zubayr b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married her to al-Miqdad b. 'Amr b. Tha'laba. She bore him 'Abd Allah and Karima. 'Abd Allah was killed on the Day of the Camel alongside 'A'isha, and 'Ali passed by him slain and said, \"What a bad nephew.\""],[6918,"She handed some meat to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he took a bite from it, then prayed without performing ablution. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6919,"Umm al-Hakam bt. al-Zubayr b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim. Rabi'a b. al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Muttalib married her, and she bore him Muhammad, 'Abbas, 'Abd Shams, 'Abd al-Muttalib, Umayya, and Arwa al-Kubra."],[6920,"She handed the Prophet ﷺ a shoulder of meat, and he ate from it, then prayed without performing ablution. Hammad b. Salama erred in this name and said Umm Hakim. Hammad b. Salama narrated from Qatada from Ishaq b. 'Abd Allah from her, and it is not sound."],[6921,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate a bone at my place, then Bilal came and called him to prayer, and he prayed without performing ablution. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[6922,"Umama bt. Hamza b. 'Abd al-Muttalib b. Hashim, and her mother was Salma bt. 'Umays b. Ma'd b. Taym, the sister of Asma' bt. 'Umays. She lived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and narrated from him."],[6923,"A mawla of hers died leaving only one daughter, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that his daughter should have half and the daughter of Hamza should have half."],[6924,"Umm Kulthum bt. 'Uqba b. Abi Mu'ayt, her mother was Arwa bt. Kurayz. Umm Kulthum embraced Islam and gave allegiance before the Hijra, and she was the first woman to emigrate after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6925,"No Qurayshi woman is known to have left her parents' house as a Muslim emigrant to Allah and His Messenger except Umm Kulthum bt. ʿUqbah. She left Makkah alone and accompanied a man from Khuzāʿah until she arrived in Madinah during the truce of al-Ḥudaybiyyah. Her two brothers, al-Walīd and ʿUmārah, went out in pursuit of her and arrived at the time of her arrival. They said, 'O Muḥammad, [fulfill] for us our condition and what you pledged to us.' Concerning her was revealed: {When believing women come to you as emigrants} [al-Mumtaḥanah 10] — the verse. She had no husband in Makkah. When she arrived in Madinah, Zayd b. Ḥārithah married her, and he was killed leaving her. Then al-Zubayr b. al-ʿAwwām married her, and she bore him Zaynab. Then he divorced her. Then ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. ʿAwf married her, and she bore him Ibrāhīm and Ḥumayd, and he died leaving her. Then ʿAmr b. al-ʿĀṣ married her, and she died leaving him."],[6926,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ."],[6927,"\"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seeking refuge from the punishment of the grave.\""],[6928,"Abū Ḥudhayfah took her and her sister Hind to pledge allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When he stipulated conditions upon them, Hind said, \"Do you know of any of these flaws and defects among the women of your people?\" Abū Ḥudhayfah said to her, \"Come on, pledge allegiance to him, for this is how he stipulates.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6929,"\"Ḥamnah bt. Jaḥsh was married to Muṣʿab b. ʿUmayr, and he was killed leaving her on the day of Uḥud. Then Ṭalḥah b. ʿUbayd Allāh married her, and she bore him Muḥammad b. al-Sajjād, by whom he was given his kunyah, and ʿAbd Allāh b. Ṭalḥah.\""],[6930,"\"Indeed, this world is sweet and green. How many a one who plunges into the world with the wealth of Allah and His Messenger will have nothing on the Day of Resurrection but the Fire.\""],[6931,"\"Umm Qays bt. Miḥṣan b. Khawwāt, sister of ʿUkkāshah b. Miḥṣan, accepted Islam early in Makkah and emigrated to Madinah with her family. She lived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and narrated from him.\""],[6932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left with her, taking her hand, in the path of Madinah until he reached Al-Baqi' Al-Gharqad. He said, \"O Umm Qays.\" I said, \"At your service and at your pleasure, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Do you see this graveyard?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Seventy thousand will emerge from it on the Day of Resurrection in the image of the moon on a full moon night, they will enter Paradise without being held accountable.\" Ukasha stood up and said, \"And me, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"And you.\" Another person stood up and said, \"And me?\" He said, \"Ukasha preceded you in it.\""],[6933,"\"Judhāmah bt. Jandal b. Wahb al-Asadiyyah accepted Islam early in Makkah, pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and emigrated to Madinah with her family.\""],[6934,"\"The Banū Ghānim b. Dūdān fully participated in the emigration, men and women, until they locked their doors. Among the women who went out in the emigration were Zaynab, Umm Ḥabībah, and Ḥamnah, daughters of Jaḥsh; Āminah bt. Ruqaysh; Umm Ḥabībah bt. Bunānah; and Judhāmah bt. Jandal. Judhāmah bt. Jandal was married to Unays b. Qatādah b. Rabīʿah of the Aws, who witnessed Badr and was martyred on the day of Uḥud. Judhāmah lived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and narrated from him, and ʿĀʾishah narrated from Judhāmah.\""],[6935,"From ʿĀʾishah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, from Judhāmah bt. Wahb al-Asadiyyah, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he intended to prohibit ghīlah (intercourse with a nursing mother). He said, \"Then I considered, and found that the Persians and the Byzantines practice ghīlah and it does not harm their children.\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about ʿazl (coitus interruptus), and he said, 'It is the hidden burial of daughters.'\" The two Shaykhs agreed on transmitting the ḥadīth of Mālik b. Anas from Abū al-Aswad without the addition, for it belongs to Yaḥyā b. Ayyūb. They transmitted its beginning."],[6936,"\"By Allah, it is as if I am looking at the Prophet of Allah ﷺ that morning when he entered the Kaʿbah, then came out of it and stood at its door, and in his hand was a wooden dove that was in the Kaʿbah. He broke it and came out with it, and when he was at the door of the Kaʿbah, he threw it away.\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[6937,"\"Fāṭimah bt. Abī Ḥubaysh b. al-Muṭṭalib b. Asad b. ʿAbd al-ʿUzzā. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaḥsh b. Riʾāb married her, and she bore him Muḥammad b. ʿAbd Allāh b. Jaḥsh. Fāṭimah bt. Abī Ḥubaysh lived, saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and narrated from him.\""],[6938,"And Busrah bt. Safwan b. Nawfal b. Asad b. 'Abd al-'Uzza b. Qusayy, who was the sister of 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt through his mother, and he is the grandfather of 'Abd al-Malik b. Marwan; and the mother of 'Abd al-Malik was 'A'ishah bt. Mu'awiyah b. al-Mughirah b. Abi al-'As b. Umayyah. Busrah lived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and narrated from him the well-known report concerning ablution for one who touches the penis."],[6939,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[6940,"When Allah willed to honor the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and initiate him into prophethood, whenever he went out to relieve himself he would go far away until he could not see any house, and he would go to mountain passes and the bottoms of valleys. He would not pass by any stone or tree but that it said, 'Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah.' He would turn to his right, his left, and behind him, but he would not see anyone. This hadith is not authentic."],[6941,"I heard Ibn Abi Nubayh narrate from his grandmother Safiyyah bt. Shaybah, from Habibah bt. Abi Tijarah, who said: We had a bench in the pre-Islamic era. She said: I looked out from an opening between al-Safa and al-Marwah, and I looked down upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was hastening, saying to his companions: 'Hasten, for Allah Almighty has prescribed for you the hastening.' She said: I saw him in the intensity of his hastening, wrapping his lower garment around his stomach, until I saw the whiteness of his armpits and his thighs. This is not authentic."],[6942,"I entered the house of Abu Husayn with a group of women from Quraysh while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was circumambulating between al-Safa and al-Marwah, hastening, his lower garment twisting around him from the intensity of his hastening, and he was saying to his companions: 'Hasten, for Allah ﷻ has prescribed for you the hastening.'"],[6943,"And Umm Farwah bt. Abi Quhafah, the sister of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the paternal aunt of 'A'ishah; her mother was Hind bt. Nufayl b. Bujayr b. 'Ubayd b. Qusayy. Abu Bakr married her to al-Ash'ath b. Qays, and she bore him Muhammad, Ishaq, Hubabah, and Quraybah."],[6944,"I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among the women of the Muslims, and we said to him: 'We have come to you, O Messenger of Allah, to pledge allegiance to you that we will not associate anything with Allah, will not steal, will not commit adultery, will not kill our children, will not bring slander that we fabricate between our hands and feet, and will not disobey you in what is right.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'In what you are able to do.' We said: 'Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than ourselves.' We said: 'Accept our pledge, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Go, for I have accepted your pledge. My word to one woman is like my word to a hundred women.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not shake hands with any of us."],[6945,"Umaymah is the daughter of Ruqayqah and Ruqayqah is her mother. Her father is ʿAbdullāh b. Bijād b. ʿUmayr b. al-Ḥārith ibn Ḥarithah b. Saʿd b. Taym b. Murrah. Her mother is Ruqayqa b. Khuwaylid b. Asad b. ʿAbdalʿuzzá, the sister of Khadījah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ.Umaymah remained single and then Ḥabīb b. Kaʿb b. ʿUtayr al-Thaqafī married her. She gave birth to al-Nahdiyyah. Umaymah b. Ruqayqah lived after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and narrated from him.[1]"],[6946,"From Umaymah, the maternal aunt of Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: I heard her say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted our pledge and took from us that we would not associate anything with Allah.' He said: 'Then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Ibn Ishaq from Ibn al-Munkadir.'"],[6947,"From Barirah, ؓ ."],[6948,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered to relieve himself, so I entered and did not see anything, and I found the scent of musk. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I did not see anything.' He said: 'The earth has been commanded to consume it from us, the company of prophets.'"],[6949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A man from Quraysh has the strength of two men from Quraysh.' Al-Zuhri said: 'Meaning attainment of sound judgment.'"],[6950,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to 'Umar b. al-Khattab: 'O 'Umar, gather your people for me.' So he gathered them, then entered upon him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have gathered them. Should they enter upon you or should you go out to them?' He said: 'Rather, I will go out to them.' The Muhajirun and the Ansar heard of that and said: 'Revelation has come regarding Quraysh.' The observer and the listener attended to hear what would be said to them. He stood among them and said: 'Is there anyone among you other than you?' They said: 'Yes, among us are our allies, the sons of our brothers, and our freedmen.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Our allies are of us, and our freedmen are of us.' Then he said: 'Do you not hear? My allies among you are the God-fearing. If you are those, then that is so; otherwise, look, then look. Let not people come with deeds while you come with burdens, and He turns away from you.' Then he called out, raising his voice: 'Indeed Quraysh are people of trustworthiness; whoever seeks to cause them calamities, Allah will cast him down upon his nostrils.' He said it three times."],[6951,"While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a woman passed by. A man from the group said, 'This is the daughter of Muhammad.' Abu Sufyan said, 'The likeness of Muhammad among the Banu Hashim is that of sweet basil in the midst of figs.' The woman went and informed the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ came out with anger recognizable on his face and said: 'What is the matter with statements that reach me from certain people? Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created the heavens and chose the highest, and He settled therein whom He willed of His creation. Then He created the creation and chose from the creation the children of Adam, and He chose from the children of Adam the Arabs, and He chose from the Arabs Mudar, and He chose from Mudar Quraysh, and He chose from Quraysh the Banu Hashim, and He chose me from the Banu Hashim. Thus I am from the Banu Hashim, from the best to the best. Whoever loves the Arabs, it is out of love for me that he loves them; and whoever hates the Arabs, it is out of hatred for me that he hates them.' It has been said regarding this chain of narration, on the authority of Muhammad b. Dhakwan, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar."],[6952,"While we were sitting in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ... and he mentioned the hadith in its entirety, similar to it."],[6953,"My father said to me: 'O my son, if you are given authority over any of the people's affairs, honor Quraysh, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever humiliates Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him ﷻ.\"' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6954,"\"Whoever seeks humiliation for Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him.\""],[6955,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever seeks humiliation for Quraysh, Allah will humiliate him ﷻ.\" Yusuf b. Abi 'Aqil is Ibn al-Hakam without doubt, and the narration from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been authenticated that a child is not punished for the crime of his father."],[6956,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say on the pulpit: \"What is the matter with people who say that my kinship will not benefit? Nay, by Allah, my kinship is connected in this world and the Hereafter. O people, I am your predecessor at the Pond. When I come, men will stand up and say: 'This one, O Messenger of Allah, is so-and-so,' and another will say: 'This one, O Messenger of Allah, is so-and-so,' and another will say: 'This one, O Messenger of Allah, is so-and-so.' I will say: 'I knew you, but you introduced innovations after me and turned back on your heels.'\""],[6957,"\"The security of the people of the earth from dissension lies in loyalty to Quraysh. Quraysh are the people of Allah. If a tribe of the Arabs opposes them, they become a party of Iblis.\""],[6958,"We would meet a group of Quraysh while they were conversing, and they would stop their conversation. We mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"What is the matter with people who converse, but when they see a man from my family, they stop their conversation? By Allah, faith will not enter the heart of a man until he loves them for the sake of Allah Almighty and for my kinship.\""],[6959,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, when Quraysh meet each other, they greet one another with smiles. But when they meet us, they meet us with unknown faces.\" He became extremely angry and then said, \"By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, faith does not enter the heart of a man until he loves you for the sake of Allah and His Messenger.\" Al-Dhahabi remained quiet on this matter in summary."],[6960,"\"The leaders are from Quraysh. Its righteous are leaders over its righteous, and its wicked are leaders over its wicked. Each has a right, so give every rightful person his due. Even if I appoint over you an Ethiopian slave with mutilated nose and ears, listen to him and obey, as long as one of you is not given a choice between his Islam and the striking of his neck. If he is given a choice between his Islam and the striking of his neck, let him offer his neck, for there is no worldly life or Hereafter for him after his Islam.\""],[6961,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: 'Would you like a fortress and the protection of the fortress of Daws?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to a storehouse of the Ansar. Tufayl migrated, and a man from his people migrated with him. The man fell ill and became distressed—or a word similar to that. He went to a horn, took a broad-bladed arrowhead, and cut his finger joints, then died. Tufayl saw him in a dream and asked, 'What did Allah do with you?' He said, 'He forgave me because of my migration to the Prophet ﷺ.' Tufayl asked, 'What is the matter with your hands?' He said, 'It was said to me: We will not set right what you corrupted of yourself.' Tufayl related this to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet said: 'O Allah, and for his hands, forgive,' and he raised his hands."],[6962,"\"They are the ones who migrated with the Prophet ﷺ to Medina.\""],[6963,"\"The emigrants will have pulpits of gold upon which they will sit on the Day of Resurrection, safe from the terror.\""],[6964,"'Umar b. al-Khattab said: Hatib b. Abi Balta'ah wrote to the people of Makkah, and Allah Almighty informed His Prophet ﷺ of it. He sent 'Ali and al-Zubayr in pursuit of the letter. They caught up with a woman on a camel and extracted the letter from a lock of her hair. They brought it to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, and it was read to him. He sent for Hatib and said: 'O Hatib, did you write this letter?' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of Allah.' He asked: 'What prompted you to do that?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I am sincere to Allah and His Messenger ﷺ, but I was a stranger among the people of Makkah, and my family was in their midst. I feared for them, so I wrote a letter that does not harm Allah and His Messenger in any way, and perhaps there is some benefit in it for my family.' 'Umar said: I drew my sword and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, let me deal with him, for he has disbelieved, and I will strike his neck.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Ibn al-Khattab, what do you know? Perhaps Allah has looked upon the people of this band—the people of Badr—and said: Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.'"],[6965,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Gently, O Talhah, for he witnessed Badr as you did. The best of you is the best to his clients.”"],[6966,"Indeed, Allah, exalted is He, looked upon the people of Badr and said: 'Do what you will, for I have forgiven you.'"],[6967,"“When the Day of Resurrection comes, I will be the leader of the prophets, their spokesman, and the possessor of their intercession, without boasting.” Sahih"],[6968,"That he said: The last sermon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivered to us, he said: “O assembly of Muhajirun, you have begun to increase, while the Ansar have ceased to grow. They are my inner garment to which I retreat, so honor their doers of good and overlook their wrongdoers.”"],[6969,"The Prophet ﷺ came out during his illness with his head wrapped in a cloth and said: “People will increase while the Ansar decrease, until they become among people like salt in food. Whoever of you is given authority, let him accept from their doers of good and overlook their wrongdoers.”"],[6970,"He said from the pulpit to the Ansar: “Indeed, the people are my outer garment and the Ansar are my inner garment. If the people were to take a valley and the Ansar a mountain pass, I would follow the mountain pass of the Ansar. Whoever is given authority over the Ansar, let him do good to their doers of good and overlook their wrongdoers. Whoever frightens them has frightened what is between these two,” and he pointed to himself. “Were it not for the emigration, I would have been a man of the Ansar.”"],[6971,"He entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, while he was in the pain in which he died, and he said, \"Say salaam to your people, for indeed they do not know hardship and patience.\" Authenticated by the chain of narration, but it was not included in Sahih collections."],[6972,"Usayd b. Hudayr al-Ashhalī came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after he had distributed some food, and mentioned to him a household of the Ansar from Banū Zafar who were in need. He said: The majority of that household were women. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “You left us, O Usayd, until what was in our hands was gone. When you hear of something that has come to us, remind me of that household.” Later, food came to him from Khaybar: barley and dates. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed it among the people, gave generously to the Ansar, and gave generously to that household. Usayd b. Hudayr said to him gratefully: “May Allah reward you, O Prophet of Allah, with the best reward for us,” or he said: “with good.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “And you, O assembly of Ansar, may Allah reward you with the finest reward,” and he said: “with good. For you, as I have known, are chaste and patient. You will see after me selfishness in authority and distribution, so be patient until you meet me at the Pond.”"],[6973,"The Ansar were afflicted by hard toil in watering, so they came to the Prophet ﷺ to ask him to pray for them or to dig a canal for them. When the Prophet ﷺ was informed, he said: “Do not ask me today for anything but that it will be granted to you.” When they heard what the Prophet ﷺ said, they said: “Pray to Allah for forgiveness for us.” He said: “O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar.”"],[6974,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met some young boys, slave women, and slaves of the Ansar and said: “By Allah, I love you.” This hadith is sahih according to Muslim's criterion, but they did not include it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[6975,"The two tribes of the Ansar, the Aws and the Khazraj, boasted to each other. The Aws said: “From us is the one for whose death the Throne of the Most Merciful shook: Sa'd b. Mu'adh. From us is the one whom the hornets protected: 'Asim b. Thabit b. al-Aflah. From us is the one whom the angels washed: Hanzalah b. al-Rahib. From us is the one whose testimony was accepted as equal to that of two men: Khuzaymah b. Thabit.” The Khazrajis said: “From us are four who collected the Qur'an; no others collected it: Ubayy b. Ka'b, Mu'adh b. Jabal, Zayd b. Thabit, and Abu Zayd.”"],[6976,"“The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter. The Tulaqa' of Quraysh and the 'Urafa' of Thaqif are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter.”"],[6977,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reviewing horses while 'Uyaynah b. Badr al-Fazari was with him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “I know more about horses than you.” 'Uyaynah said: “And I know more about men than you.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then who are the best men?” He said: “Men who carry their swords on their shoulders and their spears on the withers of their horses, from the men of Najd.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “You lie. Rather, the best men are the men of Yemen, and faith is Yemeni, extending to Lakhm, Judham, and the protected lands of Himyar. A morsel of Himyar is better than its eater, and Hadramawt is better than Banu al-Harith. By Allah, I would not care if the two Hariths perished altogether. May Allah curse the four kings: Jamd, Mikhwas, Abda'ah, and their sister al-'Amarradah.” Then he said: “My Lord commanded me to curse Quraysh twice, so I cursed them, and He commanded me to pray for them, so I prayed for them twice, twice.” Then he said: “May Allah curse Tamim b. Murrah five times, and Bakr b. Wa'il seven times. May Allah curse two tribes of Banu Tamim: Muqā'is and Mulādis.” Then he said: “'Usayyah disobeyed Allah and His Messenger; 'Abd Qays, Ja'dah, and 'Ismah.” Then he said: “Aslam, Ghifar, Muzaynah, and their allies from Juhaynah are better than Banu Asad, Tamim, Ghatafan, and Hawazin in the sight of Allah on the Day of Resurrection.” Then he said: “The worst two tribes among the Arabs are Najran and Banu Taghlib, and the most numerous tribe in Paradise is Madhhij.”"],[6978,"\"Aslam, Ghifār, Ashjaʿ, Muzaynah, Juhaynah, and whoever was from Banū Kaʿb are allies, apart from the people. Allah and His Messenger are their allies.\""],[6979,"\"Ghifār—may Allah forgive her—and Aslam—may Allah keep her safe. Indeed, I did not say it, but Allah said it.\""],[6980,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to stand in prayer and supplicate against some tribes of the Arabs, saying, 'May Allah curse Ri'lān and Dhakwān and the 'Usayyah tribe who disobeyed Allah and His Messenger, and Beni Lahyan.' And he would say, 'Ghifār was forgiven by Allah and He granted Sa'lamah safety. I did not say this, but rather Allah Almighty said it.' Then he would say the takbīr after supplicating against those whom he cursed.\" (Note: This translation might not be precise as the original text is not clear and there is a reference to a missing portion from Al-Dhahabi's work)."],[6981,"ʿĀmir b. al-Ṭufayl never entered Madinah except with a guarantee of protection from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Prophet ﷺ came, the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"O ʿĀmir, submit and you will be safe.\" He said, \"Yes, on condition that I have the settled land and you have the open land.\" He said, \"This will not be. Submit and you will be safe.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O ʿĀmir, go until we consider your matter tomorrow.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to the Anṣār and said, \"What do you think? I have called this man, but he refuses to submit unless he has the settled land and I have the open land.\" They said, \"Whatever Allah wills, then whatever you will, O Messenger of Allah. They have not taken from us even a rope for hobbling a camel except that we have taken from them two ropes. But Allah and His Messenger know best.\" Then ʿĀmir returned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to him, \"Submit and you will be safe, O ʿĀmir.\" He said, \"Nothing except that.\" And he refused unless he had the settled land and the Prophet ﷺ had the open land. The Prophet ﷺ refused. Then ʿĀmir said, \"By Allah, I will fill it against you with horses and men.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Allah will prevent that from you, and the sons of the tribe of Aws and Khazraj.\" Then ʿĀmir turned away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Allah, suffice me against him.\" So Allah struck him with a glandular swelling in the throat before he reached his family. When the swelling seized him, ʿĀmir said, \"O family of ʿĀmir, this is a gland like the gland of a young camel. So he perished at the moment it seized him, before reaching his family.\""],[6982,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever ascends the mountain pass of al-Mirār, it will be forgiven for him what was forgiven for the Children of Israel.\" The first to ascend it were the horses of Banū al-Khazraj. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"All of you are forgiven except the owner of the red camel.\" He said, \"And behold, it was a Bedouin searching for his lost camel. We said to him, 'Come, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will ask forgiveness for you.' He said, 'To find my lost camel is dearer to me than for your companion to ask forgiveness for me.'\""],[6983,"\"No harm has come to a woman who has settled between two neighbors from the Anṣār, or who has settled between her parents.\""],[6984,"Three things I heard for Banū Tamīm from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; after them I will never hate Tamīm at all. ʿĀʾishah had a vow to free a slave from the descendants of Ismāʿīl. Some captives from Banū al-ʿAnbar were taken, and he said to ʿĀʾishah, \"If it pleases you to fulfill your vow, then free one of these.\" So he made them from the descendants of Ismāʿīl. And some camels from the zakāh livestock of Banū Saʿd were brought. When he saw them, it moved him, and he said, \"These are the camels of my people.\" So he made them his people. And he said, \"They are the strongest of people in fighting during the great battles.\""],[6985,"That he heard the Prophet ﷺ, regarding the saying of Allah, exalted is He, {You are the best nation produced for mankind} [Āl ʿImrān: 110], say: \"You complete seventy nations; you are the best of them and the most noble of them in the sight of Allah, exalted is He.\""],[6986,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You fulfill seventy nations; you are the most noble of them in the sight of Allah, exalted is He, and the most excellent of them.\""],[6987,"From Abū Hurayrah, regarding the saying of Allah, exalted is He, {You are the best nation produced for mankind} [Āl ʿImrān: 110]: \"You drag them with chains and bring them into Islam.\""],[6988,"The Anṣār said, \"O Messenger of Allah, every Prophet has followers, and we have followed you, so pray to Allah to make our followers from among us.\" So he prayed for them that He make their followers from among them. He said, \"Then I conveyed that to ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Laylā, and he said, 'Zayd b. Arqam claimed that.'\""],[6989,"\"Indeed, some people of my nation will come after me; one of them would wish to purchase seeing me with his family and his wealth.\""],[6990,"We had lunch with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with us was Abū ʿUbaydah b. al-Jarrāḥ. We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is there anyone better than us? We embraced Islam with you and fought with you.\" He said, \"Yes, a people who will come after you, who believe in me though they have not seen me.\""],[6991,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you know which of the people of faith are most excellent in faith?\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, the angels?\" He said, \"They are so, and that is rightfully theirs—and what would prevent them, since Allah has placed them in the station He has placed them in? Rather, it is others.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, then the prophets whom Allah, Exalted is He, honored with prophethood and messengership?\" He said, \"They are so, and that is rightfully theirs—and what would prevent them, since Allah has placed them in the station He has placed them in? Rather, it is others.\" He said, so we said, \"Then who are they, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Peoples who will come after me in the loins of men, who will believe in me without having seen me and will find the suspended pages and act according to what is in them. These are the most excellent of the people of faith in faith.\""],[6992,"\"Glad tidings to the one who saw me, and glad tidings to the one who saw the one who saw me, and to the one who saw the one who saw the one who saw me, and believed in me.\""],[6993,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"O Salman, do not hate me, lest you depart from your religion.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, how could I hate you when through you Allah ﷻ guided me?\" He said, \"If you hate the Arabs, then you hate me.\""],[6994,"\"When Allah created the creation, He chose the Arabs; then He chose from the Arabs Quraysh; then He chose from Quraysh the Banu Hashim; then He chose me from the Banu Hashim. So I am the choicest of the choicest.\""],[6995,"Abu al-'Abbas Muhammad b. Ya'qub narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ishaq al-Saghani narrated to us: 'Abd Allah b. Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us: Yazid b. 'Awana narrated to us, from Muhammad b. Dhakwan, the maternal uncle of the children of Hammad b. Zayd, from 'Amr b. Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar. \"The narration from 'Amr b. Dinar has been authenticated. If it is from Salim, then it is unusual but sound; and if it is from Ibn 'Umar, then 'Amr b. Dinar did hear from Ibn 'Umar.\""],[6996,"\"Love of the Arabs is faith, and hatred of them is hypocrisy.\""],[6997,"Love the Arabs for three reasons: because I am an Arab, the Qur'an is Arabic, and the speech of the people of Paradise is Arabic."],[6998,"\"Preserve me in the Arabs for three qualities: because I am an Arab, the Qur'an is Arabic, and the tongue of the people of Paradise is Arabic.\""],[6999,"\"Whoever among you is able to speak Arabic, let him not speak Persian, for it bequeaths hypocrisy.\""],[7000,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever speaks in Persian, his wickedness increases and his integrity decreases.\" This narration is not authentic and its chain of transmission is weak."],[7001,"The Prophet ﷺ sent 'Ali to Yemen and said, \"Teach them the sacred laws and judge between them.\" He said, \"I have no knowledge of judging.\" So he struck his chest and said, \"O Allah, guide him for judging.\""],[7002,"Two men brought a dispute to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said to 'Amr, \"Judge between them.\" He said, \"Shall I judge between them while you are present, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Yes. If you judge correctly, you will have ten rewards; and if you exercise judgment and err, you will have one reward.\""],[7003,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ say in his sermon: \"The people of Paradise are three: a ruler who is truthful, just, and divinely guided; a man who is merciful and tender-hearted toward every relative; and a poor man who is chaste.\""],[7004,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, those who are just in this world will be upon pulpits of pearl on the Day of Resurrection, before the Most Merciful ﷻ, because of their justice in this world.\""],[7005,"\"The people of oppression and their helpers are in the Fire.\""],[7006,"\"O people, Allah does not accept the prayer of an imam who rules by other than what Allah has revealed.\""],[7007,"\"There is no one who is put in charge of ten or more and does not act justly among them, except that he will come on the Day of Resurrection in shackles and chains.\""],[7008,"Some people asked Usama b. Zayd to speak to this man—meaning Uthman b. Affan—for us. He said: \"We have spoken to him, short of opening a door, lest he be the first to open it. I do not say your rulers are your best after something I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: The governor who was obeyed in disobedience to Allah ﷻ will be brought and ordered to the Fire, and he will be cast into it, and his intestines will spill out, and he will go round in it as a donkey goes round a mill. Then the people who obeyed him will come to him and say: 'O so-and-so, where is what you used to command us?' He will say: 'I used to command you to one thing and contradict you to another.'\""],[7009,"Six whom I have cursed, and Allah has cursed them, and every prophet whose supplication is answered: the one who denies the decree of Allah, the one who adds to the Book of Allah, the one who dominates by tyranny to humiliate whom Allah has honored and honor whom Allah has humiliated, the one who makes lawful what Allah has forbidden, the one who makes lawful from my offspring what Allah has forbidden, and the one who abandons my Sunnah."],[7010,"Judges are of three types: two judges are in the Fire and one judge is in Paradise. A judge who knew the truth and ruled by it is in Paradise. A judge who knew the truth but ruled unjustly deliberately is in the Fire. And a judge who ruled without knowledge is in the Fire."],[7011,"\"Two judges are in the Fire and one judge is in Paradise: a judge who ruled with the truth is in Paradise, a judge who ruled with injustice is in the Fire, and a judge who ruled out of ignorance is in the Fire.\" They said: \"What is the sin of this one who is ignorant?\" He said: \"His sin is that he should not be a judge until he knows.\""],[7012,"\"There is no one who is in charge of any of the affairs of this nation, whether small or great, and does not act justly among them, except that Allah will cast him into the Fire.\""],[7013,"Al-Dahhak b. Qays sent with him a garment to Marwan b. al-Hakam. Marwan said to the doorkeeper: \"See who is at the door?\" He said: \"Abu Hurayrah.\" So he gave him permission, and he said: \"O Abu Hurayrah...\""],[7014,"\"Woe to the rulers, woe to the chiefs, and woe to the trustees. On the Day of Resurrection, some people will wish that their forelocks were hung from the Pleiades, dangling between heaven and earth, and that they had never taken on any responsibility.\""],[7015,"\"O Abu Dharr, I see that you are weak, so do not be put in charge of even two people, and do not take charge of the property of an orphan.\""],[7016,"\"Whoever is appointed a judge, it is as if he has been slaughtered without a knife.\""],[7017,"He said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Appoint me as a commander.\" He said: \"You are weak, and it is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection it will be disgrace and regret.\""],[7018,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, appoint me as a commander.\" He said: \"Authority is a trust, and on the Day of Resurrection it will be disgrace and regret, except for one who commands with truth and fulfills the truth incumbent upon him therein.\""],[7019,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: \"Whoever seeks judgment and seeks help for it will be left to it, and whoever does not seek it and does not seek help for it, an angel will be assigned to him to guide him aright.\""],[7020,"\"The bonds of Islam will be undone one by one. Whenever a bond is undone, the people will cling to the one that follows it. The first of them to be undone is judgment, and the last is prayer.\""],[7021,"\"Whoever appoints a man from a group while there is in that group one more pleasing to Allah than him, he has betrayed Allah, betrayed His Messenger, and betrayed the believers.\""],[7022,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq said to me when he sent me to Syria: \"O Yazid, you have relatives; perhaps you will favor them with authority. That is what I fear most for you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever is given any authority over the affairs of the Muslims and appoints over them anyone as a favor, upon him is the curse of Allah. Allah will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory deed until He admits him into Hell.'\""],[7023,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen. I said: \"You are sending me to a people of mature age while I am young.\" He said: \"When the two litigants sit before you, do not judge for one of them until you hear from the other as you heard from the first.\" Ali said: \"I have continued to be a judge ever since.\""],[7024,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah is with the judge as long as he does not act unjustly. If he acts unjustly, Allah disavows him.\" Abu al-'Awwam is 'Imran b. Dawud al-Qattan, and the chain is authentic, though they did not include it. Sahih."],[7025,"From Abu Maryam, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever is given any authority over the affairs of the Muslims and then veils himself from their need, their want, their poverty, and their destitution, Allah will veil Himself from his need, his destitution, his want, and his poverty on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[7026,"\"Whoever shuts his door against the needy, the destitute, and the poor, Allah will shut the gate of heaven against his need, his want, his poverty, and his destitution.\""],[7027,"His father 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr had a dispute with his brother 'Amr b. al-Zubayr. 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr entered upon Sa'id b. al-'As while 'Amr b. al-Zubayr was with him on the couch. Sa'id said to 'Abd Allah: \"Here.\" He said: \"No. The judgment of the Messenger of Allah and the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is that the two litigants sit before the judge.\""],[7028,"Whoever is presented with a judicial matter should judge by what is in the Book of Allah. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah, then let him judge by what the Prophet ﷺ ruled. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah and His Prophet ﷺ did not rule on it, then let him judge by what the righteous have said. If a matter comes to him that is not in the Book of Allah, and His Prophet ﷺ did not rule on it, and the righteous did not rule on it, then let him exercise his own judgment; and if he is not able, let him acknowledge and not be ashamed."],[7029,"Two men brought a dispute over a camel or a riding animal to the Prophet ﷺ, and neither of them had any proof, so the Prophet ﷺ divided it between them."],[7030,"Two men claimed a camel, and each of them produced two witnesses, so the Prophet ﷺ divided it between them. This hadith is also authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but they did not include it on the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[7031,"Abu al-Muwajjih narrated to us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Usamah b. Zayd informed me from the client of Umm Salamah, from Umm Salamah, who said: Two men came to the Prophet ﷺ disputing over an inheritance between them, and neither of them had any proof. The Prophet ﷺ ordered them to divide it and to seek what is right, then to cast lots, and then each of them should absolve the other. The chain is authentic, but they did not include it. The client of Umm Salamah is Ubaydullah b. Abi Rafi', who is cited in the two Sahihs. Authentic."],[7032,"I heard Umm Salamah say: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when two men came to him disputing over an inheritance between them, and neither of them had any proof. Each of them said to the other, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is my right that I sought from so-and-so.' He said, 'No, but go and seek what is right, then cast lots, then divide it, then let each of you absolve the other.'"],[7033,"A man claimed a right against another man, and they brought their dispute to the Prophet ﷺ. He asked the claimant for proof, and he said, 'I have no proof.' He said to the other, 'Swear,' and he swore, saying, 'By Allah, he has nothing with me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Rather, it is with you. Give him his right.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him, 'Your testimony that there is no god but Allah is an expiation for your oath.'"],[7034,"If you see my community fearing the oppressor and not saying to the oppressor, 'O oppressor,' then they have been given leave."],[7035,"Ali was sent by the Prophet ﷺ to Yemen, and three men disputing over a child were brought to him, each claiming that he was his son. He said: He took two of them aside and said, 'Are you both willing to give him up to this remaining one?' They said, 'No.' He took two of them aside and said the same to them, and they said, 'No.' Then he said, 'I see you are quarrelsome partners, and I will cast lots among you.' So he cast lots among them and assigned the child to one of them and made him pay two-thirds of the blood money to the remaining two. He said: He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he laughed until his molars showed. The two Shaykhs turned away from al-Ajlah b. Abdullah al-Kindi, but his narrations are not rejected; what is criticized about him is his doctrine. Al-Ajlah is not rejected."],[7036,"There was a slave girl belonging to Zam'ah whom he used to have intercourse with, and she suspected another man of also having intercourse with her. Zam'ah died while she was pregnant, and she gave birth to a boy who resembled the man she had suspected. Sawdah mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'As for the inheritance, it belongs to him. As for you, veil yourself from him, for he is not a brother to you.'"],[7037,"While I was sitting with Abu Hurayrah, a Persian woman came to him with her son, and her husband had divorced her. She said, 'O Abu Hurayrah,' then she spoke in Persian, saying, 'My husband wants to take my son away.' Her husband then came and said, 'Who will dispute with me?' Abu Hurayrah said, 'I will not say anything about this except that I heard that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him, and she said, 'May my father and mother be your ransom, my husband wants to take my son away, and he has been giving me water from the well of Abu Utbah, and he has benefited me.' He said, 'Cast lots for him.' Her husband said, 'Who will dispute with me over my son, O Messenger of Allah?' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'O boy, this is your father and this is your mother, so take the hand of whichever of them you wish.' The boy took his mother's hand, and she went away with him."],[7038,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled regarding a single palm tree, two palm trees, and three, when they dispute over the rights of that: he ruled that for every palm tree, the extent of its fronds is a protected zone."],[7039,"The protected zone of an ancient well is fifty cubits, and the protected zone of a new well is twenty-five cubits."],[7040,"A false witness will not move his feet until Allah makes the Fire obligatory for them."],[7041,"Indeed, before the Hour there will be the greeting of the elite, the spread of trade until a woman helps her husband in trade, the severing of kinship ties, the appearance of false testimony, and the concealment of true testimony."],[7042,"Nothing was more hateful to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than lying, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never tested anyone, even a little, without bringing out from himself [a reaction] until he renewed repentance for him."],[7043,"A man was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who would give testimony, so he said to me: “O Ibn Abbas, do not testify except to what is as clear to you as the brightness of this sun,” and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointed with his hand to the sun."],[7044,"Leave what causes you doubt for what does not cause you doubt, for truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt."],[7045,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sin? He said: “When something disturbs your heart, leave it.”"],[7046,"The testimony of a Bedouin against a villager is not permissible."],[7047,"The testimony of one who is suspect or one who has enmity is not permissible."],[7048,"Allah ﷻ [says]: {from those whom you approve as witnesses} [al-Baqarah 282]. He said: “Children are not among those who are approved.”"],[7049,"The Messenger of Allah (pbuh) said, \"Whoever supports a dispute unjustly will remain in the displeasure of Allah until they desist.\""],[7050,"Whoever supports falsehood to refute truth by his falsehood, the protection of Allah and the protection of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ are disowned from him."],[7051,"The child of adultery bears nothing of the sin of his parents. {And no bearer of burdens will bear the burden of another}"],[7052,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the child of adultery. He said: “He is the worst of the three.” And as for the second chain..."],[7053,"The child of fornication is the worst of the three."],[7054,"The Aws and the Khazraj boasted to each other, and the Aws said, \"Among us is one whose testimony was deemed equivalent to the testimony of two men: Khuzaymah b. Thābit.\""],[7055,"The Prophet ﷺ returned the oath to the claimant of the right."],[7056,"Settlement is permissible among the Muslims."],[7057,"Settlement is permissible among the Muslims, except a settlement that makes unlawful something lawful or makes lawful something unlawful. And the Muslims are bound by their conditions, except a condition that makes unlawful something lawful."],[7058,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed a restriction on Muʿādh's property and sold it to pay off a debt he owed. Authentic."],[7059,"During the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a man used to buy (goods), and he was weak in his intellect. His people came to the Prophet of Allah ﷺ and said: Prophet of Allah, stop so-and-so (to make a bargain) for he buys (goods), but he is weak in his intellect. So the Prophet ﷺ called on him and forbade him to make a bargain. He said: Prophet of Allah, I cannot keep away myself from business transactions. Thereupon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: If you cannot give up making a bargain , then say: Take , and give, and there is no attempt to deceive. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3501)"],[7060,"He named me, and I would never give that up. I said, \"Why did he name you that?\" He said, \"A man from the desert came with two camels, and I bought them from him. Then I entered my house and went out from the back and sold them, and with their price I fulfilled my need. I stayed away until I thought the Iraqi had left, but the Iraqi was still there. He seized me and took me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the story. He said, 'What led you to do what you did?' I said, 'I satisfied my need with their price, O Messenger of Allah.' He said, 'Pay it.' I said, 'I do not have it.' He said, 'You are a thief. Go, O Iraqi, and sell him until you recover your right.'\" He said, \"People began to bargain with him for me, and he turned to them and said, 'What do you want?' They said, 'We want to ransom him from you.' He said, 'By Allah, I am more entitled to him than you and more in need of Allah, the Exalted. Go, for I have freed you.'\""],[7061,"The Prophet ﷺ detained a man on suspicion."],[7062,"The Prophet ﷺ detained a man on suspicion for a day and a night as a precaution and out of caution. Ibrāhīm b. Khaytham is abandoned."],[7063,"Delay in payment by a wealthy person makes his honor and punishment lawful."],[7064,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the briber and the bribed."],[7065,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the briber and the bribed in judgment. Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[7066,"May Allah curse the briber, the bribed, and the one who walks between them."],[7067,"Whoever is appointed over ten people and judges between them according to what they like or dislike, he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hands chained to his neck. If he judges by what Allah has revealed and does not take a bribe in his judgment and does not incline wrongly, Allah will release him on the Day of Resurrection—a day when there is no chain except his chain. But if he judges by other than what Allah, Exalted is He, has revealed and takes a bribe in his judgment and shows favoritism, his left hand will be bound to his right hand and he will be cast into Hell, and he will not reach its bottom for five hundred years."],[7068,"The people of al-Taff do not pay zakah. Bilal sent a man to ask about what they say, and the man found that he was being reviled in his lineage. He returned to Bilal and informed him, so Bilal said the takbir and said: My father narrated to me from Abu Musa who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever slanders people is of illegitimate birth, and there is something of that in him.\""],[7069,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever pleases a ruler by displeasing his Lord, Exalted is He, has departed from the religion of Allah, Blessed and Exalted is He.\" ʿAllaq b. Abi Muslim was alone in narrating it, and all the narrators up to him are trustworthy. End of the Book of Commandments. ʿAllaq was alone in narrating it, and the narrators up to him are trustworthy."],[7070,"I asked permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and entered upon him in an upper room. He was lying on a mat, and part of him was on the dust, and under his head was a pillow stuffed with palm fiber, and above his head was a tanned skin, and in a corner of the room was some acacia pods. I greeted him, then sat down and said: O Messenger of Allah, you are the Prophet of Allah, His chosen one, and His select from His creation, while Kisra and Caesar are on couches of gold and beds of silk and brocade. He said: \"O Umar, those people have had their good things hastened for them, and it is about to be cut off. But we are a people whose good things have been delayed for us in our Hereafter.\""],[7071,"Whoever eats what is lawful, acts according to the Sunnah, and people are safe from his harm will enter Paradise. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this is common in your community today. He said: \"And it will be so in generations after me.\""],[7072,"Aisha reported: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would enter upon one of his wives, and she had a small skin of honey, and he would lick some of it and sit with her. That bothered them, so Aisha said to Hafsa and to some of the Prophet's wives: We said to him, \"We only smell the odor of maghafir from you.\" He said: \"It is honey that I lick at so-and-so's, and I will not return to it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7073,"Umm Sulaym had a drinking bowl, and I did not leave any drink except that I gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to drink from it: honey, milk, nabidh, and water."],[7074,"My father said: \"We went on military expeditions with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we had no food except the two black things.\" He said: \"Do you know what the two black things are?\" He said: No. He said: \"Water and dates.\""],[7075,"A month or half a month would pass upon the family of Muhammad ﷺ, and no fire would be lit in their houses for a lamp or for anything else. I said to her: What kept you alive? She said: \"Dates and water.\""],[7076,"Muhammad ﷺ did not eat two meals in a day except that one of them was dates."],[7077,"O Ibn Shaqiq, do you see this stone? It is the stone of the Prophet ﷺ. We saw ourselves by it when no one had food to fill his belly, so that one of us would take a stone and tie it to the sole of his foot with a rope or with a cord from the cords. By the One in whose hand is my soul, I saw myself when the Prophet ﷺ divided dates among us, and each of us received seven dates. Among my seven was one dry, hard date, and no good date would please me more than it. I said: Why, O Abu Hurayrah? He said: \"Because it strengthened my chewing, so I kept chewing it.\""],[7078,"Forty nights would pass upon us and no lamp or anything else would be lit in the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: We said: O our mother, how did you live? She said: On the two black things: dates and water."],[7079,"The Prophet ﷺ used to call dates and milk the two best things."],[7080,"I read in the Torah: Ablution before food is the blessing of food. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: Ablution before food and after food is the blessing of food. Qays b. al-Rabi' is alone in narrating it from Abu Hashim, and his isolated narration, despite his high status, is more than can be omitted in this book."],[7081,"I entered upon Ali b. Abi Talib, I and two men, a man from us and a man from Banu Asad, I think. He sent them both in a direction and said: You two are foreigners, so exert yourselves on behalf of your religion. Then he entered the privy. Then he came out and took a handful of water and wiped himself with it. Then he came and recited the Quran. He saw that we found that objectionable, so Ali said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to go to the privy, relieve himself, then come out and eat with us bread and meat and recite the Quran, and nothing prevented him—or perhaps he said: and nothing held him back from reciting the Quran—except major ritual impurity, or except major ritual impurity."],[7082,"The Prophet ﷺ , Abu Bakr, and Umar came to the house of Abu Ayyub. When they ate and were full, the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Bread, meat, dates, ripe fruits, and fresh dates. If you have collected such things, you should strike them with your palms and say 'Bismillah' (in the name of Allah) and ask for the blessings of Allah.\""],[7083,"My father said to my mother: If you would prepare food for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. So she prepared a tharidah, reducing it. My father went and invited him. He placed his hand on it then said: Eat, in the name of Allah. They took from around it. When they had eaten, he supplicated for them, saying: O Allah, forgive them, have mercy on them, bless them, and provide for them."],[7084,"I prepared food and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ while he was sitting. I placed it before him. He said: What is this? I said: A gift. He placed his hand and said to his companions: Eat, in the name of Allah."],[7085,"When one of you eats food, let him say: In the name of Allah. If he forgets at the beginning, let him say: In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end."],[7086,"From the Prophet ﷺ that food was brought to him. A bedouin came as if he were being driven away, and he reached for it. The Prophet ﷺ took his hand. Then a slave girl came as if she were being driven away, and the Prophet ﷺ took her hand. Then he said: When you exhausted the devil, the bedouin and the slave girl came so that he might make the food permissible through them when the name of Allah had not been mentioned over it. In the name of Allah, eat."],[7087,"He used to mention the name of Allah at the beginning of his food and at its end. I asked him: I saw your saying at the last morsel: In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end. He said: I will tell you about that. My grandfather Umayyah b. Makhshi, who was one of the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, I heard him say: A man was eating while the Prophet ﷺ was looking. He did not mention the name of Allah until it was at the end of his food. Then he said: In the name of Allah at its beginning and its end. The Prophet ﷺ said: The devil kept eating with him until he mentioned the name, then nothing remained in his stomach except that he vomited it."],[7088,"A Jewish woman gifted a roasted sheep to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the people spread out their hands, the Prophet ﷺ said to them: Withhold your hands, for a limb of its limbs informs me that it is poisoned. He sent for its owner and said: Did you poison this food of yours? She said: Yes. I wanted, if you were a liar, to relieve the people of you, and if you were truthful, I knew that Allah would inform you of it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Mention the name of Allah and eat. So we ate and nothing harmed any of us."],[7089,"He used to use his right hand for his food, drink, and clothing, and he used his left hand for what was other than that."],[7090,"When we ate food with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we would not begin until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began."],[7091,"The Prophet ﷺ was among some of his companions when 'Uthman came leading a camel carrying two sacks, with his camel's hobble tied around his waist. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"What do you have with you?\" He said, \"Flour, ghee, and honey.\" He said, \"Make it kneel.\" So he made it kneel. The Prophet ﷺ called for a large cooking pot and put into it some of that flour, ghee, and honey. Then he cooked it until it was done. The Prophet ﷺ ate, and they ate. Then he said to them, \"Eat, for this resembles the khabis of the people of Persia.\""],[7092,"I was the delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We arrived at the Messenger of Allah ﷺ but did not find him in his house; we found 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers. She ordered a harīrah for us, so she made it for us, and we were brought a qinā'—and the qinā' is a large plate—containing dates. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and said, \"Have you had anything, or shall I order something for you?\" We said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, the shepherd brought his sheep up to the fold, and with him was a lamb that was leaping about. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What did she give birth to, O so-and-so?\" He said, \"A bahmah.\" He said, \"Then slaughter for us in its place a sheep.\" Then he turned to us and said, \"Do not think—and he did not say 'let it not be thought'—that we slaughtered it for your sake. We have a hundred sheep and do not want them to increase. When the shepherd's ewe gives birth to a bahmah, we slaughter in its place a sheep.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife,\" and he mentioned her long tongue and her vulgarity. He said, \"Divorce her.\" I said, \"I have a child from her.\" He said, \"Then instruct her—he said: admonish her—and if there is any good in her, she will do it. And do not strike your wife as you strike your slave girl.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about ablution.\" He said, \"Perform ablution thoroughly, pass your fingers between the fingers, and exaggerate in sniffing water into the nose unless you are fasting.\""],[7093,"\"We made for the Prophet ﷺ a pot made of clay, and I brought it to him. He looked inside it and said, 'I thought it was meat.'\""],[7094,"From Nu'bail Al-'Anazi, from Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: When my father was killed, he left behind a debt, so I mentioned it in detail. In it, I said to my wife, \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ will come to us today at noon, so do not harm the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or speak to him.\" So he entered and she spread out a bed and a pillow for him, and he laid his head down and slept. I said to my servant, \"Slaughter these sheep, as well as this fat calf, and pour out the contents before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wakes up, and I will be with you.\" So we did not finish slaughtering them until we were done, and he was still asleep. So I said to him, \"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he wakes up, he will call for ablution, and I fear that if he finishes, he will stand up without completing his ablution until we place the sheep before him.\" So when he got up, he said, \"O Jabir, bring me something to purify myself.\" He did not finish his purification until I placed the sheep before him. Then he looked at me and said, \"It seems that you prepared a kind of soup with the meat. Call Abu Bakr for me.\" Then he called his companions who were with him, and they entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck with his hand and said, \"In the name of Allah, eat.\" So they ate until they were full, and there was still a lot of meat left. And he mentioned the rest of the hadith."],[7095,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"The tastiest meat is the meat of the back.\" This was narrated by Raqabah ibn Masqalah from this narrator of understanding, but it is not attributed to being authentic."],[7096,"\"The best meat is the meat of the back.\""],[7097,"My father ordered me to make a harīrah, so I made it. Then he ordered me to carry it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I found him in his house, and he said, \"What is this, O Jabir? Is this meat?\" I said, \"No, O Messenger of Allah, but it is a harīrah that my father ordered me to make, and then he ordered me to carry it to you.\" Then I returned to my father, and he said, \"Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"What did he say to you?\" I said, \"He said, 'Is this meat, O Jabir?'\" My father said, \"Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ desired meat.\" So he went to a domestic sheep of his, slaughtered it, and roasted it. Then he ordered me to carry it to him. He said: I carried it to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May Allah reward the Ansar well on our behalf, especially 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. Haram and Sa'd b. 'Ubadah.\""],[7098,"I startled a hare in al-Baqi', and it ran off, so I chased it. I was among those who chased it, and I outran them to it and caught it. I brought it to Abu Talhah, and he ordered that it be slaughtered. It was slaughtered and then roasted, but its hindquarter was found tough, so he sent it with me to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is this?\" I said, \"The hindquarter of a hare that Abu Talhah sent to you.\" So he accepted it from me."],[7099,"\"I used to roast the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would eat from it and then go out to the prayer.\" [Al-Hakim said: It is authentic according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim.]"],[7100,"\"I used to roast the belly of a sheep for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he had already performed ablution for the prayer, yet he would eat from it and then go out to the prayer.\""],[7101,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me while I was taking meat from the bone with my hand. He said to me, \"O Safwan.\" I said, \"At your service.\" He said, \"Bring the meat close to your mouth, for it is more wholesome and more palatable.\""],[7102,"\"Do not eat the sharītah, for it is the slaughter of the devil.\""],[7103,"\"Indeed the devils inspire their allies, and they say: 'What is slaughtered for Allah, do not eat it, but what you slaughter yourselves, eat it.' So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: 'And do not eat of that upon which the name of Allah has not been mentioned.'\""],[7104,"That his ewe was dying, so he slaughtered it with a wooden peg. I said to him, \"An iron one?\" He said, \"No, rather wood.\" Then he asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered him to eat it."],[7105,"\"A wolf bit into a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a sharp white stone, and the Prophet ﷺ permitted eating it.\""],[7106,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[7107,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[7108,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[7109,"The slaughter of the fetus, when it has hair, is the slaughter of its mother, but it should be slaughtered until the blood within it flows out."],[7110,"The slaughter of the fetus is the slaughter of its mother."],[7111,"The people of the pre-Islamic era used to eat certain things and leave certain things out of disgust. Then Allah Almighty sent His Prophet ﷺ and revealed His Book, making lawful what He declared lawful and unlawful what He declared unlawful. So whatever He made lawful is lawful, whatever He made unlawful is unlawful, and whatever He was silent about is pardoned. Then he recited this verse: {Say, \"I do not find within that which was revealed to me [anything] forbidden to one who would eat it...\"} [Al-An'am 145] to the end of the verse."],[7112,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah has set limits, so do not transgress them; He has decreed obligations, so do not neglect them; and He has forbidden certain things, so do not violate them; and your Lord has left some matters unspecified [intentionally] as a source of His Mercy upon you; so accept them [as is] and do not delve into them."],[7113,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about ghee, cheese, and fur. He said, \"The lawful is what Allah has made lawful in His Book, the unlawful is what Allah has made unlawful in His Book, and whatever He was silent about is among that which is pardoned.\""],[7114,"He used to like tharid (a dish of bread soaked in broth). I heard Abu Muhammad say: I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Ishaq say: \"Al-thufl is tharid.\""],[7115,"The food most beloved to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was tharid."],[7116,"We were invited to a meal, and among those present were Sa'id b. Jubayr, then Miqsam, then so-and-so, then so-and-so. When they placed the large serving dish, Sa'id b. Jubayr said to them, \"Has each of you heard what is said about food?\" Miqsam said, \"Tell them.\" He said, \"Ibn 'Abbas narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'Blessing descends in the middle of the food, so eat from its edges and do not eat from its middle.'\""],[7117,"We stayed for three days, and whoever went out to the mosque would take hold of two or three men according to his capacity and feed them. He said: I was among those who missed that for three days and their nights. Then I saw Abu Bakr at nightfall, so I came to him and asked him to recite to me from Surah Saba', and he reached his house. I hoped he would invite me to eat, but he recited to me until he reached the door of the house, then he stood at the door until he finished reciting the rest to me, then he entered and left me. Then I approached 'Umar and did the same with him, and he mentioned that he did the same as Abu Bakr had done. When morning came, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him. He said to the servant girl, \"Is there anything?\" She said, \"Yes, a loaf and a piece of ghee.\" He called for it, then crumbled the bread with his hand, then took that piece of ghee and mixed it with the bread, then gathered it with his hand until he made it into a tharid. Then he said, \"Go and invite ten men, you being the tenth of them.\" So I invited ten, I being the tenth. Then he said, \"Sit down,\" and I placed the bowl. Then he said, \"Eat in the name of Allah. Eat from its sides and do not eat from its top, for the blessing descends from its top.\" We ate until we were full, as if we had drawn lines in it with our fingers. Then he took from it and adjusted it and returned it, then said, \"Invite ten for me.\" He mentioned that after that he invited ten twice, ten at a time, and said, \"They left some remaining.\""],[7118,"He saw the Prophet ﷺ, when he ate food, lick the three fingers with which he ate."],[7119,"When he ate, he would lick his three fingers.”"],[7120,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ’s family was afflicted with fever, he would order broth to be made, then he would order them to sip from it. He used to say, “It relieves the sick heart, or it removes [sorrow] from the sick heart, as one of you removes dirt from her face with water.”"],[7121,"I saw the Muhājirūn and the Anṣār digging the trench around Madinah, carrying dirt on their backs, saying [rajaz verse]: “We are those who pledged allegiance to Muḥammad, upon Islam as long as we remain forever.” And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ answered them, saying: “O Allah, there is no good except the good of the Hereafter, so bless the Anṣār and the Muhājirūn.” Then a platter was brought containing a handful of barley with chaff, prepared with rancid fat, and it was placed before the people while they were hungry. It was unpleasant in the throat and had a smell."],[7122,"When she prepared tharīd, she would cover it until its steam subsided and say, “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘It is greater for blessing.’”"],[7123,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Cool down hot food, as hot food is devoid of blessings.\""],[7124,"“None of you should wipe his hand with a napkin until he licks his hand, for a man does not know in which of his food the blessing lies. Satan lies in wait for people, or for a person, at every thing, even at his food.”"],[7125,"“Satan is keenly perceptive and constantly licking; so beware of him upon yourselves. Whoever spends the night with a smell on his hand and something afflicts him, let him blame none but himself.”"],[7126,"He heard Anas b. Mālik say, “The Prophet ﷺ would let someone ride behind him, place his food on the ground, accept the invitation of a slave, and ride a donkey.”"],[7127,"“When you eat, remove your sandals, for it is more comfortable for your bodies.”"],[7128,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me from two prayers, two recitations, two manners of eating, and two manners of dressing. He forbade me from praying after dawn until the sun rises, and after ʿaṣr until the sun sets; from eating while lying on my belly; and from wearing al-ṣammāʾ and wrapping myself in a single garment with nothing covering my private parts and the sky.”"],[7129,"“Dates were placed before the Prophet ﷺ, and they began to eat two at a time, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating two at a time.”"],[7130,"I was among the people of the ṣuffa, and the Prophet ﷺ sent us ʿajwa dates, pouring them out to us. We would eat two at a time out of hunger. Whenever one of us ate two, he would say to his companions, ‘I have eaten two, so you eat two.’”"],[7131,"“The ʿajwa and the rock are from Paradise.”"],[7132,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The 'ajwah date and the rock are from Paradise.\" Thus he narrated it to us according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[7133,"\"The 'ajwah date and the rock are from Paradise.\""],[7134,"He used to eat fresh dates and throw the pits onto the mat.\""],[7135,"He used to take fresh dates with his right hand and melon with his left, and eat the fresh dates with the melon, and it was the fruit he loved most.\""],[7136,"\"Eat unripe dates with ripe dates, for when the son of Adam eats them, Satan becomes angry and says: 'The son of Adam has survived until he ate the new with the old.'\""],[7137,"\"The son of Adam fills no vessel worse than his stomach. It is sufficient for the Muslim to have a few morsels to keep his back straight. But if he must, then one third for his food, one third for his drink, and one third for his breath.\""],[7138,"I ate a tharidah of wheat bread and fatty meat, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ and began to belch. He said: \"Stop your belching, for the people who are most satiated in this world will be the most hungry on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[7139,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say, when he saw a man who was full, and the Prophet ﷺ began gesturing with his hand toward his belly, saying: \"If this were in something else, it would be better for him.\""],[7140,"\"Use olive oil as a condiment and anoint yourselves with it, for it is from a blessed tree.\""],[7141,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a wooden bowl containing milk and some honey, and he said: \"Two condiments in one vessel; I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it.\""],[7142,"\"Successful is the one who is guided to Islam and whose livelihood is sufficient and who is content with it.\""],[7143,"I went with my grandfather to a wedding feast in which Ghalib al-Qattan was present. He said: The dining table was brought and placed, and the people held back their hands. I heard Ghalib al-Qattan say: \"What is wrong with them that they do not eat?\" They said: \"They are waiting for the condiment.\" Ghalib said: \"Karimah bt. Hammam al-Ta'iyyah narrated to us from 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers, that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Honor bread, and the honor of bread is that it should not be waited for.'\" So he ate it, and we ate."],[7144,"I and a companion of mine entered upon Salman, and he brought us bread and salt. He said, \"Were it not that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from affectation, I would have gone to extra trouble for you.\" My companion said, \"If only our salt had thyme in it.\" So Salman sent his water-skin to the grocer and pawned it, and brought thyme and threw it into the salt. When we had eaten, my companion said, \"Praise be to Allah who made us content with what He has provided us.\" Salman said, \"If you had been content with what I was provided, my water-skin would not be in pawn at the grocer's.\""],[7145,"I heard Salman al-Farisi saying, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to go to extra trouble for a guest.\" Its chain is weak."],[7146,"\"The most enviable of people in my sight is a believer light of means, with a share of prayer, who worships Allah excellently and obeys Him in secret, obscure among the people, not pointed at with fingers, whose provision is barely sufficient, and who bears that patiently.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ shook his finger and said, \"His death comes quickly, his mourners are few, and his inheritance is little.\""],[7147,"\"He has succeeded who has submitted, is granted sufficiency, and Allah makes him content with what He has given him.\""],[7148,"In pre-Islamic times, people used to cut off the humps of camels and the fat tails of sheep, and eat them and use their fat. When the Prophet ﷺ came, they asked him about that, and he said, \"Whatever is cut from a beast while it is alive is dead.\""],[7149,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the cut humps of camels and the fat tails of sheep, and he said, \"Whatever is cut from a living thing is dead.\" Abd al-Rahman b. Mahdi narrated it from Sulayman b. Bilal from Zayd b. Aslam as mursal, and it is also said from Zayd b. Aslam from Ibn Umar."],[7150,"\"Whatever is cut from a beast while it is alive is dead.\""],[7151,"\"The purification of every hide is its tanning.\" I said to him, \"We travel with these non-Arabs, and they have pots in which they cook carrion and pork.\" He said, \"If they are earthenware, boil water in them and then wash them. If they are copper, wash them, for water is purifying for everything.\""],[7152,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stopped at al-Hijr, he said to his companions, \"Whoever has prepared food with this water, let him throw it away.\" He said, \"Some of them had kneaded dough and some had prepared hais, so they threw it away.\""],[7153,"A mule died with a man, so he came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask his ruling. Jabir claimed from Samura that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to its owner, \"Do you have what would suffice you apart from it?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Go and eat it.\" It is sahih according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not include it."],[7154,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we are in a land of famine, so what carrion is permissible for us?\" He said, \"When you do not drink the morning draught, nor the evening draught, and do not gather vegetables, then you may make use of it.\""],[7155,"\"If you give your family their evening drink of milk, then avoid what Allah has forbidden of carrion.\""],[7156,"A morning or evening drink suffices for necessity or dire need."],[7157,"She sent to the Prophet ﷺ a bowl of milk at the time of his breaking the fast, and that was during the length of the day and the intense heat. The messenger returned to her saying, 'Where did you get this milk?' She said, 'From a sheep of mine.' He said, 'Where did you get this sheep?' She said, 'I bought it with my own money.' So he drank. The next day, Umm 'Abd Allah came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I sent you that milk out of compassion for you from the intense heat and the length of the day, and you returned it to me with the messenger.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'With that the messengers were commanded: not to eat anything but what is good, and not to do anything but what is righteous.'"],[7158,"When one of you enters upon his brother and he feeds him food, let him eat from it and not ask him about it. If he gives him a drink, let him drink from it and not ask him about it."],[7159,"When you enter upon your Muslim brother and he feeds you food, eat and do not ask him about it. When he gives you a drink, drink it and do not ask him about it."],[7160,"May Allah protect you from rulers who will be after me.' He said, 'And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Whoever enters upon them, believes them, and helps them in their tyranny is not of me and will not come to me at the pond.' Sahih."],[7161,"May Allah protect you, O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, from the rule of the foolish.' He said, 'And what is the rule of the foolish?' He said, 'Rulers who will be after me, who do not follow my guidance and do not adopt my Sunnah. Whoever believes them in their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing, those are not of me and I am not of them, and they will not come to my pond. Whoever does not believe them in their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, those are of me and I am of them, and they will come to my pond. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, no flesh that grows from ill-gotten wealth will enter Paradise; the Fire is more deserving of it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is a means of nearness' or he said 'a proof.'"],[7162,"Whoever's flesh grows from ill-gotten wealth, the Fire is more deserving of him."],[7163,"Al-Dhahabi commented on it in the Talkhis."],[7164,"Whoever eats a morsel at the expense of a Muslim, Allah will feed him a morsel of the fire of Hell on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever puts a Muslim in a position of notoriety, Allah will put him in a position of notoriety and ostentation on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever clothes himself with a garment at the expense of a Muslim, Allah will clothe him with a garment of fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[7165,"He used to say on the pulpit: 'I strictly warn against taking the property of the two weak ones: the orphan and the woman.'"],[7166,"I heard 'A'ishah say: Umm Sunbulah gave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some milk as a gift. She came to me with it and did not find him. I said to her, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has forbidden us to eat the food of the Bedouins.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr entered. He said, 'O Umm Sunbulah, what is this with you?' She said, 'O Messenger of Allah, milk that I gave you as a gift.' He said, 'Pour it, O Umm Sunbulah.' She handed it to Abu Bakr. Then he said, 'Pour it, O Umm Sunbulah.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and drank. She said, 'I said, How cool it is on the liver.' 'A'ishah said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you told us that you had forbidden the food of the Bedouins.' He said, 'O 'A'ish, they are not Bedouins; they are the people of our desert, and we are the people of their settled areas. When they are called, they answer, so they are not Bedouins.'"],[7167,"Do not keep company except with a believer, and let no one eat your food except a pious person."],[7168,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade eating the food of those who compete in boasting."],[7169,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two meals: sitting at a table where wine is drunk, or a man eating while lying on his stomach."],[7170,"Whoever feeds his brother bread until he is satisfied, and gives him water to drink until his thirst is quenched, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seven ditches, the distance between each two ditches being a journey of five hundred years."],[7171,"The expiations are: feeding food, spreading the greeting of peace, and praying at night while people are asleep."],[7172,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a matter which, if I adhere to it, I will enter Paradise. He said: \"Spread the greeting of peace, feed food, maintain ties of kinship, and stand in prayer at night while people are asleep, and you will enter Paradise in peace.\""],[7173,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: \"Any man who earns wealth from lawful means and feeds himself and clothes himself and those under him from the creation of Allah, that is a purification for him.\" Sahih."],[7174,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am afflicted with hardship. He sent to his wives but found nothing with them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Is there any man who will host this man tonight, may Allah have mercy on him?\" A man from the Ansar stood up and said: I will, O Messenger of Allah. He went to his family and said to his wife: This is the guest of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we will not withhold anything from him. She said: By Allah, I have nothing but the children's food. He said: When the children want dinner, put them to sleep, then come and extinguish the lamp, and we will tighten our belts tonight. She did so. Then the man went early to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah has been amazed\"—or \"Allah has laughed\"—ﷻ at so-and-so and so-and-so. And Allah, the Exalted, revealed: {And they give preference over themselves, even though they are in need} [Al-Hashr: 9]."],[7175,"When one of you buys meat, let him increase its broth, for if one of you does not get meat, he will get broth, and it is one of the two meats."],[7179,"From Abu al-Ahwas. This is also sahih."],[7181,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Any Muslim who is a guest of a people, and the guest wakes up deprived, it becomes a duty upon every Muslim to help him until he takes the hospitality of his night from their crops and wealth.\" Sahih."],[7182,"When you come to a shepherd, call him three times. If he answers you, then (take), otherwise drink without causing damage. And when you come to a garden wall, call the owner of the garden three times. If he answers you, then (eat), otherwise eat without causing damage."],[7183,"I set out with my masters intending to emigrate, until we approached Madinah. They left me behind on their mounts and entered Madinah. I was struck by severe hunger. Some of the people of Madinah who passed by me said: If only you would enter one of the gardens of Madinah and get some of its dates. So I entered a garden, came to a palm tree, and cut two bunches of dates from it. Then the owner of the garden came and took me out until he brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He asked me about my situation, so I informed him. He said: \"Which of the two is better?\" I pointed to one of them. He ordered me to take it, and ordered the owner of the garden to take the other, and let me go."],[7184,"We were struck by famine, so I came to Madinah and entered one of its walled gardens. I took an ear of grain, rubbed it, ate from it, and put some of it in my garment. The owner of the garden came and beat me and took my garment. I went to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"You did not teach him when he was ignorant, nor did you feed him when he was hungry or starving.\" He said: So he returned my garment to me and ordered for me half a wasq or a wasq [of grain]."],[7185,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Banu Amr b. Awf on a Wednesday and saw something he had not seen before of their fencing around the palm trees. He said, \"If only when you come to this Eid of yours you would stay until you hear from my words.\" They said, \"Yes, by our fathers and mothers, O Messenger of Allah.\" When Friday came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed Jumu'ah with them, then prayed two rak'ahs in the mosque, whereas before that day he used to go to his house. Then he sat straight and faced the people, and the Ansar, or those of them present, followed him until he met them. He said, \"O company of the Ansar.\" They said, \"At your service, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"In the Jahiliyyah, when you did not worship Allah, you used to carry the burden of the weak, do good in your wealth, and help the wayfarer, until Allah blessed you with Islam and blessed you with His Prophet, and now you fortify your wealth. In what the son of Adam eats there is reward, and in what the predator or the bird eats there is reward.\" The people returned, and there was not one of them but demolished thirty doors from his garden."],[7186,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, we come across camels that have milk and are left unmilked, and we are in need. He said: \"Call the owner of the camels three times. If he comes, [fine]; otherwise, milk them, drink, and make it lawful, then close the udder with a string and leave the milk for its causes.\""],[7187,"When the Prophet ﷺ took the pledge from the women, a noble woman stood up to him, as if she were from the women of Mudar, and said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we are a burden on our fathers, sons, and husbands. What is lawful for us from their wealth? He said: \"Fresh dates: you may eat them and give them as gifts.\" Sufyan al-Thawri narrated it from Yunus b. Ubayd according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[7188,"A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, we are a burden on our sons and brothers. What is lawful for us from their wealth? He said: \"Fresh dates: what you eat and give as gifts.\""],[7189,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Indeed Allah, Exalted is He, will admit three people to Paradise because of a morsel of bread, a handful of dates, or the like that benefits a poor person: the one who commands it, the wife who prepares it well, and the servant who hands it to the poor. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ also said: \"Praise be to Allah who has not forgotten our servants.\""],[7190,"\"Eat, drink, and give charity without extravagance or arrogance. Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant.\""],[7191,"He sent to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ some food of vegetables containing onion or leek. He did not see the trace of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in it, so he refused to eat it. He said to him: What prevents you from eating it? He said: I did not see the trace of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I feel shy before the angels of Allah, Exalted is He, but it is not forbidden.\""],[7192,"\"The king of India sent a jar containing ginger to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He fed his companions piece by piece and fed me a piece from it.\""],[7193,"I attended a wedding feast at the house of Abd al-A'la, and with us was Abu Umamah al-Bahili. When we finished the food, he stood and said: I do not want to be a preacher, but I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, upon finishing the food, say: \"Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, not a farewell nor dispensable.\""],[7194,"When the table was removed from before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he would say: \"Praise be to Allah, abundant, good, blessed praise, not a farewell nor dispensable, our Lord.\" Sahih."],[7195,"\"To die, so we killed it and cut it up except for its shoulder.\""],[7196,"\"The grateful eater is like the patient faster.\""],[7197,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Verily, the one who eats and expresses gratitude will have a reward similar to the one who fasts and perseveres.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[7198,"The Prophet ﷺ took the hand of a leper and placed it with him in the bowl, then said, “In the name of Allah, with trust in Allah and reliance upon Him.”"],[7199,"“Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something afflicts him, let him blame no one but himself.”"],[7200,"“Verily, Satan is keenly perceptive and persistent, so beware of him for yourselves. Whoever spends the night with grease on his hand and something befalls him, let him blame no one but himself.”"],[7201,"“Whoever eats, whatever he chews with his tongue let him swallow, and whatever he picks with a toothpick let him spit out. Whoever does so has done well, and whoever does not, there is no harm.”"],[7202,"“The most beloved drink to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sweet and cold.”"],[7203,"“The most beloved drink to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sweet and cold.” Abdullah b. Muhammad b. Yahya is perished."],[7204,"“Verily, the master of drinks in this world and the Hereafter is water.”"],[7205,"The first thing for which a servant will be brought to account on the Day of Resurrection is that it will be said to him: Did I not make your body healthy and quench your thirst with cold water?"],[7206,"Fresh water was sought for him from the houses of al-Suqya.”"],[7207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to breathe three times in the vessel and say, “It is more thirst-quenching, more wholesome, and more palatable.” Anas said, “And I breathe three times while drinking.”"],[7208,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade breathing into the vessel and drinking from the mouth of the waterskin.”"],[7209,"“None of you should breathe into the vessel when he is drinking from it, but if he wants to breathe, let him move it away from him, then breathe.”"],[7211,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, in what he read to Malik, from Ayyub b. Habib, the freedman of Banu Zuhrah, from Abu al-Muthanna al-Juhani, who said: I was sitting with Marwan b. al-Hakam when Abu Sa'id al-Khudri entered. Marwan said to him, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding blowing into a drink?\" He said, \"Yes.\" A man said to him, \"I cannot quench my thirst with one breath.\" He said, \"Remove the vessel from your mouth, then breathe.\" He said, \"What if I see a speck of dirt?\" He said, \"Spill it out.\""],[7212,"The Prophet ﷺ asked for water, and I brought him some water in which there was a hair. I removed it, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"O Allah, beautify him.\" He said, \"I saw him when he was ninety-four years old, and there was not a single white hair on his head.\""],[7213,"A bucket of water was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he bent over it while standing and drank from it."],[7214,"He forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin, because that makes it stink."],[7215,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade turning waterskins inside out to drink from their mouths. After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it, a man got up at night to a waterskin, turned it inside out, and a snake came out of it upon him."],[7216,"He forbade drinking from the mouth of a waterskin."],[7217,"Tie up your waterskins and close your doors when you go to sleep at night, and cover your drinks and food, for the devil comes, and if he does not find the door closed, he enters, and if he does not find the waterskin tied, he drinks from it. And if he finds the door closed and the waterskin tied, he does not untie the tie and does not open a closed door. And if one of you does not find something to cover his vessel with, let him place a stick across it."],[7218,"She said: We used to place three covered vessels for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: a vessel for his purification, a vessel for his tooth-stick, and a vessel for his drink."],[7219,"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks from vessels of gold and silver in this world will not drink from them in the Hereafter. Then he said, \"The clothing of the people of Paradise, the drink of the people of Paradise, and the vessels of the people of Paradise.\""],[7220,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ, during the expedition of Tabuk, asked a woman for water. She said, \"I have no water except in a waterskin of mine from an animal that died.\" He said, \"Did you not tan it?\" She said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Its tanning is its purification.\""],[7221,"Raisins and dates are wine."],[7222,"The prohibition of wine was revealed concerning two tribes of the Ansar. They drank until, when they became intoxicated, they started playing with one another. When they sobered up, a man would see marks on his face, head, and beard, and he would say, \"My brother so-and-so did this to me. By Allah, if he had been kind and merciful to me, he would not have done this to me.\" They had been brothers with no rancor in their hearts, but rancor fell into their hearts. So Allah ﷻ revealed: {Indeed, wine and gambling...} [al-Ma'idah 90] up to His saying: {So will you then desist?} [al-Ma'idah 91]. Then some people among the pretentious said, \"It is filth, and it is in the belly of so-and-so who was killed on the day of Badr, and so-and-so who was killed on the day of Uhud.\" So Allah ﷻ revealed: {There is no sin upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten} [al-Ma'idah 93] until He reached: {And Allah loves the doers of good} [Al Imran 134]. According to the condition of Muslim."],[7223,"A man from the Ansar invited us before wine was forbidden. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf went forward and led them in Maghrib prayer and recited “Say: O disbelievers,” but he became confused in it. Then it was revealed: “Do not approach the prayer while you are intoxicated.”"],[7224,"He, Abd al-Rahman, and another man were drinking wine. Abd al-Rahman b. Awf led them in prayer and recited “Say: O disbelievers,” but he mixed it up. Then it was revealed: “Do not approach the prayer while you are intoxicated.”"],[7225,"He invited people from among the companions of the Prophet ﷺ, among them Ali b. Abi Talib, and he recited: “Say: O disbelievers, I do not worship what you worship” [al-Kafirun: 2] and we are worshippers of what you worshipped. Then Allah, glorified and exalted is He, revealed: “O you who believe, do not approach the prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying” [al-Nisa’: 43]. “All of these chains are sound, but the ruling is according to the hadith of Sufyan al-Thawri, for he is more reliable than everyone who narrated it from Ata’ b. al-Sa’ib.”"],[7226,"The caller of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he stood for prayer, would say: “Do not approach the prayer while you are intoxicated” [al-Nisa’: 43]."],[7227,"\"O Allah, make it clear to us about alcohol, so the verse was revealed: 'O you who have believed, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying' (Quran 4:43) until the end of the verse. The Prophet ﷺ called upon Umar and recited it to him as if he had not heard it before. Then he said, 'O Allah, make it clear to us about alcohol', so the verse was revealed: 'They ask you about wine and gambling. Say, 'In them is great sin and [yet, some] benefit for people. But their sin is greater than their benefit'' (Quran 2:219). The Prophet ﷺ called upon Umar and recited it to him as if he had not heard it before. Then he said, 'O Allah, make it clear to us about alcohol', so the verse was revealed: 'O you who have believed, indeed, intoxicants, gambling, [sacrificing on] stone altars [to other than Allah], and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan, so avoid it' (Quran 5:90) until 'Are you then desisting?' (Quran 5:91). Umar said, 'We have desisted, O Lord.'\""],[7228,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, what about our brothers who died while drinking it? He said: Then it was revealed: “There is no sin upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten” [al-Ma’idah: 93] — the verse."],[7229,"The Jews said: Are not your brothers who died drinking it? Then Allah, glorified and exalted is He, revealed: “There is no sin upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten” [al-Ma’idah: 93]. The Prophet ﷺ said: “It was said to me: You are among them.”"],[7230,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, the companions of the Prophet ﷺ went to one another and said: Wine has been forbidden and made equivalent to polytheism."],[7231,"Abu al-Abbas Muhammad b. Ya‘qub narrated to us: Muhammad b. Abd Allah b. Abd al-Hakam informed us: Ibn Wahb informed us: Abd al-Rahman b. Shurayh al-Khawlani informed me that he had a paternal uncle who used to sell wine and give its price as charity. I forbade him from that but he did not stop. I came to Madinah and met Ibn Abbas and asked him about wine and its price. He said: “It is unlawful and its price is unlawful.” Then he said: “O community of Muhammad ﷺ, if there were a book after your book or a prophet after your prophet, it would have been sent down among you as it was sent down among those before you. But that was delayed from your affair until the Day of Resurrection, and by my life, it is more severe upon you.” Sahih."],[7232,"He heard Abd Allah b. Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was visited by Jibril ﷺ , who said: O Muhammad, Allah has cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its drinker, its seller, its buyer, its server, and the one to whom it is served."],[7233,"“Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter.”"],[7234,"“Avoid wine, for it is the key to every evil.”"],[7235,"The messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever drinks wine and becomes intoxicated by it, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. If he drinks it again until he becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. If he drinks it a third time until he becomes intoxicated, his prayer will not be accepted for forty days. If he drinks it a fourth time and becomes intoxicated, then it is rightful for Allah to make him drink from the pus of Hell.\" It was asked, \"What is the pus of Hell?\" He ﷺ said, \"It is the discharge of the people of Hell.\""],[7236,"“Whoever abandons prayer once due to intoxication, it is as if he had possessed the world and all that is on it, and then it was taken away from him. And whoever abandons prayer four times due to intoxication, it is incumbent upon Allah, exalted is He, to make him drink from the clay of khabal.” It was said: What is the clay of khabal? He said: “The juice of the people of Hell.”"],[7237,"Three will not enter Paradise: the one addicted to wine, the one who severs ties of kinship, and the one who believes in sorcery. Whoever dies addicted to wine, Allah will give him to drink from the river of al-Ghuta. It was said, 'What is the river of al-Ghawta?' He said, 'A river that flows from the private parts of prostitutes, whose odor harms the people of the Fire.'"],[7238,"Three people Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection: one who is undutiful to his parents, one addicted to wine, and one who reminds others of what he has given."],[7239,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, Umar ibn Al-Khattab, and some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, sat together after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. They discussed the greatest sins, but they did not have knowledge about them. So, they sent me to Abdullah ibn Amr to ask him about it. He informed me that the greatest of sins is drinking alcohol. I went back to them and informed them, but they denied it and disputed with me until they went to Abdullah ibn Amr's house. I informed him about their denial, and he told them that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, \"There was a man from the Children of Israel who was given the choice to either drink alcohol, kill someone, commit adultery, eat pork, or be killed. If he refused, they would kill him. So, he chose to drink alcohol. After he drank it, he did not refrain from anything they wanted from him.\" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, also said to us, \"Anyone who drinks alcohol, Allah will not accept his prayer for forty nights, and if he dies within forty nights, he will die the way a pre-Islamic pagan dies.\""],[7240,"Abu Muslim al-Khawlani performed Hajj and entered upon 'A'ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. She began asking him about Syria and its cold, and he began telling her. She said, 'How do they endure its cold?' He said, 'O Mother of the Believers, they drink a drink of theirs called al-tala.' She said, 'Allah has spoken the truth and conveyed my beloved's ﷺ words. I heard him say, \"Some people of my community will drink wine, calling it by other than its name.\"'"],[7241,"From Maryam bt. Tariq, a woman of his people, she said: I was among a group of emigrant women performing Hajj, and we entered upon 'A'ishah, the Mother of the Believers. The women began asking her about containers. She said, 'O assembly of women, you mention containers, many of which were not used in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Fear Allah and avoid what intoxicates you, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Every intoxicant is forbidden. If the water of her water-skin intoxicates, then she must avoid it.\"'"],[7242,"Indeed, from wheat there is wine, from barley there is wine, from raisins there is wine, from dates there is wine, and from honey there is wine. I forbid you every intoxicant."],[7243,"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of his mission while he was in Makkah and was then concealing it. I said, 'What are you?' He said, 'I am a prophet.' I said, 'What is a prophet?' He said, 'A messenger of Allah.' I said, 'With what has He sent you?' He said, 'That Allah be worshipped, idols be broken, and ties of kinship be maintained with dutifulness and connection.'"],[7244,"He set out with his maternal cousin Mu'adh b. 'Afra' until they reached Makkah. When they descended from the mountain pass, they saw a man under a tree. This was before the coming of the six Anṣari men. When we saw him, we spoke to him and said, 'We will go to this man and leave our mounts with him while we circumambulate the House.' We greeted him with the greeting of the pre-Islamic ignorance, and he replied with the greeting of the people of Islam. We had heard about the Prophet ﷺ, so we objected and said, 'Who are you?' He said, 'Dismount.' We dismounted and said, 'Where is the man who claims and says what he says?' He said, 'I am he.' I said, 'Then present to me,' and he presented Islam to us and said, 'Who created the heavens, the earth, and the mountains?' We said, 'Allah created them.' He said, 'Who created you?' We said, 'Allah.' He said, 'Who made these idols that you worship?' We said, 'We did.' He said, 'Is the Creator more deserving of worship or the created? You are more deserving that they worship you, since you made them, and Allah is more deserving that you worship Him than something you made. I call to the worship of Allah, to the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, to maintaining ties of kinship, and to abandoning aggression by usurping people's property.' We said, 'No, by Allah, even if what you call to were false, it would be among the noblest of matters and the best of morals. Hold our mounts until we go to the House.' Mu'adh b. 'Afra' sat with him. I went to the House, circumambulated, brought out seven arrows, and assigned one of them to him. I faced the House and said, 'O Allah, if what Muhammad calls to is true, then make his arrow come out seven times.' I cast them, and his arrow came out seven times. I affirmed, 'I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.' People gathered around me and said, 'A madman! A man has turned renegade.' I said, 'Rather, a believing man.' Then I went to the upper part of Makkah. When Mu'adh saw me, he said, 'Rifa'ah has come with a face like none he left with.' I came and believed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us Surah Yusuf and 'Read in the name of your Lord who created.' Then we departed returning to Madinah. When we were at al-'Aqiq, Mu'adh said, 'I have never come to my family at night, so stay with us until morning.' I said, 'I will not stay while I have with me what I have of news.' Rifa'ah's custom was that when he went on a journey and returned, he would present himself to his people."],[7245,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, whom should I be most dutiful to?' He said, 'Your mother.' I said, 'Then whom?' He said, 'Your mother.' I said, 'Then whom?' He said, 'Your father.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, then whom?' He said, 'Then the nearest relative, then the next nearest.'"],[7246,"I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his mother, I enjoin a man concerning his father, I enjoin a man concerning his master who is close to him, even if he has harm from him that hurts him."],[7247,"I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, which person has the greatest right over a woman?' He said, 'Her husband.' I said, 'Which person has the greatest right over a man?' He said, 'His mother.'"],[7248,"Be dutiful to your mother, your father, your sister, and your brother, then the nearest to you, then the nearest."],[7249,"Indeed, Allah the Exalted enjoins you concerning the nearest relative, then the next nearest."],[7250,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I slept and saw myself in Paradise, and I heard the voice of a reciter reciting. I said: 'Who is this?' They said: 'Haritha b. al-Nu'man.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Thus is dutifulness.' And he was the most dutiful of people to his mother."],[7251,"Jahima came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I intended to go on a military expedition, and I have come to consult you.' He said: 'Do you have a mother?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Go and stay with her, for Paradise is at her feet.'"],[7252,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The pleasure of the Lord is in the pleasure of the parents, and the anger of the Lord is in the anger of the parents.\"[1]"],[7253,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I have come to pledge allegiance to you for emigration, and I left my parents weeping.' He said: 'Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep.'"],[7254,"A man married and his mother disliked that. He came to ask Abu al-Darda', who said: 'Divorce the woman and obey your mother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The mother is the middle gate of Paradise, so keep that or preserve it.\"' Shu'ba narrated it from 'Ata' b. al-Sa'ib with an explanatory annotation."],[7255,"A man's parents or one of them commanded him to divorce his wife, and he made a vow of freeing a thousand slaves or a hundred slaves and that he would have no sacrificial animal if he did it. He came to Abu al-Darda' and mentioned that he had prayed the forenoon prayer, then asked him. He said: 'Fulfill your vow and be dutiful to your parents, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The parent is the middle gate of Paradise, so if you wish, guard the gate or leave it.\"'"],[7256,"I had a wife who pleased me, and 'Umar disliked her. He said to me: 'Divorce her,' but I refused. 'Umar went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar has a wife whom I dislike, and I ordered him to divorce her, but he refused.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'O 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar, divorce your wife and obey your father.' 'Abd Allah said: 'So I divorced her.'"],[7257,"He said: 'You have knowledge from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that you do not show.' He said: 'Apart from the people?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Show me the sword.' I gave him the sword, and he extracted from it a page containing a writing. He said: 'This is what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"May Allah curse whoever slaughters for other than Allah, and whoever takes as allies other than his true patrons, and may Allah curse the one who is undutiful to his parents, and may Allah curse the one who diminishes the waymarks of the land.\"' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7258,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge allegiance to him for emigration and said: 'I have come to pledge allegiance to you for emigration, and I left my parents weeping.' He said: 'Return to them and make them laugh as you made them weep.'"],[7259,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Come toward the pulpit,\" and we all came. When he climbed a step, he said, \"Āmīn\", and when he climbed the second step he said, \"Āmīn\", and when he climbed the third step he said, \"Āmīn.” When he came down [after the sermon] we asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, we heard something from you that we had not heard before.\" He said, \"Jibrīl ﷺ [came] to me and said, (1) 'Away with the one who found Ramadan and he was not forgiven.'\", and I said, 'Āmīn.'\" \"When I climbed the second [step] he said, 'Away with the one to him when I (Allah) am mentioned and he does not send ṣalāh upon you.'\" \"When I climbed the third [step] he said, 'Away with the one who finds his parents in old age or [at least] one of them and they do not become [a means] for him to enter Jannah.' And I said, 'Āmīn.'\"[1]"],[7260,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever is kind and dutiful to his parents, good tidings to him, may Allah increase his lifespan.\""],[7261,"He said: 'Be chaste toward the women of others, your women will be chaste. Be dutiful to your fathers, your sons will be dutiful to you. Whoever's brother comes to him with an excuse, let him accept it from him, whether he is truthful or false. If he does not, he will not come to me at the Pond.'"],[7262,"He said: 'Be dutiful to your fathers, your sons will be dutiful to you. Be chaste toward the women of others, your women will be chaste. Whoever is approached with an excuse and does not accept it will not come to me at the Pond.'"],[7263,"He heard Abu Usayd Malik b. Rabi'a al-Sa'idi say: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man from Banu Salama came to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there any dutifulness left toward my parents that I may do for them after their death?' He said: 'Yes: praying for them, seeking forgiveness for them, fulfilling their covenants, honoring their friends, and maintaining the ties of kinship that you have only through them.'"],[7264,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have committed a great sin. Is there any repentance for me?' He said: 'Do you have parents?' He said: 'No.' He said: 'Do you have a maternal aunt?' He said: 'Yes.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then be dutiful to her.'"],[7265,"She said: \"A woman from the people of Dawmat al-Jandal came to me. She had come seeking the Messenger of Allah ﷺ after his death, soon after that, asking him about something she had gotten into concerning the matter of sorcery, which she had not practiced.\" 'A'ishah said to 'Urwah: \"O son of my sister, I saw her weeping when she did not find the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to heal her, so much so that I felt mercy for her. She was saying: 'I fear that I have perished. I had a husband who was absent from me, and an old woman entered upon me. I complained to her, and she said: \"If you do what I command you, perhaps he will come to you.\" When night came, she brought me two black dogs, and I mounted one of them while she mounted the other. It was not long before we stopped at Babylon, and there I saw two men hung by their feet. They said: \"What brought you here?\" I said: \"I came to learn sorcery.\" They said: \"We are only a trial, so do not disbelieve and go back.\" But I refused and said: \"No.\" They said: \"Go to that oven and urinate in it.\" So I went, but I was frightened and did not do it, then I returned to them. They asked me: \"Did you do it?\" I said: \"Yes.\" They said: \"Did you see anything?\" I said: \"I saw nothing.\" They said: \"You did not do it. Go back to your land and do not disbelieve.\" But I refused. They said: \"Go to that oven and urinate in it.\" So I went, and my skin trembled and I was afraid, then I returned to them. They said: \"What did you see?\" I said: \"I saw nothing.\" They said: \"You lied. You did not do it. Go back to your land and do not disbelieve, for you are at the height of your affair.\" But I refused. They said: \"Go to that oven and urinate in it.\" So I went and urinated in it. Then I saw a horseman masked in iron come out of me and go up into the sky until he disappeared from me and I could no longer see him. I came to them and said: \"I have done it.\" They said: \"What did you see?\" I said: \"I saw a horseman masked in iron come out of me and go up into the sky until he disappeared from me and I could no longer see anything.\" They said: \"You have spoken the truth. That was your faith leaving you. Go.\" I said to the woman: \"By Allah, I do not know anything, and they did not tell me anything.\" They said: \"Indeed, whatever you wish will come to be. Take this wheat and sow it.\" So I sowed it and said: \"Sprout,\" and it sprouted. Then I said: \"Form ears,\" and it formed ears. Then I said: \"Produce grains,\" and it produced grains. Then I said: \"Dry,\" and it dried. Then I said: \"Grind,\" and it ground. Then I said: \"Bake,\" and it baked. When I saw that whatever I wished came to be, I was dismayed and regretted it. By Allah, O Mother of the Believers, I have never done anything and will never do it again.'\" She asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ soon after the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when they were still numerous, but they did not know what to say to her. All of them were cautious and feared to give her a ruling based on what they did not know, except that they said: \"If your parents were alive, or one of them, they would suffice you.\""],[7266,"All sins Allah delays whatever He wills of them until the Day of Resurrection, except disobedience to parents, for Allah the Exalted hastens it for its doer in life before death."],[7267,"That they be allowed to give to their relatives while they were polytheists. Then it was revealed: {It is not upon you to guide them} [Al-Baqarah 272] until it reached {And whatever you spend of good, indeed Allah is Knowing of it} [Al-Baqarah 273]. So permission was granted to them. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7268,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah ﷻ said: I am al-Rahman (the Most Merciful), and it is al-rahim (the womb/tie of kinship). Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him.\""],[7269,"\"The womb is a branch from the Most Merciful. Whoever maintains it, Allah maintains him, and whoever severs it, Allah ﷻ severs him.\" Sahih."],[7270,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah ﷻ said: I am al-Rahman, and it is al-rahim. I derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him, and whoever cuts it off, I cut him off.\" Sahih."],[7271,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I am al-Rahman. I created al-rahim and derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I cut him off.\" \"This is Abu Raddad al-Laythi. Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah, Muhammad ibn Abi 'Atiq, Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah, and Sufyan ibn Husayn have added to it.\" Sahih."],[7272,"Abu al-Raddad fell ill, and 'Abd al-Rahman came to visit him. He said: \"The best of them and the most maintaining of ties, as far as I know, is Abu Muhammad.\" So 'Abd al-Rahman said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Allah ﷻ said: I am Allah, and I am al-Rahman. I created al-rahim and derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him.'\" Sahih."],[7274,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: I am al-Rahman. I created al-rahim and derived for it a name from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him.\" Sahih."],[7275,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Allah the Exalted said: I am al-Rahman. I created al-rahim and derived for it a branch from My name. Whoever maintains it, I maintain him, and whoever severs it, I sever him.\" \"I returned to mentioning the Companions, ؓ .\" Sahih."],[7276,"\"The womb is a branch from Allah. He meant a branch from the name of Allah, the name which is al-Rahman. Whoever maintains it, He maintains him, and whoever severs it, He severs him.\""],[7277,"The merciful will receive mercy from God. Show mercy to the people of the earth, and the people of heaven will show mercy to you. The womb-tie is a branch of the Most Merciful; whoever maintains it, He maintains him, and whoever severs it, He severs him."],[7278,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in a red leather tent with about forty men, and he said: “Indeed, it will be opened for you, and you will be aided and will hit the mark. Whoever of you reaches that should fear God, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and maintain his womb-tie. The likeness of one who helps his people on falsehood is like a camel that is falling into a well while pulling it by its tail.”"],[7279,"I said: “O Messenger of God, instruct me.” He said: “Establish the prayer, pay the zakat, fast Ramadan, perform Hajj to the House and ‘Umrah, be dutiful to your parents, maintain your womb-tie, honor the guest, enjoin what is right, forbid what is wrong, and move with the truth wherever it moves.”"],[7280,"“When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Al-Madinah, the people rushed towards him and it was said: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come!’ I came along with the people to see him, and when I looked at the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I realized that his face was not the face of a liar. The first thing he said was: “O people, spread (the greeting of) Salam, offer food to people and pray at night when people are sleeping, you will enter Paradise in peace.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1334)"],[7281,"I said: “O Messenger of God, when I see you my soul is pleased and my eye is comforted, so tell me about everything.” He said: “Everything is created from water.” He said: “I said: Tell me about a matter which, if I do it, I will enter Paradise.” He said: “Spread peace, feed food, maintain womb-ties, and pray at night while people sleep; then you will enter Paradise in peace.”"],[7282,"“It is written in the Torah: Whoever is pleased that his life be prolonged and his provision increased, let him maintain his womb-tie.”"],[7283,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever would be pleased that Allah prolong his life, expand his provision for him, and ward off from him an evil death, let him fear Allah and maintain the ties of kinship.”"],[7284,"Who will be pleased that their lifetime is extended and his [provisions] are increased, then he should [maintain good relations] with his relatives.\"[1]"],[7285,"“God grants a people long life and increases their wealth without having looked at them once since He created them out of hatred for them.” They said: “How is that, O Messenger of God?” He said: “By their maintaining their womb-ties.”"],[7286,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Know your lineages so that you may maintain your womb-ties. There is no closeness for a womb-tie when it is severed, even if it is near, and no distance for it when it is maintained, even if it is far.”"],[7287,"“Learn of your lineages that by which you maintain your womb-ties, for maintaining the womb-tie brings love in the family, increase in wealth, and prolongation of one’s trace.”"],[7288,"I met the Messenger of God ﷺ and I hastened and took hold of his hand, and he hastened and took hold of my hand. He said: “O ‘Uqbah, shall I tell you the best character of the people of this world and the Hereafter? Maintain ties with the one who cuts you off, give to the one who deprives you, and pardon the one who wrongs you. And whoever wants his lifespan to be extended and his provision to be expanded, let him maintain his womb-tie.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7289,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: When God ﷻ finished the creation, the womb-tie stood and took hold of the waist of the Most Merciful. He said: “Stop.” It said: “This is the station of one who seeks refuge with You from severance.” He said: “Would you not be pleased that I maintain ties with whoever maintains you and sever whoever severs you? Recite if you will: ‘So would you perhaps, if you turned away, cause corruption in the land and sever your womb-ties’ [Muhammad: 22] up to His saying ‘Do they not then reflect upon the Quran’ [al-Nisa: 82] etc.”"],[7290,"The womb-tie is a branch of the Most Merciful. It says: “O Lord, I have been severed; I have been mistreated; O Lord.” Its Lord answers it and says: “Would you not be pleased that I maintain ties with whoever maintains you and sever whoever severs you?”"],[7291,"“The womb-tie will come on the Day of Resurrection with a hook like the hook of a spindle, and it will speak with an eloquent, piercing tongue, and it will maintain ties with whoever maintained it and sever whoever severed it.”"],[7292,"There is no sin more deserving that Allah make its perpetrator suffer punishment along with what He stores for him in the Hereafter than oppression and severing ties of kinship."],[7293,"There is no sin more likely and deserving that Allah, the Exalted, make its perpetrator suffer punishment in this world along with what He stores for him in the Hereafter than severing ties of kinship and oppression."],[7294,"It is not permissible to abandon a fellow Muslim for more than three days. If they meet and one of them greets the other and the other returns the greeting, they share in the reward. If the other refuses to return the greeting, this one is free of sin and the other bears it. I think he said: And if they die while they are in a state of mutual abandonment, they will not be gathered together in Paradise."],[7295,"Whoever abandons his brother for a year is like shedding his blood."],[7296,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Who is your master, O Banu 'Ubayd?\" They said, \"Al-Jadd ibn Qays, because he is stingy.\" He responded, \"What disease is worse than stinginess? Rather, your master and the son of your master is Bashir ibn Al-Baraa ibn Ma'rur.\" This hadith is authentic according to the criteria of Muslim and it has not been rejected. Sa'id ibn Muhammad, known as Al-Warraq, is trustworthy and reliable. We have recorded it from the hadith of 'Amr ibn Dinar, narrated from Abu Salamah."],[7297,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at al-Jiʿirrānah. A woman came to him while I was a boy that day. When she drew near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he spread his cloak for her and she sat on it. I said, \"Who is this?\" They said, \"This is his mother who breastfed him.\" This hadith has a sound chain of narration, but they (al-Bukhari and Muslim) did not include it. Al-Dhahabi omitted it from the Talkhis."],[7298,"The best of companions in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his companion, and the best of neighbors in the sight of Allah is the one who is best to his neighbor."],[7299,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest. His jaʾizah (special gift) is a day and a night, and hospitality is three days. Whatever is beyond that is charity. It is not permissible for him to stay with him until he turns him out. Ibn Wahb added in his narration: And his jaʾizah is to entertain him on the day with the best of what he finds. He also said: 'yathwī' means he stays with him."],[7300,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, should honor his neighbor.\" And he mentioned the hadith until its end."],[7301,"He heard Abu Shurayh say: My ears heard it, my eyes saw it, and my heart comprehended it when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke. Then he mentioned the hadith exactly like the hadith of Malik. \"As for the two Shaykhs, neither of them used ʿAbd al-Rahman b. Ishaq as evidence.\""],[7302,"By Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe; by Allah, he does not believe.\" They said, \"What is that, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"A neighbor whose neighbor is not safe from his bawāʾiq (harmful deeds).\" They said, \"What are his bawāʾiq, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"His evil.\""],[7303,"He is not a believer whose neighbor is not safe from his ghawaʾil (treacheries/harmful acts)."],[7304,"Indeed, Allah has divided your characters among you just as He has divided your provisions among you. And indeed, Allah gives wealth to those He loves and those He does not love, but He does not give faith except to those He loves. So whoever Allah has given faith, He has loved him. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, no servant truly submits until his heart submits, and no servant truly submits until his neighbor is safe from his harmful acts.[1]"],[7305,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and complained to him about his neighbor, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, my neighbor is harming me.\" He said, \"Take out your belongings and place them on the road.\" So he took out his belongings and placed them on the road. Then everyone who passed by him asked, \"What is the matter with you?\" He said, \"I complained about my neighbor to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered me to take out my belongings and place them on the road.\" So they began to say, \"O Allah, curse him! O Allah, disgrace him!\" The man said, \"That reached the man, so he came to him and said, 'Return, for by Allah, I will never harm you again.'\""],[7306,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ complaining about his neighbor. The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Put your belongings in the road.\" He said: People began to pass by him and curse him. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what I have met from the people!\" He said, \"And what have you met from them?\" He said, \"They curse me.\" He said, \"Allah has cursed you before the people.\" He said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I will not do it again.\" He said: Then the one who had complained came to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"You have been granted safety,\" or, \"You have been cursed.\" [According to the conditions of Muslim]"],[7307,"I heard Abu Hurayra say: It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"Such-and-such a woman prays at night and fasts during the day, but there is something in her tongue that harms her neighbors; she is sharp-tongued.\" He said, \"There is no good in her; she is in the Fire.\" It was said to him, \"Such-and-such a woman performs the prescribed prayers, fasts Ramadan, and gives charity with pieces of dried curd, and she has nothing other than that, and she does not harm anyone.\" He said, \"She is in Paradise.\""],[7308,"From Abu Yahya, the freed slave of Ja'da bt. Hubayra, from Abu Hurayra, who said: It was said to the Prophet ﷺ, \"Such-and-such a woman fasts during the day, prays at night, but harms her neighbors with her tongue.\" He said, \"There is no good in her; she is in the Fire.\" It was said, \"Such-and-such a woman performs the prescribed prayers, fasts Ramadan, gives charity with pieces of dried curd, and does not harm anyone with her tongue.\" He said, \"She is in Paradise.\""],[7309,"Part of the happiness of a Muslim person in this world is a righteous neighbor, a spacious dwelling, and a comfortable mount."],[7310,"The believer is not one who spends the night while his neighbor next to him is hungry."],[7311,"It reached Umar that when Sa'd built the palace he said, \"The noise has stopped.\" So he sent Muhammad b. Maslama to him with the instruction. And at the end of it he said: Umar said, \"I disliked to command you, so that you would have the cool and I the hot, while around me the people of Madinah have been killed by hunger. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A man is not satisfied while his neighbor is hungry.'\" Its chain is good."],[7312,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have two neighbors; to which of them should I give first?\" He said, \"To the one whose door is nearer to you.\""],[7313,"\"You will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not guide you to something upon which if you do it, you will love one another?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Spread peace among yourselves; you will love one another. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you show mercy to one another.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, all of us are merciful.\" He said, \"It is not the mercy of any one of you, but rather mercy for the general public, mercy for the general public.\""],[7314,"\"My nation will be afflicted with the disease of the nations.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the disease of the nations?\" He said, \"Insolence, extravagance, boasting of abundance, mutual vying for worldly gains, mutual hatred, and mutual envy, until there is transgression.\""],[7315,"Whoever would be pleased to find the taste of faith, let him love a person only for the sake of Allah ﷻ."],[7316,"\"O Yazid b. Asad, do you love Paradise?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Then love for your Muslim brother what you love for yourself.\""],[7317,"I entered the mosque of Damascus, and there was a young man with bright front teeth, and the people were with him. When they differed about something, they referred it to him and took his opinion. I asked about him, and was told, \"This is Mu'adh b. Jabal.\" The next day I went early and found that he had preceded me, and I found him praying. He said: I waited for him until he finished his prayer, then I came to him from before his face, greeted him, and said, \"By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah.\" He said, \"For Allah?\" I said, \"For Allah?\" He said, \"For Allah?\" I said, \"For Allah.\" He said: He took hold of the fold of my cloak, pulled me to him, and said, \"Rejoice, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah ﷻ said: 'My love is incumbent for those who love one another for My sake, sit together for My sake, give generously to one another for My sake, and visit one another for My sake.'\""],[7318,"A man passed by, so I approached him and said, \"Indeed, this person informed me of a narration from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Have you heard it?\" He replied, \"He only informed you of the truth.\" So I informed him, and he said, \"I have indeed heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, regarding those who love each other for the sake of Allah, then Allah will shade them with His shade on the Day when there is no shade except His shade. And nothing is better than it.\" I asked, \"May Allah have mercy on you, what is better than it?\" He said, \"I have heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'My love is worthy for those who love each other for my sake, and my love is worthy for those who frequently visit each other for my sake, and my love is worthy for those who give generously to each other for my sake.' And I do not know with which of them He began.\" I asked, \"Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you?\" He said, \"I am 'Ubada ibn As-Samit'. And this is a authentic chain of narration according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs (Al-Bukhari and Muslim) and they did not exclude it.\" Adh-Dhahabi refrained from discussing it in his summary."],[7319,"He said regarding the shade of Allah on a day when there is no shade but His shade, then he said, and there is no doubt in the rest of it: 'Chairs of light will be placed for them; the prophets, the truthful, and the martyrs will envy them for their nearness to the Lord, Blessed and Exalted.' He said: So I narrated it to 'Ubadah b. al-Samit, and he said: I will not narrate to you except what I heard from the tongue of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, that he said: 'My love is due to those who love one another for My sake; My love is due to those who give to one another for My sake; My love is due to those who are truthful to one another for My sake; My love is due to those who visit one another for My sake; and My love is due to those who maintain ties with one another for My sake.' Shu'bah was uncertain about 'maintain ties' and 'visit one another.'"],[7320,"I heard Abu Idris al-Khawlani say: I entered the mosque of Hims and sat in a circle, all of whom were narrating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Among them was a young man; when he spoke, the people listened to him, and when one of them narrated, he listened to him. Then they dispersed, and I did not know who that young man was. Then he mentioned the hadith in full, according to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[7321,"There are servants of Allah who are neither prophets nor martyrs, yet the prophets and martyrs will envy them on the Day of Resurrection for their nearness to Allah, the Exalted, and their place with Him.' A bedouin knelt on his knees and said: O Messenger of Allah, describe them to us and make them known to us. He said: 'They are people from among the common folk of various tribes who were truthful to one another for the sake of Allah and loved one another for His sake. Allah ﷻ will place for them on the Day of Resurrection pulpits of light. The people will be afraid, but they will not be afraid. They are the friends of Allah ﷻ, upon whom there is no fear, nor shall they grieve.'"],[7322,"A man is upon the religion of his close friend, so let each of you look to whom he takes as a close friend."],[7323,"A man is upon the religion of his close friend, so let each of you look to whom he takes as a close friend."],[7324,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ, and a man said: Indeed I love him for the sake of Allah ﷻ. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Have you informed him?' He said: No. He said: 'Then inform him.' He said: So I met the man and informed him, and he said: May Allah, for whose sake you loved me, love you."],[7325,"When one of you loves his brother, let him inform him of it."],[7326,"No two men love each other for the sake of Allah the Exalted except that the better of them is the one who loves his companion more intensely."],[7327,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am so-and-so, daughter of so-and-so. He said: 'I have recognized you; what is your need?' She said: My need is that my cousin, so-and-so, the devout worshipper—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I know him.' She said: He has proposed to me. So tell me what is the right of the husband over the wife, for if it is something I can bear, I will marry him; and if I cannot bear it, I will not marry. He said: 'It is part of the right of the husband over the wife that if blood, pus, and purulent matter were to flow from him and she were to lick it with her tongue, she would not have fulfilled his right. And if it were proper for a human being to prostrate to another human being, I would have commanded the wife to prostrate to her husband when he enters upon her, because of the excellence Allah the Exalted has given him over her.' She said: By the One who sent you with the truth, I will never marry as long as I remain in this world."],[7328,"He came to al-Sham and saw the Christians prostrating to their bishops, priests, and patriarchs, and he saw the Jews prostrating to their rabbis, monks, religious sages, scholars, and jurists. He said, “Why do you do this?” They said, “This is the greeting of the prophets, upon them be blessings and peace.” I said, “Then we have more right to do this for our Prophet.” The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"They lied about their prophets just as they distorted their Book. If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command a woman to prostrate to her husband because of the greatness of his right over her. No woman will find the sweetness of faith until she fulfills the right of her husband, even if he asks her for herself while she is on the back of a camel saddle.\"[1]"],[7329,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something by which I may increase in certainty. He said: So he said: 'Call that tree.' So he called it, and it came until it greeted the Prophet ﷺ. Then he said to it: 'Return,' and it returned. He said: Then he gave him permission, and he kissed his head and his feet, and said: 'If I were to command anyone to prostrate to another, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband.'"],[7330,"The best of you are those who are best to their wives."],[7331,"Any woman who dies while her husband is pleased with her will enter Paradise."],[7332,"A woman is not to fast while her husband is present except with his permission."],[7333,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There are two prayers that will not go beyond their heads: a slave who is disobedient to his master until he returns to obedience, and a wife who disobeys her husband until she returns to obedience.\" - Al-Dhahabi, in his summary."],[7334,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a woman with her two young daughters, one of whom she was carrying while she led the other by the hand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Mothers, carriers, compassionate—were it not for what they do to their husbands, the praying women among them would enter Paradise.\""],[7335,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ with her two small sons. He gave her three dates, and she gave each of them one date. Then one of the boys cried, so she split the remaining date and gave each of them half. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Mothers, carriers, compassionate to their children—were it not for what they do to their husbands, the praying women among them would enter Paradise.\""],[7336,"Indeed, woman was created from a rib. If you try to straighten her, you will break her; so deal gently with her, and you can live with her.\" (He said it three times.)"],[7337,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Woman was created from a bent rib. If you try to straighten her, you will break her; and if you leave her, you can live with her, though there is crookedness in her.\" This is a sound chain according to the criterion of Muslim, but they did not record it on Muslim's criterion."],[7338,"Allah does not look at a woman who does not show gratitude to her husband while she cannot do without him."],[7339,"Allah does not look at a woman who does not show gratitude to her husband while she cannot do without her husband."],[7340,"Allah does not look at a woman who does not show gratitude to her husband while she cannot do without him."],[7341,"O Messenger of Allah, who has the greatest right over a woman? He said: \"Her husband.\" I said: Who has the greatest right over a man? He said: \"His mother.\""],[7342,"Whenever the Prophet ﷺ was brought something, he would say: \"Take it to so-and-so, for she was a friend of Khadijah. Take it to so-and-so, for she used to love Khadijah.\""],[7343,"He used to slaughter a sheep and send it to the friends of Khadijah bt. Khuwaylid."],[7344,"Were it not for the Children of Israel, meat would not rot; and were it not for Hawwa, no woman would betray her husband."],[7345,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: \"Do not ask a man why he strikes his wife, and do not ask him who supports him among his brothers, and do not rely on them, and do not sleep except on a mattress.\""],[7346,"That a man from the Arabs used to visit Abu Bakr, called 'Ufayr. Abu Bakr said to him: O 'Ufayr, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about love? He said: I heard him say: \"Love is inherited, and hatred is inherited.\""],[7347,"Abu Bakr al-Siddiq met a man from the Arabs called 'Ufayr. Abu Bakr said to him: What did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about love? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed love and enmity are inherited.\" Yusuf b. 'Atiyya is ruined."],[7348,"\"Shall I not guide you to charity, or to one of the greatest charities? Your daughter returned to you, having no provider other than you.\""],[7349,"\"Whoever has three daughters and is patient with their hardships and difficulties, Allah will admit him to Paradise by His mercy toward them.\" He said: Then a man said: And two, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"And two.\" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, and one? He said: \"And one.\""],[7350,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by some of his companions while a child was in the middle of the road. When his mother saw the riding animals, she feared for her son that he would be trampled, so she ran distraught, saying: My son, my son, and she carried her son. The people said: O Prophet of Allah, this woman would not throw her son into the Fire. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No, by Allah, Allah will not throw His beloved into the Fire.\" He said: So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ silenced them."],[7351,"\"Whoever has a female child born to him and does not bury her alive, does not humiliate her, and does not prefer his male children over her, Allah will admit him to Paradise because of her.\""],[7352,"A woman came to 'A'isha asking, and she had children with her. She gave her three dates. She gave each child a date, a date, and kept a date for herself. The children ate the two dates, so she took the date, split it into two halves, and gave each child of hers half a date. Then the Prophet ﷺ came, and she informed him. He said: \"What amazes you about her? Allah has had mercy on her because of her mercy to her child.\""],[7353,"\"Whoever supports two girls until they reach maturity, he and I will enter Paradise like these two,\" and he indicated with his two fingers, the index and middle. \"And two gates whose punishment is hastened in this world: oppression and disobedience to parents.\""],[7354,"\"There is no Muslim who has two daughters, and he treats them well as long as they accompany him or he accompanies them, except that they will admit him to Paradise.\""],[7355,"Abu 'Abd Allah Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah b. Dinar and Abu Bakr Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Hafid narrated to us, they said: Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Nasr narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Fitr narrated to us from Shurahbil b. Muslim from Ibn 'Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ something similar. This is an error, for this Shurahbil is Abu Sa'd Shurahbil b. Sa'd, a shaykh from the people of Madinah."],[7356,"\"Whoever does not have mercy on our young and does not recognize the right of our elders is not one of us.\""],[7357,"That the Prophet ﷺ sent him on the day of the greater pilgrimage with four [directives]: that no one should circumambulate the House naked, that none shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, that no polytheist should perform Hajj after this year of his, and that whoever had a treaty between him and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, its term is until its duration."],[7358,"I was with Ali b. Abi Talib when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him to the people of Makkah with Bara'ah. It was said: What were you proclaiming? He said: \"We were proclaiming that none will enter Paradise except a believing soul, and no one should circumambulate the House naked, and whoever has a treaty with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, its term and the duration of his treaty is up to four months; when the four months have passed, Allah is free from the polytheists and His Messenger, and no polytheist should perform Hajj after this year.\" So I kept proclaiming until my voice became hoarse."],[7359,"Abu Talib was working on Zamzam, and the Prophet ﷺ was among those carrying stones, and he was then a young boy. The Prophet ﷺ took his lower garment, stripped, and used it as protection against the stone. Then he fainted. It was said to Abu Talib: Attend to your son, for he has fainted. When the Prophet ﷺ recovered from his fainting, Abu Talib asked him about his fainting. He said: \"A visitor came to me wearing white clothes and said to me: Cover yourself.\" Ibn Abbas said: That was the first thing the Prophet ﷺ saw of prophethood, that he was told to cover himself, and his private parts were never seen from that day."],[7360,"When the House was built, people were carrying stones, and the Prophet ﷺ was carrying with them. He took the garment and placed it on his shoulder, then he was called: \"Do not uncover your private parts.\" So he threw down the stone and put on his garment."],[7361,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, our private parts, what may we expose of them and what must we cover? He said: \"Guard your private parts except from your wife or what your right hand possesses.\" I said: What if people are on top of one another? He said: \"If you can ensure that no one sees them, then let no one see them.\" I said: What if one is alone? He said: \"Then Allah is more deserving that one be modest before Him,\" and he placed his hand over his private part."],[7362,"\"The 'awrah of a man before another man is like the 'awrah of a woman before a man, and the 'awrah of a woman before another woman is like the 'awrah of a woman before a man.\""],[7363,"The Prophet ﷺ saw him when his thigh was uncovered in the mosque while he was wearing a cloak. He said: \"The thigh is part of the 'awrah.\""],[7364,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Ma'mar while I was with him, and Ma'mar's thighs were uncovered. He said: \"O Ma'mar, cover your thighs, for the thighs are 'awrah.\" And similar has been narrated from Ali b. Abi Talib and Abdullah b. Abbas from the Prophet ﷺ. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7365,"\"Do not expose your thighs, and do not look at the thigh of a living or dead person.\""],[7366,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a man and saw his thigh uncovered, and he said: \"Cover your thigh, for a man's thigh is part of his 'awrah.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7367,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ looking disheveled. He said: \"Do you have wealth?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"What kind of wealth?\" I said: All kinds of wealth, camels, slaves, horses, and sheep. He said: \"If Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you.\" Then he said: \"Do your people's camels give birth with sound ears, and you take a blade and cut their ears, saying: This is a Bahirah, and you slit them or slit their skins and say: This is a Sarm, thus making them forbidden for you and your family?\" I said: Yes. He said: \"What Allah has given you is lawful for you. Allah's blade is sharper, and perhaps he said: Allah's arm is stronger than your arm, and Allah's blade is sharper than your blade.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, what about a man whom I visited and he did not honor me or offer me hospitality, then he visited me—should I repay him as he did or offer him hospitality? He said: \"Offer him hospitality.\""],[7368,"\"Allah is beautiful and loves beauty.\""],[7369,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who loves beauty, and I have been given of it what you see, to the extent that I do not like anyone to surpass me even in the strap of my sandal. Is that arrogance? He said: \"No, but arrogance is rejecting the truth and belittling people.\""],[7370,"I was not screened—or he said: I was not held back—from three things: from private conversation, from such-and-such, and from such-and-such. He said: I came to him while Malik b. Murarah al-Rahawi was with him, and I caught the end of his speech while he was saying: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have been given of beauty what you see, and I would not like anyone to surpass me even by a shoelace of my sandal. Is that arrogance?' He said: 'That is not arrogance. Rather, arrogance is one who rejects the truth'—or he said: 'belittles the truth'—'and despises people.'"],[7371,"When the Haruriyyah went out, they gathered in a house, and they were six thousand. I came to Ali and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, delay the prayer so that I may go to these people and speak with them.' He said: 'I fear for you.' He said: 'Not at all.' He said: So I went out to them, and I put on the finest Yemeni robes. Abu Zumayl said: Abdullah b. Abbas was handsome and had a strong voice. Ibn Abbas said: I came to them while they were gathered in a house, taking their midday rest, and I greeted them. They said: 'Welcome, O Ibn Abbas. What is this robe?' I said: 'What do you find wrong with me? I saw on the Messenger of Allah ﷺ the finest of robes,' and I recited: 'Say: Who has forbidden the adornment of Allah which He has produced for His servants and the good things of provision?'"],[7372,"Jabir: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his expeditions, and a man went out in two torn garments intending to drive the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Does he not have any other two garments besides these?' It was said: 'He has two new garments in his bag.' He said: 'Bring me his bag.' So he opened it, and there were two garments in it. He said to the man: 'Take these two and wear them, and throw away the torn ones.' He did so, then drove the camels. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked after him as if amazed at his stinginess toward himself with the two garments, and said to him: 'May Allah strike your neck.' The man turned to him and said: 'In the path of Allah.' He was killed on the day of Yamamah."],[7373,"From Jabir ibn Abdullah."],[7374,"My father was a companion of Abu al-Darda' in Damascus, and there was a man there from the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from the Ansar, called Ibn al-Hanzaliyyah. He was solitary, rarely sitting with people—he was always in prayer, and when he finished, he would only engage in takbir, glorification, and tahlil until he reached his family. One day he passed by us while we were with Abu al-Darda', and he greeted. Abu al-Darda' said: 'A word that benefits us and does not harm you.' He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You are going to meet your brothers, so improve your garments and set right your riding gear until you are like a beauty spot among the people. Indeed, Allah does not love obscenity or the obscene.'"],[7375,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever gives up fine clothing while able to afford it, out of humility before Allah ﷻ, Allah ﷻ will call him on the Day of Resurrection before the heads of all creatures and let him choose whichever of the robes of faith he wishes to wear.'"],[7376,"They say about me 'pride,' yet I have ridden a donkey, hobbled a sheep, worn a rough woolen cloak, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Whoever does this has no trace of arrogance in him.'"],[7377,"It reached Umar b. Abd al-Aziz that Abu al-Ahwas was narrating a hadith from Thawban. He said: So he sent for him, and he was carried on the postal mount. He said: When he reached him and entered upon him, he greeted and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, the ride on the postal mount has indeed been hard on my leg.' He said: Umar said, as if in sympathy: 'We did not intend hardship for you, O Abu Sallam, but a hadith reached me that you narrate from Thawban from the Prophet of Allah ﷺ about the Basin, and I wished that you relate it to me directly.' Abu Sallam said: I heard Thawban say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'My Basin is between Aden and Amman al-Balqa'. Its water is whiter than milk and sweeter than honey, and its cups are as numerous as the stars. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it, ever. The first of people to arrive at it will be the poor emigrants, disheveled of hair and soiled of garments, who do not marry the pampered women, and for whom the gates [of the rulers] are not opened.' He said: Umar said: 'But I have married a pampered woman, Fatimah bt. Abd al-Malik, and the gates have been opened for me. No doubt, I will not wash my head until it becomes disheveled, nor the garment that touches my body until it becomes soiled.'"],[7378,"Adhere to these white garments: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them, for they are among the best of your clothes'—or he said: 'among the best of your attire.'"],[7379,"Adhere to these white garments: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them."],[7380,"Adhere to these white garments: let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them, for they are among the best of your clothes."],[7381,"The best of your garments is white, so clothe your living in it and shroud your dead in it. And indeed, among the best of your kohls is ithmid: it clears the sight and makes the hair grow."],[7382,"Wear white garments, for they are the purest and the most pleasant, and shroud your dead in them."],[7383,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us and saw a man with disheveled hair and said: \"Can this man not find something with which to settle his hair?\" And he saw a man with dirty clothes and said: \"Can this man not find something with which to clean his clothes?\""],[7384,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wearing a burda wrapped around him under his armpit, as if I were looking at the muscle of his upper arm trembling. I heard him say: \"O people, fear Allah. If an Abyssinian slave is appointed over you, then listen to him and obey him as long as he establishes the Book of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, among you.\""],[7385,"I met the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of the roads of Madinah, wearing an izar of cotton with a loose edge. I said: \"Peace be upon you, O Muhammad,\" or \"O Messenger of Allah.\" He said: \"'Peace be upon you' is the greeting of the dead; 'peace be upon you' is the greeting of the dead; 'peace be upon you' is the greeting of the dead. Say 'peace be upon you all,' 'peace be upon you all,' 'peace be upon you all'—that is, like this, so say it.\" Then I asked him about the izar, and he bent his back and grasped the largest part of his calf and said: \"Here; if you refuse, then here, above the ankles; if you refuse, then indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster.\""],[7386,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a bright moonlit night, wearing a red hulla, and I began to look at him and at the moon; he was more beautiful in my eyes than the moon."],[7387,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he sent him to Heraclius, and when he returned, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave him a qibtiyya and said: \"Make one piece of it a shirt, and give your wife a piece to use as a head-cover.\" When he turned away, he said: \"Tell her to put something underneath it, so that it does not describe [her shape].\""],[7388,"He used to buy for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions the hulal for a thousand dirhams and for a thousand and two hundred dirhams."],[7389,"The king of Dhu Yazan sent the Prophet ﷺ a hulla that was purchased for thirty-three camels and a she-camel, and the Prophet ﷺ wore it once."],[7390,"The prophets used to prefer wearing wool, milking sheep, and riding donkeys."],[7391,"We saw ourselves with the Prophet ﷺ when rain fell on us, and our smell was like the smell of sheep."],[7392,"We saw ourselves with the Prophet ﷺ—I think that our smell was the smell of sheep because our clothing was wool and our food was the two black things: water and dates. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7393,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one morning wearing a mirṭ with a pattern of black hair."],[7394,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ was praying while part of my mirṭ was over him."],[7395,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought some clothes, among them a khamesah [a square garment with decorative borders]. He said to his Companions, \"Who do you think is most entitled to this khamesah?\" They remained silent. Then he called Umm Khalid and dressed her in it, saying, \"Wear it out, my little girl, and make it worn. Wear it out and make it worn. Wear it out and make it worn.\" He said, \"There was a red mark on it. He began to say, 'O Umm Khalid, sana.' Sana in the language of the Abyssinians means beautiful.\""],[7396,"She made for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a black woolen jubba [long outer garment], and he wore it. When he sweated, he noticed the smell of wool, so he took it off, for he liked pleasant fragrances."],[7397,"Two men from Iraq came to him and asked him about performing the ghusl (ritual bath) on Friday. They asked if it was obligatory. Ibn Abbas said to them, \"Whoever performs the ghusl, it is better and purer.\" Then he informed them of the reason why the ghusl was initiated. During the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , people would wear wool and drink palm juice, which would cause sweat and emit an odor. The mosque was also small and had a low ceiling. One Friday, the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ came out for the sermon on a hot summer day, and the pulpit was short and had steps. As he preached to the people, he sweated, and the scent of his sweat mixed with the scent of wool, causing discomfort to some of them. The smell reached the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ while he was on the pulpit, and he said, \"O people, when this day comes, perform the ghusl and let each of you apply the best fragrance or oil he can find.\""],[7398,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing two garments dyed with saffron, a cloak and a turban."],[7399,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon. Al-Hasan and al-Husayn came forward wearing two red shirts. They began to stumble and get up, so he descended [from the pulpit], took them, and placed them before him. Then he said, \"Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth: 'Indeed, your wealth and your children are a trial' [Quran 64:15]. I saw these two and could not be patient.\" Then he resumed his sermon."],[7400,"He said: One day I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing two garments dyed with yellow safflower. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, \"What are these two garments?\" I said, \"Umm 'Abd Allah dyed them for me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I adjure you: go back to Umm 'Abd Allah and order her to light up the oven and then throw them into it.\" So I went back to her and did that."],[7401,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw on him two garments dyed with yellow safflower and said, \"These are the clothes of the disbelievers, so do not wear them.\""],[7402,"A man passed by the Prophet ﷺ wearing two red garments. He greeted, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not return the greeting."],[7403,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I do not ride on purple [dyed] saddle cloths, nor do I wear garments dyed with yellow safflower, nor do I wear a shirt with a silk border.\" Al-Hasan pointed to the collar of his shirt, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ also said, \"The perfume of men is that whose scent is apparent but its color is not, and the perfume of women is that whose color is apparent but its scent is not.\""],[7404,"The people today in the mosque, with their many tayalisah [a kind of shawl], resemble not but the Jews of Khaybar."],[7405,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold."],[7406,"He used to prevent his family from [wearing] jewelry and say, \"If you love the jewelry of Paradise and its silk, do not wear them [in this world].\""],[7407,"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter; and if he enters Paradise, the people of Paradise will wear it, but he will not wear it."],[7408,"The Prophet ﷺ only forbade solid silk when it was silk."],[7409,"There was no garment dearer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than the qamis."],[7410,"Makhrama al-Abdi and I brought cloth from Hajar. The Prophet ﷺ came to us and bought from us a man's sirwal, and there was a weigher weighing for a wage. He said to the weigher, “Weigh and give more.”"],[7411,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ acquired a new garment, he would name it a turban, a qamis, or a cloak, then say: “O Allah, to You be praise. You have clothed me with it. I ask You for its good and the good for which it was made, and I seek refuge with You from its evil and the evil for which it was made.”"],[7412,"Whoever eats food and says, ‘Praise be to Allah who fed me this and provided me with it without any might or power from me,’ his past sins will be forgiven. And whoever wears a garment and says, ‘Praise be to Allah who clothed me with this and provided me with it without any might or power from me,’ his past sins will be forgiven."],[7413,"Umar b. al-Khattab called for a new qamis of his and put it on. I do not think it had reached his collarbones before he said: “Praise be to Allah who clothed me with what I cover my private parts and adorn myself in my life.” Then he said, “Do you know why I said this? I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ call for new clothes and put them on. He said—I do not think they had reached his collarbones before he said the like of what I said—then he said: ‘By the One in whose hand is my soul, there is no Muslim servant who wears a new garment, then says the like of what I said, then deliberately takes a worn-out garment from his old clothes that he has put aside and clothes a poor, destitute Muslim with it, clothing him only for the sake of Allah, may He be exalted, except that he will be in Allah’s protection and under Allah’s guarantee as long as a single thread of it remains on him, alive and dead.’”"],[7414,"Wear turbans, and you will increase in forbearance."],[7415,"She said: On the day of the Trench I saw a man in the form of Dihya b. Khalifa al-Kalbi on a mount, conversing privately with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and on his head was a turban which he had let down over himself. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: “That was Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him). He ordered me to go out to Banu Qurayza.”"],[7416,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ on a horse, wearing a turban whose end he had let down between his shoulders. I asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: “You saw him—that was Jibril (peace and blessings be upon him).”"],[7417,"We entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to visit him while he was ill. We found him sleeping, having covered his face with an Adani cloak. He uncovered his face and said: “May Allah curse the Jews—they forbid the fat of sheep and then eat its price.”"],[7418,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who wears men’s clothing and the man who wears women’s clothing."],[7419,"A'isha used to say when this verse was revealed, “and to draw their veils over their bosoms” [al-Nur 31]: “The women took their izars and tore them from the edges, then covered themselves with them.”"],[7420,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon her while she was veiling, and he said: \"One twist, not two twists.\""],[7421,"He used to dislike ten traits: yellow dye, meaning perfumed oil; changing grey hair; dragging the lower garment; wearing gold rings; tying amulets; incantations except with the mu'awwidhat (protective chapters); playing with dice; displaying adornment to other than its rightful place; withdrawing water (semen) without its right; and harming a child without making it forbidden."],[7422,"\"O Khurayim, were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man.\" He said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: \"Your lowering your lower garment and your letting your hair grow long.\""],[7423,"The Prophet ﷺ wore a shirt that was above the ankles, and its sleeves were with the fingers."],[7424,"\"Extend my sleeve, my son, and make it stick to the tips of my fingers, and cut off what is beyond them.\" He said: So I cut from the sleeves, and the opening of the sleeves became one part above another, and I said: If only you had evened it with scissors. He said: \"Leave it, my son; thus I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do.\" Ibn Umar said: \"The shirt remained on my father until it wore out, and we did not pray until I saw some of the threads falling onto his feet.\""],[7425,"I was with Ibn Abbas when a beggar came and asked. Ibn Abbas said to him: Do you testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes. He said: And do you testify that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes, and you pray the five? He said: Yes. He said: And you fast Ramadan? He said: Yes. He said: Indeed, you have a right upon us. O boy, clothe him with a garment, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever clothes a Muslim with a garment will not cease to be in Allah's protection as long as a thread or string of it remains on him.\""],[7426,"Narrated by the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ , he said, \"Allah has not sent down a disease except that He has also sent down its cure, and in the milk of the cow, there is a cure for every disease.\""],[7427,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure. It is known to those who know it and unknown to those who do not know it.\""],[7428,"Narrated by Abdullah, he said: \"The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Verily, Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure, except for one ailment, which is old age. So, make use of the milk of the cow, for indeed it contains cure for every ailment.'\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent regarding this in his summary."],[7429,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and poetry and Arabic from the Arabs, so from whom did you take medicine? She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was a frequently ill man, and the physicians of the Arabs would come to him, and I would learn from them.\""],[7430,"They said: O Messenger of Allah, should we seek medical treatment? He said: \"Know that Allah, the Exalted, did not send down any disease except that He sent down for it a cure, except for one disease.\" They said: And what is it? He said: \"Old age.\""],[7431,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: When Sulayman son of Dawud (peace and blessings be upon him) stood in Ramadan, he would see a tree growing before him. He said: What is your name? It would say: Such-and-such. Then he would say: For what thing are you? It would say: For such-and-such. So if it was for a medicine, it was written down, and if it was for planting, it was planted. While he was praying one day, behold, a tree grew before him, and he said to it: What is your name? It said: Al-Kharrub (carob). He said: For what thing are you? It said: For the ruin of the people of this house. So Sulayman (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Allah, conceal my death from the jinn until humans know that the jinn do not know the unseen. He said: So he carved it into a staff and leaned on it for a year while dead, and the jinn worked. Then termites ate it, and he fell. When he fell, it became clear to humans that the jinn do not know the unseen. He said: \"So the jinn thanked the termites and would bring them water.\" And Ibn Abbas used to recite it thus."],[7432,"When Sulayman son of Dawud (peace and blessings be upon them) prayed a prayer, a tree would appear between his eyes. He would say to it: What are you, and for what thing have you appeared? It would say: I am the tree of such-and-such; I appeared for the disease of such-and-such. So when he prayed the morning prayer one day, a tree appeared between his eyes, and he said to it: What are you, and for what thing have you appeared? It said: I am al-Kharrub; I appeared for the ruin of this mosque. So Sulayman (peace and blessings be upon him) knew that his term had drawn near and that the Bayt al-Maqdis would not be ruined while he was alive. He called upon Allah, the Exalted, to cause the devil to faint regarding his death. The jinn used to claim that the devils knew the unseen. So he died upon his staff, and termites ate it, and he fell. Thus it became due upon the devils to bring water to the termites wherever they were, praising them in gratitude for what they did to Sulayman's staff."],[7433,"You should use the two cures: the Qur’an and honey."],[7434,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of medicines we treat with and incantations we seek cure with—do they repel anything from Allah's decree? He said: \"They are from Allah's decree.\""],[7435,"He said to the Messenger of Allah, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you see a medicine that we can use for treatment, and a talisman that we can hang with it? Does that go against Allah's decree in any way?\" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said, \"It is part of Allah's decree.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary."],[7436,"The One who sent down the disease sent down the cure."],[7437,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he said: “For every disease there is a remedy, and if the remedy reaches the disease, he is cured by the permission of Allah ﷻ.”"],[7438,"You should use the two cures: honey and the Qur’an."],[7439,"The translation of the given Arabic phrase into English is: \"The healing of Abdullah lies in reciting the Quran and drinking honey.\""],[7440,"You should use the two cures: the Qur’an and honey."],[7441,"“When one of you has a fever, let him splash cold water on himself for three nights at the time before dawn.”"],[7442,"Cool it down with Zamzam water, for indeed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it down with Zamzam water.\""],[7443,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her one day while she had spurge that she was pounding. He said: “What are you doing with this?” She said: “So-and-so drinks it.” He said: “If anything could ward off death or benefit against death, senna would.”"],[7444,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked her: “With what do you purge yourself?” She said: “I used to purge myself with spurge.” He said: “Hot, hot.” She said: “Then I purged myself with senna.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If anything contained a cure for death, senna would.”"],[7445,"“You should use senna and sanut, for in them is a cure for every disease except sam.” It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is sam? He said: “Death.”"],[7446,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to treat pleurisy with costus and oil.”"],[7447,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribing “oil and wars for pleurisy.” Qatadah said: “He administers it orally from the side that hurts.” ‘Abd al-Rahman b. Maymun narrated it from his father. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7448,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prescribed for us for pleurisy wars, oil, and costus.”"],[7449,"The first time the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell ill was in the house of Maymunah. His pain became severe until he lost consciousness. He said: The women consulted about giving him an oral-medicine injection, so they gave it to him. When he regained consciousness, he said: “This is not the act of women who came from here” – and he pointed to the land of Abyssinia. Asma’ bt. ‘Umays was among them. They said: Their conjecture is that you have pleurisy, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “That is a disease with which Allah would never afflict me. No one in the house shall remain unless he is given the oral-medicine injection, except the uncle of the Messenger of Allah” – meaning ‘Abbas. He said: “Maymunah was given it that day while she was fasting, by the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"],[7450,"O son of my sister, I saw something amazing in the respect the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed his uncle. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to suffer from flank pain, and it would become severe for him. We used to say, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has been afflicted by the kidney vein,' and we did not think to say, 'The flank pain has afflicted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' One day it became so severe for him that he fainted, and we feared for him. People rushed to him in alarm, and we thought he had pleurisy, so we gave him medicine by the side of his mouth. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was relieved and regained consciousness. He realized that he had been given the medicine and felt its effect, so he said: 'Did you think that Allah would give it power over me? Allah would never give it power over me. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, no one in the house will remain without being given that medicine except my uncle.' He said: 'I saw them administering it to them one man after another.' Aisha said: 'And who was in the house that day? We mention their virtue. All the men were given the medicine, and the medicine reached the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and they were given it one woman after another until it reached a woman among us.' Abu al-Zinad said: 'I do not think she was anyone but Maymunah.' He said: 'The people said, Umm Salamah.' She said: 'By Allah, I am fasting.' We said: 'How bad, by Allah, did you think that we would leave you while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sworn?' So we gave her the medicine."],[7451,"That the Prophet ﷺ used a nasal drop."],[7452,"The pressed dates, the rock, and the tree are from Paradise."],[7453,"The delegation of the people of Hijar from the tribe of Abd al-Qais came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. While they were sitting with him, he approached them and said, \"There is a type of date that you call it this, and another type of date that you call it that,\" until he counted all the colors of their dates. Then a man from the tribe said to him, \"By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, if I were born in the womb of Hijar, I would not be more knowledgeable than you about the hour. I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"Indeed, your land has been uplifted for me since you came to me. I have looked at it from its lowest point to its farthest point. The best of your dates is the Barni, it removes disease and there is no disease in it.\""],[7454,"The best of your dates is the barni; it removes disease, and there is no disease in it."],[7455,"From Umm al-Mundhir al-Ansariyyah, who was one of the maternal aunts of the Prophet ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and with him was Ali, who was recovering from an illness. In the house there was a hanging bunch of dates. The Prophet ﷺ stood up and took some of it, and he turned to Ali who was also taking some of it. He said: 'Leave it, for it does not suit you, as you are recovering.' So I got up and prepared barley and chard, and it was cooked. I brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'O Ali, eat of this, for it is more suitable for you.' Zayd b. al-Hubab narrated it from Fulayh b. Sulayman, and he said: from Umm Mubashshir al-Ansariyyah."],[7456,"Abu Bakr b. Ishaq informed us, Ahmad b. Salamah informed us, Ishaq informed us, Zayd b. al-Hubab informed us, Fulayh b. Sulayman al-Madani narrated to me, Ayyub b. Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari informed me, Ya'qub b. Abi Ya'qub informed me from Umm Mubashshir al-Ansariyyah, who was one of the maternal aunts of the Prophet ﷺ. She said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me, and with him was Ali, who was recovering from an illness. Then he mentioned the hadith similarly."],[7457,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ's family was afflicted with fever, he would order broth to be made, then he would order them to sip from it. He would say: 'It revives the heart of the sorrowful and relieves the heart of the sick, just as one of you women removes dirt from her face with water.'"],[7458,"I heard Ayman al-Makki say: Fatimah bt. al-Mundhir narrated to me from Umm Kulthum from Aisha that the Prophet ﷺ said: 'You should take the beneficial disliked talbinah. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it washes the stomach of one of you just as water washes dirt from his face.' He said: When one of the Prophet's family complained, the cooking pot would not cease to be on the fire until it was decided for one of the two ends: either death or life."],[7459,"There was a boy with Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha whose nostrils were dripping blood. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered and said: 'What is the matter with this boy?' She said: 'He has udhrah (a throat ailment).' He said: 'Woe to you, O group of women! Do not kill your children. Any woman whose child is afflicted with udhrah or a headache should take Indian costus.' He said: And he ordered Aisha, and she did that, and he recovered."],[7460,"A woman brought her child to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Lance his udhrah.' He said: 'Do you burn the throats of your children? Take Indian costus and wars (a dye), and administer it to him as a nasal drop.'"],[7461,"I never heard anyone complain to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of pain in his legs except that he said: 'Dye them with henna.'"],[7462,"The cure for sciatica is the fat tail of an Arabian sheep, which is melted and then divided into three parts, and drunk on three days."],[7463,"\"The Prophet ﷺ described the treatment for impotence as drinking the melted fat of a female Arab sheep. It should be neither too young nor too old, and it should be divided into three parts, with one part consumed on an empty stomach every day.\" Anas said, \"I have described this to three hundred people, and Allah Almighty has cured all of them.\" This hadith was narrated by Habib bin Ash-Shahid from Anas bin Sirin from Anas bin Malik.\""],[7464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned sciatica and said: \"Take the fat tail of an Arabian ram, neither small nor large, melt it, and drink it for three days.\" Anas b. Malik said: \"I prescribed it for more than three hundred, all of whom recovered.\" These chains of transmission are all authentic according to the conditions of the two Shaykhs, but Hammad b. Salamah rendered it problematic from Anas b. Sirin, saying: from his brother Ma'bad, from a man of the Ansar, from his father. The correct view according to us is that of al-Mu'tamir b. Sulayman and al-Walid b. Muslim. Sahih"],[7465,"«Use ithmid (antimony), for it makes the hair grow and clears the eyesight.»"],[7466,"Amr b. Yahya b. 'Umarah b. Abi Hasan informed me: Maryam bt. Iyas b. al-Bukayr, the companion of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated to me from one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ, and I think she was Zaynab, that the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her and said: \"Do you have any dharirah (a type of perfume)?\" She said: Yes. He called for it and placed it on a pimple between two toes of his foot, then said: \"O Allah, extinguisher of the great and enlarger of the small, extinguish it from me.\" And it was extinguished."],[7467,"«When Allah loves a servant, He protects him from the world just as one of you keeps guarding his sick person from water.»"],[7468,"Zayd b. Aslam from his father, who said: \"I fell severely ill during the time of Umar b. al-Khattab, and Umar called a physician for me, who put me on a strict diet until I was sucking on a date pit from the severity of the diet.\""],[7470,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed in it is a cure.\""],[7471,"A bedouin from Banu Fazarah, from Banu Umm Qirfah, entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while a cupper was cupping him with horns, making incisions with a blade. He said: \"What is this, O Messenger of Allah? Why do you let this man cut your skin?\" He said: \"This is cupping, and it is the best of what you treat yourselves with.\""],[7472,"«The best of what you treat yourselves with is cupping.»"],[7473,"From the Prophet ﷺ, similar to it."],[7474,"I entered upon Abu Hurairah while he was cupping. He said to me, \"O Abu Al-Hakam, do cupping.\" I replied, \"I have never done cupping before.\" He said, \"The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, informed me that Gabriel, peace be upon him, informed him that cupping is the best cure for people.\""],[7475,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If there is any healing in what you apply as a treatment, then it is in cupping, a drink of honey, or branding (cauterization) with fire, but I do not like to be cauterized.\""],[7476,"«The best of what you treat yourselves with are snuff, ladud (oral medicine), cupping, and walking.»"],[7477,"«I did not pass by any assembly of angels on the night I was taken on the Night Journey except that they said: 'You should use cupping, O Muhammad.'»"],[7478,"A'ishah, the wife of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, asked permission from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding cupping, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered Abu Taybah to cup her. He (the narrator) said: I think he said: \"He was her foster brother or a young servant who had not reached puberty.\""],[7479,"Whoever is cupped on the seventeenth of the month will have a cure from every disease."],[7480,"The best days for cupping are the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first."],[7481,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped on the two jugular veins, and he was cupped on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first."],[7482,"The cupping site in the middle of the head is for insanity, leprosy, drowsiness, and molar pain."],[7483,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Cupping increases intellect and increases memory. So in the name of Allah on Thursday, do not cup on Friday, Saturday, or Sunday. Cup on Monday and Tuesday. Leprosy and leukoderma do not descend except on Wednesday night. The narrators of this hadith are all trustworthy except Ghazal b. Muhammad, for he is unknown; I do not know him for integrity or criticism. The hadith is authentic from Ibn Umar as his statement, without a chain and not connected. Ghazal b. Muhammad is unknown."],[7484,"O Nafi, go and bring me a cupper, and do not bring me a very old man or a young boy. And he said: Cup on Saturday, cup on Sunday, Monday, and Tuesday, and do not cup on Wednesday."],[7485,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Cupping on an empty stomach is better; in it is cure and blessing. It increases intellect and increases memory, and it increases the memory of the one who memorizes. So whoever intends to be cupped, in the name of Allah, let him cup on Thursday. Avoid cupping on Friday, Saturday, and Sunday. Cup on Monday and Tuesday, for it is the day on which Allah averted affliction from Ayyub. Avoid cupping on Wednesday, for it is the day on which Allah afflicted Ayyub with trial. Leprosy and leukoderma do not appear except on Wednesday or Wednesday night."],[7486,"When the heat becomes intense, seek help with cupping, lest the blood of any of you becomes agitated and kills him."],[7487,"Excellent is the servant, the cupper: he relieves the back and sharpens the eyesight."],[7488,"Whoever practices medicine without having known medicine [i.e., without recognized training] is liable."],[7489,"We used to perform ruqyah [incantations] in the pre-Islamic era. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think of that? He said: Present your incantations to me. There is no harm in incantations as long as they do not involve associating partners with Allah."],[7490,"that the Prophet ﷺ saw in her house a girl whose face had a black spot. He said. \"She is under the effect of an evil eye; so treat her with a Ruqya.\" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5739)"],[7491,"When the Prophet ﷺ visited a sick person, he would sit at his head and then say seven times: I ask Allah the Magnificent, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you. If there was a delay in his appointed term, he would be cured of that pain."],[7492,"Whoever visits a sick person and says, 'I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you' seven times, he will be granted recovery, if his appointed time has not come."],[7493,"There is no Muslim servant who visits a sick person whose appointed time has not come, and says seven times, 'I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you,' except that he is granted recovery."],[7494,"Whoever enters upon a sick person whose appointed time has not come and says, 'I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you,' except that he is granted recovery."],[7495,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cauterization. We cauterized, and we neither succeeded nor prospered."],[7496,"A man from the Ansar was afflicted with a severe illness, and cauterization was prescribed for him. They came to the Prophet ﷺ, but he turned away from them. Then they came to him again, and he turned away from them. Then he said on the third or fourth time: 'If you wish, cauterize him with heated stones.'"],[7497,"He said: 'The angels did not greet me until the trace of the fire left me.'"],[7498,"Ubayy b. Ka'b fell ill, so the Prophet ﷺ sent a physician to him, who cut a vein from him and then cauterized it."],[7499,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited Sa'd b. Zurarah, who had a thorn (or a pustule). When he entered upon him, he said: 'What a bad dead person this is; the Jews say, \"If only he had warded it off,\" but I possess nothing for him, nor do I possess anything for myself. And let him not blame Abu Umamah.' So he ordered that he be cauterized, and he died."],[7500,"I heard Umar and I have not seen anyone among us who is similar, saying that Saad ibn Zurarah had an illness and the people of Medina called it \"dhabh\" (slaughter). So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized him and he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"May the Jews say about the deceased, 'If it was not for the intervention of his companion (referring to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ) and I had no control or possession over him, nor anything for myself.'\""],[7501,"Seek refuge with Allah Almighty from the evil eye, for the evil eye is real."],[7502,"The evil eye is real; it brings down the mountain peak."],[7503,"When one of you sees in himself or his brother something that pleases him, let him supplicate for blessing, for the evil eye is real."],[7504,"Sahl b. Hunayf went out with 'Amir b. Rabi'ah intending to bathe. They came to a pool, and Sahl went out intending privacy. Waki' said: meaning a screen. When he thought he had removed a woolen cloak he was wearing and placed it down, then he entered the water. He said: I looked at him and struck him with my eye. I heard a cracking sound from him in the water. I went to him and called him three times, but he did not answer me. So I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He came walking and waded into the water until I could almost see the whiteness of his shins. He struck his chest and said: 'O Allah, remove from him its heat, its cold, and its ailment.' Then he stood up, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'When one of you sees in himself, his wealth, or his brother something he loves, let him invoke blessing, for the evil eye is real.'"],[7505,"Whoever hangs an amulet, may Allah not fulfill his need; and whoever hangs a cowry shell, may Allah not give him peace."],[7506,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with a brass ring on my upper arm. He said, \"What is this?\" I said, \"From the wahinah.\" He said, \"Throw it away.\""],[7507,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever attaches something to himself is entrusted to it.\""],[7508,"I entered upon Zaynab, the wife of 'Abdullah, to treat her for a hot spot that had appeared on her face, while she was wearing a charm. As I was sitting, 'Abdullah entered. When he saw the charm, he went to a beam that was propped in the house, placed his cloak on it, then rolled up his sleeves, came to her, took hold of the charm, and pulled it until her face almost fell to the ground. Then it broke, and he left the house, saying: \"The family of 'Abdullah has become free of need from shirk.\" Then he went out and threw it behind the wall. Then he said: \"O Zaynab, would you hang charms at my place? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'He forbade ruqyah, amulets, and tawliyah.'\" Umm Najiyah said: \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, we know ruqyah and amulets; what is tawliyah?\" He said: \"Tawliyah is what arouses women.\""],[7509,"'Abdullah b. Mas'ud entered upon a woman and saw a red charm on her, so he cut it off forcefully, then said: \"The family of 'Abdullah are free of need from shirk.\" And he said: \"Among what we preserved from the Prophet ﷺ is that ruqyah, amulets, and tawliyah are from shirk.\""],[7510,"An amulet is not what is attached after affliction; an amulet is only what is attached before affliction."],[7511,"An amulet is not what is attached after affliction; an amulet is only what is attached before affliction."],[7512,"She sent her brother Makhramah to 'A'ishah, and she used to treat a sore that affected children. When 'A'ishah treated him and finished, she saw two new anklets on his legs. 'A'ishah said: \"Did you think these two anklets would ward off something Allah had decreed for him? If I had seen them, he would not have been treated by me, nor would he have been touched by me. By my life, two silver anklets are purer than these two.\""],[7513,"\"A man complained about his stomach ache, so diabetes was diagnosed for him. He mentioned that to Abdullah, who said, 'Indeed, Allah has not placed your cure in that which He has forbidden upon you.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary.\""],[7514,"When Ibn 'Umar called a physician to treat one of his companions, he stipulated that he not treat with anything Allah ﷻ has forbidden."],[7515,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that she had a touch of the devil. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"If you wish, I will supplicate to Allah ﷻ and He will heal you; and if you wish, then there will be no reckoning and no punishment.\" She said: \"O Messenger of Allah, then leave me.\""],[7516,"He said: Two men from the people of Iraq came seeking healing for their father whose urine was retained. The people directed them to Fadalah. The two men came, bringing Fadalah with them, and mentioned what had happened to them. Fadalah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever of you suffers from something, or his brother suffers, let him say: 'Our Lord who is in heaven, hallowed be Your name. Your command is in heaven and earth. As Your mercy is in heaven and earth, forgive us our sins and our errors. O Lord of the good ones, send down healing from Your healing and mercy from Your mercy upon this pain,' and he will be cured.\""],[7517,"He came with a riding party of ten to the Prophet ﷺ. He accepted the pledge of nine and withheld from pledging one man among them. They said: \"What is the matter with this man that you do not accept his pledge?\" He said: \"There is an amulet on his upper arm.\" The man cut off the amulet, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted his pledge. Then he said: \"Whoever hangs one has committed shirk.\""],[7518,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, the devil has come between me and my prayer and my recitation. He said: 'That is a devil called Khinzab. When you sense him, seek refuge in Allah from him and spit to your left.' He said: I did that, and Allah removed him from me."],[7519,"When you feel pain, place your hand where it hurts and say: 'In the name of Allah. I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what I find in this pain of mine.' Then raise your hand, then repeat that an odd number of times. Anas b. Malik said it."],[7520,"And some of her brother's sons mentioned her complaint to a man from the Zutt who practiced medicine, and he told them: 'They mention a woman bewitched; a slave girl in her room bewitched her. A boy in the room of the slave girl, a boy who has urinated in her room.' So he said: 'Bring her to me.' She was brought, and Aisha said: 'You bewitched me?' She said: 'Yes.' She said: 'Why?' She said: 'I wanted to be set free.' Aisha had granted her freedom after her death (i.e., a posthumous manumission). So she said: 'I owe it to Allah that you will never be freed. Look for the worst households in ownership and sell her to them, then buy a slave with her price and set that slave free.'"],[7521,"the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, regarding \"By the Dawn; and the Ten Nights\" (Fajr 2): The ten are the ten of [days] of Adha (Dhu al-Hijjah), the odd is the Day of Arafah, and the even is the Day of Nahr (sacrifice)."],[7522,"Whoever sees the new moon of Dhu al-Hijjah and intends to sacrifice, let him not cut any of his nails or hair until he sacrifices."],[7523,"When the first ten days of Dhu al-Hijjah enter, do not take any of your hair or nails until your sacrifice is slaughtered."],[7524,"Ibn Umar passed by a woman taking from her son's hair during the ten days and said: 'If you delayed it until the Day of Sacrifice, it would be better.'"],[7525,"A man from the 'Atik came and told Sa'id b. al-Musayyab that Yahya b. Ya'mar said: 'Whoever buys a sacrificial animal during the ten days, let him not cut his hair or nails.' Sa'id said: Yes. I said: From whom, O Abu Muhammad? He said: From the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7526,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The greatest day with Allah is the Day of Sacrifice, then the Day of Rest.' And five or six sacrificial camels were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and they began to draw near, vying for which of them he would start with. When their sides fell, he said a light word I did not understand. I asked the person next to him, and he said: He said: 'Whoever wishes may take a piece.'"],[7527,"On the Day of Sacrifice, no deed is more beloved to Allah, the Exalted, than the shedding of blood. It will come on the Day of Resurrection with its horns, hairs, and hooves. The blood falls from Allah, the Exalted, to a place before it falls to the ground, so be pleased with it."],[7528,"O Fatimah, rise to your sacrifice and witness it, for with the first drop of its blood that falls, every sin you have committed will be forgiven. And say: 'Indeed, my prayer, my rites of sacrifice, my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. And this I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims.' Imran said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is for you and your household specifically; is that for you, or for the Muslims generally? He said: 'No, rather for the Muslims generally.'"],[7529,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Fatimah (peace be upon her): 'Rise to your sacrifice and witness it, for with the first drop of its blood that falls, your past sins will be forgiven.' She said: O Messenger of Allah, is this for us, the household, specifically, or for us and the Muslims generally? He said: 'Rather, for us and the Muslims generally.' Atiyyah said this."],[7530,"Gabriel ﷺ descended to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ said to him: 'O Gabriel, how did you see our festival?' He said: The people of heaven boasted about it. Know, O Muhammad, that a young sheep (jadh') is better than the best goat; a young sheep is better than the best cow; and a young sheep is better than the best camel. If Allah knew of a better sacrifice, He would have ransomed Abraham ﷺ with it."],[7531,"He said to him: We dislike any defect in the horns and the ear. Al-Bara' said to him: Dislike for yourself whatever you wish, but do not make it unlawful for the people. Al-Bara' said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Four [defects] invalidate sacrificial animals: the one-eyed whose blindness is evident, the one with a broken leg whose fracture is evident, the sick whose sickness is evident, and the emaciated one that has no marrow."],[7532,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with the like of it. Al-Rabi' said in his book with both chains: Al-Awza'i narrated to us. The hadith of Abu Salamah from al-Bara' b. 'Azib has a sound chain, but they did not include it. Muslim, may Allah Almighty have mercy on him, only included the hadith of Sulayman b. 'Abd al-Rahman from 'Ubayd b. Fayruz from al-Bara', and that is among the criticisms leveled at Muslim, may Allah have mercy on him, due to the disagreement of the transmitters about it. The most sound of them is the hadith of Yahya b. Abi Kathir from Abu Salamah. Ayyub b. Suwayd was deemed weak by Ahmad."],[7533,"That a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"I was commanded with the Day of Sacrifice as a festival, which Allah made for this nation.\" The man said: What if I find only a borrowed female sheep or a sheep of my family, or their borrowed one—should I slaughter it? He said: \"No, but trim your nails, clip your mustache, and shave your pubic region. That is the completion of your sacrifice with Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[7534,"He forbade sacrificing an animal with a broken horn or a torn ear.\""],[7535,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade sacrificing an animal with its ears slit from the front, an animal with its ears slit from the back, an animal whose ears are slit in two lengthwise, an animal with a round hole in its ear, and an animal with its nose [or ear or lip] cut off. (Using translation from Aḥmad 609)"],[7536,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear, and not to sacrifice an animal whose ear is cut off from the front (muqabalah), nor one whose ear is cut off from the back (mudabarah), nor one with a slit ear (sharqa'), nor one with a pierced ear (kharqa').\" Abu Ishaq said: Al-muqabalah is the one whose ear tip is cut off, al-mudabarah is the one whose ear is cut from the side, al-sharqa' is the one with a slit ear, and al-kharqa' is the one with a pierced ear."],[7537,"\"And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear.\" It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri and Shu'bah from Salamah b. Kuhayl from Hujayyah b. 'Adiyy."],[7538,"And he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear.\""],[7539,"I heard 'Ali when a man asked him about a cow, and he said: It may be shared by seven. He said: And he asked him about one with a broken horn. He said: It does not harm you. He said: And he asked him about lameness. He said: If it can reach the place of sacrifice. And he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and the ear.\" All of these chains are sound, but they did not rely on Hujayyah b. 'Adiyy as an authority, and he is one of the senior companions of the Commander of the Faithful 'Ali. Sahih."],[7540,"I came to 'Utbah b. 'Abd al-Sulami and said: O Abu al-Walid, I went out looking for sacrificial animals and I found nothing that pleased me except a sheep with broken teeth, and I disliked it, so what do you say? He said: Why did you not bring it to me? I said: Glory be to Allah! It is permissible for you but not for me? He said: Yes, because you doubt and I do not doubt. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ only forbade the mustafarra (whose ear is cut off so that the ear canal is visible), the musta'salah (whose horn is removed), the bahfa' (whose eye is sunken), the mushayya'ah (which does not follow the flock due to emaciation and weakness), and the kasra' (the one with a broken leg).\""],[7541,"\"The following are not permissible for a vow: the one-eyed, the emaciated, the mangy, and the one whose teats are all cut off.\""],[7542,"We used to appoint over us in military expeditions the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, and we were in Persia. On the Day of Sacrifice, the older animals became expensive for us, so we would take an older animal in exchange for two or three young ones. A man from Muzaynah stood among us and said: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the same thing happened to us on a day like this, so we would take an older animal in exchange for two or three young ones. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, a young sheep (jadha') fulfills what a two-year-old (thaniyy) fulfills.\" It was narrated by al-Thawri from 'Asim b. Kulayb, and he named the companion in it as Mujashi' b. Mas'ud al-Sulami."],[7543,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, a young sheep (jadha') fulfills what a two-year-old (thaniyy) fulfills.\" It was narrated by Shu'bah from 'Asim b. Kulayb, and he did not name the companion."],[7544,"The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when it was a day or two before 'Id al-Adha, would give two jadha's and take a thaniyy. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'A jadha'ah suffices for what a thaniyyah suffices for.'"],[7545,"Sacrificing a jadha' from sheep is more beloved to me than sacrificing a mature goat."],[7546,"Sacrificing a jadha' from sheep is more beloved to me than sacrificing a mature goat."],[7547,"The blood of a white sheep is more beloved to me than the blood of two black ones."],[7548,"A jadha' from sheep is better than a mature goat."],[7549,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a thin, scrawny jadha' from sheep and a fat, fine jadha' from goats, and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it is the better of the two; shall I sacrifice it?' He said, 'Sacrifice it, for Allah is Self-Sufficient.'"],[7550,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas ؓ a flock of sheep, and he distributed them among his companions, and a he-goat remained, so he sacrificed it during his 'umrah."],[7551,"The Prophet ﷺ sacrificed two large, fat, salted, paired, and bleating rams. He slaughtered one of them and said, \"O Allah, this is on behalf of Muhammad and his ummah, from those who bear witness to Your Oneness, and bear witness to my Messengerhood.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[7552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed a horned, fat ram that walked in black, ate in black, and looked in black."],[7553,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered a horned ram at the prayer place, then said, 'O Allah, this is on my behalf and on behalf of those of my community who did not sacrifice.'"],[7554,"My family made me act harshly after I learned the Sunnah. We used to sacrifice one or two sheep on behalf of the household, but my family said, 'Our neighbors think we are stingy.'"],[7555,"The best sacrificial animal is the horned ram, and the best shroud is the hullah."],[7556,"I went out with Sa'd al-Zuraqi, who had been a companion, to buy sacrificial animals. He pointed to a ram with a dark head, not the tallest of rams, and said, 'It is as if it were the ram that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sacrificed.'"],[7557,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed with the people on the Day of Sacrifice. When he finished his sermon and prayer, he sacrificed a ram and slaughtered it himself, saying, \"In the name of Allah, and Allah is most great. O Allah, this is from me and from those of my community who have not sacrificed.\""],[7558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered his sacrificial animal and then said, \"O Allah, this is from me and from my community.\""],[7559,"From his grandfather 'Abd Allah b. Hisham, who had met the Prophet ﷺ. His mother Zaynab bt. Humayd took him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was small, and he wiped his head and prayed for him. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to sacrifice a single sheep on behalf of all his family.\" These hadiths all have sound chains regarding the concession of sacrificing a single sheep on behalf of a group whose number cannot be counted, contrary to those who imagine that it only suffices for one person. Reports have been narrated about sacrificing on behalf of the dead. Sahih."],[7560,"From the Prophet ﷺ and a ram for himself. He said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to sacrifice on his behalf, so I will sacrifice forever.\""],[7561,"From Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slaughtered his sacrificial animal while traveling, then said, \"O Thawban, prepare its meat.\" I continued to feed him from it until we arrived in Madinah."],[7562,"We slaughtered seventy camels on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, a camel for ten. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Let the cow be shared in the sacrificial offering.\""],[7563,"\"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and the time of sacrifice came, so we shared a cow for seven and a camel for ten.\""],[7564,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us on the two Eids to wear the best we find, to perfume ourselves with the best we find, and to sacrifice the fattest we find: a cow for seven and a camel for ten, and to proclaim the takbir, while we maintain tranquility and dignity.\" Were it not for the obscurity of Ishaq b. Buzurj, I would have judged the hadith as sound."],[7565,"I was the seventh of seven with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his journey. The time of sacrifice overtook us, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us, and each man among us contributed a dirham. We bought a sacrificial animal for seven dirhams and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we have been extravagant with it.\" He said, \"The best of sacrificial animals are the most expensive and the fattest.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us: one man took a leg, another a leg, another a hand, another a hand, another a horn, and another a horn, and the seventh slaughtered it, and they all said the takbir over it together. 'Uthman b. Zufar is reliable."],[7566,"\"O Messenger of Allah, I feel such compassion for the sheep that I slaughter it.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If you have compassion for it, Allah will have compassion for you.\""],[7567,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you intend to kill it with multiple deaths? Why did you not sharpen your blade before laying it down?\""],[7568,"\"They say: Whatever is slaughtered and Allah's name is mentioned over it, do not eat it; and whatever Allah's name is not mentioned over it, eat it.\" But Allah, exalted is He, said: {And do not eat of that over which Allah's name has not been mentioned} [Al-An'am 121]."],[7569,"“Whoever has wealth but does not offer a sacrifice, let him not come near our place of prayer.” And he said once: “Whoever finds ample means but does not slaughter, let him not come near our place of prayer.”"],[7570,"“Whoever finds ample means but does not offer a sacrifice with us, let him not come near our place of prayer.”"],[7571,"“Whoever wishes may offer the firstborn, and whoever wishes may not; and whoever wishes may offer the ‘atirah, and whoever wishes may not; and among sheep is its sacrificial animal.”"],[7572,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O people of Madinah, do not eat the meat of sacrificial animals beyond three days.” They complained to the Prophet ﷺ that they had dependents, servants, and workers, so he said: “Eat, feed others, and store.”"],[7573,"“Eat the sacrificial meats and store them.”"],[7574,"The Prophet ﷺ said: “Do you want to kill it twice? Did you sharpen your blade before laying it down?”"],[7575,"Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: “Mention the name of Allah over them standing in ranks.” He said: “Standing on three legs, with the fourth tied, saying: In the name of Allah, and Allah is Most Great. O Allah, from You and to You.”"],[7576,"Regarding a man who slaughtered and forgot to mention the name of Allah, he said: “He may eat.” And regarding a Magian who slaughters and mentions the name of Allah, he said: “Do not eat.”"],[7577,"The polytheists disputed with them, saying: “What they kill they eat, and what Allah kills they do not eat.”"],[7578,"He reported from the Prophet ﷺ who said: “No person kills a sparrow or anything larger without its due right except that Allah ﷻ will ask him about it on the Day of Resurrection.” It was said: “O Messenger of Allah, what is its due right?” He said: “Its due right is that he slaughters it and eats it, and does not cut off its head and throw it away.”"],[7579,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed whoever imitates or represents with animals.\""],[7580,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu al-Haytham b. al-Tayyihan: “Beware of the milch camel; slaughter for us a young she-goat.” So Abu al-Haytham ordered his wife, and she kneaded dough for them, and Abu al-Haytham cut the meat, cooked and grilled."],[7581,"He forbade slaughtering milk-producing animals and trading goods before sunrise."],[7582,"“Forty traits, the highest of which is giving a she-goat as a gift (minhat al-‘anz). No servant performs any one of them hoping for its reward and believing in its promise except that Allah will admit him to Paradise because of it.”"],[7583,"The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions passed by a woman, and she slaughtered a sheep for them and prepared food for them. When he returned, she said, “O Messenger of Allah, we prepared food for you, so enter and eat.” The Prophet ﷺ and his Companions entered, and they would not begin until the Prophet ﷺ began. He took a morsel but could not swallow it, so the Prophet ﷺ said, “This is a sheep slaughtered without the permission of its owners.” The woman said, “O Prophet of Allah, we do not feel shy before the family of Mu‘adh, nor do they feel shy before us. We take from them and they take from us.”"],[7584,"Jabir b. ‘Abd Allah reported that they slaughtered on the day of Khaybar domestic donkeys, mules, and horses. The Prophet ﷺ forbade them the donkeys and mules, but did not forbid them the horses."],[7585,"He caught two hares and did not find a blade to slaughter them properly, so he slaughtered them with a sharp stone. Then he came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Messenger of Allah, I hunted two hares and did not find a blade to slaughter them properly, so I slaughtered them with a sharp stone. May I eat?” He said, “Yes, eat.”"],[7586,"From Nubayshah, he said: A man asked the Prophet ﷺ saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, we used to offer sacrifices during the pre-Islamic period of Ignorance in the month of Rajab. What do you command us to do?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Offer sacrifices to Allah in any month you want and do good deeds for Allah, and feed the needy.\""],[7587,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded regarding the fara‘: one in every five."],[7588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the fara‘. He said, “The fara‘ is a duty. If you leave it until it becomes a bint makhad or a bint labun, and you carry things on it in the way of Allah or give it to a widow, that is better than slaughtering it while its meat sticks to its wool and you leave your she-camel bereft.” Sahih."],[7589,"He said concerning the fara‘ah: “It is a duty, and do not slaughter it while it is a young weanling that clings to your hand, but let it have milk until, when it is among the best of the wealth, then slaughter it.”"],[7590,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Seek forgiveness for me.” He said, “May Allah forgive you.” I said that to him once or twice, then a man said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the ‘ata’ir and the fara’i’?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Whoever wishes may offer the ‘atirah, and whoever wishes may not offer it; and whoever wishes may offer the fara‘ah, and whoever wishes may not offer it, and in the sheep is its sacrificial offering.”"],[7591,"“The boy is held in pledge by his ‘aqiqah, which is slaughtered on his behalf on his seventh day, and his head is shaved and he is named on the seventh day.”"],[7592,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the ‘aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn on the seventh day, named them, and ordered that the harm be removed from their heads."],[7593,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the ‘aqiqah for al-Husayn with a sheep and said, “O Fatimah, shave his head and give charity equal to the weight of his hair.” So we weighed it, and its weight was a dirham. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7594,"The Prophet ﷺ performed the ‘aqiqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn, two similar, equal rams for each of them. Suwar Abu Hamzah is weak."],[7595,"“Let the birds stay in their nests.”"],[7596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the ‘aqiqah. He said, “I do not like disobedience. Whoever among you has a child born, and I would like him to offer a sacrifice on his behalf, let him do so: for a boy, two sheep; and for a girl, one sheep.”"],[7597,"“With a boy there is an ‘aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him.”"],[7598,"“In the pre-Islamic era, when a boy was born to us, we would slaughter a sheep for him, shave his head, and smear his head with its blood. When Islam came, when a boy was born to us, we would slaughter a sheep for him, shave his head, and smear his head with saffron.”"],[7599,"“And for a girl, one sheep. It is cut into joints, and no bone of it is broken. He eats, feeds others, and gives charity. Let that be on the seventh day; if not, then on the fourteenth; if not, then on the twenty-first.”"],[7600,"A boy was born to me, and I was given the good news while I was with the Prophet ﷺ. I said, “I wish that in his place you had a bowl of bread and meat.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “If you say that, indeed they are a cause of miserliness, cowardice, and grief, and indeed they are the fruit of the hearts and the coolness of the eyes.”"],[7601,"“Whatever is cut from an animal while it is alive is dead meat.”"],[7602,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about cutting off the humps of camels and the fat tails of sheep. He said, “Whatever is cut from a living animal is dead meat.”"],[7603,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey and passed by a tree containing two chicks of a small red bird. We took them. He said: The small red bird came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ crying out. The Prophet ﷺ said, “Who has distressed this one by taking her chicks?” He said: We said, “We did.” He said, “Return them.”"],[7604,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, we hunt game but find no knife except flint and a split stick.” He said, “Let the blood flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of Allah ﷻ.”"],[7605,"Quraysh said to the Prophet ﷺ, “Supplicate for us that He make al-Safa gold for us, and we will believe in you.” He said, “Will you do that?” They said, “Yes.” So he supplicated, and Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, “Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sends you greetings of peace and says: If you wish, al-Safa will become gold by morning; then whoever disbelieves after that, I will punish him with a punishment with which I do not punish anyone in the worlds. And if you wish, I will open for them the door of repentance and mercy.” He said, “Rather, the door of repentance and mercy.”"],[7606,"“Among a person’s happiness is that his life is long, and Allah grants him the ability to turn back to Him.”"],[7607,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'I am as My servant thinks of Me, so let him think of Me as he wishes.'"],[7608,"Indeed, having good expectations of Allah, the Exalted, is part of the worship of Allah."],[7609,"A good deed is multiplied ten times or I increase it, and an evil deed is one or I forgive it. And if you meet Me with the earth's fill of sins but without associating any partner with Me, I will meet you with its fill of forgiveness."],[7610,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, that He said: 'O My servants, you are those who err by night and day, and I am the One who forgives sins and do not care, so ask forgiveness from Me and I will forgive you. O My servants, all of you are hungry except those whom I have fed, so ask food from Me and I will feed you. O My servants, all of you are naked except those whom I have clothed, so ask clothing from Me and I will clothe you. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were all as pious as the most pious heart of any man among you, that would not increase My dominion in anything. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, were all as wicked as the most wicked heart of any man among you, that would not decrease My dominion in anything. O My servants, if the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, all stood on a single plain and asked of Me, and I gave every person among them what he asked, that would not decrease My dominion in anything, except as the sea decreases when a needle is dipped into it once. O My servants, it is only your deeds that I keep account of for you; so whoever finds good, let him praise Allah, the Exalted, and whoever finds other than that, let him blame none but himself.'"],[7611,"Abu Dharr al-Ghifari urinated while standing up, and his urine splashed onto his legs and feet. A man said to him, \"The urine has touched your legs and feet.\" He did not respond to him until he arrived at the home of a group of people. They offered him water for purification, so he performed ablution and washed his legs and feet. Then he approached the man and asked, \"What did you say?\" The man replied, \"By now, you have already done it.\" Abu Dharr said, \"This is the cure and the remedy for sins, to seek forgiveness from Allah, the Almighty.\""],[7612,"A servant committed a sin, then said: 'My Lord, I have committed a sin, so forgive me.' His Lord said: 'My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives the sin and punishes for it,' so He forgave him. Then he remained as long as Allah willed, then committed another sin and said: 'My Lord, I have committed a sin, so forgive it for me.' His Lord, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'My servant knows that he has a Lord who forgives the sin and punishes for it. I have forgiven My servant, so let him do as he wills.' Then he returned and committed a sin and said: 'My Lord, forgive me my sin.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: 'My servant committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives the sin and punishes for the sin. Do as you will, for I have forgiven you.'"],[7613,"Whoever commits a sin and knows that he has a Lord who, if He wills, will forgive him, and if He wills, will punish him, it is incumbent upon Allah to forgive him."],[7614,"A man travels through a desolate land, and he says while under a tree, with his riding beast upon which is his provision and food. He wakes up and his riding beast has escaped. He climbs a high place and sees nothing, then climbs another high place and sees nothing. He turns and suddenly it is there, dragging its halter. He is not more joyful at it than Allah is at the repentance of His servant when he repents to Him."],[7615,"He said: 'How would you describe the joy of a man whose riding beast has escaped, dragging its reins in a barren land with no food or drink, while his food and drink are on it? He sought it until it became difficult for him, then it passed by the base of a tree and its reins got caught, and he found it hanging there.' We said: 'Severe, O Messenger of Allah.' He said: 'Indeed, by Allah, Allah is more joyful at the repentance of His servant than that man at his riding beast.'"],[7616,"Did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: 'Remorse is repentance'? He said: 'Yes, I heard him say: Remorse is repentance.' Sahih."],[7617,"He is ashamed to narrate a hadith while I am sitting. Ziyad says it from Abdullah b. Mughaffal, who said: I entered with my father upon Abdullah, and my father said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Remorse is repentance.' He said: 'Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Remorse is repentance.'"],[7618,"Abu al-Nadhr al-Faqih and Abu al-Hasan al-Anzi narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Sa'id al-Darimi narrated to us, 'Uthman ibn Salih al-Sahmi narrated to us, 'Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us from Yahya ibn Ayyub from Humaid al-Tawil who said, I said to Anas ibn Malik, \"Did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say, 'Regret is repentance'?\" He said, \"Yes.\"."],[7619,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood after stoning the Aslami and said: 'Avoid this filth which Allah has forbidden. Whoever falls into it, let him conceal himself with the concealment of Allah and repent to Allah, for whoever reveals his page to us, we will enforce upon him the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[7620,"Mu'adh b. Jabal wanted to travel and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, advise me.' He said: 'Worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, give me more.' He said: 'When you do wrong, then do good.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, give me more.' He said: 'Be upright and improve your character.'[1]"],[7621,"\"Every son of Adam is a sinner, and the best of sinners are those who repent.\""],[7622,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Every son of Adam will come on the Day of Resurrection with a sin, except what was from Yaḥyā b. Zakariyyā.\" He said, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lowered his hand to the ground and took a small stick, then said, \"That is because he had nothing of what men have except the like of this stick, and for that Allah named him a master, chaste, and a prophet among the righteous.\""],[7623,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"I never desired anything that the people of ignorance desired except on two occasions, and Allah, the Exalted, protected me from both of them. One night, a young man from the Quraysh tribe and I were pasturing sheep on the highest point of Makkah. I asked him to watch over my flock until I darken my skin with the sun for this night in Makkah, just like young boys darken. He agreed, so I left. When I reached a house near the outskirts of Makkah, I heard singing, the sound of tambourines and flutes. I asked, \"What is this?\" They said, \"Fulana married Fulan, a man from the Quraysh, and they hired musicians for their wedding.\" I became entranced by the singing and the music until my eyes became heavy with sleep, and I slept. The sun woke me up, so I returned. Again, I heard the same thing. Someone said to me what I heard before, and I became entranced by it again until my eyes became heavy with sleep, and I slept. The sun woke me up again, and I returned to my companion. He asked me, \"What did you do?\" I replied, \"I did not do anything.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'By Allah, I never desired evil after that incident. Allah honored me with Prophethood.'\""],[7624,"On the saying of Allah, Mighty and Sublime: {Those who avoid the major sins and immoralities, except the small faults} [al-Najm: 32], he said: \"It is the man who commits an immorality, falls into it, then repents from it.\" He said, he says [rajaz meter]: If You forgive, O Allah, You forgive much; and which servant of Yours does not fall into small faults?"],[7625,"I was with Abu Hurayrah, and I said, \"O Abu Hurayrah, {Those who avoid the major sins and immoralities, except the small faults} [al-Najm: 32]—so what are the small faults?\" He said, \"Everything as long as the kohl stick does not enter the kohl container; when it enters, that is zinā.\""],[7626,"\"If you were not to sin, Allah would bring a people who sin and then forgive them.\""],[7627,"The Prophet (pbuh) said, \"If the people did not commit sins, Allah, the Almighty, would have created a creation that sins, and then He would have forgiven them, for He is the All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\" Narrated by Shahida."],[7628,"\"Son of Adam, if you draw near to Me a handspan, I draw near to you an arm’s length; and if you draw near to Me an arm’s length, I draw near to you a fathom. Son of Adam, if you intend a good deed but do not do it, I record it for you as one good deed; if you do it, I record it for you as ten. If you intend an evil deed but My awe restrains you from it, I record it for you as a good deed; if you do it, I record it as one evil deed.\""],[7629,"\"Whoever remembers Allah within himself, Allah remembers him within Himself; whoever remembers Allah in a gathering, Allah remembers him in a gathering better and more numerous than the gathering in which he remembered Him. Whoever draws near to Allah a handspan, Allah draws near to him an arm’s length; whoever draws near to Allah an arm’s length, Allah draws near to him a fathom; whoever comes to Allah walking, He comes to him at a hurried pace; whoever comes to Allah at a hurried pace, Allah comes to him swiftly.\""],[7630,"\"You shall certainly enter Paradise except one who refuses and flees from Allah as a camel flees.\""],[7631,"Abū Umāmah al-Bāhilī passed by Khālid b. Yazīd b. Muʿāwiyah, who asked him about the gentlest word he had heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'All of you will enter Paradise except one who flees from Allah as a camel flees from its owner.'\" Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in the Talkhīṣ."],[7632,"\"When Allah created the heavens and the earth, He created one hundred mercies, each mercy filling what is between heaven and earth. He distributed one mercy among the creatures: by it the mother shows affection to her child, by it the wild beasts and birds drink water, and by it the creatures show mercy to one another. On the Day of Resurrection, He will restrict it to the God-fearing and add to them ninety-nine more.\""],[7633,"\"Allah has one hundred mercies. He distributed one mercy among the people of this world, sufficient for them until their appointed terms, and He withheld ninety-nine mercies for His friends. On the Day of Resurrection, Allah will take back the mercy He distributed among the people of this world to the ninety-nine and complete one hundred mercies for His friends.\""],[7634,"A Bedouin came, made his camel kneel, hobbled it, then prayed behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said the salām, he went to his camel, untied its hobble, mounted it, and then called out: \"O Allah, have mercy on me and Muḥammad, and do not associate anyone in our mercy.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Do you say he is more astray or his camel? Did you not hear what he said?\" They said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He has restricted the mercy of Allah, which is vast. Allah created one hundred mercies and sent down one mercy by which the creatures show compassion—their jinn, their humans, and their beasts—and with Him are ninety-nine mercies.\""],[7635,"Show mercy to those on the earth, and the One in the heaven will show mercy to you."],[7636,"My intimate friend and chosen one, the occupant of this chamber ﷺ, said: \"Mercy is not removed except from a wretched person.\""],[7637,"\"Allah did not create anything except that He created for it something that overcomes it, and He created His mercy to overcome His wrath.\""],[7638,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: \"Indeed, Jibril ﷺ began stuffing mud into the mouth of Pharaoh, fearing that he would say 'There is no god but Allah' and Allah ﷻ would then have mercy on him.\""],[7639,"To the Prophet ﷺ: \"If you had seen me while I was taking from the mud of the sea and stuffing it into the mouth of Pharaoh.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7640,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in one of his prayers: \"O Allah, call me to account with an easy reckoning.\" When he finished, I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the easy reckoning?\" He said: \"He will look into his record and pardon him for it. Indeed, whoever is scrutinized in the reckoning, O 'A'ishah, will perish on that day. And whatever afflicts the believer, Allah expiates for him, even the thorn that pricks him.\""],[7641,"The Prophet ﷺ came out to us and said, \"My close friend Gabriel came to me in a hurry and said, 'O Muhammad, by the One who sent you with the truth, Allah Almighty has a servant among his servants named Abdullah, who has been worshipping Allah for five hundred years atop a mountain in the sea. The mountain's width and length are thirty cubits, and it is surrounded by a four-thousand-farsakh sea from all sides. Allah, the Exalted, has granted him a pure spring of fresh water as wide as a finger, which collects in the bottom of the mountain. Additionally, there is a pomegranate tree that bears a fresh pomegranate for him every night to sustain him during the day. When the evening falls, he descends and performs ablution. Then he takes one of those pomegranates and eats it before standing for his prayer. He beseeches his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, at the time of his appointed meeting, to take his soul while he is in prostration, and to not let anything corrupt him in the earth. Allah answered his supplication and will resurrect him on the Day of Resurrection while he is still in prostration before Him. The Lord will say to him, 'Enter Paradise, O My servant, by My mercy.' But the servant will say, 'O Lord, rather by my deeds.' The Lord will repeat, 'Enter Paradise, O My servant, by My mercy.' Again, the servant will say, 'O Lord, rather by my deeds.' Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will then address the angels, 'Appraise My servant according to My favors and his deeds.' His vision will extend for five hundred years of worship, and his bodily blessings will remain beyond that. The Lord will then order, 'Take My servant to the Hellfire.' He will be dragged towards it and will cry out to his Lord, 'O Lord, by Your mercy, admit me to Paradise!' The Lord will respond, 'Return him.' He will be placed before his Lord. The Lord will ask him, 'O My servant, who created you when you were nothing?' The servant will answer, 'You, O Lord.' The Lord will ask, 'Was that by My favor or by My mercy?' The servant will answer, 'Rather, by Your mercy, O Lord.' The Lord will ask, 'Who empowered you to worship for five hundred years?' The servant will answer, 'You, O Lord.' The Lord will ask, 'Who placed you on a mountain amidst the waves, brought forth fresh water for you from salty water, and made a pomegranate tree bear a fresh pomegranate for you every night, even though it usually produces only once a year? Did you request that I take your soul in prostration, and did I grant you that?' The servant will answer, 'You, O Lord.' Allah, the Exalted, will declare, 'All of this was by My mercy, and by My mercy I will admit you to Paradise. Enter, My servant, paradise.' Jabriel said, 'O Muhammad, things are only dependent on the mercy of Allah, the Exalted.'\""],[7642,"Whoever says 'There is no god but Allah' enters Paradise, and Paradise becomes guaranteed for him. And whoever says 'Glory be to Allah and praise be to Him' one hundred times, Allah writes for him one thousand and twenty-four good deeds. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, then none of us would perish.\" He said: \"Yes, indeed one of you will come with good deeds which, if placed on a mountain, would weigh it down; then blessings will come and take those away; then the Lord will thereafter extend His mercy.\""],[7643,"“The wise man is the one who takes account of himself and strives for that which is after death. And the helpless man is the one who follows his own whims then indulges in wishful thinking about Allah.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4260)"],[7644,"\"The believer is expiated.\""],[7645,"The good deeds of the servant and his evil deeds will be brought, and some will be set off against others. If a good deed remains, Allah will expand for him in Paradise."],[7646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to him that the Trustworthy Spirit narrated to him: \"Allah the Exalted has decreed that the deeds of the servant will be brought on the Day of Resurrection—his good deeds and his evil deeds—and some will be set off against others. If one good deed remains for him, Allah will expand for him in Paradise as He wills.\" Al-Hakam b. Aban said: I went to Abu Salamah Yazdad and said to him: \"What if the good deed is gone and nothing remains?\" He said: {Those are the ones from whom We accept the best of what they did} [Al-Ahqaf 16] up to His saying {which they were promised} [Al-Ahqaf 16]."],[7647,"\"Some people will wish that they had done more evil deeds.\" They said: \"Why, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Those whose evil deeds Allah will replace with good deeds.\""],[7648,"\"Some people from my community will come with sins like mountains, and Allah will forgive them and place them upon the Jews and the Christians.\""],[7649,"This nation will be gathered into three groups: a group that will enter Paradise without reckoning, a group that will be given an easy reckoning, and a group who will come carrying on their backs sins like towering mountains. Then Allah will ask about them, though He is most knowing of them, saying: 'Who are these?' They will say: 'These are servants from among Your servants.' He will say: 'Cast them off from them and place them upon the Jews and Christians, and admit them into Paradise by My mercy.'"],[7650,"Allah has never known remorse for a sin from a servant except that He forgives him before he seeks forgiveness from Him for it."],[7651,"From Abdullah regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {so that they may return} [al-Rum 41]; he said: 'They repent.'"],[7652,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed punishment.' He said: 'He did not ask him about it.' Then the prayer was commenced, and the Prophet ﷺ prayed. When he finished his prayer, the man said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have incurred a prescribed punishment, so enforce upon me the Book of Allah.' He said: 'Did you pray with us?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'You have been forgiven.'"],[7653,"While I was standing in the market during the governorship of Ziyad, I struck one hand upon the other in amazement. A man from the Ansar, whose father had been a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, said: 'What amazes you, O Abu Burdah?' I said: 'I am amazed at a people whose religion is one, whose prophet is one, whose call is one, whose pilgrimage is one, and whose military campaigns are one, yet some of them consider it lawful to kill others.' He said: 'Do not be amazed, for I heard my father report that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Indeed, my nation is a nation shown mercy; there is no reckoning or punishment upon it in the Hereafter. Its punishment is only in killing, earthquakes, and tribulations.\"'"],[7654,"I was with Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad when the heads of Kharijites were brought. Whenever a head passed before him, he said: 'To the Fire.' Abdullah b. Yazid said to him: 'Do you not know? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The punishment of this nation has been placed in its own hands in its worldly life.\"'"],[7655,"I heard from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a hadith that, had I heard it only once or twice — until he counted seven — but I heard it more than that. He said: 'Al-Kifl was among the Children of Israel and did not refrain from any sin he committed. A woman came to him and he gave her sixty dinars on condition that he have intercourse with her. When he sat from her as a man sits from his wife, she trembled and wept. He said: \"What makes you weep? Were you compelled?\" She said: \"No, but this is an act I have never done, and only need drove me to it.\" He said: \"You would do this and have never done it before?\" Then he got down and said: \"Go, and the dinars are yours.\" Then he said: \"By Allah, al-Kifl will never disobey his Lord again.\" He died that very night, and in the morning it was written on his door: \"Al-Kifl has been forgiven.\"'"],[7656,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And she certainly desired him, and he would have desired her} [Yusuf 24]; he said: 'He sat from her as a man sits from his wife, and it was called out: \"O son of Ya'qub, will you commit adultery and be like a bird whose feathers are plucked, then it flies with no feathers?\"'"],[7657,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was admonishing his companions when three men passed by. One of them came and sat with the Prophet ﷺ; the second went on a little then sat; as for the third, he went on his way. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'As for this one who came and sat with us, he repented and Allah turned to him. As for the one who went on a little then sat, he was shy and Allah was shy of him. As for the one who went on his way, he was self-sufficient and Allah was self-sufficient from him.'"],[7658,"A captive Bedouin was brought to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I repent to Allah, Exalted is He, and I do not repent to Muhammad.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'He has recognized the truth for its people.'"],[7659,"A young man from the sons of the Muhajirun came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ turned away from him, and he repeated that to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times. When he saw that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not seek forgiveness for him, the young man said before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ three times: 'O Allah, forgive me; O Allah, forgive me; O Allah, forgive me, for Your Messenger did not seek forgiveness for me.' When the young man left, Jibril ﷺ descended to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you not seek forgiveness for the young man? For Allah has forgiven him. So catch up with him and inform him that Allah has forgiven him, and tell him to seek forgiveness for you.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ hastened after him until he caught up with him. When he caught up with him, he said: 'O young man, Allah, Exalted is He, has forgiven you, so seek forgiveness for me.' The young man said: 'O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness for Your Messenger; O Allah, I seek Your forgiveness for Your Messenger and Your Prophet, just as You forgave me. Indeed, You are vast in forgiveness and You are the Most Merciful of the merciful.'"],[7660,"Abu al-Hasan Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Isma'il b. Mihran narrated to us; my father narrated to me; Muhammad b. Wahb al-Dimashqi narrated to us; Muhammad b. Shu'ayb b. Sabur narrated to us; Muhammad b. Abi Muslim narrated to us from his father from Ata' b. Abi Rabah from Abu Hurairah, and he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner."],[7661,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Your Lord ﷻ said: 'If My servants were to obey Me, I would give them rain to drink by night and make the sun rise upon them by day, and I would not make them hear the sound of thunder.' He is truthful, but they declared it weak."],[7662,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, one of us commits a sin.\" He said, \"It is written against him.\" He said, \"Then he seeks forgiveness for it and repents?\" He said, \"He is forgiven and it is turned to him.\" He said, \"Then he returns and commits a sin?\" He said, \"It is written against him, and Allah does not grow weary until you grow weary.\""],[7663,"\"Verily Allah, exalted is He, forgives His servant or accepts the repentance of His servant as long as he has not gurgled [with the death rattle].\""],[7664,"\"Verily Allah forgives His servant as long as the veil has not fallen.\" It was said, O Messenger of Allah, and what is the veil? He said, \"That the soul dies while associating partners [with Allah].\""],[7665,"\"Whoever repents to Allah before he dies by a day, Allah accepts from him.\""],[7666,"\"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, there is no person who repents before he dies by a day except that Allah accepts his repentance.\""],[7667,"\"Whoever repents to Allah before his death by a year, Allah turns to him.\""],[7668,"\"Whoever repents before his death by a year, it is turned to him,\" until he said, \"by a month,\" until he said, \"by a week,\" until he said, \"by a day,\" until he said, \"by an hour,\" until he said, \"by a foal's gasp.\" I said, Glory be to Allah, has Allah ﷻ not said {And repentance is not for those who go on doing evil deeds, until when death presents itself to one of them, he says, 'Indeed, I have now repented'} [Al-Nisa', 18]? Then 'Abdullah said, \"I only narrate to you what I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7669,"The prescribed prayer to the prayer that follows it is an expiation for what is between them. He said, then he said after that, \"except for three: associating partners with Allah, breaking of the covenant, and abandoning the Sunnah. As for breaking the covenant, it is that you give an imam your pledge of allegiance, then you turn against him and fight him with your sword. As for abandoning the Sunnah, it is departing from the community.\""],[7670,"Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said during the Farewell Hajj: \"Behold, the friends of Allah are those who establish the five obligatory prayers that have been prescribed upon them, fast during Ramadan and consider their fasting as constantly ongoing, and give their obligatory charity while regarding it as a duty. They also abstain from major sins that Allah has forbidden.\" Then a man asked him, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the major sins?\" He replied, \"They are nine: associating partners with Allah, killing a believer without just cause, fleeing from the battlefield, usurping the property of orphans, consuming interest, falsely accusing chaste women, disobeying to the parents (especially when they are Muslims), and seeking permission to enter and reside in the Haram (the sacred sanctuary) before your permission.\" Then he said, \"A man will not die until he performs these major sins and establishes prayer and pays the mandatory charity. In this case, he shall be among the Prophet ﷺ in a house whose gates are made of gold.\""],[7671,"From Abu Hurayrah, he attributed it to the Prophet ﷺ who said: \"No one who weeps out of fear of Allah ﷻ will enter the Fire until the milk returns to the udder; and dust in the path of Allah ﷻ and the smoke of Hell will never combine in the nostrils of a Muslim.\""],[7672,"\"Whoever remembers Allah and his eyes overflow out of fear of Allah until the ground is struck by his tears, Allah, exalted is He, will not punish him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[7673,"There is no deed of a day except that it is sealed upon it, and no night except that it is sealed upon it. Then, when the servant is prevented from deeds, the recording angels say, \"O our Lord, this is the deed of Your servant before he was prevented from deeds, and You are most knowing of it.\""],[7674,"ʿAbdullāh b. ʿAbbās met ʿAbdullāh b. al-ʿĀs and he asked Ibn ʿAbbās: Which āyah in the Book of Allah is the most hopeful to you? He said: \"Say, \"O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allah.\" (Zumar 39:53). Then he said: But the statement of Ibrāhīm \"Do you not believe? He said, Indeed, but I wanted to satisfy my heart.\" (Baqarah 2:260)"],[7675,"“Paradise has eight gates, seven of which are closed and one gate is open for repentance until the sun rises from its direction.”"],[7676,"Indeed, Satan said, “By Your might, O Lord, I will not cease leading Your servants astray as long as their souls are in their bodies.” So the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said, “By My might and My majesty, I will not cease forgiving them as long as they seek My forgiveness.”"],[7677,"On the authority of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ who said: “Every word the son of Adam utters is recorded against him. If he commits a sin and wishes to repent to Allah ﷻ, let him go to his companion, stretch out his hands to Allah ﷻ, then say: ‘O Allah, I repent to You from it and will never return to it again,’ for it will be forgiven him as long as he does not return to that deed.”"],[7678,"Ubadah — meaning Ibn Qurt — said: “Indeed, today you perform deeds which in your eyes are finer than a hair, but which we used to count among the destructive sins during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said: So I said to Abu Qatadah, “How would it be if he had lived to see this time of ours?” He said, “That is exactly what I say.”"],[7679,"“There is no Muslim who commits a sin except that the angel entrusted with recording his sins waits for three hours. If he seeks Allah’s forgiveness for that sin within any of those hours, it will not be recorded against him, nor will he be punished on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[7680,"Indeed, Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: “Whoever among you knows that I have power to forgive sins, I will forgive him and will not care, as long as he does not associate anything with Me.”"],[7681,"The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone continually asks pardon, Allah will appoint for him a way out of every distress, and a relief from every anxiety, and will provide for him from where he did not reckon. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 1518)"],[7682,"“Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah is too just to double the punishment for His servant. And whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah conceals it, Allah is too generous to revisit anything He has already pardoned.”"],[7683,"“No parent has given a child a gift better than good manners.”"],[7684,"“By Allah, for one of you to discipline his child is better for him than to give half a sāʿ in charity every day.”"],[7685,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When Allah ﷻ created Adam and breathed the soul into him, he sneezed and said, ‘Praise be to Allah,’ and he praised Allah by Allah’s permission. Then his Lord said to him, ‘May Allah have mercy on you, O Adam.’”"],[7686,"When the soul was breathed into Adam and it reached his nostrils, he sneezed and said, “Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds.” Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said, “May Allah have mercy on you.”"],[7687,"Indeed, Allah the Exalted loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. So if one of you sneezes and says, ‘Praise be to Allah,’ then it is a duty upon everyone who hears him to respond, saying, ‘May Allah have mercy on you.’ And yawning is from Satan, so if one of you yawns, let him suppress it as much as he can, for when one of you yawns and says ‘Hah,’ Satan laughs at him."],[7688,"When one of you sneezes, let him place his two palms over his face and lower his voice."],[7689,"A Muslim owes another Muslim four courtesies: he should answer him when he calls him, visit him when he is ill, invoke mercy on him when he sneezes, and follow his funeral procession when he dies."],[7690,"Allah, the Exalted, loves sneezing. When one of you sneezes, every person who hears him must say, “May Allah have mercy on you.”"],[7691,"Sneezing is from Allah and yawning is from Satan. When one of you sneezes, every person who hears him must say, “May Allah have mercy on you.”"],[7692,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade people from sitting in the courtyards of elevated pathways. They said, “We cannot help it and we cannot endure that, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “If you must, then give them their due.” They said, “What is their due, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “Returning the greeting, invoking mercy on the sneezer when he praises Allah, lowering the gaze, and guiding the way.”"],[7693,"Two men sat with the Prophet ﷺ, one of whom was nobler than the other. The noble one sneezed but did not praise Allah, so the Prophet ﷺ did not invoke mercy on him. Then the other sneezed and praised Allah, so the Prophet ﷺ invoked mercy on him. The noble one said, “I sneezed and you did not invoke mercy on me, but this one sneezed and you invoked mercy on him.” He said, “You forgot Allah, so I forgot you; this one remembered Allah, so I remembered him.” Its chain is authentic but they did not include it. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in Al-Talkhis."],[7694,"I witnessed Abu Musa while he was in the house of Umm al-Fadl. She sneezed, so I invoked mercy on her, and I sneezed, but he did not invoke mercy on me. When I came to my mother and told her, when Abu Musa came to her, she said to him, “My son sneezed in your presence and you did not invoke mercy on him, while a woman sneezed and you invoked mercy on her.” He said, “Your son sneezed and did not praise Allah, so I did not invoke mercy on him, but she sneezed and praised Allah, so I invoked mercy on her. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, ‘When one of you sneezes and praises Allah, invoke mercy on him; but if he does not praise Allah, do not invoke mercy on him.’” She said, “You have done well, you have done well.”"],[7695,"Praise be to Allah and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah. Ibn Umar said, “I also say, ‘Praise be to Allah and peace be upon the Messenger of Allah,’ but this is not how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught us. When one of us sneezes, he should say, ‘Praise be to Allah in every circumstance.’”"],[7696,"The sneezer says, “Praise be to Allah in every circumstance,” and the one who invokes mercy on him says, “May Allah have mercy on you,” and he replies, “May Allah guide you and set your affairs right.”"],[7697,"When one of you sneezes, he should say, “Praise be to Allah in every circumstance,” and they should say to him, “May Allah have mercy on you,” and he should say, “May Allah guide you and set your affairs right.”"],[7698,"When one of you sneezes, he should say, “Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,” and it should be said to him, “May Allah have mercy on you,” and he should say, “May Allah forgive us and you.”"],[7699,"When one of you sneezes, he should say, “Praise be to Allah,” and it should be said to him, “May Allah have mercy on you.” When it is said to him, “May Allah have mercy on you,” he should say, “May Allah forgive us and you.”"],[7700,"We were with Salim b. Ubayd on a journey, and a man sneezed and said, \"Peace be upon you.\" He said, \"Peace be upon you and upon your mother.\" Then he was asked, and he said, \"Perhaps you found something objectionable in that.\" He said, \"I do not like that you mention my mother.\" Salim said, \"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and a man sneezed and said, \"Peace be upon you.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Peace be upon you and upon your mother.\" Then he said, \"When one of you sneezes, let him say, 'Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds,' or 'Praise be to Allah in every situation,' and let it be said to him, 'May Allah have mercy on you,' and let him say, 'May Allah forgive me and you.'\""],[7701,"We were with Salim b. Ubayd on a journey, and he mentioned the hadith in full, similar to the hadith of al-Thawri. \"It was narrated by Jarir b. Abd al-Hamid from Mansur based on a misunderstanding, as he omitted the unknown man of al-Nakha'i between Hilal b. Yasaf and Salim b. Ubayd.\""],[7702,"Salim: \"Peace be upon you and upon your mother.\" Then he said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'When one of you sneezes, let him praise Allah, and let those with him say, \"May Allah have mercy on you,\" and let him reply to them, \"May Allah forgive us and you.\"'\" The error in this narration of Jarir is apparent, for Hilal b. Yasaf did not meet Salim b. Ubayd nor see him, and between them is an unknown man. As for the wording that some jurists, who do not distinguish between sound and weak reports, have adopted regarding the Prophet's ﷺ instruction to the sneezer to say to the one who responds, \"May Allah guide you and set your affairs right,\" it leads one to suppose that this response is for the People of the Book rather than Muslims."],[7703,"The Jews used to sneeze in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ hoping that he would say to them, \"May Allah have mercy on you,\" and he used to say to them, \"May Allah guide you and set your affairs right.\""],[7704,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O Ali, ask Allah for guidance and right direction, and remember by guidance your guidance on the path, and by right direction your aiming of the arrow.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ commanded his son al-Hasan b. Ali, the master of the youth of Paradise, the like of what he commanded his father. The hadith of Yazid b. Abi Maryam, from Abu al-Jawza', from al-Hasan b. Ali regarding the supplication of qunut which the Prophet ﷺ taught: \"O Allah, guide me among those You have guided,\" is too well-known for its chain and routes to be mentioned. We have returned to the sound reports on etiquette that the two imams did not include. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7705,"He forbade a man placing one of his legs over the other while lying down."],[7706,"He forbade wrapping oneself in the samma' (a manner of wearing a garment with no opening for the hands) and that a man raise one of his legs over the other while lying on his back."],[7707,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he was leaning on the fleshy part of his hand behind his back, and he said, \"You sit like those upon whom is wrath.\""],[7708,"\"The best of gatherings is the most spacious of them.\""],[7709,"Abu Sa'id al-Khudri was informed of a funeral among his people, so he came and the people had already taken their seats. When they saw him, they rose to make room for him, but he sat in a corner and said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The best of gatherings is the most spacious of them.'\""],[7710,"I met Umar b. Abd al-Aziz in Madinah in his youth, his beauty, and his freshness. He said, \"When he became caliph, I came to him and sought permission to enter, and he permitted me. I began to stare at him, and he said to me, 'O Ibn Ka'b, why do I see you staring?' I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, because of what I see of the change in your color, the emaciation of your body, and the scattering of your hair.' He said, 'O Ibn Ka'b, how would it be if you saw me after three days in my grave, when the ants have extracted my eyeballs and they have flowed down my cheeks, and my nostrils and mouth have gushed with pus? You would be even more disapproving of me. Leave that; repeat to me the hadith of Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said, 'Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Everything has an honor, and the most honorable gathering is that which faces the qiblah. You sit together in trust. Kill the snake and the scorpion even if you are in prayer. Do not plaster your walls. None of you should look into his brother's book except with his permission. And none of you should pray behind a sleeping person or one who is ritually impure.\"' The hadith is invalid."],[7711,"\"And whoever looks into his brother's book without his permission, it is as if he looks into the Fire. Whoever wishes to be the strongest of people, let him rely upon Allah. Whoever wishes to be the most honorable of people, let him fear Allah ﷻ. Whoever wishes to be the richest of people, let him be more trusting of what is in Allah's hand than what is in his own hand.\" And he said, \"Shall I inform you of something worse than this?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"One who does not overlook a stumble, does not accept an excuse, and does not forgive a sin. Shall I inform you of something worse than this?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"One from whom no good is hoped and whose evil is not safe. Jesus son of Mary, may Allah's blessings and ﷺ , stood among the Children of Israel and said, 'O Children of Israel, do not speak wisdom before the ignorant, lest you wrong it, and do not withhold it from its people, lest you wrong them. Do not wrong a wrongdoer, and do not requite a wrongdoer, lest your virtue be nullified before your Lord. O Children of Israel, matters are three: a matter whose error is clear, so avoid it; a matter about which there is disagreement, so refer it to Allah ﷻ.'\""],[7712,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us while we were in the Suffa after Maghrib. He said, “O so-and-so, go with so-and-so,” and “O so-and-so, go with so-and-so,” until I remained among five, I being the fifth of them. He said, “Come with me.” We did so, and we entered upon Aisha, and that was before the hijab was revealed. He said, “O Aisha, feed us.” She brought a small dish of herbs. Then he said, “O Aisha, feed us.” She brought a small amount of hais, like the size of a small bird. Then he said, “O Aisha, give us something to drink.” She brought a large wooden bowl. Then he said, “If you wish, you may sleep with us, or if you wish, you may go to the mosque and sleep there.” He said: So we slept in the mosque. Then the Prophet ﷺ came to me at the end of the night and found me sleeping on my stomach. He nudged me with his foot and said, “What is it with you and this sleep? This is a sleep that Allah dislikes or detests.”"],[7713,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by a man lying on his stomach and struck him with his foot, saying, “It is a position of lying that Allah, may He be exalted, does not love.”"],[7714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a man to sit between the sun and the shade."],[7715,"The Prophet ﷺ saw me while I was sitting in the sun and said, “Move to the shade, for it is blessed.”"],[7716,"The Prophet ﷺ saw my father while he was sitting in the sun and said, “Move to the shade, for it is blessed.”"],[7717,"From Abu Abdullah, the freed slave of Abu Musa al-Ashari, from Sa’id b. Abi al-Hasan, who said: We were in a house for a testimony when Abu Bakrah entered upon us. A man stood up from his seat for him, and Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A man should not make another man rise from his seat and then sit in it, and do not wipe your hand with the garment of one you do not own.” The two shaykhs agreed on the hadith about standing, but they did not include the hadith about the garment, and its chain is authentic. Sahih."],[7718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two sitting places and two types of dress. As for the two sitting places: between the shade and the sun, and the other sitting is to sit wrapped in a garment that exposes your private parts. As for the two types of dress: one of them is to pray in a garment without covering your shoulders with it, and the other is to pray in trousers without a cloak on you."],[7719,"“I have not seen anyone more similar in manner, demeanor, and guidance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than Fatima bt. the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in her standing and sitting.” She said: “When she entered upon the Prophet ﷺ, he would stand for her, kiss her, and seat her in his place. And when the Prophet ﷺ entered upon her, she would stand from her place, kiss him, and seat him in her place.” On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[7720,"When he spoke a word, he would repeat it three times so that it would be understood from him."],[7721,"He wrote to the Prophet ﷺ and began with himself."],[7722,"Do you count the names of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Jubayr b. Mut’im used to enumerate? He said: Yes, they are six: Muhammad, Ahmad, Khatam, Hashir, Aqib, and Mahi. As for Hashir, he is sent with the Hour: “A warner to you before a severe punishment” [Saba 46]. As for Aqib, he is the last of the prophets. As for Mahi, Allah wipes through him the sins of those who follow him."],[7723,"The most beloved of your names to Allah, may He be exalted, are Abdullah and Abdur-Rahman."],[7724,"\"The most beloved of your names to God Almighty are ʿAbd Allāh and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān.\""],[7725,"\"If I live, God willing, I shall forbid that anyone be named Rabāḥ, Aflaḥ, Najīḥ, or Yasār. And if I live, God willing, I shall certainly expel the Jews from the Arabian Peninsula.\""],[7726,"\"If I live, I shall forbid that anyone be named Barakah, Nāfiʿ, or Yasār.\" He died before forbidding it."],[7727,"\"The most contemptible name before God on the Day of Resurrection is a man who calls himself 'King of Kings'—Shāhānshāh.\""],[7728,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"God's wrath is severe upon a man killed by the Messenger of God ﷺ, and God's wrath is severe upon a man who calls himself 'King of Kings.' There is no king but God ﷻ.\""],[7729,"My people, Banū al-Ḥārith b. Kaʿb, sent me as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ. When I came to him, he said to me, \"Welcome! What is your name?\" I said, \"Kathīr.\" He said, \"Rather, you are Bashīr.\""],[7730,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say on the day of the Conquest: \"No Qurayshī shall be put to death by execution after this day until the Day of Resurrection.\" He said, \"No one among the disobedient Quraysh embraced Islam except my father.\" He said, \"His name was al-ʿĀṣ, so the Messenger of God ﷺ named him Muṭīʿ.\""],[7731,"He was present with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Ḥunayn. He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Ghurāb.\" He said, \"Your name is Muslim.\""],[7732,"His grandfather named his father ʿUzayz. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he named him ʿAbd al-Raḥmān. Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it. Sahih."],[7733,"He was called Aṣram. He was among the group who came to the Prophet ﷺ. He brought a black slave boy of his whom he had bought in that land and said, \"O Messenger of God, I bought this boy and I would like you to name him and pray for blessing for him.\" He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Aṣram.\" He said, \"You are Zurʿah. What do you want?\" He said, \"A name for this boy.\" He said, \"He is ʿĀṣim,\" and he closed his hand."],[7734,"\"Who will drive these camels of ours?\" A man stood up and said, \"I will.\" He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"So-and-so.\" He said, \"Sit down.\" Then another stood up and said, \"I will.\" He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"So-and-so.\" He said, \"Sit down.\" Then another stood up and said, \"I will.\" He said, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Nājiyah.\" He said, \"You are suited for it, so drive them.\""],[7735,"My name during the Pre-Islamic era was Abd Amr, then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named me Abd al-Rahman."],[7736,"The Prophet ﷺ said to a man, \"What is your name?\" He said, \"Shihāb.\" He said, \"You are Hishām.\""],[7737,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said: \"What is your name?\" I said: \"Shihab.\" He said: \"Rather, you are Hisham.\""],[7738,"\"He named his eldest son after his uncle, Hamza, and he named Hussain after his uncle, Jafar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Ali and said, 'I have been commanded to change the names of these two.' Allah and His Messenger know best, so he named them Hasan and Hussain.\""],[7739,"that they named him Muhammad, so they brought him to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he said: \"The Ansar have done well. Name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunya, for I have been sent as a divider, distributing between you.\""],[7740,"Yahya b. Muhammad b. Yahya narrated to us, Abu al-Walid narrated to us, they both said: Shu'ba narrated to us from Sulayman, Husayn, Mansur, and Qatadah, who heard Salim b. Abi al-Ja'd reporting from Jabir b. Abdullah from the Prophet ﷺ the like of it, upon the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[7741,"I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if a child is born to me after you—may I name him with your name and give him your kunya?\" He said: \"Yes.\" Ali said: \"This was a concession for me.\""],[7742,"that she said: \"O Messenger of Allah, will you not give me a kunya?\" He said: \"Take a kunya from your son Abdullah b. al-Zubayr.\" So she became known as Umm Abdullah."],[7743,"that he said to Suhayb: \"You are a man, were it not for three traits.\" He said: \"And what are they?\" He said: \"You have taken a kunya while you have no child, you have affiliated yourself with the Arabs while you are a man from the Romans, and in you is extravagance in food.\" He said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, as for your saying that I took a kunya while I have no child, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me the kunya Abu Yahya. As for your saying that I affiliated myself with the Arabs while I am a man from the Romans, I am a man of al-Namir b. Qasit; I was captured from Mosul after I had been a boy who knew my family and lineage. As for your saying that in me is extravagance in food, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The best of you is the one who feeds others.'\""],[7744,"When the Prophet ﷺ besieged al-Ta'if, I let myself down by a pulley. He said: \"How did you manage?\" I said: \"I let myself down by a pulley.\" He said: \"You are Abu Bakra.\""],[7745,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Which of your children is the eldest?\" I said: \"Shurayh.\" He said: \"Then you are Abu Shurayh.\" Qays alone reported this from al-Miqdam, and after it I will mention a hadith reported uniquely by Mujalid b. Sa'id, and neither of them meets the criterion of this book. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7746,"I came to Umar and he said: \"What is your name?\" I said: \"Masruq.\" He said: \"Son of whom?\" I said: \"Son of al-Ajda'.\" He said: \"You are Masruq b. Abd al-Rahman.\""],[7747,"A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah,\" and he said: \"At your service.\""],[7748,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked that anyone should tread on his heels, but rather to his right and left."],[7749,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ similar to it, the hadith of Sulayman b. al-Mughira is sahih according to the condition of Muslim, though they did not include it. Upon the condition of Muslim."],[7750,"that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ departed one day and entered the Masjid, along with Abu Bakr and 'Umar. One was on his right and the other was on his left, and he was holding their hands, and he said: \"This is how we will be resurrected on the Day of Judgement.'\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3669)"],[7751,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prohibited a man from walking between two women. Its chain is authentic, but they did not include it."],[7752,"The Prophet ﷺ prohibited a man from walking between two camels while leading them. Its chain is authentic; Muhammad b. Thabit was deemed weak by al-Nasa'i."],[7753,"We set out with Qatadah, leading him to Anas while we were young boys, and we entered upon him. He said, 'How good this is,' then he spoke words encouraging them to seek knowledge. He said: He narrated to us that day that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The example of a righteous companion is like that of a perfume seller: if he does not give you some of his perfume,' or he said, 'if you do not obtain some of his perfume, some of his fragrance reaches you.'"],[7754,"I heard Anas b. Malik say: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked, it was as if he were leaning forward.' Ibn Abi Maryam said: And Yahya b. Ayyub narrated to us, saying: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to me, saying: I heard Anas b. Malik say: 'When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked, it was as if he were leaning forward.' Ibn Abi Maryam said: And someone other than Ibn Ayyub informed us of the hadith and said: 'As if he were swaying.'"],[7755,"He prohibited cutting a leather strap between two fingers."],[7756,"From Nu'bayh Al-Anazi, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whenever he left his house, we walked in front of him and left behind him for the angels.\"[1]"],[7757,"From Nubayh al-'Anazi, from Jabir b. 'Abd Allah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do not walk in front of me or behind me, for this is the station of the angels.' Jabir said: 'I came running to the Prophet ﷺ as if I were a spark.'"],[7758,"Hudhayfah saw a man sitting in the middle of a circle and said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed whoever sits in the middle of a circle.'"],[7759,"\"In Bani Salamah, it was revealed: 'And do not insult one another with nicknames' (Quran, Al-Hujurat 11). It was said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came and there was not a single person among us who did not have two or three names.' It was said, 'A man would be called and they would say, 'Muh, muh, muh,' indicating that he gets angry at this nickname.' So the verse was revealed: 'And do not insult one another with nicknames' (Quran, Al-Hujurat 11). 'The chain of narration is authentic and they did not exclude it' (Sahih).\""],[7760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us during the illness in which he died, with his head bandaged. He said: I followed him until he ascended the pulpit. He said: Then he said: 'Indeed, at this moment, I am standing at the Hawd.' Then he said: 'Indeed, a servant was offered the world and its adornment, and he chose the Hereafter.' No one among the people understood that except Abu Bakr, who said: 'May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; rather, we ransom you with our own selves, our children, our wealth, and our clients.' He said: Then he descended from the pulpit, and he was not seen until that hour."],[7761,"I heard my father Buraydah say: I was in the mosque while Abu Musa al-Ash'ari was reciting, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and said: 'Who is this?' I said: 'I am Buraydah, may I be made your ransom, O Prophet of Allah.' He said: 'This one has been given one of the flutes of the family of Dawud.'"],[7762,"We were sitting around the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he mentioned tribulation, or it was mentioned in his presence. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'When you see that people's covenants have become corrupted, their trusts have become light, and they are like this'—and he interlaced his fingers. I stood up to him and said: 'What should I do, O Messenger of Allah, may Allah make me your ransom?' He said: 'Stay in your house, control your tongue, accept what you know, abandon what you reject, attend to your own private affairs, and leave aside the affairs of the common people.'"],[7763,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade khadhf (a form of false accusation of adultery).\" A man then engaged in khadhf in front of him, and the Prophet ﷺ said, \"I am telling you about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , and by Allah, I will never speak to you again.\" The two scholars, Sheikhain (referring to the two prominent hadith scholars, Imam al-Bukhari and Imam Muslim), agreed to exclude the hadith of 'Uqbah ibn Suhban from 'Abdullah ibn Mugaffal regarding the prohibition of khadhf, and they did not include it in this context, although its chain of narration is authentic. Similar narrations have been reported from Ibn 'Umar.\""],[7764,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbidding the throwing of pebbles. Then Ibn 'Umar saw him throwing pebbles after that and said: 'I informed you that the Prophet ﷺ forbade the throwing of pebbles, and then you threw pebbles? By Allah, I will never speak to you again.'"],[7765,"She asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, saying: 'I said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted, {And you commit in your assemblies the reprehensible} [Al-'Ankabut 29]—what was that reprehensible act they used to commit?' He said: 'They used to mock the people on the road and throw pebbles at them.'"],[7766,"When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys during the night, seek refuge in Allah from the accursed devil, for they see what you do not see. And reduce going out when it is the time of their emergence, for Allah, Exalted is He, scatters in His night from His creation whatever He wills. And close the doors and mention the name of Allah over them, for the devil does not open a door that has been closed and upon which Allah's name has been mentioned. And tie the mouths of water skins, cover the vessels, and turn over the utensils."],[7767,"Restrain your children when the glow of evening dissipates, for it is an hour in which the devils penetrate."],[7768,"Beware of staying up in conversation after the stillness of the night, for you do not know what Allah may send of His creation."],[7769,"Do not let fire remain in your houses overnight, for it is an enemy. Ibn Umar would not go to sleep until he had left no fire in the house but that he extinguished it, and he was the last of the household to sleep; he would pray, and when he finished, he would not sleep until he extinguished the lamp."],[7770,"A mouse came and began to drag the wick, so the servant girl went to chase it away. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, \"Leave it.\" It came with it and dropped it before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the spot where he was sitting, and it burned from it the size of a dirham. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, \"When you sleep, extinguish your lamps, for the devil guides the like of this to this and it burns you.\""],[7771,"When he saw the new moon, he would say: \"O Allah, let it rise over us with security, faith, safety, and submission. My Lord and your Lord is Allah.\""],[7772,"When the sky rained, he would uncover his garment from his back so that the rain would fall on him. It was said to him, \"Why do you do this?\" He said, \"Indeed it is recently from its Lord, Mighty and Exalted.\""],[7773,"A wind overtook the people on the road to Makkah while Umar ibn al-Khattab was performing Hajj, and it intensified upon them. Umar ibn al-Khattab said to those around him, \"What is the wind?\" They did not answer him. I learned what Umar had asked about, so I urged my mount until I caught up with him and said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, I was informed that you asked about the wind, and I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The wind is from the spirit of Allah, Exalted is He. It brings mercy and it brings punishment, so do not curse it. Ask Allah for its good and seek refuge in Allah from its evil.'\""],[7774,"When the wind blew strongly, he would say: \"O Allah, make it a fertilizing wind, not a barren one.\""],[7775,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to make frequent mention of Khadijah. I said, \"Allah has replaced her for you,\" or perhaps Hammad said, \"Allah has given you in exchange for an old woman among the old women of Quraysh, with reddened cheeks, who perished in a previous age.\" His face changed in a way I only saw at the descent of revelation or when he saw a cloud of thunder and lightning, until he knew whether it was mercy or punishment."],[7776,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ heard thunder and lightning, he would say: \"O Allah, do not kill us with Your anger and do not destroy us with Your punishment, and grant us well-being before that.\""],[7777,"We had dinner with Abu Qatadah on the roof of a house of ours, and a star fell. We followed it with our eyes, and he forbade us and said, \"Do not follow them with your eyes, for we were forbidden from that.\""],[7778,"From ʿAmr b. Mālik al-Janbī, from Faḍālah b. ʿUbayd, from ʿUbādah b. al-Ṣāmit, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out one day upon his riding camel, with his companions before him. Muʿādh b. Jabal said, 'O Prophet of Allah, do you permit me to come up to you with a cheerful soul?' He said, 'Yes.' So Muʿādh drew near to him, and they rode together. Muʿādh said, 'May my father be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah! If only our day could be before your day—tell me, if something happens, and we see nothing, God willing—what deeds should we perform after you?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ fell silent, then said, 'Jihad in the path of Allah.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'What an excellent thing jihad is, but there is something people have more control over than that: fasting and charity.' He said, 'What an excellent thing fasting and charity are.' Then Muʿādh mentioned every good deed that a son of Adam performs, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Returning good to people is better than that.' He said, 'What then, may my father and mother be your ransom—returning good to people is better than that?' He said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pointed to his mouth and said, 'Silence except from good.'' He said, 'Will we be held accountable for what our tongues utter?' He said, 'Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck Muʿādh's thigh and said, 'O Muʿādh, may your mother be bereaved of you—or whatever Allah willed to say to him of that—will people be thrown on their faces into Hell for anything other than what their tongues have uttered? So whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent about evil. Speak good and you will gain; remain silent from evil and you will be safe.'"],[7779,"He forbids a man to be in direct skin contact with another man in a single garment, and a woman with another woman in a single garment."],[7780,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade a woman to be in direct skin contact with another woman, and a man with another man, in a single garment. Ibn Abī Laylā said, 'And I hold that it merits discretionary punishment.' Muḥammad b. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Abī Laylā, from one of the most illustrious households of the Companions among the Anṣār, and a mufti and jurist in Kufa, when he held that it merits discretionary punishment, in that he is an example to be followed."],[7781,"A man should not be in direct skin contact with another man, nor a woman with another woman."],[7782,"‘Avoid a house called the bathhouse.’ They said, 'O Messenger of Allah, it removes dirt and benefits the sick.' He said, 'Whoever enters it, let him cover himself.'"],[7783,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not send his wife to the bathhouse. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not sit at a table upon which wine is passed around."],[7784,"Some women from the people of Syria entered upon ʿĀʾishah. She said, 'Perhaps you are from the district whose women enter the bathhouse. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Any woman who puts down her clothes in other than her husband's house has torn her veil between her and Allah, Mighty and Majestic.' Shuʿbah narrated it from Manṣūr according to the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[7785,"Some women from the people of Syria entered upon ʿĀʾishah, and she said, 'Are you the ones who enter the bathhouses?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'No woman removes her clothes in other than her own house except that she has torn the veil between her and Allah, Mighty and Majestic.' A similar report has been narrated from Umm Salamah from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[7786,"Some women entered upon Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and she asked them, 'Who are you?' They said, 'From the people of Ḥimṣ.' She said, 'From the people of the bathhouses?' They said, 'Is there any harm in it?' She said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'Any woman who removes her clothes in other than her own house, Allah tears away His covering from her.'' Al-Dhahabī remained silent about it in his abridgment."],[7787,"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his neighbor. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. And whoever of your women believes in Allah and the Last Day, let her not enter the bathhouses."],[7788,"He heard Subayʿah al-Aslamiyyah say: Some women from the people of Syria entered upon ʿĀʾishah. ʿĀʾishah said, 'Who are you from?' They said, 'From the people of Ḥimṣ.' She said, 'Companions of the bathhouses?' They said, 'Yes.' ʿĀʾishah said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The bathhouse is forbidden for the women of my Ummah.'' Authentic."],[7789,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a sword be handed over unsheathed."],[7790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by a people who were passing around an unsheathed sword, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"May Allah curse the one who did this. Have I not forbidden this? When one of you draws a sword and looks at it, and then wants to hand it to his brother, let him sheathe it and then hand it to him.\""],[7791,"that his father offered him to the Prophet ﷺ to serve him. He said: “So the Prophet ﷺ passed by me, and I had just performed Salat, so he poked me with his foot and said: ‘Should I not direct you to a gate from the gates of Paradise?’ I said: ‘Of course.’ He ﷺ said: ‘There is no might or power except with Allah (Lā ḥawla wa lā quwwata illā billāh).’” (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3581)[1]"],[7792,"A Jewish boy used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. The boy fell ill, so the Prophet ﷺ came to visit him and said: \"O boy, submit; say: There is no god but Allah.\" The boy began looking at his father, and his father said to him: \"Say what Muhammad ﷺ says to you.\" So he said: \"There is no god but Allah,\" and he submitted, then he died. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to his companions: \"Pray over him,\" and the Prophet ﷺ prayed over him. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7793,"A bearer of good news came to the Prophet ﷺ to give him glad tidings of the victory of some of his cavalry while his head was in ʿA'isha's lap. He stood up and fell prostrating to Allah, the Exalted. When he finished, he began questioning the messenger, who told him, and among what he told him was the affair of the enemy. A woman had been in charge of them, so the Prophet ﷺ said: \"Men are ruined when they obey women.\""],[7794,"Allah protected me through something I heard from the Prophet ﷺ: when he learned that the king of Dhu Yazan had died and they had put a woman in charge of their affairs, the Prophet ﷺ said: \"A people will never succeed if a woman rules over them.\""],[7795,"Jarir b. ʿAbd Allah entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while his companions were with him, and every man was reluctant to give up his seat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took his cloak and threw it to him, and he received it with his chest and face, kissed it, placed it over his eyes, and said: \"May Allah honor you as you have honored me.\" Then he placed it on the back of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: \"Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, when a nobleman of a people comes to him, let him honor him.\""],[7796,"From the one riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: his mount stumbled, so he said: \"May Satan perish.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not say 'May Satan perish,' for if you say 'May Satan perish,' he becomes haughty and says: 'By my strength I brought him down.' But when 'In the name of Allah' is said, he shrinks until he becomes like a fly.\""],[7797,"I was riding behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when our camel stumbled, and I said: \"May Satan perish.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Do not say 'May Satan perish,' for he becomes haughty until he is like a house and grows strong. But say 'In the name of Allah,' for when you say 'In the name of Allah,' he shrinks until he becomes like a fly.\""],[7798,"\"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ walked, he did not turn around.\""],[7799,"\"You name your children Muhammad, then you curse them.\""],[7800,"When he sneezed, he would cover his face with his hand or with his garment and lower his voice.\""],[7801,"\"Sleeping at the beginning of the day is negligence, in its middle is [good] character, and at its end is foolishness.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7802,"He was on a journey, then arrived and hurried to his family at night, and found something sleeping with his wife. He took hold of the sword, but his wife said: \"This is so-and-so; she combed my hair.\" So he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not come to women at night unannounced.\""],[7803,"No one is forbearing except one who has stumbled, and no one is wise except one who has experience."],[7804,"\"He came to Abdur Rahman ibn Ka'b ibn Malik while he was wearing a stripped cloak. He circled around the Ka'ba, dragging himself, as he was blind and being led. I greeted him, and he asked, \"Who is this?\" I replied, \"Abdullah ibn Tha'labah.\" He asked, \"Is he from Banu Harithah?\" I said, \"Yes,\" He asked, \"Is he circumcised?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He asked, \"Did you hear your father narrating a hadith that he heard from the Prophet ﷺ?\" I said, \"I don't know.\" He said, \"Did you hear your father saying that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, 'Whoever wrongfully takes the money of a Muslim by making a false oath, a black dot will be engraved on their heart, which nothing will remove until the Day of Resurrection'?\""],[7805,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever swears an oath in order to seize thereby the property of a man, he will meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him.'"],[7806,"Whoever swears a deliberate, false oath, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7807,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the Hajj between the two jamarat, saying: 'Whoever seizes the property of his Muslim brother with a sinful oath, let him take his seat in the Fire. Let those of you who are present convey to those who are absent.' He said it twice or thrice."],[7808,"Whoever seizes the property of a Muslim man with his oath, Allah has forbidden Paradise to him and will admit him to the Fire.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, even if it is something small?' He said: 'Even if it is a tooth-stick, even if it is a tooth-stick.'"],[7809,"Whoever swears an oath by which he seizes the property of a Muslim man while he is sinful, he will meet Allah with a mutilated limb."],[7810,"He had a dispute with a man before the Prophet ﷺ concerning some land. The oath was imposed on one of them, and the other said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if he swears, I will hand over my land to him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Leave him, for whoever swears a binding oath to seize thereby the property of a Muslim man, he will meet Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection while He is filled with anger against him—may Allah pardon him or punish him.'"],[7811,"There was a dispute between Sa'id b. Zayd and the daughter of Arwa. Marwan said: 'Make peace between these two.' We spoke to him about that until we said: 'This woman has been treated fairly.' He said: 'Do you think I would diminish anything of her right? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever seizes a span of land, Allah Almighty will collar him on the Day of Resurrection with seven earths. And whoever seizes property with his oath, there is no blessing for him in it. And whoever takes charge of a people without their permission, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all the people.\""],[7812,"Among the greatest of major sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, and the false oath (al-yamin al-ghamus). No one swears by Allah a binding oath and includes in it the like of a mosquito's wing except that Allah makes it a black spot in his heart on the Day of Resurrection."],[7813,"We used to count among the sin for which there is no expiation the false oath (al-yamin al-ghamus).' It was said: 'And what is the false oath?' He said: 'A man seizing with his oath the property of another man.'"],[7814,"Whoever swears upon this pulpit of mine a sinful oath, let him take his seat in the Fire—or he said: except that the Fire becomes obligatory for him—even if it be for a green tooth-stick."],[7815,"Whoever swears upon this pulpit of mine a sinful oath, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[7816,"No servant, male or female, swears at this pulpit a false oath, even about a fresh toothstick, except that the Fire becomes incumbent for him."],[7817,"Allah permitted me to speak of a rooster whose legs are on the earth and whose neck is folded beneath the Throne, and it says: Glory be to You, how great is our Lord. He ﷺ said: \"And He replies to it: None who swears by Me falsely knows that.\""],[7818,"Ibn Umar heard a man swearing: No, I swear by the Ka'bah. Ibn Umar said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: He who swears by anyone but Allah is polytheist. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3251)"],[7819,"From Qutaylah bt. Sayfi, a woman of Juhaynah, who said: A Jewish scholar came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: You associate partners, saying: What Allah wills and you will; and you say: By the Ka'bah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Say: What Allah wills, then you will; and say: By the Lord of the Ka'bah.\""],[7820,"He is not one of us who swears by al-Amanah (trustworthiness), and he is not one of us who corrupts a man's wife or his slave."],[7821,"Whoever swears an oath, then it is as he swore: if he says he is a Jew, then he is a Jew; if he says he is a Christian, then he is a Christian; if he says he is free of Islam, then he is free of Islam. And whoever makes a claim of the pre-Islamic ignorance, he is from the crouchers of Hell.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if he fasts and prays? He said: \"Even if he fasts and prays.\""],[7822,"Whoever says: I am free of Islam, then if he is lying, he is as he said; and if he is truthful, he will never return to Islam safely."],[7823,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, some people of Quraysh came to him and said: Some of our freedmen and slaves have joined you, having no desire in the religion except to flee from our livestock and our crops. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"By Allah, O company of Quraysh, you will establish the prayer and give the zakah, or I will send against you a man who will strike your necks for the religion.\" Then he said: \"I, or the one who patches the sandal.\" Ali said: \"And I patch the sandal of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" According to the condition of Muslim."],[7824,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting with his companions narrating to them, he got up and entered. Zayd got up and sat in the Prophet's ﷺ place and began to narrate to them on behalf of the Prophet ﷺ. Meanwhile, some meat was passed by as a gift to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The people said to Zayd, and he was the youngest of them: O Abu Sa'id, if you would go to the Prophet ﷺ and convey our greetings to him and tell him: Your companions say: If you see fit to send us some of this meat. He said: \"Return to them, for they have eaten meat after you.\" Zayd came and said: I conveyed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Return to them, for they have eaten meat after you.\" The people said: We have not eaten meat, and this matter is new. Come with us to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him what this is. They came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we sent to you regarding the meat that came to you, and Zayd claimed that they have eaten meat. By Allah, we have not eaten meat. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is as if I am looking at the greenness of Zayd's meat in your teeth.\" They said: O Messenger of Allah, seek forgiveness for us. He said: And he sought forgiveness for them."],[7825,"We set out intending to go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with us was Wa'il b. Hujr. An enemy of his captured him, and the people were reluctant to swear, but I swore that he was my brother, so he was released. We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I informed him that the people were reluctant and I swore that he was my brother. He said: \"You have spoken truthfully; the Muslim is the brother of the Muslim.\""],[7826,"Whoever divorces what he does not own, there is no divorce for him; whoever frees what he does not own, there is no manumission for him; whoever vows regarding what he does not own, there is no vow for him; whoever swears an oath to commit a sin, there is no oath for him; and whoever swears an oath to sever kinship ties, there is no oath for him."],[7827,"Two brothers from the Ansar had an inheritance between them. One of them asked his companion for division, and he said: If you return to ask me for division, I will never speak to you again, and all my wealth is in the gate of the Ka'bah. Umar b. al-Khattab said: The Ka'bah is in no need of your wealth. Make expiation for your oath and speak to your brother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"There is no oath upon you and no vow in disobedience to the Lord, nor in severing kinship ties, nor in what you do not own.\""],[7828,"A man came to Adi b. Hatim and said: I have married a woman, so give me. He said: I will write for you a coat of mail and a helmet, and you will be given them. The man became displeased, so Adi swore that he would not give them to him. The man said: I had hoped you would give me a servant boy. He said: By Allah, they are dearer to me than two servant boys. The man said: Then write them for me. Adi said: Have I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"When one of you swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do that which is better.\" I have not written them for you. He said: Then he wrote them for him."],[7829,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ, he said: “Allah granted His Messenger camels as spoils, so he distributed them.” Abu Musa al-Ash'ari said, “O Messenger of Allah, give me a mount.” He said, “No.” He asked him three times, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I will not do it.” He said, “There remained four with white blazes on their humps.” He said, “O Abu Musa, take them.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, I feel ashamed. I asked you and you refused me, and you swore an oath, and I feared that some doubt had entered the mind of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “When I swear an oath and then see that something else is better, I expiate my oath and do what is better.”"],[7830,"Whenever the Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore an oath, he would not break it until Allah Almighty revealed the expiation for oaths, whereupon he said: “I do not swear an oath and then see something better than it without expiating my oath and then doing what is better.”"],[7831,"“Whoever persists in an oath concerning his family is more sinful.”"],[7832,"“When one of you persists in an oath concerning his family, it is more sinful in the sight of Allah than the expiation he has been commanded to give.”"],[7833,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “My sister has sworn to walk to the House, but walking is difficult for her.” He said, “Tell her to ride if she cannot walk. Allah has no need for your sister to suffer hardship.”"],[7834,"Regarding a man who swears to walk and then becomes unable and rides, Ibn Abbas said: “He should perform Hajj the following year, riding the distance he walked and walking the distance he rode.”"],[7835,"Some meat was given to me as a gift, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to send some of it to Zaynab. I sent it to her, but she returned it. He said, “Give her more.” I gave her more, but she returned it. He said, “I adjure you, will you not give her more?” I gave her more, but she returned it. Jealousy entered me, and I said, “She has humiliated you.” He said, “You and she are too insignificant in the sight of Allah for Him to humiliate me through any of you. I swear I will not enter upon you for a month.” He stayed away from us for twenty-nine days, then entered upon us on the evening of the thirtieth. She said, “You swore not to enter for a month.” He said, “A month is like this, and a month is like this,” and he spread his hands apart, and in the third he held back his thumb."],[7836,"Whoever swears an oath and then says, “If Allah wills,” has his exception."],[7837,"“When a man swears an oath, he may make an exception even up to a year.” This verse was revealed concerning this: {And remember your Lord when you forget} [Al-Kahf 24]. He said: “When he remembers, he makes the exception.” Ali b. Mushir said: “Al-A'mash used to act upon it.”"],[7838,"“Your oath is according to what your companion believes you by.”"],[7839,"“Swearing is either a sin or regret.”"],[7840,"“An oath is only a sin or a regret.”"],[7841,"That he heard 'Abd Allah b. 'Umar when a man from Banu Ka'b called Mas'ud b. 'Amr asked him: O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, my son was in the land of Persia among those with 'Umar b. 'Ubayd Allah, and a severe plague struck al-Basrah. When that reached me, I vowed that if Allah brought my son back, I would walk to the Ka'bah. He returned sick and died. What do you think? Ibn 'Umar said: Were you not forbidden from vows? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A vow does not bring anything forward or delay it; it only extracts something from the miser.\" Fulfill your vow."],[7842,"“A vow does not bring near to the son of Adam anything that Allah, Exalted is He, had not decreed for him, but the vow coincides with destiny, and thereby is extracted from the miser what the miser did not want to give.”"],[7843,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about that, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: “Pray here,” meaning in the Sacred Mosque. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I only vowed to pray in Jerusalem. He said: “Pray here.”"],[7844,"“There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.”"],[7845,"“There is no vow in disobedience, and its expiation is the expiation of an oath.”"],[7846,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There is no vow in disobedience.\" The man who did not mention him (Muhammad) but mentioned Yahiya is Muhammad ibn Zubeir without a doubt. He intended to say from the tribe of Hanzalah, but he said from the tribe of Hanifa. As for his statement ﷺ , \"There is no vow in disobedience,\" it is agreed upon by the two sheikhs (referring to Bukhari and Muslim) and the narrations support the authenticity on Muhammad ibn Zubeir al-Hanzali, and it is not correct."],[7848,"From 'Imran b. Husayn ؓ"],[7849,"That he said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he sent him to Yemen: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: “Make your religion sincere, and a little deed will suffice you.”"],[7850,"Two blessings which many people squander: health and free time."],[7851,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man while advising him, \"Take advantage of five before five: your youth before your old age, your health before your illness, your wealth before your poverty, your free time before your busyness, and your life before your death.\""],[7852,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by Dhu al-Hulayfah and saw a sheep lifting its leg. He said: “Do you consider this sheep insignificant to its owner?” They said: Yes. He said: “By Him in whose hand is my soul, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to its owner. If the world weighed as much as a mosquito's wing with Allah, He would not give a disbeliever a drink of water from it.”"],[7853,"I entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he had a fever. I placed my hand over the blanket and felt the heat of the fever. I said: How severe your fever is, O Messenger of Allah. He said: “Thus it is with us prophets: pain is multiplied for us so that reward is multiplied for us.” I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most severely tried? He said: “The prophets.” I said: Then who? He said: “Then the righteous. A man would be tried with poverty until he found nothing but a cloak, and he would wrap himself in it and wear it. One of them would be tried with lice until the lice killed him, and that was dearer to them than what is given to you.”"],[7854,"“Indeed, nothing remains of this world except the like of a fly buzzing in its air. So fear Allah, fear Allah regarding your brothers among the people of the graves, for your deeds are presented to them.”"],[7855,"“The heart of the son of Adam is like a sparrow; it turns over seven times a day.”"],[7856,"\"Whoever fears traveling at night - and whoever travels at night reaches his destination - Allah provides him with the most precious of goods, and indeed Allah's goods are but Paradise.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2450)"],[7857,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever fears Adlaj, and whoever reaches Adlaj has indeed reached the destination. Know that the merchandise of Allah is precious, and the merchandise of Allah is Paradise. The rumbling will follow it, and then the pebbles will follow it. Death has come with whatever it contains.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary."],[7858,"Whoever loves his worldly life harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his worldly life. So prefer what remains over what perishes."],[7859,"A man said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about these illnesses that afflict us? What reward do we have for them?' He said, 'They are expiations.' Ubayy b. Ka'b said, 'O Messenger of Allah, even if they are minor?' He said, 'Even a thorn or anything above that.' He said, 'Then Ubayy supplicated against himself that fever would not leave him until he died, so long as it did not distract him from Hajj, 'Umrah, jihad in the cause of Allah, or the prescribed prayer in congregation.' He said, 'After that, no man touched his skin except that he felt its heat until he died.'"],[7860,"There is no day's deed except that it is sealed. When a believer falls ill, the angels say, 'Our Lord, Your servant so-and-so, You have detained him.' The Lord Almighty says, 'Seal for him the like of his deeds until he recovers or dies.'"],[7861,"We were with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq when he called for a drink. He was brought water and honey. When he brought it close to his mouth, he wept and wept until he made his companions weep. They fell silent, but he did not fall silent. Then he resumed weeping until they thought they would not be able to ask him. He said, 'Then he wiped his eyes.' They said, 'O successor of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, what made you weep?' He said, 'I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I saw him pushing something away from himself, and I saw no one with him. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what are you pushing away from yourself?' He said, 'This world was presented to me, and I said to it, 'Away from me!' Then it returned and said, 'If you escape me, no one after you will escape me.'"],[7862,"When Allah loves a servant, He protects him from the world just as one of you protects his sick person from water."],[7863,"'Umar b. al-Khattab entered upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a mat that had left marks on his side. He said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would take a bed softer than this.' He said, 'What do I have to do with the world? What does the world have to do with me? By the One in whose hand is my soul, my likeness and the likeness of this world is only that of a rider who traveled on a hot day, shaded himself under a tree for an hour of the day, then departed and left it.'"],[7864,"What do I have to do with the world? My likeness and the likeness of the world is only that of a rider who rested under a tree on a hot day, then departed and left it."],[7865,"Whoever seeks what is with Allah, the sky will be his shade and the earth his bed. He will not be concerned with anything of worldly matters. He does not sow crops, yet he eats bread. He does not plant trees, yet he eats fruits, trusting in Allah Almighty and seeking His pleasure. Allah has guaranteed the seven heavens and the seven earths his provision. They toil in it and bring it lawfully, while he receives his provision in full without reckoning before Allah Almighty until certainty comes to him."],[7866,"When Abu Malik al-Ash'ari was on his deathbed, he said, 'O assembly of Ash'aris, let the present among you inform the absent that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The sweetness of the world is the bitterness of the Hereafter, and the bitterness of the world is the sweetness of the Hereafter.'"],[7867,"Give glad tidings to this nation of eminence, elevation, victory, and empowerment in the land. Whoever among them performs a deed of the Hereafter for the sake of the world will have no share in the Hereafter."],[7868,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited, 'Whomever Allah wills to guide, He opens his chest to Islam' [al-An'am 125], then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'When light enters the chest, it expands.' It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, is there a sign by which that is known?' He said, 'Yes: withdrawal from the abode of delusion, turning to the abode of eternity, and preparing for death before it descends.' 'Adi b. al-Fadl is unreliable."],[7869,"Four things only occur with wonder: silence, which is the first act of worship; humility; remembrance of Allah Almighty; and paucity of possessions."],[7871,"When a man says to the hypocrite, “O master,” he has angered his Lord, Blessed and Exalted."],[7872,"The son of Adam has no right except in these traits: a house to shelter him, a garment to cover his private parts, and a crust of bread and water."],[7873,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “O Aisha, if you wish to join me, let what suffices you of this world be like the provision of a rider: do not replace a garment until you patch it, and beware of sitting with the rich.”"],[7874,"“O Tariq, prepare for death before death descends.”"],[7875,"“Reduce your visits to the rich, for it is likely that you will not disdain the blessings of Allah ﷻ.”"],[7876,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How excellent is this world as an abode for the one who takes provision from it for his Hereafter until he pleases his Lord ﷻ. And how evil is this abode for the one whom it distracts from his Hereafter and falls short of pleasing his Lord. When a servant says, ‘May Allah make the world ugly,’ the world says, ‘May Allah make ugly the one who disobeys his Lord.’”"],[7877,"When a servant falls ill, Allah reveals to His angels: “O My angels, I have bound My servant with one of My bonds. If I take his soul, I will forgive him; and if I restore him to health, then he will sit with no sin upon him.”"],[7878,"“Whoever dies upon something, Allah will resurrect him upon it.”"],[7879,"The Prophet ﷺ admonished a man and said: “Be abstinent in this world and Allah ﷻ will love you, and be abstinent in what people possess and people will love you.”"],[7880,"I said, “O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a matter I can hold fast to.” He said, “Say, ‘My Lord is Allah,’ then remain steadfast.” He said, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you fear most for me?” He took hold of his own tongue and said, “This.”"],[7881,"“The glance is a poisoned arrow from the arrows of Iblis. Whoever abandons it out of fear of Allah, He, Mighty and Majestic, will reward him with faith whose sweetness he will find in his heart.”"],[7882,"Four traits, if they are in you, will not harm you for what you miss of this world: keeping trusts, truthful speech, good character, and moderation in eating."],[7883,"If a man were to perform a deed inside a rock with no door and no opening, his deed would still come out to the people, whatever it may be."],[7884,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah tries each one of you with balāʾ (tribulations) while He is well aware of him. [He tries him] just like one of you [purifies] his gold with fire.And from among them are (1) those who come out like the gold of Ibrīz (pure gold) and are the ones whom Allah ﷻ has saved from evil deeds; and (2) from among them is the one who comes out like gold of lesser quality and such is the one whole was [taken] by some doubts, and (3) from among them is the one who comes out like blackened gold, and such is the one who has [experienced] fitnah.\"[1]"],[7885,"Calamity continues to afflict the believer in his body and his wealth until he meets Allah Almighty with no sin upon him."],[7886,"Abdullah said: \"You pray more and fast more than the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, yet they were better than you.\" They said, \"Why?\" He said, \"They were more abstinent from this world than you, and more desirous of the Hereafter than you.\""],[7887,"He informed him that he heard Amr b. al-As saying on the pulpit: \"By Allah, I have never seen any people more desirous of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was abstinent from than you. You desire this world, while he was abstinent from it. By Allah, no three days of time passed for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except that what he owed was more than what he possessed.\""],[7888,"The world is the believer's prison and his place of hardship. When he departs from the world, he leaves behind the prison and the hardship."],[7889,"In the last age there will be ignorant worshippers and sinful reciters."],[7890,"Indeed, Allah loves every sorrowful heart."],[7891,"Wretched is the servant who is conceited and boastful and forgets the Most Great, the Most High. Wretched is the servant who is heedless and distracted and forgets the beginning and the end. Wretched is the servant who transgresses and is insolent and forgets the graves and the trials. Wretched is the servant who deceives in worldly matters at the expense of religion. Wretched is the servant who deceives in religion through doubtful matters. Wretched is the servant whom fear turns away from the truth. Wretched is the servant whom greed leads. Wretched is the servant whom desire misleads."],[7892,"You will certainly be sifted as dates are sifted from the basket, so the best of you will depart and the worst of you will remain. So die if you can."],[7893,"\"O Bilal, meet Allah poor and do not meet Him rich.\" He said, \"I said, 'How can I do that, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ?' He said, 'When you are given provision, do not hoard it; and when you are asked, do not withhold.' He said, 'I said, 'How can I do that, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'It is that, or else the Fire.'\""],[7894,"That the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah with his chin on his saddle, humbling himself."],[7895,"Whoever wakes up and this world is his greatest concern, then he has nothing to do with Allah; and whoever does not fear Allah, then he has nothing to do with Allah; and whoever does not care about the Muslims in general, then he is not one of them."],[7896,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ gesturing with his hand toward the belly of a fat man and saying, \"If this were in other than this, it would be better for you.\""],[7897,"Sa'd said to him: What makes you weep, O Abu 'Abdullah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died while he was pleased with you, and you will come to him at the Hawd and meet your companions. Salman said: Indeed, I do not weep out of dread of death or greed for this world, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ made a covenant with us, living and dead: \"Let the provision of any of you from this world be like the provision of a rider.\" And around me are these black things. He said: Around him were only a washing tub, a large bowl, and a water container. Sahih."],[7898,"\"No one increases in usury except that the end of his affair leads to poverty.\""],[7899,"\"Whoever disparages a Muslim with a word by which he shames him without right, Allah will shame him with it in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[7900,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “If you were to rely upon Allah with true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds: they set out in the morning hungry and return in the evening full.”"],[7901,"\"Give glad tidings to my Ummah of high rank, elevation, and empowerment in the lands as long as they do not seek this world by the deeds of the Hereafter. Whoever seeks this world by the deeds of the Hereafter will have no share in the Hereafter.\""],[7902,"\"Indeed, every Ummah has a trial, and the trial of my Ummah is wealth.\""],[7903,"\"Whoever loves his worldly life harms his Hereafter, and whoever loves his Hereafter harms his worldly life, so prefer what remains over what perishes.\""],[7904,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and they discussed this world and the Hereafter. Some of them said: The world is only a means to the Hereafter; in it is work, prayer, and zakah. A group of them said: The Hereafter contains Paradise. They said what Allah willed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The world compared to the Hereafter is only like one of you walking to the sea and putting his finger into it; what comes out of it is the world.\""],[7905,"On the authority of Atiyyah ibn Sa'd, who was one of the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, a person is not considered one of the righteous until he leaves what is permissible out of caution for what is impermissible.\""],[7906,"\"Water is for Water.\" [1] [1] That is, water for peforming Ghusl is obligatory when the ejaculation of water (semen) occurs. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 199)"],[7907,"\"Indeed, the righteous are subjected to hardship.\""],[7908,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever starts their day with concerns other than Allah, they are not of Allah in anything. And whoever does not show concern for the Muslims, they are not of them.\" Issac and Muqatil are not trustworthy or truthful."],[7909,"\"Thus is sincerity,\" and he gestured with the finger next to the thumb. \"And this is supplication,\" and he raised his hands level with his shoulders. \"And this is earnest entreaty,\" and he raised his hands, stretching them out."],[7910,"\"Indeed, Allah the Exalted made the entire world little, and what remains of it is only the little of the little. The likeness of what remains of it is like a watering hole, meaning a pool, whose clear water has been drunk and whose dregs remain.\""],[7911,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little, and you would go out to the high places crying out to Allah ﷻ, not knowing whether you will be saved or not saved.\""],[7912,"None of you is waiting for anything except wealth that causes tyranny, or poverty that causes forgetfulness, or a debilitating illness, or senility that leads to foolishness, or a sudden death, or the Dajjal—and the Dajjal is the worst awaited unseen—or the Hour, and the Hour is more calamitous and more bitter."],[7913,"There is no heart except that it is between two fingers of the fingers of the Most Merciful; if He wills, He keeps it upright, and if He wills, He causes it to deviate."],[7914,"O Ali, seek goodness from the merciful ones of my nation, you will live in their protection; and do not seek it from those whose hearts are hard, for the curse descends upon them."],[7915,"Increase in remembering the destroyer of pleasures: death."],[7916,"Do not acquire estates, lest you become desirous of the world."],[7917,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"O Allah, let me live as a poor person and let me die as a poor person, and gather me with the group of the poor. Verily, the most miserable of all the miserable ones is the one upon whom the misery of poverty in this world and the torment of the Hereafter are combined.\""],[7918,"Regarding this verse: {O you who believe, upon you is [responsibility for] yourselves. Those who have gone astray will not harm you when you have been guided} [al-Ma'idah 105]. Abu Tha'labah said: You have asked about it one who is well-informed. I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it before, and he said: \"O Abu Tha'labah, enjoin good and forbid evil. Then when you see miserliness obeyed, desire followed, the world preferred, and you see a matter that you must necessarily seek, then upon you is [to look after] yourself and leave them and their common people. For behind you are days of patience; patience during them is like grasping a live coal. The one who acts [righteously] during them will have the reward of fifty who do the like of his deed.\""],[7919,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was reciting: 'The mutual rivalry for piling up [worldly things] diverts you, until you visit the graves.' He said: 'The son of Adam says: My wealth, my wealth. But do you have from your wealth anything except what you wore and wore out, or ate and consumed, or gave in charity and thus sent forth [for the Hereafter]?'"],[7920,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spat into his palm, then placed his finger on it, then said: 'Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: O son of Adam, do you try to frustrate Me, when I have created you from something like this? Then when I have fashioned you and proportioned you, you walked about, and you amassed and withheld, until when it reaches the collarbones, you say: I will give charity. But how far is it now the time for charity?'"],[7921,"\"Be shy of Allah with the shyness He deserves.\" We said: O Prophet of Allah, we are shy. He said: \"That is not it. But whoever is shy of Allah with the shyness He deserves, let him guard the head and what it contains, and the belly and what it holds, and let him remember death and decay. Whoever desires the Hereafter, let him abandon the adornment of this world. Whoever does that has been shy of Allah with the shyness He deserves.\""],[7922,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"There will come a time when people gather in their mosques, but their hearts will be attached only to the dunya (worldly matters). They will have no need for Allah, so do not sit with them.\""],[7923,"The Hour has drawn near, yet the people do not increase except in greed for the world, and they do not increase except in distance from Allah."],[7924,"I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili say: When the Prophet of Allah ﷺ was sent, Iblis's soldiers came to him and said: A Prophet of Allah has been sent and his nation has emerged. Iblis said: Do they love the world? They said: Yes. He said: If they love it, I do not care if they do not worship idols. They will never escape me. I will come to them morning and evening with three things: taking wealth without its right, spending it in other than its right, and withholding it from its right. And all evil follows from this."],[7925,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about what most often causes people to enter Paradise. He said: \"Taqwa and good character.\" And he was asked about what most often causes people to enter the Fire, and he said: \"The two hollow organs: the mouth and the private parts.\""],[7926,"I heard al-Nu'man while he was on the pulpit saying, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to not find enough to fill his belly from low-quality dates while he was hungry.\""],[7927,"Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Muhammad, live as you wish, for you will die; love whom you wish, for you will part from them; and do what you wish, for you will be recompensed for it.\" Then he said, \"O Muhammad, the honor of a believer is standing in night prayer, and his might is his independence from people.\""],[7928,"\"Nobility is wealth, and generosity is piety.\""],[7929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"When the Muslims hate their scholars, show off the construction of their markets, and intermarry for the sake of accumulating dirhams, Allah ﷻ will inflict upon them four traits: drought in time, oppression from the ruler, treachery from the governors of rulings, and assault from the enemy.\""],[7930,"\"O people, indeed one of you will not die until he completes his provision, so do not deem provision slow. Fear Allah, O people, and be moderate in seeking. Take what is lawful and leave what is forbidden.\""],[7931,"\"The Prophet ﷺ ate coarse food and wore coarse clothing; he wore wool and patched sandals.\" Al-Hasan was asked, \"What is coarse?\" He said, \"Coarse barley, which the Prophet ﷺ could not swallow except with a gulp of water.\""],[7932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Your Lord, blessed and exalted, says: ‘O son of Adam, devote yourself to My worship; I will fill your heart with richness and fill your hands with provision. O son of Adam, do not distance yourself from Me, lest I fill your heart with poverty and fill your hands with preoccupation.’”"],[7933,"I heard 'Amr b. al-'As saying while he was addressing the people in Egypt: \"How far your guidance is from the guidance of your Prophet ﷺ! As for him, he was the most abstinent of people in this world, whereas you are the most desirous of it.\""],[7934,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, advise me and be brief.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"You must despair of what is in people's hands, and beware of greed, for it is present poverty. Pray your prayer as if you are bidding farewell, and beware of that for which you would have to apologize.\""],[7935,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"O Abu Dharr, do you consider abundance of wealth to be wealth?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"And do you consider scarcity of wealth to be poverty?\" I said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"No, that is not the case. Indeed, true wealth is wealth of the heart, and true poverty is poverty of the heart.\""],[7936,"He informed him, saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ among a group from Banu Sa'd b. Bakr, and I was the youngest of the people, so they left me behind with their baggage. Then they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he fulfilled their needs. Then he said, \"Is there anyone left among you?\" They said, \"Yes, a young boy with us whom we left behind with our baggage.\" He ordered them to send for me, so they came to me and said, \"Answer the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So I went to him, and when he saw me, he said, \"What Allah has enriched you with, do not ask people for anything. For the upper hand is the giving hand, and the lower hand is the receiving hand, and indeed Allah's wealth is asked for and given.\" He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke to me in our dialect."],[7937,"The heart of an old man remains young in love of two things: long life and abundant wealth."],[7938,"\"Many a disheveled, dusty person with two worn garments, from whom people's eyes turn away, if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath.\""],[7939,"Umar b. al-Khattab went out to the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and found Mu'adh b. Jabal weeping at the grave of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, \"What makes you weep, O Mu'adh?\" He said, \"Something I heard from the occupant of this grave makes me weep.\" He said, \"What did you hear?\" He said, \"I heard him say: 'Indeed, a little showing-off is polytheism. Indeed, whoever shows enmity to a friend of Allah has openly challenged Allah to war. Indeed, Allah loves the righteous, hidden ones who, when absent, are not missed, and when present, are not invited or recognized. Their hearts are lamps of guidance; they emerge from every dusty, dark place.'\""],[7940,"Whoever makes his concerns a single concern, Allah will suffice him in what concerns him of the affairs of this world and the Hereafter. And whoever is distracted by many concerns, Allah will not care in which valley of this world he perishes."],[7941,"Indeed the heart of the son of Adam is like a bird; it turns over seven times in a day."],[7942,"The hidden shirk is that a man acts for the sake of another man."],[7943,"We used to consider on the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that showing off is the lesser shirk."],[7944,"Whoever prays showing off has committed shirk, whoever fasts showing off has committed shirk, and whoever gives charity showing off has committed shirk."],[7945,"A man said, 'O Prophet of Allah, I stand in the stations seeking the Face of Allah, and I love that my standing be seen.' He said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not reply to him until it was revealed: {So whoever hopes for the meeting with his Lord, let him work righteous deeds} [al-Kahf: 110].' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7946,"A hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said, 'And what is it?' He said, 'While I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I saw in his face something that distressed me. I said, \"May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of Allah, what is it that I see in your face?\" He said, \"A matter I fear for my ummah after me.\" I said, \"And what is it?\" He said, \"Shirk and hidden desire.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will your ummah commit shirk after you?\" He said, \"O Shaddad, indeed they will not worship a sun, nor a moon, nor an idol, nor a stone, but they will show off to people with their deeds.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, is showing off shirk?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"Then what is the hidden desire?\" He said, \"One of you wakes up fasting, and a desire from the desires of this world is presented to him, and he breaks his fast.\"'"],[7947,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, 'Visit the graves, for they remind you of the Hereafter. Wash the dead, for handling an empty body is an eloquent admonition. Pray over the funerals, perhaps that will grieve you, for the grieving one is in the shade of Allah on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[7948,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, 'The grave is the first of the stages of the Hereafter. If one is saved from it, then what comes after is easier than it. And if one is not saved from it, then what comes after is more severe than it.' Sahih."],[7949,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for retribution against himself for a scratch he inflicted on a bedouin unintentionally. Then Jibril ﷺ came to him and said, 'O Muhammad, Allah did not send you as a tyrant or arrogant.' So the Prophet ﷺ called the bedouin and said, 'Take retribution from me.' The bedouin said, 'I have pardoned you, may my father and mother be your ransom. I would never do that, even if it cost me my life.' So he supplicated for good for him."],[7950,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'I love you, the People of the House.' The Prophet ﷺ said to him, 'By Allah?' He said, 'By Allah.' He said, 'Then prepare for poverty a shield, for poverty is faster to those who love us than a flood from the top of a hill to its bottom.'"],[7951,"No human being fills a vessel worse than his stomach. Sufficient for the son of Adam are a few morsels to keep his back straight. But if it must be, then one third for food, one third for drink, and one third for himself."],[7952,"“In Hell there is a valley, and in the valley there is a well called Habhab. It is incumbent upon Allah to make every tyrant dwell in it. So fear Allah, lest you dwell in it.”"],[7953,"“Love the poor and sit with them, and love the Arabs from your heart, and repel from the people what you know is in your heart.”"],[7954,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “O Abu Hurayrah, learn the laws of inheritance and teach it, for it is half of knowledge, and it will be forgotten, and it is the first thing to be taken away from my Ummah.” Hafs ibn Umar is extremely unreliable."],[7955,"Knowledge is three things; anything beyond that is superfluous: a decisive verse, an established Sunnah, or a just obligatory share."],[7956,"“Learn the Qur’an and teach it to the people, and learn the laws of inheritance and teach them to the people, for I am a man who will be taken, and knowledge will be taken away, and trials will appear until two people will dispute over an inheritance share and will not find anyone to judge between them.”"],[7957,"“Learn the laws of inheritance and teach them to the people, for I am a man who will be taken, and knowledge will be taken away until two people will dispute over an inheritance share and will not find anyone to settle the matter between them.”"],[7958,"‘Umar b. al-Khattab wrote to Abu Musa al-Ash‘ari, “When you engage in pastime, let it be archery; and when you converse, converse about the inheritance shares.”"],[7959,"Whoever among you recites the Qur’an should learn the laws of inheritance. If a Bedouin meets him and says, “O Muhajir, do you recite the Qur’an?” and he says, “Yes,” and the Bedouin says, “I also recite the Qur’an,” then the Bedouin asks, “Do you know the obligatory shares, O Muhajir?” If he says, “Yes,” the Bedouin says, “An increase of good.” If he says, “No,” I think he said, “Then what makes you better than me, O Muhajir?”"],[7960,"The wife of Sa‘d b. al-Rabi‘ came and said, “O Messenger of Allah, these are the two daughters of Sa‘d b. al-Rabi‘. Their father was martyred with you on the day of Uhud, and their paternal uncle took their wealth and left them no property.” He said, “Allah will judge in that.” Then the verse of inheritance was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to their uncle and said, “Give the two daughters of Sa‘d two-thirds, their mother one-eighth, and what remains is yours.”"],[7961,"When a man or a woman dies leaving one daughter, she gets half. If they are two or more, they get two-thirds. If there is a male with them, no one among them has a fixed share. One begins with anyone who shares with them in a fixed share, gives him his share, and what remains after that goes to the children among them, {to the male the equal of the portion of two females} [al-Nisa’ 11]. If they are two or more females, they get two-thirds."],[7962,"He said to him, “Move aside, O cousin of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” He said, “This is how we treat our elders and scholars.”"],[7963,"“Two or more constitute a group.”"],[7964,"I would have certainly gone astray then, and I am not among the rightly guided. But I judge according to what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged: for the daughter is half, for the son's daughter is one-sixth, and what remains is for the sister."],[7965,"“The inheritance of brothers from the father and mother is that they do not inherit anything along with a male child, nor with a son's child, nor with the father.”"],[7966,"Allah ﷻ says: {But if he has brothers, then for his mother is one-sixth} [al-Nisa' 11]. “But two brothers in the speech of your people are not [true] brothers.” Then Uthman b. Affan said: I cannot overturn what has been practiced before me and has spread through the regions, by which the people have been inheriting."],[7967,"“Brothers in the speech of the Arabs are two or more.”"],[7968,"“The most learned of my community in inheritance law is Zayd b. Thabit.”"],[7969,"Umar was brought a case concerning a wife and two parents, and he gave the wife one-fourth, the mother one-third of what remained, and the father what remained."],[7970,"“Allah, the Exalted, would never see me give preference to a mother over a grandfather.”"],[7971,"He was on his deathbed and said: “What did you say about kalalah?” Ibn Abbas said: And what did you say? He said: “The one who has no child.”"],[7972,"O Messenger of Allah, what is kalalah? He said: Have you not heard the verse that was revealed in the summer: {They ask you for a ruling. Say: Allah gives you a ruling concerning kalalah} [al-Nisa' 176]. Kalalah is the one who leaves neither child nor parent."],[7973,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that the debt is to be paid before the bequest.” And you recite: {after any bequest that may have been made or debt} [al-Nisa' 12]. And that the offspring of the maternal brothers inherit to the exclusion of the offspring of the paternal half-brothers, and brothers from the mother and brothers from both father and mother are closer than brothers from the father."],[7974,"“The inheritance of brothers from the father, when there is no one with them from the children of the mother and father, is like the inheritance of brothers from both father and mother, exactly: their males are like their males, and their females are like their females. But when brothers from both father and mother and brothers from the father come together, and among the children of both father and mother there is a male, then no one from the brothers from the father inherits along with him.”"],[7975,"Regarding the mushtaraka case, he said: “Suppose their father was a donkey. The father only increased them in nearness, and they were made partners in the one-third.”"],[7976,"Concerning a mother, a husband, full brothers, and maternal brothers: \"The full brothers are partners with the maternal brothers in their third, because they said, 'They are all sons of the same mother, and the father only added closeness to them, so they share in the third.'\""],[7977,"\"Something you will not find in the Book of Allah, the Exalted, nor in the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but you will find it among all people: the daughter gets half and the sister gets half.\""],[7978,"Ibn al-Zubayr used to say regarding a daughter and a sister: the wealth belongs to the daughter. So I said: \"Mu'adh judged among us in Yemen that the daughter gets half and the sister gets half.\" He said: \"You are my messenger to al-Walid ibn 'Utbah, who was his judge over Kufah, so order him to act upon that.\""],[7979,"The Prophet ﷺ said to me: \"Attach the wealth to the fixed shares, and whatever remains goes to the nearest male relative.\""],[7980,"Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us; Sufyan al-Thawri informed us.\""],[7981,"Yahya ibn Yahya narrated to us; Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah informed us.\""],[7982,"From Ibn Jurayj.\""],[7983,"As for the hadith of Ma'mar\"—rather, they unanimously agreed on its weakness, meaning 'Ali ibn 'Asim."],[7984,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, who said: A grandmother came to Abu Bakr after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"I have a right; my son's son or my daughter's son has died.\" He said, \"I do not know that you have any right in the Book of Allah, nor have I heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it, but I will ask the people.\" So he asked them, and al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah testified that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave her a sixth. He said, \"Who heard this with you?\" Muhammad ibn Maslamah testified, so Abu Bakr gave her a sixth."],[7985,"Ishaq narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed us; Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, who said: A man came to Ibn 'Abbas and said, \"A man died leaving his daughter and his full sister.\" He said, \"His daughter gets half and his sister gets nothing.\" The man said, \"But 'Umar judged otherwise: he gave the daughter half and the sister half.\" Ibn 'Abbas said, \"Are you more knowledgeable or Allah?\" I did not understand the point of this until I met Ibn Tawus and mentioned al-Zuhri's hadith to him. He said: My father told me that he heard Ibn 'Abbas say: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: {If a man dies having no child but has a sister, she gets half of what he leaves} [al-Nisa' 176]. Ibn 'Abbas said: \"Yet you say she gets half even if he has a child.\""],[7986,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? I said: \"I have something.\" He said: \"What do you have?\" I said: \"He gave her a sixth.\" He said: \"Along with whom?\" I said: \"I do not know.\" He said: \"May you not know.\""],[7987,"\"That Abu Bakr treated him as a father.\""],[7988,"That 'Umar b. al-Khattab, when he consulted them about the inheritance of the grandfather and the brothers, Zayd said, \"My opinion was that the brothers have a better right to the inheritance than the grandfather, but 'Umar at that time held the view that the grandfather has a better right to the inheritance of his son's son than his brothers.\" Zayd said, \"I argued with 'Umar, and I gave 'Umar an example for that, and 'Ali b. Abi Talib and 'Abd Allah b. 'Abbas also gave 'Umar an example that day of a flood: they struck it and diverted it in the manner of Zayd's diversion.\""],[7989,"That 'Umar, when he was stabbed, said, \"I held an opinion about the grandfather, and if you see fit to follow it, then do so.\" 'Uthman said, \"If we follow your opinion, it is right guidance; and if we follow the opinion of the old man before you, then how excellent a man of opinion he was.\""],[7990,"Indeed, part of the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ concerning the two grandmothers is that they receive one-sixth of the inheritance, divided equally between them."],[7991,"The first person to apply 'awl to the obligatory shares was 'Umar. By Allah, if he had given precedence to those whom Allah gave precedence, and put back those whom Allah put back, no obligatory share would have ever been subject to 'awl."],[7992,"A woman inherits from three: her freed slave, her foundling, and the child upon whom she has sworn li'an."],[7993,"He said concerning the inheritance of the child of li'an, \"His entire inheritance belongs to his mother.\""],[7994,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning the child of li'an, \"His 'asabah is his mother.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[7995,"A dispute concerning the child of li'an was brought to 'Ali b. Abi Talib, and he gave his inheritance to his mother and made her his 'asabah."],[7996,"Wala' is a kinship like the kinship of blood; it is not to be sold or given away."],[7997,"Wala' is a kinship from the lineage; it is not to be sold or given away."],[7998,"There is no musa'ah in Islam. Whoever made a musa'ah agreement in the Jahiliyyah, it has already attached him to his 'asabah. And whoever claims a child born outside of lawful wedlock, he neither inherits nor is inherited from."],[7999,"Whoever claims a child born to a slave woman he does not own, or to a free woman with whom he committed adultery, that child is not attributed to him, and he does not inherit. The child belongs to the family of his mother, whoever they may be."],[8000,"Indeed, the full siblings through the mother inherit from one another, to the exclusion of half-siblings through different mothers."],[8001,"The wife of Sa'd b. al-Rabi' came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, these are the two daughters of Sa'd b. al-Rabi'. Their father was killed with you on the day of Uhud as a martyr. Their paternal uncle took their wealth and left nothing for them.' He said, 'Allah will judge in that matter.' He said, 'Then the verse of inheritance was revealed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to their paternal uncle and said, \"Give the two daughters of Sa'd two-thirds, their mother one-eighth, and whatever remains is yours.\"'"],[8002,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ approached a donkey, and a man met him and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, a man left behind his paternal aunt and maternal aunt, and there is no heir for him except them.\" He (the Prophet) raised his head towards the sky and said, \"O Allah, a man left behind his paternal aunt and maternal aunt, and there is no heir for him except them.\" Then he said, \"Where is the questioner?\" He said, \"Here I am.\" He (the Prophet) said, \"There is no inheritance for them (the paternal aunt and maternal aunt).\""],[8003,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, and he remained silent. Then Jibril ﷺ came down to him and said, 'Jibril told me that they have no inheritance.'"],[8004,"The Prophet ﷺ rode to Quba' with a packsaddle on the donkey and said, 'I seek the choice of Allah, the Exalted, regarding the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt.' Then Allah, the Exalted, revealed to him that they have no inheritance. 'Thus the hadith of 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far is sound through these supporting witnesses, though the two did not include it.'"],[8005,"I entered upon Abu Bakr al-Siddiq during the illness in which he died, visiting him. I heard him say, 'I wish I had asked the Prophet ﷺ about the inheritance of the paternal aunt and the maternal aunt, for I have a need in my heart regarding it.'"],[8006,"Neither the paternal aunt, the sister of the father through both father and mother, nor the maternal aunt, nor anyone more distant in kinship from the deceased inherits."],[8007,"Far from it, far from it! Where is Ibn Mas'ud? The emigrants used to inherit from one another to the exclusion of the desert Arabs. Then it was revealed: {And those of kin are nearer to one another in the decree of Allah}."],[8008,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I am the patron of he who has no patron; I inherit his wealth and free his captive. The maternal uncle is the heir of he who has no heir; he inherits his wealth and frees his captive.'"],[8009,"Leave the girl with her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is a mother."],[8010,"Allah and His Messenger are the patrons of he who has no patron, and the maternal uncle is the heir of he who has no heir."],[8011,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had established brotherhood between a man from the emigrants and a man from the Ansar. We did not doubt that we would inherit from one another, so if Ka'b were to die and had no one to inherit from him, I thought that I would inherit from him, and likewise if I died, he would inherit from me, until this verse was revealed: {And those of kin are nearer to one another} [Al-Ahzab 6]."],[8012,"He was brought a case concerning the inheritance of a Jew who had a Muslim heir. He said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Islam increases and does not decrease.\"'"],[8013,"A Muslim does not inherit from a Christian unless he is his slave or his slave woman."],[8014,"A Muslim does not inherit from a disbeliever, nor does a disbeliever inherit from a Muslim."],[8015,"Umm Kulthum gave birth to a son for Umar. As for the other note, it has an authentic witness."],[8016,"He would not make the deceased inherit from the deceased when it was not known which of them died before the other."],[8017,"A man would enter into an alliance with another man between whom there was no kinship, so that one of them would inherit from the other. Then Allah abrogated that with the shares of inheritance: {And those of kinship are more entitled to one another in the Book of Allah} [al-Ahzab 6]. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[8018,"He heard Mu'adh b. Jabal say while he was on the pulpit: 'The estate of a man who left behind his daughter and his sister was distributed, so half was given to his daughter and half to his sister, while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was alive among them.'"],[8019,"The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Seek an heir for him,' but none was found except a client of his, the one who had freed him. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Give it to him.'"],[8020,"Yazid b. Harun narrated to us; Hammad b. Salamah informed us, meeting the criteria of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8021,"Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[8022,"They brought a dispute to Ali concerning the child of a woman divorced by li'an. The paternal relatives of his father came seeking his inheritance. He said: 'His father had disowned him,' so he gave the inheritance to his mother and made her the sole heir, and he gave them nothing."],[8023,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I gave charity to my mother, then she died and the charity returned to me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your reward is assured, and your charity has returned to you.' It was narrated by Sufyan al-Thawri and others from Abdullah b. Ata from Ibn Buraydah from his father."],[8024,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'My mother has died and she owed fasting for two months.' He said: 'Fast on her behalf.' She said: 'She owed a Hajj.' He said: 'Perform Hajj on her behalf.' She said: 'I had given her a slave girl as charity.' He said: 'Allah has rewarded you, and the inheritance has returned her to you.'"],[8025,"That he gave charity to his parents, then they died, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to him as inheritance."],[8026,"That ‘Abd Allah b. Zayd b. ‘Abd Rabbihi came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this walled garden of mine is a charity, and it is for Allah and His Messenger.' Then his parents came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it was our means of livelihood.' So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned it to them, then they died, and their son inherited it after them."],[8027,"That he gave charity with a walled garden of his. His parents came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, it was the support of our livelihood, and we had nothing besides it.' He called ‘Abd Allah and said: 'Allah, Exalted is He, has accepted your charity and returned it to your parents.' Bashir said: 'So we inherited it after that.' This hadith, although its chain is authentic according to the criteria of the two Shaykhs, I do not think that Bashir b. Muhammad al-Ansari heard from his grandfather ‘Abd Allah b. Zayd. The two Shaykhs abandoned the hadith of ‘Abd Allah b. Zayd about the call to prayer and the dream that he related to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with this chain due to the early death of ‘Abd Allah b. Zayd. It is said that he was martyred at Uhud, and it is also said a little after that. And Allah knows best."],[8028,"When a newborn cries out, it is entitled to inheritance and the funeral prayer is offered over it."],[8029,"When a newborn cries out, it is entitled to inheritance and the funeral prayer is offered over it."],[8030,"In the list of the Prophet Muhammad's possessions, two books were found containing the following statement: \"Indeed, the most oppressive of people is a man who attacks someone who does not attack him, a man who kills someone who does not kill him, and a man who withholds his blessings from those who deserve them. Whoever does these things has disbelieved in Allah and His Messenger, and his repentance will not be accepted.\""],[8031,"Among the most insolent people toward Allah, Exalted is He, is one who kills someone other than his killer, or seeks a blood claim from the people of Islam based on a pre-Islamic era blood feud, or one who makes his eyes see in sleep what they did not see."],[8032,"Abu al-‘Abbas Muhammad b. Ya‘qub narrated to us, Muhammad b. ‘Abd Allah b. ‘Abd al-Hakam narrated to us, Ibn Wahb reported to us, Yunus reported to us, from al-Zuhri, from Muslim b. Yazid, from Abu Shurayh al-Ka‘bi, from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with this same hadith. Sahih."],[8033,"When Iblis wakes up in the morning, he dispatches his troops and says: 'Whoever leads a Muslim astray today, I will place the crown on him.' One of them comes and says: 'I kept at him until he was undutiful to his father.' He says: 'He may soon be dutiful to him.' Another comes and says: 'I kept at him until he divorced his wife.' He says: 'He may soon remarry.' Another comes and says: 'I kept at him until he committed shirk.' He says: 'You are the one, you are the one.' Another comes and says: 'I kept at him until he killed.' He says: 'You are the one, you are the one,' and he places the crown on him."],[8034,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The blood of a Muslim person is not lawful except for one of three: adultery after chastity, apostasy after Islam, or killing a person unjustly, for which he is killed.' 'By Allah, I did not commit adultery in pre-Islamic times or in Islam, nor did I apostatize since I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, nor did I kill a person whom Allah has forbidden to kill. So for what will you kill me?'"],[8035,"A person remains in a state of ease in his religion as long as he has not shed forbidden blood."],[8036,"A person will always remain in a state of ease in his religion as long as he has not shed forbidden blood."],[8037,"Every sin, Allah may forgive it, except a man who dies as a disbeliever, or a man who kills a believer deliberately."],[8038,"Every sin, perhaps Allah will forgive it, except a man who dies as a polytheist or kills a believer deliberately."],[8039,"Indeed it is only four; I am not today more elderly than the day I heard them from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say during the Farewell Pilgrimage: \"Do not associate anything with Allah, do not kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, do not steal, and do not commit adultery.\""],[8040,"Whoever meets Allah, exalted is He, without associating anything with Him and without having shed sacred blood, will enter Paradise from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes."],[8041,"Whoever dies without associating anything with Allah and without having shed sacred blood will enter from whichever of the gates of Paradise he wishes."],[8042,"A slain man was killed during the time of the Prophet ﷺ in Madinah. He ascended the pulpit as a preacher and said, \"Do you not know who killed this slain man among you?\" three times. They said, \"By Allah, we know of no killer for him.\" He ﷺ said, \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, if the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth joined together to kill a believer and were pleased with it, Allah would admit them all into Hell. By the One in whose hand is my soul, no one hates us, the people of the House, except that Allah will cast him face down into the Fire.\" A weak report."],[8043,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A believer does not kill treacherously; faith is a restraint against treacherous killing.”"],[8044,"Faith is a restraint against assassination; no believer assassinates."],[8045,"Ammar entered upon Aisha on the Day of the Camel and said, \"Peace be upon you, O my mother.\" She replied, \"I am not your mother.\" He said, \"Indeed you are my mother, even if you dislike it.\" She asked, \"Who is that whose voice I hear with you?\" He said, \"Al-Ashtar.\" She said, \"O Ashtar, are you the one who wanted to kill my nephew?\" He replied, \"I was eager to kill him and he was eager to kill me, but neither of us could.\" She said, \"By Allah, if you had killed him, you would not have prospered. As for you, O Ammar, you know that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: None is to be killed except one of three: a man who kills a man and is killed for it, a man who commits adultery after being married, and a man who apostatizes from Islam.\""],[8046,"I was concealing something against the liar; I intended to enter upon him with my sword. One day I entered upon him and he said, \"By Allah, you have come to me while Gabriel has just risen from this chair.\" I reached for the hilt of my sword and said, \"What do I wait for? I will strike between his head and his body,\" until I remembered a hadith that Amr b. al-Hamiq narrated to us. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"When a man trusts another man and then kills him after he trusted him, a banner of treachery will be set up for him on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8047,"The blood of any person from the people of the Qiblah is not lawful except for one of three: he kills and is killed, a married adulterer, and one who abandons the community, or he said, \"the one who exits from the community.\""],[8048,"The blood of anyone from the people of the Qiblah is not lawful except for one of three: a man who kills and is killed for it, a married adulterer, and one who abandons the community."],[8049,"Ahmad b. Kamil al-Qadi narrated to us, Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Isa al-Qadi narrated to us, Abu Hudhayfa narrated to us, Ibrahim b. Tahman narrated to us from Mansur from Ibrahim from Abu Ma'mar from Masruq from Aisha from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[8050,"There was a woman who had two sons, both as precious as pearls. She used to insult the Prophet ﷺ and he would advise her and she would not stop, and he would scold her and she would not stop. One night, when the Prophet ﷺ mentioned her, he couldn't bear it anymore. He stood up and went to a dark spot, put it inside her and rested on it until he achieved release. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I bear witness that her blood has vanished.\""],[8051,"Abu Bakr became angry at a man, and I said, \"Who is he, O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said, \"Why?\" I said, \"To strike his neck if you command me to.\" He said, \"Would you do that?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"By Allah, the gravity of my word that I spoke has gone; his anger has subsided.\" Then he said, \"That is not for anyone after Muhammad ﷺ.\" This hadith has a sound chain according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it. On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8052,"A man spoke harshly to Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, so I said, 'O Caliph of the Messenger of Allah, shall I not kill him?' He said, 'This is only for one who reviles the Prophet ﷺ.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8053,"Whomever you find doing the deed of the people of Lut, kill the doer and the one to whom it is done."],[8054,"The following is the translation of the Arabic text: \"Al-Qa'nabi reported that Abdulrahman ibn Abdullah ibn Umar Al-Umari narrated from Suhail, from his father, from Abu Hurairah, who said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever performs an act that the people of Lot (Sodom and Gomorrah) did, then they should be stoned, both the perpetrator and the receiver.'\" Note: The translation does not include the phrase \"ساقط\" as it is not clear in this context and could have various interpretations."],[8055,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said, \"Whoever among you finds someone engaging in the same action as the people of Lot, kill both the doer and the one it is done to. And whoever finds someone engaging in bestiality, kill him and kill the animal along with him.\""],[8056,"From Ibn Abbas: He mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ said concerning the one who has intercourse with a beast: 'Kill the doer and the one to whom it is done.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8057,"Whoever has intercourse with a beast, there is no prescribed punishment upon him."],[8058,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Allah curses whoever sacrifices for other than Allah; Allah curses whoever changes the boundaries of the land; Allah curses whoever misleads a blind person from the way; Allah curses whoever reviles his parents; Allah curses whoever affiliates himself with other than his rightful patrons; Allah curses whoever does the deed of the people of Lut.\"[1]"],[8059,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Allah has cursed seven of His creation.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ repeated for each one three times, then said: 'Cursed, cursed, cursed is he who does the deed of the people of Lut; cursed is he who joins a woman and her daughter; cursed is he who reviles anything of his parents; cursed is he who has intercourse with any of the beasts; cursed is he who alters the boundaries of the land; cursed is he who slaughters for other than Allah; cursed is he who takes as patrons other than his own patrons.' Harun b. Harun al-Taymi: they declared him weak."],[8060,"Whoever falls upon a mahram relative, kill him."],[8061,"I was searching for some camels of mine that had strayed, and I was going around some tents when suddenly I saw a rider and horsemen. The people of the watering place began to seek refuge in my dwelling and surrounded my courtyard, and they brought out a man from it. They did not speak to him until they struck his neck. When they left, I asked about him, and they said: 'He had married his father's wife.'"],[8062,"I met my uncle, and with him was the banner. I said to him, 'Where are you heading?' He said, 'The Prophet ﷺ sent me to a man who married his father's wife, and he ordered me to strike his neck and take his property.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8063,"The most fearful thing I fear for my ummah is the deed of the people of Lut."],[8064,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Whoever guards what is between his jaws and his legs will enter Paradise.' The chain is authentic, and Abu Waqid is Salih b. Muhammad. Sahih."],[8065,"Whoever Allah protects from the evil of what is between his jaws and his legs will enter Paradise."],[8066,"If I had caught him, I would have struck him with the sword. Then I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'I am more jealous than Sa'd, and Allah is more jealous than I. There is no one to whom excuses are more beloved than Allah; for that reason He sent the messengers. And there is no one to whom praise is more beloved than Allah; for that reason He promised Paradise.'"],[8067,"Sa'd b. 'Ubada said: If I were to see a man with my father's wife, I would strike him with the sword, not with the flat side. This reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said: \"Are you amazed at Sa'd's jealousy? By Allah, I am more jealous than he, and Allah is more jealous than I. It is because of Allah's jealousy that He forbade indecencies, both open and secret. There is no one more jealous than Allah, and no one to whom excuses are dearer than Allah. For this reason, He has promised Paradise.\""],[8068,"\"O youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery. Whoever guards his private parts will have Paradise.\""],[8069,"\"Whoever guards what is between his jaws and what is between his legs will enter Paradise.\""],[8070,"Al-Dhahabi commented on it in al-Talkhis."],[8071,"\"Whoever guarantees for me what is between his jaws and what is between his legs, I will guarantee him Paradise.\""],[8072,"\"Guarantee me six things from yourselves and I will guarantee you Paradise: speak the truth when you talk, fulfill your promises, return trusts when you are entrusted, guard your private parts, lower your gaze, and restrain your hands.\""],[8073,"\"Accept from me six things and I will accept for you Paradise.\" They said, \"What are they?\" He said, \"When one of you speaks, let him not lie; when he promises, let him not break it; when he is entrusted, let him not betray; lower your gazes, restrain your hands, and guard your private parts.\""],[8074,"Ubay b. Kaʿb told me while he was reciting Sūrat al-Aḥzāb and said, \"I said [it was] seventy three Āyāt [long].\" He said, \"Exactly.\" I said, \"Exactly.\" He said, \"I saw it and it was definitely [similar in size] to al-Baqarah, and we use to recite in it what we recited in it. It had 'The [married] man and the, if they commit adultery, then absolutely stone them as a deterrent from Allah; for Allah is Mighty and Wise'.[1]"],[8075,"Whoever disbelieves in stoning has disbelieved in the Qur'an from where he does not realize: His saying ﷻ: \"O People of the Scripture, there has come to you Our Messenger, making clear to you much of what you used to conceal of the Scripture.\" Stoning was among what they concealed."],[8076,"she said, the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ recited the Āyah of Stoning to us: \"al-shaykhu wa-al-shaykhah idhā zanayā fārjumūhumā al-battata bimā qaḍayā min al-ladhhah (The [married] man and a woman, if they commit adultery, then absolutely stone them for what they spent in [seeking] pleasure.)\"[1]"],[8077,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The old man and the old woman, if they commit adultery, stone them absolutely.\" 'Amr said: When it was revealed, I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"Shall I write it down?\" It was as if he disliked that. 'Amr said to him: \"Do you not see that an old man, if he commits adultery and is muhsan, he is flogged and stoned; and if he is not muhsan, he is flogged; and that a previously married person, if he commits adultery and is muhsan, he is stoned.\""],[8078,"\"The old man and the old woman, if they commit adultery, stone them absolutely.\""],[8079,"\"The punishment of a sorcerer is a strike with the sword.\""],[8080,"There was a man who used to visit the Prophet ﷺ. A man bewitched him, tied knots for him, and cast them into the well of a man of the Ansar. Two angels came to visit him. One sat at his head and the other at his feet. One of them said, \"Do you know what ails him?\" He said, \"So-and-so, who used to visit him, tied knots for him and threw them into the well of So-and-so the Ansari. If only he would send a man to him to take the knots from him.\" They found the water had turned yellow. He said, \"He took the knots and untied them in it.\" He said, \"After that, the man continued to visit the Prophet ﷺ, and he did not mention anything of it to him nor reproach him.\""],[8081,"A commander among the commanders of Kufa summoned a magician to perform before the people. It reached Jundub, so he came with his sword and covered himself with it. When he saw him, he struck him with his sword, and the people dispersed from him. He said, \"O people, do not be alarmed; I only intended the magician.\" The commander seized him and imprisoned him."],[8082,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ma'iz b. Malik: \"Woe to you! Perhaps you kissed, or touched, or squeezed, or looked.\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Did you do it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" Thereupon he ordered that he be stoned."],[8083,"Ma'iz came to a man among the Muslims and said, \"I have committed an indecency, so what do you command me?\" The man said to him, \"Go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he will ask forgiveness for you.\" So Ma'iz came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked his speech, or he said his words. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to those with him: \"Does your companion have a touch of madness?\" Ibn 'Abbas said: I looked at the people to signal them, but none of them paid attention to me. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: \"Perhaps you kissed her?\" He said, \"No.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Then you touched her?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Then you did with her and did not use a euphemism?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"So stone him.\" He said: While he was being stoned, the man whom Ma'iz had come to consult threw a bone at him, and Ma'iz fell. He turned to him and Ma'iz said to him, \"May Allah fight you! When you saw me, and now you are stoning me!\" Hafs b. 'Imran al-'Adani: they deemed him weak."],[8084,"I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Ma'iz b. Malik al-Aslami came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have committed fornication and I want you to purify me.\" The Prophet ﷺ said to him, \"Go back.\" He went back until he came to him the third time. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to his people and asked them, and they praised him well. He said, \"How is his intellect? Is there any madness in him?\" They said, \"No, by Allah,\" and they praised his intellect and his religion. He came to him the fourth time and asked them about him, and they said to him the same. So he ordered them, and they dug a pit for him up to his chest, then they stoned him."],[8085,"Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have committed an indecency.\" The Prophet ﷺ turned him away several times, then he asked his people, \"Is there any harm in him?\" They said, \"There is no harm in him except that he has done something from which he thinks nothing can remove him except that the prescribed punishment be carried out on him.\" He said: He ordered us, so we went with him to Baqi' al-Gharqad. He said: We did not dig for him nor tie him, but we threw at him pieces of baked clay, bones, and stones. He crouched down, then ran, and we ran hard after him. He reached the lava field and stood facing us, and we threw at him the large stones of the lava field until he became still. Then the Prophet ﷺ stood in the evening as a preacher, praised and extolled Allah, and said: \"Now then, what is the matter with people who, when we go on an expedition and one of them stays behind with our families, he has a bleating like the bleating of a he-goat? Indeed, if any of them is brought to me having done that, I will make an example of him.\" He said: He did not revile him nor ask forgiveness for him."],[8086,"\"O Hazzal, if you had covered him with your garment, it would have been better for you.\""],[8087,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ that when Ma'iz felt the touch of the stones and death, he fled. He said, \"Why did you not leave him?\""],[8088,"Ma'iz b. Malik came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have committed fornication, so carry out the Book of Allah on me.\" He turned away from him until he came four times. He said, \"Take him and stone him.\" When the stones touched him, he panicked and ran. He said: 'Abd Allah b. Unays came out from his desert and threw at him the leg bone of a donkey and knocked him down, and the people threw at him until they killed him. His flight was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Why did you not leave him? Perhaps he would repent and Allah would accept his repentance.\""],[8089,"A woman from Ghamid came to the Prophet ﷺ and I said: \"I have committed fornication.\" He said, \"Go away.\" She went away, then returned and said, \"Perhaps you want to do to me as you did to Ma'iz b. Malik. By Allah, I am pregnant.\" He said, \"Go away until you give birth.\" Then she came with him in a rag and said, \"I have given birth, so purify me.\" He said, \"Go away until you wean him.\" She went away, then came with him, in his hand a piece of bread, and said, \"She has weaned him.\" So he ordered that she be stoned. It was also narrated by Ibrahim b. Maymun al-Sa'igh from Abu al-Zubayr from Jabir. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8090,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"I have committed fornication, so carry out the prescribed punishment on me.\" He said, \"Go away and give birth to what is in your womb.\" When she gave birth to what was in her womb, she came to him and said, \"I have committed fornication, so carry out the prescribed punishment on me.\" He said, \"Go away until you wean your child.\" When she had weaned her child, she came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have committed fornication, so carry out the prescribed punishment on me.\" He said, \"Bring someone to take care of your child.\" A man stood up and said, \"I will take care of her child.\" So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stoned her."],[8091,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said that she had committed fornication while she was pregnant. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her, \"Go away until you give birth.\" She went away, and when she gave birth, she came to him. He said, \"Go away until you breastfeed him.\" When she had breastfed him, she came to him. He said, \"Go away until you entrust him to someone.\" When she had entrusted him, she came to him, and he carried out the prescribed punishment on her."],[8092,"I have never seen a man with a stronger throw than 'Ali b. Abi Talib. A woman from Hamdan called Shuraha was brought to him, and he flogged her a hundred lashes, then ordered that she be stoned. 'Ali took a baked brick and threw it at her, and he did not miss the base of her ear. It knocked her down, and the people stoned her until they killed her. Then he said, \"I flogged her according to the Book of Allah, the Exalted, and I stoned her according to the Sunnah.\""],[8093,"He was asked, \"Did you see the Commander of the Believers, Ali b. Abi Talib?\" He said, \"I saw him, white of head and beard.\" It was said, \"Do you remember anything from him?\" He said, \"Yes, I remember that he flogged Shuraha on Thursday and stoned her on Friday, and he said, 'I flogged her according to the Book of God, and I stoned her according to the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ.'\" This is a sound chain, though in the first chain there is disagreement about Abd al-Rahman b. Abdullah b. Mas'ud's hearing from his father. Sahih."],[8094,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had committed fornication, and they had been married. They asked him to judge between them, so he judged that they be stoned. He stoned them in front of the mosque among Banu Ghanm. When the man felt the touch of the stones, he went to his companion and leaned over her to protect her from the stones. That he rose to protect her from the stones was among what God did for His Messenger ﷺ."],[8095,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that, except that he allowed it for araya. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8096,"About a man who has intercourse with his wife's slave girl, he said: \"If she made her lawful for him, he is flogged one hundred lashes; but if she did not make her lawful for him, I stone him.\""],[8097,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Whoever opposes his religion among the Muslims, then kill him. And if a slave says, \"I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and Muhammad is His slave and Messenger,\" then there is no way for us except to carry out his rights if he deserves to be punished.'\""],[8098,"A man of the Ansar accepted Islam, then apostatized and joined the polytheists. Then he regretted it and sent word to his people: \"Ask the Messenger of God ﷺ whether there is any repentance for me.\" He said: Then was revealed: {How shall God guide a people who disbelieved after their belief and bore witness that the Messenger is true, and clear signs came to them} [Al 'Imran 86] up to His saying {Except those who repent after that and make amends, for God is Forgiving, Merciful} [Al 'Imran 89]. He said: \"His people came to him, and he accepted Islam.\""],[8099,"About al-Furat b. Hayyan, who was a spy for Abu Sufyan and an ally. The Messenger of God ﷺ had ordered him killed, but he passed by a circle of the Ansar and said, \"I am a Muslim.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Among you are men whom we entrust to their faith; among them is al-Furat b. Hayyan.\""],[8100,"There were Qurayzah and al-Nadir, and he was among the nobles of Qurayzah. Whenever a man of Qurayzah killed a man of al-Nadir, he was killed for it. But when a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayzah, they said, \"Hand him over to us and we will kill him.\" They said, \"Between us and you is the Prophet ﷺ.\" So they came to him, and it was revealed: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice. Indeed, God loves the just} [al-Ma'idah 42]: a life for a life. Then it was revealed: {Is it the judgment of ignorance they seek?} [al-Ma'idah 50]."],[8101,"The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except in three cases: a married adulterer, who is stoned; a man who kills deliberately, who is killed for it and crucified or banished from the land."],[8102,"The Prophet ﷺ only gouged out the eyes of the Uraynis because they had gouged out the eyes of the shepherds."],[8103,"Ali b. Isa al-Hiri narrated to us: Muhammad b. Ishaq al-Imam narrated to us: Abu Bakr b. Muhammad b. al-Nadr al-Jarudi narrated to me: al-Fadl b. Sahl al-A'raj narrated to us: Yahya b. Abdullah narrated to us, and he mentioned something similar with his chain."],[8104,"Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him."],[8105,"Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; and whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him."],[8106,"Whoever castrates his slave, we will castrate him."],[8107,"A slave girl came to Umar b. al-Khattab and said, 'My master accused me, so he made me sit on fire until my private parts burned.' Umar asked, 'Did he see that [i.e., adultery] from you?' She said, 'No.' He asked, 'Did you confess to him anything?' She said, 'No.' Umar said, 'Bring him to me.' When Umar saw the man, he said, 'Do you punish with the punishment of Allah?' The man said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, I accused her regarding her own self.' Umar asked, 'Did you see that from her?' The man said, 'No.' Umar asked, 'Did she confess that to you?' He said, 'No.' Umar said, 'By the One in Whose hand is my soul, had I not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: A slave is not to be subjected to retaliation for [an offense against] his owner, nor a child for [an offense against] his parent, I would have exacted retaliation from you for her.' He then exposed him and struck him with one hundred lashes. Then he said to her, 'Go, for you are free for the sake of Allah, and you are the freedwoman of Allah and His Messenger.'"],[8108,"Whoever mutilates his slave, the slave is free and is the freedman of Allah and His Messenger."],[8109,"We were lodging in the house of Suwayd b. Muqarrin, and with us was a sharp-tempered, ignorant old man. I do not know what the slave woman of Suwayd said, but he slapped her. Suwayd became angrier than I ever saw him before and said, 'Could you not have hit the free part of her face? I was one of seven from the Banu Muqarrin, and we had only one servant. The youngest of us slapped her, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered us to set her free.'"],[8110,"A child is not to be subjected to retaliation for [an offense against] his parent, and the prescribed punishments are not to be carried out in mosques."],[8111,"It means: \"That the Prophet ﷺ traveled and immigrated [to Medina], and that Abu Bakr traveled and immigrated [with him], and that Umar traveled and immigrated [as well].\""],[8112,"O people, carry out the prescribed punishments on your slaves, whether they are married or unmarried. A slave woman belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed adultery, and he ordered me to flog her. I went to her and found that she had recently given birth. I feared that if I flogged her I might kill her or she might die. I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said, 'You have done well.'"],[8113,"No one is to be flogged with more than ten lashes except for a prescribed punishment from the prescribed punishments of Allah, the Exalted."],[8114,"He visited an aunt of his, and she called for food for him. The servant girl was slow, so she said, 'Why don't you hurry up, O adulteress?' Amr said, 'Glory be to Allah! You have said something terrible. Have you seen her commit adultery?' She said, 'No, by Allah.' Amr said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Any male slave or woman who says to his or her slave girl, \"O adulteress,\" without having seen her commit adultery, will be flogged by that slave girl on the Day of Resurrection, because there is no prescribed punishment for them in this world.'"],[8115,"Sahl b. Sa'd, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, told me that a man from Aslam came to the Prophet ﷺ and said that he had committed adultery with a woman whom he named, but she denied it. The Prophet ﷺ punished the man and left the woman alone. This is a sound chain of narration, though they did not record it, and its supporting evidence is sound."],[8116,"A man from Banu Bakr b. Layth came to the Prophet ﷺ and confessed four times that he had committed adultery with a woman. He was flogged with one hundred lashes, as he was a virgin. Then the Prophet ﷺ asked him for evidence against the woman, and she said, 'He has lied, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah.' So the Prophet ﷺ flogged him eighty lashes for slander."],[8117,"Hilal b. Umayyah accused his wife before the Prophet ﷺ of adultery with Sharik b. Samha'. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Produce evidence, or face the prescribed punishment on your back.'"],[8118,"Al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from his maternal uncle al-Harith b. 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet ﷺ said regarding wine: 'If he drinks it, flog him. If he repeats, flog him. If he repeats for the fourth time, then kill him.'"],[8119,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"If someone drinks alcohol, flog him. If he repeats it, flog him again. If he does it a third time, flog him. If he repeats it for the fourth time, kill him.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary."],[8120,"Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he drinks, flog him; if he drinks, flog him; if he drinks, kill him."],[8121,"Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks for the fourth time, kill him."],[8122,"Whoever drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks for the fourth time, kill him."],[8123,"If they drink wine, flog them; then if they drink, flog them; then if they drink, flog them; then if they drink the fourth time, kill them."],[8124,"When any of you drinks wine, flog him; then if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats for the fourth time, kill him."],[8125,"\"The Prophet ﷺ said regarding alcohol: 'If they drink it, then flog them. If they drink it again, then flog them. If they drink it again, then flog them. And if they drink it again, then kill them on the fourth occasion.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary.\""],[8126,"I heard a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ relating to ʿAbd al-Malik b. Marwān concerning wine that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about wine: \"If he drinks it, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; then if he repeats, flog him; then if he repeats for the fourth time, kill him.\" Then I heard Abū ʿAlī al-Ḥāfiẓ narrating this hadith to us and saying at its end: This Companion is from the people of Syria—he is Shuraḥbīl b. Aws."],[8127,"If he drinks wine, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks, flog him; then if he drinks the fourth time, kill him."],[8128,"As for the hadith of al-Naḍr, one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever drinks wine, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats, flog him; if he repeats the fourth time, kill him.\""],[8129,"From the Prophet ﷺ something similar, and he said: \"So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck al-Nuʿaymān four times.\""],[8130,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not set a fixed punishment for wine. Ibn ʿAbbās said: A man drank and became drunk, and he staggered in the mountain pass, so we took him to the Prophet ﷺ. When he came alongside the house of al-ʿAbbās, he broke loose and entered upon al-ʿAbbās and clung to him. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he laughed and said: \"Did he do that?\" And he did not order anything concerning him."],[8131,"Al-Nuʿaymān—or the son of al-Nuʿaymān—was brought as a drinker, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered those in the house to beat him. He said: \"And I was among those who beat him, and we beat him with sandals and palm stalks.\""],[8132,"Al-Nuʿaymān was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered those in the house, so they beat him with hands and sandals. And I was among those who beat him. This is according to the conditions of al-Bukhārī and Muslim."],[8133,"\"The mustache was presented during the time of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ, and during the caliphate of Abu Bakr, and part of the caliphate of Umar. We would go to it and strike it with our hands, sandals, and cloaks until it became red from the caliphate of Umar. He would then lash it forty times until it became damaged and split into eighty pieces.\""],[8134,"A drunkard was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, “Rise to him and strike him.” So they rose to him and struck him with their sandals."],[8135,"“I will not drink nabidh from jars after a drunken man was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, ‘O Messenger of Allah, I did not drink wine; rather, I drank nabidh of raisins and dates in a gourd.’ So he ordered him to be struck with hands and beaten with sandals, and he forbade raisins, dates, and gourds.”"],[8136,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn while he was moving among the people asking about the camp of Khalid b. al-Walid. Then a drunkard was brought, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered those with him to strike him with whatever was in their hands.” He said, “And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ threw dust in his face.” He said, “Then a drunkard was brought to Abu Bakr.” He said, “He sought out those who had struck him that day, and he was struck forty times.” And Umar struck forty."],[8137,"Ali, we see him when this (person) gets drunk and when this (person) fabricates lies, and upon the liar is eighty (lashes). Then Umar said, \"Inform your companion of what he said.\" Khalid was then flogged eighty times, and Umar was flogged eighty times. When a strong man heavily indulged in drinking was brought to Umar, he would flog him eighty times. And when a weak man, who was prone to making mistakes, was brought to him, he would flog him forty times. Then Uthman was flogged eighty-four times."],[8138,"Drinkers used to be beaten in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with hands, sandals, and staffs until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away. And they were more numerous in the caliphate of Abu Bakr than they had been in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr said, “If we appoint a fixed punishment for them,” and he sought an amount similar to what they used to be beaten with in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr would flog them forty lashes until he passed away. Then Umar succeeded him and flogged them likewise, forty lashes, until a man from the early Muhajirun was brought, and he had drunk. He ordered that he be flogged, and the man said, “Why do you flog me? Between me and you is the Book of Allah ﷻ.” Umar said, “In which part of the Book of Allah do you find that I should not flog you?” He said, “Allah, Exalted is He, says in His Book: {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten} [al-Ma'idah 93], to the end of the verse. I am among those who believed and did righteous deeds, then feared and believed, then feared and did good. I witnessed Badr, al-Hudaybiyyah, the Trench, and the battles with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Umar said, “Will you not respond to what he says?” Ibn Abbas said, “These verses were revealed as an excuse for those who have passed and as a proof against those who remain, because Allah ﷻ says: {O you who believe, indeed wine, gambling, sacrificing on stone altars, and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan} [al-Ma'idah 90].” Then he recited until he completed the other verse: {There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten, if they fear and believe and do righteous deeds, then fear and believe, then fear and do good} [al-Ma'idah 93]. For Allah ﷻ has forbidden drinking wine. Umar said, “You have spoken the truth. So what do you think?” Ali said, “We think that if he drinks, he becomes intoxicated; if he becomes intoxicated, he raves; if he raves, he fabricates lies; and upon the fabricator are eighty lashes.” So Umar ordered that he be flogged eighty lashes."],[8139,"A woman was a prostitute in the pre-Islamic era. A man passed by her and extended his hand to her and flirted with her. She said, “Stop! Indeed, Allah, Exalted is He, has removed polytheism and brought Islam.” So he left her and turned away, but he kept looking back at her until his face hit a wall. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said, “You are a servant for whom Allah intends good. When Allah intends good for a servant, He hastens for him the punishment for his sin; and when He intends evil, He withholds the punishment for his sin until he meets Him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8140,"I was in Madinah when a slave girl passed by me, and I grabbed her by her side. Then I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was taking the pledge of allegiance from the people. He said to me, “Are you not the one who grabbed the girl yesterday?” I said, “I will not do it again, O Messenger of Allah.” So he accepted my pledge."],[8141,"“Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from spying. If it becomes apparent to us, we take it.”"],[8142,"He guarded one night with Umar b. al-Khattab in Madinah. While they were walking, a lamp appeared to them in a house. They went toward it until when they drew near, they found a door closed upon a people who had raised voices inside. Umar, taking Abd al-Rahman by the hand, said, “Do you know whose house this is?” He said, “No.” He said, “This is the house of Rabi'ah b. Umayyah b. Khalaf, and they are now drinking. What do you think?” Abd al-Rahman said, “I think we have done what Allah has forbidden. Allah ﷻ forbade us, for He said: {And do not spy} [al-Hujurat 12], and we have spied.” So Umar turned away from them and left them."],[8143,"“Indeed, when the ruler seeks out suspicion among the people, he corrupts them.”"],[8144,"“Do not recite poetry in the mosques, and do not carry out the prescribed punishments in them.”"],[8145,"“Indeed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not cut off a hand for less than the price of a shield, a leather shield or a buckler, and both of them had value on that day.”"],[8146,"“May Allah curse the thief. If he steals an egg, his hand is cut off; and if he steals a rope, his hand is cut off.”"],[8147,"The Prophet ﷺ amputated for an egg worth twenty dirhams."],[8148,"The price of a shield in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was valued at ten dirhams."],[8149,"\"The hand was not severed during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ except in exchange for a slave, and its price at that time was a dinar.\" I heard Abu Al-Abbas saying, I heard Ar-Rabi' saying, I heard Ash-Shafi'i saying, \"This right hand is the son of the woman of Ka'b, and he is not the son of the mother of Ayyman, and he did not meet the Prophet ﷺ .\""],[8150,"And Ayman was a man of whom good was mentioned. He said: \"The hand of the thief is cut off for less than the price of a shield, and the price of a shield then was a dinar.\" Ayman ibn Umm Ayman, the Companion, brother of Usamah through his mother, is too great and noble to be attributed to obscurity and called \"a man of whom good was mentioned.\" Such wording is only used for an unknown narrator whose reliability is not established, although Jarir stopped it on Ayman and did not trace it back. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8151,"A woman who had stolen was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and she sought refuge with the stepson of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"Even if she were Fatimah, I would cut off her hand.\" Then he cut it off."],[8152,"The stepson of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was Salamah ibn Abi Salamah, and the Makhzumi woman who stole sought refuge with one of them. The two Shaykhs agreed on narrating the hadith of al-Zuhri from Urwah from Aisha that the Makhzumi woman sought refuge with Usamah ibn Zayd, and that is the correct version. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8153,"When that woman stole the velvet cloth from the house of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we considered it a grave matter. She was a woman from Quraysh, so we came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke to him, saying: \"O Messenger of Allah, we will ransom her for forty uqiyyah.\" He said: \"That she be purified is better for her.\" When we heard the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, we went to Usamah ibn Zayd and said: \"Intercede for us with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarding this woman; we will ransom her for forty uqiyyah.\" When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw the people's insistence on that, he stood up to deliver a sermon and said: \"O people, why do you make so much fuss about a punishment from among the punishments of Allah that has befallen a maidservant from among the maidservants of Allah? By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, if Fatimah bint Muhammad were to commit what this woman has committed, Muhammad would cut off her hand.\" He said: The people despaired, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut off her hand. Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr told me that after that, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ showed her mercy and maintained ties with her."],[8154,"Safwan ibn Umayyah brought a man who had stolen a hullah of his to the Prophet ﷺ, then said: \"O Messenger of Allah, give him to me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Why not before you brought him to us?\""],[8155,"I was sleeping in the mosque, wearing a khamisah of mine worth thirty dirhams. A man came and snatched it from me. The man was seized and brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered that his hand be cut off. I went to him and said: \"Will you cut off his hand for thirty dirhams? I will sell it to him and let him pay its price later.\" He said: \"Why did you not do this before you brought him to me?\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8156,"A thief who had stolen a shamlah was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, this man has stolen.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I do not think he has stolen.\" The thief said: \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take him and cut off his hand, then cauterize it, then bring him to me.\" His hand was cut off, then he was brought to him. He said: \"Repent to Allah.\" He said: \"I repent to Allah.\" He said: \"May Allah accept your repentance.\""],[8157,"A man from Muzaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think about the harisah of the mountain?\" He said: \"It is like it, and there is no punishment of amputation for any livestock except what the pen has sheltered and it reaches the value of a shield, then there is amputation. If it does not reach the price of a shield, then there is a fine of twice its value and lashes as a punishment.\""],[8158,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"No more than ten lashes should be given for a punishment below the limit set by Allah Almighty.\""],[8159,"A man stole during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"Kill him.\" They said: \"He only stole.\" He said: \"Cut off his hand.\" Then he stole again, and his hand was cut off. Then he stole during the time of Abu Bakr, and his hand was cut off. Then he stole again, and his hand was cut off, until all his limbs were cut off. Then he stole a fifth time. Abu Bakr said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ knew better about this when he ordered his execution. Take him and kill him.\" He was handed over to a group of young men from Quraysh, among them Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr. Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr said: \"Put me in charge over you.\" They put him in charge, and whenever he struck him, they struck him until they killed him."],[8160,"There is no amputation for a runaway slave if he steals, nor for a dhimmi."],[8161,"I do not recall the first man whose hand the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cut off. A thief was brought and he ordered his hand to be cut off, and it was as if grief appeared on the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. They said, “O Messenger of Allah, it seems you disliked cutting him.” He said, “And what prevents me? Do not be helpers of Satan against your brother. It is not fitting for the ruler, when a prescribed punishment reaches him, except to carry it out. Allah is Pardoning and loves pardon, so let them pardon and overlook. Do you not love that Allah should forgive you? And Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.”"],[8162,"“Pardon the prescribed punishments among yourselves, for whatever prescribed punishment reaches me has become obligatory.”"],[8163,"“Whoever's intercession comes between a prescribed punishment of Allah and its execution has opposed Allah, Exalted, in His command.”"],[8164,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, after he had stoned the Aslami: “Avoid this filth that Allah has forbidden. Whoever falls into it, let him conceal himself with the concealment of Allah and repent to Allah, for whoever exposes his page to us, we shall enforce upon him the Book of Allah, Exalted and Majestic.” According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8165,"“Whoever conceals his brother in this world, Allah will conceal him in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever relieves his brother of a distress of the distresses of this world, Allah will relieve him of a distress of the distresses of the Day of Resurrection. Allah aids the servant as long as the servant aids his brother.”"],[8166,"“No servant conceals another servant in this world except that Allah will conceal him on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[8167,"Three things I swear by them, and a fourth if I were to swear by it I would hope not to sin: Allah will not make a servant who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; no servant takes Allah as his protector in this world and then Allah entrusts him to other than Him on the Day of Resurrection; and no man loves a people except that he will be with them or among them. And the fourth, if I were to swear by it I would hope not to sin: Allah does not conceal a servant in this world except that Allah will conceal him in the Hereafter."],[8168,"“Whoever sees a private part and conceals it, it is as if he revived a buried female infant from her grave.”"],[8169,"“Ward off the prescribed punishments from the Muslims as much as you can. If you find a way out for a Muslim, then let him go, for it is better for the ruler to err in pardon than to err in punishment.”"],[8171,"The Banu Ubayriq were a clan from the Banu Zufar, and they were three: Bashir, Bishr, and Mubashshir. Bashir was called Abu Tu'mah; he was a poet and a hypocrite. He would compose poetry satirizing the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then say, “So-and-so said it.” When it reached them, they would say, “The enemy of Allah lied; none said it but he.” He said [in kamil meter]: “Is it whenever men utter a poem, they attribute it to me, saying Ubayriq said it, strutting as if I fear them—may Allah cut off their noses and sever them.” They were a people of poverty and need in the Jahiliyyah and Islam. My paternal uncle Rifa'ah b. Zayd was a wealthy man who had embraced Islam. By Allah, I used to think there was something lacking in his Islam. When he had plenty and a caravan of these Nabataeans arrived from al-Sadam carrying fine flour, he would buy for himself what suited him, while for the family he would provide barley. A caravan arrived—they were Nabataeans—carrying fine flour, and Rifa'ah bought two loads of barley and put them in an upper room of his, where there were also two of his coats of mail and the tools to repair them. Bashir came to him at night, tore open the upper room from its back, took the food, then took the weapons. When morning came, my uncle sent for me, and I came to him. He said, “We were raided last night; our food and weapons were taken.” Bashir and his brothers said, “By Allah, the only one who took your goods is Labid b. Sahl,” a man of ours of good lineage and righteousness. When that reached him, he said, “By Allah, I drew the sword.” Then he said, “O Banu al-Ubayriq, am I to steal? By Allah, either this sword will be mixed with you or you will make clear who the thief of this theft is.” They said, “Leave us; by Allah, you are innocent of this theft.” He said, “Not at all, while you have claimed it.” Then we asked around the neighborhood and spied until it was said to us, “By Allah, the Banu Ubayriq lit a fire last night, and we think it was only for your food.” We kept at it until we nearly became certain that they were its perpetrators. So I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke to him about them. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, a household among us of rudeness and folly raided my uncle, tore open an upper room of his from its back, and took food and weapons. As for the food, we have no need of it; as for the weapons, let him return them to us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “I will look into that.” They had a paternal cousin called Usayr b. 'Urwah, who gathered men of his people, then came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, “Rifa'ah b. Zayd and his nephew Qatadah b. al-Nu'man have gone to a household among us of good lineage, honor, and righteousness, accusing them of indecency and theft without evidence or testimony.” He said before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ whatever he wished, then left. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke to him, and he rebuked me severely, saying, “What an evil thing you have done and what an evil path you have walked in! You went to a household among you of good lineage and righteousness, accusing them of theft without evidence or verification.” I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what I disliked, so I left, and I wished I had gone out from my wealth and not spoken to him. When I returned home, my uncle sent to me: “O nephew, what did you do?” I said, “By Allah, I wish I had gone out from my wealth and not spoken to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about it. By Allah, I will never return to it.” He said, “Allah is the one whose help is sought.” Then the Qur'an was revealed: {Indeed, We have sent down to you the Book in truth so that you may judge between people by what Allah has shown you, and do not be an advocate for the treacherous} [al-Nisa' 105]—meaning Tu'mah b. Ubayriq. He recited until he reached {then he casts it upon an innocent person} [al-Nisa' 112]—meaning Labid b. Sahl—{And were it not for the favor of Allah upon you and His mercy, a party of them would have resolved to mislead you} [al-Nisa' 113]—meaning Usayr b. 'Urwah and his companions. Then he said, {No good is there in much of their private conversation} [al-Nisa' 114] up to His saying {and He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills} [al-Nisa' 48]—whatever his sin short of idolatry. When the Qur'an was revealed, he fled and joined Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me the two coats of mail and their tools, and I returned them to Rifa'ah. Qatadah said: When I brought them to him with what was with them, he said, “O nephew, they are in the cause of Allah, Exalted and Majestic.” I hoped that my uncle's Islam had become good, and my opinion of him had been otherwise. Ibn Ubayriq went out until he stayed with Salamah bt. Sa'd b. Sahl, sister of the Banu 'Amr b. 'Awf, and she was married to Talhah b. Abi Talhah in Makkah. He fell upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his companions, reviling them, and Hassan b. Thabit hit back at him with some verses, saying [in tawil meter]: “O stealer of the two coats of mail, if you remember one of noble standing among men, I befriend him. The daughter of Sa'd lodged you, and she began to dispute with the skin of his backside and he with her. Why did you not come to Usayr, your neighbor, seeking his favor, and not intend harm to him so that you might fend him off? You thought that what you did would remain hidden, while among you is a Prophet with revelation placed before him. Were it not for men among you whom you revile, for that its rising stars would have descended upon him. If you recall Ka'b, to what do you attribute? Is there any hide without its shanks? You found them hoping in you—you knew—as the fat one and his follower hope for rain.” When Hassan's poetry reached her, she took Ubayriq's saddle and placed it on her head until she threw it into al-Abtah, then she shaved, wailed, tore, and swore: “If you spend even one black night in my house, you would bring me Hassan b. Thabit's poetry; you would never have brought me any good.” When she expelled him, he joined al-Ta'if and entered a house with no one in it, and it fell upon him and killed him. Quraysh began to say, “By Allah, no one of Muhammad's companions leaves him while there is good in him.”"],[8172,"“Whoever commits a sin in this world and Allah conceals it for him and pardons him, Allah is too generous to return to something He has already pardoned and concealed. Whoever commits a sin in this world and is punished for it, Allah is too just to double his punishment upon a servant twice.”"],[8173,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ informed me: {Whatever misfortune befalls you} [al-Shura 30] is because of what your hands have earned, and He pardons much. “Allah is too generous to double the punishment upon them, and whatever Allah has pardoned in this world, Allah is too generous to return in His pardon.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8174,"\"Any slave who commits something of what Allah has forbidden, then the prescribed punishment is carried out on him, that sin is expiated from him.\""],[8175,"A woman afflicted [with insanity] who had committed fornication was brought to Umar, and he ordered her to be stoned. Ali b. Abi Talib passed by her while children were following her, so he said, \"What is this?\" They said, \"Umar has ordered her to be stoned.\" He said, \"So he sent her back and went with her to Umar and said, 'Do you not know that the pen has been lifted from the insane until he regains his reason, from the afflicted until he recovers, from the sleeper until he wakes, and from the child until he reaches puberty?'\""],[8176,"A pregnant insane woman was brought to Umar, and he intended to stone her. Ali said to him, \"Do you not know that the pen has been lifted from three: from the insane until he regains his reason, from the child until he reaches puberty, and from the sleeper until he wakes?\" So he let her go."],[8177,"The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the mentally deficient until he regains his reason, and from the child until he matures."],[8178,"He was with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and he traveled at night, so the people became scattered from him. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The pen has been lifted from three: from the sleeper until he wakes, from the mentally deficient until he becomes sound, and from the child until he reaches puberty.\""],[8179,"He informed him that the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ examined him on the day of Qurayzah, and they did not see that the razor had passed over his hair, meaning his pubic hair, so they left him from execution."],[8180,"\"I was a boy on the day Sa'd b. Mu'adh ruled regarding Banu Qurayzah that their fighting men should be killed and their women and children taken captive. They were uncertain about me, and they did not find that I had grown pubic hair, so here I am among you.\" End of the Book of Penalties."],[8181,"From the Prophet ﷺ who said: \"In the latter times, the dream of the believer will hardly be false. The most truthful of them in dreams are the most truthful of them in speech. Dreams are of three kinds: a good dream is glad tidings from Allah, Exalted is He; a dream that a man talks to himself; and a dream causing grief from Satan. So if any of you sees a dream that he dislikes, he should not tell anyone about it, but he should get up and pray. The dream of the believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood.\" Abu Hurayrah said, \"The fetter pleases me and I dislike the shackle; the fetter is steadfastness in religion.\""],[8182,"\"The dream of the believer is one of forty-six parts of prophethood, and it is on the wing of a bird as long as it is not related. When it is related, it occurs.\""],[8183,"When he finished the morning prayer, he would say, \"Has any of you seen a dream tonight? Indeed, nothing of prophethood will remain after me except the true dream.\""],[8184,"\"Indeed, the dream occurs according to how it is interpreted. The example of that is like a man who raises his foot and waits until he puts it down. So if any of you sees a dream, he should not tell it except to a sincere advisor or a scholar.\""],[8185,"\"Indeed, messengerhood and prophethood have ceased, so there is no messenger after me and no prophet.\" He said, \"That distressed the people.\" So he said, \"But there are the glad tidings.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what are the glad tidings?\" He said, \"The dream of a Muslim man, which is one of the parts of prophethood.\""],[8186,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about His saying, Exalted is He: {For them are good tidings in the worldly life} [Yunus 64]. He said, \"It is the righteous dream that the believer sees or is seen for him.\""],[8187,"About the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {For them are good tidings in the worldly life} [Yunus 64]. He said, \"No one has asked me other than you since I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said, 'No one has asked me about it other than you since it was revealed. It is the righteous dream that the Muslim sees or is seen for him.'\""],[8188,"\"When one of you sees a dream he likes, it is from Allah, the Exalted. Let him praise Allah for it and tell what he saw. When he sees other than that, something he dislikes, it is from Satan. Let him seek refuge in Allah from its evil and not mention it to anyone, for it will not harm him.\""],[8189,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I dreamt that my head was cut off and I was following it.\" The Prophet ﷺ rebuked him and said, \"Do not tell of Satan's playing with you in the dream.\" On the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8190,"\"The truest of dreams are in the pre-dawn hours.\""],[8191,"\" From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"Whoever lies about his dream, he will be required to knot barely kernels on the Day of Judgement.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2281)"],[8192,"\"Whoever lies about his dream will be tasked with tying a knot between two grains of barley.\""],[8193,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Whoever sees me in a dream has truly seen me, for Satan cannot impersonate me.\" My father said: I narrated this to Ibn Abbas and said, \"I saw him ﷺ, and I mentioned al-Hasan b. Ali and likened him to him.\" Ibn Abbas said, \"He used to resemble him.\""],[8194,"From Aisha: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about Waraqah. Khadijah said to him, \"He believed in you, but he died before you appeared.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I saw him in a dream, wearing white garments. If he had been among the people of the Fire, he would have worn other than that.\""],[8195,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us one day and said, \"I saw in a dream as if Jibril ﷺ was at my head and Mikail at my feet, one saying to the other, 'Strike a parable for him.' He said, 'Listen, may your ear hear, and understand, may your heart understand. Your example and the example of your community is like a king who took a house, then built a room in it, then placed a feast in it, then sent a messenger to invite people to his food. Some answered the messenger and some left him. Allah is the king, the house is Islam, the room is Paradise, and you, O Muhammad, are a messenger. Whoever answers you enters Paradise and eats from it.'\""],[8196,"The Prophet ﷺ said one day, \"Who among you has seen a dream?\" A man said, \"I saw as if a scale descended from the sky, and you and Abu Bakr were weighed, and you outweighed Abu Bakr. Then Umar was weighed against Abu Bakr, and Abu Bakr outweighed him. Then Umar and Uthman were weighed, and Umar outweighed him. Then the scale was lifted.\" Then I saw dislike in the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[8197,"I was sitting in the mosque when a man entered and they said, \"This is a man from the people of Paradise.\" So, he prayed and then left. I followed him and said, \"Indeed, the people said this and that about you.\" He said, \"It is not appropriate for anyone to lie or speak about something he does not know. And I will tell you why. I had a dream and I narrated it to the Prophet ﷺ. I saw as if I was in a green garden, and he mentioned its vastness and greenery. In the middle of the garden, there was an iron pillar. Then, a man came to me and said, 'Climb.' I said, 'I'm not able to climb.' He brought a podium from behind me and said, 'Climb.' I said, 'I'm not able to climb.' So, he helped me climb along with my clothes. When I reached the top of the pillar, there was a handle, and I inserted my hand into it. It felt like I became the owner of the ring, and indeed, the ring was in my hand. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'As for the garden, it is the garden of Islam, and as for the pillar, it is the pillar of Islam, and as for the handle, you have held onto the firmest handle of Islam until you die.'\""],[8198,"Some believing women gathered at Aisha, Mother of the Believers. One of them said, \"By Allah, Allah will never punish me, for I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I would not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor kill my child, nor bring a slander I fabricate between my hands and feet, nor disobey him in what is right, and I have fulfilled it.\" She returned to her house and was visited in her dream, and it was said to her, \"You are the one who swore against Allah, the Exalted, that He will not punish you. How about your speech about what does not concern you and your withholding what does not suffice you?\" She returned to Aisha and said to her, \"I was visited in my dream and was told such and such. I seek Allah's forgiveness and repent to Him.\"\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8199,"As if three moons fell into my chamber. I told my dream to Abu Bakr. When the Prophet ﷺ was buried in my house, Abu Bakr said, \"This is one of your moons, and it is the best of them.\""],[8200,"“Indeed I saw in a dream black sheep followed by light-colored sheep. O Abu Bakr, interpret it.” Abu Bakr said, “O Messenger of Allah, they are the Arabs who follow you, then the non-Arabs follow them until they overwhelm them.” The Prophet ﷺ said, “Thus did the angel interpret it before dawn.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8201,"“I saw many black sheep, and many white sheep entered among them.” They said, “What did you interpret it as, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “The non-Arabs will share with you in your religion and your lineages.” They said, “The non-Arabs, O Messenger of Allah?” He said, “If faith were suspended from the Pleiades, men from the non-Arabs would attain it, and the happiest of people with it would be among them.”"],[8202,"“The two young men who came to Yusuf (peace and blessings be upon him) in the dream had only lied to each other. When he interpreted their dreams, they said: ‘We were only playing.’ Yusuf said: ‘The matter about which you inquire has been decided.’”"],[8203,"Shayban the Jew came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, “O Muhammad, do you know the stars that Yusuf saw prostrating to him?” The Prophet ﷺ remained silent until Jibril ﷺ came to him and informed him of what the Jew had asked. Then the Prophet ﷺ met the Jew and said, “O Jew, will you swear by Allah to me that if I tell you, you will become Muslim?” He said, “Yes.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The stars are Hadathan, al-Tariq, al-Dhabbal, Qabis, al-ʿUdan, al-Faliq, al-Nush, al-Qaruh, Dhu al-Kanafan, Dhu al-Faraʿ, and al-Waththab. Yusuf saw them surrounding the regions of the sky, prostrating to him. He related it to his father, and his father said to him: ‘This is a matter that will be dispersed, but Allah will gather it, if He wills, later.’”"],[8204,"“Indeed I saw eleven stars.” He said, “The dreams of the prophets were revelation.”"],[8205,"“Between the dream of Yusuf and its interpretation there were forty years.”"],[8206,"“O Abu al-Hasan, a man sees a dream; some of them come true and some are false.” He said, “Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘There is no servant, male or female, who sleeps and is filled with sleep except that his soul is taken up to the Throne. The one who does not wake before reaching the Throne—that is the dream that comes true. And the one who wakes before reaching the Throne—that is the dream that is false.’” A rejected hadith."],[8207,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to say, “Has any of you seen a dream?” He said, “Then whoever wished would relate it to him. One morning he said: ‘Last night two angels came to me. One of them sat at my head and the other at my feet. The one at my feet said to the one at my head: Give the example of this man and his community. He said: His example and that of his community is like a people traveling who reached the edge of a vast desert, but they did not have enough provisions to cross the desert or to return. While they were in that state, a man came to them with combed hair, wearing a striped cloak, and said: What do you think? If I bring you to lush meadows and abundant watering places, will you follow me? They said: Yes. So he set off with them and brought them to lush meadows and abundant watering places. They ate, drank, and grew fat. Then he said to them: Did I not find you in that condition and say to you: If I bring you to lush meadows and abundant watering places, will you follow me? They said: Yes. He said: Ahead of you are meadows lusher than these and watering places more abundant than these, so follow me. One group said: By Allah, he has spoken the truth; we will surely follow. Another group said: We are content with this; we will stay here.’”"],[8208,"\"I saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, in the vision of a dream during midday. He appeared disheveled, with a dark complexion, and had a bottle containing blood with him. So I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, what is this?' He said, 'This is the blood of Al-Husayn and his companions. I have been collecting it since that day.' He then said, 'Let me count that day.' They counted and found that he was killed a day before that.\""],[8209,"\"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to sleep one night and woke up bewildered. Then he went back to sleep and woke up bewildered again, without seeing what I saw the first time. Then he went to sleep and woke up holding red soil, which he kissed. So I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is this soil?' He said, 'Jibril informed me that this is the soil on which Al-Husayn will be killed in Iraq.' So I said to Jibril, 'Show me the soil of the land on which he will be killed.' He then showed me this soil."],[8210,"“I saw in a dream as if there were two bracelets of gold on my hands, and I was concerned about them. Then it was revealed to me that I should blow on them. I blew on them and they flew away. I interpreted them as two liars who would emerge after me.” He said, “One of them is Musaylimah of al-Yamamah, and the other is al-ʿAdani of ʿAnsaʾ.”"],[8211,"“Indeed the greatest falsehood is for a man to fabricate against his own eyes, saying: I saw, when he did not see; or to fabricate against his parents; or to say: He heard me, when he did not hear me.”"],[8212,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has not sent down any disease except that He has also sent down its cure. The one who knows it, knows it, and the one who is ignorant of it, is ignorant of it.\""],[8213,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the Bedouins asking him, saying, \"O Messenger of Allah, do we have any hardship in such a matter? Do we have any hardship in such a matter?\" concerning things that are not harmful. He ﷺ said, \"O slaves of Allah, Allah has relieved us of the hardship, except for the one who wrongs a Muslim's honor. That is the one who has hardship and perishes.\" So they said, \"Should we seek medical treatment, O Messenger of Allah?\" He ﷺ said, \"Yes, seek medical treatment, O slaves of Allah, for Allah Almighty has not created a disease except that He has also created its cure except for one disease.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is it?\" He ﷺ said, \"Old age.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the best thing that a person can be given?\" He ﷺ said, \"Good manners.\""],[8214,"Abu Ahmad Muhammad b. Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to me: Yahya b. Muhammad al-Hafiz narrated to us: Yahya b. Muhammad b. Saʿid narrated to us: Ahmad b. Muhammad b. Abi al-Khanajir narrated to us in Tripoli, and he was trustworthy and reliable: Muhammad b. Musʿab al-Qarqisaʾi narrated to us, from Malik b. Mighwal, from Ziyad b. ʿIlaqah; and among them is ʿAmr b. Qays al-Mulaʾi."],[8215,"Abu Bakr and ʿUthman, the two sons of Abi Shaybah, narrated to us; they said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-Aʿmash; and among them is Shuʿbah b. al-Hajjaj."],[8216,"From Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah; among them Muhammad b. Juhadah al-Iyadi."],[8217,"Muhammad b. Juhadah narrated to us; among them Abu Hamzah Muhammad b. Maymun al-Sukkari."],[8218,"Abu al-Hasan Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah al-Sunni informed us in Marw, Abu al-Muwajjah narrated to us, 'Abdan informed us, Abu Hamzah informed us, from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah; among them Abu 'Awanah al-Waddah."],[8219,"From Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah; among them Sufyan b. 'Uyaynah al-Hilali."],[8220,"From Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah; among them 'Uthman b. Hakim al-Awdi."],[8221,"We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, as if birds were on our heads, none of us speaking, when some people from the Bedouins came and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, give us a ruling about such-and-such, give us a ruling about such-and-such.' He said, 'O people of the Bedouins, Allah has removed hardship except for one who borrows his brother's honor; that is the one who is in hardship and is ruined.' They said, 'Should we seek medical treatment, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Yes, for Allah ﷻ did not send down any disease but that He sent down for it a cure, except for one disease.' They said, 'What is it, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Old age.' They said, 'Who is the most beloved of Allah's servants to Allah?' He said, 'The best of them in character.' Among them Shayban b. 'Abd al-Rahman from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah; among them Zuhayr b. Mu'awiyah al-Ju'fi."],[8222,"The Shaykh Abu Bakr b. Ishaq informed us, Isma'il b. Qutaybah narrated to us, Yahya b. Yahya narrated to us, Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr b. Mu'awiyah informed us, from Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah, from Usamah b. Sharik; among them 'Amr b. Abi Qays al-Razi."],[8223,"'Abd al-Samad b. 'Ali b. Mukram al-Bazzar informed us in Baghdad, Ya'qub b. Yusuf al-Qazwini narrated to us, Muhammad b. Sa'id b. Sabiq narrated to me, 'Amr b. Abi Qays narrated to us, from Simak b. Harb; among them Muhammad b. Bishr b. Bashir al-Aslami, and he is one of the most esteemed trustworthy narrators."],[8224,"From Ziyad b. 'Ilaqah; among them Isra'il b. Yunus al-Sabi'i."],[8226,"\"For every disease there is a remedy; when the remedy for the disease is applied, it heals by Allah's permission ﷻ.\""],[8227,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, Allah has not sent down a disease or created a disease except that He has also sent down or created a cure for it. He has made it known to those who know it and unknown to those who do not know it, except for death.\" They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is death?\" He said, \"It is 'as-sam'\""],[8228,"That a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, my brother is complaining of his stomach.' He said, 'Give him honey to drink.' He said, 'I gave him honey to drink, but it only increased his looseness.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said on the third or fourth occasion, 'Allah has spoken the truth, and your brother's stomach has lied.' So he went and gave him honey to drink, and he was cured."],[8229,"Sulayman, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ , when he stood in his prayer place, would see a tree growing in front of him and would say, 'What is your name?' It would say, 'Such-and-such.' He would say, 'For what purpose are you?' It would say, 'For such-and-such.' If it was for a remedy, he would write it down; if it was for planting, it would be planted. While he was praying one day, he saw a tree growing in front of him and said to it, 'What is your name?' It said, 'Al-Kharnub (carob).' He said, 'For what purpose are you?' It said, 'For the destruction of this house.' Sulayman ﷺ said, 'O Allah, conceal my death from the jinn so that mankind may know that the jinn do not know the unseen.' He said, 'So he carved it into a staff and leaned upon it.' He said, 'Then the woodworm ate it, and he fell down. They found him dead after a year. Thus it became clear to mankind that if the jinn had known the unseen, they would not have remained for a year in the humiliating punishment.' \"And Ibn 'Abbas used to recite it thus: 'So the jinn thanked the woodworm, and it used to bring water to it wherever it was.'\""],[8230,"He said: O Messenger of Allah, spells we used to treat with and medicines we used to heal with, do they repel anything from Allah's decree? He said: \"They are from Allah's decree.\""],[8231,"\"You should use cow's milk, for it grazes on every tree, and it is a cure for every disease.\""],[8232,"The Prophet ﷺ said: \"You should use the two cures: honey and the Qur'an.\""],[8233,"When one of you is feverish, let him pour cold water over himself at dawn, three nights."],[8234,"From his mother, the wife of al-Zubayr."],[8235,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Fever is from the intense heat of Hell, so cool it with water.\""],[8236,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Indeed, fever is a portion of fire, so cool it down with water.\" Authenticated."],[8237,"\"You should use black myrobalan and drink it, for it is a tree among the trees of Paradise. Its taste is bitter, and it is a cure for every disease.\""],[8238,"I visited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with some women, and there was a waterskin hanging, its water dripping on him from the severity of the heat of the fever he was experiencing. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate to Allah to remove it from you.' He said: \"The people most severely tried are the prophets, then those closest to them.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8239,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"You should consume cow's milk, its fat, and avoid its meat, for its milk and fat are a remedy and healing, but its meat is a disease.\""],[8240,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me, \"With what do you purge yourself?\" I said, 'With spurge.' He said, \"Hot, hot.\" She said, 'Then I purged myself with senna.' He said, \"If there were a cure for death in anything, it would be in senna.\""],[8241,"\"Treat pleurisy with Indian costus and olive oil.\""],[8242,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, when they said, 'We feared that what the Messenger of Allah has is pleurisy': \"It is from Satan, and Allah would not give him power over me.\""],[8243,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ died from pleurisy'"],[8244,"\"The flank pain is the vein of the kidney; when it stirs, it hurts its owner. Treat it with burned water and honey.\""],[8245,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was cupped, gave the cupper his wage, and had medicine dropped in his nose."],[8246,"A woman came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, this son of mine has quinsy.\" He said, \"Do not cauterize the throats of your children. Use Indian costus and wars, and insufflate it into his nose.\" Hammad and Yahya are weak."],[8247,"I heard the Prophet of Allah ﷺ prescribing olive oil and wars for pleurisy. Qatadah said, \"He is treated by pouring medicine into the side of his mouth that is affected.\""],[8248,"The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Aisha while a woman with her child whose nostrils were bleeding was with her. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"What is the matter with this one?\" They said, \"He has quinsy.\" He said, \"Woe to you! Do not kill your children. Any woman whose child has quinsy should take Indian costus, grind it with water, and then insufflate it into his nose.\" Then he ordered Aisha, and she did it for the child, and he was cured."],[8249,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was a young servant saying, \"The tree and the ajwah date are from Paradise.\""],[8250,"When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, they brought out to the Prophet ﷺ dates from their dates, and they began eating them. He named those dates by their names, and they said, \"We are not more knowledgeable of their names than you, O Messenger of Allah.\" Then he said to a man, \"Feed us from the remainder of the muqarrabin.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"This is barni, and it is the best of your dates, and it is a remedy with no disease in it.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8251,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon me with Ali, and he was convalescing. She said, \"We had hanging clusters of grapes.\" She said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and ate, and Ali stood and ate. The Prophet ﷺ said, 'Gently, O Ali, for you are convalescing.' Ali sat down. Then I prepared chard and barley for them, and the Prophet ﷺ said, 'From this, eat now, O Ali.'\""],[8252,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"You should take the beneficial disliked talbinah. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, it cleanses the stomach of one of you just as one of you washes dirt from his face with water.\" She said, \"When any of the Prophet's ﷺ family was ill, the pot would remain on the fire until one of two outcomes occurred, either death or recovery.\""],[8253,"From his grandmother Salma, the servant of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said, \"No man complained to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of a pain in his head except that he said, 'Be cupped,' nor of a pain in his feet except that he said, 'Dye them with henna.'\""],[8254,"The Prophet ﷺ prescribed for them for sciatica to take the fat tail of a ram that is neither large nor small, melt it, divide it into three parts, and drink one part each day."],[8255,"The best of your kohl is ithmid, for it clears the vision and grows the hair."],[8256,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to apply ithmid kohl three times before sleeping every night."],[8257,"A boil appeared on my neck. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so he said: “Open it and do not leave it to eat the flesh and suck the blood.”"],[8259,"I fell ill and my family withheld everything from me, even water. I became thirsty one night when no one was with me, so I approached a hanging waterskin and drank a sip from it. I arose healthy, and I kept recognizing the health of that sip in my body.” He said: ʿAʾishah used to say: “Do not withhold anything from a sick person.”"],[8260,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “In it there is healing.”"],[8261,"“I never passed by a gathering of angels except they commanded me to practice cupping.”"],[8262,"“He used to be cupped on the seventeenth, nineteenth, and twenty-first.”"],[8263,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Cupping on an empty stomach is better, and in it there is blessing and healing. It increases intellect and increases the memory of the memorizer. Be cupped, with the blessing of Allah Almighty, on Thursday, and avoid Friday, Saturday, and Sunday. Be cupped on Monday and Tuesday, for it is the day on which Allah healed Ayyub from affliction. No leprosy or leukoderma appears except on Wednesday and Wednesday night, and Ayyub was only afflicted on Wednesday.” The narrators of this hadith are all trustworthy except this ʿUthman b. Jaʿfar, for I do not know him to be either reliable or weak."],[8264,"“Whoever is cupped on Wednesday or Saturday and then sees a white patch, let him blame no one but himself.”"],[8265,"Abu Hind cupped the Prophet ﷺ at Wajj for a pain he had, and he said: “If there is any good in what you treat yourselves with, it is cupping.”"],[8266,"“How excellent a remedy cupping is: it removes blood, clears the eyesight, and lightens the back.”"],[8267,"“Do not force your sick to eat and drink, for Allah Almighty feeds them and gives them drink.”"],[8268,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade impure medicine.”"],[8269,"“A physician mentioned medicine in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that a frog is used in medicine, so the Prophet ﷺ forbade killing it.”"],[8270,"The Prophet Muhammad ﷺ said, \"Every person has a vein in their head that is affected by leprosy, and when it becomes active, Allah sends them a cold, so do not treat it.\" It appears to be a subject."],[8271,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and before him were dates and bread. He said, “Come near and eat.” I began eating from the dates. He said, “You eat dates while you have ophthalmia?” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I am chewing from the other side.” The Prophet ﷺ smiled."],[8272,"“Beware of sitting in the sun, for it wears out the garment, makes the body odor foul, and brings out hidden disease.”"],[8273,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and in his hand was a quince. He tossed it to me and said, “Take it, Abu Muhammad, for it strengthens the heart.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8274,"When a person complained of something, or had a sore, or was wounded, the Prophet ﷺ would say with his finger like this—and he placed his forefinger on the ground then raised it—: “In the name of Allah, the dust of our earth with the saliva of some of us, our sick is healed by the permission of our Lord.”"],[8275,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to seek ruqyah for the evil eye.”"],[8276,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that Gabriel ﷺ came to him while he was feverish and said: “In the name of Allah, I perform ruqyah for you from everything that harms you, from every envy and envier, and every distress; and the name of Allah heals you.”"],[8277,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ , when a Bedouin came and said, \"O Messenger of Allah, I have a brother who is suffering from a pain.\" The Prophet ﷺ asked, \"What kind of pain does he have?\" The Bedouin replied, \"He has a swelling.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Bring him to me.\" The Bedouin brought his brother, and the Prophet ﷺ placed his hand on the affected area and recited the opening chapter of the Quran and four verses from the end of Surah Al-Baqarah: \"Your God is one God, there is no god but Him, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate\" (Quran 2:163) and the verse of the Throne (Ayat al-Kursi) and a verse from Surah Al-Imran: \"Allah bears witness that there is no god but Him\" (Quran 3:18), and a verse from Surah Al-A'raf: \"Indeed, your Lord is Allah, who created the heavens and the earth\" (Quran 7:54), and the last verses of Surah Al-Mu'minun: \"So exalted is Allah, the true King\" (Quran 23:116), and a verse from Surah Al-Jinn: \"And that, our Lord, is exalted in might\" (Quran 72:3), and ten verses from the beginning of Surah As-Saffat and three verses from the end of Surah Al-Hashr, and \"Say: He is Allah, the One\" (Quran 112:1) and the two protective Surahs (Surah Al-Ikhlas and Surah Al-Falaq). The man stood up as if he had never experienced any pain before.[1]"],[8278,"I heard Sahl b. Hunayf say: We passed by a flood stream, and I entered it and bathed in it. I came out with a fever. That was reported to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “Tell Abu Thabit to seek refuge.” He said: I said, “O my master, are incantations valid?” He said, “There is no incantation except for the evil eye, fever, or a sting.”"],[8279,"“There is no ruqyah except from the evil eye, fever, or blood that does not stop.”"],[8280,"When he suffered from ophthalmia, or one of his family or companions did, he would supplicate with these words: “O Allah, let me enjoy my sight and make it my heir, show me my vengeance upon the enemy, and help me against those who wronged me.”"],[8281,"Whoever says upon hearing a sneeze, “Praise be to Allah in every situation,” will not suffer toothache or earache."],[8282,"He used to teach them, for pains and fever, to say: “In the name of Allah, the Great. We seek refuge in Allah, the Magnificent, from the evil of a gushing vein and from the evil of the heat of the Fire.”"],[8283,"She was called al-Shifa’. She used to perform ruqyah for namlah (a skin ailment). The Prophet ﷺ said, “Teach it to Hafsah.”"],[8284,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw in the house of Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, a slave girl with a mark on her face, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"She has been affected by the evil eye, so perform ruqyah for her.\""],[8285,"A man from the Ansar called Amr b. Hazm came, and he used to perform ruqyah for snakebites. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you have forbidden ruqyah, but I perform ruqyah for snakebites.\" He said: \"Recite it to me.\" So he recited it to him, and he said: \"There is no harm in this; these are covenants.\" He said: And my maternal uncle from the Ansar came, and he used to perform ruqyah for scorpion stings. He said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you have forbidden ruqyah, but I perform ruqyah for scorpion stings.\" He said: \"Whoever is able to benefit his brother, let him do so.\""],[8286,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The nations were presented to me in a vision at the appointed time, and I saw all of them, and I was amazed by their large number and their dignity. They filled the plains and the mountains. It was said to me, 'O Muhammad, are you pleased?' I said, 'Yes, my Lord.' He said, 'For you, there are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without being held accountable. They are the ones who do not practice Aatrar (cauterization) or seek Ruqyah (healing through charms), and they rely upon their Lord.' Ukkashah bin Mihsan stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah that He may make me one of them.' So he supplicated for him. Then another man stood up and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah that He may make me one of them.' He said, 'Ukkashah has preceded you in this.'\""],[8287,"\"He has not put his trust in Allah who seeks ruqyah or cauterization.\""],[8288,"Whoever says in the evening: 'I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He has created' three times, no snake will harm him that night. He said: And when someone from his family was stung, he would say: 'Did he say the words?'"],[8289,"\"He was stung by a scorpion in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet ﷺ performed ruqyah for him and wiped him with his hand.\""],[8290,"Whoever visits a sick person whose time of death has not yet come, and says in his presence seven times: 'I ask Allah the Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you and grant you well-being,' Allah will grant him recovery from that illness."],[8291,"Three people came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"A companion of ours is sick, and cauterization has been prescribed for us. Should we cauterize him?\" He remained silent. Then they repeated, and on the third time he said: \"Cauterize him if you wish, or if you wish, heat stones and apply them.\""],[8292,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade cauterization, so we cauterized ourselves and we did not succeed and did not prosper.\""],[8293,"\"Ubayy b. Ka'b was shot in his median cubital vein, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a physician to him, who cauterized him.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8294,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cauterized As'ad b. Zurarah for a thorn injury.\" On the condition of Bukhari and Muslim."],[8295,"Sa'd b. Mu'adh was shot in his median cubital vein, and the Prophet ﷺ cauterized it with his own hand using a broad arrowhead. He said: Then it became swollen, so he cauterized it a second time."],[8296,"\"Abu Talhah cauterized me while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us, and I was not forbidden from it.\""],[8297,"Whoever hangs a shell amulet, may Allah not grant him peace; and whoever hangs a talisman, may Allah not complete [his affair] for him."],[8298,"From Zaynab, the wife of 'Abdullah, that she had a redness in her face, and an old woman entered upon her and recited a ruqya over her into a thread and tied it on her. Ibn Mas'ud entered, saw it on her, and said: 'What is this?' She said: 'I sought ruqya for the redness.' He stretched out his hand and cut it, then said: 'The family of 'Abdullah is indeed free of need from shirk.' She said: Then he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us: \"Indeed ruqā, talismans, and tawliya are shirk.\"' He said: I said: 'What is tawliya?' He said: 'Tawliya is that which arouses men.'"],[8299,"Talismans are what is hung before calamity descends; as for what is hung after it, it is not a talisman."],[8300,"They mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ that it is from the work of Shaytan."],[8301,"While we were standing with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, a man came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the duration of hope for your Ummah?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ remained silent until he asked three times, then the man turned away. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'You have asked me about something no one from my Ummah has asked me. The hope of my Ummah is a hundred years.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, is there any sign, verse, or mark for that?' He said: 'Yes: peltings, sinkings, earthquakes, and the sending of bridled devils upon the people.'"],[8302,"I indeed know two groups of people of religion from the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ in the Fire: a people who say, 'If our first ones were misguided, what is the matter with five prayers in the day and night? It is only two prayers: 'Asr and Fajr'; and a people who say, 'Faith is only words, even if he commits zina and even if he kills.'"],[8303,"I heard 'Awf b. Malik al-Ashja'i say: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Tabuk while he was in a leather tent. He said to me: 'O 'Awf, count six things before the Hour: my death, then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis, then a mortality that will take you like the qu'as of sheep, then the abundance of wealth among you so that a man will be given a hundred dinars and remain discontented, then a tribulation that will not leave any house of the Arabs but it will enter it, then a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar, but they will betray you and come to you under eighty banners, twelve thousand.' Al-Walid b. Muslim said: We discussed this hadith with a shaykh from the shuyukh of the people of al-Madinah regarding his saying 'then the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis,' and the shaykh said: Sa'id al-Maqburi informed me from Abu Hurayrah that he used to narrate these six from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he would say instead of 'the conquest of Bayt al-Maqdis': 'the construction of Bayt al-Maqdis.'"],[8304,"I arrived from al-Sham to al-Madinah seeking knowledge, and I heard Mu'adh b. Jabal say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Those who love one another for the sake of Allah will have pulpits of light on the Day of Resurrection; the martyrs will envy them.'"],[8305,"'The construction of Bayt al-Maqdis is the destruction of Yathrib, the destruction of Yathrib is the coming of the great battle, the coming of the great battle is the conquest of Constantinople, and the conquest of Constantinople is the emergence of the Dajjal.' He said: Then Mu'adh struck the shoulder of 'Umar b. al-Khattab and said: 'By Allah, that is true just as you are sitting.'"],[8306,"You will make a secure peace with the Romans, then you and they will campaign together against an enemy beyond them, and you will be victorious, take spoils, and return, until you camp at a meadow with hills. Then a man from the Romans will say, 'The cross has prevailed,' and a man from the Muslims will say, 'Rather, Allah has prevailed.' They will exchange these words between them. Then a Muslim will rise against their cross while they are not far from him and smash it; the Romans will rise against the one who smashed their cross and kill him; the Muslims will rise to their weapons and be killed. Allah ﷻ will honor that band of Muslims with martyrdom. The Romans will say to their leader: 'We have sufficed you against the might of the Arabs.' Then they will betray and gather for the great battle. They will come to you under eighty banners, under each banner twelve thousand."],[8307,"The Romans will make a secure peace with you, then you and they will campaign together against an enemy, and you will be victorious, remain safe, and conquer. Then you will be granted victory at a meadow, and a man from the Christians will raise the cross for them. A man from the Muslims will become angry, stand up to them, and smash the cross. At that, the Romans will become angry and gather for the great battle."],[8308,"Constantinople will surely be conquered, and how excellent is its commander, and how excellent is that army."],[8309,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ writing, when a man said: 'Which of the two cities will be conquered first, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The city of Heraclius,' meaning Constantinople."],[8310,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Ka'b b. 'Ujrah: 'May Allah protect you, O Ka'b, from the rule of the foolish.' He said: 'And what is the rule of the foolish, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'Rulers who will come after me, who do not follow my guidance and do not practice my Sunnah. Whoever believes their lies and helps them in their wrongdoing, those are not of me and I am not of them, and they will not come to my Pond. But whoever does not believe their lies and does not help them in their wrongdoing, those are of me and I am of them, and they will come to my Pond. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and prayer is a means of drawing near'—or he said, 'a proof.' 'O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, no flesh that grows from unlawful earnings will ever enter Paradise; the Fire is more deserving of it. O Ka'b b. 'Ujrah, people set out in the morning: one sells his soul and sets it free'—or he said, 'and destroys it.'"],[8311,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the expedition of Tabuk, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a leather tent, I passed by and he heard my voice. He said: 'O 'Awf b. Malik, enter!' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, all of me or part of me?' He said: 'Rather, all of you.' He said: So I entered. He said: 'O 'Awf, count six things before the Hour.' I said: 'What are they, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'The death of the Messenger of Allah.' 'Awf wept. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Say: one.' I said: 'One.' Then he said: 'And the conquest of Jerusalem. Say: two.' I said: 'Two.' He said: 'And a death that will occur among my nation like the sudden death of sheep. Say: three.' I said: 'Three.' He said: 'And the world will be opened to them until a man is given a hundred and he despises it. Say: four.' I said: 'Four.' 'And a trial that will not leave any Muslim except that it will enter his house. Say: five.' I said: 'Five.' 'And a truce between you and the Banu al-Asfar. They will come to you under eighty banners, each banner with twelve thousand. Then they will betray you after the time equal to a woman's pregnancy.' He said: When the year of 'Amwas came, they claimed that 'Awf b. Malik said to Mu'adh b. Jabal: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Count six things before the Hour.\" Three of them have occurred and three remain.' Mu'adh said: 'This has a duration, but there are five that I warn you of. Whoever encounters any of them and is able to die, let him die: that mutual cursing will appear on the pulpits, Allah's wealth will be given for falsehood and slander and shedding blood without right, kinship ties will be severed, and a servant will wake up not knowing whether he is astray or guided.'"],[8312,"He said: 'O Abu Dharr! How will you act when people are so hungry that you cannot rise from your mosque to your bed, nor from your bed to your mosque?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'You should be chaste.' Then he said: 'How will you act when people die until a house is worth a servant?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'You should be patient.' Then he said: 'How will you act when people attack until the people of ranks raid with blood?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He said: 'You should join those you belong to.' I said: 'What if it comes upon me?' He said: 'If you fear that the flash of the sword will dazzle you, throw a part of your cloak over your face; he will bear your sin and his sin, and he will be among the people of the Fire.' I said: 'Should I not carry weapons?' He said: 'Then you would share in it.'"],[8313,"He said: 'O Abu Dharr!' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah, at your service.' He said: 'How will you be when people are struck by hunger such that you come to your mosque and cannot return to your bed, and you come to your bed and cannot rise to your mosque?' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best'—or 'what Allah and His Messenger have chosen for me.' He said: 'You must be chaste.' Then he said: 'O Abu Dharr!' I said: 'At your service, O Messenger of Allah, at your service.' He said: 'How will you be when you see the stones of al-Zayt marked with blood?' I said: 'What Allah and His Messenger have chosen.' He said: 'Join those you belong to'—or he said, 'stick to those you belong to.' I said: 'Should I not take my sword and put it on my shoulder?' He said: 'Then you would share in it.' I said: 'What do you command me?' He said: 'Stay in your house.' I said: 'What if someone enters my house?' He said: 'If you fear that the flash of the sword will dazzle you, throw your cloak over your face; he will bear his sin and your sin.'"],[8314,"This nation will not fail Allah for half a day."],[8315,"From Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, ؓ ."],[8316,"A time will come upon you when no one will be saved except one who calls with the supplication of a drowning person."],[8317,"He stayed with 'Abd Allah b. Hawalah al-Azdi. He said to me, while he was staying in my house: 'May your mother be bereft of you! Is it not enough for Ibn Hawalah that a hundred flows to him every year?' Then he said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us around Madinah on foot to raid. We returned having gained nothing, and hardship was visible on our faces. He stood among us as a preacher and said: \"O Allah, do not entrust them to me, lest I be too weak for them; do not entrust them to themselves, lest they fail; and do not entrust them to people, lest they prefer themselves over them.\" It is authentic."],[8318,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them while clusters of dates were hanging, and one cluster had bad dates. He had a stick. He poked the cluster with the stick and said: 'If the Lord of this charity had willed, he would have given in charity something better than it. The owner of this charity will eat bad dates on the Day of Resurrection.' Then he turned to us and said: 'By Allah, O people of Madinah, you will leave it tamed for forty years for the 'awafi.' We said: 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Do you know what the 'awafi are?' They said: 'No.' He said: 'Birds and beasts.'"],[8319,"Madinah will be left in the best state it ever was, with birds and beasts eating from it."],[8320,"You will fight the Arabian Peninsula, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will fight the Romans, and Allah will grant you victory over them. Then you will fight Persia, and Allah will grant you victory over it. Then you will fight the Dajjal, and Allah will grant you victory over him."],[8321,"«The great battle, the conquest of Constantinople, and the emergence of the Dajjal will occur within seven months.»"],[8322,"I was in Kufa in my house when I heard at the door: \"Peace be upon you. May I enter?\" I said, \"And upon you be peace. Enter.\" When he entered, it was Abdullah b. Mas'ud. I said, \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what hour is this for a visit?\" And that was at the time of the midday heat. He said, \"The day became long for me, so I remembered someone with whom I could converse.\" Then he began to narrate to me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I narrated to him. He said, then he started to narrate to me and said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There will be a tribulation in which the one lying down is better than the one reclining, and the one reclining is better than the one sitting, and the one sitting is better than the one standing, and the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one running.'\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and when is that?\" He said, \"That is in the days of harj, when a man does not trust his companion.\" I said, \"What do you command me to do if I live to see that time?\" He said, \"Restrain yourself and your hand, and enter your house.\" He said, I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you think if someone enters upon me in my house?\" He said, \"Then enter your room.\" He said, I said, \"What do you think if someone enters upon me in my room?\" He said, \"Then enter your mosque and do like this,\" and he grasped his right hand on his wrist, \"and say: My Lord is Allah, until you die upon that.\""],[8323,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me for some need, then he met me on one of the roads of Madinah, then he climbed Uhud and I climbed with him. He turned his face toward Madinah and said something to it, then he said: \"Woe to its mother, or mercy on its mother, a town whose people will leave it when it is at its most fruitful, when the birds of prey and beasts will eat its fruit, and the Dajjal will not enter it, if Allah wills. Every time he wants to enter it, an angel with an unsheathed sword will meet him at every pass of its passes and prevent him from it.\""],[8324,"Regarding this verse: {And We will surely let them taste the nearer punishment before the greater punishment} [al-Sajdah: 21], he said: \"The calamities of this world: the Romans and the seizure, or the smoke.\" He said, then something was cut off, so he said: \"It is the Dajjal.\""],[8325,"The Hour will not be established until there are ten signs: a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula, the Dajjal, the smoke, the descent of Jesus son of Mary, Gog and Magog, the Beast, the rising of the sun from its west, and a fire that will emerge from the depths of Aden that will drive people to the gathering place, gathering the small ants and the ants."],[8326,"I heard Umar b. al-Khattab say, \"By the Lord of the Ka'bah, I know when the Arabs will be destroyed: when their affairs are taken over by one who did not accompany the Messenger ﷺ and did not experience the affairs of the pre-Islamic era.\""],[8327,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"The signs will be after the two hundred.\""],[8328,"«How will you be when there is a tribulation in which the best of its people is every wealthy person who remains hidden?» He said, I said, \"By Allah, it is nothing but the giving of someone who is asleep; we throw here and there and shoot at every target.\" He said, \"Will you not be like the son of the labun, neither a riding camel to be ridden nor a milking camel to be milked?\""],[8329,"Al-Harith b. Abi Rabi'ah and Abdullah b. Safwan entered, and I was with them, upon Umm Salamah, and they asked her about the army that would be swallowed up by the earth. That was in the days of Ibn al-Zubayr. Umm Salamah said, \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A seeker of refuge will seek refuge in the Sanctuary, and an army will be sent against him. When they are in a desert plain of the earth, they will be swallowed up.'\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about the one who goes out unwillingly?\" He said, \"He will be swallowed up with them, but he will be resurrected according to his intention on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then she said, \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A seeker of refuge will seek refuge in the House.'\""],[8330,"«An army will surely head for this House to attack it, until when they are in a desert plain of the earth, the middle of them will be swallowed up, and the first of them will call out to the last of them, and they will all be swallowed up completely, except for the fugitive who will report about them.» A man said to him, \"I testify that you have not lied about your grandfather, and I testify that your grandfather did not lie about Hafsah, and I testify that Hafsah did not lie about the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[8331,"\"Troops will not cease to attack this House until an army of them are swallowed up by the earth.\" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2878)"],[8332,"«There will not remain on the face of the earth any house of mud or hair but Allah will bring the word of Islam upon them, either with the might of a mighty one or the humiliation of a lowly one. Either Allah honors them and makes them from its people, or He humiliates them and they do not adhere to it.»"],[8333,"«My community will split into seventy-some sects. The greatest of them in size is a sect of people who measure matters by their own opinion, thereby forbidding what is lawful and permitting what is forbidden.»"],[8334,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"This matter (Islam) will reach the farthest regions of the day and night, and Allah will not leave a house of mud or hair, but He will make this religion enter it by either honouring a mighty person or humiliating a disgraced one. Allah will honour the Muslims with Islam and humiliate the disbelievers with kufr.\" Tameem ad-Dari used to say: \"I have realized this in my family. Whoever among them accepts Islam will find goodness, honor, and superiority. And whoever remains a disbeliever will experience humiliation, inferiority, and jizyah (tax).\""],[8335,"\"You are in a time in which the one who speaks the truth is better than the one who remains silent, and the one who stands up is better than the one who sits. After you will come a time in which the one who remains silent is better than the one who speaks, and the one who sits is better than the one who stands.\" He said: A man said, \"O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, how can a matter be such that whoever takes it today is guided and whoever takes it after today is astray?\" He said, \"You have already done it. Consider this by two men who passed by a people committing sins. Both of them disapproved, but one of you remained silent and so was safe, while the other spoke and said, 'You are doing such-and-such.' They seized him and took him to their ruler, and he did not cease—or they did not cease—until he adopted their ways and acted as they did.\""],[8336,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A man from my Ummah will be given allegiance between the Rukn and the Maqam, just like the number of the people of Badr. Then, the tribes of Iraq and the replacements from Sham (Greater Syria) will come to him, and an army from Sham will also join them. When they are in the desert, they will be swallowed by the earth, and then a man from the Quraysh, with his uncles as leaders, will defeat them by the will of Allah.\" It is said that on that day, the one who is disgraced is the one who fails to acquire any wealth except that of a dog. Abu Al-Awam Imran's weakness was not alone, and he was an outsider."],[8337,"\"The deprived one is the one who is deprived of the spoils of a dog, even if it is a rope. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, their women will surely be sold on the steps of Damascus, so much so that a woman will be returned from a piece of jewelry found on her leg.\""],[8338,"I entered the mosque and there was a circle as if their heads had been cut off. Among them was a man narrating, and it was Hudhayfah. He said: They used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the good, but I used to ask him about the evil, so that I might know it and avoid it. I knew that the good would not escape me. He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be evil after this good in which we are?\" He said, \"O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah Almighty and act according to what is in it.\" I repeated my question, and on the third time he said, \"Trial and discord.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be good after that evil?\" He said, \"O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of Allah Almighty and act according to what is in it.\" Then I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will there be good after that evil?\" He said, \"Trials at whose gates are callers to the Fire. That you should die while biting onto the stump of a tree is better for you than following any of them.\""],[8339,"\"O people, trials are overshadowing you like pieces of a dark night. O people, in them—or from them—a sheep-owner who eats from the head of his sheep, and a man behind the mountain pass holding the rein of his horse and eating from his sword.\""],[8340,"I went out to Kufa at the time Tustar was conquered to bring mules from it. I entered the mosque and there was a group of men whom you would recognize, when you saw them, as men from the Hijaz. He said: I said, \"Who is this?\" The people stared at me and said, \"Do you not know this man? This is Hudhayfah, the keeper of the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said: Hudhayfah said, \"The people used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the good, but I used to ask him about the evil.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you think that after this good which Allah has given us, there will be evil as there was before it?\" He said, \"Yes.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the protection from that?\" He said, \"The sword.\" I said, \"Is there any remnant for the sword?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He said: I said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"Then a truce on the basis of corruption.\" He said, \"A congregation on the basis of division. If Allah ﷻ has a caliph on that day, he will strike your back and take your wealth, so listen and obey. Otherwise, die biting onto the stump of a tree.\" He said: I said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"The Dajjal will emerge, and with him will be a river and a fire. Whoever falls into his fire will have his reward and his burden will be removed. Whoever falls into his river will have his burden made obligatory and his reward removed.\" I said, \"Then what?\" He said, \"Then it is only the establishment of the Hour.\""],[8341,"\"Indeed, for the trial there are pauses and fatigues. Whoever of you is able to die during its pauses, let him do so.\""],[8342,"\"Trials will be opened upon the earth like the horns of cattle.\" A veiled man passed by, and he said, \"This one on that day will be upon the truth.\" So I got up to him and took hold of the folds of his garment and said, \"Is it this one, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"This one.\" He said: And it was 'Uthman."],[8343,"He entered the house while 'Uthman was besieged in it, and he heard Abu Hurayrah asking 'Uthman for permission to speak. He permitted him, so he stood, praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"You will encounter after me a trial and discord,\" or he said, \"discord and trial.\" A speaker said to him, \"O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us?\" He said, \"Cling to the commander and his companions,\" indicating thereby 'Uthman."],[8344,"He said: Dates and fresh dates were brought near to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and they ate from them until they left nothing except a pit and what had no good in it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Do you know what this is? The best of you will go, one after another, until there remains of you only the like of this.\""],[8345,"\"You will surely be selected as dates are selected from the bowl. Your best ones will go, and your worst ones will remain. So die if you are able.\""],[8346,"\"You will surely be selected as dates are selected from the bowl. Your best ones will go, and your worst ones will remain, until there remain only those whom Allah pays no heed to. So die if you are able.\""],[8347,"\"You will surely be selected as dates are selected from the bowl. Your best ones will go, and your worst ones will remain, until there remain only those whom Allah pays no heed to. So die if you are able.\""],[8348,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The time will come when people will be sifted and only the refuse of people will remain; their covenants and trusts will be broken, and they will differ and be like this.\" And he interlaced his fingers. They said, \"So, how should we act, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"You should take what you know and leave what you deny, and you should adhere to your own affairs and leave the general matters.\" Sa'id bin Mansur said, \"The refuse of people is their despicability, and the meaning of his statement 'their covenants will be broken' is that they will not fulfill them.\""],[8349,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Hour will not come until Allah ﷻ takes away His chosen ones from the inhabitants of the earth, leaving only worthless people who do not enjoin good or forbid evil.”"],[8350,"\"The rulers will oppress you and Allah will punish them.\" According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8351,"“You will continue to be in good as long as you do not have rulers who do not see any right for you except when they wish.”"],[8352,"“If you live long, you will soon see people who go out in the morning under the wrath of Allah and return in the evening under His curse, holding in their hands whips like the tails of cows.”"],[8353,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say in his sermon: “O people, you will soon be able to distinguish the people of Paradise from the people of Hell,” or he said, “your best from your worst.” A man from among the people said: “By what, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “By good praise and bad praise. You are witnesses over one another.”"],[8354,"“There will be in the latter part of this nation men who ride on fine large saddles until they come to the doors of their mosques. Their women are clothed yet naked, with on their heads something like the humps of lean camels. Curse them, for they are cursed. If there were a nation behind you from among the nations, they would serve them just as the women of the nations before you served you.” I said to my father: “What are fine large saddles?” He said: “Large saddles.”"],[8355,"“There will come forth in this nation at the end of time men with whips like the tails of cows, who go out in the morning under the wrath of Allah and return in the evening under His anger.”"],[8356,"He mentioned tribulation and said: “A man will leave his house with his religion and return with none of it. He will come to a man who has no power to harm or benefit him or himself, and will swear to him by Allah, ‘You are this and that,’ and he will return without having fulfilled any of his need, and Allah will be angry with him.”"],[8357,"“By Him who sent me with the truth, this world will not come to an end until they are afflicted with sinking, metamorphosis, and casting.” They said: “And when is that, O Prophet of Allah, may our fathers and mothers be your ransom?” He said: “When you see women riding on saddles, female singers becoming many, false testimonies being given, Muslims drinking from vessels of the people of polytheism, gold and silver, men being satisfied with men and women with women, then prepare yourselves and be ready.” And he said thus with his hand and covered his face. Sulayman is al-Yamami, they weakened him, and the report is rejected."],[8358,"Five tribulations have been placed in this nation: a general tribulation, then a special tribulation, then a general tribulation, then a special tribulation, then the blind, deaf, all-encompassing tribulation will come, in which people become like cattle."],[8359,"I came upon Hudhayfah and Ibn Mas'ud while they were talking in the mosque. They mentioned tribulation, and Ibn Mas'ud said: “I never thought it would turn back on its heels without a cupping-glass of blood being spilled in it. A man will become a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, and a disbeliever in the morning and a believer in the evening. He will fight in tribulation today and Allah will kill him tomorrow; his heart will be overturned and his buttocks will rise.” Hudhayfah said: “You have spoken the truth; thus the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to us about tribulation.”"],[8360,"“There will come upon people a time when a man will be given a choice between incapacity and wickedness. Whoever reaches that time should choose incapacity over wickedness.”"],[8361,"“There will come upon people a time when a man will be given a choice between incapacity and wickedness. Whoever among you reaches that time should choose incapacity over wickedness.”"],[8362,"My community will be afflicted after me with tribulations like patches of dark night: a man will enter upon morning as a believer and enter upon evening as a disbeliever, and enter upon evening as a believer and enter upon morning as a disbeliever. Peoples will sell their religion for a paltry portion of this world."],[8363,"Before the Hour there will be tribulations like patches of dark night: a man will enter upon morning as a believer and enter upon evening as a disbeliever, and enter upon evening as a believer and enter upon morning as a disbeliever. Peoples will sell their religion for a paltry portion of this world."],[8364,"'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ said: \"O people, we used to know you when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was among us and revelation descended, and when there was among us news of you. Now the Prophet ﷺ has passed away and revelation has been raised, and we know you only by what I say to you. Whoever among you shows good, we think good of him and love him for it; whoever among you shows evil, we think evil of him and hate him for it. Your innermost secrets are between you and your Lord. A time came upon me when I thought that whoever recited the Quran desired thereby Allah, exalted be He, and what is with Him, but it has been imagined to me latterly that a people recite it desiring what is with people. So desire what is with Allah by your recitation and your deeds. By Allah, I do not send my agents to strike your skins or take your wealth, but I send them to teach you your religion and your sunnahs, to act justly among you, and to distribute your spoils among you. Whoever has any of that done to him, let him raise it to me, for by Him in whose hand is the soul of 'Umar, I will exact retribution for him from the agent.\" Then 'Amr b. al-'As jumped up and said: \"O Commander of the Believers, do you think that if a man among the Muslims is in charge of a flock and he disciplines some of his flock, you would exact retribution from him?\" He said: \"And why should I not exact retribution from him? For I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ exact retribution from himself. Do not strike them and thus humiliate them, do not withhold their rights and thus make them disbelieve, do not compel them and thus tempt them, and do not send them into the thickets and thus lose them.\""],[8365,"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near. Die, if you can."],[8366,"The tribulation erupted while the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ numbered ten thousand, and none of them remained aloof from it except forty men. Two hundred and forty-some men of the people of Badr stood with 'Ali, among them Abu Ayyub, Sahl b. Hunayf, and 'Ammar b. Yasir."],[8367,"The affair will only increase in severity, wealth will only increase in abundance, and the Hour will not arise except upon the worst of His creation."],[8368,"Before you there will be tribulations like patches of dark night: a man will enter upon morning as a believer and enter upon evening as a disbeliever, and enter upon evening as a believer and enter upon morning as a disbeliever. The one sitting in them is better than the one standing, the one standing in them is better than the one walking, and the one walking in them is better than the one hastening toward them.\" They said: \"What do you command us, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Be the saddle cushions of your houses.\""],[8369,"\"There will be tribulations, and then there will be a tribulation in which the one sitting is better than the one standing, the one standing is better than the one walking, and the one walking is better than the one hastening toward it. When it descends, whoever has camels, let him join his camels; whoever has sheep, let him join his sheep; and whoever has land, let him join his land.\" A man said to him: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if he has no camels, sheep, or land?\" He said: \"Let him take a stone and strike with it the edge of his sword, then let him escape if he can.\" Then he said three times: \"O Allah, have I conveyed?\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, what if I am compelled until I am taken to one of the two rows, or one of the two parties, and a man shoots me with an arrow or strikes me with a sword and kills me?\" He said: \"He will bear his sin and your sin, and he will be among the companions of the Fire.\" He said it three times. Sahih."],[8370,"There will be a tribulation: the one sitting in it is better than the one standing, the one standing in it is better than the one walking, the one walking in it is better than the one hastening, and the one hastening is better than the one riding, and the one riding is better than the one galloping."],[8371,"The affair will only increase in severity, religion will only recede, people will only become more miserly, the Hour will not arise except upon the worst of people, and there is no Mahdi except Jesus son of Mary."],[8372,"Time will only increase in severity, people will only increase in miserliness, and the Hour will not arise except upon the worst of people."],[8373,"\"A time will come upon people when they gather in mosques but there will be no true believer among them.\""],[8374,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey. When we returned, the people hastened and entered Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ asked about them and was told that they had hastened to Madinah. He said: \"It may be that they will leave it when it is at its finest. Would that I knew when a fire will emerge from Mount Warraq whose light will make the necks of Bactrian camels at Busra appear like lamps, like the light of day.\""],[8375,"A fire will emerge from Habs Sayl, moving slowly; it rests at night and travels by day, going forth in the morning and returning in the evening. It will be said: 'The fire has set out in the morning, O people, so depart early!' The fire will say: 'O people, take your midday rest!' It will be said: 'The fire has returned in the evening, O people, so return!' Whomever it overtakes, it consumes."],[8376,"He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked us shortly after he arrived: 'Where is Habs Sayl?' We said: 'We do not know.' Then a man from Banu Sulaym passed by me and I asked: 'Where have you come from?' He said: 'From Habs Sayl.' I called for my sandals and went down to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you asked us about Habs Sayl and we had no knowledge of it. This man passed by me and I asked him, and he claimed that his family is there.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: 'Where is your family?' He said: 'At Habs Sayl.' He said: 'Move your family away, for a fire is about to emerge from it that will illuminate the necks of camels in Busra.'"],[8377,"The Hour will not be established until a fire emerges from the land of the Hijaz that will illuminate the necks of camels in Busra."],[8378,"It was said to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas: 'Will you not fight? For you are one of the people of the Shura and you have more right to this matter than others.' He said: 'I will not fight until they bring me a sword that has two eyes, a tongue, and two lips, that can distinguish the disbeliever from the believer. I have already striven in jihad and I know what jihad is. I will not risk my own self if there is a man better than me.'"],[8379,"The Ummah will continue to adhere to the Shari'ah as long as three things do not appear among them: as long as knowledge is not taken away from them, the children of wickedness do not multiply among them, and the saqqarun do not appear among them. They said: 'What are the saqqarun, O Messenger of Allah?' He said: 'People who will be in the last age; their greeting among themselves when they meet will be mutual cursing.'"],[8380,"My Ummah is an Ummah upon whom mercy is shown; there is no punishment upon it in the Hereafter. Allah has placed its punishment in this world: killing, earthquakes, and tribulations."],[8381,"Thunderbolts will increase as the Hour approaches. A people will wake up and say: 'Who was struck by lightning last night?' They will say: 'So-and-so and so-and-so were struck.'"],[8382,"It was said: 'O Abu 'Abd Allah, what do you command us when those who pray fight each other?' He said: 'I command you to look for the farthest room in your house and enter it. If someone enters upon you, say: \"Here, bear my sin and your sin,\" and you will be like the son of Adam.'"],[8383,"The Hour will not be established until some tribes of the Arabs are swallowed up by the earth, and it will be said: 'Who remains of the Banu so-and-so?'"],[8384,"In my Ummah there will be sinking, metamorphosis, and casting (of stones)."],[8385,"It is as if I can see a rider who has dismounted among you, coming between the orphans and widows and what Allah has granted as spoils to their fathers, saying: 'The wealth is ours.'"],[8386,"We were sitting with 'Abd Allah b. Mas'ud when his doorkeeper came and said: 'The prayer has been established.' He stood up and we stood with him. We entered the mosque and saw the people bowing in the front of the mosque. He said the takbir, bowed, and walked; we did the same as he did. A man passed by hurrying and said: 'Peace be upon you, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman.' He replied: 'Allah has spoken the truth and His Messenger ﷺ has conveyed.' When we finished praying, he returned and went into his family. We sat in his place waiting for him to come out. Some of us said to others: 'Who among you will ask him?' Tariq said: 'I will ask him.' So Tariq asked him: 'A man greeted you and you replied: \"Allah has spoken the truth and His Messenger ﷺ has conveyed.\"' 'Abd Allah said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Before the Hour comes, greeting will be limited to the elite, and commerce will spread so much that a woman will help her husband in trade, and a man will take his wealth to the farthest parts of the earth and return saying: 'I did not profit anything.'\"'"],[8387,"One day I entered the mosque with 'Abd Allah, and the people were in bowing. A man passed by and greeted him, and he said, 'Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth; Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.' I asked him about that, and he said: 'The Hour will not come until mosques are taken as thoroughfares, until a man greets another only because he knows him, until a woman trades together with her husband, and until horses and women become expensive and then become cheap, not becoming expensive again until the Day of Resurrection.'"],[8388,"The best of people during tribulations is a man who takes hold of his horse's rein—or he said, its halter—behind the enemies of Allah, frightening them and they frightening him, or a man who withdraws in his desert, fulfilling the right of Allah Almighty that is upon him."],[8389,"'Night and day will not pass away until al-Lat and al-'Uzza are worshipped.' 'A'ishah said: I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I used to think when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed {He it is who sent His Messenger with guidance and the religion of truth to make it prevail over all religion, even if the polytheists hate it} [al-Tawbah: 33], that this would be complete.' He said: 'There will be of that what Allah wills. Then Allah will send a pleasant wind and take the soul of everyone who has the weight of a mustard seed of good in his heart. There will remain those who have no good in them, and they will revert to the religion of their forefathers.'"],[8390,"I wish that when my family ate their evening meal and drank their evening drink, they would wake up dead on their beds. It was said, 'O Abu so-and-so, are you not wealthy?' He said, 'Yes, but I heard Abu Dharr say: Soon, O son of my brother, if you live a little longer, you will see a man envied for his light circumstances as today the father of ten men is envied. Soon, if you live a little longer, you will see a man whom the ruler does not know, nor brings near, nor honors being envied as today the one whom the ruler knows, brings near, and honors is envied. Soon, O son of my brother, if you live a little longer, a funeral will pass through the market, and a man will raise his head and say, Would that I were on its bier.' He said: I said, 'Do you know what is wrong with them?' He said, 'Because of what has been.' I said, 'That is before a tremendous matter.' He said, 'Yes, tremendous, tremendous, tremendous.'"],[8391,"I heard Salamah b. Nufayl al-Sakuni, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ, say: While we were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, a man came and said, 'O Prophet of Allah, were you given food from heaven?' He said, 'I was given a hot dish.' He said, 'Was there any left over from you?' He said, 'Yes.' He said, 'What was done with it?' He said, 'It was raised up to heaven, and it was revealed to me that I will not remain among you except for a little while, and you will not remain after me except for a little while. Rather, you will remain until you say, Until when? Then you will come in separate groups, and some of you will destroy others. Before the Hour there will be a severe death and after it years of earthquakes.'"],[8392,"The Hour will not come upon my community until tribes from it join the polytheists and until tribes from it worship idols."],[8393,"Beware of tribulations. Let no one go out to them, for by Allah, no one goes out to them but they sweep him away as a torrent sweeps away dung. They are ambiguous when approaching, so that the ignorant says, 'This one seems to be approaching,' and they become clear when retreating. When you see them, gather in your houses, break your swords, cut your bowstrings, and cover your faces."],[8394,"The first tribulation arose, and none remained of those who witnessed Badr. Then the second tribulation occurred, and none remained of those who witnessed al-Hudaybiyyah. I think that if a third tribulation occurred, it would not be lifted while there is any strength (tabakh) among the people."],[8395,"There will be a tribulation in which the safest of the people—or he said, the best of the people in it—will be the western army. For that reason I came to Egypt."],[8396,"This religion will continue to stand, with Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes."],[8397,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"A group from my ummah will remain victorious on the truth until the Day of Judgment.\""],[8398,"He heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Verily, My Lord expanded the earth for me until I saw its easts and wests, and He gave me the red and white treasures, and indeed my nation will reach its dominion which is expanded for me from it. I asked my Lord for my nation, not to destroy them with a general year of disaster, so He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to subject them to an enemy from outside of them, so He gave it to me. And I asked Him not to make some of them taste the punishment of others, so He prevented me from it. And He said, 'O Muhammad, if I decree a matter, it is not reversed. Indeed, I have given you for your nation that they will not be destroyed by a general year of disaster, and I will not manifest upon them an enemy other than themselves to make them permissible to each other. Even if people from all corners of the earth gathered until some of them destroy others and capture others, I do not fear for my nation except for the misleading leaders. The Hour will not be established until tribes from my nation join the polytheists and until tribes from my nation worship idols. And when the sword is unsheathed among my nation, it will never be removed from them until the Day of Resurrection.' And he claimed, 'Nothing will be taken from a man from the people of Paradise from its fruits except that Allah will replace it with something similar.' And he said, 'There is no dinar that a man spends, seeking a greater reward, than a dinar he spends on his family, then a dinar he spends on his horse in the way of Allah, then a dinar he spends on his companions in the way of Allah.' And he claimed that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ exalted this matter and when it is the Day of Resurrection, the people of ignorance will come carrying their idols on their backs, and their Lord will ask them, 'What were you worshiping?' They will say, 'Our Lord, you did not send us a messenger, nor did a command come to us. If you had sent a messenger to us, we would have obeyed you.' So their Lord will say to them, 'Did you not promise me to obey if I commanded you?' They will say, 'Yes.' So He will take their covenants concerning that and then He will order them to plunge into Hellfire and they will enter it. They will set out until when they approach it, they will see it boiling and roaring in anger, so they will become afraid and turn back to their Lord and say, 'Our Lord, turn us back from it.' So He will say, 'Did you not give me your covenants to obey me? Plunge into it.' So they will set out until when they see it, they will turn back again and say, 'Our Lord, we cannot enter it.' He will say, 'Enter it with humiliation.' So the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said, 'If they had entered it the first time, it would have been cool and peaceful for them.'\""],[8399,"The Prophet ﷺ said: A section of my community will continue to fight for the right and overcome their opponents till the last of them fights with the Antichrist. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2484)"],[8400,"'Umar b. al-Khattab addressed us and said: 'The most frightening thing I fear for you after me is that an innocent man among you will be seized and marked as a camel is marked, and his flesh will be branded as its flesh is branded, and it will be said, \"He is disobedient,\" while he is not disobedient.' He said: Then 'Ali b. Abi Talib, while he was beneath the pulpit, said: 'When will that be, O Commander of the Believers? When will affliction intensify, zeal appear, offspring be taken captive, and tribulations crush them as a mill crushes its husks, and as fire crushes firewood?' He said: 'When will that be, O 'Ali?' He said: 'When the one who seeks understanding does so for other than the religion, and the learner learns for other than action, and the world is sought by the deeds of the Hereafter.'"],[8401,"A man entered upon me at midday. I said, 'O 'Abd Allah, what do you need?' He said, 'I came with a companion of mine to look for camels of ours, and I entered to shade myself in the shade and drink from the drink.' I got up to some sour milk mixed with water and some sour curdled milk, gave him to drink, and said, 'O 'Abd Allah, who are you?' He said, 'I am Abu Bakr, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, whom you have heard of.' She said: Then I remembered Khath'am and some of us raiding one another in the Jahiliyyah, and what Allah brought of harmony and the ropes of the tents like this—and he interlaced his fingers. She said: I said, 'O 'Abd Allah, until when will the people's affair be like this?' He said, 'As long as the leaders are upright.' She said: I said, 'What are the leaders?' He said, 'Have you not seen the encampment where there is a chief whom they follow and obey? As long as those are upright.'"],[8402,"When the first fitnah occurred, it became unclear to me, so I said: O Allah, show me a matter of the truth that I may hold fast to. He said: Then I was shown this world and the Hereafter, and between them a wall, not tall, and I was at a bridge. I said: If I cling to this bridge, perhaps I will descend to some brave slain ones and they will inform me. He said: I descended to a land with trees, and I was at a group sitting. I said: Are you the martyrs? They said: No, we are the angels. I said: Where are the martyrs? They said: Go forward to the high ranks, to Muhammad ﷺ. So I went forward, and I was at a rank—Allah knows best its vastness and beauty—and I was with Muhammad ﷺ and Ibrahim ﷺ, and he was saying to Ibrahim ﷺ : Seek forgiveness for my Ummah. Ibrahim said to him: You do not know what they innovated after you; they shed their blood and killed their imam. Why did they not do as my friend Sa'd did? I said: I think I have been shown that I should go to Sa'd and see with whom he is, and be with him. So I came to him and related the dream to him, and he was not much pleased by it, and he said: 'Indeed, he is wretched who does not have Ibrahim as a friend.' I said: With which of the two factions are you? He said: 'I am not with either of them.' I said: Then what do you command me? He said: 'Do you have livestock?' I said: No. He said: 'Buy livestock and seclude yourself with it until the matter is resolved.'"],[8403,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"A man will be pledged allegiance between the corner (of the Ka'bah) and the Maqam (place of Ibrahim), and no one will make this house permissible except its people. When they allow it, do not ask about the destruction of the Arabs. Then the Abyssinians will come and ruin it in a way that cannot be rebuilt ever again. And they are the ones who will extract its treasure.\""],[8404,"Leave the Abyssinians alone as long as they leave you alone, for none will extract the treasure of the Kaaba except the one with thin legs from Abyssinia."],[8405,"The Hour will not come until the House is no longer performed Hajj to."],[8406,"From Shu'bah, and Allah knows best, it is authentic and established from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that the House will be performed Hajj and Umrah after the emergence of Gog and Magog."],[8407,"The House will certainly be performed Hajj and Umrah after the emergence of Gog and Magog, for it is possible that it will be performed Hajj and Umrah after that, then Hajj will cease all at once."],[8408,"The people of Iraq are about to have no dirham or qafiz come to them. They said: Why is that, O Abu Abdullah? He said: Because of the Persians, they prevent that. Then he was silent for a little while, then said: The people of Syria are about to have no dinar or mudd come to them. They said: Why is that? He said: Because of the Romans, they prevent that."],[8409,"There will be in the end of this Ummah a caliph who distributes wealth without counting it."],[8410,"A time will come upon people when a man comes to a grave and lies down on it and says: Would that I were in the place of its occupant. It is not out of love for meeting Allah, but only because of the severity of the affliction he sees."],[8411,"A bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, does Islam have an end? He said: 'Yes, any household of the Arabs or non-Arabs for whom Allah intends good, He brings Islam upon them.' They said: Then what, O Messenger of Allah? He said: 'Then fitnahs occur like dark clouds.' A bedouin said: Certainly not, O Messenger of Allah? The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will return to it as black serpents, striking one another's necks.'"],[8412,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You will certainly follow the ways of those before you, span by span and cubit by cubit, until if one of them entered a lizard's hole, you would enter it, and until if one of them had intercourse with his wife on the road, you would do it.' Authentic."],[8413,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'A wind will come before the Hour in which the soul of every believer will be taken.' Authentic, but there is a break in its chain."],[8414,"'Indeed, Allah will send a wind from Yemen softer than silk, and it will not leave anyone who has in his heart the weight of a grain of faith except that it takes his soul.'"],[8415,"The Hour will not arise until Allah sends a wind that will not leave anyone in whose heart is an atom's weight of piety or restraint except it seizes him, and every people will join what their fathers used to worship in the pre-Islamic age, and there will remain a rabble of people who do not enjoin good nor forbid evil; they will copulate in the streets as beasts copulate. When that is the case, Allah's wrath will intensify upon the people of the earth, and He will establish the Hour."],[8416,"While the Prophet ﷺ was praying one night, he extended his hand and then withdrew it. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do something in this prayer that you did not do before.' He said, 'Yes, Paradise was presented to me, and I saw in it a cluster of grapes whose bunches were near, and I wanted to take something from it, but it was revealed to me to hold back, so I held back. And Hell was presented to me between me and you, until I saw my shadow and your shadows in it, so I gestured to you to hold back, but it was revealed to me to let them remain, for you have submitted and they have submitted, you have migrated and they have migrated, you have struggled and they have struggled. I saw no merit for you over them except prophethood.' So I interpreted that as what my community will face after me of tribulations."],[8417,"The passage translates to: \"He was with Maslama bin Mukhallad and Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As was with him. Abdullah said, 'The Hour will not come except upon the worst of creation. They are worse than the people of the Age of Ignorance. They will not call upon God for anything without it being returned to them.' While they were discussing this, Uqba bin Amir approached. Maslama said, 'O Uqba, listen to what Abdullah is saying.' Uqba replied, 'He knows best.'\""],[8418,"Indeed, among the last matters concerning the Kaaba is that the Abyssinians will raid the House, and the Muslims will turn toward them, and Allah will send upon them a wind whose trace is easterly, and Allah will not leave any servant in whose heart is an atom's weight of piety except it seizes him, until when they have been emptied of their best, there remains a rabble of people who do not enjoin good nor forbid evil, and every tribe will resort to what their fathers used to worship of idols and worship it, until they fornicate in the streets as beasts fornicate, and the Hour will arise upon them. Whoever tells you anything after this has no knowledge."],[8419,"Indeed, Allah has a wind that He sends at the head of every hundred years, seizing the soul of every believer."],[8420,"There will come upon my community a time when reciters are many and jurists are few, knowledge is seized, and killing increases.' They said, 'What is killing, O Messenger of Allah?' He said, 'Slaughter among you. Then after that will come a time when men recite the Quran but it does not pass their collarbones. Then after that will come a time when the hypocrite, the disbeliever, the polytheist in Allah will argue with the believer with the like of what he says.'"],[8421,"A time will come upon the people when no believer remains except he has joined Syria."],[8422,"A fire will be sent driving the people from the easts of the earth to its wests, as a broken camel is driven. It will not leave any of them behind: when they halt, it halts; when they spend the night, it spends the night."],[8423,"Various mines will appear, one of them near the Hijaz, to which the worst of people will come; it is called Pharaoh. While they are working in it, when it uncovers the gold and its output pleases them, it will be swallowed up with them."],[8424,"We prayed the Friday prayer and the people crowded together until they were like a millstone around Abu Raja al-Utaridi. They asked him about the tribulation, and he said: Two men came to the gathering of Ubada b. al-Samit and said, 'O Ibn al-Samit, repeat the hadith you told us.' He said, 'Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Soon the best wealth will be two sheep, a Makkan and a Madinan, grazing above the tops of hills, eating from the leaves of tragacanth and basham, while its owner eats from their meat and drinks from their milk, while the strongholds of the Arabs will be shaken by tribulations.\" He said it three times, then said, \"By Him in whose hand is my soul, for one of you to have three hundred sheep, eating from their meat and drinking from their milk, is dearer to him than these pillars of yours of gold and silver.\""],[8425,"How will you be when you are parted from your religion as a woman is parted from her private part?"],[8426,"How will you be when you are parted from your religion as a woman is parted from her private part, not preventing anyone who comes to her?' He said: A man said, 'May Allah disfigure the helpless one.' He said, 'Rather, you are disfigured.'"],[8427,"I did not sleep last night until morning.' I said, 'Why?' He said, 'They said the comet with a tail has appeared, and I feared that the Dajjal had come by night.'"],[8428,"The Dajjal has known signs: when springs recede, rivers dry up, sweet basil turns yellow, and Madhhij and Hamdan move from Iraq and settle in Qinnasrin, then await the Dajjal, coming in the morning or the evening."],[8429,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you have narrated the books. He said: 'From what people are you?' We said: 'From the people of Iraq.' He said: 'You, O people of Iraq, lie, and you call others liars, and you mock.' I said: 'No, by Allah, we do not call you a liar, nor do we lie about you, nor do we mock you.' He said: 'The Banu Qantura' and Kurki will not come out until they tie their horses to the palm trees of al-Aylah. How far is it from there to al-Basrah?' We said: 'Four farsakhs.' He said: 'They will send word: Make way between us and it.' He said: 'A third will join them, a third will go to al-Kufah, and a third will join the Bedouins. Then they will send word to the people of al-Kufah: Make way between us and it. A third will join them, a third will join the Bedouins, and a third will go to al-Sham.' We said: 'What is the sign of that?' He said: 'When the land is filled with the rule of boys.'"],[8430,"Allah is a just judge, blessed be His name. Those who doubt are destroyed. Indeed, after you there will be tribulations in which wealth abounds and the Quran is opened, until the man, the woman, the free, the slave, the young, and the old take it. Soon a man will read the Quran and say: 'I have read the Quran, so why do the people not follow me, though I have read the Quran?' Then he will say: 'They will not follow me until I innovate for them something other than it.' So beware of what he innovates, for what he innovates is misguidance. Beware of the slip of the wise man, for Satan puts misguidance on the tongue of the wise man and puts a word of truth on the tongue of the hypocrite.' We said: 'What makes you know, may Allah have mercy on you, that the hypocrite is given a word of truth and that Satan puts a word of misguidance on the tongue of the wise man?' He said: 'Avoid from the speech of the wise man every ambiguous thing which, when you hear it, you say, \"What is this?\" And no one explains it to you. Perhaps he will retract and speak the truth, so listen to him, for upon the truth there is light.'"],[8431,"A man from the enemies of the Muslims in al-Andalus called Dhu al-'Urf will gather a great assembly from the tribes of polytheism. Those in al-Andalus will know that they have no strength, so the strong people among the Muslims will flee in ships and cross to Tangier. The weak people and their community will remain, having no ships to cross on. Then Allah ﷻ will send an ibex, and it will cross for them in the sea. The ibex will cross, and the water will not cover its hooves. The people will see it and say: 'The ibex! The ibex! Follow it!' So the people will all cross following its tracks. Then the sea will return to what it was, and the enemy will cross in ships. When the people of Ifriqiyah sense them, they will all flee from Ifriqiyah, and with them those Muslims who were in al-Andalus, until they enter al-Fustat. That enemy will advance until they camp between Maryut and the Pyramids, a distance of five barids, and they will fill that area with evil. Then the banner of the Muslims will go out to them on the bridge, and Allah will grant them victory over them. They will defeat them and kill them as far as Alulabah, a distance of ten nights. The people of al-Fustat will use their carts and equipment as firewood for seven years. Dhu al-'Urf will escape the killing, and with him is a book which he does not look into except while he is defeated. He will find in it mention of Islam and that he is commanded in it to enter into peace. He will ask for safety for himself and for those of his companions who respond to Islam, those who came with him. He will become Muslim and so become one of the Muslims. Then in the second year a man from Abyssinia called Asis will come, having gathered a great assembly. The Muslims will flee from them from Aswan until no Muslim remains in it or below it except that he enters al-Fustat. Asis will camp with his army at Manf, which is at the head of a barid from al-Fustat. The banner of the Muslims will go out to them on the bridge, and Allah will grant them victory over them. They will kill them and take them captive until a black man is sold for a cloak."],[8432,"A man came and called out to Ibn Mas'ud, so he leaned over him and said: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, when will I go astray while I know?' He said: 'When there are rulers over you whom if you obey they will enter you into the Fire, and if you disobey them they will kill you.'"],[8433,"'When you see al-Sham as the banquet table of one man and his household, then at that time is the conquest of Constantinople.'"],[8434,"The strongholds are three: the people's stronghold on the day of the great battles is Damascus; the people's stronghold on the day of the Dajjal is the river of Abu Qatras — those who say the Bayt al-Maqdis deviate from the people; and their stronghold on the day of Ya'juj and Ma'juj is Mount Sinai."],[8435,"'When you are given a choice between lands, do not choose Armenia, for in it is a portion of the punishment of Allah, the Exalted.'"],[8436,"'The island is safe from ruin until Armenia is ruined. Egypt is safe from ruin until the island is ruined. Al-Kufah is safe from ruin until Egypt is ruined. The great battle will not occur until al-Kufah is ruined. The city of disbelief will not be conquered until the great battle occurs. The Dajjal will not come out until the city of disbelief is conquered.'"],[8437,"He used to say: 'Nuh ﷺ begot three: Sam, Ham, and Yafith. Sam begot the Arabs, the Persians, and the Romans, and in all of these there is good. Ham begot the Sudanese, the Berbers, and the Copts. Yafith begot the Turks, the Slavs, and Ya'juj and Ma'juj.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8438,"\"Do not become engaged in conflicts except by the hands of a man from the fourth or fifth generation of the descendants of Hercules, known as Tayyara.\" Dhahabi did not mention it in his summary."],[8439,"Abu Hurayrah passed by Marwan while he was building his house in the middle of the city. He said: I sat with him while the workers were working. He said: 'Build firmly, hope for a long life, and die soon.' Marwan said: 'Abu Hurayrah is speaking to the workers. What are you saying to them, O Abu Hurayrah?' He said: I said: 'Build firmly, hope for a long life, and die soon, O assembly of Quraysh — three times. Remember how you were yesterday and how you have become today: you are served by your slaves from Persia and Rome. Eat fine bread and fat meat, do not eat one another, and do not bite one another like the biting of workhorses. Be small today and you will be great tomorrow. By Allah, no man among you rises a degree except that Allah lowers him on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[8440,"'Three will fight near your treasure; each of them is the son of a caliph. Then it will not come to any one of them. Then the black banners will appear from the direction of the east, and they will fight you with a fighting such as no people have fought before.' Then he mentioned something and said: 'When you see him, pledge allegiance to him, even if crawling on snow, for he is the Caliph of Allah, the Mahdi.'"],[8441,"The best of people in times of tribulation is a man who takes hold of his horse's rein—or he said, his horse's halter—behind the enemies of Allah, frightening them and they frightening him, or a man who withdraws in his desert, fulfilling the right of Allah that is upon him."],[8442,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he came out to us rejoicing, joy recognizable in his face. We did not ask him about anything except that he informed us of it, and we were not silent except that he began speaking to us, until some youths of Banu Hashim passed by, among them al-Hasan and al-Husain. When he saw them, he embraced them and his eyes flowed with tears. We said, 'O Messenger of Allah, we keep seeing something in your face that we dislike.' He said, 'Indeed we are a household for whom Allah has chosen the Hereafter over this world. And indeed my household will face after me banishment and dispersal throughout the lands, until black banners rise from the east. They will ask for the truth and will not be given it; then they will ask for it and will not be given it; then they will ask for it and will not be given it. Then they will fight and be granted victory. So whoever of you or of your descendants reaches that, let him go to the Imam of my household, even if crawling on snow, for they are banners of guidance. They will hand them over to a man from my household whose name matches my name and whose father's name matches my father's name. He will take possession of the earth and fill it with equity and justice just as it was filled with oppression and injustice.' This is fabricated."],[8443,"Tribulation has come to you, hurling burning pebbles. The black, dark tribulation has come to you. Indeed tribulation has pauses and stings. So whoever of you is able to die during its pauses, let him do so."],[8444,"There will be a tribulation in which people fight over a pre-Islamic claim; its slain are in the Fire."],[8445,"O people, a tribulation has overshadowed you like patches of the dark night. Indeed the best of people in it—or he said, from it—is a man who owns sheep, eating from the milk of his flock, or a man behind the mountain pass, holding the rein of his horse, eating from his sword."],[8446,"There will descend upon my community in the last days a severe affliction from their rulers, the like of which has never been heard of a more severe affliction, until the spacious earth becomes constricted for them and until the earth is filled with oppression and injustice. The believer will find no refuge to which he can flee from oppression. Then Allah, Mighty and Sublime, will send a man from my progeny who will fill the earth with equity and justice just as it was filled with oppression and injustice. The inhabitants of heaven and the inhabitants of earth will be pleased with him. The earth will not withhold any of its seeds except that it brings them forth, and the sky will not withhold any of its rain except that Allah pours it upon them abundantly. He will live therein for seven, eight, or nine years, during which the living will wish for the dead because of the good that Allah, Mighty and Sublime, has done for the people of the earth."],[8447,"Years of drought will come upon the people, in which the liar will be believed, the truthful will be belied, the treacherous will be entrusted, the trustworthy will be betrayed, and the ruwaybidah will speak among them.' It was said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the ruwaybidah?' He said, 'The insignificant man who speaks about matters of the common people.'"],[8448,"There will be a tribulation in which wealth abounds and the Quran is opened, so that the believer and the hypocrite, the young and the old, the man and the woman read it. A man will read it secretly and will not be followed for it, so he will say, 'By Allah, I will read it openly.' Then he will read it openly and will not be followed for it. So he will take a mosque and invent speech that is not in the Book of Allah nor from the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Beware of him, for every innovation is misguidance.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8449,"I heard Abdullah b. Umar saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he mentioned tribulations and spoke much about them, until he mentioned the tribulation of the saddlecloths. A man said, 'What is the tribulation of the saddlecloths?' He said, 'It is a tribulation of flight and war. Then the tribulation of the dark one—or the prosperous one. Then the people will make peace upon a man like a hip upon a rib. Then the tribulation of the dark, overwhelming one, which will not leave anyone of this community except that it will slap him with a slap. When it is said that it has ended, it continues. A man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever in the evening, until the people become divided into two camps: a camp of faith with no hypocrisy in it, and a camp of hypocrisy with no faith in it. When that happens, then await the Dajjal from that day or the next.'"],[8450,"\"By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! The Hour will not be established until predators speak to people and until the tip of a man's whip and the straps on his sandal speak to him, and his thigh informs him of what occurred with his family after him.\" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2181)"],[8451,"If one of you wants to know whether tribulation has struck him or not, let him look: if he sees as lawful something he used to consider unlawful, then tribulation has struck him; and if he sees as unlawful something he used to consider lawful, then it has struck him."],[8452,"While a shepherd was tending his flock on the harrah, a wolf attacked one of the sheep. The shepherd intervened between the wolf and the sheep. The wolf sat back on its tail and said, 'O servant of Allah, do you prevent me from a provision that Allah has sent to me?' The man said, 'What a wonder! A wolf speaks to me with human speech!' The wolf said, 'Shall I tell you of something more wondrous than I? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is between the two harrahs, informing people of the news of what has already passed.' So the shepherd gathered his sheep into a corner of the corners of Madinah, then came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to the people and said, 'He has spoken the truth, by the One in Whose hand is my soul.'"],[8453,"Two groups will fight over a pre-Islamic claim at the emergence of a commander or a tribe. The faction that prevails will prevail while it is abased, and those who are near it from its enemy will desire it and will plunge into the Fire."],[8454,"A tribulation is presented to the hearts. Any heart that rejects it, a white dot is inscribed in it. Any heart that does not reject it, a black dot is inscribed in it. Then another tribulation is presented to the hearts. If the heart that rejected it the first time rejects it, a white dot is inscribed in it. If it does not reject it, a black dot is inscribed. Then another tribulation is presented to the hearts. If the one that rejected it the first two times rejects it, it becomes intensely white, pure, and clear, and no tribulation will ever harm it. If it did not reject it the first two times, it becomes black, turns back, and is overturned, so it neither recognizes truth nor rejects wrong."],[8455,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us: 'I warn you of seven tribulations that will occur after me: a tribulation that comes from al-Madinah, a tribulation in Makkah, a tribulation that comes from Yemen, a tribulation that comes from al-Sham, a tribulation that comes from the east, a tribulation that comes from the west, and a tribulation from the interior of al-Sham, which is the Sufyani.' He said: Then Ibn Mas'ud said: 'Among you are those who will witness the first of them, and among this Ummah are those who will witness the last of them.' Al-Walid b. Ayyash said: 'The tribulation of al-Madinah was from the direction of Talhah and al-Zubayr, the tribulation of Makkah was the tribulation of Abdullah b. al-Zubayr, the tribulation of al-Sham was from the direction of Banu Umayyah, and the tribulation of the east was from the direction of these ones.'"],[8456,"The first thing you will lose of your religion is khushu' (humility in prayer), and the last thing you will lose of your religion is prayer. The bonds of Islam will be undone one by one. Women will pray while they are menstruating. You will surely follow the path of those who came before you, exactly like the feather of an arrow matches another, and like a sandal matches another. You will not miss their way, nor will they miss yours, until two groups remain from many groups. One of them will say: 'What is the matter with the five prayers? Those before us went astray. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, only said: {Establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the early hours of the night} [Hud: 114]. Do not pray except three.' The other will say: 'The faith of the believers in Allah is like the faith of the angels. Among us there is no disbeliever and no hypocrite. It is Allah's right to gather them with the Dajjal.'"],[8457,"I set out with Umar and Ibn Dhulay' to Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman, and he had two rows of people with him. We said: 'O Hudhayfah, you have witnessed what we have not, you have known what we have not, and you have heard what we have not. So narrate to us something that perhaps Allah will benefit us by.' He said: 'If I narrated to you everything I have heard, you would not wait for me until the near night.' He said: We said: 'It is not about this that we ask you, but...'"],[8458,"Indeed, the corruption of my Ummah will be at the hands of foolish young men from Quraysh."],[8459,"When Uthman was killed, we entered upon Hudhayfah, and the people were with him. He said: 'By Allah, the oppressors of Mudar will not leave any believing servant of Allah except that they will kill him or tempt him, until Allah and the believers prevail over them, so that they cannot even prevent [the taking of] the tail of a watercourse.' A man said: 'Do you say this while you are a man from Mudar?' He said: 'I say nothing except what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ﷺ said.'"],[8460,"Indeed the one who is in al-Sham, meaning Marwan, by Allah, he fights only for worldly gain. And indeed the one who is in Makkah, meaning Ibn al-Zubayr, he fights only for worldly gain. And indeed those whom you call your reciters, by Allah, they fight only for worldly gain.' My father said to him: 'Then what do you command us?' He said: 'I do not see the best of people except a band that clings together,' and he gestured with his hand, 'empty bellies from people's wealth, light backs from their blood.'"],[8461,"Have you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: 'If I did, you would stone me.' He said: We said: 'Glory be to Allah! Would we do that?' He said: 'Consider, if I narrated to you that one of your mothers would come to you in a battalion, numerous in number, severe in might, would you believe it?' They said: 'Glory be to Allah! Who would believe this?' Then Hudhayfah said: 'The Humayra' will come to you in a battalion driven by its non-Arabs, where it will displease your faces.' Then he stood up and entered a private room."],[8462,"I heard Hudhayfah say: 'By Allah, I am the most knowledgeable of people about every tribulation that will occur between me and the Hour. That is not because the Messenger of Allah ﷺ narrated to me something about them that he did not narrate to others, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, while he was narrating to a gathering in which I was present, about the tribulations, and he was enumerating the tribulations: among them are three that do not leave anything, like the winds of summer, some of them small and some of them large.' So all those people went away except me."],[8463,"I certainly know a tribulation whose preceding one will be with it like the puff of a rabbit, and I certainly know the way out of it.' We said: 'What is the way out of it?' He said: 'I restrain my hand until someone comes to kill me.'"],[8464,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and informed us of what would happen until the establishment of the Hour. Those who understood it among us understood it, and those who forgot it forgot it."],[8465,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood and did not leave anything except that he mentioned it until the Hour will be established. Those who understood it understood it, and those who forgot it forgot it."],[8466,"I said, \"I see you today as a bad companion: you hear me narrate—and I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ—and you do not forbid me.\" He said, \"What is it with you and anger?\" He said, \"Then I turned to ask him, and it was Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman.\""],[8467,"It is better that it be bitter and difficult, and that it be completed before it becomes decayed or broken. When raids become mixed up, spoils are consumed, and the forbidden is made lawful, then you must hold to the frontier outpost, for it is the best of your jihad.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8468,"Islam will be effaced just as the embroidery of a garment is effaced, until it is not known what fasting, charity, or ritual sacrifice are. The Book of Allah will be taken up by night, and no verse of it will remain on earth. There will remain groups of people: the old man and the old woman, who say, \"We found our forefathers upon this phrase: there is no god but Allah, so we say it.\" Silah b. Zufar said to Hudhayfah, \"What does 'there is no god but Allah' avail them when they do not know what fasting, charity, or ritual sacrifice are?\" Hudhayfah turned away from him. He repeated it to him three times, and each time Hudhayfah turned away from him. Then, on the third time, he turned to him and said, \"O Silah, it saves them from the Fire.\""],[8469,"\"The signs are beads strung on a thread; when the thread is cut, they follow one another.\" Khalid b. al-Huwayrith said, \"We were called at dawn, and there was 'Abdullah b. 'Amr, and there was a woman from Banu al-Mughirah called Fatimah. I heard 'Abdullah b. 'Amr say, 'That is Yazid b. Mu'awiyah.' She said, 'Is that so, O 'Abdullah b. 'Amr? Do you find him written in the Book?' He said, 'I do not find him by name, but I find a man from the tree of Mu'awiyah who sheds blood, makes wealth lawful to be seized, and demolishes this House stone by stone. If that happens while I am alive, then [you will see]; otherwise, remember me.'\" He said, \"Her dwelling was on Abu Qubays. When the time of al-Hajjaj and Ibn al-Zubayr came, and she saw the House being demolished, she said, 'May Allah have mercy on 'Abdullah b. 'Amr; he had told us about this.'\""],[8470,"\"How will you be when you are asked for the truth and you give it, and when you ask for your right and it is withheld from you?\" They said, \"We will be patient.\" He said, \"You have entered it, by the Lord of the Ka'bah.\""],[8471,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said, \"There will come people with small eyes, broad faces, as if their faces were shields. They will drive the people of Islam to the places where wormwood grows. It is as if I am looking at them, having tied their horses to the pillars of the mosque.\" It was said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are they?\" He said, \"The Turks.\""],[8472,"I heard Abu Bakr Muhammad b. Yahya al-Suli the grammarian say, \"The first of the Arab poets to praise the Turks was 'Ali b. al-'Abbas al-Rumi, when he said [in the wafir meter]: When they stand firm, they are a barrier of iron; you would think our eyes are bewildered within it. And when they go forth, they are fires blazing upon the enemies, driven by borrowing. The kings of the earth: their eyes are small when they go forth, but their souls are great.\""],[8473,"\"It is as if the Turks have come to you on mules with cropped ears, until they tie them on the bank of the Euphrates.\""],[8475,"\"The Banu Qantura' b. Karkar are about to expel the people of Iraq from their land.\" I said, \"Then will they return?\" He said, \"Do you desire that?\" He said, \"And they will have a period of ease in livelihood.\""],[8476,"\"The Banu Qantura' are about to expel you from the land of Iraq.\" He said, \"I said, 'Then will they return?' He said, 'And is that dearer to you? Then they will return, and they will have there a period of ease in livelihood.'\""],[8477,"\"By the One in whose hand is my soul, the Hour will not come until you fight the Turks: small-eyed, red-faced, snub-nosed, as if their faces were layered shields.\""],[8478,"\"Have you heard of a city one side of which is on land and one side in the sea?\" They said, \"Yes, O Messenger of Allah.\" He said, \"The Hour will not come until seventy thousand of the Banu Ishaq raid it. When they come to it, they will camp, but they will not fight with weapons or shoot arrows.\" He said, \"Then they will say, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater,' and one of its sides will fall.\" Thawr said, \"I do not know it except that he said, 'The side facing the land.' Then they will say a second time, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater,' and the other side will fall. Then they will say a third time, 'There is no god but Allah, and Allah is greater,' and it will be opened for them, so they will enter and take spoils. While they are dividing the spoils, a cry will come to them that the Dajjal has appeared, so they will leave everything and return.\""],[8479,"\"The Hour will not come until you fight the Khuz and Kirman, a people from the non-Arabs with red faces, flat noses, small eyes, their faces as if they were layered shields, their shoes of hair.\""],[8480,"Once there blew a red storm in Kufah that there came a person who had nothing to say but (these words): ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud, the Last Hour has come. He (ʿAbdullah b. Masʿud) was sitting reclining against something, and he said: The Last Hour would not come until shares of inheritance are not distributed and there is no rejoicing over spoils of war. Then he said pointing towards Syria, with the gesture of his hand like this: The enemy shall muster strength against Muslims and the Muslims will muster strength against them (Syrians). I said: You mean Rome? And he said: Yes, and there would be a terrible fight and the Muslims would prepare a detachment (for fighting unto death) which would not return but victorious. They will fight until night will intervene them; both the sides will return without being victorious and both will be wiped out. The Muslims will again prepare a detachment for fighting unto death so that they may not return but victorious. When it would be the fourth day, a new detachment out of the remnant of the Muslims would be prepared and Allah will decree that the enemy should be routed. And they would fight such a fight the like of which would not be seen, so much so that even if a bird were to pass their flanks, it would fall down dead before reaching the end of them. (There would be such a large scale massacre) that when counting would be done, (only) one out of a hundred men related to one another would be found alive. So what can be the joy at the spoils of such war and what inheritance would be divided! They would be in this very state that they would hear of a calamity more horrible than this. And a cry would reach them: The Dajjal has taken your place among your offspring. They will, therefore, throw away what would be in their hands and go forward sending ten horsemen, as a scouting party. Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I know their names and the names of their forefathers and the color of their horses. They will be the best horsemen on the surface of the earth on that day or amongst the best horsemen on the surface of the earth on that day. (Using translation from Muslim 2899a)"],[8481,"\"The Hour will not come until the land of the Arabs returns to being meadows and rivers.\""],[8482,"I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: \"There will be three Egypt. One in the meeting point of the two seas, one in the Arabian Peninsula, and one in the Levant. People will be alarmed three times, and then the Dajjal will emerge with an army. He will be defeated by the people from the east, and the first Egypt to repel him will be the Egypt in the meeting point of the two seas. Its people will be divided into three groups: one group will establish and proclaim their loyalty to him, another group will join the Bedouins, and another group will follow the Egypt in the Arabian Peninsula. Then, the Egypt in the Arabian Peninsula will come, and its people will also be divided into three groups. The same process will repeat with the Egypt in the Levant. Finally, the Muslims will gather at the mountain pass of Afiq and will send an army. Their army will suffer losses, and they will face severe famine and hardship. They will be in such a dire condition that one of them will burn his bowstring and eat it. While they are in this state, a caller from the sky will call out to them, saying, 'O people, relief has come to you!' Some of them will say to others, 'Indeed, this is the voice of a satiated man.' Then, Prophet Isa (Jesus), peace be upon him, will descend at the time of Fajr prayer and lead the people in prayer. The imam of the people will step forward and say, 'O Spirit of Allah, proceed and lead us in prayer.' Isa will reply, 'You are the leaders of this Ummah, so you should lead us in prayer.' He will then lead them in prayer. When he finishes, Isa will take up arms and go towards the Dajjal. When the Dajjal sees him, he will dissolve like salt dissolves in water, and his weapon will fall beside him. Isa will then kill the Dajjal, and his companions will be defeated. On that day, no one will be spared except for the believers, even the stones will speak and say, 'O believer, there is a disbeliever behind me, so kill him.'\""],[8483,"Uthman b. Abi al-As led us in prayer."],[8484,"\"When the Umayyads reach forty, they will take Allah's servants as slaves, Allah's wealth as a grant, and Allah's Book as corruption.\""],[8485,"\"When the Umayyads reach forty, they will take Allah's servants as slaves, Allah's wealth as a grant, and Allah's Book as corruption.\""],[8486,"No child was born to anyone but that the Prophet ﷺ was brought to him, and he would supplicate for him. Marwan b. al-Hakam was brought in to him, and he said: \"He is the gecko, son of the gecko, the accursed, son of the accursed.\""],[8487,"\"When the descendants of Abu al-As reach thirty men, they will take Allah's wealth as a thing to be passed around, Allah's servants as slaves, and Allah's religion as corruption.\" Hallam said: That was objected to regarding Abu Dharr, and Ali b. Abi Talib testified: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'The green canopy has not shaded, nor has the dust-colored earth carried, one with a tongue more truthful than Abu Dharr.' And I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it.\""],[8488,"\"When the descendants of Abu al-As reach thirty men, they will take Allah's religion as corruption, Allah's servants as slaves, and Allah's wealth as a thing to be passed around.\""],[8489,"\"When the descendants of Abu al-As reach thirty men, they will take Allah's wealth as a thing to be passed around, Allah's religion as corruption, and Allah's servants as slaves.\""],[8490,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I saw in my dream as if the descendants of al-Hakam b. Abi al-As were leaping upon my pulpit as monkeys leap.\" He said: The Prophet ﷺ was never seen fully laughing until he passed away."],[8491,"\"The most hateful tribes to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ were the Umayyads, the Banu Hanifah, and Thaqif.\""],[8492,"When Muawiyah pledged allegiance to his son Yazid, Marwan said: \"It is the Sunnah of Abu Bakr and Umar.\" Abd al-Rahman b. Abi Bakr said: \"It is the Sunnah of Heraclius and Caesar.\" He said: \"Allah revealed about you: {And the one who says to his parents, 'Uff to you...'} [Al-Ahqaf: 17] to the end of the verse.\" He said: It reached Aisha, and she said: \"He lied, by Allah; it is not about him. But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the father of Marwan while Marwan was in his loins. So Marwan is a portion of the curse of Allah, Exalted is He.\""],[8493,"\"Indeed, Al-Hakam ibn Abu al-'As sought permission from the Prophet ﷺ, so the Prophet ﷺ recognized his voice and speech, and he said, 'Grant him permission, upon him is the curse of Allah, and upon those who come forth from his lineage, except for the believing ones among them. They are few in honor in this world, and in the hereafter they will be humiliated with deception and trickery. They are given in the world, but they have nothing in the hereafter except for disgrace.'\""],[8494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed al-Hakam and his son. This hadith has a sound chain of transmission, but they (al-Bukhari and Muslim) did not record it."],[8495,"The Hour will not come until the Romans land at al-A'maq. A group from Madinah, from the best people on earth at that time, will go out to them. When they line up, the Romans will say: 'Let us get to those who were captured from among us, and we will fight them.' The Muslims will say: 'No, by Allah, we will not let you get to our brothers.' They will fight them, and one third will flee, and Allah will never accept their repentance; one third will be killed, and they are the best martyrs in the sight of Allah ﷻ; and one third will remain, never being put to trial. They will reach Constantinople and conquer it. While they are dividing their spoils, having hung their weapons on olive trees, Satan will cry out: 'The Messiah has come to your families behind you.' That is false. When they reach Syria, he will come out. While they are preparing for battle and aligning the rows, the prayer—the dawn prayer—will be called. Then Isa b. Maryam (blessings of Allah be upon him) will descend and lead them. When the enemy of Allah sees him, he will dissolve like salt dissolves. If he were left alone, he would dissolve until he perishes, but Allah will kill him by his hand and show them his blood on his spear."],[8496,"You are in a time in which its scholars are many, its orators are few, its givers (of charity) are many, and the prayer in it is short while the sermon is long. So shorten the sermon and lengthen the prayer. Indeed, some eloquence is magic. Whoever desires the Hereafter harms the worldly life, and whoever desires the worldly life harms the Hereafter. O people, harm the perishable for the sake of the everlasting."],[8497,"The world will not come to an end, O Ali b. Abi Talib.” Ali said: “At your service, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Know that you will fight the Banu al-Asfar (the Romans), or those after you among the believers will fight them. The finest of the believers, the people of the Hijaz who strive in the cause of Allah, not deterred by the blame of any blamer, will go out to them, until Allah ﷻ grants them victory over Constantinople and Rome with glorification and takbir. Its fortress will collapse, and they will seize immense spoils the like of which they have never seized, until they divide them by the shield. Then a crier will cry out: 'O people of Islam, the Messiah, the Dajjal, has appeared in your lands and among your families.' The people will disperse from the wealth: some will take it and some will leave it. The one who takes will regret, and the one who leaves will regret. They will say: 'Who is this crier?' They will not know who he is. They will say: 'Send a scouting party to Ludd. If the Messiah has appeared, they will bring you news of him.' They will come and look, but they see nothing, and they see people in doubt. They will say: 'The crier cried out only because of some important news. So be determined, then be guided.' They will resolve: 'Let us all go out to Ludd. If the Dajjal is there, we will fight him until Allah judges between us and him, and He is the best of judges. If it is something else, then it is your lands, your kinsfolk, and your armies; you will have returned to them.'"],[8498,"Woe to the Arabs from an evil that has drawn near! At the head of sixty, trustworthiness will become spoils, charity a fine, testimony by mere acquaintance, and judgment by desire."],[8499,"The Beast will have three emergences over the course of time. Its first emergence will be in the farthest part of Yemen. Its mention will spread in the desert, but its mention will not enter the town—meaning Makkah. Then it will remain hidden for a long time after that. Then it will emerge a second time near Makkah, and its mention will spread among the desert dwellers and in Makkah. Then it will remain hidden for a long time. Then, while the people are in the greatest mosque in sanctity, the most beloved to Allah, and the most honored by Allah—the Sacred Mosque—they will be startled by it appearing on one side of the mosque, coming close and moving between the Black Stone and the gate of Banu Makhzum, to the right of the one exiting, in the middle of that area. The people will scatter from it in all directions, but a group of Muslims will stand firm, knowing that they cannot frustrate Allah. It will come out toward them, shaking dust from its head, and it will begin with them, polishing their faces until it leaves them like shining stars. Then it will depart into the earth; no pursuer can catch it, and no one fleeing can escape it. A man will seek refuge from it in prayer, and it will come to him from behind and say: 'O so-and-so, are you praying now?' He will turn to it, and it will brand his face. Then it will go away. People will live as neighbors in their homes, accompany each other on journeys, and share in wealth. The believer will recognize the disbeliever, until the disbeliever says: 'O believer, pay me my due,' and the believer says: 'O disbeliever, pay me my due.'"],[8500,"We were sitting with Hudhayfah when the Beast was mentioned. Hudhayfah said: 'It will emerge three times: first in some of the deserts, then it will hide. Then it will emerge in some of the towns, causing alarm and causing the rulers to shed blood. Then it will hide.' He said: 'While the people are at the greatest, most excellent, and most honorable mosque'—until we said 'the Sacred Mosque,' but he did not name it—'the earth will rise up, and the people will flee, but a group of Muslims will remain, saying: \"Nothing will save us from Allah's decree.\" Then it will come out and polish their faces until they become like shining stars. It will follow the people: neighbors in quarters, partners in wealth, and companions in Islam.'"],[8501,"People will spend the night traveling to a gathering, and the Beast of the Earth will spend the night moving toward them. They will wake up with it having placed them between its head and its tail. There is no believer but it will wipe him, and no hypocrite or disbeliever but it will brand his nose. Indeed, repentance is open until the Dajjal comes forth. The believer will be affected by him like a common cold, but he will enter the ears of the disbeliever and the hypocrite until he becomes like roasted meat. Repentance is still open. Then the sun will rise from its west."],[8502,"In His Almighty saying {And when the Word is fulfilled against them, We shall bring forth for them a beast from the earth} [Quran, Surah An-Naml 82], it is said, \"When they do not enjoin what is right and do not forbid what is wrong.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent on this in his summary."],[8503,"The Beast will come forth with the staff of Musa and the ring of Sulayman. It will polish the face of the believer with the staff and brand the nose of the disbeliever with the ring, until the people at the dining table will gather and say to this one: 'O believer,' and to this one: 'O disbeliever.'"],[8504,"A time will come upon people when a man will be envied for his light circumstances, just as a man today is envied for wealth and children.” A man asked him: “What wealth will be best on that day?” He said: “A good weapon and a good horse, with which he moves wherever he moves.”"],[8505,"On the day of the great battle, the camp of the Muslims will be in a land called al-Ghutah, in which there is a city called Damascus—the best of the Muslims' dwellings on that day."],[8506,"When the pledge of allegiance to Yazid b. Muawiyah came about, I said: 'If only I could go out to Syria and keep away from the evil of this pledge.' So I went out until I reached Syria. I was told of a place where Nawf was giving a talk, so I went to him. There was a man with weak eyes, wearing a cloak—it was Abdullah b. Amr b. al-As. When Nawf saw him, he stopped speaking. Abdullah said to him: 'Continue with what you were narrating.' He said: 'You are more entitled to speak than I; you are a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'These people—meaning the rulers—have prevented us from narrating.' He said: 'I adjure you to narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He said: 'I heard him say: \"There will be a migration after a migration; people will move to the migration place of Ibrahim. None will remain on earth except the worst of its people. Their land will cast them out, and their own souls will abhor them, and Allah will gather them to the Fire with monkeys and pigs. It will spend the night with them when they spend the night, take its midday rest with them when they rest, and eat those who lag behind.\"'"],[8507,"Abu Asim al-Nabil related to us: ‘Azrah b. Thabit related to us: ‘Ilba’ b. Ahmar related to us: Abu Zayd al-Ansari said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the morning prayer, then he addressed us until noon. Then he descended and prayed the noon prayer, then he addressed us until the afternoon. Then he descended and prayed the afternoon prayer, then he ascended and addressed us until sunset, and he informed us of what is to come.” The most retentive of us knew it."],[8508,"“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and did not leave anything that would occur from that moment until the establishment of the Hour except that he told us about it. Those who memorized it knew it, and those who forgot it forgot it. These companions of mine knew it, and indeed some of it will occur and I will have forgotten it, but when I see it, I will remember it just as a man recognizes the face of another man who has been absent from him.”"],[8509,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Verily, the people of my household will face killings and displacement after me from my nation. And indeed, the most hostile people towards us are the Banu Umayyah, Banu Al-Mughirah, and Banu Makhzoom.\""],[8510,"From the Prophet ﷺ regarding the barrier: He said: “They dig at it every day until, when they are about to break through it, the one in charge over them says, ‘Return, and you will break through it tomorrow.’ He said: Then Allah ﷻ restores it to the strongest it ever was. Until, when they reach their appointed time and Allah Most High wills, the one in charge over them says, ‘Return, and you will break through it tomorrow, if Allah Most High wills,’ and he makes an exception. He said: So they return, and it is as it was when they left it, then they break through it and come out upon the people. They drink up the waters, and the people flee from them. They shoot their arrows into the sky, and they return stained with blood. They say, ‘We have overcome the people of the earth and defeated those in the sky in power and elevation.’ He said: Then Allah ﷻ sends against them worms in their necks. He said: And they destroy them. He said: By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the beasts of the earth will grow fat, become bloated, and express gratitude, and become intoxicated from their flesh.”"],[8511,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he met Abraham, Moses, and Jesus (peace be upon them). They discussed the Hour, when it would be. They began with Abraham and asked him about it, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they asked Moses, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they returned the matter to Jesus. He said: Allah’s covenant to me regarding it is that only Allah ﷻ knows its appointed time. Then he mentioned the emergence of the Dajjal and said: I will descend and kill him. Then the people will return to their lands, and they will be met by Gog and Magog, who will come down from every slope. They will not pass by any water but drink it, nor by anything but corrupt it. They will cry out to me, and I will supplicate Allah, and He will cause them to die. The earth will stink from their odor, and they will cry out to me again, and I will supplicate Allah, and He will send rain from the sky, which will carry them and cast their bodies into the sea. Then the mountains will be pulverized, and the earth will be stretched out like a tanned hide. Allah’s covenant to me is that when that happens, the Hour will be to the people like a pregnant woman at full term whose household does not know when she will suddenly give birth, by night or by day. Al-‘Awwam said: I found confirmation of that in the Book of Allah ﷻ, then he recited: “Until, when Gog and Magog are let loose, and they descend from every height, and the true promise draws near” [Quran 21:96-97]."],[8512,"“A wind will come before the Hour and take the soul of every believer.”"],[8513,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Gog and Magog will be released and will come out upon the people, as Allah Most High said: ‘From every height they will descend’ [Quran 21:96]. They will spread corruption in the earth, and the Muslims will withdraw to their cities and fortresses, bringing their livestock with them, and they will drink the waters of the earth, until one of them passes by a river and they drink what is in it until they leave it dry. Then those after them pass by that river and say, ‘There was once water here.’ Until no one among the people remains except one who has taken refuge in a fortress or a city. Their spokesman says, ‘These are the people of the earth; we have finished with them. There remain the people of the sky.’ Then one of them shakes his spear and throws it into the sky, and it returns stained with blood as a trial and tribulation. While they are in that state, Allah sends against them worms in their necks, and they emerge in their necks, and they become dead, no sound heard from them. The Muslims say, ‘Is there a man who will risk his life for us to see what this enemy has done?’ Then a man among them volunteers for that, seeking reward with Allah, having resigned himself to being killed. He descends and finds them dead, one upon another. He calls out, ‘O Muslims, rejoice, for Allah has sufficed you against your enemy.’ So they come out of their cities and fortresses and let their livestock graze, and they find no pasture except their flesh, and they give thanks for it better than they ever gave thanks for any vegetation they had ever eaten.”"],[8514,"Gog and Magog: the first of them will pass by a river like the Tigris, and the last of them will pass and say, ‘There was once water in this river.’ No man among them will die except that he leaves a thousand or more of his offspring. After them will be three nations: Tawis, Tawil, and Nasik and Mansak."],[8515,"“Indeed Allah ﷻ divided creation into ten parts: He made nine parts the angels and one part the rest of creation. He divided the angels into ten parts: He made nine parts those who glorify Him night and day without tiring and one part for His message. He divided the creation into ten parts: He made nine parts the jinn and one part the children of Adam. He divided the children of Adam into ten parts: He made nine parts Gog and Magog and one part the rest of mankind. And the sky with its adornment.” He said: “The seventh heaven, and the sanctuary is directly opposite the Throne.”"],[8516,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I know better than the Dajjal what is with him. He has two rivers: one appears as fire blazing to the eye of the beholder, and the other as white water. If any of you encounters him, let him close his eyes and drink from the one he sees as fire, for it is cold water. Beware of the other, for it is the trial. Know that between his eyes is written ‘disbeliever’, which will be read by those who write and those who do not. One of his eyes is obliterated, with a growth over it. At the end of his affair, he will appear on the belly of the Jordan, at his house in Afiq, and everyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day in the belly of the Jordan. He will kill a third of the Muslims, rout a third, and leave a third. Night will fall upon them, and some believers will say to others, ‘What are you waiting for? Join your brothers in the pleasure of your Lord. Whoever has surplus food, let him bring it to his brother. Pray when dawn breaks, hasten the prayer, then advance against your enemy.’ When they stand to pray, Jesus son of Mary (blessings of Allah be upon him) will descend as their imam and lead them in prayer. When he finishes, he will say, ‘Open a way between me and the enemy of Allah.’ Abu Hazim said: Abu Hurayrah said: ‘He will melt as fat melts in the sun.’ And ‘Abdullah b. ‘Amr said: ‘As salt melts in water.’ Allah will empower the Muslims over them, and they will kill them, until even the tree and the stone will call out, ‘O servant of Allah, O ‘Abd al-Rahman, O Muslim, here is a Jew, kill him.’ Allah will expel them, and the Muslims will prevail. They will break the cross, kill the pig, and abolish the jizyah. While they are in that state, Allah will bring out Gog and Magog. The first of them will drink the lake, and the last of them will come and say, ‘There was once water here,’ and they will not leave a drop in it. They will say, ‘We have overcome our enemies; there was once a trace of water here.’ The Prophet of Allah ﷺ and his companions behind him will come until they enter a city of the cities of Palestine called Ludd. They will say, ‘We have overcome those on earth; come, let us fight those in the sky.’ The Prophet of Allah ﷺ will then supplicate to Allah, and Allah will send against them an ulcer in their throats, and none of them will remain alive. Their stench will harm the Muslims, and Jesus (blessings of Allah be upon him) will supplicate against them, and Allah will send a wind that will cast them all into the sea.”"],[8517,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal one morning, and he lowered and raised (his voice) until we thought he was among the palm trees. When we returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he recognized that in us and said, “What is the matter with you?” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, you mentioned the Dajjal this morning, and you lowered and raised (your voice) until we thought he was among the palm trees.” He said, “If he emerges while I am among you, I will be his opponent on your behalf. If he emerges and I am not among you, then every person is his own opponent, and Allah is my successor over every Muslim. He is a young man with curly hair, his beard prominent, as if he resembles ‘Uzza ibn Qatan. Whoever of you sees him, let him recite the opening verses of Surah al-Kahf.” Then he said, “I think he will emerge between Syria and Iraq and spread corruption right and left. O servants of Allah, be steadfast.” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, how long will he remain on earth?” He said, “Forty days: a day like a year, a day like a month, a day like a week, and the rest of his days like your days.” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, on the day like a year, will the prayer of one day suffice us?” He said, “No, estimate its proper measure.” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, how fast will he travel on earth?” He said, “Like rain driven by the wind.” He will come to a people and call them, and they will believe in him and respond to him. He will command the sky and it will rain, and command the earth and it will produce vegetation. Their livestock will return to them with longer udders, fuller teats, and wider flanks than ever before. Then he will come to another people and call them, but they will reject his words, so he will turn away from them and their wealth will follow him, and they will wake up destitute, with nothing in their hands. Then he will pass by a ruin and say to it, ‘Bring out your treasures,’ and it will depart, and its treasures will follow him like swarms of bees. Then he will call a young Muslim man and strike him with a sword, cutting him into two pieces as far apart as an arrow’s flight. Then he will call him, and he will come forward with a shining face and laughing. While he is doing that, Allah Most High will send Jesus son of Mary. He will descend at the white minaret east of Damascus, wearing two garments dyed with saffron, placing his hands on the wings of two angels. When he lowers his head, drops fall, and when he raises it, pearls like jewels roll down from it. No disbeliever can smell his breath but dies. His reach extends as far as his sight, and he will seek the Dajjal until he catches him at the gate of Ludd and kills him. Then Jesus son of Mary ﷺ , the Prophet of Allah, will come to a people whom Allah has protected from him, and he will wipe their faces and tell them of their ranks in Paradise. While they are in that state, Allah will reveal to him: ‘O Jesus, I have brought forth servants of Mine whom no one can fight. Take My servants to the mountain.’ And Allah will bring out Gog and Magog, and they will descend from every height. The first of them will pass by the Lake of Tiberias and drink what is in it. Then the last of them will pass and say, ‘There was once water here.’ The Prophet of Allah Jesus and his companions will be besieged, until the head of an ox for one of them will be better than a hundred dinars for one of you today. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ and his companions will supplicate to Allah ﷻ, and Allah will send worms in their necks, and they will fall dead as one soul. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ and his companions will descend, and they will not find a single span of ground except that Allah has filled it with their fat, stench, and blood. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ and his companions will supplicate to Allah, and He will send birds with necks like those of Bactrian camels, which will carry them and cast them wherever He wills. Then Allah will send rain that will not spare any house of mud or hair, and it will wash the earth until it leaves it like a mirror. Then He will say to the earth, ‘Produce your fruit and restore your blessing.’ On that day, a group will eat from a single pomegranate and seek shade under its skin, and milk will be blessed, until a milch camel will suffice a large group, a milch cow will suffice a tribe, and a milch sheep will suffice a clan. While they are in that state, Allah will send a pleasant wind that will take them under their arms and seize the soul of every Muslim, and the rest of the people will remain, fornicating publicly as donkeys do, and upon them the Hour will come.”"],[8518,"A boy was born to the brother of Umm Salamah, and they named him al-Walid. That was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, “You have named him with the names of your Pharaohs. There will surely be a man in this nation called al-Walid, who will be more harmful to this nation than Pharaoh was to his people.” Al-Zuhri said: “If al-Walid ibn Yazid becomes caliph, then it is he; otherwise, it is al-Walid ibn ‘Abd al-Malik.”"],[8519,"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention the Hour? He said: I heard him say, “You and the Hour are like these two.” The two Shaykhs agreed on its narration from the hadith of Shu‘bah, from Qatadah and Abu al-Tayyah, from Anas."],[8520,"The Hour will not be established until it is not said on the earth: 'Allah, Allah.'"],[8521,"The Hour will not be established until it is not said on the earth: 'There is no god but Allah.'"],[8522,"The Hour will not be established until it is not said on the earth: 'Allah, Allah,' and until a woman passes by a piece of a sandal and says, 'This once belonged to a man,' and until a man is the guardian of fifty women, and until the sky rains but the earth does not grow."],[8523,"By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the Hour will not be established upon a man who says 'There is no god but Allah' and enjoins good and forbids evil."],[8524,"The Hour will not be established until it is not said on the earth: 'Allah, Allah,' and until a woman passes by a sandal, picks it up, and says, 'This once belonged to a man,' and until there is among fifty women a single guardian, and until the sky rains but the earth does not grow."],[8525,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"The Hour will not be established until there is no one left on the face of the earth who has any need for Allah, and until a woman can be openly married in broad daylight in the middle of the road, and no one objects to it or changes it. The likeness of those people will be like the one who says, 'If you move her a little away from the road, that would be better.' On that day, Abu Bakr and Umar will be among you.\""],[8526,"The Hour will not be established except upon the dregs of people."],[8527,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited: {When comes the help of Allah and the victory, and you see people entering the religion of Allah in multitudes} [An-Nasr: 2], then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'People will leave it in multitudes just as they entered it in multitudes.'"],[8529,"I was sitting with Ali when Uqbah Abu Mas'ud came to him. Ali said to him: 'O Farrukh, are you the one who says — or is it not that you are the mufti — giving fatwas to the people?' He said: 'Indeed, I inform them of the last, and the last is worse.' He said: 'Then narrate to us what you heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about the hundred [years].' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A hundred years will not pass while there is on the earth an eye that blinks.'' Then Ali said: 'You have erred, and you erred in your first fatwa. That applies only to those who are alive on that day. Are ease and relief anything but after the hundred?'"],[8530,"The hundred will not come while there is anyone remaining on the face of the earth."],[8531,"He said about a month or so before his death: 'There is no soul born today that will reach a hundred years while it is alive on that day.'"],[8532,"He informed me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say about a month before his death: 'They ask about the Hour, but its knowledge is only with Allah. I swear by Allah, there is no soul born on the earth today that will reach a hundred years.'"],[8533,"I heard Abdullah b. Busr say: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ visited our house with Abu Bakr. I was going back and forth between my father and mother. We prepared food for him, and he ate and supplicated for us with a supplication I do not remember. Then he wiped his hand over my head and said: 'This boy will live a century.' He lived a hundred years.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the summary."],[8534,"That the Prophet ﷺ said to him: \"This boy will live a century.\" He said: So he lived a hundred years. And there was a wart on his face, so he said: \"He will not die until the wart disappears from his face.\" So he did not die until it went away. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8535,"I was with Abdullah b. Amr when a steward from Syria came to him, and two nights of Ramadan remained. Abdullah said to him: \"Did you leave my family enough to suffice them?\" He said: \"I left them provisions.\" Abdullah said: \"I adjure you to go back and leave them enough to suffice them, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'It is enough sin for a man to neglect those he is responsible for.'\""],[8536,"\"Indeed, tribulation has toils and pauses. If you can die during its pauses, then do so.\""],[8537,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The rulers from the Quraysh have not done right by you in three things: they did not show mercy when they should have shown mercy, they did not act justly when they distributed, and they did not act fairly when they judged.\""],[8538,"We were sitting one night with Abdullah while he was teaching us the Quran. A man asked him: \"O Abu Abd al-Rahman, did you ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ how many caliphs this nation will have?\" Abdullah said: \"No one has asked me about this since I came to Iraq before you.\" He said: \"We asked him, and he said: 'Twelve, the number of the chieftains of the Children of Israel.'\" I cannot permit myself to be lenient in this book regarding narrating from Mujalid and his peers, may Allah have mercy on them. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8539,"\"The Sufyani will appear over Syria, then there will be a battle between them at Qarqisiya until the birds of the sky and the beasts of the earth are satiated from their corpses. Then a rift will open behind them, and a faction of them will come until they enter the land of Khurasan. The cavalry of the Sufyani will come in pursuit of the people of Khurasan, and they will kill the Shi'a of the family of Muhammad ﷺ in Kufa. Then the people of Khurasan will come out in search of the Mahdi.\""],[8540,"\"When you see the black flags coming from Khorasan, then go to them, even if you have to crawl, because among them is the Caliph of Allah, the Mahdi.\""],[8541,"I set out with a group of my companions until we arrived in Makkah. He said: We looked for Abdullah b. Amr but did not find him. Then, near three hundred riding camels, we turned him back in the mosque. There was an old man wearing two Qatari cloaks and a turban, with no shirt. He said: \"Who are you?\" We said: \"From the people of Iraq.\" He said: \"You, O people of Iraq, lie and accuse others of lying and mock.\" We said: \"We do not lie, nor accuse others of lying, nor mock.\" He said: \"How far is it between you and al-Ayla?\" We said: \"Four parasangs.\" He said: \"It is near that the Banu Qantura' b. Karkar will drive you from Khurasan and Sijistan with a violent driving. Then they will come out until they tie their horses at the Tigris River. A people with small eyes, flat noses, as if their faces were layered shields.\""],[8542,"When Hudhayfa b. al-Yaman was dying, some Bedouins came to him and said: \"O Hudhayfa, we see you as one who is about to be taken.\" He said to them: \"A joyful servant and a beloved one who came in need. He who regrets will not prosper. O Allah, I have not shared in a traitor's treachery, so I seek refuge with You today from an evil companion. People used to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about good, but I used to ask him about evil. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we were in evil, then Allah brought us good. Is there evil after that good?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'And is there good after that evil?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'How?' He said: 'After me there will be leaders who do not follow my guidance and do not act according to my Sunnah. Men will arise whose hearts are the hearts of men in the body of a human.' I said: 'What should I do if I live to see that?' He said: 'Listen to the supreme commander, even if he strikes your back and takes your wealth.'\""],[8543,"\"This affair will remain among you, and you are its guardians, as long as you do not introduce deeds that strip it from you. If you do that, Allah will set over you the worst of His creation, and they will flay you as a branch is stripped of its bark.\""],[8544,"The faults of Sa'id b. al-As were reported to Hudhayfa, and he said: \"I do not know which of the two things you intended: seizing the authority of a people that is not yours, or repelling this tribulation. For it is sent by Allah, grazing in the land until it tramples its own reins. No one can repel it, and no one can prevent it. No one is left saying 'Allah, Allah' except that he is killed. Then Allah will send a people scattered like the scattered clouds of autumn.\" He said: \"Qaza' is a piece of thin cloud, like a shadow when it passes beneath a large cloud.\""],[8545,"\"When the scale is shortchanged, rain is withheld. When adultery increases, killing increases and plague occurs. When lying increases, turmoil increases.\""],[8546,"In Dhul-Qa'dah, the tribes will contend and depart, and the pilgrims will be plundered. There will be a great battle at Mina with many killed and blood flowing so that their blood runs over the Aqabah of the Jamrah. Their leader will flee and come between the Rukn and the Maqam and be given allegiance while he is unwilling. It will be said to him: 'If you refuse, we will strike your neck.' He will be given allegiance by a number equal to the people of Badr, with whom the inhabitant of heaven and the inhabitant of earth are pleased.\""],[8547,"\"The first thing you will lose of your religion is trustworthiness, and the last thing remaining will be prayer. This Quran that is among you will soon be taken away.\" They said: \"How will it be taken away when Allah has established it in our hearts and we have established it in our codices?\" He said: \"It will be taken away at night, and what is in your hearts and your codices will depart.\" Then he recited: {And if We willed, We could take away that which We revealed to you} (17:86)."],[8548,"“There will be rulers over you who will punish you and Allah will punish them.”"],[8549,"There will be in this nation five trials: a general trial and a specific trial, then a general trial and a specific trial, then there will be a black, dark trial in which people will be like beasts."],[8550,"“You will surely know that you are in a place where humans differ between Babel and al-Hirah. You will surely know that nine-tenths of good and one-tenth of evil are in Syria. You will surely know that nine-tenths of evil and one-tenth of good are elsewhere. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Ibn Mas'ud, it is near that the most beloved thing on the face of the earth to one of you will be to have donkeys that carry his family to Syria.”"],[8551,"Islam will wear out as a worn-out garment wears out, until people will not know what prayer, fasting, or sacrifice are, except that a man and an old woman will say, “We found people saying, 'There is no god but Allah.'” Silah b. Zufar said to him, “What will 'There is no god but Allah' avail them, O Hudhayfah, when they do not know prayer, fasting, or sacrifice?” Hudhayfah said: “O Silah, they will be saved from the Fire by 'There is no god but Allah.'”"],[8552,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ led us in the afternoon prayer, then stood as a speaker after the afternoon prayer until the setting of the sun. Those who memorized it memorized it and those who forgot it forgot it. He informed in it of what is to happen until the Day of Resurrection. He praised Allah Almighty and extolled Him, then said: “Now then, the world is sweet and green, and Allah Almighty is making you successors in it and is watching how you act. Beware of the world and beware of women. Indeed, the children of Adam were created in various categories. Among them is one who is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a believer. Among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a disbeliever. Among them is one who is born a believer, lives a believer, and dies a disbeliever. Among them is one who is born a disbeliever, lives a disbeliever, and dies a believer. Indeed, anger is a live coal kindled in the heart of the son of Adam. Do you not see the redness of his eyes and the swelling of his neck veins? When one of you feels something of that, let him cling to the ground. Indeed, the best of men is one who is slow to anger and quick to calm down, and the worst of men is one who is quick to anger and slow to calm down. If a man is quick to anger and quick to calm down, then it is equal to it. If a man is slow to anger and slow to calm down, then it is equal to it. Indeed, the best of traders is one who is good in settling debts and good in requesting repayment, and the worst of traders is one who is bad in settling debts and bad in requesting repayment. If a man is good in settling debts and bad in requesting repayment, then it is equal to it. If a man is bad in settling debts and good in requesting repayment, then it is equal to it. Indeed, let not awe of people prevent a man from speaking the truth when he knows it. Indeed, for every treacherous one there will be a banner on the Day of Resurrection according to his treachery. Indeed, the greatest treachery is the treachery of a leader of the common people. Indeed, the treacherous one's banner will be at his anus. Indeed, the most excellent jihad is a word of truth in the presence of a tyrannical ruler.” When it was near the setting of the sun, he said: “The example of what remains of the world compared to what has passed of it is like the example of what remains of this day of yours compared to what has passed.”"],[8553,"“The Book of Allah will be taken away at night and raised to heaven, so that no verse of the Qur'an, nor of the Torah, the Gospel, or the Psalms will remain on earth. It will be snatched from the hearts of men, and they will wake up not knowing what it is.”"],[8554,"We went out with Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari and said to him, “Give us instructions.” He said: “You must have piety toward Allah and adherence to the community of Muhammad ﷺ, for Allah Almighty will never gather the community of Muhammad upon misguidance. The religion of Allah is one. Beware of changing colors in the religion of Allah. You must have piety toward Allah and be patient until a righteous person finds rest and relief is obtained from a wicked person.”"],[8555,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “You must have piety toward Allah and the community, for Allah Almighty will not gather this nation upon misguidance. You must have patience until a righteous person finds rest and relief is obtained from a wicked person.”"],[8556,"“I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ throwing the pebble on the Day of Sacrifice, with no striking, no driving away, and no saying 'to you, to you.'”"],[8557,"About the Prophet ﷺ that he used to say, \"You will never cease to be in good as long as the people of your desert are self-sufficient from the people of your town.\" He said, \"And you should give them a portion of the crops and fruits so that they can be with you in the land, and do not prevent them from it due to the large number of those who will keep it hidden from you.\" He said, \"They will say, 'As long as we were hungry and you were satisfied, as long as we were poor and you were affluent, now we have been enriched and you are suffering, so grant us relief from the land's capacity.' ”He said, \"And the land will incline for you as a favor, and those who will perish will perish from it, and those who will remain will remain until the necks are freed, and then the land will be at peace with you after that, so that the freed will regret.\" He said, \"Then the land will incline for you again as another favor, and those who will perish will perish from it, and those who will remain will remain until the necks are freed, and then the land will be at peace with you.\" They will say, \"Our Lord, grant us freedom, our Lord, grant us freedom,\" and Allah will say, \"You lied, you lied. I will grant freedom.\" He said, \"And the followers of this nation will be tested with tremors, so if they repent, Allah will accept their repentance.\" He said, \"And if they revert, Allah will revert upon them with tremors, stoning, casting down, sinking, disfigurement, and lightning. So when it is said that people have perished, they have indeed perished. And Allah, the Almighty, will not punish a nation until it commits treachery.\" They said, \"And what is their treachery?\" He said, \"They confess their sins but do not repent, and hearts will find solace in what is within them of goodness and evil, just as a tree finds solace in what is within it, until a doer of good cannot increase in goodness, and an evildoer cannot repent.\" And that is because Allah, exalted and glorified, said, \"No, indeed, their hearts are covered with the evils of what they used to earn\" [Al-Mutaffifin: 14]."],[8558,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked over one of the fortresses of Madinah and said: “Do you see what I see?” They said, “No.” He said: “Indeed, I see trials falling among your houses like the falling of rain drops.”"],[8559,"He heard 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was asked, “Which of the two cities will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome?” He said: “The city of Heraclius first,” meaning Constantinople."],[8560,"Indeed, at the back of the Dajjal's head there are locks of hair, locks of hair. He will say, “I am your Lord.” Whoever says, “You are my Lord” will be tempted, and whoever says, “You have lied; my Lord is Allah, and upon Him I rely, and to Him I turn in repentance” will not be harmed, or he said, “Then there is no trial upon him.”"],[8561,"\"What trials descended tonight, and what treasures were opened? Wake the women in the chambers — his wives — for many a woman is clothed in this world but naked on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8562,"We were discussing in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ which is superior: the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ or the mosque of Jerusalem. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"One prayer in this mosque of mine is more excellent than four prayers there, and how excellent a place of prayer it is. Soon a man will have his horse's tether of land from which he can see Jerusalem, and that will be better for him than the whole world\" or he said, \"better than the world and all it contains.\""],[8563,"\"I saw as if the pillar of the Book was removed from under my pillow, and I followed it with my eyes, and behold, it was a radiant light taken up toward Syria. Indeed, faith, when trials occur, will be in Syria.\""],[8564,"\"Syria is the choice land of Allah; He drives to it His chosen servants. Whoever leaves Syria for elsewhere does so under His displeasure, and whoever enters it from elsewhere does so by His mercy.\""],[8565,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You will be drafted into armies: an army in Syria, an army in Iraq, and an army in Yemen.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, choose for me.\" He said: \"You must go to Syria; if anyone refuses, let him join his Yemen and drink from its ponds, for Allah ﷻ has guaranteed me Syria and its people.\""],[8567,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"O Allah, do not let me witness a time\" or \"may I not witness the time of a people who do not follow knowledge and are not shy before the forbearing; their hearts are non-Arab but their tongues are Arab tongues.\""],[8568,"I went out to perform Hajj. Sulayman b. Anaz, the judge of the people of Egypt, said to me: \"Convey my greetings to Abu Hurayrah and inform him that I sought forgiveness for him and his mother this morning.\" I met him and conveyed the message. He said: \"And I have sought forgiveness for him.\" Then he said: \"How did you leave Umm Hanw,\" meaning Egypt? I described its prosperity and comfort to him. He said: \"Indeed, it is the first land to be ruined, then Armenia.\" I said: \"Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" He said: \"No, but 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. al-'As told me that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'There will be migration after migration. The best of the earth's people will be the ones who cling most closely to the place of Abraham's migration. The worst of its people will remain on the earth; their lands will cast them out and Allah will find them detestable, and the Fire will gather them with apes and swine.'\" According to the conditions of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8569,"\"Soon the farthest outposts of the Muslims will be at Silah,\" and Silah is near Khaybar."],[8570,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Muslims will soon be surrounded in the city until their furthest weapon becomes a weapon.\" This narration is from Ibn Wahb narrated by Jarir and is authentic according to the condition of Muslim. He argued in his book, may Allah have mercy on him, with Abu Abdullah, may Allah have mercy on him, according to the condition of Muslim."],[8571,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about the food of the believers at the time of the Dajjal. He said: \"The food of the angels.\" They said: \"What is the food of the angels?\" He said: \"Their food is their utterance of glorification and sanctification. Whoever's utterance on that day is glorification and sanctification, Allah will remove hunger from him, and he will not fear hunger.\""],[8572,"Whoever recites Surat al-Kahf as it was revealed, then goes out to the Dajjal, the Dajjal will not be given power over him, or he will have no way against him."],[8573,"\"Soon Allah will fill your hands with non-Arabs, and they will be like whelps: they will not be hospitable, they will kill your warriors, and they will consume your spoils.\""],[8574,"On the authority of the Prophet ﷺ , he said: \"People will experience years where the liar will be believed, the truthful will be disbelieved, the trustworthy will be betrayed, the treacherous will be trusted, and the foolish will speak about public matters.\" It was asked, \"O Messenger of Allah, who are the foolish?\" He replied, \"Those who speak about matters that concern the public.\" Ibn Qudamah said: Yahya bin Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to me from al-Maqburi, who said, \"And in those years, immorality will spread.\""],[8575,"We performed Hajj and passed by the road of al-Munkadir, which people used back then, but we lost the way. While we were in that state, an Arab appeared to us as if he had sprung from the earth. He said: \"Old man, do you know where you are?\" I said: \"No.\" He said: \"You are at al-Raba'ib, and this white hill you see is the bones of Bakr b. Wa'il and Taghlib, and this is the grave of Kulayb and his brother Muhalhil.\" Then he guided us to the road and said: \"There is a man here who was a companion of the Prophet ﷺ. Would you like to visit him?\" I said: \"Yes.\" He took us to an old man with his eyebrows bound by a bandage, in a leather tent. We said to him: \"Who are you?\" He said: \"I am al-'Adda' b. Khalid, the rider of al-Sahba' in the Jahiliyyah.\" We said to him..."],[8576,"From the Prophet ﷺ, I understood it and wrote it with my own hand: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate. This is what 'Abdullah b. 'Amr narrated from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: \"Indeed, Allah the Exalted does not love the obscene person nor the one who acts obscenely.\" Sound."],[8577,"\"A time will come upon people when the sky will send down rain but the earth will not produce vegetation.\""],[8578,"Abdullah ibn Abbas told me, \"If I had not heard that you are like the people of the household, I would not have told you this hadith.\" He said, \"So, Mujahid said, 'It is in secrecy, I do not mention it to those who dislike it.' \" Ibn Abbas said, \"Among us, the people of the household, there are four: the martyr, the giver of admonition, the supported one, and the guided one.\" Mujahid said to him, \"Explain these four to me.\" He said, \"As for the martyr, he may kill his supporters and forgive his enemies. As for the giver of admonition, he gives a great amount of wealth without considering himself superior and holds a small amount of his rights. As for the supported one, he is given victory over his enemy. He is given half of what the Prophet ﷺ used to be given, and his enemy is terrified of him for a distance of two months. The supported one terrifies his enemy for a distance of one month. As for the guided one, he will fill the earth with justice as it was filled with injustice, and the cattle and wild animals will feel secure, and the earth will throw out its treasures.\" He said, \"I said, 'What are its treasures?' He said, 'Golden and silver dishes.'\""],[8579,"\"Tribulations will cover you like pieces of a dark night. The safest among people then will be a man living on a mountain peak, eating from his grazing sheep, or a man holding the reins of his horse from behind the mountain pass, eating from his sword.\""],[8580,"How will you be when a tribulation envelops you in which the elder grows senile, the young grows up, and the people take it as a sunnah, so that when it is changed they say, \"The sunnah has been changed\"? It was said, \"When will that be, O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman?\" He said, \"When your reciters become many and your jurists become few, your wealth becomes abundant and your trustworthy people become few, and the worldly life is sought through deeds of the Hereafter.\""],[8581,"Marwan approached one day and found a man placing his face on the grave. He seized him by the neck and said, \"Do you know what you are doing?\" He said, \"Yes.\" He turned to him, and behold, it was Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. He said, \"I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, not to the stone. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Do not weep over the religion when its people are in charge of it, but weep over it when someone other than its people is in charge of it.'\""],[8582,"\"A group of people from this nation will spend the night with food, drink, and amusement, and will wake up transformed into pigs. And tribes will be swallowed up, along with houses, until they wake up and say: 'Last night the tribe of so-and-so was swallowed up; last night the house of so-and-so was swallowed up.' And stones will be sent upon them, just as they were sent upon the people of Lut, and the barren wind will be sent upon them, sweeping them away as it swept away those before them, because of their drinking wine, consuming usury, wearing silk, taking singing girls, and severing ties of kinship.\" He said, \"And he mentioned another trait, but I have forgotten it.\""],[8583,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: \"You will surely conquer the treasures of Kisra Al-Abiad, or the treasures within it, with a group of Muslims.\""],[8584,"\"Hasten to good deeds before six things: the rising of the sun from the west, the smoke, the Dajjal, the beast of the earth, the private matter of one of you, and the general affair.\""],[8585,"A man said, \"O Mother of the Believers, tell us a hadith about the earthquake.\" She turned her face away from him. Anas said, \"So I said to her, 'Tell us, O Mother of the Believers, about the earthquake.'\" She said, \"O Anas, if I tell you about it, you will live sad and be resurrected, when you are resurrected, with that sadness in your heart.\" I said, \"O mother, tell us.\" She said, \"Indeed, when a woman takes off her clothes in other than her husband's house, she tears the veil between herself and Allah ﷻ. And if she perfumes herself for other than her husband, it will be fire and disgrace upon her. So when they deem fornication lawful, drink wine after that, and strike musical instruments, Allah becomes jealous in His heaven and says to the earth: 'Quake with them.' If they repent and desist, then fine; otherwise, He will collapse it upon them.\" Anas said, \"As punishment for them?\" She said, \"As mercy, blessing, and admonition for the believers, and as a deterrent, wrath, and punishment for the disbelievers.\" Anas said, \"After the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I have never heard a hadith that made me happier than this one. Rather, I live glad and will be resurrected, when I am resurrected, with that gladness in my heart—or he said, 'in my soul.'\""],[8586,"I asked my Lord for three things, and He granted me two and withheld one. I asked Him not to destroy my nation by years of famine, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to set over them an enemy from other than themselves, and He granted me that. I asked Him not to make them into factions and make some of them taste the might of others, and He withheld that from me."],[8587,"We have seen everything the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told us, except that he said: \"On the Day of Resurrection, it will be said to some men: 'Throw down your whips and enter Hell.'\""],[8588,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Khalid, there will be after me new matters, tribulations, and discord. So if you are able to be the servant of Allah who is killed, not the killer, then do so.\" Only 'Ali b. Zayd al-Qurashi narrated it from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, and the two (al-Bukhari and Muslim) did not use 'Ali as a source. Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in al-Talkhis."],[8589,"He said, \"Do you know where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed in this mosque of yours?\" I said, \"Yes,\" and I pointed to a corner of it. He said, \"Do you know the three things he supplicated for in it?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Tell me them.\" I said, \"He supplicated that no enemy from other than themselves be given power over them, and that they not be destroyed by years of famine, and these two were granted to him. And he supplicated that their might not be made to be between themselves, and that was withheld from him.\""],[8590,"The Prophet ﷺ said, \"There will be a disturbance in the month of Ramadan that will awaken the sleeper and frighten the awake. Then a faction will appear in Shawwal, followed by commotion in Dhul-Hijjah. Then the sacred limits will be violated in Muharram, and death will occur in Safar. The tribes will then dispute in Rabee' al-Awwal. Astonishment, the greatest astonishment, will occur between Jumada I and Rajab. Then a she-camel that is used for carrying water will be better than a treasure of a hundred thousand.\"[1]"],[8591,"I visited Abu Hurayrah and leaned him against my chest, then I said: O Allah, cure Abu Hurayrah. He said: \"O Allah, do not return it (i.e., the illness).\" Then he said: \"If you are able, O Abu Salamah, to die, then die.\" I said: O Abu Hurayrah, we love life. He said: \"By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, there will come upon the scholars a time when death will be dearer to one of them than red gold. One of you will come to the grave of his brother and say: Would that I were in his place.\""],[8593,"\"Allah is about to fill your hands with non-Arabs and make them lions who do not flee, and they will strike your necks and consume your spoils.\""],[8594,"\"There will be rulers over you who abandon from the Sunnah the like of this\" – and he pointed to the base of his finger. \"If you abandon them, they will bring the great calamity. There was no nation except that the first thing they abandoned from their religion was the Sunnah, and the last thing they gave up was prayer. Were it not that they feel ashamed, they would not pray.\""],[8595,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent an expedition to Dumat al-Jandal and said: \"Go, for you will find Ukaydir of Duma outside hunting game, so seize him firmly.\" They went and found him as he had told them, so they seized him. The people of the city fortified themselves and looked down upon the Muslims, speaking to them. A man from the Muslims said to one of those who looked down: I remind you of Allah, do you find Muhammad in your Book? He said: No. Another beside him said: We find him in our Book resembling a Qurayshi; a pen from Satan makes him appear. The man said: O Abu Bakr, have these people not disbelieved? He said: \"Yes, and you will disbelieve.\" When the army returned and Musaylimah emerged and claimed prophethood, the man said to Abu Bakr: Do you not remember your saying while we were at Dumat al-Jandal: 'And you will disbelieve'? Was that the matter of Musaylimah? He said: \"No, that is at the end of time.\""],[8596,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"A man called the Sufyani will emerge in the depths of Damascus, and most of those who follow him will be from Kalb. He will kill until he rips open the bellies of women and kills children. Qays will rally against them, but he will kill them until not even the end of a ravine is defended.\" \"A man from my household will emerge in al-Harrah, and news of him will reach the Sufyani. He will send against him a contingent of his army, but the man will defeat them. The Sufyani and those with him will then march against him until, when they reach a desert plain, the earth will swallow them. None of them will survive except the one who reports what happened to them.\"[1]"],[8597,"They came with Abu Musa on a military expedition. When they camped at a place, he said: \"We used to talk that before the Hour there will be harj.\" They said: What is harj, O commander? He said: \"Killing.\" We said: We kill a lot; in a year, if Allah wills, we kill more than a hundred thousand. He said: \"It is not your killing the polytheists, but your killing one another.\" We said: Will we have our intellects on that day? Abu Musa said: \"The intellects of most of that time will be removed, and a remnant of people will be left, most of whom think they are upon something, but they are not upon anything. By Allah, I do not find for myself or for you, if it overtakes me and you, in what we recite from the Book of our Lord and in what our Prophet enjoined upon us, any way except that we should not exit from it as we entered into it.\""],[8598,"The devil of al-Radhah will be descended upon by a man from Bajilah called al-Ashhab or Ibn al-Ashhab, the horse herder, and the horse herder is a sign among the oppressive people."],[8599,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The lifespan of Islam will be for thirty-five or thirty-six years. If they are destroyed, the religion will be revived for them for seventy years.\" Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, with what has passed or with what remains?\" He replied, \"With what remains.\""],[8600,"The emergence of the Beast will be after the rising of the sun from its west. When it emerges, it will strike Iblis while he is prostrating. The believers will enjoy themselves on earth after that for forty years, not wishing for anything except that it is given to them, and they find it, with no injustice or oppression. Things will have submitted to the Lord of the worlds willingly and unwillingly, so much so that a predatory animal will not harm a beast or a bird. A believer will be born and will not die until he completes forty years after the emergence of the Beast of the earth. Then death will return among them, and they will remain like that as long as Allah wills. Then death will hasten among the believers, and no believer will remain. The disbeliever will say: We used to be terrified of the believers, but none of them remains, and repentance is not accepted from us. Then they will copulate with one another in the roads like the copulation of beasts. One of them will stand with his mother, sister, or daughter and have intercourse with her in the middle of the road. One will get off her and another will mount her, not disapproving or changing. The best of them that day will be the one who says: If you would move aside from the road, it would be better. They will remain like that until none of the children of legitimate marriage remains, and the people of the earth will be children of fornication. They will remain like that as long as Allah wills. Then Allah will make the wombs of women barren for thirty years; no woman will give birth, and there will be no child on earth. All of them will be children of adultery, the worst of people, and upon them the Hour will arise."],[8601,"I was in Madinah when I saw a man from whom the people fled when they saw him. I said: Who are you? He said: I am Abu Dharr, the companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I said: Why do the people flee from you? He said: \"I forbid them from treasures with that which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid them.\" I said: Our grants have increased today and reached a high amount; do you fear anything for us? He said: \"As for today, no, but it is near that they will become the price of your religion. When they become the price of your religion, then leave them and beware of them.\""],[8602,"\"Indeed, Allah will send to this nation at the head of every hundred years one who will renew for it its religion.\""],[8603,"\"Indeed, Allah will send at the head of every hundred years one who will renew for it its religion.\""],[8604,"Abu al-Muwajjah narrated to us, Abdan informed us, Abdullah informed us, Sufyan informed us from Jami' b. Abi Rashid from Abu Ya'la Mundhir al-Thawri from al-Hasan b. Muhammad b. Ali from a freedwoman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, she said: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Aishah or upon one of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ while I was with him, and he said: \"When evil appears and they do not forbid it, Allah sends His punishment upon them.\" A man said: O Prophet of Allah, even if there are righteous people among them? He said: \"Yes, what befell them will befall them, then they will go to Allah's forgiveness and mercy\" – or \"to Allah's mercy and forgiveness.\" Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8605,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Hour, his cheeks would redden, his anger would intensify, and his voice would rise as if he were a warner of an army saying, “It will come upon you in the morning or evening.”"],[8606,"Abu al-Darda’ said to me, “How do you see the people?” I said, “They are fine: their call is one, their imam is one, their enemy is expelled, and their grants and provisions are abundant.” He said, “Then how will it be when their hearts detest one another, their tongues curse one another, their enmity appears, their mutual bonds are corrupted, and they strike one another’s necks?”"],[8607,"“My ummah will not be tried until there appear among them tamāyuz, tamāyul, and maqāmiʿ.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, what is tamāyuz?” He said, “Tamāyuz is a tribal zeal that people will introduce after me in Islam.” I said, “Then what is tamāyul?” He said, “A tribe will incline against another tribe and regard its sanctity as violable.” I said, “Then what are maqāmiʿ?” He said, “The march of the garrisons against one another; their necks will clash in war.”"],[8608,"I entered the mosque with ʿAbd Allah. The people were bowing, so he bowed. A man passed by and greeted him. ʿAbd Allah said, “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.” Then he joined the row. When he finished, I asked him about his saying, “Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth.” He said, “He used to say: ‘The Hour will not come until mosques are taken as thoroughfares, until a man greets another man only out of acquaintance, until a woman and her husband engage in trade together, and until horses and women become expensive, then become cheap, and they will not become expensive again until the Day of Resurrection.’”"],[8609,"I came to them to fight alongside them, until I remembered a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: it reached him that Kisra or one of the kings of the Persians died, and they put a woman in charge of their affairs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “A people will not succeed if a woman rules over them.”"],[8610,"I was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ, and he mentioned the fitnah, or it was mentioned to him. He said, “When people’s covenants become corrupted, their trusts become light, and they become like this”—and he interlaced his fingers. I stood up to him and said, “How should I act at that time, O Messenger of Allah? May Allah make me your ransom.” He said, “Restrain your tongue, sit in your house, take what you know and leave what you disapprove of, attend to your own self, and leave aside the affairs of the common people.”"],[8611,"When Ibn al-Zubayr was besieged and the doors of the mosque were fortified against the people of Syria, he heard two of his freedmen behind him speaking. He turned to them and said, “No one has followed the scriptures as I have followed them. I have read the scriptures and heard the hadiths, and I found everything false except what is in the Book of Allah, Exalted is He.” Then he went out and touched the Corner, then entered upon his mother Asma’ and kissed her and kissed between the veil and the face above the forehead. She said, “What sound do I hear?” It was said to her, “The people of Syria.” She said, “Are they all Muslims?” It was said to her, “Yes, they claim so.” She said, “I have seen Islam; if they gathered over a sheep, they would not eat it.” Then she said, “O my son, die honorably and do not surrender.” ʿAbd Allah said, “Where are the people of Egypt?” They said to him, “At the gate, the gate of Banu Jumaʿ,” and it was the gate with the most people. He charged against them, and they were routed as far as the market. Khubayb was striking them with the sword from behind them, saying, “Charge!” and no one entered upon him. Then he charged again and they were routed. When they saw that, they brought in a black man. When they saw him, they turned to deceive him. The black man entered until he was between the curtains of the Kaʿbah. When he came to him, Ibn al-Zubayr went out to him and struck him, cutting off both his legs. He began to struggle along, then he fell, and he did not turn to him until a stone came and hit him near the ear, and he fell, and they killed him."],[8612,"When al-Hajjaj prevailed over Ibn al-Zubayr, killed him, and mutilated him, then he entered upon the mother of ʿAbd Allah, who was Asma’ bt. Abi Bakr. She said, “How do you seek permission to enter upon me when you have killed my son?” He said, “Your son violated the sanctity of Allah’s sanctuary, so I killed him as a heretic and a disobedient one, until Allah made him taste a painful punishment, and I did such-and-such to him.” She said, “You lie, O enemy of Allah and enemy of the Muslims. By Allah, you killed him while he was one who fasted much, prayed much, was dutiful to his parents, and upheld this religion. If you ruined his worldly life, he has ruined your hereafter. And indeed...”"],[8613,"From Husayn, he mentioned the hadith in a similar manner and added to it: Al-Hajjaj said, “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth, and you spoke the truth. I am the destroyer; I destroy the hypocrites.”"],[8614,"I used to come to Madinah and meet some of the companions of the Messenger of Allah. The one I most loved to meet was Ubayy b. Kaʿb. I arrived in Madinah during the time of ʿUmar. They established the dawn prayer, and ʿUmar came out with some men. A man among the people looked at the faces of the people, recognized them, and did not recognize me. He pushed me and stood in my place. I prayed without understanding my prayer. When he finished, he said, “O my son, may Allah not grieve you. I did not do what I did out of ignorance. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us, ‘Be in the row that is nearest to me.’ I looked at the faces of the people and recognized them except you.” Then he sat down. I have never seen men stretch their necks toward something as they did toward him, and behold, it was Ubayy b. Kaʿb. Among what he said was: “The people of the covenant have perished, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah. The people of the covenant have perished, by the Lord of the Kaʿbah. By Allah, I do not grieve for them; I only grieve for the Muslims they destroyed.”"],[8615,"“The destruction of my ummah will be at the hands of young boys from Quraysh.”"],[8616,"“The corruption of my ummah will be at the hands of foolish young boys from Quraysh.”"],[8617,"Gog and Magog: a span, two spans, and three; and they are from the children of Adam."],[8618,"The Dajjal will emerge from a land in the east called Khurasan, followed by peoples whose faces are like hammered shields."],[8619,"Regarding the Prophet ﷺ, he said, \"The Antichrist will emerge from here or here or from here, but rather he will emerge from here,\" meaning the east."],[8620,"Hisham, these people are passing by to a man whom we saw more of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than, and preserved more from him. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Between the creation of Adam and the establishment of the Hour, there is no tribulation greater in the sight of Allah than the Dajjal.”"],[8621,"I was in the Hijr with Hudhayfah, and he mentioned a hadith, then said: “The knots of Islam shall be undone one by one, and there shall be misleading leaders, and after that the three Dajjals will emerge.” I said: O Abu Abdullah, did you hear this that you say from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: Yes, I heard it—rather, it is denounced."],[8622,"I was in Kufa when it was said that the Dajjal had emerged. He said: We came to Hudhayfah ibn Asid while he was narrating, and I said: This Dajjal has emerged. He said: Sit. So I sat. Then the arif came to me and said: This Dajjal has emerged, and the people of Kufa are fighting him. He said: Sit. So I sat. Then it was announced that it was a lie, a dyer. He said: We said: O Abu Sarihah, you only made us sit for some matter, so narrate to us. He said: If the Dajjal were to emerge in your time, the children would pelt him with pebbles. But the Dajjal will emerge amid hatred from the people, scantiness of religion, and evil discord. He will come to every watering place, and the earth will be folded for him like the folding of a ram's hide, until he comes to Madinah. He will prevail over its outskirts and be barred from its interior. Then he will go to the mountain of Iliya' and besiege a band of Muslims. Those who are over them will say: What are you waiting for with this tyrant? Fight him until you meet Allah or victory is granted to you. They will resolve to fight him when morning comes. When morning comes, Jesus son of Mary will be with them, and he will kill the Dajjal and rout his companions, until even the tree, the stone, and the clod say: O believer, here is a Jew with me, so kill him. He said: In him are three signs: he is one-eyed, and your Lord is not one-eyed; and written between his eyes is 'kafir,' which every believer, literate or illiterate, reads. And no mount will be subjected to him except the donkey—so he is filth upon filth. Then he said: I am more afraid for myself and for you of other than the Dajjal. He said: We said: What is it, O Abu Sarihah? He said: “Tribulations like patches of dark night.” He said: We said: Which people are worst in it? He said: “Every eloquent preacher and every rider who spreads (news).” We said: Which people are best in it? He said: “Every rich person who is hidden.” I said: I am neither rich nor hidden. He said: “Then be like the weaned camel calf: no back to be ridden and no udder to be milked.”"],[8623,"The Dajjal will emerge amid scantiness of religion and retreat of knowledge. He will have forty days to roam: one day like a year, one day like a month, one day like a week, and the rest of his days like your days. He will have a donkey to ride, the width between its ears forty cubits. He will come to the people and say: I am your Lord, though your Lord is not one-eyed. Written between his eyes is K F R, which every believer, literate or illiterate, reads. He will pass by every water and watering place except Madinah and Makkah—Allah has forbidden them to him, and the angels stand at their gates."],[8624,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal and said: “If he emerges while I am among you, I will be his adversary. If he emerges while I am not among you, then every person is his own adversary, and Allah is my successor over every Muslim. Indeed, he is blind in one eye, as if it were the eye of 'Abd al-'Uzza ibn Qatan al-Khuza'i. Indeed, written between his eyes is 'kafir,' which every Muslim reads. Whoever of you meets him, let him recite the opening of Surat al-Kahf. He will emerge from between Syria and Iraq, causing corruption right and left. O servants of Allah, stand firm.” He said it three times. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how long will he remain on earth? He said: “Forty days: a day like a year, a day like a month, a day like a week, and the rest of his days like your days.” They said: O Messenger of Allah, how should we perform prayer on that day—a full day's prayer or should we estimate? He said: “Rather, estimate.”"],[8625,"“Whoever of you hears of the emergence of the Dajjal, let him keep far from him. For a man will come to him thinking he is a believer, and he will keep following him because of the specious things he sees.”"],[8626,"“Whoever hears of the Dajjal, let him keep far from him”—he said it three times—“for a man will come to him and follow him, thinking he is truthful because of the specious things he has been sent with.”"],[8627,"We were on a journey heading to Kufa with the Commander of the Faithful 'Ali ibn Abi Talib. When we reached a distance of two or three nights' travel from Harura', some people broke away from us. We mentioned that to 'Ali, and he said: Do not be alarmed by their affair, for they will return. We halted. The next day, twice as many broke away. We mentioned that to 'Ali, and he said: Do not be alarmed by their affair, for their matter is insignificant. 'Ali said: Do not initiate fighting with them until they are the ones who initiate against you. They knelt on their knees, and we shielded ourselves with our shields. They began shooting us with arrows and bolts. Then they drew near to us and leveled their spears at us. Then they attacked us with swords, until they were about to put the swords to us. A man from 'Abd al-Qays called Sa'sa'ah ibn Suhan went out to them and called out three times. They said: What do you want? He said: I remind you of Allah, lest you go out in a land that becomes a disgrace upon the people of the earth. And I remind you of Allah, lest you depart from the religion as an arrow passes through the game. When we saw that they had put the swords to us, 'Ali said: Rise up with the blessing of Allah Almighty. It was only a short while of the day until we had laid low those we laid low and those who fled fled. 'Ali praised Allah and said: My close friend ﷺ told me: “The leader of these is a man with a deformed hand; on the nipple of his breast are small hairs like the tail of a jerboa. So search for him.” They searched for him but did not find him. We came to him and said: We did not find him. He said: Search for him, for by Allah, I have not lied nor been lied to. We kept searching for him until 'Ali himself came to the end of the battlefield that had been theirs. He kept saying: Turn over this one, turn over that one, until a man from Kufa came and said: Here he is. 'Ali said: Allah is Greatest. By Allah, no one will come to you telling you that his father was an angel. The people began saying: This is an angel, this is an angel. 'Ali said: Son of whom? They said: We do not know. Then a man from Kufa came and said: I am the most knowledgeable of people about this one. I was training a filly for so-and-so, son of so-and-so, an old man from Banu so-and-so, and I would put light saddlebags on her back and bring her back and forth. The filly bolted, and he called me: O boy, look, for the filly has bolted. I said: I see a phantom like a bucket or a sheep. Then this one appeared before us. He said: Who is the man? He said: A man from the people of Yamamah. He said: What has brought you, disheveled and pale? He said: I came to worship Allah in the prayer place of Kufa. He took him by the hand—there were only four of us, besides Allah—until he brought him to the house. He said to his wife: Allah Almighty has brought you good. She said: By Allah, I am in need of that; what is it? He said: This man, disheveled and pale as you see, came from Yamamah to worship Allah in the prayer place of Kufa. He worshiped Allah there and called the people until they gathered to him. 'Ali said: Indeed, my close friend ﷺ told me: “They are three brothers from the jinn; this is the eldest of them, the second has a large following, and the third has weakness.” Muslim, may Allah have mercy on him, included the hadith of the deformed one in abridged form in the authentic collection, but they did not include it with this wording. “Its chain is authentic.”"],[8629,"We were with Hudhayfah in this mosque, and he said: “Tribulations have come to you, throwing with violence; then the one after it throws with crushing; then the one after it is dark. There is no man among you, until he sees what you see, who has not seen the tribulation of the Messiah, and then he will never see it.” He said: Among us was a bedouin from Rabi'ah—there was no living person among us other than him. He said: Glory be to Allah, O companions of Muhammad ﷺ! How can that be with the Messiah, when he has been described to us as broad of forehead, prominent of neck, and wide between the shoulders? Then I saw Hudhayfah pause from it for a moment. He said: I adjure you by Allah, do you know how I said it? He said: You said: “There is no man among you, until he sees what you see, who has not seen the tribulation of the Dajjal, and then he will never see it.” He said: Then I saw Hudhayfah struggling with his face. He said: I said: Is it because he preserved the hadith as it is? He said: Yes. Then he said a weak word: “Do you consider the Day of the House, yesterday? For it was a general tribulation that enveloped the people.” He said: Among us was a bedouin from Rabi'ah—there was no living person among us other than him. He said: Glory be to Allah, O companions of Muhammad! Then where are those who drive our camels and dig into our houses? He said: “Those are the transgressors,” twice. He said: “I went out on the day of Jara'ah, and I knew that not a cupping glass of blood was shed in it, and I forbade none but Ibn al-Hisramah.” Among us was a bedouin from Rabi'ah—there was no living person among us other than him. He said: Glory be to Allah, O companions of Muhammad ﷺ! Ibn al-Hisramah to the exclusion of others? He said: “When it approaches, it is for the one who stands and the one who speaks; Ibn al-Hisramah is a man of much speech.”"],[8630,"From the hadith of 'Amr al-Hadrami of the people of Homs, from Abu Umamah al-Bahili, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us one day, and most of his sermon was mention of the Dajjal, telling us about him until he finished his sermon. Among what he said to us that day: Allah Almighty did not send a prophet except that he warned his nation about the Dajjal. I am the last of the prophets, and you are the last of the nations, and he will inevitably emerge among you. If he emerges while I am among you, I will be the adversary of every Muslim. If he emerges among you after me, then every person is his own adversary, and Allah is my successor over every Muslim. He will emerge from a gap between Iraq and Syria, causing corruption right and left. O servants of Allah, stand firm. He will begin by saying: I am a prophet, though there is no prophet after me. Then he will go on until he says: I am your Lord, though you will not see your Lord until you die. Written between his eyes is 'kafir,' which every believer reads. Whoever of you meets him, let him spit in his face and recite the openings of Surat al-Kahf. He will be given power over one soul of the children of Adam; he will kill it and then bring it back to life. He will not go beyond that, and he will not be given power over any other soul. Part of his tribulation is that with him is a garden and a fire: his fire is a garden, and his garden is a fire. Whoever is tested with his fire, let him close his eyes and seek help from Allah; it will become coolness and safety for him, as the fire became coolness and safety for Abraham ﷺ . Part of his tribulation is that he will pass by a tribe, and they will believe in him and affirm him, so he will pray for them, and the sky will rain upon them from that day, the earth will become fertile for them from that day, and their livestock will return to them in the evening from that day, greater than they were, fatter, fuller in flanks, and more abundant in milk. He will pass by a tribe, and they will disbelieve in him and deny him, so he will pray against them, and no grazing animal will go out for them. His days are forty: a day like a year, a day like a month, a day like a week, and a day like the (ordinary) days. The last of his days is like a mirage: a man will be at the gate of Madinah in the morning and reach its other gate before evening. They said: How should we pray, O Messenger of Allah, in those short days? He said: “Estimate them, then pray as you estimate in the long days.”"],[8631,"Hearken! Every prophet warned his nation about the Dajjal, and indeed he, on this day of his, has eaten food. I am making a covenant that no prophet before me made for his nation. Hearken! His right eye is effaced in its pupil, protruding and not hidden; it is as if it were a spittle on the side of a wall. Hearken! His left eye is like a brilliant star. With him is something like Paradise and something like Fire: the Fire is a green meadow and the Paradise is dusty, full of smoke. Hearken! Before him are two men who warn the people of the villages; whenever they enter a village they warn its people, and when they leave it, the first of the companions of the Dajjal enters it. He will enter all villages except Makkah and Madinah, for they are forbidden to him. And the believers are scattered throughout the earth, and Allah will gather them for him. A man among the believers says to his companions: 'I will go to this man and see whether he is the one the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us about or not.' Then he turns away, and his companions say to him: 'By Allah, we will not let you go to him. If we knew that he would kill you when you went to him, we would let you go, but we fear that he will tempt you.' But the believing man refused them except to go to him. So he set out walking until he came to one of his outposts, and they seized him and asked him: 'What is your matter and what do you want?' He said to them: 'I want the lying Dajjal.' They said: 'Do you say that?' He said: 'Yes.' So they sent to the Dajjal: 'We have seized someone who says such and such; shall we kill him or send him to you?' He said: 'Send him to me.' So he was taken until he was brought to the Dajjal. When he saw him, he recognized him by the description of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Dajjal said to him: 'What is your matter?' The believing servant said: 'You are the lying Dajjal about whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ warned us.' The Dajjal said to him: 'Do you say this?' He said: 'Yes.' The Dajjal said to him: 'You will obey me in what I command you, or I will split you into two halves.' The believing servant called out and said: 'O people, this is the lying Messiah; whoever disobeys him is in Paradise and whoever obeys him is in the Fire.' The Dajjal said to him: 'By the One I swear by, you will obey me or I will split you into two halves.' The believing servant called out and said: 'O people, this is the lying Messiah; whoever disobeys him is in Paradise and whoever obeys him is in the Fire.' He said: Then he stretched out his leg and placed his blade on the base of his tail and split him into two halves. When he had done that to him, the Dajjal said to his allies: 'Have you seen? If I bring this one back to life for you, will you not know that I am your Lord?' They said: 'Yes.' Atiyyah said: Abu Sa'id al-Khudri narrated to me that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then he struck one of his halves, or the ground near him, and he stood up straight. When his allies saw him, they believed him and were certain that he was their Lord, and they answered him and followed him.' The Dajjal said to the believing servant: 'Will you not believe in me?' The believer said to him: 'I am now more insightful about you than before.' Then he called out among the people: 'Hearken! This is the lying Messiah; whoever obeys him is in the Fire and whoever disobeys him is in Paradise.' The Dajjal said: 'By the One I swear by, you will obey me or I will slaughter you or throw you into the Fire.' The believer said to him: 'By Allah, I will never obey you.' So he ordered that he be laid down. He said: Abu Sa'id said to me that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then he placed two plates of brass between his collarbones and his neck.' He said: Abu Sa'id said: 'I did not know what brass was before that day.' 'He went to slaughter him but was unable, and he was not given power over him after he had killed him.' He said: The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'Then he took him by his hands and feet and threw him into the Paradise, which is dusty, full of smoke, and he thinks it is the Fire. That man is the closest of my nation to me in rank.' He said: Abu Sa'id said: 'The companions of Muhammad ﷺ thought that that man was none other than Umar b. al-Khattab until Umar went his own way.' He said: Then I said to him: 'How will he perish?' He said: 'Allah knows best.' I said: 'I was told that Jesus son of Mary ﷺ is the one who will destroy him.' He said: 'Allah knows best, except that Allah will destroy him and those who follow him.' He said: I said: 'Who will be after him?' He said:"],[8632,"A black cloud will rise over you before the Hour from the direction of the west, like a shield. It will keep rising in the sky until it fills the sky. Then a caller will call out: 'O people!' The people will turn to one another: 'Did you hear?' Some of them say yes, and some doubt. Then he calls out a second time: 'O people!' The people say: 'Did you hear?' They say: 'Yes.' Then he calls out: 'O people, the command of Allah has come, so do not seek to hasten it.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, two men will be spreading out a garment and will never fold it up or finish selling it, and a man will be plastering his cistern and will never water anything from it, and a man will be milking his she-camel and will never drink it, and the people will be preoccupied.'"],[8633,"I was with Abdullah b. Umar when a young man came to him asking about letting the turban hang down. Ibn Umar said: 'I will tell you about that with knowledge, if Allah Almighty wills.' He said: 'I was the tenth of ten in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Ibn Mas'ud, Hudhayfah, Ibn Awf, and Abu Sa'id al-Khudri. A young man from the Ansar came, greeted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then sat down and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, which of the believers is best?\" He said: \"The one with the best character.\" He said: \"Which of the believers is most astute?\" He said: \"The one who remembers death most and best prepares for it before it comes to them; those are the astute ones.\" Then the young man fell silent.' Sahih."],[8634,"Talhah b. Abdullah b. Awf narrated to me from Abu Bakrah, the brother of Ziyad through his mother."],[8635,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about him what he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: 'To proceed: you have spoken much about this man. Indeed, he is one of thirty liars who will emerge before the Dajjal. There is no town but that the terror of the Messiah will enter it, except Madinah. On that day, over every pass of its passes there will be two angels driving away from it the terror of the Messiah.'"],[8636,"He informed him that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, delivered a sermon, praised Allah as He deserves, then said: 'To proceed: you have spoken much about Musaylimah. Indeed, he is a liar among the total of thirty liars who will emerge before the Dajjal.'"],[8637,"The terror of the false Messiah will not enter Madinah. On that day it will have seven gates, and at each gate there will be two angels."],[8638,"O Allah, bless the people of Madinah in their mudd and their sa', and bless them in their city. O Allah, Ibrahim ﷺ is Your servant and Your intimate friend, and I am Your servant and Your messenger. Ibrahim asked You for Makkah, and I ask You for Madinah the like of what Ibrahim asked You for Makkah, and the like of it with it. Hearken! Madinah is interlaced with angels; over every pass of it there are two angels guarding it. The plague and the Dajjal will not enter it. Whoever intends evil for its people, Allah will melt him as salt melts in water."],[8639,"He mentioned the Dajjal and described him with a description I do not remember. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will our hearts on that day be as they are today?' He said: 'Or better.'"],[8640,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'There has been no prophet after Noah but that he warned his nation about the Dajjal, and I warn you about him.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ described him to us and said: 'You will meet him, or some of those who saw me and heard from me will meet him.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, will our hearts on that day be as they are today?' He said: 'Or better.' Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8641,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed the people and said: 'The Day of Deliverance! What is the Day of Deliverance?' three times. It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the Day of Deliverance?' He said: 'The Dajjal will come and ascend Uhud, then look out and see Madinah. He will say to his companions: \"Do you not see this white palace? This is the mosque of Ahmad.\" Then he will come to Madinah and find at every pass of its passes an angel with a drawn sword. Then he will come to the Sabkhah of al-Jurf and pitch his tent. Then Madinah will shake with three tremors, and no hypocrite man or woman, no wicked man or woman will remain except that they will go out to him. Thus Madinah will be purified, and that is the Day of Deliverance.'"],[8642,"By Allah, were it not for something, I would not have narrated a hadith to you. They said: 'You said the Hour will not come until such and such.' He said: 'I only said such and such will not happen until a great event occurs, and that has already happened: the House was burned and such and such.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The Dajjal will come forth and remain among my nation as long as Allah wills, remaining forty'—and I do not know whether it is nights, months, or years. He said: 'Then Allah will send Jesus son of Mary ﷺ , as if he were Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi.' He said: 'He will seek him until he destroys him.' He said: 'Then the people will remain for seven years, with no enmity between any two.' He said: 'Then Allah will send a cold wind from the direction of Syria, and it will not leave anyone who has an atom's weight of faith in his heart except that it will take his soul, even if one of you were in the heart of a mountain, it would enter upon him.' I heard this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'the heart of a mountain.' He said: 'Then the worst of people will remain, those who do not enjoin good or forbid evil, in the lightness of birds and the minds of wild beasts.' He said: 'Then Satan will come to them and say: \"Will you not respond?\" They will say: \"What do you command us?\" He said: 'He will command them to worship idols, and they will worship them. Meanwhile, their provision will be abundant and their livelihood good.' He said: 'Then the trumpet will be blown, and no one will hear it except he will incline his ear. The first to hear it will be a man plastering the cistern of his camels.' He said: 'He will fall down stunned, then the people will fall down stunned. Then Allah will send rain like dew, and their bodies will grow.' He said: 'Then it will be blown again, and behold, they will be standing, looking on. Then it will be said: \"Come to your Lord, and stop them; indeed they are to be questioned.\"' He said: 'Then it will be said: \"Bring forth the delegation of the Fire.\"' He said: 'It will be said: \"How many?\" It will be said: \"From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.\""],[8643,"“I see what you do not see and I hear what you do not hear. The heaven has creaked, and it has a right to creak: there is not in it—or there is not from it—a space of four fingers except an angel is placing his forehead prostrating to Allah the Exalted. By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would not enjoy women upon the beds, and you would go out to the high places crying out to Allah. By Allah, I wish I were a tree that is cut down.”"],[8644,"“Men of my community will meet Jesus son of Mary (peace be upon them both) and will witness the fighting against the Dajjal.”"],[8645,"“Whoever of you meets Jesus son of Mary, let him convey to him my greetings of peace, may Allah bless them both and grant them peace.”"],[8646,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Islam will wear out as the embroidery of a garment wears out, until it is not known what fasting is, nor charity, nor sacrifice. And the Book of Allah ﷻ will be taken up in a night, and not a verse of it will remain on earth. And there will remain groups of people: an old man and an old woman, saying, ‘We found our fathers upon this word, “There is no god but Allah,” so we say it.’” Then Silah said, “And what will ‘There is no god but Allah’ avail them when they do not know what fasting, charity, or sacrifice is?” Hudhayfah turned away from him, and he repeated it to him three times, and each time he turned away from him. Then he turned to him on the third time and said: “O Silah, it will save them from the Fire; it will save them from the Fire; it will save them from the Fire.”"],[8647,"The signs have passed except four: the Dajjal, the Beast, Yajuj and Majuj, and the rising of the sun from its west. And the sign with which Allah ends is the sun. Then he recited: {Do they wait only for the angels to come to them?}"],[8648,"On the night the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was taken on the Night Journey, he met Ibrahim, Musa, and Isa (peace be upon them). They began with Ibrahim and asked him about the Hour, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they asked Musa, but he had no knowledge of it. Then they referred the matter to Isa, and he said, “Allah covenanted with me regarding what is before its occurrence; as for its occurrence, none knows it except Allah ﷻ.” Then he mentioned the emergence of the Dajjal: “I will descend and kill him. Then the people will return to their lands, and Yajuj and Majuj will come upon them, and they will descend from every elevation. They will not pass by any water but they will drink it, nor by anything but they will corrupt it. Then they will cry out to me, and I will call upon Allah, and He will send the sky with water, and it will carry them and cast their bodies into the sea. Then the mountains will be blown away, and the earth will be stretched out like the stretching of leather. And Allah covenanted with me that when the Hour comes upon people, it will be like a pregnant woman who is due: her family does not know when it will come upon them with its birth, whether at night or by day.” Al-Awwam said: I found the confirmation of that in the Book of Allah ﷻ, then he recited: {Until when Yajuj and Majuj are let loose, and they descend from every elevation, and the true promise has drawn near.} [Al-Anbiya’ 97]"],[8649,"“The signs are beads strung on a thread; when the thread is cut, they follow one another.”"],[8650,"Hudhayfah went out to the outskirts of Kufa with a man. He turned toward the side of the Euphrates and said to his companion, “How will you be on the day when you see them emerging—or emerging from it—without tasting a drop of its water?” A man said, “Do you think that, O Abu Abdullah?” He said, “I do not think it; I know it.”"],[8651,"I was sitting with Hudhayfah and Abu Mas'ud when the people of Kufa despised Sa'id ibn al-'As on the Day of Jara'ah. Abu Mas'ud said, “I did not think we would return without shedding blood there.” Hudhayfah said, “By Allah, I knew that we would return on our heels without shedding a cupping-glassful of blood. And I knew nothing of that except something I learned while Muhammad ﷺ was alive: ‘A man may enter the morning a believer and enter the evening a disbeliever with nothing of his religion with him, and enter the evening a believer and enter the morning a disbeliever with nothing of his religion with him. He fights in the tribulation of today, and Allah ﷻ will kill him tomorrow. His heart will be overturned, and his anus will rise above him.’” I said, “His lower part?” He said, “His anus.”"],[8652,"“When they do not enjoin good and do not forbid evil.”"],[8653,"“There will be a generation after sixty years who neglect the prayer and follow desires, and they will meet with ruin. Then there will be a generation after sixty years who recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. Three kinds of people recite the Quran: a believer, a hypocrite, and a wicked person.”"],[8654,"“By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the Hour will not come until obscenity and miserliness appear, the trustworthy is betrayed, the treacherous is trusted, the mountain goats perish, and the tusus appear.” They said, “O Messenger of Allah, what are the mountain goats and what are the tusus?” He said, “The mountain goats are the faces of people and their nobles, and the tusus are those who were beneath the feet of people, unknown.”"],[8655,"Three persons sat with Marwan in Madinah and heard him narrating about the signs, the first of which is the emergence of the Dajjal. The group rose from Marwan and sat with Abdullah b. Amr and told him what Marwan had said. Abdullah said: Marwan did not say anything. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"The first of the signs to appear will be the rising of the sun from its west or the beast, whichever of them comes first, the other will follow it closely.\" Then he began to narrate and said, \"That is because when the sun sets, it comes beneath the Throne and prostrates and asks permission to return, but nothing is answered to it.\" He said, \"Then it returns and asks permission to return, but nothing is answered to it. It says: O Lord, how far is the east! Who will take me to the people? Until when night comes, it comes and asks permission, and it is said to it: Rise from your place.\" He said, \"Abdullah used to read the scriptures and he recited: 'That day no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith.'\""],[8656,"\"When the great battles occur, a contingent from the mawali will go forth from Damascus; they are the noblest of the Arabs in horsemanship and the best in weaponry. Through them Allah will support the religion.\""],[8657,"\"A fire will be sent upon the people of the east, and it will drive them to the west. It will spend the night with them wherever they spend the night, and take the midday rest with them wherever they rest. It will have whatever falls from them and lags behind, driving them like a broken camel.\""],[8658,"When a man from among us came to Madinah, he would stay in the Suffah. If he had an overseer there, he would stay with his overseer; if he had no overseer there, he would stay in the Suffah. I came to Madinah and had no overseer there, so I stayed in the Suffah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us every day with a mudd of dates shared between two, and he would clothe us in coarse cloth. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed one of the daytime prayers with us. When he said the salam, the people of the Suffah called out to him from the right and left: O Messenger of Allah, the dates have burned our stomachs and the coarse cloth has worn out. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went to his pulpit, ascended it, praised Allah and extolled Him, then mentioned the hardship he had faced from his people until he said, \"There came upon me and my companion a period of more than ten nights when we had no food except berir.\" I said to Abu Harb, \"What is berir?\" He said, \"Bad food, the fruit of the arak tree.\" He said, \"We came to these brothers of ours from the Ansar, and their main food was dates, so they shared them with us. By Allah, if I could find bread and meat for you, I would fill you with it. But perhaps you will live to see a time, or whoever among you lives to see it, when large platters will be brought to you morning and evening, and you will wear garments like the coverings of the Kaaba.\" Dawud said: Abu Harb said to me, \"O Dawud, do you know what the coverings of the Kaaba were in those days?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"White garments that were brought from Yemen.\" Sahih."],[8659,"From Abu Salamah, and he mentioned it in a similar manner."],[8660,"\"Al-Lat and al-Uzza will be worshipped, and Allah will send a pleasant wind and take the soul of every one who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of good. There will remain those in whom there is no good, and they will return to the religion of their forefathers.\""],[8661,"Uthman b. Affan narrated a parable for fitnah. He said, \"The parable of fitnah is like a group of three who accompanied each other on a journey. They traveled at night and came together to a fork of three roads. One of them said, 'To the right,' and took the right and lost the way. The other said, 'To the left,' and took the left and lost the way. The third said, 'I will stay in my place until morning,' and took the road and reached morning and took the road.\""],[8662,"A son of Abdullah b. Salam wanted to go towards Syria. Abdullah looked at him from above a house and said, \"O my son, do not grieve me with your own self. For the cry of every Muslim will surely come from Syria.\""],[8663,"I set out with Zur'ah b. Damrah al-Ash'ari to Umar b. al-Khattab. We met Abdullah b. Amr. He said, \"It is imminent that no Arab will remain in the land of the non-Arabs except one killed or taken captive whose blood is to be judged.\" Zur'ah said, \"Will the polytheists prevail over Islam?\" He said, \"From whom are you?\" He said, \"From Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'ah.\" He said, \"The Hour will not arise until the women of Banu Amir push against each other at Dhu al-Khalasah, an idol that was worshipped in the pre-Islamic era.\" He said, \"We mentioned the statement of Abdullah b. Amr to Umar b. al-Khattab. Umar said three times, 'Abdullah b. Amr knows best what he says.' Then Umar b. al-Khattab gave a sermon on Friday and said, 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"A group of my ummah will continue to be victorious upon the truth until the command of Allah comes.\"' He said, 'We mentioned the statement of Umar to Abdullah b. Amr. He said, \"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ spoke the truth. When that happens, it is as I said.\"'"],[8664,"I heard a man say to Abdullah b. Amr, \"You say that the Hour will arise at such and such time.\" He said, \"I had resolved not to narrate anything to you. I only said to you: after a short while you will see a great matter.\" That was the burning of the House. Shu'bah said: Abdullah b. Amr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The Dajjal will emerge among my ummah and remain among them for forty\"—I do not know whether he said days, or forty years, or forty nights, or forty months—\"then Allah will send Isa son of Maryam ﷺ , as if he were Urwah b. Mas'ud al-Thaqafi. He will seek him and destroy him. Then people will remain after him for years with no enmity between any two. Then Allah will send a wind from the direction of Syria, and no one will remain in whose heart is the weight of an atom of faith except it will take his soul, even if one of you were in the heart of a mountain, it would enter upon him.\" Abdullah said, \"I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The worst of people will remain, in the lightness of birds and the minds of beasts. They will not recognize any good nor reject any evil. The devil will appear to them and say, 'Will you not respond?' He will command them to worship idols, and they will worship them, and while they are in that state their provisions will flow and their livelihood will be good. Then the trumpet will be blown, and no one will hear it except he will incline his ear. The first to hear it will be a man plastering his watering trough, and he will be stunned. Then no one will remain except he is stunned. Then Allah will send—or Allah will send down—rain like shade or dew. Al-Nu'man, the doubter, said: their bodies will grow. Then it will be blown again, and behold, they will be standing looking. Then it will be said, 'Come to your Lord.' 'And stop them, indeed they are to be questioned.' Then it will be said, 'Bring out the contingent of the Fire.' It will be said, 'How many?' It will be said, 'From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.' On that day, 'children will be made gray-haired' and 'the shin will be uncovered.'\""],[8665,"Abu al-Tahir and Abu al-Rabi' al-Misri narrated to us, they said: Abdullah b. Wahb narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman b. Shuraih informed me from Rabi'ah b. Sayf al-Ma'afiri from Ishaq b. Abdullah that Awf b. Malik al-Ashja'i came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during a victory of his, greeted him, then said, \"Congratulations to you, O Messenger of Allah. Allah has strengthened your victory, made your religion prevail, and war has laid down its burdens.\" He said, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in a tent of leather. He said, \"Enter, O Awf.\" He said, \"Shall I enter all of me or part of me?\" He said, \"Enter all of you.\" He said, \"War will not lay down its burdens until there are six things. The first of them is my death.\" Awf wept. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Say: one. The second is the conquest of Jerusalem. The third is a fitnah that will occur among the people like the scab of sheep. The fourth is a fitnah that will occur among the people in which no household will remain except their share of it will enter upon them. The fifth is that a boy will be born among Banu al-Asfar from the children of kings. He will grow in a day as a boy grows in a week, and grow in a week as a boy grows in a month, and grow in a month as a boy grows in a year. When he reaches twelve years, they will make him king over them. He will stand among them and say, 'How long will these people overcome us in the noble parts of our land? I think we should march against them until we expel them from it.' The orators stood up and praised his opinion. He sent to the islands and the mainland for the construction of ships. Then he loaded fighters into them until he landed between Antioch and al-Arish.\" Ibn Shuraih said, \"I heard someone say that they were twelve companies, under each company twelve thousand. The Muslims will gather to their leader in Jerusalem and agree in their opinion to march to the city of the Messenger ﷺ until their outposts are at al-Sarh and Khaybar.\" Ibn Abi Ja'far said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"They will drive my ummah from the places where wormwood grows.\" He said, or al-Harith b. Yazid said, \"They will stay there. A third will flee from them, a third will be killed, and Allah ﷻ will defeat them with the patient third.\" Khalid b. Yazid said, \"On that day, by Allah, he will strike with his sword and thrust with his spear, and the Muslims will follow him until they reach the narrow pass near Constantinople. They will find that its water has dried up, so they will cross to the city until they camp there. Allah will demolish their walls with takbir. Then they will enter it and divide their wealth by shields.\" Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri said, \"While they are in that state, a rider will come to them and say, 'You are here while the Dajjal has gone to your families.' It was only a lie. Whoever heard the scholars regarding that remained upon what he had attained, but others dispersed. The Muslims will build mosques in Constantinople and raid beyond that until the Dajjal emerges—the sixth.\""],[8666,"He was with Ibn Abbas, and with him was Ibn al-Zubayr in a group. Abu Hurayrah entered upon them and said, \"Die!\" Ibn al-Zubayr said to him, \"O Abu Hurayrah, the religion is established, jihad is established, prayer, zakah, Hajj, and the fasting of Ramadan.\" Abu Hurayrah said, \"If you die before you reach what the good-doer cannot increase in goodness nor the wrongdoer can desist from his wrongdoing.\""],[8667,"\"It never was a state of truth but that Adam was granted victory over Iblis, and never a state of falsehood but that Iblis was granted victory over Adam. Iblis was commanded to prostrate, and he disobeyed, so Adam was granted victory over him—until the two men fought, one of them killing his companion, so Iblis was granted victory over him. And there will be trials: a private trial, a public trial, a private trial, and a public trial.\" It was said, \"O Commander of the Faithful, what is the private trial and the public trial, and the private trial and the public trial?\" He said, \"There will be two leaders, a leader of truth and a leader of falsehood, and there will be a defection from truth to falsehood and from falsehood to truth—this is the private trial. And there will be two leaders, a leader of truth and a leader of falsehood, and there will be a defection from truth to falsehood and from falsehood to truth—this is the public trial.\""],[8668,"\"There will be a trial in which people will be sifted as gold is sifted in the mine. Do not revile the people of Syria, but revile their oppressors, for among them are the Abdal. Allah will send upon them a flood from the sky that will drown them, so that even if foxes fought them, the foxes would defeat them. Then Allah will raise at that time a man from the family of the Messenger ﷺ with twelve thousand if they are few, or fifteen thousand if they are many, their sign or mark being 'Amit, Amit' under three banners. The people of seven banners will fight them, each banner's holder hoping for kingship. They will fight and be defeated, then the Hashimi will prevail, and Allah will restore to the people their affection and their blessing. They will remain so until the Dajjal comes forth.\""],[8669,"We were with 'Ali when a man asked him about the Mahdi. 'Ali said, \"Far from it!\" Then he made a gesture with his hand, counting seven, and said, \"That one will come forth at the end of time, when a man says 'Allah, Allah' and is killed. Allah will gather for him a people scattered like patches of clouds, and Allah will unite their hearts. They will feel lonely with no one, and they will not rejoice in anyone. They will be joined by the number of the companions of Badr—the first ones did not outstrip them, and the last ones will not catch up with them—and by the number of the companions of Talut who crossed the river with him.\" Abu al-Tufayl said: Ibn al-Hanafiyyah said, \"Do you want him?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"He will come forth from between these two pillars.\" I said, \"No doubt, by Allah, I will not see them until I die.\" And he died there—meaning Makkah, may Allah the Exalted protect it."],[8670,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ , he said: \"One of the signs of the Hour is that the wicked will be elevated and the righteous will be humiliated, and speech will be abundant, while actions will be scarce, and the Quran will be recited by people whom nobody will reject.\" It was asked, \"What is meant by 'the Quran will be recited by people whom nobody will reject'?\" He replied, \"No one will dispute the Quran except those who deny it.\" This hadith was narrated by Al-Awza'i on the authority of Amr ibn Qais Al-Sakuni."],[8671,"I went out with my father in the delegation to Mu'awiyah and heard a man narrating to the people, saying: \"Among the signs of the Hour are that the wicked will be raised and the righteous will be lowered, that action and deeds will be stored away and speech will prevail, and that the Muthanna will be recited among a people with no one among them to change it or disapprove of it.\" It was said, \"What is the Muthanna?\" He said, \"What has been written besides the Book of Allah ﷻ.\" He said: Then I narrated this hadith to some people, among them Isma'il b. 'Ubayd Allah, and he said, \"I was with you in that gathering. Do you know who the man was?\" I said, \"No.\" He said, \"'Abd Allah b. 'Amr.\""],[8672,"We were with 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr b. al-'As when he was asked, \"Which of the two cities will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome?\" He called for a box, Tuhum (meaning an old, worn box), took out a book from it, looked into it, then said, \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ writing down what he said when he was asked, 'Which of the two cities will be conquered first, Constantinople or Rome?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'The city of Heraclius will be conquered first'—meaning Constantinople.\""],[8673,"\"Cling to this obedience and the community, for it is the rope of Allah which He commanded. What you dislike in the community is better than what you love in division. Allah the Exalted never created anything but that He set for it an end. This religion has been completed, and it is heading toward decrease. The signs of that are that kinship ties will be severed, wealth will be taken without its right, blood will be shed, a relative will complain of his kinship and nothing will return to him, and a beggar will go around between the two Fridays with nothing placed in his hand. While they are in that state, a cry like the lowing of a cow will be heard, and all the people will think that it only came from their direction. While the people are like that, the earth will cast out pieces of its liver—gold and silver—and after that no amount of gold or silver will benefit.\""],[8674,"He said to Abu Mas'ud: \"I had two companions who were my refuge—Hudhayfah and Abu Musa. I adjure you by Allah, if you heard anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the tribulations, tell me; otherwise, exercise your best judgment for me.\" He said: Abu Mas'ud praised Allah and extolled Him, then said, \"Cling to the great majority of the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ, for Allah will never gather the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance ever. And be patient until the righteous one finds rest and relief is obtained from the wicked one.\""],[8675,"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Cling to obedience to Allah and to this community, for Allah the Exalted will never gather the Ummah of Muhammad ﷺ upon misguidance ever. And cling to patience until the righteous one finds rest and relief is obtained from the wicked one.\""],[8676,"\"Allah ﷻ will send a wind containing bitter cold that will not leave on the face of the earth any believer but that he dies from that wind. Then the Hour will arise upon the worst of people.\""],[8677,"\"The Hour will not arise until Allah sends a wind that will not leave anyone in whose heart is an atom's weight of piety or understanding but that it will seize him, and every people will be joined to what their forefathers used to worship in the Jahiliyyah.\""],[8678,"She heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The first army of my Ummah to raid by sea have made it obligatory.\" She said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, am I among them?\" He said, \"You are among them.\" Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The first of my Ummah to raid the city of Caesar will be forgiven.\" I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, am I among them?\" He said, \"No.\""],[8679,"\"The Hour will not arise until the earth is filled with oppression, injustice, and aggression. Then a man from my household will come forth who will fill it with equity and justice as it was filled with oppression and aggression.\""],[8680,"The Mahdi is from us, the People of the House, with a high nose, aquiline, prominent forehead. He will fill the earth with equity and justice as it was filled with tyranny and oppression. He will live like this,” and he spread his left hand and two fingers of his right hand, the index and the thumb, and held up three."],[8681,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ mention the Mahdi and he said: “Yes, he is true, and he is from the sons of Fatimah.” Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in the Talkhis."],[8682,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ mentioned the Mahdi and said: “He is from the progeny of Fatimah.”"],[8683,"“At the end of my community the Mahdi will emerge. Allah will send him rain, the earth will bring forth its vegetation, he will give wealth in abundance, livestock will increase, and the community will become great. He will live seven or eight,” meaning years."],[8684,"“The earth will be filled with tyranny and oppression, then a man from my family will emerge.”"],[8685,"There will be in my community the Mahdi. If he is delayed, then seven, otherwise nine. My community will enjoy in his time a blessing the like of which they have never enjoyed. The earth will bring forth its produce and withhold nothing from them. Wealth on that day will be heaped up. A man will stand and say, “O Mahdi, give me,” and he will say, “Take.”"],[8686,"“Indeed, the gaze of the companion of the trumpet, since he was entrusted with it, has been ready, looking toward the Throne, fearing that he will be commanded before his gaze returns to him. His eyes are like two shining stars.”"],[8687,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How can I enjoy myself while the bearer of the horn (Angel Israfil) has placed it to his mouth and has bowed his forehead, and he is listening attentively, waiting for when he will be commanded?\" The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"What should we say, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said, \"Say: Allah is sufficient for us and He is the best Disposer of affairs, and in Allah let those who trust, put their trust.\" This narration is attributed to Abu Sa'eed Atiyyah and is considered weak."],[8688,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How can I be at ease when the companion of the horn has put the horn to his mouth, bowed his forehead, and inclined his ear, waiting for when he will be commanded to blow?” We said, “O Messenger of Allah, what should we say?” He said, “Say: Sufficient for us is Allah, and He is the best disposer of affairs; upon Allah we rely.” We have not written it from the hadith of al-A’mash from Abu Salih from Abu Sa’id except with this isnad. Were it not that Abu Yahya al-Taymi is on the route, I would have ruled the hadith as authentic according to the condition of the two Shaykhs. This hadith has an origin from the hadith of Zayd b. Aslam from Ata’ b. Yasar from Abu Sa’id. Abu Yahya is weak."],[8689,"There is no morning except that two angels call out. One of them says: “O Allah, give the one who spends a replacement,” and the other says: “O Allah, give the one who withholds destruction.” And two angels are entrusted with the trumpet, waiting for when they will be commanded to blow. And two angels call out, one saying: “Woe to men from women,” and the other saying: “Woe to women from men.”"],[8690,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him about the trumpet. He said: “A horn that is blown into.”"],[8691,"“Indeed, among the best of your days is Friday. On it Adam was created, on it he was taken, on it is the blowing of the trumpet, and on it is the thunderbolt. So increase in sending prayers upon me on it, for your prayers are presented to me.” They said, “How are our prayers presented to you when you have decayed?” He said, “Indeed, Allah, exalted is He, has forbidden the earth to consume the bodies of the prophets.”"],[8692,"He said: “O Messenger of Allah, will all of us see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection, and what is the sign of that in His creation?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you not all look at the moon unobstructed?” They said, “Yes.” He said, “Allah is greater.” He said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, how does Allah bring the dead to life, and what is the sign of that in His creation?” He said, “Have you not passed by the valley of your family when it was barren?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Then you passed by it swaying green?” He said, “Yes.” He said, “Thus does Allah bring the dead to life, and that is His sign in His creation.”"],[8693,"He went as a delegate to the Prophet ﷺ, and with him was Nahīk ibn ʿĀṣim ibn Mālik ibn al-Muntafiq. He said: We arrived in Madinah at the end of Rajab, and we prayed the dawn prayer with him. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among the people to deliver a sermon and said: “O people, I have withheld my voice from you for four days so that I might make you hear. Is there any man here whom his people have sent?” They said, “Make known to us what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is saying,” then (they feared) perhaps he might be distracted by his own thoughts or by the talk of his companion, or that the misguided might distract him. “Indeed, I will be asked: Have I conveyed (the message)? So listen and you will live; listen and you will live. Sit down!” So the people sat, while I and my companion remained standing until his heart and gaze were free for us. I said, “O Messenger of Allah, I want to ask you about my need, so do not be hasty with me.” He said, “Ask whatever you wish.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah, do you have any knowledge of the unseen?” By Allah, he laughed and nodded his head, and he knew that I was seeking (something) by my slip of the tongue. He said: “Your Lord has reserved the keys of five matters of the unseen; none knows them except Allah,” and he gestured with his hand. I said, “And what are they, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Knowledge of the time of death: He knows when the death of each of you will be, and you do not know it. And He knows the day of rain: it looks down upon you while you are in distress and fear; and he kept laughing, knowing that your relief was near.” Laqīṭ said: I said, “O Messenger of Allah, we will never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs.” “And He knows what will be tomorrow: He knows what you will eat tomorrow, and you do not know it. And He knows the Day of the Hour,” and I think he also “mentioned what is in the wombs.”"],[8694,"\"People will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection barefoot, naked, and uncircumcised.\" 'A'isha said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what about the private parts?\" He said, \"For every person on that Day there will be a matter to preoccupy him.\""],[8695,"The Truthful, the One to Whom Truth is Told ﷺ narrated to me: \"People will be gathered in three groups: a group fed, clothed, and riding; a group walking and striving; and a group dragged by the angels on their faces to the Fire.\" We said, \"O Abu Dharr, we have recognized these and these, but what about those who walk and strive?\" He said, \"Allah will cast an affliction upon the riding animals, so no riding animal will remain.\""],[8696,"I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, where do you command me to go?\" He swept his hand towards Sham (Syria) and said, \"Indeed, you will be gathered as men on foot and on mounts, being dragged on your faces, here.\" And he swept his hand with it."],[8697,"\"You will be gathered here barefoot, naked, walking and riding, and on your faces you will be presented to Allah, and over your mouths there will be muzzles. The first part of any of you to speak will be his thigh.\""],[8698,"\"No, by Allah, they will not be gathered on their feet, nor will they be driven like cattle. Rather, they will be brought upon she-camels from the she-camels of Paradise, the like of which the creatures have never seen. Their saddles will be of gold and their reins of chrysolite. They will sit upon them until they knock at the gate of Paradise.\""],[8699,"O Messenger of Allah, woe for our nakedness! Will men and women be gathered together, looking at one another's private parts? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For every person on that Day there will be a matter to preoccupy him. Men will not look at women, nor women at men. Each will be occupied from the other.\""],[8700,"\"The last two to be gathered will be two shepherds from Muzaynah, heading for Madinah, calling their sheep. They will find it full of wild beasts, until when they reach Thaniyat al-Wada', they will fall on their faces.\""],[8701,"I entered the mosque and found an old man picking lice from himself. I greeted him, and he returned the greeting. I sat by him and said, \"Who are you, O uncle?\" He said, \"Rather, who are you, O son of my brother?\" I said, \"I am Ma'bad b. Khalid.\" He said, \"Welcome. I knew your father; he was with me in Damascus. Your father and I were the first two horsemen to halt at the gate of 'Adhra', a town in Syria.\" I said, \"Who are you?\" He said, \"I am Abu Sarihah al-Ghifari, a companion of the Prophet ﷺ.\" I said, \"Tell me from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" He said, \"Yes. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Two men from Muzaynah will be gathered; they are the last of people to be gathered. They will come from a mountain they have climbed until they reach the landmarks of people and find the earth turned into wild beasts. They will come to Madinah, and when they reach the outskirts of Madinah, they will say, 'Where are the people?' They will see no one. One of them will say, 'The people are in their houses.' They will enter the houses, and there is no one in them, and on the beds are foxes and cats. They will say, 'Where are the people?' One of them will say, 'The people are in the mosque.' They will come to the mosque and find no one. They will say, 'Where are the people?' One of them will say, 'The people are in the market; the markets have occupied them.' They will go out until they come to the markets and find no one in them. They will proceed until they come to the mountain pass, and there are two angels upon it. The angels will seize their feet and drag them to the land of gathering, and they are the last of people to be gathered.\""],[8702,"When the verse {O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the convulsion of the [final] Hour is a terrible thing} [al-Hajj: 1] was revealed upon the Prophet ﷺ while he was on a journey, he raised his voice with it until his companions gathered around him. He said, \"Do you know what day this is? The day when Allah will say to Adam, 'O Adam, arise and send forth the delegation of the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine.'\" That weighed heavily upon the Muslims. The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Be moderate, draw near, and rejoice. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, you are among the nations only like a mole on the flank of a camel or a spot on the foreleg of a beast. With you are two creations that, whenever they are with anything, they increase it greatly: Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and those who have perished from the disbelievers of jinn and mankind.\" This is a sound chain according to the conditions of the two shaykhs, but they did not include it."],[8703,"Abdullah b. Muhammad al-Dawraqi informed us: Muhammad b. Ishaq al-Imam narrated to us: Muhammad b. Yahya narrated to us: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, and he related the hadith exactly as it is. Then Muhammad b. Yahya said at its end: \"This hadith, according to us, is not preserved from Anas. Rather, what is preserved with us is the hadith of Qatadah from al-Hasan from 'Imran b. Husayn.\""],[8704,"The Imam of the Imams, Muhammad b. Yahya al-Dhuhli, has ruled, but Muhammad b. Isma'il and Muslim b. al-Hajjaj did not include a single letter in this chapter, and they mentioned that al-Hasan did not hear from 'Imran b. Husayn."],[8705,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and the pace of travel had spread his companions out. He raised his voice with these two verses: {O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the convulsion of the [final] Hour is a terrible thing} [al-Hajj: 1]. Abu Musa recited up to His saying {but the punishment of Allah is severe} [al-Hajj: 2]. When his companions heard that, they urged their mounts on, knowing that he was about to say something. He said, \"Do you know what day that is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That is the day when Adam will be called, and his Lord will call him, saying: 'O Adam, send forth the delegation of the Fire: from every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.'\" His companions were struck silent, until no one showed even a smile. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw what had befallen his companions, he said, \"Work and rejoice. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are with two creations that, whenever they are with anything, they increase it greatly: Ya'juj and Ma'juj, and those who have perished from the children of Adam and the children of Iblis.\" Some of what the people were feeling was relieved. Then he said, \"Work and rejoice. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, you are among people only like a mole on the flank of a camel or a spot on the foreleg of a beast.\" This is how Sa'id b. Abi 'Arubah narrated it from Qatadah."],[8706,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys... and he mentioned the hadith similarly. We have also narrated this hadith from 'Abdullah b. 'Abbas."],[8707,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited this verse while his Companions were with him: {O mankind, fear your Lord. Indeed, the convulsion of the [final] Hour is a terrible thing} [al-Hajj:1] to the end of the verse. Then he said, \"Do you know which day that is?\" They said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"That is the day when Allah will say to Adam, 'Arise and send forth the portion of the Fire,' or he said, 'a portion to the Fire.' Then he will say, 'O Lord, from how many?' He said, 'From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise.'\" That distressed the people, and gloom and sorrow fell upon them. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise.\" So they rejoiced. Then the Prophet ﷺ said, \"Work and rejoice, for you are between two creations that were never with anyone except that they outnumbered them: Ya'juj and Ma'juj. You are among mankind—or among the nations—like a black hair on the side of a camel, or like a mark on the foreleg of a she-camel. Indeed, my nation is one part of a thousand parts.\""],[8708,"We were sitting in the mosque on Friday when he said, \"Indeed, the greatest day of this world is Friday. On it Adam was created, and on it the Hour will be established. The most honored of Allah's creation to Allah is Abu al-Qasim ﷺ.\" [The narrator] said: I said, \"May Allah have mercy on you. Then where are the angels?\" He said: He looked at me and laughed, then said, \"O son of my brother, do you know what the angels are? The angels are merely a creation like the creation of the heavens, the earth, the winds, the clouds, and the rest of creation that does not disobey Allah in anything. Paradise is in the heaven, and the Fire is in the earth. When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah will raise the creation nation by nation and prophet by prophet until Ahmad and his nation are the last of the nations as a center.\" He said: Then he will stand, and his nation will follow him, its righteous and its wicked. Then the bridge of Hell will be placed, and they will take the bridge. Allah will obliterate the sights of His enemies, and they will fall into it from the left and the right. The Prophet ﷺ and the righteous with him will be saved. The angels will meet them and show them their dwellings in Paradise—on your right, on your left—until he reaches his Lord, exalted is He. Then a chair will be placed for him on the right of Allah, exalted is He. Then a caller will call out, \"Where is 'Isa and his nation?\" Then he will stand, and his nation will follow him, its righteous and its wicked. They will take the bridge. Allah will obliterate the sights of His enemies, and they will fall into it from the left and the right. The Prophet ﷺ and the righteous with him will be saved. The angels will meet them and show them their dwellings in Paradise—on your right, on your left—until he reaches his Lord. Then a chair will be placed for him on the other side. He said: Then the prophets and nations will follow them until the last of them is Nuh—may Allah have mercy on Nuh."],[8709,"He recited, \"On the Day when the sky will split open with clouds, and the angels will be sent down in successive descent\" [al-Furqan 25]. He said: The heaven of this world will split open, and the angels will descend upon every heaven. The inhabitants of the heaven of this world will descend, and they will be more numerous than those on earth among the jinn and humankind. The inhabitants of the earth will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the inhabitants of the second heaven will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the heaven of this world and the inhabitants of the earth. They will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the inhabitants of the third heaven will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the second heaven, the heaven of this world, and the inhabitants of the earth. They will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the inhabitants of the fourth heaven will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the third heaven, the second, this world, and the inhabitants of the earth. They will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the inhabitants of the fifth heaven will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the fourth heaven, the third, the second, this world, and the inhabitants of the earth. They will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the inhabitants of the sixth heaven will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the fifth heaven, the fourth, the third, the second, this world, and the inhabitants of the earth. They will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the inhabitants of the seventh heaven will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the sixth heaven, the fifth, the fourth, the third, the second, this world, and the inhabitants of the earth. They will say: Is our Lord among you? They will say: No. Then the Karubiyyun will descend, and they will be more numerous than the inhabitants of the seven heavens, the earths, and the bearers of the Throne. They will have horns with joints like the joints of reed-spears. The space between the foot of one of them is such and such; from the hollow of his foot to his ankle is a journey of five hundred years; from his ankle to his knee is a journey of five hundred; from his knee to the tip of his nose is a journey of five hundred years; and from his collarbone to the place of the earring is a journey of five hundred years.[1]"],[8710,"From 'Abdullah regarding His saying, exalted is He, {On the Day the earth will be replaced by another earth, and the heavens [as well]} [Ibrahim:48], he said: \"A white, pure earth on which no blood has been shed and no sin has been committed. The caller will make them hear, and the sight will penetrate them—barefoot, naked, as they were created, until sweat bridles them.\""],[8711,"From 'Abdullah regarding His saying, exalted is He, {On the Day the earth will be replaced by another earth, and the heavens [as well]} [Ibrahim:48], he said: \"A white, pure earth on which no blood has been shed and no sin has been committed. The caller will make them hear, and the sight will penetrate them—barefoot, naked, as they were created, until sweat bridles them.\""],[8712,"The earth will be stretched out on the Day of Resurrection, stretched out for the greatness of the Most Merciful. Then no human being among the children of Adam will have except the place of his two feet. Then I will be called as the first of mankind, and I will fall down prostrating. Then permission will be given to me, and I will stand and say, 'O Lord.'"],[8713,"From a man of knowledge, whom he did not name, that the earth will be stretched out on the Day of Resurrection. Then he mentioned the hadith similarly: \"And as for the hadith of Ma'mar.\""],[8714,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"The earth will be stretched out on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he mentioned the same exactly. According to the condition of al-Bukhari and Muslim."],[8715,"He heard Uqbah ibn Aamir al-Juhani saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying, \"The sun will come very close to the earth, causing people to sweat. Among them, there will be those whose sweat will reach their ankles, and others will have it reach their knees, while some will have it reach their waist. There will also be those whose sweat will reach their shoulders, and some will have it reach their necks. And there will be those whose whole body will be covered in sweat.\" Then the Prophet ﷺ pointed with his hand and folded it, placing it under his chin. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ doing this. He further stated, \"And there will be those whose sweat will cover their entire body, and he motioned with his hand above his head indicating that the sweat will reach above their heads. However, the head will not be affected by the sweat, and the moisture will circulate around it, moving clockwise and counter-clockwise.\""],[8716,"\"Sweat will bridle the people.\" One of the two said, \"Up to the lobe of his ears,\" and the other said, \"It will bridle him.\" Then Ibn 'Umar said, indicating with his finger beneath the lobe of his ear."],[8717,"\"The people of Paradise will be detained after they cross the Sirat on a bridge, where some of them will be made to give to others the injustices they committed against them in this world, until when they are purified and cleansed, permission will be given for them to enter Paradise. Indeed, one of them will be more acquainted with his dwelling in the Hereafter than he was with his dwelling in this world.\""],[8718,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited the verse {The Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds} [al-Mutaffifin:6]. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"How will it be for you when Allah gathers you as arrows are gathered in a quiver for fifty thousand years, then Allah does not look at you?\""],[8719,"When this verse and this surah were revealed to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: {Indeed, you are to die, and indeed they are to die. Then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord will dispute} [al-Zumar:31], al-Zubayr said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will what was between us in this world, along with the particular sins, be repeated upon us?\" He said, \"Yes, it will certainly be repeated upon you until every rightful owner is given his right.\" Al-Zubayr said, \"By Allah, the matter is indeed severe.\""],[8720,"We lived for a period of time, and we did not think that this verse was revealed except about us and about the People of the Book: {Indeed, you are to die, and indeed they are to die. Then indeed you, on the Day of Resurrection, before your Lord will dispute} [al-Zumar:31]. I said, \"We dispute? As for us, we worship none but Allah; as for our religion, it is Islam; as for our Book, it is the Qur'an—we will never alter or distort it; as for our qiblah, it is the Ka'bah; as for our sacred things or sanctity, it is one; and as for our prophet, he is Muhammad ﷺ. So how would we dispute?\" Until some of us struck the faces of others with swords, and I knew that it was revealed about us."],[8721,"Regarding His saying, exalted is He, {This is a Day they will not speak} [al-Mursalat:35], and {You hear nothing but a whisper} and {And they will approach one another, questioning each other} [al-Saffat:27], and {Here, read my record!}—what is this? He said, \"Woe to you! Have you asked anyone about this before me?\" He said, \"No.\" He said, \"Indeed, if you had asked, you would have perished. Did not Allah, blessed and exalted, say, {And indeed, a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of those which you count} [al-Hajj:47]?\" He said, \"Yes.\" \"And for every measure of a day of these days, there is a color of these colors.\""],[8722,"I asked Yunus b. ʿAbd al-Aʿlā al-Ṣadafī about the cause of the death of ʿAbd Allāh b. Wahb, and he said: The Book of Terrors was being read to him, and a report was read to him, so he fell down unconscious. We carried him and brought him into the house, and he remained ill until he died ؓ."],[8723,"From the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"I am the master of the people on the Day of Resurrection. My Lord will call me, and I will say: 'Here I am, at Your service, blessed are You, here I am, and Your mercy, and the guided one is the one whom You guide, and I am Your servant before You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. Blessed are You, Lord of the House.'\" He said: \"And indeed, falsely accusing a chaste woman certainly demolishes the work of a hundred years.\" Muslim has cited it as a witness."],[8724,"I said to Abū al-Dardāʾ: \"Will you not seek for your guests what men seek for their guests?\" He said: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Indeed, before you is a steep and difficult pass; those heavily burdened will not cross it.' So I love to lighten my load for that pass.\""],[8725,"\"The record of a man will be raised on the Day of Resurrection, and the grievances of the children of Adam will keep following him until no good deed remains, and sins of theirs are added upon him.\""],[8726,"On the Day when the servants—or he said: the people—will be gathered barefoot, naked, uncircumcised, and having nothing with them. Then He will call them with a voice that the far one hears as the near one hears: 'I am the King, I am the Judge. It is not fitting for anyone from the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while anyone from the people of the Fire has a grievance against him, until I settle it for him. And it is not fitting for anyone from the people of the Fire to enter the Fire while anyone from the people of Paradise has a grievance against him, until I settle it for him—even a slap.' He said: We said: 'How, when we come to Allah ﷻ naked, barefoot, uncircumcised, and having nothing?' He said: 'With good deeds and bad deeds.'"],[8727,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the earth will be stretched out like a hide, and Allah will gather the creatures—humans, jinn, beasts, and wild animals. On that day, Allah will establish retribution among the beasts, until the hornless sheep exacts retribution from the horned one for its goring. When Allah finishes retribution among the beasts, He will say to them: 'Be dust,' and they will become dust. Then the disbeliever will see it and say: 'Would that I were dust!'"],[8728,"The registers are three: a register that Allah will not forgive anything of, a register that Allah will not pay any attention to, and a register that Allah will not leave anything of. As for the register that Allah will not forgive anything of, it is associating partners with Allah ﷻ. Allah ﷻ said: {Indeed, Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, but He forgives what is less than that to whom He wills} [al-Nisāʾ 48]. As for the register that Allah will not pay any attention to at all, it is the servant's wronging himself in what is between him and his Lord. As for the register that Allah will not leave anything of, it is the grievances of the servants among themselves—retribution is inevitable."],[8729,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting, we saw him laugh until his front teeth showed. ʿUmar said to him: \"What made you laugh, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be your ransom?\" He said: \"Two men from my community knelt before the Lord of Might. One of them said: 'O Lord, take my right from my brother.' Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to the claimant: 'What will you do with your brother, while none of his good deeds remain?' He said: 'O Lord, let him carry some of my burdens.'\" He said: \"And the eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ overflowed with tears. Then he said: 'Indeed, that day is tremendous; people will need to have some of their burdens carried for them.' Then Allah, Exalted, said to the claimant: 'Raise your gaze and look at the gardens.' He raised his head and said: 'O Lord, I see cities of gold and palaces of gold crowned with pearls. For which prophet is this, or for which truthful one, or for which martyr?' He said: 'This is for the one who pays the price.' He said: 'O Lord, who can own that?' He said: 'You can own it.' He said: 'By what?' He said: 'By your pardoning your brother.' He said: 'O Lord, I have pardoned him.' Allah ﷻ said: 'Take your brother by the hand and enter him into Paradise.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: 'Fear Allah and reconcile what is between you, for Allah, Exalted, reconciles between the Muslims.'\""],[8730,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever would like to look at the Day of Resurrection as if seeing it with his own eye, let him recite: 'When the sun is wrapped up,' 'When the sky is cleft asunder,' and 'When the sky is split open.'\""],[8731,"Indeed, disgrace will cling to a man on the Day of Resurrection until he says: 'O Lord, Your sending me to the Fire would be easier for me than what I am facing,' and he knows what is in it of severe punishment."],[8732,"We conversed one night in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spoke at length. He said: Then we returned to our houses. When morning came, we went to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: \"The prophets were presented to me tonight with their followers from their communities. A prophet would come with three of his people, a prophet with a band, a prophet with a small group, and a prophet with no one from his people, until Moses b. ʿImrān came to me in a large crowd of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, they impressed me, and I said: 'O Lord, who are these?' He said: 'This is your brother Moses b. ʿImrān and those who followed him from the Children of Israel.' He said: I said: 'O Lord, where is my community?' It was said to me: 'Look to your right.' And behold, the hills—the hills of Makkah—were blackened with the faces of men. I said: 'O Lord, who are these?' He said: 'Your community.' He said: It was said to me: 'Are you pleased?' I said: 'O Lord, I am pleased.' He said: Then it was said to me: 'Indeed, with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.' He said: ʿUkkāsha b. Miḥṣan, the brother of Banū Asad b. Khuzayma, stood up and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, supplicate your Lord to make me one of them.' He said: 'O Allah, make him one of them.' Then another man stood up and said: 'O Prophet of Allah, supplicate your Lord to make me one of them.' He said: 'ʿUkkāsha has preceded you to it.' He said: Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom. If you are able to be among the seventy, then be so. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the hills. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon, for I saw there many people jostling.' He said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, I hope that those who follow me from my community will be a quarter of the people of Paradise.' He said: We said 'Allāhu akbar.' Then he said: 'Indeed, I hope that you will be a third.' We said 'Allāhu akbar.' Then he said: 'Indeed, I hope that you will be half.' We said 'Allāhu akbar.' He said: Then the Prophet of Allah ﷺ recited: {A multitude from the former generations and a multitude from the later generations} [al-Wāqiʿa 40]. He said: The Muslims went back to discussing these seventy, and they said: 'We think they are people who were born in Islam and continued acting upon it until they died upon it.' Their talk reached the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, and he said: 'It is not so; rather, they are those who do not seek ruqya, do not cauterize, do not take omens, and upon their Lord they rely.'\""],[8733,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'What is with you, O ʿĀʾisha?' She said: 'I remembered the Fire and wept. Will you remember your families on the Day of Resurrection?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'As for three stations, no one will remember anyone: until he knows whether his scale is light or heavy; at the books, until it is said: {Here, read my record}, until he knows where his book will fall—in his right hand, in his left hand, or from behind his back; and at the bridge, when it is placed across the middle of Hell, its edges having many hooks and many thorns by which Allah withholds whomever He wills of His creation, until he knows whether he will be saved or not.'"],[8734,"We sat with Abdullah b. Amr in al-Hijr, and he said: \"Weep, and if you cannot weep, then pretend to weep. If you knew the knowledge, one of you would pray until his back broke, and he would weep until his voice ceased.\""],[8735,"\"If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and food and drink would not go down easily for you, and you would not sleep on beds, and you would forsake women, and you would go out to the high places crying out and weeping. And I wish that Allah had created me a tree that is cut down.\""],[8736,"\"If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little. Hypocrisy will appear, trust will be lifted, mercy will be withheld, the trustworthy will be accused, and the untrustworthy will be entrusted. Extravagance and sin have settled upon you.\" They said: \"What are extravagance and sin, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Tribulations like patches of dark night.\""],[8737,"\"I see what you do not see, and I hear what you do not hear. The heaven creaked, and it had a right to creak, for there is not a space of four fingers in it but an angel is placing his forehead prostrating to Allah. By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much, and you would not enjoy women on beds, and you would go out to the high places crying out to Allah. And I wish that I were a tree that is cut down.\""],[8738,"\"O Allah, call me to account with an easy reckoning.\" He said: I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is the easy reckoning?\" He said: \"That He looks at his evil deeds and overlooks them for him. Indeed, whoever is closely questioned about his account on that day will perish. And whatever afflicts the believer, Allah expiates from his evil deeds, even the thorn that pricks him.\""],[8739,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was raising my hands and saying, \"O Allah, call me to account with an easy reckoning.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do you know what that reckoning is?\" I said: \"Allah, exalted is He, mentioned in His Book: {Then he will be judged with an easy reckoning} [al-Inshiqaq: 8].\" He said to me: \"O A'ishah, whoever is judged will be condemned. That is the passing before Allah, the Exalted.\" Al-Harish said: Al-Bukhari said about his hadith: \"It is to be examined.\""],[8740,"\"The least punished of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection will be a man for whom two sandals of fire will be made, from which his brain will boil on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[8741,"\"The least punished of the people of the Fire will be one who has two sandals and two straps of fire, from which his brain will boil as a cooking pot boils. And he will think that no one in the Fire has a more severe punishment than him, while he is the least punished of them.\""],[8742,"I heard Khaythamah also mention this hadith from al-Nu'man b. Bashir."],[8743,"\"The least punished of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection will be a man for whom an ember is placed on the soles of his feet, from which his brain will boil.\""],[8744,"\"The least punished of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection will be a man on the soles of whose feet there are two embers, from which his brain will boil as a cooking pot and a long-necked earthenware flask boil.\""],[8745,"\"The least punished of the people of the Fire on the Day of Resurrection will be a man wearing two sandals of fire, from which his brain will boil. Among them are those who are in the Fire up to their knees, with segments of punishment; among them are those upon their cloaks, with segments of punishment; among them are those up to their collarbones, with segments of punishment; and among them are those who are completely submerged in it.\""],[8746,"The least punished of the people will be Abu Talib, and in his two feet will be two sandals of fire from which his brain will boil."],[8748,"People will be gathered at the bridge of Hell, upon it are thorns and hooks. The people will pass, and some of them will pass like lightning, some like a lean horse, some will run, some will walk, some will crawl, and the angels will be on its two sides saying: 'O Allah, grant safety, grant safety,' and the hooks will snatch them. He said: As for its inhabitants who are its rightful inhabitants, they will neither die nor live. And as for some people who are taken for sins and errors, they will burn and become charcoal, then they will be taken in groups, groups, and thrown onto a river of Paradise, and they will sprout as a seed sprouts in the silt of a flood. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Have you seen the ṣabghāʾ (a plant)? Then after that permission is given for them and they enter Paradise.' Abu Sa'id said: One of them will be given the like of the world. He said: And on the ṣirāṭ there are three trees, and the last one to exit the Fire will be on its edge. He will say: 'O Lord, bring me near to this tree so that I may be in its shade and eat from its fruit.' He said: He will say: 'Your covenant and your protection that you will not ask Me for anything else.' He will say: 'My covenant and my protection that I will not ask for anything else.' So he will be moved to it, and he will see another tree better than it, and he will say: 'O Lord, this one I will eat from its fruit and be in its shade.' So he will be moved to it. Then he will see another better than it, and he will say: 'O Lord, this one I will eat from its fruit and be in its shade.' So he will be moved to it. He said: Then he will hear the voices of the people and see their blackness, and he will say: 'O Lord, admit me into Paradise.' Abu Sa'id said: Then after that he mentioned the companions of the Prophet ﷺ; he mentioned it, and one of them said: 'He will be given the like of the world and its like with it.' And another said: 'The like of the world and ten times its like.'"],[8749,"The ṣirāṭ will be placed between the two sides of Hell, upon it are thorns like the thorns of saʿdān. Then the people will try to cross, so there will be one who is saved and unharmed, one who is wounded but then spared, and one who is held back and thrown headlong into it. When Allah the Exalted has finished judging between the servants, the believers will look for men who in the world used to pray their prayers, give their zakāh, fast their fasts, perform their Hajj, and go on their expeditions. They will say: 'O our Lord, there were servants among Your servants who were with us in the world, praying with our prayers, giving zakāh with our zakāh, fasting with our fasts, performing Hajj with our Hajj, and going on expeditions with our expeditions, but we do not see them.' He said: He will say: 'Go to the Fire, and whoever you find in it, bring him out.' He said: They will find them, and the Fire has taken hold of them according to the measure of their deeds. Among them is one whom it has taken up to his two feet, among them one whom it has taken up to his two knees, among them one whom it has taken up to his waist, among them one whom it has taken up to his two breasts, and among them one whom it has taken up to his neck, but the faces have not been covered. He said: They will extract them and throw them into the water of life. It was said: 'O Prophet of Allah, what is the water of life?' He said: 'The washing of the people of Paradise, and they will sprout in it as a plant sprouts in the scum of a flood. Then the prophets will intercede for everyone who bore witness that there is no god but Allah sincerely, and they will extract them from it. Then Allah will turn with His mercy to those who are in it, and He will not leave in it anyone in whose heart there is an atom's weight of faith except that He brings him out of it.'"],[8750,"The scale will be set up on the Day of Resurrection, and if the heavens and the earth were weighed in it, it would contain them. The angels will say: 'O Lord, for whom will this weigh?' Allah the Exalted will say: 'For whomever I will of My creation.' The angels will say: 'Glory be to You, we have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped.' And the ṣirāṭ will be placed like the edge of a razor. The angels will say: 'Who will cross this?' He will say: 'Whomever I will of My creation.' They will say: 'Glory be to You, we have not worshipped You as You deserve to be worshipped.'"],[8751,"Among the people of the Fire are those whom the Fire takes up to his two ankles, among them those whom it takes up to his two knees, among them those whom it takes up to his waist, and among them those whom it takes up to his collarbone."],[8752,"Regarding His saying, Exalted is He: {And there is none of you except he will come to it} [Maryam: 71]—he narrated to me that ʿAbdullāh b. Masʿūd narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The people will enter the Fire, then they will depart from it according to their deeds. The first of them will be like the blink of lightning, then like the wind, then like the racing of a horse, then like a rider in his saddle, then like the running of a man, then like his walking.'"],[8753,"From ʿAbdullāh: {And there is none of you except he will come to it} [Maryam: 71]. He said: 'They will come to it, then they will depart from it according to their deeds.'"],[8754,"From ʿAbdullāh: {And there is none of you except he will come to it} [Maryam: 71]. He said: 'They will come to it, then they will depart from it according to their deeds.' ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Mahdī said: I narrated to Shuʿbah from Isrāʾīl from al-Suddī from Murrah from ʿAbdullāh, raised to the Prophet ﷺ, but I deliberately leave it."],[8755,"We differed here about al-wurūd. Some people said: No believer will enter it, and others said: They will all enter it, then Allah will save those who feared. I said to him: We differed about it in Basra. Some people said: No believer will enter it, and others said: They will all enter it, then Allah will save those who feared. So he pointed with his two fingers to his two ears and said: May they be deaf if I have not heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Al-wurūd is the entry. Neither a righteous person nor a wicked person will remain except that he will enter it, and it will be coolness and safety for the believer as it was for Ibrāhīm, until the Fire—or he said Hell—will have a roaring from its flames.' Then he said: 'Then Allah will save those who feared and will leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees.'"],[8756,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Exalted is He: {And there is none of you except he will come to it} [Maryam: 71]. He said: 'There is none of you except he will enter it; it has been upon your Lord an inevitability decreed. Then Allah will save those who feared and will leave the wrongdoers in it on their knees.'"],[8757,"A man will surely take the hand of his father on the Day of Resurrection, and the Fire will surely cut it, intending to enter him into Paradise. He said: Then it will be called out: 'Indeed, Paradise will not be entered by a polytheist. Verily, Allah has forbidden Paradise to every polytheist.' He said: Then he will say: 'O Lord, my father,' so he will be turned into an ugly form and a foul smell, and he will leave him. He said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ thought that it was Ibrāhīm ﷺ , and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not add anything to them beyond that."],[8758,"ʿAbdullāh b. Rawāḥah wept, and his wife wept. He said: 'What makes you weep?' She said: 'I saw you weeping, so I wept.' He said: 'I have been informed that I will come to it, but I have not been informed that I will depart from it.'"],[8759,"I recalled the saying of Allah ﷻ {And there is none of you but will pass over it} [Maryam 71], and I do not know whether I will be saved from it or not."],[8760,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah will gather the people, and the believers will stand when Paradise is brought near. They will come to Adam ﷺ and say, \"O our father, open Paradise for us.\" He will say, \"Did anything expel you from Paradise except the error of your father Adam? I am not the one for that. Go to Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah.\" They will come to Ibrahim, and Ibrahim will say, \"I am not the one for that. I was only a friend from behind a veil. Go to the Prophet Musa, whom Allah spoke to directly.\" They will come to Musa, and he will say, \"I am not the one for that. Go to the Word of Allah and His Spirit, 'Isa.\" 'Isa will say, \"I am not the one for that.\" They will come to Muhammad ﷺ, and he will stand and permission will be given to him, and the trust and the ties of kinship will be sent with him, and they will stand on the right and left of the bridge. Then the first of you will pass like lightning. I said, \"May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, what is the passing of lightning?\" He said, \"Have you not seen how lightning passes and returns in the blink of an eye? Then like the passing of the wind, and the passing of birds, and the speed of mounts. Their deeds will carry them, and your Prophet will be standing on the bridge saying, 'My Lord, grant safety, grant safety.'\" He said, \"Until people's deeds fall short, until a man comes and cannot pass except by crawling.\" He said, \"And on the two edges of the bridge there are hooks suspended, commanded to seize those they are ordered to seize. Some will be scratched but saved, and some will be piled into the Fire. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Abu Hurayrah, the depth of Hell is seventy autumns.\""],[8761,"A man will meet his father on the Day of Resurrection and say to him, \"O my father, what kind of son was I to you?\" He will say, \"The best of sons.\" He will say, \"Will you obey me today?\" He will say, \"Yes.\" He will say, \"Take hold of my waist wrapper.\" He will take hold of his waist wrapper, then they will go until he comes to Allah, Blessed and Exalted, while He is presenting the creation. He will say, \"O My servant, enter from whichever gate of Paradise you wish.\" He will say, \"O my Lord, and my father with me, for You promised me that You would not disgrace me.\" He said, \"Then Allah will transform his father into a hyena, and he will turn away from him, and he will fall into the Fire, and he will seize him by his nose. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, will say, 'O My servant, is this your father?' He will say, 'No, by Your might.'\""],[8763,"From the Prophet ﷺ, who said: \"There are no two Muslims who have four children die, except that Allah will admit them to Paradise by the excess of His mercy toward them.\" We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and three?\" He said, \"And three.\" We said, \"O Messenger of Allah, and two?\" He said, \"And two.\" Then he said, \"Indeed, among my nation there are those who will be magnified in the Fire until he becomes one of its corners, and indeed among my nation there are those who will enter Paradise by his intercession more than the tribe of Mudar.\""],[8764,"\"This fire of yours is one part of seventy parts of the Fire of Hell. If it had not been dipped in water twice, you would not have been able to benefit from it. By Allah, it is sufficient. Indeed, it beseeches Allah or seeks refuge with Allah that He never returns it to the Fire again.\""],[8765,"\"Indeed, in the Fire there are serpents like the necks of Bactrian camels. One of them will bite a person with a single bite, and he will feel its heat for forty autumns.\""],[8766,"From 'Abdullah regarding the saying of Allah ﷻ {We increased them in punishment upon punishment} [Al-Nahl 88], he said: \"Scorpions whose fangs are like tall palm trees.\""],[8767,"Indeed, the earths: between each earth and the one that follows it is a distance of five hundred years' journey. The uppermost of them is on the back of a fish whose two ends meet in the sky. The fish is on a rock, and the rock is in the hand of an angel. The second is the place of the wind's subjection. When Allah willed to destroy 'Ad, He commanded the keeper of the wind to send upon them a wind to destroy 'Ad. He said, \"O Lord, shall I send upon them a wind the size of a bull's nostril?\" The Compeller, Blessed and Exalted, said to him, \"Then it would suffice the earth and whoever is on it, but send upon them the size of a ring.\" This is the one about which Allah ﷻ said in His Mighty Book: {It spared nothing that it came upon, but made it like decayed bones} [Al-Dhariyat 42]. The third contains the stones of Hell. The fourth contains the brimstone of Hell. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, does the Fire have brimstone?\" He said, \"Yes, by the One in whose hand is my soul, in it there are valleys of brimstone. If the firmly rooted mountains were sent into it, they would melt. The fifth contains the serpents of Hell. Their mouths are like valleys. They bite the disbeliever with a bite, and no flesh remains on his bones. The sixth contains the scorpions of Hell. The smallest scorpion among them is like saddled mules. It strikes the disbeliever with a strike, and its strike makes him forget the heat of Hell. The seventh is Saqar, and in it is Iblis, shackled in iron, one hand before him and one hand behind him. When Allah wills to release him for whatever He wills of His servants, He releases him.\""],[8768,"When this verse was revealed in Al-Muzzammil: {And leave Me with the deniers, the possessors of ease, and give them respite a little. Indeed, with Us are fetters and a blazing Fire} [Al-Muzzammil 12], it was only a short while until the Battle of Badr occurred."],[8770,"\"Hell will be brought on that Day, and it will have seventy thousand reins, with each rein seventy thousand angels dragging it.\""],[8771,"\"The molar tooth of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like Mount Uhud, the thickness of his skin seventy cubits, his upper arm like Al-Bayda', his thigh like Warqan, and his seat from the Fire will be the distance between me and Al-Rabadhah.\""],[8772,"\"Indeed, the thickness of the disbeliever's skin will be forty-two cubits by the cubit of the Compeller, and his molar tooth like Mount Uhud.\""],[8773,"Indeed, the molar tooth of the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection will be like (Mount) Uhud, and his head like al-Bayda', and his thigh like Warqan, and the thickness of his skin seventy cubits, and indeed his sitting place in the Fire will be as (the distance) between al-Madinah and al-Rabadhah. Abu Hurayrah said: It used to be said his belly would be like the belly of Idam."],[8774,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, the sea is Jahannam.” They said to Ya'la: Allah ﷻ said, {a fire whose tent encloses them} [al-Kahf 29]. He said: “By the One in Whose hand is my soul, I will never enter it until I meet Allah, and not a drop of it will touch me.”"],[8775,"“I saw smoke from the Mosque of Dirar when it collapsed.”"],[8776,"“Wayl is a valley in Jahannam into which the disbeliever falls for forty autumns before reaching its bottom, and al-Sa'ud is a mountain in the Fire in which he climbs for seventy autumns, falling from it likewise forever.”"],[8777,"“Indeed, in Jahannam there is a valley, and in that valley there is a well called Habhab. It is incumbent upon Allah, Exalted is He, to make every tyrant dwell in it.” So beware lest you be one of them, O Bilal."],[8778,"“A period of fifty thousand years will be set up for the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection, during which he did not work in this world, and he will think that he is being reprieved.”"],[8779,"“By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the distance between the edge of the Fire and its bottom is like a rock whose weight is seven pregnant camels with their fat, flesh, and offspring, falling between the edge of the Fire and its bottom until it reaches its bottom for seventy autumns.”"],[8780,"“By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the distance between the edge of the Fire and its bottom until it reaches its bottom is seventy autumns.”"],[8781,"“Indeed, a man may utter a word, not thinking it will reach what it has reached, by which he falls for seventy autumns in the Fire.”"],[8782,"\"He reprieved them for forty years, and then responded to them [saying], 'Indeed, you are to remain [here]'. And they will say, 'Our Lord, remove us from it, and if we were to return [to evil], we would indeed be wrongdoers'. He will say, 'Remain despised therein and do not speak to Me'. Indeed, there was a party of My servants who said, 'Our Lord, we have believed, so forgive us and have mercy upon us, and You are the best of the merciful ones'. But you took them in mockery to the point that they made you forget My remembrance, and you used to laugh at them. Indeed, I have rewarded them this Day for their patient endurance - that they are the attainers [of success].\"\" (Qur'an 43:77-80)"],[8783,"“The seat of the disbeliever in the Fire is a journey of three days, and every molar tooth is like (Mount) Uhud, and his thigh is like Warqan, and his skin, apart from his flesh and bones, is forty cubits.”"],[8785,"“If an iron mace were placed on the earth and the two heavy species (humans and jinn) gathered to lift it, they could not lift it from the earth.”"],[8786,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Prophet of Allah, I did not come to you until I had left behind more than these—meaning the two hands altogether—and I do not come to your religion nor to you, and I was a man who understood nothing except what Allah and His Messenger taught me. So I ask you by the Face of Allah: with what did our Lord send you? He said: “With Islam.” He said: I said: O Prophet of Allah, and what is the sign of Islam? He said: “That you say, ‘I have submitted my face to Allah,’ and you establish prayer and give zakah. Every Muslim is sacred to another Muslim; they are brothers, becoming so. Allah does not accept from a Muslim who associates others after having submitted any deed until he separates from the polytheists to the Muslims. What is wrong with me, holding you by your waist-wrappers away from the Fire? Verily, my Lord is calling me, and indeed He will ask me: ‘Did you convey to My servants?’ And I will say: ‘My Lord, I have conveyed to them.’ So let those present among you convey to those absent. Then you will be called with the fronts of your mouths muzzled with the fidam. Then the first thing to become clear of one of you will be his thigh and his palm.” He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is our religion, and where is what you perfect with your hand?"],[8787,"\"The canopy of the Fire is four walls, each wall of which is a journey of forty years.\""],[8788,"I heard 'Abd Allah b. 'Amr saying: Indeed, the wall that Allah, the Exalted, mentioned in the Quran—\"Then a wall will be placed between them, which has a gate, its interior containing mercy and its exterior, from its side, punishment\" [al-Hadid 13]—is the eastern wall; its interior is the mosque and what surrounds it, and its exterior is the Valley of Jahannam."],[8789,"\"If an iron hammer of Jahannam were to strike the mountain, it would crumble as it strikes the people of the Fire and become dust.\""],[8790,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ laughed one day, or smiled, and then said: \"Will you not ask me what I laughed about?\" He said: \"I marvel at the argument of the servant with his Lord on the Day of Resurrection. He says: 'O Lord, did You not promise me that You would not wrong me?' He says: 'Indeed.' He says: 'I will not accept any witness against me except from myself.' Then He says: 'Is it not sufficient that I am a witness and the noble recording angels?'\" He said: \"So he repeats this speech several times, then a seal is placed over his mouth, and his limbs speak of what he used to do. Then he says: 'Away with you and perish! I was arguing on your behalf.'\""],[8791,"\"If a bucket of ghassaq were poured into the world, it would make the people of the world stink.\""],[8792,"I heard Mutarrif narrate that he had two wives. He went to one of them, and she began to remove his turban and said: \"Have you come from your other wife?\" He said: \"I have come from 'Imran b. Husayn, who narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he said: 'The least of the inhabitants of Paradise are women.'\""],[8793,"We were with 'Amr b. al-'As on a Hajj or 'Umrah. When we were at Marr al-Zahran, there was a woman in her howdah, placing her hand on it, wearing rings. When we descended into the mountain pass, we saw many crows, among them a white-footed crow with a red beak and red legs. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"None of the women will enter Paradise except like this crow among these crows.\""],[8794,"We were with 'Amr b. al-'As on a Hajj or 'Umrah. There was a woman with rings on her hand, and she had placed her hand on her howdah. 'Amr b. al-'As entered a mountain pass and then said: \"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in this mountain pass when there were many crows and a white-footed crow with a red beak and red legs. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'None of the women will enter Paradise except as much as this crow among these crows.'\""],[8795,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"O women, give charity even from your adornments, for you are the majority of the inhabitants of Hell.\" A woman who was not from the elite of women asked, \"Why are we the majority of the inhabitants of Hell, O Messenger of Allah?\" He replied, \"Because you curse frequently and show ingratitude to your husbands. I have not seen anyone more deficient in intelligence and religion than you.”"],[8796,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave us a sermon and said: \"O assembly of women, give charity, even from your jewelry, for you are the majority of the inhabitants of Jahannam on the Day of Resurrection.\" She said: \"'Abd Allah was a man of light means, so I said to him: 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for me: Is spending on my husband and orphans in my care sufficient for me as charity?'\" She said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had an awe-inspiring presence, so 'Abd Allah said to me: 'Go and ask him.'\" She said: \"I went and reached the door, where there was a woman from the Ansar whose need was the same as mine.\" She said: \"Bilal came out to us, and we said to him: 'Ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for us: Is spending on our husbands and on orphans in our care sufficient for us as charity?'\" She said: \"Bilal went in to him and said: 'At the door are Zaynab—' He said: 'Which of the Zaynabs?' He said: 'Zaynab, the wife of 'Abd Allah, and Zaynab, a woman from the Ansar, are asking you about spending on their husbands and orphans in their care: Is that sufficient for them as charity?'\" She said: \"Bilal came out to us and said: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"They will have two rewards: the reward of kinship and the reward of charity.\"'”"],[8797,"'Ubadah b. al-Samit was on the eastern wall of Jerusalem, weeping. Some of them said: \"What makes you weep, O Abu al-Walid?\" He said: \"From here...\""],[8798,"\"Water like molten metal, like the dregs of oil; when it is brought near his mouth, the skin of his face falls into it.\""],[8799,"\"Indeed, the dissolute are the people of the Fire.\" They said: \"O Messenger of Allah, who are the dissolute?\" He said: \"Women.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of Allah, are they not our mothers, sisters, and wives?\" He said: \"Indeed, but when they are given, they are not grateful, and when they are tested, they are not patient.\""],[8800,"While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the noon prayer, the people were in rows behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. We saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reaching for something; he kept reaching for it, and he stepped back, and the people stepped back. Then he stepped back a second time, and the people stepped back. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do something today that you did not use to do in prayer.\" He said, \"Paradise with its splendor and radiance was presented to me, and I reached for a bunch of its grapes. Had I taken it, those between heaven and earth would have eaten of it without diminishing it, but it was withheld from me. Then the Fire was presented to me, and when I felt its scorching heat, I stepped back from it. Most of those whom I saw in it were women: if they are entrusted, they divulge; if they ask, they are importunate; if they are asked, they are stingy; and if they are given, they do not give thanks. I saw in it 'Amr b. Luhayy dragging his intestines in the Fire. The one I saw who most resembled him is Ma'bad b. Aktham al-Khuza'i.\" Ma'bad said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you fear for me because of his resemblance? He is my father.\" He said, \"No, you are a believer and he is a disbeliever. He was the first to lead the Arabs to worship idols.\""],[8801,"\"The Fire was presented to me, and I saw in it 'Amr b. Luhayy b. Qama'ah b. Khindif, Abu 'Amr, dragging his intestines in the Fire. He was the first to dedicate animals to idols and changed the covenant of Ibrahim ﷺ . The one I saw who most resembled him is Aktham b. Abi al-Jawn.\" He said: Aktham said, \"O Messenger of Allah, will his resemblance harm me?\" He said, \"No, you are a Muslim and he is a disbeliever.\""],[8802,"When the Day of Resurrection comes, the disbeliever will be confronted with his deeds, but he will deny and dispute. It will be said to him, \"Your neighbors will testify against you,\" but he will say, \"They lie.\" It will be said, \"Your family and clan,\" but he will say, \"They lie.\" It will be said, \"Swear,\" and they will swear. Then Allah will silence them, and their own tongues will testify against them, and He will cast them into the Fire."],[8803,"\"The people of the Fire will weep until, were ships to sail in their tears, they would sail, and they will weep blood—meaning in place of tears.\""],[8804,"\"Were seven pregnant camels with their fat to be taken and cast from the edge of Hell, they would not reach its bottom for seventy years.\""],[8805,"Al-Buraq was brought to me, and I rode behind Jibril ﷺ . He traveled with us; when he ascended, his legs rose, and when he descended, his hands rose. He said: He traveled with us through a land that was gloomy and stinking until we came out to a land that was spacious and pleasant. I said, \"O Jibril, we were traveling through a gloomy, stinking land, then we came out to a spacious, pleasant land.\" He said, \"That was the land of the Fire, and this is the land of Paradise.\" He said: I came to a man standing in prayer. He said, \"Who is this with you, O Jibril?\" He said, \"This is your brother Muhammad.\" He welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me and said, \"Ask ease for your community.\" I said, \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said, \"This is your brother 'Isa ibn Maryam, peace and blessings be upon him.\" He said: We traveled on and I heard a voice and grumbling. We came to a man. He said, \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said, \"This is your brother Muhammad.\" He welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me and said, \"Ask ease for your community.\" I said, \"Who is this, O Jibril?\" He said, \"This is your brother Musa.\" I said, \"Against whom was his grumbling and voice?\" He said, \"Against his Lord.\" I said, \"Against his Lord?\" He said, \"Yes, that is known from his intensity.\" He said: Then we traveled on and saw lamps and light. He said: I said, \"What is this, O Jibril?\" He said, \"This is the tree of your father Ibrahim, peace and blessings be upon him. Shall we draw near to it?\" I said, \"Yes.\" We drew near, and he welcomed me and prayed for blessing for me. Then we went on until we came to Bayt al-Maqdis. I tethered the mount to the ring to which the prophets tether, then I entered the mosque. The prophets whom Allah ﷻ has named and those He has not named were gathered for me, and I prayed with them, except for these three: Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa, peace and blessings be upon them."],[8806,"This community will be gathered into three groups: a group that will enter Paradise without reckoning, a group that will be given an easy reckoning, and another that will pass on their backs with loads like towering mountains. Allah will ask about them, though He knows best, and will say, \"These are servants of My servants who did not associate anything with Me, and on their backs are sins and errors. Remove them and place them upon the Jews and the Christians, and enter Paradise by My mercy.\""],[8807,"\"Cunning, deceit, and treachery are in the Fire.\""],[8808,"Has the redness risen yet? When he saw it, he said, \"No welcome.\" Then he said, \"Two angels, Harut and Marut, asked Allah Almighty to descend to earth, and they were sent down to earth. They used to judge between people. When evening came, they would say some words and ascend with them to heaven. A woman of the fairest among people was sent to them, and desire was cast upon them. They kept putting her off, but it was cast into their hearts. They continued doing so until she promised them an appointment. She came to them at the appointment and said, 'Teach me the word by which you ascend.' They taught her the word, and she spoke it and ascended with it to heaven. She was transformed and made as you see. When evening came to them, they spoke the word by which they used to ascend to heaven, but they did not ascend. It was sent to them: 'If you wish, the punishment of the Hereafter; and if you wish, the punishment of this world until the Hour arises, on condition that you meet Allah Almighty; then if He wills, He will punish you, and if He wills, He will have mercy on you.' One of them looked at his companion, and one of them said to his companion, 'Rather, we choose the punishment of this world a thousand thousand times over.' So they are being punished until the Hour arises.\""],[8809,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ mention \"the extent of sweat from the son of Adam.\" One of them said, \"To the lobes of his ears,\" and the other said, \"The sweat will bridle him.\" Ibn 'Umar gestured and drew a line with his index finger between the lobe of his ear."],[8810,"We visited a man who was feverish with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I placed my hand on him and said, \"By Allah, I have never seen a man with more intense heat than him today.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Shall I tell you of one with more intense heat than him on the Day of Resurrection? Those two men riding and turning their backs\"—referring to two men among his companions at that time."],[8811,"From the Messenger of Allah ﷺ : \"Indeed, when Allah intends goodness for His servant, He hastens punishment for him in this world. And when Allah intends harm for His servant, He restrains him with his sins until he faces him on the Day of Resurrection.\" Adh-Dhahabi remained silent about this in his summary."],[8812,"We stopped at a parasang from al-Mada'in. When Friday came, he attended, and I attended with him. Hudhayfah delivered a sermon to us, saying: \"Allah ﷻ says: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split} [Al-Qamar 1]. Indeed, the Hour has drawn near; indeed, the moon has split; indeed, the world has announced its parting; indeed, today is the training ground and tomorrow is the race.\" I said to my father, \"Will people race tomorrow?\" He said, \"O my son, you are ignorant. He means deeds today and recompense tomorrow.\" When the next Friday came, we attended, and Hudhayfah delivered a sermon to us, saying: \"Allah ﷻ says: {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split} [Al-Qamar 1]. Indeed, the world has announced its parting; indeed, today is the training ground and tomorrow is the race; indeed, the goal is the Fire, and the winner is the one who races to Paradise.\""],[8813,"“The earth consumes everything of a human being except the coccyx.” It was said: “And what is it, O Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Like a mustard seed; from it they will be created.”"],[8814,"A group of Qur'an reciters entered upon Abu Dharr while a black woman was with him wearing a Qatawani cloak, with no embroidered garments or perfume. Abu Dharr said: “Do you know what this one says? She tells me to go to Iraq. If I went to Iraq, they would say: 'This is a companion of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ,' and they would incline toward us with worldly things. Indeed, my close friend Abu al-Qasim ﷺ entrusted to me that the bridge of Hell is slippery and causes feet to slip, and in our burdens there is corruption; perhaps we may be saved from them.”"],[8815,"Regarding His saying, may He be exalted: {And indeed, a day with your Lord is like a thousand years of those which you count} [al-Hajj 47], he said: “Who are you?” The man mentioned that he was from such-and-such. Ibn Abbas said: “Then what about a day whose measure is fifty thousand years?” The man said: “May Allah have mercy on you. I only asked you so that you would tell us.” Ibn Abbas said: “Two days that Allah, may He be exalted, mentioned in His Book; Allah knows best about them. He disliked speaking about Allah's Book without knowledge.”"]]);
